window.TEAMS_FULL = {"6040":{"team":"McGill","id":"6040","section":"Undergrad","country":"Canada","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/mcgill/","projectTitle":"LanTurn","projectTitle_zh":"LanTurn","tagline":"Lanmodulin displayed on yeast, harvested by light-triggered flocculation, deployed on-site as a tolling service for mine tailings","tagline_zh":"將 lanmodulin 展示於酵母表面，以光觸發絮凝收集菌體，並以現場代工服務的形式部署於礦場尾礦","summary":"McGill engineered Saccharomyces cerevisiae EBY100 to display lanmodulin variants on its surface via the Aga1-Aga2 system for selective rare-earth binding, and to flocculate on command through a blue-light VP16-EL222 / C120 optogenetic circuit driving a truncated 678FLO1 flocculin, so that REE-loaded cells can be separated by gravity settling instead of centrifugation. Light-induced flocculation reached 66-75 percent against 24-25 percent in dark controls, and LanM surface display was confirmed by flow cytometry and confocal microscopy. The commercial case is a full industrial techno-economic analysis rather than a canvas: gate-to-gate CAPEX and OPEX, a unit cost of $11.83-20.58 USD per kg REO, a full-scale NPV case study on the Ashram tailings in Nunavik, Quebec, and seven separate sensitivity analyses. They were nominated for Best Entrepreneurship (Undergrad) and Best Biomanufacturing.","summary_zh":"McGill 改造 Saccharomyces cerevisiae EBY100，透過 Aga1-Aga2 系統將 lanmodulin 變異體展示於細胞表面以選擇性結合稀土元素，並以藍光 VP16-EL222 / C120 光遺傳學迴路驅動截短的 678FLO1 絮凝素，使細胞可依指令絮凝，讓吸附稀土的細胞以重力沉降取代離心分離。光誘導絮凝達 66-75%，暗處對照組為 24-25%；LanM 表面展示則以流式細胞術與共軛焦顯微術確認。其商業論證是完整的工業級技術經濟分析，而不是一張商業模式圖：涵蓋 gate-to-gate 的資本支出與營運支出、每公斤 REO 11.83-20.58 美元的單位成本、以魁北克 Nunavik 的 Ashram 尾礦為對象的全規模 NPV 個案研究，以及七項獨立的敏感度分析。他們入圍 Best Entrepreneurship（大學部）與 Best Biomanufacturing。","awards":["Best Entrepreneurship — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Biomanufacturing Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Technology Readiness Levels (NASA nine-level scale, chosen specifically because Canadian cleantech and mining funding programmes gate on TRL) as the backbone of a four-phase staged development plan, each phase carrying goals, named partners, a funding figure and source, and a risk-and-mitigation table. Plus techno-economic analysis in three parts (gate-to-gate, full-scale case study, sensitivity), competitor tiering into direct, substitute and future, a four-option exit plan, a skill-gap analysis mapped against the advisory board, an IP and freedom-to-operate review, and a one-year incorporation plan with a one-pager.","frameworks_zh":"以技術成熟度等級（TRL，NASA 的九級量表；之所以選用，是因為加拿大的清潔科技與礦業補助計畫都以 TRL 作為門檻）作為四階段分期開發計畫的骨幹，每一階段都列出目標、具名合作夥伴、資金金額與來源，以及風險與緩解對策表。此外還有分成三部分的技術經濟分析（gate-to-gate、全規模個案研究、敏感度分析）、把競爭者分為直接、替代與未來三層的分析、四種選項的退場計畫、對照顧問團成員盤點的技能缺口分析、智慧財產權與 freedom-to-operate 檢視，以及附一頁式簡介的一年期公司設立計畫。","dataviz":"A tabbed entrepreneurship page with a Sankey flowchart of critical-materials flows, a rare-earth demand-and-project-gap chart, a TEA workflow flowsheet, CAPEX/OPEX tables for both gate-to-gate and full-scale cases, a financial-analysis panel, and seven sensitivity charts (adsorption capacity, desorption efficiency, product purity discount, feedstock grade, yeast dosing concentration, PLS pH, discount rate), plus a tolling-model process diagram and an advisory-board gallery.","dataviz_zh":"以分頁呈現的創業頁面，包含關鍵原料流向的 Sankey 流程圖、稀土需求與專案缺口圖、技術經濟分析的工作流程圖、gate-to-gate 與全規模兩種情境的資本支出與營運支出表、財務分析面板，以及七張敏感度圖表（吸附容量、脫附效率、產品純度折價、原料品位、酵母投加濃度、PLS pH 值、折現率），另有代工模式的製程示意圖與顧問團名錄。","datascience":"Genuinely industrial-grade analysis. Mass balances built in Excel at a PLS flowthrough of 1,200,000 cubic metres per year, 1 g/L REE and 80 percent target recovery; unit-cost benchmarking per kg TREO against solvent extraction, column-immobilised lanmodulin and a Caulobacter-based bioadsorbent; NPV of USD 51M over 15 years in the high-uptake case versus USD -0.2M in the low-uptake case, with payback of 2.6-5.9 years. The sensitivity work generates actual engineering targets: breakeven at about 23 mg/g adsorption capacity, rising to about 35 mg/g once a 20-30 percent impurity discount on mixed REO is applied; every 5 percent loss of desorption efficiency costs roughly USD 10M of project value; profitability is governed almost entirely by initial PLS pH rather than the bioadsorbent's operating pH; and the low-uptake case goes negative above a 15 percent discount rate. Separately, the TORCH dry-lab project runs GROMACS molecular dynamics with QM/MM to engineer the LanM binding site, including a real debugging story about periodic boundary conditions inflating RMSD tenfold.","datascience_zh":"真正達到工業水準的分析。以 Excel 建立質量平衡，條件為 PLS 年處理量 1,200,000 立方公尺、稀土濃度 1 g/L、目標回收率 80%；並以每公斤 TREO 的單位成本，對照溶劑萃取、管柱固定化 lanmodulin 與以 Caulobacter 為基礎的生物吸附劑做基準比較；高採用情境下 15 年 NPV 為 5,100 萬美元，低採用情境為 -20 萬美元，回收期 2.6-5.9 年。敏感度分析產出的是真正可用的工程目標：吸附容量約 23 mg/g 為損益平衡點，若計入混合 REO 的 20-30% 雜質折價，門檻升到約 35 mg/g；脫附效率每下降 5%，專案價值約減少 1,000 萬美元；獲利能力幾乎完全取決於 PLS 的初始 pH 值，而不是生物吸附劑的操作 pH 值；折現率高於 15% 時，低採用情境就轉為負值。另外，乾實驗室的 TORCH 專案以 GROMACS 分子動力學搭配 QM/MM 改造 LanM 的結合位點，其中還包括一段真實的除錯經歷：週期性邊界條件讓 RMSD 被放大十倍。","software":"TORCH, a QM/MM and molecular-dynamics pipeline for optimising the lanmodulin binding site, with custom scripts for RMSD, clustering, radial distribution functions and explicit oxygen-distance coordination counting.","software_zh":"TORCH，一套用於最佳化 lanmodulin 結合位點的 QM/MM 與分子動力學流程，並自行撰寫程式計算 RMSD、分群、徑向分布函數，以及依氧原子距離明確計算配位數。","stack":["GROMACS","VMD","Python","Excel mass-balance and TEA models","S. cerevisiae EBY100 / pYD1 Aga1-Aga2 display","VP16-EL222 / C120 optogenetics","flow cytometry","confocal microscopy","ICP-MS","Xylenol Orange colorimetry"],"techniques":["yeast surface display with FLAG-tag detection","blue-light-inducible flocculation and Helm's flocculation assay","REE adsorption and desorption from flocs","restriction-enzyme cloning with LiOAc/SDS yeast colony PCR","sulfuric acid leaching of real tailings samples","sensitivity and NPV analysis"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"They host their own annual synthetic-biology conference, On the Verge, themed in 2026 as 'On the Verge of Running Out: Building the Bioeconomy', deliberately assembling corporate industry leaders, startup founders, policy experts, researchers and students around resource extraction. They also ran school and summer-camp workshops (microbial painting, acid-base chemistry) and are responding to a teacher's request for more advanced genetic-engineering workshops by exploring chromoproteins for new colours.","publicEngagement_zh":"團隊自辦年度合成生物學會議 On the Verge，2026 年主題為 On the Verge of Running Out: Building the Bioeconomy，刻意圍繞資源開採議題，聚集企業界領袖、新創創辦人、政策專家、研究者與學生。他們也在學校與夏令營舉辦工作坊（微生物繪畫、酸鹼化學），並回應一位老師希望有更進階基因工程工作坊的請求，正嘗試以色素蛋白提供新的顏色選擇。","ihp":"Over 100 stakeholders engaged, with a consultation map that traces who informed what and who they were referred to next, explicitly arguing that no consultation stands alone. The consequential ones are documented as reversals. They abandoned ultra-purification of REEs entirely after Dr. Michael Free and others showed the separation factor cannot support the claim and that the economics would hinge on only the last 0.9 percent of purity, repositioning instead on selective pre-solvent-extraction concentration. Feedstock choice came from Dr. Jayme Fehyl-Buska and Dr. Kevin Moran of CVW Sustainable Royalties; Ms. Julia Vilela Carvalho of UNEP steered them to fresh rather than legacy tailings for liability and environmental-regulation reasons; Peter van Alphen, Bastien Fresia and Gilles Roy of Nuvau Minerals Corp. confirmed mines have space and are used to disposing of new materials, which is why the process was designed around equipment mines already run, and recommended the tolling model. Protocol-level consultations repeatedly rescued failing experiments: Dr. Denzel Ignacia raised the flocculation induction OD to 3-5, Mira Loock supplied a surface-display-specific protocol at OD 0.8-1.2 that finally produced positive metal-binding results, Michael Bellucci spotted restriction sites less than 30 bp apart as the reason digests failed. Jan Morrill of Earthworks pushed back on their sustainability framing by insisting re-mining can inflict the same harm as direct mining and taught them a Free, Prior and Informed Consent framework. Dr. Yvette Baninla widened the analysis to the geopolitics of offshore REE processing and Indigenous consultation.","ihp_zh":"接觸超過 100 位利害關係人，並以一張諮詢地圖標示誰影響了哪一項決定、又被轉介給誰，明確主張沒有任何一次諮詢能獨立成立。真正造成影響的諮詢，都以推翻原案的形式記錄下來。在 Dr. Michael Free 等人指出分離因子無法支撐其主張、而且經濟性其實只取決於純度最後的 0.9% 之後，團隊徹底放棄稀土超高純度精煉，改將定位轉向溶劑萃取前的選擇性濃縮。原料選擇來自 CVW Sustainable Royalties 的 Dr. Jayme Fehyl-Buska 與 Dr. Kevin Moran；UNEP 的 Ms. Julia Vilela Carvalho 以責任歸屬與環境法規為理由，引導他們選擇新產生的尾礦而非舊有尾礦；Nuvau Minerals Corp. 的 Peter van Alphen、Bastien Fresia 與 Gilles Roy 確認礦場有足夠空間、也習慣處置新產生的物料，這正是製程被設計成圍繞礦場既有設備的原因，他們並建議採用代工模式。實驗流程層面的諮詢一再救回失敗的實驗：Dr. Denzel Ignacia 建議把絮凝誘導的 OD 提高到 3-5；Mira Loock 提供專為表面展示設計、在 OD 0.8-1.2 進行的實驗流程，終於做出金屬結合的陽性結果；Michael Bellucci 看出限制酶切位相距不到 30 bp 正是切割失敗的原因。Earthworks 的 Jan Morrill 反駁他們的永續論述，強調再開採可能造成與直接開採同等的傷害，並教他們自由、事先與知情同意（FPIC）的框架。Dr. Yvette Baninla 把分析擴及稀土境外加工的地緣政治與原住民族諮詢議題。","realWorld":"Among the strongest commercialisation cases in iGEM 2026, and the only one in this group with real third-party commitments on paper. The business model is a B2B on-site tolling service: the mine keeps ownership and legal liability for its tailings, LanTurn operates a small modular plant on site and returns a concentrated mixed rare earth oxide, which avoids transport cost and keeps tailings-management liability off LanTurn's books. That model was recommended by Nuvau Minerals Corp. and then re-validated at the REM3 Executive Summit with potential offtakers and feedstock providers. Unit economics are properly built rather than asserted: $11.83-20.58 USD per kg REO gate-to-gate, with about 92 percent of CAPEX in desorption columns and resins and 54-68 percent of OPEX in fermentation, compared against solvent extraction (at worst 12 percent more expensive, at best 370-720 percent cheaper on impure low-grade feedstock), column-immobilised lanmodulin (16-100 percent cheaper) and a lanthanide-binding-tag bioadsorbent. The design choices are individually cost-justified, which is rare: surface display versus purified LanM in agarose resin, flocculation versus continuous centrifugation (though they honestly note this saves only $0.21 per kg TREO and is 'not hugely significant'), and light induction versus copper, ethanol or galactose. The Ashram case study is a real deposit with 51 Mt of flotation tailings at about 0.4 percent TREO, giving a USD 51M NPV over 15 years with a 2.6-year payback in the optimistic case and a marginally negative NPV with a 5.9-year payback in the pessimistic case, and they say so rather than quoting only the good number. The headline $560 billion of locked value in tailings is derived, not borrowed: tailings tonnage times REE concentration times market prices, with a 70 percent discount applied for mixed rather than pure REEs, and they immediately contextualise it against a global REE market of only about USD 4.5 billion. Institutional traction is concrete: entry into the Dobson Lean Startup Accelerator at McGill's Dobson Centre for Entrepreneurship in September 2026, ongoing mentorship from Felicity Meyer, a cleantech investment manager at BoxOne Ventures, guidance from Chris Corkery on McGill's research-commercialisation and tech-transfer route, an eleven-person advisory board spanning hydrometallurgy, mining, VC, biomanufacturing and regulatory affairs, published letters of support from Bastien Fresia of Nuvau Minerals Corp. and Dr. Boyd Davis of Kingston Process Metallurgy, real tailings samples already secured from a large Canadian mining company that plans to continue research with them, and named scale-up facilities (Concordia Bioprocessing Facility at 1000 L, KPM's 10,000 sq ft Kingston pilot plant and its biomining division launching 2027, a Sudbury bioleaching facility). The funding plan is staged and specific: about $28,800 across four quarters for the laboratory phase from university funds and non-dilutive grants (NSERC, NRC IRAP, NFRF), then angel and cleantech VC after incorporation, with later phases pointing at NRCan's CMRDD programme (typically $4M+ for TRL 6-8) and MICA Canada (up to $2.5M for TRL 7-9), benchmarked against actual biomining raises (Allonnia USD 20M Series A, pH7 USD 32M Series B). The IP work is the real thing rather than a slogan: they checked that the foundational yeast surface-display patents US6699658B1 and US7465787B2 have expired, identified live LanM patents (CA3170828A1, CA3223988A1, US20240183787A1) and a pending Princeton application WO2025240129A2 that explicitly claims EL222/C120 optogenetics in S. cerevisiae, and concluded they must differentiate technically, disclose to McGill's Tech Transfer Office before publishing anything patentable, and run a formal freedom-to-operate analysis. Blunt caveats: there is no incorporated company yet, only a one-year incorporation plan; no revenue, no signed tolling contract and no term sheet; and they state outright that many TEA parameters are literature estimates rather than their own measurements, which is exactly why the sensitivity analysis exists as a de-risking to-do list for the wet and dry labs. Their ethical self-assessment is unusually unflattering, admitting LanTurn neither remediates tailings nor meaningfully reduces their volume, that re-mining can reintroduce mining harms to communities that have not seen a project for decades, and that the rare earths will mostly end up in consumer goods and defence rather than the clean-energy story, with a stated commitment not to market it otherwise.","realWorld_zh":"是 iGEM 2026 中商業化論證最紮實的隊伍之一，也是本組唯一有第三方書面承諾的隊伍。商業模式是 B2B 的現場代工服務：尾礦的所有權與法律責任留在礦場，LanTurn 在現場營運一座小型模組化廠房，交回濃縮的混合稀土氧化物，既省去運輸成本，也讓尾礦管理責任不落在 LanTurn 帳上。這個模式由 Nuvau Minerals Corp. 建議，之後又在 REM3 Executive Summit 上與潛在買方和原料供應者再次驗證。單位經濟是算出來的，不是喊出來的：gate-to-gate 每公斤 REO 11.83-20.58 美元，其中約 92% 的資本支出在脫附管柱與樹脂，54-68% 的營運支出在發酵；並與溶劑萃取（最差情況貴 12%，最好情況在不純的低品位原料上便宜 370-720%）、管柱固定化 lanmodulin（便宜 16-100%）以及鑭系結合標籤生物吸附劑比較。設計選擇逐項都有成本依據，這相當少見：表面展示對比固定於 agarose 樹脂的純化 LanM、絮凝對比連續離心（不過他們老實指出這只省下每公斤 TREO 0.21 美元，並不特別顯著），以及光誘導對比銅、乙醇或半乳糖誘導。Ashram 個案研究用的是真實礦床，有 51 Mt 浮選尾礦、TREO 品位約 0.4%；樂觀情境下 15 年 NPV 為 5,100 萬美元、回收期 2.6 年，悲觀情境下 NPV 略為負值、回收期 5.9 年，而他們把兩者都講出來，不只引用好看的數字。尾礦中鎖住 5,600 億美元價值這個標題數字是自己推導的，不是引用來的：尾礦噸數乘以稀土濃度乘以市場價格，並因為是混合稀土而非純稀土而打了 70% 折扣，接著立刻把它與全球稀土市場僅約 45 億美元的規模並列對照。機構層面的進展也很具體：2026 年 9 月進入 McGill Dobson Centre for Entrepreneurship 的 Dobson Lean Startup Accelerator；BoxOne Ventures 清潔科技投資經理 Felicity Meyer 持續提供指導；Chris Corkery 就 McGill 的研究商業化與技術移轉路徑提供建議；十一人顧問團涵蓋濕法冶金、礦業、創投、生物製造與法規事務；公開 Nuvau Minerals Corp. 的 Bastien Fresia 與 Kingston Process Metallurgy 的 Dr. Boyd Davis 的支持信；已從一家大型加拿大礦業公司取得真實尾礦樣品，對方並打算與他們繼續合作研究；放大生產設施也都指名（Concordia Bioprocessing Facility 的 1000 L 規模、KPM 位於 Kingston 的 10,000 平方英尺試量產廠及其 2027 年成立的生物採礦部門、Sudbury 的生物浸出設施）。募資計畫分階段而且寫得很細：實驗室階段四個季度約需 28,800 美元，來自校內經費與不稀釋股權的補助（NSERC、NRC IRAP、NFRF）；公司設立後再找天使與清潔科技創投；後續階段則指向 NRCan 的 CMRDD 計畫（TRL 6-8 通常為 400 萬美元以上）與 MICA Canada（TRL 7-9 最高 250 萬美元），並以實際的生物採礦募資案做對照（Allonnia 的 2,000 萬美元 A 輪、pH7 的 3,200 萬美元 B 輪）。智慧財產權的工作是真做而不是口號：他們查證酵母表面展示的基礎專利 US6699658B1 與 US7465787B2 已到期，找出仍有效的 LanM 專利（CA3170828A1、CA3223988A1、US20240183787A1），以及 Princeton 一件尚在審查的申請案 WO2025240129A2，該案明確主張在 S. cerevisiae 中使用 EL222/C120 光遺傳學，並據此結論他們必須在技術上做出區隔、在發表任何可專利內容前先向 McGill 技術移轉辦公室揭露，並進行正式的 freedom-to-operate 分析。保留事項也講得直白：公司尚未設立，只有一份一年期的設立計畫；沒有營收、沒有簽定的代工合約、也沒有投資條件書；他們並直言技術經濟分析中許多參數是文獻估計值而非自己量測的結果，而這正是敏感度分析存在的理由：它是給濕實驗室與乾實驗室的降風險待辦清單。他們的倫理自我評估罕見地不替自己說話，承認 LanTurn 既沒有修復尾礦，也沒有實質減少尾礦量；再開採可能把採礦的傷害重新帶回那些幾十年沒有新礦場的社區；而這些稀土多數會流向消費產品與國防，而不是清潔能源的故事，並明確承諾不會用後者來行銷。","partners":["Nuvau Minerals Corp. (Peter van Alphen, Bastien Fresia, Gilles Roy; tolling model advice and a letter of support)","Kingston Process Metallurgy Inc. (Dr. Boyd Davis, Dr. Fariborz Faraji; letter of support, scale-up and demonstration, biomining division launching 2027)","BoxOne Ventures (Felicity Meyer, cleantech investment manager; ongoing mentorship)","McGill Dobson Centre for Entrepreneurship / Dobson Lean Startup Accelerator (entered September 2026; Dr. Neils Billou)","Chris Corkery, McGill research commercialisation and tech transfer","Concordia Bioprocessing Facility (Dr. Lalit Kumar; 1000 L fermentation scale-up)","National Research Council Canada (mine tailings samples)","An unnamed large Canadian mining company (real tailings samples, intends to continue research together)","UNEP Minerals Unit (Julia Vilela Carvalho), Earthworks (Jan Morrill), C2M2A (Marilyn Spink)","Dr. Andrew Zimmerman, University of Florida (biochar conversion of spent yeast)","The Lumb Group, McGill; Mira Loock; Dr. Denzel Ignacia; Dr. Kevin Gardner; Barstow lab and REEgen (in contact)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6040/wiki/entrep-page/tab-2/pt-financial-analysis.avif","caption":"Financial analysis of the Ashram tailings re-mining case study, giving USD 51M NPV over 15 years in the high-uptake scenario against a marginally negative NPV in the low-uptake case","caption_zh":"Ashram 尾礦再開採個案研究的財務分析：高採用情境下 15 年 NPV 為 5,100 萬美元，低採用情境則略為負值","credit":"Team McGill, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6040/wiki/entrep-page/tab-2/pt1-opex-capex.avif","caption":"Gate-to-gate CAPEX and OPEX breakdown for LanTurn, showing desorption columns and resins at about 92 percent of capital cost and fermentation at 54-68 percent of operating cost","caption_zh":"LanTurn 的 gate-to-gate 資本支出與營運支出拆解：脫附管柱與樹脂約佔資本成本 92%，發酵佔營運成本 54-68%","credit":"Team McGill, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6040/wiki/entrep-page/tab-3/tolling-model-2.avif","caption":"The B2B tolling business model: the mine keeps ownership and liability for its tailings, LanTurn processes on site and returns a concentrated mixed rare earth oxide","caption_zh":"B2B 代工商業模式：尾礦的所有權與責任留在礦場，LanTurn 在現場處理並交回濃縮的混合稀土氧化物","credit":"Team McGill, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6040/wiki/entrep-page/tab-2/ashram-map.avif","caption":"The proposed Ashram Rare Earths Project in Nunavik, Quebec, chosen as the demonstration case because its tailings are too dilute for existing methods but rich enough for LanTurn","caption_zh":"位於魁北克 Nunavik 的 Ashram 稀土專案規劃案，被選為示範案例，因為其尾礦對現有方法來說太稀，但對 LanTurn 已足夠富集","credit":"Team McGill, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Run the techno-economic analysis early and let its sensitivity results set the lab's experimental targets: McGill's TEA produced a hard number (about 35 mg/g adsorption capacity once the mixed-oxide impurity discount is applied) that became the wet lab's de-risking goal, which is how commercialisation work earns its place rather than sitting beside the science. Pair that with their TRL-staged plan, where each phase names its funding figure, funding source and named partner facility, so an institution can see exactly what the next stage costs and who must say yes.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"及早做技術經濟分析，並讓敏感度分析的結果來設定實驗室的實驗目標：McGill 的技術經濟分析算出一個硬指標（計入混合氧化物雜質折價後約 35 mg/g 的吸附容量），這個數字成為濕實驗室的降風險目標；商業化工作要這樣才站得住腳，而不是擺在科學旁邊各做各的。再搭配他們以 TRL 分期的計畫，每一階段都寫明資金金額、資金來源與具名的合作設施，讓機構一眼就看出下一階段要花多少錢、需要誰點頭。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/mcgill/","https://2026.igem.wiki/mcgill/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/mcgill/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/mcgill/assets/index-DZ45NXgC.js"],"rank":14},"6041":{"team":"UOregon","id":"6041","section":"Overgrad","country":"United States","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/uoregon/","projectTitle":"AquaFlock","tagline":"E. coli engineered to sequester groundwater nitrate as cyanophycin, then flocculate so the nitrogen can be harvested back as fertilizer","summary":"UOregon engineered E. coli to pull excess environmental nitrate into the nitrogen storage polymer cyanophycin and, once a cyanophycin threshold is reached, to express flocculation proteins so cells sink and can be harvested as a fertilizer substitute, closing the nitrogen loop. The target users are rural well owners and farmers in Oregon whose water is rarely tested. The education practice is the standout: three original curricula built for three audiences with increasing prior knowledge, developed through an explicit Design-Build-Test-Learn loop and grounded in Universal Design for Learning plus STEAM. The team also built an offline desktop search engine indexing the full text of 1,354 iGEM team wikis and 20,761 pages from 2022-2025.","awards":["Best Education — Nominee (Overgrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Education itself was run as a DBTL engineering cycle, with a documented Reflective Theory of Change diagram and a standardised success rubric (engagement, science understanding, creativity), both adapted from an Oregon State University STEM Research Center presentation at the Polar STEAM Summit 2026. Learning objectives were written against the measurable verbs of Bloom's Taxonomy (Remember, Understand, Apply, Analyze, Evaluate, Create).","dataviz":"Hand-illustrated scientific diagrams throughout: all educational materials were digitally illustrated by hand by the team, including a central-dogma comic, illustrated workbooks, and illustrated synthetic-biology-tool cards used as a tactile matching activity.","datascience":"Post-workshop feedback surveys with section-level ranking; for Workshop 3, 8 of 15 respondents had heard of synthetic biology before attending, and bioethics and science communication ranked as the favourite sections, with the illustrated workbook, real-world examples and small-group discussions named the most effective learning tools.","software":"iGEM Wiki Search: a desktop application that searches the full text of 1,354 team wikis and 20,761 pages from the 2022-2025 competitions from a single search box, running offline with no server. It automates wiki collection and processing, builds a full-text index, ranks whole projects rather than individual pages, crawls responsibly, handles JavaScript-only wikis, and was tested cross-platform. The team benchmarked it explicitly against iGEM's Phoenix Project (metadata only) and iGEM Munich 2024's Data Explorer (2019 wikis only, no source links), and links every result back to its original page.","stack":["desktop application (offline)","full-text indexing","web crawler with JavaScript rendering","Universal Design for Learning (UDL) framework","STEAM curriculum design","Bloom's Taxonomy"],"techniques":["cyanophycin nitrogen-storage pathway engineering","flocculation-protein inducible circuit","split biosensor","nitrate sequestration assays","AquaFlock hardware settling system"],"frameworks_zh":"教育本身就以 DBTL 工程迴圈的方式執行，並留下反思式改變理論（Reflective Theory of Change）圖與一套標準化的成效評分量表（參與度、科學理解、創造力），兩者都改編自奧勒岡州立大學 STEM Research Center 在 Polar STEAM Summit 2026 的報告。學習目標則依 Bloom's Taxonomy 的可測量動詞撰寫（記憶、理解、應用、分析、評鑑、創造）。","dataviz_zh":"全程使用手繪科學圖解：所有教材都由團隊成員親手數位繪製，包括一本中心法則漫畫、插畫式學習手冊，以及用於配對活動的插畫版合成生物學工具卡（可動手操作）。","datascience_zh":"工作坊後的回饋問卷採分段排序設計；第三場工作坊中，15 位回覆者有 8 人在參加前就聽過合成生物學，生物倫理與科學傳播被評為最喜歡的段落，插畫手冊、真實世界案例與小組討論則被指為最有效的學習工具。","software_zh":"iGEM Wiki Search：一款桌面應用程式，從單一搜尋框即可檢索 2022-2025 年各屆 1,354 個隊伍 wiki、20,761 個頁面的全文，離線執行、無需伺服器。它自動化了 wiki 的收集與處理、建立全文索引、以整個專案而非單一頁面為排序單位、以負責任的方式爬取、能處理僅靠 JavaScript 渲染的 wiki，並做過跨平台測試。團隊明確地把它與 iGEM 的 Phoenix Project（僅有詮釋資料）以及 iGEM Munich 2024 的 Data Explorer（僅 2019 年 wiki、無原始連結）做比較，並讓每一筆結果都連回原始頁面。"},"good":{"publicEngagement":"UOregon's central design principle is quotable and transferable: 'Accessibility should lower the barrier of entry into complex science, not the complexity of the science itself.' Instead of one generic outreach talk, the team wrote three original curricula for three audiences with increasing prior knowledge and ran them as three DBTL iterations across June, July and October 2026, carrying the lessons of each into the next. Workshop 1 ('Intro to Synthetic Biology') was a one-hour session plus an illustrated take-home worksheet delivered to 30 high school students at the Oregon Humane Society summer camp; students reviewed the central dogma and plasmid parts and then designed their own engineered bacterium to solve a problem of their choosing. Post-event debriefs with students and camp staff produced four concrete fixes (establish prior knowledge first, add more real-world relevance, shorten transitions to reduce cognitive load, create more peer-interaction points), which were fed directly into Workshop 2. Workshop 2 ('Engineering SynBio Solutions') was a two-hour session for 20 high school students at SAIL (Student Academy to Inspire Learning), an existing University of Oregon STEM summer camp for students from diverse learning backgrounds; materials were a fully illustrated workbook, a hand-drawn comic that told the central dogma as a story, slides, and hands-on activities, with each of five sections framed by its own guiding question and sequenced to scaffold from foundational biology to CRISPR and plasmids to genetic circuits to experimental design. Workshop 3 ('SynBio Solutions to Real-World Problems') was a two-hour session for 20 first- and second-year undergraduate science students at the University of Oregon, funded by a University of Oregon Knight Campus Graduate Student Association outreach mini-grant; because this audience already had foundational biology, the team swapped the comic for a matching-game refresher, added directed evolution and de novo protein design alongside CRISPR and plasmids, and then extended into two sections the earlier workshops could not reach: small-group bioethics analysis of three real-world synthetic biology applications, and a science-communication activity in which students decorated tote bags to explain what they had learned to an audience of their own choosing. Evidence of impact is tied to the standardised rubric rather than headcount alone: engagement, understanding and creativity were tracked across iterations through direct post-workshop feedback forms and indirect observation, Workshop 2 students asked unprompted questions beyond the taught material (one asked whether CRISPR and plasmids could be used at once), and the Workshop 3 survey ranked bioethics and science communication highest. Beyond workshops, the team published a comic illustrating the AquaFlock project's journey and released the iGEM Wiki Search desktop tool specifically to make it easier for future teams to find and build on predecessors' work - an education contribution aimed at the iGEM community itself.","ihp":"Human Practices was framed around rural equity: people living outside major cities receive less financial backing, less testing of wells and waterways, and less proactive healthcare, so the project is designed as a circular chain of agricultural, health and economic support for communities marginalised by municipal systems. The team mapped a four-step implementation path (in the home, then at the agricultural source, then harvest, then reduce/reuse/recycle) and stated the striking design goal that 'our product is made to eventually become obsolete' once nitrate levels fall out of the unsafe range. A field trip to the Metropolitan Wastewater Management Commission regional wastewater treatment facility serving Eugene and Springfield let the team interview plant operators, who confirmed nitrate control (alongside PFAS and silicon) is an unsolved challenge, validating a gap their smaller-scale system could fill. Four UN SDGs were adopted as focal areas: 3 (good health), 4 (quality education), 6 (clean water and sanitation) and 12 (responsible consumption and production).","realWorld":"The intended users are rural Oregon well owners and farmers; harvested flocs become a local fertilizer substitute, localising fertilizer access and cutting nitrate at source. Context established on the description page: roughly half of applied nitrogen fertilizer is taken up by plants and the rest leaches as nitrate, driving eutrophication, harmful algal blooms and hypoxia as well as direct human health risk from contaminated drinking water.","partners":["Oregon Humane Society (summer camp, Workshop 1 venue and audience)","SAIL - Student Academy to Inspire Learning, University of Oregon STEM summer camp (Workshop 2)","University of Oregon Knight Campus Graduate Student Association (outreach mini-grant funding Workshop 3)","Metropolitan Wastewater Management Commission (MWMC) Regional Wastewater Treatment Facility, Eugene-Springfield","Oregon State University STEM Research Center (Reflective Theory of Change and success-measurement frameworks)"],"publicEngagement_zh":"UOregon 的核心設計原則值得引用也可被其他隊伍沿用：「無障礙應該降低進入複雜科學的門檻，而不是降低科學本身的複雜度。」團隊沒有只做一場通用的外推演講，而是為先備知識遞增的三種受眾撰寫三套原創課程，並在 2026 年 6 月、7 月與 10 月以三次 DBTL 迭代實際執行，把每一次的經驗帶進下一次。第一場工作坊（Intro to Synthetic Biology）是一小時課程加一份插畫回家作業單，對象是奧勒岡人道協會夏令營的 30 位高中生；學生複習中心法則與質體組成，然後自行設計一株工程菌來解決自選的問題。活動後與學生及營隊人員的檢討產出四項具體修正（先建立先備知識、增加真實世界關聯、縮短段落轉換以降低認知負荷、增加同儕互動點），並直接帶入第二場工作坊。第二場工作坊（Engineering SynBio Solutions）是兩小時課程，對象是 SAIL（Student Academy to Inspire Learning，奧勒岡大學既有的 STEM 夏令營，招收來自多元學習背景的學生）的 20 位高中生；教材包含一本全插畫學習手冊、一本把中心法則說成故事的手繪漫畫、投影片與動手活動，五個段落各有自己的引導問題，並刻意從基礎生物學鋪陳到 CRISPR 與質體、再到基因迴路與實驗設計。第三場工作坊（SynBio Solutions to Real-World Problems）是兩小時課程，對象是奧勒岡大學 20 位大一、大二理學院學生，由奧勒岡大學 Knight Campus 研究生協會的外推小額補助支持；由於這群受眾已有基礎生物學，團隊把漫畫換成配對遊戲式複習，在 CRISPR 與質體之外加入定向演化與 de novo 蛋白質設計，再延伸出前兩場無法觸及的兩個段落：針對三個真實合成生物學應用的小組生物倫理分析，以及一個科學傳播活動，讓學生彩繪提袋，向自選的受眾說明自己學到什麼。成效證據扣在標準化量表上，而不只是人數：參與度、理解與創造力透過工作坊後的直接回饋表與間接觀察在各次迭代間追蹤，第二場的學生主動問出超出授課範圍的問題（有人問 CRISPR 與質體能否同時使用），第三場的問卷則把生物倫理與科學傳播排在最前面。工作坊之外，團隊出版了一本描繪 AquaFlock 專案歷程的漫畫，並釋出 iGEM Wiki Search 桌面工具，目的正是讓未來的隊伍更容易找到並接續前人的工作——這是一項針對 iGEM 社群本身的教育貢獻。","ihp_zh":"人類實踐以鄉村公平為框架：住在大城市以外的人得到較少財務支持、水井與水體較少被檢測、也較少獲得主動的醫療照護，因此本專案被設計成一條循環的鏈，為被市政系統邊緣化的社區提供農業、健康與經濟上的支持。團隊繪出四步落地路徑（先在住家、再到農業污染源、接著收取、最後減量／再利用／回收），並提出一個很鮮明的設計目標：「我們的產品被設計成最終會被淘汰」——一旦硝酸鹽濃度降回安全範圍即不再需要。團隊走訪服務 Eugene 與 Springfield 的 Metropolitan Wastewater Management Commission 區域污水處理廠，訪談廠務操作人員，他們確認硝酸鹽控制（與 PFAS、矽並列）仍是未解的難題，印證了這套較小規模系統可以補上的缺口。團隊選定四項聯合國 SDG 作為焦點：3（健康與福祉）、4（優質教育）、6（潔淨水與衛生）與 12（責任消費與生產）。","realWorld_zh":"預期使用者是奧勒岡州的鄉村水井持有者與農民；收取下來的絮凝物成為當地的肥料替代品，使肥料取得在地化，同時從源頭減少硝酸鹽。專案說明頁建立了脈絡：施用的氮肥大約只有一半被植物吸收，其餘淋溶成硝酸鹽，造成優養化、有害藻華與缺氧，也對飲用受污染水源的人體健康構成直接風險。"},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6041/wiki/pages/education/edu-wksp1-main-photo.avif","caption":"Workshop 1: one-hour intro to synthetic biology for 30 high school students at the Oregon Humane Society camp","credit":"Team UOregon, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"第一場工作坊：為奧勒岡人道協會營隊 30 位高中生舉辦的一小時合成生物學入門"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6041/wiki/pages/education/edu-wksp2-main-photo.avif","caption":"Workshop 2 at the SAIL STEM summer camp: 20 high school students working through the illustrated workbook and comic","credit":"Team UOregon, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"在 SAIL STEM 夏令營的第二場工作坊：20 位高中生使用插畫學習手冊與漫畫"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6041/wiki/pages/education/edu-wksp1-wkst.avif","caption":"The hand-illustrated take-home worksheet from Workshop 1, covering the central dogma and plasmid parts","credit":"Team UOregon, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"第一場工作坊的手繪回家作業單，內容涵蓋中心法則與質體組成"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6041/wiki/pages/education/wksp3-1.avif","caption":"Workshop 3 for 20 undergraduate science students, adding bioethics discussion and a tote-bag science-communication activity","credit":"Team UOregon, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"第三場工作坊，對象為 20 位大學部理學院學生，新增生物倫理討論與提袋科學傳播活動"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6041/wiki/pages/education/measuring-success.avif","caption":"The team's standardised measure of success across workshop iterations: engagement, science understanding and creativity","credit":"Team UOregon, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"團隊在各次工作坊迭代間使用的標準化成效量表：參與度、科學理解與創造力"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Run outreach as a DBTL cycle with a fixed success rubric: build three differentiated versions of the same curriculum for audiences at different prior-knowledge levels, debrief with the host staff after each delivery, and score every iteration on the same three criteria (engagement, understanding, creativity) so improvement is demonstrable rather than asserted.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/uoregon/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uoregon/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/uoregon/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/uoregon/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/uoregon/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/uoregon/field-trip","https://2026.igem.wiki/uoregon/sustainability"],"projectTitle_zh":"AquaFlock","tagline_zh":"改造 E. coli 將地下水中的硝酸鹽固定為氮儲存聚合物 cyanophycin，再誘導細胞絮凝沉降，使氮得以回收作為肥料","summary_zh":"UOregon 改造 E. coli，把環境中過量的硝酸鹽轉入氮儲存聚合物 cyanophycin，並在 cyanophycin 累積達到閾值後表現絮凝蛋白，使細胞沉降、可被收取作為肥料替代品，藉此閉合氮循環。目標使用者是奧勒岡州水質少有檢測的鄉村水井持有者與農民。最突出的是教育實踐：針對先備知識遞增的三種受眾，自行開發三套原創課程，以明確的 Design-Build-Test-Learn 迴圈迭代，並以通用學習設計（UDL）與 STEAM 為基礎。團隊另外做了一套離線桌面搜尋引擎，索引 2022-2025 年 1,354 個 iGEM 隊伍 wiki、共 20,761 個頁面的全文。","gemsTakeaway_zh":"把外推當成 DBTL 迴圈來跑，並搭配一套固定的成效量表：為先備知識不同的受眾做出同一套課程的三種差異化版本，每次執行後都與主辦單位人員檢討，並以同樣的三項標準（參與度、理解、創造力）為每次迭代評分，讓進步是可被證明的，而不是自己宣稱的。","rank":7},"6043":{"team":"Vilnius-Lithuania","id":"6043","section":"Undergrad","country":"Lithuania","village":"Foundational Advance","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/vilnius-lithuania/","projectTitle":"BMClick: One Shell to Click Them All","projectTitle_zh":"BMClick：一殼點擊萬物","tagline":"Bacterial microcompartment shells rebuilt outside the cell and made programmable by click chemistry, plus Ladder Detector, which annotates a gel in about a minute.","tagline_zh":"把細菌微區室外殼在細胞外重建，並以點擊化學使其表面可程式化；另有 Ladder Detector，約一分鐘標註完一張電泳膠影像。","summary":"BMClick rebuilds bacterial microcompartments (BMCs), the proteinaceous shells bacteria use to sequester metabolic reactions, in vitro and makes their surface programmable through click chemistry at an amber-codon-incorporated non-canonical amino acid, turning a natural containment system into a modular platform for working with purified biomolecules. The aim is to recover the organisation a cell provides, protecting therapeutic nucleic acids from nucleases, separating the steps of a reconstructed pathway, and extending the temperature and pH range over which enzymes work, while keeping the precision of in vitro conditions. The project also produced functional macroscopic materials from BMC-T shell proteins, and in vitro encapsulation was demonstrated with a HiBiT-SpyCatcher cargo and confirmed by cryo-EM. The dry-lab deliverable is Ladder Detector, a React + FastAPI web app that segments bands in a gel photograph using GelGenie's released U-Net models and then identifies which commercial ladder was run in the marker lane, a step no existing tool automated.","summary_zh":"BMClick 在體外重建細菌微區室（BMC）——細菌用來區隔代謝反應的蛋白質外殼——並透過在以 amber 密碼子嵌入的非天然胺基酸上進行點擊化學，使外殼表面可程式化，把一套天然的包覆系統變成處理純化生物分子的模組化平台。目標是重現細胞所提供的組織性：保護治療用核酸不被核酸酶分解、分隔重建路徑中的各個步驟、擴大酵素可作用的溫度與 pH 範圍，同時保有體外條件的精確性。團隊也用 BMC-T 外殼蛋白做出具功能的巨觀材料，並以 HiBiT-SpyCatcher 載物示範體外包覆，再由 cryo-EM 確認。乾實驗的產出是 Ladder Detector：一個 React + FastAPI 網頁應用程式，先用 GelGenie 已釋出的 U-Net 模型分割電泳膠照片中的條帶，再判定標記道跑的是哪一種市售分子量標準品（ladder）——這一步是現有工具都沒有自動化的。","awards":["Best New Basic Part — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Software — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Presentation — Nominee (Undergrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"React web client plus a Python FastAPI server exposing a REST API documented as OpenAPI 3.1 (Ladder Detector API 0.1.0, Apache 2.0), with five endpoints split into a Segmentation group (GET /segmentation-models, POST /segment-image, POST /extract-band-details) and a Ladder group (GET /markers, POST /detect-ladder). There is deliberately no database layer: the application collects and stores no user data and keeps all configuration in files on the server. Deployment is Docker Compose with three services (frontend on 5173, backend on 8000, interactive API docs at /docs), and the segmentation models are pulled at build time from the GelGenie model registry on Hugging Face, so a HF access token is a prerequisite alongside Git and Docker.","frameworks_zh":"React 網頁前端搭配 Python FastAPI 伺服器，對外提供以 OpenAPI 3.1 文件化的 REST API（Ladder Detector API 0.1.0，Apache 2.0），共五個端點，分為 Segmentation 群組（GET /segmentation-models、POST /segment-image、POST /extract-band-details）與 Ladder 群組（GET /markers、POST /detect-ladder）。刻意不設資料庫層：應用程式不收集也不儲存任何使用者資料，所有設定都放在伺服器上的檔案裡。部署採 Docker Compose，共三個服務（前端 5173、後端 8000、互動式 API 文件在 /docs），分割模型在建置時從 Hugging Face 上的 GelGenie 模型庫拉取，因此除了 Git 與 Docker 之外，還需先備妥 Hugging Face 存取權杖。","dataviz":"The core output is the annotated gel image itself: upload a photograph, optionally crop or rotate, mark the marker lanes, and the app detects bands and writes the size labels on. Accepted input is PNG, JPEG, WebP and TIFF; the annotated result comes back as PNG. Where automation is imperfect the user gets real editing tools rather than a take-it-or-leave-it answer: a brush, an eraser and a magic wand for refining band detection, plus the ability to override the identified ladder or edit assigned values directly. A project can be saved and reloaded as a .gelproj file carrying the band segmentation and lane markup, and frontend and backend exchange JSON.","dataviz_zh":"核心輸出就是標註好的電泳膠影像本身：上傳照片，必要時裁切或旋轉，標出標記道，應用程式便偵測條帶並把大小標籤寫上去。可接受的輸入格式為 PNG、JPEG、WebP 與 TIFF，標註結果以 PNG 回傳。在自動化不完美的地方，使用者拿到的是真正的編輯工具，而不是只能全盤接受或放棄的答案：筆刷、橡皮擦與魔術棒可修正條帶偵測，也可以直接覆寫判定出的 ladder 或編輯指定的數值。專案可存成 .gelproj 檔再載回，檔內帶著條帶分割與道次標記；前後端之間以 JSON 交換資料。","datascience":"The ladder-identification evaluation is the strongest part of the work. The team contacted Thermo Fisher Scientific for the band patterns of its DNA, RNA and protein ladders, scoped to six ladders their own lab uses, and then built a dataset of 172 marker-lane samples by combining their own gels, figures from published articles, and donated photographs solicited from the Vilnius University Life Sciences Center community and the organisers of the International Biology Olympiad. Because the algorithm is not machine learning but still has tunable parameters, they split 30% for parameter tuning and 70% for evaluation, used K-fold cross-validation within the tuning set, manually grouped samples that came from the same source or the same image so related samples could not leak across the split, and stratified by ladder. Four combinations were then tested on the held-out set: Dynamic Time Warping reached 52.42% (absolute run distance) and 62.90% (relative), while adjusted Needleman-Wunsch reached 89.52% and 91.13%. They published per-class tables, stated the two relevant baselines explicitly (about 17% for guessing one of six, about 26% for always guessing the most common class), and diagnosed their own failure case: Protein_6 was consistently confused with DNA_14 because both ladders have the same number of bands, so the gap penalties that normally separate ladders of different band counts provide no signal and only band positions remain. Relative run distance was chosen over absolute despite similar overall accuracy, because it handled Protein_6 better (61.9% vs 47.62%) and is the simpler of the two. Measured end-to-end annotation time is about one minute or less.","datascience_zh":"ladder 判定的評估是整份工作最紮實的部分。團隊向 Thermo Fisher Scientific 取得其 DNA、RNA 與蛋白質 ladder 的條帶圖譜，範圍限定在自家實驗室實際使用的六種 ladder，再結合自己跑的膠體、已發表文獻中的圖，以及向 Vilnius University Life Sciences Center 社群與 International Biology Olympiad 主辦方徵集到的照片，建成 172 個標記道樣本的資料集。由於演算法並非機器學習，但仍有可調參數，他們切出 30% 做參數調整、70% 做評估，在調參集內使用 K-fold 交叉驗證，並人工把來自同一來源或同一張影像的樣本歸為同一組，使相關樣本不會跨切分洩漏，同時依 ladder 分層。接著在保留測試集上比較四種組合：Dynamic Time Warping 的準確率為 52.42%（絕對移動距離）與 62.90%（相對移動距離），調整過的 Needleman-Wunsch 則達 89.52% 與 91.13%。他們公開各類別表格，明確列出兩條相關基線（六選一隨機猜測約 17%，永遠猜最常見類別約 26%），也診斷了自己的失敗案例：Protein_6 一直被誤判為 DNA_14，因為兩種 ladder 的條帶數相同，平常能區分不同條帶數 ladder 的 gap penalty 因此提供不了訊息，只剩條帶位置可用。整體準確率相近，他們仍選相對移動距離而非絕對值，因為它在 Protein_6 上表現較好（61.9% 對 47.62%），而且是兩者中較簡單的做法。實測端到端標註時間約一分鐘以內。","software":"Ladder Detector solves a real and unglamorous problem: gel annotation is done by hand, is repetitive and inconsistent, and the team found that although several gel-analysis tools exist, none automated the annotation step, even though almost every published gel figure is annotated. The pipeline has two stages. Band segmentation reuses rather than reinvents: GelGenie (Aquilina et al., Nature Communications 2025) showed that a lightweight U-Net and nnU-Net clearly beat classical Watershed and Multi-Otsu approaches, so Ladder Detector runs GelGenie's released models, defaulting to the Universal lightweight U-Net (seconds on an ordinary CPU) with nnU-Net and a sharp-band fine-tune selectable. Ladder identification is the team's own contribution, and the design decision behind it is instructive: their first idea was an image classifier over marker-lane crops, which they dropped after a consultation on two grounds, that they could not gather enough samples to train it reliably and that an image classifier would likely latch onto resolution, lighting or gel provenance instead of the band positions that actually distinguish ladders. They moved to numerical data instead, extracting band centroids from the segmentation mask and deriving absolute run distance (distance from the top of the lane) and relative run distance (normalised by lane height). The absolute approach exploits the empirical near-linearity of migration distance against log10(size): for each ladder in the registry, both sequences are min-max normalised, the log sizes inverted, aligned with an adjusted Needleman-Wunsch, a least-squares line fitted to the matched pairs, and the ladder scored by R-squared minus a penalty per unmatched band. The relative approach compares against per-ladder reference profiles taken from vendor charts and scores 1 - RMSE with the same unmatched-band penalty. The process flow deliberately keeps two human checkpoints, segmentation review and marker-lane selection, and the wiki explains why: segmentation is not always accurate, and when a gel has several marker lanes the app has no reliable way to tell which holds the ladder. The API exists specifically so the tool can become one step in an automated pipeline. It was deployed as a public web client at https://ladder-detector.onrender.com, which is the right instinct, but as of checking the service returns 'This service has been suspended by its owner', so the only working route today is self-hosting: 'git clone https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/vilnius-lithuania/ladder-detector.git', add a Hugging Face token to backend/.env, 'docker compose up --build'. Honest limitations are listed: only six ladders supported because of data availability, segmentation imperfect enough to need manual correction, and the classical identification approach possibly improvable by a trained model given a larger dataset. Licence Apache 2.0; it is described as a prototype.","software_zh":"Ladder Detector 解決的是一個真實又不起眼的問題：電泳膠標註都靠手工，重複而且不一致；團隊發現雖然已有數種膠體分析工具，卻沒有一個把標註這一步自動化，即使幾乎每張發表的膠體圖都有標註。流程分兩階段。條帶分割選擇沿用而非重造：GelGenie（Aquilina 等人，Nature Communications 2025）已證明輕量 U-Net 與 nnU-Net 明顯優於傳統 Watershed 與 Multi-Otsu 方法，因此 Ladder Detector 直接執行 GelGenie 釋出的模型，預設為 Universal 輕量 U-Net（在普通 CPU 上只需數秒），另可選用 nnU-Net 與針對銳利條帶微調的版本。ladder 判定才是團隊自己的貢獻，而背後的設計決策很值得參考：他們最初的想法是對標記道裁切影像做影像分類，在一次諮詢後放棄，理由有兩點——他們蒐集不到足以可靠訓練的樣本量，而且影像分類器很可能抓住的是解析度、打光或膠體來源，而不是真正能區分 ladder 的條帶位置。他們改用數值資料，從分割遮罩取出條帶質心，推導出絕對移動距離（距道次頂端的距離）與相對移動距離（以道次高度正規化）。絕對法利用了移動距離對 log10（大小）近乎線性的經驗關係：對註冊表中的每一種 ladder，兩組序列都做 min-max 正規化、將 log 大小反轉、以調整過的 Needleman-Wunsch 對齊，再對配對點做最小平方直線擬合，並以 R-squared 減去每個未配對條帶的罰分來為該 ladder 評分。相對法則是與各 ladder 取自廠商圖表的參考圖譜比對，以 1 - RMSE 計分，並採同樣的未配對條帶罰分。流程刻意保留兩個人工檢查點——分割結果審閱與標記道選擇——wiki 也說明了原因：分割並非總是準確，而且當一張膠體上有多個標記道時，應用程式無法可靠判斷哪一道才是 ladder。API 的存在就是為了讓這個工具能成為自動化流程中的一個環節。它曾以公開網頁前端部署在 https://ladder-detector.onrender.com，這個直覺是對的，但查核時該服務回傳 'This service has been suspended by its owner'，所以今天唯一可行的路徑是自行架設：'git clone https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/vilnius-lithuania/ladder-detector.git'，在 backend/.env 加入 Hugging Face 權杖，再執行 'docker compose up --build'。限制也誠實列出：因資料可得性只支援六種 ladder；分割仍不夠準確、需要人工修正；而傳統的判定方法在資料集更大時，或許可由訓練過的模型做得更好。授權為 Apache 2.0；團隊自述這是一個原型。","stack":["React","Python","FastAPI","REST / OpenAPI 3.1","Docker + Docker Compose","Hugging Face model registry","GelGenie U-Net and nnU-Net models","PyTorch (via GelGenie models)","JSON","Render (deployment, now suspended)","Apache 2.0","iGEM GitLab"],"techniques":["U-Net / nnU-Net semantic segmentation of gel bands","band centroid extraction per lane","adjusted Needleman-Wunsch sequence alignment","Dynamic Time Warping (evaluated and rejected)","log10 size vs migration distance least-squares fitting with R-squared scoring","min-max normalisation for scale-invariant matching","RMSE scoring against vendor reference profiles","gap-penalty scoring for unmatched bands","grouped and stratified train/test splitting to prevent leakage","K-fold cross-validation for parameter tuning","amber-codon non-canonical amino acid incorporation and click chemistry (wet lab)","cryo-EM confirmation of in vitro shell assembly"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education was rebuilt from scratch after a stakeholder told them their plan was wrong. The team had scouted a venue, contacted student organisations and planned to book a music band for one large science festival; Ieva Lingytė, a past team lead, warned them that a bigger event does not mean a bigger audience and that they should go to people rather than expect people to come to them. They scrapped it. The replacement framework borrows Ray Oldenburg's 'third place' sociology: home is the first place, university and formal events the second, and informal public spaces where people gather by choice (cafés, museums, clubs, shelters) the third, where status matters little and conversation is the main activity. Every event was then placed inside a community that already existed, with the format kept flat and walk-away-able for someone with no biology background who had not planned to meet science that evening: genetics discussed through the animals in the room at a cat shelter, fungi taught as a painting workshop ('Science Paints') at the MO Museum, and slots joined at the 'BŪTENT!' discussion festival and the VU Alumni Festival where the audience already existed. They iterated on format too, shortening and sharpening the questions for the second 'Science Talks' after the first showed people wanted more direct ones, and the discussion festival surfaced recognising fake science marketing as the topic people were most misinformed about. Separate consultations with Uršulė Barkauskaitė and Austėja Klevaitė specifically covered adapting activities for older adults, a group the team had no resources to involve meaningfully before.","publicEngagement_zh":"教育活動在一位利害關係人指出他們的規劃有問題之後，整個重做。團隊原本已勘好場地、聯繫學生組織，還打算為一場大型科學節請樂團演出；前任隊長 Ieva Lingytė 提醒他們，活動辦得更大並不等於觸及更多人，應該走向人群，而不是期待人群走過來。他們把原案全部作廢。新的架構借用 Ray Oldenburg 的「第三場所」社會學：家是第一場所，大學與正式活動是第二場所，而人們出於自願聚集的非正式公共空間（咖啡館、博物館、俱樂部、收容所）是第三場所，在那裡身分地位並不重要，交談才是主要活動。於是每場活動都放進一個本來就存在的社群裡，形式刻意保持平等、可隨時離席，讓沒有生物背景、當晚也沒打算遇到科學的人能自在參與：在貓咪收容所藉現場的動物談遺傳學、在 MO Museum 以繪畫工作坊（「Science Paints」）教真菌，並加入「BŪTENT!」討論節與 VU Alumni Festival 既有觀眾的場次。形式也經過迭代：第一場「Science Talks」顯示大家想要更直接的問題，第二場便把題目縮短並問得更尖銳；討論節則讓「辨識假科學行銷」浮現為民眾最容易被誤導的主題。另外與 Uršulė Barkauskaitė 和 Austėja Klevaitė 的個別諮詢，專門處理如何為年長者調整活動——這是團隊先前沒有資源好好納入的族群。","ihp":"More than 30 stakeholder meetings over 9 months, structured as open dialogue aimed at constructive criticism rather than presentation, with each insight systematically evaluated afterwards and failing approaches dropped. They named the loop the CLICK cycle (Consider, Listen, Implement, Check, Know your limitations) and published five values including Critical Reflection, which they define as examining their own baseline assumptions and being honest about limitations given that parts of the platform could have therapeutic value. Advice is mapped on an interactive timeline where every meeting records Description, Insights, Integration and Next steps, with three explicit revision points. Concrete redirections: alumni from the 2023 'Exullose' and 2025 'iXPOSE' teams set a realistic nine-month scope; the Kerfeld Laboratory advised on BMC assembly and protein modification; Prof. Rolandas Meškys shaped turning in vitro assembling BMC proteins into a modular platform; Dr. Yali Wang confirmed BMC-T functional material formation was possible after the team's own tests had repeatedly failed; critique from Ieva Lingytė (Biomatter Designs) and Dr. Juozas Nainys (Atrandi Biosciences) expanded a narrow thermostability aim into pH resistance testing and pushed them to find more creative applications, which produced the three-branch toolkit; and a consultation with Augustas Rinkevičius is recorded as 'Rethinking our ladder detection', the meeting that moved the software off an image classifier onto numerical band-distance matching.","ihp_zh":"9 個月內超過 30 場利害關係人會談，形式是開放對話、以取得建設性批評為目的，而不是做簡報；每則意見事後都系統性評估，行不通的方向就放掉。他們把這個循環命名為 CLICK cycle（Consider、Listen、Implement、Check、Know your limitations），並提出五項價值，其中 Critical Reflection 被定義為檢視自己的預設前提，並在平台部分內容可能具治療價值的前提下誠實面對限制。建議都標在一條互動時間軸上，每場會談記錄 Description、Insights、Integration 與 Next steps，並有三個明確的修正節點。具體的轉向包括：2023 年「Exullose」與 2025 年「iXPOSE」團隊的校友幫他們把範圍收斂到九個月做得到的程度；Kerfeld Laboratory 就 BMC 組裝與蛋白質修飾提供建議；Prof. Rolandas Meškys 促成把體外自組裝的 BMC 蛋白轉為模組化平台的方向；在團隊自己多次試驗失敗後，Dr. Yali Wang 確認 BMC-T 功能性材料的形成是可行的；Ieva Lingytė（Biomatter Designs）與 Dr. Juozas Nainys（Atrandi Biosciences）的批評，把原本只看耐熱性的狹窄目標擴展到 pH 耐受性測試，並推動他們找出更有創意的應用，進而產生三條分支的工具箱；而與 Augustas Rinkevičius 的諮詢記錄為「Rethinking our ladder detection」，正是讓軟體從影像分類器轉向數值條帶距離比對的那場會議。","realWorld":"Commercial viability was reviewed with industry rather than assumed: Ieva Lingytė at Biomatter Designs and Dr. Juozas Nainys at Atrandi Biosciences reviewed and reprioritised the three project paths, Dr. Ignas Galminas took a pitch on the platform's commercial potential, Eglė Radzevičienė advised on intellectual property and industry realities, and the Vilnius University Innovation department ran a market analysis in October. Therapeutic plausibility of BMC shells as drug-delivery nanocarriers was checked with Prof. Aurelija Žvirblienė rather than claimed. The team also presented at the Nordic iGEM Conference.","realWorld_zh":"商業可行性是和業界一起檢視出來的，不是自己假設的：Biomatter Designs 的 Ieva Lingytė 與 Atrandi Biosciences 的 Dr. Juozas Nainys 審視並重新排序了專案的三條路徑，Dr. Ignas Galminas 聽取關於平台商業潛力的提案，Eglė Radzevičienė 就智慧財產權與產業現實提供建議，Vilnius University 創新部門則在 10 月做了市場分析。BMC 外殼作為藥物遞送奈米載體的治療可行性，也是向 Prof. Aurelija Žvirblienė 求證過，而非逕行宣稱。團隊另外在 Nordic iGEM Conference 發表。","partners":["Kerfeld Laboratory","Thermo Fisher Scientific (ladder band-pattern data)","Vilnius University Life Sciences Center community (gel image donations)","International Biology Olympiad organisers (gel image donations)","Biomatter Designs","Atrandi Biosciences","Promega","Vilnius University Innovation department","MO Museum","BŪTENT! discussion festival","iGEM Vilnius-Lithuania alumni (Exullose 2023, iXPOSE 2025)","Caszyme, Seqvision, Thorlabs, Noatech, SnapGene (sponsors)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6043/wiki/software-images/original-photo-vs-result-2.avif","caption":"The original gel electrophoresis photograph next to Ladder Detector's automatically annotated result.","caption_zh":"原始的膠體電泳照片，與 Ladder Detector 自動標註後的結果並列。","credit":"Team Vilnius-Lithuania, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6043/wiki/software-images/tech-stack.avif","caption":"Ladder Detector's technology stack: a React web client over a Python FastAPI server, with no database layer because no user data is stored.","caption_zh":"Ladder Detector 的技術堆疊：React 網頁前端架在 Python FastAPI 伺服器上；因為不儲存使用者資料，所以沒有資料庫層。","credit":"Team Vilnius-Lithuania, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6043/wiki/software-images/ladder-detector-final-process-flow.avif","caption":"The process flow, showing which steps the application performs and which two verification checkpoints are deliberately left to the user.","caption_zh":"流程圖，顯示哪些步驟由應用程式執行，以及哪兩個驗證檢查點刻意留給使用者。","credit":"Team Vilnius-Lithuania, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6043/wiki/software-images/metric-explanation-dark.avif","caption":"The two metrics derived from band centroids: absolute run distance from the top of the lane, and the same value normalised by marker-lane height.","caption_zh":"由條帶質心推導出的兩項指標：自道次頂端起算的絕對移動距離，以及同一數值以標記道高度正規化後的相對移動距離。","credit":"Team Vilnius-Lithuania, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Build on the published model rather than training your own, and say why: Ladder Detector takes GelGenie's peer-reviewed U-Net weights for segmentation and spends its own effort on the one step nobody had automated, then rejects an image classifier on the explicit grounds that it would learn lighting and resolution instead of band positions. The transferable practice is their evaluation hygiene, a grouped and stratified split that stops samples from the same gel image leaking between tuning and test, stated random and majority-class baselines, per-class accuracy tables, and a published diagnosis of the one class the method fails on.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"用已發表的模型，而不是自己訓練一個，並且把理由說清楚：Ladder Detector 直接採用 GelGenie 經同儕審查的 U-Net 權重做分割，把自己的力氣花在沒人自動化過的那一步；並明確說明為何不用影像分類器——那會學到打光與解析度，而不是條帶位置。真正可移植的作法是他們的評估紀律：以分組與分層切分，避免同一張電泳膠影像的樣本在調參集與測試集之間洩漏；明列隨機猜測與多數類別兩條基線；提供各類別準確率表格；並公開診斷方法唯一失敗的那個類別。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/vilnius-lithuania/","https://2026.igem.wiki/vilnius-lithuania/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/vilnius-lithuania/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/vilnius-lithuania/education","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/vilnius-lithuania/ladder-detector","https://ladder-detector.onrender.com/"],"rank":21},"6045":{"team":"UNILausanne","id":"6045","section":"Overgrad","country":"Switzerland","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/unilausanne/","projectTitle":"ASTACi: Detect, Disarm, Defend","projectTitle_zh":"ASTACi：偵測、解除、防禦","tagline":"A field-deployable LAMP assay for the crayfish plague pathogen, a sub-CHF-10 open-source incubator to run it, and an ecological model that decided which treatment strategy to pursue.","tagline_zh":"一套可現地部署、用於偵測螯蝦瘟病原的 LAMP 檢測法，一台成本低於 10 CHF 的開源恆溫加熱裝置來執行它，以及一個生態模型來決定該採取哪一套處理策略。","summary":"UNILausanne addressed crayfish plague, caused by the oomycete Aphanomyces astaci, with three complementary strategies: detect the pathogen in water with loop-mediated isothermal amplification, disarm the invasive signal crayfish that carries it using RNAi, and defend native crayfish with a protective protein supplement. The measurement work asks whether the LAMP assay is specific enough to separate A. astaci from the closely related A. frigidophilus, sensitive enough to be useful, and robust enough to survive real lake and river water. The hardware is C.L.A.W., a hand-sized USB-powered incubator built with the original author of the MobileLAMP design, fully open-source at under CHF 10 per unit. A stochastic two-species population model was validated against a documented field case and then used to decide how to split effort between the disarm and defend strategies.","summary_zh":"UNILausanne 以三項互補策略處理由卵菌 Aphanomyces astaci 引起的螯蝦瘟：以迴圈介導等溫擴增（LAMP）偵測水中的病原、以 RNAi 解除攜帶病原的入侵種訊號螯蝦的威脅，並以具保護作用的蛋白質補充劑防禦原生螯蝦。量測工作所問的問題是：這套 LAMP 檢測是否專一到足以把 A. astaci 與近緣的 A. frigidophilus 區分開來、是否靈敏到足以實用，以及是否穩健到能承受真實的湖水與河水。硬體是 C.L.A.W.，一台手掌大小、以 USB 供電的恆溫加熱裝置，與 MobileLAMP 設計的原作者共同打造，完全開源且單台成本低於 10 CHF。一個隨機性的雙物種族群模型先以一個有文獻紀錄的野外案例驗證，再用來決定該如何在「解除」與「防禦」兩項策略之間分配資源。","awards":["Best Measurement — Nominee (Overgrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Measurement is organised around three stated requirements for a field assay (distinguish the pathogen from close relatives, offer a low detection limit, remain reliable under different environmental conditions), which become the specificity, sensitivity and robustness sections. The model is organised as sensitivity analysis, then validation against a real documented outcome, then use, with assumptions and limitations listed as expandable sections and each parameter annotated with its definition, the value used and the basis for that value, including explicit statements of 'no literature value exists' where none does.","frameworks_zh":"量測以現地檢測的三項明定需求為架構（把病原與近緣物種區分開來、提供低檢測極限、在不同環境條件下維持可靠），這三項分別對應專一性、靈敏度與穩健性三個章節。模型的編排依序為敏感度分析、對照真實文獻紀錄結果的驗證，最後才是應用；假設與限制以可展開區塊逐條列出，每個參數都標註其定義、所採用的數值以及該數值的依據，在確實查無資料時也明白寫出「文獻中並無此數值」。","dataviz":"Annotated agarose gel panels paired with photographs of colorimetric tube results; a qPCR standard curve of Ct against log10 template concentration with a linear regression over the assay's linear range; a temperature-stability plot showing three individual C.L.A.W. runs in grey, the mean +/- SD in orange and a shaded band marking the 60 to 65 C LAMP window, analysed and plotted in R 4.5.1 with ggplot2; an animated monthly-cycle schematic of the ecological model; interactive population-trajectory charts with median lines, shaded likely-outcome ranges, hoverable values, a toggleable data table and clickable legend entries; a heat-map grid of percentage native decline across competition and transmission values with the selected cell outlined.","dataviz_zh":"加註說明的瓊脂糖凝膠電泳圖，與呈色反應管的照片並列；qPCR 標準曲線以 Ct 對 log10 模板濃度作圖，並在檢測的線性範圍內做線性迴歸；溫度穩定性圖以灰線呈現 C.L.A.W. 的三次個別運行、以橙色呈現平均值 +/- SD，並以陰影帶標出 60 至 65 C 的 LAMP 作用區間，全部以 R 4.5.1 搭配 ggplot2 分析與繪製；生態模型的月週期示意圖以動畫呈現；互動式族群軌跡圖附有中位數線、標示可能結果範圍的陰影區、可滑過查看的數值、可切換顯示的資料表與可點選的圖例項目；熱圖網格呈現原生族群衰退百分比隨競爭與傳播參數的變化，並以外框標示所選取的格位。","datascience":"Specificity was engineered rather than assumed: multiple LAMP primer sets were designed and compared, with the best-performing set placing the F3 primer over a 10 bp deletion present in A. frigidophilus, and the team found that removing the optional loop primers eliminated false positives, a result they turn into a recommendation for other teams. Sensitivity was established by serial dilution with three replicates per level, giving a preliminary limit of detection of 5.5 x 10^-5 ng template per reaction, about 5 x 10^-6 ng/uL in the final reaction, below which amplification became inconsistent; a missing band in one lane is attributed to a probable pipetting error rather than quietly dropped. That figure is then benchmarked against the gold standard by running a qPCR standard curve for A. astaci, Ct against log10 concentration in triplicate, with a lowest detected concentration of about 1 x 10^-7 ng/uL, so the team can say its assay sits within one order of magnitude of the reference method instead of claiming parity. Robustness testing produced the most useful negative result: lake and river water pH was measured (5.8 for distilled, 7.04 to 7.11 for Lake Geneva, 7.26 to 8.16 for river water), samples were spiked with synthetic DNA, and amplification was robust across the range on gel, but the pH-sensitive colorimetric readout failed to change colour at higher starting pH, so the assay is robust and its readout is not. The team converts this into three explicit recommendations: run a no-template control with every new primer set, drop the loop primers if the NTC gives false positives, and check environmental pH or confirm a colorimetric negative by gel before calling a sample clean. Hardware is calibrated rather than trusted: a thermometer placed directly in the tube bore read about 10 C above the display, so the thermostat is set to 52.5 C to reach 62.5 C in the tube, and this calibration step is written into the published manual; heating from 27 to 62.5 C takes about five minutes with an overshoot to around 70 C at eight minutes because the sensor sits under the block, so the protocol specifies a 10-minute preheat, after which the tube bore holds 62.7 +/- 1.2 C over 30 minutes across three independent runs. The ecological model is stochastic with many replicates per condition reported as medians with percentile bands, is subjected to a sensitivity analysis to identify which parameters matter, and is then validated by sweeping competition and transmission against a real documented displacement (Bubb, Thom and Lucas tracked 15 invasive and 20 native crayfish at a river site in 2003 and found zero natives on resurvey in 2005); the team chose moderate competition with beta = 0.9, a 95% match, over the closest 97% fit because the latter would have contradicted their neutral-habitat baseline, and they state that the remaining gap was left open rather than closed by adjusting habitat.","datascience_zh":"專一性是設計出來的，而不是假定而來：團隊設計並比較了多組 LAMP 引子，表現最佳的一組把 F3 引子設計在 A. frigidophilus 具有的一段 10 bp 缺失上；團隊並發現移除選用性的 loop 引子即可消除假陽性，並把這項結果寫成給其他團隊的建議。靈敏度以序列稀釋建立，每一稀釋度做三個重複，得到初步檢測極限為每次反應 5.5 x 10^-5 ng 模板，約相當於最終反應中的 5 x 10^-6 ng/uL，低於此量時擴增就變得不一致；某一道缺失的條帶被歸因於可能的移液操作失誤，而不是被悄悄剔除。這個數字接著以黃金標準方法對標：團隊為 A. astaci 建立 qPCR 標準曲線，以三重複做 Ct 對 log10 濃度作圖，最低可偵測濃度約為 1 x 10^-7 ng/uL，因此團隊得以說自家檢測與參考方法相差在一個數量級之內，而不是宣稱兩者相當。穩健性測試產生了最有用的負面結果：團隊量測了湖水與河水的 pH（蒸餾水 5.8、日內瓦湖 7.04 至 7.11、河水 7.26 至 8.16），在樣本中加入合成 DNA，凝膠結果顯示擴增在整個範圍內都穩健，但對 pH 敏感的呈色判讀在起始 pH 偏高時無法變色，因此檢測本身穩健，其判讀方式則不然。團隊把這一點轉化為三項明確建議：每組新引子都要跑無模板對照（NTC）、若 NTC 出現假陽性就捨棄 loop 引子，以及在判定樣本乾淨之前先檢查環境 pH，或以凝膠確認呈色法的陰性結果。硬體是經過校正而不是直接信任：直接插入試管孔的溫度計讀值比顯示值高約 10 C，因此恆溫器設定在 52.5 C 才能讓管內達到 62.5 C，這道校正步驟也寫進了公開的操作手冊；由 27 C 升溫至 62.5 C 約需五分鐘，並在第八分鐘超調至約 70 C，原因是感測器位於加熱塊下方，因此流程規定須預熱 10 分鐘，之後在三次獨立運行中，試管孔於 30 分鐘內維持在 62.7 +/- 1.2 C。生態模型為隨機模型，每一條件下執行多次重複，結果以中位數搭配百分位區間呈現；模型先經敏感度分析找出真正重要的參數，再以掃描競爭與傳播參數的方式，對照一起有文獻紀錄的實際取代事件進行驗證（Bubb、Thom 與 Lucas 於 2003 年在一處河段追蹤 15 隻入侵種與 20 隻原生螯蝦，2005 年複查時原生個體數為零）；團隊選了中等競爭、beta = 0.9、吻合度 95% 的組合，而不是吻合度最高的 97%，因為後者會與他們設定的中性棲地基準相矛盾，而他們也說明剩餘的落差是被保留下來，而不是靠調整棲地參數來消除。","software":"C.L.A.W. is fully open-source with a published assembly manual containing a parts list with prices and suppliers, step-by-step assembly instructions, wiring diagrams, and guidance on settings and calibration; STL files for the base, cover, lid, tube support and button are provided with an interactive 3D viewer on the wiki. The design builds on the published MobileLAMP device and the team worked with its corresponding author to correct a missing circuit connection. Analysis and plotting were done in R 4.5.1 with ggplot2.","software_zh":"C.L.A.W. 完全開源，並公開了組裝手冊，內含標示價格與供應商的零件清單、逐步組裝說明、接線圖，以及設定與校正的指引；底座、外殼、上蓋、試管座與按鈕的 STL 檔案皆有提供，並在 wiki 上搭配互動式 3D 檢視器。這套設計以已發表的 MobileLAMP 裝置為基礎，團隊並與其通訊作者合作，修正了一處缺漏的電路連接。分析與繪圖以 R 4.5.1 搭配 ggplot2 完成。","stack":["Vazyme fluorescent LAMP/RT-LAMP kit","NEB WarmStart Colorimetric LAMP 2X master mix","Agarose gel electrophoresis","TaqMan qPCR (Vralstad assay)","R 4.5.1 with ggplot2","3D printing (STL)","USB power bank electronics","Stochastic two-species population simulation"],"techniques":["Primer-set comparison for specificity","Loop-primer removal to suppress false positives","Serial dilution limit of detection with replicates","Benchmarking against a gold-standard method","Environmental matrix (lake and river water) testing","pH measurement of sample matrices","No-template controls on every primer set","Thermometer-in-tube calibration of a heater","Temperature stability as mean +/- SD across runs","Parameter sensitivity analysis","Model validation against a documented field outcome"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"An education page and a games section accompany the project, alongside an inclusivity page that includes a dyslexia-friendly display option on the wiki itself.","publicEngagement_zh":"專案另設有教育頁面與遊戲區，以及一個包容性頁面；wiki 本身也提供對閱讀障礙者友善的顯示選項。","ihp":"A conversation with La Maison de la Riviere, a Swiss foundation for aquatic ecosystem research and conservation, changed a decision the model had already made. The simulations showed monotonically that moving effort from protein supplementation toward RNAi always helped the native population, which suggested abandoning the defend strategy. The foundation described native crayfish reintroduced into a lake with no invasive crayfish present that still died because A. astaci was already in the water, a case the model could not represent because it tracks the pathogen only through the invasive population. The team kept developing the defend strategy for that use case and documented explicitly that the model's scope, not the strategy, was the limitation.","ihp_zh":"與瑞士水域生態系研究暨保育基金會 La Maison de la Riviere 的一場對話，推翻了模型原本已經做出的決定。模擬結果單調地顯示，把資源從蛋白質補充移往 RNAi 永遠對原生族群有利，這意味著應該放棄「防禦」策略。該基金會描述了一個案例：原生螯蝦被重新引入一座並沒有入侵種螯蝦的湖泊，卻仍然死亡，因為 A. astaci 早已存在於水中。模型無法呈現這種情形，因為它只透過入侵種族群追蹤病原。團隊因此為這個使用情境繼續發展「防禦」策略，並明確記錄下來：限制來自模型的適用範圍，而不是這項策略本身。","realWorld":"The target users are named and the design follows from them: fishermen and conservationists who must run the test at the water's edge without a laboratory, which is why C.L.A.W. runs from a standard USB power bank, costs under CHF 10, and is published with everything needed to rebuild it. The outlook section lists three concrete improvements with reasons (a heated lid to stop condensation reducing the reaction volume, a larger aluminium block so controls can run alongside samples, and freeze-dried reagents for a self-contained field kit), and the next steps for the assay are stated as replacing synthetic DNA with isolated pathogen DNA and then with environmental samples, possibly with a pre-enrichment step.","realWorld_zh":"目標使用者被明確指名，設計也由此推導而來：必須在沒有實驗室的水邊執行檢測的漁民與保育工作者，這正是 C.L.A.W. 以標準 USB 行動電源供電、成本低於 10 CHF，並公開了重製所需一切資料的原因。展望一節列出三項具體改良並說明理由（加熱上蓋以避免冷凝水減少反應體積、加大鋁製加熱塊讓對照組能與樣本同時進行、以及凍乾試劑以做成自給自足的現地套組）；檢測本身的下一步則明定為先以分離自病原的 DNA 取代合成 DNA，再進一步改用環境樣本，並可能加入預先富集（pre-enrichment）步驟。","partners":["Dr Ganga Chinna Rao Devarapu (corresponding author, MobileLAMP)","La Maison de la Riviere","Vazyme","New England Biolabs","IDT","Microsynth","Twist Bioscience","Promega"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6045/wiki/hardware/frame-023.webp","caption":"C.L.A.W. (Compact LAMP ASTACi Water-incubator), the team's hand-sized, USB-powered LAMP incubator. It is fully open-source, built from off-the-shelf and 3D-printed parts for under CHF 10 per device.","caption_zh":"C.L.A.W.（Compact LAMP ASTACi Water-incubator），團隊自製的手掌大小、USB 供電 LAMP 恆溫加熱裝置。完全開源，以市售零件與 3D 列印件組成，單台成本低於 10 CHF。","credit":"Team UNILausanne, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6045/wiki/figure-hardware/claw-stability-graph.avif","caption":"Temperature in the C.L.A.W. tube bore over a 30-minute incubation after a 10-minute preheat, read every five minutes with a glass thermometer inserted directly into the bore. Grey lines are the three individual runs, orange is mean +/- SD, and the shaded band marks the 60 to 65 C LAMP window; the bore held 62.7 +/- 1.2 C.","caption_zh":"預熱 10 分鐘後，C.L.A.W. 試管孔在 30 分鐘恆溫反應期間的溫度，以直接插入孔內的玻璃溫度計每五分鐘讀取一次。灰線為三次個別運行，橙色為平均值 +/- SD，陰影帶標示 60 至 65 C 的 LAMP 作用區間；管孔維持在 62.7 +/- 1.2 C。","credit":"Team UNILausanne, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6045/wiki/measurement/fig2.avif","caption":"Agarose gel of LAMP amplicons across a serial dilution of template DNA, three replicates per level, establishing a preliminary limit of detection of 5.5 x 10^-5 ng per reaction. The team attributes the one missing band to a probable pipetting error rather than removing the lane.","caption_zh":"模板 DNA 序列稀釋後 LAMP 產物的瓊脂糖凝膠電泳，每一稀釋度三個重複，據此建立每次反應 5.5 x 10^-5 ng 的初步檢測極限。團隊把唯一缺失的條帶歸因於可能的移液操作失誤，而不是把該道結果移除。","credit":"Team UNILausanne, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6045/wiki/measurement/fig3.avif","caption":"qPCR standard curve for A. astaci, Ct against log10 template concentration in triplicate with a linear regression over the assay's linear range. Benchmarking against this gold standard lets the team state that their LAMP assay sits within one order of magnitude rather than claiming equivalence.","caption_zh":"A. astaci 的 qPCR 標準曲線，以三重複呈現 Ct 對 log10 模板濃度，並在檢測的線性範圍內做線性迴歸。對標這項黃金標準方法，讓團隊得以說自家 LAMP 檢測相差在一個數量級之內，而不是宣稱兩者等效。","credit":"Team UNILausanne, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Test the readout in the matrix it will actually meet, not only the chemistry: the team's LAMP amplification worked in river water while its pH-based colour change did not, a failure invisible in distilled-water validation and the kind that quietly produces false negatives in the field.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"要在判讀方式真正會遇到的樣本基質中測試它，而不只是測試化學反應：這支團隊的 LAMP 擴增在河水中可行，但以 pH 為基礎的變色判讀卻失效；這種失效在蒸餾水驗證中完全看不出來，而且正是會在現場悄悄產生假陰性的那一類問題。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/unilausanne/measurement","https://2026.igem.wiki/unilausanne/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/unilausanne/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/unilausanne/","https://2026.igem.wiki/unilausanne/design-detect","https://2026.igem.wiki/unilausanne/human-practices"],"rank":7},"6053":{"team":"HKSSC","id":"6053","section":"High School","country":"Hong Kong","village":"Food & Nutrition","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/hkssc/","projectTitle":"Engineering E. coli to express prbA, a paraben-degrading esterase, as a pre-treatment for food waste recycling","projectTitle_zh":"改造 E. coli 表現除對羥基苯甲酸酯的酯酶 prbA，作為廚餘回收的前處理步驟","tagline":"If preservatives are designed to stop microbes, can we design microbes to stop preservatives?","tagline_zh":"既然防腐劑的設計目的是抑制微生物，我們能不能設計微生物來分解防腐劑？","summary":"HKSSC (St. Stephen's College, Hong Kong) noticed a bottleneck nobody was talking about: Hong Kong's O-PARK organic resources recovery centre runs anaerobic digestion on food waste, but the chemical preservatives already in that waste inhibit the very microbes doing the digesting. They cloned prbA, a paraben esterase from Enterobacter cloacae that hydrolyses parabens to 4-hydroxybenzoic acid and needs no complex cofactors, into pET22b+ under a T7 promoter with a pelB signal peptide directing it to the periplasm, then characterised it with CFU-based MIC assays, a pNPA esterase assay and HPLC. They won Best New Basic Part at high school level largely on the strength of the prbA part family - including the previously unregistered native promoter and RBS, which they located in silico with BPROM and then built into a promoterless GFP reporter construct. The dry lab and statistics are the standout: structure-guided mutant design in HotSpot Wizard on an AlphaFold model, and a Michaelis-Menten kinetic analysis defended with two-way ANOVA, a Brown-Forsythe Levene variance check and Welch-Satterthwaite contrasts with Holm correction.","summary_zh":"HKSSC（香港聖士提反書院）注意到一個少有人談的瓶頸：香港 O-PARK 有機資源回收中心以厭氧消化處理廚餘，但廚餘中既有的化學防腐劑會抑制負責消化的微生物本身。他們將 prbA（來自 Enterobacter cloacae 的對羥基苯甲酸酯酯酶，可將 paraben 水解為 4-hydroxybenzoic acid，且不需複雜輔因子）選殖進 pET22b+，置於 T7 啟動子下，並以 pelB 訊號肽導向周質空間，再以 CFU 為基礎的 MIC 試驗、pNPA 酯酶活性試驗與 HPLC 進行特性分析。他們以 prbA 元件家族的實力拿下高中組最佳新基礎元件獎——其中包括此前未註冊的天然啟動子與 RBS，團隊先用 BPROM 以電腦預測其位置，再建成無啟動子的 GFP 報告基因構築。乾實驗與統計是全隊亮點：以 AlphaFold 模型在 HotSpot Wizard 中進行結構導向的突變體設計，以及一套以雙因子 ANOVA、Brown-Forsythe（基於中位數的 Levene）變異數檢定與經 Holm 校正的 Welch-Satterthwaite 對比加以支撐的 Michaelis-Menten 動力學分析。","awards":["Top 10 (High School)","Best New Basic Part — Winner (High School)","Best Education — Nominee (High School)","Best Village Project — Nominee (Agriculture / Food & Nutrition / Fashion & Cosmetics / Art & Design)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Three distinct computational strands. (1) Structure and protein engineering: the prbA structure was taken from AlphaFold and visualised in UCSF Chimera, which revealed a long flexible N-terminal tail consistent with the 31-residue signal peptide and justified the Cycle 2 switch to pelB periplasmic targeting. HotSpot Wizard 3.1 (Loschmidt Laboratories) was then used for a full structure-guided mutagenesis workflow: stability hotspots were ranked by B-factor and relative accessible surface area (ASA), buried residues filtered out, and three candidates triaged - A198 (50% ASA, highest flexibility) rejected because the Correlated Positions tab showed it needs a compensating mutation elsewhere; P329 rejected because only one amino acid occurs at that homologous position; N240 (34% ASA) selected, with Amino Acid Frequencies showing histidine as the commonest homolog residue and Mutational Landscape giving Asp/His/Ser an 88% probability of preserving function. They used the Design Library function with a minimal frequency threshold of 10% to generate degenerate codons for saturation mutagenesis at N240 and back-translated an E. coli K12-optimised mutant sequence. A second, separate hotspot run targeted catalytic efficiency rather than stability, prioritising A221 and A140 (mutability score 6, both in the catalytic pocket and substrate access tunnel) and designing an RCY degenerate codon library giving 50% Ala / 50% Thr with ~94% chance of seeing both variants in 5 colonies. (2) Molecular docking: methyl-paraben (PubChem CID 117065203) was docked across the whole prbA structure using HotSpot Wizard's docking module and visualised in Chimera to confirm N240 is not in the ligand-binding region - and they honestly flagged that histidine ionises near pH 6, so the mutation could backfire. Earlier docking with CB-Dock2 in PyMOL identified the catalytic serines. (3) Promoter prediction: BPROM was run on the 247 bp upstream region of prbA, predicting a sigma-70 promoter with an LDF score of 5.30 (threshold 0.20), a consensus -10 box TATAAT at position 163 (score 68), a near-consensus -35 box TTGAAA at 142 (score 23), 21 bp spacing and TSS at 178. (4) Enzyme kinetics: a Michaelis-Menten model fitted to pNPA assay data, plus a 35-page mathematical modelling report, with Monod kinetics recommended by Professor Patrick Lee for future digester-scale work.","frameworks_zh":"運算工作分成三條（實為四條）明確路線。(1) 結構與蛋白質工程：prbA 結構取自 AlphaFold，並以 UCSF Chimera 視覺化，從中看出一段長而柔軟的 N 端尾巴，與 31 個殘基的訊號肽相符，也成為 Cycle 2 改用 pelB 周質導向的依據。接著以 HotSpot Wizard 3.1（Loschmidt Laboratories）執行完整的結構導向突變流程：依 B-factor 與相對可及表面積（ASA）排序穩定性熱點，濾除埋藏殘基，並篩選出三個候選位點——A198（ASA 50%、柔軟度最高）因 Correlated Positions 頁顯示它需要在別處有補償性突變而捨棄；P329 因該同源位置只出現一種胺基酸而捨棄；最後選定 N240（ASA 34%），其 Amino Acid Frequencies 顯示組胺酸是同源序列中最常見的殘基，Mutational Landscape 則給出 Asp/His/Ser 有 88% 機率保留功能。他們用 Design Library 功能、以 10% 的最低頻率門檻，為 N240 的飽和突變產生簡併密碼子，並反轉譯出一段以 E. coli K12 最佳化的突變序列。另有一次獨立的熱點分析針對催化效率而非穩定性，優先考慮 A221 與 A140（可突變性分數 6，兩者都位於催化口袋與受質進入通道內），並設計出 RCY 簡併密碼子庫，產生 50% Ala / 50% Thr，在 5 個菌落中看到兩種變異體的機率約 94%。(2) 分子對接：methyl-paraben（PubChem CID 117065203）以 HotSpot Wizard 的對接模組對整個 prbA 結構進行對接，並在 Chimera 中視覺化，確認 N240 不在配體結合區——他們也誠實指出組胺酸在 pH 6 附近會解離，因此這個突變可能反而不利。更早期則以 PyMOL 搭配 CB-Dock2 對接，找出催化用的絲胺酸。(3) 啟動子預測：對 prbA 上游 247 bp 區域執行 BPROM，預測出一個 sigma-70 啟動子，LDF 分數 5.30（門檻 0.20），位置 163 處有共有序列 -10 box TATAAT（分數 68），位置 142 處有接近共有序列的 -35 box TTGAAA（分數 23），間距 21 bp，TSS 位於 178。(4) 酵素動力學：以 Michaelis-Menten 模型擬合 pNPA 試驗數據，另有一份 35 頁的數學建模報告；李柏熙（Patrick Lee）教授建議未來放大到消化槽尺度時改用 Monod 動力學。","dataviz":"The wiki carries a 35-page mathematical modelling PDF embedded inline for the kinetics section. More interesting is how they made the data defensible rather than merely pretty: initial velocity versus substrate concentration plotted for all four enzyme conditions (1 and 10 ug/mL porcine liver esterase control, 1 and 8 ug/mL recombinant prbA), Michaelis-Menten fits overlaid, and the statistical validation laid out as readable tables with the F statistics, degrees of freedom and p-values spelled out and each test explained in plain language for a non-statistician reader. Every chart in results is captioned with a complete alt text describing the plate layout or chromatogram, and both HPLC calibration chromatograms and time-course chromatograms (T0, T1, T2, T4) are shown rather than just a summary number.","dataviz_zh":"wiki 在動力學段落內嵌了一份 35 頁的數學建模 PDF。更值得注意的是他們讓數據站得住腳、而非只求好看：四種酵素條件（1 與 10 ug/mL 豬肝酯酶對照、1 與 8 ug/mL 重組 prbA）的初始速度對受質濃度都有作圖，疊上 Michaelis-Menten 擬合曲線，統計驗證則整理成易讀的表格，把 F 統計量、自由度與 p 值一一列出，並用非統計背景讀者也看得懂的語言逐項解釋每個檢定。結果頁的每張圖都有完整的替代文字說明盤面配置或層析圖譜，HPLC 的校正層析圖與時間序列層析圖（T0、T1、T2、T4）也都完整呈現，而非只給一個總結數字。","datascience":"This is the most statistically disciplined high school dataset of the five teams reviewed. Because they could only measure enzyme input by total powder weight rather than molar concentration, they refused to report kcat/Km and instead defined a mass-normalised catalytic capacity metric Q = Vmax / (Cmass x Km), valid only in the low-substrate regime (S << Km), with units cancelling to L g-1 min-1. Recombinant prbA at 1 ug/mL scored Q = 9.518 L g-1 min-1 versus Q = 4.545 for commercial porcine liver esterase at the same mass concentration - a 2.09-fold advantage. They then proved the difference was not pipetting noise: a two-way ANOVA across 4 enzyme conditions x 7 non-zero substrate concentrations gave enzyme condition F(3,64) = 52.530, p = 3.01e-17; substrate F(6,64) = 92.111, p = 1.49e-29; interaction F(18,64) = 21.012, p = 3.15e-20. A Brown-Forsythe Levene test (median-based, chosen over mean-based Levene precisely because outliers drag the mean) returned p = 0.01898, rejecting equal variances - so rather than ignore it they switched to Welch-Satterthwaite contrasts with Holm correction for multiple comparisons, confirming significance at 0.25 mM (p = 0.03452), 0.20 mM (p = 0.04225) and 0.10 mM (p = 0.00408). Separately, they chose CFU plate counts over OD600 for MIC determination because OD600 is confounded by precipitation and dead cells, and built an OD600-to-CFU/mL standard curve for proper per-cell normalisation. MIC was bracketed empirically: 400-500 mg/L methyl-paraben for wild-type BL21(DE3), 1000-1500 mg/L for the Cycle 1 prbA-idt construct, and 500-600 mg/L for the Cycle 2 pelB construct - and they published the awkward finding that Cycle 2 was worse than Cycle 1, diagnosed it from faint SDS-PAGE bands as a protein-isolation methodology problem, and opened Cycle 3 with 6xHis-tag IMAC purification to fix it.","datascience_zh":"這是所審五隊高中組中統計最為嚴謹的一份資料。由於他們只能以總粉末重量、而非莫耳濃度來量測酵素投入量，他們拒絕報告 kcat/Km，改為定義一個以質量標準化的催化容量指標 Q = Vmax / (Cmass x Km)，並限定只在低受質區間（S << Km）成立，單位相消後為 L g-1 min-1。在相同質量濃度下，1 ug/mL 的重組 prbA 得到 Q = 9.518 L g-1 min-1，市售豬肝酯酶則為 Q = 4.545——高出 2.09 倍。接著他們證明這個差異不是移液誤差：對 4 種酵素條件 x 7 個非零受質濃度所做的雙因子 ANOVA 顯示，酵素條件 F(3,64) = 52.530、p = 3.01e-17；受質 F(6,64) = 92.111、p = 1.49e-29；交互作用 F(18,64) = 21.012、p = 3.15e-20。Brown-Forsythe Levene 檢定（基於中位數，之所以不用基於平均數的 Levene，正是因為離群值會拉動平均數）得到 p = 0.01898，拒絕變異數齊一——他們沒有略過這點，而是改用經 Holm 多重比較校正的 Welch-Satterthwaite 對比，確認在 0.25 mM（p = 0.03452）、0.20 mM（p = 0.04225）與 0.10 mM（p = 0.00408）具顯著性。另外，他們在測定 MIC 時選擇 CFU 平盤計數而非 OD600，因為 OD600 會被沉澱與死菌混淆，並建立 OD600 對 CFU/mL 的標準曲線，以便做出正確的單細胞標準化。MIC 以實驗夾擠出區間：野生型 BL21(DE3) 為 400-500 mg/L methyl-paraben，Cycle 1 的 prbA-idt 構築為 1000-1500 mg/L，Cycle 2 的 pelB 構築為 500-600 mg/L——他們公開了 Cycle 2 比 Cycle 1 更差這個尷尬結果，並從 SDS-PAGE 上微弱的條帶診斷出這是蛋白質分離方法的問題，進而開啟 Cycle 3，改以 6xHis-tag IMAC 純化來修正。","software":"Two released pieces of software, both genuinely built rather than mocked up. FoodSafe is a native iOS app in Swift (source at https://github.com/judeliucodex/Foodsave, initial scaffold AI-assisted then refined by the software team) with two features: a 60-second swipe-left/swipe-right food-sorting game (100 points per correct call plus combo bonuses, backed by a food library for post-game review) and an AI-assisted food safety checker that sends a photo to DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash's vision model and returns a danger-meter rating with the observations behind the judgement. They are explicit about the limits - a photograph cannot establish safety, pathogens can be invisible, and the meter is an AI estimate, not a measurement - and about distribution, noting it is on TestFlight for invited testers rather than the App Store. Microbe Wars is a browser-based 2D arena game written entirely in Python by the team and hosted at https://igem-game.vercel.app, where the player fights paraben enemies as prbA using weapons like an enzyme pipette, with campaign/endless/practice modes, four difficulty tiers and a levelling system. On the parts side they contributed BBa_26SZRXOY (prbA CDS), BBa_264E443U and BBa_26XQ4J7K (stop/start-codon-free variants), BBa_262HI0IB (native promoter + RBS, the Best New Basic Part), composite parts BBa_26SU8KOK (pelB + prbA) and BBa_26MSEOFB (native promoter/RBS + GFPuv), colony PCR and Gibson primers, and a curated 'PrbA's Family' part collection (UUID 9f037d92-78bb-470b-b139-c4ce28d4cc86).","software_zh":"兩套實際發布的軟體，都是真的做出來、不是畫出來的。FoodSafe 是以 Swift 寫成的原生 iOS 應用程式（原始碼在 https://github.com/judeliucodex/Foodsave，初始骨架借助 AI 生成，之後由軟體組改寫），有兩項功能：一個 60 秒左右滑動分類廚餘的小遊戲（每答對一題 100 分，另有連擊加成，並搭配一個食物資料庫供賽後複習），以及一個 AI 輔助的食品安全檢查器，將照片送入 DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash 的視覺模型，回傳一個危險程度評級以及支撐該判斷的觀察依據。他們明確說明限制——照片無法證明食物安全、病原可能看不見、這個評級是 AI 的估計而非量測——也明確說明散布方式，指出它放在 TestFlight 供受邀測試者使用，而非上架 App Store。Microbe Wars 是一款完全由隊員以 Python 寫成的瀏覽器 2D 競技場遊戲，架在 https://igem-game.vercel.app，玩家化身 prbA、使用酵素移液管等武器對抗 paraben 敵人，有戰役／無盡／練習三種模式、四個難度階層與升級系統。元件方面，他們貢獻了 BBa_26SZRXOY（prbA CDS）、BBa_264E443U 與 BBa_26XQ4J7K（去除終止／起始密碼子的版本）、BBa_262HI0IB（天然啟動子 + RBS，即最佳新基礎元件）、複合元件 BBa_26SU8KOK（pelB + prbA）與 BBa_26MSEOFB（天然啟動子/RBS + GFPuv）、菌落 PCR 與 Gibson 引子，以及一組策劃過的「PrbA's Family」元件集合（UUID 9f037d92-78bb-470b-b139-c4ce28d4cc86）。","stack":["AlphaFold","UCSF Chimera","HotSpot Wizard 3.1","CB-Dock2","PyMOL","BPROM","PubChem","Michaelis-Menten kinetics","two-way ANOVA","Brown-Forsythe Levene test","Welch-Satterthwaite contrasts with Holm correction","Swift / iOS / TestFlight","DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash vision API","Python","Vercel","GitHub","HPLC","pNPA spectrophotometric esterase assay"],"techniques":["structure-guided saturation mutagenesis site triage (ASA, B-factor, correlated positions, mutational landscape)","degenerate codon library design","whole-surface molecular docking to rule out interference with the active site","in silico sigma-70 promoter prediction then promoter-trap GFP validation","CFU-based MIC rather than OD600, with an OD600-to-CFU standard curve","mass-normalised catalytic capacity metric (Q) when molar data is unavailable","variance-homogeneity diagnostics driving the choice of post-hoc test","multiple-comparison correction","publishing a negative/contradictory cycle result and diagnosing it"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education ran under a framework they called LITTLE GEM (Gauge, Engage, Modify), reaching ages 3 to 101 across one kindergarten (Pods Kindergarten, Wan Chai), two primary schools (SSCPS and Shap Pat Heung Rural Committee Kung Yik She Primary School), a senior centre run by Suicide Prevention Services, their own school, and partner high school teams. Formats were built per audience rather than recycled: a DNA rainbow coin-toss game booth at a public carnival that engaged over 170 participants in three hours; a 'Find a Match' food-waste card game and DNA clay-modelling for 3-6 year olds; strawberry and banana DNA extraction for primary students; a Kahoot quiz; a live beta test of the FoodSafe app; and an original comic book, 'The Tragedy of Margaret in Food Waste', which they also staged as a drama skit with Margaret the frog as the lead. For the elderly they ran a physical food-waste card-matching game and clay craft. Internally, the HKSSC iGEM Club ran 8 after-school workshops over 7 months for ages 11-16 (4 lab, 3 IHP, 1 software) covering DNA, pipetting and serial dilution with P200 and P10 micropipettes across 28 participants, gel electrophoresis, and DNA keychain making, with Wayground quizzes for review - a deliberate pipeline for future team members. They measured learning rather than attendance: at SSCPS, 0% of 20 students knew what iGEM was and 10% knew synthetic biology before the workshop, versus 100% able to state iGEM's core goal and define synthetic biology afterwards, with 100% successfully extracting visible DNA; at KYS the post-presentation Kahoot returned 90% (18/20) accuracy. They also moved from one-off baseline surveys to paired pre/post questionnaires after realising the carnival survey only measured perception, not learning gain.","publicEngagement_zh":"教育工作在他們自稱 LITTLE GEM（Gauge、Engage、Modify）的架構下進行，觸及 3 歲到 101 歲的對象，場域包括一所幼稚園（灣仔 Pods Kindergarten）、兩所小學（SSCPS 與十八鄉鄉事委員會公益社小學）、一間由生命熱線（Suicide Prevention Services）經營的長者中心、自己的學校，以及合作的高中隊伍。活動形式是依對象設計、而非重複套用：在一場公眾嘉年華設置 DNA 彩虹擲幣遊戲攤位，3 小時內吸引超過 170 人參與；為 3 至 6 歲孩童設計「Find a Match」廚餘配對卡牌遊戲與 DNA 黏土模型；帶小學生做草莓與香蕉的 DNA 萃取；一場 Kahoot 問答；FoodSafe 應用程式的現場 beta 測試；以及一本原創漫畫《The Tragedy of Margaret in Food Waste》，他們還把它改編成由青蛙 Margaret 擔任主角的短劇。對長者則安排實體的廚餘配對卡牌遊戲與黏土手作。團隊內部，HKSSC iGEM Club 在 7 個月間為 11 至 16 歲學員辦了 8 場課後工作坊（4 場濕實驗、3 場 IHP、1 場軟體），共 28 位參與者，內容涵蓋 DNA、以 P200 與 P10 微量移液器進行吸量與連續稀釋、膠體電泳，以及 DNA 鑰匙圈製作，並用 Wayground 測驗複習——這是為未來隊員刻意鋪設的人才管道。他們量測的是學習成效、不是人數：在 SSCPS，工作坊前 20 位學生中有 0% 知道 iGEM 是什麼、10% 知道合成生物學，工作坊後 100% 能說出 iGEM 的核心目標並定義合成生物學，且 100% 成功萃取出可見的 DNA；在公益社小學，演講後的 Kahoot 正確率為 90%（18/20）。他們也在察覺嘉年華問卷只量到觀感、而非學習增益之後，從一次性的基線調查改為前後配對問卷。","ihp":"IHP ran on a six-step cycle of their own design, the iCycle (Identify, Initiate, Interact, Insight, Improve, and a sixth step, Inspire), with the deliberate twist that Improve feeds back into Interact so broad stakeholders can be revisited. Stakeholders were sorted into four functions - Information, Implementation, Safety & Technical, and iGEMer feedback - and they covered the whole disposal-to-treatment pipeline: public and restaurants (disposal), EPD (collection), O-PARK (treatment). The design changes are specific. CityU Professor Patrick Lee told them flatly that engineered microbes cannot legally be placed in collection bins in Hong Kong and must be used in a controlled environment with a kill switch, which reshaped their entire safety and implementation framing; he also said demonstrating paraben loss is stronger evidence than showing translation and told them to use both HPLC and the pNPA assay alongside Monod kinetics - which is exactly what the results page then does. HKU advised them they were over-engineering enzyme optimisation, that expressing the protein was enough to demonstrate the concept, that they should focus on the bacteria rather than the enzyme, and that instead of immediately adding a kill switch they should compare growth rates of wild-type versus transgenic E. coli and determine MIC by growing bacteria across paraben concentrations - which became the project's central experimental design. The Environmental Protection Department replied by institutional email with real operating data: food waste pH is 4-6 and varies with contents, impurities are removed and the waste slurried with process water, and the slurry stabilises in a buffer tank for 2-3 days before digestion. HKSSC acted on both constraints, testing their microbes under different pH conditions (which is also why pH stability became the target of the HotSpot Wizard work) and adding bin-contamination messaging to their education workshops. The HKUST Black Soldier Fly Bin team confirmed preservatives are a real but under-documented problem, endorsed pre-treatment in the bin before food reaches O-PARK, and pointed out HKSSC had not considered how to feed their E. coli - advising a layer of food replaced weekly. The KYS student survey revealed a misconception that catering, not households, produces most food waste, and that students knew about the problem but not the solutions, so the team added Smart Food Waste Bin content to the comic and to later activities. The elderly survey showed forgetting purchased food was a key driver of waste, which generated a planned 'food record' fridge-inventory reminder feature for the FoodSafe app.","ihp_zh":"IHP 以他們自行設計的六步循環 iCycle（Identify、Initiate、Interact、Insight、Improve，以及第六步 Inspire）運作，刻意安排的巧思是讓 Improve 回饋到 Interact，使廣泛的利害關係人可以再次接觸。利害關係人依功能分為四類——資訊、實作、安全與技術、iGEMer 回饋——並覆蓋了從丟棄到處理的整條鏈：公眾與餐廳（丟棄）、環保署（收運）、O-PARK（處理）。設計上的改動相當具體。香港城市大學的 Patrick Lee 教授直言，在香港不可能合法把工程菌放進收集桶，必須在受控環境中使用並配備致死開關，這重塑了他們整個安全與落地的論述框架；他也指出證明 paraben 被分解比展示蛋白質被轉譯更有力，並要他們同時使用 HPLC 與 pNPA 試驗、再搭配 Monod 動力學——結果頁做的正是這些。香港大學方面則提醒他們在酵素最佳化上過度工程化，能把蛋白質表現出來就足以證明概念，重點應放在細菌而非酵素，而且不要急著加致死開關，應先比較野生型與轉殖 E. coli 的生長速率，並在一系列 paraben 濃度下培養細菌來測定 MIC——這後來成為整個專題的核心實驗設計。環境保護署以機構電子郵件回覆了真實的運轉資料：廚餘 pH 為 4-6 並隨成分變動，雜質會先去除、廚餘再與製程水打成漿液，漿液在緩衝槽中穩定 2-3 天後才進入消化。HKSSC 針對這兩項限制都採取了行動，在不同 pH 條件下測試他們的菌（這也是 pH 穩定性成為 HotSpot Wizard 工作目標的原因），並在教育工作坊中加入廚餘桶污染的宣導內容。香港科技大學的黑水虻廚餘桶團隊確認防腐劑確實是個真問題但文獻記載不足，支持在食物進入 O-PARK 之前就在桶內做前處理，也指出 HKSSC 沒有考慮要怎麼餵養他們的 E. coli——建議鋪一層食物並每週更換。公益社小學的學生問卷揭露了一個迷思，以為大部分廚餘來自餐飲業而非家戶，也顯示學生知道問題存在但不知道解法，因此團隊在漫畫與後續活動中加入了智慧廚餘桶的內容。長者問卷顯示忘記自己買過的食物是浪費的主要成因之一，由此催生了 FoodSafe 應用程式規劃中的「食物記錄」冰箱庫存提醒功能。","realWorld":"The intended deployment is a pre-treatment step dropped into infrastructure that already exists - the EPD's smart food-waste bins in public rental housing estates and the front end of O-PARK's anaerobic digestion line - rather than a new facility, and the team repeatedly checks the design against real operating constraints (pH 4-6, impurities, 2-3 day buffer-tank residence, and the legal bar on releasing GMOs into public bins). They frame the contribution as a reusable framework rather than a single product: parabens are one preservative class, and the enzymatic pre-treatment approach is pitched as adaptable to other persistent inhibitors and micropollutants. Impact is mapped to SDG 4 (target 4.7), SDG 7 (target 7.2, higher biomethane yield from more complete digestion), SDG 11, SDG 12 (targets 12.4 and 12.5) and SDG 13. There is no formal business model, revenue forecast or regulatory filing plan on the wiki, and FoodSafe deliberately stops short of public App Store release on cost and effort grounds - both stated plainly rather than overclaimed.","realWorld_zh":"預期的落地方式是把一個前處理步驟放進既有的基礎設施——環保署在公共屋邨設置的智慧廚餘桶，以及 O-PARK 厭氧消化線的前端——而不是另建新設施，團隊也反覆用真實運轉限制（pH 4-6、雜質、緩衝槽 2-3 天的停留時間，以及不得將基改生物釋放到公共收集桶的法規門檻）檢驗設計。他們把貢獻定位為可重複使用的框架、而非單一產品：paraben 只是防腐劑的一類，酵素前處理的做法被定位為可延伸到其他難分解的抑制物與微量污染物。影響力對應到 SDG 4（細項 4.7）、SDG 7（細項 7.2，更完整的消化帶來更高的生物甲烷產率）、SDG 11、SDG 12（細項 12.4 與 12.5）與 SDG 13。wiki 上沒有正式的商業模式、營收預估或法規申請計畫，FoodSafe 也因成本與人力考量而刻意不公開上架 App Store——兩者都直白說明，沒有誇大。","partners":["Hong Kong Environmental Protection Department (EPD), Organic Waste Infrastructure group","O-PARK (Organic Resources Recovery Centre)","Professor Patrick Lee, City University of Hong Kong","The University of Hong Kong (enzyme characterisation and biosafety consultation)","HKUST Black Soldier Fly Bin team","Yataki Japanese Restaurant","Suicide Prevention Services (carnival booth and Elderly Community Centre)","Pods Kindergarten","St. Stephen's College Preparatory School (SSCPS)","Shap Pat Heung Rural Committee Kung Yik She Primary School (KYS)","HongKong-PuiChing iGEM team","Asia-Pacific iGEMer Community (APiC) and Greater Bay Area SynBio Alliance (iGBA)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6053/wiki/modelling/image1.avif","caption":"The prbA paraben esterase structure retrieved from AlphaFold and visualised in UCSF Chimera; the long flexible N-terminal tail matches the 31-residue signal peptide and justified switching to pelB periplasmic targeting.","caption_zh":"取自 AlphaFold、並以 UCSF Chimera 視覺化的 prbA 對羥基苯甲酸酯酯酶結構；長而柔軟的 N 端尾巴與 31 個殘基的訊號肽相符，成為改用 pelB 周質導向的依據。","credit":"Team HKSSC, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6053/wiki/results/image20.avif","caption":"Initial velocity versus pNPA substrate concentration for all four enzyme conditions, fitted to Michaelis-Menten kinetics - the data behind the mass-normalised catalytic capacity metric Q showing recombinant prbA outperforming commercial liver esterase 2.09-fold at equal mass.","caption_zh":"四種酵素條件下初始速度對 pNPA 受質濃度的關係，並以 Michaelis-Menten 動力學擬合——這是支撐質量標準化催化容量指標 Q 的數據，顯示在相同質量下重組 prbA 的表現優於市售肝酯酶 2.09 倍。","credit":"Team HKSSC, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6053/wiki/software/image14.avif","caption":"FoodSafe's AI-assisted food safety checker: a photographed apple rated 'Totally Fine' by DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash's vision model, with the supporting observations shown so users can inspect the reasoning rather than just the verdict.","caption_zh":"FoodSafe 的 AI 輔助食品安全檢查器：一顆拍照上傳的蘋果被 DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash 的視覺模型評為「Totally Fine」，並列出支撐的觀察依據，讓使用者能檢視判斷理由、而不只看到結論。","credit":"Team HKSSC, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6053/wiki/software/image10.avif","caption":"Microbe Wars campaign gameplay - a browser-based 2D arena game written in Python by the team, in which players fight paraben enemies as prbA.","caption_zh":"Microbe Wars 的戰役模式畫面——一款由隊員以 Python 寫成的瀏覽器 2D 競技場遊戲，玩家化身 prbA 對抗 paraben 敵人。","credit":"Team HKSSC, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"The copyable thing here is statistical honesty as a competitive advantage: HKSSC could not measure molar enzyme concentration, so instead of quietly reporting an invalid kcat/Km they invented and justified a mass-normalised metric (Q) valid only below Km, then ran a two-way ANOVA, discovered unequal variances with a median-based Brown-Forsythe test, and switched to Welch-Satterthwaite contrasts with Holm correction rather than ignoring the violation. Pair that with their habit of publishing the cycle that went backwards (Cycle 2's MIC was worse than Cycle 1's) and diagnosing why - a high-school-plus centre will gain more credibility from that than from any extra experiment.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"此處最值得借鏡的是把統計上的誠實變成競爭優勢：HKSSC 無法量測酵素的莫耳濃度，於是他們沒有默默報出一個不成立的 kcat/Km，而是自行定義並論證一個以質量標準化的指標（Q），並明確限定只在低於 Km 的區間成立；接著跑雙因子 ANOVA，用基於中位數的 Brown-Forsythe 檢定發現變異數不齊一，便改用經 Holm 校正的 Welch-Satterthwaite 對比，而不是忽略這項違反。再加上他們習慣把走回頭路的循環也公開（Cycle 2 的 MIC 比 Cycle 1 更差）並診斷原因——對一個高中以上層級的中心而言，這比多做一個實驗更能贏得可信度。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/hkssc/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hkssc/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/hkssc/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/hkssc/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/hkssc/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/hkssc/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/hkssc/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/hkssc/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/hkssc/contribution","https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6053/wiki/modelling/wiki-modelling-final.pdf","https://github.com/judeliucodex/Foodsave","https://igem-game.vercel.app","https://api.igem.org/v1/teams/6053"],"rank":110},"6054":{"team":"SJTU-BioX-Shanghai","id":"6054","section":"Undergrad","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/sjtu-biox-shanghai/","projectTitle":"Dual-Armor","projectTitle_zh":"Dual-Armor（雙重護甲）","tagline":"An engineered living dressing that breaks open wound biofilm, clears pathogens and supports tissue repair in chronic wounds","tagline_zh":"一種工程化活體敷料，能破壞傷口生物膜、清除病原菌，並支持慢性傷口的組織修復","summary":"SJTU-BioX-Shanghai built Dual-Armor, an engineered-microbe dressing for chronic wounds, targeting the biofilm that a meta-analysis of 2,666 chronic wounds found in 68% of cases; about 18.6 million people develop diabetic foot ulcers each year and roughly 65% recur within five years. The team's inclusivity work is the most systematically theorised of the 2026 cohort: they built a two-layer framework in which four dimensions (VOICE, OPPORTUNITY, ACCESSIBILITY, PARTICIPATION) locate where participation is blocked and a five-step pathway, HEALS (Hear, Examine, Act, Learn, Share), governs how each barrier is answered. Twelve activities are each written up against both layers, and patient input visibly changed the product: Dual-Armor was repositioned from a stand-alone treatment to an auxiliary post-debridement dressing, and patients' fear of live bacteria touching the wound drove the physical-containment hardware design.","summary_zh":"SJTU-BioX-Shanghai 做出 Dual-Armor，一款用於慢性傷口的工程菌敷料，針對的是生物膜——一項涵蓋 2,666 例慢性傷口的統合分析發現其中 68% 有生物膜；每年約有 1,860 萬人罹患糖尿病足潰瘍，約 65% 在五年內復發。該隊的包容性工作是 2026 年各隊中理論化最系統的：他們建立了一個雙層架構，以四個面向（VOICE、OPPORTUNITY、ACCESSIBILITY、PARTICIPATION）定位參與在哪裡受阻，並以五步路徑 HEALS（Hear、Examine、Act、Learn、Share）規範每一道障礙如何被回應。十二項活動都分別對照兩個層次寫成紀錄，病人的意見也明顯改變了產品：Dual-Armor 從獨立療法重新定位為清創後的輔助敷料，而病人對活菌接觸傷口的恐懼促成了實體圍阻硬體的設計。","awards":["Inclusivity Award — Nominee (Undergrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Self-built two-layer inclusivity framework: four dimensions named by the question each asks - VOICE (Can I be heard?), OPPORTUNITY (Can I get in?), ACCESSIBILITY (Can I engage in a way that works for me?), PARTICIPATION (Can I stay and contribute?) - plus HEALS (Hear, Examine, Act, Learn, Share) as the common action pathway every activity follows. Education was mapped onto three learner pathways (students: Understand to Learn to Create; public: Encounter to Understand; peer educators: Share to Adapt to Continue) and grounded in Constructionism and UDL 3.0, applied retrospectively as a mirror rather than imposed in advance. Photovoice was used with a proper citation to Wang and Burris (1997).","frameworks_zh":"自建的雙層包容性架構：四個面向各以它所提出的問題命名——VOICE（我能被聽見嗎？）、OPPORTUNITY（我能進得來嗎？）、ACCESSIBILITY（我能以適合自己的方式參與嗎？）、PARTICIPATION（我能留下來並有所貢獻嗎？）——再加上 HEALS（Hear、Examine、Act、Learn、Share），作為每一項活動共同遵循的行動路徑。教育工作對應到三條學習者路徑（學生：理解—學習—創造；大眾：接觸—理解；同儕教育者：分享—調整—延續），並以建構論與 UDL 3.0 為基礎，但是回溯性地當成一面檢視的鏡子，而非事前強加的框架。Photovoice 的使用也正確引用了 Wang 與 Burris（1997）。","dataviz":"Co-designed care journey maps with colour-coded burden stickers marking pain, inconvenience, cost and psychological pressure; a handbook development flow figure; the four-dimension and HEALS framework figures; stakeholder overview of included groups.","dataviz_zh":"共同設計的照護歷程圖，以顏色標示的負擔貼紙標記疼痛、不便、費用與心理壓力；手冊開發流程圖；四面向與 HEALS 架構圖；納入族群的利害關係人總覽。","datascience":"Paired pre/post questionnaires across activities: six patient questionnaires and six in-depth inpatient interviews with published anonymised results (66.7% had three or more episodes of infection, worsening or recurrence in the previous year; 83.3% described the wound's impact on daily life as large or very large); the Beneath the Wound role-play playtest collected five anonymous questionnaires at a 100% response rate, with mean self-rated understanding of five core concepts rising from 1.8 to 3.52/5, understanding of MRSA from 1.2 to 3.4/5 (the largest gain), inclusivity-experience mean 4.03/5, and 'every role carried real weight' and 'the host favored no position' both 4.4/5; pre/post testing at the Life Science x AI summer camp. The team repeatedly states sample limits rather than overclaiming.","datascience_zh":"各項活動都採配對的前後測問卷：六份病人問卷與六場住院病人深度訪談，並公開去識別化結果（66.7% 在過去一年內有三次以上的感染、惡化或復發；83.3% 形容傷口對日常生活的影響為大或非常大）；「Beneath the Wound」角色扮演試玩收回五份匿名問卷，回收率 100%，五項核心概念的自評理解度平均從 1.8 升到 3.52/5，對 MRSA 的理解從 1.2 升到 3.4/5（增幅最大），包容性體驗平均 4.03/5，「每個角色都有實際份量」與「主持人不偏袒任何立場」都是 4.4/5；Life Science x AI 夏令營也做了前後測。該隊一再說明樣本的限制，而不是過度宣稱。","software":"Two open-source tools, both built from a named barrier. LabSafeMom gives pregnant, pregnancy-planning or breastfeeding researchers per-protocol risk guidance: submit a protocol and get a structured risk overview, safety controls and a PPE checklist against a knowledge base of 119 hazard entries built from public occupational-health references including NIOSH. Critically it has two separated modes - Basic runs entirely in the browser against a local deterministic rule set with no generative model, so the same input always yields the same reasoning and every score is traceable to a stated rule and reference; Enhanced adds natural-language protocol analysis only when the user supplies their own API key, and risk scores still come from auditable rules. Every report states it is an aid for discussion with an institutional EHS office and a qualified clinician, never a substitute. LabMate reduces bench friction for new researchers: it ingests protocols as PDF, TXT, Markdown, CSV or pasted text in Chinese or English, generates a preparation checklist, guides steps with smart timers, keeps an exportable lab record (Markdown, text or print), offers a Chinese-English toggle, four themes (Light, Lab, Dark, Sunset) and large-font options, and runs locally and offline with privacy-first handling.","software_zh":"兩項開源工具，都是從一項被指名的障礙出發做出來的。LabSafeMom 為懷孕、準備懷孕或哺乳中的研究人員提供逐一實驗流程的風險指引：送入一份流程，就得到結構化的風險總覽、安全管制措施與個人防護裝備檢核表，依據的是一個含 119 筆危害條目的知識庫，由 NIOSH 等公開職業衛生資料建立。關鍵在於它有兩個彼此分離的模式——Basic 完全在瀏覽器中依本地的確定性規則集運作，不用生成式模型，因此同樣的輸入永遠得到同樣的推論，每個分數都可追溯到明確的規則與出處；Enhanced 只在使用者自行提供 API key 時才加入自然語言的流程分析，而風險分數仍然來自可稽核的規則。每份報告都註明它是與校內 EHS 單位及合格臨床醫師討論時的輔助，絕不是替代。LabMate 則降低新進研究人員在實驗台上的摩擦：可讀入 PDF、TXT、Markdown、CSV 或直接貼上的中英文流程文字，生成準備檢核表，以智慧計時器引導步驟，保留可匯出的實驗紀錄（Markdown、純文字或列印），提供中英文切換、四種主題（Light、Lab、Dark、Sunset）與大字型選項，並以隱私優先的方式在本地離線運作。","stack":["browser-based deterministic rule engine (LabSafeMom Basic mode)","optional user-supplied-key LLM analysis (Enhanced mode)","offline-first local protocol parser (LabMate)","accessible web front end with dyslexia-font and animation toggles","Photovoice participatory method","paired pre/post survey instruments"],"techniques":["biofilm disruption","pathogen clearance by engineered microbes","naringenin-related mechanisms","physical containment hardware for live-bacteria dressings","post-debridement auxiliary dressing design"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"The framing sentence is the one to steal: 'Open is not enough. A door can stand open while some people never have the chance to reach it.' Under VOICE, the team visited the vascular disease department of Shanghai Hospital of Integrated Traditional Chinese and Western Medicine, collecting six patient questionnaires and six in-depth inpatient interviews plus conversations with attending clinicians and ward care workers, and published the bilingual instrument and the anonymised results as PDFs. Patients' top fears were recurrent infection, healing time, pain and amputation risk; clinicians focused on debridement, exudate management and dressing fit; care workers identified post-discharge dressing changes and disinfection as the weakest link in the care chain. This directly repositioned Dual-Armor as an auxiliary dressing for continuous post-debridement care and drove the physical-containment hardware. A Photovoice study then handed the camera to patients, who chose which objects and scenes represented their treatment - wheelchairs, bedside equipment, nursing supplies - and explained why; for inpatients who could not shoot themselves, the team operated the camera but the subject, the explanation and the consent to display always remained the participant's. The authorised, de-identified photographs with the participants' own accounts became an exhibition at Shanghai Jiao Tong University that drew more than one hundred visits, with faces, wound close-ups, bed numbers and records deliberately excluded. The team's reflection is unusually principled: 'creating an opportunity for expression does not give the researchers ownership of the images', and the quality of an exhibition can never take priority over informed consent. Co-design went further: patients, caregivers and care workers drew the whole chronic-wound care journey with colour-coded stickers for pain, inconvenience, cost and psychological pressure, and caregivers added the hidden labour of accompanying visits and watching for abnormalities. The questions they raised repeatedly ('what do I do when the dressing sticks to the wound?', 'which smell means something is wrong?') became the actual table of contents of a 23-page Home-Care Handbook, which translates professional guidance into red-amber-green warning signals, a six-step dressing-change method and hand-fillable care record tables, deliberately offers an executable alternative after every 'do not do this', and gives separate dressing-change options for urban and primary-care settings. The draft was reviewed by clinicians from burn and reconstructive surgery and from endocrinology, who corrected the iodine and hydrogen peroxide guidance, the timing of diabetic foot care and primary-care dressing substitutes. The handbook is published free in Chinese and English, with printable appendix tables so it works for people without digital devices. The team also wrote Beneath the Wound, a 46-page host-facilitated ethics role-play (plus 10 pages of character cards in five- and six-player sets) in which players take the parts of a 72-year-old diabetic-foot patient, family members, the attending physician and ethics roles, and reach a decision with no standard answer over about two and a half hours; information is deliberately distributed - the physician holds risk data, the ethics member remembers past failures, the family waits for authority, the patient carries fear - so players must persuade each other with incomplete information. The full script and cards are released for other teams. Under OPPORTUNITY, the team ran no-prerequisite synthetic biology lessons at a middle school in Bazhong, Sichuan and a small rural class in Hou'an Village, Taizhou, Zhejiang, chosen precisely because students there rarely meet frontier science, using physical role-play of the central dogma and a 'Building a Cell Factory' design task, requiring no specialised equipment, delivered partly by video lesson in Hou'an, and evaluated with pre- and post-questionnaires; students produced their own posters, plasmid maps and models. These were followed by guided SJTU wet-lab visits to supply the missing middle step between a school lesson and university research, and by sustained mentoring of VGA-Pinion, a first-time US high-school team, from emails and online meetings through to an in-person Shanghai lab visit, with advice on project narrative, model-parameter grounding and Human Practices structure, always framed as ideas rather than decisions made for them. Under ACCESSIBILITY, 'Touch Life, See Hope' was a braille chronic-wound postcard co-creation at SJTU in which participants from several majors learned the braille alphabet, writing board and stylus, then discovered that accessibility is redesign rather than transcription - a tactile reader cannot skim, so messages had to be shortened, care advice separated from decorative text, and card layout built around how a finger moves; the cards carry Dual-Armor characters so sighted and non-sighted readers recognise them, and an 11-page English Braille Postcard Co-Creation Toolkit was released so others can run the session. 'Light Deep in the Lilong' is a sixteen-page bilingual illustrated story about Grandma Li, a 76-year-old retired Chinese-language teacher with an unhealed diabetic foot wound, written for the readers conventional material ignores - above all children in the patient's family - with wound microbes as characters mapped one-to-one onto Dual-Armor's functional modules; a bilingual audio edition is in preparation so reading need not depend on sight, and the story was read live to students in Bazhong. The wiki itself is an accessibility artefact, prompted by a senior student with ADHD who reported reading difficulty on many websites: it uses the Okabe-Ito colourblind-safe palette (#E69F00, #56B4E9, #F0E442, #D55E00, #0072B2), a one-click dyslexia-friendly font toggle, a one-click animation kill switch and a reading progress bar. Under PARTICIPATION the team turned inward to people already in science, building LabSafeMom for pregnant researchers and LabMate for new bench members. Education also produced a Base-Pairing Challenge card game, a diabetes scripted game, 'Dual-Armor Werewolf' (a social-deduction game where E. coli, S. epidermidis, immune cells and S. aureus are the roles and naringenin mechanisms are built into role relationships), a picture book and audiobook, clay cell-model making, a bioethics debate with no preset answer, and a six-step student design task (Problem, Chassis, Function, Safety, Teamwork, Presentation). Finally, the team co-authored a cross-team Education Activity Handbook with other university iGEM teams, taking responsibility for Part 7 on spatialised education and exhibitions with their Urban Orienteering chapter, explicitly so that future iGEMers do not start from scratch.","publicEngagement_zh":"值得借用的是那句定調的話：「開放還不夠。門可以一直開著，但有些人始終沒有機會走到門前。」在 VOICE 面向，該隊走訪上海市中西醫結合醫院的周圍血管科，收集六份病人問卷與六場住院病人深度訪談，並與主治醫師及病房照護員對談，再把雙語問卷工具與去識別化結果以 PDF 公開。病人最害怕的是感染復發、癒合時間、疼痛與截肢風險；臨床醫師關注清創、滲液管理與敷料貼合度；照護員指出出院後的換藥與消毒是整條照護鏈最弱的一環。這直接把 Dual-Armor 重新定位為清創後持續照護用的輔助敷料，也推動了實體圍阻硬體。接著的 Photovoice 研究把相機交給病人，由他們自己選擇哪些物件與場景代表自己的治療——輪椅、床邊設備、護理用品——並說明原因；對無法自己拍攝的住院病人，由團隊代為操作相機，但拍攝對象、說明內容與展示的同意權始終屬於參與者。這些經授權、去識別化的照片連同參與者自己的敘述，成為上海交通大學的一場展覽，參觀超過一百人次，並刻意排除臉部、傷口特寫、床號與病歷。該隊的反思格外有原則：「創造一個表達的機會，並不等於研究者取得了影像的所有權」，展覽的品質也絕不能優先於知情同意。共同設計走得更遠：病人、家屬照顧者與照護員一起畫出完整的慢性傷口照護歷程，用不同顏色的貼紙標記疼痛、不便、費用與心理壓力，照顧者還補上了陪同就醫與留意異常這些看不見的勞動。他們反覆提出的問題（「敷料黏在傷口上的時候該怎麼辦？」、「哪一種氣味代表出了問題？」）直接成為一本 23 頁《居家照護手冊》的實際目錄。手冊把專業指引轉譯成紅—黃—綠三級警示訊號、六步換藥法與可手寫填寫的照護紀錄表，刻意在每一句「不要這樣做」之後都給出一個可執行的替代做法，並針對都市與基層醫療場域分別提供換藥選項。草稿由燒傷整形外科與新陳代謝科的臨床醫師審閱，他們修正了碘與過氧化氫的使用指引、糖尿病足照護的時機，以及基層可用的敷料替代品。手冊以中英文免費公開，並附可列印的附錄表格，讓沒有數位裝置的人也用得上。該隊還寫了《Beneath the Wound》，一份 46 頁、由主持人帶領的倫理角色扮演腳本（另有 10 頁角色卡，分五人與六人兩種配置），玩家分別扮演一位 72 歲的糖尿病足病人、家屬、主治醫師與倫理相關角色，在約兩個半小時內做出一個沒有標準答案的決定；資訊被刻意分散配置——醫師掌握風險數據、倫理成員記得過去的失敗、家屬等待權威表態、病人承受恐懼——因此玩家必須在資訊不完整的情況下彼此說服。完整腳本與角色卡已釋出給其他隊伍。在 OPPORTUNITY 面向，該隊在四川巴中的一所國中與浙江台州后安村的一個小型鄉村班級開設零先修要求的合成生物學課程，選這兩個地點正是因為當地學生少有機會接觸前沿科學；課程用肢體角色扮演演示中心法則，加上一項「打造細胞工廠」的設計任務，完全不需要專門器材，在后安村有一部分以影片授課，並以前後測問卷評估；學生自己做出海報、質體圖譜與模型。之後再安排到上海交大的導覽式濕實驗室參訪，補上學校課程與大學研究之間缺掉的中間一環；另外也長期輔導首次參賽的美國高中隊伍 VGA-Pinion，從電子郵件、線上會議一路到實地到上海參訪實驗室，在專案敘事、模型參數依據與 Human Practices 架構上提供建議，而且一貫定位為提供想法，不是替他們做決定。在 ACCESSIBILITY 面向，「Touch Life, See Hope」是在上海交大舉辦的點字慢性傷口明信片共創活動，來自多個系所的參與者先學點字字母、點字板與點字筆，接著就發現無障礙是重新設計而不是逐字轉譯——觸覺讀者無法快速瀏覽，所以訊息必須縮短、照護建議必須與裝飾性文字分開，卡片版面也要照手指移動的方式重新安排；卡片上放了 Dual-Armor 的角色，讓視覺與非視覺讀者都認得出來，並釋出一份 11 頁的英文點字明信片共創工具包，讓別人也能照著辦。「Light Deep in the Lilong」是一則 16 頁的雙語繪本故事，主角是李奶奶，一位 76 歲、退休的國文老師，有一處遲遲未癒的糖尿病足傷口；故事寫給傳統素材忽略的讀者，尤其是病人家裡的孩子，傷口微生物被寫成角色，並與 Dual-Armor 的功能模組一一對應；雙語有聲版正在製作，讓閱讀不必依賴視覺，故事也在巴中現場朗讀給學生聽。wiki 本身就是一件無障礙產出，起因是一位患有 ADHD 的高年級學生反映許多網站讀起來很吃力：網站採用 Okabe-Ito 色盲友善配色（#E69F00、#56B4E9、#F0E442、#D55E00、#0072B2）、一鍵切換的讀寫障礙友善字型、一鍵關閉動畫，以及閱讀進度條。在 PARTICIPATION 面向，該隊轉向已經身在科學領域裡的人，為懷孕的研究人員做 LabSafeMom，為新進實驗室成員做 LabMate。教育方面也產出了鹼基配對挑戰卡牌遊戲、糖尿病劇本遊戲、「Dual-Armor 狼人殺」（一款社交推理遊戲，角色就是 E. coli、S. epidermidis、免疫細胞與 S. aureus，柚皮素的作用機制則寫進了角色關係裡）、一本繪本與有聲書、黏土細胞模型製作、一場沒有預設答案的生物倫理辯論，以及一項六步驟的學生設計任務（問題、載體、功能、安全、團隊合作、簡報）。最後，該隊與其他大學 iGEM 隊伍合著了一本跨隊《教育活動手冊》，負責第 7 章空間化教育與展覽的部分，貢獻「城市定向」一章，明確就是為了讓未來的 iGEMer 不必從零開始。","ihp":"The project began with a team member's own fall injury and the experience of caring for the wound. Patient and caregiver evidence was treated as design input rather than validation: ward findings are documented on the Integrated Human Practices page and traced through to three specific changes (product repositioning to post-debridement auxiliary dressing, physical containment of live bacteria, and the decision to co-write a care handbook with clinical staff). The team draws an explicit principle: patients may not decide gene circuits or material parameters, but they decide what the technology must respond to, and lack of specialist knowledge is never a reason to exclude them from design. Limits are stated rather than hidden - six patients cannot represent everyone, and acceptance expressed in a hypothetical interview must still be verified in real use.","ihp_zh":"專案的起點是一位隊員自己跌倒受傷、並照護那處傷口的經驗。病人與照顧者的證據被當成設計輸入，而不是事後驗證：病房訪查的發現記錄在 Integrated Human Practices 頁面，並一路追溯到三項具體改變（產品重新定位為清創後輔助敷料、活菌的實體圍阻，以及決定與臨床人員共同撰寫照護手冊）。該隊明確提出一項原則：病人也許不決定基因迴路或材料參數，但他們決定這項技術必須回應什麼，而缺乏專業知識永遠不能成為把他們排除在設計之外的理由。限制是寫明的而非藏起來的——六位病人無法代表所有人，在假設性訪談中表達的接受度，仍然必須在真實使用中驗證。","realWorld":"Open, reusable outputs: the 23-page Home-Care Handbook in Chinese and English with printable records; the Beneath the Wound full script, host guide and character cards; the Braille Postcard Co-Creation Toolkit; the bilingual illustrated story and forthcoming audio edition; LabSafeMom and LabMate as live apps with open source; teaching decks for the central dogma, cell factory, bioethics debate and engineered-microorganism design; game cards; and the co-authored cross-team Education Activity Handbook. A beginner's guide for new iGEM teams covering schedule planning, stage tasks and common questions is planned for open release on the wiki.","realWorld_zh":"開放、可重複使用的產出：23 頁中英文《居家照護手冊》，附可列印的紀錄表；《Beneath the Wound》的完整腳本、主持人指南與角色卡；點字明信片共創工具包；雙語繪本故事與即將推出的有聲版；LabSafeMom 與 LabMate 都是可直接使用的應用程式並且開源；中心法則、細胞工廠、生物倫理辯論與工程微生物設計的教學簡報；遊戲卡牌；以及合著的跨隊《教育活動手冊》。另有一份給 iGEM 新隊伍的入門指南，涵蓋時程規劃、各階段任務與常見問題，計畫在 wiki 上公開釋出。","partners":["Shanghai Hospital of Integrated Traditional Chinese and Western Medicine - vascular disease department (patients, clinicians, ward care workers)","clinicians in burn and reconstructive surgery and endocrinology (handbook review)","Bazhong Middle School, Sichuan","Hou'an Village rural class, Taizhou, Zhejiang","Shanghai Jiao Tong University (exhibition venue, wet lab visits, braille co-creation)","VGA-Pinion (first-time US high-school iGEM team, project AstraEV)","ECNU iGEM","iGEM East China Regional Exchange teams","co-authors of the cross-team Education Activity Handbook","East China Five Universities Science & Art Micro-painting Competition"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6054/wiki/images/inclusivity/braille-1.avif","caption":"'Touch Life, See Hope': writing chronic-wound knowledge onto braille postcards, with an open English toolkit released so others can run it","caption_zh":"「Touch Life, See Hope」：把慢性傷口知識寫上點字明信片，並釋出開放的英文工具包讓別人也能照著辦","credit":"Team SJTU-BioX-Shanghai, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6054/wiki/images/inclusivity/act2-exhibition-1.avif","caption":"The de-identified Photovoice exhibition at Shanghai Jiao Tong University, visited by more than one hundred people","caption_zh":"上海交通大學的去識別化 Photovoice 展覽，參觀人次超過一百","credit":"Team SJTU-BioX-Shanghai, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6054/wiki/images/inclusivity/act3-journey-map.avif","caption":"Co-drawn chronic-wound care journey maps with colour-coded burden stickers, which became the handbook's table of contents","caption_zh":"共同繪製的慢性傷口照護歷程圖，附顏色標示的負擔貼紙，後來成為手冊的目錄","credit":"Team SJTU-BioX-Shanghai, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6054/wiki/images/inclusivity/act4-playtest.avif","caption":"First playtest of 'Beneath the Wound', a two-and-a-half-hour ethics role-play about an experimental living therapy","caption_zh":"「Beneath the Wound」首次試玩，一場關於實驗性活體療法、長達兩個半小時的倫理角色扮演","credit":"Team SJTU-BioX-Shanghai, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6054/wiki/images/inclusivity/labsafemom-ui-1.avif","caption":"LabSafeMom: auditable per-protocol hazard guidance for pregnant researchers, with a deterministic browser-only default mode","caption_zh":"LabSafeMom：為懷孕研究人員提供可稽核的逐流程危害指引，預設模式是確定性、只在瀏覽器執行","credit":"Team SJTU-BioX-Shanghai, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6054/wiki/images/inclusivity/bazhong-1.avif","caption":"No-prerequisite synthetic biology lessons at a middle school in Bazhong, Sichuan, using role-play instead of equipment","caption_zh":"四川巴中一所國中的零先修合成生物學課程，以角色扮演取代器材","credit":"Team SJTU-BioX-Shanghai, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Adopt SJTU's two-layer discipline: classify every engagement by which barrier it removes (can I be heard, get in, engage in my format, stay and contribute) and run each one through Hear-Examine-Act-Learn-Share, ending every activity with a downloadable artefact someone else can run - a toolkit, a script, a handbook - and a written statement of what the evidence does not prove.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"值得借用 SJTU 的雙層紀律：把每一項參與活動依它所排除的障礙分類（我能被聽見嗎、我能進得來嗎、我能用適合自己的形式參與嗎、我能留下來並有所貢獻嗎），並讓每一項都走完 Hear-Examine-Act-Learn-Share，每項活動都以一份別人可以直接拿去執行的可下載產出作結——工具包、腳本、手冊——再加上一段明白寫出證據尚未能證明什麼的說明。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/sjtu-biox-shanghai/","https://2026.igem.wiki/sjtu-biox-shanghai/inclusivity","https://2026.igem.wiki/sjtu-biox-shanghai/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/sjtu-biox-shanghai/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/sjtu-biox-shanghai/description"],"rank":7},"6058":{"team":"HK-Joint-School","id":"6058","section":"High School","country":"Hong Kong","village":"Manufacturing / Environment","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/hk-joint-school/","projectTitle":"FlaminGone","projectTitle_zh":"FlaminGone","tagline":"A non-toxic biological fire-retardant coating, plus PyroForge, a live protein-language-model web app that predicts thermostability from sequence alone.","tagline_zh":"無毒的生物性防火塗層，外加 PyroForge：一個已上線的蛋白質語言模型網頁應用，僅憑序列就能預測熱穩定性。","summary":"FlaminGone replaces halogenated chemical fire retardants with a self-assembling biological coating: E. coli's CsgA curli subunit forms an amyloid scaffold, fused to hydrophobic BslA for weatherproofing and polyethylene-binding peptides for substrate anchoring, in a two-layer system that sidesteps secretion limits and steric hindrance. Under fire testing the matrix forms a dense char shield that halts flame propagation and self-extinguishes, BslA prevents rain washout across weathering, and Arabidopsis assays indicated no ecotoxicity. To design the fusion peptides without waiting on crystal structures, the team built PyroForge, a publicly deployed web application that uses a frozen ESM-2 650M protein language model as a feature extractor under three lightweight custom-trained heads predicting melting temperature, folding free energy and per-mutation stability change, then scans every single-residue substitution and returns a ranked shortlist. For a high school team the engineering rigour is remarkable: a published S669 benchmark against 21 competing methods, Zenodo-archived weights and datasets with DOIs, 226-respondent user acceptance testing, and documented bugs that changed the model's reported accuracy.","summary_zh":"FlaminGone 以能自組裝的生物塗層取代含鹵素的化學阻燃劑：用 E. coli 的 CsgA curli 次單元形成類澱粉蛋白支架，融合疏水性的 BslA 以提供耐候能力、以及聚乙烯結合胜肽以錨定在基材上，並採用雙層設計繞開分泌量上限與立體障礙的問題。火燒測試中，這個基質會形成緻密的碳化屏障，阻止火焰延燒並自行熄滅；BslA 在耐候測試中可防止被雨水沖掉；Arabidopsis 試驗也顯示沒有生態毒性。為了不必等晶體結構就能設計融合胜肽，團隊做了 PyroForge：一個已公開部署的網頁應用，把凍結參數的 ESM-2 650M 蛋白質語言模型當作特徵擷取器，上面接三個自行訓練的輕量預測頭，分別預測熔解溫度、摺疊自由能與各突變造成的穩定性變化，接著掃描每一個單一殘基取代並回傳排序後的候選清單。以高中隊伍而言，其工程嚴謹度相當突出：公開與 21 種競爭方法對比的 S669 基準測試、在 Zenodo 上以 DOI 典藏的權重與資料集、226 人參與的使用者接受度測試，以及把改變了模型回報準確度的程式錯誤完整記錄下來。","awards":["Best Software — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"React + TypeScript + Vite + Mantine frontend over a FastAPI backend with Pydantic schema validation that rejects malformed inputs at the API boundary with HTTP 400 before they reach the queue. Celery with Redis splits work across three purpose-separated queues: 'fast' for sequence predictions and registry search using the resident ESM-2 (about 1 s), 'heavy' for GPU-bound mutation scanning and model training (minutes), and 'io' for network-bound ESMFold calls with waits up to 300 s, specifically so long network waits never occupy a GPU worker slot. Six Docker containers run on a GPU host via Docker Compose and a systemd unit, with only an Nginx reverse proxy exposed publicly and FastAPI, Redis and the workers isolated on the internal Docker network. Nginx also enforces the rate limiting, because the deployment is intentionally unauthenticated. The backend exposes five engines through a central registry (Prediction, Optimization, Visualization, Registry, Procurement) and rejects checkpoints whose normalization statistics do not match.","frameworks_zh":"前端為 React + TypeScript + Vite + Mantine，後端為 FastAPI，並以 Pydantic 做結構驗證，格式錯誤的輸入在 API 邊界就以 HTTP 400 擋掉，不會進到工作佇列。Celery 搭配 Redis 把工作分到三條依用途區分的佇列：fast 處理使用常駐 ESM-2 的序列預測與 Registry 搜尋（約 1 秒）、heavy 處理吃 GPU 的突變掃描與模型訓練（數分鐘）、io 處理受網路限制、等待最長 300 秒的 ESMFold 呼叫，這樣設計正是為了讓漫長的網路等待不會佔住 GPU 工作者的名額。六個 Docker 容器透過 Docker Compose 與一個 systemd unit 跑在 GPU 主機上，對外只開放 Nginx 反向代理，FastAPI、Redis 與工作者都隔離在內部 Docker 網路。流量限制也由 Nginx 執行，因為這套部署刻意不做身分驗證。後端透過一個中央登錄機制提供五個引擎（Prediction、Optimization、Visualization、Registry、Procurement），並會拒絕正規化統計量不相符的模型檢查點。","dataviz":"Seven workflow-ordered UI cards: sequence input (protein or DNA, with the longest ORF translated), composition descriptors, thermodynamic prediction with a plus/minus 95% confidence interval and a High/Low/Unavailable reliability flag keyed to sequence length relative to the training distribution, the ranked mutation shortlist, a browser 3D structure from ESMFold coloured by per-residue stability from the mutation scan, an iGEM Registry homology search that reports how many parts were searched and the snapshot build date so a zero-hit result stays interpretable, and codon optimisation reporting CAI and GC content with a hand-off to a DNA vendor. Long operations run asynchronously with the client polling every two seconds; fast ones return synchronously. History lives in browser local storage, managed from a sidebar, with large structure files stripped to fit quota, and an error boundary isolates individual card failures so one broken card does not take the page down. Benchmark results are published as figures: the S669 pooled-versus-within-protein comparison, the grouped cross-validation precision distribution, and the held-out scatter for all three heads.","dataviz_zh":"介面依工作流程排成七張卡片：序列輸入（蛋白質或 DNA，DNA 會轉譯最長的 ORF）、組成特徵描述、帶 ±95% 信賴區間的熱力學預測（並依序列長度相對於訓練分布的位置標示 High／Low／Unavailable 可信度）、排序後的突變候選清單、由 ESMFold 產生並在瀏覽器中呈現的 3D 結構（依突變掃描得到的各殘基穩定性上色）、iGEM Registry 同源搜尋（會回報搜尋了多少零件以及快照的建立日期，讓零命中的結果仍然可以解讀），以及回報 CAI 與 GC 含量、可直接轉交 DNA 合成廠商的密碼子最佳化。耗時的操作以非同步執行，前端每兩秒輪詢一次；快的操作則同步回傳。歷史紀錄存在瀏覽器 local storage 並由側邊欄管理，過大的結構檔會被剝除以符合容量限制；錯誤邊界會隔離單張卡片的失敗，讓一張壞掉的卡片不會拖垮整個頁面。基準測試結果以圖表公開：S669 的 pooled 與 within-protein 對比、分組交叉驗證的精確率分布，以及三個預測頭在保留集上的散布圖。","datascience":"ESM-2 650M is frozen and used only to map sequences to 1,280-dimensional vectors, with three light heads on top: a PCA-100 to Ridge plus gradient boosting model for Tm trained on Meltome Atlas (4,000 training proteins, 1,106 held out, 5,106 total), an MLP [128, 1024, 128, 1024] for dG whose architecture came from a Hyperband neural architecture search, and an MLP [256, 256, 256] with dropout 0.324 for ddG trained on the Tsuboyama 2023 mega-scale dataset (494,370 rows across 449 parent proteins). The ddG head takes both the mutant embedding and the mutant-minus-wildtype difference embedding, which removes sequence-invariant features and sharpens within-protein ranking at the acknowledged cost of cross-protein absolute comparison. Internal validation is grouped cross-validation across 266 parent proteins: top-5 precision 73.6% genuinely stabilising against a 19.8% baseline, with per-protein precision reported as varying from 0% to 100% and roughly 20% of proteins scoring below 50%. External benchmarking on S669 (669 variants, 94 proteins, no prior tuning) places PyroForge 18th of 22 methods on pooled ranking but 2nd of 22 on within-protein ranking and 1st among sequence-only methods, with a +0.248 Spearman improvement over zero-shot ESM-2 (95% CI +0.051 to +0.502); the team explains that this split is exactly what their design choice predicts. Limitations are published rather than buried: Ssym shows only a non-statistically-significant trend, ranking quality drops sharply beyond 400 residues, and the Tm Pearson r of 0.810 is said to overstate performance because the distribution is bimodal between thermophiles and mesophiles, with weaker within-group ordering. Trusted regimes are tabulated (scanning and folding to 400 aa, dG and ddG trusted at 10-72 aa, Tm training window 20-400 aa) and out-of-bounds inputs return low-confidence flags rather than failing silently. Four engineering iterations are documented with their numbers: random row splits leaked protein identity and inflated correlation to 0.85, which grouped parent-protein splitting corrected to a realistic 0.46; training on forward mutations only gave inconsistent reverse predictions (r = 0.27), fixed to 0.95 by appending negated reverse mutations; expanding Tm training from 237 proteins to the Meltome Atlas cut held-out error to 5.9 degrees C; and a sign-inversion bug had the optimizer ranking the most destabilising mutations first, fixed and locked down with an end-to-end regression test. Unit tests encode thermodynamic invariants directly: ddG(wt to wt) = 0, ddG(A to B) = -ddG(B to A), batched scan consistency against single-pair prediction, complete parent-protein holdout with no split overlap, a sign floor so top-k never returns predicted-destabilising variants, and CAI normalisation within synonymous codon families.","datascience_zh":"ESM-2 650M 參數凍結，只用來把序列映射成 1,280 維向量，上面接三個輕量預測頭：Tm 使用 PCA-100 接 Ridge 再加梯度提升模型，以 Meltome Atlas 訓練（4,000 個訓練蛋白質、1,106 個保留、合計 5,106 個）；dG 使用 [128, 1024, 128, 1024] 的 MLP，架構來自 Hyperband 神經架構搜尋；ddG 使用 [256, 256, 256]、dropout 0.324 的 MLP，以 Tsuboyama 2023 的大規模資料集訓練（449 個親代蛋白質、共 494,370 列）。ddG 預測頭同時吃突變體的嵌入向量與「突變體減野生型」的差值嵌入向量，這會去掉與序列無關的特徵、強化同一蛋白質內部的排序能力，代價是跨蛋白質的絕對值比較變差，這點他們自己也承認。內部驗證採跨 266 個親代蛋白質的分組交叉驗證：前五名中真正具穩定化效果的精確率為 73.6%，基線為 19.8%；他們也如實回報各蛋白質的精確率從 0% 到 100% 不等，約有 20% 的蛋白質低於 50%。S669 的外部基準測試（669 個變異、94 個蛋白質、事前未做任何調校）中，PyroForge 在 pooled 排序上是 22 種方法中的第 18 名，但在蛋白質內部排序上是 22 種中的第 2 名，且在純序列方法中排名第 1，Spearman 相關比 zero-shot ESM-2 高出 +0.248（95% 信賴區間 +0.051 至 +0.502）；團隊並說明這樣的落差正是他們的設計選擇所預期的結果。限制是公開寫出來而不是藏起來：Ssym 上只呈現未達統計顯著的趨勢；序列超過 400 個殘基後排序品質明顯下降；Tm 的 Pearson r 為 0.810，但他們自己說這高估了實際表現，因為分布在嗜熱菌與嗜溫菌之間呈雙峰，組內的排序能力較弱。可信範圍以表格列出（掃描與摺疊預測到 400 個胺基酸、dG 與 ddG 的可信範圍為 10-72 個胺基酸、Tm 的訓練視窗為 20-400 個胺基酸），超出範圍的輸入會回傳低可信度標記，而不是無聲失敗。四次工程迭代都附上數字：隨機切分資料列會洩漏蛋白質身分、使相關係數虛高到 0.85，改為依親代蛋白質分組切分後修正為較真實的 0.46；只用正向突變訓練會讓反向預測不一致（r = 0.27），補上取負號的反向突變後提升到 0.95；Tm 的訓練資料從 237 個蛋白質擴大到 Meltome Atlas 後，保留集誤差降到 5.9 °C；另外有一個正負號反轉的錯誤，讓最佳化器把最不穩定化的突變排在最前面，修正後並以端對端回歸測試鎖住。單元測試直接把熱力學不變量寫進去：ddG(wt to wt) = 0、ddG(A to B) = -ddG(B to A)、批次掃描結果必須與單一配對預測一致、親代蛋白質完全保留且各切分之間沒有重疊、設下正負號底線讓 top-k 永遠不會回傳預測為不穩定化的變異，以及同義密碼子家族內的 CAI 正規化。","software":"PyroForge is live and needs no installation: https://pyroforge.26650078.xyz/, hosted on the team's own GPU server, with a QR code on the wiki and a three-step try-it path (New, paste the sample protein G B1 domain sequence, Run Prediction, Run Optimization). That makes it one of the few 2026 iGEM software tools a stranger can actually use in a browser. The problem it addresses is concrete: most established thermostability predictors need a solved 3D structure, which blocks work on newly designed or novel sequences with no PDB counterpart, so PyroForge is deliberately sequence-only and uses no structural data during prediction. The workflow is Input, Predict, Optimize, Fold, Order. Browser-only execution was explicitly ruled out with reasons given (ESM-2 650M needs about 2.5 GB of weights, a site-saturation scan is O(L x 20) sequential forward passes, and a 60-residue scan takes about a minute on a GPU using around 5.6 GB VRAM), which is why the architecture committed to a server backend with a job queue. Scope exclusions are equally explicit: no user accounts and no server-side storage, so analyses stay in the browser, and no live pricing, with synthesis quotes delegated to vendors. Four hard constraints shaped the design and are documented: ESM-2 and PyTorch are not fork-safe so the worker is single-slot and length caps, task timeouts and per-IP rate limits are enforced; Apple MPS produces near-constant ESM-2 embeddings that collapse predictions to the training mean, so serving hardware must match training hardware (and the team therefore refuses to publish its MPS-collected latency numbers as product figures); the deployment is unauthenticated on an open school GPU server so all security sits at the reverse proxy; and the folding service and iGEM Registry snapshot are separate services that report their status to the UI. Operational problems were solved rather than papered over: the public iGEM FASTA endpoint returned 403s, so the pipeline digests MySQL dumps directly and yields 22,294 clean protein parts; the archived ESM Atlas API returned 504s, so ESMFold was moved to a self-hosted instance on a second GPU with ESM Atlas kept only as an outage fallback. Reproducibility is unusually complete for iGEM: source under Apache 2.0 at https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/hk-joint-school/pyroforge, a full software document (user guide, API reference, deployment, provenance, known limits) and an engineering document as PDFs, and datasets and trained weights archived on Zenodo with DOIs (10.5281/zenodo.23455762 for the embedding archive and Meltome Tm file, 10.5281/zenodo.23456193 for the three model weights plus their evaluation reports), with ESM-2 and ESMFold weights deliberately not redistributed but loaded from their original releases at runtime, and a DATA.md documenting column definitions and what was actually verified. The tool was also used for its own project: PyroForge proposed mutations on an AI-designed fire-retardant peptide, and in a burnt-net assay the optimised Alp2 coating burned 8.5 cm (SD 0.4) against Alp1's 10.5 cm (SD 0.5), with more char formation. The team then adds the caveat themselves, noting that a different coating in the same project, CsgA-BslA-PEbp, burned less still at 7.1 cm, so the assay does not claim PyroForge beat every other design. Honest security posture: access control and TLS are listed as future work before exposure beyond the internal trusted network.","software_zh":"PyroForge 已經上線而且不需安裝：https://pyroforge.26650078.xyz/，架在團隊自己的 GPU 伺服器上，wiki 上附 QR code，並提供三步驟的試用路徑（New、貼上範例的 protein G B1 domain 序列、Run Prediction、Run Optimization）。這讓它成為 2026 年 iGEM 少數幾個陌生人真的可以在瀏覽器裡直接使用的軟體工具。它要解決的問題很具體：多數既有的熱穩定性預測工具都需要已解出的 3D 結構，這讓沒有 PDB 對應結構的新設計或新穎序列無法處理，因此 PyroForge 刻意只用序列，預測過程完全不使用結構資料。工作流程為 Input、Predict、Optimize、Fold、Order。純瀏覽器端執行被明確排除，並附上理由（ESM-2 650M 的權重約需 2.5 GB、飽和突變掃描是 O(L x 20) 次連續前向運算、60 個殘基的掃描在 GPU 上約需一分鐘並佔用約 5.6 GB VRAM），這也是架構最後選擇伺服器後端搭配工作佇列的原因。不做什麼也同樣寫得清楚：沒有使用者帳號、伺服器端不儲存任何資料，所以分析結果留在瀏覽器裡；也不提供即時報價，合成報價交給廠商處理。有四項硬性限制形塑了整個設計，而且都寫進文件：ESM-2 與 PyTorch 並非 fork-safe，所以工作者只有單一名額，並強制長度上限、任務逾時與單一 IP 的流量限制；Apple MPS 產生的 ESM-2 嵌入向量近乎常數，會讓預測塌陷到訓練集平均值，因此服務用的硬體必須與訓練用的硬體一致（團隊也因此拒絕把在 MPS 上量到的延遲數字當作產品規格公布）；部署在學校開放的 GPU 伺服器上且不做身分驗證，所有安全性都落在反向代理；摺疊預測服務與 iGEM Registry 快照是獨立的服務，各自把狀態回報到介面上。營運上的問題是真的被解決，而不是含糊帶過：iGEM 公開的 FASTA 端點回傳 403，於是流程改為直接消化 MySQL dump，整理出 22,294 個乾淨的蛋白質零件；已封存的 ESM Atlas API 回傳 504，於是把 ESMFold 改成架在第二張 GPU 上的自架服務，ESM Atlas 只留作停機時的備援。可重現性在 iGEM 中算是罕見地完整：原始碼以 Apache 2.0 授權放在 https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/hk-joint-school/pyroforge，另有完整的軟體文件（使用手冊、API 參考、部署說明、資料來源、已知限制）與工程文件的 PDF，資料集與訓練好的權重以 DOI 典藏在 Zenodo（10.5281/zenodo.23455762 為嵌入向量封存檔與 Meltome Tm 檔案，10.5281/zenodo.23456193 為三個模型權重及其評估報告）；ESM-2 與 ESMFold 的權重刻意不再散布，而是在執行時從其原始發布處載入，並以一份 DATA.md 記錄欄位定義與實際驗證過的內容。這個工具也真的用在自己的專案上：PyroForge 針對一條以 AI 設計的阻燃胜肽提出突變建議，在燒網測試中，最佳化後的 Alp2 塗層燒毀長度為 8.5 cm（標準差 0.4），Alp1 則為 10.5 cm（標準差 0.5），且碳化層更多。團隊接著自己補上但書：同一個專案中另一種塗層 CsgA-BslA-PEbp 燒毀長度更短，只有 7.1 cm，所以這項測試並未宣稱 PyroForge 勝過其他每一種設計。資安態度也很誠實：存取控制與 TLS 被列為未來工作，要在對內部可信網路以外開放之前補上。","stack":["React","TypeScript","Vite","Mantine","FastAPI","Pydantic","Celery","Redis","Nginx","Docker Compose","systemd","PyTorch","ESM-2 650M","ESMFold (self-hosted + ESM Atlas fallback)","scikit-learn (PCA, Ridge, gradient boosting)","Zenodo (DOI archiving)","iGEM Registry MySQL dump ingestion","Apache 2.0","iGEM GitLab"],"techniques":["protein language model embeddings as frozen features","difference-embedding (mutant minus wildtype) for within-protein mutation ranking","site-saturation mutational scanning","Hyperband neural architecture search","grouped (parent-protein-disjoint) cross-validation","antisymmetry augmentation with negated reverse mutations","S669 and Ssym external benchmarking","Spearman within-protein versus pooled ranking analysis","confidence intervals and out-of-distribution reliability flagging","Codon Adaptation Index optimisation","ESMFold structure prediction with per-residue stability heatmapping","homology search against an iGEM Registry protein snapshot","invariant-based unit testing of thermodynamic properties","user acceptance testing with a structured survey"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education was built on a declared framework of one vision, four core philosophies and a set of user-specific strategies, with every initiative formatted for a particular age group and interest rather than reused, and each event documented with execution details, feedback analysis method and measured impact so other teams can reproduce it. The range extends unusually far down the age scale, including a Synthetic Biology Carnival at St. Dominic Anglo-Chinese Kindergarten built around sensory stimulation and mutual prosocial learning. The team's stated method is companionship and mutual engagement rather than monologue, and they publish a timeline and quantified impact per domain. The software itself was also engaged with the public: user acceptance testing surveyed 226 people through the complete analysis workflow.","publicEngagement_zh":"教育工作建立在一個明確宣告的框架上：一個願景、四項核心理念，以及一組針對不同使用者的策略；每一項活動都為特定年齡層與興趣量身設計，而不是重複套用，並且每場活動都記錄執行細節、回饋分析方法與量測到的影響，讓其他團隊可以複製。年齡範圍往下延伸得異常遠，包括在 St. Dominic Anglo-Chinese Kindergarten 舉辦、以感官刺激與彼此間利社會學習為設計主軸的合成生物學嘉年華。團隊自述的方法是陪伴與相互參與，而不是單向演講，並公布時間軸與各領域的量化影響。軟體本身也做了公眾參與：使用者接受度測試讓 226 人實際走完完整的分析流程。","ihp":"Stakeholders were grouped into three categories with distinct purposes: Target Users (public and industry, for safety, deployment, cost, liability and market acceptance), Science (subject experts, to validate the scientific basis), and ESG (regulators, testing bodies and environmental stakeholders, for sustainability and certification). The pivot is clearly recorded: the team started focused on improving fire retardancy and interviewed fire safety experts to build a verification plan, then consulted management at a major Hong Kong real estate developer (SHKP) who told them the critical problem with halogenated retardants is the toxic gases they release, including hydrogen chloride, hydrogen bromide and carcinogenic dioxins. The research focus shifted to making the coating non-toxic and low-smoke. An environmental analysis expert then reviewed the redesigned coating and shaped which metrics the verification plan should measure. For the software, the external benchmark exists because of one specific conversation: Prof. Joshua Ho of the School of Biomedical Sciences at the University of Hong Kong told them to run a head-to-head comparison with methods already in use, and the team ran S669 against 21 other methods and published the result including the places it ranks poorly. The 226-person UAT produced three documented fixes: ESMFold timeouts (resolved by moving folding to their own GPU), an optimization view that did not make sequence position and substitution coordinates readable (redesigned to highlight mutated positions and list the top five with residue numbers), and protein-only input (expanded to accept DNA).","ihp_zh":"利害關係人被分成三類，各有不同目的：Target Users（公眾與產業界，針對安全性、部署方式、成本、責任歸屬與市場接受度）、Science（領域專家，用以驗證科學基礎），以及 ESG（主管機關、檢測單位與環境相關的利害關係人，針對永續性與認證）。轉向的過程記錄得很清楚：團隊一開始專注於提升阻燃效果，並訪談消防安全專家以建立驗證計畫，之後向香港一家大型地產開發商（SHKP）的管理階層請益，對方指出含鹵素阻燃劑真正嚴重的問題在於它們釋放的有毒氣體，包括氯化氫、溴化氫與致癌的戴奧辛。研究重心因此轉向讓塗層無毒且低煙。接著一位環境分析專家檢視重新設計後的塗層，並決定了驗證計畫應該量測哪些指標。至於軟體，外部基準測試之所以存在，是因為一次具體的對話：香港大學生物醫學學院的 Prof. Joshua Ho 要他們與實際在使用的方法做正面比較，於是團隊跑了 S669、對比 21 種其他方法，並把結果連同排名難看的部分一併公布。226 人的使用者接受度測試帶來三項有記錄的修正：ESMFold 逾時（改由自家 GPU 執行摺疊預測解決）、最佳化檢視畫面無法清楚呈現序列位置與取代座標（重新設計成標示突變位置，並列出前五名及其殘基編號），以及原本只接受蛋白質輸入（擴充為也接受 DNA）。","realWorld":"The problem framing is quantitative: 43% of all fire disasters occurred in the past decade according to a study in Science, and WHO projects extreme fire events increasing in frequency by up to 50% by the end of the century, with 2025 Los Angeles and San Diego fires causing 31 deaths, over 200,000 evacuations and more than 18,000 destroyed structures. The coating is positioned as a spray-on product for firefighters and communities whose non-negotiable requirement, set by stakeholders, is being low-smoke, non-toxic and biodegradable rather than merely effective. Arabidopsis assays were run to check ecotoxicity, BslA weatherproofing was tested across weathering for rain washout, and the team notes the platform extends to other industrial materials by swapping the binding domain. PyroForge's own industrial framing is thermostable enzymes that improve reaction efficiency and reduce cooling demand.","realWorld_zh":"問題的鋪陳是有數字的：根據 Science 的一項研究，所有火災災難中有 43% 發生在過去十年；WHO 預測到本世紀末，極端火災事件的發生頻率最多會增加 50%；2025 年洛杉磯與聖地牙哥的大火造成 31 人死亡、逾 200,000 人撤離、超過 18,000 棟建築物毀損。這款塗層被定位為提供給消防人員與社區的噴塗產品，而利害關係人設定的不可妥協條件是低煙、無毒且可生物分解，而不只是有效。團隊以 Arabidopsis 試驗檢查生態毒性，並在耐候測試中驗證 BslA 防雨水沖刷的能力，也指出只要替換結合結構域，這個平台就能延伸到其他工業材料。PyroForge 自身的產業定位則是耐熱酵素，用以提升反應效率並降低冷卻需求。","partners":["Sun Hung Kai Properties (SHKP)","Prof. Joshua Ho, School of Biomedical Sciences, University of Hong Kong","Ir. Prof. Yuen (fire safety)","Prof. Ruan","Prof. Chan","Dr. Wong","Prof. Guan","St. Dominic Anglo-Chinese Kindergarten"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6058/wiki/software/system-archi.avif","caption":"PyroForge system architecture: Nginx reverse proxy as the only public surface, with FastAPI, Redis and three purpose-separated Celery queues (fast, heavy, io) isolated on the internal Docker network.","caption_zh":"PyroForge 的系統架構：Nginx 反向代理是唯一對外開放的介面，FastAPI、Redis 與三條依用途區分的 Celery 佇列（fast、heavy、io）都隔離在內部 Docker 網路中。","credit":"Team HK-Joint-School, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6058/wiki/software/optimization.avif","caption":"The Optimization card: a site-saturation scan over every single-residue substitution, ranked by predicted ddG, returning a top-five shortlist with residue numbers.","caption_zh":"Optimization 卡片：對每一個單一殘基取代做飽和突變掃描，依預測的 ddG 排序，回傳含殘基編號的前五名候選清單。","credit":"Team HK-Joint-School, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6058/wiki/software/s669-pooled-vs-within.avif","caption":"The S669 benchmark against 21 other methods: 18th of 22 on pooled ranking but 2nd of 22 within-protein and 1st among sequence-only methods, exactly the trade-off the difference-embedding design predicts.","caption_zh":"與 21 種其他方法比較的 S669 基準測試：pooled 排序在 22 種中排第 18，但蛋白質內部排序排第 2、純序列方法中排第 1，正是差值嵌入設計所預期的取捨。","credit":"Team HK-Joint-School, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6058/wiki/software/visualization.avif","caption":"The Visualization card: an ESMFold 3D model rendered in the browser with residues coloured by per-residue stability scores taken from the mutation scan.","caption_zh":"Visualization 卡片：在瀏覽器中呈現的 ESMFold 3D 模型，殘基依突變掃描得到的各殘基穩定性分數上色。","credit":"Team HK-Joint-School, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Run the head-to-head external benchmark and publish the ranks you lose on: PyroForge's S669 result (18th of 22 pooled, 2nd of 22 within-protein, 1st among sequence-only) is more convincing than a flattering number because the team explains why their architecture produces exactly that split. The second transferable practice is their bug ledger, where a random train/test split that inflated correlation from 0.46 to 0.85 and a sign-inversion that ranked the most destabilising mutations first are both published with the invariant unit tests now preventing them.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"去做正面對決的外部基準測試，並把自己輸掉的名次也公布出來：PyroForge 的 S669 結果（pooled 排序 22 名中的第 18、蛋白質內部排序 22 名中的第 2、純序列方法中的第 1）之所以比一個好看的數字更有說服力，是因為團隊解釋了為什麼他們的架構必然產生這樣的落差。第二項可以借鏡的做法是他們的錯誤紀錄簿：隨機切分訓練與測試集使相關係數從 0.46 虛高到 0.85，以及正負號反轉讓最不穩定化的突變被排在最前面，兩件事都公開寫出來，並附上如今用來防堵它們的不變量單元測試。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/hk-joint-school/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hk-joint-school/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/hk-joint-school/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/hk-joint-school/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/hk-joint-school/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/hk-joint-school/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/hk-joint-school/contribution","https://pyroforge.26650078.xyz/","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/hk-joint-school/pyroforge","https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23455762","https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23456193"],"rank":7},"6060":{"team":"DTU-Denmark","id":"6060","section":"Overgrad","country":"Denmark","village":"Bioremediation","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/dtu-denmark/","projectTitle":"Enzymatic degradation of wind turbine blade epoxy","tagline":"A chemo-enzymatic route to the resin fraction of decommissioned wind turbine blades, assessed honestly against the alternatives","summary":"DTU engineered laccases (ItL-03 from a spruce bark beetle gut metagenome, CueO variants and homologues) and unspecific peroxygenases (PaDa-I, WamPa, PabUPO-II, MroUPO, Fett) to attack the amine crosslinks of cured epoxy from wind turbine blades, layered on top of a published acid-plus-peroxide solvolysis pretreatment. They used NNBT, a small water-soluble molecule carrying the tertiary amine of the crosslink, as a defined model substrate, and showed by MALDI-TOF that PaDa-I performs N-dealkylation on it with Purpald confirmation of lactaldehyde release. The decisive work is a prospective comparative life-cycle assessment in SimaPro (ReCiPe 2016 Midpoint H) of five end-of-life routes, which found their own enzymatic route is NOT the best option on almost any indicator - and they published that. Seven interviews across DTU Wind, DTU Sustain, DTU Chemistry, SDU and industry, plus documented non-responses from Siemens Gamesa, Orsted and MAKEEN Energy, drove changes to the chemical target, the model substrate, the host organism, the enzyme-ranking criterion and the project's stated goal.","awards":["Best New Basic Part — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Presentation — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Sustainable Development Impact — Winner (Overgrad)","Best Bioremediation Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Three parallel enzyme-discovery pipelines agreed after advice from the 2025 team's dry-lab head: an 'easy' track of literature enzymes known to oxidise the relevant bonds, a 'medium' track of homologue mining, and a 'hard' track of rational engineering and generative design. Plus a prospective comparative LCA (SimaPro, ReCiPe 2016 Midpoint H, functional unit of blade mass with cutting/transport/metal separation excluded as identical across routes) and a Kremser-equation model of the countercurrent solvent extraction stage.","dataviz":"An interactive clickable process-flow diagram that zooms from the five-route overview into the enzymatic routes with every parameter on the box (acid molarity, temperature, residence time, enzyme loading in mg/L, number of reuses, recovery fractions); one SDG per plot with burdens above zero and credits below; an interactive stakeholder map where each pin opens the interview, colour-coded by engagement status so non-responses stay visible.","datascience":"Sequence mining of UniProt, Pfam and BLAST rather than metagenomic libraries; multiple sequence alignment to transfer organic-solvent-tolerance mutations from PaDa-I onto GroGu and PabUPO-II; a novel substrate-access-channel discovery pipeline used in place of docking affinity ranking; molecular dynamics; generative enzyme design on the DTU HPC. Every LCA parameter is published with its source, the mismatch between source and use, and a 'weakest link' label (e.g. partition coefficients taken from a 1980 phenol-extraction paper using MIBK rather than ethyl acetate, flagged explicitly).","software":"LCA input data, assumptions and mapping code released open source so other teams can rebuild the model in SimaPro or another tool; lectures, workshops and guides collected on the contribution page.","stack":["SimaPro","Ecoinvent","ReCiPe 2016 Midpoint (H)","Boltz-2","molecular dynamics","BAGEL","Raygun","BLAST / UniProt / Pfam","DTU HPC","Opentrons liquid handler"],"techniques":["molecular docking (deliberately demoted)","substrate channel geometry analysis","multiple sequence alignment mutation transfer","generative protein design","Gibson assembly (laccases)","Golden Gate (UPOs)","96-well colorimetric screening (ABTS, NNBT, NBD, Purpald)","CO-difference spectroscopy for correctly folded heme","MALDI-TOF product identification","prospective LCA with contribution analysis"],"frameworks_zh":"在徵詢 2025 年隊伍乾實驗室負責人的建議後，確立三條並行的酵素探索管線：「容易」路線為文獻中已知能氧化相關鍵結的酵素，「中等」路線為同源蛋白探勘，「困難」路線為理性工程與生成式設計。此外還有一項前瞻式比較 LCA（SimaPro、ReCiPe 2016 Midpoint H，功能單位為葉片質量，切割／運輸／金屬分離因在各路線間相同而排除），以及一個以 Kremser 方程式建立的逆流溶劑萃取段模型。","dataviz_zh":"一張可互動點擊的製程流程圖，可由五路線總覽放大到各酵素路線，每個方塊上都標出參數（酸的莫耳濃度、溫度、滯留時間、以 mg/L 表示的酵素投加量、再利用次數、回收率）；每一項 SDG 各自一張圖，負擔畫在零線以上、效益畫在零線以下；還有一張可互動的利害關係人地圖，點選圖釘即展開該場訪談，並以顏色標示互動狀態，讓無回應者仍然看得見。","datascience_zh":"以 UniProt、Pfam 與 BLAST 做序列探勘，而非總體基因組資料庫；以多序列比對把 PaDa-I 的有機溶劑耐受突變轉移到 GroGu 與 PabUPO-II 上；以一套新的底物進入通道探索流程取代以嵌合親和力排序；分子動力學模擬；在 DTU HPC 上執行生成式酵素設計。每一個 LCA 參數都連同來源、來源與實際用途之間的落差，以及一個「最弱環節」標籤一併公開（例如分配係數取自 1980 年一篇使用 MIBK 而非乙酸乙酯的酚萃取論文，明確標示出來）。","software_zh":"LCA 的輸入資料、假設與對映程式碼皆以開源釋出，讓其他隊伍能在 SimaPro 或其他工具中重建模型；講座、工作坊與指南則整理在貢獻頁面上。"},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education was pointed at the specific blind spot the project exposed rather than at synthetic biology in general: visits to international high schools taught the wind sector's end-of-life emissions and the idea of thinking in full sustainability circles early, and a Lifelong Learning workshop took the same low-impact recycling discussion to an audience of working professionals. For the iGEM community they ran a BioBrick workshop, an intellectual-property introduction ('Protecting Your Ideas'), a World Cafe team-to-team roundtable and a podcast, and presented at the Nordic iGEM Conference. State of Green gave them a platform to put the blade-waste problem to people from ministries, academia and the energy sector.","ihp":"DTU's IHP is built as a decision trail, not a visitor log: every interview card carries an explicit 'Implementation' list, and there is a separate section on approaches they chose NOT to pursue. The single biggest change came from Dr Javier (Postdoc, DTU Sustain, one of the few in his group working on resin chemistry rather than glass-fibre recovery) across two interviews on 3 March and 24 June 2026. He posed what the team calls the sharpest experimental question raised in the project - can an enzyme replace the cleaving solvent, acting on a swollen but still crosslinked network? - and told them to start from a well-documented literature pretreatment rather than invent one and layer enzymes on top. The result was a hard reframing: the enzymatic step stopped being a standalone degradation claim and became a complement to solvolysis, with a new explicit objective of testing whether enzymes could substitute for part of the solvent-cleavage step, and a second research line on engineering solvent tolerance into the enzymes. Justine Beauson (Senior Researcher, Composites Manufacturing and Testing, DTU Wind) was the first contact; she confirmed thermoset epoxy is what is coming down now, referred the team to a turbine OEM, and in a 6 October email follow-up explained that the Blade Material Passport is compiled independently of any thinking about disposal and will tell you a blade is epoxy but never the formulation - which is why the team abandoned any attempt to match real blade resin and why 'collaboration between the production and the waste-management industries' became the organising claim on the sustainability page. Jesper Kjaer Jorgensen (Postdoc, Composites, DTU) then supplied fully cured SWANCOR 2519-1A/BS, a commercial non-NDA amine-cured bisphenol-A epoxy, and agreed with the team's hypothesis that the tertiary amine crosslink is the vulnerable point: the team writes plainly that 'without those cubes we would have had either no workable material or a different one', and the target shifted from the epoxy backbone to the amine crosslinks, changing which bonds they went after, how they measured degradation and which products they hoped to recover. Robert (PhD, Eukaryotic Molecular Cell Biology) delivered the hardest reality check - thermoset degradation is heavily researched, the field contains many low-quality papers with missing controls and uncharacterised substrates, and a six-month student project cannot run a metagenomic discovery campaign - and the team's response is laid out item by item: they screened roughly 33 enzymes rather than thousands, worked from public databases rather than metagenomic libraries, used a colorimetric assay rather than a fluorescent reporter, added MALDI-TOF, and had a postdoc rather than students perform the hazardous epoxy pretreatment. Carlos G. Acevedo-Rocha (Senior Researcher, Computational Protein Engineering, BRIGHT) told them not to base findings on docking affinity values because there is no significant correlation with experimental activity, and endorsed their early-stage channel-discovery pipeline: they abandoned the plan to filter homologue candidates on Boltz-2 affinity scores and rebuilt candidate selection around channel geometry plus molecular dynamics. Cecilia Castellvi Domingo (PhD, heterologous expression of UPOs) changed the chassis and the protocol - Komagataella phaffii on an episomal AP17 backbone rather than S. cerevisiae or E. coli, harvest at day 5 instead of day 6 to reduce proteolysis, lower induction temperature, and the CO-difference spectrum assay that gave them a direct measurement of correctly folded heme-containing enzyme (0.019 uM in a six-fold concentrated sample) that activity assays could not. Lykke Margot Ricard (Associate Professor in Sustainable Innovation, SDU, who had mapped Danish blade treatment options for the Danish EPA) asked who the retaker is, and in response every workstream was required to name a recoverable product, the quality it would need and a potential buyer - which is also why the team says the ideal process recovers a product rather than incinerating residues. The European Environment Agency answered that it holds no data on retired blade management, that the WEEE Directive does not cover wind turbines and that no dedicated EU legislation exists, so there is no reporting obligation; the team then marked the landfill share as an unverifiable input in the LCA rather than quoting a number. Most unusually, they publish their failures of access: Siemens Gamesa never replied to email and had no relevant expert at the DSE careers fair, nobody at Orsted could speak to blade end-of-life, MAKEEN Energy did not reply, and the team states outright that the groups with the greatest influence over adoption 'were therefore among the least represented in our discussions, limiting our analysis' - and makes those gaps visible on the stakeholder map, which rates each group by influence over adoption and interest separately, including 'unknown' for potential buyers of recovered compounds because no market has been shown to exist.","realWorld":"The need is a quantified bottleneck rather than a slogan: Danish blade waste currently goes to mixed-waste landfill or is shipped abroad by lorry and ferry, the Danish wind industry's voluntary landfill ban took effect on 1 January 2026, a Danish EPA screening detected bisphenol A in every tank leaching test on blade material, and the EEA confirmed there is no EU legislation or reporting obligation for wind-turbine waste at all pending the WEEE revision in the Circular Economy Act. SDGs are justified target by target with numbers from their own LCA, and the headline finding is one most teams would hide: in the base industrial scale-up scenario (projected to about 2035) the enzymatic route emits 2.1 kg CO2 eq per kg of blade against 1.4 for solvolysis and 0.9 for pyrolysis, adds 0.38 person-equivalents of human carcinogenic toxicity against 0.022 for solvolysis, uses about 36% more water, and cement co-processing is best on almost every indicator - so they state that enzymatic and solvolysis are the only routes with clear net burdens, trace the hotspot to the H2O2 supply chain and UPO production, and convert that into a research direction (make UPO production more efficient, recover a product instead of incinerating residues, reuse immobilised enzyme and compute the break-even number of reuses). SDG targets are matched one-to-one with their own data on SDG 3 (illness from hazardous chemicals), 6 (water-use efficiency), 7 (renewable share and clean-energy research cooperation), 8 (the Energy Transition Alliance estimate that a UK blade-recycling segment could add 20,000 jobs to offshore wind's 60,000-by-2030 target), 9, 12, 13, 14, 15 and 17. Limitations are declared inside the SDG analysis rather than buried: unknown reaction product, no demonstration of enzyme performance on real blade material, one blade type only, transport excluded by the system boundary, microplastic and BPA leaching not characterised by ReCiPe, and no penalty in the cut-off model for losing glass fibre as a resource. What happens next: the LCA inputs, assumptions and mapping code are open source, the OEM's requirements (handle multi-material blades at reasonable cost and pace) are recorded as requirements for future development rather than achievements, and relationships with State of Green, the Center for Biosolutions and DTU are described as collaborations that can continue beyond iGEM.","partners":["DTU Wind and Energy Systems","DTU Sustain","DTU Chemistry","DTU Biotechnology and Biomedicine","DTU Biosustain","University of Southern Denmark (SDU Innovation and Design Engineering)","Biotechnology Research Institute for the Green Transition (BRIGHT)","European Environment Agency","State of Green","Center for Biosolutions","an anonymous wind turbine OEM","Tailwind Bio","Danish Working Environment Authority (Arbejdstilsynet) epoxy certification"],"publicEngagement_zh":"教育瞄準的是這個專案所揭露的特定盲點，而不是泛泛的合成生物學：團隊走訪國際高中，講授風電產業的生命終期排放，以及及早以完整永續循環來思考的觀念；一場 Lifelong Learning 工作坊則把同樣關於低衝擊回收的討論帶給在職專業人士。對 iGEM 社群，他們辦了 BioBrick 工作坊、一場智慧財產權入門課（Protecting Your Ideas）、一場 World Cafe 形式的隊際圓桌，以及一集 podcast，並在 Nordic iGEM Conference 上報告。State of Green 則提供了舞台，讓他們把葉片廢棄物問題帶到部會、學界與能源業人士面前。","ihp_zh":"DTU 的 IHP 是一條決策軌跡，而不是一本訪客簽到簿：每一張訪談卡都附有明確的「落實」清單，另有一個專節說明他們「選擇不走」的方向。最大的一次轉向來自 Dr Javier（DTU Sustain 博士後，該組少數研究樹脂化學而非玻璃纖維回收的人）在 2026 年 3 月 3 日與 6 月 24 日的兩場訪談。他提出了團隊認為整個專案中最犀利的實驗問題——酵素能否取代裂解溶劑，直接作用在已膨潤但仍交聯的網狀結構上？——並建議他們從文獻中記載完整的前處理出發，而不是自己發明一套，再在上面疊加酵素。結果是一次徹底的重新定位：酵素步驟不再是獨立的降解主張，而成為溶劑分解的補充，並新增一個明確目標——測試酵素能否取代部分溶劑裂解步驟，同時開出第二條研究線，為酵素工程化出溶劑耐受性。Justine Beauson（DTU Wind 複合材料製造與測試資深研究員）是第一位聯繫對象；她確認現在退役下來的正是熱固性環氧樹脂，把團隊轉介給一家風機原廠（OEM），並在 10 月 6 日的電子郵件追問中說明，Blade Material Passport 的編製完全沒有考慮處置問題，只會告訴你葉片是環氧樹脂，卻絕不會給你配方——這正是團隊放棄去比對真實葉片樹脂的原因，也是「生產業與廢棄物管理業之間的協作」成為永續頁面核心主張的原因。接著 Jesper Kjaer Jorgensen（DTU 複合材料博士後）提供了完全固化的 SWANCOR 2519-1A/BS，一款無保密協議限制的商用胺固化雙酚 A 環氧樹脂，並同意團隊的假說：三級胺交聯是脆弱點。團隊直言「沒有那些方塊，我們手上要麼沒有可用的材料，要麼是另一種材料」，標的也因此從環氧樹脂主鏈轉到胺類交聯，改變了他們要攻擊哪些鍵結、如何量測降解，以及期望回收哪些產物。Robert（真核分子細胞生物學博士生）給出最嚴厲的現實檢驗——熱固性材料降解已被大量研究、該領域有許多缺少對照、底物未經鑑定的低品質論文，而一個六個月的學生專案不可能跑完整的總體基因組探索——團隊的回應逐條列出：他們篩選約 33 個酵素而非數千個、以公開資料庫而非總體基因組資料庫為起點、採用比色分析而非螢光報告子、加入 MALDI-TOF，並讓博士後而非學生執行危害性的環氧樹脂前處理。Carlos G. Acevedo-Rocha（BRIGHT 計算蛋白質工程資深研究員）告訴他們不要把結論建立在嵌合親和力數值上，因為那與實驗活性並無顯著相關，同時認可他們早期階段的通道探索流程：於是他們放棄以 Boltz-2 親和力分數篩選同源候選的計畫，改以通道幾何加上分子動力學重建候選篩選。Cecilia Castellvi Domingo（研究 UPO 異源表現的博士生）改變了宿主與操作流程——改用帶 episomal AP17 骨架的 Komagataella phaffii，而非 S. cerevisiae 或 E. coli；第 5 天而非第 6 天收取以減少蛋白水解；降低誘導溫度；以及 CO 差異光譜分析，讓他們得到正確折疊、含血基質酵素的直接量測值（六倍濃縮樣品中為 0.019 uM），這是活性分析做不到的。Lykke Margot Ricard（SDU 永續創新副教授，曾為丹麥環保署盤點丹麥葉片處理選項）問了「接手的人是誰？」，於是每條工作線都被要求指名一項可回收的產物、它需要達到的品質，以及可能的買家——這也是團隊主張理想製程應回收產物而非焚燒殘渣的原因。歐洲環境署答覆說他們並未掌握退役葉片管理的資料、WEEE 指令並不涵蓋風力機、也沒有專門的歐盟法規，因此不存在通報義務；團隊於是在 LCA 中把掩埋比例標記為無法驗證的輸入，而不是引用一個數字。最不尋常的是，他們把自己接觸失敗的部分也公開了：Siemens Gamesa 從未回信，在 DSE 就業博覽會上也沒有相關專家；Orsted 沒有人能談葉片生命終期；MAKEEN Energy 未回覆。團隊直接寫出，對採用與否影響力最大的那些群體「因此也是我們討論中代表性最低的，限制了我們的分析」，並把這些缺口標示在利害關係人地圖上——該圖分別以對採用的影響力與興趣程度評比每個群體，連回收化合物的潛在買家也標為「未知」，因為尚未有證據顯示市場存在。","realWorld_zh":"需求是被量化的瓶頸，而不是一句口號：丹麥的葉片廢棄物目前進入混合廢棄物掩埋場，或以卡車與渡輪運往國外；丹麥風電業自願性的掩埋禁令自 2026 年 1 月 1 日起生效；丹麥環保署的篩查在葉片材料的每一次槽式浸出試驗中都檢出雙酚 A；而歐洲環境署確認，在《循環經濟法》修訂 WEEE 之前，歐盟對風力機廢棄物根本沒有任何法規或通報義務。各項 SDG 都以團隊自己 LCA 的數字逐一標的論證，而最醒目的發現是多數隊伍會藏起來的：在工業規模放大的基準情境（推估至約 2035 年）下，酵素路線每公斤葉片排放 2.1 kg CO2 eq，相較溶劑分解為 1.4、熱裂解為 0.9；人體致癌毒性增加 0.38 人當量，相較溶劑分解為 0.022；用水量多約 36%；而水泥共處理在幾乎每一項指標上都最佳——於是他們明白寫出，酵素路線與溶劑分解是唯二有明顯淨負擔的路線，將熱點追溯到 H2O2 供應鏈與 UPO 生產，並把它轉化為研究方向（提高 UPO 生產效率、回收產物而非焚燒殘渣、重複使用固定化酵素並計算損益兩平的再利用次數）。SDG 標的與他們自己的資料一對一對應，涵蓋 SDG 3（危害性化學物質致病）、6（用水效率）、7（再生能源佔比與潔淨能源研究合作）、8（Energy Transition Alliance 估計英國葉片回收產業可為離岸風電 2030 年 6 萬個就業目標再增加 2 萬個工作機會）、9、12、13、14、15 與 17。限制條件寫在 SDG 分析之內，而非埋在角落：反應產物未知、未在真實葉片材料上展示酵素效能、只用一種葉片類型、運輸被系統邊界排除、微塑膠與 BPA 浸出未被 ReCiPe 納入特徵化，以及在截斷模型中沒有對玻璃纖維作為資源的損失給予懲罰。接下來的走向：LCA 的輸入、假設與對映程式碼皆為開源；OEM 的要求（能以合理成本與速度處理多材料葉片）被記錄為未來開發的需求而非已達成的成果；與 State of Green、Center for Biosolutions 及 DTU 的關係則被描述為可在 iGEM 之後延續的合作。"},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6060/wiki/human-practices/stakeholder-photos/javier.webp","caption":"Javier, postdoc at DTU Sustain working on resin chemistry, whose question about whether an enzyme could replace the cleaving solvent reframed the whole project as a complement to solvolysis","credit":"Team DTU-Denmark, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"Javier，DTU Sustain 從事樹脂化學研究的博士後，他關於酵素能否取代裂解溶劑的問題，讓整個專案重新定位為溶劑分解的補充"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6060/wiki/human-practices/stakeholder-photos/lykke.avif","caption":"Lykke Margot Ricard (SDU), who mapped Danish blade treatment options for the Danish EPA and made every workstream name a recoverable product and a buyer","credit":"Team DTU-Denmark, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"Lykke Margot Ricard（SDU），曾為丹麥環保署盤點丹麥葉片處理選項，要求每條工作線都指名一項可回收產物與一位買家"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6060/wiki/header-illustrations/engagement-human-practices.avif","caption":"Header illustration for the integrated human practices section, which is organised as an interactive stakeholder map rated by influence over adoption and interest","credit":"Team DTU-Denmark, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"整合式人類實踐章節的標頭插畫，該章節以一張依採用影響力與興趣程度評比的互動式利害關係人地圖編排"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6060/wiki/education/photos/sog-1.avif","caption":"At State of Green, where the team put the blade-waste problem to people from ministries, academia and the energy sector","credit":"Team DTU-Denmark, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"在 State of Green，團隊把葉片廢棄物問題帶到部會、學界與能源業人士面前"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Run a comparative LCA against the incumbent technologies early enough that it can still change the research plan, and publish it even when it says your own route loses - then convert each losing indicator into a named engineering target, and record the stakeholders who never replied so the gaps in your evidence base are visible rather than invisible.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/dtu-denmark/","https://2026.igem.wiki/dtu-denmark/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/dtu-denmark/sustainability","https://2026.igem.wiki/dtu-denmark/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/dtu-denmark/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/dtu-denmark/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/dtu-denmark/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/dtu-denmark/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/dtu-denmark/software"],"rank":47},"6064":{"team":"DKU","id":"6064","section":"Undergrad","country":"China","village":"Software & AI","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/dku/","projectTitle":"PeptiCraft","tagline":"An AI-assisted platform that turns a product brief into a traceable shortlist of recombinant fusion-protein candidates for skincare and medical aesthetics.","summary":"PeptiCraft addresses a specific physical problem: a free 10-30 residue bioactive peptide has essentially no structural stability, is degraded quickly by proteases, cannot be cast or gelled into a material, and diffuses away from where it is needed. The team's hypothesis is that such a peptide can be rescued by gene-fusing it to a structural scaffold, here a 364-residue recombinant Bombyx mori silk fibroin (FibLNT8-10xRep-FibHCT) chosen because its mechanical behaviour comes from sequence repeats rather than a folded globular core and therefore survives editing. The dry lab streamed 849,416,450 published protein sequences, kept the 19.9 million that are 3-30 standard residues, and ran them down an eight-round funnel to 496 assembled constructs across four functional directions, with a 99.9975% overall rejection rate. Three antioxidant candidates and a scaffold-only control were then expressed in E. coli and assayed: Top1 roughly doubled the scaffold's radical-scavenging capacity (TEAC 0.375 vs 0.195 mmol TE/g, p = 0.0075), no construct was cytotoxic to human keratinocytes, and no construct significantly protected cells against oxidative stress.","awards":["Best Software & AI Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A live, publicly accessible web application at https://pepticraft.pages.dev (Cloudflare Pages) serving 496 constructs over 19 endpoints, with a three-step workflow: define your needs (functions and product format), design the protein, review recommended expression strategies. The computational pipeline behind it is built as sixteen discrete predictive services, declared per stage and started on demand rather than run continuously, because keeping every service alive left a GPU context allocated per service until the card filled; in practice two to five live services at a time, which the team describes as removing contention rather than managing it. State lives in a columnar database rather than CSV hand-offs, with checkpoint and resume, progressive batch writes, and every result write as an upsert keyed on candidate identifier so batches can be re-run without duplicates and different rounds can write different columns of the same row. Batch size is explicitly chosen as the amount of work the team is willing to recompute, not as a performance parameter, on the stated assumption that a fourteen-hour pipeline will fail somewhere. Source: https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/dku/pepticraft-2, with a PeptiCraft-Project-Master-Reference.md in docs/.","dataviz":"The platform's defining display is the safety panel, which resolves to four verdicts rather than three: clear, exceeded, borderline and not assessed, so that an unmeasured gate can never be read as a passed one. Of the 496 constructs, 198 carry no immunogenicity measurement from either pathway and say so. Where a value exists it is shown against its applicable range, because the MHC class I predictor accepts only 5-15 residue peptides and returns zero outside that window, so a stored zero is not evidence of low immunogenicity. Alongside the constructs the platform serves a hand-compiled reference layer: 8 scaffold protein clusters with 16 patent sequence variants carrying real amino-acid sequences and graded E1-E5 by evidence level, and 15 curated linker entries with literature provenance. Five application routes (injectable filler, wound dressing, mask patch, topical film, hair care) are ordered by barrier integrity and each binds its own immunogenicity threshold (0.35, 0.35, 0.50, 0.50, 0.60). Every number on a candidate is traceable to its source. The wiki itself publishes the funnel as a diagram with per-source pass rates and reports the round-by-round wall-clock times.","datascience":"The pipeline is governed by five explicitly stated principles that are the project's methodological contribution. (1) Hierarchical filtering, never cross-attribute averaging: each round either sorts and takes a percentile or applies a threshold and eliminates, on the grounds that a blend is only meaningful when components share a unit and a direction, which antioxidant activity and haemolysis risk do not. (2) Safety is a hard threshold: toxicity (ToxinPred3 at 0.38), haemolysis (HemoPI2 at 0.55) and MHC class I immunogenicity (MHCflurry at 0.50, tightened to 0.35 for wound dressing and injectable routes) are pass-or-eliminate, never scored, weighted or compensable, while MHC class II (NetMHCIIpan) is a soft signal and allergenicity (AlgPred2) and B-cell epitope (BepiPred-3.0) are reported only. (3) The functional activity score is used exactly once, in round 1, so the two channels stay independent. (4) The pipeline has exactly one weighted average and its weights come from the data, computed as each component's winsorised standard deviation (truncated at the 5th and 95th percentiles so one outlier cannot dominate) normalised to sum to one, with any manual coefficient invalid without a recorded justification, which is a rule against tuning weights after seeing which constructs won. (5) Order by cost: moving the toxicity predictor out of round 1 onto a 50,000-sequence subset took it from an estimated 22 hours to about 48 minutes with no effect on the result. The design feature that makes the whole thing falsifiable is a dual channel: a Bottom channel of candidates predicted to be poor is carried through the entire identical pipeline as a matched negative control (100 of the 250 constructs in the v1.4 run, 206 of the 496 on the platform), so if both channels behave the same at the bench the pipeline's central assumption is refuted. Round 8 re-predicted the top ten of each channel with a second, independent structure model: mean confidence 0.52 against 0.42 for the primary, same trend and same ordering at the top. The final structural score is published as a formula: 0.40 x SASA + 0.40 x (1 - Aggrescan3D) + 0.20 x normalised pLDDT, with confidence at half weight because a predicted structure is evidence about a construct, not the construct itself. Verification: 115 backend tests (113 pass, 2 skipped), 91 static-data-layer assertions, and 58 end-to-end walkthrough assertions, where the static walkthrough serves the export directory over HTTP, reads it with the frontend's own data layer, compares an interface-assembled sequence against the service's sample residue by residue, and fails if any read reaches the network. Data scale: a 367,717,240-row per-tool score table at roughly 130 GB, plus a second immunogenicity pathway of about 147.5M rows across 131 alleles.","software":"PeptiCraft is one of the very few 2026 iGEM software tools that is both live and candid about its own limits. Four things make it worth copying. First, the pipeline's own history is published as four versions with their failure modes, and the team says plainly that the version that succeeded was not a better implementation but a different arrangement of where each kind of judgement is allowed to happen. Version 1.1's hard filters removed 94% of an already-curated antioxidant peptide set on safety grounds alone. Version 1.2 ran end to end on 1,081,772 sequences in six and a half hours and its output exposed two composition errors found by inspecting the arithmetic of stored results rather than by any crash: safety attributes could be outvoted because small safety coefficients sat inside a weighted total alongside a strong activity term, and the antioxidant signal leaked past the channel split because the later ranking composite still carried an antioxidant term at the largest coefficient, which weakened the very comparison the dual channel existed to enable. A third error was found the same way: a construct-level composite assigned half the final weight turned out to have a spread of only 0.011 between its 25th and 75th percentiles across the top ninety, so at half weight it was ordering on noise, and it was removed. All three were fixed by changing the pipeline's structure rather than by adjusting coefficients. Second, every elimination is recorded with its cause, with discarded candidates written out rather than dropped along with the tool and score that removed them, which makes the funnel auditable after the fact and lets a rejection rate be stated per round. Third, the team re-evaluated the 18 predictive tools against their own library and reclassified what each can actually support: three can eliminate a candidate, two can rank, one ranks weakly. Fourth, the composition of the output is reported as a consequence rather than a choice: a 30-residue ceiling removes almost all of a full-length reference proteome (0.33% pass rate) and almost none of a metagenomic small-protein catalogue (3.07%), so 96.3% of the surviving pool is metagenomic and only 3.7% carries functional annotation, which the team notes means experimental evidence for these sequences is scarce and the output is a set of predictions. One planned reduction step was tested and abandoned and said so: clustering at 90% identity achieved only 0.2-5% reduction because short peptides are too diverse for identity clustering. The wet-lab comparison is reported with unusual statistical restraint: the developability composite's ordering of the three tested candidates matched the measured TEAC ordering exactly while the antioxidant predictor's ordering was nearly its reverse, and the team immediately points out that three candidates cannot support a rank-correlation statistic, that a chance match has probability one in six, that the composite scores span only 0.024, that adjacent TEAC differences are not individually significant, and that the agreement is therefore compatible with measurement error alone. They then state it as a hypothesis for future work rather than a finding: exposure may predict activity better than sequence score, because a peptide buried in the scaffold cannot reach what it reacts with.","stack":["Cloudflare Pages (live deployment)","columnar database with checkpoint/resume","GPU-hosted predictive microservices","ToxinPred3","HemoPI2","MHCflurry","NetMHCIIpan","AlgPred2","BepiPred-3.0","AnOxPePred","SoDoPE","TemStaPro","OmegaFold / ESMFold","AlphaFold (cross-validation)","Aggrescan3D","SASA computation","iGEM GitLab"],"techniques":["hierarchical single-criterion filtering","hard safety vetoes with no compensation","winsorised-standard-deviation data-derived weighting","dual-channel (selected vs control) screening with matched negatives","cost-ordered pipeline scheduling","combinatorial linker and insertion-position enumeration","re-scoring solubility and thermal stability on the assembled fusion rather than the free peptide","relative solvent-accessible surface area of the functional region","aggregation-propensity indexing","pLDDT normalisation","independent second-model structure cross-validation","REML mixed-effects modelling with Dunnett comparisons","ABTS/TEAC radical-scavenging assay","upsert-keyed idempotent batch writes"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Science publicity followed one stated principle: start with a familiar question, explain the science, connect it back to PeptiCraft, and close with a question that invites reflection. Twelve distinct topics were covered across four entry points (skincare and peptides 4, protein engineering 4, AI-assisted biology 3, safety and responsibility 1), published through Instagram and Rednote, moving from 'what are peptides in skincare' and 'why can combining beneficial ingredients still create problems' through linkers, silk fibroin and skin-barrier delivery to whether AI can design biology. Two campus events pushed past explanation into argument: 'Beyond ChatGPT', co-run with the DKU AI Club, walked from transformers to AlphaFold, ESM/ESMFold and generative protein design with PeptiCraft as the case study, deliberately using it to explain why protein design is hard and why experimental validation remains necessary; and a bioethics debate with the DKU Debate Society on the motion that AI-designed cosmetic bioengineering should not get a free pass. A 'Campus Voices' video interviewed students as prospective users about whether they would use AI-designed skincare and what would make them trust or distrust it, and the team reports the split answer (interest in discovery alongside demands for stronger evidence) while explicitly stating these individual perspectives should not be treated as conclusions about wider public attitudes.","ihp":"Ten exchange activities produced six specific, named design changes, including the entire cell-based assay programme and the rule that an application's immunogenicity threshold is set by barrier integrity, which is why the five application routes each carry their own threshold. Scientific exchanges ran with XJTLU, Synbiopunk x CCiC, the VIT Gathering and the SJTU-Software AI x Synthetic Biology Roundtable; the industry exchange was a company visit to Changzhou Taimeirui Biotechnology, which brought production, cost and translation into focus. The team contributed to the JLU-NBBMS Dry Lab Summer Course and to a collaborative handbook, 'Together with iGEM: Across Villages, From Myths to Facts'. The most unusual feature is the human practices page itself, which answers four questions about PeptiCraft and refuses to overclaim on any of them: its current role is early-stage research support and commercial advantage remains unproven; early feedback exposed an unclear link between tool outputs and recommendations, which prompted clearer workflow displays, score explanations and missing-assessment labels, but independent user testing is still needed to establish whether people interpret recommendations correctly; the Top1 ABTS result does not establish ranking accuracy, cellular protection or lower research costs; and the page states outright that the effects of all this engagement on understanding and adoption remain unmeasured.","realWorld":"The market case is sourced: a US$450bn global beauty industry in 2025 projected to US$590bn by 2030 at about 5% annual growth (McKinsey State of Beauty), collagen raw materials at US$1.41bn growing 11.0% CAGR 2020-2023 with Chinese retail collagen products at RMB 58.42bn growing 41.9% CAGR, and peptides already appearing in 17% of 88 sensitive-skin facial cosmetics in a Portuguese pharmacy sample. The project restricts itself explicitly to topical and cosmetic-material use, functional skincare and dressing products where activity is delivered by a material that stays where it is applied, and states that nothing in the work concerns systemic delivery. Silk fibroin was chosen partly because it already has an established recombinant E. coli expression route in the literature, which the team says makes the wet lab tractable rather than speculative. The team's own list of what practical application would still require is specific: reproducible software, verified sequence-to-result links, suitable prediction models, user testing, and for product translation consistent production, storage and formulation studies, application-specific function and safety evidence, cost assessment, and a clear regulatory pathway.","partners":["Changzhou Taimeirui Biotechnology","SJTU-Software","XJTLU-Software","JLU-NBBMS","TJUSLS_China","NJTECH-CHINA-A","Tsinghua-A","PekingHSC","HKUST (GZ)","DUT-China","JLU-SPH","JLU-FBH","JLU-CP","DKU AI Club","DKU Debate Society","Duke Kunshan University Innovation and Entrepreneurship","SnapGene (sponsor)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6064/wiki/project-20261020/image8.avif","caption":"PeptiCraft's library page safety panel, which resolves to four verdicts (clear, exceeded, borderline, not assessed) so an unmeasured gate can never be read as a passed one.","credit":"Team DKU, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6064/wiki/project-20261020/image4.avif","caption":"The screening funnel: 849 million published sequences scanned down to 19.9 million short-peptide candidates, with per-source pass rates showing why 96.3% of the pool is metagenomic.","credit":"Team DKU, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6064/wiki/project-20261020/image5.avif","caption":"Combined Trolox Equivalent Antioxidant Capacity with Dunnett annotations across four independent experiments: Top1 at 0.375 against the scaffold control's 0.195 mmol TE/g.","credit":"Team DKU, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6064/wiki/project-20261020/image10.avif","caption":"Baseline-corrected protection ratios in HaCaT cells under oxidative stress, where no construct showed significant protection.","credit":"Team DKU, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Carry a deliberately unpromising control channel through the identical pipeline, so the screen's central assumption can be refuted at the bench rather than merely presented, and make safety a non-compensable veto that no activity score can outvote. Equally transferable is their reporting of a positive result: when the composite's ordering matched the measured ordering of three candidates, they computed that a chance match has probability one in six and labelled the agreement compatible with measurement error, then restated it as a hypothesis instead of a finding.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/dku/","https://2026.igem.wiki/dku/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/dku/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/dku/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/dku/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/dku/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/dku/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/dku/social-engagement","https://2026.igem.wiki/dku/education","https://pepticraft.pages.dev/","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/dku/pepticraft-2"],"rank":7},"6072":{"team":"GEMS-Taiwan","id":"6072","section":"High School","country":"Taiwan","village":"Space, Foundational Advance, Software & AI, Biomanufacturing","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/","projectTitle":"ReLEAF","projectTitle_zh":"ReLEAF","tagline":"A stress-responsive optogenetic bioreactor that predicts crop stress from field sensors and forecasts, then uses green light to make plant-protective proteins on the farm.","tagline_zh":"一套逆境響應式的光遺傳學生物反應器：先由田間感測器與氣象預報推估作物逆境，再以綠光在農場端生產保護植物的蛋白質。","summary":"ReLEAF closes a loop: field sensors and weather forecasts feed a stress-index model, the model sets a green-light dose, green light drives the cyanobacterial CcaSR two-component system in Bacillus subtilis WB800, and the cells secrete ACC deaminase into a hollow-fiber perfusion bioreactor that lets protein out and keeps cells in. The unit is about 40 x 24 x 62 cm, designed to stand beside a Taiwanese smallholder paddy where the average agricultural manager is 63.8 years old and precision agriculture is otherwise out of reach. It swept the high-school technical awards (Measurement, Hardware, Integrated Human Practices) largely on provenance discipline: four self-built devices with release build manuals, a digital twin that caught a failing photometer 26.7 hours before it died, a pre-registered growth forecast scored against a later run, and an input ledger that marks every number as measured, cited or modelled. Its distinguishing quality is honesty — the wiki repeatedly withdraws its own claims, and that is also where its dry-lab weaknesses are visible.","summary_zh":"ReLEAF 把整件事做成一個閉環：田間感測器與氣象預報餵給逆境指數模型，模型決定綠光劑量，綠光驅動 Bacillus subtilis WB800 中來自藍綠菌的 CcaSR 雙組分系統，菌體再把 ACC deaminase 分泌到中空纖維灌流式生物反應器裡——蛋白質可以出去，菌留在裡面。整台機器約 40 x 24 x 62 cm，設計上就是要擺在台灣小農的稻田旁；台灣農業經營者平均年齡 63.8 歲，精準農業對他們本來遙不可及。這個專案幾乎囊括高中組的技術類獎項（Measurement、Hardware、Integrated Human Practices），主要靠的是來源標註的紀律：四台自製裝置都附有釋出版組裝手冊；數位孿生在光度計徹底失效前 26.7 小時就抓到它正在壞；一份預先登錄的生長預測被後來的實驗實際評分；還有一份輸入明細帳，把每個數字標明是自己量的、引用的，還是模型算的。它最特別的品質是誠實——wiki 一再撤回自己先前的主張，而這也正是乾實驗弱點看得見的地方。","awards":["Top 10 (High School)","Best Measurement — Winner (High School)","Best Hardware — Winner (High School)","Best Presentation — Nominee (High School)","Best Wiki — Nominee (High School)","Best Integrated Human Practices — Winner (High School)","Best Village Project — Nominee (Space / Foundational Advance / Software & AI / Biomanufacturing)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Four strands. (1) A fitted crop-stress index: rather than weighting temperature, water and light by expert judgement, they fitted weights to Taiwan's own harvest record — 25 years of county rice yields from the Agriculture and Food Agency against ERA5 daily reanalysis weather (2001-2025), treating a season below the county trend as a stressed season, and exhaustively scoring all 2^15 - 1 = 32,767 combinations of fifteen candidate stress terms on held-out years. First and second rice crops were fitted separately; the second crop pays for wind, light and badly timed water, and heat adds nothing once those three are in — which the wiki notes undercuts the wet lab's heat programme. County error over 2016-2025 was 365 kg/ha against 419 for a plain trend line (32% error reduction on the second crop). A genuinely prospective test was frozen on 26 September 2026 before any county published; four of sixteen counties reported at 7.9% error against the trend's 8.8%, which the team correctly calls too few to establish performance. (2) Protein design (the GRAFT methodology: Generate, Restraints, Assembly, Flex, Triage) selected and shaped three protectants before any cloning — BoPEP4 (a 23-aa Brassica oleracea plant elicitor peptide docked against the PEPR1 receptor and run as nine all-atom MD trajectories), LEA14 (151-aa late embryogenesis abundant protein, five N-His constructs including a borrowed K-segment membrane-binding motif joined by a GGGGS linker), and ACC deaminase. The standout findings are negative and caught in time: a C-terminal 6xHis purification tag that every earlier check had approved was shown in simulation to cap the chemical group forming the peptide's strongest receptor contact, so the tag moved to the N-terminus; an Asn23 clamp was found to be five contacts rather than one salt bridge; a truncation ladder identified 9-23 as the production length (33% less mass) with the grip holding 98.5% of frames for 7-23 against 77.1% for the next rung down; and an AlphaFold confidence gate set before the result came back was failed for LEA14 with its partner, so by prior agreement no structure was handed on. For ACC deaminase no mutant was ordered at all, because the modelling said the enzyme meets far less substrate than it could handle and the largest available gain is a change to the medium (apoplast pH 5.5, where the Glu12-His227 contact holds in 99.9% of frames). (3) A reactor digital twin: an autoencoder trained on the healthy first 120 hours of a 434-hour run, scoring a sensor axis (the reference beam, which never passes through the culture) separately from a process axis (specific growth rate), so it can distinguish a culture event from a failing instrument; plus a Kalman-filter batch forecaster and a logistic growth prior fitted from the light plate. (4) Dose and fleet models: an arithmetic ledger from millilitres on a petri dish to US dollars per hectare, and a payback curve plotted across the whole efficacy axis.","frameworks_zh":"共四條線。(1) 擬合出來的作物逆境指數：他們沒有憑專家判斷去給溫度、水分與光照配權重，而是拿台灣自己的收穫紀錄來擬合——農糧署 25 年的各縣市稻作產量，對上 ERA5 逐日再分析氣象資料（2001-2025），把低於縣市趨勢的期作視為逆境期作，並在保留年份上窮舉評分十五個候選逆境項的全部 2^15 - 1 = 32,767 種組合。一期與二期稻作分別擬合；二期要付的代價是風、光與時機不對的水分，而這三項進去之後，熱逆境再加也沒有貢獻——wiki 自己指出，這一點削弱了濕實驗的熱逆境主軸。2016-2025 年的縣市誤差為 365 kg/ha，單純趨勢線則是 419（二期稻作誤差降低 32%）。真正前瞻性的檢驗在 2026 年 9 月 26 日、任何縣市公布數據之前就封存；十六個縣市中有四個已回報，誤差 7.9%，趨勢線為 8.8%，團隊也正確地說這太少，還不足以確立效能。(2) 蛋白質設計（GRAFT 方法論：Generate、Restraints、Assembly、Flex、Triage）在任何選殖之前就先選定並調整了三種保護蛋白——BoPEP4（23 個胺基酸的 Brassica oleracea 植物誘導胜肽，與 PEPR1 受體進行分子對接，並跑了九條全原子分子動力學軌跡）、LEA14（151 個胺基酸的晚期胚胎發育豐富蛋白，五種 N 端 His 構築體，其中一個借用了 K-segment 膜結合模體，以 GGGGS 連接子接上）與 ACC deaminase。最突出的發現都是負面的，而且及時被攔下來：一個先前每道檢查都放行的 C 端 6xHis 純化標籤，在模擬中被證明會蓋住形成該胜肽最強受體接觸的化學基團，於是標籤改到 N 端；Asn23 的夾持被發現是五個接觸，而不是一個鹽橋；截短系列指出 9-23 是生產用長度（質量少 33%），其中 7-23 的夾持在 98.5% 的幀中維持，再短一階則只有 77.1%；而一道在結果出來之前就設好的 AlphaFold 信心門檻，LEA14 與其夥伴蛋白並未通過，於是依先前的約定，沒有任何結構被往下傳。至於 ACC deaminase，一個突變體都沒有訂，因為模型顯示這個酵素實際遇到的受質遠少於它處理得來的量，而可取得的最大增益是改變環境介質（質外體 pH 5.5，此時 Glu12-His227 接觸在 99.9% 的幀中維持）。(3) 反應器數位孿生：用一次 434 小時實驗中健康的前 120 小時訓練自編碼器，並把感測軸（參考光束，從不穿過培養液）與製程軸（比生長速率）分開評分，因此能區分是培養事件還是儀器故障；另有 Kalman 濾波器批次預測器，以及由光照板擬合出的 logistic 成長先驗。(4) 劑量與機隊模型：一條從培養皿上的毫升數一路算到每公頃美元的算術帳，以及一條畫滿整個效力軸的回收期曲線。","dataviz":"The wiki's signature device is provenance colour-coding. The M4 dose ledger is drawn as a single top-to-bottom chain from 1.67 mL on a 10 cm plate to US$3800 capital per hectare, with a rail down the left that is green while every row still rests on a measurement and turns amber at the rice canopy correction, so a reader can see exactly where measurement stops and modelling begins; rows below inherit the model and two add assumptions of their own. Every model input is tabulated with a provenance column (seven from their own bench, four public records, two published constants, one from Geospatial Analysis, one neither measured nor cited), and the five assumptions get a table of 'what rests on it' and 'what would overturn it'. A timing diagram overlays the three-day Central Weather Administration forecast horizon, the three arrival arms the plant team ran, and the 5.4-day reactor lead time on a days-from-stress axis to show visually that they do not fit. The three disagreeing timing runs are shown side by side with the third panel re-reading the middle panel's own tubes as total chlorophyll instead of per gram, so the ranking visibly reverses — the figure argues against the team's own earlier claim. Decay figures plot both candidate interpretations through the same 28-hour reading and label the 22-fold divergence ('What one endpoint cannot say'). The payback plot marks their own 68-years-at-efficacy-1 point and Geospatial Analysis's 4.9-year estimate on the same axis and names the disagreement rather than hiding it. The digital twin UI itself puts optical density, pH, four pressure traces and the pump and valve controls on one screen; the description page opens with an interactive seven-block system map and a GIS choropleth of county nighttime temperature with circles scaled by rice yield trend.","dataviz_zh":"這個 wiki 的標誌性手法是用顏色標示資料來源。M4 劑量帳被畫成一條自上而下的單一鏈條，從 10 cm 培養皿上的 1.67 mL 一路到每公頃 US$3800 的資本支出，左側有一條軌道：只要每一列仍站在量測之上就是綠色，到了稻作冠層校正那一列轉為琥珀色，讀者因此能清楚看見量測在哪裡結束、模型從哪裡開始；下方各列繼承這個模型，其中兩列還各自加上自己的假設。每一項模型輸入都列表標註來源欄（七項出自自己的實驗桌、四項公開紀錄、兩項已發表常數、一項來自 Geospatial Analysis、一項既沒量也沒引用），五條假設則各有一張「什麼建立在它之上」與「什麼會推翻它」的表。一張時序圖把中央氣象署三天的預報時程、植物組跑的三條到達時間臂，以及 5.4 天的反應器前置時間疊在同一條「距逆境天數」軸上，用看的就知道它們對不起來。三次互相矛盾的時序實驗並排呈現，第三格把第二格自己的管子改以總葉綠素而非每克葉綠素重新解讀，排序因此明顯翻轉——這張圖是在反駁團隊自己先前的主張。衰減圖把兩種可能的解讀都畫過同一個 28 小時讀值，並標出 22 倍的分歧（「單一端點說不出的事」）。回收期圖把自己算出的「效力為 1 時 68 年」那一點，和 Geospatial Analysis 的 4.9 年估計放在同一條軸上，並直接點名這個分歧，而不是藏起來。數位孿生介面本身把光密度、pH、四路壓力曲線以及泵與閥的控制放在同一個畫面；專案描述頁一開頭就是一張七區塊的互動系統圖，以及一張以縣市夜間溫度著色、圓圈大小依稻作產量趨勢縮放的 GIS 分級著色圖。","datascience":"Three practices lift this above typical high-school dry lab. First, pre-registration: on 1 October, before any WB800 bioreactor run, they registered a specific growth rate of 0.2986 h^-1 with a 90% interval of 0.2705-0.3300, a logistic curve shape with an NRMSE pass threshold of 15%, and inoculum-conditional times to OD 0.5, together with stated pass criteria. Run 6 gave 0.286 +/- 0.010 h^-1 (R2 0.978), inside the interval; the curve-shape endpoint was recorded as not scored because the prior misses the first seven hours by 30% and the run passes the prior's ceiling before hour 7. Run 7 was explicitly excluded from scoring because its three-hour lag has no term in the registered logistic and its fitted rate swings 0.16-0.46 h^-1 with the window choice. Second, anomaly detection with a diagnostic split: the autoencoder flagged the photometer at 216.3 h, 26.7 h before the OD channel failed at 243.0 h, and the window table shows the sensor axis at 100% alarms with the process axis at 0% during the drift — the model names which subsystem is broken, not just that something is. Third, forecast benchmarking against persistence rather than against nothing: the Kalman filter beat a no-change baseline by 41% at 2 h on the September run and by 24% at 8 and 12 h on run 7, with global-linear, exponential and local-linear alternatives reported as losers and the honest caveat that most of the run is above the photometer's linear range so the model forecasts the reading, not biomass. Other measurement work: the in-line photometer tracks a benchtop BioDrop with slope 1.018 (R2 0.995) to OD 1.2 across 45 paired TiO2 points and an iGEM silica protocol run in 2.5 mg steps, with a dilute-and-restore test returning within 0.2%; wall shear computed from pressure sensors and from the flow meter agree to 2.8%, so each sensor checks the other; and leaf-sensor bench characterisation found a +0.47 to +1.71 degC site-dependent offset against the air reference across 540 paired readings, with the conclusion stated that a 1.2-1.9 degC bias can hide or invent the very water-stress signal the twin would act on. Honest dry-lab weaknesses, stated by the team: a secreted-activity figure of 7.25 mU/mL at n = 1 and below quantitation; two induction runs that disagree on the sign of activity change over hours; the published CcaSR Hill curve (Castillo-Hair et al. 2019) assumed valid at 20 L when every induction was run at a single light intensity, so nothing tests it; a rice canopy correction of x2.44 that is modelled, not measured, and spans 1.68-3.52; a minimum effective dose that is unknown because the spray experiment varied salt and timing but never the applied amount; a withdrawn efficacy coefficient of 0.58; and only 17 of 25 modelled seasons ever crossing the trigger, so a ten-unit fleet runs on 4.3% of the calendar.","datascience_zh":"有三項做法讓這份乾實驗明顯高於一般高中水準。第一是預先登錄：10 月 1 日、在任何 WB800 生物反應器實驗之前，他們就登錄了比生長速率 0.2986 h^-1、90% 區間 0.2705-0.3300、logistic 曲線形狀與 15% 的 NRMSE 通過門檻，以及依接種量而定的到 OD 0.5 時間，並寫明通過標準。第 6 次實驗得到 0.286 +/- 0.010 h^-1（R2 0.978），落在區間內；曲線形狀這個端點被記為未評分，因為先驗在前七小時低估了 30%，而實驗在第 7 小時之前就超過先驗的上限。第 7 次實驗被明確排除在評分之外，因為它三小時的遲滯期在登錄的 logistic 模型裡沒有對應項，而擬合速率會隨視窗選擇在 0.16-0.46 h^-1 之間擺動。第二是帶診斷切分的異常偵測：自編碼器在 216.3 小時就標記光度計異常，比 OD 通道在 243.0 小時失效早了 26.7 小時，而視窗表顯示漂移期間感測軸是 100% 警報、製程軸是 0%——這個模型指出的是哪個子系統壞了，而不只是「有東西不對」。第三是預測要和持續性基線比，而不是不比：Kalman 濾波器在 9 月那次實驗的 2 小時預測比不變基線好 41%，在第 7 次實驗的 8 與 12 小時預測好 24%，全域線性、指數與局部線性等替代方案都被列為落敗者，並誠實加註：實驗大部分時間都在光度計的線性範圍之上，所以模型預測的是讀值，不是生物量。其他量測工作：線上光度計與桌上型 BioDrop 在 OD 1.2 以內的對應斜率為 1.018（R2 0.995），依據 45 組配對 TiO2 點與一份以 2.5 mg 為階的 iGEM 二氧化矽協議，稀釋後再回復的測試誤差落在 0.2% 之內；由壓力感測器與流量計分別算出的管壁剪應力一致到 2.8%，兩個感測器互為查核；葉面感測器的實驗桌特性化在 540 組配對讀值中發現，相對於空氣參考值有 +0.47 到 +1.71 degC、隨位置而異的偏移，並明白寫出結論：1.2-1.9 degC 的偏差足以隱藏或憑空製造出數位孿生要據以行動的那個水分逆境訊號。團隊自己列出的乾實驗弱點：分泌活性 7.25 mU/mL 只有 n = 1，而且低於定量極限；兩次誘導實驗對活性在數小時內變化的正負號彼此矛盾；已發表的 CcaSR Hill 曲線（Castillo-Hair 等人，2019）被假設在 20 L 規模仍成立，但每次誘導都只跑單一光強度，所以根本沒有東西在檢驗它；稻作冠層校正係數 x2.44 是模型算的、不是量的，範圍落在 1.68-3.52；最低有效劑量未知，因為噴施實驗變動了鹽度與時機，卻從未變動施用量；一個已撤回的效力係數 0.58；以及 25 個模擬期作中只有 17 個曾越過啟動門檻，所以十台機組的機隊一年只運作 4.3% 的日子。","software":"The digital twin is released MIT-licensed at https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/gems-taiwan/digital-twin. It reads live OD600, pH, four pressure channels and turbine flow from the reactor loop, drives a pinch valve and four Luer valves, runs the autoencoder sensor alarm and the Kalman batch forecast, computes lumen pressure drop, transmembrane pressure and a fouling ratio through a hydraulic model, and applies the BLASTAM leaf-blast infection rule (a wet period counts when the leaf stays wet at least 10 hours at a mean of 22-25 degC, no infection below 15 or above 25 degC, past hours from the sensor and future hours estimated as wet at 90% relative humidity) to tell a grower to look for lesions five to ten days later. The team is clear about what is not wired up: green-light induction is tested but not integrated, dissolved-oxygen calibration did not hold, the protectant amount cannot be read in-line and comes from hand-drawn ELISA and DNPH samples, and every model so far has run on recorded data after a run with a person making every decision — so it is honestly a digital shadow moving toward a twin. Four open hardware devices ship with build manuals and print files: the hollow-fiber perfusion bioreactor (10-page assembly guide, 17-page brochure, 16-page user manual), a Pro and a Slim in-line photometer (12- and 13-page guides), and a 24-tube dual-wavelength light plate apparatus (10-page guide), plus a floating hydroponics plate with 13 seed positions, a 6.5 MB hardware notebook covering 23 March to 17 October 2026, and an LLM-assisted QGIS geospatial workflow over 346 farming townships with the data-preparation prompt published. Also contributed: 35 Registry parts in five SubtiToolKit Golden Gate modules, a 15-page plant protocol, a twentyfold scale-down of the ACC deaminase DNPH activity assay onto a 96-well plate, and waste-media protocols (hay, okara and sugarcane extracts benchmarked against LB).","software_zh":"數位孿生以 MIT 授權釋出於 https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/gems-taiwan/digital-twin。它讀取反應器迴路的即時 OD600、pH、四路壓力通道與渦輪流量，驅動一個夾管閥與四個 Luer 閥，執行自編碼器感測警報與 Kalman 批次預測，透過水力模型計算管腔壓降、跨膜壓與積垢比，並套用 BLASTAM 稻熱病感染規則（葉面在平均 22-25 degC 下保持潤濕至少 10 小時才算一個濕潤期，低於 15 degC 或高於 25 degC 不發生感染，過去的時數取自感測器，未來的時數則在相對濕度 90% 時估為潤濕），以提醒農民在五到十天後去找病斑。團隊很清楚講出哪些還沒接起來：綠光誘導測過但尚未整合、溶氧校正撐不住、保護蛋白的量無法線上讀取而要靠人工取樣的 ELISA 與 DNPH、而且到目前為止每個模型都是在實驗結束後跑錄下來的資料、每個決策都由人做——所以老實說它是一個正朝數位孿生前進的「數位影子」。四台開源硬體裝置都附組裝手冊與列印檔：中空纖維灌流式生物反應器（10 頁組裝指南、17 頁產品說明、16 頁使用手冊）、Pro 與 Slim 兩款線上光度計（12 頁與 13 頁指南），以及 24 管雙波長光照板裝置（10 頁指南），另有一塊 13 個種子位的浮動水耕板、一份涵蓋 2026 年 3 月 23 日至 10 月 17 日的 6.5 MB 硬體筆記本，以及一套以 LLM 輔助、涵蓋 346 個農業鄉鎮的 QGIS 地理空間工作流程，連資料整備用的提示詞都公開。其他貢獻還包括：五個 SubtiToolKit Golden Gate 模組共 35 個 Registry 元件、一份 15 頁的植物實驗協議、把 ACC deaminase 的 DNPH 活性分析縮小二十倍搬到 96 孔盤，以及廢棄培養基協議（乾草、豆渣與甘蔗萃取液，以 LB 為對照基準）。","stack":["Python","autoencoder (anomaly detection)","Kalman filter","logistic growth fitting","exhaustive subset selection over 2^15 feature combinations","ERA5 reanalysis","QGIS","LLM-assisted GIS data preparation","AlphaFold (with pre-set confidence gate)","molecular docking","all-atom molecular dynamics","Arduino / ESP32","SHT31 air sensor","SN-3001-YM-N01 leaf sensor","Modbus RTU over RS485","I2C","BLASTAM leaf blast model","Hill function inversion (CcaSR transfer function)","MAD-based outlier filtering","GitLab (iGEM), MIT licence"],"techniques":["pre-registered prediction with stated pass criteria, scored after the fact","provenance ledger marking every input measured / cited / modelled","assumption register with falsification conditions","held-out and prospective (frozen-forecast) validation","forecast benchmarking against a persistence baseline","two-axis autoencoder separating sensor fault from process event","in-line photometer cross-calibration against a benchtop spectrophotometer (TiO2 and SiO2 standards)","dilute-and-restore proportionality test","redundant sensing (wall shear from pressure vs from flow)","anti-His ELISA and DNPH colorimetric activity assay","sensitivity analysis showing the activity term cancels out of the capital result","explicit withdrawal of an unsupported efficacy coefficient","payback plotted across the full efficacy axis instead of a point estimate"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"140 students across 5 schools in tiered lessons for elementary, junior high and high school audiences, with pre- and post-Kahoot surveys per cohort and the results published as per-question accuracy charts — including the failures, such as DNA base pairing where only 30% of students answered correctly. Everything is released on a dedicated education website: three lesson plans, three slide decks, two card games, two online games and a plant stress simulator (CropShield), free to download, with the stated aim of making the lessons work without the team in the room. Hands-on activities included plant stress experiments, planter making, an ATCG card game and vocabulary work. The team also edited its own claims down for honesty — a visible wiki comment records removing a '49-point' improvement claim and a 'standard teaching methods' comparison, and correcting a student count from 144 to 140. Separately, a Taiwan-specific engagement channel: a LINE official account called 'Nong You Zhu Shou' (Farmer's Assistant) with six functions — latest news, product introduction, crop stress alerts, a crop assistant AI chatbot keyed to terms like salinity, heat stress and pests, a Farmer's Diary where users post weather, crop photos, soil moisture and pest conditions and earn tokens redeemable for LINE stickers, and a Google Form feedback loop — built because interviews at the Farmer Expo and with Ms. Chen Hui-Wen showed smallholders could not reach the information that already exists online. A public event at Taipei Water Garden Organic Farmers' Market on 5 September 2026 (Taiwan Coffee x Cocoa Gelato Festival) drew over 400 visitors with over 200 registered participants, running a forum, booth activities including a data-physicalisation installation and a ring toss, and a plant stress event.","publicEngagement_zh":"5 所學校、140 位學生，課程按國小、國中與高中分層設計，每個群組都做課前與課後 Kahoot 問卷，結果以逐題正確率圖表公開——包括失敗的部分，例如 DNA 鹼基配對只有 30% 的學生答對。所有材料都放在專門的教育網站上免費下載：三份教案、三份簡報、兩款卡牌遊戲、兩款線上遊戲與一個植物逆境模擬器（CropShield），目標明確寫著要讓這些課程在團隊不在現場時也能運作。實作活動包括植物逆境實驗、做盆器、ATCG 卡牌遊戲與單字練習。團隊也為了誠實而修掉自己的說法——wiki 上留有一則可見的註記，記錄刪去「進步 49 分」的主張與和「標準教學法」的比較，並把學生人數從 144 更正為 140。另外還有一條台灣特有的互動管道：一個名為「農友助手」的 LINE 官方帳號，共六項功能——最新消息、產品介紹、作物逆境警示、以鹽害、熱逆境與蟲害等關鍵詞觸發的作物小幫手 AI 聊天機器人、使用者可張貼天氣、作物照片、土壤含水量與蟲害狀況並賺取可兌換 LINE 貼圖的點數的「農友日誌」，以及一條 Google 表單回饋迴路——會做這個，是因為在農業博覽會以及與陳慧文女士的訪談中發現，小農根本接觸不到網路上早就存在的資訊。2026 年 9 月 5 日在台北水花園有機農夫市集辦的公開活動（台灣咖啡 x 可可冰淇淋節）吸引超過 400 位到訪者、超過 200 位報名參與者，內容有一場論壇、含資料實體化裝置與套圈圈的攤位活動，以及一場植物逆境活動。","ihp":"31 stakeholders over seven months, structured as a project evolution map in four stages with named dates, plus four thematic expert pipelines (deployment, protectant design, plant and stress biology, bioreactor and hardware) and continuous engagement with five core experts. The decisive change came at the very start: the original design released engineered Bacillus subtilis into the soil with a DesK-DesR system reading temperature directly. Prof. Chen Wen-Liang (10 April) and bioprocess experts said two things were wrong — the bacteria could not be contained, and biological sensing was neither precise nor controllable enough — so sensing moved out of the cell into electronic sensors and an AIoT model, and a hollow-fiber perfusion bioreactor was built to hold the bacteria in while letting the protectants out. That one conversation produced the entire architecture. Other changes with a clear before/after: Dr. Paul Verslues (Academia Sinica, 3 April) argued that supplying pure proline is inefficient and risks suppressing the plant's own P5CS1 biosynthesis and proline-redox balance, so they abandoned proline delivery for a plant-regulation framework using bacterial signals and precursors, shifted from stress recovery to early detection, and re-scored outcomes on root growth and biomass. Dr. Elizabeth Sattely (Stanford, 27 June) told them their proof of concept was too broad and to do one stress very well instead of many superficially, and to look at peptides — which is why BoPEP4 entered the panel and why plant testing narrowed to heat and salinity. CH Biotech (9 July) pushed them toward computational screening to optimise protectants, comparison of root irrigation vs foliar vs drone spray, production cost per area, and Taiwanese regulatory research before acting. Prof. Huang Chieh-Chen (NCHU, 28 July and 6 August) moved the reactor from continuous to periodic operation, raised seedling-stage application, warned that excessive protectant concentrations harm plants so thresholds must be validated, and supplied the B. subtilis WB800 strain the project now runs on. Prof. Cheng Mei-Chun (28 August) found that inconsistent plant ages and treatment conditions meant earlier results may have reflected unintended stress rather than treatment, and the protocols were standardised in response. Yes Health iFarm (11 August) prompted reconsidering the 8/16 light cycle for 12/12, adding DO and OD to parameter planning, switching from pure oxygen to gentle aeration, and minimising transplants because transplantation itself is a stressor. Most interesting is the natural-farming thread: at a public forum co-hosted with Green Media on 5 September, Dr. Li Hsu-Ying and Ms. Chen argued that a plant protected from every stress never builds tolerance — 'raising a crop is like raising a child'. Rather than dismiss it, the team made that the specification for M1: the reactor should fire only when a threshold that genuinely reflects crop condition is crossed, which is why the 32% error reduction matters as evidence for a release rule rather than as a number. A farmer at the same forum asked whether the system breaks organic certification; the team researched the regulations and concluded it cannot be used on organic farms, then interviewed Mr. Chen Ke-Wei of the Lanyang River Friendly Farming Production Cooperative to work out what that means commercially. The project's origin question came from Ghanaian farmers via Gilbert Nkpeniyeng of Ubuntu Social Enterprise Ghana (1 February).","ihp_zh":"七個月內 31 位利害關係人，整理成一張分四階段、標明日期的專案演進圖，另有四條主題式專家管道（佈署、保護蛋白設計、植物與逆境生物學、生物反應器與硬體），並與五位核心專家持續往來。決定性的轉變發生在最開頭：最初的設計是把工程改造的 Bacillus subtilis 釋放到土壤裡，用 DesK-DesR 系統直接感測溫度。Chen Wen-Liang 教授（4 月 10 日）與生物製程專家指出兩件事錯了——細菌無法被圍堵，而生物式感測既不夠精準也不夠可控——於是感測從細胞內搬到體外的電子感測器與 AIoT 模型，並做出中空纖維灌流式生物反應器，把細菌留住、讓保護蛋白出去。那一場對話就決定了整個架構。其他有清楚前後對照的改變：Dr. Paul Verslues（中央研究院，4 月 3 日）指出直接供給純脯胺酸效率不佳，還可能抑制植物自身的 P5CS1 生合成與脯胺酸氧化還原平衡，於是他們放棄遞送脯胺酸，改採以細菌訊號與前驅物調節植物的架構，從逆境復原轉向早期偵測，並把成果指標改以根部生長與生物量重新評分。Dr. Elizabeth Sattely（Stanford，6 月 27 日）告訴他們概念驗證鋪得太廣，應該把一種逆境做得很好，而不是多種都做得很淺，並建議去看胜肽——這就是 BoPEP4 進入候選名單、植物測試收斂到熱逆境與鹽害的原因。CH Biotech（7 月 9 日）推動他們用計算篩選來最佳化保護蛋白、比較根部灌注、葉面噴施與無人機噴灑、計算每單位面積的生產成本，並在行動前先做台灣的法規研究。Huang Chieh-Chen 教授（中興大學，7 月 28 日與 8 月 6 日）把反應器從連續操作改為週期操作、提出在苗期施用、警告保護蛋白濃度過高會傷害植物因此門檻必須驗證，並提供了這個專案現在使用的 B. subtilis WB800 菌株。Cheng Mei-Chun 教授（8 月 28 日）發現植株年齡與處理條件不一致，意味著早期結果反映的可能是非預期的逆境而不是處理效果，團隊因此標準化了實驗協議。Yes Health iFarm（8 月 11 日）促使他們重新考慮把 8/16 光週期改為 12/12、把溶氧與 OD 納入參數規劃、從純氧改為溫和通氣，並盡量減少移植，因為移植本身就是一種逆境。最有意思的是自然農法這條線：9 月 5 日與 Green Media 共同主辦的公開論壇上，Dr. Li Hsu-Ying 與陳女士主張，一株被保護到完全沒有逆境的植物永遠建立不起耐受性——「養作物就像養小孩」。團隊沒有打發掉這個意見，而是把它變成 M1 的規格：反應器只有在一個真正反映作物狀態的門檻被跨越時才該啟動，這也正是那 32% 誤差降低之所以重要的原因——它是釋放規則的證據，而不只是一個數字。同一場論壇上有位農民問這套系統會不會破壞有機認證；團隊去查了法規，結論是它不能用在有機農場，接著訪談蘭陽溪友善耕作生產合作社的 Chen Ke-Wei 先生，釐清這在商業上意味著什麼。這個專案最初的問題，來自迦納農民，經由 Ubuntu Social Enterprise Ghana 的 Gilbert Nkpeniyeng 轉達（2 月 1 日）。","realWorld":"Positioned as a social enterprise with the vision 'every farmer is a biomanufacturer', deployed through farmer collectives and pilot cooperatives rather than direct sales, because the fleet analysis shows a reactor owned by a single farm is idle most of the season. The MVP is costed component by component: current bioreactor US$2280, leaf humidity sensor US$125, a drop-in sealed bacteria cartridge US$90 that opens automatically once seated so no one handles an open culture, and a Field Console mobile app; capital works out at about US$3800 per hectare before refills, service or labour. The regulatory target is contained-use answers in Taiwan by October 2027, and the team worked the pathway with Director Wu Tzu-Hsien (12 October), who pointed out their cost model was missing factory, labour, bacterial cultivation and waste-management costs, and with Prof. Chang Hung-Hao (31 August), who told them to narrow the initial application to a specific stress and crop. A conversation with Bioeconomy Corporation at BIO Asia-Taiwan redirected expansion research toward Southeast Asia, where agricultural sectors are large and GMO rules looser than the US or EU. Smart Agriweek Taiwan identified young farmers as the realistic early adopters and flagged that older farmers need a separate persuasion route. SWOT and PESTLE analyses name the real threats plainly: unclear regulation for cell-free agricultural biologics that may fall between biological pesticide and synthetic-biology-derived compound; protectant washing away; biofouling reducing yield; and the fact that only 3.47% of Taiwan's farmland was organic or eco-friendly by 2024, which both bounds and shapes the market. The payback analysis is the most commercially honest thing on the wiki: on their own loss figure of US$138 per hectare per crop, no point on the efficacy axis returns the capital on a useful horizon — 68 years even at perfect efficacy — while Geospatial Analysis reaches 4.9 years from a net benefit of US$1931 per crop, and the team states that the two do not yet price the same hectare rather than quietly adopting the favourable number. Deliverables include an 85-page business plan, a farmer-friendly user manual, and the three bioreactor documents.","realWorld_zh":"定位是社會企業，願景為「讓每一位農民都是生物製造者」，透過農民團體與試點合作社佈署，而非直接銷售，因為機隊分析顯示單一農場自己擁有一台反應器，大半個產季都在閒置。MVP 逐項估價：現行生物反應器 US$2280、葉面濕度感測器 US$125、一個 US$90 的密封式菌體卡匣（放到位後自動開啟，所以沒有人需要接觸開放的培養液），以及一個 Field Console 手機應用程式；資本支出約為每公頃 US$3800，不含補充、維修與人力。法規目標是在 2027 年 10 月前取得台灣封閉系統使用的答案；團隊和 Wu Tzu-Hsien 主任（10 月 12 日）一起走這條路徑，對方指出他們的成本模型漏掉廠房、人力、菌體培養與廢棄物管理成本，另與 Chang Hung-Hao 教授（8 月 31 日）討論，對方要他們把初期應用收斂到特定逆境與特定作物。在 BIO Asia-Taiwan 與 Bioeconomy Corporation 的一次對話，把擴張研究的方向轉往東南亞——那裡農業部門規模大，GMO 規範也比美國或歐盟寬鬆。Smart Agriweek Taiwan 指出青農才是現實中的早期採用者，並提醒年長農民需要另一套說服路徑。SWOT 與 PESTLE 分析把真正的威脅講得很白：無細胞農業生物製劑的法規定位不明，可能卡在生物農藥與合成生物學衍生化合物之間；保護蛋白會被沖走；生物積垢會降低產出；以及到 2024 年台灣只有 3.47% 的農地屬有機或友善耕作——這既限制也形塑了市場。回收期分析是整個 wiki 上商業上最誠實的一塊：以他們自己每公頃每期作 US$138 的損失數字來算，效力軸上沒有任何一點能在有用的時間尺度內回收資本——即使效力完美也要 68 年——而 Geospatial Analysis 以每期作 US$1931 的淨效益算出 4.9 年，團隊明白寫出這兩者定價的並不是同一公頃土地，而不是悄悄採用那個好看的數字。交付成果包括一份 85 頁的營運計畫書、一份對農民友善的使用手冊，以及三份生物反應器文件。","partners":["Prof. Chen Wen-Liang (containment and business plan)","Dr. Paul Verslues (Academia Sinica)","Dr. Elizabeth Sattely (Stanford University)","Prof. Drew Endy (Stanford University)","Dr. Jennifer Brophy","Prof. Cheng Mei-Chun","Prof. Huang Chieh-Chen (National Chung Hsing University; supplied B. subtilis WB800)","Prof. Huang Tzu-Pi (National Chung Hsing University)","Prof. Chang Jo-Shu","Prof. Chang Hung-Hao","Dr. Lin Wei-Yi","CH Biotech (Taiwan)","Yes Health iFarm","World Vegetable Center","Green Media (public forum co-host)","Gilbert Nkpeniyeng, Ubuntu Social Enterprise Ghana","Dr. Li Hsu-Ying and Ms. Chen (natural farming)","Mr. Chen Ke-Wei, Lanyang River Friendly Farming Production Cooperative","Ms. Chen Hui-Wen","Director Wu Tzu-Hsien","Mr. Riddler Lu","Taipei Expo Farmers Market","BIO Asia-Taiwan Exhibition","Taiwan SMART Agriweek","Bureau Francais de Taipei","Owl Lab","Geospatial Analysis (partner team)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6072/wiki/software/twin-screen-20261018-software.webp","caption":"The ReLEAF digital twin control screen on 18 October 2026, showing optical density, pH, four pressure traces and the pump and valve controls for a live bioreactor run on one page.","caption_zh":"2026 年 10 月 18 日的 ReLEAF 數位孿生控制畫面，在同一頁顯示即時生物反應器實驗的光密度、pH、四路壓力曲線以及泵與閥的控制。","credit":"Team GEMS-Taiwan, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6072/wiki/software/fig-r3-run434-software.svg","caption":"The 434-hour run: optical density above and the photometer's reference channel below, with the autoencoder sensor alarm at 216.3 hours marked 26.7 hours before the OD channel failed.","caption_zh":"那次 434 小時的實驗：上為光密度，下為光度計的參考通道，自編碼器的感測警報標在 216.3 小時，比 OD 通道失效早了 26.7 小時。","credit":"Team GEMS-Taiwan, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6072/wiki/model/stress-validation-island-model.webp","caption":"Island first-crop rice yield against predictions made from earlier years only; county error over 2016-2025 is 419 kg/ha for the plain trend and 365 kg/ha for the fitted stress-index model.","caption_zh":"全島一期稻作產量與僅以較早年份資料所做預測的對照；2016-2025 年的縣市誤差，單純趨勢線為 419 kg/ha，擬合出的逆境指數模型為 365 kg/ha。","credit":"Team GEMS-Taiwan, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6072/wiki/description/bioreactor-front-description.webp","caption":"The ReLEAF hollow-fiber perfusion bioreactor, about 40 x 24 x 62 cm, built to stand beside the field it supplies and to let protectant protein out while keeping the engineered bacteria in.","caption_zh":"ReLEAF 中空纖維灌流式生物反應器，約 40 x 24 x 62 cm，設計上就是要擺在它所供應的田邊，讓保護蛋白出去、把工程改造的細菌留在裡面。","credit":"Team GEMS-Taiwan, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"The transferable asset is the provenance discipline, and it is cheaper than it looks: tag every number in a model as measured-by-us, cited, or modelled; publish an assumption register that states what would overturn each step; and when two of your own runs disagree, show both and name the disagreement instead of picking the flattering one. Pair that with one pre-registered, date-stamped prediction scored against a later experiment — GEMS-Taiwan's registered growth rate is the single highest-credibility item on its wiki, and it cost nothing but committing in writing before the data arrived.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"可以帶走的資產是來源標註的紀律，而它比看起來便宜得多：把模型裡每個數字標成「我們量的」、「引用的」或「模型算的」；公開一份假設清單，逐條寫出什麼情況會推翻這一步；當自己的兩次實驗互相矛盾時，兩筆都放出來並指出矛盾，而不是挑那個好看的。再搭配一項預先登錄、有日期戳記的預測，並由後續實驗實際評分——GEMS-Taiwan 登錄的生長速率是整個 wiki 上可信度最高的一項，而它的成本只是在資料出現之前先把話寫下來。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/software/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/measurement/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/hardware/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/protein-design/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/results/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/education/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/entrepreneurship/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/contribution/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gems-taiwan/parts/","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/gems-taiwan/digital-twin"],"rank":169},"6077":{"team":"UOttawa","id":"6077","section":"Undergrad","country":"Canada","village":"Bioremediation","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/uottawa/","projectTitle":"Nulfur","projectTitle_zh":"Nulfur","tagline":"Break bonds, not the fuel: engineered biodesulfurization as a polishing step for refractory sulfur in diesel.","tagline_zh":"斷鍵，而不是斷燃料：以工程化生物脫硫作為柴油中難脫除硫化物的精製步驟。","summary":"Nulfur rebuilds the four-enzyme 4S biodesulfurization pathway (DszA, DszB, DszC plus a flavin reductase) from Rhodococcus erythropolis inside Pseudomonas putida KT2440, targeting dibenzothiophene (DBT) — the refractory sulfur compound that conventional hydrodesulfurization struggles to remove without running at 300-400 C and 3-6 MPa. Rather than replacing hydrodesulfurization, the team reframed the project after industry consultation as a modular side-stream polishing step on diesel. The project won on the strength of its alternative chassis work: because P. putida is a non-model organism, the team built the missing toolkit from scratch (a Golden Gate-compatible broad-host-range vector, a measured four-promoter set, and a working heat-shock transformation protocol) and published it as a handbook for other teams. That platform contribution, paired with an unusually deep dry lab (COBRApy genome-scale modelling, a FoldX/ThermoMPNN protein engineering pipeline, and an agentic AI research platform called Cofactor), won Best Alternative Platform and Best Wiki and Best Bioremediation Project nominations.","summary_zh":"Nulfur 把源自 Rhodococcus erythropolis 的四酶 4S 生物脫硫途徑（DszA、DszB、DszC 加上一個黃素還原酶）重建於 Pseudomonas putida KT2440 之中，標的是二苯并噻吩（DBT），也就是傳統加氫脫硫必須在 300-400 C、3-6 MPa 條件下才勉強能處理的難脫除硫化物。團隊在與業界諮詢後，並未把專案定位為取代加氫脫硫，而是重新定義為柴油上的模組化側流精製步驟。本專案的獲獎實力來自替代底盤的工作：由於 P. putida 屬於非模式生物，團隊從零建立起原本缺乏的工具組（一個相容於 Golden Gate 的廣宿主範圍載體、一組經過量測的四啟動子系列，以及一套可用的熱休克轉型流程），並把它整理成供其他團隊使用的手冊。這項平台貢獻，搭配一個深度罕見的乾實驗（COBRApy 基因組尺度代謝模型、FoldX/ThermoMPNN 蛋白質工程流程，以及名為 Cofactor 的代理式 AI 研究平台），為團隊贏得 Best Alternative Platform，並入圍 Best Wiki 與 Best Bioremediation Project。","awards":["Top 10 (Undergrad)","Best Alternative Platform — Winner (Undergrad)","Best Wiki — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Bioremediation Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Three distinct computational layers. (1) Genome-scale metabolic modelling: the published P. putida KT2440 model iJN1463 was extended in COBRApy with the heterologous 4S pathway reactions (DszA/B/C/D), and flux balance analysis solved through GLPK over a 1000-point sweep of the DBT exchange flux bound showed metabolism never bottlenecks uptake, while forcing DszB flux revealed an NADH-limited ceiling of 9.80 mmol gDCW-1 h-1 that formate co-feeding raises 25.5% to 12.30. (2) A first-principles mass-transfer model of the biphasic reactor combining Hinze-Kolmogorov droplet-breakup scaling, film theory at the stagnant-sphere limit (Sh = 2), micellar solubilization above the CMC and Michaelis-Menten uptake, solved by bisection for the steady-state free DBT concentration; it predicts rhamnolipid raises effective DBT availability 2.8- to 34-fold. (3) A protein engineering pipeline that screened over 1,100 candidate substitutions in DszB and DszC using ConSurf conservation grades, MD-derived backbone RMSF, and an ensemble of FoldX (empirical force field) plus ThermoMPNN (deep learning on ProteinMPNN embeddings) for ddG, then validated catalytic integrity with explicit-solvent GROMACS MD (amber99sb-ildn, TIP3P) and AutoDock Vina ligand docking before shortlisting five mutants per enzyme.","frameworks_zh":"三個不同的計算層次。(1) 基因組尺度代謝模型：團隊在 COBRApy 中把已發表的 P. putida KT2440 模型 iJN1463 擴充，加入異源 4S 途徑的反應（DszA/B/C/D），並以 GLPK 求解通量平衡分析，對 DBT 交換通量上限做 1000 點掃描，結果顯示代謝從未成為攝取的瓶頸；而強制給定 DszB 通量後，則揭露出一個受 NADH 限制的上限 9.80 mmol gDCW-1 h-1，共餵入甲酸可將此上限提高 25.5% 至 12.30。(2) 雙相反應器的第一原理質傳模型，結合 Hinze-Kolmogorov 液滴破裂尺度律、停滯球極限下的薄膜理論（Sh = 2）、CMC 以上的微胞增溶，以及 Michaelis-Menten 型攝取，並以二分法求解穩態的游離 DBT 濃度；模型預測鼠李糖脂可讓有效的 DBT 可得量提高 2.8 至 34 倍。(3) 一條蛋白質工程流程，以 ConSurf 保守性等級、由分子動力學模擬得到的主鏈 RMSF，以及 FoldX（經驗力場）加上 ThermoMPNN（在 ProteinMPNN 嵌入向量上做深度學習）的集成來估算 ddG，篩選 DszB 與 DszC 中超過 1,100 個候選取代；接著以顯式溶劑的 GROMACS 分子動力學模擬（amber99sb-ildn、TIP3P）與 AutoDock Vina 配體對接驗證催化功能是否完好，最後為每個酶挑出五個突變體入選名單。","dataviz":"The wiki is a server-rendered-feel React site with a genuinely engineered visual layer: a WebGL/Three.js distillation-tower scene and animated pathway loop on the landing page, every equation rendered as its own labelled SVG so the derivation reads as a chain, and predictor-agreement scatter plots (Figure 9) that shade the quadrant where FoldX and ThermoMPNN both call a substitution stabilising and enlarge it to label the five mutations actually sent to the bench. The Human Practices page is built as a clickable stacked column where each band is one of seven kinds of conversation across 21 entries, so a judge can jump straight to the stakeholder group they care about. Every figure carries a long descriptive alt attribute that states the figure's actual numbers, not just its subject.","dataviz_zh":"這個 wiki 是一個讀起來像伺服器渲染的 React 網站，視覺層確實經過工程設計：首頁有以 WebGL/Three.js 製作的蒸餾塔場景與動畫化的途徑迴圈；每一條方程式都各自渲染成帶標註的 SVG，使整段推導讀起來像一條連貫的鏈；預測器一致性散布圖（圖 9）則把 FoldX 與 ThermoMPNN 同時判定該取代具穩定化效果的象限加上底色，並將該象限放大，標示出實際送進實驗台的五個突變。人類實踐頁面做成可點選的堆疊柱狀圖，每一段代表 21 筆紀錄中七類對話之一，讓評審可以直接跳到自己關心的利害關係人族群。每張圖都附有長篇描述性的 alt 屬性，寫出該圖實際的數值，而不只是它的主題。","datascience":"The headline data-science contribution is turning the protein engineering loop into a measured, auditable artefact. The team built a six-arm evaluation suite for Cofactor with four ablation regimes (bare, bare_prompt, tools, full) that add exactly one harness layer each, then scored outcomes: 37 deterministic probes in Arms A and B all pass, Arm C recorded zero workflow violations across 27 scorable runs under the phase machine versus two in the bare condition, and Arm D found the ungrounded condition hallucinated amino-acid positions while both grounded conditions did not. Arm E asked the agent to reconstruct the initial experimental designs of six published papers (three postdating the model's knowledge cutoff) and audited tool transcripts for contamination. On the wet-lab side, the promoter library was quantified as log-normalized mScarlet-i fluorescence per OD600 corrected for media background and P. putida autofluorescence, which revealed only three distinct expression tiers rather than the four reported in the literature.","datascience_zh":"最突出的資料科學貢獻，是把蛋白質工程的迭代迴圈變成一個可量測、可稽核的產出。團隊為 Cofactor 建立了六組評估套件，含四種消融（ablation）設定（bare、bare_prompt、tools、full），每一種剛好多加一層外框機制，然後對結果評分：A、B 兩組中 37 項確定性探測全數通過；C 組在階段狀態機之下，27 次可評分執行中記錄到零次流程違規，而在 bare 條件下為兩次；D 組則發現未加接地的條件會虛構出胺基酸位置，而兩種有接地的條件都沒有。E 組要求代理重建六篇已發表論文的初始實驗設計（其中三篇發表於模型知識截止日之後），並稽核工具的操作紀錄以檢查是否受到汙染。濕實驗方面，啟動子庫以每 OD600 的 mScarlet-i 螢光取對數歸一化後定量，並扣除培養基背景與 P. putida 自體螢光，結果顯示只有三個明顯的表現量層級，而非文獻報告中的四個。","software":"Cofactor, an agentic protein engineering platform released under MIT licence at https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uottawa/cofactor. It wraps a general-purpose LLM in an explicit phase state machine whose preconditions are checked against a 16-table SQLite store (.cofactor/research.sqlite3, WAL journaling, foreign keys) rather than against the model's claims, so runs resume across sessions and the research record stays readable without the tool. A deterministic tool layer covers sequence operations, RFC10 compliance checking, codon optimisation, restriction analysis, solubility scanning, and retrieval from UniProt, NCBI, RCSB PDB, AlphaFold, PubMed and Europe PMC; an ExecutionManager submits jobs to local, SSH or Slurm backends. Three frontends ship: a FastAPI web UI, a Textual TUI and a CLI, all bring-your-own-key and model-agnostic against any OpenAI-compatible endpoint. The team also released the P. putida handbook with protocols and the sanitized Golden Gate-ready pBBR1MCS-2 vector to the iGEM Registry.","software_zh":"Cofactor 是一個代理式蛋白質工程平台，以 MIT 授權釋出於 https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uottawa/cofactor。它把一個通用 LLM 包在一個明確的階段狀態機之中，各階段的前置條件是對照一個 16 張表的 SQLite 資料庫（.cofactor/research.sqlite3，WAL 日誌、外鍵）來檢查，而不是採信模型自己的說法，因此執行可以跨工作階段續跑，研究紀錄也不必依賴這個工具就能讀懂。確定性的工具層涵蓋序列操作、RFC10 相容性檢查、密碼子最佳化、限制酶切位分析、溶解度掃描，以及從 UniProt、NCBI、RCSB PDB、AlphaFold、PubMed 與 Europe PMC 擷取資料；ExecutionManager 則負責把運算工作送往本機、SSH 或 Slurm 後端。平台提供三種前端：FastAPI 網頁介面、Textual TUI 與 CLI，全部採自備金鑰、不限模型，可對接任何 OpenAI 相容端點。團隊同時釋出了 P. putida 手冊（含實驗流程）以及經過整理、可直接用於 Golden Gate 的 pBBR1MCS-2 載體至 iGEM Registry。","stack":["COBRApy","GLPK","iJN1463 genome-scale model","FoldX","ThermoMPNN","ProteinMPNN embeddings","ConSurf","GROMACS","amber99sb-ildn / TIP3P","AutoDock Vina","Python 3.11","SQLite (WAL)","FastAPI","Textual TUI","Slurm / SSH job submission","React","Three.js / WebGL","Open Babel"],"techniques":["Flux balance analysis","Genome-scale metabolic model extension","Hinze-Kolmogorov droplet-breakup scaling","Film-theory interfacial mass transfer","Micellar solubilization modelling","Michaelis-Menten uptake kinetics","Bisection root-finding","Sensitivity analysis over droplet size","ddG ensemble prediction","Molecular dynamics (RMSF, native-contact persistence)","Ligand docking","LLM agent harness with phase-gated state machine","Ablation-based evaluation (4 regimes, 6 arms)","Rubric scoring by two independent judges","Techno-economic analysis","Life cycle assessment","HAZOP / P&ID process safety analysis"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education is organised around four stated principles - Access, Adapt, Engage, Extend - and each initiative is written up against one of them. The team ran bilingual (English/French) sessions for 370+ children aged 4-13 in the Ottawa-Carleton District School Board's International and Indigenous Languages Program summer school, reached 70 more through the Ottawa Catholic School Board, and visited AcadeCap International School for ages 4-7. Original hands-on activities include Lava Lamps (oil properties), The Art of Consortia (a collaborative mural standing in for microbial division of labour), Mix and Match Genes, The Power of Bacterial DNA, and a Heavy vs Light Oil worksheet. For durability they published a free interactive children's magazine, Bio-Builder, distributed through local Ottawa public libraries explicitly to reach low-income families who cannot buy such resources, plus a demo list, infographics, a science and research podcast, and a full downloadable resource library of presentations and worksheets so the activities run without the team present. They also hosted the Great Canadian iGEM Incubator poster competition (with QGEM) and the Great Canadian Meetup pitch competition, both with published scoring rubrics.","publicEngagement_zh":"教育工作圍繞四項明定原則展開，即觸及（Access）、調適（Adapt）、參與（Engage）、延伸（Extend），每項活動都對應其中一項撰寫成果。團隊在 Ottawa-Carleton District School Board 的 International and Indigenous Languages Program 暑期學校，為 370 位以上 4 至 13 歲兒童舉辦英法雙語課程，又透過 Ottawa Catholic School Board 再觸及 70 人，並造訪 AcadeCap International School 面向 4 至 7 歲學童。原創的動手活動包括 Lava Lamps（油的性質）、The Art of Consortia（以共同創作壁畫類比微生物的分工）、Mix and Match Genes、The Power of Bacterial DNA，以及一份 Heavy vs Light Oil 學習單。為了讓成果能持續，團隊出版了免費的互動式兒童雜誌 Bio-Builder，並明確選擇透過渥太華當地公共圖書館發行，以觸及買不起這類資源的低收入家庭；此外還有示範清單、資訊圖表、一檔科學與研究播客，以及一座可完整下載的資源庫，收錄簡報與學習單，讓這些活動在團隊不在場時也能照樣進行。團隊另主辦了 Great Canadian iGEM Incubator 海報競賽（與 QGEM 合辦）以及 Great Canadian Meetup 提案競賽，兩者都公開了評分量表。","ihp":"21 conversations across seven categories, each logged in the same three-part structure: why we went, what we heard, what we changed. The changes are concrete. Dr. Jinwen Chen (Natural Resources Canada, CanmetENERGY-Devon) and Dr. Stephen Larter (Calgary, petroleum geochemist) both told the team to abandon heavy diluted bitumen for diesel because of viscosity, mass-transfer and emulsion-separation barriers, and because diesel carries a hard <10 ppm sulfur limit and concentrated refractory DBTs - the team moved its entire target stream to diesel polishing. Dr. Rasha Maal-Bared warned that viscous crude mixes in localised laminar flow, which put static mixing elements and bioreactor sizing into the continuous-flow design. Patrick Lumley (Safe Sulphur Systems, 33 years in sulfur recovery) said the aqueous sulfite byproduct needs pH control to prevent SO2 release and that Claus-plant load reduction is economically worthless - so a pH control loop went into the P&ID and the business case was rebuilt around hydrogen savings and reduced hydrotreating severity instead of sulfur throughput. Larter's warning about microbially influenced corrosion added corrosion and material-compatibility criteria to the reactor design. Faculty of Engineering Design Day feedback forced the pivot from a full HDS-replacement narrative to the complementary polishing model. Dr. Corrie DaCosta, a protein chemist, was consulted specifically about what Cofactor's output report must contain to be usable by the person doing the engineering, and the report format changed as a result.","ihp_zh":"七個類別、共 21 場對話，每一場都以相同的三段式結構記錄：我們為何去談、我們聽到了什麼、我們改了什麼。這些改動都很具體。Dr. Jinwen Chen（Natural Resources Canada, CanmetENERGY-Devon）與 Dr. Stephen Larter（Calgary，石油地球化學家）都建議團隊放棄重質稀釋瀝青、改做柴油，理由是黏度、質傳與乳化分離上的障礙，以及柴油有硬性的 <10 ppm 含硫上限且難脫除的 DBT 濃度較高，於是團隊把整個目標物流改為柴油精製。Dr. Rasha Maal-Bared 提醒，黏稠原油會以局部層流的方式混合，這一點把靜態混合元件與生物反應器尺寸納入了連續流設計。Patrick Lumley（Safe Sulphur Systems，於硫回收領域有 33 年經驗）指出，水相的亞硫酸鹽副產物需要 pH 控制以避免釋出 SO2，而減輕 Claus 製程負載在經濟上毫無價值，於是 P&ID 中加入了一個 pH 控制迴圈，商業論述也從硫處理量改為重建在節省氫氣與降低加氫處理嚴苛度之上。Larter 對微生物影響腐蝕的提醒，為反應器設計增加了腐蝕與材料相容性的準則。工學院 Design Day 的回饋，則促使團隊從「完全取代 HDS」的敘事轉向互補式的精製模式。團隊還特地向蛋白質化學家 Dr. Corrie DaCosta 請教 Cofactor 的輸出報告必須包含什麼內容，才能讓真正動手做工程的人用得上，報告格式也因此修改。","realWorld":"A fully worked commercialization case. Market sizing: TAM ~$3.1B (global HDS catalyst market), SAM ~$66M (Canada's 2.2% share, 16 refineries, ~2M bbl/day), SOM ~$1.4M from a single-refinery side-stream demo at a $0.40/bbl royalty on a 10,000 bbl/day stream. Revenue model is per-barrel licensing royalties, validated in conversation with an operations and project engineer. A techno-economic analysis compares BDS against HDS CAPEX of $16-42M USD for a 20,000-25,000 bbl/day refinery and projects 50-60% CAPEX reduction from eliminating high-pressure hydrogen hardware; a life cycle assessment with a declared system boundary and BDS/HDS inventories backs the environmental claim rather than asserting it. A staged timeline runs from proof of concept (2026) through publication and NSERC Alliance / Mitacs Accelerate / CRIN non-dilutive funding (2027), pilot demonstration on real feedstock plus formal pre-engagement with Environment and Climate Change Canada under New Substances Notification regulations for contained LMO deployment (2028-29), to licensing (2030+) and expansion into biodenitrogenation. The team deliberately targets smaller, older refineries facing Euro V limits with constrained hydrogen capacity rather than major oil sands operators, on Lumley's advice, and flags biogas producers as a faster early-revenue path. Risk analysis, SWOT, Business Model Canvas and a competitive positioning matrix are all published, and the team is explicit that Nulfur is harm reduction during the energy transition - \"a bridge, not a destination\".","realWorld_zh":"一份完整做到底的商業化論證。市場規模：TAM 約 31 億美元（全球 HDS 觸媒市場）、SAM 約 6,600 萬美元（加拿大佔 2.2%，16 座煉油廠，約 200 萬桶/日）、SOM 約 140 萬美元，來自單一煉油廠側流示範，以 10,000 桶/日的物流按每桶 $0.40 收取授權金計算。營收模式為按桶計價的授權金，並在與一位營運與專案工程師的對話中得到驗證。技術經濟分析把 BDS 與 HDS 相比，後者在 20,000 至 25,000 桶/日規模的煉油廠需 1,600 萬至 4,200 萬美元的資本支出，並推估取消高壓氫氣設備可減少 50-60% 資本支出；一份具明確系統邊界並附 BDS/HDS 清單的生命週期評估，支撐了環境效益的說法，而不是只是斷言。分階段時程由概念驗證（2026）、發表論文與申請 NSERC Alliance / Mitacs Accelerate / CRIN 等非稀釋性資金（2027）、以真實進料進行先導示範並依《新物質通報》法規就封閉式 LMO 部署正式向 Environment and Climate Change Canada 進行事前溝通（2028-29），到技術授權（2030 年以後）與擴展至生物脫氮。團隊依 Lumley 的建議，刻意以面臨 Euro V 限值且氫氣產能受限的中小型、老舊煉油廠為目標，而不是大型油砂業者，並指出沼氣生產者是更快取得初期營收的途徑。風險分析、SWOT、商業模式圖（Business Model Canvas）與競爭定位矩陣全部公開，團隊也明白表示 Nulfur 是能源轉型期間的傷害減緩，「一座橋，而非終點」。","partners":["Natural Resources Canada (CanmetENERGY-Devon)","Environment and Climate Change Canada, Low Carbon Fuels Division","Safe Sulphur Systems Ltd.","CDM Smith","Spanish National Research Council (CSIC), Systems Biology Program","Bedford Institute of Oceanography, Fisheries and Oceans Canada","Institute for Oil Sands Innovation / University of Alberta","University of Calgary","Queen's University","Arabian Gulf University","Hawk & Squirrel Innovation Inc.","Ottawa-Carleton District School Board (IILP Summer Program)","Ottawa Catholic School Board","AcadeCap International School","Ottawa Public Libraries","uOttawa eHub RevUp Circuit","MindFuel Tech Futures Challenge","QGEM (Great Canadian iGEM Incubator)","Clean Resource Innovation Network (CRIN)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6077/wiki/dry-lab/protein-engineering/fig-3.svg","caption":"Predictor-agreement scatter for 437 scored DszB mutations: the shaded quadrant is where FoldX and ThermoMPNN both call a substitution stabilising, enlarged to label the five variants advanced to the wet lab.","caption_zh":"437 個評分過的 DszB 突變的預測器一致性散布圖：加底色的象限是 FoldX 與 ThermoMPNN 同時判定該取代具穩定化效果的區域，放大後標示出推進到濕實驗的五個變異體。","credit":"Team UOttawa, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6077/wiki/dry-lab/cofactor/figures/fig-4b.avif","caption":"The Cofactor GUI - a local FastAPI web interface over the agentic protein engineering platform, showing chat, hypothesis and evidence views, job tracking and artifact browsing.","caption_zh":"Cofactor 的圖形介面，一個架在代理式蛋白質工程平台之上的本機 FastAPI 網頁介面，可見對話、假說與證據檢視、工作追蹤與產出檔案瀏覽。","credit":"Team UOttawa, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6077/wiki/dry-lab/consortia/fig-3.avif","caption":"Rate gain in DBT uptake from interfacial-area enhancement and micellar solubilization in isolation and combined; the shaded region is the synergy in excess of the product of the two isolated effects.","caption_zh":"界面面積增加與微胞增溶分別單獨作用與兩者併用時，DBT 攝取速率的增益；加底色的區域是超出兩個單獨效果相乘的協同作用部分。","credit":"Team UOttawa, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6077/wiki/education/adapt/art-consortia/pxl-20260716-173536329-mp.avif","caption":"The Art of Consortia activity in the Ottawa-Carleton District School Board summer language programme, where children build a shared mural to learn how a microbial consortium divides labour.","caption_zh":"在 Ottawa-Carleton District School Board 暑期語言課程中進行的 The Art of Consortia 活動，孩童共同創作一幅壁畫，藉此認識微生物群落如何分工。","credit":"Team UOttawa, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6077/wiki/process/igem-p-id-final.avif","caption":"Process and instrumentation diagram for the full-scale biodesulfurization plant, including the pH control loop added after Patrick Lumley warned that uncontrolled sulfite pH would release SO2.","caption_zh":"全規模生物脫硫廠的製程與儀控圖（P&ID），其中包含在 Patrick Lumley 提醒未受控制的亞硫酸鹽 pH 會釋出 SO2 之後才加入的 pH 控制迴圈。","credit":"Team UOttawa, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Copy uOttawa's human-practices template literally: a single page where every one of 21 stakeholder conversations is logged in the same three fields - why we went, what we heard, what we changed - with the change written as a specific design edit (a pH loop in the P&ID, a switch of feedstock, static mixers). It costs nothing to adopt, makes a student team's reasoning auditable, and is the clearest way a school research centre can show that outside input actually moved the project rather than decorating it.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"照字面抄下 uOttawa 的人類實踐範本：用單一頁面，把 21 場利害關係人對話全部以相同的三個欄位記錄下來，也就是我們為何去談、我們聽到了什麼、我們改了什麼，而「改了什麼」要寫成具體的設計變更（P&ID 中的一個 pH 控制迴圈、換掉進料、加裝靜態混合器）。採用它不花任何成本，卻能讓學生團隊的推理過程可被稽核，也是一個校內研究中心最清楚的方式，用以證明外部意見確實推動了專案，而不只是拿來裝飾。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/uottawa/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uottawa/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/uottawa/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/uottawa/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/uottawa/alternative-platform","https://2026.igem.wiki/uottawa/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/uottawa/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/uottawa/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/uottawa/process-design-and-analysis","https://2026.igem.wiki/uottawa/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/uottawa/parts","https://2026.igem.wiki/uottawa/gcm","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uottawa/cofactor"],"rank":110},"6078":{"team":"UPF-Barcelona","id":"6078","section":"Undergrad","country":"Spain","village":"Food & Agriculture","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/upf-barcelona/","projectTitle":"Vinesys","projectTitle_zh":"Vinesys","tagline":"Where the rain runs out, the roots hold on: engineering root-associated Bacillus subtilis to hold water around grapevine roots.","tagline_zh":"雨水用盡之處，根系仍然守住：改造根際共生的 Bacillus subtilis，把水留在葡萄藤根部周圍。","summary":"Vinesys engineers Bacillus subtilis to colonise the grapevine rhizosphere and overexpress gamma-PGA, a water-retaining biopolymer, plus ACC deaminase to trim the drought-stress hormone precursor ACC, forming a thin hydration shell where the bacterium attaches to the root. Drought is detected by a two-layer switch: an osmolarity-responsive promoter plus a salt-dependent intein (HutMCM2) that the team re-engineered in silico to splice at the roughly 600-725 mM intracellular K+ that B. subtilis actually reaches, rather than its native 1.5 M. The dry lab produced three distinct deliverables: RK4 solver, a standalone no-code genetic-circuit designer and simulator; a documented molecular-dynamics pipeline for tuning salt-dependent proteins; and iGEMforge, a Claude Code plugin of four research skills that they evaluated honestly and then declined to use for project decisions. Awards came for Software, Model and Education.","summary_zh":"Vinesys 改造 Bacillus subtilis，使其定殖於葡萄藤根際並過量表現保水生物聚合物 gamma-PGA，同時表現 ACC deaminase 以削減乾旱逆境荷爾蒙前驅物 ACC，在細菌附著於根部之處形成一層薄薄的保水殼。乾旱以雙層開關偵測：一個對滲透壓有反應的啟動子，加上一個依賴鹽濃度的內含肽（HutMCM2）；團隊以電腦重新改造該內含肽，使其在 B. subtilis 實際可達到的約 600-725 mM 胞內 K+ 濃度下進行剪接，而非其天然的 1.5 M。乾實驗產出三項明確的成果：RK4 solver，一套獨立、免寫程式的基因迴路設計與模擬工具；一條有完整文件的分子動力學流程，用於調校依賴鹽濃度的蛋白質；以及 iGEMforge，一個內含四項研究技能的 Claude Code 外掛——他們誠實地評估了它，然後決定不拿它來做專題決策。獲獎項目為軟體、模型與教育。","awards":["Best Software — Winner (Undergrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"RK4 solver is a desktop Python application with a GUI built in Dear PyGui, structured as three partially independent modules (GUI, compiler, solver) so the solver can be driven from Python without drawing anything on screen. It ships for Windows, macOS and Linux. Interchange is handled by two formats: a readable personal JSON format and SBML Level 3, which gives round-trip compatibility with COPASI and Tellurium. The molecular-dynamics pipeline runs ColabFold/AlphaFold for structures, FoldX for stability screening, MAFFT and BLAST for candidate selection, UCSF Chimera for inspection, and OpenMM with Amber force fields (tleap setup) for the simulations. iGEMforge is a Claude Code plugin: four Markdown SKILL files plus a couple of Python scripts in a folder, deliberately with no subagents, hooks or custom MCP servers.","frameworks_zh":"RK4 solver 是一套桌面 Python 應用程式，介面以 Dear PyGui 建構，架構分成三個部分獨立的模組（介面、編譯器、解算器），因此解算器可以直接用 Python 驅動、不必在畫面上畫出任何東西。它提供 Windows、macOS 與 Linux 版本。資料交換支援兩種格式：一種可讀的自訂 JSON 格式，以及 SBML Level 3，後者讓它能與 COPASI 和 Tellurium 雙向往返。分子動力學流程以 ColabFold/AlphaFold 取得結構，以 FoldX 做穩定性篩選，以 MAFFT 與 BLAST 挑選候選，以 UCSF Chimera 檢視，並以 OpenMM 搭配 Amber 力場（由 tleap 建置）執行模擬。iGEMforge 則是一個 Claude Code 外掛：四個 Markdown SKILL 檔加上幾支 Python 腳本放在一個資料夾裡，刻意不使用子代理、hook 或自訂 MCP 伺服器。","dataviz":"RK4 solver's results screen plots species concentrations while every parameter has a live slider that takes effect during the running simulation, which is the core interaction idea. The editor uses blocks whose icons follow SBOL Visual glyphs, with input pins always on the left and output pins on the right so links read left to right, collapsible blocks, and a diagnostics/warnings pane with connection rules that refuse to let you build an invalid circuit. The wiki itself is built as explanatory interactive JavaScript rather than static figures: an in-browser Euler-vs-RK4 comparison on x'' = -x, a step-through animation of the solver's operator stack, a replayable eval harness showing the same prompt answered with and without an iGEMforge skill, and a hoverable stakeholder map on the entrepreneurship page.","dataviz_zh":"RK4 solver 的結果畫面會繪製各物種濃度，而每個參數都配有即時滑桿，在模擬執行中就會生效，這是整個互動設計的核心想法。編輯器使用方塊，其圖示沿用 SBOL Visual 的字符，輸入接點一律在左、輸出接點在右，使連線由左讀到右；方塊可折疊，並有一個診斷／警示面板，其連接規則會直接拒絕讓你搭出不合法的迴路。wiki 本身是以解說性的互動 JavaScript 做成、而非靜態圖表：一個在瀏覽器內針對 x'' = -x 比較 Euler 與 RK4 的示範、一段逐步播放解算器運算子堆疊的動畫、一個可重播的評估面板展示同一道提示在有與沒有 iGEMforge 技能下的回答差異，以及創業頁面上一張可滑過查看的利害關係人地圖。","datascience":"The solver was validated numerically against COPASI: three example circuits were exported to SBML and re-simulated in COPASI under LSODA with identical parameters, initial concentrations and simulation time, and every quantity that means the same thing in both tools agreed within 0.21%, most within 0.01%. The apparent 13.4% and 98.5% discrepancies on free mazF and mazE were traced to a labelling difference in rapid-equilibrium binding, not integration error, and resolved by comparing totals (mazF + 2*FEF, mazE + FEF), which then matched within 0.01% and 0.09%. iGEMforge was evaluated in two rounds: 11 hand-graded assertion tests in round one, then 28 cases run three times per arm (with-skill vs. without-skill) using Claude Code's `claude plugin eval` with an LLM-as-a-judge against team-written rubrics, including real cases, synthetic cases with deliberately planted flaws, and 'silence' cases where a skill should stay out of the way. The MD work used replicas, a wild-type positive control at its known 1.5 M threshold, an uncharged no-effect control, and re-ran its analysis under several different attack-distance cutoffs to show the conclusion did not depend on one arbitrary value.","datascience_zh":"解算器以數值方式對 COPASI 驗證：三個範例迴路匯出為 SBML，並在相同參數、起始濃度與模擬時間下用 COPASI 的 LSODA 重跑，凡是在兩套工具中意義相同的量值都在 0.21% 以內吻合，多數在 0.01% 以內。游離 mazF 與 mazE 上看似 13.4% 與 98.5% 的差異，被追溯為快速平衡結合下標示方式的差別、而非積分誤差，改以總量比較（mazF + 2*FEF、mazE + FEF）後即分別在 0.01% 與 0.09% 以內吻合。iGEMforge 經過兩輪評估：第一輪是 11 項人工評分的斷言測試，第二輪則是 28 個案例、每個組別（有技能對無技能）各跑三次，使用 Claude Code 的 `claude plugin eval`，以 LLM 當評審、對照隊員自行撰寫的評分準則，案例涵蓋真實情境、刻意植入瑕疪的合成情境，以及技能應當不出手的「沉默」情境。分子動力學工作使用了重複模擬、一個在已知 1.5 M 門檻下的野生型正對照、一個不帶電的無效應對照，並在數個不同的作用距離截斷值下重跑分析，以證明結論不取決於某一個任意選定的數值。","software":"RK4 solver is the main tool: a free, open-source, cross-platform application that turns a hand-drawn genetic circuit into a running ODE simulation with no code at all, aimed squarely at iGEM teams, high-school and undergraduate students, and explicitly not at replacing COPASI or SimBiology. Eight block types are implemented (production with Hill activation/repression, degradation, complex formation in rapid-equilibrium or kinetic mode, extracellular species with six dosing regimes, cell entry, export, catalysis with Michaelis-Menten or mass action, and a link probe), and the compiler translates the drawing into a flat list of stack operators which the solver evaluates with Euler or 4th-order Runge-Kutta. The architecture is worth copying: the translator sorts each block's contribution by the species it points to rather than by the block's own species, a redesign forced by discovering that complex formation was writing its negative terms into the wrong derivative. It was validated twice, against COPASI numerically and against the team's own biocontainment toxin-antitoxin model biologically, and it was user-tested, with non-expert testers building and tuning a toggle switch in 5 to 20 minutes after a short introduction to the notation. Limitations are stated plainly on the wiki (deterministic only, partial SBML import, custom block unfinished, GUI not yet as intuitive as they want) with a three-horizon roadmap including SBOL-based integration with the iGEM Registry that would pull part parameters in and mark any user override as traceably overwritten. Source: https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/upf-barcelona/upf-software (team repo https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/upf-barcelona). It is distributed as a downloadable cross-platform application, not a hosted web service, so there is no click-and-use URL. The second tool, iGEMforge, is the most interesting negative result of the season: a Claude Code plugin of four skills (scientific-evidence, experimental-design, mathematical-modeling, bio-wiki-animations) built over two DBTL cycles, in which round-one hand-grading suggested the skills helped (bio-wiki-animations 12/13 assertions with the skill against 5/12 without) but round two with three runs per arm and an LLM judge showed no clear average gain (experimental-design -0.11, scientific-evidence +0.04, mathematical-modeling no clear difference), at substantially higher token cost (309k vs 224k; 468k vs 201k). Testing revealed that three of four skills intermittently stalled waiting on user confirmation and returned nothing; cycle two fixed it with a single rule written into the skills ('state the assumption or caveat and continue'), which restored output in 3 of 3 runs but still did not beat the base model. The team's conclusion, published on the wiki, is that the evidence was too thin to use iGEMforge for Vinesys decisions, and they list cost, privacy, over-trust and installation risks explicitly.","software_zh":"RK4 solver 是主要工具：一套免費、開源、跨平台的應用程式，能把手繪的基因迴路變成可執行的 ODE 模擬，完全不需寫程式，明確針對 iGEM 隊伍、高中與大學部學生，也明確表示不是要取代 COPASI 或 SimBiology。已實作八種方塊類型（具 Hill 活化／抑制的生產、降解、以快速平衡或動力學模式處理的複合物形成、含六種投藥方式的胞外物種、進入細胞、輸出、以 Michaelis-Menten 或質量作用處理的催化，以及一個連線探針），編譯器把圖轉成一份扁平的堆疊運算子清單，解算器再以 Euler 或四階 Runge-Kutta 求解。它的架構值得借鏡：轉譯器是依每個方塊所指向的物種、而非方塊自身的物種來歸類其貢獻項，這項重新設計是在發現複合物形成會把負項寫進錯誤的微分式之後被迫做的。它驗證了兩次，一次是數值上對 COPASI，一次是生物上對團隊自己的生物圍堵毒素－抗毒素模型；也做過使用者測試，非專家測試者在簡短介紹符號後，於 5 到 20 分鐘內就能搭出並調校一個雙穩態開關。限制在 wiki 上直白列出（僅支援確定性模擬、SBML 匯入不完整、自訂方塊尚未完成、介面還沒有他們想要的那麼直覺），並附上一份三階段路線圖，其中包括以 SBOL 為基礎與 iGEM Registry 整合，可自動帶入元件參數，並把使用者的任何覆寫標記為可追溯的覆寫。原始碼：https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/upf-barcelona/upf-software （團隊 repo https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/upf-barcelona ）。它以可下載的跨平台應用程式形式散布，不是架在網路上的服務，因此沒有可以點開就用的網址。第二項工具 iGEMforge 是本季最有意思的負面結果：一個包含四項技能（scientific-evidence、experimental-design、mathematical-modeling、bio-wiki-animations）的 Claude Code 外掛，歷經兩輪 DBTL 開發；第一輪的人工評分看起來技能有幫助（bio-wiki-animations 在有技能時通過 12/13 項斷言，無技能時 5/12），但第二輪每組跑三次並加上 LLM 評審後，顯示平均並無明確增益（experimental-design -0.11、scientific-evidence +0.04、mathematical-modeling 無明確差異），而 token 成本卻顯著更高（309k 對 224k；468k 對 201k）。測試還發現四項技能中有三項會間歇卡住、等待使用者確認而什麼都不回；第二輪以寫進技能的一條規則修掉（「說明該假設或保留條件並繼續」），使 3 次執行都恢復輸出，但仍未勝過基礎模型。團隊公開在 wiki 上的結論是，證據太薄弱，不足以用 iGEMforge 來做 Vinesys 的決策，並明確列出成本、隱私、過度信任與安裝等風險。","stack":["Python","Dear PyGui","SBML Level 3","SBOL Visual","JSON","COPASI (validation target)","Tellurium","OpenMM","Amber force field / tleap","ColabFold","AlphaFold","FoldX","MAFFT","BLAST","UCSF Chimera","Claude Code plugin (Markdown skills + Python)","claude plugin eval","iGEM GitLab","JavaScript (interactive wiki figures)"],"techniques":["ODE modelling of genetic circuits","4th-order Runge-Kutta and Euler integration","stack-machine operator compilation of differential equations","Hill activation/repression kinetics","rapid-equilibrium and kinetic complex formation","Michaelis-Menten catalysis","molecular dynamics with near-attack-conformation (NAC) readout","ddG stability screening","pLDDT/PAE structure confidence assessment","LLM-as-a-judge evaluation with pre-written rubrics","A/B testing with planted-flaw synthetic cases","SBML round-trip cross-validation"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education is organised around an explicit six-step method the team named WONDER (Who, Objectives, Notice, Dialogue, Evidence, Record), whose last step feeds back into the first like a DBTL cycle, and which is rooted in Catalan educacio del lleure (leisure education) practice that several team members came from through scouting. Audiences were plotted on two axes, age and prior synbio interest, and the session language (Catalan, Spanish or English) was chosen from the barrier they wanted to lower. Each session required a before-and-after measure, at least one artefact participants made themselves, a rubric completed within 24 hours, and a written summary within a day covering what actually happened and what they would change, published on the wiki so other teams can run the session without them. Activities spanned a MiniGEM where pre-university students designed their own synthetic biology projects, an escape room at CosmoCaixa, La Nit de la Recerca, the UPF Summer School, a role-play at the PRBB, SynBYSS, Centre Civic Guinardo, scout groups (Cau La Floresta) and several schools, plus a round table with iGEM UB.","publicEngagement_zh":"教育工作圍繞團隊自行命名的六步方法 WONDER（Who、Objectives、Notice、Dialogue、Evidence、Record）展開，最後一步會像 DBTL 循環那樣回饋到第一步；這套方法源自加泰隆尼亞的 educació del lleure（休閒教育）實務，幾位隊員是透過童軍活動帶著這個背景進來的。對象依兩個軸向配置——年齡與既有的合成生物學興趣——使用的語言（加泰隆尼亞語、西班牙語或英語）則依他們想降低的哪一道門檻來決定。每一場活動都必須有前後對照的量測、至少一件由參與者自己動手做出的成品、在 24 小時內填完的評分表，以及一天內寫成的書面摘要，說明實際發生了什麼、以及下次會改什麼，並公開在 wiki 上，讓其他隊伍不需要他們在場也能照著辦。活動包括一場讓大學前學生自己設計合成生物學專題的 MiniGEM、在 CosmoCaixa 的密室逃脫、La Nit de la Recerca、UPF 暑期學校、在 PRBB 的角色扮演、SynBYSS、Centre Cívic Guinardó、童軍團（Cau La Floresta）與數所學校，另有一場與 iGEM UB 的圓桌。","ihp":"Human practices is written as three acts with a stated principle of intentionality: every design choice should have a reason statable to an outsider, and where there is none they say so. 32 people outside the team across 8 countries, 52 documented exchanges and 103 survey respondents, with 9 of 10 project phases opened to outside input. The first grower they met corrected their founding premise, that drought was killing Catalan vineyards, by explaining that summer water stress is necessary for proper ripening and the real damage is to next season's crop; a second grower said vines did die in the first drought year, and the team kept both rather than reconciling them. A gamma-PGA geneticist in Pavia shrank the central claim from bulk soil water retention to a local hydration shell at the root. A Bordeaux researcher set a condition the design cannot meet (no deficit at flowering, moderate deficit later) and the team publishes it as a limit, not a feature. Two further conventions are worth copying: advice they chose not to follow stays on the page with the reason, and disagreements they could not resolve are printed unresolved. They also disclose that one advisor, Dr. Carolina Elizondo, holds an iGEM role, so readers can weigh her input.","ihp_zh":"人類實踐寫成三幕，並明示一項「刻意為之」的原則：每個設計選擇都應該有一個能對外人說清楚的理由，沒有理由的地方就直接說沒有。團隊外共 32 人、跨 8 個國家，52 次有紀錄的往來與 103 份問卷回覆，10 個專題階段中有 9 個開放外部意見。他們見到的第一位果農就糾正了他們的立論前提——他們原以為乾旱正在殺死加泰隆尼亞的葡萄園——說明夏季的水分逆境對正常成熟是必要的，真正受損的是下一季的收成；第二位果農則說在乾旱的第一年葡萄藤確實有死亡，團隊把兩種說法都保留下來，沒有去調和。一位在帕維亞研究 gamma-PGA 的遺傳學家把核心主張從整體土壤保水縮小為根部局部的保水殼。一位波爾多的研究者設下了這個設計做不到的條件（開花期不可有水分虧缺、之後可中度虧缺），團隊把它當成限制、而非賣點公開出來。另外兩項慣例值得借鏡：他們選擇不採納的建議連同理由留在頁面上，而無法化解的分歧就以未解決的狀態印出來。他們也揭露其中一位顧問 Dr. Carolina Elizondo 在 iGEM 內擔任職務，讓讀者得以衡量她的意見。","realWorld":"The entrepreneurship page is explicit that the current value is knowledge, education and visibility rather than product sales, with the project at contained laboratory proof of concept and no environmental release. More than 50 organisations were contacted since June 2026; wineries Clos Montblanc (DO Conca de Barberà), Sumarroca and Vallformosa (DO Penedès) were interviewed about how a new input would fit existing practice, with Vallformosa noting that acting at root level could mean lower adoption friction. IRTA, the Catalan government's agrifood research institute, reviewed the approach against its own Penedès soil-and-water initiative and provided winery contacts. The regulatory finding was that certification, not GMO status, is the binding constraint, and the business work reached a cost per hectare and a route to a field trial. Scale context: 52,000 ha of Catalan vineyard, 8,500 viticulturists, EUR 3.27 bn annual turnover, reservoirs at 14.3% in 2024.","realWorld_zh":"創業頁面明確表示目前的價值在於知識、教育與能見度，而不是產品銷售，專題處於封閉實驗室的概念驗證階段，沒有任何環境釋放。自 2026 年 6 月起接觸了超過 50 個組織；酒莊 Clos Montblanc（DO Conca de Barberà）、Sumarroca 與 Vallformosa（DO Penedès）接受訪談，談一項新投入品要如何融入既有做法，其中 Vallformosa 指出在根部層次作用可能代表採用阻力較低。加泰隆尼亞政府的農食研究機構 IRTA 以其自身的 Penedès 土壤與水計畫審視了這套做法，並提供酒莊人脈。法規上的發現是，真正的約束條件是認證、而不是基改身分；商業評估則推算出每公頃成本與一條走向田間試驗的路徑。規模背景：加泰隆尼亞葡萄園 52,000 公頃、8,500 位葡萄種植者、年營業額 32.7 億歐元，2024 年水庫蓄水率 14.3%。","partners":["IRTA (Institut de Recerca i Tecnologia Agroalimentàries)","Celler Clos Montblanc","Sumarroca","Vallformosa","Ajuntament de Barcelona (Departament de Ciència i Innovació)","CosmoCaixa","PRBB","iGEM UB","Anthropic (sponsor)","University of Pavia (gamma-PGA genetics)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6078/wiki/dry-lab/software/figure6.avif","caption":"Screenshot of the RK4 solver editor with the biocontainment toxin-antitoxin circuit built from linked blocks.","caption_zh":"RK4 solver 編輯器的畫面截圖，圖中是以連結方塊搭建的生物圍堵毒素－抗毒素迴路。","credit":"Team UPF-Barcelona, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6078/wiki/dry-lab/software/figure7.avif","caption":"RK4 solver output: internal resveratrol, mazF and FEF levels over time under sinusoidal resveratrol production.","caption_zh":"RK4 solver 的輸出：在正弦式的白藜蘆醇生產下，胞內白藜蘆醇、mazF 與 FEF 濃度隨時間的變化。","credit":"Team UPF-Barcelona, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6078/wiki/dry-lab/software/figure4.avif","caption":"The first hand-drawn sketches of the RK4 solver blocks, designed in the style of electronic circuit diagrams.","caption_zh":"RK4 solver 方塊最早的手繪草圖，設計上刻意採用電子電路圖的風格。","credit":"Team UPF-Barcelona, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Validate a simulator against the established tool in the field and publish the discrepancy table, including the one that looked like a 98% error and turned out to be a labelling difference, because that table is what makes a student-built solver trustworthy. Their AI work is the sharper lesson for a research centre: build the agent plugin, then actually A/B evaluate it with planted-flaw cases and an LLM judge, and be willing to publish that it did not beat the base model and that you therefore did not use it.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"把自己寫的模擬器拿去和該領域既有的標準工具對驗，並公開差異對照表，包括那個看起來像 98% 誤差、實際上只是標示方式不同的項目——因為正是這張表讓學生自建的解算器變得可信。他們的 AI 工作對研究中心而言是更鋭利的一課：先把代理人外掛做出來，再真的用植入瑕疪的案例與 LLM 評審做 A/B 評估，並且願意公開它沒有勝過基礎模型、因此自己也沒有採用。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/upf-barcelona/","https://2026.igem.wiki/upf-barcelona/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/upf-barcelona/igem-forge","https://2026.igem.wiki/upf-barcelona/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/upf-barcelona/dry-tips","https://2026.igem.wiki/upf-barcelona/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/upf-barcelona/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/upf-barcelona/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/upf-barcelona/description","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/upf-barcelona/upf-software"],"rank":26},"6089":{"team":"BAID-China","id":"6089","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/baid-china/","projectTitle":"Neurofilux","projectTitle_zh":"Neurofilux","tagline":"An AI-designed antibody sandwich assay for blood neurofilament light chain, for cheap non-invasive early screening of neurodegenerative disease","tagline_zh":"以 AI 設計抗體的血液神經絲輕鏈三明治免疫檢測，用於低成本、非侵入性的神經退化疾病早期篩檢","summary":"BAID-China built Neurofilux, a blood test for neurofilament light chain (NfL), a biomarker of neuronal damage that rises years before Alzheimer's or ALS symptoms appear but is currently detectable only by expensive, invasive or insufficiently sensitive methods. They expressed the NfL rod domain (residues 93-396) as antigen, used the generative model RFantibody to design candidate antibodies, screened them with a multi-objective scoring pipeline, validated eight candidates experimentally and found two pairs outperforming commercial antibodies in sandwich ELISA, then converted the validated antibodies into nanobodies for stability and cost. Their inclusivity work is organised around a self-defined 3A framework - Adaptation, Awareness, Accessibility - and centres on a tactile magnetic genetic-circuit kit for blind children, developed in two phases and donated to a school for the visually impaired.","summary_zh":"BAID-China 做出 Neurofilux，一項檢測血液中神經絲輕鏈（NfL）的檢驗。NfL 是神經元損傷的生物標記，在阿茲海默症或 ALS 症狀出現前數年就會上升，但目前只能靠昂貴、侵入性或靈敏度不足的方法偵測。他們表現 NfL 的 rod domain（第 93–396 號殘基）作為抗原，用生成式模型 RFantibody 設計候選抗體，以多目標評分流程篩選，實驗驗證八個候選，找出兩組在三明治 ELISA 中表現優於市售抗體的配對，再把已驗證的抗體轉換為奈米抗體以提升穩定性並降低成本。他們的包容性工作圍繞自訂的 3A 架構——Adaptation、Awareness、Accessibility——核心是一套給視障兒童的觸覺磁性基因迴路教具，分兩階段開發，最後捐贈給一所視障學校。","awards":["Inclusivity Award — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Self-defined 3A inclusivity framework (Adaptation: convert visually-presented science into tactile, auditory and interactive forms; Awareness: dispel stereotypes and spread barrier-free science; Accessibility: remove visual, language and technical thresholds), with every activity required to map onto at least one dimension. Grounded in a literature review citing Hayes and Proulx (2023) on barriers for visually impaired science students and CAST (2024) Universal Design for Learning, plus Design Thinking, Empathy Mapping and Universal Design concepts taught by an invited expert. Accessibility work was benchmarked against WCAG.","frameworks_zh":"自訂的 3A 包容性架構（Adaptation：把以視覺呈現的科學內容轉換為觸覺、聽覺與互動形式；Awareness：破除刻板印象並推廣無障礙科學；Accessibility：移除視覺、語言與技術門檻），並要求每一項活動至少對應其中一個面向。基礎來自一份文獻回顧，引用 Hayes 與 Proulx（2023）關於視障科學學生所面對障礙的研究，以及 CAST（2024）的通用學習設計，另外還有外聘專家講授的設計思考、同理心地圖與通用設計概念。無障礙工作則以 WCAG 作為對標基準。","dataviz":"All wiki charts redrawn in the eight-colour Okabe-Ito colour-blind-safe palette, chosen because each colour keeps enough luminance difference to stay readable in greyscale; the team published a colour-blindness simulation figure verifying that elements remain distinguishable under red-green, blue-yellow and total colour-blindness simulation.","dataviz_zh":"wiki 上所有圖表都改用八色的 Okabe-Ito 色盲友善配色，選用理由是每個顏色之間都保有足夠的亮度差，轉成灰階後仍可閱讀；該隊並公開一張色盲模擬圖，驗證在紅綠色盲、藍黃色盲與全色盲模擬下各元素仍可區辨。","datascience":"Multi-objective computational scoring to rank AI-generated antibody candidates by predicted sensitivity; comparative legal and building-code research across China, Egypt, Pakistan and the United States compiled into an open-access international accessibility database; pre-activity knowledge survey of junior and senior high school students on neurodegenerative disease awareness.","datascience_zh":"以多目標計算評分，依預測靈敏度排序 AI 生成的候選抗體；比較中國、埃及、巴基斯坦與美國的法規與建築規範研究，彙整成一個開放取用的國際無障礙資料庫；針對國中與高中學生進行活動前的神經退化疾病認知調查。","software":"RFantibody generative AI model used for de novo antibody design, followed by computational screening and virtual validation of nanobody conversions; a laboratory accessibility audit tool and evaluation form built on universal design principles; a wiki accessibility plugin offering a five-step text magnifier, a language switcher and one-click return-to-top, with semantic HTML restructured so screen readers can parse the navigation hierarchy.","software_zh":"使用 RFantibody 生成式 AI 模型進行全新抗體設計，接著對奈米抗體轉換版本做計算篩選與虛擬驗證；依通用設計原則建立一套實驗室無障礙稽核工具與評估表；一個 wiki 無障礙外掛，提供五級文字放大、語言切換與一鍵回到頂端，並重寫為語意化 HTML，讓螢幕閱讀器能解析導覽階層。","stack":["RFantibody (generative antibody design)","multi-objective computational screening","sandwich ELISA","Okabe-Ito colour palette","semantic HTML / screen-reader-compatible markup","WCAG","trilingual wiki (Chinese, English, French)"],"techniques":["NfL rod domain (93-396 aa) expression as antigen","antibody pair selection for sandwich ELISA","nanobody conversion","CDR loop design on dominant epitopes","planned digital ELISA at fg/mL sensitivity"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"BAID-China started from evidence rather than instinct: a literature review on STEM barriers for disabled students (high lab benches, reading instrument data, observing phenomena, the need for written or sign-language support) plus a field visit to Bethel China, a charity for preschool children with visual impairments, where they identified two concrete problems - classes run with several children to one teacher, which blocks understanding, and tactile picture books that deliver touch sensation but almost no actual knowledge content. Both findings set the agenda. First strand: a team member, Audrey, joined the iGEM community project 'Accessibility in Synbio Labs' at the iGEM Annual Community Day in early 2026 and led BAID-China's inclusivity group through Phase 1 (research and database development) and Phase 2 (lab audits) alongside iGEM members from China, Egypt, Pakistan and the United States. With team Concordia-Shanghai they researched China's Accessibility Environment Construction Law, the Law on the Protection of Persons with Disabilities and GB 55019-2021 General Specifications for Accessibility in Architecture and Municipal Engineering, focusing on doorway clearance and wheelchair turning diameter, and the national research sets were compiled into an open-access comparative international database. The audit tool was then reviewed by Chloe Franklin, a scientist who uses a wheelchair, whose feedback changed it substantially: replace the Yes/No/N/A format with a scale that reflects degrees of accessibility because wheelchair users' needs differ widely; add specific measurable criteria with dimensional requirements; and weight audit items by importance, since building entrances, elevators, emergency evacuation routes and restrooms are foundational while equipment height and storage can be adjusted more easily. The team logged her suggestions, took them to weekly meetings, produced a new version, and credits co-creators by name (Sami from Team Toronto 2026, Mohamed, Sophie and Linda). They are honest that pilot testing was not completed within the season and commit to continuing next year. Second strand, and the signature contribution: Chloe Franklin's remark that a beautiful accessible lab on a high floor of a building with no accessible elevator is meaningless pushed the team from physical access to information access. They built a tactile magnetic genetic-circuit kit in which each component is a distinct shape rather than a colour or diagram: two circles of different sizes for input signals (large = normal cell, small = cancer cell), a star for an activator, an X for a repressor, an arrow for a promoter, a rectangle for a gene, a semicircle for a terminator and a pentagon for the output (anticancer drug release). This was embedded in a 45-minute workshop of four activities, run five times for more than 110 participants in total. Activity One sent sighted participants into the team's own laboratory in a wheelchair, where they discovered the doorway was barely wider than the chair, a slope and uneven bricks blocked independent movement, and bench spacing left no turning room. Activity Two brought in David Doyle, Project Head of the Accessibility in Synbio Labs community project, to teach Design Thinking, Empathy Mapping and Universal Design - the point being that environments should be designed around users rather than users adapting to environments. Activity Three recreated a standard Chinese middle-school microscope exercise, but half the participants were denied visual access: one student described cell shapes, features and spatial arrangement in words while the others had to reconstruct the specimen on paper, which reliably failed, demonstrating that people can sit in the same classroom and receive very different amounts of information. Activity Four had blindfolded participants assemble, by touch alone, a circuit that releases a drug when cancer cells are detected but not when normal cells are present. Phase 1 feedback exposed real design flaws - unclear verbal instructions about logical relationships between blocks, and block shapes and sizes that were hard to grasp or distinguish - which taught the team that simply converting a visual circuit diagram into differently shaped magnets is not sufficient. For Phase 2 they contacted a Beijing school for the visually impaired and visited twice. The first visit was deliberately not a lesson: team members read biology picture books to the children, using a caterpillar's growth to introduce change in living things, while observing how the children used language to describe scientific phenomena and how they responded to different question types. Because the seven participating children were aged 3-8 and had no basis for promoters, terminators or expression regulation, the team stripped the terminology out and kept only the Input-Regulation-Output logic, recast as a 'sound machine': children explored block shapes by touch, assembled the machine, and a volunteer clapped three times as the audio output when it worked. The star block was introduced as the machine's 'good assistant' that makes it run and the X block as the 'bad assistant' that stops it, so activation and repression were learned through immediate auditory feedback. The kit was then donated to the school so teachers can keep using and adapting it for different ages. Third strand: wiki accessibility treated as a deliverable with real user testing. All charts were redrawn in the Okabe-Ito palette and verified against red-green, blue-yellow and total colour-blindness simulations; the page code was rebuilt with semantic tags so screen readers can identify headings, paragraphs and buttons; an accessibility plugin in the lower right corner offers five text sizes with line and character spacing adjusted in step so layout does not break when enlarged, aimed explicitly at elderly readers; and the entire project is translated into Chinese, English and French with two switching paths. The team then invited a person with red-green colour blindness, elderly users and non-native English speakers to test it and iterated on their feedback. Fourth strand: public science communication on neurodegenerative disease, prompted by a survey finding that most junior high school students did not know what neurodegenerative diseases are, associated them only with memory decline in the elderly, or said 'this has nothing to do with me', while high school students had the capacity but no systematic channel; an interview with the local health bureau director in the Guangying area established that medical staff, government and charities are all delivering information but public acceptance is low and prevention habits are not forming, partly because the material is monotonous and dependent on visual text.","publicEngagement_zh":"BAID-China 從證據而非直覺出發：先做了一份關於身障學生 STEM 障礙的文獻回顧（實驗檯過高、讀取儀器數據、觀察現象，以及對文字或手語支援的需求），再實地走訪 Bethel China 這個服務學齡前視障兒童的公益機構，在那裡指認出兩個具體問題——課程是幾個孩子配一位老師，這會阻礙理解；而觸覺繪本給得了觸感，卻幾乎沒有實際的知識內容。這兩項發現定下了後續的工作議程。第一條路線：隊員 Audrey 在 2026 年初的 iGEM Annual Community Day 加入 iGEM 社群專案「Accessibility in Synbio Labs」，並帶領 BAID-China 的包容性小組，與來自中國、埃及、巴基斯坦與美國的 iGEM 成員一起完成第 1 階段（研究與資料庫建置）與第 2 階段（實驗室稽核）。他們與 Concordia-Shanghai 隊共同研究中國的《無障礙環境建設法》、《殘疾人保障法》與 GB 55019-2021《建築與市政工程無障礙通用規範》，聚焦門口淨寬與輪椅迴轉直徑，各國的研究成果最後彙整成一個開放取用的國際比較資料庫。稽核工具隨後由使用輪椅的科學家 Chloe Franklin 審閱，她的意見帶來實質修改：把 Yes/No/N/A 的格式改成能反映無障礙程度的量尺，因為輪椅使用者的需求差異很大；加入附具體尺寸要求的可量測標準；並依重要性為稽核項目加權，因為建築入口、電梯、緊急疏散路線與衛浴是基礎條件，而設備高度與儲物位置相對容易調整。該隊把她的建議逐項記錄，帶進每週會議，產出新版本，並具名致謝共同創作者（Team Toronto 2026 的 Sami，以及 Mohamed、Sophie 與 Linda）。他們坦言試行測試並未在本賽季內完成，並承諾明年繼續。第二條路線，也是該隊的招牌貢獻：Chloe Franklin 說過，一間漂亮的無障礙實驗室若位於沒有無障礙電梯的高樓層，就毫無意義——這句話把團隊從實體通行推向資訊取得。他們做出一套觸覺磁性基因迴路教具，每個元件以不同形狀而非顏色或圖示區分：兩個大小不同的圓形代表輸入訊號（大 = 正常細胞，小 = 癌細胞）、星形是活化子、X 形是抑制子、箭頭是啟動子、長方形是基因、半圓是終止子、五邊形是輸出（釋放抗癌藥物）。這套教具嵌入一場 45 分鐘、四個活動的工作坊，共舉辦五場，累計超過 110 位參與者。活動一讓明眼參與者坐輪椅進入該隊自己的實驗室，他們發現門口只比輪椅寬一點、一道斜坡與不平整的磚面讓人無法自行通行，實驗檯間距也完全沒有迴轉空間。活動二請來「Accessibility in Synbio Labs」社群專案的負責人 David Doyle 講授設計思考、同理心地圖與通用設計——重點在於環境應該圍繞使用者來設計，而不是讓使用者去適應環境。活動三重現中國國中標準的顯微鏡實驗，但有一半參與者被剝奪視覺管道：由一位學生用言語描述細胞形狀、特徵與空間排列，其他人必須在紙上重建該標本，結果一律失敗，示範了人們可以坐在同一間教室，卻接收到差距極大的資訊量。活動四則讓戴眼罩的參與者純靠觸覺組裝一組迴路，使其在偵測到癌細胞時釋放藥物、在正常細胞存在時不釋放。第 1 階段的回饋暴露出真正的設計缺陷——關於積件之間邏輯關係的口頭說明不夠清楚，積件的形狀與大小也不易掌握或區辨——這讓該隊明白，單純把視覺迴路圖換成不同形狀的磁鐵並不足夠。第 2 階段他們聯繫北京一所視障學校，前後拜訪兩次。第一次刻意不上課：隊員為孩子朗讀生物繪本，用毛毛蟲的成長引入生物的變化，同時觀察孩子如何用語言描述科學現象、以及他們對不同問法的反應。因為參與的七位孩子年齡在 3 至 8 歲之間，對啟動子、終止子或表現調控毫無基礎，該隊把術語全部拿掉，只保留「輸入—調控—輸出」的邏輯，改寫成一台「聲音機器」：孩子用觸覺探索積件形狀、組裝機器，成功時由一位志工拍手三下作為聲音輸出。星形積件被介紹為讓機器運轉的「好幫手」，X 形積件則是讓它停下來的「壞幫手」，於是活化與抑制透過即時的聽覺回饋被學會。教具隨後捐給這所學校，讓老師能持續使用並針對不同年齡調整。第三條路線：把 wiki 無障礙當成一項交付成果，並做了真實的使用者測試。所有圖表改用 Okabe-Ito 配色，並以紅綠色盲、藍黃色盲與全色盲模擬驗證；頁面程式碼以語意化標籤重建，讓螢幕閱讀器能辨識標題、段落與按鈕；右下角的無障礙外掛提供五種文字大小，行距與字距同步調整，放大時版面不會破掉，明確是為年長讀者設計；整個專案並翻譯成中文、英文與法文，提供兩種切換途徑。該隊接著邀請一位紅綠色盲者、年長使用者與非英語母語者實測，再依回饋反覆修改。第四條路線：關於神經退化疾病的科普。起因是一份調查發現，多數國中生不知道神經退化疾病是什麼，只把它與老年人的記憶衰退連在一起，或是說「這跟我沒關係」，而高中生雖有能力理解，卻缺乏系統性的管道；另一場對光影地區衛生主管的訪談指出，醫療人員、政府與公益組織都在傳遞資訊，但公眾接受度低、預防習慣也沒有養成，部分原因是素材單調且依賴視覺文字。","ihp":"The project's human practices thread runs through disease awareness and screening access: interviews with the local health bureau director in the Guangying area on why existing neurodegenerative-disease education fails to land, plus in-school surveys establishing an age-stratified knowledge gap, shaped the public communication strategy to differentiate content depth by audience. The inclusivity work is itself integrated practice - the Chloe Franklin and David Doyle consultations each produced documented, traceable changes to an artefact rather than general encouragement.","ihp_zh":"該專案的 human practices 主線貫穿疾病認知與篩檢可得性：對光影地區衛生主管的訪談探討現有神經退化疾病教育為何無法打中受眾，加上校內調查確立了依年齡分層的知識落差，兩者共同形塑了依受眾區分內容深度的科普策略。包容性工作本身就是整合式實踐——與 Chloe Franklin 和 David Doyle 的諮詢，各自都在某件產出上留下有紀錄、可追溯的修改，而不只是泛泛的鼓勵。","realWorld":"Open outputs: the comparative international laboratory-accessibility legal database, the laboratory accessibility audit tool PDF, the audit evaluation form PDF, the Chinese legal research document, the trilingual accessible wiki itself, and the physical tactile magnetic genetic-circuit kit, which was donated to a Beijing school for the visually impaired for continued teaching use. Commitments are explicit: pilot testing of the audit tool continues into the next season in collaboration with the wider iGEM community.","realWorld_zh":"開放產出：國際實驗室無障礙法規比較資料庫、實驗室無障礙稽核工具 PDF、稽核評估表 PDF、中國法規研究文件、三語無障礙 wiki 本身，以及實體的觸覺磁性基因迴路教具——後者已捐贈給北京一所視障學校，供其持續教學使用。承諾也寫得明確：稽核工具的試行測試將延續到下一賽季，與更廣的 iGEM 社群合作進行。","partners":["Bethel China (charity for preschool children with visual impairments; seven children tested the kit)","a school for the visually impaired in Beijing (kit donated)","iGEM community project 'Accessibility in Synbio Labs' (David Doyle, Project Head)","Chloe Franklin, scientist and wheelchair user (audit tool review)","Concordia-Shanghai iGEM (joint Chinese legal research)","Team Toronto 2026 (Sami) and Mohamed, co-creators of the audit tool","iGEM members from Egypt, Pakistan and the United States","Guangying area local health bureau"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6089/wiki/5.avif","caption":"Workshop Activity One: participants navigate the team's own laboratory in a wheelchair and record the barriers they meet","caption_zh":"工作坊活動一：參與者坐輪椅通行該隊自己的實驗室，並記錄沿途遇到的障礙","credit":"Team BAID-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6089/wiki/12.avif","caption":"Workshop Activity Three: one participant describes a microscope specimen in words while others try to reconstruct it on paper","caption_zh":"工作坊活動三：一位參與者用言語描述顯微鏡標本，其他人試著在紙上把它重建出來","credit":"Team BAID-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6089/wiki/16.avif","caption":"Workshop Activity Four: blindfolded participants build a genetic circuit from shape-coded magnetic pieces by touch alone","caption_zh":"工作坊活動四：戴眼罩的參與者純靠觸覺，用形狀編碼的磁性積件搭出一組基因迴路","credit":"Team BAID-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6089/wiki/24.avif","caption":"Phase 2 at a Beijing school for the visually impaired: seven children aged 3-8 build a 'sound machine' using the tactile kit","caption_zh":"第 2 階段在北京一所視障學校：七位 3 至 8 歲的孩子用這套觸覺教具組出一台「聲音機器」","credit":"Team BAID-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6089/wiki/in1.avif","caption":"The Okabe-Ito colour-blind-safe palette adopted for every chart on the wiki, verified with colour-blindness simulation","caption_zh":"wiki 上每一張圖表都採用的 Okabe-Ito 色盲友善配色，並以色盲模擬驗證","credit":"Team BAID-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6089/wiki/28.avif","caption":"Across five workshop sessions the team reached more than 110 participants","caption_zh":"五場工作坊累計觸及超過 110 位參與者","credit":"Team BAID-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Build the accessible teaching aid, then pilot it twice: first with sighted participants under blindfold so you catch your own design flaws in a controlled setting, then with the actual users after stripping out the terminology they do not yet have - and donate the finished kit to the partner school so it keeps teaching after you leave.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"先做出無障礙教具，再試教兩次：第一次讓明眼參與者戴上眼罩，在可控情境下抓出自己的設計缺陷，第二次面對真正的使用者，並先把他們還不具備的術語全部拿掉——最後把完成的教具捐給合作學校，讓它在你們離開之後繼續被用來教學。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/baid-china/","https://2026.igem.wiki/baid-china/inclusivity","https://2026.igem.wiki/baid-china/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/baid-china/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/baid-china/entrepreneurship"],"rank":7},"6090":{"team":"BOKU-Vienna","id":"6090","section":"Overgrad","country":"Austria","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/boku-vienna/","projectTitle":"Algaeneering","projectTitle_zh":"Algaeneering","tagline":"Engineering the microalga Chlamydomonas reinhardtii into a vitamin C and folate factory to fight hidden hunger","tagline_zh":"把微藻 Chlamydomonas reinhardtii 改造成維生素 C 與葉酸工廠，對抗隱性飢餓","summary":"BOKU-Vienna overexpressed GGP (vitamin C) and GTPCHI plus ADCS (folate) in Chlamydomonas reinhardtii using Golden Gate Level 0/1/2 assembly, reaching a 4.5x increase in vitamin C in the GGP strain. The project was framed around hidden hunger, which affects an estimated two billion people, and was linked to UN SDGs 2, 3 and 12. Its education practice was built on an explicit didactic framework (the Didactic Triangle) and spanned four goals: sparking curiosity, classroom science, public dialogue and educational media. A genome-scale metabolic model was coupled to a calibrated bioreactor model and a nutritional impact model to translate lab titres into how many people a production plant could feed.","summary_zh":"BOKU-Vienna 以 Golden Gate Level 0/1/2 組裝，在 Chlamydomonas reinhardtii 中過表現 GGP（維生素 C）以及 GTPCHI 加 ADCS（葉酸），GGP 菌株的維生素 C 提高了 4.5 倍。專案以隱性飢餓為主軸，估計影響全球約 20 億人，並連結到聯合國永續發展目標 SDG 2、3 與 12。教育實踐建立在明確的教學框架（教學三角）之上，涵蓋四項目標：引發好奇、課堂科學、公眾對話與教育媒體。他們也把基因組尺度代謝模型接上經校正的生物反應器模型與營養影響模型，把實驗室效價換算成一座生產廠能餵養多少人。","awards":["Best Education — Nominee (Overgrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Genome-scale metabolic modelling of C. reinhardtii (iCre1355, mixotrophic version) with flux balance analysis (FBA), flux variability analysis (FVA), in-silico knockouts and enzyme protein-cost ranking; dynamic FBA bioreactor model calibrated and validated against the team's own flask cultures; a nutritional impact model converting measured vitamin content into daily requirements and people supplied.","frameworks_zh":"C. reinhardtii 的基因組尺度代謝模型（iCre1355，混營版本），搭配通量平衡分析（FBA）、通量變異分析（FVA）、電腦模擬基因剔除與酵素蛋白成本排序；動態 FBA 生物反應器模型以團隊自己的搖瓶培養資料校正與驗證；另有營養影響模型，把量測到的維生素含量換算成每日需求量與可供應人數。","dataviz":"Interactive 'Try the trade-off' widget on the wiki: sliders let a visitor pick a vitamin and see (left) maximum vitamin flux versus growth rate from the genome-scale model and (right) the calibrated flask culture's biomass, ammonium, acetate and vitamin titre over up to 120 h, with the team's own measured points overlaid and a harvest-point marker. Each graph carries an explicit 'How to read this graph' panel and a parameter-provenance table.","dataviz_zh":"wiki 上的互動元件 Try the trade-off：訪客可用滑桿選擇一種維生素，左側顯示基因組尺度模型算出的最大維生素通量與生長速率之間的取捨，右側顯示經校正的搖瓶培養在最多 120 小時內的生物量、銨、乙酸與維生素效價，並疊上團隊自己的量測點與收穫時間點標記。每張圖都附一個明確的「如何讀這張圖」面板與參數來源表。","datascience":"Lab-to-model feedback loop: flask measurements (biomass, ammonium, acetate, vitamin titre) were used to calibrate model parameters, and the model's pre-registered 1-10x overexpression band was compared against the measured 4.5x vitamin C result. Known model gaps were stated openly (measured ammonium ~2 mM below model; no cell-death term).","datascience_zh":"實驗室與模型之間形成回饋迴圈：搖瓶量測（生物量、銨、乙酸、維生素效價）用來校正模型參數，模型事先登記的 1-10 倍過表現區間則與實測的 4.5 倍維生素 C 結果對照。已知的模型落差也公開寫明（實測銨濃度比模型低約 2 mM；模型沒有細胞死亡項）。","software":"Custom interactive children's learning platform (web app, guided by an algae mascot, virtual-microscope zoom from cell to molecule, 3D DNA double helix with VR headset support, base-pairing puzzle game) and a separate 13-module self-paced interactive learning platform with mini-games (lac operon switch, PCR exponential-growth slider, mRNA translation, Cas9 cut-site finder), instant feedback, no sign-up, and a teacher preview mode that unlocks all modules for classroom prep.","software_zh":"自製的互動式兒童學習平台（網頁應用，由一隻藻類吉祥物帶路，虛擬顯微鏡可從細胞縮放到分子，3D DNA 雙螺旋並支援 VR 頭戴裝置，還有鹼基配對拼圖遊戲），以及另一個 13 個模組、可自行調整進度的互動學習平台，內含小遊戲（lac operon 開關、PCR 指數成長滑桿、mRNA 轉譯、Cas9 切位尋找），提供即時回饋、免註冊，並有教師預覽模式可解鎖所有模組供課前準備。","stack":["genome-scale metabolic model iCre1355","flux balance analysis","flux variability analysis","dynamic FBA","web-based interactive learning platform","WebVR / 3D DNA model","Kahoot","Mentimeter / QR-code live surveys"],"techniques":["Golden Gate Assembly (Level 0 to Level 2)","C. reinhardtii transformation (UVM4)","vitamin C and folate assays","microscopy","protein-cost analysis of enzyme targets","bioreactor scale-up scenario modelling"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"BOKU-Vienna ran a four-pillar education strategy explicitly grounded in the Didactic Triangle (learner-educator-content), and designed every child-facing print and digital resource in the dyslexia-friendly ABeeZee font. Pillar 1 (sparking curiosity) included a three-day Children's University (KinderUNI) booth built as a six-station progressive learning path: project poster, live Chlorella tubes and Chlamydomonas microscope images, a handcrafted 3D algae organelle model, a custom web learning platform plus a VR headset for exploring a 3D DNA double helix, an interactive genetic-engineering poster, and a gamified 'plasmid toss' into a large algae model to represent transformation; gummy-bear DNA building ran alongside. The same station set was then carried to Karwan Haus, a Caritas Wien refugee shelter in Vienna, on 17 August 2026 for children aged 4-12, with the flyer translated into four languages, Arabic- and Russian-speaking team members explaining stations, illustration-heavy materials, child-sized lab coats and goggles lent by KinderUNI BOKU, Lego-brick Golden Gate Cloning, stamps and science badges; in the exit survey most children chose 'I would love to work in science in the future'. Pillar 2 put a three-week, four-visit curriculum into two primary schools (Ruckergasse in Vienna and Neuarzl in Tyrol) with strawberry DNA extraction, lab-safety and pipetting sessions, a construct-assembly exercise for the GGP enzyme, vitamin C detection, Kahoot recaps and a field trip to the ZOOM Children's Museum where pupils wrote, drew and voiced two stop-motion films about algae and genetic modification; a middle-school workshop ('Code of Life - How We Program Cells') added a red-cabbage anthocyanin biosensor experiment, and a high-school visit to BG/BRG Tulln had students identify C. reinhardtii against Spirulina and Chlorella under the microscope. Measured impact: in the primary-school pre/post evaluation, zero children named science as a desired profession at the start versus five at the end, and 75.0% said they had become curious about programming cells (16.7% wanted to learn more first, 8.3% said they definitely want to do it in future). Pillar 3 (public dialogue) comprised a booth at Austria's Long Night of Research (24 April 2026) with a live visitor survey board on GMO acceptance and awareness that over 5 billion people face micronutrient deficiency, the Muthgassen Summer Festival, a 'Future of Food' panel discussion at TU Wien's Boecklsaal on 3 October 2026 with about 60 attendees and four panelists spanning algae cosmetics (Rita Mota), UNICEF Austria malnutrition work (Michael Blauensteiner), algae production engineering (Lukas Neuwirth, ex-Ecoduna) and microalgae research (Johannes Stadlmann), run in three blocks with anonymous QR-code audience polling and spirulina cotton candy, plus a pub quiz for about thirty STEM and non-STEM students. Pillar 4 produced durable media: an illustrated German children's book 'Welche Sprache spricht das Leben?' co-developed with KinderBOKU (characters such as 'Grandma Polymerase' who knits DNA together), launched at Vienna's Pappenheimgasse public library for a 4th-grade and a 5th-grade class with a copy donated to the library's lending collection and a copy given to every child; a comic advised by Martina Froehlich of KinderBOKU; the German-language podcast 'AlgaeHearing' on Spotify, deliberately in German because accessible German science content is scarce; the 13-module interactive learning platform with a teacher preview mode; and a feature article in the German-language life-science magazine BioSpektrum (issue 32, 4 June 2026). Critically, all tested worksheets, workshop guides and experiment protocols were published as downloadable Open Educational Resources on eduvidual.at, the official learning platform of the Austrian Federal Ministry of Education, Science and Research, so Austrian teachers nationwide can reuse them. Named-attribution testimonials were collected from the teacher at Ruckergasse, the head of the Pappenheimgasse library, the head of KinderBOKU and a social worker at Karwan Haus.","publicEngagement_zh":"BOKU-Vienna 推動四大支柱的教育策略，明確以教學三角（學習者—教育者—內容）為基礎，並把所有面向兒童的印刷與數位素材都以對閱讀障礙友善的 ABeeZee 字體設計。支柱一（引發好奇）包含為期三天的兒童大學（KinderUNI）攤位，設計成六站循序漸進的學習動線：專案海報、活體 Chlorella 試管與 Chlamydomonas 顯微照片、手工製作的 3D 藻類胞器模型、自製網頁學習平台搭配 VR 頭戴裝置探索 3D DNA 雙螺旋、互動式基因工程海報，以及把質體投進大型藻類模型以代表轉形的遊戲化「丟質體」活動；旁邊同時進行用軟糖熊搭 DNA 的活動。同一組站點在 2026 年 8 月 17 日搬到維也納的 Karwan Haus（Caritas Wien 的難民收容所），對象是 4-12 歲兒童：傳單翻成四種語言、由會說阿拉伯語與俄語的隊員解說各站、素材以插圖為主、兒童尺寸的實驗衣與護目鏡由 KinderUNI BOKU 出借，另有樂高積木版 Golden Gate Cloning、印章與科學徽章；離場問卷中多數孩子選了「我以後很想做科學工作」。支柱二把一套為期三週、共四次到校的課程帶進兩所小學（維也納的 Ruckergasse 與提洛邦的 Neuarzl），內容包括草莓 DNA 萃取、實驗安全與移液練習、GGP 酵素的構築組裝練習、維生素 C 檢測、以 Kahoot 複習，以及到 ZOOM 兒童博物館的校外教學，學生在那裡自己撰稿、繪圖並配音完成兩部關於藻類與基因改造的停格動畫；國中階段的工作坊（Code of Life - How We Program Cells）加入紅甘藍花青素生物感測器實驗；到 BG/BRG Tulln 高中的參訪則讓學生在顯微鏡下分辨 C. reinhardtii 與 Spirulina、Chlorella。量測到的影響：小學課程的前後測中，一開始沒有任何孩子把科學列為想從事的職業，結束時有五位；75.0% 表示自己對改寫細胞的程式產生了好奇（16.7% 想先多了解一些，8.3% 表示未來一定要做）。支柱三（公眾對話）包括 2026 年 4 月 24 日奧地利研究長夜的攤位，現場設有看板調查訪客對基因改造的接受度，以及對全球逾 50 億人面臨微量營養素缺乏的認知；Muthgassen 夏日慶典；2026 年 10 月 3 日在 TU Wien Boecklsaal 舉辦的 Future of Food 論壇，約 60 人出席，四位與談人分別來自藻類化妝品（Rita Mota）、UNICEF Austria 的營養不良工作（Michael Blauensteiner）、藻類生產工程（Lukas Neuwirth，前 Ecoduna）與微藻研究（Johannes Stadlmann），分三段進行，搭配匿名 QR code 現場投票與螺旋藻棉花糖；另有一場約三十位 STEM 與非 STEM 學生參加的酒吧問答。支柱四產出可長期留存的媒材：與 KinderBOKU 共同開發的德文插畫童書 Welche Sprache spricht das Leben?（書中有像「聚合酶奶奶」這樣把 DNA 編織起來的角色），在維也納 Pappenheimgasse 公共圖書館對一個四年級與一個五年級班級舉行發表會，捐一本給圖書館的外借館藏，並送給每位孩子一本；由 KinderBOKU 的 Martina Froehlich 擔任顧問的漫畫；在 Spotify 上的德語 podcast AlgaeHearing，刻意用德語，因為平易近人的德語科學內容相當稀少；有教師預覽模式的 13 模組互動學習平台；以及在德語生命科學雜誌 BioSpektrum 刊出的專題文章（第 32 期，2026 年 6 月 4 日）。最關鍵的是，所有經過實測的學習單、工作坊指引與實驗流程，都以可下載的開放教育資源發布在 eduvidual.at，也就是奧地利聯邦教育、科學與研究部的官方學習平台，讓全國教師都能重複使用。他們也收集了具名的推薦意見，分別來自 Ruckergasse 的老師、Pappenheimgasse 圖書館館長、KinderBOKU 負責人與 Karwan Haus 的一位社工。","ihp":"Human Practices was structured into three sequential phases, each with its own stakeholder set: (1) lab experts for technical feasibility, which changed key design decisions; (2) outside critics on GMOs, sustainability and ethics, where the team explicitly sought disconfirming rather than validating views; (3) nutrition and product-design conversations about who should be prioritised as a target group and how the product would be delivered. The team framed iHP against the reflective/responsible/responsive triad, mapped the project to SDGs 2, 3 and 12, and used the 'Future of Food' panel plus audience polling as a live iHP instrument. The panel's main takeaway was recorded honestly as 'our work is meaningful, but GMO-based projects are not without risk and open questions, especially when implemented at a larger scale'.","ihp_zh":"人類實踐分成三個依序進行的階段，各有自己的利害關係人：（1）實驗室專家，用於確認技術可行性，這一階段改變了關鍵設計決策；（2）針對基因改造、永續性與倫理的外部批評者，團隊明確尋求能證反自己的意見，而不是來背書的意見；（3）營養與產品設計的對話，討論該優先服務哪一個目標族群、產品又該如何遞送。團隊以反思性、負責性、回應性三者構成的框架檢視整合式人類實踐，把專案對應到 SDG 2、3 與 12，並把 Future of Food 論壇與現場投票當作即時的人類實踐工具。論壇的主要結論也誠實記錄下來：我們的工作有意義，但以基因改造為基礎的專案並非沒有風險與未解的問題，尤其是放大到更大規模實施的時候。","realWorld":"The impact model translated measured vitamin content into concrete figures: 25 g dry algae per day covers one daily folate requirement and 116 g covers vitamin C; a hypothetical 100 m3 production plant at wild-type folate content could cover the yearly folate need of roughly 900 adults or 490 pregnant women. The design reactor scenario produced 0.46 g/L/day, nitrogen-capped, at about 1.5x the flask vitamin titre. The team also published a separate 'iGEM guide' page for teams starting out.","realWorld_zh":"影響模型把量測到的維生素含量換算成具體數字：每天 25 g 乾藻可滿足一日的葉酸需求，116 g 可滿足維生素 C；若以野生型的葉酸含量計算，一座假想的 100 m3 生產廠可覆蓋約 900 名成人或 490 名孕婦一年的葉酸需求。設計反應器情境的產量為 0.46 g/L/day，受氮源上限限制，維生素效價約為搖瓶的 1.5 倍。團隊另外也做了一個給新手隊伍的 iGEM 指南頁面。","partners":["KinderBOKU / KinderUNI BOKU (BOKU University children's science programme)","Caritas Wien - Karwan Haus refugee shelter","ZOOM Children's Museum, Vienna","Pappenheimgasse public library, Vienna","Ruckergasse Primary School, Vienna","Neuarzl Primary School, Tyrol","BG/BRG 21 bilingual middle school","BG/BRG Tulln high school","TU Wien (Boecklsaal venue)","eduvidual.at - Austrian Federal Ministry of Education, Science and Research learning platform","BioSpektrum magazine","UNICEF Austria (panelist)","Stroeck (sponsor, panel catering)","Polymun"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6090/wiki/hp-and-education/kinderuni/kinderuni-02.avif","caption":"Children at the Children's University (KinderUNI) six-station synthetic biology booth in Vienna","caption_zh":"維也納兒童大學（KinderUNI）六站式合成生物學攤位上的孩子們","credit":"Team BOKU-Vienna, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6090/wiki/hp-and-education/karwan-haus/karwan-haus-golden-gate-assembly-via-lego-bricks.avif","caption":"Teaching Golden Gate assembly with Lego bricks at Karwan Haus, a Caritas Wien refugee shelter","caption_zh":"在 Caritas Wien 的難民收容所 Karwan Haus 用樂高積木教 Golden Gate 組裝","credit":"Team BOKU-Vienna, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6090/wiki/hp-and-education/childrensbook/childrensbook-front.avif","caption":"The team's illustrated German children's book, co-developed with KinderBOKU and donated to a Vienna public library","caption_zh":"團隊與 KinderBOKU 共同開發的德文插畫童書，並捐贈給維也納一間公共圖書館","credit":"Team BOKU-Vienna, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6090/wiki/hp-and-education/lernplattform/1-overview-of-our-interactive-learning-platform-with-13-modules.avif","caption":"The free 13-module interactive learning platform, with no sign-up and a teacher preview mode","caption_zh":"免費的 13 模組互動學習平台，免註冊並具教師預覽模式","credit":"Team BOKU-Vienna, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6090/wiki/hp-and-education/panel-discussion/panel-discussion-people.avif","caption":"The 'Future of Food' public panel discussion at TU Wien, about 60 attendees with live QR-code polling","caption_zh":"在 TU Wien 舉辦的 Future of Food 公開論壇，約 60 人出席並以 QR code 現場投票","credit":"Team BOKU-Vienna, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6090/wiki/hp-and-education/primary-school/primary-school-02.avif","caption":"Pupils extracting DNA during the three-week primary-school curriculum","caption_zh":"三週小學課程中正在萃取 DNA 的學生","credit":"Team BOKU-Vienna, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Publish every tested worksheet, workshop guide and experiment protocol as open educational resources on the national ministry education platform (as BOKU did on eduvidual.at), so school use continues after the project ends, and measure the same cohort before and after (career aspirations plus curiosity items) so learning gain is a number, not an anecdote.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"把每一份實測過的學習單、工作坊指引與實驗流程，都當作開放教育資源發布在國家教育部的學習平台上（就像 BOKU 放在 eduvidual.at 那樣），讓專案結束後學校仍能繼續使用；並對同一批學生做前後測（職業志向加上好奇心題項），讓學習成效成為一個數字，而不是一則軼事。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/boku-vienna/","https://2026.igem.wiki/boku-vienna/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/boku-vienna/inclusivity","https://2026.igem.wiki/boku-vienna/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/boku-vienna/model"],"rank":7},"6096":{"team":"XJTLU-China","id":"6096","section":"Undergrad","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-china/","projectTitle":"dogmaOS — programming translation rhythm for soluble protein expression","tagline":"Design where and for how long the ribosome should pause, then re-engineer the host tRNA pool to make that pause possible.","summary":"XJTLU-China asked whether soluble yield of hard-to-express recombinant proteins in E. coli can be improved by deliberately programming *where* translation slows down, rather than by maximising expression. Their dry-lab system catmaOS (Codon-Aware Translation Modeling and Analysis Operating System) chains four models: structural co-translational folding priority (M1), evolutionary conserved slow-codon evidence (M2), a five-layer translation-kinetics and ribosome-traffic engine with constrained Pareto selection (M3-A to M3-E), and host tRNA-pool intervention design (M4). The framework picked a single synonymous G-CSF design (W1-S) out of six candidates and an engineered BL21-AlaPro chassis, both of which went to the bench; Four-Leaf Clover RT-qPCR then measured the actual tRNA knockdown and that number was fed back into M3-A as an updated host context. It won Best Model (Undergraduate) and Best Education (Undergraduate).","awards":["Best Measurement — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Model — Winner (Undergrad)","Best Education — Winner (Undergrad)","Best Wiki — Nominee (Undergrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"catmaOS is a four-model, five-layer multiscale pipeline and is unusually explicit about what each layer is and is not. M1 is a structural-bioinformatics scoring model: it builds a residue-level evidence table from PDB coordinates (G-CSF, PDB 1RHG chain B, UniProt P09919, RefSeq NM_000759.4), runs DSSP for secondary structure and relative solvent accessibility, solves a self-consistent native-contact occupancy model as chain length grows (Jacobs-Shakhnovich) to detect folding events at a 1 kBT free-energy-drop threshold with a 4 Angstrom contact cutoff, adds Kyte-Doolittle hydrophobic exposure, cysteine-neighbourhood scores, DSSP transition and beta-initiation tracks and an AGGRESCAN-style aggregation propensity, then fuses them with availability-aware weights into a 0-100 priority score and shifts it downstream by a 35-codon ribosome exit-tunnel offset (scanned 30-40 codons for sensitivity). M2 is a comparative-genomics model: MAFFT L-INS-i protein alignment projected back to codons with PAL2NAL, GtRNAdb/tRNAscan-SE high-confidence tRNA gene copy numbers per species, a frozen codon-anticodon wobble-penalty table, a tRNA-adaptation-style effective supply W_s(c) converted to within-species relative 'resistance', a top-25%-resistance slow-codon label, a strict same-amino-acid filter, and Henikoff position-based sequence weighting to produce a weighted slow-codon conservation score with an explicit effective-coverage track. M3 is the kinetic core: M3-A decomposes intrinsic codon dwell into decoding (inverse effective cognate/wobble supply with a near-cognate competition term, K_dec = 0.80, gamma_near = 0.50), peptidyl-transfer (proline/EF-P arrest context), basal translocation and ViennaRNA RNAplfold local-unpaired-probability RNA resistance, with four ablation configurations A0-A3 to attribute mechanism; M3-B feeds that rate vector into TWO independent ribosome-traffic backends — a deterministic Ribosome Flow Model with Extended Objects (RFMEO) steady state and a stochastic Gillespie kinetic Monte Carlo extended-object TASEP (5 replicates, SEM bands, warm-up discarded) — and cross-validates them with Pearson, Spearman, concordance and top-k hotspot overlap plus an alpha-beta boundary-sensitivity grid; M3-C maps traffic-safe dwell envelopes, exit-tunnel availability gates, relative contact-order folding demand, a finite-state productive-pathway propagator p_{L+1} = p_L exp(s Q_L dt_L) run over a 0.5/1/2 scale grid (direction called 'robust' only when the sign holds across scales), and a time-weighted unsatisfied-native-contact exposure proxy E_U = sum_L U(L) tau(L); M3-D closes a first-order steady-state mRNA balance M_ss = k_tx / (k_deg,eff + mu) with a scikit-learn mRNA-decay predictor trained on 5,486 curated E. coli half-life records (Chen 2015, Selinger 2003) split gene-grouped 3,883/765/838; M3-E generates synonymous candidates under reading-frame, GC, motif, restriction-site and homopolymer constraints and selects by constrained Pareto dominance over four frozen objectives (maximise terminal flux J, minimise ribosome load R, maximise productive-pathway C4, minimise exposure C5), with exact enumeration for small spaces and NSGA-II for large ones, scored for precision/recall against exact fronts. M4 extends design to the host: it maps target codons to BL21 tRNA genes, clusters and promoters with a weighted K-12-to-BL21 transfer score (S_map = 0.45 S_signature + 0.20 S_ordered + 0.15 S_count + 0.15 I_80 + 0.05 I_200), proposes copy-number reduction or 1-3 substitutions in a 29-bp promoter core against 15/30/50% weakening tiers, and ranks them with a three-model ML ensemble trained on 112,955 measured core promoters from the published MBRS L4 library (Zhou 2025), held out by -35/-10 motif pairs (67,978/7,680/37,297) achieving r = 0.677, MAE = 0.506 on log2(1+strength).","dataviz":"Eighteen numbered model figures that read as a single argument. Aligned multi-track profiles put six normalised structural feature tracks (F1-F6) above the availability-aware composite score so a reader can see which feature drove a peak; priority profiles are paired with an evidence-coverage track underneath so a high score with thin evidence cannot be misread as a finding. Figure 8 is a tunnel-length sensitivity heatmap (rows = assumed exit-tunnel length 30-40 codons, columns = codon position, fixed 0-100 teal scale, light-grey cells for genuinely unavailable data rather than zero) so the reader can watch high-priority bands migrate as an assumption changes. Figure 11 is a codon-level audit matrix (18 homolog rows x codons 110-121, green = slow in that species' tRNA context, white = comparable, grey = non-comparable). Figure 14 is a log2(candidate/WT) dwell heatmap restricted to edited positions only, with the x-axis explicitly flagged as non-continuous and the legend explaining that +1 means 2x. Figure 16 is a three-panel dot plot of WT-normalised flux, ribosome load and exposure on matched candidate rows, deliberately NOT collapsed into one score. KMC traces carry +/- SEM bands and separate unblocked residence from blocked waiting. Captions state the direction of preference and whether a quantity is measured or a relative model proxy.","datascience":"Two supervised models were trained from public measurement data and one from their own: an mRNA degradation proxy (D2) on 5,486 curated E. coli half-life records with gene/protein/CDS-grouped splits, a 29-bp promoter-strength ensemble on 112,955 measured core promoters held out by -35/-10 motif pairs (a genuinely out-of-distribution split, r = 0.677), and a codon-occupancy regression on 107,627 codon-level Ribo-seq observations across 125 genes with a documented 14-nt P-site offset, first/last 10 codons excluded, and gene-held-out evaluation (22,025 test observations). The team audits its own provenance in public: several dataset source fields are annotated 'unconfirmed', 'remains to be confirmed' or 'not an attributed published dataset size' rather than quietly cited. Model 4's proL promoter screen predicted 0.727 (native) vs 0.386/0.366/0.358 (P1-P3); the built strain BL21-AlaPro was then measured by Four-Leaf Clover RT-qPCR, showing rpoD-normalised mature tRNA falling from 63.98 to 23.42 (alaXW) and 6.828 to 2.254 (proL), and those measured numbers were returned to M3-A as a new effective-supply table for a full A-E rerun. The headline wet-lab readout: TolB-G-CSF model-designed sequence in the engineered host reached a mean soluble/insoluble ratio of 0.140 vs 0.075 for the commercial sequence in WT host (DnaK-normalised, n = 3 biological replicates, ~1.87-fold). Crucially the team also reports the negative result honestly — for PfCHT1 and leptin, insoluble bands weakened but no clear soluble enrichment appeared, and the results figure is literally titled 'Solubility Gains Remain Unclear'.","software":"catmaOS 4.02.06 ships as a downloadable Windows x64 source release with Setup.cmd/Start.cmd, a pinned requirements-lock.txt, a private .venv, a local browser workspace on 127.0.0.1:8767 (sequences never leave the user's machine), a 28-page PDF user manual, and four precomputed read-only interactive demos embedded in the wiki with JSON/CSV export. Every run emits a reproducibility bundle: request.json (typed input, label, source, parameters), result.json on a versioned schema 1.0.0 with input hash, module status and reproducibility record, curves.csv, metrics.csv, exact_candidates.csv, native/evidence-result.json and run.log, all zipped per run_id. The design rule stated on the page — 'missing values stay missing' and 'a completed run confirms the requested task finished; it does not imply every model was executed' — is the discipline most teams lack.","stack":["Python 3.14","NumPy","SciPy","pandas","Biopython","scikit-learn","Matplotlib","DSSP","MAFFT L-INS-i","PAL2NAL","ViennaRNA / RNAplfold","AGGRESCAN","GtRNAdb / tRNAscan-SE","NSGA-II","custom RFMEO solver","custom Gillespie KMC"],"techniques":["co-translational folding free-energy model","structural bioinformatics / DSSP feature fusion","exit-tunnel coordinate mapping with sensitivity scan","comparative genomics codon alignment","tRNA adaptation index-style supply model","Henikoff sequence weighting","ODE/steady-state ribosome flow model (RFMEO)","stochastic Gillespie kinetic Monte Carlo TASEP with extended objects","finite-state Markov folding-pathway propagation","steady-state mRNA mass balance","multi-objective constrained Pareto optimisation","NSGA-II genetic algorithm","machine-learning regression (promoter strength, mRNA decay, codon occupancy)","out-of-distribution held-out validation","ablation studies","backend cross-validation","parameter-scenario robustness analysis","model-to-measurement feedback loop"],"frameworks_zh":"catmaOS 是一條四模型、五層的多尺度管線，並且異常明確地說明每一層「是什麼」與「不是什麼」。M1 是結構生物資訊評分模型：它由 PDB 座標（G-CSF，PDB 1RHG 鏈 B，UniProt P09919，RefSeq NM_000759.4）建立殘基層級的證據表，以 DSSP 取得二級結構與相對溶劑可及性，隨鏈長增長求解一個自我一致的原生接觸佔據模型（Jacobs-Shakhnovich），以 1 kBT 自由能下降為閾值、4 Angstrom 接觸截斷來偵測摺疊事件，再加入 Kyte-Doolittle 疏水暴露、半胱胺酸鄰域分數、DSSP 轉換與 beta 起始軌跡，以及 AGGRESCAN 式的聚集傾向，然後以考量資料可得性的權重融合成 0-100 的優先度分數，並依 35 個密碼子的核醣體出口通道偏移往下游位移（並掃描 30-40 個密碼子做敏感度分析）。M2 是比較基因組學模型：以 MAFFT L-INS-i 做蛋白質比對、用 PAL2NAL 投影回密碼子，取用 GtRNAdb/tRNAscan-SE 各物種高可信度 tRNA 基因套數，搭配一張凍結的密碼子—反密碼子搖擺懲罰表，將 tRNA 適應度式的有效供給 W_s(c) 轉換為物種內的相對「阻力」，以阻力前 25% 標記慢密碼子，施加嚴格的同一胺基酸過濾，並以 Henikoff 位置式序列加權產生一個加權慢密碼子保守度分數，另附明確的有效覆蓋度軌跡。M3 是動力學核心：M3-A 把密碼子的內在停留時間分解為解碼（有效同源/搖擺供給的倒數，加上近同源競爭項，K_dec = 0.80、gamma_near = 0.50）、胜肽基轉移（脯胺酸/EF-P 停滯情境）、基礎轉位，以及以 ViennaRNA RNAplfold 局部未配對機率表示的 RNA 阻力，並以四組消融設定 A0-A3 歸因機制；M3-B 把該速率向量輸入兩套獨立的核醣體流量後端——一個是確定性的含延伸物件核醣體流量模型（RFMEO）穩態解，一個是隨機 Gillespie 動力學蒙地卡羅的延伸物件 TASEP（5 次重複、SEM 帶、捨棄暖機段）——並以 Pearson、Spearman、一致性係數與前 k 名熱點重疊度交叉驗證，另加一張 alpha-beta 邊界敏感度網格；M3-C 繪出流量安全的停留時間包絡、出口通道可得性閘門、相對接觸次序的摺疊需求、一個在 0.5/1/2 尺度網格上執行的有限狀態生產性路徑傳遞子 p_{L+1} = p_L exp(s Q_L dt_L)（只有當正負號在各尺度間維持一致時才稱該方向「穩健」），以及一個時間加權的未滿足原生接觸暴露代理量 E_U = sum_L U(L) tau(L)；M3-D 以 scikit-learn 的 mRNA 衰減預測器（訓練於 5,486 筆整理過的 E. coli 半衰期記錄，Chen 2015、Selinger 2003，按基因分群切分為 3,883/765/838）閉合一階穩態 mRNA 平衡 M_ss = k_tx / (k_deg,eff + mu)；M3-E 在讀框、GC 含量、motif、限制酶切位與同聚物等限制下產生同義候選，並以四個凍結目標的受限 Pareto 支配進行選擇（最大化末端通量 J、最小化核醣體負載 R、最大化生產性路徑 C4、最小化暴露 C5），小搜尋空間用精確列舉、大空間用 NSGA-II，並以對照精確 Pareto 前緣的精確率/召回率評分。M4 把設計延伸到宿主：它將目標密碼子對映到 BL21 的 tRNA 基因、基因簇與啟動子，使用加權的 K-12 到 BL21 轉移分數（S_map = 0.45 S_signature + 0.20 S_ordered + 0.15 S_count + 0.15 I_80 + 0.05 I_200），提出降低套數或在 29 bp 啟動子核心做 1-3 個置換，對應 15/30/50% 的弱化層級，並以三模型 ML 整合（訓練於已發表 MBRS L4 資料庫的 112,955 個實測核心啟動子，Zhou 2025，依 -35/-10 motif 配對留出，67,978/7,680/37,297）排序，在 log2(1+強度) 上達到 r = 0.677、MAE = 0.506。","dataviz_zh":"十八張編號的模型圖，讀起來像一條完整的論證。對齊的多軌剖面圖把六條正規化的結構特徵軌（F1-F6）放在考量可得性的綜合分數之上，讓讀者看出是哪個特徵推高了某個峰；優先度剖面圖下方必定配一條證據覆蓋度軌，使「高分但證據薄弱」不會被誤讀成發現。圖 8 是通道長度敏感度熱圖（列為假設的出口通道長度 30-40 個密碼子，行為密碼子位置，固定 0-100 的藍綠色標尺，真正無資料的格子以淺灰表示而非以零填補），讓讀者看見高優先度帶隨著假設改變而遷移。圖 11 是密碼子層級的稽核矩陣（18 列同源蛋白 x 密碼子 110-121，綠色代表在該物種的 tRNA 情境下為慢密碼子，白色代表可比較，灰色代表不可比較）。圖 14 是只限於被編輯位置的 log2(候選/WT) 停留時間熱圖，x 軸明確標示為非連續，圖例也說明 +1 意即 2 倍。圖 16 是以 WT 正規化的通量、核醣體負載與暴露三面板點圖，候選列彼此對齊，刻意不壓縮成單一分數。KMC 軌跡附有 +/- SEM 帶，並把未受阻的停留與受阻的等待分開呈現。圖說都標明偏好的方向，以及該量是實測值還是相對的模型代理量。","datascience_zh":"兩個監督式模型由公開量測資料訓練，另一個由團隊自己的資料訓練：mRNA 降解代理模型（D2）以 5,486 筆整理過的 E. coli 半衰期記錄訓練，並按基因/蛋白質/CDS 分群切分；29 bp 啟動子強度整合模型以 112,955 個實測核心啟動子訓練，依 -35/-10 motif 配對留出（這是真正的分布外切分，r = 0.677）；密碼子佔據回歸則用了橫跨 125 個基因的 107,627 筆密碼子層級 Ribo-seq 觀測值，記錄了 14 nt 的 P 位偏移、排除頭尾各 10 個密碼子，並採基因留出評估（22,025 筆測試觀測）。團隊公開稽核自己的資料來源：有幾個資料集的來源欄位被標註為「未確認」、「尚待確認」或「非來自有明確出處的已發表資料集規模」，而不是悄悄引用。模型 4 的 proL 啟動子篩選預測值為 0.727（原生）對 0.386/0.366/0.358（P1-P3）；建成的 BL21-AlaPro 菌株隨後以 Four-Leaf Clover RT-qPCR 量測，顯示以 rpoD 正規化的成熟 tRNA 由 63.98 降至 23.42（alaXW）、由 6.828 降至 2.254（proL），而這些實測值被送回 M3-A 作為新的有效供給表，完整重跑 A-E。濕實驗室的主要讀值：在工程宿主中，模型設計序列 TolB-G-CSF 的可溶/不可溶比平均達 0.140，相較於野生型宿主中商用序列的 0.075（以 DnaK 正規化，n = 3 生物重複，約 1.87 倍）。關鍵的是，團隊也誠實報告負面結果——PfCHT1 與 leptin 的不可溶條帶變弱，但沒有出現明顯的可溶性富集，結果圖的標題就直接寫著「Solubility Gains Remain Unclear」（可溶性提升仍不明確）。","software_zh":"catmaOS 4.02.06 以可下載的 Windows x64 原始碼版本發布，附 Setup.cmd/Start.cmd、鎖定版本的 requirements-lock.txt、私有 .venv、在 127.0.0.1:8767 上執行的本機瀏覽器工作區（序列絕不離開使用者的機器）、一份 28 頁 PDF 使用手冊，以及四個預先計算、嵌入 wiki 的唯讀互動示範，可匯出 JSON/CSV。每次執行都會產出一份可重現性包：request.json（具型別的輸入、標籤、來源、參數）、採版本化綱要 1.0.0 的 result.json（含輸入雜湊、模組狀態與可重現性記錄）、curves.csv、metrics.csv、exact_candidates.csv、native/evidence-result.json 與 run.log，全部依 run_id 打包成 zip。頁面上明文寫出的設計規則——「缺失值就保持缺失」以及「一次完成的執行只確認所請求的任務已結束，不代表每個模型都真的跑過」——正是多數隊伍缺少的紀律。"},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Best Education winner (Undergraduate). The team built an explicit education framework rather than a list of events: a four-tier 'Lifelong Learning Pathway' (interest inspiration, knowledge building, interdisciplinary co-creation, professional impact) that replaces age-banding with depth of engagement, crossed with a four-stage activity structure (Reach, Construct, Dialogue, Extension) and Gardner's theory of multiple intelligences as the design lens for choosing an activity format. They reached over 2,000 people through 21 activities — workshops, exhibitions and the Learning Mall Premium online platform — and produced 18 reusable education toolkits, with the Extension stage deliberately designed so each activity leaves behind a game, handbook or toolkit rather than ending at the event.","ihp":"A CARE framework distilled from stakeholder conversations: Create Accessibility, Accountable Storytelling, Real-world Alignment, Ethical Design. It originated in a question from Dr Lanlan Han about who actually benefits and how strong the evidence is. The interview timeline is structured as Problem / Design / Scope, and the team documents how it narrowed its own claim: starting from 'boost heterologous protein expression in E. coli', literature and interviews with Dr Antony Kam and industry expert Dr Xijun Piao (CATUG Biotechnology, Suzhou) pushed them to redefine success as soluble usable protein rather than total expression, and to state explicitly that dogmaOS is 'not positioned as a universal protein-production platform'. Mid-stage consultations with Dr Yongtao Zhu, Dr Chun Chan, Prof Sheng Yang (Shanghai Institutes for Biological Sciences, CAS), Prof Zhiliang Lu, Dr Avinash Pandreka (Oxford Suzhou Centre for Advanced Research), Dr Kozo Hamada and Prof Zhongmei Liu (Jiangnan University) convinced them that translation speed alone could not explain folding outcomes, which is what created Model 3 and Model 4.","realWorld":"Target selection was driven by real demand: G-CSF, leptin, PfCHT1 and FGF2 were chosen with researchers and protein-production companies as proteins that are hard to express in E. coli and have clear research or clinical uses spanning public health, rare disease and basic research. The team maps the project to SDGs 3, 9, 12 and 17. Accessibility is the commercial thesis — rather than selling a service, catmaOS is released as free local software so academic labs and iGEM teams with only basic E. coli facilities can do upstream optimisation instead of paying for repeated trial-and-error. Safety is built in: non-pathogenic strains, BSL-1 practice, autoclaved waste, and FLP-FRT removal of the kanamycin cassette after lambda-Red genome editing.","partners":["Xi'an Jiaotong-Liverpool University","CATUG Biotechnology (Suzhou) Co., Ltd.","Shanghai Institutes for Biological Sciences, Chinese Academy of Sciences","Oxford Suzhou Centre for Advanced Research","Jiangnan University","GenScript","SnapGene"],"publicEngagement_zh":"Best Education 得主（大學部）。團隊建立的是明確的教育框架，而不是一串活動清單：一條四層的「終身學習路徑」（興趣啟發、知識建構、跨領域共創、專業影響），以參與深度取代年齡分層，再與四階段活動結構（觸及、建構、對話、延伸）交叉，並以 Gardner 的多元智能理論作為選擇活動形式的設計視角。他們透過 21 場活動——工作坊、展覽與 Learning Mall Premium 線上平台——觸及超過 2,000 人，並產出 18 套可重複使用的教育工具包；「延伸」階段是刻意設計的，讓每場活動都留下一個遊戲、手冊或工具包，而不是在活動結束時就終止。","ihp_zh":"他們從利害關係人對話中萃取出一套 CARE 框架：Create Accessibility（創造可及性）、Accountable Storytelling（負責任的敘事）、Real-world Alignment（與真實世界對齊）、Ethical Design（倫理設計）。它源自 Dr Lanlan Han 的一個問題：究竟誰會受益，以及證據有多強。訪談時間軸依「問題／設計／範圍」編排，團隊也記錄了自己如何收斂主張：起點是「提升 E. coli 中的異源蛋白表現」，但文獻以及與 Dr Antony Kam 和產業專家 Dr Xijun Piao（蘇州 CATUG Biotechnology）的訪談，促使他們把成功重新定義為「可用的可溶性蛋白」而非總表現量，並明確聲明 dogmaOS「並不被定位為通用的蛋白質生產平台」。中期與 Dr Yongtao Zhu、Dr Chun Chan、Prof Sheng Yang（中國科學院上海生命科學研究院）、Prof Zhiliang Lu、Dr Avinash Pandreka（牛津蘇州先進研究中心）、Dr Kozo Hamada 與 Prof Zhongmei Liu（江南大學）的諮詢，說服他們單憑轉譯速度無法解釋摺疊結果——這正是模型 3 與模型 4 誕生的原因。","realWorld_zh":"標的的選擇由真實需求驅動：G-CSF、leptin、PfCHT1 與 FGF2 是與研究人員及蛋白質生產公司共同選定的，它們都在 E. coli 中難以表現，且在公共衛生、罕見疾病與基礎研究上有明確的研究或臨床用途。團隊把專案對應到 SDG 3、9、12 與 17。可及性就是其商業論點——catmaOS 不以服務販售，而是以免費的本機軟體釋出，讓只有基本 E. coli 設備的學術實驗室與 iGEM 隊伍能自行做上游最佳化，而不必付錢去反覆試誤。生物安全內建在設計中：使用非病原菌株、遵循 BSL-1 操作、廢棄物高壓滅菌，並在 lambda-Red 基因組編輯後以 FLP-FRT 移除卡那黴素抗性卡匣。"},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6096/wiki/assets/drylab/model/figure-08.svg","caption":"Figure 8: exit-tunnel sensitivity heatmap. Rows are assumed ribosome exit-tunnel lengths of 30-40 codons, columns are G-CSF codon positions, and the fixed 0-100 teal scale shows structural priority. Light-grey cells mark genuinely unavailable structural data rather than a score of zero, so the reader can watch high-priority bands migrate as a modelling assumption changes.","credit":"Team XJTLU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"圖 8：出口通道敏感度熱圖。列為假設的核醣體出口通道長度 30-40 個密碼子，行為 G-CSF 的密碼子位置，固定的 0-100 藍綠色標尺表示結構優先度。淺灰色格子標示真正缺乏結構資料之處，而不是以零分充數，讓讀者看見高優先度帶隨著建模假設改變而遷移。"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6096/wiki/assets/drylab/model/figure-11.svg","caption":"Figure 11: codon-level audit matrix for reference positions 110-121. Each row is a retained homolog; green marks codons called slow in that species' own tRNA context, white marks other comparable synonymous codons, grey retains non-comparable cells. Positions 115 and 121 were slow in all 18 homologs while 118 was slow in none.","credit":"Team XJTLU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"圖 11：參考位置 110-121 的密碼子層級稽核矩陣。每一列是一個保留下來的同源蛋白；綠色標示在該物種自身 tRNA 情境下被判為慢的密碼子，白色標示其他可比較的同義密碼子，灰色則保留不可比較的格子。位置 115 與 121 在全部 18 個同源蛋白中都是慢的，而 118 在任何一個中都不是。"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6096/wiki/assets/merge-20261020/catmaos-figure-12.svg","caption":"Figure 12: the full 'how long to pause' panel, linking synonymous candidate generation to intrinsic dwell (M3-A), kinetic Monte Carlo ribosome traffic with SEM bands (M3-B), folding trajectories and contact exposure (M3-C), the mRNA decay proxy (M3-D) and the constrained objective screen (M3-E) in which four of six candidates pass the flux and ribosome-burden gates.","credit":"Team XJTLU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"圖 12：完整的「該停多久」面板，把同義候選的產生串連到內在停留時間（M3-A）、附 SEM 帶的動力學蒙地卡羅核醣體流量（M3-B）、摺疊軌跡與接觸暴露（M3-C）、mRNA 衰減代理模型（M3-D），以及受限目標篩選（M3-E），其中六個候選有四個通過通量與核醣體負擔的閘門。"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6096/wiki/assets/drylab/model/figure-16.svg","caption":"Figure 16: throughput, ribosome load and exposure trade-offs for wild type plus six synonymous candidates, shown as three WT-normalised panels on matched rows and deliberately not collapsed into a single score. W1-F had flux 0.781 and load 1.079, failing the flux >= 0.95 constraint; W1-S passed on all four objectives and went to the bench.","credit":"Team XJTLU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"圖 16：野生型加六個同義候選的產出量、核醣體負載與暴露之間的取捨，以三個以 WT 正規化的面板呈現、候選列彼此對齊，並刻意不壓縮成單一分數。W1-F 的通量為 0.781、負載為 1.079，未通過通量 >= 0.95 的限制；W1-S 四個目標全部通過，進入濕實驗室。"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Pair every model score with an explicit evidence-coverage track and run a sensitivity scan over your least-defensible assumption (here, exit-tunnel length), so a figure shows not just the answer but how much of it is real data; and keep competing objectives as separate aligned panels rather than summing them into one invented score. Both are achievable with matplotlib by a motivated 16-year-old and immediately make a model honest.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-china/","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-china/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-china/software/","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-china/measurement/","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-china/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-china/results/","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-china/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-china/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-china/education/"],"projectTitle_zh":"dogmaOS — 以程式化的轉譯節奏提升可溶性蛋白質表現","tagline_zh":"設計核醣體該在哪裡、停多久，再重新改造宿主的 tRNA 庫讓這個停頓成為可能。","summary_zh":"XJTLU-China 要問的是：在 E. coli 中難以表現的重組蛋白，其可溶產量能否透過刻意規劃轉譯*在哪裡*變慢來提升，而不是靠把表現量最大化。他們的乾實驗室系統 catmaOS（Codon-Aware Translation Modeling and Analysis Operating System）串接四個模型：結構上的共轉譯摺疊優先度（M1）、演化上保守的慢密碼子證據（M2）、含受限 Pareto 選擇的五層轉譯動力學與核醣體流量引擎（M3-A 至 M3-E），以及宿主 tRNA 庫的干預設計（M4）。這套框架從六個候選中挑出單一個同義密碼子設計（W1-S），以及一個工程化的 BL21-AlaPro 載體株，兩者都進了濕實驗室；接著以 Four-Leaf Clover RT-qPCR 量測實際的 tRNA 剔除程度，再把這個數字回饋進 M3-A 作為更新後的宿主情境。本專案獲得 Best Model（大學部）與 Best Education（大學部）。","gemsTakeaway_zh":"為每一個模型分數都配上一條明確的證據覆蓋度軌，並對你最站不住腳的那個假設（此處是出口通道長度）做敏感度掃描，讓一張圖不只呈現答案，也呈現其中有多少是真實資料；同時把互相競爭的目標維持為各自對齊的面板，而不是加總成一個自創的分數。這兩件事用 matplotlib、一個有心的 16 歲學生就做得到，而且立刻能讓模型變得誠實。","rank":66},"6098":{"team":"ICJFLS","id":"6098","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/icjfls/","projectTitle":"ORA-GUARD","projectTitle_zh":"ORA-GUARD","tagline":"An engineered oral probiotic that degrades the sulfur compounds causing halitosis instead of sterilising the mouth","tagline_zh":"一株工程改造的口腔益生菌，分解造成口臭的硫化合物，而不是把整個口腔消毒","summary":"ICJFLS engineered Streptococcus salivarius K12, a GRAS oral probiotic, to express a Sox enzyme cluster plus an MTO enzyme that catalytically degrade the volatile sulfur compounds (H2S, methanethiol, dimethyl sulfide) responsible for bad breath, positioning it as a Live Biotherapeutic Product rather than a mouthwash. Plasmid expression was abandoned after stability tests showed near-total plasmid loss within five days without selection, so the cassettes were moved into the chromosome by CRISPR-Cas9, and a four-layer biosafety system (D-alanine auxotrophy via alr knockout, a PcspA RNA-thermometer suicide switch, no antibiotic resistance markers) was added in direct response to public fear of live GMO bacteria. The entrepreneurship case is numerically specific, with per-dose cost, retail price, gross margin and a named contract manufacturer. They were nominated for Best Entrepreneurship in the High School section.","summary_zh":"ICJFLS 把 Streptococcus salivarius K12 這株列為 GRAS 的口腔益生菌加以工程改造，使其表現 Sox 酵素叢集與一個 MTO 酵素，以催化方式分解造成口臭的揮發性硫化物（H2S、甲硫醇、二甲基硫），並把產品定位為活體生物治療產品（LBP），而不是漱口水。質體表現在穩定性測試顯示沒有選擇壓力時五天內質體幾乎全部流失後便被放棄，改以 CRISPR-Cas9 把表現卡匣送進染色體；同時針對民眾對活體 GMO 細菌的恐懼，直接加上四層生物安全系統（以 alr 基因剔除造成的 D-丙胺酸營養缺陷、PcspA RNA 溫度計自殺開關、不使用抗生素抗性標記）。創業面的論證有具體數字：每劑成本、零售價、毛利率，以及指名的委外製造商。他們入圍高中組 Best Entrepreneurship。","awards":["Best Entrepreneurship — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"TAM-SAM-SOM with figures carried through to a revenue target, Business Model Canvas, three-tier business model (B2C subscription, B2B2C through dental clinics, technology licensing), cost structure and pricing with gross margin, a capability gap analysis, a 2026-2035 development roadmap, a risk register, and a comparative regulatory table for LBPs across the US, EU and China. Seven named appendices are listed, including a five-year financial projection model and a patent landscape and IP strategy.","frameworks_zh":"TAM-SAM-SOM，且數字一路貫通到營收目標；Business Model Canvas；三層式商業模式（B2C 訂閱、透過牙科診所的 B2B2C、技術授權）；成本結構與定價含毛利率；能力缺口分析；2026-2035 開發路線圖；風險清單；以及一份美國、歐盟與中國三地 LBP 法規的比較表。另列出七份具名附錄，包括五年財務預測模型與專利地圖及智財策略。","dataviz":"Twelve entrepreneurship figures plus six data tables: TAM/SAM/SOM breakdown, business model canvas, revenue projection chart, product-format panel, roadmap, capability-gap chart and the three-jurisdiction LBP regulatory comparison. Survey results are charted as public attitudes, concerns and information needs.","dataviz_zh":"12 張創業相關圖表加上 6 張資料表：TAM/SAM/SOM 拆解、商業模式圖、營收預測圖、產品形式面板、路線圖、能力缺口圖，以及三個法律管轄區的 LBP 法規比較。問卷結果則繪成民眾態度、顧慮與資訊需求三類圖表。","datascience":"A 745-response questionnaire analysed by age, gender and region, with roughly one third of respondents having experienced halitosis, and results segmented into pain points, safety concerns and information needs. In-vitro degradation efficiency in artificial saliva was benchmarked against purified enzymes. Plasmid-stability passaging produced the five-day loss figure that drove the architecture change.","datascience_zh":"一份 745 份回覆的問卷，依年齡、性別與地區分析，約三分之一的受訪者曾有口臭經驗，結果再切分為痛點、安全顧慮與資訊需求。人工唾液中的體外分解效率以純化酵素為對照基準。質體穩定性的連續傳代實驗則產生了那個五天流失的數字，直接促成架構變更。","software":"","stack":["S. salivarius K12 chassis","CRISPR-Cas9 genomic integration","Sox enzyme gene cluster","MTO enzyme","PcspA RNA thermometer","artificial saliva in-vitro system"],"techniques":["chromosomal integration instead of plasmid expression","D-alanine auxotrophy by alr knockout","temperature-inducible toxin kill switch","VSC quantification in artificial saliva","plasmid retention passaging assay"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A 745-response online questionnaire spanning ages, genders and regions, surfacing the three questions the public actually asks about live engineered bacteria: will it get out of control in the body, will there be side effects, could it be transmitted to others. They then reported a finding most teams would bury, that patients care about what is in it for me and how it works rather than technical sophistication, and rewrote their communication from 'the technology is advanced' to 'it is safe and effective for you'. They also ran public education activities and attended CCIC, the Conference of China iGEMer Community.","publicEngagement_zh":"一份跨年齡、性別與地區、共 745 份回覆的線上問卷，問出了民眾對活體工程細菌真正會問的三個問題：它會不會在體內失控、會不會有副作用、會不會傳染給別人。接著他們報告了一項多數團隊會藏起來的發現：病人在意的是「這對我有什麼好處」和「它怎麼作用」，而不是技術有多精密；於是他們把溝通訊息從「技術很先進」改寫為「它對你安全又有效」。他們也辦了公眾教育活動，並出席 CCIC（Conference of China iGEMer Community）。","ihp":"An explicit dialogue-reflection-iteration-redialogue loop with six documented stakeholder groups, and in each case the design consequence is named. Public fear turned a single safety mechanism into the four-layer defence system. Practising dentists and an oral microbiology researcher killed the original oral-capsule concept on the grounds that capsules have limited local effect in the mouth, which is what produced the mouthwash, lozenge, chewing gum and toothpaste format set and raised the priority on mucosal adhesion and colonisation. At CCIC, senior teams warned that gene editing in non-model organisms would be a bottleneck, so L. reuteri was adopted as a backup chassis, and they shared kill-switch leakage data that caused the team to drop a high-leakage design for the temperature-inducible one. A bioethics professor and a biosafety policy advisor are the reason plasmid expression was abandoned for CRISPR-Cas9 chromosomal integration and why genome-stability and animal toxicology studies were pre-planned.","ihp_zh":"一條明確的對話—反思—迭代—再對話迴路，涵蓋六個有紀錄的利害關係人群體，而且每一次都指出設計上的後果。民眾的恐懼把單一安全機制變成四層防護系統。執業牙醫與一位口腔微生物學研究者否決了最初的口服膠囊構想，理由是膠囊在口腔內的局部作用有限，這才產生漱口水、口含錠、口香糖與牙膏這組產品形式，並把黏膜黏附與定殖的優先度往上提。在 CCIC，資深團隊警告在非模式生物中做基因編輯會是瓶頸，因此團隊把 L. reuteri 納為備用底盤菌株；他們也分享了致死開關的洩漏數據，使團隊捨棄一個高洩漏設計，改用溫度誘導型的版本。一位生物倫理學教授與一位生物安全政策顧問，則是他們放棄質體表現、改走 CRISPR-Cas9 染色體嵌入的原因，也是基因體穩定性與動物毒理學研究被預先排入計畫的原因。","realWorld":"This is a genuine business case with real numbers, and it is the unit economics that separate it from the typical canvas exercise. They state a production cost of roughly RMB 0.5 per dose for freeze-dried bacterial powder plus RMB 0.3 for packaging and filling, totalling about RMB 0.8 per dose falling to RMB 0.3-0.5 at volume; retail pricing of RMB 199 for a 30-dose mouthwash bottle and RMB 159 for a 30-tablet box; and a resulting gross margin of 70-80 percent benchmarked against high-end probiotics. The SOM is built bottom-up rather than taken as a share of the TAM: 100,000 halitosis sufferers at an average RMB 200 per month giving roughly RMB 20 million (about USD 2.8 million) in year one or two, through Tmall, JD.com, Douyin and dental-clinic channels. Market research is partly real and partly desk work: the 745-response questionnaire and dentist interviews are theirs, while the USD 13.44 billion global halitosis market and the RMB 77.9 billion China oral-care figure come from Insight Partners, Frost and Sullivan and similar reports. The competitive analysis is specific and fair, naming BLIS Technologies' BLIS K12 and correctly observing that its deodorising mechanism is indirect because it works through salivaricin bacteriocins, whereas ORA-GUARD catalytically destroys the VSC molecules. The regulatory analysis is the strongest part and is genuinely credible: they identify that NMPA's 2020 biological-products registration classification treats LBPs as therapeutic biological products containing microorganisms, note honestly that neither NMPA nor the FDA has yet issued complete LBP-specific technical guidance, and draw the correct strategic conclusion that this is both policy risk and a chance to help set the standard, with early regulator engagement as the stated tactic. Partners are named rather than implied: Shandong Bona Technology Group for probiotic fermentation and freeze-drying, with industrialisation discussions already begun, and Shijia Doctor Dental Hospital as a clinical and channel partner. Be blunt about the gaps, though. There is no registered company, no incubator place, no grant and no investor commitment; investment partners are described only as a category ('biotechnology VCs and oral care industry funds'). The IP position is weaker than it first reads: the strain construction strategy and genetic circuits are said to form technical barriers that are 'planned to be protected through patent applications', so nothing is filed. The revenue projection figure is labelled as internal estimates, and the appendices (five-year financial model, patent landscape) are listed as titles rather than linked documents, so the deepest financial work is asserted rather than shown. Continuation is a licensing-and-partnering intent rather than a funded plan, and an LBP approval route of that length will outlast any student team unless the Bona relationship becomes a formal transfer.","realWorld_zh":"這是一份有真實數字的商業論證，而把它和典型的商業模式圖作業區分開來的，正是單位經濟。他們寫出冷凍乾燥菌粉每劑生產成本約 RMB 0.5，加上包裝與充填 RMB 0.3，每劑合計約 RMB 0.8，量產後可降到 RMB 0.3-0.5；零售定價為 30 劑漱口水一瓶 RMB 199、30 錠一盒 RMB 159；由此得出的毛利率為 70-80%，並以高階益生菌為對照基準。SOM 是自下而上建起來的，而不是從 TAM 取一個比例：100,000 名口臭患者、每人每月平均 RMB 200，在第一或第二年約為 RMB 2,000 萬（約 USD 280 萬），通路為 Tmall、JD.com、Douyin 與牙科診所。市場研究一部分是實作、一部分是桌面作業：745 份問卷與牙醫訪談是他們自己做的，而全球口臭市場 USD 134.4 億與中國口腔照護 RMB 779 億這兩個數字則來自 Insight Partners、Frost and Sullivan 等報告。競爭分析具體而公允，指名 BLIS Technologies 的 BLIS K12，並正確指出其除臭機制是間接的——它透過 salivaricin 細菌素作用——而 ORA-GUARD 是以催化方式破壞 VSC 分子。法規分析是最強的一段，也確實可信：他們指出 NMPA 2020 年的生物製品註冊分類把 LBP 視為含微生物的治療用生物製品，誠實說明 NMPA 與 FDA 都還沒有發布完整的 LBP 專屬技術指引，並得出正確的策略結論——這既是政策風險，也是參與制定標準的機會，而他們明講的戰術是及早與法規機關往來。合作夥伴是指名的，不是暗示的：Shandong Bona Technology Group 負責益生菌發酵與冷凍乾燥，產業化討論已經開始；Shijia Doctor Dental Hospital 則是臨床與通路夥伴。不過缺口要講白：沒有登記公司、沒有進駐育成中心、沒有補助、也沒有投資人承諾；投資夥伴只以類別描述（「生技創投與口腔照護產業基金」）。智財的位置也比初讀起來弱：菌株建構策略與基因迴路被說成構成技術門檻，而這些是「計畫透過專利申請加以保護」，所以其實什麼都還沒提出申請。營收預測被標為內部估計，附錄（五年財務模型、專利地圖）只列標題而沒有連結文件，所以最深的財務工作是宣稱而非展示。後續發展是授權與合作的意向，而不是有資金的計畫；而一條那麼長的 LBP 審批路徑，會比任何學生團隊都活得久——除非與 Bona 的關係變成正式的技術移轉。","partners":["Shandong Bona Technology Group Co., Ltd. (probiotic fermentation, freeze-drying, technology transfer and industrialisation discussions)","Shijia Doctor Dental Hospital and dental clinics (clinical trials and channel)","Practising dentists and an oral microbiology researcher (dosage form and colonisation advice)","A bioethics professor and a biosafety policy advisor","CCIC (Conference of China iGEMer Community) experts and past award-winning teams","University synthetic biology laboratories"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6098/wiki/entrepre/fig-3-entrepre.avif","caption":"TAM, SAM and SOM analysis for ORA-GUARD, with the SOM built bottom-up from 100,000 target users at RMB 200 per month","caption_zh":"ORA-GUARD 的 TAM、SAM 與 SOM 分析，其中 SOM 由 100,000 名目標使用者、每人每月 RMB 200 自下而上建立","credit":"Team ICJFLS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6098/wiki/entrepre/fig-11-entrepre.avif","caption":"Comparative overview of Live Biotherapeutic Product regulatory pathways in the US, EU and China","caption_zh":"美國、歐盟與中國的活體生物治療產品法規路徑比較總覽","credit":"Team ICJFLS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6098/wiki/entrepre/fig-10-entrepre10.avif","caption":"ORA-GUARD development roadmap from 2026 proof of concept to 2035","caption_zh":"ORA-GUARD 從 2026 年概念驗證到 2035 年的開發路線圖","credit":"Team ICJFLS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6098/wiki/entrepre/fig-12-entrepre.avif","caption":"Gap analysis between current team capabilities and the capabilities needed to commercialise ORA-GUARD","caption_zh":"團隊現有能力與將 ORA-GUARD 商業化所需能力之間的缺口分析","credit":"Team ICJFLS, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Insist on three numbers before any market slide: cost per dose, price per unit and resulting gross margin, built from the actual process (freeze-drying plus fill-and-finish) rather than from a market-report percentage. And copy their SOM discipline, where the obtainable market is users times spend per user per month, not a fraction of a global TAM.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"在任何市場投影片之前，先要求三個數字：每劑成本、每單位售價，以及由此得出的毛利率，而且要從真實製程（冷凍乾燥加上充填包裝）算出來，不是從市場報告的百分比推出來。另外值得照抄的是他們的 SOM 紀律：可取得市場是使用者人數乘以每人每月花費，而不是全球 TAM 的一個比例。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/icjfls/","https://2026.igem.wiki/icjfls/entrepreneurship/","https://2026.igem.wiki/icjfls/human-practices/"],"rank":7},"6102":{"team":"ZJU-China","id":"6102","section":"Undergrad","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/zju-china/","projectTitle":"NEST","projectTitle_zh":"NEST","tagline":"A sequence-defined SELP hydrogel with a SnoopTag2 plug socket, so one cartilage scaffold can be reconfigured by swapping functional peptides","tagline_zh":"一款序列明確定義的 SELP 水凝膠，搭配 SnoopTag2 插槽，因此同一個軟骨支架只要更換功能性胜肽就能重新配置","summary":"ZJU-China built NEST, a silk-elastin-like protein (SELP) hydrogel carrying SnoopTag2 as a standardised ligation interface, so that repair peptides (Link-N, a chondroitin-sulfate-retaining CPC module, a magnetically responsive anisotropy module, a mitochondrial delivery module) can be attached without redesigning the material. They engineered a SnoopLigase2-ZJU variant for the ligation chemistry, purified SELP by inverse transition cycling optimised to 65 degrees C in PBS with 2 M NaCl, and validated GAG binding by AviTag-BirA site-specific biotinylation onto streptavidin beads with DMMB quantification. The commercial case is a full process-economics build rather than a canvas, with equipment, land, working capital, medium, IPTG, kanamycin, labour by shift and waste volumes all costed, plus a 2026-2042 stage-gated roadmap and a ten-year discounted cash-flow model. They were nominated for Best Entrepreneurship (Undergrad) and Best Biomanufacturing.","summary_zh":"ZJU-China 打造了 NEST，一種帶有 SnoopTag2 作為標準化連接介面的絲蛋白-彈性蛋白樣蛋白（SELP）水凝膠，使修復用胜肽（Link-N、一個可保留硫酸軟骨素的 CPC 模組、一個具磁響應性的非等向性模組、一個粒線體遞送模組）能夠直接接上，而不必重新設計材料本身。團隊為這套連接化學改造出 SnoopLigase2-ZJU 變異體，以反相轉變循環純化 SELP 並將條件最佳化為含 2 M NaCl 的 PBS、65 度 C，並以 AviTag-BirA 位點專一性生物素化接到鏈黴親和素磁珠上、再以 DMMB 定量來驗證 GAG 結合。商業論證是一份完整的製程經濟模型，而不是一張商業模式圖：設備、土地、營運資金、培養基、IPTG、卡那黴素、按班別計算的人力與廢棄物量全部估算成本，另有 2026-2042 的階段關卡路線圖與一套十年折現現金流模型。團隊入圍 Best Entrepreneurship（大學部）與 Best Biomanufacturing。","awards":["Best Entrepreneurship — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Biomanufacturing Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"TAM-SAM-SOM with a documented estimation basis and a stated conversion coefficient from osteoarthritis prevalence to the cartilage-repair addressable population, three-tier competitor analysis, NREL-style techno-economic cost structure (fixed capital investment, land, working capital, variable and fixed operating costs, annual capex), a ten-year cash-flow and NPV model, a Sustainable Business Model Canvas, a tiered critical/high risk register tied to stage-gate decisions, a staged financing plan from angel through Series B, a skill-gap analysis across eight capability areas, and a TCFD-shaped ESG framework (governance, strategy, risk and opportunity, metrics and targets).","frameworks_zh":"TAM-SAM-SOM 架構，附有明確記錄的估算依據，以及一個由骨關節炎盛行率換算到軟骨修復可觸及人口的轉換係數；三層級競爭者分析；NREL 式的技術經濟成本結構（固定資本投資、土地、營運資金、變動與固定營運成本、年度資本支出）；一套十年現金流與 NPV 模型；一張永續商業模式圖；一份依關鍵/高風險分級並綁定階段關卡決策的風險清冊；一套由天使輪到 B 輪的分階段籌資計畫；橫跨八個能力領域的技能落差分析；以及一個依 TCFD 架構撰寫的 ESG 框架（治理、策略、風險與機會、指標與目標）。","dataviz":"Nine entrepreneurship figures: SAM and SOM projections, a three-panel budget classification and estimation-basis summary, the 2026-2042 roadmap across R&D, manufacturing, regulatory, fundraising and commercialisation lanes, a ten-year cash-flow chart distinguishing inflows, outflows, net and discounted cash flows, the business model canvas, a skills radar, and three competition-award photographs. A downloadable NEST cost sheet PDF carries the underlying calculations, and five per-module notebook PDFs back the wet-lab work.","dataviz_zh":"九張創業相關圖表：SAM 與 SOM 推估、一張三面板的預算分類與估算依據彙總、橫跨研發、製造、法規、募資與商業化五條軌道的 2026-2042 路線圖、一張區分流入、流出、淨現金流與折現現金流的十年現金流圖、商業模式圖、一張技能雷達圖，以及三張競賽獲獎照片。可下載的 NEST 成本表 PDF 內含底層計算，另有五份各模組的實驗紀錄 PDF 支撐濕實驗成果。","datascience":"The costing is done from first principles rather than from benchmarks. Required SELP output for the initial market is derived first, then equipment is sized against it, giving major equipment of CNY 7.45 million (about USD 1.11 million) estimated with input from Beijing Weixinkang Medical. Consumables are itemised: roughly CNY 290,700 per year for the three main LB components, 7.47 kg of IPTG and 1.57 kg of kanamycin annually, plus PBS and sodium chloride for purification, and about 31,360 L of spent culture medium as annual waste. Labour is modelled as a sum over operations of fully loaded hourly cost, with day and night shifts priced separately against actual Zhejiang biomanufacturing job adverts (CNY 6,000-8,000 per month, conservatively the low end) and Hangzhou cleaner salaries, totalling about CNY 2.6603 million per year. The cash-flow model uses a 10 percent real cost of capital, a 13.27 percent revenue CAGR from a cartilage-repair market report and 2 percent annual cost inflation at a fixed USD 1 = CNY 6.72.","datascience_zh":"成本估算是從第一原理做起，而不是照抄業界標竿。團隊先推導出初期市場所需的 SELP 產量，再據此估算設備規模，得到主要設備約 745 萬 CNY（約 111 萬 USD），此數字參考了 Beijing Weixinkang Medical 的意見。耗材逐項列出：三種主要 LB 成分每年約 290,700 CNY、每年 7.47 kg 的 IPTG 與 1.57 kg 的卡那黴素，加上純化用的 PBS 與氯化鈉，以及每年約 31,360 L 的廢培養基。人力成本以各項操作的全額負擔時薪加總建模，日班與夜班分別定價，依據浙江生物製造業的實際徵才廣告（每月 6,000-8,000 CNY，保守取下限）與杭州清潔人員薪資，合計每年約 266.03 萬 CNY。現金流模型採 10% 的實質資金成本、取自一份軟骨修復市場報告的 13.27% 營收 CAGR，以及每年 2% 的成本通膨，匯率固定為 1 USD = 6.72 CNY。","software":"","stack":["E. coli BL21(DE3)","SELP (silk-elastin-like protein) inverse transition cycling","SnoopTag2 / SnoopLigase2-ZJU","AviTag-BirA biotinylation","streptavidin magnetic beads","DMMB GAG assay","Fe3O4 magnetic nanoparticles with DogTag-TVN","DOPE/DOTAP/DSPE-PEG-Mal liposomes","confocal microscopy and TEM"],"techniques":["modular peptide-peptide ligation as a product interface","temperature and salt-optimised ITC purification (65 C, 2 M NaCl)","site-specific biotinylation for immobilised binding assays","TEV and ULP1 protease processing","liposome-mitochondria complex assembly and uptake","lyophilisation and hydrogel re-formation"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A committed rather than rhetorical plan: during R&D they intend to spend at least CNY 50,000 annually on patient education, public lectures and open science materials, support SynEduGlobal for synthetic-biology education, establish a charitable fund for rural medical outreach and cartilage-health awareness, and continue working with Non-place Studio to use art to build understanding of synthetic biology and empathy for people with cartilage injuries. They also name limited public understanding of hydrogel therapy as a genuine commercial risk to patient confidence and access, not just a communications gap.","publicEngagement_zh":"這是一份有承諾而非只是說法的計畫：團隊打算在研發期間每年至少投入 50,000 CNY 於病患教育、公眾講座與開放科學素材，支持 SynEduGlobal 推動合成生物學教育，設立一筆慈善基金用於偏鄉醫療推廣與軟骨健康意識宣導，並持續與 Non-place Studio 合作，以藝術建立社會對合成生物學的理解，以及對軟骨損傷患者的同理。團隊也把公眾對水凝膠療法理解有限一事，指認為對病患信心與可及性的實質商業風險，而不只是溝通上的落差。","ihp":"Their iHP is organised as design-build-test-learn cycles, with an Implementation stage split into hardware, industrial production and entrepreneurship cycles. The entrepreneurship cycle consulted stakeholders across manufacturing, sales, government regulation, finance and entrepreneurship support, and the documented consequence is specific: they gave cost greater weight in the material design, built the detailed business model, went looking for a CDMO partner, and secured a first expression of investment interest. Clinicians fed back that the material's complexity could complicate market approval, which pushed attention toward regulatory simplicity. Professor Erik Forsberg guided the cash-flow and NPV analysis, and Beijing Weixinkang Medical supplied the equipment cost estimates, so industry input is embedded in the numbers rather than quoted alongside them.","ihp_zh":"他們的整合式人類實踐以設計-建構-測試-學習（DBTL）循環編排，其中「落實」階段再分為硬體、工業生產與創業三個循環。創業循環諮詢了製造、銷售、政府法規、財務與創業輔導等各方利害關係人，而留下紀錄的後果相當具體：團隊在材料設計中給了成本更高的權重、建立了詳細的商業模式、開始尋找 CDMO 夥伴，並取得了第一份投資意向。臨床醫師回饋指出材料的複雜度可能使上市審查變得棘手，這使團隊把注意力轉向法規上的簡潔性。Erik Forsberg 教授指導了現金流與 NPV 分析，Beijing Weixinkang Medical 則提供設備成本估算，因此業界意見是嵌進數字裡，而不是擺在數字旁邊引用。","realWorld":"A genuinely serious venture attempt with one glaring soft spot. The strong parts first. The business model is a phased B2B: research partnerships and technology-development licensing early to build relationships and validate demand, then supply of implant material and delivery solutions to clinical institutions, with orthopaedic companies and hospitals as customers and patients explicitly identified as beneficiaries rather than initial sales targets. Research grants and equity are accounted separately from operating income, which is a distinction most teams blur. The MVP is honestly narrow, the SELP-SnoopTag2 hydrogel alone, with production and storage stability already demonstrated in the lab and the remaining path stated plainly: classification confirmation, product testing, animal studies, clinical trials, NMPA registration, and a medical-device manufacturing licence for the manufacturer, expected to take ten years. The first indication is focal knee-cartilage defects in China, chosen for surgical volume and clinical-evidence base. The cost model is the standout: equipment, land, working capital, itemised media and reagents, shift-differentiated labour, and waste volumes, published as a downloadable cost sheet. Financing is staged and concrete, with real named programmes and amounts: Hangzhou's 5050 Plan (CNY 1 million start-up, up to CNY 10 million in R&D grants), up to CNY 6 million for a first Class III registration manufactured in Hangzhou via Hangzhou Medical Port, up to USD 500,000 from the GenScript Life Science Research Fund, and crucially a named investor, Ms. Zhang Jie of Huadan Angel, who in a stakeholder interview expressed willingness to discuss roughly CNY 1.5 million after first-round samples meet expectations. Industrial relationships are specific and functional rather than decorative: Weixinkang and Lanyiwei on Class III manufacturing and market access, Yuanyi Bio on fermentation and purification, Yiru Bio on scale-up, Shanghai Lingjiu Medical as a possible CDMO, WuXi AppTec's device-testing centre for registration testing, and Evonik, Arthrex and Smith+Nephew as international targets. They won Gold at Zhejiang University's Dandelion Student Innovation Competition (with prize money) and two Golds at SynBio Challenges 2026, in both the main and the industry track, the latter for the SnoopLigase2-ZJU enzyme system, which is independent validation outside iGEM. IP is planned with real specificity: a Chinese invention patent to be filed in November 2026 covering the SELP-SnoopTag2 structure, manufacturing and purification methods, hydrogel formulation, crosslinking system and peptide attachment, with a prior-art search on SnoopTag2, SELP and Ru/SPS crosslinking before any public data release, and the correct observation that treatment methods are not patentable in China so claims must sit on products and manufacturing. The roadmap is stage-gated across 2026-2042 with a criterion and a required-resources list for each window, and they say outright that they will not assign a break-even year or market-share forecast without a defensible financial model. Now the blunt part. That restraint is contradicted by the headline number: a ten-year NPV of about USD 427 million on an initial investment of about USD 8.69 million, produced by assuming NEST captures 10, 25, 50, 75 and then 100 percent of its SOM in years one to five and holds 100 percent of SOM for years six to ten. Capturing the entire serviceable obtainable market and keeping it, for a Class III implant that by their own roadmap will not be registered until roughly 2037, is not a scenario; it is an upper bound, and they label it only as 'favorable assumptions'. There is also no incorporated entity (the name NexCode Biotechnologies appears but no registration is claimed), no filed patent yet, no signed investment, and no animal data at all, which they state clearly as a limitation on any safety or efficacy claim. The honest reading is that the cost side of this model is excellent and the revenue side is aspirational.","realWorld_zh":"這是一次真正認真的創業嘗試，但有一處明顯的軟肋。先談強的部分。商業模式是分階段的 B2B：早期以研究合作與技術開發授權建立關係並驗證需求，之後再向臨床機構供應植入材料與遞送方案，客戶為骨科公司與醫院，而病患被明確定義為受益者，而不是初期的銷售對象。研究補助與股權募資與營運收入分開記帳，這是多數團隊會混在一起的區分。MVP 的範圍很誠實地窄，只有 SELP-SnoopTag2 水凝膠本身，其生產與儲存穩定性已在實驗室中驗證，剩下的路徑也明白寫出：分類確認、產品檢測、動物試驗、臨床試驗、NMPA 註冊，以及製造商的醫療器材製造許可，預期需要十年。第一個適應症是中國的膝關節局部軟骨缺損，選擇理由是手術量與臨床證據基礎。成本模型是最突出的部分：設備、土地、營運資金、逐項列出的培養基與試劑、區分班別的人力，以及廢棄物量，全部做成可下載的成本表公開。籌資規劃分階段且具體，列出真實的計畫名稱與金額：杭州的 5050 計畫（100 萬 CNY 創業金，研發補助最高 1,000 萬 CNY）、透過 Hangzhou Medical Port 在杭州製造並取得第一張第三類註冊最高可得 600 萬 CNY、GenScript Life Science Research Fund 最高 500,000 USD，而關鍵是還有一位具名投資人，Huadan Angel 的 Zhang Jie 女士，她在利害關係人訪談中表示，待第一輪樣品達到預期後，願意洽談約 150 萬 CNY。產業關係具體且具功能性，而不是拿來裝飾：Weixinkang 與 Lanyiwei 負責第三類製造與市場准入、Yuanyi Bio 負責發酵與純化、Yiru Bio 負責放大量產、Shanghai Lingjiu Medical 為可能的 CDMO、WuXi AppTec 的器材檢測中心負責註冊檢測，而 Evonik、Arthrex 與 Smith+Nephew 則列為國際目標對象。團隊在浙江大學 Dandelion Student Innovation Competition 獲金獎（含獎金），並在 SynBio Challenges 2026 的主賽道與產業賽道各拿一面金獎，後者是憑 SnoopLigase2-ZJU 酶系統，屬於 iGEM 之外的獨立驗證。智財規劃也有實際的細節：預計於 2026 年 11 月提出一件中國發明專利，涵蓋 SELP-SnoopTag2 結構、製造與純化方法、水凝膠配方、交聯系統與胜肽接合，並在任何資料公開前先就 SnoopTag2、SELP 與 Ru/SPS 交聯做先前技術檢索；團隊也正確地指出治療方法在中國不可專利，因此請求項必須落在產品與製造上。路線圖在 2026-2042 間設有階段關卡，每個時間窗都附一條判準與一份所需資源清單，而他們也直言，在沒有站得住腳的財務模型之前，不會指定損益兩平年度或市佔率預測。現在談直白的部分。這份自制卻被最醒目的那個數字推翻了：以約 869 萬 USD 的初始投資，推出約 4.27 億 USD 的十年 NPV，而算法是假設 NEST 在第一到第五年分別拿下 SOM 的 10%、25%、50%、75% 然後 100%，並在第六到第十年持續握有 100% 的 SOM。對一項依他們自己的路線圖大約要到 2037 年才會註冊完成的第三類植入物來說，吃下整個可服務可取得市場並一直守住，並不是一種情境，而是一個上限；他們卻只把它標為「有利假設」。此外，公司實體並不存在（文中出現 NexCode Biotechnologies 這個名稱，但沒有宣稱已完成登記）、專利尚未提出、投資尚未簽約，動物實驗資料也完全沒有，而這一點他們自己明確列為任何安全性或療效主張的限制。誠實的讀法是：這個模型的成本面極為出色，營收面則屬一廂情願。","partners":["Beijing Weixinkang Medical Co., Ltd. (Class III manufacturing, sales qualification, market access; equipment cost estimates)","Lanyiwei (Class III medical-device manufacturing and market access)","Yuanyi Bio (synthetic-biology production, fermentation, purification)","Yiru Bio (entrepreneurship and scale-up experience)","Shanghai Lingjiu Medical Technology (biomedical materials, prospective CDMO)","Huadan Angel (Ms. Zhang Jie; expressed willingness to discuss ~CNY 1.5 million early investment)","Professor Erik Forsberg (cash-flow and NPV methodology)","WuXi AppTec medical-device testing centre (prospective registration testing)","Zhejiang University School of Innovation and Entrepreneurship (Dandelion competition)","Non-place Studio (art and public understanding), SynEduGlobal (education)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6102/wiki/images/hp/entrepreneurship/003.avif","caption":"NEST development roadmap and milestones for R&D, manufacturing, regulatory affairs, fundraising and commercialisation, 2026-2042","caption_zh":"NEST 在研發、製造、法規事務、募資與商業化各方面的開發路線圖與里程碑，2026-2042","credit":"Team ZJU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6102/wiki/images/hp/entrepreneurship/004.avif","caption":"Ten-year cash-flow analysis separating inflows, outflows, net and discounted cash flows at a 10 percent real cost of capital","caption_zh":"十年現金流分析，以 10% 的實質資金成本區分流入、流出、淨現金流與折現現金流","credit":"Team ZJU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6102/wiki/images/hp/entrepreneurship/005.avif","caption":"NEST sustainable business model canvas for the phased B2B licensing-then-supply model","caption_zh":"NEST 的永續商業模式圖，對應先授權再供貨的分階段 B2B 模式","credit":"Team ZJU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6102/wiki/images/hp/entrepreneurship/009.avif","caption":"Gold Award for the SnoopLigase2-ZJU enzyme system in the industry track of SynBio Challenges 2026","caption_zh":"SnoopLigase2-ZJU 酶系統在 SynBio Challenges 2026 產業賽道獲得金獎","credit":"Team ZJU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Copy their bottom-up cost sheet: size the required output first, then let equipment, media, IPTG and antibiotic quantities, shift-differentiated labour rates taken from real local job adverts, and annual waste volumes fall out of it, and publish the whole thing as a downloadable file. Then apply the discipline they stated but did not follow on their own revenue line: never model capturing 100 percent of a serviceable obtainable market, and label any such figure as an upper bound rather than a forecast.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"抄下他們那份自下而上的成本表：先把所需產量定出來，再讓設備、培養基、IPTG 與抗生素用量、取自真實當地徵才廣告並區分班別的人力費率，以及年度廢棄物量全部由此推導出來，最後把整份資料做成可下載的檔案公開。接著，把他們自己說了卻沒有做到的紀律套用到營收那一側：永遠不要把模型設定成拿下可服務可取得市場的 100%，而且任何這類數字都該標示為上限，而不是預測。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/zju-china/","https://2026.igem.wiki/zju-china/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/zju-china/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/zju-china/assets/wiki-Bwf3O9W2.js","https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6102/wiki/hp-file/nest-cost-sheet.pdf"],"rank":14},"6105":{"team":"Mingdao","id":"6105","section":"High School","country":"Taiwan","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/mingdao/","projectTitle":"Waste-to-Watt — bioethanol from plastic-coated paper containers","tagline":"Turn the coffee cups and lunch boxes 7,000 students throw away every day into fuel, by pairing enzymes with a glucose-eating microbe in one pot.","summary":"Mingdao take used paper containers — coffee cups, lunch boxes, ramen bowls — and break their cellulose to glucose with an enzyme cocktail for fermentation to bioethanol. The obstacle is end-product inhibition: cellulase is inhibited by cellobiose and beta-glucosidase by glucose. Their answer is Simultaneous Saccharification and Fermentation, putting Zymomonas mobilis in the same vessel as a glucose sink so neither enzyme ever sees inhibitory product. Three models carry it: a Michaelis-Menten competitive-inhibition fit to their own pNPG assay data giving Km, Vmax and Ki for BglA at fermentation-compatible conditions; a Monod fit to their own Z. mobilis growth curves giving mu_max, Ks and biomass yield; and a coupled ODE in SciPy that feeds every one of those measured parameters into a closed-versus-open simulation of the real one-pot reactor. Every parameter in model three came from their own bench.","awards":["Best Model — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Three models in strict dependency order, and the thing that makes this exemplary for a school team is that the third model contains no borrowed numbers — every parameter was measured by the students in models one and two. MODEL 1 is classical enzyme kinetics on BglA beta-glucosidase from Thermotoga maritima, cloned into pET-24a(+) and auto-induced in E. coli BL21(DE3) in Studier's ZYM-5052 medium. They deliberately characterised it at fermentation-compatible conditions (34 C, Bis-Tris pH ~6.4) rather than the enzyme's thermophilic optimum of 80-100 C, because those are the conditions Z. mobilis can survive. The pNPG assay was run as a two-dimensional matrix: three substrate concentrations (1, 2.5, 5 mM) crossed with a 1000-to-0 mM two-fold glucose dilution series, read kinetically at 405 nm over 30 min. Absorbance was converted to product with their own pNP standard curve (Abs405 = 4.0005 x [pNP, mM] + 0.0477, R2 = 0.9989, n = 3). Initial velocity was extracted by a Python script that uses R2 to define the linear region of each progress curve — they require R2 >= 0.995 and discard conditions that fail, which is why two glucose points are explicitly omitted from Table 4. Km and Vmax were first estimated by Lineweaver-Burk double-reciprocal linearisation (Vmax = 0.36 Abs/min, Km = 2.49 mM), then re-estimated by a GLOBAL FIT of the competitive-inhibition Michaelis-Menten equation v = Vmax[S] / (Km(1 + [I]/Ki) + [S]) across all glucose and all pNPG levels at once (Vmax = 0.45 Abs/min, Km = 3.73 mM, Ki = 121 mM) — and they explain why the global fit is the better estimate, because it uses every data point instead of the three zero-glucose ones. MODEL 2 is Monod kinetics on Z. mobilis, grown across a glucose gradient (0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4, 8, 20 mM) in RM medium at 34 C with OD600 read every 30 min for 8 h and glucose tracked in parallel with a household FORA G31 blood-glucose meter. Specific growth rate was obtained the textbook way — convert OD600 to ln(OD600), identify the log phase as the linear region, take the slope with Excel SLOPE and confirm linearity with RSQ, selecting the log-phase window per condition because higher glucose sustains exponential growth longer — then a Python script fitted the Monod equation mu = mu_max[S]/(Ks + [S]) by non-linear regression, giving mu_max = 0.55 /h and Ks = 0.16 mM. They also built their own OD600-to-dry-cell-weight calibration (dilution series, pellets dried at 80 C for 24 h, medium blank subtracted) giving DCW = 1.56 x OD600 - 0.032 (R2 = 0.99), and derived the biomass yield Y_X/S = 0.064 g/g from the 20 mM condition. MODEL 3 is a coupled ODE system for the fed-batch SSF vessel, integrated with scipy.integrate.solve_ivp using RK45 (Dormand-Prince 5(4)), comparing a closed system (enzyme alone) against an open system (enzyme plus 0.05 g/L Z. mobilis inoculum) with cellobiose fed in and the stoichiometric 1 cellobiose to 2 glucose conversion. All seven parameters are listed with their provenance stated in the code comments: Vmax 0.45, Km 3.73, Ki 121 from Model 1; mu_max 0.55, Ks 0.16, Y_X/S 0.064 from Model 2. The result is the proof of concept: in the closed system glucose accumulates, the enzyme is inhibited and the reaction stalls; in the open system Z. mobilis holds glucose low and near-complete saccharification is achieved.","dataviz":"The figures are plain but rigorous, and the discipline is in the captions and the metadata. Every figure names the instrument (BioTek Synergy H1 microplate reader; FORA G31 glucose meter, FORA Taiwan, range 20-600 mg/dL), the buffer and temperature, the replicate count, and the error measure — and where error bars are too small to see the caption says so and points to the table of values. Every figure links its own raw CSV by filename (1mM_pNPG_various_Glucose_Mingdao_MODEL.csv, Kinetics_pNPG_1_2.5_5mM_Glucose_0_to_1000mM.csv, and so on) and every analysis names the Python script that produced it (MODEL_1_enzyme_kinetics_analyzer.py, MODEL_1_lineweaver_burk_analysis.py, MODEL_1_calculate_Ki.py, MODEL_2_Z_mobilis_monod_fit.py, MODEL_3_Coupled_ODE_for_SSF_Simulation.py). The dual-axis growth-and-consumption plot (OD600 rising on the left axis as residual glucose falls on the right) makes the coupling visible in one picture. The ln(OD600)-versus-time panel shows the actual linear fits the growth rates came from rather than just reporting mu. The coupled ODE section is presented as a four-panel simulation of 7-day fed-batch SSF plus a direct closed-versus-open comparison. Most distinctively, the Model 3 page is written as a TUTORIAL: three worked examples build up from dy/dt = ry (exponential growth), through dy/dt = ry(1 - y/K) (logistic S-curve, with a second panel showing the growth rate falling as y approaches K), to a four-variable coupled system of biomass, nutrient, oxygen and pH — each with its complete, downloadable, commented Python script printed in full on the wiki, each with plain-language explanations of what RK45 does and why a coupled system cannot be solved one equation at a time.","datascience":"This is the cohort's clearest example of a model fitted entirely to the team's own measurements and then read against literature with real care. Each fitted parameter is compared to published values with the discrepancy explained rather than hidden: Vmax is far below Mehmood's 238 IU/mg for purified enzyme, which they attribute correctly to two causes — crude lysate in which the recombinant protein is only an estimated 30-40% of total protein, so their Vmax is a relative rate and not a mass-normalised specific activity, and operation at 34 C rather than the 80-100 C thermophilic optimum, supported by Li et al.'s finding that the same enzyme peaks at 90 C and declines sharply toward 30 C. Their mu_max of 0.55 /h sits inside the reported 0.3-1.1 /h range for Z. mobilis. Their Ks of 0.16 mM is 3-7x lower than published values, and rather than claiming a better result they warn it 'should be regarded as an approximate estimate and not over-interpreted' because it falls below their lowest tested glucose concentration (0.25 mM) and because the organism grew on yeast extract alone at 0 mM glucose (mu = 0.29 /h). Their OD-to-DCW factor of 1.56 g/L per OD600 looked 4x higher than E. coli cuvette values, so they worked out why — a 96-well plate with 100 uL gives a ~0.31 cm light path versus 1 cm in a cuvette — and rescaled it (1.56 x 0.31 = 0.48 g/L per OD600) to land inside the literature range, then explained why they benchmarked against E. coli at all (no published Z. mobilis value exists, and both are similarly sized rod-shaped Gram-negative bacteria). Y_X/S = 0.064 g/g matched the reported 0.055-0.06 g/g, and they read the low value correctly as favourable, since it means most glucose goes to ethanol rather than cell mass while still acting as a sink. Limitations are stated squarely: n = 1 per condition in the inhibition matrix, with robustness argued only from consistency across the three independent substrate levels; three substrate points is 'just enough to obtain a rough estimate' of Km and Vmax; and the central caveat that all enzyme parameters were measured on pNPG while the real SSF feed is cellobiose, so applying them is an approximation — with ten Kate et al.'s distinct cellobiose values cited as evidence it will matter, and direct cellobiose characterisation named as future work. They also scope the simulation honestly: 'this season's simulation tested one inoculum (0.05 g/L) against one feed rate; scanning a range of inocula and enzyme loadings is the next step.' The explicit choice of which target to model is itself good practice: they modelled beta-glucosidase because it is the part they characterised themselves, because glucose inhibition is the rate-limiting bottleneck, and because it is the step the Z. mobilis sink directly relieves, while cellulase was an existing documented BioBrick (BBa_K118023) and cellobiose inhibition of it is declared future work.","software":"All scripts and raw data are published with running instructions in the team's software repository, named per figure so any reader can reproduce a specific number. The Model 3 page functions as a free standing teaching resource: simpleODE.py, extendedODE.py and coupledODE.py are each printed in full and downloadable, with the SciPy and Dormand-Prince references cited properly. The analysis scripts were written with AI-assisted coding tools under the guidance of Kai-Hsiang Chen, a teacher at the school's Information Technology and Digital Learning Center — credited by name, which is the right way to be transparent about how a high school team got to a non-linear global fit.","stack":["Python","NumPy","SciPy (scipy.integrate.solve_ivp, RK45 / Dormand-Prince 5(4); non-linear regression)","Matplotlib","Excel (SLOPE, RSQ)","BioTek Synergy H1 microplate reader","FORA G31 glucose meter","AI-assisted coding tools"],"techniques":["Michaelis-Menten enzyme kinetics","Lineweaver-Burk double-reciprocal linearisation","competitive product-inhibition model and Ki determination","global non-linear fitting across a two-dimensional substrate x inhibitor matrix","R2-gated selection of the linear region for initial-rate extraction","standard-curve calibration (pNP absorbance to concentration)","Monod growth kinetics","log-linear specific growth rate estimation","OD600-to-dry-cell-weight calibration with light-path correction","biomass yield (Y_X/S) determination","coupled ODE system integration with adaptive-step Runge-Kutta","closed-versus-open counterfactual simulation","parameter provenance tracking from assay to simulation","literature benchmarking of fitted parameters with discrepancy analysis"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"The project itself grew out of the school's own waste stream — more than 7,000 students and 400 staff eat lunch at Mingdao High School every school day — which gives every conversation about it an immediate, local referent. Materials from the Human Practices work are published as downloads.","ihp":"The best-structured high school Human Practices narrative in this set, because it starts from a question the students genuinely could not answer. Sitting with a used paper container in front of them, somebody asked where it actually goes, and none of them knew, despite having sorted those containers into their own bin for years because a sign told them to. They then wrote down five open questions and took each one to the people who could answer it: where does our paper waste actually go (following one container as far as they could); why will nobody take it, given that it is collected separately and has a price; is the problem already solved, since they had heard used paper containers become recycled tissue paper — and they state explicitly that if that were true for their waste there would be no need for a synthetic biology solution at all; could they build the paper-to-fuel conversion themselves, having never used an enzyme, a fermenting microbe or a vessel; and could the process ever leave the laboratory. The page is organised as two acts, Act I Following the Waste (outward, to the problem that defines the project) and Act II Building the Answer (back to the bench), with further sections on what the technology would do to the stakeholders involved, where they agreed and disagreed, and how each of the five questions was answered. Setting out in advance a condition under which their own project would be unnecessary is a standard of intellectual honesty worth copying.","realWorld":"Plastic-coated paper containers are the category everyone in the recycling chain would rather not receive, which is the market gap the project aims at. The engineering choice is driven by that reality: Simultaneous Saccharification and Fermentation in one vessel avoids the separate hydrolysis and fermentation steps that would make a small-scale, on-site unit impractical, and the model's stated purpose is to estimate how much Z. mobilis to inoculate in a fermentor to match the glucose production rate of beta-glucosidase — a directly operational question. The team also note that accepting lower enzyme activity at 34 C is a deliberate trade for compatibility with the microbe, and that the coupled system lets even a sub-optimal-temperature enzyme run effectively by keeping glucose low.","partners":["Mingdao High School","Mingdao High School Information Technology and Digital Learning Center"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6105/wiki/model2.avif","caption":"The Waste-to-Watt SSF fermentor: cellulase and beta-glucosidase saccharify paper-container cellulose to glucose while Zymomonas mobilis simultaneously ferments that glucose to bioethanol, so neither enzyme ever accumulates enough product to inhibit itself.","credit":"Team Mingdao, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6105/wiki/model-fig1-v2.avif","caption":"Glucose-gradient inhibition of 1 mM pNPG hydrolysis by BglA beta-glucosidase, across a 1000-to-0 mM two-fold glucose dilution series read kinetically at 405 nm. The same matrix was run at 2.5 and 5 mM pNPG, and the three datasets were fitted globally to the competitive-inhibition equation to give Ki = 121 mM.","credit":"Team Mingdao, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6105/wiki/model20.avif","caption":"The team's own OD600-to-dry-cell-weight calibration for Z. mobilis (pellets dried at 80 C for 24 h, medium blank subtracted), giving DCW = 1.56 x OD600 - 0.032 with R2 = 0.99. When the factor looked 4x higher than E. coli values, they worked out that a 96-well plate gives a ~0.31 cm light path versus 1 cm in a cuvette and rescaled it back into the literature range.","credit":"Team Mingdao, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6105/wiki/model24.avif","caption":"The payoff: the coupled ODE comparison of a closed system (beta-glucosidase alone, where glucose accumulates, the enzyme is inhibited and the reaction stalls) against an open system (beta-glucosidase plus Z. mobilis, where the microbe holds glucose low and near-complete saccharification is reached). Every parameter in this simulation was measured by the team in Models 1 and 2.","credit":"Team Mingdao, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"This is the template for a school-level model done properly: measure your own kinetic and growth parameters at the conditions your real system will actually run at, fit them with a named equation and a script you publish, and then build one coupled simulation in which every single parameter traces back to one of your own measurements — plus a closed-versus-open counterfactual so the simulation answers a yes/no design question. Mingdao also show how to benchmark against literature: when a fitted value disagrees, explain the mechanism (light-path length, crude lysate purity, sub-optimal temperature) rather than hiding it.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/mingdao/","https://2026.igem.wiki/mingdao/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/mingdao/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/mingdao/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/mingdao/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/mingdao/contribution/"],"rank":7},"6108":{"team":"GU Frankfurt","id":"6108","section":"Overgrad","country":"Germany","village":"Therapeutics","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/gu-frankfurt/","projectTitle":"HIDE","projectTitle_zh":"HIDE","tagline":"Hiding a transplanted organ from the immune system instead of suppressing the immune system","tagline_zh":"把移植器官藏起來不讓免疫系統看見，而不是去壓制免疫系統","summary":"Around 183,000 transplants a year are followed by lifelong immunosuppression, which protects the graft by weakening the whole patient. HIDE attacks the cause instead: a synNotch receptor carrying a computationally designed binder recognises the donor organ's mismatched HLA class I alleles, triggers production and export of shRNA in extracellular vesicles, and silences only those 'non-self' HLAs by RNA interference, leaving the rest of the immune system intact. Three research fields are bridged at once (synNotch, RNAi, exosome delivery), with the binder and the shRNA both designed in silico by the dry lab and validated by FACS, qPCR, western blot and nanoparticle tracking analysis. It won Best Part Collection and Best Education because the by-products are as usable as the therapy: HUSH, an open-source RNAi design framework for polymorphic gene families, and TRUST, a framework for communicating about death and grief that iGEM did not previously have.","summary_zh":"每年約有 183,000 例移植手術，術後隨之而來的是終身免疫抑制——為了保住移植物，卻削弱了整個病人。HIDE 改從病因下手：一個帶有以電腦設計的結合子（binder）的 synNotch 受體辨識捐贈器官上不相配的 HLA class I 等位基因，觸發 shRNA 的生產並以胞外囊泡輸出，再透過 RNA 干擾只沉默那些「非自體」的 HLA，其餘免疫系統維持完整。此專題一次串起三個研究領域（synNotch、RNAi、exosome 遞送），結合子與 shRNA 都由乾實驗以電腦設計，並以 FACS、qPCR、西方墨點法與奈米顆粒追蹤分析驗證。它拿下最佳元件集合與最佳教育獎，因為其副產物和療法本身一樣好用：HUSH，一套針對多型性基因家族的開源 RNAi 設計框架；以及 TRUST，一套談論死亡與哀傷的溝通框架，這是 iGEM 此前所沒有的。","awards":["Top 10 (Overgrad)","Best Part Collection — Winner (Overgrad)","Best Software — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Education — Winner (Overgrad)","Best Presentation — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Therapeutics Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Two pipelines solving an allele-discrimination problem that has no off-the-shelf method. For the binder, the team deliberately picked the harder target: HLA-A*01 (allele frequency around 15%) rather than the more common HLA-A*02, because A*01 carries fewer polymorphisms relative to other common alleles and therefore makes a specific binder harder to design; an IPD-IMGT multiple sequence alignment of HLA-A*01:01:01:01 against A*02:01:01:01 and A*03:01:01:01 located the usable mismatches, concentrated in and around the peptide-binding groove of the polymorphic alpha1 and alpha2 domains. They then generated roughly 2,000 de novo binders with BindCraft and RFdiffusion3, scored affinity and specificity against target and off-target HLAs with Boltz-2 and AlphaFold, and carried the eight most promising designs into molecular dynamics simulations for stability, across six design batches with combined MD results. For the shRNA, sequence alignment identified nucleotide-level discriminating positions, candidates were designed and evaluated with siDirect, and every candidate was screened against the human genome for off-targets in other human mRNAs. HUSH then added 150 further shRNAs with alignment-aware targeting.","frameworks_zh":"兩條流程，處理一個沒有現成方法的等位基因辨別問題。在結合子方面，團隊刻意挑了較難的標的：選 HLA-A*01（等位基因頻率約 15%）而非更常見的 HLA-A*02，因為 A*01 相對於其他常見等位基因的多型性較少，要設計出具專一性的結合子因此更難；他們以 IPD-IMGT 把 HLA-A*01:01:01:01 與 A*02:01:01:01、A*03:01:01:01 做多序列比對，找出可用的不相配位點，這些位點集中在多型性的 alpha1 與 alpha2 區域的胜肽結合溝及其周邊。接著以 BindCraft 與 RFdiffusion3 產生約 2,000 個從頭設計的結合子，用 Boltz-2 與 AlphaFold 對標的與非標的 HLA 評估親和力與專一性，再把最有潛力的 8 個設計帶入分子動力學模擬檢驗穩定性，前後共六批設計並彙整模擬結果。在 shRNA 方面，序列比對找出核苷酸層級的辨別位點，候選序列以 siDirect 設計與評估，每個候選都再對人類基因組篩查在其他人類 mRNA 上的脫靶可能。HUSH 之後又追加了 150 條具序列比對意識的標靶 shRNA。","dataviz":"The wiki is built as an explorable system rather than a document. The dry-lab overview is a hover-and-click hitbox diagram where each component (Binder, shRNA, HUSH) reveals its rationale and links through to its own results page. The HLA class I architecture is a draggable 3D structure coloured by domain (alpha1, alpha2, alpha3, beta2m) so the reader can see for themselves that the variation sits in the groove. The MSA is shown in classic dash notation against the A*01 reference so each mismatch is countable. MD runs are published as per-binder, per-allele animations (for example binder FR57 against HLA-A*01, A*02 and A*03 side by side), which makes specificity visible rather than tabulated. The HUSH page embeds a working mockup of the five-stage wizard with sample data that the reader can step through, and the mascot Heidi narrates each step. Human practices is an interactive stakeholder map filterable by affiliation and by part of the construct, so a reader can ask 'who shaped the binder?' and get an answer. Education statistics are presented as before-and-after pairs, not totals.","dataviz_zh":"這個 wiki 做成一套可探索的系統、而不是一份文件。乾實驗總覽是一張可滑過與點擊的熱區圖，每個組件（Binder、shRNA、HUSH）都會展開其設計理由，並連到各自的結果頁。HLA class I 的結構以可拖曳的 3D 模型呈現、依區域上色（alpha1、alpha2、alpha3、beta2m），讀者自己就看得出變異位在結合溝上。多序列比對以傳統的破折號記法對照 A*01 參考序列呈現，使每個不相配位點都數得出來。分子動力學的結果以每個結合子、每個等位基因為單位的動畫發表（例如把結合子 FR57 對 HLA-A*01、A*02 與 A*03 並排呈現），讓專一性看得見、而非只列成表。HUSH 頁面內嵌一個可運作的五階段精靈模擬界面，附上範例資料供讀者逐步操作，並由吉祥物 Heidi 逐步解說。人類實踐做成一張可依所屬單位、也可依構築的哪個部分篩選的互動利害關係人地圖，讀者可以直接問「是誰影響了結合子的設計？」並得到答案。教育成效以前後對照的成對數據呈現，而不是總量。","datascience":"HUSH exists because the team audited the tool landscape and found it stagnant: commercial RNAi designers are proprietary black boxes whose algorithms and option sets are undocumented, and even non-commercial siDirect is neither open-source nor pipeline-integrable, while recent published advances for discriminating highly similar sequences had been implemented nowhere. HUSH therefore folds multiple sequence alignment into the design step itself: a target sequence plus an optional panel of related sequences (the alleles to spare) switches on allele-aware targeting and an MSA stage, and the tool inspects the input up front (molecule type, length, GC content, panel size) and warns, for example, that a GC-rich target may cause the seed filter to reject every candidate, then offers to relax that filter in the criteria step. Protein input is flagged because it must be resolved to a transcript first. Safety is a scoring stage, not a disclaimer: candidates are aligned with Bowtie against NCBI human RefSeq, and the team proposes extending the standard off-target check to known single-nucleotide polymorphisms that could create unwanted off-targets. Designed siRNAs convert to shRNAs with hairpin-loop guidance and thermodynamic evaluation of structure integrity.","datascience_zh":"HUSH 之所以存在，是因為團隊盤點了工具生態後發現它停滯不前：商用 RNAi 設計工具是專有的黑盒子，演算法與選項設定都沒有文件，就連非商業的 siDirect 也既非開源、也無法整進流程，而近年已發表的、用於辨別高度相似序列的進展則完全沒有任何實作。因此 HUSH 把多序列比對折進設計步驟本身：輸入一條標的序列，再加上一組可選的相關序列（也就是要保留的等位基因），就會啟動具等位基因意識的標靶設定與一個比對階段；工具會在一開始就檢視輸入（分子類型、長度、GC 含量、序列組大小）並提出警示，例如 GC 含量高的標的可能導致種子區過濾器把所有候選都剔除，接著在條件設定步驟提供放寬該過濾器的選項。蛋白質輸入會被標記，因為必須先解析為對應的轉錄本。安全性是一個評分階段、不是免責聲明：候選序列以 Bowtie 對 NCBI human RefSeq 比對，團隊並提議把標準脫靶檢查擴及已知的單核苷酸多型性，因為這些位點可能造成不想要的脫靶。設計好的 siRNA 會在髮夾環的設計指引與結構完整性的熱力學評估下轉換為 shRNA。","software":"HUSH (Human genome-Universal Silencing Hairpin designer), open-source on GitLab, ships in four interfaces around one core HushSession object: a guided five-step web wizard plus a compact expert mode exposing thermodynamic constants and selection rules, a CLI for one-shot pipeline use, a persistent in-terminal shell with saved input and panels, and an MCP server so an AI agent can drive it. A REST API provides compatibility for external pipelines. The three stated design tenets are research-first (every option documented with the research behind it), accessibility (upload a sequence and be guided, with proposed optimal choices derived from the sequence), and safety. The team also released START (SynBio Travellers, an educational browser game) and TRUST (a sensitive-topics framework), and the wiki repository is gitlab.igem.org/2026/gu-frankfurt.","software_zh":"HUSH（Human genome-Universal Silencing Hairpin designer）在 GitLab 上開源，圍繞同一個核心的 HushSession 物件提供四種介面：一個有引導的五步網頁精靈，外加一個精簡的專家模式可直接調整熱力學常數與篩選規則；一個供一次性整進流程使用的 CLI；一個可保存輸入與序列組、常駐於終端機的互動介面；以及一個 MCP 伺服器，讓 AI 代理人能驅動它。另有 REST API 供外部流程相容接取。他們明示的三項設計原則是研究優先（每個選項都附上背後研究的文件）、易用性（上傳序列就會被引導，並依序列推導出建議的最佳選項）與安全性。團隊另外釋出了 START（SynBio Travellers，一款教育用瀏覽器遊戲）與 TRUST（敏感議題框架），wiki 的程式庫在 gitlab.igem.org/2026/gu-frankfurt。","stack":["BindCraft","RFdiffusion3","Boltz-2","AlphaFold","molecular dynamics simulation","siDirect","Bowtie","NCBI RefSeq","IPD-IMGT/HLA alignment tool","GitLab (open source)","REST API","MCP server","CLI + terminal shell + web wizard"],"techniques":["de novo protein binder generation at ~2000-candidate scale","affinity and specificity co-scoring against off-target alleles","MD stability triage of top candidates","multiple sequence alignment driven allele discrimination","genome-wide off-target screening","SNP-aware off-target proposal","shRNA hairpin thermodynamic evaluation","synNotch receptor engineering","extracellular-vesicle RNA delivery","qPCR, FACS, western blot, nanoparticle tracking analysis readouts"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A five-media strategy (game, workshops, social dialogue, print, audio) built on training the team first: 19 members took the 'Basics of Science Communication' workshop from NaWik, the German National Institute for Science Communication, and used its core-message, cloverleaf and arrow tools as the basis of everything after. Outputs were then measured, not just counted: nine school workshops at two schools reached over 140 students, with the share who knew that the family decides when no donation wish is documented rising from 66.1% to 91.9%, and 103 of 147 students saying they would talk to others (counted conservatively at four people each as a take-home estimate). HIDE & SEEK, a printed educational magazine distributed in pharmacies, doctors' practices and gyms, raised average correct answers across four knowledge questions from 88% to 100%. They ran a Night of Science survey booth, presented HIDE on hr3 radio (about one million daily listeners), were featured in BIOspektrum, UniReport and Wissen wird, appeared on iGEM Lund's podcast 'The Sequence', built the START browser game, and distributed hundreds of organ donation cards.","publicEngagement_zh":"一套五種媒介的策略（遊戲、工作坊、社會對話、印刷、聲音），建立在先訓練自己團隊的基礎上：19 位成員上了德國國家科學傳播研究所 NaWik 的「科學傳播基礎」工作坊，並以其核心訊息、四葉草與箭頭等工具作為之後一切工作的基礎。產出接著被量測、不只是計數：在兩所學校舉辦九場校園工作坊、觸及超過 140 位學生，知道「在沒有書面捐贈意願紀錄時由家屬決定」的比例從 66.1% 升至 91.9%，147 位學生中有 103 位表示會再去告訴別人（保守以每人四位計算，作為擴散效果的估計）。《HIDE & SEEK》是一本在藥局、診所與健身房發放的印刷版教育雜誌，使四道知識題的平均正確率從 88% 提升到 100%。他們在 Night of Science 設了問卷攤位、在 hr3 廣播（每日約一百萬聽眾）介紹 HIDE，獲 BIOspektrum、UniReport 與 Wissen wird 報導，上了 iGEM Lund 的播客《The Sequence》，做出 START 瀏覽器遊戲，並發送了數百張器官捐贈卡。","ihp":"50 stakeholders in 44 interviews across six countries, sorted into five functions (defining the need, designing the therapy, route to the clinic, the donation debate, sensitive communication and education) and mapped against the part of the construct each one shaped. Documented changes: DSO and Eurotransplant quantified the logistics and donor shortage that justify the project; Prof. Urs Christen's account of lifelong immunosuppression side effects pushed the team toward a personalised approach; Dr. Venugopal Gudipati made binder accuracy the governing constraint on the receptor arm, and Dr. Gregory Allen shaped the synNotch design; CAR-T experts set the manufacturing, logistics and cost frame for an autologous therapy. In the donation debate the team interviewed politicians on both sides (Dr. Armin Grau and Helge Lindh), found both agreed the real deficit is education, and wrote a political proposal to make their workshops a mandatory part of school curricula, presented on 22 September 2026 to the cross-party Bundestag group 'Freiwilligkeit in der Organspende', which agreed to consider it. The largest change was procedural: interviewing people with lived transplant experience showed the team that iGEM has biosafety guidance but nothing on sensitive topics, which iGEM's own Human Practices committee confirmed when asked, so they built TRUST (Talking Responsibly and Understanding Sensitive Topics) with Dr. Katharina Karcher of the MASTERY project at Birmingham, transplant psychologist Dr. Angela Buchholz (who showed that unfamiliar language creates fear rather than understanding), supervisor Ariane Mantey-Strauss, ethicist Dr. Timo Sauer, nurse Sanjin Krupic, DSO's PD Dr. Ana Paula Barreiros, and former iGEM Safety and Security chief Alonso Flores, who pushed back that no framework can move responsibility off the teams themselves.","ihp_zh":"六個國家、44 場訪談、50 位利害關係人，依五項功能分類（界定需求、設計療法、通往臨床的路徑、捐贈議題的公共辯論、敏感溝通與教育），並對應到各自影響了構築的哪個部分。有紀錄的改動包括：DSO 與 Eurotransplant 量化了支撐本專題立論的物流與捐贈者短缺狀況；Prof. Urs Christen 對終身免疫抑制副作用的描述，推動團隊走向個人化的做法；Dr. Venugopal Gudipati 使結合子的準確性成為受體這一端的首要約束條件，Dr. Gregory Allen 則形塑了 synNotch 的設計；CAR-T 專家為一項自體療法設定了製造、物流與成本的框架。在捐贈議題的辯論上，團隊訪談了立場相對的兩位政治人物（Dr. Armin Grau 與 Helge Lindh），發現雙方都同意真正的缺口在教育，於是撰寫了一份政治提案，主張把他們的工作坊納入學校課綱的必修內容，並於 2026 年 9 月 22 日向德國聯邦議院跨黨派小組「Freiwilligkeit in der Organspende」提出，該小組同意納入考慮。最大的改動是程序上的：訪談有移植親身經驗的人之後，團隊發現 iGEM 有生物安全指引、卻完全沒有敏感議題的指引，詢問後 iGEM 自己的人類實踐委員會也確認如此，於是他們建立了 TRUST（Talking Responsibly and Understanding Sensitive Topics），合作者包括伯明罕 MASTERY 計畫的 Dr. Katharina Karcher、移植心理師 Dr. Angela Buchholz（她指出陌生的語彙製造的是恐懼、不是理解）、督導 Ariane Mantey-Strauss、倫理學者 Dr. Timo Sauer、護理師 Sanjin Krupic、DSO 的 PD Dr. Ana Paula Barreiros，以及前 iGEM 安全與保安負責人 Alonso Flores——後者反駁說，任何框架都無法把責任從隊伍自己身上移開。","realWorld":"The commercialisation strategy is an exclusive licensing agreement: HIDE retains the intellectual property while a large pharmaceutical partner takes manufacturing, distribution and payer negotiation, chosen because an autologous cell therapy's facility, consumable and specialist-salary costs cannot be matched by a start-up. Miltenyi Biotec has issued a letter of support. The analysis names the customer chain (pharmaceutical companies, statutory health insurers, transplant centres) rather than patients, because an advanced cell therapy cannot be sold direct, and works through German reimbursement specifically: near-universal statutory coverage funded at 14.6% of income, with price set by negotiation with the manufacturer. The page carries cost of goods per dose, a seven-year forecast, a regulatory roadmap with milestones and risks, a Business Model Canvas, SWOT and skill-gap analyses the team describes as an honest look at their own gaps, a PEST analysis, and a mapping to the UN Sustainable Development Goals. Input came from the iGEM Entrepreneurship Bootcamp, Innovectis and the Charite Berlin Regulatory Support Unit.","realWorld_zh":"商業化策略是獨家授權協議：HIDE 保留智慧財產權，由一家大型製藥夥伴承接製造、通路與付費方的議價，之所以這樣選，是因為自體細胞療法所需的廠房、耗材與專業人力薪資成本，新創公司無法負擔。Miltenyi Biotec 已出具支持函。分析中指名的客戶鏈是製藥公司、法定健保與移植中心、而不是病人，因為先進細胞療法無法直接銷售給病人；並具體走過德國的給付制度：近乎全民的法定保險以所得的 14.6% 籌資，價格則由與製造商議價決定。該頁面附有每劑的銷貨成本、七年期預測、含里程碑與風險的法規路線圖、商業模式畫布、團隊自稱是誠實檢視自身缺口的 SWOT 與技能落差分析、PEST 分析，以及對聯合國永續發展目標的對應。意見來源包括 iGEM 創業訓練營、Innovectis 與柏林 Charité 的法規支援單位。","partners":["Miltenyi Biotec (letter of support)","NaWik, National Institute for Science Communication","Deutsche Stiftung Organtransplantation (DSO)","Eurotransplant","Cross-party Bundestag group 'Freiwilligkeit in der Organspende'","Dr. Katharina Karcher, MASTERY, University of Birmingham","Dr. Angela Buchholz, University Hospital Hamburg-Eppendorf","Alonso Flores, former iGEM Safety and Security Programme Chief","Innovectis (Goethe University technology transfer)","Regulatory Support Unit, Charite Berlin","Prof. Rainer Blasczyk, Hannover Medical School","Prof. Klemens Budde, Charite","MD PhD Gregory Allen","Prof. Jens Kurreck, TU Berlin","iGEM Lund ('The Sequence' podcast)","hr3 (Hessischer Rundfunk)","BIOspektrum"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6108/wiki/images/drylab/hush/hush-1-input-page.avif","caption":"HUSH step one: the target sequence to silence plus an optional panel of related alleles to spare, with live input inspection reporting molecule type, length, GC content and readiness, and warning when a GC-rich target may defeat the seed filter.","caption_zh":"HUSH 的第一步：輸入要沉默的標的序列，再加上一組可選的、要保留的相關等位基因序列；系統即時檢視輸入並回報分子類型、長度、GC 含量與是否就緒，並在 GC 含量高的標的可能使種子區過濾器失效時提出警示。","credit":"Team GU Frankfurt, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6108/wiki/images/drylab/hush/hush-architecture.svg","caption":"HUSH architecture: one central HushSession interface serving the web wizard, the CLI, the terminal shell and the MCP server, so the same design logic is reachable by a newcomer, a pipeline or an AI agent.","caption_zh":"HUSH 的架構：一個中央的 HushSession 介面同時支撐網頁精靈、CLI、終端機互動介面與 MCP 伺服器，使同一套設計邏輯對新手、對流程、對 AI 代理人都可取用。","credit":"Team GU Frankfurt, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6108/wiki/images/wetlab/wetlab-figures-fixed/synnotch/fig-19-fr57-facs.svg","caption":"FACS characterisation of the designed binder FR57 in the synNotch receptor, testing whether a de novo binder discriminates HLA-A*01 from the near-identical A*02 and A*03 alleles.","caption_zh":"以 FACS 對 synNotch 受體上設計出的結合子 FR57 做特性分析，檢驗一個從頭設計的結合子能否把 HLA-A*01 與幾乎相同的 A*02、A*03 等位基因區分開來。","credit":"Team GU Frankfurt, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6108/wiki/images/education-page/images-cropped/workshop-figure-1.avif","caption":"One of nine school workshops on organ donation and synthetic biology, measured with before-and-after knowledge questions; the proposal to make these workshops curriculum-mandatory reached the German Bundestag.","caption_zh":"九場器官捐贈與合成生物學校園工作坊中的一場，以前後知識題量測成效；把這些工作坊納入課綱必修的提案已送進德國聯邦議院。","credit":"Team GU Frankfurt, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Two things are directly copyable. First, HUSH's premise: when the standard tool for your problem is a proprietary web form, the gap itself is a publishable contribution, so build the open version with the alignment step folded in and the safety check scored rather than disclaimed. Second, treat outreach as an experiment with a pre-and-post instrument (66.1% to 91.9% on a single factual question is worth more than 'we reached 500 people'), and build a TRUST-style written protocol before students run any activity touching death, illness or grief.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"有兩點可以直接借鏡。第一是 HUSH 的立論前提：當你問題領域裡的標準工具是一個專有的網頁表單，這個缺口本身就是可發表的貢獻，所以就把開源版本做出來，把序列比對這一步整合進去，並把安全性檢查做成評分、而不是免責聲明。第二是把科普當成實驗來做，備好前後測工具（在單一事實題上從 66.1% 提升到 91.9%，比「我們觸及 500 人」有價值得多），並在學生執行任何涉及死亡、疾病或哀傷的活動之前，先建立一份 TRUST 那樣的書面規範。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/gu-frankfurt/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gu-frankfurt/drylab","https://2026.igem.wiki/gu-frankfurt/binder-design","https://2026.igem.wiki/gu-frankfurt/hush","https://2026.igem.wiki/gu-frankfurt/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/gu-frankfurt/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/gu-frankfurt/trust","https://2026.igem.wiki/gu-frankfurt/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/gu-frankfurt/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/gu-frankfurt/start"],"rank":143},"6110":{"team":"TU Delft","id":"6110","section":"Overgrad","country":"Netherlands","village":"Biomanufacturing","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-delft/","projectTitle":"MOSAIC","projectTitle_zh":"MOSAIC","tagline":"A modular elastin-like polypeptide coating platform that lets one implant surface be tuned to the tissue, and the patient, it sits in.","tagline_zh":"一個模組化的類彈性蛋白多肽塗層平台，讓同一種植入物表面能依其所在的組織、以及病人本身來調整。","summary":"MOSAIC is a modular implant coating built from elastin-like polypeptides (ELPs) that can be swapped part by part so a single platform serves many implants and tissues. The team's insight is that an implant coating has to match the stiffness and biochemistry of its target tissue: tissue stiffness spans 0.1 kPa in brain to over 1 MPa in bone, while titanium is around 100 GPa, so a one-size coating gives cells the wrong signal. They built five linked models to steer design before the lab work - an XGBoost predictor of ELP transition temperature, coarse-grained molecular dynamics of the surface-tethered hydrogel, an omics pipeline turning transcriptomic and proteomic atlases into tissue-specific coating recipes, a SuperPro Designer scale-up of ELP manufacturing, and a life-cycle assessment of that process - and they ran Value Sensitive Design across 13 interviews so stakeholders shaped the construct while it could still change. It took the Overgrad Grand Prize along with Best Wiki, Best Integrated Human Practices and Best Biomanufacturing Project.","summary_zh":"MOSAIC 是一種以類彈性蛋白多肽（ELP）構成的模組化植入物塗層，可逐一替換部件，因此單一平台就能服務多種植入物與組織。該隊的洞見是：植入物塗層必須匹配目標組織的硬度與生化特性；組織硬度從腦部的 0.1 kPa 到骨骼的超過 1 MPa，而鈦約為 100 GPa，所以一體適用的塗層只會給細胞錯誤的訊號。他們建了五個互相銜接的模型，在進實驗室之前先引導設計——以 XGBoost 預測 ELP 轉變溫度、對表面接枝水膠做粗粒化分子動力學模擬、一條把轉錄體與蛋白體圖譜轉成組織專一塗層配方的體學流程、用 SuperPro Designer 做 ELP 生產的放大模擬，以及該製程的生命週期評估——並在 13 場訪談中貫徹價值敏感設計（Value Sensitive Design），讓利害關係人在構築體還能改的階段就參與塑形。本隊拿下 Overgrad 組總冠軍，同時獲得最佳 Wiki、最佳整合式人類實踐與最佳生物製造專案。","awards":["Grand Prize Winner (Overgrad)","Top 10 (Overgrad)","Best Model — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Presentation — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Wiki — Winner (Overgrad)","Best Integrated Human Practices — Winner (Overgrad)","Best Entrepreneurship — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Biomanufacturing Project — Winner"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Five models, each tied to a design question. (1) LCST prediction: an XGBoost regressor trained on 230 literature-curated entries predicting ELP transition temperature from sequence composition, length, charge, hydrophobicity and solution conditions, with monotonic constraints forcing predicted LCST to fall as NaCl, ELP concentration or hydrophobicity rise, 216-combination exhaustive grid search over six hyperparameters under composition-grouped 5-fold CV, and a held-out set of 43 entries covering only 10 unique sequences; MAE 3.17 C, beating a linear fit of the Meyer-Chilkoti empirical relation, a 5-nearest-neighbour model and a mean baseline. (2) Molecular dynamics: coarse-grained CALVADOS 0.8.0 with CALVADOS 2 residue parameters in OpenMM 8.2 (one bead per residue, implicit solvent, Debye-Huckel screening, 293.15 K, 10 fs timestep, Langevin thermostat) simulating 16-chain surface-tethered ELP brushes on DelftBlue, the TU Delft supercomputer - chosen explicitly because ELPs are intrinsically disordered and AlphaFold is of limited use. Three MD modules resolve hydrogel stiffness (inter-chain lysine contacts as a proxy), crosslink placement (bridges versus wasted intra-chain loops) and RGD motif solvent accessibility, analysed by response surface modelling and per-lysine regression. (3) Omics-guided motif selection: an enhancement-based test across Human Protein Atlas bulk RNA-seq, the Proteome Atlas DIA-MS intensities, Tabula Sapiens single-cell via CZ CELLxGENE, and GEO datasets (GSE104782, GSE169396, GSE147287, GSE114007), annotated by matrisome, integrin and protease category, with per-dataset thresholds (HPA: >4x the mean of other tissues above 1 nTPM, plus stricter floors of 10 nTPM for ECM ligands and 3 nTPM for integrins) producing an ECM adhesion domain, an integrin target and a targetable protease per implant tissue. (4) Large-scale production: a pilot bioprocess in SuperPro Designer with three consecutive reactors reaching 5.11 g/L ELP, sized to coat 117 million and 22 million continuous glucose monitors, with full catabolic, anabolic and glycerol metabolic balances, downstream ITC/salting-out, homogenisation, flocculation, ion exchange and lyophilisation. (5) Environmental impact: an ISO 14040-style LCA of that flowsheet expressed in eco-costs across 14 categories (acidification, water stress, biodiversity and land-use change, carbon footprint, freshwater ecotoxicity, eutrophication, human toxicity cancer and non-cancer, landfill, metals scarcity, particulate matter, photochemical ozone, plastic soup, resource use), framed against the ESPR and the fact that wearables emit 1.1-6.1 kg CO2e per device.","frameworks_zh":"五個模型，每個都綁定一個設計問題。(1) LCST 預測：以 XGBoost 迴歸器在 230 筆文獻整理的資料上訓練，從序列組成、長度、電荷、疏水性與溶液條件預測 ELP 轉變溫度，並施加單調性約束，強制預測的 LCST 隨 NaCl、ELP 濃度或疏水性上升而下降；在依組成分組的 5 折交叉驗證下，對六個超參數做 216 組合的窮舉網格搜尋，並保留一組 43 筆、只涵蓋 10 條獨特序列的測試集；MAE 3.17 °C，優於 Meyer-Chilkoti 經驗關係式的線性擬合、5 近鄰模型與平均值基準線。(2) 分子動力學：在 OpenMM 8.2 中使用 CALVADOS 0.8.0 搭配 CALVADOS 2 的殘基參數（每個殘基一顆珠、隱式溶劑、Debye-Huckel 屏蔽、293.15 K、10 fs 時間步、Langevin 恆溫器），在台夫特理工大學的超級電腦 DelftBlue 上模擬 16 條鏈的表面接枝 ELP 刷層——明確選擇這條路線，是因為 ELP 本質上是無序蛋白質，AlphaFold 的用處有限。三個 MD 模組分別解析水膠硬度（以鏈間離胺酸接觸作為替代指標）、交聯位置（形成橋接、還是浪費在鏈內迴圈）與 RGD 模體的溶劑可及性，並以反應曲面模型與逐一離胺酸迴歸分析。(3) 體學導引的模體選擇：跨 Human Protein Atlas 的 bulk RNA-seq、Proteome Atlas 的 DIA-MS 強度、透過 CZ CELLxGENE 取得的 Tabula Sapiens 單細胞資料，以及 GEO 資料集（GSE104782、GSE169396、GSE147287、GSE114007）進行一項基於富集程度的檢定，並依基質體、整合素與蛋白酶類別註解，各資料集設有各自門檻（HPA：高於其他組織平均值 4 倍且大於 1 nTPM，另對 ECM 配體加設 10 nTPM、對整合素加設 3 nTPM 的較嚴下限），為每種植入組織產出一個 ECM 黏附區域、一個整合素標靶與一個可作為標靶的蛋白酶。(4) 大規模生產：在 SuperPro Designer 中建立先導製程，三座串聯反應器達到 5.11 g/L ELP，規模設定為可塗覆 1.17 億與 2,200 萬台連續血糖監測器，並具備完整的分解代謝、合成代謝與甘油代謝平衡，下游則包含 ITC／鹽析、均質化、絮凝、離子交換與冷凍乾燥。(5) 環境衝擊：對該流程圖做 ISO 14040 形式的生命週期評估，以生態成本表示，涵蓋 14 個類別（酸化、水資源壓力、生物多樣性與土地利用變化、碳足跡、淡水生態毒性、優養化、人體毒性之致癌與非致癌、掩埋、金屬稀缺、懸浮微粒、光化學臭氧、塑膠濃湯、資源使用），並以 ESPR 以及穿戴式裝置每台排放 1.1–6.1 kg CO2e 的事實作為對照框架。","dataviz":"Best Wiki winner, and the mechanics are worth copying: the wiki is authored in Markdown with structured components (Image with named figure references, FigNum auto-numbering, Collapsable deep-dive blocks, Reference by DOI) and it publishes a machine-readable mirror - every page is served as plain .md at /tu-delft/<page>.md with an llms.txt index, so the whole wiki is readable without JavaScript. The MOSAIC Designer ships as a live four-step in-browser app (annotate, codon-shuffle, swap, assemble-and-export). The clearest single visual argument is a pair of dot plots of the same six-VPGVG protein: one codon per amino acid leaves 190 repeated 8 nt stretches as diagonal stripes, the scrambled spelling leaves 3. The scale-up model is presented as an interactive flowsheet where clicking any equipment unit opens its specifications and stream details, and the entrepreneurship page carries a BOM Sankey, a company-analysis matrix and a CGM signal/lag model.","dataviz_zh":"最佳 Wiki 得主，而其技術做法值得照抄：wiki 以 Markdown 撰寫，搭配結構化元件（Image 帶具名圖號引用、FigNum 自動編號、Collapsable 深入段落、以 DOI 引用的 Reference），並發佈一份可被機器讀取的鏡像——每一頁都在 /tu-delft/<page>.md 以純 .md 形式提供，另附 llms.txt 索引，因此整個 wiki 不需 JavaScript 也能閱讀。MOSAIC Designer 以瀏覽器內四步驟的實際應用程式發佈（註解、密碼子打散、替換、組裝並匯出）。最清楚的單一視覺論證是同一個含六段 VPGVG 蛋白質的兩張點圖：每個胺基酸只用一種密碼子時，留下 190 段重複的 8 nt 片段，呈現為斜向條紋；改用打散的拼法後只剩 3 段。放大模型以互動式流程圖呈現，點選任一設備單元就會開啟其規格與物流細節；創業頁面則有一張 BOM 桑基圖、一個公司分析矩陣與一個 CGM 訊號／延遲模型。","datascience":"Their data engineering is as careful as the modelling. For LCST they searched 86 candidate sources (71 papers or reviews, 15 patents) and hand-extracted sequence, transition temperature, ELP-to-buffer concentration, buffer type, pH and added NaCl; where values existed only as published figures they built their own browser-based LCST Extractor that calibrates axes against tick marks, lets the user trace points along a curve, smooths with LOESS and takes the transition temperature from the steepest change in absorbance - a reproducible digitisation step instead of visual estimation. They treat two rows as the same ELP when amino acid composition matches and keep all rows of one ELP in the same fold, which is an explicit leakage guard, and they document the limitation that composition-only features cannot distinguish block from alternating arrangements of the same residues. The omics pipeline is the other half: it converts public transcriptomic and proteomic atlases into concrete, orderable sequence recipes per tissue, with documented fallback motifs when no tissue signature resolves.","datascience_zh":"他們的資料工程做得和建模一樣細。為了 LCST，他們檢索 86 個候選來源（71 篇論文或綜述、15 件專利），人工擷取序列、轉變溫度、ELP 對緩衝液的濃度、緩衝液種類、pH 與額外添加的 NaCl；若數值只存在於已發表的圖中，他們自建瀏覽器端的 LCST Extractor，以刻度線校正座標軸，讓使用者沿曲線描點，以 LOESS 平滑，並取吸光度變化最陡處作為轉變溫度——這是一個可重現的數位化步驟，取代目測估計。當胺基酸組成相同時，他們把兩列資料視為同一條 ELP，並把同一條 ELP 的所有資料列放在同一折內，這是明確的資料洩漏防範；他們也記錄了限制：只用組成特徵無法區分同樣殘基是以區塊式還是交替式排列。體學流程是另一半：它把公開的轉錄體與蛋白體圖譜轉換成每種組織具體、可直接下單的序列配方，並在找不出組織特徵時記錄備用模體。","software":"Four tools on iGEM GitLab. MOSAIC ELP Designer (https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/tu-delft/mosaic-elp-designer) solves the problem that repetitive ELP genes are near-impossible to synthesise: it annotates a pasted protein into parts and linkers, codon-scrambles the parts using a De Bruijn-window repeat check (default k = 3 codons, repeats counted from 6 to 18 nt, homopolymer rule on, BsaI/NdeI/BseRI/BamHI/XbaI excluded on both strands), designs compatible Golden Gate cut sites in the locked linkers so every new part combination assembles with the same overhangs, checks synthesisability, and exports order-ready library sequences; it runs as a web app at https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-delft/designer. LCST Prediction (https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/tu-delft/lcst-prediction) is a Python pipeline with clean_data.ipynb, features.py, train_model.py, test_model.py, run_pipeline.py and predict.py, and bundles the LCST Extractor digitiser under tools/curve_extract. Molecular Dynamics Simulator (https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/tu-delft/molecular-dynamics-simulator) wraps the CALVADOS/OpenMM brush setup and per-module analysis. Tissue-Specific ELP Design (https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/tu-delft/tissue-specific-elp-design) is the omics pipeline. Data deposited at doi:10.5281/zenodo.23532676.","software_zh":"iGEM GitLab 上四項工具。MOSAIC ELP Designer（https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/tu-delft/mosaic-elp-designer）解決重複性高的 ELP 基因幾乎無法合成的問題：它把貼入的蛋白質註解為部件與連接子，以 De Bruijn 視窗重複檢查打散部件的密碼子（預設 k = 3 個密碼子，重複長度從 6 計算到 18 nt，啟用同聚物規則，並在雙股上排除 BsaI/NdeI/BseRI/BamHI/XbaI），在鎖定的連接子中設計相容的 Golden Gate 切位，使每一組新的部件組合都能以相同的 overhang 組裝，再檢查可合成性，最後匯出可直接下單的函式庫序列；它也以網頁應用程式的形式在 https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-delft/designer 運行。LCST Prediction（https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/tu-delft/lcst-prediction）是一條 Python 流程，包含 clean_data.ipynb、features.py、train_model.py、test_model.py、run_pipeline.py 與 predict.py，並把 LCST Extractor 數位化工具收錄在 tools/curve_extract 下。Molecular Dynamics Simulator（https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/tu-delft/molecular-dynamics-simulator）封裝了 CALVADOS/OpenMM 的刷層設定與各模組分析。Tissue-Specific ELP Design（https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/tu-delft/tissue-specific-elp-design）則是那條體學流程。資料存放於 doi:10.5281/zenodo.23532676。","stack":["XGBoost","scikit-learn","Python / Jupyter","CALVADOS 0.8.0 (CALVADOS 2 parameters)","OpenMM 8.2","DelftBlue HPC","SuperPro Designer","Idemat / eco-costs LCA","Human Protein Atlas","Proteome Atlas (DIA-MS)","Tabula Sapiens via CZ CELLxGENE Census","NCBI GEO","De Bruijn-graph codon scrambling","Golden Gate / MoClo assembly design","LOESS smoothing","Markdown + component-based wiki with llms.txt","QCM-D (MVP validation)","iGEM GitLab","Zenodo"],"techniques":["monotonic feature constraints encoding known physics into a tree model","composition-grouped cross-validation as a leakage guard","exhaustive grid search with 5-fold CV on the training split only","benchmarking against a published empirical equation, kNN and a mean baseline","coarse-grained MD of intrinsically disordered proteins","response surface modelling and per-lysine regression on MD trajectories","bridge-versus-loop crosslink partition analysis","solvent-accessible-surface-area motif accessibility","enhancement-based tissue-specificity testing across four omics resolutions","techno-economic process simulation with full metabolic balances","ISO 14040 life-cycle assessment in single-indicator eco-costs","figure digitisation with axis calibration and LOESS","repeat-aware codon optimisation for synthesisable repetitive genes"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Outreach was built as two-way exchange rather than broadcast, and the recurring artefact is the DNA bracelet: visitors translate a DNA sequence to RNA to protein, each protein becoming a differently coloured bead, so they leave with both the concept and the object. They ran it at the Weekend of Science on the TU Delft campus in The Hague (part of a national programme of 2,000 activities in one weekend), at Neighbours' Day in the district where team members live using beads donated by a local artist, and alongside a codon wheel and a 'building blocks' horse-race game. They put a pond scoop next to a microscope and taught children to focus it, letting curiosity do the teaching for the younger visitors who found the implant problem itself uninteresting. Delft Dialogue brought the Human Practices co-lead, team lead and outreach manager on to discuss the technology's implications for medicine. They also hosted a PhD student from the Daan Brinks Lab for a cloning knowledge exchange and met other iGEM teams, noting specifically what they learned from Brussels' bees and Wageningen's PFAS project.","publicEngagement_zh":"外展活動被設計成雙向交流而非單向播送，反覆出現的產出是 DNA 手鍊：參觀者把一段 DNA 序列轉譯成 RNA 再轉成蛋白質，每種蛋白質對應一顆不同顏色的珠子，於是他們同時帶走概念與實物。他們在海牙台夫特理工校區的 Weekend of Science（一個週末內 2,000 場活動的全國性計畫的一部分）辦過，也在隊員居住的社區的 Neighbours' Day 辦過，珠子由當地一位藝術家捐贈，同場還有密碼子轉盤與一個「積木」賽馬遊戲。他們在顯微鏡旁放了一支撈池水的網勺，教孩子自己對焦，讓好奇心替他們教學——對那些覺得植入物問題本身很無聊的年幼參觀者尤其有效。Delft Dialogue 則請來 Human Practices 共同負責人、隊長與外展經理，討論這項技術對醫療的意涵。他們也接待了 Daan Brinks Lab 的一位博士生進行選殖技術交流，並與其他 iGEM 隊伍交流，特別提到從布魯塞爾隊的蜜蜂專案與 Wageningen 隊的 PFAS 專案學到的東西。","ihp":"Best IHP winner, and the structure is the reason. They used Value Sensitive Design in three explicit passes - conceptual (who MOSAIC affects), empirical (13 semi-structured interviews plus literature) and technical (values translated into design requirements) - adapted the Rathenau Institute's iGEM Guide to the Future into five actor groups (directly affected, those who govern access, industry, those who inform, nature), placed every actor on a power-interest grid using two questions (can this actor formally block market access, and does it have a direct stake), borrowed a 1-3 MCDA scoring scale to extend GRADE, and got formal TU Delft Human Research Ethics Committee approval before any interviews. Requirements they could not meet this year became explicitly labelled Future Perspectives rather than quiet omissions. The concrete changes: a philosopher of technology pointed out that modularity is simultaneously the strength and the regulatory risk, which pushed them to involve patients, clinicians and regulators while the construct was still open and to be wary of words like 'biomimicry' that make people assume safety. Antibiotic-resistance concerns made them drop antibiotics from the antimicrobial module entirely and search the literature for alternatives, landing on antimicrobial peptides. Kirby Lattwein (Erasmus MC, cardiovascular device infections) said their assays would not predict real-world performance, so they switched to clinically relevant strains and media and ran the AMP work in her lab on three clinical isolates from LVAD driveline infections plus two reference strains, and added LVAD drivelines as a use case. Surgeon Robin Atallah told them every minute in the operating room costs 50-70 euros and that surgeons resist deviating from routine, which pushed them toward a manufacturer-pre-coated implant rather than an in-theatre paste. Ambiguity about protein coatings in permanent blood contact made them set blood-contacting implants aside and focus on tissue-embedded and skin-crossing implants. Amir Zadpoor's point that loosening is a major failure mode drove the omics-guided motif model. A CGM industry interviewee's distinction between sensor and adhesive focused the MVP on the inserted sensor and his warning that manufacturers have little incentive to reduce sensor replacement sales sent the entrepreneurship team back to the business model.","ihp_zh":"最佳整合式人類實踐得主，而結構正是得獎原因。他們以三個明確階段運用價值敏感設計——概念階段（MOSAIC 影響到誰）、實證階段（13 場半結構訪談加上文獻）與技術階段（把價值轉譯為設計需求），並把 Rathenau Institute 的 iGEM Guide to the Future 改寫成五類行動者（直接受影響者、管控取得管道者、產業、提供資訊者、自然），再以兩個問題（這個行動者能否正式阻擋市場准入、以及它是否有直接利害關係）把每個行動者定位在權力—利益矩陣上，另外借用 1–3 分的 MCDA 評分尺度來擴充 GRADE，並在任何訪談之前取得台夫特理工大學人類研究倫理委員會的正式核准。今年做不到的需求被明確標示為 Future Perspectives，而不是悄悄省略。具體的改變如下：一位技術哲學家指出模組化同時是強項也是法規風險，這促使他們在構築體還開放時就納入病人、臨床醫師與法規人員，並對「生物擬態」這類會讓人誤以為安全的字眼保持警覺。對抗生素抗藥性的顧慮使他們把抗生素完全從抗微生物模組中移除，並回頭查文獻尋找替代方案，最後落在抗菌肽。Kirby Lattwein（Erasmus MC，心血管裝置感染）指出他們的分析方法無法預測真實世界表現，於是他們改用臨床相關菌株與培養基，並在她的實驗室中以三株來自 LVAD 傳動線感染的臨床分離菌加上兩株參考菌株進行抗菌肽實驗，也把 LVAD 傳動線納為應用場景。外科醫師 Robin Atallah 告訴他們，手術室裡每一分鐘要花 50–70 歐元，而外科醫師抗拒偏離既有流程，這把他們推向由製造商預先塗覆的植入物，而非在手術室現場塗抹的膏劑。蛋白質塗層在永久接觸血液情境下的不確定性，使他們暫時放下接觸血液的植入物，專注於埋入組織與穿皮的植入物。Amir Zadpoor 指出鬆動是主要的失效模式，這推動了體學導引的模體模型。一位 CGM 產業受訪者區分了感測器與黏貼膠，使 MVP 聚焦在植入體內的感測器；而他提醒製造商幾乎沒有動機去減少感測器替換的銷售，則讓創業小組回頭重做商業模式。","realWorld":"The MVP is deliberately the hardest possible test rather than the best-performing coating: a single construct, (VPGIG)23-VPGKG-LDASTVYAVTGRGDSPASSAASA-(VPGIG)24, with one lysine placed directly beside the RGD domain mid-chain, bonded through that lysine to a polydopamine-primed CGM polyurethane membrane, validated by QCM-D for attachment and a cell-adhesion assay against scrambled-RDG and lysine-free controls on the same purified batch. Commercially they chose continuous glucose monitors after a regulatory-driven application screen: they studied EU MDR and FDA pathways in detail (notified body versus 510(k)/PMA, Rule 14 class III escalation when a coating carries an active substance, Annex IX 4.10 review for changes to an approved device) and let that analysis eliminate candidates. The business model is ELP supply paid as a royalty per coated sensor, set as a share of the partner's net price per sensor, which they justify as how medical-technology licences are normally priced, with contracts structured to limit risk. They ran TAM/SAM/SOM, Porter's Five Forces, SWOT with explicit strategies, CGM market consolidation and GLP-1 agonist trend analysis, and three competitor case studies (LipoCoat, Surmodics, Bactiguard). Scale-up is costed for 117 million and 22 million CGMs per year with full technical and financial KPIs, backed by the LCA. IP is mapped as US and European ELP patent landscapes against TU Delft's ownership policy, with an explicit discussion of IP versus open-source science. A 3D-printed-organ bioink route is flagged as future work, since ELPs phase-transition reversibly above a set temperature.","realWorld_zh":"MVP 刻意設計成最嚴苛的測試，而不是表現最好的塗層：單一構築體 (VPGIG)23-VPGKG-LDASTVYAVTGRGDSPASSAASA-(VPGIG)24，在鏈中段 RGD 區域旁邊只放一個離胺酸，並透過該離胺酸鍵結到以聚多巴胺預處理的 CGM 聚胺酯薄膜上，以 QCM-D 驗證附著，並在同一批純化產物上，以打亂序列的 RDG 與無離胺酸的對照組進行細胞黏附試驗。商業上，他們在一輪由法規驅動的應用篩選後選定連續血糖監測器：他們詳細研究歐盟 MDR 與 FDA 的途徑（公告機構對比 510(k)/PMA、當塗層帶有活性物質時依規則 14 升級為第三類、核准器材變更時依附錄 IX 第 4.10 節審查），並讓這份分析淘汰其他候選。商業模式是 ELP 供應以每片已塗覆感測器的權利金計價，設定為合作夥伴每片感測器淨價的一定比例，他們以醫療科技授權的常見定價方式為理由，並以能限縮風險的方式設計合約。他們做了 TAM/SAM/SOM、波特五力分析、附明確策略的 SWOT、CGM 市場整併與 GLP-1 受體促效劑趨勢分析，以及三個競爭者案例研究（LipoCoat、Surmodics、Bactiguard）。放大生產則依每年 1.17 億與 2,200 萬台 CGM 計算成本，附完整的技術與財務 KPI，並以 LCA 為後盾。智慧財產權部分，他們把美國與歐洲的 ELP 專利佈局對照台夫特理工大學的所有權政策加以盤點，並明確討論了智財與開源科學之間的張力。3D 列印器官用生物墨水的路線被標為未來工作，因為 ELP 在特定溫度之上會可逆地發生相變。","partners":["Kirby Lattwein, Erasmus Medical Center (cardiovascular device infections; hosted the AMP assays)","Dr. Robin Atallah (bone-anchored prostheses surgeon)","Prof. Amir Zadpoor, TU Delft (implant loosening)","Prof. Gijsje Koenderink, TU Delft","Dirk Eijkel","Luca Hodes (ELP functionalisation / bioink idea)","Nikolas Gaio and Tim Bruines (industry interviews)","Daan Brinks Lab, TU Delft","TU Delft Human Research Ethics Committee","Rathenau Institute (iGEM Guide to the Future framework)","DHPC DelftBlue supercomputer"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6110/wiki/software/workflow.avif","caption":"What the MOSAIC Designer takes over: from a researcher's amino acid sequence through part identification, codon scrambling, Golden Gate cut-site design and synthesis feasibility checks to order-ready library sequences.","caption_zh":"MOSAIC Designer 接手了哪些工作：從研究者的胺基酸序列，經過部件識別、密碼子打散、Golden Gate 切位設計與合成可行性檢查，一路到可直接下單的函式庫序列。","credit":"Team TU Delft, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6110/wiki/software/annotate.avif","caption":"The MOSAIC Designer annotation step in the browser: a pasted sequence split into parts and linkers, each listed with its range, length and sequence, auto-filled from the detected repeat motif.","caption_zh":"瀏覽器中的 MOSAIC Designer 註解步驟：貼入的序列被切分為部件與連接子，各自列出範圍、長度與序列，並由偵測到的重複模體自動填入。","credit":"Team TU Delft, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6110/wiki/model/bioinformatics-pipeline-blockscheme.avif","caption":"The omics-guided motif selection pipeline: public transcriptomic and proteomic data filtered to implant-relevant tissues, annotated by matrisome, integrin and protease category, and reduced by an enhancement test to a per-tissue coating recipe.","caption_zh":"體學導引的模體選擇流程：公開的轉錄體與蛋白體資料先篩選到與植入物相關的組織，依基質體、整合素與蛋白酶類別註解，再以富集程度檢定收斂成每種組織的塗層配方。","credit":"Team TU Delft, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6110/wiki/outreach/bracelets/workshop-preview.avif","caption":"The DNA bracelet workshop, run at the Weekend of Science and Neighbours' Day: visitors translate DNA to RNA to protein, with each protein becoming a coloured bead they take home.","caption_zh":"在 Weekend of Science 與 Neighbours' Day 舉辦的 DNA 手鍊工作坊：參觀者把 DNA 轉譯成 RNA 再轉成蛋白質，每種蛋白質變成一顆可以帶回家的彩色珠子。","credit":"Team TU Delft, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Adopt their two cheap, high-leverage habits. First, build known physics into a small model instead of hoping it learns it: monotonic constraints on NaCl, concentration and hydrophobicity let 230 hand-curated data points beat a published empirical equation, which is exactly the regime a school lab works in. Second, make the wiki machine-readable - authoring pages as Markdown and publishing them at <page>.md with an llms.txt index cost them almost nothing and made the Best Wiki winner fully legible to any reader or tool, including judges skimming on a bad connection.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"值得採用他們兩個便宜又高槓桿的習慣。第一，把已知的物理直接寫進小模型，而不是指望模型自己學會：對 NaCl、濃度與疏水性施加單調性約束，讓 230 筆人工整理的資料點勝過已發表的經驗公式，而這正是學校實驗室所處的資料規模。第二，讓 wiki 可被機器讀取——用 Markdown 撰寫頁面、並在 <page>.md 發佈，再加一份 llms.txt 索引，幾乎沒有額外成本，卻讓這個最佳 Wiki 得主對任何讀者或工具都完全可讀，包括在連線品質不佳時快速瀏覽的評審。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-delft/","https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-delft/llms.txt","https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-delft/description.md","https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-delft/model.md","https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-delft/software.md","https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-delft/results.md","https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-delft/engineering.md","https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-delft/human-practices.md","https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-delft/entrepreneurship.md","https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-delft/outreach.md","https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-delft/contribution.md","https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-delft/parts.md","https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-delft/experiments.md"],"rank":289},"6115":{"team":"BNDS-China","id":"6115","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/bnds-china/","projectTitle":"OrbitColi","projectTitle_zh":"OrbitColi","tagline":"An AND-logic-gate engineered probiotic that senses oxidative stress in space and produces vitamin B2 and trehalose to protect astronauts","tagline_zh":"以 AND 邏輯閘設計的工程益生菌，在太空中感測氧化壓力並生產維生素 B2 與海藻糖來保護太空人","summary":"BNDS-China built OrbitColi, an engineered E. coli probiotic designed to sense oxidative conditions arising from cosmic radiation and microgravity and respond by producing vitamin B2 and trehalose, replacing fixed-dose supplements that degrade over multi-year missions. The scientific framing is quantitative: ISS crews receive 100-200 mSv per year against a 20 mSv occupational limit, and a three-year Mars round trip may accumulate 300-450 mSv. The team's distinguishing contribution is methodological: they invented and applied a five-step education framework, R.E.A.C.H. (Recognize, Experience, Apply, Communicate, Harvest), to every single outreach activity, with a pre-event diagnostic survey and a matched post-event survey, and they report their own failures against it. Integrated Human Practices used a parallel STAR framework (Scan, Test, Assemble, Reflect) across five cycles.","summary_zh":"BNDS-China 做了 OrbitColi，一株經改造的 E. coli 益生菌，設計用來感測宇宙輻射與微重力造成的氧化環境，並以生產維生素 B2 與海藻糖作為回應，取代在多年任務中會變質的固定劑量補充品。科學鋪陳是有數字的：國際太空站組員每年接受 100-200 mSv，職業曝露上限為 20 mSv，而三年的火星往返任務可能累積 300-450 mSv。團隊最具辨識度的貢獻在方法層面：他們自創並實際套用一套五步教育框架 R.E.A.C.H.（Recognize、Experience、Apply、Communicate、Harvest）到每一場推廣活動，搭配活動前的診斷性問卷與相對應的活動後問卷，而且會依這個框架回報自己哪裡做失敗了。整合式人類實踐則以平行的 STAR 框架（Scan、Test、Assemble、Reflect）跑了五個循環。","awards":["Best Education — Nominee (High School)","Best Wiki — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Two self-designed frameworks, both documented and reusable: R.E.A.C.H. for education (Recognize the audience's pre-existing attitudes before teaching; Experience through interactive formats; Apply by moving the audience from listeners to designers; Communicate to close the loop by harvesting informed project feedback into Integrated Human Practices; Harvest by quantifying the event's success and planning the next iteration) and STAR for iHP (Scan, Test, Assemble, Reflect) across five cycles: problem validation, end-user and market needs, technical design, biosafety and ethics, and production and final-product development. The REACH structure is published in detailed appendices so other teams can reuse it.","frameworks_zh":"兩套自行設計、都有文件且可重複使用的框架：教育用的 R.E.A.C.H.（Recognize，教之前先認識受眾原有的態度；Experience，以互動形式讓他們親身體驗；Apply，讓受眾從聽眾變成設計者；Communicate，把出於理解的專案回饋收攏回整合式人類實踐，閉合迴圈；Harvest，量化這場活動的成效並規劃下一次迭代），以及人類實踐用的 STAR（Scan、Test、Assemble、Reflect），共跑五個循環：問題驗證、終端使用者與市場需求、技術設計、生物安全與倫理，以及生產與最終產品開發。REACH 的結構以詳細附錄公開，讓其他團隊可以直接沿用。","dataviz":"Before-and-after bar charts of self-reported technique familiarity and interest; questionnaire-result figures published for each activity (pre and post); a timeline figure of all educational activities; pre-interview and final stakeholder influence/relevance maps for iHP, with the honest caveat printed on the figure that inclusion in the pre-interview map does not mean an interview took place.","dataviz_zh":"自評技術熟悉度與興趣的前後對比長條圖；每場活動都公布問卷結果圖（前測與後測）；一張涵蓋所有教育活動的時間軸圖；以及人類實踐的訪談前與最終版利害關係人影響力／相關性地圖，圖上還老實標註：出現在訪談前的地圖上並不代表訪談真的發生過。","datascience":"Systematic paired pre/post surveying with reported N and percentages, e.g. kindergarten cohort N = 14 matched responses, 21 student athletes aged 10-13 surveyed before and after, 16 valid responses per question from the elderly session, eight older adults aged 68-82 interviewed at the scoping stage, and two school-wide perception surveys on synthetic biology and on attitudes to engineered-bacteria consumption and space microbial applications, all published as downloadable files.","datascience_zh":"系統性的配對前後測問卷，都回報 N 值與百分比，例如幼兒園組 N = 14 份可配對回覆、21 位 10-13 歲學生運動員在活動前後各受測一次、長者場次每題 16 份有效回覆、在前期範疇界定階段訪談 8 位 68-82 歲長者，以及兩份全校性認知調查（對合成生物學的看法，以及對食用工程菌與太空微生物應用的態度），全部以可下載檔案公開。","software":"The project includes hardware and software components presented to audiences for feedback; the team learned an AI protein-design workflow from team NBJF (generate structure, fill amino-acid sequence, in-silico screening, wet-lab validation) and explicitly reserved wet-lab capacity because high in-silico scores can lose function in reality.","software_zh":"專案包含硬體與軟體元件，並拿給受眾試用以收集回饋；團隊向 NBJF 隊伍學到一套 AI 蛋白質設計流程（先生成結構、再填入胺基酸序列、電腦模擬篩選、濕實驗驗證），並明確保留濕實驗的量能，因為電腦模擬分數很高的設計在現實中仍可能失去功能。","stack":["R.E.A.C.H. education framework","STAR iHP framework","paired pre/post questionnaires","downloadable lesson slide decks and protocols","AND logic-gate genetic circuit design"],"techniques":["oxidative-stress-responsive promoter sensing","AND logic gate circuit","vitamin B2 and trehalose biosynthesis","protein thermal and radiation resistance engineering","strawberry DNA extraction","fluorescent E. coli painting"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"BNDS-China's practice is distinctive because every activity is written up against the same five-step template, R.E.A.C.H., which forces a pre-event diagnostic, an interactive delivery, a design task, a project-feedback loop and a quantified post-event evaluation - and the team reports honestly where a step was skipped. The highest-value example is a kindergarten programme for pre-literate 5-6 year olds. The Recognize step established through a pre-event survey that children already saw microbes as invisible enemies (hand-washing framing) and that 71.43% preferred interactive games to lectures. The team then rendered BioBrick standard assembly as a colour-coded tactile block system: a blue 'switch' promoter block that must come first, a red 'function' coding-sequence block compared to a light bulb, a yellow 'stop' terminator block compared to a vehicle brake, and a green 'little house' vector and chassis block, with assembly order taught as a chanted mantra ('Flip open the blue switch, let the red function bloom, halt with the yellow brake, and live inside the green room!'). Children worked in pairs and trios called 'syndicates' with visual challenge cards posing local problems (make plants glow to light a path to a playground at night; make a flower that masks the smell of garbage). The cleverest design move: the team deliberately rationed parts, giving one table switches but no coding blocks and the next table the reverse, so children had to discover what they lacked, approach other groups and barter - a lived introduction to the open-source iGEM Registry. A five-act puppet show, 'Microscopic Defense Line', dramatised a grazed arm at cell scale, and deliberately avoided weapons or war imagery: the White Blood Cell puppet hugged the bacterium to represent phagocytosis, two red blood cell actors held hands to bridge a vessel, and platelet actors pressed yellow paper against stretchy cloth to show clotting. Measured results from matched surveys (N = 14): before, 78.57% did not know what it meant to pass a function from one organism to another and 64.29% did not know or only vaguely knew what a gene is; after, 92.86% described synthetic biology as 'building blocks', 92.86% knew the promoter starts expression and 100% knew the coding sequence determines function; 42.86% had thought the body fights invaders like 'little soldiers' and none knew clots form, versus 100% afterwards understanding both white blood cell clearance and platelet repair; 100% enjoyed the activities and 92.86% wanted more science stories. The feedback even changed the project: children asked why immune clearance has to kill ('Can't they just change them? Make them friends?') and worried what happens if the yellow stop block falls off, which the team mapped onto transcriptional runaway, biocontainment and biocontamination and used to question their own antagonistic-clearance therapeutic model. Other formats, each with REACH write-ups: a BioCamp lecture on the whole molecular toolkit (PCR, gel electrophoresis, Southern/Northern/Western blotting, qPCR, rtPCR, FISH, CRISPR-Cas9, gene circuits) where each technique was framed by the question it answers, with the team candidly recording that the Apply and Communicate steps did not happen and that students still found the techniques complicated without hands-on work, and publishing the fix (fewer techniques per session, add pipetting and gel loading, one workflow diagram); a formal debate on 9 March 2026 with the BNDS British Debate Club on whether synthetic biology should modify human traits unrelated to serious disease, supported by a purpose-written Synthetic Bio Debate Information Packet covering definitions, design principles, systems thinking, intervention targets, risks, ethics and governance, with pre- and post-debate questionnaires; a campus art exhibition on environmental protection with a pop-art digital painting and an explanatory signboard, made with a visual-arts student, where the recorded criticism was that the symbols were too abstract; a bilingual comic published in the school newspaper BNDS Review and released as downloadable Chinese and English digital versions; and merchandise-as-conversation-starter at the Hongchuanghui Fair and school carnival, with original E. coli, yeast and budding-yeast cartoon designs on postcards, stickers and acrylic hair clips, where the team explicitly explained which features were biological and which were artistic licence. The inclusivity work is specific about barriers. At Tianyun Rehabilitation Center in Liulihe, Fangshan District, Beijing, working with hearing-impaired children and children with genetic conditions, the team discovered the children had no independent electronic devices and that a conventional questionnaire did not suit their communication needs, so after consulting the centre's teachers they switched to an illustrated storybook, 'Little Chef Mimi and Her Magical Yeast Friends', plus a colouring activity, and relied on the teachers to interpret the children's sign language - concluding that inclusive science education is about making sure every child's voice can be heard, not just making knowledge easier. For children with osteogenesis imperfecta ('porcelain doll' patients), the team first interviewed directors of the Sun and Rain Center rare-disease organisation, who explicitly advised against treating participants as fragile or showing pity; sessions were kept short, and when the team noticed holding pens was physically hard for some children, they abandoned the planned drawing activity mid-session for an open discussion and a 'wishing' segment, then shifted their long-term approach to accessible online workshops and distributing game materials directly to hospitals. For 21 student athletes aged 10-13 with limited access to systematic biology teaching or lab equipment, three experiments (strawberry DNA extraction, saliva pH around exercise, ruler-drop reaction tests) tied biology to their own bodies; afterwards all 21 reported confidence in understanding and completing experiments and all answered the DNA and synthetic-biology questions correctly. A lecture for older adults, built on scoping interviews with eight people aged 68-82 whose concerns were medical safety, side effects and the reliability of health information, used genetically modified food, vaccines and microbial insulin as familiar anchors, taught how to spot misleading health advertising and how AI can help check claims, and included making DNA-themed bracelets and illustrated tote bags carrying health-scam reminders; of 16 post-event responses, 15 (93.75%) rejected a misleading miracle-product claim, all 16 answered the GM food, vaccine, insulin and AI-checking items as intended, 81.25% found explanations easy to understand and 87.5% called the activity very helpful.","publicEngagement_zh":"BNDS-China 的做法之所以特別，是因為每一場活動都依同一套五步模板 R.E.A.C.H. 寫成紀錄，這套模板強制要求活動前診斷、互動式進行、一項設計任務、一條把回饋帶回專案的迴圈，以及可量化的活動後評估；而且團隊會誠實交代哪些步驟被跳過了。最有價值的例子是為尚未識字的 5-6 歲幼兒設計的幼兒園課程。Recognize 階段透過活動前問卷確認：孩子原本就把微生物看成看不見的敵人（來自洗手教育的框架），而且 71.43% 偏好互動遊戲而不是聽講。團隊接著把 BioBrick 標準組裝做成一套用顏色區分、可以動手操作的積木系統：藍色的「開關」是啟動子積木，必須放第一個；紅色的「功能」是編碼序列積木，比喻成燈泡；黃色的「停止」是終止子積木，比喻成車子的煞車；綠色的「小房子」則是載體與底盤積木，組裝順序以口訣教唱（打開藍色的開關，讓紅色的功能綻放，用黃色的煞車停住，住進綠色的房間！）。孩子以兩三人一組（稱為「小聯盟」）進行，並用圖像式挑戰卡提出身邊的問題（讓植物發光，照亮晚上通往遊樂場的小路；做一朵能蓋掉垃圾臭味的花）。最巧妙的設計是：團隊刻意限量發放零件，一桌只有開關、沒有編碼積木，另一桌剛好相反，孩子必須自己發現缺了什麼，再去找別組交換，用身體經驗認識開放共享的 iGEM Registry。一齣五幕偶戲「微觀防線」以細胞尺度演出手臂擦傷的過程，並刻意避開武器或戰爭的意象：白血球偶是用擁抱細菌來表現吞噬作用，兩位紅血球演員牽手搭成血管，血小板演員則把黃紙壓在有彈性的布上來表現凝血。配對問卷（N = 14）量到的結果：活動前，78.57% 不知道把一個生物的功能傳給另一個生物是什麼意思，64.29% 不知道或只模糊知道基因是什麼；活動後，92.86% 用「積木」描述合成生物學，92.86% 知道啟動子負責開始表現，100% 知道編碼序列決定功能；活動前有 42.86% 以為身體是像「小士兵」那樣對抗入侵者，沒有人知道會形成血塊，活動後則 100% 同時理解白血球的清除作用與血小板的修補；100% 喜歡這些活動，92.86% 希望聽到更多科學故事。回饋甚至改變了專案：孩子問為什麼免疫清除一定要殺死對方（不能把它們改造一下、變成朋友嗎？），也擔心黃色的停止積木掉了會怎樣；團隊把這些問題對應到轉錄失控、生物圍堵與生物污染，並用來反問自己以拮抗清除為基礎的治療模式是否恰當。其他形式也都有 REACH 紀錄：BioCamp 講座介紹整套分子工具（PCR、凝膠電泳、Southern／Northern／Western blotting、qPCR、rtPCR、FISH、CRISPR-Cas9、基因迴路），每項技術都以它要回答的問題來切入；團隊坦白記錄 Apply 與 Communicate 兩步並未發生，學生在沒有動手操作的情況下仍覺得這些技術很複雜，並公布改法（每場少講幾項技術、加入移液與上膠練習、用一張流程圖統整）；2026 年 3 月 9 日與 BNDS British Debate Club 合辦的正式辯論，題目是合成生物學是否應該修改與重大疾病無關的人類特徵，並特別編寫一份 Synthetic Bio Debate Information Packet 作為資料，涵蓋定義、設計原則、系統思考、介入標的、風險、倫理與治理，辯論前後都做問卷；以環境保護為題的校園藝術展，與一位視覺藝術科學生合作完成一幅普普風數位畫作與一面解說看板，紀錄中收到的批評是符號太抽象；在校刊 BNDS Review 刊出的雙語漫畫，並釋出可下載的中文與英文數位版；以及在 Hongchuanghui Fair 市集與校園嘉年華上用周邊商品開啟對話，把原創的 E. coli、酵母與芽生酵母卡通設計做成明信片、貼紙與壓克力髮夾，團隊並明確說明哪些特徵有生物學依據、哪些是藝術想像。在包容性方面，他們把障礙講得很具體。在北京市房山區琉璃河的天運康復中心，面對聽覺障礙兒童與罹患遺傳疾病的孩子，團隊發現這些孩子沒有可自行使用的電子設備，常規問卷也不符合他們的溝通需求，因此在請教中心老師後改用插畫故事書 Little Chef Mimi and Her Magical Yeast Friends 搭配著色活動，並依靠老師為孩子的手語翻譯；他們的結論是，包容性的科學教育重點在於讓每個孩子的聲音都能被聽見，而不只是把知識講得更簡單。面對成骨不全症（俗稱瓷娃娃）的孩子，團隊先訪談罕見疾病組織 Sun and Rain Center 的負責人，對方明確建議不要把參與者當成易碎的人、也不要表現同情；活動因此刻意縮短，當團隊注意到有些孩子握筆在生理上很吃力時，他們當場放棄原訂的繪畫活動，改成開放討論與一段「許願」環節，之後也把長期做法轉向可及性較高的線上工作坊，並直接把遊戲素材送到醫院。針對 21 位 10-13 歲、較難接觸系統性生物教學或實驗設備的學生運動員，三個實驗（草莓 DNA 萃取、運動前後的唾液 pH 值、落尺反應測試）把生物學和他們自己的身體連在一起；活動後 21 人全部表示有信心理解並完成實驗，DNA 與合成生物學的題目也全部答對。為長者設計的講座建立在對 8 位 68-82 歲長者的前期訪談上，他們關心的是醫療安全、副作用與健康資訊的可信度；講座以基因改造食品、疫苗與微生物生產的胰島素作為熟悉的切入點，教如何辨識誤導性的健康廣告，以及如何用 AI 幫忙查證說法，並包含製作 DNA 主題手環與印有防詐健康提醒的插畫提袋；活動後 16 份回覆中，有 15 份（93.75%）駁斥了一項誤導性的神奇產品宣稱，16 人在基因改造食品、疫苗、胰島素與用 AI 查證的題目上都如預期作答，81.25% 覺得解說容易理解，87.5% 認為這場活動很有幫助。","ihp":"Five iHP cycles (problem validation, end-user and market needs, technical design, biosafety and ethics, production and final product) were each run through the team's STAR loop. A pre-interview stakeholder map linked each cycle to the expert groups whose input it needed, and a final map recorded each stakeholder's influence on the project and the project's relevance to them. The team documented a hard limit transparently: regulatory restrictions prevented them from interviewing astronauts or national regulatory authorities. Aerospace food and nutrition experts defined the nutritional context; space medicine and clinical experts shaped the health-need and biosafety assessment. Education fed directly back into design, most notably the kindergarten children's biocontainment and mutualism questions. A cross-team exchange with team NBJF on AI protein design taught the team to compartmentalise the workflow and to avoid over-reliance on in-silico prediction, and they adopted NBJF's 'phenomenon-first, jargon-later' principle for explaining their AND logic-gate probiotic to lay audiences.","ihp_zh":"五個人類實踐循環（問題驗證、終端使用者與市場需求、技術設計、生物安全與倫理、生產與最終產品）都走過團隊自己的 STAR 迴圈。訪談前的利害關係人地圖把每個循環連到它需要哪些專家群，最終版地圖則記錄每位利害關係人對專案的影響力，以及專案對他們的相關性。團隊也透明記下一項硬性限制：法規限制使他們無法訪談太空人或國家主管機關。航太食品與營養專家界定了營養層面的脈絡；太空醫學與臨床專家則形塑了健康需求與生物安全評估。教育直接回饋到設計，最明顯的例子就是幼兒園孩子關於生物圍堵與互利共生的提問。與 NBJF 隊伍關於 AI 蛋白質設計的交流，讓團隊學會把流程切成區塊、避免過度依賴電腦模擬預測，他們也採用 NBJF 的先講現象、後講術語原則，向一般大眾解釋他們的 AND 邏輯閘益生菌。","realWorld":"The project targets a documented gap in astronaut health protection: pre-packaged vitamins and antioxidants provide fixed dosing that cannot track real-time biochemical change, and shelf-life degradation makes them unreliable over multi-year missions. Education outputs were deliberately packaged for reuse: an openly available children's book, downloadable comic in Chinese and English, the debate information packet, lecture slide decks, bilingual activity PowerPoints, the strawberry DNA extraction protocol, and detailed REACH appendices so other teams and educators can replicate the structure rather than just the activities.","realWorld_zh":"專案針對的是太空人健康防護上一個有紀錄的缺口：預先包裝的維生素與抗氧化劑只能提供固定劑量，無法跟隨即時的生化變化，而保存期限的衰減又讓它們在多年任務中不可靠。教育產出也刻意包裝成可重複使用的形式：公開取用的童書、可下載的中英文漫畫、辯論資料包、講座投影片、雙語活動 PowerPoint、草莓 DNA 萃取流程，以及詳盡的 REACH 附錄，讓其他團隊與教育者能複製的是這套結構，而不只是活動本身。","partners":["BNDS British Debate Club","Tianyun Rehabilitation Center, Liulihe, Fangshan District, Beijing (hearing-impaired and genetic-disease children)","Sun and Rain Center (rare-disease organisation, osteogenesis imperfecta families)","BNDS Review (International Department student newspaper)","iGEM team NBJF (AI protein design exchange)","Hongchuanghui Fair","local kindergarten","youth sports school / student athlete programme","senior citizens' club ('iGEM and seniors together club')"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6115/wiki/edu/image20.webp","caption":"Kindergarten children with the BioBrick 'building block' constructs they assembled in small 'syndicates'","caption_zh":"幼兒園孩子與他們在「小聯盟」中組裝出來的 BioBrick 積木構築","credit":"Team BNDS-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6115/wiki/edu/image22.webp","caption":"The five-act puppet show 'Microscopic Defense Line', which showed phagocytosis as a hug rather than combat","caption_zh":"五幕偶戲「微觀防線」，把吞噬作用演成擁抱而不是戰鬥","credit":"Team BNDS-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6115/wiki/edu/image24.webp","caption":"Guiding children at Tianyun Rehabilitation Center through the storybook 'Little Chef Mimi and Her Magical Yeast Friends'","caption_zh":"在天運康復中心帶著孩子讀故事書 Little Chef Mimi and Her Magical Yeast Friends","credit":"Team BNDS-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6115/wiki/edu/image29.webp","caption":"Student athletes aged 10-13 extracting strawberry DNA during the under-resourced-children workshop","caption_zh":"10-13 歲的學生運動員在資源不足兒童工作坊中萃取草莓 DNA","credit":"Team BNDS-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6115/wiki/edu/image36.webp","caption":"Older adults showing the DNA-themed bracelets they made during the health-literacy lecture","caption_zh":"長者展示他們在健康識能講座中做的 DNA 主題手環","credit":"Team BNDS-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Adopt a single named template for every outreach event - BNDS-China's R.E.A.C.H. (Recognize with a pre-event diagnostic, Experience, Apply, Communicate project feedback back into design, Harvest with a matched post-event survey) - and publish the results including the steps you failed to complete; the paired pre/post numbers and the honest gaps are what turn a scrapbook of events into evidence.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"為每一場推廣活動採用同一套有名字的模板：BNDS-China 的 R.E.A.C.H.（Recognize 以活動前診斷開始、Experience、Apply、Communicate 把專案回饋帶回設計、Harvest 以相對應的活動後問卷收尾），並把結果連同自己沒做完的步驟一起公布；正是那些配對的前後測數字與誠實交代的缺口，讓一堆活動紀錄變成證據，而不只是剪貼簿。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/bnds-china/","https://2026.igem.wiki/bnds-china/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/bnds-china/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/bnds-china/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/bnds-china/contribution"],"rank":14},"6119":{"team":"UMA Malaga","id":"6119","section":"Undergrad","country":"Spain","village":"Diagnostics","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/uma-malaga/","projectTitle":"Frida","tagline":"A SHERLOCK-type LwCas13a screen for rare-disease variants, with Diana, a tool that takes a disease name all the way to a plate map.","summary":"Frida uses CRISPR/LwCas13a (SHERLOCK-type collateral cleavage read as fluorescence) to screen for the mutations behind rare genetic diseases, with cystic fibrosis as the model disease and a tandem gRNA assembly system (Neith) for multiplexing. Because a single disease can have hundreds of pathogenic variants and each needs its own guide, the team built Diana (diana-grna-designer), a free MIT-licensed web app, command-line tool and F# library that goes from a disease name, OMIM number or MONDO id, through ClinVar's variant list, to ranked and scored guide RNAs, to an order-ready oligo list, to a combinatorial pooling plan and a decoder for the positive wells. The engineering is unusually disciplined for iGEM: 1,164 unit and component tests plus 75 Playwright browser tests, automated axe-core WCAG 2.2 AA accessibility scans of every page state, every dependency pinned and checksum-verified, and exports in GenBank, SBOL 3 and SBOL 2 that are read back by Biopython and pySBOL3 as part of the test suite. Most striking, the wet lab contradicted the software's central heuristic and the team published that: the synthetic-mismatch substitution rule did not discriminate alleles in the placements tried, so the rule became an option to compare rather than a promise.","awards":["Best Alternative Platform — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Software — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Diagnostics Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A single Blazor Server application (ASP.NET Core 9, C#, Razor components over SignalR, Bootstrap 5) calling an F# library ('gRNA') directly in the same process, with the grna CLI as a second front end over the identical calls so the web page and the terminal always agree. Native science runs as child processes: Bowtie 1.3.1 against a GRCh38 no-ALT index for off-targets, and ViennaRNA via Python 3 for folding. Everything ships in one Docker image (Compose v2) that bakes in the genome index deliberately, because Bowtie memory-maps the index and a volume or bind mount makes alignment more than ten times slower. External calls are limited to NCBI E-utilities, dbSNP Variation Services, ClinVar and the Monarch Initiative. The F# library also builds as a NuGet package (unpublished) referenceable from any .NET project, and the repository carries an agent skill so an AI assistant can install, start, health-check and drive the tool.","dataviz":"Ranked guide tables with nine sortable columns (spacer, GC score, GC %, homopolymers, off-targets, folding energy, unpaired share of spacer, mismatches against the other allele, score), filters on score, off-targets, GC range, allele mismatches and sequence fragment, the seed region underlined and the mutation marked in red, and status conveyed by shape and text rather than colour alone. Off-target chips read none/unique/caution/6+ saturated; expanding a row lists every GRCh38 alignment with chromosome, position, strand and mismatches. RNA structure is shown as dot-bracket plus a FORNA force-directed diagram rendered inside the page, so the sequence never leaves the machine unless the user clicks 'Open in FORNA'. Pooling produces a clickable, keyboard-navigable 96- or 384-well plate map where hovering a well lists its guides, and decoded positive wells are marked with a plus sign. Every term carries a plain-language tooltip, held in one file (HelpText.cs). Light and dark themes, a skip link, keyboard-operable tabs, and automated axe-core scans across WCAG 2.0-2.2 A and AA for every page state.","datascience":"Validation is reported as a matrix of what each part of the tool rests on, with three honest categories: automated tests, real sequences and services, and wet lab, where 'Tested' means lab work has started with no results yet and 'Not shown' is recorded as a result rather than a gap. Numbers: 1,164 NUnit/bUnit cases (1,151 pass, 13 self-skip when live services or ViennaRNA are absent), 75 Playwright/Chromium tests against a deterministic pipeline stand-in, pooling invariants proved over many (V, K) pairs (each guide in exactly R wells, no pool over K, every guide with a unique well set, consistent addressing on both plate formats), and decoding tested for single hits, collisions and dropouts. Hand checks rebuilt the rs334 and F508del designs from the NCBI sequences and confirmed the top deletion guides occur only in the deleted sequence, 6-8 letters from any wild-type window. The whole web flow was re-run against the real container on 2026-10-18 (cystic fibrosis disease search returning 1,517 ClinVar records, five designs, adapters, structure, shortlist, pooling and decoding). Performance was timed inside the container: 8-10 s for a transcript-position design, 28-38 s for a chromosome-position design (dominated by the NCBI download of the whole accession), 17 s for the disease search, about 1 s for a 100-guide pooling plan and 97 s for 100,000 guides. Export correctness was checked structurally: the annotated parts tile the sequence with no gap or overlap and equal the oligo DNA across all 64 combinations of repeat, adapters, flanks and T7 promoter, and the files are read back by Biopython and pySBOL3 with no error or warning.","software":"Diana has three chained but independently usable parts. Disease variants looks a disease up in the Monarch Initiative knowledge graph and lists the ClinVar records NCBI links to its OMIM number, showing ClinVar's own classification and review stars without re-interpreting them, capped at 3,000 records with the list flagged incomplete when it truncates. The Builder takes up to 50 inputs per run as rsIDs (resolved through NCBI Variation Services, keeping only the disease-relevant allele by default so rs334 gives one notation rather than twelve) or strict HGVS including c. positions on NM_/XM_ transcripts, which it converts using the GenBank coding range and says so in a notice; a c. position on a genomic record is refused with advice, because introns would put the guides in the wrong place. It then slides a window (23 nt default, 18-60 allowed) over both the original and mutated sequence on both strands, labels which strand is complementary to the mRNA and puts it first because LwCas13a binds RNA, and scores every candidate on four transparent criteria: GC content against a 40-60% target, homopolymer runs of 4 or more, Bowtie off-target hits in GRCh38 with up to two mismatches, and ViennaRNA minimum free energy of the complete guide under Turner 2004. Candidates sort on the ascending key (off-targets, -energy, -GC score, homopolymers), and the derived 0-1 score is explicitly a relative rank, not a prediction of activity. Two structure checks (is the direct-repeat hairpin intact in the fold, how much of the spacer stays unpaired) and an allele-discrimination count (fewest letters by which the target differs from the other allele, with a 'not discriminating' flag at 0 or 1) inform the choice without changing the ranking. The complete gRNA is built from the 36-nt LwCas13a direct repeat plus the spacer, optionally wrapped in the team's own Frida adapter (BsmBI Type IIS sites plus AAAC and GCTT fusion sites, so the repeat is acquired during Golden Gate assembly instead of being synthesised for every guide) and the BioBricks RFC[10] prefix/suffix adapter, which nest correctly so the junctions complete the standard sequences exactly. Cloning checks scan the DNA that would actually be ordered, on both strands, for ten enzymes (BsaI, BsmBI, SapI, BbsI, EcoRI, XbaI, SpeI, PstI, NotI, EcoRV), excluding sites an adapter carries on purpose, and show RFC[10] and RFC[1000] compatibility badges mirroring the Registry's own Assembly Compatibility rules. Guide Pooling then offers three combinatorial layouts (2D Fragmented, 2D Matrix, 3D) with stated well-count formulas, picks the cheapest automatically, places the result on 96- or 384-well plates and decodes a screen afterwards, distinguishing definite from ambiguous implications rather than hiding the collision case; the classic binary log2 model is deliberately excluded because it requires K = V/2 and breaks the five-guides-per-tandem-array limit. For 100 guides at K = 5 that is 40 wells instead of 100 reactions, a 60% saving. Exports: oligo CSV with optional T7 promoter and top/bottom strands plus a Restriction sites column so the warning travels with the order, FASTA, annotated GenBank, SBOL 3 (RDF/XML, Sequence Ontology roles) and SBOL 2 (added only because a libSBOLj-based tool rejected the SBOL 3 file). CSV fields starting with =, +, - or @ are neutralised so a spreadsheet does not execute them. Deployment is local by design: 'git clone https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uma-malaga/diana-grna-designer.git && ./start.sh', which checks Docker, disk and Compose, then reports success only once http://localhost:5000/healthz answers; about 10 GB disk and 3 GB RAM. There is no hosted design API, and the wiki says why (the 4 GB index and native tools make a public server costly, and local running keeps patient-adjacent data private) and then demonstrates that a HTTP front end would be thin by writing and running a minimal ASP.NET Core /export endpoint over the same library, while labelling that sketch a test of the idea rather than a shipped service. What is live and clickable is the example gallery at https://diana-grna-designer-7723f5.igem.wiki/, which publishes the unedited grna output for rs334 (48 candidate spacers), F508del (36 candidates) and a 100-guide pooling plan, each recording the date (2026-10-19), the commit (19a8e08), the Docker image sha256, the tool versions (Bowtie 1.3.1, ViennaRNA 2.7.2), the exact commands run, and the note that a second run the same day gave identical designs. Documentation is layered: README.md for usage, architecture, configuration and troubleshooting; docs/ for the runtime contract, library usage, a manual test plan and a validation record; and BIOLOGICAL_REPORT.md, which maps each biological step to the code for a non-programming audience and lists the open scientific questions. The 'Extending Diana' section walks a specific future feature (a wobble-aware allele check) through all six places in the codebase it would touch, with a sketch of the F# function. Licence MIT, with third-party licences listed (Bowtie Artistic 2.0; ViennaRNA free for academic use, commercial use requiring a separate licence), and an explicit statement that parts of the code were written with an AI coding assistant and reviewed by the team, which remains responsible.","stack":[".NET 9 / ASP.NET Core","Blazor Server","C#","F#","SignalR","Bootstrap 5","Python 3","Bowtie 1.3.1","ViennaRNA 2.7.2","Docker + Compose v2","NUnit","bUnit","Playwright (Chromium)","axe-core","Biopython (export verification)","pySBOL3 / pySBOL2","SBOL 3 and SBOL 2","GenBank flat file","HGVS","NCBI E-utilities / dbSNP Variation Services","ClinVar","Monarch Initiative API","FORNA","GRCh38","MIT licence","iGEM GitLab"],"techniques":["LwCas13a / SHERLOCK guide RNA design","sliding-window candidate generation on both strands","multi-criteria scoring and lexicographic ranking","short-read alignment for off-target counting","RNA secondary structure minimum free energy (Turner 2004)","synthetic-mismatch (substitution rule) allele discrimination","combinatorial group testing / pooled screening (2D fragmented, 2D matrix, 3D layouts)","ambiguity-aware decoding of pooled positives","Type IIS Golden Gate adapter design","restriction-site screening against RFC[10] and RFC[1000]","SPDI to HGVS conversion","property-based invariant testing over (V, K) pairs","automated accessibility auditing","dependency pinning with checksum verification","resumable batch processing with distinct exit codes"],"frameworks_zh":"一個單一的 Blazor Server 應用程式（ASP.NET Core 9、C#、以 SignalR 承載的 Razor 元件、Bootstrap 5），在同一行程內直接呼叫一個 F# 函式庫（gRNA），並以 grna 命令列工具作為第二個前端、呼叫完全相同的介面，因此網頁與終端機永遠一致。原生科學工具以子行程執行：以 Bowtie 1.3.1 對 GRCh38 no-ALT 索引比對脫靶，以 Python 3 呼叫 ViennaRNA 做結構摺疊。所有東西都裝進一個 Docker 映像（Compose v2），並刻意把基因組索引烘進映像，因為 Bowtie 以記憶體映射方式讀取索引，改用 volume 或 bind mount 會讓比對慢上十倍以上。對外呼叫僅限 NCBI E-utilities、dbSNP Variation Services、ClinVar 與 Monarch Initiative。這個 F# 函式庫也可建置成 NuGet 套件（未發布），供任何 .NET 專案引用；程式庫中另附一個 agent skill，讓 AI 助理能安裝、啟動、健康檢查並操作這個工具。","dataviz_zh":"排序後的嚮導表格有九個可排序欄位（spacer、GC 分數、GC %、同聚物、脫靶數、摺疊能量、spacer 未配對比例、與另一對偶基因的錯配數、分數），可依分數、脫靶數、GC 範圍、對偶基因錯配與序列片段篩選，種子區以底線標示、突變以紅色標出，狀態同時以形狀與文字傳達，而不只靠顏色。脫靶標籤分為 none/unique/caution/6+ 飽和；展開一列會列出每一個 GRCh38 比對結果，含染色體、位置、股向與錯配數。RNA 結構以 dot-bracket 加上在頁面內繪製的 FORNA 力導向圖呈現，因此除非使用者點選「Open in FORNA」，序列絕不離開本機。混樣功能會產生可點擊、可用鍵盤巡覽的 96 孔或 384 孔盤位圖，滑過某孔即列出其中的嚮導，解碼後的陽性孔以加號標記。每個術語都附有平實語言的提示說明，統一放在一個檔案（HelpText.cs）中。另有亮色與暗色主題、跳至主要內容的連結、可鍵盤操作的頁籤，以及對每個頁面狀態橫跨 WCAG 2.0-2.2 A 與 AA 等級的 axe-core 自動掃描。","datascience_zh":"驗證以一張矩陣呈現工具每個部分各自建立在什麼基礎上，並誠實分成三類：自動化測試、真實序列與線上服務，以及濕實驗室；其中「已測試」意指實驗工作已開始但尚無結果，而「未顯示」被記錄為一項結果而非缺漏。數字如下：1,164 個 NUnit/bUnit 案例（1,151 通過，13 個在缺少線上服務或 ViennaRNA 時自行跳過）、75 個以確定性管線替身為對象的 Playwright/Chromium 測試、在許多 (V, K) 組合上證明的混樣不變量（每個嚮導恰好出現在 R 個孔、沒有任何池超過 K、每個嚮導都有唯一的孔位集合、兩種盤型的定址一致），以及針對單一命中、碰撞與漏失的解碼測試。人工檢查則從 NCBI 序列重建了 rs334 與 F508del 的設計，確認排名最前的缺失型嚮導只出現在被刪除的序列中，且與任何野生型視窗相距 6-8 個字母。整個網頁流程在 2026-10-18 以真實容器重跑一次（囊狀纖維化疾病查詢回傳 1,517 筆 ClinVar 記錄，以及五個設計、轉接子、結構、候選名單、混樣與解碼）。效能在容器內計時：轉錄本位置設計 8-10 秒、染色體位置設計 28-38 秒（主要耗在從 NCBI 下載整個 accession）、疾病查詢 17 秒、100 個嚮導的混樣計畫約 1 秒、100,000 個嚮導 97 秒。匯出正確性以結構方式檢查：標註的部件完整鋪滿序列、沒有空隙或重疊，並在 repeat、轉接子、側翼與 T7 啟動子的全部 64 種組合下都與寡核苷酸 DNA 相符；檔案再由 Biopython 與 pySBOL3 讀回，無任何錯誤或警告。","software_zh":"Diana 有三個彼此串接、但也可獨立使用的部分。「疾病變異」會在 Monarch Initiative 知識圖譜中查詢疾病，並列出 NCBI 連結到其 OMIM 編號的 ClinVar 記錄，照 ClinVar 自己的分類與審查星等呈現、不重新解讀，上限為 3,000 筆，截斷時會標示清單不完整。Builder 每次最多接受 50 筆輸入，可為 rsID（透過 NCBI Variation Services 解析，預設只保留與疾病相關的對偶基因，因此 rs334 只給出一種標記而非十二種），或嚴格的 HGVS，包括 NM_/XM_ 轉錄本上的 c. 位置——後者會用 GenBank 的編碼區範圍換算，並在通知中明示；若在基因組記錄上給 c. 位置則會被拒絕並附上建議，因為內含子會讓嚮導落在錯誤的位置。接著它在原始與突變序列的雙股上滑動視窗（預設 23 nt，允許 18-60），標示哪一股與 mRNA 互補並把它排在前面（因為 LwCas13a 結合 RNA），並以四項透明標準為每個候選評分：GC 含量相對 40-60% 的目標、長度 4 以上的同聚物、在 GRCh38 中容許最多兩個錯配的 Bowtie 脫靶命中數，以及在 Turner 2004 參數下完整嚮導的 ViennaRNA 最小自由能。候選以遞增鍵排序（脫靶數、-能量、-GC 分數、同聚物），而導出的 0-1 分數被明確說明為相對排名，不是活性預測。另有兩項結構檢查（摺疊後 direct-repeat 髮夾是否完整、spacer 有多少比例保持未配對）與一個對偶基因區辨計數（標的與另一對偶基因相差的最少字母數，為 0 或 1 時標記「無法區辨」），用於輔助選擇但不改變排名。完整的 gRNA 由 36 nt 的 LwCas13a direct repeat 加上 spacer 組成，可選擇再包上團隊自己的 Frida 轉接子（BsmBI Type IIS 切位加上 AAAC 與 GCTT 融合位，使 repeat 在 Golden Gate 組裝過程中取得，而不必為每個嚮導各合成一次）以及 BioBricks RFC[10] 前/後綴轉接子，兩者能正確嵌套，使接點恰好補完標準序列。選殖檢查會掃描真正會被下訂的 DNA（雙股）是否含有十種酵素的切位（BsaI、BsmBI、SapI、BbsI、EcoRI、XbaI、SpeI、PstI、NotI、EcoRV），並排除轉接子刻意帶入的切位，另顯示對應 Registry 自身組裝相容性規則的 RFC[10] 與 RFC[1000] 相容性標章。Guide Pooling 則提供三種組合式佈局（2D Fragmented、2D Matrix、3D）並列出各自的孔數公式，自動挑出最省的一種，把結果放到 96 孔或 384 孔盤上，並在篩檢後解碼，區分「確定」與「模稜兩可」的推論，而不是把碰撞情形藏起來；經典的二元 log2 模型被刻意排除，因為它要求 K = V/2，會違反每條串聯陣列最多五個嚮導的限制。以 100 個嚮導、K = 5 計算，這是 40 個孔而非 100 次反應，節省 60%。匯出格式包括：寡核苷酸 CSV（可選加 T7 啟動子、含上下股，並附一個限制酶切位欄位，讓警示隨訂單一起傳遞）、FASTA、有註解的 GenBank、SBOL 3（RDF/XML，使用 Sequence Ontology 角色）與 SBOL 2（純粹因為某個基於 libSBOLj 的工具拒收 SBOL 3 檔案才加上）。CSV 中以 =、+、- 或 @ 開頭的欄位會被中和，以免試算表將其當公式執行。部署刻意只在本機：「git clone https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uma-malaga/diana-grna-designer.git && ./start.sh」，它會檢查 Docker、磁碟與 Compose，只有在 http://localhost:5000/healthz 有回應後才報告成功；約需 10 GB 磁碟與 3 GB 記憶體。沒有提供託管的設計 API，wiki 也說明了原因（4 GB 的索引與原生工具讓公開伺服器成本高昂，而本機執行能讓貼近病患的資料保持私密），接著又以同一函式庫寫出並實際執行一個極簡的 ASP.NET Core /export 端點，示範 HTTP 前端其實很薄，同時把這份草稿標示為概念驗證而非正式服務。真正上線可點的是 https://diana-grna-designer-7723f5.igem.wiki/ 的範例展示區，公開了 rs334（48 個候選 spacer）、F508del（36 個候選）與一份 100 嚮導混樣計畫的未經編輯 grna 輸出，每份都記錄日期（2026-10-19）、commit（19a8e08）、Docker 映像的 sha256、工具版本（Bowtie 1.3.1、ViennaRNA 2.7.2）、實際執行的指令，以及同日第二次執行得到完全相同設計的註記。文件分層撰寫：README.md 說明用法、架構、設定與疑難排解；docs/ 收錄執行期契約、函式庫用法、人工測試計畫與驗證紀錄；BIOLOGICAL_REPORT.md 則為非程式背景的讀者把每個生物步驟對應到程式碼，並列出尚未解決的科學問題。「Extending Diana」一節把一個具體的未來功能（考慮搖擺配對的對偶基因檢查）走過程式庫中會被動到的全部六個位置，並附上 F# 函式的草稿。授權為 MIT，並列出第三方授權（Bowtie 為 Artistic 2.0；ViennaRNA 學術使用免費、商業使用需另行授權），同時明確聲明部分程式碼是在 AI 程式助理協助下撰寫、由團隊審閱，責任仍由團隊承擔。"},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A survey of 227 people probed public awareness of rare diseases, and the team reported it with the limits visible: 90.7% recognised the importance of early diagnosis and 87.7% knew newborn screening differs between Spain's autonomous communities, but only 11% identified the cost as a share of family income and only 9.3% the true global prevalence. They also surfaced an awareness-engagement gap, with 63% reporting no rare-disease activity in the past year (144 of 227 chose 'none of the above'). Demographics are published in full (gender, education, age, occupation, contact with a patient) and the wiki states explicitly that the sample is exploratory, that the percentages describe the sample and are not estimates for the general population, and that the reference answers themselves need validating before an overall knowledge score can be claimed.","ihp":"The human practices team (named Athena) ran an iterative cycle they call BARI: Bibliographic research, Application, Reflection, Integration, explicitly not a linear pipeline, with each cycle able to send them back to reconsider an earlier assumption. The substantive shift was away from treating Frida as a technology gap: conversations with patients, healthcare professionals, researchers and patient associations revealed territorial inequalities in newborn screening across Spanish autonomous communities, differences in care pathways, and the consequences of diagnostic delay, which moved the question from 'can we build a detector' to 'where in the diagnostic pathway could such a tool actually respond to a need'. The team also records that screening programmes are not definitive diagnostic tools and require confirmatory testing, and that the associated wait can cause irreversible damage in infants. The wet-lab feedback into the software is the clearest integration of all: the lab's failure to discriminate alleles, traced partly to G-U wobble pairs that LwCas13a tolerates, was published, demoted the substitution rule to one option among the ranked candidates, turned the rule's positions and spacer length into user settings so revised placements can be tested without changing code, and set a wobble-aware allele check as the next feature.","realWorld":"Frida targets the rare-disease diagnostic odyssey, where heterogeneous presentation and many candidate mutations can mean years of uncertainty and repeated consultations. The project grew out of the University of Málaga's existing screening and early-detection research, and the PIs' professional network provided the first stakeholder contacts. Diana is deliberately shaped for a clinical-adjacent setting: no account needed, nothing persisted, loopback-only binding, non-root container, and local-only deployment so sequence data never leaves the researcher's machine.","partners":["University of Málaga (UMA) screening and early-detection groups","rare disease patient associations","Spanish newborn screening professionals","Anthropic (sponsor)","GenScript (sponsor)","Integrated DNA Technologies (sponsor)"],"publicEngagement_zh":"一份 227 人的問卷調查探詢公眾對罕見疾病的認識，而團隊在報告時把限制攤開來說：90.7% 認同早期診斷的重要性、87.7% 知道新生兒篩檢在西班牙各自治區之間有差異，但只有 11% 能指出成本佔家庭收入的比例、只有 9.3% 答對真實的全球盛行率。他們也揭露了認知與行動之間的落差：63% 表示過去一年沒有參與任何罕見疾病相關活動（227 人中有 144 人選擇「以上皆非」）。人口統計資料完整公開（性別、教育程度、年齡、職業、是否認識病患），wiki 並明確指出這份樣本屬探索性質、百分比只描述該樣本而非一般大眾的推估值，而且參考答案本身也需要先經驗證，才能宣稱一個整體的知識分數。","ihp_zh":"人類實踐小組（取名 Athena）執行一套他們稱為 BARI 的迭代循環：Bibliographic research（文獻研究）、Application（應用）、Reflection（反思）、Integration（整合），並明確說明這不是線性流程，每一輪都可能把他們送回去重新檢視先前的某個假設。實質的轉向是不再把 Frida 當成一個技術缺口的填補：與病患、醫療專業人員、研究者及病友協會的對話揭露了西班牙各自治區之間新生兒篩檢的地域不平等、照護路徑的差異，以及診斷延誤的後果，使問題從「我們能不能做出一個偵測器」轉為「在診斷路徑的哪一個環節，這樣的工具才真的回應了某個需求」。團隊也記錄下：篩檢計畫並非確診工具，必須有確認性檢驗，而隨之而來的等待可能在嬰兒身上造成不可逆的傷害。濕實驗室回饋到軟體上的部分是所有整合中最明確的一項：實驗未能區分對偶基因（部分原因追溯到 LwCas13a 可容忍的 G-U 搖擺配對）被如實公開，使取代規則降級為排序候選中的一個選項，並把該規則的位置與 spacer 長度改成使用者可調的設定，讓修正後的放置方式無須改程式即可測試，同時把「考慮搖擺配對的對偶基因檢查」列為下一個功能。","realWorld_zh":"Frida 針對的是罕見疾病的「診斷漂流」：症狀表現異質、候選突變眾多，往往意味著數年的不確定與一再的就診。專案源自馬拉加大學既有的篩檢與早期偵測研究，指導教授的專業人際網絡則提供了最初的利害關係人聯繫。Diana 刻意為貼近臨床的場景而設計：不需帳號、不留存任何資料、僅綁定 loopback、容器以非 root 執行，且只能本機部署，使序列資料絕不離開研究者的機器。"},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6119/wiki/images/software/v6-07-builder-ranked-table.avif","caption":"Diana's ranked spacer table: GC score, homopolymers, off-targets, assembly compatibility badges, folding energy, unpaired spacer share, mismatches against the other allele and the relative score, with the seed underlined and the mutation in red.","credit":"Team UMA Malaga, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"Diana 的 spacer 排序表：GC 分數、同聚物、脫靶數、組裝相容性標章、摺疊能量、spacer 未配對比例、與另一對偶基因的錯配數，以及相對分數；種子區以底線標示、突變以紅色呈現。"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6119/wiki/images/software/v6-11-disease-results.avif","caption":"The ClinVar variants of cystic fibrosis pulled through the Monarch Initiative knowledge graph, with classification, review stars and conditions shown as ClinVar gives them.","credit":"Team UMA Malaga, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"透過 Monarch Initiative 知識圖譜取得的囊狀纖維化 ClinVar 變異，分類、審查星等與疾病條件皆照 ClinVar 原樣呈現。"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6119/wiki/images/software/v6-22-pooling-plate-map.avif","caption":"The combinatorial pooling plate map: hovering a well shows which guides go into that tube, and arrow keys move between wells.","credit":"Team UMA Malaga, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"組合式混樣的盤位圖：滑過某孔即顯示哪些嚮導會進入該管，方向鍵可在孔位之間移動。"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6119/wiki/images/software/v6-14-builder-complete-grna.avif","caption":"The complete gRNA card: the LwCas13a direct repeat in green and the chosen spacer in magenta, with choices for the repeat, the Frida and BioBricks adapters and custom flanks.","credit":"Team UMA Malaga, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"完整 gRNA 卡片：綠色為 LwCas13a 的 direct repeat，洋紅色為選定的 spacer，並可選擇 repeat、Frida 與 BioBricks 轉接子以及自訂側翼。"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Publish a validation matrix that separates what automated tests prove, what a real run against live services proves, and what the bench has actually shown, and record 'not shown' as a result: Diana's wiki states outright that its ranking order, its substitution rule and its pooling layout are untested in the lab, and that the lab contradicted the substitution rule. A research centre should pair that honesty with Diana's two reusable mechanics, a pure scientific core (F#) that the GUI, the CLI and an AI agent skill all sit on as thin front ends, and a published example gallery pinned to a commit, image digest and exact commands so strangers can see real output without installing anything.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/uma-malaga/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/uma-malaga/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/uma-malaga/","https://diana-grna-designer-7723f5.igem.wiki/","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uma-malaga/diana-grna-designer","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/uma-malaga"],"projectTitle_zh":"Frida","tagline_zh":"一套用於罕見疾病變異的 SHERLOCK 型 LwCas13a 篩檢，並搭配 Diana——一個能從疾病名稱一路做到盤位圖的工具。","summary_zh":"Frida 使用 CRISPR/LwCas13a（SHERLOCK 型的旁側切割，以螢光讀出）篩檢罕見遺傳疾病背後的突變，以囊狀纖維化作為模式疾病，並以串聯 gRNA 組裝系統（Neith）實現多重檢測。由於單一疾病可能有數百個致病變異、每個都需要自己的嚮導，團隊開發了 Diana（diana-grna-designer）——一個免費、採 MIT 授權的網頁應用程式、命令列工具與 F# 函式庫，能從疾病名稱、OMIM 編號或 MONDO id 出發，經過 ClinVar 的變異清單，產生排序並評分的嚮導 RNA、可直接下訂的寡核苷酸清單、組合式混樣（pooling）計畫，以及陽性孔位的解碼器。這個專案的工程紀律在 iGEM 中相當罕見：1,164 個單元與元件測試，加上 75 個 Playwright 瀏覽器測試、對每個頁面狀態自動執行 axe-core WCAG 2.2 AA 無障礙掃描、所有相依套件皆鎖定版本並驗證檢查碼，匯出的 GenBank、SBOL 3 與 SBOL 2 檔案還會在測試套件中由 Biopython 與 pySBOL3 讀回驗證。最醒目的是，濕實驗室推翻了軟體的核心啟發式規則，而團隊照實公開：在所嘗試的放置位置上，人工錯配取代規則並未能區分對偶基因，於是該規則從承諾降級為一個可供比較的選項。","gemsTakeaway_zh":"公開一張驗證矩陣，把「自動化測試能證明什麼」、「對線上服務的真實執行能證明什麼」與「濕實驗室實際展示了什麼」分開，並把「未顯示」記錄為一項結果：Diana 的 wiki 直接寫明，它的排序順序、取代規則與混樣佈局都未在實驗室中驗證，而實驗結果還推翻了取代規則。研究單位應該把這份誠實，與 Diana 的兩項可重複使用的機制搭配起來：一個純粹的科學核心（F#），讓 GUI、CLI 與一個 AI agent skill 都只作為薄前端架在上面；以及一個釘住 commit、映像摘要與確切指令的公開範例展示區，讓陌生人不必安裝任何東西就能看到真實輸出。","rank":21},"6122":{"team":"Cornell","id":"6122","section":"Undergrad","country":"United States","village":"Fashion & Cosmetics","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/","projectTitle":"Klothos","projectTitle_zh":"Klothos","tagline":"A smart bandage: engineered probiotics inside electrospun alginate nanofibers that release an anti-fibrotic peptide only where a wound is scarring badly.","tagline_zh":"一款智慧敷料：把工程改造的益生菌包在靜電紡絲的海藻酸鈉奈米纖維裡，只在傷口正走向嚴重疤痕化的地方釋放抗纖維化胜肽。","summary":"Every scar treatment on the market today starts after the scar has formed — silicone sheeting, intralesional steroid, laser and grafts are all passive or reactive, and none addresses fibrosis biology during the critical healing window. Klothos intervenes during healing instead: engineered bacteria secrete 810A, a 12-amino-acid peptide that binds the exposed C-terminal domain of CTGF (CCN2) and blocks fibroblast-to-myofibroblast activation, and expression is held behind a two-input AND gate built from the Pseudomonas syringae hrpR/hrpS/hrpL system so the peptide is only made when reactive oxygen species (via TrxC) and hypoxia (via Pfnr) are both present — the signature of unchecked remodelling. The bacteria are encapsulated in an alginate/PEO nanofiber matrix spun on a coaxial electrospinner the team designed and built themselves, because commercial instruments cost far more than an undergraduate team can reach. It won Best Hardware and Best Presentation on the strength of that open, flat-packable, interlock-protected electrospinner plus a modular 3D-printed coaxial spinneret adapter, and Best Fashion & Cosmetics on a project that is unusually complete end to end: 20-plus risk-rated commercialisation analysis, a six-phase FDA path, and a human practices programme built around people who actually live with scars.","summary_zh":"今天市面上每一種疤痕療法都是在疤痕形成之後才開始——矽膠片、病灶內類固醇注射、雷射與植皮，全都是被動或反應式的，沒有一種在癒合的關鍵時間窗內處理纖維化的生物學。Klothos 改在癒合過程中介入：工程改造的細菌分泌 810A，一段 12 個胺基酸的胜肽，會結合 CTGF（CCN2）暴露出來的 C 端結構域，阻斷纖維母細胞轉為肌纖維母細胞的活化；而其表現被關在一個以 Pseudomonas syringae 的 hrpR/hrpS/hrpL 系統建成的雙輸入 AND 邏輯閘之後，因此只有在活性氧（經 TrxC）與缺氧（經 Pfnr）同時存在時才會製造胜肽——那正是重塑失控的特徵。細菌被包覆在海藻酸鈉/PEO 奈米纖維基質中，而這層基質是用團隊自行設計並製作的同軸靜電紡絲機紡出來的，因為市售機器的價格遠超大學部團隊能負擔的範圍。他們憑著這台開源、可拆平收納、設有安全互鎖的靜電紡絲機，加上一個模組化的 3D 列印同軸噴絲頭轉接件，拿下 Best Hardware 與 Best Presentation；又以一個從頭到尾罕見完整的專案拿下 Best Fashion & Cosmetics：20 多項標定風險等級的商業化分析、一條六階段的 FDA 路徑，以及一套真正圍繞著帶著疤痕生活的人所建立的人類實踐計畫。","awards":["Top 10 (Undergrad)","Best Hardware — Winner (Undergrad)","Best Education — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Presentation — Winner (Undergrad)","Best Fashion & Cosmetics Project — Winner"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Cornell's modelling splits cleanly into wet lab and product development. On the biology side: a production-degradation ODE (dF/dt = alpha*X - delta_F*F) for SUMO-His-810A accumulation against biomass; a Hill function for Tet and future inducible promoter activity; Michaelis-Menten kinetics for SUMO protease cleavage to recover active peptide; an ELISA-based Hill-Langmuir binding isotherm for 810A against CTGF/C, fixed at n=1 because there is a single site, with an explicit note that a fitted n far from 1 would indicate error rather than cooperativity; and a quadratic ligand-depletion model for the regime where accessible CTGF and peptide concentrations are comparable and the ordinary Langmuir assumption breaks. Downstream of binding they built a reduced-order dynamic systems model of fibroblast state transition, parameterised from a protein interaction network assembled in STRING v12.5 — filtered on the Scarring Human Phenotype Ontology term HP:0100699, recovering 48 weighted edges, merged with CCN2's 20 nearest first-degree and 10 nearest second-degree neighbours, surfacing SMAD3, FN1 and TGFB2 as major nodes. Those nodes and weights were then run in Netflux as a logic-based ODE network (normalised node activity with a time constant, modified Hill activation and inhibition functions) using COL1A1 accumulation as the proxy for extracellular matrix hardening, and the simulation tracks the downstream TGF-beta inhibition reported in Xiao et al. 2020. Wound environment is modelled explicitly: ROS as a transient peak function calibrated against Carney et al. 2019 time-series qRT-PCR of SOD1, MGST1 and PRDX6 in hypertrophic scars, oxygen as an exponential recovery function, each feeding a Hill-function promoter. AlphaFold was used to render 810A and the CTGF/C-810A-6xHis complex. On the hardware side: a semi-empirical predictor of shell-solution viscosity (polymer overlap and entanglement statistics via Mark-Houwink), conductivity (mobile ion contribution) and surface tension (surfactant adsorption with a CMC/CAC plateau), the Fridrikh scaling law for terminal jet radius from flow rate, jet current and surface tension, plus continuity-based flow rate and stepper-motor plunger speed models.","frameworks_zh":"Cornell 的建模清楚分成濕實驗與產品開發兩塊。生物學這側：一條描述 SUMO-His-810A 相對於生物量累積的生產—降解 ODE（dF/dt = alpha*X - delta_F*F）；一條描述 Tet 與未來誘導型啟動子活性的 Hill 函數；SUMO 蛋白酶切割以回收活性胜肽的 Michaelis-Menten 動力學；一條以 ELISA 為基礎、描述 810A 對 CTGF/C 結合的 Hill-Langmuir 結合等溫線，因為只有單一結合位而把 n 固定為 1，並明確註記若擬合出的 n 遠離 1，代表的是誤差而不是協同性；以及一個二次式的配體耗竭模型，用於可接觸的 CTGF 與胜肽濃度相當、普通 Langmuir 假設失效的情形。在結合之後的下游，他們建了一個纖維母細胞狀態轉換的降階動態系統模型，參數取自在 STRING v12.5 組成的蛋白質交互作用網路——以 Scarring 的 Human Phenotype Ontology 詞條 HP:0100699 過濾，取得 48 條加權邊，再與 CCN2 最近的 20 個一階鄰點與 10 個二階鄰點合併，浮現出 SMAD3、FN1 與 TGFB2 等主要節點。這些節點與權重接著在 Netflux 中以基於邏輯的 ODE 網路執行（帶時間常數的正規化節點活性、修改過的 Hill 活化與抑制函數），以 COL1A1 的累積作為細胞外基質硬化的替代指標，模擬並追蹤 Xiao 等人 2020 年報告的下游 TGF-beta 抑制。傷口環境也有明確建模：ROS 以一個暫態峰值函數描述，並以 Carney 等人 2019 年在肥厚性疤痕中對 SOD1、MGST1 與 PRDX6 的時間序列 qRT-PCR 校準；氧氣則用指數回復函數，兩者各自餵進一個 Hill 函數型啟動子。AlphaFold 則用來呈現 810A 以及 CTGF/C-810A-6xHis 複合體。硬體這側：一個半經驗預測器，用來推估殼層溶液的黏度（以 Mark-Houwink 處理高分子重疊與糾纏統計）、導電度（可動離子貢獻）與表面張力（界面活性劑吸附，帶 CMC/CAC 平台），加上由流率、射流電流與表面張力推出終端射流半徑的 Fridrikh 標度律，以及基於連續方程的流率與步進馬達推桿速度模型。","dataviz":"The standout is the Unified Readiness Classifier, which collapses three separate property predictions into a single green/yellow/red call on whether a formulation should go to the electrospinner at all — green means proceed to voltage-window testing, yellow allows one short trial or minor reformulation, red means reformulate first. It is rendered as a spinning-viability contour map over sodium alginate and PEO weight percentages produced by Monte Carlo sampling against literature results, so a reader can see the spinnable region rather than read a table of numbers. The alginate molecular-weight analysis is similarly well-framed: one plot puts viscosity on the left axis spanning more than four orders of magnitude while conductivity and surface tension on the right axis stay flat, which makes the whole argument visible at a glance — conductivity caps how much alginate you can dissolve, molecular weight decides whether that limit is reachable, and the optimum is interior rather than monotonic. The STRING network is shown as a force-directed layout and the Netflux run as normalised activity curves for CTGF, TGFB1, FN1, COL1A1, SMAD2 and SMAD3 together. The wiki itself is a scroll-driven 3D island journey ('scroll to travel, click an island to explore') with an interactive AND-gate widget letting the reader switch each input signal on and off, and a WebGL model of the electrospinner.","dataviz_zh":"最突出的是 Unified Readiness Classifier：它把三項各自獨立的性質預測收斂成一個綠/黃/紅的判斷，決定某個配方到底該不該送上靜電紡絲機——綠色代表可進入電壓窗測試，黃色允許一次短時間試紡或小幅調整配方，紅色代表先重新配方再說。它畫成一張以蒙地卡羅取樣對照文獻結果、橫跨海藻酸鈉與 PEO 重量百分比的可紡性等高線圖，讀者因此是看到可紡區域，而不是去讀一張數字表。海藻酸鈉分子量的分析框架也同樣好：同一張圖把跨越四個數量級以上的黏度放在左軸，而導電度與表面張力放在右軸且維持平坦，整個論點一眼就看得出來——導電度決定海藻酸鈉最多能溶多少、分子量決定那個上限是否達得到，而最佳點落在中間而非單調方向上。STRING 網路以力導向佈局呈現，Netflux 的執行結果則把 CTGF、TGFB1、FN1、COL1A1、SMAD2 與 SMAD3 的正規化活性曲線畫在一起。wiki 本身是一段由捲動驅動的 3D 島嶼旅程（「捲動前進，點島探索」），帶有一個互動式 AND 閘元件讓讀者自行開關兩路輸入訊號，以及一個靜電紡絲機的 WebGL 模型。","datascience":"The classifier is the clearest case of turning data into a predictive tool: rather than measuring solutions after purchase, Cornell predicts viscosity, conductivity and surface tension from formulation inputs (alginate concentration, PEO concentration and molecular weight, surfactant type and concentration, salt or buffer content, temperature) and uses the prediction to avoid spinning runs that cannot work. They name candidate implementations — logistic regression, random forest, or Gaussian process classification, favouring the Gaussian process on a small dataset because it returns uncertainty — and define a two-level validation plan: property-level (mean absolute error for viscosity, percent error for conductivity, absolute error in mN/m for surface tension against held-out measured formulations) and outcome-level (whether predicted-green formulations actually produce stable shell-only fibres, judged on Taylor cone formation, current stability, bead formation, dry deposition and fibre diameter distribution). They say outright that the classifier matters more than exact numerical accuracy, and that literature Mark-Houwink, CMC and adsorption constants are starting estimates to be recalibrated against the team's own measurements. Fibre morphology was quantified by image analysis: tortuosity as the ratio of fibre contour length to end-to-end distance, with a >1.10 threshold defining 'curly', giving 8% curly and 92% straight. Failure diagnosis was also model-driven — droplet breakup was traced to insufficient PEO chain entanglement at 100 kDa, leading them to raise PEO from 1.5% to 2% and cut back PS80 surfactant.","datascience_zh":"那個分類器是把資料變成預測工具最清楚的例子：Cornell 不是買了溶液再去量，而是從配方輸入（海藻酸鈉濃度、PEO 濃度與分子量、界面活性劑種類與濃度、鹽或緩衝液含量、溫度）預測黏度、導電度與表面張力，再用預測結果避開不可能成功的紡絲實驗。他們指名候選做法——邏輯斯迴歸、隨機森林或高斯過程分類——並在小資料集上偏好高斯過程，因為它會回報不確定性；也定義了兩層驗證計畫：性質層（黏度看平均絕對誤差、導電度看百分比誤差、表面張力看 mN/m 的絕對誤差，對照保留的實測配方）與結果層（被預測為綠色的配方是否真的紡出穩定的純殼層纖維，依 Taylor 錐形成、電流穩定性、珠狀缺陷、乾燥沉積與纖維直徑分佈判定）。他們直說分類結果比精確數值準確度更重要，也直說文獻上的 Mark-Houwink、CMC 與吸附常數只是起始估計值，要用團隊自己的量測重新校準。纖維形態以影像分析量化：彎曲度定義為纖維輪廓長度與端到端距離之比，以 >1.10 為「捲曲」門檻，結果是 8% 捲曲、92% 平直。失敗診斷同樣由模型驅動——液滴破碎被追溯到 100 kDa 下 PEO 鏈糾纏不足，因此他們把 PEO 從 1.5% 提高到 2%，並減少 PS80 界面活性劑。","software":"No standalone software release; the released artefact is the hardware. The electrospinner is published openly as a bill of materials, CAD files, circuit diagrams, assembly documentation, an operation manual and a dedicated safety manual, designed to be disassembled and flat-packed for transport by teams in shared or temporary workspaces. Control is an ESP32 DevKitC microcontroller driving an AHV24V30KVR5MAW high-voltage module (24 V in, up to 30 kV out) for digitised control in place of a potentiometer, with an access-door interlock and emergency stop that cut power and ground the high-voltage circuit. A separate contribution is the modular 3D-printed coaxial needle adapter, which keeps metal needle tips for conductivity while 3D-printing the structure, adaptable across needle gauges and core-shell flow configurations. They also publish a disulfide-bond-optimised SHuffle expression protocol (6xHis-SUMO fusion, SUMO as chaperone and clean cleavage handle) framed for reuse on other hard-to-express proteins such as insulin-like growth factors, antibody fragments and venom peptides, plus protocols for alginate preparation, crosslinking viability testing, escape testing, light microscopy ImageJ analysis and spectrographic bacterial settling.","software_zh":"沒有獨立的軟體釋出；真正釋出的成果是硬體。靜電紡絲機以材料清單、CAD 檔、電路圖、組裝文件、操作手冊與一本專門的安全手冊公開，並刻意設計成可拆解、可平板化收納，方便在共用或臨時工作空間裡的團隊搬運。控制端是 ESP32 DevKitC 微控制器，驅動一個 AHV24V30KVR5MAW 高壓模組（輸入 24 V，輸出可達 30 kV），以數位控制取代可變電阻；另有門蓋安全互鎖與緊急停止，會切斷電源並把高壓電路接地。另一項貢獻是模組化的 3D 列印同軸針頭轉接件：結構用 3D 列印，但保留金屬針尖以維持導電性，可適配不同針號與各種核—殼流配置。他們也公開一份針對雙硫鍵最佳化的 SHuffle 表現協議（6xHis-SUMO 融合，SUMO 同時作為分子伴護蛋白與乾淨的切割把手），並明白寫成可供其他難表現蛋白重複利用，例如類胰島素生長因子、抗體片段與毒液胜肽；此外還有海藻酸鈉製備、交聯後存活率測試、逃逸測試、光學顯微鏡 ImageJ 分析與以分光法測菌體沉降的各項協議。","stack":["STRING v12.5","Netflux (logic-based ODE network simulation)","AlphaFold","ImageJ","Monte Carlo sampling","Gaussian process / random forest / logistic regression classification","ESP32 DevKitC microcontroller","AHV24V30KVR5MAW 30 kV high-voltage module","CAD and 3D printing (coaxial spinneret, enclosure, extruder)","SDS-PAGE, Ni-NTA affinity chromatography, LC-MS, ELISA","16S rRNA sequencing against the NIH database"],"techniques":["Production-degradation ODE modelling","Hill function promoter induction modelling","Michaelis-Menten enzyme kinetics","Hill-Langmuir / one-site Langmuir binding isotherm fitting to ELISA dose-response","Quadratic ligand-depletion equilibrium modelling","Reduced-order signalling network modelling","Protein-protein interaction network assembly filtered by Human Phenotype Ontology term","Logic-based network simulation with modified Hill activation and inhibition","Transient-peak and exponential-recovery environmental signal models","Mark-Houwink viscosity scaling and polymer entanglement statistics","Fridrikh scaling law for terminal jet radius","Semi-empirical property prediction with a green/yellow/red readiness classifier","Fibre tortuosity quantification by image analysis","AND-gate transcriptional logic (hrpR/hrpS/hrpL)"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Cornell ran an unusually wide and genuinely iterative education programme. Plasmid Pals, their own educational game, was playtested with Big Brothers Big Sisters participants who then suggested how to make it more interactive. Plasmid bracelets plus an open-ended idea board asking visitors how they would use synthetic biology to change the world evolved into age-adapted versions for daycare, the Sciencenter and the State Fair — and when reading and spelling turned out to be barriers for roughly 20 preschoolers, the team switched to a cooking analogy (DNA as cookbook, RNA as copied recipe, protein as finished dish), writing up the lesson that activities must match developmental ability. A summer-camp session had about 80 students debate which scientific problems deserve funding using live polls, and a 30-minute lesson drew another 20-25 minutes of student-led questions about research careers and contributing without lab access. STEM Her Way was a four-session series in which high school girls learned synthetic biology and presented their own research proposals, rated 4.7/5 by 15 respondents across seven countries with every respondent recommending it. A shadowing programme drew more than 260 applications from the US and 17 countries for six high school scholars, later extended to five international students whose own project proposals the team helped assess for feasibility — a participant from Uzbekistan brought soil salinity as a community problem and the students developed Salt Guardians around it. They also ran a worldwide synthetic biology governance competition (regulatory pathways, biosafety and containment, access and equity, plus an open governance challenge), produced a narrative synthetic biology podcast, taught Lambert iGEM how to prepare stakeholder questions by sharing their own Human Practices deck and brainstorming guide, and swapped children's books with NUGEM — NUGEM translating Cornell's into Kazakh and Russian while Cornell translated NUGEM's into Mandarin, Spanish and French.","publicEngagement_zh":"Cornell 的教育計畫不只範圍罕見地廣，而且真的有迭代。他們自製的教育遊戲 Plasmid Pals 先找 Big Brothers Big Sisters 的參與者試玩，對方接著建議怎麼讓它更互動。質體手鍊搭配一塊開放式想法板（問參訪者會怎麼用合成生物學改變世界），後來演化出適配不同年齡的版本，用在托育機構、Sciencenter 與州博覽會——而當他們發現閱讀與拼字對約 20 位學前兒童是障礙時，便改用烹飪類比（DNA 是食譜書、RNA 是抄下來的食譜、蛋白質是做好的菜），並把「活動必須配合發展能力」這一課寫下來。一場夏令營課程讓約 80 位學生用即時投票辯論哪些科學問題值得被資助；一堂 30 分鐘的課後，又延伸出 20-25 分鐘由學生主導的提問，問的是研究職涯，以及沒有實驗室可用時要怎麼做出貢獻。STEM Her Way 是四場系列活動，高中女生在其中學合成生物學並發表自己的研究提案，15 位回覆者（來自七個國家）給出 4.7/5 的評分，且每位都願意推薦。隨行見習計畫為六個高中名額吸引到來自美國與 17 個國家的 260 多份申請，後來又擴大到五位國際學生，團隊協助評估他們自己的專案提案可行性——一位來自烏茲別克的參與者把土壤鹽化當作社區問題帶進來，學生們便圍繞它發展出 Salt Guardians。他們還辦了一場全球性的合成生物學治理競賽（法規路徑、生物安全與圍堵、取得與公平性，另加一個開放治理挑戰），製作了一檔敘事型合成生物學 podcast，透過分享自己的人類實踐簡報與腦力激盪指南，教 Lambert iGEM 如何準備利害關係人問題，並與 NUGEM 交換童書——NUGEM 把 Cornell 的譯成哈薩克語與俄語，Cornell 則把 NUGEM 的譯成中文、西班牙語與法語。","ihp":"Several interviews changed the project rather than decorating it. The clearest is hardware: advised not to build their own high-voltage power supply (especially from microwave parts) because the electrical risk is serious, the team dropped the homemade supply entirely, consulted Cornell's Afridi Lab, and bought a commercial regulated unit while sourcing other parts through Digi-Key and Mouser to hold cost down — the advice was that boosting voltage is easy but a stable regulated DC output is the hard part. Dr Insoo Hyun reframed safety itself: he introduced weighing risks and benefits against existing alternatives rather than assuming absolute safety, and warned that familiarity with a microorganism from food use does not demonstrate safety in an open wound, also pressing them to choose experimental models that resemble real wound conditions rather than the most convenient ones. Dr Joseph Fins pushed on preclinical evidence and asked whether delivering the peptide directly, without living bacteria, would be safer and simpler — which the team now carries explicitly as a documented de-risking architecture, with the trade-off (a pre-loaded matrix gives a fixed dose and loses the AND-gated release) stated rather than hidden. Dr Andrew Leask's input on CCN2/CTGF signalling shaped the target rationale, and reviewer pressure to confirm H2O2 is still detectable at the wound stage they target led them to work on sensor sensitivity and add the hypoxia AND gate for specificity. Burn survivor and former burn nurse Amy Acton and Andrea at the Phoenix Society for Burn Survivors changed how the team talks: survivors need support long after wounds heal — financial help for compression garments and procedures, emotional support, connection with others — treatments are costly, uncomfortable and variable, so do not promise how much a treatment will reduce scarring. Roughly 20 older adults and visitors at open events taught them that a scar's size or appearance does not predict its personal impact, and that open conversation surfaced concerns their structured survey questions missed; they concluded existing scales describe the scar but not what the person would want improved. Alison Bateman-House at NYU identified composition and method-of-production as their strongest patent claims and walked them through the one-year US grace period and PCT economics, which fed directly into the commercialisation plan. A kelp-farming conversation moved the sustainability case from biodegradability to sourcing, noting that North American kelp farmers' binding constraint is finding buyers rather than growing kelp since wild-harvested seaweed is substantially cheaper — a point that complicates rather than flatters their own narrative.","ihp_zh":"有幾場訪談是真的改了專案，而不是拿來裝飾。最清楚的是硬體：有人建議他們不要自製高壓電源（尤其不要用微波爐零件），因為電氣風險很嚴重，團隊因此完全放棄自製電源，去諮詢 Cornell 的 Afridi Lab，改買市售的穩壓機組，其他零件則透過 Digi-Key 與 Mouser 採購以壓低成本——那條建議是：把電壓升上去很容易，難的是穩定的穩壓直流輸出。Dr Insoo Hyun 重新定義了「安全」本身：他引入的是把風險與效益放在既有替代療法之上來權衡，而不是假設絕對安全；他也警告，某種微生物在食品中用得熟悉，並不表示它在開放傷口中是安全的，並要求他們選擇近似真實傷口條件的實驗模型，而不是最方便的那些。Dr Joseph Fins 針對臨床前證據施壓，並問：不帶活菌、直接遞送胜肽會不會更安全也更簡單——團隊現在明確把這條列為有紀錄的降風險架構，並把取捨（預先載藥的基質只能給固定劑量，會失去 AND 閘控制的釋放）寫出來而不是藏起來。Dr Andrew Leask 關於 CCN2/CTGF 訊息傳遞的意見形塑了標的的立論依據；而審查者要求確認在他們瞄準的傷口階段 H2O2 是否仍可偵測，則促使他們去處理感測靈敏度，並加上缺氧這一路 AND 閘以取得專一性。燒傷倖存者暨前燒傷護理師 Amy Acton 與 Phoenix Society for Burn Survivors 的 Andrea 改變了團隊說話的方式：倖存者在傷口癒合後很久仍需要支持——壓力衣與各項療程的經濟協助、情緒支持、與他人的連結——療法昂貴、不舒服而且效果不一，所以不要承諾一項療法能把疤痕減少多少。公開活動上約 20 位年長者與參訪者則教會他們：疤痕的大小或外觀無法預測它對個人的衝擊，而開放式對話浮現出的顧慮，是他們結構化問卷題目漏掉的；他們的結論是現有量表描述的是疤痕，而不是當事人想改善的東西。NYU 的 Alison Bateman-House 指出組成與製造方法是他們最強的專利請求項，並帶他們走過美國一年寬限期與 PCT 的經濟考量，這些直接進了商業化計畫。一場關於海帶養殖的對話，把永續性的論點從可生物降解轉向了原料來源，指出北美海帶養殖者真正的瓶頸是找到買家、而不是把海帶種出來，因為野採海藻便宜得多——這一點讓他們自己的敘事變得更複雜，而不是更好聽。","realWorld":"This is the most developed commercial package of the five. Target market is quantified: burn centres and academic hospitals in the American Northeast, where 2,255 medical institutions — 26 verified burn centres, 604 hospitals (31 with ACGME dermatology residencies) and 1,625 medical spas — serve an estimated 1.8 million addressable patients per year, or 2.2 patients per institution per day, with academic hospitals and verified burn centres targeted first as likeliest to trial new technology. The regulatory analysis identifies the real hazard: Klothos is a combination product (alginate nanofiber device plus engineered live bacteria), so FDA assigns a primary mode of action deciding whether CBER leads via IND/BLA or CDRH via 510(k)/PMA, and misclassification could force a restart costing an estimated 18-24 months and $500K-plus — hence a formal Pre-RFD consultation with the Office of Combination Products before committing development resources. They cite Azitra's engineered S. epidermidis with an open IND and FDA Fast Track as precedent that CBER will accept an IND for topical engineered bacteria. A six-phase plan runs from prototype and fibroblast assays, through an IND/IDE-enabling package with dermal safety, immunogenicity, biodistribution and microbial containment, to Phase I (with viable-organism monitoring because it is a live biotherapeutic) and a Phase II randomised controlled trial in surgical, burn, hypertrophic-scar-risk and revision-scar settings scored on POSAS, VSS and SCAR-Q. A freedom-to-operate analysis covers ten patents across four technology areas, with specific flags (the University of Manitoba colour-changing antibacterial nanofiber US20220047523A1 and NYCU's pending pH-sensitive electrospun bandage would need review before adding a pH indicator), plus PCT costs of roughly $17K to hold in 150 signatories and $20K per country thereafter. They map regulatory strategy across seven regions, including the MHRA consultation on modernising the GTMP definition (closed 22 June 2026) and Korea's MFDS review reforms cutting target timelines from about 420 to 295 days. Over 20 risks across technical, market, financial and regulatory categories are rated on severity, likelihood and detectability with mitigations and rendered as a heat map; a skill gap radar names what the 45-plus member team cannot yet do (pricing, physician adoption, launch strategy, clinical trial design) and how they would fill it. Reimbursement is treated honestly: novel combination products often lack an established billing code, so they model unit economics under both self-pay and reimbursed scenarios. The team won an ANSA grant and flagged Cornell's technology transfer office licensing terms as a Year 1 gating factor for any spinout.","realWorld_zh":"這是五個案例中商業化套件做得最完整的一份。目標市場有量化：美國東北部的燒傷中心與教學醫院，共 2,255 家醫療機構——26 家經認證的燒傷中心、604 家醫院（其中 31 家設有 ACGME 皮膚科住院醫師訓練）與 1,625 家醫美中心——服務估計每年 180 萬名可觸及病人，換算為每家機構每天 2.2 位病人，並優先瞄準最可能試用新技術的教學醫院與認證燒傷中心。法規分析點出真正的風險：Klothos 是組合式產品（海藻酸鈉奈米纖維裝置加上工程改造的活菌），因此 FDA 會指定一個主要作用模式，決定是由 CBER 走 IND/BLA 還是 CDRH 走 510(k)/PMA；分類錯誤可能迫使整個流程重來，估計代價是 18-24 個月與 50 萬美元以上——所以他們在投入開發資源之前，先向 Office of Combination Products 提出正式的 Pre-RFD 諮詢。他們引用 Azitra 已有 IND 並取得 FDA Fast Track 的工程改造 S. epidermidis 作為前例，證明 CBER 會接受外用工程細菌的 IND。六階段計畫從原型與纖維母細胞試驗開始，經過一套支持 IND/IDE 的資料包（皮膚安全性、免疫原性、生體分佈與微生物圍堵），到第一期臨床（因為是活體生物治療產品，需監測活菌），再到在手術、燒傷、肥厚性疤痕高風險與疤痕修整等情境下、以 POSAS、VSS 與 SCAR-Q 評分的第二期隨機對照試驗。自由實施分析涵蓋四個技術領域共十件專利，並標出具體警訊（University of Manitoba 的變色抗菌奈米纖維 US20220047523A1 與 NYCU 審查中的 pH 敏感靜電紡絲敷料，在加入 pH 指示劑之前都需要先行審視），另列出 PCT 成本：維持 150 個簽約國約 17K 美元，之後每個國家約 20K 美元。他們把法規策略攤在七個地區上，包括 MHRA 關於現代化 GTMP 定義的諮詢（2026 年 6 月 22 日結束）與韓國 MFDS 把目標審查時程從約 420 天縮短到 295 天的改革。超過 20 項風險分成技術、市場、財務與法規四類，依嚴重度、發生可能性與可偵測性評分，附上緩解措施並畫成熱圖；一張技能缺口雷達圖則指名這個 45 人以上的團隊目前做不到的事（定價、醫師採用、上市策略、臨床試驗設計）以及他們打算怎麼補。給付問題處理得很誠實：新穎的組合式產品往往沒有既成的給付代碼，因此他們把單位經濟同時放在自費與有給付兩種情境下計算。團隊拿到一筆 ANSA 補助，並把 Cornell 技術移轉辦公室的授權條件標為任何衍生公司在第一年的關卡因素。","partners":["Dr Andrew Leask (CCN2/CTGF signalling and pathological scarring)","Dr Insoo Hyun (bioethics)","Dr Joseph Fins (medical ethics)","Alison Bateman-House, NYU Grossman School of Medicine (medical ethics and IP)","Amy Acton, Phoenix Society for Burn Survivors","Lisa Placanica (prescription/outpatient model)","Afridi Lab, Cornell (high-power electronics)","Cornell technology transfer office and biosafety office / IBC","Lambert iGEM (human practices mentoring)","NUGEM (children's book translation exchange)","STEM Her Way","Big Brothers Big Sisters","Ithaca Sciencenter","Cornell Division B Science Olympiad","ANSA grant programme"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6122/wiki/modeling/productdev-14-spinning-viability-alginate-peo-classifier-map.avif","caption":"Predicted spinning viability across sodium alginate and PEO weight percentages, generated by Monte Carlo sampling over the viscosity, conductivity and surface tension models — the map behind the green/yellow/red readiness classifier that decides whether a formulation reaches the electrospinner.","caption_zh":"以蒙地卡羅取樣跑過黏度、導電度與表面張力模型後，預測出的海藻酸鈉與 PEO 重量百分比可紡性分佈——這張圖就是決定一個配方能不能上靜電紡絲機的綠/黃/紅就緒分類器背後的地圖。","credit":"Team Cornell, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6122/wiki/modeling/wetlab-17-fig4-string-ctgf-scarring-network.avif","caption":"Force-directed CTGF (CCN2)-centred protein interaction and scarring regulatory network built in STRING v12.5 by filtering on Human Phenotype Ontology term HP:0100699, with SMAD3, FN1 and TGFB2 as major nodes. Its 48 weighted edges became the parameters of the Netflux fibroblast simulation.","caption_zh":"以 Human Phenotype Ontology 詞條 HP:0100699 過濾、在 STRING v12.5 建出的以 CTGF（CCN2）為中心的蛋白質交互作用與疤痕化調控網路，力導向佈局呈現，主要節點為 SMAD3、FN1 與 TGFB2。其 48 條加權邊成為 Netflux 纖維母細胞模擬的參數。","credit":"Team Cornell, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6122/wiki/engineering-success/hardware-extruder-reservoir-coaxial-needle-collection-plate/eng-suc-hardware-web-2-0-fig-1.avif","caption":"The custom coaxial electrospinner: extruder, reservoir, coaxial needle and collection plate, built from inexpensive stock parts and 3D-printed components and designed to flat-pack for teams working in shared or temporary spaces.","caption_zh":"自製的同軸靜電紡絲機：擠出器、儲液槽、同軸針頭與收集板，由便宜的現成零件與 3D 列印件組成，並設計成可平板化收納，適合在共用或臨時空間工作的團隊。","credit":"Team Cornell, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6122/wiki/hardware/microscope/gfp-coaxial.avif","caption":"Micrograph of coaxially electrospun fibres containing GFP-expressing engineered E. coli, showing that cells remain fluorescent and therefore viable after encapsulation.","caption_zh":"含有表現 GFP 的工程改造 E. coli 的同軸靜電紡絲纖維顯微影像，顯示菌體在包覆之後仍有螢光，因此仍具活性。","credit":"Team Cornell, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Build the cheap version of the instrument and publish it properly. Cornell's winning move was deciding that an electrospinner — normally a specialised commercial purchase — could be made from stock parts and 3D prints, then releasing the bill of materials, CAD, circuit diagrams, assembly guide, operation manual and a separate high-voltage safety manual with interlocks and an emergency stop designed in. For a school-based centre the paired lesson is the readiness classifier: predict a formulation's viscosity, conductivity and surface tension from its recipe, label it green/yellow/red, and spend scarce lab time only on green — a cheap model that saves expensive experiments is worth more than an elaborate one that does not change what you do next.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"把儀器的便宜版本做出來，然後好好公開它。Cornell 的關鍵一手，是判斷靜電紡絲機——通常得向廠商專購——可以用現成零件加 3D 列印做出來，接著把材料清單（BOM）、CAD、電路圖、組裝指南、操作手冊，以及一本獨立的高壓安全手冊（連同設計進去的安全互鎖與緊急停止）全部釋出。對校園型的中心來說，配套的一課是那個就緒分類器：從配方預測溶液的黏度、導電度與表面張力，標成綠/黃/紅，只把稀少的實驗時間花在綠色的配方上——一個能省下昂貴實驗的簡單模型，價值高於一個做得精緻卻不改變你下一步的模型。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/","https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/circuitry","https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/extrusion-mechanism","https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/encasement","https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/fibers","https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/wet-lab","https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/measurement","https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/notebook","https://2026.igem.wiki/cornell/timeline"],"rank":155},"6123":{"team":"BASIS-China","id":"6123","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/basis-china/","projectTitle":"HEAL — Hairball Elimination and Lysis","tagline":"Keratinases for cat hairballs, held inside the cat by a kill switch keyed to bile acid, with the containment claim measured against real sewage and soil concentrations","summary":"BASIS-China engineered E. coli to express keratinases and proteases (p-Ker, Protease 1, Protease 2, MGY1820, MGY4907) with thioredoxin and thioredoxin reductase as synergistic helpers and LGOX plus KatG as gut antioxidant modules, aimed at digesting cat hairballs. The safety engineering is the standout: a bile-acid-responsive suicide switch in which membrane sensors TcpH and CadC-TcpP activate the pCadBA promoter to produce the unstable CcdA antitoxin, while the stable CcdB toxin is expressed constitutively, so the cell survives only where bile acid is present. Four Anderson promoters (J23100, J23102, J23104, J23114) were built to tune CcdB strength, and the response threshold was measured at roughly 0.1-0.2 mM taurocholic acid, then compared against feline duodenal bile salts at 15-42 mM and against published sewage and soil bile-acid levels orders of magnitude below the threshold. They won the Safety and Security Award in the High School section and were nominated for Best New Basic Part.","awards":["Best New Basic Part — Nominee (High School)","Safety and Security Award — Winner (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A published five-step characterisation framework for environmentally responsive kill switches, written because the team found limited end-to-end guidance in existing iGEM wikis: confirm construction by gel and sequencing; tune toxin expression across promoters of differing strength to find an operating window; characterise the concentration-dependent growth response by time course; compare the measured response range against published signal concentrations in both the intended host and the likely receiving environments; and add an orthogonal reporter readout alongside growth. Alongside it, a transferable design concept (use an endogenous molecule abundant in the target host's intestine and scarce outside it) with the caveat that bile-acid composition varies by species so adopters must establish their own host's signal profile.","dataviz":"Circuit diagrams for the switch in both the bile-acid-present and bile-acid-absent states, a promoter-variant design figure, assembly gels against the expected 3,704 bp fragment, OD600 growth curves at 0 and 30 mM TCA, serial-dilution spot plates across six TCA concentrations (0, 0.1, 1, 10, 15, 30 mM) for all four promoter variants plus empty vector, 270-minute time-course growth curves per promoter across 0-1 mM, fluorescence panels for all four variants, and a supplemented-versus-depleted sfGFP comparison. The iGEM approval email and a 17-page laboratory safety rules PDF are embedded.","datascience":"The containment claim is quantified on both sides, which is what distinguishes it. The switch threshold is placed at approximately 0.1-0.2 mM TCA, with limited growth below 0.2 mM and similar growth rates above 0.4 mM. That is then set against feline duodenal bile salts at 15-42 mM (Reber and Mosley), sewage total bile acids at 184-356 micrograms per litre, which they convert to roughly 4.7 x 10^-4 to 9.1 x 10^-4 mM using a representative molecular weight of 392.6 g/mol (Sebok et al.), and soil deoxycholic acid at 13.3 pmol/g in archaeological soil from Pompeii, converted to 1.33 x 10^-5 mmol/kg (Porru et al.). They show the unit conversions and then state that total bile salts and soil-associated bile acids are not directly equivalent to TCA in culture medium.","software":"","stack":["E. coli DH5-alpha and BL21(DE3)","SnapGene","TcpH and CadC-TcpP bile-acid sensors with pCadBA","CcdA/CcdB toxin-antitoxin","Anderson promoter series BBa_J23100/J23102/J23104/J23114","sfGFP fused to CcdB","pET-28a and pET-32a","Ni-NTA affinity chromatography","SDS-PAGE"],"techniques":["bile-acid-gated conditional viability","promoter-strength tuning of a toxin to set an operating window","serial-dilution spot plating across an inducer gradient","time-course growth response curves","reporter fluorescence after inducer withdrawal as a viability proxy","in-vitro keratin degradation on washed shed hair and pharmaceutical-grade beta-keratin"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"","ihp":"An interview with an experienced stray-cat rescuer from Xiaobabenben in Shenzhen reframed the product requirement: limited volunteer capacity, poor acceptance of existing remedies and stress-related overgrooming pushed the team toward palatable formats cats would take voluntarily, minimising restraint and forced administration, and made gastrointestinal safety and animal comfort explicit evaluation priorities. The more unusual engagement was with iGEM itself: knowing that the Animal Use Form is not available to high-school teams, they contacted the iGEM Safety and Regulatory Committee before collecting any samples, and Chris Isaac, Director of Responsibility at iGEM HQ, approved the collection without an Animal Use Form on the basis that routine grooming causes no harm, which they then documented on their official Project Safety Form as instructed and published the approval email.","realWorld":"No company, no patent, no pricing and no funding here, so the material worth taking is the safety practice, and it is the most rigorous high-school biocontainment work in this group. Four features make it serious. First, the switch is engineered as a tunable system rather than a single construct: four Anderson promoters of differing strength drive CcdB so the operating window can be matched to a required kill sensitivity, and all four variants are characterised in parallel in every assay, with empty vector alongside. Second, the containment claim is tested against the actual release pathway rather than a lab abstraction. They ask where the bacteria would end up after excretion, find published bile-acid concentrations for sewage and soil, convert them into the same units as their assay, and show the receiving environments sit three to four orders of magnitude below their measured threshold. Third, the evidence hierarchy is stated explicitly and never collapsed. They separate 'evidence of construct assembly, conditional growth suppression, and reporter expression' from 'evidence required to demonstrate containment in real-world settings', and they list, in their own words, what still stands in the way: residual bile acids in faecal material, differences between laboratory medium and environmental conditions, circuit drift over time, and possible horizontal transfer. They add two caveats most teams would omit, that genetic containment neither removes extracellular DNA nor replaces waste decontamination, and that their delivery microcapsules are designed to release bacteria in the intestine and therefore must not be counted as physical containment. They also note sfGFP tracks the circuit but does not independently establish viability, and that soil and sewage total bile acids are not equivalent to TCA in medium. Fourth, the chassis plan is honest about its own role: BSL-1 E. coli is declared a proof-of-concept model only, chosen because high-school teams may not use untested wild isolates or run animal trials, with the translational chassis identified as GRAS feline-native probiotics (Lactiplantibacillus plantarum, Lactobacillus acidophilus, Bifidobacterium animalis) to be ported into only after validation and under veterinary compliance. Enzyme safety is argued mechanistically rather than asserted, noting that gut mucus is glycoprotein-based while keratinases target cross-linked keratin disulfides, and substrate safety is covered by using washed, sterilised naturally shed hair and pharmaceutical-grade beta-keratin. Laboratory risk management is reagent-specific rather than generic, naming beta-mercaptoethanol (fume hood only, sealed tubes), unpolymerised acrylamide (pre-cast gels preferred, dedicated hazardous waste), kanamycin and ampicillin with the resistance marker on each vector identified and media neutralised and autoclaved before disposal, and Ni-NTA nickel waste segregated for hazardous recycling, plus a preference for blue LED over UV transilluminators. Waste is bleached at 10 percent for at least 30 minutes or autoclaved at 121 degrees C for 30 minutes before discharge. Continuation is community-facing: the five-step framework, the design concept, and characterisation data for the circuit and all four promoter variants submitted to the Registry as a reference for future teams building bile-acid-responsive kill switches, with the honest framing that the data are 'a starting point for further validation, rather than a claim that this circuit is ready for unrestricted deployment'. No animal trials were conducted, and they say so repeatedly rather than once.","partners":["iGEM Safety and Regulatory Committee / Chris Isaac, Director of Responsibility, iGEM HQ (proactive animal-use consultation and written approval)","Xiaobabenben stray-cat rescue, Shenzhen (animal-welfare and administration-format requirements)","Avant Nanshan Science Innovation Center (certified BSL-1 facility, lab managers, safety training)","Sangon Biotech, Shanghai (gene synthesis)","Cat owners who supplied routinely groomed shed hair"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6123/wiki/safety-20261021/switch-promoters.webp","caption":"Four Anderson promoter variants driving ccdB, built to tune toxin strength and find the suicide switch's operating window rather than ship a single construct","credit":"Team BASIS-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6123/wiki/safety-20261021/gfp-tca-withdrawal.webp","caption":"sfGFP fluorescence before and after taurocholic acid withdrawal, used as an orthogonal readout alongside growth and reported with the caveat that it does not independently establish viability","credit":"Team BASIS-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6123/wiki/safety/igem-approval.webp","caption":"Written approval from iGEM HQ's Director of Responsibility for the shed-hair collection, obtained before any samples were taken and documented on the Project Safety Form","credit":"Team BASIS-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6123/wiki/safety/2.avif","caption":"Behaviour of the suicide switch with and without bile acid: the unstable CcdA antitoxin is made only when the sensor is on, leaving the stable CcdB toxin unopposed outside the host","credit":"Team BASIS-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Characterise any containment switch the way they did: tune the toxin across a promoter series to find an operating window, measure the response threshold as a number, then look up the signal concentration in the actual receiving environment, convert it into your assay's units, and show the gap — a containment claim is only as good as the comparison behind it. Pair that with their evidence ledger, a 'what our results establish' section beside a 'what remains before real-world use' section, and with asking the governing body in advance rather than assuming an unavailable form means the work cannot be done compliantly.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/basis-china/","https://2026.igem.wiki/basis-china/safety-and-security/","https://2026.igem.wiki/basis-china/contribution/","https://2026.igem.wiki/basis-china/description/","https://registry.igem.org/parts/BBa_26NOEGF3"],"rank":33},"6124":{"team":"Madrid-UCM","id":"6124","section":"Undergrad","country":"Spain","village":"Bioremediation","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/madrid-ucm/","projectTitle":"rePhlow: A modular synthetic-biology platform for phosphorus capture and valorisation from industrial wastewater","projectTitle_zh":"rePhlow：一個用於從工業廢水中捕集並加值利用磷的模組化合成生物學平台","tagline":"Phosphorus should not reach nature as pollution, and it should not leave industry as waste.","tagline_zh":"磷不該以污染的形式進入自然，也不該以廢棄物的形式離開工業。","summary":"rePhlow intercepts phosphorus in a defined industrial wastewater stream rather than attempting to 'solve eutrophication'. An immobilised enzyme panel (phosphatases, phospholipases, phytase) releases phosphorus from organic and condensed fractions; engineered Pseudomonas putida KT2440 carrying heterologous ppk1 and the Accumulibacter Pst high-affinity transport system, with pitB/ppx/ppkB knocked out by CRISPR base editing, accumulates it as polyphosphate inside core-shell alginate-chitosan capsules; the recovered polyP then feeds a coupled PPK2/DHAK biocatalytic cascade producing dihydroxyacetone phosphate. The capsules sit in a basket-type rotating-bed bioreactor the team built themselves, with encapsulation doubling as the EU contained-use regulatory strategy. The project is explicitly framed as a two-sided business: paid to remove phosphorus, paid again for the phosphorus recovered.","summary_zh":"rePhlow 選擇在一條明確界定的工業廢水流中攔截磷，而不是試圖「解決優養化」。一組固定化酶（磷酸酶、磷脂酶、植酸酶）先把磷從有機態與縮合態組分中釋放出來；經改造的 Pseudomonas putida KT2440 帶有異源 ppk1 與 Accumulibacter 的 Pst 高親和性運輸系統，並以 CRISPR 鹼基編輯剔除 pitB/ppx/ppkB，在核殼式海藻酸鹽-幾丁聚醣膠囊內把磷累積成聚磷酸鹽；回收得到的 polyP 再送入 PPK2/DHAK 偶聯的生物催化串聯，生產磷酸二羥丙酮。這些膠囊放在團隊自行打造的籃式旋轉床生物反應器中，而包覆本身同時就是歐盟封閉使用（contained use）的法規策略。這個專案明確定位為一門雙邊收費的事業：除磷收一次錢，回收到的磷再收一次。","awards":["Best Sustainable Development Impact — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Entrepreneurship — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Bioremediation Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A genome-scale constraint-based model of P. putida KT2440 (iJN1463, 2,927 reactions) was used to ask which conditions and genes actually limit polyphosphate accumulation, then systematically reduced to a kinetic model. Parsimonious FBA identified the active metabolic core, flux variability analysis separated reactions with real flexibility (respiration, redox balancing) from those that are merely accessory, and flux coupling analysis justified lumping the Entner-Doudoroff route into one net reaction while deliberately keeping oxidative phosphorylation as its own module. The result is a 45-reaction core and then a handful of lumped modules in which every rate law can be written and every parameter traced to a source. The team states plainly what the model cannot do: no explicit genetic or enzymatic regulation, borrowed kinetic constants from related species, the anaerobic half of an EBPR process not modelled, and conclusions valid only for aerobic polyP accumulation on a fixed medium.","frameworks_zh":"團隊以 P. putida KT2440 的基因組尺度限制式模型（iJN1463，2,927 個反應）去問：到底哪些條件與基因真正限制了聚磷酸鹽的累積，再系統性地把它縮減成一個動力學模型。簡約通量平衡分析（pFBA）找出活躍的代謝核心，通量變異性分析把真正具有彈性的反應（呼吸作用、氧化還原平衡）與僅屬附屬的反應區分開來，而通量耦合分析則為把 Entner-Doudoroff 途徑併為單一淨反應提供了依據，同時刻意保留氧化磷酸化作為獨立模組。結果是一個 45 個反應的核心，外加少數幾個集總模組，其中每一條速率式都寫得出來、每一個參數都能追溯到來源。團隊也明白說出模型做不到什麼：沒有明確的基因或酵素層級調控、動力學常數借自近緣物種、EBPR 製程的厭氧那一半並未建模，以及結論僅適用於固定培養基下的好氧 polyP 累積。","dataviz":"An interactive D3 force-directed metabolic flux map (shipped as a separate MetabolicNetworkGraph chunk) renders the 45-reaction core with line thickness proportional to pFBA flux and grey lines for zero-flux branches. Plotly-gl3d renders phenotype phase planes for PolyP flux over glucose x O2 and phosphate x glucose uptake. The sustainability page carries an interactive LCA slider that moves capsule phosphorus loading from 0 to 12 mg P/g and shows which side of the ~8 mg P/g climate crossover a given loading falls on. The entrepreneurship page carries a customer-facing sizing and quotation demo built on the team's own financial model.","dataviz_zh":"一張互動式 D3 力導向代謝通量圖（以獨立的 MetabolicNetworkGraph 區塊載入）呈現 45 個反應的核心，線條粗細與 pFBA 通量成正比，零通量分支以灰線表示。Plotly-gl3d 繪製了 PolyP 通量在葡萄糖 x O2 以及磷酸鹽 x 葡萄糖攝取兩組座標下的表型相平面。永續性頁面放了一個互動式 LCA 滑桿，可把膠囊的磷負載量由 0 調到 12 mg P/g，並顯示某一負載量落在約 8 mg P/g 氣候衝擊交叉點的哪一側。創業頁面則放了一個面向客戶的規模估算與報價示範，建立在團隊自己的財務模型之上。","datascience":"Single-variable sensitivity sweeps on ammonium, phosphate and oxygen uptake capacity, ATP-maintenance demand (ATPM as an energetic stress proxy) and PPK1 capacity as a multiple of the reference pFBA flux, yielding concrete predictions: PPK1 is essential but its reference capacity is already sufficient, and nitrogen limitation permits rather than forces polyP storage. On the commercial side, a ten-year financial model with declared sensitivity: capsule service life drives everything, giving a Year-5 gross margin of 54.7% at 500 reuse cycles, 25.7% at 100 cycles and -10.6% at 50. The LCA is run with an explicit sensitivity on phosphorus captured per gram of capsule.","datascience_zh":"團隊對銨、磷酸鹽與氧的攝取能力、ATP 維持需求（以 ATPM 作為能量壓力的代理指標），以及 PPK1 容量（以參考 pFBA 通量的倍數表示）做了單變數敏感度掃描，得到具體預測：PPK1 不可或缺，但其參考容量已經足夠，而氮限制是允許而非強迫 polyP 儲存。商業面則有一套十年財務模型並明白標示敏感度：膠囊使用壽命主導一切，在重複使用 500 次時第 5 年毛利率為 54.7%、100 次時為 25.7%、50 次時則為 -10.6%。LCA 也以每公克膠囊所捕集的磷量做了明確的敏感度分析。","software":"An ISO 14040/14044-aligned life cycle assessment built in openLCA over 16 impact categories, with the openLCA workbook, the full LCA report and a step-by-step LCA tutorial published as a reusable contribution for other iGEM teams. Protein work used PROSS (phylogenetic sequence information plus Rosetta energy calculations) for DHAK stabilisation, AlphaFold for SpyTag/SpyCatcher fusion models, PyMOL for superposition onto PDB 1UN9, and SWISS-MODEL homology models to guide affinity-tag placement and expression-host choice.","software_zh":"一份符合 ISO 14040/14044 的生命週期評估，以 openLCA 建立，涵蓋 16 個衝擊類別；openLCA 工作檔、完整 LCA 報告與一份逐步操作的 LCA 教學都已公開，作為可供其他 iGEM 團隊重複使用的貢獻。蛋白質工作方面，DHAK 的穩定化使用 PROSS（親緣序列資訊加上 Rosetta 能量計算），SpyTag/SpyCatcher 融合模型使用 AlphaFold，並以 PyMOL 疊合到 PDB 1UN9，另以 SWISS-MODEL 同源模型指引親和標籤的放置位置與表現宿主的選擇。","stack":["Python","React","React Router","Vite","D3.js","Plotly (gl3d)","openLCA","PROSS/Rosetta","AlphaFold","PyMOL","SWISS-MODEL","iJN1463 genome-scale model"],"techniques":["parsimonious FBA","flux variability analysis","flux coupling analysis","phenotype phase plane analysis","model reduction and reaction lumping","ODE kinetic modelling with traced parameters","structure-based enzyme stability redesign","homology modelling","life cycle assessment (ISO 14040/44)","techno-economic modelling with sensitivity analysis","TAM/SAM/SOM market sizing"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A public survey found respondents rated their own knowledge of water pollution at 2.4 out of 5 and only 54% knew phosphorus can become a contaminant, yet 89% would support recycling phosphorus from wastewater into a useful resource, and views on GM microorganisms for treatment leaned favourable. The team's conclusion is unusually specific and actionable: the barrier to acceptance is not resistance to the biotechnology but the invisibility of the problem. Outreach leaned on science comedy, a format the team actually won with: Diego performed monologues at the National Museum of Natural Sciences (MNCN-CSIC) and the Museum of Human Evolution in Burgos, and took first place at the 4th Monologos de Ciencia Complutense. Other activities were school talks at IES Alameda de Osuna and IES Humanejos, a live alginate-bead synthesis demonstration at Madrid es Ciencia, a talk to DIS Abroad Scandinavia students at Compluemprende covering both the science and the business model, a hands-on session at the Lamarr vocational camp, and best-poster plus best-oral-presentation awards at the XVIII UCM Health Sciences Students' Congress, where veterinary professionals raised animal toxin exposure in eutrophic waters as an angle the team had not considered. The team also hosted the iGEM European Meetup in Malaga, submitted to the MSP-Vector peer-reviewed iGEM journal (ranked among the three best submissions and refereeing three other teams' papers in turn), and ran a joint 'war on two fronts' campaign with iGEM UPF Barcelona's Vinesys contrasting water scarcity with nutrient pollution.","publicEngagement_zh":"一份公眾問卷發現，受訪者自評對水污染的了解程度為 5 分中的 2.4 分，只有 54% 知道磷可能成為污染物，但有 89% 支持把廢水中的磷回收成有用資源，而對於使用基改微生物處理廢水的看法則偏向正面。團隊的結論異常具體且可行動：接受度的障礙不在於對生物技術的抗拒，而在於這個問題本身看不見。科普推廣主要倚重科學喜劇，而這也是團隊真正拿下名次的形式：Diego 在國立自然科學博物館（MNCN-CSIC）與 Burgos 的人類演化博物館表演科學單口，並在第 4 屆 Monologos de Ciencia Complutense 奪得第一名。其他活動包括在 IES Alameda de Osuna 與 IES Humanejos 的校園演講、在 Madrid es Ciencia 現場示範海藻酸鹽珠的合成、在 Compluemprende 向 DIS Abroad Scandinavia 的學生講授科學內容與商業模式、在 Lamarr 技職營隊的動手課程，以及在第 18 屆 UCM 健康科學學生研討會同時獲得最佳海報與最佳口頭報告獎，會上獸醫專業人士提出了優養化水域中動物接觸毒素的議題，這是團隊原本沒有想到的切角。團隊另主辦了在 Malaga 舉行的 iGEM 歐洲聚會，並投稿至同儕審查的 iGEM 期刊 MSP-Vector（獲評為三篇最佳投稿之一，並反過來為另外三支團隊的論文擔任審稿），還與 iGEM UPF Barcelona 的 Vinesys 合辦了一場「兩線作戰」聯合宣傳，把缺水與營養鹽污染並置對照。","ihp":"This is one of the most rigorously structured integrated human practices sections of the year, and the structure is the contribution. The team adapted the EPSRC AREA framework (Anticipate, Reflect, Engage, Act) because it found that 'safe' and 'responsible' meant different things to different team members, and built a five-rung integration ladder with an explicit closure criterion: relevant concern recorded (consultation only); input produced a traceable modification; modification entered a construct, protocol, experiment, model or communication output; evidence generated to assess the modified design; the revised design taken back to the person whose input triggered it; and only when their response produces a further change is the loop described as closed. Twenty-five stakeholder encounters are documented with date, affiliation, the question asked, the challenge raised and what changed. The strongest chain starts with Bio-Oils Huelva's La Rabida biodiesel plant (20 March 2025), which described the phosphorus concentration, pH and temperature of its degumming effluent and warned that any new treatment would have to fit around existing infrastructure; the team turned those ranges into a semi-synthetic effluent recipe used before any real sample existed, made modular retrofit-compatibility an explicit design requirement ('a mid-sized industrial facility cannot rebuild its infrastructure around an experimental technology'), and later ran the engineered strain on real Bio-Oils effluent, where it accumulated more phosphorus than the wild type and survived. Aurelio Hidalgo (CBM, CSIC-UAM) reframed the enzyme problem before any design was fixed: 'an enzyme that is simply expressed and released is spent once; at the scale of a treatment stream, a single-use biocatalyst is neither economical nor recoverable', which killed both of the team's placeholders (secretion and a consortium) and moved the enzyme panel onto a reusable solid support, cleanly separating phosphorus release from uptake and storage. Silvia Diaz del Toro then pointed out that nothing in the design distinguished an enzyme that was immobilised from one verified to stay immobilised, so enzyme retention and leaching became explicit safety requirements and the immobilisation chemistry was selected to minimise detachment rather than to maximise activity; Juan Manuel Bolivar converted that into a de-risked model system with a characterised support, a characterised enzyme and an assay that works at the acidic pH the real enzymes need, because the team's first colorimetric assay would have failed there. Repsol (21 October 2025) said flatly that living GMOs would not be acceptable without convincing evidence that environmental release had been prevented, which elevated containment evidence above removal performance as a condition for implementation and generated a culture plus qPCR monitoring campaign with a divert-and-inactivate protocol. CEDEX, the public water-technology research body, told the team its malachite-green assay should not be presented as equivalent to an official reference method, after which rePhlow was reframed as a complement to established treatment rather than a replacement and method validation was written in as a necessary next step. The closed loop the team is proudest of is materials: Carmen Garcia Payo and Loreto Garcia Fernandez proposed core-shell capsules over simple beads, the team built them but could not see the internal structure, took that problem straight back to the same researchers, and received magnetite as an optical tracer plus cryosectioning, which became a wall-thickness measurement and leakage-testing pipeline. Two further things lift this above a meeting log: the team documents a change it chose not to make (Elvira Mateos' Accumulibacter polyamine route, declined because the metabolic burden outweighed an unquantifiable gain, written up explicitly because 'not adding a pathway is a design decision too'), and it records a non-expert voice, Inmaculada Alonso, a long-term resident near the San Juan reservoir, who described eutrophication as a slow change she had watched for decades without ever being told why. That conversation shifted the team towards perceptible restoration outcomes and clear communication as deliverables, and the team itself notes that one resident cannot represent everyone affected.","ihp_zh":"這是今年結構最嚴謹的整合式人類實踐章節之一，而這個結構本身就是貢獻。團隊改用了 EPSRC 的 AREA 框架（Anticipate、Reflect、Engage、Act），原因是他們發現「安全」與「負責」對不同團員而言意思並不相同；他們並建立了一個五階整合階梯，附明確的閉環判準：記錄到相關疑慮（僅為諮詢）；意見產生了可追溯的修改；修改進入了某個構築體、實驗流程、實驗、模型或溝通產出；產生了證據以評估修改後的設計；修改後的設計被帶回給當初提出意見的人；而只有當對方的回應又再引發一次改變時，這個迴圈才被稱為閉合。25 場利害關係人接觸都記錄了日期、單位、所問的問題、對方提出的挑戰，以及因此改變了什麼。最強的一條鏈始於 Bio-Oils Huelva 的 La Rabida 生質柴油廠（2025 年 3 月 20 日），該廠說明了其脫膠廢水的磷濃度、pH 與溫度，並警告任何新處理技術都必須配合既有設施；團隊把這些範圍轉成一份半合成廢水配方，在拿到任何真實樣本之前就先使用，並把模組化的改裝相容性列為明確的設計要求（「一座中型工業廠不可能為了一項實驗性技術重建自己的基礎設施」），後來也把工程菌株放到真實的 Bio-Oils 廢水中運行，結果累積的磷比野生型更多且存活下來。Aurelio Hidalgo（CBM, CSIC-UAM）在任何設計定案之前就重新框定了酶的問題：「一個只是表現出來並釋放到環境中的酶，用一次就沒了；在處理一整條廢水流的規模上，單次使用的生物催化劑既不經濟也無法回收」，這句話否決了團隊原本的兩個暫定方案（分泌表現與菌群共培養），把酶組移到可重複使用的固體載體上，乾淨地把磷的釋放與磷的吸收儲存分開。接著 Silvia Diaz del Toro 指出，設計中並沒有任何東西能區分「已被固定化的酶」與「經驗證會持續固定不脫落的酶」，於是酶的保留率與流失成為明確的安全要求，固定化化學的選擇標準也改為最小化脫落，而不是最大化活性；Juan Manuel Bolivar 則把這一點轉化成一個已去風險的模式系統，包含一個已表徵的載體、一個已表徵的酶，以及一套能在真實酶所需的酸性 pH 下運作的分析方法，因為團隊最初的呈色分析法在那個 pH 下會失效。Repsol（2025 年 10 月 21 日）直言，若無法提供足以說服人的證據證明已防止環境釋放，活體 GMO 不會被接受，這使「圍阻的證據」在實施條件上的位階高於除磷效能，並促成了一套培養加 qPCR 的監測計畫，以及一份分流並去活化的處置流程。公立水處理技術研究機構 CEDEX 告訴團隊，他們的孔雀綠呈色法不應被呈現為等同官方參考方法，此後 rePhlow 被重新定位為既有處理程序的補充而非替代，方法確效也被寫入為必要的下一步。團隊最自豪的閉合迴圈出現在材料上：Carmen Garcia Payo 與 Loreto Garcia Fernandez 建議採用核殼式膠囊而非單純的珠體，團隊做出來了卻看不到內部結構，於是把這個問題直接帶回給同一批研究人員，得到磁鐵礦作為光學示蹤劑以及冷凍切片的建議，最後發展成一套壁厚量測與滲漏測試流程。另有兩件事讓這一章超越了會議紀錄：團隊記錄了一項他們決定不做的改動（Elvira Mateos 提出的 Accumulibacter 多胺途徑，因代謝負擔大於無法量化的效益而婉拒，並特意寫下來，因為「不加入一條途徑同樣是一個設計決定」）；以及他們記錄了一位非專家的聲音，Inmaculada Alonso，San Juan 水庫附近的長期居民，她描述優養化是一種她看了幾十年、卻從來沒有人向她解釋過原因的緩慢變化。那場對話讓團隊轉向把「可被感知的復原成果」與「清楚的溝通」當成交付項目，而團隊自己也指出，一位居民無法代表所有受影響的人。","realWorld":"Need is framed with its own data, not a logo wall: 63% of assessed inland water bodies already eutrophic, ~1.15 million km2 of coastal waters with eutrophication potential, and the Mar Menor as a named Spanish case where a 2016 bloom destroyed over 80% of seagrass meadows, local income fell by an estimated share relative to unaffected areas and property values dropped. The team visited Mar Menor, Donana and the Embalse de San Juan to ground this. Nine SDG interactions were scored using the seven-point Nilsson, Griggs and Visbeck framework across SDGs 6, 9, 12, 13 and 14, and 22 stakeholder conversations were tracked through a Sustainability Model Canvas adapted from iGEM Hangzhou-BioX 2024, with six of them traced to engineering decisions and open loops marked as open. The most credible single act on this page is self-contradiction: the team's own ISO 14040/44 openLCA study over 16 impact categories finds that at the capsule loading it has actually achieved (1.5 mg P/g) rePhlow has a HIGHER climate-change impact than the chemical precipitation comparator, identifies phosphorus captured per gram of capsule as the single reversing variable, and publishes the ~8 mg P/g crossover rather than listing an achievement its own instruments contradict. Regulation is handled as strategy rather than context: Directive (EU) 2024/3019 replaces the Urban Wastewater Treatment Directive from August 2027 with phosphorus limits phased 2033-2045, but the team notes the binding obligation for its customer is the facility permit, not the urban Directive, and that EU law distinguishes contained use of GM microorganisms from deliberate release, making encapsulation plus downstream ultrafiltration a regulatory pathway as much as a safety feature; contained-use notification carries real 45-day and 90-day administrative lead times that are placed on the critical path. The cost model is stated as assumption, not result, at TRL 2-3: Business Plan V3 gives EUR 9,460 direct cost per module at a 50.2% gross margin, a pilot at EUR 69,800 of equipment plus EUR 450,000 cash cost, EUR 20,000 founder capital matched to the minimum share capital of the national technology-company grant line (up to EUR 250,000 at 70% of a >=EUR 175,000 budget), and a declared cost-of-goods sensitivity modelled twice at laboratory and bulk industrial prices. Two revenue models are offered: direct purchase of the module plus consumables and service, or Phosphorus-as-a-Service in which rePhlow retains ownership and therefore carries the capsule-lifetime risk itself. The beachhead is mid-sized agro-industrial and biofuel facilities with Bio-Oils Huelva as first prospective customer, and the four-phase plan has hard gates: four measurements (encapsulated-to-free uptake ratio, capsule service life in real effluent, phosphorus speciation of the Bio-Oils stream, enzyme leaching per cycle) must exist before Phase 2 opens, and at least one customer willing to pay the quoted price is required before scale-up rather than after. After the Jamboree: incorporation, a university technology-transfer novelty and freedom-to-operate assessment before deciding what to protect, a 12-month host-site pilot, then contract manufacturing, with the stated test that 'until repeat orders and positive unit economics without grant support both hold, rePhlow is a funded project rather than a company'.","realWorld_zh":"需求是用自己的資料撐起來的，不是貼一排機構標誌：已評估的內陸水體中有 63% 已呈優養化、約 115 萬 km2 的沿岸水域具優養化潛勢，並以西班牙的 Mar Menor 為具名案例，2016 年的一次藻華摧毀了超過 80% 的海草床，當地所得相對於未受影響地區下降了一定比例，房地產價值也隨之下跌。團隊實地走訪了 Mar Menor、Donana 與 Embalse de San Juan 來讓這些數字落地。九組 SDG 交互作用以 Nilsson、Griggs 與 Visbeck 的七點量表框架評分，涵蓋 SDG 6、9、12、13 與 14；22 場利害關係人對話則以改編自 iGEM Hangzhou-BioX 2024 的永續模式圖追蹤，其中六場可追溯到具體的工程決策，未閉合的迴圈也標記為未閉合。這一頁最可信的單一舉動是自我否證：團隊自己那份涵蓋 16 個衝擊類別的 ISO 14040/44 openLCA 研究發現，在他們實際達到的膠囊負載量（1.5 mg P/g）下，rePhlow 的氣候變遷衝擊高於化學沉澱的對照方案；研究指認每公克膠囊所捕集的磷量是唯一能翻轉結論的變數，並公開了約 8 mg P/g 的交叉點，而不是去列舉一項自家儀器數據並不支持的成就。法規被當成策略而非背景處理：歐盟指令 (EU) 2024/3019 將自 2027 年 8 月起取代都市廢水處理指令，磷限值分階段於 2033 至 2045 年生效，但團隊指出對其客戶具約束力的其實是廠區許可，而不是這份都市指令；他們也指出歐盟法規區分基改微生物的封閉使用與刻意釋放，使包覆加上下游超過濾既是安全措施，也同時是一條法規路徑；封閉使用通報有實際的 45 天與 90 天行政前置時間，而這些時間被放進了關鍵路徑。成本模型在 TRL 2-3 階段被明確陳述為假設而非結果：商業計畫 V3 給出每模組 9,460 EUR 的直接成本、50.2% 的毛利率，一座先導廠需 69,800 EUR 設備費加 450,000 EUR 現金成本，以及 20,000 EUR 的創辦人資本，後者對應國家級技術公司補助方案所要求的最低實收資本（在預算 >= 175,000 EUR 時最高補助 70%、上限 250,000 EUR），並明確以實驗室價格與工業大宗價格各做一次銷貨成本敏感度分析。團隊提出兩種營收模式：直接購買模組加耗材與服務，或 Phosphorus-as-a-Service，由 rePhlow 保留所有權，因此也自行承擔膠囊壽命的風險。灘頭堡市場是中型農工業與生質燃料廠，Bio-Oils Huelva 為第一個潛在客戶；四階段計畫設有硬性關卡：在第 2 階段開啟之前，必須先有四項量測（包覆與游離狀態的吸收比、膠囊在真實廢水中的使用壽命、Bio-Oils 廢水流的磷型態分析、每個循環的酶流失量），而且在放大量產之前、而非之後，必須至少有一個願意以報價付費的客戶。Jamboree 之後的規劃是：公司登記、在決定要保護什麼之前先做一次校內技轉的新穎性與自由實施評估、為期 12 個月的駐場先導運行，之後才進入委外製造；他們並明白立下檢驗標準：「在重複訂單與不靠補助也成立的正向單位經濟同時出現之前，rePhlow 都只是一個拿到資金的專案，而不是一家公司」。","partners":["Bio-Oils Huelva (biodiesel producer, La Rabida plant; industrial collaborator, effluent samples and first prospective customer)","Repsol (energy and petrochemical operator; containment requirements)","CEDEX, Centro de Estudios y Experimentacion de Obras Publicas (public water-technology research body)","Canal de Isabel II (water utility)","IMDEA Water","Centro de Biologia Molecular Severo Ochoa (CBM, CSIC-UAM)","Instituto de Quimica Organica General (IQOG-CSIC) - research stay for the revalorisation module","Centro de Investigaciones Biologicas (CIB-CSIC) - CRISPR base-editing plasmids","Fabrica UCM and Compluemprende (UCM entrepreneurship programmes)","APTenisa Launch, run by La Salle Technova Barcelona and subsidised by ENISA","Viroque Energy","iGEM UPF Barcelona (Vinesys) - joint water campaign","MSP-Vector peer-reviewed iGEM journal (Maastricht University)","Non-dilutive funders: FECYT, Santander X, Promega Iberica"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6124/wiki/assets/human-practices/travel-archive/bio-oils-01.webp","caption":"The Bio-Oils Huelva biodiesel plant, whose degumming effluent ranges became rePhlow's semi-synthetic test stream and later its first real sample.","caption_zh":"Bio-Oils Huelva 生質柴油廠，其脫膠廢水的數值範圍成為 rePhlow 的半合成測試水流，後來也成為第一個真實樣本的來源。","credit":"Team Madrid-UCM, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6124/wiki/assets/human-practices/travel-archive/cedex-01.webp","caption":"A CEDEX researcher showing the team the water-technology laboratory; this visit made them stop presenting their malachite-green assay as a finished method.","caption_zh":"一位 CEDEX 研究人員帶團隊參觀水處理技術實驗室；這次參訪讓他們不再把自己的孔雀綠呈色法當成已完成的方法來呈現。","credit":"Team Madrid-UCM, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6124/wiki/assets/human-practices/travel-archive/repsol-02.webp","caption":"The rePhlow team with Repsol specialists, the session in which containment evidence was made a precondition for industrial acceptability.","caption_zh":"rePhlow 團隊與 Repsol 的專家，正是在這場會談中，圍阻的證據被定為工業端可接受性的前提條件。","credit":"Team Madrid-UCM, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6124/wiki/assets/human-practices/travel-archive/embalse-san-juan-01.webp","caption":"Field sampling at the Embalse de San Juan reservoir, where a long-term resident described decades of eutrophication she had never had explained to her.","caption_zh":"在 Embalse de San Juan 水庫進行田野採樣，一位長期居住在此的居民在這裡描述了她經歷數十年、卻從未有人向她解釋過的優養化。","credit":"Team Madrid-UCM, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Copy Madrid's five-rung integration ladder with its closure rule: a stakeholder loop counts as closed only when the revised design has been taken back to the person who triggered the change and their response produces a further change. Copy also their willingness to publish an LCA that currently rules against their own technology, with the single reversing variable and its crossover value named.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"抄下 Madrid 的五階整合階梯以及它的閉環判準：一個利害關係人迴圈只有在修改後的設計被帶回給當初促成改變的那個人、而對方的回應又再引發一次改變時，才算真正閉合。也抄下他們願意公開一份目前判定對自家技術不利的 LCA，並明確指出那個唯一能翻轉結論的變數及其交叉點數值。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/madrid-ucm/","https://2026.igem.wiki/madrid-ucm/assets/index-CDWW7OSW.js","https://2026.igem.wiki/madrid-ucm/assets/MetabolicNetworkGraph-C3qAiQFO.js","https://2026.igem.wiki/madrid-ucm/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/madrid-ucm/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/madrid-ucm/sustainability","https://2026.igem.wiki/madrid-ucm/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/madrid-ucm/project-description","https://2026.igem.wiki/madrid-ucm/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/madrid-ucm/education-communication","https://2026.igem.wiki/madrid-ucm/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/madrid-ucm/safety-and-security","https://2026.igem.wiki/madrid-ucm/collaboration-partnership"],"rank":21},"6125":{"team":"Squirrel-Beijing","id":"6125","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/squirrel-beijing/","projectTitle":"PNPeeker","tagline":"A whole-cell sensor that reports the bioavailable fraction of p-nitrophenol in soil, paired with a five-enzyme pathway that destroys it and a cold-triggered suicide switch","summary":"Squirrel-Beijing targeted p-nitrophenol, a US EPA priority pollutant found in more than 32 percent of Chinese agricultural soils at 0.8-30.5 micrograms per gram in places, and attacked the measurement problem rather than just the pollutant: HPLC reports total concentration, but ecological risk depends on the bioavailable fraction, which only a living sensor can read. They engineered the PobR transcriptional regulator with its PpobA promoter into an RFP reporter circuit showing concentration-dependent response from 0.001 to 10 mg/L, reconstructed the five-enzyme hydroquinone pathway (pnpA, B, C, E, D) that converts pNP all the way to beta-ketoadipate, and achieved 87-95 percent pNP removal at 10-500 micrograms per litre within 24 hours. They won Best New Composite Part in the High School section and were nominated for Best Village Project.","awards":["Best New Composite Part — Winner (High School)","Best Village Project — Nominee (Climate Crisis / Conservation / Bioremediation)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Parts presented with explicit medal-tier labelling (Gold Medal Part, Silver Medal Part, Bronze Medal Part) so a reader can see which contribution criterion each satisfies, plus a dedicated 'Applications for Future iGEM Teams' section with four named reuse routes. For collaboration they defined P-E-A-F (Preparation, Exchange, Action, Feedback) as a transferable framework for cross-team work. The entrepreneurship page runs TAM-SAM-SOM, PEST, Porter's Five Forces, SWOT, 4Ps, Business Model Canvas, a milestone timeline, a five-year financial forecast, a five-category risk register and three exit routes.","dataviz":"Characterisation figures that answer the questions a reuser actually asks: normalised GFP/OD600 promoter activity across five temperatures over 0-10 hours, growth curves of the lysis strain at 16, 25 and 37 degrees C over 12 hours, PCR gels confirming expected fragment sizes (GFP 717 bp, T4 Holin 657 bp, T4 Lysozyme 492 bp), the TAM-SAM-SOM illustration, the P-E-A-F framework diagram and a five-year financial forecast chart. A 28-term project glossary sits beside every page.","datascience":"Numbers are reported with ranges and conditions attached rather than as single best values: the sensor's response spans 0.001-10 mg/L, degradation is 87-95 percent across an initial-concentration range of 10-500 micrograms per litre at 24 hours, and the cold promoter reaches about 270.2 A.U. at 20 degrees C against 14.1 A.U. at 37 degrees C, a 19.2-fold window, with 15, 25 and 30 degrees C values all given so another team can pick an induction temperature. PobR itself was improved by computational screening (docking plus molecular dynamics) followed by site-directed mutation.","software":"","stack":["E. coli","PobR / PpobA regulatory pair","pnpABCDE hydroquinone pathway","J23100 promoter with B0034 RBS","pCspA cold-inducible promoter with T4 Holin and T4 Lysozyme","RFP and GFP reporters","molecular docking and molecular dynamics","BioBrick RFC#10 assembly"],"techniques":["whole-cell biosensing of bioavailable pollutant fraction","computational regulator engineering then site-directed mutagenesis","dual-operon splitting of a long pathway to avoid transcription attenuation","temperature- and time-resolved promoter characterisation","cold-triggered lysis biocontainment","standardised quantitative pNP detection validated in complex environmental matrices"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"The 28-term project glossary deserves counting as public engagement in its own right, since it defines every technical term used across the wiki in plain language and is linked from every page. Its entry for OD600 is the giveaway on quality: it states that OD600 is a proxy for culture turbidity and 'does not by itself establish cell viability or complete cell lysis', which is a caveat on their own headline lysis result rather than a textbook definition.","ihp":"Expert interviews drove the project's framing toward bioavailability rather than total concentration, and the team captain made a specific management decision about them: recognising that the dry team could interview fluently but could not field highly technical follow-ups, and that the wet-lab team had the knowledge but not the interview role, the captain personally attended every human-practices expert interview to capture professional questions and suggestions on site and minimise information loss across the knowledge gap between subgroups. That is a documented organisational fix to a problem most teams never name.","realWorld":"Two things to assess here, and the parts work is the stronger. On reusability, this is close to a model contribution. Every part is codon-optimised for E. coli and BioBrick RFC#10 compatible, so adoption needs no re-synthesis. Each part description states its position in the pathway and what it hands to the next step, so the five degradation enzymes read as a sequence rather than five entries. The composite parts are quantified with the conditions stated (the reporter circuit over 0.001-10 mg/L; the pnpABCDE module at 87-95 percent removal from 10-500 micrograms per litre in 24 hours), which is what lets another team tell whether their own result matches. The dual-operon design is explained as a solution to a named general problem, transcription attenuation in long polycistronic mRNAs causing downstream genes to under-express, and offered as a transferable strategy for any long pathway, which is the difference between publishing a part and publishing a technique. Best of all, they chose to satisfy the Bronze contribution criterion properly: rather than registering another new part, they took an existing Registry entry, BBa_K5083099, and generated the characterisation data it was missing, a full temperature gradient (15, 20, 25, 30, 37 degrees C) crossed with culture time, plus growth curves of the lysis strain at 16, 25 and 37 degrees C, concluding with exactly the practical guidance a reuser needs: strong induction at 15-20 degrees C with low basal expression at 30-37, high GFP at 20 degrees C, and clear density collapse to about 0.11 OD at 16 degrees C by 12 hours. They also label their own evidence carefully, saying the lysis data 'preliminarily demonstrate' an association between lower temperature and decreased cell density rather than claiming proven containment. The 'Applications for Future iGEM Teams' section then spells out four concrete reuse routes: swap the reporter to port the sensor to a colorimetric or portable platform; reuse the degradation module or borrow the operon-splitting strategy for a different pathway; use the temperature-resolved data to design a cold suicide switch; or combine sensing and degradation modules via RFC#10 for an integrated monitor-and-remediate strain, which they built themselves as a demonstration. On the commercial side the work is competent but thinner than the parts work, though it does carry real unit economics: pricing anchored at 30-50 percent of the HPLC/GC-MS comprehensive per-test cost of 150-300 RMB, giving 150 RMB per kit (lyophilised strain tube, reaction buffer, operating manual), against a unit cost of 75 RMB falling to 45 RMB at scale, so gross margin runs 50 percent to about 70 percent; a five-year forecast from 500 to 15,000 kits with break-even in year three at roughly 4,000 kits and 600,000 RMB revenue; and a start-up need of about 450,000 RMB over years one and two. The SOM is built bottom-up from Guangdong's roughly 2.5 million hectares of arable land with its three assumptions stated (South China at about 20 percent of the national market, biosensor penetration at 5-8 percent, initial share 3-5 percent), landing at USD 2-4 million. Be blunt, though: there is no registered entity, no patent, no incubator place, no investor conversation and no letter of intent, the funding sources are listed as categories (iGEM grants, school research funding, angel or incubator seed money, supervisor channels) rather than named prospects, and the regulatory discussion is a risk category rather than a mapped approval route. The venture is a well-constructed plan on paper; the parts are a real, usable deliverable.","partners":["Partner iGEM teams engaged through the P-E-A-F collaboration framework","Academic experts consulted in human practices (attended personally by the team captain)","Supervisor collaboration channels named as a prospective funding route"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6125/wiki/contribution/img1.avif","caption":"Supplementary characterisation of the existing Registry part BBa_K5083099: PCR confirmation of GFP, T4 Holin and T4 Lysozyme fragments, normalised pCspA activity across temperatures and times, and growth curves of the lysis strain","credit":"Team Squirrel-Beijing, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6125/wiki/contribution/img2.avif","caption":"Time-resolved response of the pCspA cold-inducible promoter at five temperatures, the data a future team needs to choose an induction temperature","credit":"Team Squirrel-Beijing, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6125/wiki/contribution/img4.avif","caption":"The Preparation-Exchange-Action-Feedback (P-E-A-F) collaboration framework, published as a transferable method for cross-team work","credit":"Team Squirrel-Beijing, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6125/wiki/entrepreneurship/img1.avif","caption":"TAM-SAM-SOM market sizing, with the obtainable market built bottom-up from Guangdong arable hectarage and three stated penetration assumptions","credit":"Team Squirrel-Beijing, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Make one deliverable per project be characterisation data added to somebody else's existing part, chosen because that part lacked the numbers a user would need, and report it as a parameter sweep (temperature crossed with time, with all intermediate values shown) rather than a single demonstration. Then write an explicit 'Applications for Future Teams' section naming who could reuse each module and how, and keep a plain-language glossary whose entries state the limits of your own measurements, as theirs does for OD600.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/squirrel-beijing/","https://2026.igem.wiki/squirrel-beijing/parts/","https://2026.igem.wiki/squirrel-beijing/contribution/","https://2026.igem.wiki/squirrel-beijing/entrepreneurship/"],"rank":33},"6133":{"team":"GreatBay-SCIE","id":"6133","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/greatbay-scie/","projectTitle":"Expelliodor — Expel the Odor, on Your Terms","projectTitle_zh":"Expelliodor — 除去體味，由你決定","tagline":"Three de novo designed proteins that stop axillary odour before it forms, without killing the skin microbiome.","tagline_zh":"三個從頭設計的蛋白質，在體味形成之前就阻斷它，同時不殺死皮膚微生物相。","summary":"Axillary odour arises when Staphylococcus hominis imports the odourless precursor Cys-Gly-3M3SH through the peptide transporter PepTSh and converts it to 3M3SH. Rather than killing skin bacteria, GreatBay-SCIE attacked the uptake step three ways: a de novo small-molecule binding protein that sequesters the precursor, a de novo protein binder designed to lock PepTSh in its inward-facing conformation, and a cyclodextrin glucanotransferase engineered to glycosylate the precursor so the transporter no longer recognises it. This is the most sophisticated de novo protein design campaign of any high school team in the cohort — RFdiffusion3, Proteina-Complexa, ProteinMPNN, RoseTTAFold3 co-folding, 50-ns MD with MM/GBSA, and SPURS-guided thermostability engineering — organised around two frameworks they invented: a Characterize stage prepended to DBTL, and a funnel-shaped decision-gated workflow that spends expensive methods only on candidates that survive cheap ones. Nine precursor binders and five transporter binders were actually tested in vitro, with 4 of 9 and 4 of 5 significantly reducing 3M3SH.","summary_zh":"腋下體味的成因是 Staphylococcus hominis 透過胜肽運輸蛋白 PepTSh 把無味的前驅物 Cys-Gly-3M3SH 送進細胞，再轉換成 3M3SH。GreatBay-SCIE 沒有選擇殺死皮膚細菌，而是從三個方向攻擊這個攝入步驟：一個從頭設計的小分子結合蛋白把前驅物隔離起來、一個從頭設計的蛋白質結合子把 PepTSh 鎖在朝內的構形、以及一個經改造的環糊精葡萄糖轉移酶（CGTase）為前驅物加上糖基，使運輸蛋白不再認得它。這是本屆所有高中隊伍中最精巧的從頭蛋白質設計工作——RFdiffusion3、Proteina-Complexa、ProteinMPNN、RoseTTAFold3 共折疊、搭配 MM/GBSA 的 50 ns 分子動力學，以及由 SPURS 指引的熱穩定性工程——並圍繞他們自創的兩套框架組織起來：在 DBTL 之前加上一個 Characterize（特性描述）階段，以及一條漏斗狀、設有決策關卡的流程，讓昂貴的方法只花在通過便宜方法篩選的候選上。實際進入體外測試的有九個前驅物結合子與五個運輸蛋白結合子，其中 9 個中有 4 個、5 個中有 4 個顯著降低了 3M3SH。","awards":["Best Model — Nominee (High School)","Best Integrated Human Practices — Nominee (High School)","Inclusivity Award — Winner (High School)","Best Village Project — Nominee (Agriculture / Food & Nutrition / Fashion & Cosmetics / Art & Design)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Two methodological contributions frame everything. The CHARACTERIZE-DBTL framework inserts a stage before Design with four substages — Problem Definition (what the design must achieve, in what context, with what intervention points), Target Definition (the exact molecule, protein, conformational state, interface or reaction to engineer, with boundaries), Mechanistic Characterization (assess the plausibility of the proposed mechanism against experimental, structural and computational evidence), and Design Specification (translate all of that into explicit requirements that become the literal inputs to the design tool). The DECISION-GATED WORKFLOW is a funnel in which each successive evaluation is more expensive than the last, so a large generated set is cut by cheap co-folding metrics before anything reaches molecular dynamics and only a handful reach the bench — explicitly chosen because they are a high school team with limited wet-lab resources. The Characterize stage paid off concretely in each of the three routes. For the PRECURSOR BINDER, characterisation established that 3M3SH exists as two stereoisomers with different smells, that the sweat-and-onion-like (S) form is the odour-relevant one, and that deep-learning design tools frequently introduce stereochemical errors — so the design specification became 'use Cys-Gly-(S)-3M3SH with explicitly defined stereochemistry as input and verify ligand chirality after structure generation before any candidate advances'. Two independent design routes were run in parallel for comparison: RFdiffusion3 (via Rosetta Foundry, with ProteinMPNN sequence redesign and RoseTTAFold3 co-folding validation, ranked by RF3's own ranking_score) and Proteina-Complexa (a partially-latent flow-matching model, ranked by a custom composite score). Top binders from each route went to 50-ns MD scored on ligand RMSD and MM/GBSA binding free energy. For the TRANSPORTER BINDER, characterisation drew on published MD showing that the inward-to-outward transition is the rate-limiting step of PepTSh's transport cycle, so stabilising the inward-facing state should block transport; they took the experimental inward-facing crystal structure (PDB 6EXS), built an outward-facing homology model in SWISS-MODEL, and compared them to find extracellular electrostatic networks (K64-E323, and the R184/D182/E340/R337 cluster) and hydrophobic patches present only in the inward-facing state — those became the target interface, with a specification of an 80-120 residue binder and a preference for compact designs to improve accessibility through a Gram-positive cell wall. Design was RFdiffusion3 backbone generation, ProteinMPNN sequence design, RF3 co-folding, interface-placement filtering, then a composite score of 0.50 x normalised ranking score + 0.25 x normalised pLDDT + 0.25 x normalised inverse PAE, then MD. For CGTase, characterisation enumerated the three modifiable groups on the precursor (amino, carboxyl, hydroxyl) and selected reactions by compatibility with the actual application environment — mildly acidic human skin with no external supply of ATP or NADH — which ruled out cofactor-dependent chemistry and left hydroxyl transglycosylation by CGTase; molecular docking from the 1CXL template with cluster analysis of poses, followed by MD of the wild-type complex, showed the non-native substrate stays stably accommodated in the catalytic pocket and identified which interactions were weak (around the carboxylate group and the hydrophobic tail), which became the rational-design targets for nine point mutants, each re-evaluated by MD. Two further optimisation campaigns followed: CGTase thermostability via SPURS (an AI stability predictor) after excluding conserved, ligand-binding and calcium-coordinating residues, with FireProt-style pairwise compatibility filtering and a diversity-preserving beam search assembling multi-point mutants at depths of 2, 4, 6 and 8 substitutions; and precursor-binder affinity via an adapted LASErMPNN neural-proofreading strategy, saturating point mutations within 5 Angstrom of the ligand, averaging probabilities across decoding orders and dropout to reduce sensitivity to individual predictions, ranking by delta-NLL = ln[P(a)/P(b)], and filtering out buried polar residues introduced without a suitable hydrogen bond.","frameworks_zh":"兩項方法論貢獻框定了全部工作。CHARACTERIZE-DBTL 框架在 Design 之前插入一個階段，內含四個子階段——問題界定（設計必須達成什麼、在什麼情境下、有哪些可介入的切入點）、標的界定（要工程改造的確切分子、蛋白質、構形狀態、介面或反應，並劃出邊界）、機制特性描述（依實驗、結構與運算證據評估所提機制的合理性），以及設計規格（把上述一切轉譯為明確要求，直接成為設計工具的輸入）。DECISION-GATED WORKFLOW（設有決策關卡的流程）則是一個漏斗，其中每一道後續評估都比前一道更昂貴，因此一大批生成結果先被便宜的共折疊指標篩掉，之後才有東西進入分子動力學，最後只有少數幾個上實驗檯——他們明白說這是因為自己是濕實驗資源有限的高中隊伍。Characterize 階段在三條路線上都帶來具體收穫。在前驅物結合子方面，特性描述確立了 3M3SH 以兩種氣味不同的立體異構物存在，其中帶汗味與洋蔥味的 (S) 型才是與體味相關的那一種，而深度學習設計工具經常引入立體化學錯誤——因此設計規格就寫成「以立體化學明確定義的 Cys-Gly-(S)-3M3SH 作為輸入，並在結構生成後、任何候選晉級之前，先驗證配體掌性」。他們並行跑了兩條獨立的設計路線以作比較：RFdiffusion3（經由 Rosetta Foundry，以 ProteinMPNN 重新設計序列、以 RoseTTAFold3 共折疊驗證，並依 RF3 自身的 ranking_score 排序）與 Proteina-Complexa（一個部分潛在的流匹配模型，依自訂的複合分數排序）。兩條路線中最佳的結合子都進入 50 ns 分子動力學，以配體 RMSD 與 MM/GBSA 結合自由能評分。在運輸蛋白結合子方面，特性描述引用已發表的分子動力學研究，顯示由內向外的轉換是 PepTSh 運輸循環的速率決定步驟，因此穩定住朝內狀態應可阻斷運輸；他們取用實驗測得的朝內晶體結構（PDB 6EXS），在 SWISS-MODEL 中建出朝外的同源模型，兩者相比以找出只在朝內狀態存在的胞外靜電網絡（K64-E323，以及 R184/D182/E340/R337 這組）與疏水區塊——這些就成了標的介面，規格則訂為 80-120 個殘基的結合子，並偏好結構緊緻的設計，以提升穿過革蘭氏陽性細胞壁的可及性。設計流程為 RFdiffusion3 生成骨架、ProteinMPNN 設計序列、RF3 共折疊、介面位置過濾，再以 0.50 x 標準化 ranking score + 0.25 x 標準化 pLDDT + 0.25 x 標準化 PAE 倒數的複合分數排序，最後進入分子動力學。在 CGTase 方面，特性描述列舉了前驅物上三個可修飾的官能基（胺基、羧基、羥基），並依與實際應用環境的相容性來挑選反應——弱酸性的人體皮膚，沒有外來的 ATP 或 NADH 供應——這排除了需要輔因子的化學反應，剩下由 CGTase 進行的羥基轉糖基化；以 1CXL 為模板的分子對接並對結合姿態做群聚分析，接著對野生型複合物做分子動力學，顯示這個非天然受質能穩定地容納在催化口袋中，也指出哪些交互作用較弱（羧酸根附近與疏水尾端），這些就成了九個點突變體的理性設計標的，每一個都再以分子動力學重新評估。之後還有兩輪最佳化：CGTase 的熱穩定性以 SPURS（一個 AI 穩定性預測模型）進行，先排除保守殘基、配體結合殘基與配位鈣離子的殘基，再以 FireProt 式的兩兩相容性過濾，並用保留多樣性的 beam search 在 2、4、6、8 個取代的深度上組裝多點突變體；前驅物結合子的親和力則以改寫過的 LASErMPNN 神經網絡校讀策略進行，對配體 5 埃以內的位點做飽和點突變，跨不同解碼順序與 dropout 平均機率以降低對單一預測的敏感度，依 delta-NLL = ln[P(a)/P(b)] 排序，並濾掉那些被引入卻沒有合適氫鍵的埋藏極性殘基。","dataviz":"Structural figures are used as arguments rather than decoration. The inward- versus outward-facing PepTSh comparison is drawn as four aligned panels — the inward structure, a close-up of its intact electrostatic network with dashed contacts and named residues, the outward homology model, and the same close-up showing those contacts broken — so the reader can see for themselves why the inward state is the one worth stabilising, with consistent colouring (green C-terminal bundle, blue N-terminal bundle, orange TMA/TMB) carried across every panel. The target interface is then shown three ways: the region highlighted on the whole structure, a side view with the extracellular direction arrowed, and a close-up with hotspot residues in orange bordering a green hydrophobic patch. The Characterize stage and the funnel-shaped decision-gated workflow are each drawn as schematics, the funnel visibly narrowing through each evaluation gate. MD trajectories are embedded as videos for all three systems. Most valuable of all, Figures 7 and 11 plot computational metric against experimental outcome — A412 signal reduction, calculated as 100 x (1 - mean binder A412 / mean control A412) — with each tested binder as a point, OLS regression lines, and both Pearson r and Spearman rho reported, separately for the two design routes. Every caption gives the n (n = 4 for RFdiffusion3, n = 5 for Proteina-Complexa and for transporter binders) and the full composite-score formula with its weights written out, so the figure can be re-derived. Assay figures carry error bars (+/- SD, n = 3) with significance asterisks defined.","dataviz_zh":"結構圖是當成論證使用、不是裝飾。朝內與朝外的 PepTSh 比較畫成四張對齊的面板——朝內結構、其完整靜電網絡的特寫（虛線標示接觸、並標出殘基名稱）、朝外的同源模型，以及同一區域顯示那些接觸已斷開的特寫——讓讀者自己看出為什麼朝內狀態才是值得穩定的那一個；配色（綠色 C 端束、藍色 N 端束、橘色 TMA/TMB）在每張面板間保持一致。標的介面接著以三種方式呈現：在整體結構上標出該區域、一張以箭頭標示胞外方向的側視圖，以及一張特寫，圖中橘色的熱點殘基圍繞著綠色的疏水區塊。Characterize 階段與漏斗狀的決策關卡流程各畫成一張示意圖，漏斗明顯隨每道評估關卡收窄。三套系統的分子動力學軌跡都以影片內嵌。最有價值的是圖 7 與圖 11，把運算指標對實驗結果作圖——A412 訊號降幅，計算方式為 100 x (1 - 結合子 A412 平均值 / 對照 A412 平均值)——每個受測結合子為一個點，附 OLS 迴歸線，並同時報告 Pearson r 與 Spearman rho，兩條設計路線分開呈現。每則圖說都給出 n 值（RFdiffusion3 為 n = 4，Proteina-Complexa 與運輸蛋白結合子為 n = 5），並把完整的複合分數公式連同權重寫出來，使圖可以被重新推導。試驗圖都帶誤差棒（+/- SD，n = 3）並定義顯著性星號。","datascience":"The genuinely unusual thing here is that the team treat their own scoring metrics as hypotheses to be tested against wet-lab data, and publish the result honestly even when it undermines them. Of 22 planned binders (11 per design tool), 9 were tested; 4 of 9 significantly reduced 3M3SH production, and 4 of 5 transporter binders did, with a maximum 21% reduction. Correlating metric against outcome gave a route-dependent answer: in the RFdiffusion3 branch the interface metrics agreed with experiment and all three MD metrics (MM/GBSA delta-G, and the mean and SD of ligand RMSD over 10-50 ns) showed the expected trend, while in the Proteina-Complexa branch the custom composite score correlated best (Pearson r = 0.76, Spearman rho = 0.60) but the MD metrics did NOT agree — and the team propose a specific mechanistic reason, that RF3 (a diffusion model, like RoseTTAFold3) may predict Proteina-Complexa outputs (partially latent flow matching) less accurately, so ligand RMSD may partly measure relaxation of a poor predicted pose rather than true instability. For the transporter binders they draw the sharper statistical lesson: 'in a filtered set of candidates, a single metric may have too little variation to support confident prediction of actual experimental performance' — i.e. gating on a metric destroys the variance you would need to validate it. They state plainly that the small candidate set 'cannot establish statistically significant relationships', that the results 'cannot concretely verify the usefulness of the single metrics and the weighted metrics we set', and they name the fixes: more independent MD runs, explicit entropy correction, an implicit membrane model in the free-energy calculation, a second folding tool such as AlphaFold, and larger datasets to recalibrate weights. The thermostability work produced a real, interpretable result in both directions: for the T370R/F183W parent, WR2, WR4 and WR8 all improved over the parent with WR8 best, suggesting SPURS (trained on pairwise mutagenesis data) can learn patterns that extrapolate to multi-point mutants and that the design introduced beneficial epistasis; but for the T370K parent only KR2 improved and the higher-order mutants did not, which the team diagnose as the beam search's path dependence — an ineffective mutation introduced at depth 4 is inherited by every deeper mutant. They are equally candid about build failures: the intended T370K mutant came back as T370L, so only T370R/F183W was tested as designed and the rational-design hypothesis is 'not fully verified because of the limited dataset'.","datascience_zh":"此處真正不尋常之處在於，團隊把自己的評分指標當成有待用濕實驗資料檢驗的假說，並在結果不利於自己時也誠實公開。原計畫 22 個結合子（每套設計工具 11 個）中有 9 個受測；9 個中有 4 個顯著降低 3M3SH 生成，運輸蛋白結合子則是 5 個中有 4 個，最大降幅 21%。把指標對結果做相關分析，答案隨路線而異：在 RFdiffusion3 這一支，介面指標與實驗一致，三個分子動力學指標（MM/GBSA 的 delta-G，以及 10-50 ns 間配體 RMSD 的平均值與標準差）都呈現預期趨勢；而在 Proteina-Complexa 這一支，自訂的複合分數相關性最好（Pearson r = 0.76、Spearman rho = 0.60），但分子動力學指標卻不一致——團隊並提出一個具體的機制性解釋：RF3（與 RoseTTAFold3 一樣是擴散模型）對 Proteina-Complexa（部分潛在的流匹配）的輸出可能預測得較不準，因此配體 RMSD 有部分可能量到的是一個不佳預測姿態的鬆弛過程、而非真正的不穩定。對運輸蛋白結合子，他們提出了更鋭利的統計教訓：「在一組已被篩選過的候選中，單一指標的變異量可能太小，不足以支撐對實際實驗表現的可信預測」——也就是說，拿某個指標當關卡篩選，會毀掉你驗證它所需的變異量。他們直白說明候選集太小「無法建立具統計顯著性的關係」、結果「無法確實驗證我們所設定的單一指標與加權指標是否有用」，並點名修正方向：更多次獨立的分子動力學、明確的熵修正、在自由能計算中加入隱式膜模型、第二個折疊工具（例如 AlphaFold），以及更大的資料集以重新校準權重。熱穩定性這部分在兩個方向上都得出真實且可解讀的結果：以 T370R/F183W 為親本時，WR2、WR4 與 WR8 都優於親本、WR8 最佳，顯示 SPURS（以兩兩突變資料訓練）可以學到能外推到多點突變體的規律，也顯示該設計引入了有益的上位效應；但以 T370K 為親本時只有 KR2 改善，更高階的突變體則沒有，團隊診斷這是 beam search 的路徑依賴性——在深度 4 引入的一個無效突變，會被每一個更深的突變體繼承。他們對構築失敗同樣坦白：原本要做的 T370K 突變體回來時變成 T370L，因此只有 T370R/F183W 是依設計受測，理性設計的假說「因資料集有限而未完全驗證」。","software":"FoundryUI, a node-based visual programming workbench for de novo protein design, explicitly inspired by ComfyUI (and by Blender and GameMaker as precedents for making technical workflows accessible). It wraps four Rosetta Foundry tools — RFdiffusion3, RoseTTAFold3, ProteinMPNN and LigandMPNN — as connectable nodes for input, generation, sequence redesign, folding, filtering, visualisation and saving, with typed connections that refuse incompatible links, 3D selectors so residues and atoms can be picked directly off a structure in the GUI rather than typed as indices, and sessions and runs so results survive a dropped connection. It ships pre-built workflows for ligand-binder design, protein-binder design, enzyme design, MPNN sequence design and folding prediction, and reads and writes PDB, FASTA, mmCIF, SMILES, JSON and CSV so outputs stay usable elsewhere. The stated motivation is collaboration as much as accessibility: a command line does not show why a step was chosen or how data moved between stages, whereas a graph does — making a workflow easier to explain, modify and hand to the next team. They tested it by teaching it: FoundryUI was used in a school club education activity so students could approach protein modelling through biological decisions instead of commands. All automation scripts are uploaded as reusable workflows for future iGEM teams.","software_zh":"FoundryUI 是一套以節點為基礎的視覺化程式設計工作台，用於從頭蛋白質設計，明確受 ComfyUI 啟發（並以 Blender 與 GameMaker 作為把技術流程變得平易近人的先例）。它把 Rosetta Foundry 的四個工具——RFdiffusion3、RoseTTAFold3、ProteinMPNN 與 LigandMPNN——包裝成可互連的節點，涵蓋輸入、生成、序列重新設計、折疊、過濾、視覺化與儲存，連接有型別、會拒絕不相容的連線；並提供 3D 選取器，讓殘基與原子可以直接在介面上從結構點選、而不必以索引輸入；還有工作階段與執行紀錄，使結果在連線中斷後仍然保留。它內附預建的工作流程，涵蓋配體結合子設計、蛋白質結合子設計、酵素設計、MPNN 序列設計與折疊預測，並可讀寫 PDB、FASTA、mmCIF、SMILES、JSON 與 CSV，讓輸出在別處仍然可用。他們聲明的動機中，協作與易用性同樣重要：命令列不會顯示某一步為何被選擇、資料如何在各階段之間流動，而一張流程圖會——這讓工作流程更容易解釋、修改並交給下一屆隊伍。他們用教學來測試它：FoundryUI 被用在校內社團的教育活動中，讓學生能透過生物學上的決策、而不是透過指令來接觸蛋白質建模。所有自動化腳本都以可重複使用的工作流程上傳，供未來的 iGEM 隊伍取用。","stack":["RFdiffusion3","Proteina-Complexa","ProteinMPNN","LigandMPNN","RoseTTAFold3","Rosetta Foundry","SPURS","LASErMPNN","SWISS-MODEL","molecular dynamics with MM/GBSA","molecular docking with pose clustering","FoundryUI (own software)","Python automation scripts"],"techniques":["de novo small-molecule binder design","de novo protein-protein binder design","inverse folding / sequence design","co-folding structure validation (pLDDT, PAE, ipSAE)","stereochemistry verification of generated ligands","conformational-state-selective targeting (inward vs outward transporter state)","homology modelling for comparative structure analysis","interface hotspot and hydrophobic patch identification","molecular docking with hierarchical pose clustering","50-ns molecular dynamics simulation","MM/GBSA binding free energy estimation","ligand RMSD stability analysis","rational enzyme active-site redesign","AI stability prediction (SPURS)","FireProt-style pairwise epistasis compatibility filtering","diverse beam search for multi-point mutant assembly","neural proofreading with delta-NLL ranking and decoding-order averaging","composite multi-metric scoring with explicit weights","decision-gated resource-aware candidate funnelling","metric-versus-experiment correlation analysis (Pearson and Spearman)","epistasis analysis across mutation depth","Ellman's assay quantification of thiol product"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Inclusivity Award winner, and the work is built on a framework (LIFT+: Learn, Intervene, Feedback, Transfer, Beyond) with six named target groups reachable in China who face barriers to synthetic biology — the blind community, the Deaf community, children on the autism spectrum, people from low socioeconomic backgrounds, modelling beginners, and older adults with limited formal education. Each group is introduced by a real scientist from that community paired with a sourced statistic: Wanda Diaz Merced, the blind astrophysicist who pioneered sonification of astronomical data, alongside the finding that only 2.1% of blind children globally have access to specialised education services; Temple Grandin alongside the 14.95% four-year-college enrolment rate for individuals with autism; Derek Braun, the deaf geneticist who built Gallaudet's first molecular genetics laboratory, alongside the ~80% of school-age deaf children out of school in low- and middle-income countries; Gabriel Reyes, founder of FLi Sci, alongside OECD data that 37% of disadvantaged students are low performers in science versus 12% of advantaged; and Jia Lanpo, the Zhoukoudian paleoanthropologist who had only a high school education, alongside the 17-point generational gap in tertiary education between adults aged 55-64 and 25-34. Deliverables include 20 tactile biology graphics covering 20 topics across 5 categories for the blind community, and — connecting directly to their dry lab — FoundryUI used as the teaching vehicle for computational protein design beginners. The page itself has an interactive animated version and a text-based alternative, which is the inclusivity principle applied to their own wiki.","publicEngagement_zh":"本隊獲包容性獎，整套工作建立在一個框架（LIFT+：Learn、Intervene、Feedback、Transfer、Beyond）之上，並指名六個在中國可觸及、且在接觸合成生物學時面臨障礙的對象群體——盲人社群、聽障社群、自閉症譜系兒童、社會經濟弱勢者、建模初學者，以及受正式教育有限的年長者。每個群體都由一位出身該社群的真實科學家開場，並搭配一項有出處的統計數據：Wanda Diaz Merced，開創以聲音化呈現天文資料的盲人天文物理學家，對應的數據是全球僅 2.1% 的盲童能取得特殊教育服務；Temple Grandin，對應自閉症者四年制大學的 14.95% 入學率；Derek Braun，建立 Gallaudet 第一座分子遺傳學實驗室的聽障遺傳學家，對應中低所得國家約 80% 學齡聽障兒童未就學；FLi Sci 創辦人 Gabriel Reyes，對應 OECD 資料中弱勢學生有 37% 的科學表現落後、優勢學生則為 12%；以及只受過高中教育的周口店古人類學家賈蘭坡，對應 55-64 歲與 25-34 歲成人在高等教育上 17 個百分點的世代落差。成果包括為盲人社群製作的 20 張觸覺生物學圖、涵蓋 5 大類 20 個主題，以及——直接與其乾實驗相連——以 FoundryUI 作為運算蛋白質設計初學者的教學載體。該頁面本身同時提供互動動畫版與純文字替代版，這正是把包容性原則套用在自己的 wiki 上。","ihp":"46 stakeholder interactions across local and international surveys, potential-customer interviews, expert discussions, industry meetings, written proposals and community seminars, organised into a five-stage framework with stakeholders classified into four groups by how they affect the team and how the team affects them, plus a closing 'Feedback to Future' section that explains how they decided which feedback to prioritise and revisited stakeholders to reflect. The clearest evidence that the integration was real is that it changed the project's own name: they started with 'Expelliodor — Expel the Odor', then, prompted by social scientists on stigma, asked whether 'expel' implied that odour is something everyone should eliminate, and why axillary odour should be judged differently from hair or eye colour. They concluded that underarm odour is a natural physiological trait rather than a flaw to be corrected and that managing it should be a matter of choice, and changed the slogan to 'Expel the Odor, on Your Terms' — keeping the scientific goal while adding personal autonomy. Medical experts pushed safety, industry professionals pushed real-world feasibility, and the whole design philosophy of not broadly suppressing skin bacteria or blocking sweat glands follows from that engagement.","ihp_zh":"46 次利害關係人互動，涵蓋本地與國際問卷、潛在客戶訪談、專家討論、產業會議、書面提案與社群講座，組織成一套五階段框架，並依「他們如何影響團隊」與「團隊如何影響他們」把利害關係人分成四類，最後附一個「Feedback to Future」段落，說明他們如何決定要優先處理哪些意見，以及如何回頭再找利害關係人反思。整合確實發生過的最明確證據是，它改了專題自己的名字：他們一開始用「Expelliodor — Expel the Odor」，之後在社會科學研究者就汙名化提問的促使下，自問「expel（除去）」是否暗示體味是每個人都該消除的東西，以及為什麼腋下體味要被用和髮色或眼睛顏色不同的標準評價。他們的結論是，腋下體味是自然的生理特徵、不是待矯正的缺陷，要不要處理它應該是個人選擇，於是把標語改成「Expel the Odor, on Your Terms」——保留科學目標，同時加上個人自主。醫學專家推動安全性，產業人士推動實際可行性，而整個「不廣泛抑制皮膚細菌、不阻塞汗腺」的設計哲學，正是從這些交流而來。","realWorld":"The entrepreneurship case is grounded in population genetics rather than vague market size: the ABCC11 odour-associated allele occurs at roughly 99.99% in African, 97.48% in European, 96.05% in Oceanian, 92.42% in American, 62.22% in Southern Asian and 21.54% in Eastern Asian populations, so even in East Asia where it is least common the absolute population means tens of millions may be affected — and limited public awareness compounds misunderstanding, stigma and discrimination. The team position Expelliodor against the actual failure modes of existing products (masking fragrances, aluminium-salt antiperspirants that suppress perspiration, and broad antibacterials that disturb the axillary microbiome) and argue their three strategies are complementary in time: the precursor binder captures what is already there, CGTase continuously modifies newly secreted precursor, and the transporter binder blocks uptake. CGTase thermostability optimisation was undertaken specifically for industrial production and transportation, which is why heat resistance during storage was a design objective at all.","realWorld_zh":"創業論證建立在族群遺傳學上、而不是模糊的市場規模：與體味相關的 ABCC11 等位基因在非洲族群出現率約 99.99%，歐洲 97.48%、大洋洲 96.05%、美洲 92.42%、南亞 62.22%、東亞 21.54%，因此即使在出現率最低的東亞，以絕對人口計仍可能有數千萬人受影響——而公眾認知不足又加劇了誤解、汙名與歧視。團隊把 Expelliodor 對照既有產品真正的失效模式來定位（以香味遮蓋、以鋁鹽止汗劑抑制排汗、以廣效抗菌劑擾亂腋下微生物相），並主張他們的三套策略在時間上互補：前驅物結合子捕捉已經存在的前驅物、CGTase 持續修飾新分泌的前驅物、運輸蛋白結合子則阻斷攝入。CGTase 的熱穩定性最佳化是專為工業生產與運輸而做，這也是儲存期間的耐熱性之所以成為設計目標的原因。","partners":["GreatBay-SCIE (Shenzhen College of International Education)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6133/wiki/drylab/model/overview-fig3.avif","caption":"The funnel-shaped decision-gated workflow: successive evaluation gates remove designs from a large generated space until a small testing set remains, with each gate more computationally expensive than the last. Designed explicitly so a high school team with limited wet-lab resources spends molecular dynamics time only on candidates that already survived cheap co-folding filters.","caption_zh":"漏斗狀的決策關卡流程：一道道評估關卡把設計從龐大的生成空間中逐步剔除，直到剩下一小組進入測試，而每一道關卡的運算成本都比前一道更高。這是刻意設計的，讓一支濕實驗資源有限的高中隊伍只把分子動力學的時間花在已通過便宜共折疊過濾的候選上。","credit":"Team GreatBay-SCIE, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6133/wiki/drylab/model/overview-fig6a-u.avif","caption":"Four RFdiffusion3 precursor binders plotted as computational metric against measured A412 signal reduction, with MM/GBSA binding free energy and both the mean and the standard deviation of MD ligand RMSD over 10-50 ns. All three MD metrics showed the expected trend in this branch — while the same metrics failed in the Proteina-Complexa branch, which the team report and explain rather than omit.","caption_zh":"四個 RFdiffusion3 前驅物結合子，以運算指標對實測 A412 訊號降幅作圖，指標包括 MM/GBSA 結合自由能，以及 10-50 ns 間分子動力學配體 RMSD 的平均值與標準差。在這一支中三個分子動力學指標都呈現預期趨勢——而同樣的指標在 Proteina-Complexa 那一支則失效，團隊選擇把這點報出並加以解釋，而非略過。","credit":"Team GreatBay-SCIE, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6133/wiki/drylab/model/overview-fig8b.avif","caption":"Close-up of the inward-facing PepTSh transporter (PDB 6EXS) showing the extracellular electrostatic network as dashed contacts linking K64 to E323 and connecting R184, D182, E340 and R337. Comparing this against the same region in an outward-facing homology model, where those contacts are broken, is what defined the binder's target interface.","caption_zh":"朝內構形的 PepTSh 運輸蛋白（PDB 6EXS）特寫，以虛線接觸顯示胞外靜電網絡，連結 K64 與 E323，並串起 R184、D182、E340 與 R337。把這張圖與朝外同源模型中同一區域（那些接觸已斷開）相比，正是界定結合子標的介面的依據。","credit":"Team GreatBay-SCIE, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6133/wiki/drylab/model/overview-fig9c.avif","caption":"The selected target interface on the extracellular surface of PepTSh: orange hotspot residues bordering a green hydrophobic patch on the blue extracellular face. These features exist only in the inward-facing conformation, so a binder that holds them is designed to block the inward-to-outward transition that published molecular dynamics identified as the rate-limiting step of transport.","caption_zh":"選定的標的介面位於 PepTSh 的胞外表面：藍色胞外面上，橘色的熱點殘基圍繞著綠色的疏水區塊。這些特徵只存在於朝內構形，因此一個能抓住它們的結合子，設計上即是要阻斷已發表分子動力學所指出的速率決定步驟——由內向外的轉換。","credit":"Team GreatBay-SCIE, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Add a Characterize stage before Design: write down the biological mechanism, the exact target and the application environment, and turn them into an explicit design specification that becomes the literal input to your tool — GreatBay's specification to use the (S) stereoisomer and verify chirality after generation prevented a whole class of silent AI-design error. Then plot every computational score you used against the wet-lab outcome and report the correlation, including the honest finding that gating on a metric removes the variance you would need to validate it.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"在 Design 之前加上一個 Characterize 階段：把生物機制、精確標的與應用環境寫下來，並轉成一份明確的設計規格，讓它直接成為工具的輸入——GreatBay 在規格中規定使用 (S) 立體異構物、並在生成後驗證掌性，這一步就擋掉了一整類無聲無息的 AI 設計錯誤。接著把你用過的每一個運算指標對濕實驗結果作圖、報告相關性，連同那個誠實的發現也一併報出：拿某個指標當關卡篩選，會把你驗證該指標所需的變異量給消掉。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/greatbay-scie/","https://2026.igem.wiki/greatbay-scie/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/greatbay-scie/software/","https://2026.igem.wiki/greatbay-scie/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/greatbay-scie/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/greatbay-scie/measurement/","https://2026.igem.wiki/greatbay-scie/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/greatbay-scie/inclusivity/","https://2026.igem.wiki/greatbay-scie/education/","https://2026.igem.wiki/greatbay-scie/entrepreneurship/"],"rank":47},"6145":{"team":"MIT-MAHE","id":"6145","section":"Undergrad","country":"India","village":"Food & Agriculture / Manufacturing","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/mit-mahe/","projectTitle":"MAHEK","projectTitle_zh":"MAHEK","tagline":"Sustainable cuminaldehyde from Pseudomonas putida, and NetFlux, a web tool that turns a genome-scale metabolic model into a drawable pathway and a ranked list of knockouts.","tagline_zh":"用 Pseudomonas putida 永續生產枯茗醛，並開發 NetFlux——一個把基因組尺度代謝模型化成可繪製路徑與剔除策略排序清單的網頁工具。","summary":"MAHEK addresses the fragrance industry's dependence on petrochemical synthesis and wasteful seed extraction by producing cuminaldehyde biologically. The chassis is Pseudomonas putida F1, a solvent-tolerant soil bacterium that already makes cuminaldehyde as an intermediate in p-cymene degradation; CRISPR-Cas9-mediated homologous recombination knocks out cymC, the p-cumic aldehyde dehydrogenase, arresting the pathway exactly at the target compound. The dry lab's deliverable is NetFlux, a React + FastAPI web application that compresses a genome-scale metabolic model into a readable 'production corridor' using a novel extraction algorithm (SCOPE) and then pools OptKnock and OptForce into one co-ranked list of knockout and regulation strategies, each traced to the gene and linked to BiGG. The team also won the Inclusivity Award for work with visually impaired learners that ended in Vision Empower adopting their tactile models for use in schools across India.","summary_zh":"MAHEK 針對香料產業依賴石化合成、以及種子萃取耗費資源的問題，改以生物方式生產枯茗醛（cuminaldehyde）。宿主是 Pseudomonas putida F1，一株耐溶劑的土壤細菌，它在 p-cymene 降解途徑中本來就會產生枯茗醛作為中間產物；以 CRISPR-Cas9 介導的同源重組剔除 cymC（p-cumic 醛脫氫酶），讓途徑恰好停在目標化合物。乾實驗的交付成果是 NetFlux，一個 React + FastAPI 的網頁應用程式，它以自創的擷取演算法（SCOPE）把基因組尺度代謝模型壓縮成一條可讀的「生產走廊」，再把 OptKnock 與 OptForce 的結果匯整成單一的共同排序清單，列出剔除與調控策略，每一項都追溯到對應基因並連結到 BiGG。該隊也以針對視障學習者的工作獲得包容性獎，成果是 Vision Empower 採用了他們的觸覺模型，用於印度各地的學校。","awards":["Best Software — Nominee (Undergrad)","Inclusivity Award — Winner (Undergrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"React + TypeScript single-page frontend split into three modules (parameter panel, pathway map viewer, interventions table) sharing one run state; FastAPI backend with Pydantic request/response schemas, auto-generated OpenAPI 3.1 documentation and a Swagger UI at /docs; a JobManager running strain design on a bounded background worker pool so heavy requests do not time out; SQLite (mfghub.db) as the model/reaction/metabolite/gene/medium catalogue, rebuilt from the GEMs on every server image build; and Docker Compose bringing up database, API and web client together. Core science runs on COBRApy.","frameworks_zh":"React + TypeScript 的單頁前端分成三個模組（參數面板、路徑圖檢視器、干預策略表格），共用同一份執行狀態；FastAPI 後端採 Pydantic 的請求／回應結構，自動生成 OpenAPI 3.1 文件並在 /docs 提供 Swagger UI；以 JobManager 在有上限的背景工作者池上執行菌株設計，避免繁重的請求逾時；以 SQLite（mfghub.db）作為模型／反應／代謝物／基因／培養基的目錄，每次建置伺服器映像時都由 GEM 重新產生；並以 Docker Compose 一次啟動資料庫、API 與網頁用戶端。核心科學運算跑在 COBRApy 上。","dataviz":"Pathways are drawn as interactive metabolic maps flowing strictly left to right, with line width proportional to mass flow, metabolites as nodes carrying compartment suffixes, reactions as arrows colour-coded by their FVA annotation, and the substrate-to-target corridor explicitly highlighted. Hovering a reaction opens an inspection card with reaction name and ID, knockout-candidate status, flux and FVA range, coupling and bounds, subsystem, gene associations and gene rules, and its producers and consumers. Each click of Generate opens its parameters in a new tab so settings can be compared side by side. Results export as GraphML, JSON and CSV straight from the browser. The interventions table shows a baseline header (wild-type growth rate, yield floor and ceiling) against which every ranked design is judged, and separates committed 'Ranked Designs' from weaker single-reaction 'Hypotheses (leads)', with the wiki telling users not to compare yield numbers across the two tables.","dataviz_zh":"路徑以互動式代謝圖繪製，嚴格由左至右流動，線寬與質量流成正比，代謝物為節點並帶有區室後綴，反應為箭頭並依其 FVA 註解上色，由基質到目標產物的走廊則被明確標示強調。將游標停在某個反應上會開啟檢視卡，列出反應名稱與 ID、是否為剔除候選、通量與 FVA 範圍、耦合關係與上下界、所屬子系統、基因關聯與基因規則，以及它的生產者與消耗者。每次點選 Generate 都會在新分頁開啟當次參數，方便並排比較設定。結果可直接從瀏覽器匯出為 GraphML、JSON 與 CSV。干預策略表格以一列基準值為標頭（野生型生長速率、產率下限與上限），作為評判每一項排序設計的依據，並把已確信的「Ranked Designs」與較弱的單一反應「Hypotheses (leads)」分開，wiki 上也告訴使用者不要跨這兩張表比較產率數字。","datascience":"Benchmarked without a ground truth by defining what a useful pathway must do and measuring that instead. SCOPE was run on 9 GEMs with up to 5 target products each, 40 organism-product pairs in total: 100% of extracted pathways were fully connected from substrate to target, and the mean corridor was 55.1 reactions against a mean model size of 934, i.e. 7.8% of the network (models up to 1,762 reactions reduced to about 55). Essential reactions were identified independently with FVA and then checked for recall: 20.3 essential reactions per product on average, 17.5 retained, overall recall 0.863, above 0.90 in five of nine organisms, with the weakest cases (iJN1463 at 0.616, iJN1026 at 0.719) reported rather than hidden. Eleven curated GEMs ship with the tool, covering bacteria, a cyanobacterium, an archaeon, yeast and a diatom. The metabolic model behind the wet lab extended iJN1463 with the full p-cymene degradation route (cymA, cymB, cymC, cmtA-cmtE), linking to native metabolism through OP4ENH.","datascience_zh":"在沒有真實標準的情況下進行基準測試，做法是改為定義一條有用的路徑必須做到什麼，然後量測它。SCOPE 在 9 個 GEM 上執行，每個最多 5 個目標產物，共 40 組物種—產物配對：所有擷取出的路徑都 100% 從基質到目標完整連通，走廊平均 55.1 個反應，相對於平均模型規模 934 個反應，即網路的 7.8%（最多 1,762 個反應的模型被縮減到約 55 個）。必需反應另以 FVA 獨立判定，再檢查召回率：每個產物平均 20.3 個必需反應，保留 17.5 個，整體召回率 0.863，在九個物種中有五個高於 0.90，而表現最差的案例（iJN1463 為 0.616、iJN1026 為 0.719）是公開報告而非隱藏。工具內附十一個經整理的 GEM，涵蓋細菌、一種藍綠菌、一種古菌、酵母與一種矽藻。濕實驗背後的代謝模型則把 iJN1463 擴充為完整的 p-cymene 降解路線（cymA、cymB、cymC、cmtA-cmtE），並透過 OP4ENH 與原生代謝相連。","software":"NetFlux solves two linked problems in metabolic engineering: genome-scale models are too large to read, and strain-design algorithms waste most of their compute on reactions that can never carry flux. Its five-stage pipeline is the substance. Stage 1 solves FBA then pFBA and converts the flux distribution into a Mass Flow Graph (nodes = reactions, edges = metabolite mass flow). Stage 2 applies FASTCC against a fixed consistency threshold to strip blocked reactions, which the team identifies as the single largest source of computational expense. Stage 3 is SCOPE, their GUDIE-derived extractor: log-normalise the heavy-tailed edge weights, compute a flux-coupling score per reaction against the target, seed an interest signal at the target and propagate it with Personalised PageRank, combine coupling and interest into a per-edge score, expand outward over a bounded number of hops admitting reactions above a threshold anchored to the target's immediate neighbourhood, then an optional repair step that closes a broken corridor with a flux-weighted shortest path. Stage 4 annotates the corridor with FVA so each reaction is typed as essential-and-fixed, flexible, or a natural up/downregulation candidate. Stage 5 pools OptForce and OptKnock and co-ranks their proposals into one ordered list, resolving each to a gene linked to BiGG. Two design decisions stand out for reuse: the REST API is versioned, OpenAPI 3.1-specified and language-agnostic with async job polling (submit, get a job_id, poll), and all compute is deliberately RAM-only, with uploaded models referenced by short-lived tokens, a 30-minute SessionCache, and nothing a client submits ever written to disk or database. Users can upload their own GEM as .json or .sbml. It is self-hosted rather than publicly deployed: 'git clone https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/mit-mahe/netflux && docker compose up --build', then http://localhost:5173/, with stated system requirements of 2-4 GB RAM, any modern multi-core CPU and no GPU. A video guide and a step-by-step interpretation guide are on the wiki, and the limitation is stated plainly: constraint-based predictions describe what the network allows at steady state, not kinetics or regulation, so every strategy is a wet-lab hypothesis. Repo: https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/mit-mahe/netflux (team repo https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/mit-mahe).","software_zh":"NetFlux 解決代謝工程中兩個相連的問題：基因組尺度模型太大而無法閱讀，而菌株設計演算法把大部分運算浪費在永遠不可能帶有通量的反應上。它的五階段流程才是實質內容。階段 1 先解 FBA，再解 pFBA，並把通量分布轉換為質量流圖（節點＝反應，邊＝代謝物的質量流）。階段 2 以固定的一致性門檻套用 FASTCC，剔除受阻反應，該隊指出這正是運算成本最大的單一來源。階段 3 是 SCOPE，他們由 GUDIE 衍生出的擷取器：先把重尾分布的邊權重做對數正規化，計算每個反應相對於目標的通量耦合分數，在目標處播下興趣訊號並以個人化 PageRank 傳播，把耦合與興趣合成每條邊的分數，再在有上限的跳數內向外擴展，納入分數高於某門檻（該門檻以目標的鄰近區域為基準）的反應，最後還有一個選用的修補步驟，以通量加權的最短路徑補起斷掉的走廊。階段 4 以 FVA 註解走廊，讓每個反應被歸類為必需且固定、具彈性，或可自然上調／下調的候選。階段 5 匯整 OptForce 與 OptKnock，把兩者的提案共同排序成單一清單，並各自解析到連結 BiGG 的基因。兩項設計決策特別值得借用：REST API 有版本控制、以 OpenAPI 3.1 規格描述、與語言無關，並採非同步工作輪詢（送出、取得 job_id、輪詢）；以及所有運算刻意只在記憶體中進行，上傳的模型以短效期權杖引用，搭配 30 分鐘的 SessionCache，用戶端送出的任何資料都不會寫入磁碟或資料庫。使用者可上傳自己的 GEM，格式為 .json 或 .sbml。它採自行架設而非公開部署：「git clone https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/mit-mahe/netflux && docker compose up --build」，然後開啟 http://localhost:5173/，所列系統需求為 2-4 GB RAM、任何現代多核心 CPU，不需 GPU。wiki 上有影片指南與逐步判讀指南，限制也寫得很直白：基於約束的預測描述的是網路在穩態下允許什麼，而不是動力學或調控，因此每一項策略都是待濕實驗驗證的假說。程式庫：https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/mit-mahe/netflux（團隊程式庫 https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/mit-mahe）。","stack":["React","TypeScript","FastAPI","Pydantic","Python","COBRApy","SQLite","Docker","Docker Compose","OpenAPI 3.1 / Swagger UI","REST / JSON-over-HTTP","GraphML","SBML","BiGG database","KaTeX (wiki maths)","iGEM GitLab"],"techniques":["Flux Balance Analysis (FBA)","parsimonious FBA (pFBA)","Flux Variability Analysis (FVA)","Mass Flow Graph representation of metabolism","FASTCC flux-consistency pruning","flux coupling analysis","Personalised PageRank network propagation","GUDIE-style user-defined subgraph extraction","flux-weighted shortest-path repair","OptKnock bilevel knockout search","OptForce intervention search","co-ranking of competing optimisation outputs","recall benchmarking against independently derived essential reactions","CRISPR-Cas9 homologous recombination (wet lab)"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Sessions were run across India in English, Hindi, Telugu, Kannada and Marathi so language would not be a barrier, and deliberately extended beyond students: the team visited old age homes to learn how residents' associations with traditional scents had changed over their lifetimes, then introduced them to synthetic biology. Workshops included household-materials DNA extraction from bananas at Purple Space Library Manipal (50 students, grades 1-7, split by age group), recombinant DNA via insulin at GenWise Camp, and deeper project discussion with grade 11-12 biology students at Vidya Mandir Chennai. Teachers were walked through each protocol step so they could keep running the demonstration after the team left. 'Beyond Sight', an audio-only podcast, carried five conversations with visually impaired professionals (a radio jockey, a geneticist, the founder of assistive-technology company TorchIT, an ophthalmologist, and one of only three blind women to have submitted before the Supreme Court of India). A Colourblind Awareness Day Instagram series ran on 6 September.","publicEngagement_zh":"活動在印度各地以英語、印地語、泰盧固語、坎納達語與馬拉提語進行，讓語言不成為障礙，並刻意延伸到學生以外的族群：該隊走訪養老院，了解住民對傳統香氣的連結如何隨一生改變，再向他們介紹合成生物學。工作坊包括在 Purple Space Library Manipal 用家中材料從香蕉萃取 DNA（50 位學生，1 至 7 年級，依年齡分組）、在 GenWise Camp 以胰島素講解重組 DNA，以及在 Vidya Mandir Chennai 與 11、12 年級生物學生進行更深入的專案討論。他們也帶老師走過每一個實驗步驟，讓團隊離開後老師能繼續操作示範。純音訊的 podcast「Beyond Sight」收錄五場與視障專業人士的對談（一位廣播主持人、一位遺傳學家、輔助科技公司 TorchIT 的創辦人、一位眼科醫師，以及印度最高法院僅有三位曾出庭陳述的盲人女性之一）。色盲意識日的 Instagram 系列則於 9 月 6 日發布。","ihp":"Stakeholder analysis walked the whole cumin supply chain, from traders who buy directly from farmers to internationally working perfumers, finding that each group holds a different version of the same problem. Hard numbers anchor the premise: India supplies about 70-80% of world cumin, the 2026 crop was projected at 9.0-9.2 million bags against roughly 11 million in 2025 (a 15-20% decline), hydrodistillation yields about 2.56% essential oil, and cuminaldehyde is a fraction of that. The decisive conversation was with Givaudan, which revealed that fragrance houses procure whole cumin essential oil rather than isolated cuminaldehyde; this redirected the team's target customer from fragrance houses to aroma compound manufacturers, where demand for isolated, sustainably produced cuminaldehyde actually exists. The inclusivity work was itself integrated rather than decorative: conversations with Vision Empower (IIIT Bangalore) identified that Indian educational structures restrict visually impaired students from science, and the team then built tactile models, trialled them with Mrs Nagarathna, a visually impaired educator, revised on her feedback, and tested with a ninth-grade student. Fixes were deliberately minimal and buildable from cheap materials: the existing DNA model distinguished bases only by colour, so each base got a texture instead (adenine smooth tape, thymine jute, guanine bubble wrap, cytosine velvet) wrapped around the existing model so it did not need rebuilding; the mitosis model's components were only drawn on, so they were rebuilt in clay with pipe-cleaner chromosomes. Vision Empower approved both the content and the models and will use them across their associated schools. A separate conversation with an Indian Sign Language expert established that, unlike ASL, ISL has no centralised place to learn it, which the team records as a gap they did not close.","ihp_zh":"利害關係人分析走遍整條小茴香供應鏈，從直接向農民收購的貿易商到跨國工作的調香師，發現每個群體掌握的是同一個問題的不同版本。具體數字支撐了前提：印度供應全球約 70-80% 的小茴香，2026 年產量預估為 900 萬至 920 萬包，相對於 2025 年的約 1,100 萬包（下降 15-20%），水蒸餾的精油產率約 2.56%，而枯茗醛只佔其中一部分。關鍵的一場對話來自 Givaudan，對方透露香料公司採購的是整支小茴香精油，而非分離純化的枯茗醛；這使該隊把目標客戶從香料公司轉向香氣化合物製造商，因為對分離、永續生產之枯茗醛的需求其實存在於那裡。包容性工作本身是整合進專案的，不是裝飾：與 Vision Empower（IIIT Bangalore）的對談指出印度的教育結構限制了視障學生接觸科學，該隊因此製作觸覺模型，先與視障教育者 Nagarathna 女士試用、依她的回饋修改，再與一位九年級學生測試。修改刻意最小化、並可用便宜材料自行製作：原有的 DNA 模型只用顏色區分鹼基，於是每個鹼基改以不同質感區分（腺嘌呤用平滑膠帶、胸腺嘧啶用麻布、鳥嘌呤用氣泡紙、胞嘧啶用絨布），直接包覆在原模型上，不必重做；而細胞分裂模型的構造原本只是畫上去的，便改用黏土重做，染色體以毛根製作。Vision Empower 核可了內容與模型，並將在其合作學校推廣使用。另一場與印度手語專家的對談則確認，與美國手語不同，印度手語沒有集中的學習管道，該隊把這點記錄為自己沒有解決的缺口。","realWorld":"A consumer survey found the barrier is information rather than opposition, with respondents already aware of land use, extraction and climate pressures and nearly half willing to pay slightly more for lower environmental impact, though more were worried about long-term effects of ingredients made by engineered microorganisms. Producer-side work found that Indian companies import aroma compounds from China, the UAE and France despite domestic cumin dominance, and that price is the deciding factor for buyers because raw material cost passes straight to consumers. The team wrote 'An iGEMer's Guide to Upscaling', a structured upscaling and biomanufacturing guide, after finding no iGEM-oriented resource bridging flask scale to industrial scale, and 'The Aroma Atlas', a catalogue of everyday scents, their active ingredients and current production methods, as a starting point for teams looking for compounds worth making sustainably. Six cym operon genes were submitted to the Registry as basic parts (BBa_26CFFF0H, BBa_26R7VUFV, BBa_26MJ8EI9, BBa_26SS8791, BBa_26AS8UG2, BBa_26AW7YAF).","realWorld_zh":"一份消費者調查發現，障礙在於資訊而非反對：受訪者本來就知道土地利用、萃取與氣候壓力，近半數願意為較低的環境衝擊多付一點錢，不過更多人擔心工程微生物所製成分的長期影響。生產端的調查則發現，印度企業儘管本國小茴香產量居主導地位，仍從中國、阿聯與法國進口香氣化合物，而價格是買方的決定因素，因為原料成本會直接轉嫁給消費者。該隊發現沒有任何面向 iGEM、能從搖瓶規模接到工業規模的資源，於是寫了結構化的放大與生物製造指南《An iGEMer's Guide to Upscaling》；另外還做了《The Aroma Atlas》，彙整日常香氣、其活性成分與目前的生產方式，作為其他隊伍尋找值得永續生產之化合物的起點。cym 操縱子的六個基因已作為基礎元件提交到 Registry（BBa_26CFFF0H、BBa_26R7VUFV、BBa_26MJ8EI9、BBa_26SS8791、BBa_26AS8UG2、BBa_26AW7YAF）。","partners":["Vision Empower / IIIT Bangalore","Givaudan","Score Foundation / Project Eyeway","TorchIT","Navjeevan Blind School, Pune","Purple Space Library Manipal","GenWise Camp","Vidya Mandir Senior Secondary School, Chennai","Manipal Academy of Higher Education","Anthropic (sponsor)","BioRender, GenScript, IDT, NEB, SnapGene (sponsors)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6145/wiki/dry-lab/software/fig-2-architecture.avif","caption":"NetFlux architecture: React/TypeScript frontend, FastAPI backend with Pydantic schemas and a bounded JobManager worker pool, over a SQLite model catalogue and precomputed Mass Flow Graphs.","caption_zh":"NetFlux 架構：React/TypeScript 前端、搭配 Pydantic 結構與有上限 JobManager 工作者池的 FastAPI 後端，底層是 SQLite 模型目錄與預先計算的質量流圖。","credit":"Team MIT-MAHE, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6145/wiki/dry-lab/software/fig-1-pipeline.avif","caption":"The five-stage NetFlux pipeline: Mass Flow Graph construction, FASTCC pruning, SCOPE/GUDIE corridor extraction, FVA annotation, and the pooled OptKnock/OptForce design engine.","caption_zh":"NetFlux 的五階段流程：建構質量流圖、FASTCC 修剪、SCOPE/GUDIE 走廊擷取、FVA 註解，以及匯整 OptKnock/OptForce 的設計引擎。","credit":"Team MIT-MAHE, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6145/wiki/dry-lab/software/fig-4-user-guide.avif","caption":"An extracted production corridor drawn automatically from a genome-scale model, flowing left to right with line width proportional to mass flow and reactions coloured by FVA annotation.","caption_zh":"由基因組尺度模型自動繪出的生產走廊，由左至右流動，線寬與質量流成正比，反應則依 FVA 註解上色。","credit":"Team MIT-MAHE, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6145/wiki/dry-lab/software/fig-6-user-guide.avif","caption":"The intervention strategy suite: ranked designs with yield floor, retained growth, coupling strength and the specific gene to edit, separated from weaker exploratory leads.","caption_zh":"干預策略組合：已排序的設計列出產率下限、保留的生長、耦合強度與應編輯的具體基因，並與較弱的探索性線索分開。","credit":"Team MIT-MAHE, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"When there is no ground truth to benchmark against, define what a correct output must satisfy and measure that: NetFlux's credibility rests on three published numbers (100% corridor connectivity, 7.8% of the network retained, 0.863 recall of independently FVA-derived essential reactions), with the weakest organisms named. A research centre should also copy the ephemeral-compute design, user-uploaded models held in RAM behind short-lived tokens and never written to disk, which makes a shared analysis service usable with data people will not hand over.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"當沒有真實標準可供對標時，就定義一個正確輸出必須滿足哪些條件，然後去量測它：NetFlux 的可信度建立在三個公開數字上（走廊連通性 100%、僅保留網路的 7.8%、對獨立以 FVA 推得之必需反應的召回率 0.863），而且把表現最差的物種指名出來。研究中心也值得照抄它的短暫運算設計——使用者上傳的模型只存在記憶體中，以短效期權杖存取，絕不寫入磁碟，這讓一個共用的分析服務也能處理別人不願交出的資料。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/mit-mahe/","https://2026.igem.wiki/mit-mahe/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/mit-mahe/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/mit-mahe/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/mit-mahe/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/mit-mahe/inclusivity","https://2026.igem.wiki/mit-mahe/implementation","https://2026.igem.wiki/mit-mahe/contribution","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/mit-mahe/netflux"],"rank":33},"6151":{"team":"Uni-Padua-IT","id":"6151","section":"Undergrad","country":"Italy","village":"Space","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/uni-padua-it/","projectTitle":"C.O.S.M.I.C. (Cyanobacterial Oxygen Supply for Martian Inhabitant Complexes)","tagline":"A Nostoc-based life-support chassis for Mars, plus ReTIsigner, an open codon optimiser for the 35,799 hosts other tools ignore.","summary":"Uni-Padua-IT engineered the filamentous cyanobacterium Nostoc sp. PCC 7120 as a Martian life-support organism: it fixes CO2 into breathable oxygen, degrades the perchlorates that poison Martian water (via native NarB and a heterocyst-compartmentalised pcrABD plus chlorite dismutase), and carries pprA from Deinococcus radiodurans for radiation-damage repair, behind a copper-dependent MazF kill switch. Because no free codon optimiser listed their chassis, they forked TIsigner into ReTIsigner, a frequency-weighted codon optimiser that reads any of the 35,799 Kazusa codon usage tables, enforces GC bounds, actively excises RFC restriction sites and reports CAI, GC and translation-initiation opening energy. ReTIsigner was validated in silico over 100 sequences and four hosts, then in vivo: a ReTIsigner-optimised eYFP gave a 2.16-fold common-effect increase in specific fluorescence across DH5-alpha and BL21 (p = 0.002, permutation test stratified by strain). They also built an open-source acoustic (piezo + Arduino) bubble sensor so oxygen production can be followed without opening a sealed culture.","awards":["Best Software — Winner (Undergrad)","Best Wiki — Winner (Undergrad)","Best Space Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"SvelteKit single-page frontend built from scratch, talking to a Flask backend over a single documented HTTP endpoint (POST /optimise); a worker pool behind Flask shells out to the compiled scientific binaries. The whole stack is shipped as a two-stage Docker image (Node.js 22 build stage; Miniconda runtime pinning Python 3.6.9, ViennaRNA 2.5.1 and Infernal 1.1.5) exposing port 5050.","dataviz":"Results view compares input against each optimised sequence in a results card showing CAI, GC content and opening energy, so sequences no longer have to be analysed one at a time in external tools. A built-in guided tour walks a first-time user through every field of the run configuration. Exports in three reproducible formats (CSV, PDF, FASTA), each recording the full run configuration plus the computed analyses. Validation figures (specific-fluorescence bar charts and ratio plots with 95% CIs) are published as SVG on the wiki, and the system is explained with two architecture diagrams: the POST /optimise request path and one iteration of the annealing loop.","datascience":"In silico benchmark over 100 coding sequences optimised for four hosts spanning roughly 31-75% GC, recording GC, CAI, opening energy and failure rate with and without a codon usage table: supplying a table cut the failure rate from 52% to 2% while leaving opening energy essentially unchanged (mean difference +/-0.06 kcal/mol). Wet-lab validation used independent cultures as the unit of replication, three cultures per sample each in technical triplicate, fluorescence compared at matched optical density rather than fixed time, two detection channels, and a permutation test stratified by strain; the team explicitly states the confidence interval (about 1.6-2.8x) and what the data does not license them to claim.","software":"ReTIsigner is a free, Apache 2.0-licensed codon optimiser for non-model hosts, and it is the clearest example this year of forking an existing scientific tool rather than rebuilding one. The team started from TIsigner (Bhandari, Lim & Gardner), contacted its authors for feedback on their proposal, and then added four things TIsigner lacked: frequency-weighted synonymous codon sampling driven by any Kazusa codon usage table (35,799 organisms) instead of one-amino-acid-one-codon, an optional GC bound enforced as a feasibility filter, active position-targeted removal of restriction sites with a re-check for newly introduced sites, and in-app CAI/GC analysis per output sequence. The restriction-site work is the headline engineering result: optimising perchlorate reductase subunit A for Nostoc under RFC 10 and RFC 1000 constraints was still running after 15 hours under the original random-substitution behaviour, and completed in seconds afterwards, yielding registry part BBa_268WDVEB. Architecturally the optimiser sits behind POST /optimise so it is usable headlessly without the Svelte interface, and the Docker image removes the platform problem that ViennaRNA and Infernal binaries create on Windows ('docker build -t retisigner . && docker run -p 5050:5050 retisigner'). It ships a user guide, a development guide documenting the system and its API calls, a video tutorial (https://video.igem.org/w/rN6WnodTKYxiNitzfSUVZ3) that optimises BBa_E0040 GFP for Clostridium acetobutylicum ATCC 824, and a public repository at https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uni-padua-it/retisigner-svelte (team repo: https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/uni-padua-it). It is self-hosted via Docker rather than offered as a hosted public web service, which is the one gap: there is no URL a stranger can click. They also positioned ReTIsigner honestly against the field, reproducing Table 1 of Demissie et al. (2025) and adding their own row with a tilde rather than a tick in the CAI column, and comparing feature-by-feature against the two previous iGEM codon optimisers (HebrewU 2018, MIT 2023). They published an open call for collaboration on 9 August 2026 offering to optimise any team's sequence for their chassis and received no replies, and they say so on the wiki.","stack":["SvelteKit","Svelte","Node.js 22","Python 3.6.9","Flask","Docker (multi-stage)","Miniconda/Conda","ViennaRNA 2.5.1 (RNAplfold)","Infernal 1.1.5","REST/HTTP API","Apache 2.0","iGEM GitLab","Arduino (hardware)"],"techniques":["Simulated annealing search","frequency-weighted synonymous codon sampling","mRNA translation-initiation opening-energy minimisation","Codon Adaptation Index (CAIcal/Sharp-Li definition)","GC-bound feasibility filtering","active restriction-site excision","Kazusa codon-usage-table parsing","permutation testing stratified by strain","in silico benchmarking across GC-spanning hosts","acoustic (piezoelectric) frequency-sweep sensing"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A public survey on space research and biotechnology directly reshaped the team's communication: 76.5% of respondents rated using living organisms for oxygen and water highly while only 28.2% rated colonisation highly, so the team separated the usefulness of the technology from support for settling Mars; 42.2% knew little or nothing about GMOs, so explanations of what they modify and why were rewritten more accessibly; and 94.8% called a genetic safety system fundamental or very important, so the kill switch and confined bioreactor were given more space. Education activities grew out of the same consultations.","ihp":"Human practices is written as a sequence of questions with an explicit 'what we changed' and, unusually, a 'what we couldn't fix' for each. Consultations with photosynthesis and cyanobacteria professors (Nicoletta La Rocca, Daniela Billi) cut the cold-tolerance module. iGEM Darmstadt 2025, who had built the same perchlorate constructs in B. subtilis, warned them off pcrABCD's oxygen sensitivity, which led to testing native NarB first and then compartmentalising pcrABD in heterocysts. A presentation to NASA's Open Science Data Repository Analysis Working Group moved the radiation module from survival-at-high-dose to genome integrity over generations, and pushed them toward a terrestrial use case (perchlorate in groundwater near propellant plants) when the Moon turned out to have no perchlorate. ESA flight-operations engineers (Davide Vertuani, Paolo Ferri) made them reason about the journey, not just arrival. Philosopher Telmo Pievani and space-habitat designer Serena Crotti changed how the bioreactor is framed within a crew's daily life. Most relevant to a dry-lab centre: they took their hardware manual and code to an instrumentation professor and an electronics PhD student (Simone Del Favero, Samuele Faccin) before publishing, and as a result weakened their own claim (the sensor detects gas bubbles, it does not measure oxygen), redrew the circuit with no crossing wires, documented timing resolution, and added a table separating proven from untested.","realWorld":"The team identified a terrestrial application independent of any Mars mission: perchlorate contaminates groundwater near propellant and pyrotechnics manufacturing and is regulated, and biological removal is already an active research area. They were unable to secure an ionising radiation source (INFN Legnaro's Van de Graaff accelerator unavailable; IOV Padova's linear accelerator caps at roughly 6 Gy/min against a 6 kGy LD50), and report that the pprA radiation claim is therefore untested rather than glossing over it.","partners":["iGEM Darmstadt 2025","NASA Open Science Data Repository Analysis Working Group","European Space Agency (flight operations)","University of Padua (Biology, Chemistry, Information Engineering)","University of Rome Tor Vergata","TISIGNER authors (Bhandari, Lim, Gardner)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6151/wiki/software/new-frontend.avif","caption":"The ReTIsigner interface the team built from scratch in SvelteKit, replacing the original TIsigner form.","credit":"Team Uni-Padua-IT, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6151/wiki/software/guided-tour.avif","caption":"The in-app guided tour that walks a first-time user through configuring a whole optimisation run.","credit":"Team Uni-Padua-IT, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6151/wiki/software/results-opt.avif","caption":"The results card: input sequence against an optimised output, with CAI and GC content computed in-app.","credit":"Team Uni-Padua-IT, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6151/wiki/software/request-schema.avif","caption":"System architecture: the SvelteKit frontend posts a run to Flask, which hands it to a worker pool that shells out to RNAplfold and Infernal.","credit":"Team Uni-Padua-IT, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6151/wiki/software/optimisation-schema.avif","caption":"One iteration of the simulated annealing search, with the team's two additions: restriction-site removal before scoring and a GC-bound feasibility check.","credit":"Team Uni-Padua-IT, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Fork and extend an existing, cited scientific tool instead of building a new one, and validate the extension at the bench: ReTIsigner's credibility comes from a 2.16-fold wet-lab expression result, a 52%-to-2% failure-rate benchmark, and a published 'what we are entitled to claim' section that names its own limits. A research centre should also copy their packaging discipline, one Docker command plus a documented HTTP endpoint so the engine is reusable headlessly, and their habit of sending documentation to an outside instrumentation expert before publishing it.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/uni-padua-it/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uni-padua-it/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/uni-padua-it/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/uni-padua-it/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/uni-padua-it/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/uni-padua-it/judging","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/uni-padua-it/retisigner-svelte","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/uni-padua-it"],"rank":59},"6157":{"team":"UCAS-China","id":"6157","section":"Undergrad","country":"China","village":"Therapeutics","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/","projectTitle":"PARCEL","tagline":"An inhaled, protein-based mRNA carrier that makes airway cells produce their own asthma medicine.","summary":"PARCEL is an inhaled mRNA delivery platform built from elastin-like polypeptides (ELPs) rather than lipid nanoparticles. The fusion protein ELP-Pum2-EEP13 uses Pum2 to grab mRNA carrying a PRS tag in its 3' UTR, ELP phase separation to encapsulate and protect it, an endosomal escape peptide to get out of the endosome, and a Sortase A-conjugated anti-UPK1B scFv to target airway club cells; the cargo is mRNA for SLPI (inhibiting neutrophil elastase and the mucus hypersecretion it triggers) plus a lower dose of IFN-lambda-1 (antiviral defence and Th2 suppression). It won 1st Runner-up and Best Integrated Human Practices because the stakeholder work genuinely steered the science: clinicians moved the project from rescue therapy to maintenance therapy, and an asthma mechanism researcher killed one of the two original cargoes outright. The dry lab is unusually complete, modelling the whole chain from E. coli production through nebulizer aerosol deposition to a PK-PD readout in FEV1 and FeNO, with every module feeding the next.","awards":["1st Runner-up (Undergrad)","Top 10 (Undergrad)","Best New Composite Part — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Wiki — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Integrated Human Practices — Winner (Undergrad)","Best Therapeutics Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Six connected modules sharing parameters and declared input-output relationships. (1) Production: a SimBiology ODE model of a quorum-sensing kill switch (LuxI/LuxRm A1 variant, pLuxRm-driven lysis) combining growth-dependent dilution with AHL kinetics, swept across Anderson promoters to find the one that lyses the culture just before ELP phase transition - this chose the promoter the wet lab used. (2) Assembly: AlphaFold 3 predicted the three fusion-protein monomers (1052-1322 residues), coarse-grained into Martini 3 and run in GROMACS for 2-3 microseconds at 298 K, 1 bar, 150 mM NaCl, 50 mg/mL protein, with pLDDT used to justify stabilising the Pum2 fold while leaving ELP flexible; alongside this they built CAPE (Coverage and Assembly Prediction for Protein Ensembles), a reduced free-energy model calibrated against wet-lab data, and used Bayesian optimization over CAPE as the objective to redistribute ELP repeats around Pum2 instead of brute-forcing every combination. (3) Pulmonary delivery: MPPD v3.04 on the adult Yeh-Schum five-lobe geometry screened log-normal aerosol size distributions, flow rates and inhaled volumes against deposition in the last three conducting generations per lobe, then ANSYS Fluent CFD simulated 3D airway transport, feeding a distal airway and airway-surface-liquid transport model and a reference cell-composition mapping that converts deposition into surface contacts per club cell. (4) Intracellular release: a hybrid ODE-stochastic model of one particle per endosome (median 560 nm, ~2,400 fusion chains and therefore 2,400 EEP copies per particle), tracking acidification, ELP disassembly, EEP-mediated membrane opening and RNA degradation to output intact cytosolic RNA over time, with intact RNA tracked separately from fluorescent label. (5) PK-PD: a four-compartment model (bone marrow, blood, airway wall, epithelial lining fluid) with 25 species, 53 assignment rules and 51 reactions, adapted from Gadkar et al.'s severe asthma immune network, giving four clinical readouts - FeNO, FEV1, relative goblet-cell count and 15-minute mucin release - used to compare SLPI:IFN-lambda-1 payload ratios and dosing frequency. (6) Response prediction: an affine mapping baseline plus residual CellFlow (flow matching) trained on public cytokine-perturbation scRNA-seq.","dataviz":"The model landing page opens with a scripted animation that walks the whole mechanism in sequence - the E. coli shell fills with protein, lyses, chains assemble into PARCEL, the particle travels into the bronchi, binds a club-cell receptor, is endocytosed, disassembles, releases mRNA, and mucus drops one step per round - with replay and skip controls and a text fallback when JavaScript is off. AlphaFold monomer structures are embedded as interactive viewers with pLDDT and protein-region colouring and cartoon/C-alpha toggles, so a reader can see directly why Pum2 was treated as rigid and ELP as flexible. The wiki also carries font-size controls (A-/Default/A+) for accessibility. On the software side, the AeroEase Android app turns raw device timestamps into an expandable-card Overview with a seven-day activity chart and a date-filtered History, and the FeroEase app plots live temperature, pH and OD600 with a falling-trend detector that flags the harvest window.","datascience":"Two concrete pieces. The target screen: using the Human Lung Cell Atlas they compared healthy adult club cells against other lung epithelial cells on fold change, adjusted p-value and detection fraction, and from 68 genes passing the criteria selected UPK1B - 2.28-fold enriched, adjusted p = 0.00559, RNA detected in 45.92% of club cells versus 3.43% of other epithelial cells. They then checked antibody accessibility (Human Surfaceome; UniProt O75841, 260 aa, four transmembrane regions, extracellular stretches at 37-60 and 108-229) and cross-tissue selectivity (archived GTEx: 0.11 TPM lung vs 21.90 TPM bladder; Human Protein Atlas showing membranous expression in urothelium), and stated plainly that UPK1B is not club-cell exclusive so the analysis prioritises an experimental candidate rather than demonstrating selective targeting. The response-prediction benchmark is equally honest: affine mapping cut mean-expression error 7.1% against predicting no change and beat the mean-response baseline, while the nonlinear residual CellFlow model improved some mean-expression predictions but worsened distributional agreement and the selected RNA panels - so they kept affine as the reference model and named cross-donor validation and RNA reconstruction as the open problems. Tasks were set up as donor-held-out rotations on GSE249307 and GSE246368 with unpaired source and target cells.","software":"Four software deliverables. AeroEase, an Android companion app for the nebulizer, syncs ESP32-C3 button timestamps over BLE through a validated handshake with checksum, session and duplicate checks, clock calibration from the phone, and acknowledgement only after durable storage, then presents them as a locally stored medication-use diary with daily and seven-day counts, date-filtered history, CSV export, and a rule-based offline assistant that answers questions without any cloud call; the team repeatedly states the records document device actions, not delivered dose or confirmed inhalation. FeroEase, written in Flutter, monitors the two-stage fermentation over Wi-Fi with temperature, pH, stirring control and a falling-OD600 trend detector that identifies the lysis harvest window a bench fermenter does not report. The bioinformatics pipeline for club-cell target selection is the third. A browser-based quiz game supports the education activities. Hardware: AeroEase is a portable vibrating-mesh nebulizer on an ESP32-C3 with rechargeable power, session logging, BLE, a gravity-fed reservoir and physically separated liquid and electronics compartments in a modular 3D-printed housing; FeroEase is an ESP32-S3 two-stage culture platform with pH and temperature sensing, controlled heating, motor stirring and transmitted-light OD600 tracking. Build resources and a user manual with source code access are published on the wiki.","stack":["AlphaFold 3","GROMACS","Martini 3 coarse-grained force field","MATLAB SimBiology","MPPD v3.04 (Multiple-Path Particle Dosimetry)","ANSYS Fluent","CellFlow (flow matching)","Human Lung Cell Atlas (HLCA)","Human Surfaceome","UniProt","GTEx","Human Protein Atlas","GEO (GSE249307, GSE246368)","Flutter","Android / Kotlin","ESP32-C3","ESP32-S3","Bluetooth Low Energy","SQLite (on-device)"],"techniques":["Coarse-grained molecular dynamics","Reduced free-energy modelling (custom CAPE model)","Bayesian optimization for sequence design","Quorum-sensing ODE modelling with growth dilution","Computational fluid dynamics aerosol deposition","Regional lung dosimetry screening","Hybrid ODE-stochastic single-endosome simulation","Compartmental PK-PD with Hill-function assignment rules","Differential expression with detection-fraction filtering","Affine distribution mapping","Flow matching for single-cell perturbation response","Donor-held-out cross-validation","Membrane topology and surfaceome annotation screening","SWOT analysis"],"frameworks_zh":"六個相互連接的模組，共用參數並明確宣告輸入輸出關係。(1) 生產：以 SimBiology 建立一個群體感應自殺開關的 ODE 模型（LuxI/LuxRm A1 變異體，由 pLuxRm 驅動裂解），結合生長造成的稀釋與 AHL 動力學，掃過各個 Anderson 啟動子，找出恰好在 ELP 相變之前讓培養液裂解的那一個——這決定了濕實驗室使用的啟動子。(2) 組裝：以 AlphaFold 3 預測三個融合蛋白單體（1052-1322 個殘基），粗粒化為 Martini 3 並在 GROMACS 中以 298 K、1 bar、150 mM NaCl、50 mg/mL 蛋白濃度執行 2-3 微秒，並以 pLDDT 作為「穩定 Pum2 摺疊、同時保留 ELP 柔性」的依據；同時他們建立了 CAPE（Coverage and Assembly Prediction for Protein Ensembles），一個以濕實驗室資料校準的簡化自由能模型，並以 CAPE 為目標函數做貝氏最佳化，重新分配 Pum2 周圍的 ELP 重複單元，而不是暴力枚舉所有組合。(3) 肺部遞送：以 MPPD v3.04 在成人 Yeh-Schum 五肺葉幾何上，針對各肺葉最後三個傳導分支世代的沉積量，篩選對數常態的氣霧粒徑分布、流速與吸入體積；再以 ANSYS Fluent CFD 模擬三維呼吸道傳輸，接著餵入末端呼吸道與呼吸道表面液層的傳輸模型，以及一個參考細胞組成對映，把沉積量換算為每個棒狀細胞的表面接觸數。(4) 細胞內釋放：一個每個內體一顆粒的 ODE-隨機混合模型（中位粒徑 560 nm，每顆約 2,400 條融合蛋白鏈、因此有 2,400 份 EEP），追蹤酸化、ELP 解組裝、EEP 媒介的膜開孔與 RNA 降解，輸出隨時間變化的完整細胞質 RNA 量，並把完整 RNA 與螢光標記分開追蹤。(5) PK-PD：一個四區室模型（骨髓、血液、呼吸道壁、上皮襯液），含 25 個物種、53 條指派規則與 51 個反應，改編自 Gadkar 等人的重度氣喘免疫網路，產出四項臨床讀值——FeNO、FEV1、相對杯狀細胞數與 15 分鐘黏液素釋放量——用於比較 SLPI:IFN-lambda-1 的載量比與給藥頻率。(6) 反應預測：一個仿射對映的基線，加上以公開細胞激素擾動 scRNA-seq 訓練的殘差式 CellFlow（flow matching）。","dataviz_zh":"模型首頁一開始就是一段腳本化動畫，依序走過整個機制——E. coli 外殼充滿蛋白、裂解、蛋白鏈組裝成 PARCEL、顆粒進入支氣管、結合棒狀細胞受體、被內吞、解組裝、釋出 mRNA，而黏液每一輪下降一階——並附重播與跳過控制，在 JavaScript 關閉時還有純文字替代版本。AlphaFold 單體結構以互動檢視器嵌入，可依 pLDDT 與蛋白區域著色、並切換 cartoon/C-alpha 呈現，讓讀者直接看出為何 Pum2 被視為剛性、ELP 被視為柔性。wiki 另附字級控制（A-/預設/A+）以提升無障礙性。軟體方面，AeroEase Android 應用程式把裝置的原始時間戳轉成可展開卡片的總覽，含七日活動圖表與可依日期篩選的歷史紀錄；FeroEase 應用程式則即時繪出溫度、pH 與 OD600，並以下降趨勢偵測器標出收取時機。","datascience_zh":"兩項具體工作。標靶篩選：他們以 Human Lung Cell Atlas 比較健康成人棒狀細胞與其他肺上皮細胞的倍數變化、校正後 p 值與偵測比例，從 68 個通過門檻的基因中選出 UPK1B——富集 2.28 倍、校正後 p = 0.00559，RNA 在 45.92% 的棒狀細胞中被偵測到，其他上皮細胞僅 3.43%。接著他們檢查抗體可及性（Human Surfaceome；UniProt O75841，260 個胺基酸，四個跨膜區，細胞外區段在 37-60 與 108-229）與跨組織選擇性（存檔的 GTEx：肺 0.11 TPM 對膀胱 21.90 TPM；Human Protein Atlas 顯示尿路上皮有膜上表現），並直言 UPK1B 並非棒狀細胞專屬，因此這份分析是在排序一個可供實驗的候選，而非證明選擇性標靶。反應預測的基準測試同樣誠實：仿射對映相較於「預測沒有變化」把平均表現量誤差降低 7.1%，也優於平均反應基線；而非線性的殘差 CellFlow 模型雖改善了部分平均表現量預測，卻使分布一致性與所選的 RNA panel 變差——因此他們保留仿射模型作為參考模型，並把跨捐贈者驗證與 RNA 重建列為未解問題。任務設定為在 GSE249307 與 GSE246368 上以捐贈者留出輪替，來源細胞與目標細胞未配對。","software_zh":"四項軟體產出。AeroEase 是霧化器的 Android 伴隨應用程式，透過 BLE 同步 ESP32-C3 按鈕的時間戳，採用帶檢查碼、session 與重複檢查的驗證握手、以手機校正時鐘，並且只有在資料持久儲存後才回覆確認；接著把這些資料呈現為本機儲存的用藥日誌，含每日與七日次數、依日期篩選的歷史、CSV 匯出，以及一個規則式的離線助理，不需任何雲端呼叫即可回答問題；團隊反覆強調這些紀錄記載的是裝置動作，而非實際遞送劑量或已確認的吸入。FeroEase 以 Flutter 撰寫，透過 Wi-Fi 監測兩階段發酵，提供溫度、pH、攪拌控制，以及一個 OD600 下降趨勢偵測器，用來判定一般實驗室發酵槽不會回報的裂解收取窗口。第三項是用於棒狀細胞標靶選擇的生物資訊管線。另有一個瀏覽器版益智遊戲支援教育活動。硬體方面：AeroEase 是建立在 ESP32-C3 上的可攜式振動篩網霧化器，具可充電電源、session 記錄、BLE、重力供液儲槽，以及在模組化 3D 列印外殼中實體隔開的液體與電子艙；FeroEase 則是一套 ESP32-S3 兩階段培養平台，具 pH 與溫度感測、受控加熱、馬達攪拌與穿透光 OD600 追蹤。製作資源與含原始碼取得方式的使用手冊都公開在 wiki 上。"},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education was designed from two findings in their own clinician interviews and 461-person questionnaire: patients stop medication once they feel better, and parents refuse to start it for children out of fear of side effects, so compliance - not just awareness - became the target. Activities are segmented by audience. For children: a booth with biology-themed games at the Huairou District National Science Popularization Month fair (September 2026), doubling as a questionnaire collection point, plus a Life Science Classroom proposal for fifth and sixth graders in Huairou primary schools teaching respiratory tract structure through illustrations and interactive demos, published as a downloadable PDF so other teams can run it. For university students: an iGEM Winter Camp training new members with offline wet-lab tutorials (plasmid extraction, PCR, homologous recombination, protein purification) and online dry-lab and modelling tracks, and an annual Microbial Painting competition open to all majors as a recruitment funnel - which failed to produce the expected colony patterns, and the team published the three reasons why (cell sedimentation from static suspension, insufficient streaking density, IPTG induction of EGFP suppressing growth) and used it to teach participants that negative results are normal and troubleshooting is the skill. For the general public: a Public Science Day stall and a browser quiz game on synthetic biology and iGEM.","ihp":"The team formalised its own cycle, RCSF (Reflect-Connect-Share-Feedback), as a deliberate parallel to the DBTL engineering cycle, and ran the project through nine documented iterations with 20 individuals, teams and institutions across six defined communities (academia, medical professionals, industry, supervisors, patients and families, the public), 44 asthma patient representatives and 419 public representatives from under-10s to over-60s. Each community is introduced with who they are, what they know, and why their position matters. The changes are specific and traceable. Doctor Fei Wang's input moved the project from rapid-acting therapy to asthma maintenance treatment, which reset the whole target population. Professor Huaiyong Chen, who studies respiratory disease mechanisms, explained that in asthma many club cells differentiate into mucus-producing goblet cells - supporting the shift away from immune cells to airway epithelium - and told them that NKX2-1, one of their two original cargoes, matters in development but has little effect in adulthood, so it was dropped and SLPI took its place. Professor Pingsheng Liu's survey of liposome, LNP and polymeric carrier limitations fed directly into the ELP carrier rationale and the protein sequence design. Professor Yufei Xia flagged subtle flaws in the experimental design and walked them through the standard in vivo/in vitro validation workflow. Yaozhong Cao, a former iGEMer, argued with them about target specificity, which is upstream of the UPK1B antibody screen. Professor Xiaoru Huang, an ethics of science and technology researcher, reviewed the biosafety and bioethics discipline. They contacted the Huairou District Bureau of Landscaping and Forestry about local pollen and catkin management, grounding the project in Beijing's own regulation (the Measures implementing the Forest Law, effective 1 January 2026) and in observed thunderstorm asthma cases. Patient work was handled with explicit informed consent and privacy statements, and the questionnaire reports its own demographics (21 recovered, 21 currently medicated, 419 unaffected). The team states its guiding principle as 'local people solving local problems', and the HP group's standing job was to track every subteam's bottlenecks and feed external input back into each one.","realWorld":"The entrepreneurship work is a self-critical commercial assessment rather than a pitch. The team states outright that PARCEL's case must rest on defined unmet needs rather than technological novelty, and tabulates the strengths as well as the limitations of inhaled corticosteroids, bronchodilators and biologics before positioning PARCEL as a non-hormonal, lower-frequency, modular maintenance option. The SWOT names real weaknesses: delivery efficiency and duration of expression were only shown in HEK293T in vitro, so mucus, mucociliary clearance, local enzymes and immune uptake remain unaddressed; a combined protein-plus-mRNA product multiplies CMC burden across ELP molecular weight, purity, impurity profile and phase-transition behaviour and mRNA sequence integrity and stability, then payload ratio, condensate characteristics, batch consistency and storage; and the team lists the expertise it does not have (toxicology, regulatory affairs, clinical development, IP, market access). Opportunities are equally concrete - the modular Pum2/PRS-tag design means a new payload needs no new carrier, CAS institutes supply the analytical capability they lack, and China's pay-for-performance medical insurance pilot offers a reimbursement pathway for a therapy that can demonstrate efficacy. They commit to re-reviewing the SWOT at each development milestone.","partners":["Institute of Biophysics, Chinese Academy of Sciences","Institute of Process Engineering, Chinese Academy of Sciences","Institute of Chemistry, Chinese Academy of Sciences","Tsinghua University","Haihe Hospital, Tianjin University","Inner Mongolia International Hospital of Mongolian Medicine","Qingdao Municipal Hospital","Central Hospital of Kaifeng, Henan Province","Meishan Cardio Cerebrovascular Disease Hospital","242 Hospital, Shenyang Medical College","Weikang Pingsheng (Beijing) Biotechnology Co., Ltd.","Huairou District Bureau of Landscaping and Forestry, Beijing","iGEM ENTER team (Harvard Medical School)","Conference of China iGEMer Community (CCiC)","Huairou District primary schools","GenScript","MathWorks","SnapGene"],"publicEngagement_zh":"教育是從團隊自己的臨床訪談與 461 人問卷中的兩項發現設計出來的：病患一覺得好轉就停藥，而家長因為害怕副作用而拒絕讓孩子開始用藥——因此目標變成服藥遵從性，而不只是知識認知。活動依受眾分層。對兒童：在懷柔區全國科普月市集（2026 年 9 月）設攤，辦生物主題遊戲，同時兼作問卷蒐集點；另提出一份「生命科學課堂」方案，針對懷柔區小學五、六年級學生，透過插畫與互動示範教授呼吸道結構，並以可下載 PDF 發布，讓其他隊伍也能照著做。對大學生：辦 iGEM 冬令營培訓新成員，實體課程教濕實驗（質體萃取、PCR、同源重組、蛋白質純化），線上則有乾實驗與建模組；還有一年一度、不限系所的「微生物繪畫」競賽作為招募漏斗——這項活動並未長出預期的菌落圖樣，團隊公開了三個原因（靜置懸浮液造成細胞沉降、塗盤密度不足、IPTG 誘導 EGFP 抑制生長），並藉此教參與者：負面結果是正常的，排除問題才是真功夫。對一般大眾：公眾科學日攤位，以及一個關於合成生物學與 iGEM 的瀏覽器益智遊戲。","ihp_zh":"團隊把自己的循環形式化為 RCSF（Reflect-Connect-Share-Feedback），刻意與工程的 DBTL 循環平行，並讓專案走過九次有記錄的迭代，涉及六個明確界定社群（學界、醫療專業人員、產業、指導教師、病患與家屬、公眾）中的 20 位個人、團隊與機構，以及 44 位氣喘病患代表和 419 位從未滿 10 歲到 60 歲以上的公眾代表。每個社群在介紹時都說明他們是誰、知道什麼，以及為何他們的立場重要。改變具體且可追溯。王飛醫師的意見把專案從速效治療轉向氣喘長期控制治療，整個目標族群因此重設。研究呼吸道疾病機制的陳懷勇教授說明，在氣喘中許多棒狀細胞會分化為產生黏液的杯狀細胞——支持了從免疫細胞轉向呼吸道上皮的方向——並告訴他們兩個原始貨物之一的 NKX2-1 在發育期重要、但在成年期影響甚微，因此該基因被捨棄，由 SLPI 取代。劉平生教授對微脂體、LNP 與高分子載體限制的梳理，直接進入 ELP 載體的立論與蛋白序列設計。夏宇飛教授指出實驗設計中細微的缺陷，並帶他們走過標準的體內／體外驗證流程。前 iGEMer 曹耀中與他們就標靶專一性爭論過，而這正位於 UPK1B 抗體篩選的上游。研究科技倫理的黃小茹教授審閱了生物安全與生物倫理的規範。他們也就當地花粉與柳絮管理聯繫懷柔區園林綠化局，把專案扣回北京自身的法規（《森林法》實施辦法，2026 年 1 月 1 日生效）與觀察到的雷雨氣喘案例。涉及病患的工作都有明確的知情同意與隱私聲明，問卷也報告自身的人口組成（21 位已康復、21 位正在用藥、419 位未受影響）。團隊把自己的指導原則寫為「在地的人解決在地的問題」，而 HP 組的常態任務就是追蹤各子組的瓶頸，並把外部意見回灌到每一組。","realWorld_zh":"創業部分是一份自我批判的商業評估，而不是推銷說詞。團隊直接寫明，PARCEL 的立論必須建立在明確未被滿足的需求之上，而不是技術新穎性，並在把 PARCEL 定位為非荷爾蒙、較低給藥頻率、模組化的長期控制選項之前，先列表比較吸入型皮質類固醇、支氣管擴張劑與生物製劑各自的優點與限制。SWOT 直指真正的弱點：遞送效率與表現持續時間只在 HEK293T 的體外系統中展示過，因此黏液、黏液纖毛清除、局部酵素與免疫吞噬都還沒處理；蛋白加 mRNA 的複合產品會讓 CMC 負擔倍增，橫跨 ELP 分子量、純度、雜質輪廓與相變行為，以及 mRNA 序列完整性與穩定性，再加上載量比、凝聚體特性、批次一致性與保存；團隊也列出自己不具備的專業（毒理、法規事務、臨床開發、智慧財產、市場准入）。機會同樣具體——模組化的 Pum2/PRS 標籤設計意味著換新貨物不需要新載體；中科院各所能提供他們缺少的分析能力；中國的醫保按療效付費試點，為能展示療效的療法提供了給付途徑。他們承諾在每個開發里程碑重新檢視這份 SWOT。"},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6157/wiki/humanpractices/hp-overview0.avif","caption":"The Human Practices overview: 20 individuals and institutions across six defined communities, 44 asthma patient representatives and 419 public representatives, mapped onto nine project iterations of the team's own RCSF cycle.","credit":"Team UCAS-China, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"人類實踐總覽：六個明確界定社群中的 20 位個人與機構、44 位氣喘病患代表與 419 位公眾代表，對映到團隊自創 RCSF 循環的九次專案迭代。"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6157/wiki/software/upk1b-volcano-2.avif","caption":"The club-cell antibody target screen: UPK1B highlighted in the differential-expression volcano against other lung epithelial cells, 2.28-fold enriched with adjusted p = 0.00559 and detected in 45.92% of club cells.","credit":"Team UCAS-China, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"棒狀細胞抗體標靶篩選：UPK1B 在與其他肺上皮細胞比較的差異表現火山圖中被標出，富集 2.28 倍、校正後 p = 0.00559，並在 45.92% 的棒狀細胞中被偵測到。"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6157/wiki/hardware/aeroease/pictures/fig6-hardware-2-yhz.avif","caption":"The AeroEase portable vibrating-mesh nebulizer prototype, built on an ESP32-C3 with BLE session logging and a modular 3D-printed housing separating the liquid reservoir from the electronics.","credit":"Team UCAS-China, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"AeroEase 可攜式振動篩網霧化器原型，建立在 ESP32-C3 上，具 BLE session 記錄，模組化 3D 列印外殼把液體儲槽與電子元件隔開。"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6157/wiki/education/education-huairou0.avif","caption":"The team's booth at the Huairou District National Science Popularization Month fair, running biology games with children while collecting the public asthma-perception questionnaire.","credit":"Team UCAS-China, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"團隊在懷柔區全國科普月市集的攤位，與兒童進行生物遊戲，同時蒐集公眾氣喘認知問卷。"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6157/wiki/software/app-charts-3up.avif","caption":"The AeroEase Android app turning raw BLE device timestamps into a medication-use diary with daily and seven-day activity charts, date-filtered history and CSV export, all stored on the phone.","credit":"Team UCAS-China, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"AeroEase Android 應用程式把 BLE 裝置的原始時間戳轉為用藥日誌，含每日與七日活動圖表、依日期篩選的歷史與 CSV 匯出，全部儲存在手機本機。"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Steal the RCSF cycle: UCAS-China gave human practices the same named, repeatable four-step loop (Reflect, Connect, Share, Feedback) that engineering gets with DBTL, mapped every stakeholder into one of six communities with a stated reason for including them, and then showed nine iterations where the loop closed - including dropping a cargo gene because one researcher said it does nothing in adults. A school research centre can run that loop on any project, and the second lesson is just as cheap to copy: publish what failed, as they did with the microbial painting that never grew, and the reasons why.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/model-part1","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/model-part2","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/model-part3","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/model-part4","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/model-part5","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/model-part6","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/inclusivity","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucas-china/measurement"],"projectTitle_zh":"PARCEL","tagline_zh":"一種吸入式、以蛋白質為基礎的 mRNA 載體，讓呼吸道細胞自己製造氣喘藥。","summary_zh":"PARCEL 是一個吸入式 mRNA 遞送平台，以類彈性蛋白多肽（ELP）而非脂質奈米顆粒構成。融合蛋白 ELP-Pum2-EEP13 以 Pum2 抓取 3' UTR 帶有 PRS 標籤的 mRNA，利用 ELP 的相分離把它包裹並保護起來，再以內體逃脫肽離開內體，並以 Sortase A 接合的抗 UPK1B scFv 鎖定呼吸道棒狀細胞（club cell）；所攜帶的貨物是 SLPI 的 mRNA（抑制嗜中性球彈性蛋白酶及其引發的黏液過度分泌），加上較低劑量的 IFN-lambda-1（抗病毒防禦與 Th2 抑制）。本專案獲得亞軍與 Best Integrated Human Practices，因為利害關係人工作真的導引了科學：臨床醫師把專案從急救治療轉向長期控制治療，而一位氣喘機制研究者則直接否決了兩個原始貨物之一。乾實驗室的完整度相當罕見，從 E. coli 生產、經霧化器氣霧沉積，一路模擬到以 FEV1 與 FeNO 表示的 PK-PD 讀值，每一個模組都餵給下一個。","gemsTakeaway_zh":"把 RCSF 循環學走：UCAS-China 讓人類實踐擁有和工程的 DBTL 一樣有名字、可重複的四步迴圈（Reflect、Connect、Share、Feedback），把每位利害關係人歸入六個社群之一並說明納入理由，然後展示了九次確實閉合的迭代——包括因為一位研究者說某基因在成年期沒有作用，就直接拿掉一個貨物基因。學校的研究單位在任何專案上都能跑這個迴圈；第二個教訓同樣便宜好學：公開失敗的部分，就像他們公開那場始終沒長起來的微生物繪畫活動，以及失敗的原因。","rank":212},"6158":{"team":"HongKong-JSS","id":"6158","section":"High School","country":"Hong Kong","village":"Agriculture","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-jss/","projectTitle":"MerMAID - MerR-based Mercury Assay for In-field Detection","projectTitle_zh":"MerMAID - MerR-based Mercury Assay for In-field Detection","tagline":"One mercury ion among a billion molecules of water - a living sensor that glows red, read by a portable detector fed by a modular sample-extraction platform.","tagline_zh":"十億個水分子中的一個汞離子——一個會發紅光的活體感測器，由可攜式偵測器讀取，前端再接上模組化的樣品萃取平台。","summary":"HongKong-JSS is a four-school joint team (Y.W.C.A. Hioe Tjo Yoeng College, Po Leung Kuk Celine Ho Yam Tong College, Pentecostal School, Yan Oi Tong Tin Ka Ping Secondary School) that built a complete mercury-screening system for agricultural water and soil: a MerR-regulated E. coli biosensor expressing mRFP1e, a portable modular fluorescence reader, and a motorised sample-extraction platform that turns soil and water into a standard assay input. They designed, built and tested 13 biosensor prototypes - 2 aptamer-based and 11 protein-based - of which two protein designs responded to Hg2+, with the best showing low background, a response down to about 1 ppb (0.005 uM, roughly sixfold below the WHO drinking-water guideline of 6 ug/L), no cross-response to Cd2+, Pb2+ or Zn2+ at the concentrations tested, and retained function after alginate encapsulation. It took 1st Runner-up Grand Prize in the High School section and won Best Village Project, and the reason is visible on every page: the wiki's standing rule is that every number carries its conditions and a source, and the team separates demonstrated results from deployment claims more rigorously than most university teams.","summary_zh":"HongKong-JSS 是四校聯隊（Y.W.C.A. Hioe Tjo Yoeng College、Po Leung Kuk Celine Ho Yam Tong College、Pentecostal School、Yan Oi Tong Tin Ka Ping Secondary School），為農業用水與土壤做出一整套汞篩檢系統：一個由 MerR 調控、表現 mRFP1e 的 E. coli 生物感測器、一台可攜式模組化螢光讀取儀，以及一座可把土壤與水轉換成標準檢測輸入的電動樣品萃取平台。他們設計、製作並測試了 13 個感測器原型——2 個基於適體（aptamer）、11 個基於蛋白質——其中兩個蛋白質設計對 Hg2+ 有反應，表現最好的背景值低、反應可下探到約 1 ppb（0.005 uM，約為 WHO 飲用水指引值 6 ug/L 的六分之一），在測試濃度下對 Cd2+、Pb2+ 或 Zn2+ 沒有交叉反應，而且在海藻酸鈉包覆後仍保有功能。他們拿下高中組 1st Runner-up Grand Prize 與 Best Village Project，而理由在每一頁都看得見：這個 wiki 的常規是每個數字都要帶著它的條件與來源，而且團隊把「已展示的結果」和「佈署時的主張」分得比多數大學團隊更嚴格。","awards":["1st Runner-up (High School)","Top 10 (High School)","Best New Composite Part — Nominee (High School)","Best Model — Nominee (High School)","Best Hardware — Nominee (High School)","Best Presentation — Nominee (High School)","Best Village Project — Winner (Agriculture / Food & Nutrition / Fashion & Cosmetics / Art & Design)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"The headline model is a calibration-and-inverse-prediction framework rather than a mechanistic simulation, and it is unusually well executed. Image signals were defined explicitly before any fitting: colour response C = 1 - (G_pellet / G_white) from green-channel intensity measured in ImageJ on pellets photographed against a white tile, and fluorescence response F = R_pellet / R_background from red-channel intensity inside a light box, with the matched untreated control from the same run and timepoint subtracted (delta-C, delta-F) and no OD normalisation. They then fitted a log-linear model delta-S = A + b log10(c / 0.005 uM) with 0.005 uM chosen as the reference so A is directly interpretable, giving delta-C = 0.04363 + 0.07591 log10(c/0.005) and delta-F = 0.42290 + 1.08721 log10(c/0.005). Crucially, calibration and validation data were separated up front - 20 calibration measurements from four runs (2, 6, 8 and 13 October) and 10 held-out validation measurements from two further runs (14 and 15 October) for each readout, all at the four-hour timepoint across 0.005, 0.01, 0.03, 0.05 and 0.1 uM. The model was inverted to estimate unknown concentration, c-hat = 0.005 uM x 10^((delta-S - A)/b), and scored by RMSE on the held-out runs: approximately 0.0483 uM for colour and 0.0319 uM for fluorescence, with all numerical predictions included so that failures were not hidden (a 0.1 uM sample on 15 October was estimated at 0.246 uM by colour). On the hardware side they ran CAD-based dry-lab studies for a UV advanced-oxidation-process reactor, modelling fluid flow dynamics, UV photo-oxidation kinetics and lamp exposure times for both a batch quartz-tube reactor and a thin-layer millifluidic cassette, computing a residence time of 192.6 s and a modelled minimum-to-maximum light ratio of 92.2% across the 1 mm layer; the filter assembly was developed parametrically in OpenSCAD. Promoter selection also used in silico promoter-strength analysis, which predicted J23106 to be comparable to P429 and so added it as a comparison design.","frameworks_zh":"主要的模型是一套校正與反推預測的框架，而不是機制性模擬，而且執行得罕見地好。影像訊號在任何擬合之前就先明確定義：顏色反應 C = 1 - (G_pellet / G_white)，取自把菌體沉澱物放在白色磁磚上拍照後、以 ImageJ 量得的綠色通道強度；螢光反應 F = R_pellet / R_background，取自燈箱內的紅色通道強度；並扣除同一批次、同一時間點的對應未處理對照（delta-C、delta-F），不做 OD 正規化。接著擬合一條對數線性模型 delta-S = A + b log10(c / 0.005 uM)，之所以選 0.005 uM 當參考點，是為了讓 A 可直接解讀，結果為 delta-C = 0.04363 + 0.07591 log10(c/0.005) 與 delta-F = 0.42290 + 1.08721 log10(c/0.005)。關鍵在於校正與驗證資料一開始就分開——每一種讀值都有來自四個批次（10 月 2、6、8、13 日）的 20 筆校正量測，以及來自另外兩個批次（10 月 14、15 日）的 10 筆保留驗證量測，全部取第四小時的時間點，濃度為 0.005、0.01、0.03、0.05 與 0.1 uM。模型被反轉來估計未知濃度，c-hat = 0.005 uM x 10^((delta-S - A)/b)，並在保留批次上以 RMSE 評分：顏色約 0.0483 uM，螢光約 0.0319 uM，而且所有數值預測都列出來，失敗不被藏起（10 月 15 日一個 0.1 uM 的樣品，用顏色估成 0.246 uM）。硬體方面，他們為一座 UV 高級氧化程序（AOP）反應器做了基於 CAD 的乾實驗研究，為批次式石英管反應器與薄層毫流體匣兩種設計建模流體流動、UV 光氧化動力學與燈管曝照時間，算出滯留時間 192.6 s，並在 1 mm 厚的液層內模擬出 92.2% 的最小/最大光強比；濾材組件則以 OpenSCAD 參數化開發。啟動子的選擇也用了電腦模擬的啟動子強度分析，預測 J23106 與 P429 相當，因此把它加為比較用設計。","dataviz":"Presentation is built around separating what was measured from what is assumed. Charts show individual run points alongside coloured means and error bars rather than only pooled summaries, the model page plots known versus estimated concentration against a dashed perfect-prediction line with out-of-calibration-range estimates marked separately, and tables consistently split 'experimental finding' from 'design goal' and 'prototype performance' from 'deployment claim'. Every figure caption states its conditions. The hardware readout itself is a data-visualisation artefact: Detection Unit V3.0 pairs a Hamamatsu C12880 miniature spectrometer (288-pixel detector, 340-850 nm, 12 nm typical FWHM) with two ESP32-S3-N16R8 microcontrollers driving a local TFT display and a Wi-Fi-connected web interface that shows the recorded spectrum and the raw signal at a user-selected target wavelength, with online data logging, registered devices, selected-wavelength trends and recorded runs reviewable on a phone or computer. A red/amber/green status display was added later, and the team deliberately separated device status, fluorescence reading, concentration estimate and safety judgement on screen so that a green operational light cannot be misread as 'this sample is safe'.","dataviz_zh":"呈現方式圍繞著「把量到的和假設的分開」來建構。圖表會把個別批次的點與有顏色區分的平均值及誤差棒一起畫出來，而不是只給彙總值；模型頁把已知濃度對估計濃度畫在一條虛線完美預測線旁，並把落在校正範圍外的估計值另外標記；表格則一貫地把「實驗發現」與「設計目標」、「原型表現」與「佈署主張」切開。每張圖的說明都寫明其條件。硬體讀取端本身就是一件資料視覺化成品：Detection Unit V3.0 把 Hamamatsu C12880 微型光譜儀（288 像素偵測器、340-850 nm、典型半高寬 12 nm）與兩顆 ESP32-S3-N16R8 微控制器配在一起，驅動一個本機 TFT 顯示器與一個連 Wi-Fi 的網頁介面，顯示記錄到的光譜與使用者選定目標波長的原始訊號，並支援線上資料記錄、已註冊裝置、選定波長的趨勢，以及可在手機或電腦上回顧的歷史批次。紅/黃/綠狀態顯示是後來加的，而團隊刻意在畫面上把裝置狀態、螢光讀值、濃度估計與安全判斷分開，以免綠色的運作指示燈被誤讀成「這個樣品是安全的」。","datascience":"The analysis is notable for publishing its own limitations as a work plan. They state that the pooled model does not separately estimate run-to-run variation, that the reported concentrations are point estimates with no uncertainty intervals, that no detection or quantification limit has been established, and that rounded signal values were used as fitting inputs. They then specify the fixes concretely: a random-intercept mixed model delta-S_ri = A + b log10(c_ri/0.005) + u_r + e_ri with run-specific slopes only if the data support them and with convergence and singularity checks; inverse-calibration intervals that distinguish prediction for a new run from prediction for a run containing a measured reference standard; a per-run intercept correction A_r = delta-S_standard,r - b log10(c_standard/0.005) estimated from a known standard run alongside every experiment; leave-one-run-out cross-validation over six folds with the warning that selecting and evaluating on the same cross-validation results produces optimistic estimates; and comparison of the local log-linear fit against a four-parameter logistic model if data across 0.001-5 uM becomes available. They also ran and reported an exploratory sensitivity check swapping calibration runs, and honestly noted that because the validation runs were examined during that comparison they no longer constitute a completely untouched final assessment. Results-page statistics use two-sided paired t-tests across five independent paired runs with explicit notice that p-values are unadjusted for the three readouts. Hardware performance was quantified the same way: automated water delivery gave a coefficient of variation of 1.95% against 7.41% across 10 manual syringe runs, drainage retained volumes of 0.28, 0.31 and 0.30 mL (mean ~0.30 mL, about 95% liquid recovery), and reducing tubing bore from 7 mm to 1 mm over a 10 cm segment was computed to cut geometric dead volume accordingly.","datascience_zh":"這份分析最值得注意的地方，是把自己的限制當成工作計畫公開。他們寫明：彙總模型沒有單獨估計批次間變異、報告的濃度是點估計而沒有不確定區間、尚未建立偵測極限或定量極限，以及擬合輸入用的是四捨五入後的訊號值。接著他們把修法具體寫出來：一個隨機截距混合模型 delta-S_ri = A + b log10(c_ri/0.005) + u_r + e_ri，只有在資料支持時才加入批次專屬斜率，並做收斂與奇異性檢查；反向校正的區間，並區分「對一個新批次的預測」與「對一個含有已量測參考標準品的批次的預測」；每批次的截距校正 A_r = delta-S_standard,r - b log10(c_standard/0.005)，由每次實驗旁同時跑的已知標準品估得；六折的留一批次交叉驗證，並附上警語：在同一組交叉驗證結果上同時做選擇與評估會產生過於樂觀的估計；以及若未來取得 0.001-5 uM 範圍的資料，就把局部對數線性擬合與四參數邏輯斯模型比較。他們也做了並報告一次交換校正批次的探索性敏感度檢查，並誠實指出：因為驗證批次在那次比較中已被看過，它們已不再構成完全未經接觸的最終評估。結果頁的統計使用五組獨立配對批次的雙尾配對 t 檢定，並明確註明 p 值未針對三種讀值做多重比較校正。硬體效能也用同樣方式量化：自動化給水的變異係數為 1.95%，而 10 次人工針筒操作為 7.41%；排液殘留體積為 0.28、0.31 與 0.30 mL（平均約 0.30 mL，約 95% 液體回收率）；而把 10 cm 管段的管徑從 7 mm 縮到 1 mm，經計算可相應減少幾何死體積。","software":"Open hardware and firmware rather than a bioinformatics tool. The Detection Unit CAD is published in Onshape (https://cad.onshape.com/documents/2228cb45d05bdbc67479791d) and the firmware and software at https://github.com/hkjssplkchc2026/mercurysense, containing ESP32 firmware, the C12880 spectrometer driver, acquisition instructions and Python/web monitoring software, with a live monitoring web app for reviewing spectra and runs. The Extraction Unit code is at https://github.com/davidlueng986-alt/MerMAID-Extraction-Unit. An itemised bill of materials is published with a ~USD 357 core-component subtotal (LED 2x 560 nm at USD 2.60, etc.), and the team states plainly that this overshot the USD 40 affordability target stakeholders had asked for. The detection unit went through four versions (AS7343 14-channel spectral sensor in a laser-cut acrylic box, to an opaque 3D-printed enclosure with recessed lid and adjustable optical mounts, to the C12880 spectrometer with interchangeable filters, fluid handling and web interface) and the extraction platform through three, with state-machine control sequences published for the water, soil and UV-AOP modules together with error-handling tests covering pump timeouts, watchdog recovery, soil-mass checks, stirring feedback, reagent availability and weighing faults. An educational browser game, 'Small Signal: a MerMAID field school', is published as a 3-5 minute pixel-art laboratory game in which players build a biological signal path, compare an unknown sample with its controls, and decide what the evidence supports - and is labelled a beta prototype whose educational effectiveness has not yet been evaluated. Repository: https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/hongkong-jss.","software_zh":"釋出的是開源硬體與韌體，而不是生物資訊工具。Detection Unit 的 CAD 公開在 Onshape（https://cad.onshape.com/documents/2228cb45d05bdbc67479791d），韌體與軟體在 https://github.com/hkjssplkchc2026/mercurysense，內含 ESP32 韌體、C12880 光譜儀驅動程式、擷取說明與 Python/網頁監控軟體，另有一個可回顧光譜與歷史批次的即時監控網頁應用程式。萃取單元的程式碼在 https://github.com/davidlueng986-alt/MerMAID-Extraction-Unit。材料清單逐項公開，核心元件小計約 USD 357（例如 2 顆 560 nm LED 為 USD 2.60），而團隊也直說這超出了利害關係人要求的 USD 40 可負擔門檻。偵測單元走過四個版本（雷射切割壓克力盒內的 AS7343 14 通道光譜感測器，到帶內凹上蓋與可調光學固定座的不透光 3D 列印外殼，再到搭配可更換濾片、流體操作與網頁介面的 C12880 光譜儀），萃取平台走過三個版本，並公開水、土壤與 UV-AOP 模組的狀態機控制序列，以及涵蓋泵浦逾時、watchdog 復歸、土壤質量檢查、攪拌回饋、試劑可用性與秤重故障的錯誤處理測試。另有一款教育用瀏覽器遊戲「Small Signal: a MerMAID field school」，是一個 3-5 分鐘的像素風實驗室遊戲，玩家在其中建立一條生物訊號路徑、把未知樣品與其對照比較，並判斷證據能支持什麼——而它被標明為 beta 原型，教育成效尚未評估。版本庫：https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/hongkong-jss。","stack":["ImageJ (green/red channel intensity extraction)","log-linear calibration with inverse prediction","RMSE on held-out runs","planned random-intercept mixed model and leave-one-run-out cross-validation","four-parameter logistic model (proposed)","paired two-sided t-tests","Onshape CAD","OpenSCAD (parametric filter assembly)","3D printing and laser cutting","ESP32-S3-N16R8 microcontrollers","Hamamatsu C12880MA miniature spectrometer","AS7343 spectral sensor","Python / web monitoring interface","GitHub","CFD and UV photo-oxidation kinetics dry-lab simulation","alginate encapsulation"],"techniques":["pre-registered split of calibration and validation runs before fitting","control subtraction within the same run and timepoint","inverse calibration to estimate unknown concentrations","flagging estimates outside the calibration range instead of reporting them silently","including failed predictions in the error metric","exploratory calibration-set sensitivity check, with disclosure that it contaminated the held-out set","publishing a specific statistical work plan for unmodelled run-to-run variance","coefficient-of-variation comparison of automated versus manual fluid handling","spectral matching of LED, excitation filter and reporter emission to suppress background","interface design that separates device status from safety judgement"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Nine targeted outreach events reaching over 2,400 participants, organised as an explicit four-tier framework. Tier 1 (primary students and parents, over 1,600 people) ran interactive Open Day and Information Day booths at Y.W.C.A. Hioe Tjo Yoeng College and Po Leung Kuk Celine Ho Yam Tong College with strawberry DNA extraction and live gel electrophoresis demonstrations. Tier 2 (over 730 secondary peers) covered Microbiology 101 for Grade 10 students on microbe handling, laboratory safety, cleanliness and contamination prevention, and a morning assembly for 700 Grade 7-12 students that framed synthetic biology through agricultural mercury contamination and explained how cellular components can be repurposed as logic gates and biosensors. Tier 3 is the most durable: a two-day Teacher Biotech Training Workshop for 30 local school teachers covering PCR and agarose gel electrophoresis, combined with a standing loan programme letting those teachers borrow DNA samples and laboratory equipment from the team - a deliberate attempt to leave teaching capacity behind after the competition ends. Tier 4 took the work into public and civic space: an exhibitor stand at InnoEX 2026, the international innovation and technology exhibition in Hong Kong, and a presentation alongside the Drainage Services Department at its Annual Media Briefing, which put the project on an official government webpage and into local news. They also ran a street interview with 30 members of the public specifically about a 'mercury-free' produce certification label, finding unanimous support for the idea, 14 people rating it very important for public health, 12 supporting it even at higher vegetable prices, 22 willing to buy certified produce at normal prices and 4 willing to pay extra - while also recording that 19 respondents remained somewhat or very worried about engineered bacteria leaking from the sealed device against only 8 who were not, a finding they published rather than buried. The browser game 'Small Signal' extends this by teaching the reasoning - compare the unknown against its controls, then decide what the evidence can support.","publicEngagement_zh":"九場有明確對象的推廣活動、超過 2,400 位參與者，並編排成一套明示的四層架構。第一層（國小學生與家長，超過 1,600 人）在 Y.W.C.A. Hioe Tjo Yoeng College 與 Po Leung Kuk Celine Ho Yam Tong College 的開放日與資訊日設互動攤位，示範草莓 DNA 萃取與現場膠體電泳。第二層（超過 730 位中學同儕）包括為 10 年級學生開的 Microbiology 101，內容涵蓋微生物操作、實驗室安全、清潔與污染預防，以及一場 700 位 7 至 12 年級學生的朝會，從農業汞污染切入合成生物學，並說明細胞元件如何被改用成邏輯閘與生物感測器。第三層最耐久：為 30 位本地學校教師辦的兩天教師生技培訓工作坊，涵蓋 PCR 與瓊脂膠體電泳，再搭配一個常設的借用方案，讓這些教師可以向團隊借 DNA 樣品與實驗設備——這是刻意要在競賽結束後把教學能力留下來。第四層把成果帶進公共與公民空間：在香港的國際創新科技展 InnoEX 2026 設攤，並在渠務署的年度媒體簡報會上與該署一同發表，使專案登上官方政府網頁與本地新聞。他們也針對一個「無汞」農產認證標籤，對 30 位市民做街訪，發現這個想法獲得一致支持：14 人認為它對公共衛生非常重要、12 人即使蔬菜價格因此較高仍支持、22 人願意以正常價格購買認證農產、4 人願意多付錢——同時也記錄下有 19 位受訪者對工程改造細菌從密封裝置洩漏仍有些或非常擔心，而不擔心的只有 8 位；這個發現他們選擇公開而非埋掉。瀏覽器遊戲「Small Signal」則延伸這條線，教的是推論方式——先把未知樣品和它的對照比較，再判斷證據能支持什麼。","ihp":"Human Practices ran on a stated operating principle - respond promptly to stakeholder feedback, and let it drive the next hardware revision - structured across four stages and a five-question cycle (Inspiration, Intercommunication, Investigation, Implementation, Impact) with the rule that each engagement must end in either a documented change or a documented reason for no change. There is also a five-tier Target User Prioritisation Pyramid which they explicitly label a working framework rather than a validated exposure ranking, and which puts underserved communities near suspected contamination sources such as informal e-waste processing sites above farmers, researchers, regulators and the general public. The traceable changes: the Drainage Services Department's guidance moved them off the chromoproteins used in earlier projects onto mRFP1e as a dual readout - visible colour for non-specialists plus a more sensitive fluorescence channel for quantification - and DSD, the Water Supplies Department and university researchers together pushed them to test lower concentrations, benchmark against international reference values, and assess cross-response to interfering heavy metals (hence the Cd2+/Pb2+/Zn2+ selectivity panel). Koo's Farm and local wet market vendors demanded numerical readings instead of qualitative colour indicators, which is the direct reason the AS7343 14-channel sensor was replaced by the wavelength-resolved Hamamatsu C12880 and why a numerical display and web readout exist. University professors said soil particulates must be removed before optical measurement and recommended a modular design, which produced the separate water, soil and planned organic-mercury extraction modules. Users reported excessive syringe force on the V1 filter stack (2 um pre-filter plus 0.45 um membrane), so manual syringe delivery was replaced by pump-driven dosing - measured as an improvement from 7.41% to 1.95% coefficient of variation. On-site trials at Blue Girl Organic Farm and Yeung Marine Products Limited with agricultural soil extracts, irrigation water and fish pond water (run without GM bacteria, since they could not legally be taken out of the lab) produced requests for clearer indicators and better protection against water and mud, answered with a red/amber/green status display, a reinforced housing, and maintenance access and modularity designed into the proposed V4.0. A second public survey combining street interviews with hands-on demonstrations for 195 people found 87.7% more confident that ordinary people could participate in checking soil and water safety and 84.1% finding the digital readout easy to understand - and the team immediately noted that perceived confidence and readability do not establish analytical accuracy, and separated device status from safety judgement in the interface as a direct result. More Happy Farm said plainly that not every farmer wants to own a device, which pushed them towards a service model. Throughout, they keep stating what their evidence does not cover: a response in a controlled biological assay does not establish accurate measurement in soil extracts, reliable operation of the complete device, or suitability for regulatory decisions.","ihp_zh":"人類實踐依一條寫明的運作原則進行——對利害關係人的回饋迅速回應，並讓它驅動下一次硬體改版——架構分四個階段、搭配五問循環（Inspiration、Intercommunication、Investigation、Implementation、Impact），規則是每次互動都必須以一項有紀錄的改變、或一項有紀錄的「為何不改」作結。另有一座五層的目標使用者優先序金字塔，他們明確標示這是一個工作用框架，而不是經過驗證的暴露風險排序；金字塔把靠近疑似污染源（例如非正式電子廢棄物處理場）的弱勢社區，排在農民、研究者、法規機關與一般大眾之上。可追溯的改變包括：渠務署的建議讓他們放棄早期專案使用的發色蛋白，改用 mRFP1e 做雙重讀值——給非專業者看的可見顏色，加上更靈敏、可供定量的螢光通道；渠務署、水務署與大學研究者則一起推動他們測試更低濃度、對照國際參考值做基準比較，並評估干擾重金屬的交叉反應（因此有了 Cd2+/Pb2+/Zn2+ 的選擇性測試組）。Koo's Farm 與本地街市攤商要求的是數值讀數、不是定性的顏色指示，這正是 AS7343 14 通道感測器被換成可分辨波長的 Hamamatsu C12880 的直接原因，也是數值顯示與網頁讀值存在的原因。大學教授指出土壤顆粒必須在光學量測前移除，並建議模組化設計，於是產生了分開的水模組、土壤模組與規劃中的有機汞萃取模組。使用者反映 V1 的濾材疊層（2 um 前濾加 0.45 um 濾膜）需要的推針力過大，因此人工針筒給液被換成泵浦驅動給液——實測變異係數從 7.41% 改善到 1.95%。在 Blue Girl Organic Farm 與 Yeung Marine Products Limited 用農地土壤萃取液、灌溉水與魚塘水做的現地試驗（因為基改細菌依法不能帶出實驗室，所以是在沒有基改細菌的情況下進行）帶回了「指示要更清楚」與「要更能防水防泥」的要求，回應方式是紅/黃/綠狀態顯示、強化外殼，以及在提案中的 V4.0 設計進維護入口與模組化。第二次公眾調查結合街訪與對 195 人的實機示範，發現 87.7% 更有信心認為一般人也能參與檢查土壤與水的安全、84.1% 覺得數位讀值容易理解——而團隊立刻指出，感受到的信心與可讀性並不等於分析準確度，並因此直接在介面上把裝置狀態與安全判斷分開。More Happy Farm 則直白表示，不是每個農民都想自己擁有一台裝置，這把他們推向服務模式。整份文件中，他們一再說明自己的證據沒有涵蓋什麼：在受控生物檢測中有反應，並不代表在土壤萃取液中能準確量測、不代表整台裝置能可靠運作，也不代表適合用於法規決策。","realWorld":"The commercial concept is Certification-as-a-Service rather than instrument sales: farmers pay an annual subscription, the team visits to test soil on site with MerMAID, passing farms receive a 'Heavy Metal-Free' certificate and logo for supermarket packaging that lets them command a premium, and random surprise re-tests throughout the year (affordable precisely because the test is cheap and fast) guard the certificate's integrity. The plan is backed by a SWOT matrix, a competitor comparison against off-site laboratory testing (HKD 500+ per test, weeks of turnaround) and quick chemical test strips, and a five-step business plan naming AFCD, the Hong Kong Organic Resource Centre and premium supermarkets as the partners whose endorsement would make the certificate a standard. What lifts it above a typical student business plan is the case-study section: they analyse three real commercial analogues - Hygiena's reader-plus-consumables-plus-records model, SGS's accredited food-safety testing service, and Hong Kong's AFCD/VMO Accredited Farm Scheme - and draw out the uncomfortable implications, including that MerR-responsive bioavailable Hg(II) and a reference method's total-mercury result may be different measurands that cannot be assumed to agree just because both are labelled mercury, that a logo on packaging cannot replace a sample-to-report record tied to farm, location, date, sample ID and method scope, and that the full cost per valid result must include consumables, controls, staff time, storage, failed runs and waste handling. They state outright that the USD 350 build cost missed the USD 40 target, that the certification journey is a proposed direction, that the current prototype does not establish that any farm or product is heavy-metal-free, and that they claim no certification authority. Real-world constraints are acknowledged rather than wished away: engineered microbes cannot legally be placed in bins or taken into the field in Hong Kong, the on-site demonstrations therefore ran without GM bacteria, and the sub-five-minute loading and readout sequence is distinguished from the five hours of reporter expression the actual assay needs.","realWorld_zh":"商業概念是「認證即服務」，而不是賣儀器：農民付年度訂閱費，團隊到場用 MerMAID 檢測土壤，通過的農場取得「無重金屬」證書與標章，可用在超市包裝上取得溢價，而全年不定期的突擊複檢（正因為檢測便宜又快才負擔得起）則守住證書的可信度。這套計畫有 SWOT 矩陣支撐，另有與委外實驗室檢測（每次 HKD 500 以上、等待數週）以及快速化學試紙的競品比較，還有一份五步驟營運計畫，指名漁農自然護理署（AFCD）、香港有機資源中心與高階超市為能讓這張證書變成標準的背書夥伴。真正讓它高於一般學生商業計畫的是案例研究那一節：他們分析了三個真實的商業對照——Hygiena 的「讀取儀＋耗材＋紀錄」模式、SGS 的認證食品安全檢測服務，以及香港 AFCD/VMO 的認可農場計畫——並把令人不舒服的推論攤出來，包括：MerR 所反應的生物可利用 Hg(II) 與參考方法測得的總汞，可能是兩個不同的被測量，不能因為都叫「汞」就假定一致；包裝上的標章無法取代一份綁定農場、地點、日期、樣品編號與方法範圍的「樣品到報告」紀錄；而每一筆有效結果的完整成本，必須把耗材、對照、人力時間、保存、失敗批次與廢棄物處理都算進去。他們直說 USD 350 的製作成本沒達到 USD 40 的目標、認證這條路只是提案方向、目前的原型並不能證明任何農場或產品無重金屬，而且他們不主張自己具有任何認證權限。現實限制也是承認而不是迴避：在香港，工程改造的微生物依法不能丟進垃圾桶或帶到田間，因此現地示範是在沒有基改細菌的情況下進行；而五分鐘以內的裝填與讀取流程，也和實際檢測所需的五小時報告基因表現時間明確區分開來。","partners":["Drainage Services Department (DSD), Hong Kong - external adviser, including Dr Van","Environmental Protection Department (EPD)","Agriculture, Fisheries and Conservation Department (AFCD)","Water Supplies Department (WSD)","WEEE-PARK","Dr. Li Wai Chin, The Education University of Hong Kong","Prof. Liang and CUHK researchers","Blue Girl Organic Farm","Yeung Marine Products Limited","HKFYG Jockey Club Organic Farm","Koo's Farm","More Happy Farm","local wet market vendors","InnoEX 2026","IDT, New England Biolabs, Twist Bioscience, miniPCR/miniOne, BTEA (sponsors)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6158/wiki/model/figure-1.avif","caption":"Control-subtracted colour and pellet-fluorescence signals against log mercury concentration, with each calibration run coloured separately and the pooled log-linear fit overlaid.","caption_zh":"扣除對照後的顏色與菌體沉澱物螢光訊號對汞濃度對數作圖，每個校正批次以不同顏色標示，並疊上彙總後的對數線性擬合線。","credit":"Team HongKong-JSS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6158/wiki/model/figure-2.avif","caption":"Known versus estimated mercury concentration for the held-out validation runs, against a dashed perfect-prediction line, with estimates falling outside the calibration range marked separately rather than dropped.","caption_zh":"保留驗證批次的已知濃度對估計濃度，搭配一條虛線完美預測線；落在校正範圍之外的估計值另外標記，而不是直接刪掉。","credit":"Team HongKong-JSS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6158/wiki/hardware/hw13.avif","caption":"Detection Unit V3.0: the Hamamatsu C12880 miniature spectrometer with its driver board, an ESP32-S3-N16R8 for Wi-Fi, and the mobile web interface showing the recorded spectrum and raw signal at a selected wavelength - the upgrade stakeholders forced by demanding numbers, not colours.","caption_zh":"Detection Unit V3.0：Hamamatsu C12880 微型光譜儀與其驅動板、負責 Wi-Fi 的 ESP32-S3-N16R8，以及顯示記錄光譜與選定波長原始訊號的手機網頁介面——這次升級，是利害關係人要求數字而非顏色所逼出來的。","credit":"Team HongKong-JSS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6158/wiki/education/edu05-new-png.avif","caption":"The two-day Teacher Biotech Training Workshop for 30 local school teachers, covering PCR and agarose gel electrophoresis and backed by an ongoing DNA sample and equipment loan programme so the teaching capacity outlasts the team.","caption_zh":"為 30 位本地學校教師辦的兩天教師生技培訓工作坊，涵蓋 PCR 與瓊脂膠體電泳，並以持續的 DNA 樣品與設備借用方案為後盾，讓教學能力比團隊活得更久。","credit":"Team HongKong-JSS, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Adopt their calibration discipline wholesale: split runs into calibration and validation before fitting anything, subtract a control from the same run and timepoint, invert the fit to predict unknowns, report RMSE on the held-out runs with the failures left in, flag out-of-range estimates, and then publish the statistical work you have not done yet (run-aware mixed model, inverse-calibration uncertainty intervals, leave-one-run-out cross-validation, a per-run reference standard) as a named plan. The second lesson is their teacher-capacity play - training 30 local teachers in PCR and gel electrophoresis and lending them the reagents and kit - which multiplies a school team's reach far more cheaply than any one-off workshop.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"把他們的校正紀律整套搬走：在擬合任何東西之前就先把實驗批次分成校正組與驗證組；扣掉同一批次、同一時間點的對照；把擬合式反轉來預測未知樣品；在保留的批次上報告 RMSE，而且把失敗案例留在裡面；標出超出範圍的估計值；然後把自己還沒做的統計工作（考慮批次的混合模型、反向校正的不確定區間、留一批次交叉驗證、每批次一個參考標準品）寫成一份具名的計畫公開。第二課是他們培養師資的這一手——訓練 30 位本地教師做 PCR 與膠體電泳，並把試劑與器材借給他們——這比任何一次性的工作坊都更便宜地放大了一支校隊的影響範圍。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-jss/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-jss/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-jss/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-jss/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-jss/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-jss/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-jss/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-jss/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-jss/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-jss/contribution","https://github.com/hkjssplkchc2026/mercurysense","https://github.com/davidlueng986-alt/MerMAID-Extraction-Unit","https://cad.onshape.com/documents/2228cb45d05bdbc67479791d","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/hongkong-jss","https://api.igem.org/v1/teams/6158"],"rank":219},"6165":{"team":"SMS-Shenzhen","id":"6165","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"Climate Crisis / Conservation / Bioremediation (inferred from project scope; no village stated on the wiki)","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/sms-shenzhen/","projectTitle":"kisMET - selective biosorption of residual metals from battery-recycling wastewater","tagline":"Catching the last one percent of lithium, cobalt, nickel and manganese without more chemistry","summary":"kisMET targets the tail-end wastewater of spent lithium-ion battery recycling, where metal concentrations fall to parts-per-million and solvent extraction stops being economic. The team engineered Komagataeibacter rhaeticus to decorate its own bacterial cellulose with a secreted fusion protein built from a signal peptide, a carbohydrate-binding module, a HiBiT reporter tag and a swappable ion-binding peptide, assembled by Golden Gate on a pSEVA331 backbone under a rhamnose-inducible promoter. Four SP/CBM scaffolds and an eight-member ion-binding-peptide panel were designed so the binding specificity can be changed without redesigning the platform. Evidence so far covers cultivation, construct and reporter comparisons, single-metal binding experiments and cellulose-degradation assays; the team states clearly that selectivity in mixed wastewater, closed-loop cellulose reuse and complete metal recovery are design objectives, not results.","awards":["Best New Composite Part — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A prospective carbon-footprint and techno-economic model, built in two levels: Level A is a preliminary estimate of the material-production module using the team's own measured fermentation parameters, and Level B is the full wastewater-treatment system, deferred until adsorption and recycling performance exist. The functional unit is treatment of one tonne of end-of-pipe battery-recycling wastewater, with the system boundary held identical for the kisMET route and the chemical-precipitation baseline (reagent manufacturing and sludge disposal only; pump and agitation energy excluded). Emission factors are taken from peer-reviewed literature using ecoinvent v3.9.1 global-average datasets, cradle-to-gate. There is no mechanistic or kinetic model - no Langmuir or Freundlich isotherm fitting, no adsorption kinetics, no structural modelling of the ion-binding peptides - which is the clearest gap in an adsorption project.","dataviz":"Engineering and Results figures for HiBiT reporter signals, construct and scaffold comparisons, single-metal (Li/Co/Ni/Mn) experiments and cellulose degradation; a plasmid design schematic showing interchangeable IBP modules alongside the circular map of the optimised pSEVA331 construct; an LCA system-boundary diagram separating the Level A and Level B modules; an SDG interaction map. Education reports platform analytics as a table with the caveat that reach is not a measure of learning.","datascience":"Scenario and sensitivity reasoning rather than inferential statistics: medium raw-material emissions computed for a 40 mL YPD batch, then scaled under three dry bacterial-cellulose yield scenarios because the team's own dry-weight yield was never measured, then expressed per tonne of wastewater; emission offsets calculated per metal for substitution of virgin salts and separately for cellulose recycling substituting only the glucose carbon source. The honesty is the notable part: outputs are labelled as trend analysis only, bead productivity is taken from published shake-flask ranges for the same strain, local Chinese grid factors are excluded, and the whole thing is described as a qualitative trend comparison and not an ISO-compliant LCA. The team also states which named parameters are the priority model inputs (fermentation yield, adsorption performance, cycle number) following expert advice.","software":"No software deliverable beyond the wiki itself. There is an explicit generative-AI disclosure stating that AI was used only for readability editing and website implementation, and that no scientific claim, data figure, gel image, microscopy image, measurement plot or reference was model-generated.","stack":["spreadsheet-level carbon-footprint and techno-economic model","ecoinvent v3.9.1 literature emission factors","HiBiT luminescent reporter quantification","Golden Gate assembly design with interchangeable modules","public sequence databases for SP / CBM / IBP module retrieval","spectrophotometry and metal-concentration readings","wiki built from a public repository"],"techniques":["functional-unit and system-boundary definition for a comparative footprint","three-scenario yield sensitivity analysis to cover an unmeasured parameter","per-metal substitution offset accounting","cost-per-use rather than cost-per-batch framing for a reusable bead (taken directly from an industry interview)","explicit trade-off register (removal efficiency vs energy, valorisation vs reagent burden, cellulose recycling vs enzyme input, cost vs treatment stability)","sample fractionation reasoning (residual liquid A vs digestion liquid B) to keep figure interpretation within what controls support"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"The most intellectually honest education page in this cohort, and worth reading as a model regardless of its scale. Four channels, chosen because the audience already uses them rather than building a team website: a WeChat official account, a Xiaohongshu account, a printed two-page bilingual handbook, and two offline events (a school-wide iGEM club class for 59 students on 14 September 2026, and a community booth at Xiangmi Park on 2 October 2026 reaching over 70 visitors, run jointly with iGEM team Yucai-SZ). Three stated principles, each derived from something that failed: teach the phenomenon before the technology (their third and best post never mentions kisMET at all, only where the metal in water comes from); keep the channel open in both directions; and republish the same material in two formats. The analytics are reported against the team's own interest: the team introduction outperformed the project introduction roughly two to one, the purely scientific piece reached the fewest readers, and across three posts and 1,206 reads they received zero comments - from which they conclude that an open door is not an invitation, and propose polls and photo requests instead. The handbook uses one visual language and three analogies (a sponge for the cellulose bead, a magnet for the ion-binding peptide, one grain of rice in a swimming pool for ppm) and is released under CC BY 4.0 for other teams to print, translate or re-analogise.","ihp":"A five-stage programme on a Motivation -> Message -> Move reflection loop, built almost entirely from industry interviews, and it genuinely relocated the project's target user. Lu Binda (SUSTech doctoral student working on Juhefeng's battery-recycling R&D) mapped the value chain and established that front-end and back-end companies have entirely different wastewater. The team then visited Meizhou Zhongrun, a front-end physical recycler, and learned it sells electrode powder downstream and generates little wastewater - so it is not a customer. That finding redirected them to GEM, a downstream hydrometallurgical company, which confirmed that lithium, nickel, cobalt and manganese do remain in the tail stream after solvent extraction and require precipitation or adsorption. Further interviews covered Dynanonic, professional wastewater treatment firms, officials from the Ministry of Ecology and Environment on biosafety and compliance, and Li Zongjin of Lingzhu Tech twice - the second time producing industrial cost ranges for every process step and the modelling rule that cost per use, not cost per batch, decides whether a reusable bead can compete.","realWorld":"The platform is deliberately modular: swapping the ion-binding peptide retargets it at rare earths from e-waste or other heavy metals without touching the core system. Acting on advice from BIT-China and their industry interviews, the team chose to pursue technology licensing with established battery companies rather than founding a company - a realistic read of their own position. Named limitations are published rather than buried: Komagataeibacter fermentation is oxygen-transfer and shear-sensitive in stirred bioreactors, candidate peptides have only been tested in single-metal solutions, and cellulose breakdown does not by itself demonstrate that engineered cells have been inactivated, so a validated containment and disposal procedure is still required. Their closing self-assessment - that as a high-school team they offer not scale but time, willingness to re-explain, and the honesty to say when an explanation failed - is the right framing.","partners":["Juhefeng / Lu Binda, SUSTech (battery recycling R&D)","Meizhou Zhongrun (front-end physical recycling)","GEM (downstream hydrometallurgical recycling)","Dynanonic","Li Zongjin, Lingzhu Tech (fermentation scale-up, TEA and LCA)","Ministry of Ecology and Environment officials","iGEM team BIT-China (commercial pathway advice)","iGEM team Yucai-SZ (joint Xiangmi Park community booth)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6165/wiki/description-fig3-ibp-swap.avif","caption":"Molecular design of the pSEVA331 expression system, showing the interchangeable ion-binding-peptide modules that let the platform be retargeted to a different metal without redesign.","credit":"Team SMS-Shenzhen, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6165/wiki/education-handbook-page-b-kismet-kombucha.avif","caption":"Page B of the bilingual printed handbook, telling the kombucha bacterial-cellulose story and introducing the sponge and magnet analogies; released under CC BY 4.0 for reuse.","credit":"Team SMS-Shenzhen, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6165/wiki/education-wechat-article-stats.avif","caption":"The WeChat account back end, reported by the team against their own interest: the team introduction outperformed the project introduction, and the purely scientific post reached the fewest readers of all.","credit":"Team SMS-Shenzhen, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6165/wiki/hp-gem.avif","caption":"Interview with GEM, the downstream hydrometallurgical recycler whose confirmation that metals remain in the tail stream after solvent extraction validated kisMET's target application point.","credit":"Team SMS-Shenzhen, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"The dry lab is real but narrow: a spreadsheet-level carbon-footprint and techno-economic model with a defined functional unit, literature emission factors and a three-scenario sensitivity sweep is squarely within one high-school season and is exactly the kind of modelling most teams skip, yet for an adsorption project the absence of any isotherm or kinetics fitting is a conspicuous hole that a single afternoon with their own single-metal data would have filled. The limiting factor is mentorship rather than tooling, compute or time - nobody told them that Langmuir and Freundlich fits are a spreadsheet exercise, while someone clearly did teach them how to scope an LCA.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/sms-shenzhen/","https://2026.igem.wiki/sms-shenzhen/attributions","https://2026.igem.wiki/sms-shenzhen/team","https://2026.igem.wiki/sms-shenzhen/safety"],"rank":7},"6166":{"team":"GHCIS","id":"6166","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"Climate Crisis, Conservation & Bioremediation","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/ghcis/","projectTitle":"ARGUS","tagline":"A paper-based toehold-switch assay plus a browser-based image-analysis and surveillance platform for environmental antimicrobial resistance gene monitoring.","summary":"ARGUS pairs a cell-free, paper-based toehold switch assay for three antimicrobial resistance genes (mcr-1, blaNDM-1, blaKPC-2) with portable temperature-control hardware and a full-stack web platform that reads the colorimetric plate from a phone photo, grades each gene, and stores location-linked records for regional review. Recombinase polymerase amplification feeds trigger RNA to switches that drive colour-producing enzymes — blue for MCR1 (GusA), yellow for NDM1 (XylE), purple-shifted for KPC2 (LacZ). The project is framed inside the One Health approach, targeting the gap between institution-led metagenomic surveys and the routine, fine-grained environmental monitoring that networks like CARSS do not cover. It won Best Software and Best Part Collection on the strength of a genuinely deployable platform (Docker or native Node, SQLite, role-based access, documented deployment) and a NUPACK design pipeline that reproduced a published sequence grammar and then found an error in it — all presented with an unusually disciplined limitations section that refuses to claim sensitivity, specificity or a detection limit it has not measured.","awards":["Top 10 (High School)","Best Part Collection — Winner (High School)","Best Software — Winner (High School)","Best Wiki — Nominee (High School)","Best Village Project — Nominee (Climate Crisis / Conservation / Bioremediation)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"The modelling is a toehold switch design and screening pipeline in locally installed NUPACK 4.1.0.1 (rna95-nupack3 Serra-Turner 1995 material model, 37 degC, 1.0 M Na+, 0 M Mg2+, 100 nM switch and 100 nM trigger, maximum complex size 2). They reproduced the 36-nt mRNA sensor sequence grammar from Table S4 of Green et al. 2014 exactly, and verified the construction formula against four published sequences (mCherry B, mCherry C, cat, aadA) with exact matches on all four before designing anything new. Each switch is 126 nt: GGG leader, 30-nt exposed toehold, 6-bp target-driven invasion region, stem-loop containing the RBS and AUG, 9-nt programmed refolding module, 21-nt linker and the first 9 nt of GFP. For every 36-nt window across each complete CDS they computed the NUPACK base-pairing matrix of the full mRNA and scored target local single-strandedness, switch toehold single-strandedness, the normalised ensemble defect of the intended OFF conformation, and mean occupancy of the 15 expected stem base pairs — excluding windows with GC content below 30% or above 70%, four consecutive identical bases, a GGGG stretch created by the GGG leader, or a stop codon in the switch reading frame, and requiring candidate start positions at least 15 nt apart. Notably, they found that Equation 5 of the original supplementary information is internally inconsistent (it describes higher local single-strandedness as preferable while ranking the total score low-to-high), kept the published weights of 5, 4 and 3, and converted both single-strandedness terms into deficits so that lower penalty ranks better. Conservation screening used family CDSs from NCBI AMRFinderPlus release 2026-08-07.1: the primary designs cover 98/98 blaNDM, 295/295 blaKPC and 37/37 mcr-1 panel sequences exactly, with the alternatives' exceptions named (NDM1-S3 misses blaNDM-56, KPC2-S3 misses blaKPC-248). Cross-reactivity was computed as a tube-equilibrium matrix: cognate activation proxies of 0.906 (NDM1-S1), 0.940 (KPC2-S1) and 0.873 (MCR1-S1) against off-diagonal values from 8.10e-07 to 2.92e-04. Input integrity was checked and hashed (SHA256 prefixes recorded per file), including catching that the blaNDM-1 SnapGene record is stored in reverse orientation so the reverse complement had to be used — exactly the kind of silent error that would have produced a useless trigger.","dataviz":"Figures are oriented so higher is always better on the candidate-metrics panel, which is a small but real accessibility decision. The NUPACK cross-gene activation proxy matrix is drawn as a heatmap of the three primary designs so the three-order-of-magnitude gap between diagonal and off-diagonal is immediately legible. The sensor sequence architecture is rendered as an annotated 126-nt schematic. In the software, the data visualisation is the product: the administration console combines maps, regional rankings, per-gene trend charts and record-level inspection, with configurable alert rules and CSV/JSON export, while the client presents each plate as a four-grade result per gene (Negative, Weak Positive, Positive, Strong Positive) over the reviewed photograph. An annotated one-sample example plate figure documents the expected output for a published example image so anyone can reproduce the workflow end to end. The team is explicit that this example is a reproducible workflow demonstration, not a validation dataset, and that regional maps describe submitted records under the selected filters rather than population prevalence.","datascience":"The colour-grading algorithm is the headline and it is specified completely enough to reimplement. Analysis runs locally in JavaScript in the browser with no external AI or image-conversion service at runtime. The pipeline prepares the image (max dimension 2400 px; grid detection on a working image of max 1400 px), locates the active well grid (9, 12 or 15 wells for one, two or three loaded samples, always including the positive and negative control in every gene row), averages all sRGB pixels inside a disk of half the well radius, converts through linear RGB and XYZ D65 to CIE Lab, and then deliberately discards lightness L*, projecting only on a* and b* so the score tracks chromatic change. For a sample s with same-row negative control n and positive control p it computes the control direction v = p - n, a normalised score t = ((s - n) . v) / (v . v), and a residual r = ||(s - n) - tv||, so NC sits at t = 0 and PC at t = 1 and scores are not clamped to that interval. Quality gates are quantitative: control separation must satisfy ||v|| >= 2, the residual must satisfy r <= max(4, 0.6 x ||v||), expected directions are delta-b < 0 for MCR1, delta-b > 0 for NDM1 and delta-a - delta-b > 0 for KPC2, and missing, black, identical, reversed or insufficiently separated controls or |t| > 100 produce no estimate at all. Crucially, an absent classification is defined as unresolved and the documentation states it must not be treated as Negative — a failure mode most teams would silently default. Per-gene thresholds are published (MCR1 t < 0.20 Negative to t >= 1.60 Strong Positive; NDM1 and KPC2 on their own scales), along with the deliberately awkward note that a sample at MCR1 t = 1.00 is Weak Positive under the sample thresholds even though the PC label displays Strong Positive, because the PC and NC labels are control-role defaults rather than independent validation. The limitations section then declines to claim what was not measured: the 0, 3 and 5 micromolar trigger RNA conditions do not establish sensitivity, specificity, a detection limit or a concentration calibration, and the team states that large-scale real-world samples will be needed to set optimal colour thresholds and evaluate sensitivity, specificity, NPV and PPV. Wet-lab feedback iteratively adjusted the colour interpretation and capture workflow, and the team notes this aligned software with their process but does not substitute for testing across devices and lighting conditions.","software":"ARGUS is a complete, deployable web platform released at https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/ghcis/argus with a hosted client, a user guide PDF, a README quick start and a lossless example plate image (assets/example-plate.webp). Architecture: a browser client for field users and an administration console for institutions, with image processing in the browser and reviewed results validated server-side and persisted to SQLite, with documented backup procedures. Deployment is genuinely turnkey — Docker Engine or Desktop with Compose v2 via scripts/deploy.sh, or native Node.js (24.21.0 pinned in .nvmrc, documented minimum 22.16) via scripts/deploy-native.mjs, both of which build, check readiness and print local and LAN access links; public HTTPS deployment takes a domain and email, and automatic street-level location uses a Geoapify key. Three roles are implemented — field user, administrator and root — where field users work only with their own captures, administrators review regional data, export records and manage alerts, and root manages accounts and audit or demonstration-data operations; passwords are 12-200 characters, an initial root password is generated privately, and existing passwords survive restart and redeployment. Records are searchable by gene, result and date, downloadable as JSON summaries, and printable to PDF. The team also honestly flags that local analysis still depends on the server for authentication and storage, that a retained upload draft does not make it offline, that SQLite allows only one application instance per database volume, and that institution verification, jurisdiction-specific permissions, a documented versioned integration API and connections to CARSS or WHO networks all remain future work with no endorsement claimed. Hardware is released as STEP and STL files (top cover, backing card, electronic enclosure, sleeve, sample stage, three RPA unit variants) covering the ARGUS Temperature Controller — a three-layer design giving constant temperature for RPA and the colorimetric reaction plus stable uniform illumination for software-assisted capture — and the ARGUS Test Strip Card, whose substrate was chosen with material recovery and biodegradability in mind.","stack":["NUPACK 4.1.0.1 (local install)","rna95-nupack3 / Serra-Turner 1995 material model","NCBI AMRFinderPlus (release 2026-08-07.1)","GenBank / SnapGene sequence records","JavaScript (in-browser image analysis)","Node.js 24.21.0","Docker + Compose v2","SQLite","REST API with role-based access control","Geoapify geocoding","CIE Lab colour space (sRGB -> linear RGB -> XYZ D65 -> Lab)","recombinase polymerase amplification (RPA)","cell-free paper-based expression","GusA / XylE / LacZ colorimetric reporters","STEP and STL CAD","GitLab (iGEM)"],"techniques":["exhaustive sliding-window candidate scanning over full CDSs","ensemble defect and base-pairing probability analysis","tube equilibrium cross-reactivity matrix","family-level conservation coverage screening","sequence integrity checking with SHA256 hashing and orientation verification","reproduction and error-correction of a published scoring equation","chromaticity-only colour classification (L* discarded)","same-row internal control projection with normalised score and residual","explicit quality gates and an unresolved (not Negative) failure state","staged two-round experimental validation plan with predefined replacement designs","role-based access control and audit separation","reproducible one-command deployment"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A tiered education programme with its own documented iteration framework, INSPIRE (Identify the audience, Notice prior knowledge and needs, Set learning goals, Plan content and format, Implement the activity, Review responses and feedback, Evolve the design), applied uniformly to every activity so each record shows design, delivery, feedback and the resulting change. Four audience groups are defined with explicit prior-knowledge characteristics, stage goals and formats: primary school (stories, analogies, stickers, games, scenario Q&A), junior high (pre-class questions, mechanism explanations, group discussion and retelling), high school (posters, questionnaires, lectures, cards, experiments, peer exchange) and the general public (visual-text content, social media). The feedback-to-change table is the strongest artefact: teachers preferred familiar health examples so hygiene activities and organ stickers were added; children struggled with abstract concepts so stories and analogies replaced them; poster votes lacked explanations so posters plus a questionnaire were introduced; the questionnaire revealed interests and gaps which drove targeted lectures; long lectures reduced engagement so a 'Biology Werewolf' social-deduction game was created; Werewolf rounds ran too long so a 5-8 minute online version was built; online participation lacked learning evidence so Club Fair question cards were added; students preferred hands-on learning so medicinal-herb experiments were introduced; students struggled with protein function so examples and group discussion were added. Partner feedback from Ulink prompted platform-specific adaptations for Xiaohongshu and WeChat, and questions raised at a Morning Meetup caused a revision of the afternoon pitch. The team also traced a knowledge gap found in human practices — that the public associates AMR with hospitals and personal antibiotic use but has weak understanding of the One Health links between animals, environment and humans — directly into the education content, extending it from rational antibiotic use to livestock and environmental transmission pathways.","ihp":"A deliberately sequenced, evidence-first process rather than a stakeholder list. They began by asking not 'who should we interview' but 'who would be affected, who would participate in use or deployment, and who could change the project's direction', grouping stakeholders into five exploratory categories and then deliberately starting with the public — not because the public decides anything, but to build a social-needs baseline whose gaps would determine who to approach next. A bilingual online questionnaire returned 281 valid responses: safety, result accuracy and price were selected by 72.24%, 61.57% and 46.98% of respondents; 67.26% worried about inaccurate results and 55.87% about product safety; 44.48% worried they would not know what to do after detecting a risk and 33.45% that they could not understand the results. The methodological discipline here is notable for a high-school team: because questions Q12-Q19 branched on respondents' stated first priority, the price and speed branches had small samples, so they explicitly refused to convert 'within RMB 30' or 'results within 30 minutes' into product requirements and instead carried them forward as questions to validate with frontline users. They then re-mapped stakeholders on power and interest axes, noting that the map represented types rather than named interviewees and that specific participants were identified only as each cycle raised new questions. Concrete design changes are tabulated: frontline practitioners wanted information useful for antibiotic selection, so the team retained preliminary monitoring and data support while explicitly acknowledging the unmet diagnostic need rather than overclaiming; industry advice on hardware and consumable costs replaced a proposed microfluidic format with cellulose filter paper and revised strip assembly and substrate use; and industry advice to swap the expression system for crude lysate was considered and rejected, keeping the current cell-free system because of background-interference concerns — a documented decision to not follow advice, with a reason. Expert discussions about controlled access to environmental and public-health data are what produced the three-tier role model in the software.","realWorld":"ARGUS is positioned for institution-led procurement rather than consumer sale: government monitoring programmes or authorised implementing institutions buy and organise the system, trained frontline inspectors, veterinary-service personnel or environmental monitoring staff run the screening, and farms and herders support sample access, with results recorded in a defined programme and escalated for confirmatory testing. The near-term target is preliminary screening of water samples from livestock breeding sites, with medical wastewater named as a separate adjacent application and any clinical use explicitly deferred to independent validation and regulatory assessment. The long-term scale target price is about US$3.73 per routine screen, subject to cost and production validation, with a target detection time of about 40 minutes and isothermal amplification at roughly 37-42 degC. The proposed governance model assigns national coordination, provincial review and local sample collection to different institutional levels, and the team is careful to state that implementing it requires verified organisational identities, jurisdiction-restricted permissions and defined reporting responsibilities, that possible alignment with CARSS would require agreement on remit, data definitions and reporting interfaces, and that no official endorsement, institutional adoption or network connection is claimed at this stage. Product boundaries are written into the marketing position: environmental AMR preliminary screening and trend monitoring only, never the sole basis for clinical diagnosis, administrative penalties or individual medication decisions, and an alert should prompt investigation rather than be read as a population prevalence estimate. The named development path is broader validated applications (more phones, lighting conditions, assay batches and independent samples, with a shared evaluation dataset for measuring classification consistency), then a versioned integration API with defined schemas, authentication, permissions, error responses and reproducible examples distinguishing capture identifiers from sample positions and describing location precision, sampling time, assay version, controls and quality status, then institution-led deployment.","partners":["Ulink (education platform feedback)","Frontline livestock practitioners and grassroots veterinarians","Industry advisors on hardware and consumable cost","AMR, molecular detection, environment and public-health technical experts","Agricultural and livestock management authorities (engagement target)","CARSS / China Antimicrobial Resistance Surveillance System (named alignment goal, not a partnership)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6166/wiki/software/figure-02.avif","caption":"ARGUS feature map: client functions (location, plate photographs, local four-grade analysis, personal records), console functions (regional review, alerts, exports), account management and operations.","credit":"Team GHCIS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6166/wiki/software/figure-05.avif","caption":"The local colour recognition and storage pipeline: image preparation, active well-grid detection, central well pixel sampling, conversion to CIE Lab, control validation, gene-specific grading and SQLite storage.","credit":"Team GHCIS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6166/wiki/model/candidate-nupack-metrics.avif","caption":"NUPACK metrics for the nine toehold switch candidates across mcr-1, blaNDM-1 and blaKPC-2, with every column oriented so higher values are preferable.","credit":"Team GHCIS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6166/wiki/hardware/assembled-controller.avif","caption":"The assembled ARGUS Temperature Controller with viewing window, power connection and temperature control unit, providing both the reaction environment and uniform illumination for phone-based image capture.","credit":"Team GHCIS, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Two things to copy. In software, write the algorithm down to the equation and the threshold — same-row internal controls, a chromaticity-only projection, numeric quality gates, and an explicit 'unresolved, and not to be read as Negative' state — then ship it with one-command Docker deployment and a reproducible example input, because a tool a judge can actually run beats a screenshot of one. In human practices, copy their refusal to convert a small branched survey sample into a product requirement: carrying '30 minutes' forward as a question to validate rather than a specification is the single cheapest credibility gain available to a student team.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/ghcis/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ghcis/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ghcis/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ghcis/software/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ghcis/hardware/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ghcis/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ghcis/results/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ghcis/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ghcis/education/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ghcis/entrepreneurship/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ghcis/inclusivity/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ghcis/contribution/","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/ghcis/argus"],"rank":136},"6174":{"team":"Hongwen School","id":"6174","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/hongwen-school/","projectTitle":"BrewXOS","tagline":"Creating additional value within an existing spent-grain economy: brewer's spent grain to candidate arabinoxylan oligosaccharides.","summary":"Hongwen School (Shanghai and Qingdao) engineered Bacillus subtilis WB600 to secrete xylan-degrading enzymes that convert the arabinoxylan fraction of brewer's spent grain (BSG) into candidate arabinoxylan oligosaccharides (AXOS). Five strains - single Xyn2 and Xyn11A, two dual combinations with the GH62 arabinofuranosidase Abf62A, and a triple construct - were compared; the triple strain reached 257.10 +/- 5.55 U/mL apparent supernatant activity and a parental-adjusted index of 107.91 +/- 6.64 mg xylose equivalents per gram dry BSG after 12 h, 32.8% above the better dual strain. Alongside this they built BrewXOS Fermenter Mini, a small fermentation-monitoring prototype with a main-cap/sub-cap lid, headspace O2/CO2 sensing and a touchscreen interface, and tested it with real users. The Human Practices work is the best part of the project: a GRAIN x TRACE framework forces every stakeholder interaction to end in a named change plus the evidence for it, or be flagged as an open loop.","awards":["Best Hardware — Nominee (High School)","Best Sustainable Development Impact — Nominee (High School)","Best Village Project — Nominee (Agriculture / Food & Nutrition / Fashion & Cosmetics / Art & Design)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"GRAIN x TRACE, the team's own two-tier Human Practices documentation framework: GRAIN (Ground the problem, Reframe the purpose, Adapt the science, Iterate toward implementation, Nourish the ecosystem) tracks project-wide evolution while TRACE (Trigger, Relevant voices, Advice and tensions, Change, Evidence and evaluation) records each interaction, with a stated closed-loop rule that advice without a change, or a plan without implementation proof, is explicitly flagged rather than presented as integrated. Published as a reusable template. There is no Model or Software page and no in-silico work - the team does not claim any.","dataviz":"Survey charts for the 219-response questionnaire (awareness of BSG and prebiotics, trust factors); paired strain-comparison plots showing apparent supernatant activity and 12 h reducing-sugar change with means and SD (n = 3); process traces of temperature, pH and headspace O2/CO2 from the 18 h integrated hardware run; CAD and layout diagrams of the Fermenter Mini.","datascience":"Careful descriptive statistics with stated limits rather than inference: survey percentages reported against each question's own denominator and explicitly not extrapolated nationally (44.29% of respondents were minors, 43.38% middle-school students); DNS reducing-sugar yields parental-adjusted against WB600 controls and labelled as an operational index, not verified AXOS mass; a 22% AX content assumption flagged where it drives a derived 49.05% apparent conversion index; user-task timings and error counts (5 min 40 s to 1 min 50 s; errors 2 to 0) reported with the caveat that the user sample is too small to generalise. No LCA or TEA has been done and the team says so.","software":"Arduino firmware for BrewXOS Fermenter Mini, structured into separate modules for sensor acquisition, display update, command parsing and serial output, with bidirectional UART at 9600 bps to a serial touchscreen HMI. A debugging episode is documented in detail: the touchscreen required raw hexadecimal command framing with a %%% terminator, and after fixing the formatting the buttons and sliders could drive the pumps, stirrer and UV-C. Alarm thresholds were moved out of firmware constants into touchscreen-configurable, power-loss-persistent settings after a user complained that different strains need different limits.","stack":["Bacillus subtilis WB600 (six-protease-deficient secretion host)","pDG1730 integration vector (amyE locus)","E. coli DH5a for propagation","Arduino Mega 2560 with expansion board","serial touchscreen HMI (UART)","waterproof DS18B20 temperature probe","pH probe, headspace O2 and CO2 sensors","PTC heater and thermoelectric cooler via relays","peristaltic pumps, UV-C strip","3D-printed split lid, motor mount, sensor slots and casing","CAD/STEP assembly export"],"techniques":["colony PCR artefact diagnosis by annealing-temperature and template-concentration variation","restriction digestion and sequencing confirmation","multi-tier (single, dual, triple) modular gene assembly with per-tier strain stocks and sequencing records","DNS reducing-sugar assay with D-xylose calibration","TLC against xylobiose and xylotriose standards","enzyme activity assay at 55 C, pH 5.0","task-based external user testing of hardware with timed repeats and error counts"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Outreach was derived from measured knowledge gaps rather than chosen first: 74.88% of 219 survey respondents reported little or no knowledge of prebiotics and senior interviewees repeatedly confused probiotics with prebiotics, so the team ran senior-living-community workshops on four topics - prebiotics versus probiotics, dietary fibre and gut microbiota, and how to spot exaggerated therapeutic claims and incomplete safety disclosure - using plain-language analogies ('food components that certain beneficial gut microbes can use') while still naming the microbes and enzymes involved. Clinicians set the limits: prebiotics were framed as general dietary support and microbiome shifts were not presented as treatment. Evaluation used teach-back rather than a comprehension question: identical three-question show-of-hands polls before and after, plus asking participants to restate the core concepts in their own words, with short verbal feedback instead of long forms for older participants. The team keeps the distinction between acting on a knowledge gap and proving a durable change, saying there is no longitudinal data. They also published six reusable assets (a B. subtilis construction troubleshooting log, a selection-marker and host-compatibility guide, a multi-tier assembly decision framework, the hardware package with BOM/CAD/sensor matrix, the GRAIN x TRACE template and a senior-outreach toolkit), each with an explicit boundary clause.","ihp":"This is one of the strongest high-school IHP records of the year because the register of changes is specific, attributed and sometimes negative. Mr Zhou at the Brewing Industry Association gave macro figures (35-36 million kL of beer a year, roughly 5.5-6 million t of wet spent grain, summer output 20-30% above winter, over 80% already in the animal feed chain, an economic transport radius of about 50 km) and the team responded by retiring its founding premise - BrewXOS is not competing with dumping but with a mature feed pathway - and rebuilding its economics as full cost accounting per tonne of wet grain, with near-site or in-park third-party processing instead of in-house brewery lines. Manager Wu of a 300,000 t/year brewery (50,000 t wet BSG, collected by buyers at near-zero cost) confirmed it and the team redefined breweries as raw-material partners who already have an acceptable option. Master He, a municipal landfill worker of six years, supplied the counterweight: 60-90 t/month at nearly 80% moisture, handling costs of 70-80 RMB/t driven by leachate, odour, liner and labour, persisting not from indifference but from absent local off-takers - so the team deleted both extreme narratives, fixed 70-80 RMB/t as a local baseline and upgraded localised processing from a business preference to a hard environmental constraint, because a route relying on high-energy drying or long-haul transport would eat its own gains. Dr Chen, a gastroenterologist at Ruijin Hospital, delivered the single strongest design change: she gave a three-tier evidence ladder (mechanistically plausible / observed in healthy populations / demonstrated in clinical patients), pointed out that marketing AXOS as suitable for IBS directly conflicts with low-FODMAP management, and the team formally struck 'designed specifically for IBS', 'relieves IBS symptoms' and 'improves the gut environment' from its positioning, rewrote the wiki to separate in vitro, healthy-human and patient evidence, and added human tolerance testing as a mandatory milestone. Professor Xu (College of Life Sciences, Zhejiang University) produced three laboratory changes: he stopped a primer redesign by identifying two ~90 bp direct repeats capable of PCR template switching, so the team kept its 1,571 bp clones, raised the annealing temperature and watched the spurious ~400 bp band fade; he made them re-annotate pDG1730 by host role, which replaced erythromycin and ampicillin with spectinomycin for B. subtilis selection and turned lawn-like background into isolated verified colonies; and he pushed them from one-step assembly to tiered construction and to add Abf62A as a testable hypothesis, not an assumed improvement, explicitly because excessive debranching could collapse AXOS into low-substitution XOS. Professor Qing Zhao (Shanghai Chenshan Plant Science Research Center, CAS) moved them from endpoint assays to process logging, which is why the hardware project exists at all; a hardware engineer then rejected their monolithic lid and produced the main-cap/sub-cap architecture, a deepened recessed motor seat and sliding probe slots so routine fluid handling no longer disturbs the impeller shaft and wiring. Downstream, Ms Yang (dairy QC) narrowed the goal from 'a BrewXOS yogurt' to ingredient compatibility in plain fermented milk; Ms Han (Swire Coca-Cola Nanjing) listed pH 2.5-4, hot-fill and a 9-12 month shelf life and said plainly that a premium would not be paid for environmental claims, so RTD beverages became a long-term specification-setting target; Pharmacist Tang moved pharmacies from launch channel to late-stage channel; and Mr Shen of a Chongming ecological farm ('I never look at the price per ton - I look at the cost per kilogram of gain') converted the feed route from wet grain or liquid AXOS into a standardised premix pourable into an existing mixer, judged on feed conversion ratio, diarrhoea rate and mortality. The team also publishes what it rejected - diverting all spent grain away from feed, leading with sustainability, launching a consumer product - with reasons.","realWorld":"Need is grounded in the literature (BSG is about 85% of brewing's solid byproducts, roughly 20 kg wet grain per 100 L of beer at 60-80% moisture, a 2025 review estimating about 37.8 million t/year globally) and then immediately qualified by field evidence that feed conversion already works in most Chinese settings, so the project's claim is additional value in regions with unstable disposal channels and dense brewery clusters, not displacement. SDG claims are narrow and target-level: SDG 12 (12.2, 12.5 and 12.6) and SDG 9 (9.5, moving toward 9.4) are the primary goals with SDGs 3 and 8 held explicitly as aspirations, and the page says what it cannot support - no measured waste diversion at commercial scale, no demonstrated industrial resource-efficiency gain, no quantified learning improvement. Implementation is an evidence-gated five-stage sequence (product identity; process balance; application evaluation; net-impact comparison; partner validation) with plain fermented milk as the immediate compatibility matrix, beverages long-term, pharmacies late-stage and a feed premix as a parallel route. The regulatory position is stated rather than finessed: China's 2024 National Health Commission approval of sugarcane-bagasse arabinoxylan specifies source, process and intake limits and does not extend to spent-grain-derived AXOS, so BrewXOS has no novel-food clearance and the team refuses to blur AX and AXOS in public materials. Costs are handled as a bill of materials (RMB 3,480.29 for the prototype, flagged as material cost rather than total ownership) plus a local illustration from the landfill data (RMB 4,200-7,200/month handling at that site; treating 10% of the flow would give 6-9 t wet BSG and roughly 130-194 kg xylose equivalents/month, marked as arithmetic rather than a forecast). After the Jamboree the roadmap is structural characterisation and batch consistency, a safety panel (microbial counts, mycotoxins, heavy metals, pesticide residues, processing impurities), clarifying the filing pathway, fermented-milk compatibility baselines, hardware calibration and safety validation, LCA and TEA so a fair comparison with the feed route is possible, re-engaging the same stakeholders to check whether the changes answered them, and publishing the open-source assets with their boundaries annotated. The team states that no LCA or TEA exists yet and therefore no net environmental benefit may be claimed.","partners":["Brewing Industry Association (Mr Zhou)","Qiandao Lake Brewery, Zhejiang (Manager Wu; donated the BSG feedstock)","Local municipal landfill solid-waste operations (Master He)","Dr Chen, gastroenterologist, Ruijin Hospital","Professor Xu, College of Life Sciences, Zhejiang University","Professor Qing Zhao, Shanghai Chenshan Plant Science Research Center, Chinese Academy of Sciences","Engineer Sun, food industry R&D","Hardware engineer (lid structural design consultant)","Dairy enterprise yogurt QC (Ms Yang)","Swire Coca-Cola Nanjing (Ms Han)","Pharmacist Tang and a retail pharmacy","Ecological farm, Chongming, Shanghai (Mr Shen)","iGEM Shanghai-SDG 2025 (cross-team exchange on bioprocessing hardware and SDG assessment)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6174/wiki/public/hp/integration-pathway.webp","caption":"The GRAIN x TRACE integration pathway: how stakeholder input reshaped problem definition, purpose, scientific design, implementation strategy and knowledge sharing, with TRACE recording each question-to-change-to-evidence loop.","credit":"Team Hongwen School, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6174/wiki/public/hp/brewery-visit.webp","caption":"Brewery visit during the Ground phase, where an existing low-cost feed outlet for spent grain forced the team to abandon its assumption that breweries needed a new disposal technology.","credit":"Team Hongwen School, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6174/wiki/public/hp/farm-visit.webp","caption":"Farm visit and interview in Chongming, Shanghai, where cost per kilogram of weight gain turned the animal-feed route into a standardised premix concept.","credit":"Team Hongwen School, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6174/wiki/public/hp/gastroenterologist-consultation.webp","caption":"Consultation with a gastroenterologist at Ruijin Hospital, whose three-tier evidence framework led the team to remove all IBS-related claims from the project positioning.","credit":"Team Hongwen School, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Copy the TRACE closed-loop rule: log every stakeholder interaction as Trigger, Relevant voice, Advice and tensions, Change and Evidence, and mark an interaction as an open loop whenever there is advice without a project change or a plan without proof of implementation. It converts engagement from a photo gallery into an auditable decision ledger, and the companion 'what we did not adopt, and why' table is what makes the adopted changes credible.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/hongwen-school/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongwen-school/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongwen-school/sustainability","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongwen-school/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongwen-school/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongwen-school/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongwen-school/parts","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongwen-school/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongwen-school/safety-and-security","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongwen-school/assets/index-BCz246wW.js","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongwen-school/assets/HumanPracticesArticle-C7wSXf0T.js","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongwen-school/assets/sustainability-Bw_LueMp.js","https://registry.igem.org/collections/c1986de4-b393-49a8-8341-4f5d4b150efe"],"rank":21},"6177":{"team":"SEHS","id":"6177","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"Therapeutics / health (inferred from project scope; no village stated on the wiki)","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/sehs/","projectTitle":"FusionDrive - an anti-TIGIT-IL-2v fusion protein for gastric cancer immunotherapy","tagline":"Release the immune brake and bias the accelerator, in one molecule","summary":"Starting from the high gastric-cancer burden in their home province of Shandong, SEHS designed FusionDrive, a fusion protein joining an anti-TIGIT antibody to an engineered IL-2 variant through a G4S linker. The antibody Fab blocks CD155-TIGIT inhibitory signalling to reverse T-cell exhaustion, while the Fc-fused IL-2v carries a low-alpha/high-beta modification that reduces CD25 binding and so biases stimulation away from regulatory T cells. Across five DBTL cycles the team built the antibody, the wild-type IL-2 fusion and the variant fusion in CHO cells and compared them by SDS-PAGE, TIGIT-binding ELISA (EC50 0.6317 nM for the antibody, 1.335 nM after IL-2 fusion) and flow cytometry for CD25 and pSTAT5. Because the iGEM high-school White List left Jurkat as the only available T-cell line, they used PHA induction to create CD25-high and CD25-low populations as a stand-in for the Treg receptor phenotype.","awards":["Best Alternative Platform — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"No computational model of any kind: there is no Model or Software page on the site, and no docking, structure prediction or kinetic simulation anywhere in the project. The design reasoning is literature-driven (lowalpha/highbeta IL-2 variants, G4S linker flexibility) rather than simulated. The hardware page does include a comparative literature review of three published protein-detection instruments used to specify a device.","dataviz":"Clean, interpretable assay figures: concentration-response ELISA binding curves for all three molecular formats with fitted EC50 values, flow-cytometry panels reporting both positive-cell percentage and mean fluorescence intensity, PHA induction screening results, and pSTAT5 response split across CD25-defined subpopulations. Figure captions state what is being compared.","datascience":"Dose-response curve fitting to extract EC50 is the real quantitative work, and it is done properly - including diagnosing why the first ELISA saturated (the TIGIT-Fc coating antigen was being detected by the anti-human IgG1-HRP secondary) and re-running with His-tagged TIGIT. Flow-cytometry gating is used to separate populations and compare signalling within each, with both %positive and MFI reported rather than one summary number. No inferential statistics (no ANOVA, no stated replicate counts or error bars in the text), so the analysis is descriptive rather than statistical.","software":"None.","stack":["TIGIT-binding ELISA with EC50 curve fitting","flow cytometry (CD25, pSTAT5; %positive and MFI)","SDS-PAGE under reducing and non-reducing conditions","CHO transient expression and protein purification","SolidWorks-style CAD for the compact detection device","Gibson assembly / homologous recombination cloning with Sanger verification"],"techniques":["concentration-response curve fitting and EC50 comparison across three molecular formats","assay-interference troubleshooting and antigen substitution","phenotype-based model adaptation (PHA-induced CD25-high population as a Treg receptor proxy)","subpopulation-resolved signalling comparison","comparative literature review to specify instrument requirements"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Modest and mostly instrumental to the Human Practices work rather than a programme in its own right. There is an online questionnaire with 131 respondents (concerns clustered on efficacy, long-term side effects and cost, plus a stated appetite for disease knowledge), school outreach including a session with 15 final-year high-school students with a post-activity feedback survey, and a dual-use forum organised with two Shandong University academics after the iGEM Safety and Security Committee raised dual-use analysis. The Education page exists but is empty.","ihp":"Genuinely project-shaping, organised around four questions and a stakeholder table that pairs each input with the team's response and its outcome status. The pivot is documented honestly: the team began assuming alcohol consumption meant liver cancer, and oncologist Dr Meng Min redirected them to gastric cancer, pointing out that because gastric cancer is predominantly East Asian it receives less targeted-drug investment than globally prevalent cancers. Professor Yang Zhe's warning about excessive immune activation reframed the bifunctional design and set 'advanced gastric cancer, combination therapy' as the research context. Antibody engineer Professor Liu Zhifang's point that binding must be re-measured after adding modules is directly why TIGIT binding was tested separately for all three formats. A WuXi AppTec expert (anonymised as Dr Z) pushed them to distinguish a change in response bias from a change in overall activity, and reviewed their questionnaire wording. A patient's family member (Ms Wang) shifted the evaluation goal toward completing treatment rather than efficacy alone. The Safety and Security Committee exchange is what selected CHO cells as the chassis.","realWorld":"The Alternative Platform page is the real deliverable and the most transferable thing here: a documented mammalian expression and functional-evaluation workflow built entirely inside the 2025-onward iGEM high-school White List, which bans Check-in and Animal Use forms. CHO cells produce the molecules, Jurkat cells measure the response, and the team shows how to translate a tumour-immunology question into something testable with only a whitelisted cell line - including the PHA/CD25 trick that substitutes a receptor phenotype for an unavailable cell type. Contribution also covers the fusion-protein workflow, the modular architecture, documented assay interference, and a compact organoid-chip detection device prototype (sample chamber, constant-temperature heating, illumination, image acquisition, control system) specified as a low-cost alternative to a microplate reader. The business plan covers staged financing and technology licensing.","partners":["Dr Meng Min, oncologist","Professor Yang Zhe (tumour immunology)","Professor Liu Zhifang, antibody engineering","WuXi AppTec drug-development expert (anonymised as Dr Z)","Shandong University academics (dual-use forum)","iGEM Safety and Security Committee","President Zhang Zhongjiang (health communication and business planning)","a patient's family member (anonymised as Ms Wang)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6177/wiki/description/fig-03.avif","caption":"From design to initial validation: the five engineering cycles taking FusionDrive from anti-TIGIT antibody to wild-type IL-2 fusion to the low-alpha/high-beta IL-2 variant fusion.","credit":"Team SEHS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6177/wiki/alternative-platform/fig-04.avif","caption":"TIGIT-binding ELISA concentration-response curves for the three molecular formats, the dataset from which the team fitted EC50 values of 0.6317 nM (antibody) and 1.335 nM (IL-2 fusion).","credit":"Team SEHS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6177/wiki/alternative-platform/fig-08.avif","caption":"pSTAT5 responses across CD25-defined Jurkat populations, the readout built to test the low-alpha design using only a whitelisted cell line.","credit":"Team SEHS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6177/wiki/alternative-platform/fig-01.avif","caption":"Overview of the FusionDrive mammalian cell expression and functional evaluation platform, built entirely within the iGEM high-school White List.","credit":"Team SEHS, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"SEHS is a wet-lab-first project whose dry lab is thin but not decorative: EC50 curve fitting and subpopulation-resolved flow-cytometry analysis are real quantitative work and well within high-school reach, yet an antibody-cytokine fusion project with no structure prediction, no linker modelling and no docking is leaving free analysis on the table. The limiting factor is clearly mentorship rather than tooling or compute - the team had access to CHO culture and a flow cytometer, which is far rarer than a free AlphaFold or HDOCK run, so someone simply never pointed them at the computational side.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/sehs/","https://2026.igem.wiki/sehs/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/sehs/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/sehs/alternative-platform","https://2026.igem.wiki/sehs/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/sehs/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/sehs/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/sehs/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/sehs/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/sehs/parts","https://2026.igem.wiki/sehs/safety"],"rank":7},"6178":{"team":"HFI","id":"6178","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"Therapeutics","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/","projectTitle":"TWO EcN, ONE METABOLIC MISSION - A Probiotic Synergistic Therapy for the Rare Disease Hyperlysinemia","projectTitle_zh":"TWO EcN, ONE METABOLIC MISSION — 以益生菌協同療法治療罕見疾病高離胺酸血症","tagline":"A dual-strain E. coli Nissle 1917 consortium, physically stapled together with SpyTag/SpyCatcher, that degrades dietary lysine in the gut so hyperlysinemia patients can escape lifelong diet restriction.","tagline_zh":"一組以 SpyTag/SpyCatcher 實體釘接在一起的雙菌株 E. coli Nissle 1917 群落，在腸道中分解飲食來源的離胺酸，讓高離胺酸血症患者得以擺脫終身飲食限制。","summary":"HFI (International Department, The Affiliated High School of South China Normal University, Guangzhou) built an orally delivered live biotherapeutic for hyperlysinemia, a rare AASS-mutation disorder with no approved therapy and an incidence near 1 in 411,000. They split the human saccharopine pathway across two EcN populations - an upstream strain expressing LKR and SDH, a downstream strain expressing ALDH and AASDHPPT - knocked out the endogenous ldcC lysine decarboxylase by CRISPR-Cas9 to remove background lysine consumption, and covalently coupled the two strains using eCPX-displayed SpyTag/SpyCatcher so intermediates pass between cells over a short diffusion distance. Biosafety is handled by a dual-input kill switch where an arabinose-driven Bxb1 serine integrase inverts the lysis-E cassette and an oxygen-sensing PcyoA promoter only fires outside the anaerobic gut. The project won because the dry lab genuinely steered the wet lab (NetLogo screening picked the RBS before cloning), the part collection was fully characterised with HPLC-MS, and the education and IHP programmes were unusually systematic for a high school team.","summary_zh":"HFI（廣州華南師範大學附屬中學國際部）為高離胺酸血症打造了一款口服的活體生物療法；這是一種由 AASS 突變造成的罕見疾病，目前沒有核准療法，發生率約為 1/411,000。他們把人體的 saccharopine 代謝路徑拆分到兩群 EcN 上——上游菌株表現 LKR 與 SDH，下游菌株表現 ALDH 與 AASDHPPT——並以 CRISPR-Cas9 剔除內源的 ldcC 離胺酸脫羧酶，以消除背景的離胺酸消耗；再以 eCPX 展示的 SpyTag/SpyCatcher 把兩個菌株以共價方式耦合起來，使中間產物在很短的擴散距離內於細胞間傳遞。生物安全由一個雙輸入致死開關處理：由阿拉伯糖驅動的 Bxb1 絲胺酸整合酶會把 lysis-E 卡匣反轉，而感測氧氣的 PcyoA 啟動子只有在離開厭氧的腸道環境後才會啟動。此專題之所以勝出，是因為乾實驗確實引導了濕實驗（NetLogo 篩選在選殖之前就選定了 RBS）、元件集合以 HPLC-MS 做了完整特性分析，而教育與 IHP 的規劃對一支高中隊伍而言異常地系統化。","awards":["Top 10 (High School)","Best Part Collection — Nominee (High School)","Best Education — Winner (High School)","Best Presentation — Nominee (High School)","Best Wiki — Nominee (High School)","Best Village Project — Winner (Infectious Diseases / Therapeutics / Diagnostics / Oncology)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Two complementary models, both used to make decisions rather than decorate the wiki. First, an agent-based stochastic contact model in NetLogo 3D 7.0.4: 200 cells (100 SpyTag type A, 100 SpyCatcher type B) random-walk in a periodic box spanning -16 to 16 units, diffusion speed 0.17 per tick, interaction radius 1.4, 2,000 ticks; each successful A-B contact creates an undirected graph edge, decrements both cells' remaining binding capacity, and merges cluster IDs, so a bacterial aggregate is literally a connected component of a graph. They swept seven RBS parts (B0032, B0033, B0035, B0029, B0031, B0030, B0034) mapped to 5-100 surface display sites and tracked mean cluster size, max cluster size and the full size distribution, expanding the noisy 30-site condition to 60 replicate runs to characterise its stochastic variance (max 109.6 +/- 34.5). Second, a mass-conserving 13-state-variable compartmental ODE simulator of the lysine cascade: metabolites L (lysine), S (saccharopine), A (AASA) and P (AAA) across three compartments (extracellular medium, upstream SpyCatcher cytoplasm, downstream SpyTag cytoplasm), Michaelis-Menten rate laws with half-saturation 0.2, a saturating contact signal H = B/(0.05+B) converting occupied binding capacity into extra inter-strain exchange conductance g_CT, integrated with fourth-order Runge-Kutta at base step 0.001 (reported backbone mass-balance error ~3.77e-15), with toxic AASA exposure summarised by trapezoidal AUC.","frameworks_zh":"兩個互補的模型，都是用來做決策、而不是裝點 wiki。第一個是在 NetLogo 3D 7.0.4 中建的代理人隨機接觸模型：200 個細胞（100 個 SpyTag 的 A 型、100 個 SpyCatcher 的 B 型）在 -16 到 16 單位的週期性邊界盒中隨機漫步，擴散速度為每 tick 0.17，交互作用半徑 1.4，共 2,000 個 tick；每一次成功的 A-B 接觸就建立一條無向圖的邊、把兩個細胞剩餘的結合容量各減一，並合併群集 ID，因此一個細菌聚集體實際上就是圖上的一個連通分量。他們掃過七個 RBS 元件（B0032、B0033、B0035、B0029、B0031、B0030、B0034），對應到 5 到 100 個表面展示位點，並追蹤平均群集大小、最大群集大小與完整的大小分布，其中把雜訊較大的 30 位點條件擴充到 60 次重複執行，以描述其隨機變異（最大值 109.6 +/- 34.5）。第二個是一個質量守恆、含 13 個狀態變數的隔室 ODE 模擬器，描述離胺酸的串聯反應：代謝物 L（離胺酸）、S（saccharopine）、A（AASA）與 P（AAA），分布在三個隔室（胞外培養基、上游 SpyCatcher 的細胞質、下游 SpyTag 的細胞質）；採 Michaelis-Menten 速率式、半飽和常數 0.2，並以一個飽和式的接觸訊號 H = B/(0.05+B) 把已佔用的結合容量轉換為額外的跨菌株交換傳導 g_CT，以四階 Runge-Kutta 積分、基礎步長 0.001（報告的骨幹質量平衡誤差約 3.77e-15），並以梯形法 AUC 彙總具毒性的 AASA 暴露量。","dataviz":"Both models were ported to interactive browser pages embedded in the wiki, so a judge or reader can move the sliders and re-run the simulation live with no local install: the ODE metabolic simulator at https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/static/model/metabolism.html and the NetLogo cluster model at https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/static/model/netlogo.html. Outputs are dynamic cluster visualisations, metabolite time-course curves and quantitative readouts. Alongside this they reported the full cluster-size distribution (not just means), particle-weighted versus number-weighted distributions, and a table pairing each RBS part number with its translational strength tier and simulated outcome, which makes the in-silico screen auditable.","dataviz_zh":"兩個模型都移植成內嵌於 wiki 的互動網頁，使評審或讀者不必在本機安裝任何東西就能拉動滑桿、即時重跑模擬：ODE 代謝模擬器在 https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/static/model/metabolism.html ，NetLogo 群集模型在 https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/static/model/netlogo.html 。輸出為動態的群集視覺化、代謝物時間曲線與定量讀數。除此之外，他們報告了完整的群集大小分布（不只是平均值）、以顆粒加權與以數量加權的分布對照，以及一張把每個 RBS 元件編號與其轉譯強度等級、模擬結果並列的表格，使這次電腦篩選可供查核。","datascience":"The dry lab was used specifically to fill a measurement gap: they could not quantify the short-lived intermediates saccharopine and AASA in the wet lab, so the ODE model predicted them and exposed an explicit design trade-off - at SC:ST 2:1 lysine clearance is fastest (residual lysine 0.0519) but AASA peaks highest (0.3767, AUC 10.43), while at 1:2 AASA stays low (peak 0.1123, AUC 3.14) but 0.2980 lysine is left unconsumed. That framing (two goals that cannot be maximised at once) drove the choice of co-culture ratios actually tested. The cluster model's prediction that moderate display (B0035, 15 sites, mean max cluster 48.67 cells, about 24% of the system) sits in the usable middle regime while 50+ sites collapses 91-98% of cells into one giant component was then checked at the bench by fluorescence microscopy with ImageJ quantification of red-green overlapping cluster count and core area (3 clusters/field at 2:1 rising to 16 at 1:1 and 14 at 1:2, mean core area 15.04 to 19.41 um2), and the simulated ratio ranking matched the HPLC lysine-removal ranking. Measurement side: a cheap ninhydrin colorimetric screen was calibrated against FDAA-derivatised HPLC-MS (lysine derivative at 17.04 min, m/z 398.1, calibration R2 = 0.9985).","datascience_zh":"乾實驗被明確用來填補量測上的缺口：他們在濕實驗中無法定量短命的中間產物 saccharopine 與 AASA，於是用 ODE 模型預測，並藉此揭露一個明確的設計取捨——在 SC:ST 為 2:1 時離胺酸清除最快（殘餘離胺酸 0.0519），但 AASA 的峰值也最高（0.3767，AUC 10.43）；而在 1:2 時 AASA 維持在低位（峰值 0.1123，AUC 3.14），卻有 0.2980 的離胺酸未被消耗。這種「兩個目標無法同時最大化」的框架，決定了實際測試的共培養比例。群集模型預測中等展示量（B0035、15 個位點，最大群集平均 48.67 個細胞，約為整個系統的 24%）落在可用的中間區域，而 50 個位點以上則會讓 91-98% 的細胞塌縮成單一巨大連通分量；這項預測接著在實驗檯上以螢光顯微鏡檢驗，並用 ImageJ 定量紅綠重疊的群集數與核心面積（2:1 時每視野 3 個群集，1:1 升至 16 個、1:2 為 14 個，核心面積平均 15.04 至 19.41 um2），模擬得到的比例排序與 HPLC 測得的離胺酸移除排序一致。量測方面：以 FDAA 衍生化的 HPLC-MS 校正了一套便宜的 ninhydrin 比色篩檢（離胺酸衍生物滯留時間 17.04 分鐘、m/z 398.1，校正曲線 R2 = 0.9985）。","software":"No standalone software tool was released, but the two models are published as free-standing interactive web pages inside the wiki (metabolism.html and netlogo.html) and the complete NetLogo source (setup, go, update-cluster-distribution, avg-cluster-size, max-cluster-size, sweep-rbs, scan-catcher-series procedures) is printed in full on the Model page so another team can rerun the screen. Repository: https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/hfi. They also contributed a documented part collection to the Registry including BBa_26S7HLMM (ldcC target sequence) and BBa_269KMPAL (pEcgRNA-ldcC), plus the two models listed as community contributions.","software_zh":"沒有釋出獨立的軟體工具，但兩個模型以可獨立運作的互動網頁發布在 wiki 內（metabolism.html 與 netlogo.html），而完整的 NetLogo 原始碼（setup、go、update-cluster-distribution、avg-cluster-size、max-cluster-size、sweep-rbs、scan-catcher-series 等程序）則完整印在 Model 頁上，讓其他隊伍可以重跑這次篩選。程式庫：https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/hfi 。他們也向 Registry 貢獻了一組有完整文件的元件集合，包括 BBa_26S7HLMM（ldcC 標的序列）與 BBa_269KMPAL（pEcgRNA-ldcC），另有兩個模型列為社群貢獻。","stack":["NetLogo 3D 7.0.4","agent-based / graph connected-component modelling","ODE system (13 state variables, 3 compartments)","fourth-order Runge-Kutta integration","Michaelis-Menten kinetics","trapezoidal AUC integration","interactive HTML/JS model front-ends","ImageJ","HPLC-MS (FDAA derivatisation)","CRISPR-Cas9 genome editing","GitLab"],"techniques":["in-silico RBS strength screening before cloning","replicate-expanded stochastic variance characterisation (n=60 at the unstable condition)","cluster-size distribution analysis","strain-ratio flux trade-off analysis (AASA peak vs AUC vs residual lysine)","model-to-bench validation by fluorescence microscopy + ImageJ","colorimetric assay calibrated against HPLC-MS","mass-balance error reporting as a numerical sanity check"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education was designed from survey data rather than guesswork, and ran on an explicit five-step cycle they named CLEAR (Connect, Layer, Engage, Assess, Reinforce) in which every activity had to report a measured outcome and a change for the next iteration. Highlights: a self-written microbiology comic book issued in Cantonese and Mandarin dialect versions, with English, Japanese and German recorded audiobooks and text versions in Arabic, German, Russian, French, Korean, Portuguese, Japanese, Thai, Spanish and Indonesian - explicitly supplied as text so local educators can generate their own AI text-to-speech audio in languages the team does not speak. They ran a 100+ student conference at HFI International, a HFI Academic Summit with hands-on fruit DNA extraction, recorded lab-technique video lessons (pipetting, agarose gel electrophoresis, clean bench, plus an SMA rare-disease case study) on iGEM Video and Bilibili, an online Q&A session on Tencent Meeting, a university biology major exhibition poster, a Gobi Desert biology trip, a synthetic biology student society, outreach at the Guangzhou Social Welfare Institute, and a professional session with HSBC on financial literacy. Impact was measured with paired pre/post surveys: at the Academic Summit (n=24) correct identification of synthetic biology rose 79% to 96% with the 'synthetic biology is another name for genetic testing' misconception falling 8% to 0%, and correct understanding that DNA is in every living cell including fruit cells rose 42% to 88%. They also tracked platform metrics honestly, noting that 15 WeChat posts drew 248 likes, 955 views, 63 shares and zero comments, concluding one-way delivery was failing and pivoting to interactive formats, after which video lessons drew comments for the first time.","publicEngagement_zh":"教育工作是依問卷資料設計、而非憑猜測，並依他們命名為 CLEAR（Connect、Layer、Engage、Assess、Reinforce）的明確五步循環運作，其中每項活動都必須回報一項可量測的結果與下一輪的一項改動。亮點包括：一本自行創作的微生物學漫畫，發行粵語與國語方言版本，並錄製英語、日語與德語有聲書，另提供阿拉伯語、德語、俄語、法語、韓語、葡萄牙語、日語、泰語、西班牙語與印尼語的文字版——文字版是刻意提供的，讓各地教育者能用 AI 文字轉語音自行生成團隊成員不會說的語言的音檔。他們在 HFI 國際部辦了一場 100 人以上的學生會議、一場包含動手做水果 DNA 萃取的 HFI 學術高峰會，在 iGEM Video 與 Bilibili 上發布實驗技術影片課程（吸量操作、瓊膠電泳、無菌操作檯，另有一則 SMA 罕病案例研究），在騰訊會議上辦線上問答，在大學生物科系展覽張貼海報，辦了一趟戈壁沙漠生物考察，成立了合成生物學學生社團，到廣州市社會福利院做科普，並與匯豐銀行合辦一場金融素養的專業講座。成效以前後配對問卷量測：在學術高峰會（n=24）中，能正確辨識合成生物學的比例從 79% 升至 96%，「合成生物學只是基因檢測的另一個說法」這個迷思從 8% 降到 0%，而正確理解 DNA 存在於每個活細胞、包括水果細胞中的比例從 42% 升至 88%。他們也誠實追蹤平台數據，指出 15 篇微信貼文獲得 248 個讚、955 次瀏覽、63 次分享與零則留言，由此判斷單向傳遞行不通，轉而採用互動形式，之後影片課程才首次出現留言。","ihp":"IHP ran through a named six-step cycle (LYSERA: Listen, Yield, Shape, Execute, Reflect, Apply) across six sequenced phases - stakeholder mapping on an interest/power matrix, a 434-response public survey, technical validation, clinical and patient engagement, commercial and regulatory consultation, and peer review - then looped back through phases 3 to 6 a second time. The changes are concrete. Dr. Mingjun Sun (Sichuan University, synthetic biology and AI protein design) argued the lag between lysine detection and enzyme expression would make the probiotics miss the postprandial treatment window, so HFI abandoned the lysine-responsive promoter entirely and switched to constitutive expression of all degradation enzymes; he also warned that SpyTag/SpyCatcher aggregation risk scales with expression level and suggested building a computational model instead of trial and error, which is the direct origin of the NetLogo cluster model and the choice of medium-to-low strength RBS. Professor Liujie Huo questioned whether intestinal lysine concentration tracks blood lysine at all, forcing them to re-examine the physiological basis and repositioning of the product. The public survey changed the language of every outreach material: 'genetically modified' was replaced with 'engineered' across all materials because the survey showed the former triggered unease, and because 76.04% of respondents had heard of rare diseases but could not name one while only 8.29% could name three, education was rebuilt to start from absolute basics. Survey findings that 56.22% supported national insurance coverage and 59.45% preferred prescription-drug regulation validated the hospital-first go-to-market route and tiered pricing. Mr. Guodong Huo of the Illness Challenge Foundation insisted patients are not defined by their condition, which set a non-stigmatising language policy and a no-false-hope rule for all materials. Safety feedback (protease degradation risk) added simulated intestinal fluid stability tests to the experimental plan.","ihp_zh":"IHP 以一個命名過的六步循環（LYSERA：Listen、Yield、Shape、Execute、Reflect、Apply）貫穿六個依序推進的階段——以興趣／影響力矩陣繪製利害關係人地圖、一份 434 份回覆的公眾問卷、技術驗證、臨床與病友端接觸、商業與法規諮詢，以及同儕審閱——之後再把第 3 到第 6 階段跑過第二輪。改動相當具體。四川大學的孫明軍博士（合成生物學與 AI 蛋白質設計）指出，從偵測到離胺酸到酵素表現之間的時間落差會讓益生菌錯過餐後的治療窗口，於是 HFI 徹底放棄了對離胺酸有反應的啟動子，改為讓所有分解酵素都以組成型表現；他也警告 SpyTag/SpyCatcher 的聚集風險會隨表現量上升，建議建一個運算模型、而不是靠試誤，這正是 NetLogo 群集模型與選用中低強度 RBS 的直接來源。霍丽洁教授則質疑腸道內的離胺酸濃度究竟是否與血中離胺酸連動，迫使他們重新檢視產品的生理學基礎與定位。公眾問卷改變了所有科普材料的用語：所有材料中的「基因改造」都換成了「工程改造」，因為問卷顯示前者會引發不安；又因為 76.04% 的受訪者聽過罕見疾病但說不出任何一種、只有 8.29% 能說出三種，教育內容便重建為從最基本處開始。問卷顯示 56.22% 支持納入國家醫保、59.45% 偏好以處方藥方式管理，這佐證了先走醫院的上市路徑與分級定價。病痛挑戰基金會的霍国东先生強調病人不該被其疾病定義，這確立了所有材料的非汙名化用語政策與「不給假希望」原則。安全性方面的意見（蛋白酶降解風險）則讓實驗計畫加上了模擬腸液的穩定性測試。","realWorld":"A full commercial dossier for EcN-BioShield covering unmet need, TAM/SAM/SOM, PESTEL, Porter's Five Forces, SWOT, competitor analysis against lysine-free medical foods such as Hyper LYS Anamix Infant (UK NHS ~GBP 54 per 400 g can, roughly GBP 1,500-2,000/year), a Business Model Canvas, and a 20-year financial projection. Pricing was set at 2,000 CNY per 30-capsule bottle (24,000 CNY per patient-year) after stakeholder consultation on affordability, with a modelled initial funding requirement of 1,260,000 CNY, break-even in year 16.79 and cumulative payoff of 59,020,546 CNY by year 20 - unusually long-horizon honesty for a student plan. They mapped three regulatory routes in parallel because hyperlysinemia is not in China's Rare Disease Catalog and there is no settled Live Biotherapeutic Product registration pathway, including applying to NMPA's Center for Drug Evaluation for Orphan Drug Designation. Risk management is broken out by regulatory, clinical, commercial, technical, public-acceptance, competitive and financial risk, with an early/mid/long-term (1-5, 5-10, 11+ year) milestone timeline. Ethical commitments include tiered pricing plus advocacy for national insurance coverage, no overstatement of readiness, age-appropriate formulations, and patient-data confidentiality.","realWorld_zh":"EcN-BioShield 有一份完整的商業文件，涵蓋未滿足需求、TAM/SAM/SOM、PESTEL、波特五力、SWOT，以及對照無離胺酸醫療食品（如 Hyper LYS Anamix Infant，英國 NHS 每 400 g 罐約 54 英鎊，約每年 1,500-2,000 英鎊）的競爭分析，另有商業模式畫布與一份 20 年財務預測。價格在就可負擔性諮詢利害關係人後，訂為每瓶 30 顆膠囊 2,000 人民幣（每位患者每年 24,000 人民幣），模型推算初始資金需求為 1,260,000 人民幣，於第 16.79 年損益兩平，到第 20 年累積回報 59,020,546 人民幣——對一份學生計畫而言，這種長期視野的誠實相當罕見。他們並行規劃了三條法規路徑，因為高離胺酸血症並未列入中國的罕見病目錄，而活體生物治療產品也沒有定案的註冊途徑，其中包括向 NMPA 藥品審評中心申請孤兒藥資格。風險管理依法規、臨床、商業、技術、公眾接受度、競爭與財務分別拆開，並附一條短／中／長期（1-5、5-10、11 年以上）的里程碑時程。倫理承諾包括分級定價並同時倡議納入國家醫保、不誇大技術成熟度、提供符合各年齡層的劑型，以及病人資料保密。","partners":["Dr. Mingjun Sun, Sichuan University","Professor Liujie Huo","Professor Shengbo Wu","Professor Ran An","Professor Xiaofeng Yang","Dr. Guangquan Chen (clinician)","Mr. Guodong Huo, Illness Challenge Foundation (rare disease advocacy)","Mr. Junhao Li, Mr. K and Mr. Mao Ye (commercial / regulatory advisers)","HSBC (financial literacy and investment workshop)","2nd iGBA Exchange Event","South China Regional iGEM Exchange","HKUST (GZ) iGEM team","Guangzhou Social Welfare Institute","Cataverse Lab"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6178/wiki/model/4.avif","caption":"NetLogo agent-based output: simulation trajectories (A) and cluster-size distributions (B) under different SpyCatcher binding capacities, showing the transition from fragmented association at low display to near-global condensation at 50+ sites.","caption_zh":"NetLogo 代理人模型輸出：不同 SpyCatcher 結合容量下的模擬軌跡（A）與群集大小分布（B），顯示從低展示量時的零散結合，到 50 個位點以上時近乎全域凝聚的轉變。","credit":"Team HFI, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6178/wiki/model/1.avif","caption":"The team's NetLogo 3D model interface used to screen candidate RBS parts for SpyCatcher surface display before any cloning was done.","caption_zh":"團隊用來在任何選殖工作開始之前篩選 SpyCatcher 表面展示候選 RBS 元件的 NetLogo 3D 模型介面。","credit":"Team HFI, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6178/wiki/model/10.avif","caption":"HPLC quantification of residual lysine in culture supernatant across three strain ratios, with and without the SpyTag/SpyCatcher binding module - the wet-lab test of the model's prediction (the 2:1 ratio performed best, as simulated; the crosslinking benefit itself was not significant).","caption_zh":"以 HPLC 定量三種菌株比例下培養上清液中的殘餘離胺酸，並比較有無 SpyTag/SpyCatcher 結合模組——這是對模型預測的濕實驗檢驗（2:1 比例表現最佳，與模擬一致；但交聯本身帶來的益處並不顯著）。","credit":"Team HFI, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6178/wiki/education/figure-9.avif","caption":"The HFI Academic Summit, where a hands-on fruit DNA extraction activity was added in response to feedback that the previous session had been too academically dense; pre/post surveys measured the learning gain.","caption_zh":"HFI 學術高峰會；因前一場活動被反映過於學術密集，這次加入了動手做水果 DNA 萃取的活動，並以前後問卷量測學習增益。","credit":"Team HFI, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Copy HFI's habit of making the dry lab a gatekeeper for the wet lab: a free NetLogo agent-based model screened seven candidate RBS parts and picked B0035 before a single plasmid was built, and an ODE model predicted the intermediates the team physically could not measure - both then republished as live browser sliders so a reader can rerun them. The second transferable move is their CLEAR/LYSERA discipline of refusing to log any outreach or stakeholder meeting unless it produced a measured outcome (paired pre/post surveys, engagement metrics including the embarrassing zero-comment result) and a named change in the next iteration.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"值得借鏡的是 HFI 讓乾實驗擔任濕實驗守門人的習慣：一個免費的 NetLogo 代理人模型篩過七個候選 RBS 元件、在一個質體都還沒做出來之前就選定了 B0035，而一個 ODE 模型則預測了團隊實際上量不到的中間產物——兩者之後都以可在瀏覽器即時操作的滑桿重新發布，讓讀者能自己重跑。第二項可移植的做法是他們 CLEAR／LYSERA 的紀律：任何科普活動或利害關係人會面，若沒有產出可量測的結果（前後配對問卷、互動數據，包括那個令人難為情的零留言結果）以及下一輪具名的改動，就不予登錄。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/measurement","https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/inclusivity","https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/awards","https://2026.igem.wiki/hfi/static/model/metabolism.html","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/hfi","https://api.igem.org/v1/teams/6178"],"rank":143},"6185":{"team":"Lambert-GA","id":"6185","section":"High School","country":"United States","village":"Conservation","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/","projectTitle":"SWARM - de novo minibinders against Deformed Wing Virus paired with multiplexed RNAi against Varroa destructor","projectTitle_zh":"SWARM——針對殘翅病毒的 de novo minibinder，搭配針對蜂蟹蟎 Varroa destructor 的多工 RNAi","tagline":"Protecting honeybees by hitting both the virus and the mite that carries it, with the first reported minibinder confirmed to bind DWV's VP3.","tagline_zh":"同時打擊病毒與攜帶病毒的蟎來保護蜜蜂，並做出已確認可結合 DWV VP3 的首例 minibinder。","summary":"Lambert iGEM (Suwanee, Georgia) built SWARM to attack the two linked causes of honeybee colony collapse: Deformed Wing Virus and the Varroa destructor mite that vectors it. US beekeepers reported losing 55.6% of managed colonies between April 2024 and April 2025, and Georgia's large operations lost roughly 88,000 colonies in nine months. SWARM pairs a computationally designed 79-amino-acid minibinder against the exposed P-domain of DWV's VP3 capsid protein - experimentally confirmed by biolayer interferometry at KD = 603.6 nM (95% CI 497.1-733.3 nM), to the team's knowledge the first reported minibinder with confirmed binding to VP3 - with a multiplexed dsRNA construct silencing three Varroa salivary-gland genes (Vd-CHIsal, Vd-CHIBIN, VdAV422) at once to blunt resistance. Both components are delivered through feeding practices beekeepers already use. They took the High School Grand Prize plus Best Model, Best Wiki, Best Sustainable Development Impact and Best Village Project, and the modelling is the headline: four linked models spanning protein design benchmarking on 5,721 experimentally labelled designs, oral pharmacokinetics with Sobol sensitivity analysis, a 13-ODE RNAi network, and an individual-based six-year colony epidemiology simulation across two climates.","summary_zh":"Lambert iGEM（喬治亞州 Suwanee）做出 SWARM，攻擊造成蜜蜂蜂群崩解的兩個相連原因：殘翅病毒（DWV）與傳播它的蜂蟹蟎 Varroa destructor。美國養蜂人報告在 2024 年 4 月至 2025 年 4 月間損失了 55.6% 的管理蜂群，喬治亞州的大型蜂場在九個月內損失約 88,000 個蜂群。SWARM 把一個以計算設計、長 79 個胺基酸的 minibinder（針對 DWV 的 VP3 外殼蛋白中暴露的 P-domain，並以生物層干涉技術實驗確認 KD = 603.6 nM，95% CI 497.1-733.3 nM，就該隊所知是首例確認可結合 VP3 的 minibinder）與一個多工 dsRNA 構築體配對，後者同時靜默三個 Varroa 唾液腺基因（Vd-CHIsal、Vd-CHIBIN、VdAV422）以降低抗性風險。兩個組件都透過養蜂人原本就在用的餵食方式投遞。該隊拿下高中組總冠軍，外加最佳模型、最佳 Wiki、最佳永續發展影響與最佳 Village 專案，而建模是最醒目的部分：四個互相銜接的模型，涵蓋在 5,721 個有實驗標註的設計上做蛋白質設計基準測試、含 Sobol 敏感度分析的口服藥物動力學、一個 13 條 ODE 的 RNAi 網路，以及一個跨兩種氣候、以個體為基礎的六年蜂群流行病學模擬。","awards":["Grand Prize Winner (High School)","Top 10 (High School)","Best Model — Winner (High School)","Best Hardware — Nominee (High School)","Best Wiki — Winner (High School)","Best Sustainable Development Impact — Winner (High School)","Best Village Project — Winner (Climate Crisis / Conservation / Bioremediation)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Four models, each doing distinct work. (1) Minibinder design. No de novo minibinder or validated minibinder epitope existed for DWV, so they compared isolated P-domain structures against the assembled capsid to assess which surfaces are actually accessible, and investigated five candidate epitopes (an initial C-terminal region at I405/F408, EP-1 at I302/Y359/R395, EP-2 at V322/Q325/Y346, the QP/A-ridge at Q325/P326, and a putative catalytic triad at H277/S278/D294). They benchmarked computational confidence metrics against 5,721 labelled designs across 41 protein targets (849 confirmed binders, 4,872 non-binders) using ROC-AUC: minimum ipSAE scored 0.806 and ipSAE 0.801 pooled, Boltz-2 ipTM only 0.628, and a combined 38-metric ensemble just 0.541 - barely above chance - so adding metrics did not help. They also found minimum ipSAE degrades when comparing designs within a single target, which is exactly their use case, so they built a filtering framework combining predicted interface quality, amino-acid composition, predicted aggregation propensity, independent monomer prediction and cross-tool agreement; the motivating evidence was a candidate whose repeated minimum ipSAE predictions ranged from 0.000 to 0.676. Designs were generated with three independent tools - Mosaic, BindCraft and BoltzProt - with Boltz and Protenix used for additional structural evaluation; across 1,176 pairwise comparisons the median Jaccard similarity between BindCraft and Mosaic target-contact residue sets was 0.000 and their predicted interface centres were a median 42.9 angstroms apart, proving the tools explore genuinely different surfaces. Round 1 submitted 15 designs and produced zero confirmed binders (including 5G51_V4_seed01 at ipSAE 0.927 and ipTM 0.958, which failed); Round 2 generated 103 candidate entries, submitted 20, and produced one confirmed binder, l79_s469532_mpnn9, a BindCraft design associated with the QP/A-ridge that notably did not have the highest minimum ipSAE in the batch. Total compute spend was under USD 400 across 35 tested candidates, which they contrast against the USD 10,000 GPU budget per single-target campaign in Anthropic's 2026 autonomous binder-design technical report. (2) Minibinder dosing. A two-compartment oral pharmacokinetic model following functional protein from feeder to crop to gut to hemolymph: dG/dt = R_crop(t) - (ka + kt + kg)G and dH/dt = kaG - khH, with crop emptying fitted from Fournier et al. as V_crop = max(0, 17.966 - 0.159 t_min) uL reaching zero at about 113 minutes, digestive half-lives sampled log-normally around 31 and 54 minute values measured for native Manse-AS peptide in Myzus persicae and Acyrthosiphon pisum aphid gut extracts, and circulating stability from a juvenile hormone esterase analogue. 1,000 parameter sets were simulated for a 40,000-bee colony over 56 days; at a selected 100 nM average circulating concentration the median requirement was 29.60 g prepared protein (0.529 g/day prepared, 0.447 g/day active swallowed). Sobol total-effect sensitivity indices on log10(course mass), from 1,024 base samples and 7,168 model evaluations, ranked circulating functional loss 0.606, digestive loss 0.263, gut absorption 0.116, hemolymph volume 0.018 and intestinal transit 0.005 - and they reported that the gram-scale analysis failed its numerical checks so only the log-scale ranking is given. (3) RNAi model. A 13-species, 23-reaction ODE network in MATLAB SimBiology covering Dicer-2 processing of multiplexed dsRNA into three siRNAs, Ago2 loading into RISC, RISC-mediated Michaelis-Menten cleavage of a targeted Renilla transcript, untargeted Firefly as the control, plus transcription, translation, plasmid dilution, protein turnover and free-RNA degradation, with every rate parameter tabulated against its source and explicitly labelled as a measurement, a team estimate or an assumption. Predicted signal decrease was 37.50% with one siRNA, 67.51% with two, 83.41% with three directly delivered siRNAs, and 83.04% with the multiplexed dsRNA construct - the key result, since it predicts that bundling three guides into one molecule preserves knockdown. Local normalised sensitivity put RISC-mediated cleavage (Vm_1) at -1.72, the dominant assumption, while free Ago2 was near zero. (4) Epidemiological model. An individual-based six-year daily simulation of a two-deep-box Langstroth hive with about 42,000 brood cells, tracking adult bees individually by age, task, infection status and relative syrup intake, and mites on adults individually with sealed-cell brood and mites grouped by developmental day. It composes published frameworks - Sumpter and Martin for mite-virus-colony dynamics, Khoury/Myerscough/Barron for the saturating colony-size term N/(w+N) and forager recruitment R = alpha - sigma(F/N), Betti/Wahl/Zamir for infection-driven mortality, BEEPOP and BEEHAVE for seasonal development and weather-dependent foraging, and Martin and Calis for mite development and transfer. Daily weather was generated from NOAA 1991-2020 climate normals and 2011-2020 daily records preserving warm/cold runs, with foraging requiring a dry day above 12.8 C; 20 matched weather sequences per scenario across Atlanta and Ithaca gave 800 six-year simulations. Minibinder protection enters per bee as p_i(t) = 1 - exp(-K x_i u(t)) calibrated to 52.6% mean reduction in infection probability at full uptake with a lognormal intake distribution (mean-to-median ratio 1.68, sigma 1.0214); RNAi enters as an exposure state dF_i/dt = k_u x_i u(t)(1 - F_i) - k_loss F_i feeding f_treated(t_c) = f_0[1 - r_max F(t_c)] at brood capping, with r_max = 93.6% from an external study reporting 0.13 offspring per treated mother mite versus 2.04 in control.","frameworks_zh":"四個模型，各自承擔不同的任務。(1) minibinder 設計。DWV 既沒有 de novo minibinder，也沒有經驗證的 minibinder 抗原決定位，於是他們把單獨的 P-domain 結構與組裝完成的外殼相比，評估哪些表面實際上可及，並研究五個候選抗原決定位（最初是 I405/F408 的 C 端區域、EP-1 於 I302/Y359/R395、EP-2 於 V322/Q325/Y346、QP/A 脊於 Q325/P326，以及推測的催化三元體 H277/S278/D294）。他們以 ROC-AUC 把計算信心指標對照 41 個蛋白質標靶、共 5,721 個有標註的設計（849 個確認的結合者、4,872 個非結合者）做基準測試：最小 ipSAE 得 0.806、合併的 ipSAE 得 0.801，Boltz-2 的 ipTM 只有 0.628，而把 38 項指標合起來的集成模型只有 0.541——幾乎只比亂猜好一點，所以加更多指標並沒有幫助。他們還發現，若是在單一標靶內部比較不同設計，最小 ipSAE 的表現會退化，而那恰恰是他們的使用情境，於是他們建了一個篩選框架，結合預測的介面品質、胺基酸組成、預測的聚集傾向、獨立的單體預測與跨工具一致性；促成這個決定的證據是某個候選的最小 ipSAE 重複預測值從 0.000 到 0.676 之間擺盪。設計以三個獨立工具生成——Mosaic、BindCraft 與 BoltzProt——另以 Boltz 與 Protenix 做額外的結構評估；在 1,176 組兩兩比較中，BindCraft 與 Mosaic 的標靶接觸殘基集合的 Jaccard 相似度中位數為 0.000，兩者預測的介面中心相距中位數 42.9 Å，證明這些工具探索的其實是不同的表面。第 1 輪送出 15 個設計，確認的結合者為零（包括 ipSAE 0.927、ipTM 0.958 的 5G51_V4_seed01，它失敗了）；第 2 輪產生 103 個候選條目、送出 20 個，得到一個確認的結合者 l79_s469532_mpnn9，這是一個與 QP/A 脊相關的 BindCraft 設計，而且值得注意的是它的最小 ipSAE 並非該批中最高。35 個測試候選的運算總花費不到 400 美元，他們把這個數字對照 Anthropic 2026 年自主結合蛋白設計技術報告中每一個單一標靶戰役 10,000 美元的 GPU 預算。(2) minibinder 劑量。一個兩室口服藥物動力學模型，追蹤有功能的蛋白質從餵食器到蜜胃、到腸道、再到血淋巴：dG/dt = R_crop(t) - (ka + kt + kg)G 與 dH/dt = kaG - khH，蜜胃排空由 Fournier 等人的資料擬合為 V_crop = max(0, 17.966 - 0.159 t_min) uL，約在 113 分鐘歸零；消化半衰期以對數常態分布取樣，中心落在 Myzus persicae 與 Acyrthosiphon pisum 蚜蟲腸道萃取物中對原生 Manse-AS 肽所量到的 31 與 54 分鐘；循環中的穩定性則取自一個幼生荷爾蒙酯酶的類比物。他們為一個 40,000 隻蜜蜂的蜂群模擬 1,000 組參數、為期 56 天；在選定的平均循環濃度 100 nM 下，需求量中位數為 29.60 g 配製蛋白（每日配製 0.529 g，每日實際吞下的活性成分 0.447 g）。以 1,024 個基礎樣本、7,168 次模型評估計算 log10（療程質量）的 Sobol 總效應敏感度指數，排序為循環中功能損失 0.606、消化損失 0.263、腸道吸收 0.116、血淋巴體積 0.018、腸道通過 0.005——而且他們報告以公克為單位的分析沒有通過數值檢查，所以只提供對數尺度的排序。(3) RNAi 模型。在 MATLAB SimBiology 中建立的 13 個物種、23 個反應的 ODE 網路，涵蓋 Dicer-2 把多工 dsRNA 切成三種 siRNA、Ago2 載入 RISC、RISC 介導並符合 Michaelis-Menten 動力學地切割被標靶的 Renilla 轉錄本、未被標靶的 Firefly 作為對照，再加上轉錄、轉譯、質體稀釋、蛋白質更新與游離 RNA 降解，每個速率參數都列表並附來源，並明確標示它是量測值、團隊估計值或假設值。預測的訊號下降為：一種 siRNA 37.50%、兩種 67.51%、三種直接投遞的 siRNA 83.41%，而多工 dsRNA 構築體為 83.04%——這是關鍵結果，因為它預測把三條導引序列綁進同一個分子仍能維持抑制效果。局部正規化敏感度把 RISC 介導的切割（Vm_1）排在 -1.72，是最主導的假設，而游離 Ago2 則接近零。(4) 流行病學模型。一個以個體為基礎、以日為單位、為期六年的模擬，對象是一個兩層深箱的 Langstroth 蜂箱、約 42,000 個子脾巢房，逐一追蹤成蜂的年齡、任務、感染狀態與相對糖水攝取量，成蜂身上的蟎也逐一追蹤，封蓋巢房與其中的蟎則依發育天數分組。它組合了多個已發表的框架——Sumpter 與 Martin 的蟎—病毒—蜂群動態、Khoury/Myerscough/Barron 的飽和型蜂群規模項 N/(w+N) 與採集蜂招募 R = alpha - sigma(F/N)、Betti/Wahl/Zamir 的感染致死率、BEEPOP 與 BEEHAVE 的季節性發育與天氣相依採集行為，以及 Martin 與 Calis 的蟎發育與轉移。每日天氣由 NOAA 1991-2020 氣候正常值與 2011-2020 每日紀錄生成，並保留暖期與冷期的連續性，採集行為則要求當日無雨且高於 12.8 °C；亞特蘭大與 Ithaca 兩地每個情境各有 20 組配對天氣序列，共 800 次六年模擬。minibinder 的保護以每隻蜂的 p_i(t) = 1 - exp(-K x_i u(t)) 進入模型，校準為完全攝取時感染機率平均下降 52.6%，攝取量採對數常態分布（平均值對中位數比 1.68，sigma 1.0214）；RNAi 則以暴露狀態 dF_i/dt = k_u x_i u(t)(1 - F_i) - k_loss F_i 進入，在封蓋時代入 f_treated(t_c) = f_0[1 - r_max F(t_c)]，其中 r_max = 93.6% 取自一份外部研究，該研究報告處理過的母蟎平均產下 0.13 個後代，對照組為 2.04。","dataviz":"The Best Wiki award is earned by making the models inspectable rather than illustrated. The VP3 epitope map is an interactive 3D viewer with five selectable, labelled regions and a toggle to overlay the confirmed minibinder's predicted pose, backed by a table giving each region's residues, structural rationale and experimental outcome. All 35 submitted minibinder designs are published in a sortable, filterable, searchable table - by design round, by experimental result - with each row expandable to show ipTM, ipSAE (labelled as to whether it is directional minimum ipSAE), design region, BLI sensor loading, the assay note and the source record, plus a full CSV download; failures and 'no usable result' entries are given equal prominence to the one success. A separate full-screen minibinder viewer shows the VP3 and GFP designs. The epidemiological model has a clickable four-stage 'one day in the model' diagram, a weekly-resolution Colony Viewer, and location-switchable figure sets for Atlanta and Ithaca covering colony survival, annual pollination, per-crop pollination and crop bloom windows, with results expressed relative to a paired Varroa-free colony under matched weather. Sensitivity results are shown as Matplotlib SVGs with bootstrap error bars. PRINCE ships a local web application with an interactive Structural context panel showing geometry findings, assessment status and crystal-contact summaries with per-residue measurements, JSON and CSV export, and two screencast demo videos (web app and CLI). The Modeling Instructional Series is seven videos teaching other teams a four-stage workflow for turning wet-lab protocols into MATLAB SimBiology models.","dataviz_zh":"最佳 Wiki 這個獎是靠把模型做成可檢視而非只是插圖贏來的。VP3 抗原決定位圖是一個互動式 3D 檢視器，有五個可選取、已標註的區域，並可切換疊上已確認 minibinder 的預測結合姿態，背後還有一張表格列出每個區域的殘基、結構上的理由與實驗結果。所有 35 個送出的 minibinder 設計都公開在一張可排序、可篩選、可搜尋的表格中——可依設計輪次、依實驗結果排序——每一列都可展開顯示 ipTM、ipSAE（並標示它是否為方向性的最小 ipSAE）、設計區域、BLI 感測器載入量、試驗備註與來源紀錄，另附完整 CSV 下載；失敗與「無可用結果」的條目與唯一的成功案例被同等醒目地呈現。另有一個全螢幕的 minibinder 檢視器展示 VP3 與 GFP 的設計。流行病學模型配有一張可點選的四階段「模型中的一天」圖、一個週解析度的 Colony Viewer，以及可切換地點（亞特蘭大與 Ithaca）的圖組，涵蓋蜂群存活、年度授粉量、各作物授粉量與作物開花期，所有結果都相對於同一天氣條件下配對的無 Varroa 蜂群表示。敏感度分析結果以 Matplotlib SVG 呈現，附拔靴法誤差棒。PRINCE 附一個在本機執行的網頁應用程式，其互動式 Structural context 面板顯示幾何分析結果、評估狀態與晶體接觸摘要，並附逐一殘基的量測值、JSON 與 CSV 匯出，以及兩支錄影示範（網頁版與 CLI）。Modeling Instructional Series 是七支影片，教其他隊伍一套四階段流程，把濕實驗流程轉成 MATLAB SimBiology 模型。","datascience":"The defining habit is turning other people's experimental data into a decision rule, then keeping the honest ledger. PRINCE's antibody epitope ranker was trained on 6,937 experimentally observed antibody-antigen interfaces across 1,549 antigen clusters, split by antigen cluster with sequence-homology checks between train, validation and test; it scored a cluster-averaged top-three majority-hit rate of 50.8% across 251 test clusters against 23.3% random, and on the harder retrospective subset of 93 clusters with no training homolog at 30% sequence identity or above it scored 45.8% against 23.8% random. An earlier residue-level benchmark on 110 common interfaces gave PRINCE a macro AUROC of 0.6722 against BepiPred-3.0 at 0.6524 and PeSTo at 0.6521, and the lightweight web-app scorer was benchmarked separately at 0.648 against 0.645 for exposure alone - a near-null result they published. Separately they retrospectively analysed 1,307 experimentally tested minibinder designs across 15 targets and found that across the 13 targets evaluable for site-level comparison the best-performing site averaged a 64% success rate against a 32% target-wide average, meaning site choice roughly doubles the hit rate; ranking by surface exposure alone put the best site in the top three for 10 of 13 targets (77%) against about 49% random, reported p = 0.032. Reporter work was properly calibrated with linear fits RLU_R = 206,101[Rluc] + 70,894 and RLU_F = 624[Fluc] + 57.8. Model validation against external data is laid out as a side-by-side table of published observation versus model output with an interpretation column that repeatedly says the comparison does not constitute validation: simulated managed mite loads of 2.42 (Atlanta) and 1.26 (Ithaca) per 100 bees against the USDA APHIS National Honey Bee Survey mean of 4.14 in positive samples, 27.8% and 8.8% of colony-months above three mites per 100 bees against 41.7% of survey samples, median untreated survival of 2.1 and 2.0 years against a Finnish study's 4-5 years from low initial infestation, and a simulated mean autumn population of 285 mites (range 165-514) against an observed 340. Headline outcome: all untreated colonies were lost by the end of year three, while SWARM alone retained 96.7% of reference crop pollination in Atlanta and 94.7% in Ithaca at year six against 45.1% and 79.8% for amitraz under an assumed five-year decline in effectiveness, with SWARM ahead in all 20 paired simulations at each location. Under the chosen assumptions RNAi supplied most of the benefit and the minibinder a smaller increment - a conclusion that undercuts their own flagship protein work, and they say so.","datascience_zh":"最具代表性的習慣，是把別人的實驗資料轉成一條決策規則，然後老實記帳。PRINCE 的抗體抗原決定位排序器訓練於 1,549 個抗原叢集中、共 6,937 個實驗觀察到的抗體—抗原介面，並依抗原叢集切分，且在訓練、驗證與測試集之間做序列同源性檢查；它在 251 個測試叢集上取得叢集平均的前三名多數命中率 50.8%，相對於隨機的 23.3%，而在較困難的回溯子集（93 個叢集，訓練集中沒有序列相同度 30% 以上的同源物）上取得 45.8%，相對於隨機的 23.8%。較早一次在 110 個常見介面上的殘基層級基準測試，PRINCE 的宏觀 AUROC 為 0.6722，BepiPred-3.0 為 0.6524、PeSTo 為 0.6521；而輕量版網頁應用程式的評分器另外測得 0.648，相對於僅用暴露程度的 0.645——這是一個近乎無差異的結果，而他們照樣公開。另外，他們回溯分析了 15 個標靶上 1,307 個經實驗測試的 minibinder 設計，發現在可做位點層級比較的 13 個標靶中，表現最好的位點平均成功率為 64%，相對於全標靶平均的 32%，也就是說選位點大約讓命中率翻倍；單憑表面暴露程度排序，就能在 13 個標靶中有 10 個（77%）把最佳位點排進前三名，相對於隨機約 49%，報告的 p = 0.032。報告基因的工作也做了適當校準，線性擬合為 RLU_R = 206,101[Rluc] + 70,894 與 RLU_F = 624[Fluc] + 57.8。對外部資料的模型驗證以並排表格呈現，一欄是已發表的觀察值、一欄是模型輸出，另加一欄判讀，而該欄一再指出這些比較並不構成驗證：模擬的管理蜂群蟎負荷為每 100 隻蜂 2.42（亞特蘭大）與 1.26（Ithaca），對照 USDA APHIS National Honey Bee Survey 陽性樣本平均值 4.14；蟎數高於每 100 隻蜂三隻的蜂群月份比例為 27.8% 與 8.8%，對照調查樣本的 41.7%；未處理蜂群的存活中位數為 2.1 與 2.0 年，對照一份芬蘭研究從低初始感染起算的 4-5 年；而模擬的秋季平均蟎數為 285 隻（範圍 165-514），對照觀察值 340。主要結果：所有未處理的蜂群在第三年結束前全部覆滅，而只用 SWARM 的蜂群在第六年仍保有亞特蘭大 96.7%、Ithaca 94.7% 的參考作物授粉量，相對於 amitraz 在假設效力五年遞減下的 45.1% 與 79.8%，且在每個地點的全部 20 組配對模擬中 SWARM 都領先。在所選定的假設下，大部分效益來自 RNAi，minibinder 只提供較小的增量——這個結論削弱了他們自己的招牌蛋白質工作，而他們照實寫了出來。","software":"PRINCE (released open source) is the team's software tool: it ranks candidate binding sites on a user-supplied protein structure before any compute is spent on design, combining a trained site ranker over geometric, atomic and protein-language-model features with a lightweight structural surface scorer, a crystal-contact and geometry checker that compares a chain alone against its crystal surroundings to flag where neighbouring copies cover a proposed site and where sections are missing or atomic positions uncertain, and a literature-evidence layer. It ships as a locally run web application for interactive use and a CLI for automated workflows, with JSON/CSV export, documentation, a command-line reference and a reproduction guide. Model: https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/lambert-ga/prince-model ; web app: https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/lambert-ga/prince-webapp ; team repo: https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/lambert-ga. Hardware (Best Hardware nominee): Vapor-X, an automated vacuum dryer built on the Clausius-Clapeyron relation, using a 12 V vacuum pump to lower pressure in a sealed Mason jar while a flexible resistive heating pad gently warms the sample, controlled by a Raspberry Pi Pico W on a custom PCB with an OLED display and rotary encoder for target temperature, vacuum strength and drying time. Prototype components cost USD 80.07 (USD 95.52 including PCB assembly) against USD 5,000-25,000 for a benchtop lyophiliser. It was validated externally: testing at the University of Alabama at Birmingham recovered 38 of 43 measured compounds (88.4%) within 5% of undried controls, and testing at Georgia Institute of Technology showed GFP fluorescence comparable to controls after drying GFP DNA and cell lysates; internal Bradford-assay work and a classroom deployment assessed recovery and usability. Also released: the seven-video Modeling Instructional Series for teams with no modelling experience, and the full model result records and 1,000 paired parameter records for the dosing model as downloadable JSON and CSV.","software_zh":"PRINCE（已開源釋出）是該隊的軟體工具：它在任何運算花在設計之前，先對使用者提供的蛋白質結構排序候選結合位點，結合一個以幾何、原子與蛋白質語言模型特徵訓練的位點排序器、一個輕量的結構表面評分器、一個晶體接觸與幾何檢查器（把單一鏈與其晶體環境相比，標示鄰近複本在哪裡覆蓋了擬選位點、以及哪裡有區段缺失或原子位置不確定），再加上一層文獻證據。它同時提供在本機執行的網頁應用程式供互動使用，以及供自動化流程使用的 CLI，附 JSON/CSV 匯出、說明文件、指令列參考與重現指南。模型：https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/lambert-ga/prince-model ；網頁應用程式：https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/lambert-ga/prince-webapp ；團隊程式庫：https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/lambert-ga。硬體（最佳硬體入圍）：Vapor-X，一台依 Clausius-Clapeyron 關係式打造的自動真空乾燥機，用 12 V 真空泵降低密封梅森罐內的壓力，同時以可彎折的電阻式加熱墊輕微加溫樣品，並由自製 PCB 上的 Raspberry Pi Pico W 控制，配備 OLED 顯示器與旋轉編碼器，可設定目標溫度、真空強度與乾燥時間。原型零件成本 80.07 美元（含 PCB 組裝為 95.52 美元），對照桌上型冷凍乾燥機的 5,000 至 25,000 美元。它也經過外部驗證：在阿拉巴馬大學伯明罕分校的測試中，43 個量測化合物有 38 個（88.4%）回收率落在未乾燥對照組的 5% 以內；在喬治亞理工學院的測試中，乾燥 GFP DNA 與細胞裂解液後的 GFP 螢光與對照組相當；另有內部 Bradford 蛋白質定量工作與一次課堂實地使用，評估回收率與可用性。另外釋出的還有：為毫無建模經驗的隊伍製作的七支影片 Modeling Instructional Series，以及劑量模型的完整模型結果紀錄與 1,000 組配對參數紀錄，皆可下載為 JSON 與 CSV。","stack":["BindCraft","Mosaic","BoltzProt","Boltz-2","Protenix","ipSAE / minimum ipSAE / ipTM / pLDDT confidence metrics","ROC-AUC benchmarking","Jaccard similarity of interface contact sets","self-consistency RMSD","protein language model features","scikit-learn","MATLAB SimBiology","ODE systems (13 species, 23 reactions)","individual-based / agent-based colony simulation","Sobol variance-based sensitivity analysis","local normalised sensitivity coefficients","Matplotlib","biolayer interferometry (BLI, via Adaptyv Bio)","dual-luciferase reporter assay","Sf9 insect cell culture","NOAA climate normals and daily records","Raspberry Pi Pico W","custom PCB","3D printing","Nebius GPU compute","Opentrons","GitLab"],"techniques":["benchmarking design-confidence metrics against thousands of labelled experimental outcomes instead of trusting them","detecting metric instability by repeating predictions on the same candidate","measuring tool diversity quantitatively (Jaccard 0.000, 42.9 angstrom interface separation) to justify using three design tools","site-level rather than design-level success analysis (best site 64% vs target-wide 32%)","cluster-split benchmarking with sequence-homology checks and a no-homolog retrospective subset","variance-based global sensitivity analysis with bootstrap intervals and disclosed failed numerical checks","paired-weather-sequence experimental design so treatments are compared under matched conditions","composing several published models into one individual-based simulation with per-framework attribution","separating measured inputs from assumed inputs in every parameter table","publishing all 35 tested designs including failures and unusable assays, with a CSV download","external third-party hardware validation at two universities"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Over 30 initiatives reaching more than 530 participants worldwide, organised around three stated principles (quality information, diversity and outreach, hands-on lessons) and mapped individually to UN SDGs. For elementary audiences they wrote and illustrated an original children's book, 'The Mite-ty Adventure of Bentley the Bee', for ages 5-9, iterated against feedback from elementary teachers, designed to be legible to readers with colour vision deficiencies, translated into 13 languages, read aloud to first-graders at Sharon Elementary, and now held in the Atlanta Botanical Garden's library as part of its pollinator education. They also ran a Sharon Elementary Critter Club workshop in which students learned pollination while physically preparing the plots of their own pollinator garden. For middle school they ran Riverwatch workshops and a week-long Biotech Bootcamp for 62 campers structured one day per iGEM committee, with candy DNA models, micropipetting, strawberry DNA extraction, a C. elegans RNAi feeding experiment observed under the microscope across the week, and a 'germiest place in school' swabbing experiment; pre/post survey comparisons were collected. For older audiences there were pollinator presentations, a high school debate, a Connectivity Night, webinars, a keynote at the NWGA RESA STEM for Tomorrow Forum, a Concrete Jungle workshop, a Gardener's Handbook with practical pollinator-friendly planting guidance, a Bee PSA, mentorship, and a GBA Fall Conference and mini jamboree. Two inclusivity programmes carry the Best Sustainable Development Impact award. Flowers for the Future partners with a non-profit supporting Afghan girls barred from school past sixth grade to obtain a GED; Lambert teaches a multi-week 'Intro to Synthetic Biology' course there (central dogma, units and dimensional analysis, DNA and mutations, gene expression, genetic engineering techniques including transformation, transfection, viral vectors and CRISPR, PCR and gel electrophoresis, experimental design, scientific writing, bioethics), now in its third semester and reaching about 120 students, with a linked FFF-BioBuilderClub. Exceptional Science! brings kinesthetic science lessons to the neurodivergent class at their own school - acid-base reactions, genetics, density, candy DNA models, a rainbow pinwheel density experiment - plus a honeybee/DWV movement game where students first forage freely as healthy bees and then may only hop, citing research that physical activity improves inhibition and rule-switching response times in children with ADHD; they also published a Neurodivergent Handbook.","publicEngagement_zh":"超過 30 項活動，觸及全球 530 位以上參與者，圍繞三項明示原則組織（優質資訊、多元與外展、動手操作的課程），並逐項對應到聯合國 SDG。針對小學受眾，他們自寫自畫了一本童書《The Mite-ty Adventure of Bentley the Bee》，適合 5 至 9 歲，依小學老師的回饋反覆修改，設計上考量色彩視覺缺陷讀者也能閱讀，翻譯成 13 種語言，在 Sharon Elementary 朗讀給一年級學生，現在也收藏於亞特蘭大植物園圖書館，成為其授粉者教育的一部分。他們還辦了 Sharon Elementary Critter Club 工作坊，學生一邊學授粉，一邊實際整理自己授粉花園的苗床。針對國中，他們辦了 Riverwatch 工作坊與為期一週、62 位營隊學員參加的 Biotech Bootcamp，架構上每天對應一個 iGEM 委員會，內容包括糖果 DNA 模型、微量吸管操作、草莓 DNA 萃取、一整週在顯微鏡下觀察的 C. elegans RNAi 餵食實驗，以及一項「學校裡最多細菌的地方」採樣實驗；並收集了前後測問卷比較。針對年齡更長的受眾，則有授粉者主題演講、一場高中辯論、一場 Connectivity Night、數場線上研討會、NWGA RESA STEM for Tomorrow Forum 的主題演講、一場 Concrete Jungle 工作坊、一本附實用授粉友善種植指引的《Gardener's Handbook》、一支蜜蜂公益宣導片、師徒輔導，以及 GBA 秋季會議與一場迷你 jamboree。兩項包容性計畫撐起了最佳永續發展影響獎。Flowers for the Future 與一個支援被禁止升學到六年級以上的阿富汗女孩考取 GED 的非營利組織合作；Lambert 在那裡開設為期數週的「合成生物學入門」課程（中心法則、單位與因次分析、DNA 與突變、基因表現、基因工程技術包含轉形、轉染、病毒載體與 CRISPR、PCR 與凝膠電泳、實驗設計、科學寫作、生物倫理），目前已進入第三學期，觸及約 120 位學生，並附設一個 FFF-BioBuilderClub。Exceptional Science! 則把身體動覺式的科學課帶進自己學校的神經多樣性班級——酸鹼反應、遺傳學、密度、糖果 DNA 模型、彩虹風車密度實驗——另有一個蜜蜂／DWV 的肢體遊戲，學生先以健康蜜蜂的身分自由採集，之後只能用跳的方式移動，依據的是運動能改善 ADHD 兒童抑制控制與規則切換反應時間的研究；他們也出版了一本《Neurodivergent Handbook》。","ihp":"IHP ran across four sequenced phases (food insecurity/agriculture/city planners, beekeepers, experts and professors, then policymakers and governmental organisations), with every interaction processed through a four-step cycle they call H.I.V.E. - Hear, Inquire, Validate, Evolve - and a hard rule that a cycle is incomplete unless it ends in a concrete change or a documented reason why no change was warranted. Each stakeholder is also tagged with the SDGs they bear on, which is how the SDG scoring on the Sustainability page is built. The pivots are named, dated and attributed on a published timeline. February 2026: Dr. Aashish Manglik (UCSF) told them computational nanobody discovery still needs libraries of hundreds to thousands of candidates - 'For our computational design projects, we still make libraries of hundreds or thousands of candidates' - so testing 10 to 50 would likely fail even with a correct pipeline, and pointed them at BindCraft and Protenix; the team abandoned nanobodies for minibinders, which changed the entire wet lab. July 2026: Dr. Morgane Golan prompted the move to Sf9 cells as the RNAi model system. August 2026: Tudor Cotet and Corey Howe of Adaptyv Bio told them to stop targeting the P-domain broadly and focus designs on specific binding hotspots, and Cotet reviewed the failed first campaign before round two. September 2026: Dr. Mark Styczynski (Georgia Tech) pushed them off over-specific model parameters onto literature-supported ones, which is why every parameter table now carries a source attribution and an honest label; and Samantha Houck's input added SDG 11 to their framework. Professors Benjamin Lamp and Tatsuhiko Kadowaki, both DWV specialists, narrowed the target to VP3's exposed P-domain and warned how hard epitope selection is without experimental binding data, which made epitope evaluation a first-class modelling step and directly motivated PRINCE - as did Dr. Michael Hecht (Princeton) emphasising the uncertainty of epitope selection. Professor Raymond Owens (Oxford / Rosalind Franklin Institute) reframed binder choice around production cost and failure rate. Entomologist Dr. Jeff Pettis answered the ecological question head-on, saying eliminating Varroa would be 'completely fine' because they are obligate parasites invasive to the US, which underpins the safety case; he also named the political context, that pollinators are undervalued and under-resourced. On the practice side, Peter Helfrich (President, Metro Atlanta Beekeepers Association) identified DWV as the most dangerous threat and stressed that treatments must not harm brood, which made brood safety an explicit project priority; board member Claressa Lucas supplied the line that frames the whole project, 'It's not a matter of if there are Varroa mites. Every colony has them.' Professor Lewis Bartlett (University of Georgia) endorsed sucrose solution as a practical delivery vehicle, and contacts associated with Norroa, the registered RNA-based Varroa treatment, informed the syrup-pouch format. Sharanya Madhavan of Concrete Jungle, after six months of conversations and a joint workshop, connected bee health to rising food insecurity and urban pollinator corridors, which reshaped the outreach programme.","ihp_zh":"IHP 分四個依序進行的階段（糧食不安全／農業／城市規劃者、養蜂人、專家與教授，最後是政策制定者與政府組織），每一次互動都走過他們稱為 H.I.V.E. 的四步循環——Hear、Inquire、Validate、Evolve——並設下一條硬規則：除非最後導致一項具體改變，或留下不需改變的理由紀錄，否則該循環不算完成。每位利害關係人也標註其所關聯的 SDG，永續頁面上的 SDG 評分就是這樣建起來的。所有轉向都在公開的時間軸上具名、標日期並註明來源。2026 年 2 月：Dr. Aashish Manglik（UCSF）告訴他們，計算式奈米抗體探索仍然需要數百到數千個候選的函式庫——「在我們的計算設計專案裡，我們還是會做數百或數千個候選的函式庫」——所以即使流程正確，只測 10 到 50 個很可能會失敗，並把他們引向 BindCraft 與 Protenix；該隊於是放棄奈米抗體改做 minibinder，這改變了整個濕實驗。2026 年 7 月：Dr. Morgane Golan 促成改用 Sf9 細胞作為 RNAi 的模式系統。2026 年 8 月：Adaptyv Bio 的 Tudor Cotet 與 Corey Howe 告訴他們不要廣泛針對整個 P-domain，而要把設計聚焦在特定的結合熱點，Cotet 並在第二輪之前檢視了失敗的第一輪戰役。2026 年 9 月：Dr. Mark Styczynski（喬治亞理工）把他們從過度特定的模型參數推向有文獻支持的參數，這就是為什麼現在每張參數表都附來源出處與誠實標註；而 Samantha Houck 的意見則為他們的架構加上 SDG 11。兩位 DWV 專家 Benjamin Lamp 與 Tatsuhiko Kadowaki 教授把標靶收斂到 VP3 暴露的 P-domain，並提醒在沒有實驗結合資料的情況下選抗原決定位有多困難，這使抗原決定位評估成為第一級的建模步驟，也直接催生了 PRINCE——Dr. Michael Hecht（普林斯頓）強調抗原決定位選擇的不確定性亦然。Raymond Owens 教授（牛津／Rosalind Franklin Institute）則把結合蛋白的選擇重新框定在生產成本與失敗率上。昆蟲學家 Dr. Jeff Pettis 直接回答了生態問題，他說消滅 Varroa 會「完全沒問題」，因為牠們是對美國而言入侵性的專性寄生者，這支撐了安全性論述；他也點明政治脈絡：授粉者被低估、資源不足。實務一端，Peter Helfrich（大亞特蘭大養蜂人協會會長）指出 DWV 是最危險的威脅，並強調處理方式絕不能傷害蜂子，這使蜂子安全成為專案的明確優先項；理事 Claressa Lucas 則提供了為整個專案定調的一句話：「問題不是有沒有蜂蟹蟎。每一個蜂群都有。」Lewis Bartlett 教授（喬治亞大學）認可糖水是可行的投遞載體；而與已登記之 RNA 型 Varroa 處理劑 Norroa 相關的聯絡人，則提供了糖漿袋形式的資訊。Concrete Jungle 的 Sharanya Madhavan 在六個月的對話與一場合辦工作坊之後，把蜂群健康與日益嚴重的糧食不安全、都市授粉者廊道連結起來，這重塑了外展計畫。","realWorld":"A business-to-business licensing strategy rather than a direct-sales fantasy: established agricultural biotechnology manufacturers would produce and distribute SWARM through existing commercial networks, priced at USD 39.99 per hive treatment against an estimated mature manufacturing cost of USD 25.00, targeting commercial beekeepers who supply pollination services to high-value agriculture. The plan models 300,000 annual treatments by 2034 (base case 150,000, long-term goal one million), giving roughly USD 12 million in retail sales and USD 525,000 in licensing royalties under a proposed 5% royalty, and is supported by TAM/SAM/SOM, market competition and SWOT analysis, an AIDA distribution model, beekeeper return-on-investment calculations, revenue and sales forecasts, manufacturing and operating expense breakdowns, break-even analysis and a risk-management section. The four-year plan is sequenced around the real regulatory gate: 2027 R&D, 2028 product optimisation and safety, 2029 field validation and partnerships, 2030 commercialisation preparation, with a manufacturing partner and pesticide registration secured before launch - sensible given Norroa/Vadescana was registered as a biopesticide in 2025 and is the obvious precedent. Vapor-X is handled as a separate commercialisation track, offered either through manufacturer licensing or open-source release to educational and research laboratories, with prototype and commercial manufacturing cost breakdowns and an explicit open-source contribution to future iGEM teams. Implementation is built around equipment beekeepers already own: dsRNA in a sealed flexible syrup pouch with an adhesive cover over proboscis-sized feeding openings placed in the brood box (modelled on the Norroa format, where worker bees redistribute syrup into brood stores and nurse bees incorporate it into brood food), and the minibinder as a dried packet mixed into sucrose solution and served through a standard hive-top feeder. Throughout, the team draws the line clearly: BLI established binding to a VP3 construct, not neutralisation of assembled virus; neither component has been tested in a honeybee colony; the 100 nM circulating concentration is a selected simulation value, not an established protective threshold; and the RNAi potency figure is an external conditional effect, not a measurement of SWARM's own construct. Impact is mapped through a 'Roots-to-Fruits' model linking seven SDGs - 2, 4, 5, 8, 11, 15 and 17.","realWorld_zh":"商業策略是企業對企業的授權，而不是直接銷售的幻想：由既有的農業生技製造商透過現有商業網路生產與配銷 SWARM，定價為每蜂箱療程 39.99 美元，對照成熟量產後估計的 25.00 美元製造成本，目標客戶是為高價值農業提供授粉服務的商業養蜂人。計畫預估 2034 年達到年銷 300,000 份療程（基準情境 150,000，長期目標 100 萬），在擬議 5% 權利金下帶來約 1,200 萬美元零售額與 525,000 美元授權金，並以 TAM/SAM/SOM、市場競爭與 SWOT 分析、AIDA 配銷模型、養蜂人投資報酬計算、營收與銷售預測、製造與營運費用拆解、損益兩平分析與風險管理章節支撐。四年計畫依真正的法規關卡排序：2027 研發、2028 產品最佳化與安全性、2029 田間驗證與合作、2030 商業化準備，並在上市前先取得製造夥伴與農藥登記——考慮到 Norroa/Vadescana 已於 2025 年登記為生物農藥、是最明顯的先例，這樣的安排很合理。Vapor-X 則作為獨立的商業化路線處理，可選擇授權給製造商或對教育與研究實驗室開源釋出，並附原型與量產的成本拆解，以及明確要對未來 iGEM 隊伍開源貢獻的承諾。實作方式圍繞養蜂人已有的器材設計：dsRNA 裝在密封的軟質糖漿袋中，袋上以黏貼封膜覆蓋口器大小的餵食開口，放入育子箱（參考 Norroa 的形式，由工蜂把糖漿重新分配到子脾儲存區，再由育兒蜂將其納入蜂子的食物）；minibinder 則做成乾燥包，混入糖水後以標準的蜂箱上部餵食器供應。全程中該隊都把界線畫得很清楚：BLI 證實的是對一個 VP3 構築體的結合，而不是對組裝完成病毒的中和；兩個組件都還沒在真正的蜂群中測試過；100 nM 循環濃度是模擬中選定的數值，不是已確立的保護門檻；而 RNAi 的效力數字來自外部研究的條件性效果，不是對 SWARM 自身構築體的量測。影響力以一個「Roots-to-Fruits」模型對應到七項 SDG——2、4、5、8、11、15 與 17。","partners":["Dr. Aashish Manglik, University of California, San Francisco","Professor Benjamin Lamp","Professor Tatsuhiko Kadowaki","Dr. Michael Hecht, Princeton University","Professor Raymond Owens, University of Oxford / Rosalind Franklin Institute","Dr. Mark Styczynski, Georgia Institute of Technology (Styczynski Lab)","Dr. Jeff Pettis, entomologist","Professor Lewis Bartlett, University of Georgia","Professor Jamie Ellis","Professor Jennifer Leavey, Georgia Tech","Dr. Morgane Golan","Tudor Cotet and Corey Howe, Adaptyv Bio (minibinder design advice and BLI testing)","an engineer at Boltz (target structure and hotspot redirection)","Metro Atlanta Beekeepers Association (Peter Helfrich, Claressa Lucas)","Concrete Jungle (Sharanya Madhavan)","GreenLight Biosciences","representatives associated with Norroa / Vadescana","Flowers for the Future (Afghan girls' GED programme)","University of Alabama at Birmingham (John Moore - Vapor-X validation)","Georgia Institute of Technology (Vapor-X GFP validation)","Nebius, Boltz, Twist Bioscience, GenScript, Promega, New England Biolabs, Opentrons, Addgene (sponsors)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6185/wiki/modeling/img-6251.avif","caption":"The epidemiological model pipeline: how minibinder protection (assigned per bee from its syrup intake) and RNAi exposure at brood capping enter the individual-based colony simulation.","caption_zh":"流行病學模型的流程：minibinder 保護（依每隻蜂的糖水攝取量逐一指派）與封蓋時的 RNAi 暴露，如何進入以個體為基礎的蜂群模擬。","credit":"Team Lambert-GA, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6185/wiki/modeling/no-treatment-against-the-swarm-therapeutic-atlanta.avif","caption":"Simulated adult bee population in Atlanta over six years: seasonal cycles persist under SWARM while the untreated colony trajectory declines to zero - all untreated colonies were lost by the end of year three.","caption_zh":"亞特蘭大六年間的模擬成蜂族群：在 SWARM 之下季節性週期得以維持，而未處理蜂群的軌跡則一路降到零——所有未處理蜂群在第三年結束前全部覆滅。","credit":"Team Lambert-GA, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6185/wiki/modeling/crop-pollination-delivered-per-year-atlanta-georgia-blueberry-watermelon-squash-cucumber-apple.avif","caption":"Predicted annual crop pollination in Atlanta (blueberry, watermelon, squash, cucumber, apple), each treatment normalised against its own matched Varroa-free colony before averaging across 20 weather sequences.","caption_zh":"亞特蘭大的年度作物授粉量預測（藍莓、西瓜、南瓜、小黃瓜、蘋果），每種處理都先對照自己配對的無 Varroa 蜂群正規化，再在 20 組天氣序列間取平均。","credit":"Team Lambert-GA, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6185/wiki/hardware/vapor-x-prototype.avif","caption":"Vapor-X, the team's USD 80 automated vacuum dryer, with its Mason jar vacuum chamber, heated sample stand, OLED display and rotary encoder - externally validated at UAB (38 of 43 compounds recovered within 5% of undried controls) and Georgia Tech.","caption_zh":"Vapor-X，該隊 80 美元的自動真空乾燥機，配有梅森罐真空腔、加熱樣品座、OLED 顯示器與旋轉編碼器——並經 UAB（43 個化合物中有 38 個回收率落在未乾燥對照組的 5% 以內）與喬治亞理工外部驗證。","credit":"Team Lambert-GA, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"The transferable insight is that Lambert beat the metric rather than trusting it: they benchmarked ipSAE, ipTM and a 38-metric ensemble against 5,721 labelled experimental designs, found the ensemble barely beat chance (ROC-AUC 0.541) and that their eventual hit did not even have the best score, then showed with 1,307 prior designs that choosing the right epitope roughly doubles the hit rate (64% at the best site vs 32% target-wide) and released that insight as open-source software, PRINCE - landing the first confirmed DWV VP3 binder on under USD 400 of compute. A high-school-plus centre should copy that whole posture: cheap compute plus a public dataset plus honest benchmarking, and publish every tested candidate including the failures in a sortable, downloadable table.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"可轉移的洞見是：Lambert 不是信任指標，而是打敗了指標。他們拿 ipSAE、ipTM 與一個 38 項指標的集成模型，對 5,721 個有實驗標註的設計做基準測試，發現集成模型幾乎只比亂猜好一點（ROC-AUC 0.541），而他們最終成功的那個設計甚至不是分數最高的；接著他們用 1,307 個先前的設計證明，選對抗原決定位大約可讓命中率翻倍（最佳位點 64%，相對於全標靶平均 32%），並把這個洞見以開源軟體 PRINCE 釋出——總計用不到 400 美元的運算費用，就做出首例確認可結合 DWV VP3 的結合蛋白。高中以上的研究單位都值得照抄這整套姿態：便宜的運算加上公開資料集加上誠實的基準測試，並把每一個測過的候選（包括失敗的）都公開在一張可排序、可下載的表格裡。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/","https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/model-design","https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/model-minibinder","https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/model-rnai","https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/model-epidemiological","https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/implementation","https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/safety","https://2026.igem.wiki/lambert-ga/contribution","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/lambert-ga/prince-model","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/lambert-ga/prince-webapp","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/lambert-ga","https://api.igem.org/v1/teams/6185"],"rank":301},"6187":{"team":"Toronto","id":"6187","section":"Overgrad","country":"Canada","village":"Bioremediation","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/toronto/","projectTitle":"PetaBite","tagline":"Planetary-scale bioprospecting for plastic-degrading enzymes: mine 300M candidates, then match an enzyme to each real-world condition.","summary":"PetaBite attacks PET and microplastic pollution by abandoning the field's usual strategy of engineering a handful of known enzymes and instead searching the natural sequence landscape at planetary scale. The dry lab rebuilt PETadex from scratch into PETadex V2: 1.74 billion plastic-degrading enzyme homologs recovered from NCBI nr and the Logan assembly of the entire Sequence Read Archive, filtered by 53 hand-curated catalytic HMMs to 291,922,243 complete catalytic ORFs, each annotated with the pH, temperature, salinity and environment of the sample it came from. They paired this with PETai activity labels scraped from literature by an LLM pipeline and by 20+ human curators, pretrained PlasticESM (LoRA adapters on ESM-C) on the corpus, and built a hardware bioreactor array to feed condition-specific measurements back into the model. They won Best Model largely for scientific honesty: a homology-component-grouped split showed that sequence length beats their own embeddings, and they reported that rather than the inflated random-split numbers.","awards":["Top 10 (Overgrad)","Best Model — Winner (Overgrad)","Best Hardware — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Wiki — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Entrepreneurship — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Bioremediation Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"The PETadex V2 pipeline chains DIAMOND homology search against NCBI nr (42,053,081 hits down to 7,825,107 non-redundant sequences at E < 1e-5) with 53 catalytic profile HMMs built by a jackhmmer-analogous four-iteration loop that only advanced homologs retaining every canonical catalytic residue, then searched 2,740,458 catalytic-domain centroids against the Logan assembly of the SRA (87.0 Pb of raw reads compressed to 1.8 Pb of contigs) to recover 5.57 billion hits and 291,922,243 complete catalytic ORFs. Structures came from AlphaFold DB (575,770 hits, via UniProt idmapping) plus their own ESMFold2 run: 1,793,781 sequences folded in 16.6 hours on up to 80 GPUs (851.6 GPU-hours, median pLDDT 92.3), benchmarked against 244 experimental PDB structures to choose the full model under 150 aa and ESMFold2-Fast above it at 32 diffusion steps and 3 refinement loops. On the learning side they continued masked-language-model pretraining of ESM-C 300M on PETadex using LoRA adapters on all four projections of every transformer block (240 adapter tensors, 14.7M trainable parameters, backbone frozen) to produce PlasticESM, and probed its embeddings with ridge regression under homology-component-grouped cross-validation. Supporting layers include CATH and Pfam domain assignment, SignalP 6.0 secretion prediction over all ORFs, Biopython ProtParam biochemical properties, InterProScan plus HMMER accessory-domain analysis, and a reconstruction of the TED (The Encyclopedia of Domains) novelty-discovery pipeline adapted to PETadex HMMs.","dataviz":"The wiki is the clearest dataviz work in the cohort: a 300-million-protein 'PETadex Model Landscape' rendered as three explorable layers (what we found, what we know, what we predict), a draggable component map of the 46 PETadex-PAZy families, a 3D structure viewer that highlights the catalytic triad, oxyanion hole and docked PET dimer for each of 16 CATH fold groups, and a BioSample viewer that drills from a real sample (e.g. SAMN03075713, Arctic tundra soil) down through its sequencing run to individual ORFs and their 90% identity clusters. The Sharded DIAMOND search and the per-enzyme record card both ship as live in-page demos that replay ten real searches, sped up from 45 seconds to two. There is also a 'PETadex Project Calendar' that walks week by week from March to October with an explicit 'What went wrong, and what we changed' panel per workstream, and a PETamon mini-game that teaches why no single enzyme cleans up every plastic.","datascience":"Their central data-science contribution is turning a literature corpus into training labels and then proving honestly that the labels, not the corpus, are the bottleneck. An automated LLM extraction pipeline gathered 11,000 identifiers via the PAZy API, screened them to 900 seed papers, expanded by forward and backward citation to 50,000 candidates, filtered to ~4,600, converted full texts to structured JSON with Docling, Grobid and PyMuPDF, and extracted 51,455 cleaned measurement entries across 31,441 enzymes; Claude Sonnet benchmarked best (95.0% precision, 87.1% recall) with zero hallucinated enzymes across 32 double-scraped papers. In parallel, 20+ members spent 450+ hours hand-extracting 61 papers through a standardized interactive HTML schema with autogenerated IDs and built-in error checks, giving a ground truth where 78% of independent scraper pairs agreed within 10%. The benchmark result is the headline: under random five-fold splits stock ESM-C reached rho = 0.72 on kcat and 0.74 on melting temperature, but splitting folds by connected homology component dropped the same embeddings by 0.49 to 1.01 while a single sequence-length column lost at most 0.18 — because 90-92% of labelled sequences have a homologous relative elsewhere in the set. Length itself reached rho = +0.343 on kcat and beat both embeddings on all twelve target sets, so they reported the negative result, published the model card alongside the weights so nobody reuses the adapters expecting activity prediction, and designed round 2 to be chosen by model uncertainty rather than predicted activity.","software":"Two tools released under MIT at https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/toronto/petabite. LOBSTER (Library Optimization for Bioprospecting Sequences Through Economical Recombination) splits PETase cores into fragment positions and designs degenerate-codon oligos that combinatorially assemble by Golden Gate to cover as many natural cores as possible — it synthesized a 1,744-sequence library at 45% of individual-synthesis cost (55% nucleotide reduction) for the IsPETase and LCC 90% identity clusters. Sharded DIAMOND Search splits the 307M-sequence corpus into 32 shards searched in parallel by serverless cloud workers, returning ranked neighbours for a pasted protein in under a minute with nothing to install, live at petadex.net. Datasets are on Zenodo (PETadex catalytic ORF corpus v1.1 + sharded search DB, 23.8 GB, doi:10.5281/zenodo.23457986) and Hugging Face (petadex/plasticesm-dualseed, petadex/catalytic-orfs-90pid, petadex/petai-activity-labels, each label source published separately); analysis notebooks live at github.com/petadex/igem-toronto and github.com/petadex/petabite. Hardware: a parallel bioreactor array, up to 96 units, at about $204 CAD per reactor, with PID temperature control holding 37 C within +/-0.3 C, dual-photodiode OD600 with three-point quadratic calibration (R^2 = 0.993 on yeast), peristaltic pumps under Arduino PWM control, 150 RPM stirring, and a single-file Python dashboard over USB serial; it grew E. coli over 4 hours in the final test.","stack":["DIAMOND","HMMER / jackhmmer-style iterative HMM building","MMseqs2 (cross-check)","USEARCH","Logan SRA assembly","NCBI nr","PAZy","PlasticDB","BacDive","NCBI BioSample","ESM-C 300M / ESMC-600M","LoRA (PlasticESM)","ESMFold2 / ESMFold2-Fast","AlphaFold DB","ColabFold v1.5.5","SignalP 6.0","InterProScan","CATH","Pfam","Foldseek","umap-learn","scikit-learn ridge regression","Biopython ProtParam","Weights & Biases","Hugging Face Datasets","Docling","Grobid","PyMuPDF","Claude Sonnet (LLM extraction)","Parquet","AWS S3 + serverless workers","Arduino Nano","Python (dashboard)"],"techniques":["planetary-scale metagenomic homology mining","catalytic-residue-constrained profile HMMs","hierarchical clustering at 90/60/30% identity","homology-component-grouped cross-validation","permutation tests and fold-centred scoring","model-free controls (sequence length, amino-acid composition)","continued masked-language-model pretraining with LoRA adapters","UMAP embedding atlas with shuffled/random/fragment negative controls","silhouette scoring per CATH domain","LLM literature extraction benchmarked against double-human curation","uncertainty-driven active learning for round 2 library selection","degenerate-codon Golden Gate library design","sharded parallel sequence search","PID temperature control and dual-photodiode OD600 calibration"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Toronto hosted three conferences, including a 'Rethink plastic' microplastics conference built around two questions (what happens to plastic once it enters the environment, and what can we realistically do about it), deliberately framing PetaBite as one approach among many alongside prevention, policy and community action. They mentored two high-school synthetic biology teams, ran sustained exchanges with four universities abroad, and carried out eight campus collaborations across the University of Toronto reaching over 800 students and community members. Outreach ran on humour rather than lecture: a promotion video combining live action with original animation and PETase-inspired axolotl mascots, a 'Road to Jamboree' Instagram Reels series using trends and familiar formats, and a newsletter, The Waterfront, with 300+ subscribers. Instagram content drew over 105,000 views, 250+ new followers, 2,500+ profile visits and 374 link clicks through to the project and the conference.","ihp":"Roughly 70 stakeholders across four continents, and the changes are specific. A public event where biosafety dominated the questions told them containment has to come before technical detail, so every subsequent public-facing event opened with containment. Regulatory and ethics conversations led them to prioritize enzyme candidates with close homology to naturally occurring proteins and to lead with a contained bioreactor rather than dosing enzymes into open process streams. A researcher's clarification that PETases are only a subset of plastic-degrading enzymes made them explicitly define scope throughout the documentation. Hardware feedback on optical channels led them to separate the optical-density path from the colorimetric degradation readout so dye cannot corrupt cell-density estimates, and a GFP recommendation gave them a route to reporting activity per enzyme rather than per cell; the same conversations reframed the 40 mL reactor as the directed-evolution and Michaelis-Menten instrument and split off the 1,000-to-50 intermediate screen as a separate smaller-format problem. A CGM-adjacent interviewee's distinction between sensor and adhesive reshaped MVP scope. Indigenous knowledge holders reframed plastic pollution as a matter of relationships among people, land and water rather than a technical problem, which fed country-specific regulatory profiles for Pakistan, India, Nigeria, Indonesia and Canadian Indigenous communities addressing waste colonialism and ethics dumping. All of this was codified into a reusable MERGE framework (Multidisciplinary outreach, Education, Regulatory oversight, Global database, Environmental consideration) and a Regulatory Oversight Framework covering Canada's Roadmap for Open Science, FAIR, the Nagoya Protocol, dual-use research of concern, PIPEDA, the Directive on Automated Decision-Making and the EU AI Act.","realWorld":"PetaScale is the commercialization arm, explicitly framed as taking PetaBite from 0-to-1 to 1-to-n. The beachhead is wastewater treatment plants, validated through 20 feasibility conversations with operators, engineers and managers across Ontario, Alberta and Newfoundland, with PETases immobilized in packed-bed reactors so the enzyme stays contained. Three adjacent verticals are mapped: microfibre filtration, landfill leachate and textile effluent. Their differentiation is explicit against Carbios, Samsara Eco and Protein Evolution, all of which build around one engineered enzyme and one operating window (Carbios amorphizes PET and runs near 70 C) — PetaScale instead matches the enzyme to the site's existing temperature, pH and salinity so no heating or pretreatment is needed. Regulatory mapping covers CEPA, EPA TSCA Section 5 and provincial discharge permits, with tailwinds from EU Regulation 2023/2055, Directive 2024/3019 and Canada's Federal Plastics Registry. Validation signal: their associate RNAlab screened 161 randomly selected natural enzymes and two outperformed FAST-PETase. They tested the model across five Canadian national and four global competitions plus two international conferences, placed top 3 in six, attended Y Combinator Startup School, Web Summit Vancouver, SynBioBeta Global and the Canadian Food Forward Summit, completed the Wilbe incubator sprint, opened early discussions with three Canadian VC firms, and raised support from 17 sponsors.","partners":["RNAlab (associate lab, Logan project)","Environment and Climate Change Canada","U.S. EPA","U of T Trash Team","Wastewater treatment plant operators across Ontario, Alberta and Newfoundland","Wilbe startup incubator","Y Combinator Startup School","SynBioBeta Global","Web Summit Vancouver","Indigenous knowledge holders (Canada)","Four partner universities abroad","Two mentored high-school iGEM teams"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6187/wiki/drylab-page/figures/petadex-workflow-overview.svg","caption":"Overview of the PETadex V2 discovery pipeline: curated PAZy enzymes seed catalytic HMMs, which mine NCBI nr and the Logan SRA assembly down to 291,922,243 complete catalytic ORFs.","credit":"Team Toronto, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6187/wiki/drylab-page/figures/homology-leakage.svg","caption":"The team's headline negative result: the same ridge probe scored under homology-component-grouped splits (hollow) versus random five-fold splits (filled). ESM-C embeddings gain 0.49-1.01 from the random split; a single sequence-length column gains at most 0.18.","credit":"Team Toronto, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6187/wiki/drylab-page/figures/landscape-spin-poster.avif","caption":"The interactive PETadex Model Landscape, which lets a visitor explore 300 million proteins in three layers: what was found, what is known about each sequence, and what the model predicts.","credit":"Team Toronto, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6187/wiki/hardware-notebook/overview/finalresult/1.avif","caption":"The final parallel bioreactor build: about $204 CAD per unit, with PID temperature control, dual-photodiode OD600, peristaltic pumps and stirring, driven from a single-file Python dashboard over USB serial.","credit":"Team Toronto, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Copy their evaluation discipline, not their compute budget: grouping train/test splits by homology component and forcing every model to beat zero-parameter controls (sequence length, amino-acid composition) is free, and it is what turned a plausible-looking rho = 0.72 into an honest negative result that reviewers rewarded. Pair that with their hybrid labelling pattern — an LLM extraction pipeline benchmarked against a small, double-scored, schema-driven human corpus — which is exactly the right shape for a school research centre that has many students and little GPU time.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/toronto/","https://2026.igem.wiki/toronto/project/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/toronto/dry-lab/overview/","https://2026.igem.wiki/toronto/dry-lab/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/toronto/software/","https://2026.igem.wiki/toronto/hardware/","https://2026.igem.wiki/toronto/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/toronto/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/toronto/entrepreneurship/","https://2026.igem.wiki/toronto/beyond-the-bench/outreach/","https://2026.igem.wiki/toronto/contribution/","https://2026.igem.wiki/toronto/safety-and-security/"],"rank":124},"6196":{"team":"TAU-Israel","id":"6196","section":"Overgrad","country":"Israel","village":"Therapeutics / Foundational Advance","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/tau-israel/","projectTitle":"CERNAL","tagline":"A biological compiler: supply RNA expression data, get ranked RNA logic-gate circuit designs that fire only in the cell state you specify.","summary":"CERNAL treats the transcriptome as a fingerprint of cellular state and compiles that fingerprint into an RNA logic circuit: it picks the transcripts that distinguish a target cell from its neighbour, scans each transcript for an accessible, unique, constructible trigger window, designs a toehold-style switch whose hairpin hides the ribosome binding site until that trigger unzips it, combines switches into AND and NOT gates, ranks every candidate on shared thermodynamic metrics, and assembles the winner into an annotated plasmid. Because the sensing element is the cell's own RNA rather than a characterised transcription factor, the approach is intended to be host-agnostic, and the team demonstrated it in three proofs of concept: endometriosis logic in HEK293T, a PFOA/PFAS biosensor in E. coli, and CRISPRa gates in yeast. The software is a Django Ninja + React 19 application with a strictly isolated scientific engine, a versioned HTTP API with Python, R and MATLAB clients, SBOL 3 export, and an IBBIS Common Mechanism biosecurity gate that withholds sequence files when screening cannot be completed. The team filed a provisional patent through Tel Aviv University's TTO and built a full market case around cell and gene therapy developers.","awards":["Best Software — Nominee (Overgrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A React 19 static single-page application (TanStack Router, React Query for server state, polling and mutations) built into Django's static assets, over Django Ninja typed HTTP routes with a shared error envelope, Django ORM models for persistent state, and a thin django-q2 task that dispatches work through the engine interface. The v1 runtime deliberately uses SQLite with write-ahead logging, foreign keys and a busy timeout, plus a single ORM-backed queue worker, so the queue is a database table and no separate broker (Redis, RabbitMQ) is needed; rate-limit state also lives in a database cache rather than per-process counters. Worker timeout is one hour with max attempts set to one, explicitly to avoid silently repeating an expensive calculation. The scientific engine is a separate package: it does not import Django, routers, application modules, the database or Django settings, configuration arrives as frozen request records, and an abstract-syntax-tree test catches ordinary, conditional and function-local imports that would break that boundary. Platform code may import only engine.contract and engine.client, never the scientific internals, which means the engine runs and is tested with no web server, database or network, and could be moved to a remote process behind the same request/result interface. Requirements: Python 3.13, uv, Node 22+ for the frontend build, ViennaRNA and Biopython; run './do install && ./do migrate && ./do superuser && ./do build-frontend' then the dev server and a worker in a second terminal, because without the worker submissions just sit queued.","dataviz":"The project landing page is an extended scroll-driven explainer that animates the actual mechanism: zooming into a cytoplasm of coloured transcripts, lining them up by abundance to show the state fingerprint, highlighting the transcripts strong in cell A only versus cell B only, picking one, finding the trigger window, then showing the hairpin lock with its buried RBS being unzipped by the key, and finally the same locks becoming AND and NOT gates. The software page is organised as a 'field guide' with chapters, every claim linked to its implementation record, and a five-step auto-playing screen recording of a real run (recorded from the local app on 11 October 2026) with per-step 'you should see' statements and a static-image fallback for users without JavaScript. The results explorer shows ranked candidates with full metric decomposition, construct views, warnings, and the rejected candidates kept visible; user decision tags (none, pinned, shortlisted, rejected, synthesize) are annotations that explicitly do not change any computational or release result. Run states are drawn as a six-state machine with eight permitted transitions.","datascience":"Validation is answered against the Best Software ballot questions one by one, each linked to an implementation or measurement record, and separated into four kinds of evidence that the wiki says do not substitute for one another: software checks, recorded execution, structure comparisons and host experiments. Two external comparisons anchor the predictions: the RNA-accessibility score was compared against published in-cell SHAPE measurements across 450 E. coli RNA records, and the switch-ranking metrics were tested against Green et al.'s measured toehold ON/OFF ratios. Gene selection used published expression data for the PFOA analysis and, separately, an endometriosis analysis with healthy-tissue context, stratifying AREG and SELE across superficial peritoneal and deep ovarian lesions. The AND-gate study enumerated hundreds of thousands of candidate designs, and examining the best and worst of each architecture surfaced failure modes before anything was built, notably switches that score well only because they stay closed and targets that look good only on paper. At the bench, dozens of toehold candidates were designed and a subset tested in bacteria, with bacterial NOT-gate results, yeast guide-RNA experiments and human-cell input-expression studies providing different pieces of evidence; the wiki says testing is ongoing and names the remaining gate-validation work. Capabilities are labelled Implemented, Conditional (execution or release depends on infrastructure, data or screening) or Incomplete, with the stated rule that missing evidence is never scored as a numerical zero and a high score cannot fill it. The removed off-target scanner is explicitly not replaced by a zero-valued measurement. The recorded demonstration run is reported with its failure included: a 711-nt mCherry input produced 21 ranked designs, but FASTA, GenBank and SBOL release was held because the screening service was unavailable.","software":"CERNAL is the most engineering-mature iGEM software this year, and its distinguishing feature is that almost every claim is qualified by what it does not establish. The pipeline runs: differential-expression table or direct transcript in; gene ranking; sliding-window trigger enumeration scored by ViennaRNA-predicted accessibility (RNAplfold partition functions, base-pair probabilities, minimum free energy) with positions and sequence context retained; gate design across six families (single-input toehold, prokaryotic and eukaryotic AND, prokaryotic and eukaryotic NOT, CRISPR-based); cross-family ranking on shared metric definitions with normalisation and weights so candidates from compatible gate families sit in one list; circuit composition from a Boolean expression; and annotated plasmid assembly with RFC10 and RFC1000 restriction-site checks against the selected assembly standard. Three interfaces sit over one engine: a guided four-step web wizard (inputs, logic, payload, vector), a versioned HTTP API with OpenAPI docs at /api/docs and five core endpoints (GET /api/version for capabilities, POST /api/design returning a job handle, GET /api/design/{id} for cheap polling, GET /api/design/{id}/results with ?format=csv, GET /api/artifacts/{id}/download with ownership checks), and an optional LLM chatbot for picking a reference gene. Client packages ship for Python, R and MATLAB plus curl examples, and the team publishes which clients are actually verified: Python has recorded live-server CI conformance, R has later checks, MATLAB has archived wrapper defects and no fresh conformance claimed. API keys carry a cern_live_ prefix with only a SHA-256 digest stored, two scopes (read, design), expiry, revocation, 60 requests per minute and two concurrent runs by default, and an object owned by another account returns 404 rather than confirming its existence. Strict submission rejects misspelled constraint keys with a structured 422 and suggestions rather than silently applying a default, and the stated compatibility promise within an API schema version is additive-only. Formats: RNA sequences and differential-expression tables in, custom GenBank backbones in, FASTA, annotated GenBank, SBOL 3 (preserving sequence features, part roles and provenance) and CSV out, with Biopython handling GenBank and ViennaRNA the thermodynamics. Two things are unusual. First, biosecurity is wired into the pipeline, not bolted on: an IBBIS Common Mechanism integration (HMM sequence-profile models plus similarity search) screens the final switch and the assembled construct and holds sequence export when screening evidence is unavailable or unresolved, and the wiki states that a hold is not a completed screen. Second, the team separates scientific computation from AI-assisted development and says so in a dedicated section: the reviewed runtime contains no generative AI, LLM, neural network, trained classifier or remote inference service, the Python and JavaScript manifests include no AI inference SDK, and design runs send no biological data to an AI provider, while AI assistance used in interface design, coding and documentation is recorded in attribution. Reproducibility is handled by publishing a fixed 7.1 MiB source snapshot (revision 9a5ca657) with a checksum manifest, noting candidly that this revision was not on the public repository when checked and that the public repo may contain a different revision, so the snapshot is not substituted for it. Documentation is layered: a public documentation index, architecture diagrams, a scientific-engine module map, an API reference generated into a committed file with a freshness test that detects drift, decision records (including one on choosing SBOL 3), typed contracts and docstrings on cross-component data, and a repository map for new contributors. Four named reuse points are offered for teams who want only a piece: the engine contract, gate-family hooks, the scoring layer and the window utility. Repo: https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/tau-israel/cernal. A hosted deployment exists at https://cernal.app (also cernal.duckdns.org, same host) but it is gated, the wiki says to sign in with a lab account or request access, and the host did not respond when checked, so the dependable route is the published source snapshot and a local install. Upstream credit is kept explicit: a separate eukaryotic AND research notebook reads ranked CSVs exported from the third-party NucSyn Platform, and the wiki states that NucSyn is neither invoked nor bundled by the production engine and that the two sets of scores remain distinct.","stack":["Python 3.13","Django","Django Ninja","django-q2","SQLite (WAL)","uv","React 19","TanStack Router","React Query","Vite","Node 22+","ViennaRNA (RNAplfold, RNAfold, RNAcofold)","Biopython","SBOL 3","GenBank","OpenAPI","IBBIS Common Mechanism","Python / R / MATLAB client packages","DESeq2-style differential expression input","iGEM GitLab"],"techniques":["RNA secondary-structure prediction via partition functions and base-pair probabilities","accessibility profiling of sliding trigger windows","toehold switch design (hairpin-sequestered RBS)","prokaryotic and eukaryotic AND and NOT gate architectures","CRISPRa gate design","cross-family metric normalisation and weighted ranking","Boolean circuit composition","differential-expression gene ranking with Benjamini-Hochberg adjustment and log2 fold thresholds","benchmarking predictions against in-cell SHAPE data","benchmarking against Green et al. measured ON/OFF ratios","HMM sequence-profile biosecurity screening","architecture-boundary enforcement via AST import tests","state-machine run lifecycle with explicit terminal outcomes","transactional result import with checksum verification"],"frameworks_zh":"一個 React 19 靜態單頁應用程式（TanStack Router、以 React Query 管理伺服器狀態、輪詢與變更），建置進 Django 的靜態資源中，底層是 Django Ninja 的具型別 HTTP 路由（共用的錯誤封包格式）、以 Django ORM 模型保存狀態，以及一個透過引擎介面派送工作的輕量 django-q2 任務。v1 執行環境刻意使用啟用 write-ahead logging、外鍵與 busy timeout 的 SQLite，加上單一個以 ORM 為後端的佇列工作者，因此佇列就是一張資料庫表，不需要獨立的訊息中介（Redis、RabbitMQ）；速率限制狀態也存在資料庫快取，而不是各行程各自計數。工作者逾時設為一小時、最大嘗試次數設為一，明確是為了避免無聲地重跑一次昂貴的計算。科學運算引擎是獨立套件：它不 import Django、路由、應用模組、資料庫或 Django 設定，設定值以凍結的請求紀錄形式傳入，並有一個抽象語法樹測試會抓出會破壞這條界線的一般、條件式與函式內 import。平台程式碼只能 import engine.contract 與 engine.client，絕不能碰科學內部實作，這表示引擎在沒有網頁伺服器、資料庫或網路的情況下也能執行與測試，並可在相同的請求／結果介面後方移到遠端行程。環境需求：Python 3.13、uv、前端建置需 Node 22+、ViennaRNA 與 Biopython；執行「./do install && ./do migrate && ./do superuser && ./do build-frontend」後啟動開發伺服器，並在第二個終端機開一個工作者，因為沒有工作者時送出的任務只會一直排隊。","dataviz_zh":"專案首頁是一段長捲動式的導覽解說，動畫呈現真正的機制：鏡頭推進一個充滿彩色轉錄本的細胞質，依豐度排列以顯示狀態指紋，標出只在細胞 A 或只在細胞 B 高表現的轉錄本，挑出一個，找到觸發視窗，接著展示把 RBS 埋起來的髮夾鎖被鑰匙拉開，最後同樣的鎖變成 AND 與 NOT 閘。軟體頁面編排成一本分章的「田野指南」，每項主張都連到對應的實作紀錄，另有一段五步驟自動播放的真實執行螢幕錄影（2026 年 10 月 11 日自本機應用程式錄製），每一步都附「你應該會看到什麼」的敘述，並為關閉 JavaScript 的使用者提供靜態圖片替代。結果瀏覽器以完整的指標分解呈現排序後的候選，含構築檢視與警示，並且被淘汰的候選仍然看得見；使用者的決策標記（無、釘選、入選、淘汰、送合成）只是註記，明確不會改變任何計算或釋出結果。執行狀態畫成一個六狀態機，含八種允許的轉換。","datascience_zh":"驗證是逐題對照 Best Software 評分表的問題來回答，每一題都連到一筆實作或量測紀錄，並分成四種彼此不可互相取代（wiki 明言）的證據：軟體檢查、已記錄的執行、結構比較，以及宿主實驗。兩項外部比較為預測結果提供錨點：RNA 可及性分數與已發表的細胞內 SHAPE 量測在 450 筆 E. coli RNA 記錄上比較；開關排序指標則對照 Green 等人實測的 toehold ON/OFF 比值檢驗。基因選擇在 PFOA 分析中使用已發表的表現資料，另有一項子宮內膜異位症分析納入健康組織作為對照，把 AREG 與 SELE 分別依腹膜淺層病灶與卵巢深層病灶分層。AND 閘研究枚舉了數十萬個候選設計，而檢視每種架構中最好與最差的案例，在任何東西被建造之前就浮現了失效模式，特別是那些「只因為一直維持關閉所以分數漂亮」的開關，以及只在紙上好看的標的。在實驗台上，他們設計了數十個 toehold 候選並測試其中一部分於細菌中，細菌 NOT 閘結果、酵母嚮導 RNA 實驗與人類細胞輸入表現研究各提供了不同片段的證據；wiki 說明測試仍在進行，並指名尚待完成的閘驗證工作。各項能力分別標示為已實作（Implemented）、有條件（Conditional，執行或釋出取決於基礎設施、資料或篩查）或未完成（Incomplete），並明訂一條規則：缺少的證據絕不以數值零計分，高分也不能填補它。被移除的脫靶掃描器明確不以一個零值量測來替代。那次有記錄的示範執行連失敗一起報告：一個 711 nt 的 mCherry 輸入產生 21 個排序設計，但因篩查服務無法使用，FASTA、GenBank 與 SBOL 的釋出被扣住。","software_zh":"CERNAL 是今年工程成熟度最高的 iGEM 軟體，而它最與眾不同之處在於，幾乎每一項主張都附帶說明它「沒有」證明什麼。管線流程為：輸入差異表現表格或直接給定轉錄本；基因排序；以滑動視窗枚舉觸發序列，並以 ViennaRNA 預測的可及性評分（RNAplfold 分配函數、鹼基配對機率、最小自由能），保留位置與序列脈絡；跨六個家族的閘設計（單輸入 toehold、原核與真核 AND、原核與真核 NOT、CRISPR 式）；以共用的指標定義、搭配正規化與權重做跨家族排序，使相容閘家族的候選能並列於同一份清單；由布林運算式組出迴路；最後進行帶註解的質體組裝，並依選定的組裝標準做 RFC10 與 RFC1000 限制酶切位檢查。三個介面架在同一個引擎上：一個四步驟引導式網頁精靈（輸入、邏輯、酬載、載體）；一個版本化的 HTTP API，在 /api/docs 提供 OpenAPI 文件與五個核心端點（GET /api/version 查詢能力、POST /api/design 回傳工作代號、GET /api/design/{id} 供低成本輪詢、GET /api/design/{id}/results 可加 ?format=csv、GET /api/artifacts/{id}/download 並檢查所有權）；以及一個選用的 LLM 聊天機器人協助挑選參考基因。客戶端套件提供 Python、R 與 MATLAB 版本並附 curl 範例，團隊也公開哪些客戶端真正經過驗證：Python 有針對實際伺服器的 CI 一致性紀錄，R 有後續檢查，MATLAB 則有已歸檔的包裝器缺陷、且未聲稱有新的一致性驗證。API 金鑰帶 cern_live_ 前綴、只儲存 SHA-256 摘要，具兩種範圍（read、design）、有效期限、撤銷機制，預設每分鐘 60 次請求與兩個並行執行；屬於其他帳號的物件會回傳 404，而不是確認它存在。嚴格的提交模式會以結構化的 422 與建議拒絕拼錯的限制鍵，而不是悄悄套用預設值；而在同一個 API 綱要版本內，相容性承諾明訂為「僅增不減」。格式方面：輸入為 RNA 序列與差異表現表格、可帶入自訂 GenBank 骨架；輸出為 FASTA、帶註解的 GenBank、SBOL 3（保留序列特徵、部件角色與來源資訊）與 CSV，GenBank 由 Biopython 處理、熱力學由 ViennaRNA 處理。有兩點不尋常。第一，生物安全是接進管線內部、而非事後外掛：整合 IBBIS Common Mechanism（HMM 序列輪廓模型加上相似度搜尋）篩查最終開關與組裝完成的構築，並在篩查證據不可得或未釐清時扣住序列匯出；wiki 也明言，一次扣住並不等於一次完成的篩查。第二，團隊在專節中把科學運算與 AI 輔助開發分開並明白說出：經審查的執行環境不含任何生成式 AI、LLM、神經網路、訓練好的分類器或遠端推論服務，Python 與 JavaScript 的相依清單中沒有任何 AI 推論 SDK，設計執行也不會把生物資料送到任何 AI 供應商；而介面設計、寫程式與文件撰寫中使用的 AI 協助則記錄在貢獻聲明裡。可重現性的處理方式是發布一份固定的 7.1 MiB 原始碼快照（修訂版 9a5ca657）與檢查碼清單，並坦言在查核時這個修訂版並不在公開程式庫上、公開程式庫可能含有不同修訂版，因此該快照並不取代公開程式庫。文件分層：公開文件索引、架構圖、科學運算引擎的模組地圖、產生到一個已版控檔案中的 API 參考（附偵測漂移的新鮮度測試）、決策紀錄（包括選擇 SBOL 3 的那一則）、跨元件資料的型別契約與 docstring，以及給新貢獻者的程式庫導覽。對只想取用其中一部分的隊伍，他們指名提供四個可重用的接點：引擎契約、閘家族掛鉤、評分層與視窗工具。程式庫：https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/tau-israel/cernal 。另有託管部署於 https://cernal.app （以及同一主機的 cernal.duckdns.org），但有存取限制，wiki 說明需以實驗室帳號登入或申請權限，而查核時該主機沒有回應，因此可靠的路徑是已發布的原始碼快照加上本機安裝。上游來源的歸屬也保持明確：一份獨立的真核 AND 研究筆記本讀取自第三方 NucSyn Platform 匯出的排序 CSV，而 wiki 明言正式環境的引擎既不呼叫也不包裝 NucSyn，兩套分數也維持區分。"},"good":{"publicEngagement":"The team ran a Mini-Jamboree where CERNAL was demonstrated live to other iGEM teams and then surveyed the participants (7 responses): all agreed synthetic biology lacks a generalizable approach for designing intracellular circuits responding to user-defined stimuli, 71.4% said they would use such a tool during iGEM and 85.7% afterwards, with interest spread across biosensing (57.1%), cell engineering (57.1%), and diagnostics, therapeutics and environmental sensing (28.6% each). The team states plainly that this is a directional signal from a small, self-selected group of peers and not market evidence, and that its value is that the demand they claim was checked with outside users rather than asserted. AIS-China was given the interface to use and returned three concrete usability fixes that the team adopted: clearer placement of downloads, a more prominent New Circuit entry point, and meaningful run names. A video walkthrough, in-app FAQ and public FAQ source support new users.","ihp":"Human practices operated under a stated 'Responsibility-by-Design' philosophy whose point was to turn the phrase into constraints. Patient accounts set the design goal: Shir Parchef waited 18 years for an endometriosis diagnosis and underwent an 11-hour procedure with six surgeons; Netta Ben Moshe was told incapacitating pain was ordinary cramps; Helen Altschuler described patients' willingness to support research because so little else exists. From these the team set the target as eliminating pathology rather than masking symptoms, and without systemic hormonal ablation. Dr. Berkowitz told them a therapy that shrinks lesions without relieving pain or preserving fertility has no clinical utility, which made them stratify AREG and SELE across both superficial peritoneal and deep ovarian lesions so the logic covers the 'invisible' lesions driving the worst pain rather than only what imaging shows. Several loops closed by narrowing the claim rather than widening it: after input from Dr. Berman the PFAS biosensor is positioned as a low-cost triage tool that prioritises which of Israel's hundreds of wells need urgent lab testing, explicitly not a replacement for LC-MS, and the team states it has not solved RNA delivery. Conversations with Neta Agmon about practical inputs and outputs and with AIS-China about user workflow shaped which interfaces were documented for reuse.","realWorld":"A provisional patent application was filed through Tel Aviv University's technology transfer office. The market case is built from Alliance for Regenerative Medicine sector data: 1,089 commercial cell and gene therapy developers in a US$1.7B total addressable market, of which 553-731 use genetic modification, and applying a stated 30% in-house design assumption gives a beachhead of 166-219 accounts worth US$0.25-0.33B, with four organisations shortlisted for first contact and HEK293/HEK293T chosen as the entry cell line because it is widely used in industry. The competitive positioning is specific rather than dismissive: Cello 2.0 maps circuit specifications to characterised parts and Asimov Kernel provides construct design, simulation and workflow tools, but both depend on predefined specifications, characterised parts or host-specific workflows, whereas CERNAL starts from transcriptomic state; the wiki notes these citations support design context and are not an absolute claim that no competing route exists. The MVP is a 5-10 week design-partner cycle from discovery to structured feedback, and the team reports CERNAL has already produced 730 E. coli and 110 yeast circuit candidates as a routine pipeline rather than a demo.","partners":["Tel Aviv University technology transfer office","endometriosis patients and advocates (Shir Parchef, Netta Ben Moshe, Helen Altschuler)","clinicians (Dr. Berkowitz)","water-research and PFAS analysis experts (Dr. Berman)","AIS-China (interface user testing)","Neta Agmon","IBBIS (Common Mechanism screening)","NucSyn Platform (upstream, offline data interface)","Alliance for Regenerative Medicine (market data)"],"publicEngagement_zh":"團隊辦了一場 Mini-Jamboree，向其他 iGEM 隊伍現場示範 CERNAL，並對參與者做問卷（7 份回覆）：所有人都同意合成生物學缺少一套可通用的方法來設計回應使用者自訂刺激的細胞內迴路，71.4% 表示會在 iGEM 期間使用這樣的工具、85.7% 表示在 iGEM 之後會使用，興趣分布於生物感測（57.1%）、細胞工程（57.1%），以及診斷、治療與環境感測（各 28.6%）。團隊直言這只是來自一小群自我選擇的同儕的方向性訊號，不是市場證據，其價值在於他們所宣稱的需求是向外部使用者查核過的，而不是自己斷言的。他們把介面交給 AIS-China 實際使用，對方回報了三項具體的易用性修正並被採納：下載位置更清楚、New Circuit 入口更顯眼、執行名稱要有意義。另有影片導覽、應用程式內 FAQ 與公開 FAQ 原始檔支援新使用者。","ihp_zh":"人類實踐以明確宣示的「Responsibility-by-Design」哲學運作，其重點是把這個詞變成實際的約束條件。病患的敘述設定了設計目標：Shir Parchef 等了 18 年才確診子宮內膜異位症，並接受一場由六名外科醫師進行、長達 11 小時的手術；Netta Ben Moshe 被告知那種使人無法行動的疼痛只是普通經痛；Helen Altschuler 描述病患之所以願意支持研究，是因為其他選擇實在太少。由此團隊把目標設定為消除病理本身而非掩蓋症狀，且不訴諸全身性的荷爾蒙抑制。Dr. Berkowitz 告訴他們，一種能縮小病灶但不能緩解疼痛、也不能保全生育力的療法在臨床上沒有用處，於是他們把 AREG 與 SELE 同時依腹膜淺層與卵巢深層病灶分層，讓邏輯涵蓋那些造成最嚴重疼痛、卻「看不見」的病灶，而不只是影像上顯示的部分。有幾個迴圈是以收窄主張而非擴大主張來閉合的：在 Dr. Berman 提供意見後，PFAS 生物感測器被定位為低成本的初篩工具，用來判斷以色列數百口井中哪些需要緊急送實驗室檢驗，明確不是 LC-MS 的替代品；團隊也聲明自己並未解決 RNA 遞送問題。與 Neta Agmon 關於實務輸入與輸出的討論，以及與 AIS-China 關於使用者工作流程的交流，則決定了哪些介面會被寫成可重用的文件。","realWorld_zh":"團隊透過台拉維夫大學技術移轉辦公室提出臨時專利申請。市場論證建立在 Alliance for Regenerative Medicine 的產業資料上：1,089 家商業化細胞與基因治療開發商、總可觸及市場 17 億美元，其中 553-731 家使用基因改造；再套用明確標示的「30% 自行設計」假設，得到 166-219 個客戶的灘頭市場、價值 2.5-3.3 億美元，並列出四個優先接洽的組織；入門細胞株選擇 HEK293/HEK293T，因為它在產業中廣泛使用。競爭定位具體而不輕蔑：Cello 2.0 把迴路規格對映到已鑑定部件，Asimov Kernel 提供構築設計、模擬與工作流程工具，但兩者都依賴預先定義的規格、已鑑定部件或特定宿主的流程，而 CERNAL 的起點是轉錄體狀態；wiki 也註明這些引用是用來支撐設計脈絡，並非絕對主張「不存在任何競爭路徑」。MVP 是一個 5-10 週的設計夥伴循環，從探索到結構化回饋；團隊並報告 CERNAL 已以常規管線（而非示範）產出 730 個 E. coli 與 110 個酵母迴路候選。"},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6196/wiki/software/01-inputs.avif?v=4","caption":"CERNAL's Inputs panel: E. coli selected as host and a 711-nucleotide mCherry transcript entered as a Direct Trigger mRNA, from the recorded five-step walkthrough.","credit":"Team TAU-Israel, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"CERNAL 的輸入面板：選定 E. coli 為宿主，並輸入一段 711 個核苷酸的 mCherry 轉錄本作為 Direct Trigger mRNA，取自那段錄製的五步驟導覽。"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6196/wiki/software/cernal-s03-generated-v1.webp","caption":"The three decisions behind one RNA design: recognition-site selection, compatible switch design and comparison, with host experiments and not computation establishing function.","credit":"Team TAU-Israel, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"一個 RNA 設計背後的三項決策：辨識位點選擇、相容開關設計與比較，並明示功能是由宿主實驗、而非計算所確立。"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6196/wiki/software/cernal-s19-generated-v1.webp","caption":"The engine/platform boundary: the engine takes a versioned request and returns candidates plus an artifact manifest, with a source-level import test enforcing the separation.","credit":"Team TAU-Israel, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"引擎與平台的界線：引擎接受一個版本化的請求，回傳候選設計加上一份產物清單，並以原始碼層級的 import 測試強制這道分隔。"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6196/wiki/software/cernal-s21-generated-v1.webp","caption":"The automation surface: query the version endpoint for capabilities, submit a design once, keep the job handle, poll status, inspect results and request only permitted files.","credit":"Team TAU-Israel, iGEM 2026 wiki","caption_zh":"自動化介面：先向 version 端點查詢能力，提交設計一次，保留工作代號，輪詢狀態，檢視結果，並只索取被允許的檔案。"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Build the scientific engine as a package that cannot import the web framework, the database or the settings, and enforce it with an automated import test, so the science can be run, tested and reused headlessly and the UI is only one of three front ends. Then adopt their reporting discipline: label every capability Implemented, Conditional or Incomplete, never score a missing measurement as zero, publish a recorded run that includes the step where it failed, and keep AI-assisted development in the attribution record and out of the scientific runtime.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/tau-israel/","https://2026.igem.wiki/tau-israel/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/tau-israel/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/tau-israel/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/tau-israel/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/tau-israel/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/tau-israel/contribution","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/tau-israel/cernal","https://cernal.app"],"projectTitle_zh":"CERNAL","tagline_zh":"一個生物編譯器：輸入 RNA 表現資料，得到排序後的 RNA 邏輯閘迴路設計，只在你指定的細胞狀態下啟動。","summary_zh":"CERNAL 把轉錄體當成細胞狀態的指紋，並把這個指紋編譯成 RNA 邏輯迴路：它挑出能把目標細胞與鄰近細胞區分開來的轉錄本，掃描每個轉錄本尋找可及、專一且可建構的觸發視窗，設計 toehold 式開關——其髮夾結構會把核醣體結合位藏起來，直到觸發序列把它拉開——再把多個開關組合成 AND 與 NOT 閘，以共用的熱力學指標為每個候選排序，最後把勝出者組裝成帶註解的質體。由於感測元件是細胞自身的 RNA 而非已鑑定的轉錄因子，這套方法的設計意圖是與宿主無關，團隊也以三個概念驗證示範：HEK293T 中的子宮內膜異位症邏輯、E. coli 中的 PFOA/PFAS 生物感測器，以及酵母中的 CRISPRa 閘。軟體是一個 Django Ninja + React 19 應用程式，具嚴格隔離的科學運算引擎、版本化的 HTTP API（附 Python、R 與 MATLAB 客戶端）、SBOL 3 匯出，以及一道 IBBIS Common Mechanism 生物安全閘門——在篩查無法完成時扣住序列檔案不放。團隊透過台拉維夫大學技轉辦公室提出臨時專利申請，並圍繞細胞與基因治療開發商建立了完整的市場論證。","gemsTakeaway_zh":"把科學運算引擎做成一個不能 import 網頁框架、資料庫或設定檔的套件，並以自動化的 import 測試強制執行，讓科學部分能在無介面的情況下執行、測試與重用，而 UI 只是三個前端之一。接著採用他們的報告紀律：把每項能力標示為已實作、有條件或未完成；絕不把缺少的量測計為零；公開一次連失敗步驟一起呈現的錄製執行；並把 AI 輔助開發留在貢獻聲明中、排除在科學執行環境之外。","rank":7},"6197":{"team":"HangzhouFourteenAP","id":"6197","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"Space, Foundational Advance, Software & AI, Biomanufacturing","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/hangzhoufourteenap/","projectTitle":"DCO (Dental Calculus Obstructor)","tagline":"A four-enzyme cocktail plus a hydroxyapatite-binding antimicrobial peptide coating that dismantles dental plaque biofilm before it mineralises into calculus.","summary":"DCO is a three-module biological oral care system: an enzyme cocktail that degrades the organic matrix holding plaque biofilm together, a tooth-binding antimicrobial peptide that coats enamel to block re-colonisation, and a controlled-release system to coordinate them. The enzymes are two recombinantly expressed glycoside hydrolases — PmGH87 (alpha-1,3-glucanase) and CoGH66 (alpha-1,6-glucanase), which act cooperatively because CoGH66 removes alpha-1,6 branches and exposes new PmGH87 cleavage sites — plus commercially sourced DNase I and papain for extracellular DNA and protein. It addresses a real and specific burden: 96.7% of Chinese adults aged 35-44 have dental calculus, over 900 million have periodontal disease, only 20.1% of elderly people saw a dentist in the past year, and the dentist-to-population ratio is about 1:7,768. It won Best Village Project on a tight problem-to-product chain, a FoldX mutation-prioritisation pipeline whose prediction was wrong and whose failure is reported in full, and an unusually commercially literate entrepreneurship section that refuses to make anti-calculus claims it cannot support.","awards":["Top 10 (High School)","Best Measurement — Nominee (High School)","Best Presentation — Nominee (High School)","Best Wiki — Nominee (High School)","Best Integrated Human Practices — Nominee (High School)","Best Village Project — Winner (Space / Foundational Advance / Software & AI / Biomanufacturing)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Two computational pipelines, both modest in tooling but well-reasoned and, importantly, both reported against their experimental outcome. (1) A CoGH66 mutation prioritisation pipeline built to avoid screening hundreds of mutants in the wet lab. Starting from the substrate-bound structure PDB 8IUB (CoGH66 with isomaltotriose bound, so no re-docking was needed), they used PyMOL to extract all protein residues within 4.0 A of the substrate, giving an 18-residue binding pocket (Y166, D167, Q169, Q172, I190, Y217, L219, H250, L252, F256, I260, D293, L295, N395, K429, E430, Y431, N434) consistent with the published catalytic cleft and +2 to -4 subsites. Domain annotation came from CD-Search (Glyco_hydro_66 at residues 22-560, E-value 0) and InterPro (glycosidases at 104-440), with sequence translation via Novopro. They then layered evolutionary information: BLASTp against the NCBI non-redundant protein database, deliberately selecting homologs from different bacterial species at 30-70% identity to avoid over-representing near-identical sequences and to capture naturally tolerated substitutions, aligned with MAFFT and visualised as an ESPript conservation map. Of the 18 contact residues, seven (Y166, Q169, Q172, I190, H250, N395, K429) showed species-specific natural substitutions and were taken as plastic; the remaining eleven were conserved and deliberately left alone. Mutants were built in PyMOL, repaired and scored in FoldX for both stability change and binding change, with an operational priority threshold of binding delta-delta-G < -1 kcal/mol chosen explicitly because it exceeds typical FoldX error. (2) Antimicrobial peptide selection: after a literature review identified four hydroxyapatite-binding AMP candidates, they used AlphaFold Server to predict peptide-calcium ion coordination as a first computational filter, reasoning that hydroxyapatite presents Ca2+ as the primary interaction site, and ranked candidates by pTM and interface pTM (ipTM) scores. SHABP (21 aa, cyclic and disulfide-constrained) and G12R (18 aa, linear alpha-helical) both reached pTM around 0.4, above DNase-fused and HBAMP alternatives, and both were advanced into parallel experimental validation on the grounds of their distinct structural strategies (conformational stability versus membrane disruption).","dataviz":"The model page leads with a schematic workflow diagram of the whole mutation-prioritisation pipeline, so the logic from structure to alignment to energy calculation is readable before any numbers appear, and ends with a three-dimensional localisation figure placing the two prioritised positions in the pocket (protein green, mutated positions red with arrows, substrate yellow, other 4.0 A contacts cyan). The genuinely notable choice is an interactive 3D model of the CoGH66-isomaltotriose complex embedded in the wiki as a glTF file exported from PyMOL, so a reader can rotate the enzyme and inspect the contact residues rather than squint at a static render — a cheap but effective way to make a structural argument inspectable. Tables carry the natural substitutions observed per non-conserved position with counts, and the full FoldX energy results for every tested mutant rather than only the winners. Measurement figures pair the physical artefact with its quantification throughout: a 96-well plate photograph alongside the bar chart derived from it for the DNS reducing-sugar assay, the crystal violet extracts, and the acridine orange fluorescence images with the ImageJ intensity quantification in the identical group order so the reader can check the numbers against the wells. Standard curves are shown with their regression equations and R2 values (BCA at Y = 0.8964X - 0.2574, R2 = 0.9951).","datascience":"The most valuable dry-lab content is a documented computational failure. The pipeline predicted Y166Q as the top candidate (the only mutant meeting the -1 kcal/mol binding threshold, at -1.63 kcal/mol) with Q172P as a secondary candidate retained despite only -0.38 kcal/mol because of its predicted stabilising effect and natural occurrence in homologs. Site-directed mutagenesis (reverse PCR with back-to-back mutation-carrying primers, DpnI digestion of methylated parental template, self-ligation), colony PCR at the expected ~1726 bp, and Sanger sequencing confirmed both constructs (Y166Q TAC to CAG; Q172P CAG to CCG). The DNS activity assay then inverted the ranking: Q172P gave the highest apparent activity at net OD 1.881, wild type 0.996, and Y166Q only 0.629 — the computational winner was worse than wild type. The team's response is the right one: they revised the ranking in the text, named Q172P the leading experimental candidate, reclassified Y166Q as a mechanistic probe rather than quietly dropping it, and had already flagged in advance that Q172P introduces a proline and may alter main-chain conformation so its FoldX estimate should be read with caution. They also controlled the comparison properly rather than letting protein load explain the result: BCA quantification gave WT 12.1, Y166Q 10.9 and Q172P 9.1 microgram/mL, crude lysates were normalised to equal total protein before the DNS assay, and the wiki explicitly notes that Q172P's lower total protein means its activity signal cannot be attributed to a higher load. The measurement work on the artificial dental calculus model is similarly self-critical. Gravimetric analysis of six treatment conditions (negative control, four single-component omissions, complete cocktail) found no significant weight-loss differences, and the team attributed this to balance sensitivity and to non-uniform mineralisation producing variability that masked the effect, then moved to more sensitive assays rather than reporting a null as a result. Crystal violet quantification at OD gave the complete cocktail a significant reduction against the negative control (p < 0.05), with the papain-omission comparison reported honestly as a trend toward significance at p = 0.08 and interpreted as papain playing a supporting rather than dominant role under single-treatment conditions. Acridine orange fluorescence with ImageJ quantification showed significance against the negative control and against the DNase-I-omission group, supporting the mechanistic model that eDNA cleavage lets the other enzymes penetrate, while the overall small between-group differences led them to conclude that the primary mode of action is structural matrix dismantling rather than direct bactericidal potency. Limitations are stated plainly, including that the B. subtilis surrogate model does not replicate the Streptococcus mutans-specific EPS composition the glucanases actually target. The AlphaFold peptide screen also carries its own caveat: the team notes that peptide-Ca2+ coordination cannot fully replicate crystal-surface binding, that pTM around 0.4 indicates only moderate confidence, and that the scores were used for relative ranking rather than as affinity estimates.","software":"No standalone released software tool; the dry lab is a documented analysis pipeline rather than a product, and the wiki itself is a React/Vite single-page application with GSAP animation. Released reusable resources instead: the full mutation-prioritisation methodology as a reproducible protocol, the interactive glTF structural model, PDF slide decks for all four education audiences (two elementary sessions dated 5-28 and 6-11, a high school deck, and an elderly-residents deck), a consolidated enzyme stabilisation and controlled-release guide offered as a generalised framework for multi-enzyme formulations across biocatalysis, food processing and environmental remediation, and a 'lessons learned for future iGEM teams' section. Constructs were expressed from codon-optimised genes in pET-32a via seamless cloning, carrying an N-terminal thioredoxin (TrxA) tag for soluble expression, a 6xHis tag for IMAC purification and an enterokinase site for optional tag removal, under T7 promoter control in E. coli Rosetta(DE3), with CoGH66 confirmed at approximately 76.54 kDa. The team also documented a safety-driven substitution they consulted the iGEM committee about: because Streptococcus mutans is not on the iGEM White List they used B. subtilis as a surrogate in the artificial calculus model, and because Aspergillus niger is not listed they used commercially available edible fungi as a material source.","stack":["PyMOL","FoldX","MAFFT","ESPript","BLASTp / NCBI non-redundant database","NCBI CD-Search","InterPro","AlphaFold Server (pTM / ipTM)","glTF (interactive 3D export)","ImageJ","PDB 8IUB","Novopro translation tool","DNS (3,5-dinitrosalicylic acid) reducing-sugar assay","BCA protein quantification","crystal violet biofilm quantification","acridine orange fluorescence microscopy","pET-32a / E. coli Rosetta(DE3)","React + Vite + GSAP (wiki)"],"techniques":["structure-guided binding-pocket contact extraction at 4.0 A","evolutionary tolerance filtering via homolog MSA conservation mapping","FoldX delta-delta-G stability and binding energy calculation with a pre-set error-aware threshold","reporting a failed computational prediction and reclassifying the candidate as a mechanistic probe","total-protein normalisation before activity comparison (BCA then equal-load DNS)","site-directed mutagenesis by reverse PCR with DpnI selection and self-ligation","Sanger sequencing verification of point mutations","single-component omission (leave-one-out) assay design to test synergy","escalation from an insensitive assay (gravimetry) to more sensitive orthogonal assays","Student's t-test with reported non-significant and borderline p values","AlphaFold interface confidence scores for relative peptide ranking","White List-driven surrogate organism substitution with committee consultation"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Four-tier education (primary school, high school, elderly residents, general public) with the explicit design principle that they did not just teach knowledge but recorded what changed after participants went home — brushing, flossing, denture care, diet, dental visits and attitudes toward synthetic biology. The best single tool is a tangible genetic circuit built from electronic building blocks: a touch sensor stands for the promoter, a toggle switch module for the lac operator, a button for lactose as inducer, an LED for the RBS, a small fan for the target gene and a manual power-off switch for the terminator, so children physically discover that touching the sensor alone does nothing because the operator blocks by default, and that the circuit only runs when the inducer is held. For younger children they wrote child-friendly science comics and ran plaque disclosing tablets as a reveal — children chewed the tablets, rinsed, saw red and blue patches on their own teeth, were asked to guess and ask questions first, and were then shown microscope images with the framing 'this is not dirt, this is a city'. The team records the emotional shift honestly: children moved from fearing bacteria to being curious about them and from passive listening to asking and designing. High school sessions used a full script and deck covering project background, enzyme mechanism, experimental process and application value, and specifically targeted the soft-plaque-versus-hard-calculus confusion. The nursing home session simplified everything into plain language and images and delivered concretely actionable care: a soft-bristled small-headed brush at 45 degrees to the gumline, gentle brushing with no horizontal scrubbing, bedtime brushing more important than morning, floss or interdental brushes rather than toothpicks, and denture care rules (rinse after meals, remove and soak overnight, never boiling water, never toothpaste, never sleep in them), with the explicit disclaimer that this is science communication and does not replace professional dental advice. Public outreach at Wushan Square used display boards, roll-up banners, hand fans and leaflets on plaque versus calculus and scaling misconceptions.","ihp":"Twelve named advisors spanning clinical dentistry, periodontics, microbial control, pharmaceutics, gene circuit regulation, management and marketing, and oral care product regulatory and quality management, engaged in a staged problem-framing process. Problem framing combined a 350-respondent user questionnaire, an in-depth clinical interview with Dr. Lei Lihong (Second Affiliated Hospital, Zhejiang University School of Medicine) and an industry interview with Mr. Fan Wenjun (healthcare investment), triangulated against the Fourth National Oral Health Epidemiological Survey specifically to avoid bias from a single interview source. The survey quantified both misconception and the knowing-doing gap: 61% worry that scaling damages enamel, 23% believe brushing removes calculus, only 6% claim to fully understand it; and separately, 52% know calculus forms at the gingival margin and in deep interdental spaces but only 25% floss or use an irrigator daily, 48% know brushing cannot remove calculus but only 38% get scaling once or twice a year, and 84% know calculus causes periodontitis but only 25% have a six-monthly examination. The project-defining intervention came from Dr. Wang Yongwu (Hangzhou First People's Hospital), who said that using enzymes to dissolve already-mineralised calculus is 'like an egg hitting a stone' — and the team did not just accept the efficacy point but derived a safety consequence from it: because calculus and enamel and dentin are both calcium phosphate mineralised tissues, any non-selective demineralising agent would risk enamel or dentin demineralisation, sensitivity or erosion. That reframed the entire target from mineralised calculus to the organic matrix of the early pre-mineralisation biofilm, which is the intervention window the whole project now occupies. Dr. Lei and Dr. Yuan Yifang (Affiliated Stomatological Hospital of Zhejiang Chinese Medical University) corroborated it and specified what to attack: the polysaccharide-protein cross-linking and the stabilising role of eDNA that together hold the biofilm's three-dimensional structure against salivary washing. Four design constraints emerged from the interview set — efficacy validation, penetration ability, cytotoxicity safety and stability assurance — which became the selection criteria for the enzyme cocktail and delivery system. A second concrete pivot: experts pointed out that enzymatic removal does not prevent recolonisation because salivary proteins form a pellicle within minutes, which is why the hydroxyapatite-binding AMP module exists at all; the computational peptide screen was conducted on their explicit recommendation. A third: on discovering that bovine pancreatic DNase I is already commercially available at roughly 80-160 yuan per 100 mg and widely used, they strategically stopped trying to recombinantly express it and concentrated the synthetic biology effort on the glycoside hydrolases where the EPS matrix offered a real opportunity. Dr. Lei also set a boundary the team kept: any active ingredient in a daily product must be safe and must not disrupt the normal oral microbiome or damage soft tissues.","realWorld":"The most commercially literate section of the five teams, and notable for restraint. The problem is scoped deliberately narrowly: the project does not aim to replace professional scaling, but to serve adults who cannot or will not undergo frequent scaling with a daily, safe, evidence-based product that interferes with plaque maturation and reduces mineralisation risk before it happens — daily prevention and risk reduction, not treatment of existing calculus or periodontal disease. Target segment is urban young people aged 20-30, students and people one to five years into their first jobs, chosen because they have purchasing power, care about social image and have not yet entrenched habits. Channels are specified rather than gestured at: online seeding on Douyin, Xiaohongshu and Bilibili, e-commerce subscriptions, and offline placement in convenience stores, beauty collection stores and supermarkets, with trial experience areas in beauty collection stores. A B-end clinic seed-trial path runs in parallel with the C-end consumer path, and contingencies are written down (if clinic repeat-purchase is below expectation, optimise usage instructions and physician script training; if C-end subscription retention declines, control ad spend pace and iterate the product experience). Six quarterly milestones run from improving the dual recombinant enzyme lab data and stability, patent drafting and seed trials in three to five clinics, through pilot scale-up and third-party safety testing, to daily chemical regulatory filing, first commercial production, retail rollout and a monthly subscription. A three-year P&L is projected (revenue 45 with net -30 and about 35% gross margin, then revenue 280 with net +120 and about 58% gross margin, then revenue 950 with net +530 and about 65% gross margin). IP strategy notes that existing Chinese patents in this space are mostly single-enzyme or simple multi-enzyme combinations and rarely apply microcapsule encapsulation systematically to oral enzyme care, and acquisition by listed biotech oral care entrants such as Bloomage Biotech or Weimeizi (Saky) is named as the exit after commercial validation. Most creditable: all marketing materials and product claims will state explicitly that the product does not replace professional scaling or periodontal treatment, and the portable chewing gum format is to be marketed only for post-meal freshness with no preventive or anti-calculus claim at all — a team voluntarily giving up its best marketing line because it has not earned it yet. Sustainability is argued concretely rather than with SDG slogans: all four actives are proteins expected to degrade to amino acids and peptides after use, and no live organisms are released.","partners":["Dr. Lei Lihong, Associate Chief Physician, Second Affiliated Hospital, Zhejiang University School of Medicine","Dr. Wang Yongwu, Director and Chief Physician of Stomatology, Hangzhou First People's Hospital","Dr. Yuan Yifang, Affiliated Stomatological Hospital of Zhejiang Chinese Medical University","Dr. Huang Jie, Attending Physician of Stomatology, Hangzhou First People's Hospital","Prof. Jia Shiliang, Zhejiang University of Technology (microbial control and protocol validation)","Prof. Yu Haining, Zhejiang University of Technology (natural products and gut microecology)","Dr. Wang Zhiguo, Institute of Aging Research, Hangzhou Normal University (tRNA engineering, gene circuit regulation)","Dr. Shi Jing, Zhejiang University / Texas A&M / Westlake University","Mr. Fan Wenjun, Hangzhou Zhuanjiabang Medical Investment Management","Dr. Wang Haoran, Founder and CEO, Niulan Biotech","Prof. Wu Shiqi, Zhejiang University of Finance and Economics (business plan, market analysis)","Mr. Yu Feng, Quality and Research Center Director, Hangzhou Namei Zhikang Technology (oral care regulatory filing and QC)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6197/wiki/content/model/modeling-figure1.avif","caption":"The CoGH66 mutation prioritisation workflow: PyMOL contact identification in PDB 8IUB, mapping onto the MAFFT/ESPript conservation map to select substitutable sites, point mutation in PyMOL, and FoldX delta-delta-G calculation to rank candidates.","credit":"Team HangzhouFourteenAP, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6197/wiki/content/model/modeling-figure5.avif","caption":"Expression and BCA quantification of CoGH66 wild type and the two predicted mutants: SDS-PAGE, the BCA plate, the standard curve (Y = 0.8964X - 0.2574, R2 = 0.9951) and the resulting concentrations (WT 12.1, Y166Q 10.9, Q172P 9.1 microgram/mL) used to normalise total protein before the activity assay.","credit":"Team HangzhouFourteenAP, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6197/wiki/content/engineer/engineering-figure12.avif","caption":"Enzymatic degradation of artificial dental calculus: the BF, MU and BF+MU model samples, before/after images for each omission condition, the non-significant gravimetric weight-loss panel, and the crystal violet absorbance quantification where the complete cocktail is significantly below the no-enzyme control and the papain-omission comparison sits at p = 0.08.","credit":"Team HangzhouFourteenAP, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6197/wiki/content/education/education-figure11.avif","caption":"A primary school pupil assembling the lac-operon genetic circuit from electronic building blocks, with the small fan standing in for the target gene driven by the touch-sensor promoter, toggle-switch operator and button inducer.","credit":"Team HangzhouFourteenAP, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Their best transferable move is reporting the computational prediction that lost: FoldX picked Y166Q, the bench picked Q172P, and the wiki revises its own ranking and demotes the failed candidate to a mechanistic probe while showing that BCA normalisation rules out protein load as the explanation. A high-school dry lab earns more credibility from one honestly scored wrong prediction with the confound controlled than from three unvalidated ones. Also copy the cheap inspectability trick — export the docked structure as a glTF so a reader can rotate it — and the commercial restraint of marketing a format with no efficacy claim until the evidence exists.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/hangzhoufourteenap/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hangzhoufourteenap/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hangzhoufourteenap/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hangzhoufourteenap/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hangzhoufourteenap/measurement/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hangzhoufourteenap/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hangzhoufourteenap/education/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hangzhoufourteenap/entrepreneurship/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hangzhoufourteenap/sustainable/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hangzhoufourteenap/safety/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hangzhoufourteenap/assets/index-CoIamzKT.js","https://2026.igem.wiki/hangzhoufourteenap/assets/Model-CLIAyY10.js","https://2026.igem.wiki/hangzhoufourteenap/assets/HumanPractice-B3gOYwBY.js"],"rank":124},"6199":{"team":"SUIS-SFLS","id":"6199","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/suis-sfls/","projectTitle":"TyroFix","tagline":"Recyclable magnetic-bead tyrosinase that cheaply DOPA-modifies recombinant mussel adhesive protein, sold as a B2B raw material","summary":"SUIS-SFLS expressed three microbial tyrosinases, immobilised them on magnetic beads so the enzyme can be magnetically recovered and reused, and used the recycled catalyst to hydroxylate Mfp3-linker-Mfp6 fusion mussel foot proteins into DOPA-bearing wet adhesives for skin and wound repair. The commercial thesis is unusually self-aware: after expert interviews they abandoned the idea of selling a finished dressing and repositioned as an upstream B2B raw-material supplier, splitting the same protein stock into TyroFix Mini (cosmetic grade) and TyroFix ProMax (Class II medical grade) and running both regulatory tracks in parallel from day one so that test data never has to be repeated. They are the only high-school team here with a genuine financial model, including capex, cost per litre, pricing, gross margin and breakeven year for each line, published as downloadable PDFs. They were nominated for Best Entrepreneurship in the High School section.","awards":["Best Entrepreneurship — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Golden-circle style Why/How/What mission, PESTLE run separately for each product line, SWOT per line, 4P marketing model, Business Model Canvas, a stakeholder power-interest map, TAM-SAM-SOM per line with stated assumptions, a five-phase 36-month milestone plan, and a two-line financial model with breakeven analysis.","dataviz":"Thirteen entrepreneurship figures including two separate PESTLE diagrams, competitive positioning, purity and performance indicator panels, a technology roadmap, a business model canvas, a milestone chart and two financial-planning charts. Two downloadable PDFs (financial-planning-mini.pdf, financial-planning-promax.pdf) carry the underlying budgets. Survey results are reported with response percentages and mean Likert scores.","datascience":"A 290-response consumer survey quantified to a usable level: over 90 percent reporting skin issues, acne and marks at 62.76 percent, dryness at 48.62 percent, sensitivity at 45.17 percent, satisfaction with existing repair products at 3.34 out of 5, weak efficacy as the main complaint at 72.61 percent, safety at 82.07 percent and repair efficacy at 75.86 percent as the top purchase factors, willingness to try at 3.57 out of 5, and over 60 percent accepting CNY 100-150 with CNY 110-120 as the sweet spot. Cost modelling is benchmarked against recombinant human insulin industrial fermentation.","software":"","stack":["magnetic-bead immobilised tyrosinase","E. coli expression","Mfp3-linker-Mfp6 fusion constructs","chromatography and TFF ultrafiltration","HPLC purity assay","NIH/3T3 cytotoxicity assay"],"techniques":["enzyme immobilisation and magnetic recovery","controlled DOPA hydroxylation","three DBTL cycles on fermentation and purification","wet adhesion measurement in kPa","endotoxin quantification","lyophilisation and reconstitution feasibility"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A 290-response online questionnaire that went beyond sentiment into purchase behaviour, capturing preferred formats, trusted information sources (dermatologists, real user reviews, official brand channels), trial triggers (free samples at 30.69 percent, professional recommendation at 30 percent) and an explicit price band. They also read the result honestly, noting that trust comes from experimental and clinical data (76.21 percent) and transparent mechanism (63.79 percent), and then used those channels to plan promotion rather than inventing a campaign.","ihp":"Five named expert interviews, each with the background stated, the question asked, the feedback, the team's reflection and the concrete project adjustment. Dr. Dongfeng Wang (Deputy Chief Physician, Wuhan Petrochemical Hospital) converted vague 'good adhesion' into care-process requirements and gave quantitative design targets: film formation in about 5 seconds, breathability with water resistance, partial degradation in 3-5 days, and validation moving from superficial to deeper wounds. Mr. Yanxuan Song (medical device engineer and founder of a Guangzhou tech-beauty chain) widened their notion of cost to include purification, storage, transport and handling losses, and suggested lyophilised powder with a reconstitution solution to cut cold-chain burden. Mr. Jiujiang Zhang of CIRS Group, a Class II and III device regulatory specialist, established the rule that shared raw-material origin does not permit shared submission pathways. Mr. Xiaofei Ji, an ISO 13485 internal auditor and NPDP holder who has taken more than ten Class III products to approval, delivered the decisive advice: a student team should start at raw-material supply, treat reproducibility and batch records as early concerns, and settle IP before approaching any manufacturer. That advice visibly rewrote the deliverable, from a finished dressing to a characterised protein plus quality documentation.","realWorld":"The most financially literate high-school entrepreneurship case in this set, and the honesty is what makes it credible. Each line has a built-up cost model rather than a percentage: Mini needs about CNY 6.8 million of equipment (seed shakers, a 200 L fermenter, high-pressure homogeniser, chromatography system, industrial centrifuge, TFF ultrafiltration) depreciated straight-line over six years, about CNY 2.3 million of R&D, and about CNY 71 per litre to produce against a $12-18 per litre price, giving roughly 34 percent gross margin and cumulative profitability in year 3 to 4. ProMax adds an aseptic filling line, sterile filtration and a lyophiliser for about CNY 11.65 million, carries about CNY 8.15 million of R&D split CNY 5.1 million expensed and CNY 3.05 million capitalised, costs about CNY 163.5 per litre against a $22-32 price, and yields only about 15.9 percent gross margin with breakeven in year 5 to 6. Volume ramps are stated (Mini 1,000 then 5,000 then 15,000 then 30,000 litres; ProMax 200 then 1,000 then 3,000 then 8,000), and the whole budget is downloadable as two PDFs. The regulatory path is the most detailed of any team in this group and is clearly researched rather than guessed: ordinary non-special-use cosmetic filing with NMPA plus a CMA-certified safety assessment for a new cosmetic ingredient and a three-year post-market monitoring period, versus provincial Class II contact-wound-dressing registration requiring ISO 13485, 100,000-class cleanrooms, GB/T 16886 biocompatibility and a clinical evaluation route, with the deliberate choice of the equivalent-product comparison pathway to avoid human trials. They identify the specific trap that cosmetic test reports cannot be reused for device registration and design around it by running both safety programmes in parallel, and cite Giant Biogene and Fu Erjia as real companies that use the shared-campus, separated-workshop model they intend to copy. Market sizing is more careful than usual, with Frost and Sullivan figures for both markets, stated percentage assumptions for SAM, and a SOM expressed as a penetration range tied to winning 10-15 recurring B2B accounts or 2-3 licensed device partners. Now the blunt part. There is no registered entity, no funding, no incubator place, no signed letter of intent and no patent filed, only a stated plan to file three categories of patents before any external collaboration. More seriously, the competitive-efficacy section blurs sources: head-to-head performance claims against Komfymed's recombinant collagen dressing, and a 65-patient trial where MAP hydrogel healed wounds in 5.7 days versus 7.3 for rhEGF, read as literature values for mussel adhesive protein generally rather than data the team generated, yet are written as 'our advantage'. A reader should treat those numbers as borrowed benchmarks. Their own SWOT is candid about this, listing an absent intended use, no confirmed device classification, no design controls, no risk-management file, no biocompatibility package and no clinical evidence strategy. Continuation is a licensing-and-supply intent built on a correct strategic insight (cash from the fast cosmetic line funds the slow medical line), but the entity that would execute it does not yet exist.","partners":["Dr. Dongfeng Wang, Deputy Chief Physician, Wuhan Petrochemical Hospital (clinical wound care)","Mr. Yanxuan Song, medical device engineer and founder of Guangzhou Baiyoubai Tech-Beauty Chain (clinic operations and procurement)","Dr. Shengbo Wu (synthetic biology)","Mr. Jiujiang Zhang, CIRS Group Medical Devices Division (Class II and III regulatory affairs)","Mr. Xiaofei Ji, medical device development and quality systems expert (value-chain positioning)","SnapGene and Tsingke (listed sponsors)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6199/wiki/entrepreneurship/figure-11.avif","caption":"Financial planning for TyroFix Mini: capex, R&D spend, CNY 71 per litre production cost and the volume ramp to 30,000 litres by year five","credit":"Team SUIS-SFLS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6199/wiki/entrepreneurship/figure-12.avif","caption":"Financial planning for TyroFix ProMax, the Class II medical line, showing the lower 15.9 percent gross margin and later breakeven","credit":"Team SUIS-SFLS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6199/wiki/entrepreneurship/figure-9.avif","caption":"Business model canvas for the two-line B2B raw-material supply model","credit":"Team SUIS-SFLS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6199/wiki/entrepreneurship/figure-10.avif","caption":"Thirty-six-month milestone plan across five phases, from DBTL cycles to first B2B supply agreements","credit":"Team SUIS-SFLS, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Adopt their repositioning discipline: ask industry experts where a student-scale team actually belongs in the value chain, and be willing to drop the finished product for an upstream raw material plus characterisation and quality documentation, which is a deliverable a small lab can genuinely own. Then publish the budget as a downloadable model with capex, cost per unit, price, gross margin and breakeven year, so the plan can be criticised on its arithmetic rather than its adjectives.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/suis-sfls/","https://2026.igem.wiki/suis-sfls/entrepreneurship/","https://2026.igem.wiki/suis-sfls/human-practices/"],"rank":7},"6214":{"team":"HongKong-HS","id":"6214","section":"High School","country":"Hong Kong","village":"Diagnostics","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-hs/","projectTitle":"AmpliRen - a urine-based home screening kit concept for chronic kidney disease using urinary miRNA and hybridisation chain reaction","projectTitle_zh":"AmpliRen——以尿液 miRNA 與雜交鏈反應建構的慢性腎臟病居家篩檢套組概念","tagline":"Early signals. Made visible. A small sample telling a bigger story.","tagline_zh":"及早的訊號，看得見的呈現。一份小小的檢體，說出更大的故事。","summary":"HongKong-HS is a five-school joint team (Wah Yan College Kowloon, Pope Paul VI College, C&MA Sun Kei Secondary School, Tsung Tsin Christian Academy, St. Paul's School Lam Tin) tackling chronic kidney disease, which affects roughly 788 million adults worldwide, has risen past 405,000 recorded adult cases in Hong Kong, and is usually caught only at stage 3-5 because creatinine-based eGFR does not move until about half of kidney function is gone. AmpliRen detects two urinary microRNAs - miR-21-5p for fibrosis severity and miR-192-5p as an early warning, together reported at 89% sensitivity and 82% specificity - and amplifies the signal enzyme-free at room temperature with hybridisation chain reaction, whose G-rich hairpin loops fold into G-quadruplexes that bind hemin to form a DNAzyme and oxidise TMB into a colour change visible in natural light. The project is a genuine four-cycle engineering story: the team started with toehold switches designed in miRADAR and screened in NUPACK, found EGFP output too weak and invisible, pivoted to HCR, then to G-quadruplex-containing probes, then to hemin/TMB colorimetry. It was nominated for Best Wiki on one of the most ambitious scroll-driven, 3D-visualised wikis in the competition.","summary_zh":"HongKong-HS 是由五校組成的聯隊（九龍華仁書院、保祿六世書院、宣道會鄭榮之中學、崇真書院、藍田聖保祿學校），處理的是慢性腎臟病：全球約有 7.88 億成人受影響，香港的成人紀錄病例已超過 405,000 例，而由於基於肌酸酐的 eGFR 要等到腎功能大約失去一半才會變動，病情通常要到第 3 至 5 期才被發現。AmpliRen 偵測兩種尿液 microRNA——miR-21-5p 反映纖維化嚴重度，miR-192-5p 作為早期警訊，兩者合併的報告數據為靈敏度 89%、專一性 82%——並以雜交鏈反應（HCR）在室溫下不用酵素放大訊號；其富含 G 的髮夾環會折疊成 G-四聯體，結合血基質（hemin）形成 DNAzyme，氧化 TMB 產生在自然光下即可看見的顏色變化。這個專題是一段貨真價實、歷經四輪的工程故事：團隊一開始用 miRADAR 設計、在 NUPACK 中篩選 toehold switch，發現 EGFP 的輸出太弱、看不見，轉而改用 HCR，再改用含 G-四聯體的探針，最後改成 hemin/TMB 比色。它以本屆最具野心的捲動敘事、3D 視覺化 wiki 之一獲最佳 wiki 提名。","awards":["Top 10 (High School)","Best Wiki — Nominee (High School)","Best Village Project — Nominee (Infectious Diseases / Therapeutics / Diagnostics / Oncology)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"The dry lab is nucleic-acid thermodynamics rather than protein design, and it is used as a hard screen at every cycle. Candidate toehold switches were generated with miRADAR, the design tool released by the 2024 Wageningen iGEM team - a deliberate reuse of another team's software rather than reinventing it - producing 9 candidates for miR-21-5p and 7 for miR-192-5p. Every candidate was then simulated in NUPACK (RNA mode, 37 C, default model options and algorithm settings, 1 uM toehold and 3 uM miRNA to keep the trigger in excess) and scored against five explicit criteria: bound-toehold equilibrium concentration, absence of unintended secondary structure downstream of the ribosome binding site (which would block the ribosome and cause false negatives), hybrid minimum free energy (HMFE) versus toehold minimum free energy (TMFE) so that the bound state is thermodynamically favoured and the switch does not prefer to dimerise with another switch, C-G content for hairpin stability, and RBS location. They tabulated the HMFE-TMFE difference for every candidate in kcal/mol and read NUPACK's base-pair equilibrium-probability plots to check that loop-maintaining base pairs drop to low probability on target binding so the switch can fully linearise - selecting toeholds 6 and 7 for miR-192-5p and 7 and 9 for miR-21-5p. The same NUPACK workflow was then reapplied to HCR: H1/H2 hairpin pairs (the miR-21-5p pair adopted from Miao et al. 2016, the miR-192-5p pair built in house) were simulated at 37 C with 1 uM hairpin and 3 uM miRNA, confirming long H1-H2 polymer formation with target but also predicting unintended H1-H2 binding in the absence of target - a background-leakage problem the model found before the gel did. Minimum-free-energy structures were computed for H1 alone, H2 alone, H1+miRNA and the full miRNA-H1-H2 complex for both targets. In Cycle 4, double-loop G4H1/G4H2 hairpins based on Peng et al. (2022) had InG4 G-quadruplex motifs inserted into the loops, and NUPACK was used to confirm both complex formation and that the InG4 sequences sit in the loops where they can fold and leave the polymer after HCR. The two probe pairs were deliberately given different geometries - longer stems and smaller loops for miR-192-5p, shorter stems and larger loops for miR-21-5p.","frameworks_zh":"乾實驗做的是核酸熱力學、而非蛋白質設計，而且在每一輪都被當成硬性篩選使用。候選 toehold switch 以 miRADAR 產生，那是 2024 年 Wageningen iGEM 隊伍釋出的設計工具——刻意重複利用別隊的軟體、而不是重新造一次輪子——為 miR-21-5p 產出 9 個候選、為 miR-192-5p 產出 7 個。每個候選接著在 NUPACK 中模擬（RNA 模式、37 C、預設模型選項與演算法設定，toehold 1 uM、miRNA 3 uM 以維持觸發端過量），並依五項明確標準評分：已結合 toehold 的平衡濃度、核糖體結合位下游是否沒有非預期的二級結構（若有會阻擋核糖體並造成偽陰性）、雜合最小自由能（HMFE）與 toehold 最小自由能（TMFE）的對比（使結合態在熱力學上占優，且開關不會偏好與另一個開關形成雙體）、維持髮夾穩定的 C-G 含量，以及 RBS 的位置。他們把每個候選的 HMFE-TMFE 差值以 kcal/mol 列表，並閱讀 NUPACK 的鹼基配對平衡機率圖，確認在結合標的後維持環狀結構的鹼基配對機率會降到很低，使開關能完全線性化——最後為 miR-192-5p 選定 toehold 6 與 7、為 miR-21-5p 選定 7 與 9。同一套 NUPACK 流程之後再套用到 HCR：H1/H2 髮夾對（miR-21-5p 那一對取自 Miao 等人 2016 年的研究，miR-192-5p 那一對則自行建構）在 37 C、髮夾 1 uM、miRNA 3 uM 下模擬，確認在有標的時會形成長的 H1-H2 聚合物，但也預測在沒有標的時 H1 與 H2 會發生非預期的結合——這個背景洩漏問題，是模型比膠片更早發現的。兩個標的都計算了 H1 單獨、H2 單獨、H1+miRNA 以及完整 miRNA-H1-H2 複合物的最小自由能結構。在第四輪，他們依 Peng 等人（2022）設計的雙環 G4H1/G4H2 髮夾把 InG4 這種 G-四聯體基序插入環中，並用 NUPACK 確認複合物會形成、以及 InG4 序列確實位在環上，使其能折疊並在 HCR 之後離開聚合物。兩對探針被刻意賦予不同的幾何形狀——miR-192-5p 用較長的莖與較小的環，miR-21-5p 則用較短的莖與較大的環。","dataviz":"The wiki itself is the data-visualisation achievement and is why it was nominated for Best Wiki. The landing page is a scroll-driven narrative that zooms from two kidneys, through tissue and the filtration barrier, down to the molecular signal, with each stage labelled as an illustrative view rather than clinical eGFR categories. The HCR mechanism is animated across four scroll states - two locked hairpins, target binding and toehold opening, chain growth into a double-stranded nanowire, then potassium-dependent G-quadruplex folding with hemin - so a reader physically watches the amplification cascade instead of reading a paragraph about it. Epidemiology is presented as individually sourced stat cards, each carrying its own population, year and citation (788 million adults globally, GBD 2023/The Lancet 2025; 87% unaware, CDC 2026 NHANES 2021-2023; 405,833 Hong Kong adult cases 2021, Yue et al.; 2,571 on the transplant waiting list; 1,226 registered deaths in 2024) with an explicit note that one figure is a recorded-case count, not a current population estimate. The kit concept is presented as an interactive unboxing with three fitted compartments and a pannable close-up, and the team labels it openly as AI-assisted imagery and animation made with Higgsfield and as a research concept, not a validated diagnostic product. The engineering page is built as a clickable 22-note timeline across four Design-Build-Test-Learn cycles. Every figure carries a full descriptive caption and alt text.","dataviz_zh":"這份 wiki 本身就是資料視覺化上的成就，也是它獲最佳 wiki 提名的原因。首頁是一段捲動驅動的敘事，從兩顆腎臟一路放大穿過組織與過濾屏障、下探到分子訊號，每個階段都標註為示意性的呈現、而非臨床 eGFR 分期。HCR 的機制以四個捲動狀態做成動畫——兩個鎖住的髮夾、標的結合並打開 toehold、鏈成長為雙股奈米線，然後是依賴鉀離子的 G-四聯體折疊與 hemin 結合——讓讀者實際看著整段放大串聯反應發生，而不是讀一段文字描述。流行病學以逐項標註來源的數據卡呈現，每張卡都帶自己的族群、年份與引用（全球 7.88 億成人，GBD 2023／The Lancet 2025；87% 不知情，CDC 2026，NHANES 2021-2023；香港 2021 年成人病例 405,833，Yue 等人；2,571 人在移植等候名單上；2024 年登錄死亡 1,226 人），並明確註明其中一個數字是紀錄病例數、不是當前的族群估計值。套組概念以互動式開箱呈現，內有三個嵌合的隔間與可平移的特寫，團隊也公開標註那是用 Higgsfield 製作的 AI 輔助圖像與動畫，且屬研究概念、不是經驗證的診斷產品。工程頁面做成一條可點擊的 22 則註記時間軸，橫跨四輪 Design-Build-Test-Learn 循環。每張圖都附完整的敘述性圖說與替代文字。","datascience":"Analysis is modest in volume but correctly specified. Cell-free EGFP expression was compared with and without target miRNA across five repeats against both positive controls (pET-14b-EGFP with no toehold) and no-plasmid negative controls, read on a fluorometer at 488 nm excitation and 507-513 nm emission, with significance tested by one-sample t-test on fold change; the honest outcome was that miR-21 candidates showed no significant difference, miR-192-5p-6 was significant but minimal at 1.03-fold, and miR-192-5p-7 showed a more pronounced 1.51-fold increase that did not reach significance - and they reported that rather than spin it. ThT fluorescence and hemin/TMB colorimetric assays were analysed by one-way ANOVA with Dunnett post-hoc against the 0 pM control: miR-21 gave significant signal at 100 pM, 10 nM and 100 nM (n=3, p<0.001), while miR-192 was significant at 100 nM (p=0.01 and p=0.002) but also, unexpectedly, significantly lower than control at 1 nM - an anomaly they diagnosed as free miR-192-5p G4H1 self-folding into a G-quadruplex and producing colour without target, and then turned into a concrete future-work list (splitting the G4, stabilising the hairpin stem, tuning C-G/A-T content, optimising toehold length). Plasmid work was confirmed by Sanger sequencing and miniprep A260/280 purity, and gel evidence was escalated from agarose to PAGE when agarose smearing proved inconclusive.","datascience_zh":"分析在量上不多，但規格設定正確。無細胞的 EGFP 表現在有無標的 miRNA 兩種條件下各做五次重複比較，並同時對照正對照（pET-14b-EGFP、不含 toehold）與無質體的負對照，以螢光儀在激發 488 nm、發射 507-513 nm 下讀取，並以單樣本 t 檢定檢驗倍數變化的顯著性；誠實的結果是 miR-21 的候選沒有顯著差異，miR-192-5p-6 雖達顯著但幅度極小（1.03 倍），而 miR-192-5p-7 顯示較明顯的 1.51 倍上升卻未達顯著——他們照實報告，沒有美化。ThT 螢光與 hemin/TMB 比色試驗以單因子 ANOVA 搭配 Dunnett 事後檢定、對照 0 pM 控制組分析：miR-21 在 100 pM、10 nM 與 100 nM 都有顯著訊號（n=3，p<0.001），miR-192 則在 100 nM 顯著（p=0.01 與 p=0.002），但也出現意料之外的結果——在 1 nM 時顯著低於控制組；他們診斷這個異常是游離的 miR-192-5p G4H1 自行折疊成 G-四聯體、在沒有標的時就產生顏色，並把它轉化成一份具體的後續工作清單（拆分 G4、穩定髮夾莖部、調整 C-G/A-T 含量、最佳化 toehold 長度）。質體工作以 Sanger 定序與 miniprep 的 A260/280 純度確認，膠片證據則在瓊膠出現拖尾、結果不明確時升級為 PAGE。","software":"No standalone software or hardware was released. The dry lab is the application of existing tools - NUPACK for thermodynamic simulation and another iGEM team's miRADAR for candidate generation - plus a bespoke wiki front end. Two toehold switch candidates per target were cloned into pET-14b-EGFP using XbaI and NdeI sites between the T7 promoter and the EGFP reporter and verified by Sanger sequencing, and an mCherry colorimetric variant was in progress when the season ended.","software_zh":"沒有釋出獨立的軟體或硬體。乾實驗是既有工具的應用——以 NUPACK 做熱力學模擬、以另一支 iGEM 隊伍的 miRADAR 產生候選——再加上一個訂製的 wiki 前端。每個標的有兩個 toehold switch 候選，以 XbaI 與 NdeI 位點選殖進 pET-14b-EGFP、置於 T7 啟動子與 EGFP 報告基因之間，並以 Sanger 定序確認；一個 mCherry 比色版本在賽季結束時仍在進行中。","stack":["NUPACK","miRADAR (Wageningen iGEM 2024)","one-way ANOVA with Dunnett post-hoc","one-sample t-test","Sanger sequencing","cell-free expression + fluorometry","microplate reader","PAGE and agarose gel electrophoresis","ThT fluorescence assay","hemin / TMB G-quadruplex DNAzyme colorimetry","Higgsfield (AI-assisted concept imagery)","scroll-driven 3D web visualisation"],"techniques":["HMFE vs TMFE thermodynamic ranking of toehold candidates","equilibrium base-pair probability inspection to verify hairpin linearisation on target binding","in-silico prediction of background leakage (unintended H1-H2 binding without target) before bench testing","MFE structure comparison across free hairpin, hairpin+target and full ternary complex","loop-position verification for inserted G-quadruplex motifs","fold-change analysis against both positive and no-plasmid negative controls","escalating gel resolution (agarose to PAGE) when a result is inconclusive","diagnosing a statistically anomalous result as probe self-folding and converting it into a redesign list"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education reached over 800 participants and was built on three stated principles - a Cascading Peer-Educator Model, Gamified Educational Experiences, and Reflective Learning. The peer-educator model is the distinctive one: rather than only teaching end-learners, they trained non-iGEM junior-form Science Team members as Student Facilitators with both content and facilitation skills, then had those facilitators independently run workshops for their schoolmates, and published a training guide for holding a secondary school workshop plus a CKD brochure for older adults so the materials outlive the team. Activities were designed per audience and deliberately low-cost and replicable: at Salesian Yip Hon Millennium Primary School's STEAM Day (about 600 students and parents) they ran a micropipette drip-art station, a magnetic miRNA detection game in which only the target miRNA card hides a magnet so it alone sticks to a paper toehold-switch model, and a health-knowledge ping-pong ball toss into an illustrated face; at Shek Lei Catholic Primary School, strawberry DNA extraction delivered entirely in Cantonese with terms simplified ('cell walls' became 'the surface of the strawberry') and a 'Blood Vessel Clearing Game' using paper, drawing supplies and a hand-made wooden vessel model, with students drawing their own food items and testing whether they fit through. Secondary outreach covered St. Paul's School (Lam Tin) with 169 participants and Hoi Ping Chamber of Commerce Secondary School with 19, using a micropipetting precision-dyeing challenge and a 'Detective on Call' online DNA fingerprinting game. They also ran a card game for community-centre children including ethnic-minority children, an elderly workshop, a Hong Kong Joint Secondary Schools Science Fair booth, and regional middle-school outreach in the Greater Bay Area. Reflection was built in with structured worksheets, exit cards and open Q&A, and every activity records what they changed next - after noticing their terminology was too advanced for young children they switched to plainer language, more gestures and more Cantonese, and they adapted in real time when a student asked 'Why strawberries? Why not apples?' by adding an impromptu discussion.","publicEngagement_zh":"教育工作觸及超過 800 位參與者，建立在三項明示的原則上——階梯式同儕教育者模式、遊戲化的教育體驗，以及反思式學習。同儕教育者模式是最特別的一項：他們不只教最終學習者，而是把非 iGEM 的初中科學隊成員訓練成學生輔導員，同時傳授內容與帶領技巧，再讓這些輔導員自行為同校同學舉辦工作坊；他們並公開了一份中學工作坊的帶領指南與一本給長者的慢性腎臟病手冊，使材料能在團隊之後繼續存在。活動依對象設計，刻意低成本且可複製：在慈幼葉漢千禧小學的 STEAM 日（約 600 位學生與家長）他們設了微量移液器滴畫站、一個磁性 miRNA 偵測遊戲（只有標的 miRNA 卡片裡藏有磁鐵，因此只有它會黏上紙做的 toehold switch 模型），以及把健康知識乒乓球投進繪製臉孔的投擲遊戲；在石籬天主教小學，草莓 DNA 萃取全程以粵語進行、術語也簡化（「細胞壁」改成「草莓的表面」），另有一個用紙、繪圖用品與手工木製血管模型做的「清血管遊戲」，讓學生自己畫食物、再測試它們能不能通過。中學端的科普涵蓋藍田聖保祿學校 169 位參與者與海壩商會中學 19 位，使用微量移液精準染色挑戰與「Detective on Call」線上 DNA 指紋遊戲。他們也為社區中心的兒童（包括少數族裔兒童）辦了卡牌遊戲、辦了長者工作坊、在香港聯校科學展覽設攤，並在大灣區做了區域性的中學科普。反思被制度化為結構式學習單、離場卡與開放問答，每項活動都記錄下一次改了什麼——在發現自己的術語對幼童太進階後，他們改用更淺白的語言、更多手勢與更多粵語；當一位學生問「為什麼是草莓？為什麼不是蘋果？」時，他們當場加入一段即興討論來應對。","ihp":"IHP was organised as four parallel two-way feedback loops (Public, Healthcare, Science, Industry) feeding both the wet lab and the education team, structured over three stages (Understanding the Problem, Identifying the Needs, Develop & Co-design) and processed through a four-step cycle they call LIVP (Locate, Iterate, Validate, Propose). The design changes are traceable to named people. Professor Chan Ting Fung (RNA biology) assessed the toehold-switch limitations and identified HCR as the alternative worth trying for signal amplification - the single biggest pivot in the project - and later recommended expanding the H1/H2 sequence design space to mask the ribosome binding site to eliminate background leakage, noted that lithium interference in urine is negligible, and told them to test sodium's effect on the DNAzyme experimentally. Professor Szeto Cheuk Chun (Head of Medicine and Therapeutics, CUHK, whose research is urinary biomarkers) confirmed miRNA as near-ideal for urine because of its stability, told them to run miR-21-5p and miR-192-5p in parallel as a complementary test (which is why the kit has two detection pathways and a six-well chamber), said biomarkers are detectable in urine that has not been high-speed centrifuged so they could drop centrifugation from the workflow, warned that urinary chromogens may interfere with a visible colour readout, set a user-experience target of roughly half an hour to result, and endorsed a colour change readable under natural light - which is precisely why the team ended up on G4/hemin colorimetry rather than ThT fluorescence, since ThT needs UV excitation and a fluorescence reader. Professor Ma Ming Yao established that the kit must be positioned as a screening flag prompting medical follow-up, never a diagnosis, and that false positives and negatives must be managed responsibly, and that high-risk patients are the target - which reshaped how the whole wiki speaks about the product and prompted a community education workshop for the elderly. A medical laboratory technologist insisted on a clear, reasonable cut-off concentration for the target miRNA, rigorous quality control, timely sample processing, and a larger sample size for credibility, which pushed the team towards a multi-target design. E-SENSE Innovation & Technology Limited said clinicians will only recommend a home test backed by real-world clinical data with low false-positive and false-negative rates, which pushed the wet lab to run the cell-free EGFP validation and the HCR sensitivity series. Public input was quantified: a street interview of 137 people and an online survey of 283 found 52% had never heard of CKD or diabetic kidney disease and only 28% had heard of both, 60% did not know or were unsure that early kidney disease can be symptomless, and 63.2% of street respondents cited absence of symptoms as their reason for not getting screened.","ihp_zh":"IHP 組織成四條並行的雙向回饋迴路（公眾、醫療、科學、產業），同時回饋到濕實驗與教育組，結構上分三個階段（理解問題、界定需求、開發與共同設計），並透過他們稱為 LIVP（Locate、Iterate、Validate、Propose）的四步循環處理。設計上的改動都可追溯到具名的人。陳廷鋒教授（RNA 生物學）評估了 toehold switch 的限制，並指出 HCR 是值得一試的訊號放大替代方案——這是整個專題最大的一次轉向——之後又建議擴大 H1/H2 的序列設計空間以遮蔽核糖體結合位、消除背景洩漏，並指出尿液中鋰的干擾可忽略，要他們以實驗檢驗鈉對 DNAzyme 的影響。司徒卓俊教授（香港中文大學內科及藥物治療學系主任，研究領域為尿液生物標記）確認 miRNA 因其穩定性而近乎是尿液檢測的理想對象，要他們把 miR-21-5p 與 miR-192-5p 並行作為互補檢測（這就是套組有兩條偵測路徑與六孔反應室的原因），指出生物標記在未經高速離心的尿液中仍可偵測、因此可以把離心從流程中去掉，並警告尿中的色素可能干擾可見光的顏色讀取，另訂下約半小時內出結果的使用體驗目標，並支持採用自然光下即可判讀的顏色變化——這正是團隊最終走向 G4/hemin 比色、而非 ThT 螢光的原因，因為 ThT 需要紫外激發與螢光讀取儀。馬明耀教授確立了這套套組必須定位為提示就醫追蹤的篩檢旗標、絕不是診斷，偽陽性與偽陰性必須負責任地管理，且目標對象是高風險患者——這重塑了整個 wiki 談論產品的方式，也促成了一場為長者舉辦的社區教育工作坊。一位醫務檢驗師堅持標的 miRNA 必須有清楚、合理的判讀切點、嚴謹的品質管制、及時的檢體處理，以及更大的樣本數以取得可信度，這推動團隊走向多標的設計。E-SENSE Innovation & Technology Limited 則表示，臨床醫師只會推薦有真實世界臨床數據支撐、且偽陽性與偽陰性率都低的居家檢測，這推動濕實驗去做無細胞 EGFP 驗證與 HCR 的靈敏度系列實驗。公眾意見也有量化：街訪 137 人與線上問卷 283 份顯示，52% 從未聽過慢性腎臟病或糖尿病腎病變、只有 28% 兩者都聽過，60% 不知道或不確定早期腎病可能完全沒有症狀，而街訪受訪者中有 63.2% 把沒有症狀列為自己不去篩檢的理由。","realWorld":"The intended product is an at-home urine screening kit, costed against a system where each Hong Kong dialysis patient runs about HKD 50,000 per year and where confirming CKD currently needs repeat clinic visits over a three-month window because uACR varies by 30% or more day to day and cystatin C is several times the price of creatinine and rarely reimbursed. Every design decision is pulled towards deployability: urine rather than blood, no centrifuge, enzyme-free isothermal amplification at room temperature, and a colour change readable in natural light without any instrument. The team is consistently careful about regulatory and clinical positioning - the kit is repeatedly described as a screening flag that prompts follow-up and complements, rather than replaces, eGFR and uACR, and the kit visualisation is explicitly captioned as a research concept, not a validated diagnostic product. What is not present on the wiki is a business model, pricing, manufacturing plan or named regulatory pathway; industry engagement with E-SENSE is framed around clinical credibility and usability requirements rather than commercialisation, and the honest gap they name is the need for real-world paired clinical data before a home device is justified.","realWorld_zh":"預期產品是一套居家尿液篩檢套組，其成本論證放在這樣的制度背景下：香港每位洗腎病人每年約需 50,000 港元，而目前要確診慢性腎臟病需要在三個月內多次回診，因為 uACR 的日間變異達 30% 以上，而 cystatin C 的價格是肌酸酐的數倍且很少獲得給付。每個設計決策都被推向可部署性：用尿液而非血液、不需離心、在室溫下不用酵素的恆溫放大，以及不需任何儀器、在自然光下即可判讀的顏色變化。團隊在法規與臨床定位上始終謹慎——套組被反覆描述為提示追蹤的篩檢旗標，是 eGFR 與 uACR 的補充、而非取代，套組的視覺呈現也明確標註為研究概念、不是經驗證的診斷產品。wiki 上沒有的是商業模式、定價、製造計畫或指名的法規路徑；與 E-SENSE 的產業交流也是圍繞臨床可信度與可用性要求、而非商業化，而他們自己點名的誠實缺口是：在居家裝置站得住腳之前，仍需要真實世界的配對臨床資料。","partners":["Professor Szeto Cheuk Chun, Chinese University of Hong Kong (urinary biomarkers)","Professor Chan Ting Fung (RNA biology)","Professor Ma Ming Yao (nephrologist)","Professor Tang Chi Wai, Sydney (nephrologist)","Dr. Au Wing Han (nephrologist)","E-SENSE Innovation & Technology Limited","a clinical medical laboratory technologist","Salesian Yip Hon Millennium Primary School","Shek Lei Catholic Primary School","St. Paul's School (Lam Tin)","Hoi Ping Chamber of Commerce Secondary School","Wageningen iGEM 2024 (miRADAR software reused)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6214/wiki/project/engineering/fig-10-complex-formation-of-toehold-7-for-mir-192-5p-nupack.avif","caption":"NUPACK equilibrium complex-formation analysis for toehold 7 against miR-192-5p; the red bars show the active toehold-miRNA complex concentration used to rank candidates alongside the HMFE-versus-TMFE comparison.","caption_zh":"以 NUPACK 分析 toehold 7 對 miR-192-5p 的平衡態複合物生成；紅色長條顯示有活性的 toehold-miRNA 複合物濃度，這與 HMFE 對 TMFE 的比較一併用來為候選排序。","credit":"Team HongKong-HS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6214/wiki/project/engineering/fig-46-mirna-h1-h2-complex.avif","caption":"Predicted minimum-free-energy structure of the miR-192-5p-H1-H2 hybridisation chain reaction complex, used to verify polymer formation and that the inserted G-quadruplex motifs sit in the hairpin loops.","caption_zh":"miR-192-5p-H1-H2 雜交鏈反應複合物的預測最小自由能結構，用來確認聚合物會形成，以及插入的 G-四聯體基序確實位在髮夾環上。","credit":"Team HongKong-HS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6214/wiki/project/results/hcr/results-fig18-coloured-result-of-h1-h2-g-quadruplex-with-hemin-and-tmbs.avif","caption":"The naked-eye readout the whole project was redesigned to reach: HCR products with G-quadruplex/hemin DNAzyme oxidising TMB across a range of miR-21 and miR-192 concentrations, stopped with sulphuric acid and read at 450 nm.","caption_zh":"整個專題為之重新設計、最終要達到的肉眼讀數：HCR 產物上的 G-四聯體/hemin DNAzyme 在一系列 miR-21 與 miR-192 濃度下氧化 TMB，以硫酸終止反應後於 450 nm 讀取。","credit":"Team HongKong-HS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6214/wiki/education/figure-5.avif","caption":"A primary student using the team's magnetic toehold-switch model to simulate miRNA detection - only the target miRNA card contains a hidden magnet, so molecular specificity becomes something a child can feel.","caption_zh":"一位小學生用團隊的磁性 toehold switch 模型模擬 miRNA 偵測——只有標的 miRNA 卡片裡藏著磁鐵，於是分子專一性變成一個小孩摸得到的東西。","credit":"Team HongKong-HS, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Two things to steal. First, NUPACK plus a reused iGEM software tool (Wageningen's miRADAR) is a complete, free, high-school-feasible dry lab: HongKong-HS ranked 16 candidate switches on explicit thermodynamic criteria (HMFE vs TMFE, downstream secondary structure blocking the RBS, equilibrium base-pair probability) and predicted the background-leakage failure mode before the gel showed it. Second, their wiki proves that the best data visualisation is mechanism animation plus per-figure provenance - every statistic carries its own population, year and source, and the AI-generated product imagery is labelled as such, which is exactly the standard a research centre's outputs should hold itself to.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"有兩點值得借走。第一，NUPACK 再加上一個重複利用的 iGEM 軟體工具（Wageningen 的 miRADAR）就構成一套完整、免費、高中可行的乾實驗：HongKong-HS 依明確的熱力學標準（HMFE 對 TMFE、下游二級結構是否遮蔽 RBS、平衡態鹼基配對機率）為 16 個候選開關排序，並在膠片顯示之前就預測出背景洩漏這種失效模式。第二，他們的 wiki 證明最好的資料視覺化就是機制動畫加上每張圖各自的出處——每一項統計數據都附上自己的族群、年份與來源，AI 生成的產品圖也如實標註，而這正是一個研究中心的產出應該自我要求的標準。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-hs/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-hs/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-hs/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-hs/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-hs/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-hs/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-hs/safety","https://2026.igem.wiki/hongkong-hs/contribution","https://api.igem.org/v1/teams/6214"],"rank":84},"6219":{"team":"XJTLU-Software","id":"6219","section":"Undergrad","country":"China","village":"Software & AI","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-software/","projectTitle":"AMPilot","tagline":"An AI research workbench for antimicrobial peptide design, where the application owns the research record and the model only ever receives a request.","summary":"AMPilot is a live, hosted AI-assisted research workbench for antimicrobial peptide design, built around the argument that a conversation is an entry point but the research has to live in inspectable materials. Sources stay linked to their records, candidate sequences stay in files, and documents remain editable after the conversation moves on, across twelve implemented research stages grouped into five phases from framing a question to a bench handoff. The team wrote their own agent harness rather than using LangChain, LlamaIndex, AutoGen, DSPy or LiteLLM, specifically so the application rather than a framework owns the saved research state and the policy that turns it into model context, and so that a model proposal becomes an executable action only through a validated tool boundary. The sequence generator, TC-SRF, adapts the ProtFlow latent flow-matching pipeline with scientific-text conditioning via cross-attention and adaptive normalisation plus a constraint-aware decoder that refuses a residue unless some allowed suffix can still satisfy the stated length, charge and composition contract. Validation includes a 16-participant randomised AB/BA crossover user study, which is the most rigorous usability evidence any iGEM software team produced this year.","awards":["Best Software & AI Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A Vue frontend rendering documents, files, questions and progress from server state, over a Python backend (Python 3.11, Node.js 22.12+) whose two named components are StudioRunner, which reads the workspace, runs the engine and reconciles delivery, and CompatibleEngine, which owns the inner model and tool loop and sends ordinary JSON over HTTP via httpx. Persistent state is SQLite with WAL, foreign-key checks and a busy timeout, holding tasks, sources, attachments, research items, questions, decisions and versioned documents, with transactions and version checks so a stale edit cannot silently overwrite a newer document. There are three deliberately separated entry points: five public scientific API routes that need no account, the authenticated hosted workbench (which locks the engine to the self-developed compatible path), and a local MCP bridge started with 'npm run mcp' that accepts a loopback backend and exposes a filtered read-only tool subset, with generation, evaluation, document writing and construct creation excluded by a mutating-tool filter. The team is explicit about what 'self-developed' does and does not mean: the dependency manifest has no agent framework, but ordinary libraries, external language models and scientific packages remain dependencies, and using an SDK would not inherently surrender control of message history; an optional Codex app-server adapter exists but delegates its inner runtime and is kept as a separate, non-conflated path. Licence Apache-2.0, with the TC-SRF-AMP generator MIT-licensed and carrying its own upstream attribution. Live at https://ampilotlab.com (Guest mode with checkpoints in the browser; API docs at /docs, OpenAPI at /openapi.json); source at https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/xjtlu-software/ampilot, pinned at commit 31c2491 for the wiki.","dataviz":"The workbench presents a sequence workspace where a circular plasmid map and the base-level sequence stay connected to the original GenBank annotations, a public knowledge base with separate entry points into catalogues of sequences, MIC values, literature, drugs, clinical trials and patents, and a progress rail that makes unfinished stages visible. The rail's twelve stages are checked against saved outputs rather than against a conversational claim that a stage is complete, which is the key design idea. The measurement planner uses a typed claim rather than free text: a reading carries its quantity and endpoint, unit and subject, target organism, basis (predicted, observed or inferred), the model and the data it was fitted on, and the conditions and scope within which its interpretation applies, with compatible quantities and units checked at that boundary. Every screenshot on the wiki is captioned with its capture date (17 October 2026), the record shown, and an explicit statement that it illustrates the interface and not a biological outcome or a measured user benefit.","datascience":"Three layers of evidence, all dated and tied to commits. CI: on 2026-10-20 the team retrieved GitLab's job records and JUnit report for pipeline 776168 at commit 1ca9596, with all six jobs (lint, bundle, frontend, backend-rest, backend-science, backend-agent) passing: 2,622 backend tests passed with 43 skipped and 0 failures, plus 153 frontend tests. They then publish exactly what CI skipped and why (7 for a missing curated document index, 24 for an uninstalled clinical library, 2 for a missing research corpus, 2 for the unvendored HemoPI2 program, and so on), stating that the pipeline's fallback permits such skips so a green pipeline is not evidence every scientific model ran, and that a module skipped at collection can stand for more than one uncollected test. A separate fresh local full-suite run on a Mac mini at the same commit gave 2,677 passed, 1 skipped, 0 failed, and the team discloses that one installed regressor's digest differs from the public asset manifest, records both digests, and says the run tests the installed environment rather than certifying byte-identical assets. A local storage microbenchmark measured 400 reads and 400 writes across 8 workers on synthetic data (read 294.1 ops/s at P95 32.47 ms, write 2,895.6 ops/s at P95 4.86 ms, Python 3.11.16, SQLite 3.53.4, Darwin arm64, WAL with synchronous=FULL) and says plainly that this measures storage operations, not simultaneous users or model throughput. The TC-SRF checkpoint was inspected on 19 October 2026 under a restricted CPU load with a matching SHA-256: training step 10,000, best validation total loss 0.1246988252 at step 10,000, zero stale validation evaluations, with the team stating these are stored training state rather than a newly measured score and that they do not prove convergence, recover the loss trajectory or establish validation-set independence. The user study is the standout: 16 participants (8 bioinformatics postgraduates, 8 experimental researchers), each using both a conventional toolchain (PubMed plus web tools plus local scripts) and AMPilot, in a randomised AB/BA crossover with 8 per order, parallel tasks crossed with tools, and at least 48 hours between sessions. Tasks were salt-tolerant short cationic peptides for P. aeruginosa and protease-resistant short amphipathic peptides for MRSA. Results: completion 11/16 conventional vs 15/16 AMPilot; task time 142.5 +/- 28.6 vs 41.2 +/- 37.3 minutes with non-completions assigned the 180-minute cap, a paired reduction of 101.3 minutes (95% CI 81.4-121.2, SEM 9.35); operation and format errors 3.8 +/- 1.2 vs 0.4 +/- 0.5; System Usability Scale 58.2 +/- 9.4 vs 84.5 +/- 6.2. A completers-only sensitivity analysis is reported separately and labelled descriptive rather than paired because the subsets differ. The team states the study supports integration for these tasks and does not establish improved candidate activity, general effectiveness, or a population-wide usability ranking.","software":"The engineering argument is about who owns context, and it is the most interesting one in iGEM 2026. A long research task accumulates source passages, candidate evaluations, document versions and revised decisions; sending every repeated body is wasteful, but replacing them with a fluent model-written summary erases their identity and scope. AMPilot therefore constructs each request from explicit records with a preserved path back to omitted detail, under three stated rules (retention of identifiers, current verdicts and tool order; non-mutation, meaning a request is projected and the saved record is never overwritten; retrieval, meaning the place omitted evidence can be read again is always named). Concretely: the two most recent eligible search responses stay intact while older ones become source indexes only when the replacement is shorter, with a route back via read_source(source_id); the two most recent heavy analysis reads stay whole while older ones are truncated at 400 serialized characters per field without generating a new model-written summary, with a route back via read_research_item(item_id); and when the outer snapshot is rebuilt, revoked decisions move from confirmed_decisions into withdrawn_decisions so a retracted choice stops acting as a requirement while remaining in the audit record. Two loops with two responsibilities: an outer pass reads the workspace and builds the snapshot, while the inner provider loop projects a request-local copy of the message list, streams the response, validates and executes tool calls, matches results to tool-call IDs and appends receipts, with a 32-logical-response budget across a turn (and the honest note that transport retries and evidence-review calls fall outside that count). The tool registry supplies JSON Schema to the model and validates incoming arguments again on the server, refusing unknown tools, invalid arguments and mutations without an active task, and the wiki adds that a valid schema establishes a well-formed request, not a correct scientific conclusion. Delivery reconciliation is the mechanism that most directly addresses LLM failure: after the engine returns, StudioRunner checks promised work against saved outputs and outstanding questions, because 'a fluent closing message is not a delivery receipt', and if a summary fails evidence review after a report was already saved, a deterministic receipt links to the existing work instead of publishing the unchecked summary. Failure handling is designed rather than incidental: a stop records a cancelled task state, supersedes pending proposals, terminates the TC-SRF subprocess and kills it after a grace period, and rejects late publication by checking task status before any workspace write; a version conflict returns a conflict rather than overwriting, so an agent cannot silently restore figures the researcher removed; and an unresolved claim keeps the evidence and stores objections with the draft rather than treating them as approval. Five public API routes expose single functions without a chat thread: POST /api/v1/peptides/evaluate, POST /api/v1/peptides/assay, POST /api/v1/constructs/design (GenBank and SBOL out), GET /api/v1/corpus/search and POST /api/v1/measurements/plan, each row on the wiki carrying its own stated limit (the public corpus route is lexical and explicitly not the local BGE-M3 hybrid retrieval pipeline; the measurement route returns 503 when its bundle is unavailable). Reproducibility is staged honestly: a fresh checkout is described as a starting point rather than every runtime dependency, with predictor and explorer assets fetched through a manifest and SHA-256-checked, local artifacts rebuilt and content-checked, and optional neural services configured separately, with the note that fetched-file checksums and rebuilt-artifact content checks are different guarantees and that not all SQLite or serialized model files are byte-identical across platforms. Data lifecycle is recover-first: Trash stops active work and retains the research, permanent removal requires an exact-record confirmation plus a check that background work has stopped, file cleanup failures stay queued for retry, and the 30-day maintenance command is described as administrator-operated rather than an automatic timer, with the explicit statement that row deletion is not physical-media erasure and that the guide does not promise regulatory compliance. Deployment limits are named too: replicated recovery and a PostgreSQL migration remain work to validate before anyone describes this as distributed high availability. A smaller reusable amp-select package is published separately.","stack":["Python 3.11","Vue","Node.js 22.12+","SQLite (WAL)","httpx","JSON Schema tool contracts","OpenAPI","MCP (local read-only bridge)","ProtFlow latent flow-matching","Hourglass / CHEAP / HPCT protein compression","12-layer transformer velocity field","BGE-M3 hybrid retrieval (local)","GenBank","SBOL","GitLab CI (6 jobs)","Apache-2.0 (AMPilot) / MIT (TC-SRF-AMP)"],"techniques":["application-owned agent harness with bounded logical-response budget","non-destructive request projection with routes back to omitted evidence","delivery reconciliation of promised work against saved outputs","optimistic-concurrency version conflict handling","latent flow matching with text conditioning (cross-attention plus adaptive layer normalisation)","condition-consistency auxiliary loss","constraint-aware look-ahead decoding over length, charge, composition and fixed positions","typed measurement claims with unit and quantity compatibility checking","lexical and semantic (BGE-M3 hybrid) literature retrieval with provenance","study-conditioned measurement planning","randomised AB/BA crossover user study with paired analysis and 95% CIs","System Usability Scale measurement","asset-manifest checksum verification"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education is organised as three pathways (observe and explain; design and test; critique and deliberate) joined by adaptation and a shared foundation in synthetic biology and engineering thinking, reaching 6 learner groups, over 300 participants, 8 or more organisations and institutions, and 15 or more activities. The plan was built from expert advice before delivery rather than after: the team took the question of how to help people with very different backgrounds find their own way in to Dr Justin Fendos, trained at the Yale Teaching Center and founding director of the Dongseo Scientific Teaching Center in South Korea, across two visits, and shaped the plan around how he adapts materials to a syllabus and to a learner's stage. The stated aim was to teach the ideas behind synthetic biology even where they extend beyond AMPilot itself.","ihp":"The guiding image is a ship built inside a glass bottle: it may have beautiful sails and never know whether it can withstand real wind. The team's framework insists software teams should not move from idea to implementation, but should ground the idea in social reality, narrow it to a real bottleneck, translate that into a scope, and only then develop along two parallel tracks of fitting real practice and learning to act responsibly. Stakeholders deliberately spanned clinical medicine, infection and antimicrobial resistance research, environmental science and One Health, and experimental AMP work, grouped by principal contribution and engaged at every stage rather than in one round of interviews. A respiratory physician with over ten years of clinical experience at Nanjing Brain Hospital, including severe respiratory infection and respiratory failure, and a documented case at a hospital in Wuhu, Anhui where a patient acquired a resistant infection, anchored the clinical reality. Environmental and One Health input then widened the frame from hospital treatment to the pathways by which antibiotics, resistant bacteria and resistance genes circulate, and the team records the resulting complication honestly: pollution sources, microbial communities and detection capacity vary, and no single indicator can fully describe the risk. The 16-participant crossover study is itself an integrated human practices output, run by the HP team and reported on the software page with its design, its confidence intervals and its stated limits.","realWorld":"The problem is anchored in The Lancet's 2024 global burden estimate: 4.71 million deaths associated with bacterial antimicrobial resistance in 2021, 1.14 million attributable to it, and a reference-scenario projection of roughly 1.91 million attributable deaths annually by 2050, with knock-on effects on surgery and cancer care that depend on effective infection control. The named audiences are AMP researchers at universities and research institutions, synthetic biology and iGEM teams, and early-stage R&D professionals in biopharmaceutical companies. The team frames the longer-term goal as making the workflow reusable for other functional peptides by swapping domain knowledge, generation and evaluation models and experimental requirements. Contributions are offered at three independently usable levels: the software and its interfaces, an organised AMP knowledge base, and human practices questions and editable records for connecting stakeholder engagement to design.","partners":["Nanjing Brain Hospital (respiratory medicine)","AMR and One Health researchers","Dr Justin Fendos (Yale Teaching Center / Dongseo Scientific Teaching Center)","DKU (scientific exchange)","SJTU-Software (AI x Synthetic Biology Roundtable)","Xi'an Jiaotong-Liverpool University"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6219/wiki/software/ampilot-live-sequence-workspace-v2.avif","caption":"The live AMPilot sequence workspace: a circular map of the public reference record 1S with the base-level sequence and annotation list kept connected to the original GenBank annotations.","credit":"Team XJTLU-Software, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6219/wiki/software/ampilot-live-knowledge-explorer-v2.avif","caption":"The live public knowledge base, with separate entry points into the sequence, MIC, literature, drug, clinical-trial and patent catalogues.","credit":"Team XJTLU-Software, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6219/wiki/software/ampilot-live-research-canvas-v2.avif","caption":"The New research screen with an unsent example request to review evidence for AMP stability, captured as the entry interface rather than a completed run.","credit":"Team XJTLU-Software, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6219/wiki/software/case-candidate-009.avif","caption":"An actual candidate expanded in AMPilot, showing its sequence, calculated properties and predicted MIC alongside the evidence it came from.","credit":"Team XJTLU-Software, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Make the application, not the model, own the research record: AMPilot checks a stage complete against saved outputs rather than a conversational claim, reconciles promised work against what was actually written because a fluent closing message is not a delivery receipt, and shortens repeated context by replacing bodies with indexes that name exactly how to read the detail again instead of substituting an AI summary. Then prove the tool's value the way they did, with a randomised AB/BA crossover study reporting completion, time with confidence intervals, error counts and SUS, and with a published list of exactly which CI tests were skipped and why.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-software/","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-software/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-software/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-software/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-software/user-guide","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-software/deployment-guide","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-software/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-software/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-software/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/xjtlu-software/results","https://ampilotlab.com","https://ampilotlab.com/docs","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/xjtlu-software/ampilot"],"rank":7},"6220":{"team":"WHU-China","id":"6220","section":"Undergrad","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/whu-china/","projectTitle":"DifferPhase","tagline":"Phase-separated condensates split plasmids unevenly at division, so one founder population differentiates into a stable division of labour","summary":"WHU-China built DifferPhase, a platform that uses liquid-liquid phase separation to force asymmetric inheritance at cell division, so a single founder population can differentiate into several engineered sub-populations each carrying a different part of a long metabolic pathway. A YhjH-mCherry-PopZ fusion (Ymp) condenses at the cell pole and locally degrades c-di-GMP, so one daughter inherits the condensate and stays a low-c-di-GMP founder while the other becomes a high-c-di-GMP buffer cell; Slr supplies c-di-GMP to set up the gradient, and a tripartite split-GFP sensor built from GFP10-PilZ and FimX-GFP11 reports c-di-GMP in real time. Two orthogonal partitioning systems (ParB/parS and SopB/sopC) then drive different plasmids into different daughters, and a cross-interlocked dual toxin-antitoxin pair holds the resulting multi-plasmid state without antibiotics. They won Best New Composite Part in the Undergrad section and were nominated for Best New Basic Part.","awards":["Best New Basic Part — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best New Composite Part — Winner (Undergrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Parts organised as a four-module architecture rather than a flat list (founder cell maintenance, buffer cell dedifferentiation, differentiation, plasmid maintenance), with each module's basic and composite parts grouped under a stated function, so a reader can take one module without the rest. Contribution is written as six separable deliverables: the platform, the founder-maintenance module, the asymmetric partitioning tool, the plasmid-maintenance toolkit, a semi-solid medium protocol, and the human-practices material.","dataviz":"Module-level schematics for each of the four contributions (LLPS differentiation platform, Ymp founder maintenance, ParBS/SopBC asymmetric partitioning, dual-TA plasmid maintenance toolkit), plasmid maps, and confocal images of polar condensates. Parts tables carry Registry IDs linked directly to each entry, with type and main function in separate columns.","datascience":"Quantitative readouts are designed into the parts rather than added afterward: the split-GFP sensor turns an intracellular second messenger into fluorescence, an MrkH/pmrkA-sfGFP cassette reports c-di-GMP-dependent activation, a parS-lacZ-J23106-mCherry-LAA reporter uses LAA-tagged degradation so fluorescence decays once the plasmid is lost (making partitioning failure measurable), and eCFP, mTagBFP and eYFP variants let several plasmids be tracked in the same field. A double-layer plate swimming assay provides a cheap quantifiable proxy for intracellular c-di-GMP.","software":"","stack":["E. coli DH5-alpha, MG1655 and BL21(DE3)","PopZ condensates from Caulobacter crescentus","YhjH c-di-GMP phosphodiesterase","Slr diguanylate cyclase from Synechocystis PCC 6803","tripartite split-GFP (GFP1-9 / GFP10-PilZ / FimX-GFP11)","ParB-parS and SopB-sopC partitioning systems","EL222 blue-light transcription factor with pBLI","LasR/pLas and FleQ quorum circuits","ccdA/ccdB and mazE/mazF toxin-antitoxin pairs","confocal microscopy with agarose embedding"],"techniques":["engineered asymmetric division via condensate inheritance","orthogonal plasmid partitioning","sopC repeat-number variation to tune partitioning","cross-interlocked dual toxin-antitoxin plasmid maintenance","dual-inducer (arabinose/IPTG) orthogonal control from one plasmid","double-layer plate swimming assay"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Three campus pop-up events, online and in-person teaching outreach, and science comics, each pitched at a different audience and explicitly framed as inviting discussion of the technology's limitations as well as its possibilities rather than only promoting it. Channels include WeChat and Xiaohongshu.","ihp":"Campus and medical-student surveys plus interviews with residents living near East Lake in Wuhan, chosen because the platform's candidate applications include water purification, so the people consulted are the ones who would live next to a deployment. Those conversations were used to understand information needs, attitudes and specific safety concerns rather than to gauge enthusiasm. Cross-disciplinary expert discussions and exchanges with other iGEM teams were then used to interrogate the platform's underlying principles and application requirements, and the team states that these perspectives clarified which questions the project still needs to answer around effectiveness, safety and public concern.","realWorld":"There is no venture, no company and no commercial claim here, and the implementation discussion is deliberately conditional: the engineered strains are designed for controlled laboratory use only, there is no plan for environmental release, and they state that any future move toward practical products would require sealed equipment and comprehensive safety testing first. Natural rubber biosynthesis is presented as a conceptual demonstration of the platform, not as a product, with cancer therapy, water purification and plastic degradation named as directions the architecture could serve. So the real-world value is as reusable infrastructure, and on that count this is one of the better part contributions of the year. What makes these parts genuinely inheritable is fourfold. First, modular packaging: 34 parts are grouped into four functionally independent modules, and the contribution text names, for each module, who else could use it and for what, so a future team can adopt the plasmid-maintenance toolkit without touching the differentiation platform. Second, every part description states its provenance and its role in the circuit, not just its identity, including which organism a protein came from and what it contributes to the system (PopZ as the condensate scaffold ensuring asymmetric inheritance, Slr as the c-di-GMP source that establishes the gradient). Third, measurement is built in: the split-GFP c-di-GMP sensor, the MrkH-driven reporter, and especially the LAA-tagged mCherry reporter whose signal decays on plasmid loss turn otherwise invisible behaviours into assayable ones, which is what lets another team verify the part works in their hands. Fourth, and most unusually, they publish the engineering failures as part annotations: the dual-input araC-pBAD-YmP / T7-lacO-Slr circuit is documented as needing stronger T7-optimised terminators to reduce read-through, and several cassettes are annotated with the specific biTT or T7 terminator placement used to prevent read-through between transcription units. An honest note about where the terminator problem bites is more useful to a reuser than a clean claim. The dual-TA design also removes antibiotic selection entirely, which they correctly frame as reducing the spread of resistance, and the safety reasoning is specific rather than boilerplate: all chassis are BSL-1 whitelist Risk Group 1 strains, MazF and CcdB are acknowledged as potent toxins whose killing is confined to the engineered population, and no gene used encodes a virulence factor. They also standardised and published protocols (Ymp condensate confocal imaging with induction, embedding and imaging parameters; the double-layer swimming assay with medium formulations, inoculation method and data-interpretation guidance), which is the part of a contribution that usually goes missing. Continuation is framed as community reuse rather than a company: tools, protocols and a reference framework offered to future teams building multi-cell division-of-labour systems, with sopC mutants and optimisation schemes earmarked for submission as further parts.","partners":["Wuhan University School of Life Sciences (BSL-1 facilities, Regulations on the Management of Laboratory Biosafety)","Residents near East Lake, Wuhan (interviews on water-purification application and safety concerns)","Cross-disciplinary academic experts and other iGEM teams (principle and application review)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6220/wiki/whu-contribution2-fig1.avif","caption":"The LLPS-mediated platform for cellular functional differentiation, offered as a reference framework for future multi-cell division-of-labour systems","credit":"Team WHU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6220/wiki/whu-contribution2-fig3.avif","caption":"ParBS and SopBC orthogonal condensate partitioning, the reusable tool for driving different plasmids into different daughter cells","credit":"Team WHU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6220/wiki/whu-contribution2-fig4.avif","caption":"Cross-interlocked dual toxin-antitoxin plasmid maintenance toolkit: each plasmid supplies the antitoxin for the other's toxin, so neither can be lost and no antibiotic selection is needed","credit":"Team WHU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6220/wiki/whu-contribution2-fig2.avif","caption":"Ymp (YhjH-mCherry-PopZ) founder-cell maintenance module, with the published confocal protocol for observing polar condensates","credit":"Team WHU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Package parts the way WHU did: group them into functionally independent modules, and for each module state in writing who outside the project could reuse it and for what, so adopters can take one piece without the whole system. Then ship the three things that actually make reuse possible — a built-in measurement part (their LAA-tagged reporter that decays on plasmid loss), the standardised protocol with induction, sample-prep and imaging parameters, and an honest annotation of the known weakness, such as terminator read-through, recorded on the part itself.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/whu-china/","https://2026.igem.wiki/whu-china/parts/","https://2026.igem.wiki/whu-china/contribution/","https://2026.igem.wiki/whu-china/safety/","https://2026.igem.wiki/whu-china/description/"],"rank":33},"6222":{"team":"WageningenUR","id":"6222","section":"Overgrad","country":"Netherlands","village":"Bioremediation","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/wageningenur/","projectTitle":"Triton","projectTitle_zh":"Triton","tagline":"Capture, degrade and sense trifluoroacetate: a three-module biological system for the smallest forever chemical, aimed at reverse-osmosis concentrate.","tagline_zh":"捕捉、分解並偵測三氟乙酸鹽：針對最小的永久性化學物質設計的三模組生物系統，目標是逆滲透濃縮液。","summary":"Triton targets trifluoroacetate (TFA), the ultra-short-chain PFAS that makes up more than 98% of all PFAS measured in EU river and groundwater and was found in the blood of all 110 Europeans tested in a 2026 study. Rather than one trick, they built three modules shaped entirely by stakeholder input: a de novo protein binder on bacterial cellulose beads to concentrate TFA out of reverse-osmosis concentrate, a growth-coupled directed hyper-evolution platform to push fluoroacetate dehalogenases from monofluoroacetate toward difluoroacetate and then TFA, and a riboswitch biosensor for continuous on-site monitoring. The dry lab contributed two reusable tools - PIGEON, an active-learning in silico evolution loop that lifted a Boltz-2 binding probability by over 33%, and DISARM, which retargets existing aptamers to new small-molecule ligands without SELEX. They took 1st Runner-up Grand Prize plus Best Measurement, Best Presentation and Best Bioremediation Project.","summary_zh":"Triton 針對的是三氟乙酸鹽（TFA）——這種超短鏈 PFAS 佔歐盟河川與地下水所測得全部 PFAS 的 98% 以上，而 2026 年一項研究在 110 位受測歐洲人的血液中全數驗出。他們沒有只靠一招，而是做了三個完全由利害關係人意見塑形的模組：把 de novo 蛋白質結合體固定在細菌纖維素微珠上，用來把 TFA 從逆滲透濃縮液中濃縮出來；一個與生長耦合的定向超演化平台，把氟乙酸脫鹵酶從單氟乙酸推向二氟乙酸、再推向 TFA；以及一個核糖開關生物感測器，用於現場連續監測。乾實驗貢獻了兩項可重複使用的工具——PIGEON，一個主動學習的 in silico 演化迴圈，把 Boltz-2 的結合機率提升超過 33%；以及 DISARM，不需 SELEX 就能把現有核酸適體重新導向新的小分子配體。該隊拿下總冠軍亞軍，外加最佳量測、最佳簡報與最佳生物復育專案。","awards":["1st Runner-up (Overgrad)","Top 10 (Overgrad)","Best Measurement — Winner (Overgrad)","Best Presentation — Winner (Overgrad)","Best Wiki — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Integrated Human Practices — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Entrepreneurship — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Bioremediation Project — Winner"],"dry":{"frameworks":"The capture module is a full generative-plus-evaluative protein design stack. They first searched the literature and the PDB for anything reported to bind TFA and found no strong binder, then generated de novo candidates with Proteina-Complexa and BoltzGen (both denoising generative models, seeded with the TFA conformation taken from PDB 4FVX), reasoning that evolution never had selective pressure to bind a molecule that did not exist before 1922. Every candidate was scored with Boltz-2 rather than docking, with the choice justified explicitly: AutoDock Vina treats the protein as rigid and correlated poorly with experiment (R^2 = 0.604 on a 2016 benchmark), while Boltz-2 is trained on millions of experimental binding measurements and approaches free-energy-perturbation accuracy over 1000x faster. No natural or de novo scaffold passed 0.540, held by the L-2-haloacid dehalogenase RSc1362 (PDB 3UMB). Rational pocket design came next: they mined the literature for residues that prefer the CF3 group over CH3 (arginine, methionine, glycine, histidine, glutamine, phenylalanine) with their distance preferences, used PLIP to find TFA-contacting residues, and applied a three-criterion automated mutation script - 12 of 14 mutable scaffolds improved, with a caltractin A4H substitution jumping 0.118 to 0.518, and RSc1362_v2 reaching 0.566. Then PIGEON (Protein In silico Guided Evolution and Optimization Network) closed the loop: ESM3 embeddings of the RSc1362 family paired with Boltz-2 scores train a ridge regression under repeated leave-one-out CV; ESM3 guided decoding then proposes mutations against a custom objective that rewards binding gains while preserving pTM and charges binding losses tenfold (so a 0.01 binding loss would need +0.67 pTM to break even); binding-pocket residues are protected, four designs per parent across ten parents per round, best-per-parent carried forward, newly folded scores appended to the training set. Over 50 rounds RSc1362_v3 reached 0.723, a 33% gain over wild type, with the regression's Spearman rho rising from 0.65 to 0.92 and mean pTM flat - evidence the gain was learned, not lucky. Degradation design was grounded in published QM/MM work mapping the full FAcD catalytic cycle (Asp-His-Asp triad, fluoride-binding pocket His150/Trp151/Tyr213) onto MFA, DFA and TFA, which showed the rate-determining step shifts from nucleophilic attack to C-F activation after the first fluorine and that the barrier rises ~11.8 kcal/mol from MFA to DFA but only ~1.8 from DFA to TFA; that single insight set their whole strategy of evolving for DFA first.","frameworks_zh":"捕捉模組是一整套生成加評估的蛋白質設計堆疊。他們先在文獻與 PDB 中搜尋任何被報告可結合 TFA 的蛋白質，結果沒有找到強結合者，於是用 Proteina-Complexa 與 BoltzGen（兩者都是去噪生成模型，以取自 PDB 4FVX 的 TFA 構形為起點）生成 de novo 候選，理由是演化從未有過結合一個 1922 年之前並不存在的分子的選擇壓力。每個候選都以 Boltz-2 而非對接評分，而這個選擇有明確理由：AutoDock Vina 把蛋白質視為剛性，與實驗的相關性不佳（2016 年一項基準測試中 R^2 = 0.604），而 Boltz-2 訓練於數百萬筆實驗結合量測，接近自由能擾動的精度，速度卻快 1000 倍以上。沒有任何天然或 de novo 骨架超過 0.540，該分數由 L-2-鹵酸脫鹵酶 RSc1362（PDB 3UMB）保持。接著是理性的口袋設計：他們從文獻中整理出偏好 CF3 基團勝於 CH3 的殘基（精胺酸、甲硫胺酸、甘胺酸、組胺酸、麩醯胺酸、苯丙胺酸）及其距離偏好，用 PLIP 找出接觸 TFA 的殘基，並套用一個三項判準的自動突變腳本——14 個可突變骨架中有 12 個改善，其中 caltractin 的 A4H 取代從 0.118 跳到 0.518，RSc1362_v2 則達到 0.566。然後由 PIGEON（Protein In silico Guided Evolution and Optimization Network）把迴圈閉合：RSc1362 家族的 ESM3 嵌入搭配 Boltz-2 分數，在反覆的留一交叉驗證下訓練一個脊迴歸；再由 ESM3 的引導式解碼針對自訂目標函數提出突變，該函數獎勵結合力提升、同時維持 pTM，並把結合力的損失以十倍計價（因此 0.01 的結合力損失需要 +0.67 的 pTM 才能打平）；結合口袋的殘基受到保護，每輪有十個親代、每個親代四個設計，各親代取最佳者進入下一輪，新折疊出的分數再附加回訓練集。經過 50 輪，RSc1362_v3 達到 0.723，比野生型提升 33%，而迴歸模型的 Spearman rho 從 0.65 升到 0.92、平均 pTM 持平——證明這個提升是學來的，不是碰巧。分解模組的設計則建立在已發表的 QM/MM 研究上，該研究把完整的 FAcD 催化循環（Asp-His-Asp 三元體、由 His150/Trp151/Tyr213 構成的氟離子結合口袋）對應到 MFA、DFA 與 TFA，結果顯示在第一個氟之後，速率決定步驟從親核攻擊轉為 C-F 活化，而能障從 MFA 到 DFA 上升約 11.8 kcal/mol，從 DFA 到 TFA 卻只上升約 1.8；僅憑這個洞見，就定下了他們先針對 DFA 演化的整體策略。","dataviz":"The wiki is a scroll-driven explainer that teaches the problem before the solution: TFA's ECHA Repr. 1B classification, the 110-of-110 blood result, the >98%-of-all-PFAS share and the 34-of-36 tap water samples each land as their own beat, with a stacked TFA-versus-all-other-PFAS bar and a four-property card (accumulating, unregulated, unbreakable, tiny) before the three-step Capture/Degrade/Sense walkthrough. Stakeholder quotes are first-class design elements, each with a named face, rather than buried on a human practices page - Peter Fischer's 'it's not a question of if TFA will be added to the Drinking Water Directive, it's a question of when' and Bert van der Wal's 'a TFA binder would be fantastic, then you have gold in your hands' carry the narrative. The measurement page is built as a decision aid rather than a result log: a comparison scorecard across five media lets another team pick conditions for their own question. The front page also includes a scoring widget that opens the visitor's own mail client to send feedback to the team.","dataviz_zh":"這個 wiki 是以捲動帶動的解說，先把問題教懂再談解法：TFA 的 ECHA Repr. 1B 分類、110 人中 110 人驗出的血液結果、佔全部 PFAS 超過 98% 的比例，以及 36 份自來水樣本中 34 份驗出，各自成為一個節拍；在進入捕捉／分解／偵測三步驟導覽之前，先有一張 TFA 對其他所有 PFAS 的堆疊長條圖，以及一張四項性質卡（會累積、未受管制、無法分解、極小）。利害關係人的引語是第一級的設計元素，各自配上具名的人物照片，而不是被埋在 human practices 頁面裡——Peter Fischer 的「TFA 會不會被納入飲用水指令不是問題，問題是何時」以及 Bert van der Wal 的「有了 TFA 結合蛋白會非常棒，那你手上就握著黃金」撐起了整篇敘事。量測頁面被做成決策輔助工具而非結果紀錄：一張橫跨五種介質的比較評分表，讓其他隊伍能依自己的研究問題挑選條件。首頁還有一個評分小工具，會開啟訪客自己的郵件程式，把回饋寄給團隊。","datascience":"The Best Measurement work is the data-science highlight because they treated an assay as a product. Starting from the Belcher alizarin-lanthanum fluoride chemistry as used qualitatively by Bygd et al., they rebuilt it as a quantitative method: a ratiometric readout found by searching for the isosbestic point and selecting the optimal numerator wavelength in each medium, with stated acceptance thresholds (R^2 >= 0.95, >= 40 nm separation, >= 20% signal change, positive slope) and selection by lowest LOD, then LOD = 3.3 sigma/b and LOQ = 10 sigma/b with an explicit rule for which sigma to use. Fixed conditions are all stated (100 uM 1:1 alizarin:lanthanum, 84 mM acetate buffer pH 5.2, 25 v/v% acetone added after a 1-hour dark incubation, per-well volumes in 96-well format) and the data analysis is written as a procedure rather than a result, so another team reproduces the method even if their numbers differ. They characterised it as a tool across four fluorochemicals (MFA, DFA, TFA, PFOA), two hosts (E. coli MG1655, P. putida KT2440) and five media (demi water, M9, HEPES-buffered M9, 20 mM HEPES, tap water), and documented the limits as carefully as the working range: phosphate interferes, response saturates above 40 uM, 5 mM fluorochemicals suppress signal up to 60%. Controls are enumerated by class - measurement (10 blank wells for sigma, 40 uM spike, literature condition reproduced before any change), matrix (M9 as a phosphate-interference control, 93-hour incubated supernatant, fluorochemical spikes) and biological (wild-type and empty-vector negatives, MFA as a should-work substrate, PFOA as a should-not).","datascience_zh":"獲得最佳量測的工作是資料科學上的亮點，因為他們把一項分析法當成產品來做。起點是 Bygd 等人以定性方式使用的 Belcher 茜素—鑭氟離子化學，他們把它重建為定量方法：以搜尋等吸收點並在每種介質中挑選最佳分子波長的方式，得到一組比值式讀值，並訂有明確的驗收門檻（R^2 >= 0.95、分離度 >= 40 nm、訊號變化 >= 20%、斜率為正），再以最低 LOD 作為選擇依據，接著以 LOD = 3.3 sigma/b 與 LOQ = 10 sigma/b 計算，並明訂應採用哪一個 sigma。固定條件全部寫明（100 uM、1:1 的茜素比鑭，84 mM 醋酸緩衝液 pH 5.2，暗處培養 1 小時後加入 25 v/v% 丙酮，以 96 孔格式列出每孔體積），而資料分析是寫成一套程序而非一個結果，因此其他隊伍即使數值不同也能重現方法。他們把它當成工具加以特性化，橫跨四種氟化合物（MFA、DFA、TFA、PFOA）、兩種宿主（E. coli MG1655、P. putida KT2440）與五種介質（去離子水、M9、HEPES 緩衝的 M9、20 mM HEPES、自來水），並把限制記錄得和可用範圍一樣仔細：磷酸鹽會干擾、反應在高於 40 uM 後飽和、5 mM 的氟化合物會把訊號壓抑達 60%。對照組依類別一一列出——量測類（10 個空白孔用於求 sigma、40 uM 加標、在任何改動之前先重現文獻條件）、基質類（以 M9 作為磷酸鹽干擾對照、培養 93 小時的上清液、氟化合物加標）與生物類（野生型與空載體陰性對照、以 MFA 作為應當有效的底物、以 PFOA 作為應當無效的底物）。","software":"PIGEON and DISARM, both with code on the iGEM GitLab at https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/wageningenur. PIGEON is the generalisable one: an active-learning loop over ESM3 embeddings, ridge regression and ESM3 guided decoding against a user-defined objective, which the team explicitly documents as retargetable to solubility, thermostability or ipTM rather than only Boltz-2 binding probability, and which they distinguish from a conventional ML model because it proposes mutations rather than only scoring given inputs. DISARM (Detecting Interaction Sites for Aptamer Retargeting by Mutation) recommends mutations that retarget an existing aptamer or riboswitch to a new ligand of similar size: it identifies favourable nucleotide positions around the ligand, compares them with the existing aptamer's nucleotide positions and backbone connection points, and returns 50 candidates while preserving secondary structure - positioned as a partial replacement for SELEX, or at least a rational starting library. They validated 10 DISARM riboswitches in the wet lab (4 PFOA, 4 TFA, 2 scrambled controls) and reported honestly that one PFOA riboswitch met the success criterion and no TFA riboswitch did. The contribution page also packages a reusable defluorination framework - the fluoride assay with calibration procedure, controls, sample prep and analysis workflow plus a step-by-step experimental video - and a hypermutation platform and expression architecture described as adaptable to any enzyme.","software_zh":"PIGEON 與 DISARM，程式碼都放在 iGEM GitLab 的 https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/wageningenur。PIGEON 是可泛用的那一個：一個在 ESM3 嵌入、脊迴歸與 ESM3 引導式解碼之上針對使用者自訂目標運作的主動學習迴圈；該隊明確記錄它可改用於溶解度、熱穩定性或 ipTM，而不限於 Boltz-2 的結合機率，並說明它與一般機器學習模型的區別在於它會提出突變，而不只是為既有輸入評分。DISARM（Detecting Interaction Sites for Aptamer Retargeting by Mutation）則推薦突變，把現有的核酸適體或核糖開關重新導向尺寸相近的新配體：它找出配體周圍有利的核苷酸位置，與現有適體的核苷酸位置及骨架連接點相比，並在維持二級結構的前提下回傳 50 個候選——定位是部分取代 SELEX，或至少提供一個理性的起始函式庫。他們在濕實驗中驗證了 10 個 DISARM 核糖開關（4 個 PFOA、4 個 TFA、2 個打亂序列對照），並誠實報告只有一個 PFOA 核糖開關達到成功標準，TFA 則沒有任何一個達到。貢獻頁面還包裝了一套可重複使用的去氟框架——氟離子分析法連同校正程序、對照組、樣品前處理與分析流程，外加一支逐步示範的實驗影片——以及一個被描述為可適用於任何酵素的超突變平台與表現架構。","stack":["Boltz-2","BoltzGen","Proteina-Complexa","ESM3 (embeddings + guided decoding)","Ridge regression (scikit-learn)","PLIP (Protein-Ligand Interaction Profiler)","AutoDock Vina (benchmarked against, not used)","AMBER / molecular dynamics","Protein Data Bank","AlphaFold (model AF-P00506-F1)","Python","iGEM GitLab","96-well plate UV-Vis absorbance (400-700 nm)","BLASTp / BLASTn against patent sequence databases"],"techniques":["de novo binder generation by denoising generative models","learned affinity prediction in place of rigid-body docking","literature-derived CF3 residue-preference rules applied as automated pocket mutations","active-learning in silico directed evolution with a custom multi-objective reward","asymmetric penalty weighting to prevent objective gaming (10x on binding loss)","binding-pocket residue protection during mutagenesis","repeated leave-one-out cross-validation on small design sets","tracking surrogate-model Spearman rho across rounds as evidence of learning","ratiometric absorbance assay with isosbestic-point calibration","LOD/LOQ determination from blank replicates","per-medium recalibration as a documented local step","growth-coupled directed hyper-evolution","in silico aptamer retargeting as a SELEX alternative"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Triton has no separate education or outreach page; its public-facing work is the wiki itself, built as a scroll-driven public explainer that teaches why TFA matters before it mentions synthetic biology - the ECHA reproductive-toxicity classification, the 110-of-110 blood study, the >98% PFAS share, the 34-of-36 tap water result - with named stakeholder quotes and faces carrying the argument, a front-page feedback widget that opens the visitor's own mail client, and a step-by-step experimental video for the fluoride assay published for other labs to follow. Their documented engagement effort went into the professional and policy community rather than schools: over 30 stakeholders through interviews, company visits and events, with every stakeholder given an explanation of why the team reached out, what was learned and what was or was not incorporated, plus a published analysis of future regulatory and industrial developments offered as a starting point for anyone working on TFA contamination.","publicEngagement_zh":"Triton 沒有獨立的教育或外展頁面；它面向公眾的工作就是 wiki 本身，做成以捲動帶動的公眾解說，在提到合成生物學之前先講清楚 TFA 為何重要——ECHA 的生殖毒性分類、110 人中 110 人的血液研究、佔 PFAS 超過 98% 的比例、36 份自來水中 34 份的結果——論證由具名的利害關係人引語與照片撐起，首頁有一個會開啟訪客自己郵件程式的回饋小工具，另有一支氟離子分析法的逐步實驗影片，公開供其他實驗室照著做。他們有紀錄的互動投注在專業與政策社群，而非學校：透過訪談、企業參訪與活動接觸超過 30 位利害關係人，每一位都附上為何主動聯繫、學到什麼、以及哪些有被納入或沒有被納入的說明，另外還公開一份對未來法規與產業發展的分析，提供給任何投入 TFA 污染議題的人作為起點。","ihp":"The most traceable chain of design changes in the cohort, and the shifts are structural rather than cosmetic. They started intending only to degrade TFA; stakeholders told them they were missing an essential step. Peter Fischer (Aqualab Zuid, one of six companies legally tasked with assessing Dutch drinking water quality) showed that TFA can only be measured by LC-MS on samples shipped to a central lab, so it is expensive, discontinuous and ex situ - which meant the bioreactor could not be operated at all, and directly created the biosensor module. Frank Schoonenberg (process engineer, Vitens) explained that reverse osmosis filters TFA but does not destroy it, that the resulting concentrate is currently discharged, and that discharging it will be prohibited - so they designed Triton to treat RO concentrate rather than drinking water, filling a need nobody currently serves. Bert van der Waal and Peyman Salehian then showed that even 5-10x RO concentration leaves TFA far too dilute (an ideal 10x on the Dutch 2.2 ug/L indicative value reaches only 22 ug/L against a milligram-per-litre target), which created the capture module. Amanda Larasati ruled out ion exchange resins because resin leaching bars them from Dutch water infrastructure. Tue Kjaergaard Nielsen warned that measuring TFA reduction produces false positives because TFA adsorbs to surfaces rather than being degraded, pushing them to measure released fluoride instead. Clemens Mayer (molecular evolution, Groningen) led them to directed evolution for an enzyme that does not yet exist. Amin Espah Borujeni helped redesign the riboswitch proof-of-concept experiments after the published plasmid failed to reproduce. Regulatory interviews established that a product containing no viable GMOs faces a considerably simpler approval path, which they explored alongside deliberate release and which shaped biosafety from an early stage. They also document conflicting stakeholder views and explain why some were not implemented.","ihp_zh":"這是本屆最可追溯的一條設計變更鏈，而且這些轉向是結構性的，不是門面功夫。他們一開始只打算分解 TFA；利害關係人告訴他們漏掉了一個必要步驟。Peter Fischer（Aqualab Zuid，法定負責評估荷蘭飲用水品質的六家公司之一）指出 TFA 目前只能把樣品送到中央實驗室以 LC-MS 量測，所以昂貴、不連續且屬於異地檢測——這意味著生物反應器根本無法運轉，也直接催生了生物感測器模組。Frank Schoonenberg（Vitens 製程工程師）說明逆滲透能濾掉 TFA 但不會把它破壞，產生的濃縮液目前直接排放，而未來排放將被禁止——於是他們把 Triton 設計成處理逆滲透濃縮液而非飲用水，填補了目前無人服務的需求。接著 Bert van der Waal 與 Peyman Salehian 指出，即使逆滲透濃縮 5 至 10 倍，TFA 仍然遠遠太稀（以荷蘭 2.2 ug/L 的指標值理想濃縮 10 倍也只到 22 ug/L，而目標是每公升毫克等級），這催生了捕捉模組。Amanda Larasati 排除了離子交換樹脂，因為樹脂析出使它們無法用於荷蘭的水利基礎設施。Tue Kjaergaard Nielsen 警告，量測 TFA 的減少會產生偽陽性，因為 TFA 會吸附到表面而非被分解，這促使他們改為量測釋出的氟離子。Clemens Mayer（分子演化，格羅寧根）引導他們走向定向演化，去做一個目前還不存在的酵素。Amin Espah Borujeni 在已發表質體無法重現之後，協助他們重新設計核糖開關的概念驗證實驗。法規訪談確立了不含活體基改生物的產品，核准路徑會明顯簡單許多，他們把這條路徑與刻意釋放一併探討，並在早期就以此形塑生物安全設計。他們也記錄了利害關係人之間相互衝突的意見，並說明為何有些沒有採納。","realWorld":"Implementation is specified as a real retrofit rather than a concept: Triton sits downstream of existing split-stream reverse osmosis at a drinking water plant, with the capture module as a granular filter of bacterial cellulose beads carrying TFA-binding proteins attached through a cellulose-binding domain, eluted with a wash buffer so beads are reused, feeding a three-day bioreactor where evolved dehalogenase turns TFA into oxalate and fluoride while the riboswitch biosensor monitors continuously. Biosafety is specified per module: the beads contain no living cells and need no extra measures, the biosensor's small water stream is collected and autoclaved, and the bioreactor effluent gets UV sterilisation before discharge. Timeline is roughly 10 years to drinking-water implementation, with permitting, certification and grid congestion named as the bottlenecks rather than construction, and the biosensor identified as the faster path. The market analysis is sharply scoped - not water treatment, not PFAS at large, but the destruction of PFAS that filtration cannot retain, noting destruction was 24.9% of the PFAS treatment market in 2025 and is the fastest-growing segment at a projected 10.1% CAGR against 7.1% overall. The business plan runs a six-phase TRL 3 to 9 roadmap with a gate per phase, a cost analysis across physical and human capital, 2.6M euro to raise and break-even in 2033, six commercial and adoption risks each with a mitigation, five technical failure modes each with a fallback, an operational plan with a Dreyfus-model skill gap analysis resolved build/borrow/outsource, and a SWOT identifying a co-development partner as the predominant stakeholder. IP is worked out concretely: the software is not patentable because its source is deposited on the iGEM GitLab (but is copyright-protected), while BLASTp against the patented protein database returned only 43.30% maximum identity for DAR3835 and H1_ML against claims requiring 95%, so the evolved enzymes remain patentable.","realWorld_zh":"實作被指定為真正的既有設施改裝，而不是一個概念：Triton 設在飲用水廠既有分流式逆滲透的下游，捕捉模組是一座以細菌纖維素微珠構成的顆粒濾床，微珠上透過纖維素結合區域接上 TFA 結合蛋白，以沖洗緩衝液洗脫後微珠可重複使用，接著進入一座停留三天的生物反應器，由演化後的脫鹵酶把 TFA 轉成草酸鹽與氟離子，同時由核糖開關生物感測器連續監測。生物安全依模組分別規定：微珠不含活細胞，不需額外措施；生物感測器的小量水流會被收集並高壓滅菌；生物反應器出流則在排放前先經紫外線滅菌。時程上約需 10 年才能進入飲用水應用，而被指名的瓶頸是許可、認證與電網壅塞，而不是施工，生物感測器則被認定是較快的路徑。市場分析的範圍劃得很銳利——不是水處理、也不是整個 PFAS 領域，而是過濾無法攔住之 PFAS 的破壞處理；文中指出破壞處理在 2025 年佔 PFAS 處理市場的 24.9%，且是成長最快的區段，預估年複合成長率 10.1%，相對於整體的 7.1%。商業計畫包含一份六階段、TRL 3 到 9 的路線圖，每階段設有關卡，一份涵蓋實體與人力資本的成本分析，需募資 260 萬歐元並於 2033 年損益兩平，六項商業與採用風險各附緩解措施，五種技術失效模式各附備案，一份以 Dreyfus 模型做技能落差分析並以自建／借用／外包解決的營運計畫，以及一份把共同開發夥伴認定為最主要利害關係人的 SWOT。智慧財產權也處理得很具體：軟體因原始碼已存放於 iGEM GitLab 而不可申請專利（但受著作權保護），而以 BLASTp 比對專利蛋白質資料庫，DAR3835 與 H1_ML 對要求 95% 相同度的專利請求項只有最高 43.30% 相同度，因此演化後的酵素仍可申請專利。","partners":["Vitens (Frank Schoonenberg, process engineer)","Aqualab Zuid (Peter Fischer, scientific advisor)","Prof. Bert van der Waal, Wageningen University (environmental sciences)","Peyman Salehian (enzyme development)","Clemens Mayer, University of Groningen (molecular evolution)","Amin Espah Borujeni (riboswitch design)","Tue Kjaergaard Nielsen","Amanda Larasati","WaterIQ (Freddy Dekkers)","Harrie Timmer","RIVM","Arcadis","Witteveen+Bos","Nijhuis Saur","Bas Eickhout (policy)","Christos Batianis and Enrique Asin-Garcia, Wageningen University"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6222/wiki/text-images/general/triton-wholesystem-v5.avif","caption":"The full Triton system: reverse-osmosis concentrate passes a bacterial-cellulose capture filter to concentrate TFA, then a bioreactor where evolved dehalogenase cleaves the C-F bond while a riboswitch biosensor monitors concentration continuously.","caption_zh":"完整的 Triton 系統：逆滲透濃縮液先通過細菌纖維素捕捉濾床把 TFA 濃縮起來，再進入生物反應器，由演化後的脫鹵酶切開 C-F 鍵，同時由核糖開關生物感測器連續監測濃度。","credit":"Team WageningenUR, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6222/wiki/text-images/dry-lab/capturing-drylab/kevin-engineering-figure-7b.webp","caption":"Fifty rounds of PIGEON in silico evolution across five runs, lifting RSc1362's Boltz-2 binding probability from 0.540 to 0.723 while the surrogate model's Spearman rho rises from 0.65 to 0.92 and mean pTM stays flat.","caption_zh":"五次執行、各 50 輪的 PIGEON in silico 演化，把 RSc1362 的 Boltz-2 結合機率從 0.540 提升到 0.723，同時代理模型的 Spearman rho 從 0.65 升到 0.92，平均 pTM 保持持平。","credit":"Team WageningenUR, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6222/wiki/text-images/measurement/triton-measurement-scorecard.avif","caption":"The medium comparison scorecard from the Best Measurement work, which lets another team choose assay conditions for their own research question rather than copying a single validated setup.","caption_zh":"最佳量測工作中的介質比較評分表，讓其他隊伍能依自己的研究問題挑選分析條件，而不是照抄單一組已驗證的設定。","credit":"Team WageningenUR, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6222/wiki/text-images/measurement/triton-measurement-cuvettes.webp","caption":"The alizarin-lanthanum fluoride assay in practice: the spectral shift on fluoride release is visible to the naked eye above roughly 20 uM, so no fluoride electrode, ion chromatography or 19F-NMR is needed.","caption_zh":"實際操作中的茜素—鑭氟離子分析法：氟離子釋出時的光譜位移在大約 20 uM 以上就肉眼可見，因此不需要氟離子電極、離子層析或 19F-NMR。","credit":"Team WageningenUR, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Build the measurement first and publish it as a product, not a result: their fluoride assay won Best Measurement because the protocol, the LOD/LOQ derivation, the acceptance thresholds, the comparison across five media and the documented failure modes (phosphate interference, saturation above 40 uM) all let another lab decide in advance whether it fits - and it needs only a 96-well plate reader and two cheap reagents, which is squarely within a high-school research centre's reach. The companion habit worth copying is PIGEON's reward design: charging a loss in the primary objective tenfold against the secondary one stops a model from quietly trading away the thing you actually care about.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"先把量測做出來，並且把它當成產品而不是結果來發表：他們的氟離子分析法之所以贏得最佳量測，是因為操作流程、LOD/LOQ 的推導、驗收門檻、五種介質間的比較，以及記錄下來的失效模式（磷酸鹽干擾、高於 40 uM 後飽和），全都讓另一間實驗室能事先判斷它適不適合自己——而且只需要一台 96 孔盤判讀儀與兩種便宜試劑，完全落在高中研究單位的能力範圍內。另一個值得照抄的習慣是 PIGEON 的獎勵設計：把主要目標的損失以十倍計價於次要目標之上，可以阻止模型悄悄把你真正在意的東西交換掉。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/wageningenur/","https://2026.igem.wiki/wageningenur/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/wageningenur/design/","https://2026.igem.wiki/wageningenur/dry-lab-overview/","https://2026.igem.wiki/wageningenur/capturing/","https://2026.igem.wiki/wageningenur/capturing-dry-lab/","https://2026.igem.wiki/wageningenur/degradation/","https://2026.igem.wiki/wageningenur/sensing/","https://2026.igem.wiki/wageningenur/riboswitch/","https://2026.igem.wiki/wageningenur/measurement/","https://2026.igem.wiki/wageningenur/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/wageningenur/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/wageningenur/entrepreneurship/","https://2026.igem.wiki/wageningenur/implementation/","https://2026.igem.wiki/wageningenur/contribution/"],"rank":264},"6236":{"team":"ZQT-Nanjing","id":"6236","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"Biomanufacturing / sustainable production (inferred from project scope; no village stated on the wiki)","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/zqt-nanjing/","projectTitle":"EcToBloom","tagline":"A greener, low-salt route to ectoine, finished as a compostable bacterial-cellulose repair mask","summary":"EcToBloom rebuilds the ectoine biosynthesis route (ectB-ectA-ectC from halophilic bacteria) in non-halophilic E. coli BL21(DE3) so that ectoine can be made under conventional low-salt fermentation instead of the industrial high-salt 'bacterial milking' process that corrodes equipment and produces untreatable saline wastewater. A second engineered strain carries acsAB and acsCD to make its own bacterial cellulose membrane, which is combined with a silk fibroin layer and loaded with ectoine to give a preservative-free, compostable three-layer repair mask. Titres rose from 0.503 g/L (same-batch wild type) to 4.425 g/L in the first engineered strain, 5.344 g/L on an optimised medium and 6.852 g/L after introducing the feedback-desensitised LysC T352I aspartokinase. The team also explored wheat-straw hydrolysate and other paper wastes as non-food carbon sources.","awards":["Best New Composite Part — Nominee (High School)","Best Project Promotion Video — Winner (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"No mathematical or computational model. The Model, Software, Measurement and Hardware pages are left as unedited iGEM template text (award blurb plus 'Inspirations' links), so the project has no kinetic model, no flux analysis and no in-silico design loop. The engineering logic is reasoned verbally from pathway biochemistry (feedback inhibition of LysC, pathway stoichiometry via a single operon) rather than simulated.","dataviz":"Figure-led quantitative reporting across Results and Description: a titre roadmap annotating each stage's value, bar charts with individual replicate dots and SD error bars, 0-48 h growth curves (OD600) with error bars, production time courses, four single-factor screening panels (carbon source, initial glucose, nitrogen source, NH4Cl concentration), plasmid maps, annotated gel panels, and a stakeholder impact map on Human Practices. Figures carry long explanatory captions that state what the bars, dots and error bars are.","datascience":"Real but basic experimental data analysis: n = 3 biological replicates throughout, mean +/- SD, fold-change comparisons restricted to same-batch controls, HPLC quantification against a standard calibration curve, and single-factor medium optimisation. Notably careful about statistical honesty for a high-school team: they refuse to add titres from different batches into a 'cumulative improvement', flag that the wild-type signal sits near the method's limit of quantification with high between-replicate variance, and list blank matrices, spike-recovery and peak-purity checks as the follow-up needed.","software":"No software deliverable. Their 'code' contribution is the published source of a synthetic-biology educational card game, released so other teams can fork, translate and extend it.","stack":["HPLC (C18 reverse phase, acetonitrile:water 20:80, 210 nm) with standard calibration curve","OD600 growth curves with dilution-corrected linear range","agarose gel electrophoresis + colony PCR + Sanger sequencing verification","alkaline purification and dry-weight quantification of intracellular vs extracellular cellulose","plasmid map / pathway figure production"],"techniques":["same-batch controlled fold-change comparison","mean +/- SD with n = 3 biological replicates and per-replicate data points plotted","single-factor screening (carbon source, glucose concentration, nitrogen source, NH4Cl concentration)","growth-vs-production time-course analysis to assess metabolic burden","limit-of-quantification reasoning and explicit refusal to pool across batches","rational point-mutation design (LysC T352I) from literature feedback-inhibition mechanism"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"The strongest dimension of this project. A BLOOM-framework education programme runs across four age bands with different media for each: food-chain lessons, comics and perler-bead biology art for kindergarten and primary pupils; mini STEM research projects and lab visits for middle schoolers; genetic-circuit design, ethics debating ('Can we do it - but should we?'), knowledge competitions and a purpose-built 'Synthetic Biology Laboratory' card game for high schoolers; plus science journaling and a shared educational website built with team NBJF. A separate strand studies gender equity in science ('Do girls really have equal freedom to choose science?'), including a student-and-parent study of post-Gaokao major choice, and a campus sustainability strand ('Waste Detectives', 'Is it really green?'). The wiki landing page is itself a piece of science communication built like a promotional video: a relatable domestic scene (face mask on the sofa), then the hidden cost, then the named molecule, then a hard cost-comparison table ($385/kg ectoine against $0.33-0.89/kg glycerin), then the two engineering modules, then the vision - concrete-consequence-first rather than mechanism-first. The award-winning promotion video itself is not embedded on the wiki, so only this narrative architecture can be verified here.","ihp":"A five-stage Aspiration -> Action -> Analysis -> Adaptation loop with documented project changes at each stage. Stage 1: a 397-response questionnaire on skincare habits and dryness (67.51% reported regular skincare routines, over 80% linked dryness to weather or environment), which narrowed the project from general skincare to barrier repair and widened the target user beyond naturally dry skin. Stage 2: interviews with students, parents, adult consumers, beauty retail staff and a facial-mask industry expert. Stage 3: technical feasibility with Nanjing Tech University researchers (Dr Huang Luming, Dr Fu Yangkai) and Tian Xiaodong of the Institute of Microbiology, CAS - this is where carbon/nitrogen optimisation and the upstream metabolic-engineering idea came from. Stage 4: a dermatologist, mask manufacturers and a cosmetic formulator set the boundaries of what the team could claim. Stage 5: farmers on wheat-straw supply, an environmental researcher on saline and fermentation wastewater risk, plus biosafety and commercialisation. Closes with a stakeholder impact map and reflection.","realWorld":"The project is framed end-to-end as a manufacturing-route substitution rather than a molecule demo: low-salt fermentation to cut corrosion and saline wastewater, agricultural residue as feedstock, in-house membrane production so the mask substrate is not a purchased black box, and a compostable end-of-life. Cost framing is explicit (ectoine at $385.46/kg against hyaluronic acid at $43-113/kg; reactor cost estimates of EUR 3,000/m3 for salt-resistant materials). Contributions are deliberately packaged for reuse: three registered parts with full Registry documentation (BBa_K5481012 acsAB-acsCD bacterial cellulose module, BBa_26XUR2FA LysC T352I, and an ectABC-lysC* composite), published game code, and a reusable questionnaire plus report framework for the women-in-STEM study. The Entrepreneurship page is unfilled template.","partners":["Nanjing Tech University (Dr Huang Luming, Dr Fu Yangkai)","Institute of Microbiology, Chinese Academy of Sciences (Tian Xiaodong)","iGEM team NBJF (shared educational website)","facial mask industry expert 'Director Jin' and mask manufacturers","dermatologist and cosmetic formulator","local wheat farmers","environmental researcher (saline/fermentation wastewater)","Nanjing Foreign Language School and six other Nanjing-area partner schools"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6236/wiki/description/img1-v2008.avif","caption":"The EcToBloom low-salt green manufacturing platform: engineered chassis, renewable feedstock, biosynthesised ectoine and biodegradable mask, ending in the three-layer BC-Silk-Ectoine repair mask.","credit":"Team ZQT-Nanjing, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6236/wiki/results/img1.avif","caption":"Roadmap of experimental results, annotating the titre reached at each stage: wild type 0.503 g/L, engineered strain 4.425 g/L, optimised medium 5.344 g/L, LysC T352I strain 6.852 g/L.","credit":"Team ZQT-Nanjing, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6236/wiki/human-practices/img17-v1126.avif","caption":"Stakeholder impact map closing the five-stage Human Practices loop, from consumers and retail staff to metabolic engineers, dermatologists, farmers and environmental researchers.","credit":"Team ZQT-Nanjing, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6236/wiki/education/img17.avif","caption":"'Synthetic Biology Laboratory', the team's purpose-built card game for high-school learners, whose code was published so other teams can modify and translate it.","credit":"Team ZQT-Nanjing, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Everything ZQT-Nanjing actually did on the dry side - replicated HPLC titres with error bars, single-factor medium screening, growth-versus-production curves, a 397-person survey and a genuinely excellent multi-age communication programme - is reachable by a motivated high-school team in one season, and it won the video award without a single line of modelling: their Model, Software, Measurement and Hardware pages are untouched template text. The limiting factor here is not compute or tooling but mentorship and framing: nobody appears to have suggested that even a two-ODE growth-and-product model or a simple cost model of the low-salt route would have cost a week and turned a strong wet-lab story into a complete one.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/zqt-nanjing/","https://2026.igem.wiki/zqt-nanjing/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/zqt-nanjing/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/zqt-nanjing/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/zqt-nanjing/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/zqt-nanjing/measurement","https://2026.igem.wiki/zqt-nanjing/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/zqt-nanjing/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/zqt-nanjing/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/zqt-nanjing/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/zqt-nanjing/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/zqt-nanjing/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/zqt-nanjing/parts"],"rank":33},"6242":{"team":"GCGS","id":"6242","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"Infectious Diseases, Therapeutics, Diagnostics & Oncology","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/gcgs/","projectTitle":"PathoLogic","tagline":"A dual-response engineered E. coli Nissle 1917 probiotic, delivered as an inhalable live biotherapeutic, that degrades Pseudomonas aeruginosa biofilm in cystic fibrosis lungs.","summary":"PathoLogic engineers E. coli Nissle 1917 into a living sensor that fires only when it detects two simultaneous signals of the cystic fibrosis airway — low iron (via Fur) and high C4-HSL quorum-sensing molecule from Pseudomonas aeruginosa (via RhlR) — wired as an AND gate. On dual activation, Lysis E lyses the cells to release alginate lyase, which degrades the alginate-based extracellular polymeric matrix that shields P. aeruginosa from antibiotics and immunity. The product concept is a spray-dried, matrix-protected inhalable live biotherapeutic positioned as an adjunct, not a replacement, for inhaled antibiotics. It won Best New Improved Part on a genuinely instructive two-cycle engineering story: adding SsrA degradation tags to RhlR killed the leakage but also killed the induction, and only replacing the weak wild-type Prhl with the engineered Prhl(LR) recovered a working sensor. The dry lab is the thinnest of the five high-school Top 10 teams; its strength is wet-lab characterisation discipline and an exceptionally thorough regulatory and stakeholder analysis.","awards":["Top 10 (High School)","Best New Improved Part — Winner (High School)","Best Presentation — Nominee (High School)","Best Wiki — Nominee (High School)","Best Village Project — Nominee (Infectious Diseases / Therapeutics / Diagnostics / Oncology)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"GCGS has no dedicated model or software page (both routes 404) and this is the clear weak point relative to the other four Top 10 high-school teams. The one modelling claim is a circuit-level simulation of the Fur-RhlR dual-response AND gate, which predicted that the low transcriptional activity of the native rhl promoter would prevent the full circuit from functioning — consistent with the 2016 Tokyo_Tech iGEM team's finding of weak native Prhl activity — and which therefore justified upgrading to the engineered Prhl(LR) (BBa_K1529310) in design cycle 2b. The simulation's structure, parameters, equations and software are not documented on the wiki, so it reads as a design-justification step rather than a reproducible model. No protein structure prediction, docking, molecular dynamics, flux analysis or machine learning appears anywhere on the wiki; the alginate lyase and Lysis E modules were taken from literature rather than computationally designed. Quantitative analysis is instead concentrated in assay-level fitting: the dual-response circuit's C4-HSL response under low-iron conditions was fitted by linear regression against log concentration (Y = 2.582X + 39.04, R2 = 0.894), yielding a limit of detection of 53.1 nM that the team mapped against physiologically relevant C4-HSL concentrations measured in clinical sputum, plus cross-reactivity testing against related signal molecules and a growth-curve validation in artificial lung fluid over 48 h showing the engineered strain remains viable with a moderate relative growth decrease on dual-signal stimulation, consistent with Lysis-E-driven conditional autolysis.","dataviz":"Figures are conventional but competently used and consistently paired with their physical source. The engineering and improve pages present AND-logic characterisation as four-condition bar panels, growth curves across the full C4-HSL dose gradient per construct with 8-hour endpoint comparisons and significance annotation, and a dedicated analytical-performance figure carrying the dose-response regression, limit of detection and cross-reactivity results together. Agarose gels, transformation plates, colony PCR and Sanger traces are shown for every construction step rather than asserted. The circuit designs are drawn side by side as 'existing part BBa_K2315014' against 'the improved part', so the specific change in each cycle is visible rather than described. Human practices and education present survey data as high-resolution chart figures (398 valid responses on the public survey). The landing page uses an animated scroll narrative structured as Sense / Respond / Restore to make the AND gate legible before any biology, and a dual-response system diagram carries the mechanism. There is no interactive or computational visualisation, no dashboard and no in-browser tool.","datascience":"The genuine intellectual contribution is a clean design-build-test-learn argument about a trade-off, which is a form of data reasoning even without computation. Cycle 2a fused four SsrA degradation tags (LAA, LVA, ASV, AAV, spanning a range of known degradation kinetics) to the C-terminus of RhlR on the wild-type Prhl, assembled all five constructs including the untagged control onto pTrc99k by homologous recombination, and ran 8-hour time-course dose-response experiments across blank, solvent-only, 10 micromolar, 100 micromolar and 1 mM C4-HSL in sequence-verified DH5-alpha. The result was interpreted carefully rather than selectively: growth curves showed only LAA suffered a small but significant final-density reduction (p < 0.05), consistent with its fastest protein turnover imposing extra proteolytic burden, while LVA, ASV and AAV showed no significant growth penalty — so the tags are not generally toxic. Fluorescence showed all tags reduced basal background as intended, but LAA, LVA and AAV lost induction so completely that no statistically significant difference remained between blank control and 1 mM C4-HSL, and only the moderate-rate ASV tag retained weak but distinguishable induction. The team drew the correct general conclusion: when a promoter's maximal transcriptional output is weak, the SsrA-driven degradation rate can exceed the synthesis rate, so tuning protein turnover cannot compensate for inadequate transcriptional capacity — background suppression and induced output cannot both be optimised from the degradation side alone. Cycle 2b tested that inference by swapping in Prhl(LR) and re-characterising the whole panel, identifying RhlR-SsrA-ASV-Prhl(LR) as the combination achieving both low leakage and robust induction, which was then integrated into the final AND gate. Human practices also drove a methodological change: because experts noted iron limitation varies across patient airways, characterisation was switched from a single fixed low-iron concentration to a dose-response design, and because the public survey flagged off-target activation concerns, low uninduced leakage became an explicit selection criterion rather than a nice-to-have.","software":"No software released and no software page. Contributions are biological and documentary: the optimised composite part pCon-RhlR-SsrA-ASV-Prhl(LR)-GFP (BBa_26QSD9SO) submitted to the Registry as a reusable C4-HSL biosensor for future teams, an improvement on the existing part BBa_K2315014 originally characterised by Shanghai_tech_2017, and a part collection page documenting the Fur and RhlR sensing modules, the Lysis E effector-release module and the alginate lyase cargo. Alginate lyase expression was confirmed at the theoretical ~42.2 kDa with supernatant and pellet fractionation. No repository link appears on the wiki for either code or hardware.","stack":["E. coli Nissle 1917 (EcN) chassis","E. coli DH5-alpha","pTrc99k backbone","homologous recombination assembly","Fur iron-responsive regulator","RhlR / Prhl and Prhl(LR) quorum-sensing promoter (BBa_K1529310)","SsrA ClpXP degradation tags (LAA / LVA / ASV / AAV)","Lysis E","alginate lyase","GFP reporter","artificial lung fluid model","linear regression dose-response fitting","circuit-level simulation (undocumented tooling)"],"techniques":["two-cycle design-build-test-learn with a documented trade-off","degradation-tag variant screening across a kinetic range","AND-gate logic characterisation across four input conditions","time-course dose-response with solvent and blank controls","limit-of-detection determination by log-linear regression","cross-reactivity testing against related signal molecules","growth-penalty control to separate toxicity from circuit effect","colony PCR and Sanger sequencing verification","SDS-PAGE with supernatant/pellet fractionation","physiologically-matched validation in artificial lung fluid","stakeholder-driven switch from fixed-concentration to dose-response characterisation"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Audience-segmented education from primary school through university students to industry professionals, governed by a self-designed GCGS reflective cycle (Gather information, Construct and conduct, Synthesize and sustain) applied after every activity, with the content depth and communication strategy varied per group. The distinguishing feature is a written ethics policy for rare disease communication, derived directly from expert advice rather than invented: person-first language, participants review any content referencing their stories before publication, no overly emotional narratives, no framing that implies patients are a burden, anonymity respected, and no fabricated data. A WeChat official account was launched in Chinese to serve the Chinese-speaking general public after the survey showed over 60% of respondents had never heard of cystic fibrosis and nearly half were unaware of the biofilm mechanism; it publishes rare-disease knowledge aimed at patients' psychological needs and gives patients a platform to connect and support each other, which is unusually thoughtful for a high-school outreach channel. Objectives are differentiated by tier — sparking curiosity in young students through hands-on activities, helping non-biology-major students grasp synthetic biology principles, reducing stigma through responsible communication with the public, and giving professionals and industry stakeholders technical and translational insight. Education strategy was explicitly treated as an output of the human practices work rather than a parallel track.","ihp":"Seven structured expert interviews plus a 398-response bilingual public survey, organised around a self-designed reflective model and reaching into regulation, manufacturing and finance rather than stopping at academia. The clearest documented change is a scope reduction the team accepted against its own interest: Dr. Guangquan Chen (Tongji University School of Medicine, with clinical and research experience in CF) gave candid feedback that the VOC diagnostic module, while feasible, was not innovative because existing research already confirms CF patients exhale characteristic VOCs without engineered bacteria. The team de-emphasised the VOC module, repositioned it as a future extension, and refocused entirely on biofilm degradation and antibiotic-adjuvant therapy. Dr. Ran An (Shanghai Jiao Tong University) identified four biosafety risks and ranked horizontal gene transfer highest; the team added a temperature-sensitive kill switch as a second containment layer on top of the existing mission-complete self-lysis system, and explicitly declined the pH-sensitive switch as technically challenging — a documented rejection with a reason, echoed independently by Dr. Xin Wang (Henan University of Technology), who noted insufficient pH difference inside and outside the body and pressed for multi-layered containment including auxotrophy against pulmonary over-colonisation, leakage to the digestive tract and horizontal gene transfer. Dr. Wang also raised that long-term antibiotic therapy already disrupts the CF lung microbiota and an engineered probiotic may interfere further, which the team adopted as a named safety endpoint: monitoring the impact of the engineered strain on respiratory microbial composition in future studies. Dr. An separately forced a positioning correction, stressing that the product must clearly present its adjunctive role because the biofilm is the target, not standalone infection treatment — language that now runs through the whole wiki. Dr. Baoshan Xu (Hospital of Stomatology, Sun Yat-sen University, rare genetic diseases) set the communication priority order as eliminating stigma first, building inclusion second, sharing disease knowledge third, and recommended person-first language, avoiding emotional narratives and letting patients review content, which became the education ethics policy. Two experimental design changes came from stakeholder input: dose-response characterisation across a low-iron gradient instead of a single fixed concentration, to reflect heterogeneous airway iron limitation between patients, and low uninduced leakage elevated to a critical selection criterion because the public survey showed off-target activation was a top concern. Commercial and regulatory engagement included Ms. Qing Yao (co-founder and chairwoman of Guangzhou Hanguang Pharmaceutical, a 25-year-old top-50 Chinese OTC pharmaceutical company), an anonymised biopharmaceutical R&D and industry strategy expert, HSBC investment and commercial banking professionals, Prof. Tao Wei (Guangdong Shaohe Biotechnology and South China Agricultural University, computational biology) and Dr. Huihui Bao (China National Center for Food Safety Risk Assessment).","realWorld":"A rare-disease market analysis grounded in Chinese reimbursement reality rather than global TAM arithmetic. CF is in China's First Rare Disease Catalog (2018), was once considered extremely rare in Asian populations at roughly 1 in 32,000 births against 1 in 3,300 in Caucasian populations, and is severely under-diagnosed — reported Chinese cases in the past decade reached 2.5 times the total reported in the preceding thirty years, with current estimates possibly exceeding 20,000 patients. Over 78% of adult CF patients develop chronic P. aeruginosa infection. The unmet need is stated precisely: no approved therapy directly targets and degrades the biofilm matrix, inhaled antibiotics cannot penetrate it, airway clearance improves symptoms without eliminating pathogens, and CFTR modulators (elexacaftor/tezacaftor/ivacaftor) work only for specific genotypes, are expensive and cannot reverse established structural lung damage. The access model follows expert advice that rare disease drugs do not need broad distribution: regional CF diagnosis and treatment centres and expert networks are the efficient channel, with respiratory physicians at those centres as the prescribing decision-makers. Payer analysis is survey-grounded — over 90% of respondents preferred public or collective payment, with 51.26% supporting rare disease funds combined with charity and 40.45% supporting national insurance against only about 8% for self-pay — and expert input that commercial insurers show limited willingness to cover rare diseases led the team to prioritise the National Healthcare Security Administration and local rare disease funds. They identify that few inhaled live biotherapeutic products have been approved for clinical use in China, so the regulatory and clinical pathway is genuinely unclear, and name long-term platform expansion to other chronic P. aeruginosa lung infections such as COPD and bronchiectasis. The product form is a spray-dried, matrix-protected EcN formulation designed to reach deep lung tissue.","partners":["Dr. Ran An, Shanghai Jiao Tong University (gut microbiota regulation, biosafety)","Dr. Xin Wang, Henan University of Technology (synthetic biology, enzyme engineering, formulation)","Dr. Baoshan Xu, Hospital of Stomatology, Sun Yat-sen University (rare genetic diseases, communication ethics)","Dr. Guangquan Chen, Tongji University School of Medicine (CF genetics and molecular diagnostics)","Ms. Qing Yao, Guangzhou Hanguang Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","Prof. Tao Wei, Guangdong Shaohe Biotechnology / South China Agricultural University","Dr. Huihui Bao, China National Center for Food Safety Risk Assessment","HSBC (investment and commercial banking professionals)","An anonymised biopharmaceutical R&D and industry strategy expert","Shanghai_tech_2017 iGEM team (origin of improved part BBa_K2315014)","Tokyo_Tech 2016 iGEM team (native Prhl activity finding)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6242/wiki/improve/figure-1.avif","caption":"The modification strategy for the RhlR response system across both improvement cycles: SsrA degradation tags on RhlR, then replacement of wild-type Prhl with the engineered Prhl(LR).","credit":"Team GCGS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6242/wiki/improve/ssra-tag-circuit-replacement.avif","caption":"Genetic circuit designs compared: the existing Registry part BBa_K2315014 against the improved RhlR-SsrA tag construct built in cycle 2b.","credit":"Team GCGS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6242/wiki/engineering/analytical-performance.avif","caption":"Analytical performance of the Fur-RhlR dual-response circuit: C4-HSL dose-response under low iron fitted as Y = 2.582X + 39.04 (R2 = 0.894), giving a limit of detection of 53.1 nM, with cross-reactivity results.","credit":"Team GCGS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6242/wiki/ihp/survey-figure-8-high-resolution.avif","caption":"Public survey results on synthetic biology awareness and attitudes (398 valid responses): 30% had heard only the term and 27% had never heard of synthetic biology or genetically engineered bacteria, while 50% viewed it as a valuable technology requiring strict ethical review and safety oversight.","credit":"Team GCGS, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Copy the engineering logic, and read the gap as a warning. Their transferable asset is a two-cycle DBTL that isolates a real trade-off — SsrA tags cut leakage but, on a weak promoter, degradation outruns synthesis and kill induction too, so you must raise transcriptional capacity rather than keep tuning turnover — plus the discipline of running a growth-curve control so a signal loss cannot be mistaken for toxicity. The warning is that GCGS reached High School Top 10 with essentially no model or software page, and it is the one clear hole in an otherwise strong wiki: a modest, fully documented ODE model of their own AND gate, with parameters and code, would have cost little and closed it.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/gcgs/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gcgs/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gcgs/improve/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gcgs/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gcgs/results/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gcgs/part-collection/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gcgs/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gcgs/education/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gcgs/entrepreneurship/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gcgs/contribution/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gcgs/notebook/"],"rank":117},"6243":{"team":"William-and-Mary","id":"6243","section":"Undergrad","country":"United States","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/william-and-mary/","projectTitle":"BROKEN: Building Resilient Optimized Engineered Networks","tagline":"Bringing failure analysis from mature engineering disciplines into synthetic biology: detect, mitigate and predict how genetic circuits break.","summary":"William & Mary argued that synthetic biology measures whether a circuit works and almost never measures how long it keeps working. BROKEN therefore ran longitudinal experiments on four previously engineered circuits in laboratory cultures and in seawater microcosms, following them through serial passaging to deterioration rather than stopping at initial success. The team paired functional readouts (OD600, beta-carotene production, GFP, biofilm morphology, starch hydrolysis, colony-forming units) with molecular verification (PCR, restriction digests, gels, NanoDrop) and with multi-omics (RNA-seq, genomic DNA sequencing, long-read plasmid sequencing), then built mechanistic ODE models and machine-learning approaches to predict time to failure. The reliability framing came directly from Integrated Human Practices and turned safety into the project's central motivation, which is reflected in its Safety and Security Award.","awards":["Best Measurement — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Presentation — Nominee (Undergrad)","Safety and Security Award — Winner (Undergrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A stated measurement philosophy of multitiered (population, circuit output, viability, DNA integrity, transcription), multimodal (optical, biochemical, microbiological, sequencing) and redundant measurement, with the explicit rationale that a falling fluorescence signal could equally mean circuit dysfunction, reduced growth, altered reporter maturation or changed physiology. An extension of the standard Design-Build-Test-Learn cycle so that engineering does not end at a functioning construct but continues through systematic longevity and failure testing in both laboratory and realistic environmental conditions, with results feeding back into design.","dataviz":"Longitudinal fluorescence and beta-carotene time-course figures, kill-switch and thymineless-death assay panels, DNA mutation tables for the corrosion-prevention construct, leakiness panels and circuit-expression comparisons across experiments, all numbered as a continuous figure series across the results and measurement pages.","datascience":"The headline measurement contribution is absolute-style fluorescence calibration: the team prepared concentration series of fluorescein and sulforhodamine 101 in PBS, measured four replicates at each concentration with PBS blanks to assess solvent background, fitted linear regressions of fluorophore concentration against RFU with reported R2 greater than 0.99, and then used published extinction coefficients and quantum yields to estimate conversion factors between the calibration dyes and S65T GFP, mKate2, mCherry and cpGFP, so that plate-reader readings could enter the mathematical models as concentration-like variables instead of instrument-dependent arbitrary units. They state the limitation plainly, that because dye and protein optical properties differ these conversions are estimates contingent on the correction factors. Normalisation is handled explicitly: beta-carotene is reported as A454/OD600 so that per-cell production is separated from cell number, uncontaminated LB is measured as a blank, and OD600 is used both to standardise serial transfers and to interpret every fluorescence comparison. Where optical turbidity cannot answer the biological question, the technique changes: CFU counts are used for kill-switch viability and for thymineless death and rescue, on the advice of Dr Andrei Kuzminov, with plating on thymidine-supplemented medium so that the assay does not itself impose further starvation. Reporter maturation delay was built into measurement timing after Dr Sean Sleight pointed out that a delay in fluorescence is not a delay in transcription. The RNA-seq pipeline is specified end to end: fastp for adapter trimming and quality filtering, SortMeRNA for residual rRNA removal, HISAT2 alignment against combined host-plus-plasmid references built as merged FASTA and GFF files, featureCounts for gene-level assignment and DESeq2 for differential expression; genome assemblies from Plasmidsaurus were annotated with Bakta in Geneious Prime and variant tables exported. Modelling carries uncertainty properly: SciPy least-squares fits of the lambda-repressor model give R2 = 0.82 and chi2/dof = 0.88 at 30 C, and the team reports that the 42 C prediction degrades to R2 = 0.55 with chi2/dof = 7.57, six to eight times worse than the in-sample value and therefore larger than measurement noise explains, rather than presenting the prediction as validated. A light-responsive fit is reported as poor at the assumed error (chi2/dof = 4.7, p = 0.0009) with the specific failure described (the dark curve fits, the light curve is flat then bursts). Because the labelled dataset is tiny (N = 16), model selection uses leave-one-out and leave-one-series-out rather than a train/test split, with benchmarking across OLS, Ridge, Lasso, Elastic Net, random forest and Gaussian process; Ridge on circuit fraction plus stress genes gives leave-one-out R2 = 0.61, and a classifier reaches AUC 0.880 and accuracy 0.830, both reported with the caveat that 16 samples cannot establish a general predictor.","software":"All modelling and analysis code is published with documentation on the team's iGEM GitLab, with instructions for both terminal use and a web interface. A Guidebook for Circuit Failure Measurement is released as a PDF, offering a tiered approach scaled to a laboratory's budget, from accessible functional assays through molecular diagnostics to sequencing and multi-omics. Longitudinal RNA-seq and DNA-seq datasets are released for the community, paired with functional, growth and viability measurements so that molecular change can be linked to observed performance. The hardware, software, alternative-platform and entrepreneurship wiki pages remain unfilled iGEM templates.","stack":["fastp","SortMeRNA","HISAT2","featureCounts","DESeq2","Bakta","Geneious Prime","Plasmidsaurus (Oxford Nanopore long-read)","SciPy (least_squares)","scikit-learn-style regression benchmarking","Plate reader fluorescence and OD600","Flow-cytometry-free CFU viability"],"techniques":["Fluorescein and sulforhodamine 101 calibration curves (R2 > 0.99)","Dye-to-protein conversion factors via extinction coefficient and quantum yield","OD600 normalisation and blank subtraction","A454/OD600 product normalisation","CFU viability in place of turbidity","Reporter maturation-aware timing","Longitudinal serial passaging to a failure endpoint","Seawater microcosm environmental testing","chi2/dof goodness of fit","Leave-one-out and leave-one-series-out validation","Model benchmarking on a fixed small dataset"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"","ihp":"Integrated Human Practices reframed the project three times over. Contributors from aerospace, civil and electrical engineering backgrounds pushed the team to adopt not only the methods of failure engineering but its mindset, that failure should be anticipated and designed for rather than observed after the fact. The most consequential shift was the recognition that circuit failure is a biosafety problem, not a performance problem, which moved safety from a secondary consideration to the central motivation and underpins the team's Safety and Security Award. Technical guidance entered the DBTL cycle directly: Dr Alex Porter pressed the team on the gap between laboratory performance and behaviour under realistic environmental conditions, which produced the seawater microcosm experiments; Dr Sean Sleight raised fluorescent-protein maturation, which changed measurement timing; and Dr Andrei Kuzminov argued that OD600 and fluorescence could not measure survival during thymineless death, which replaced the planned readout with CFU-based viability.","realWorld":"The project's deliverables are aimed at the field rather than at a product: an open-source set of standard operating protocols written so that someone who was not present can follow them, a tiered Guidebook for Circuit Failure Measurement scaled to different budgets, publicly released longitudinal multi-omics datasets for comparative failure analysis and model validation, and a proposed extension of DBTL that adds systematic longevity and failure testing. The team also models building on previously published circuits rather than treating initial characterisation as an endpoint, and frames kill switches and other safety-critical circuits as the components that most need the failure analysis mature engineering disciplines already apply.","partners":["Dr Alex J. Porter","Dr Sean Sleight","Dr Andrei Kuzminov","Plasmidsaurus"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6243/wiki/figures/figure1-betacarotene-assay.avif","caption":"Beta-carotene assay following circuit output over serial passaging. Absorbance at 454 nm is normalised to OD600 so that a fall in total pigment can be separated from a fall in cell number.","credit":"Team William-and-Mary, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6243/wiki/figures/figure3-killswitch-assay.avif","caption":"Kill-switch assay. Colony-forming unit counts before and after induction are used instead of OD600 or fluorescence, because the intended output of a kill switch is loss of viability rather than loss of reporter signal.","credit":"Team William-and-Mary, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6243/wiki/figures/figure10-thymineless-rescue.avif","caption":"Thymineless rescue measured by CFU on thymidine-supplemented medium, an assay design adopted after Dr Andrei Kuzminov advised that optical density and fluorescence would not measure survival directly.","credit":"Team William-and-Mary, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6243/wiki/figures/fig11-hd260828-gfp-fluorescence-timecourse.avif","caption":"GFP fluorescence time course for an engineered construct. Raw plate-reader RFU values are converted toward concentration-like units using fluorescein and sulforhodamine 101 calibration curves (R2 > 0.99) before entering the mathematical models.","credit":"Team William-and-Mary, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Calibrate fluorescence against a dye concentration series before any number leaves the plate reader, and report model fits with chi2/dof against the measurement error rather than R2 alone, so that an out-of-sample prediction that is six times worse than the in-sample fit is visible as a failure instead of being dressed up as a moderate correlation.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/william-and-mary/measurement","https://2026.igem.wiki/william-and-mary/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/william-and-mary/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/william-and-mary/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/william-and-mary/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/william-and-mary/engineering"],"rank":40},"6244":{"team":"QingdaoAcademy","id":"6244","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/qingdaoacademy/","projectTitle":"UPKeep","tagline":"From green tides to new possibilities: enzymes that turn collected Ulva into sugars for further biological use.","summary":"QingdaoAcademy (Qingdao, Shandong) built UPKeep around the Ulva prolifera green tides that wash onto the Yellow Sea coast each summer. Stage 1 uses a free, configurable cellulosome - four enzyme modules (Cel9A, Cel6B, Cel9B-N, BglC) docked onto a CBM3a-bearing scaffoldin via cohesin-dockerin pairs - to open the cellulose-rich cell wall; Stage 2 applies an INPNC-Uly1040 ulvan lyase fusion to depolymerise ulvan into oligosaccharides proposed as a cosmetic moisturising ingredient. Containment is an iron-responsive Fur/ccdB-TetR/ccdA toxin-antitoxin circuit, modelled as a 13-state ODE system, while interface selection rests on a 25-pair AlphaFold 3 screen with HADDOCK and PRODIGY follow-up. The Human Practices work is unusually well engineered for a first-year high-school team: thirteen numbered design decisions, each with the stakeholder, what was said, what changed and the follow-up evidence.","awards":["Best New Basic Part — Nominee (High School)","Best Sustainable Development Impact — Nominee (High School)","Best Village Project — Nominee (Agriculture / Food & Nutrition / Fashion & Cosmetics / Art & Design)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Two linked models. (1) Cellulosome recognition: all 25 cohesin-dockerin pairings screened with AlphaFold Server (AF3), two protein chains plus two calcium ions per request, seed 101, five outputs each - 125 structures - ranked by five-output mean protein-pair ipTM with bidirectional interchain PAE, interface contacts and pose spread examined; seven pairs (the five intended A-a, B-b, C-c, F-f, T-t plus the two highest-scoring mismatches B-c and T-b) taken through HADDOCK refinement and PRODIGY affinity estimation against the native 1OHZ reference. (2) Iron-responsive containment: a 13-state ODE model (sensed intracellular iron, Fur RNA, total and iron-bound Fur, shared ccdB/TetR transcript, TetR, ccdA RNA, free CcdB, free CcdA, inactive complex, a damage proxy, log population and log survival) in hours, used to study response delay after iron withdrawal or restoration, how the iron threshold shifts with the chosen endpoint, and which parameters dominate that threshold.","dataviz":"Matplotlib-generated SVG figures throughout: an LCA climate comparison separating enzymatic gross emissions, the residue-substitution credit and the net result across three scenarios; log-axis water and energy comparisons; a 25x25 ipTM heat matrix with the intended diagonal outlined and the two mismatch candidates highlighted in orange; predicted Kd on a logarithmic axis with per-model dots and cluster spans; interactive 3D structure viewers with a pLDDT colour mode; a stakeholder influence-versus-impact map and an SDG interaction map, both downloadable as SVG and PNG; survey charts transcribed from original screenshots with each question's own denominator retained.","datascience":"Reproducibility is treated as a deliverable: submitted sequences, AF3 requests, structures, a configuration-status manifest, per-model metrics for all 125 AF3 structures and all 25 pair summaries are downloadable as JSON, with official page snapshots, plain-text logs and parsed values archived under a result-snapshots directory and task/cluster filenames linking models to local inputs. HADDOCK scores are reconstructed from saved energy terms with the default weighting (Evdw + 0.2 Eelec + Edesolv + 0.1 Eair) and reported as mean +/- population SD over four cluster representatives. Pose uncertainty is quantified rather than hidden (mean/max pairwise dockerin Ca RMSD after cohesin alignment of about 10.99/17.76 A for T-t), and the team notes that B-b and B-c Kd ranges overlap with median dG differing by 0.05 kcal/mol, so cross-binding must be tested experimentally rather than declared resolved. A process LCA on a basis of 1 t fresh Ulva at 90% moisture gives 34 kWh, 8,800 L water and 264 kg CO2e gross, with a residue-substitution credit sweep (0-1 kg soybean meal displaced per kg theoretical remaining dry matter) producing a 34.4-264 kg CO2e/t net range; a literature-based nutrient conversion gives 18-54 kg N and 2.5-9.2 kg P per dry tonne.","software":"No standalone software tool. Dry-lab outputs are the AF3/HADDOCK/PRODIGY screening archive, the ODE reconstruction (independently re-derived from the report's equations and parameter tables on 20 October 2026, with added parameter stress tests), the LCA and nutrient-accounting workbooks, the downloadable activity-classification CSV, and an AP242 STEP CAD assembly of the Ulva collection ROV exported from Onshape.","stack":["AlphaFold Server (AF3)","HADDOCK","PRODIGY","molecular 3D viewer with pLDDT colouring","ODE integration with sensitivity and parameter stress tests","Matplotlib v3.11.2","Onshape (AP242 STEP export)","Wenjuanxing online survey platform"],"techniques":["interface screening by ipTM, interchain PAE and contact analysis","docking refinement and binding-affinity estimation","cross-binding and selectivity risk identification","13-state ODE dynamics, threshold and sensitivity analysis","scenario life-cycle assessment with substitution credits","nitrogen and phosphorus material-flow accounting","colony-PCR template-preparation comparison (direct colony vs 2/10 suspension vs liquid culture)","moisture-uptake gravimetry under controlled humidity and hydroxyl-radical scavenging assay"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Engagement was sequenced on survey evidence rather than instinct: of 259 respondents 228 had at least heard of Ulva (88.03%) but only 34 claimed familiarity, and 142 of 263 knew little or nothing about synthetic biology (53.99%), so the booklet starts with everyday coastal effects and existing post-collection uses before engineered bacteria, surface display or cellulosomes appear at all. A harbour interviewee's remark that online video would reach people better than a poster at the pier redirected the channel strategy to short videos on Bilibili, Xiaohongshu, Douyin and WeChat Channels. A joint activity with OUC-Haide (the 17-C collaboration) was cross-checked before delivery and two content errors - a pH item and an mRNA pairing error - were found and corrected, with simulations, three-level hints and a reset path added. Continued participation runs through the school biology club and repeated lessons rather than one-off events, and the team keeps SDG 4 targets 4.4 and 4.7 separate from its claims about measured learning.","ihp":"Twenty-two HP activities across six activity types are compressed into a register of thirteen numbered decisions (D01-D13), each naming the stakeholder, the quote, the change and the follow-up record - and several of them killed the team's favourite ideas. D02 is the clearest: the team wanted one system in which E. coli produced enzymes and degraded Ulva in a single reaction, but Seawin's Technical Director explained that cells and different enzymes each need their own temperature, pH and nutrient conditions, and Vland's Chief Scientist added that cells themselves generate metabolic acid, so the one-step process was split into separate cell-culture and enzyme-reaction steps and the planned pH-based function switch was abandoned entirely (D03). D04 came from peer pressure plus specialist correction: CCiC judges and teams flagged the expression burden of an extracellular cell-anchored cellulosome, and a Shanxi University doctoral researcher warned against loading too many cohesins onto one scaffoldin because of cleavage risk, so the team moved to a free cellulosome, accepting extraction and purification as explicit tasks, and planned separate expression followed by assembly. D05 is an honest unresolved tension rather than a tidy win: the cellulosome researcher supported adding BglC to hydrolyse accumulating cellobiose while Vland warned that glucose would then inhibit downstream, so the enzyme was retained with the trade-off written into the reaction-condition study. D06 dismantled the CBS-inspired shortcut of feeding hydrolysate straight into culture - Bright Moon pressed on carbon, nitrogen and aeration and Vland demanded composition analysis and experimental validation, so growth and enzyme production became separately measured questions, later yielding the observation that at pH 7 a 40% hydrolysate medium supported growth and target-protein expression with a longer lag phase. D07 is the strongest stakeholder-to-design chain: a beauty-salon manager said she would hesitate to trust Qingdao Ulva as a raw material because of possible pollution, which the team carried into a joint consultation with Professors Ning Wu and Jing Wang at the Institute of Oceanology, CAS, where contamination resolved into two concrete, separately measurable requirements - seaweed's high salt content means inadequate desalting could cause osmotic imbalance on skin, so ultrafiltration desalting and concentration entered the sample-preparation plan, and because E. coli is the production host, endotoxin must be specifically measured and controlled for higher-end or damaged-skin use. Biosafety specialist Prof. Zhihang Chen then converted an end-stage pair of controls (heat treatment plus a kill switch) into process-wide control, separating live cells, nucleic acids and endotoxin, each with its own treatment and assessment target, and prompting work on ClearColi and Rosetta chassis compatibility. D08 had Gather Great Ocean puncture the assumption that a mature brown-seaweed business implies a market for ulvan oligosaccharides - its Ulva powder goes to aquaculture feed, and it told the team to first establish what advantage ulvan oligosaccharides have over other materials - which sent them to the two professors for assay methods they could actually run (moisture uptake by desiccator and balance, in vitro antioxidant assays) and added molecular-weight profiling after the 500 Da skin-penetration literature. D13 reframed feedstock itself: the Yellow Sea Fisheries Research Institute separated ecological abundance, visible shoreline biomass and what a processor can reliably obtain, and added sand removal, dewatering and acquisition cost, so the team retained a reduced-supply scenario instead of assuming continued large blooms. Even packaging was corrected - YUTOECO's engineering manager said the proposal was still too broad, so inner contact packaging is now specified around sealing, barrier and storage needs and only the outer layer explores moulded plant fibre.","realWorld":"The real-world case is anchored in the existing Qingdao system rather than in a waste narrative: harbour workers, the Municipal Marine Development Bureau and processors described coordinated pier collection, dewatering and drying, trucking to downstream companies, feed and fertiliser uses and decayed material returned to sea - so the team compares four handling routes on cost, product value and nutrient destination and positions UPKeep as an added high-value step, noting Gather Great Ocean's blunt 'there is no waste material'. SDGs are claimed at target level with the team's own numbers: SDG 12 (12.2, 12.5, 12.6, 12.8) carries the LCA, with the enzymatic scenario at 264 kg CO2e/t gross and about 35 kg CO2e/t net when each kg of remaining dry matter displaces 1 kg of soybean meal at 2.75 kg CO2e/kg, 34 kWh/t against 389 kWh/t for the feed-meal route, and 8,800 L/t water driven chiefly by membrane diafiltration; SDG 14 (14.1, 14.2) carries nitrogen and phosphorus accounting to final destination and marine-ecology consultation; SDG 9 (9.4) the process and enzyme-recovery work; SDG 3 (3.9) storage, odour and coastal handling exposure; SDG 4 (4.4, 4.7) education; and SDG 8 (8.2, 8.8) worker protection and cost responsibility. The SDG dialogue partner was Professor Pierre Failler (Economics, University of Portsmouth), whose advice - 'do the economics first, and don't mix the concepts' and 'doing a single project on its own is very difficult, you need a cluster model' - made the team keep the business plan and the LCA as separate documents. The most concrete real-world act is not a product: after Hongdao interviews about slippery coastal working conditions, on 6 October 2026 the team filed a proposal through Qingdao's 12319 public-service platform requesting anti-slip footwear and gloves for frontline sanitation workers, and received an official reply on 9 October describing purchase and distribution of anti-slip equipment, safety reminders, site inspection and weather-based adjustment of operations; the remotely operated Ulva collection vehicle (a 648 x 462 x 419 mm PVC-framed ROV with a forward nylon-mesh basket, published as an AP242 STEP model) is justified on the same worker-exposure grounds. Entrepreneurship is deliberately modest - the first offer is an oligosaccharide research sample plus production route, assay results and a proposed quality-information sheet to cosmetic ingredient developers, with a cream-base-versus-cream-plus-ingredient demonstrator, revenue only after formulation qualification, and cost priorities named as enzyme production and recovery, purification, drying, batch quality and packaging. Regulatory status is not claimed anywhere; residue destined for fertiliser is explicitly excluded where it contains engineered cells, and no packaging prototype has been made.","partners":["Qingdao Municipal Marine Development Bureau","Hongdao fishing harbour fishers, boat operators, coastal sanitation workers and residents","Seawin Biotech (Technical Director, two consultations)","Vland Biotech (Chief Scientist, two consultations)","Bright Moon Seaweed Group (company visit and R&D consultation)","Qingdao Gather Great Ocean Algae Industry Group","Yellow Sea Fisheries Research Institute, Chinese Academy of Fishery Sciences","Professors Ning Wu and Jing Wang, Institute of Oceanology, Chinese Academy of Sciences","Prof. Zhihang Chen (biosafety)","Cellulosome researcher, Shanxi University","Professor Pierre Failler, University of Portsmouth (SDG consultation, 20 October 2026)","YUTOECO / YUTO (packaging engineering)","iGEM OUC-Haide (17-C collaboration)","CCiC conference and Unconference participants","A student and a beauty salon manager (prospective skincare users)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6244/wiki/engagement/qa-8fac1d1be36d-hp01-8fac1d1be3.avif","caption":"HP01: interviews at Hongdao fishing harbour with fishers, boat operators, coastal sanitation workers and residents, which corrected the team's assumption that the Ulva utilisation chain was undeveloped.","credit":"Team QingdaoAcademy, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6244/wiki/engagement/qa-38a681455267-hp03-38a6814552.avif","caption":"HP03: consultation with the Qingdao Municipal Marine Development Bureau on existing collection, transport and post-collection handling, used to locate the project's point of entry.","credit":"Team QingdaoAcademy, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6244/wiki/engagement/qa-2a0007cd5e6a-hp12-2a0007cd5e.avif","caption":"HP12: joint consultation with Professors Ning Wu and Jing Wang at the Institute of Oceanology, CAS, where a user's contamination worry became separate desalting and endotoxin requirements.","credit":"Team QingdaoAcademy, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6244/wiki/engagement/qa-74aa66d13ac0-hp16a-74aa66d13a.avif","caption":"HP16: visit to Bright Moon Seaweed, whose R&D staff redirected the team's effort onto enzyme selection and ratios and onto membrane separation and sample condition.","credit":"Team QingdaoAcademy, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Keep a numbered decision register like UPKeep's D01-D13, where each row is initial idea / stakeholders / what we heard / what we changed / why it matters, cross-linked to the interview record and to the experiment that tests the change - including rows where two advisers disagreed and the tension was retained rather than resolved. Their second habit is worth copying too: push a vague public worry ('Ulva might be polluted') to experts until it becomes separately measurable specifications (desalting, endotoxin, DNA residue, live-cell viability).","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/qingdaoacademy/","https://2026.igem.wiki/qingdaoacademy/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/qingdaoacademy/sustainability","https://2026.igem.wiki/qingdaoacademy/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/qingdaoacademy/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/qingdaoacademy/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/qingdaoacademy/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/qingdaoacademy/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/qingdaoacademy/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/qingdaoacademy/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/qingdaoacademy/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/qingdaoacademy/team"],"rank":21},"6245":{"team":"ABOA","id":"6245","section":"Overgrad","country":"Finland","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/aboa/","projectTitle":"Benzophe-none","tagline":"Degrading benzophenone-3 before it reaches our waters","summary":"ABOA (University of Turku) set out to express the benzophenone-3 (BP-3, oxybenzone) catabolic pathway of Rhodococcus oxybenzonivorans in E. coli so that this sunscreen UV filter could be destroyed inside a wastewater treatment plant rather than released into the Baltic and the oceans. The team built a modular restriction-based plasmid system (10 plasmids, 10 genes covering four pathway steps, codon-optimised and RFC10/RFC1000 compatible) that lets homologous flavin reductases and flavin-dependent oxidoreductases be co-expressed, separated, swapped and re-tagged between 6xHis and GST using only NcoI, NdeI and XhoI. Enzyme expression and solubility were obtained to varying degrees, but the activity question was not resolved: BP-3 and BP-1 absorbance overlaps NADH so the spectrophotometric assay was inconclusive, and the triple-quadrupole LC-MS run failed on missing controls and incompatible vials. The team says this plainly and positions the work as a first step plus a designed-but-untested 28-part Golden Gate system (38 parts in total) handed to the community.","awards":["Best Sustainable Development Impact — Nominee (Overgrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"No modelling framework. The /model, /software and /hardware pages are unfilled iGEM template stubs carrying only the award description text, which is worth stating plainly: this project has essentially no dry-lab component.","dataviz":"Hand-drawn schematic figures only: the proposed R. oxybenzonivorans catabolic pathway, the plasmid map set, the LC-MS detection strategy, the Golden Gate assembly map, and a single process diagram running from the Golden Gate construct to a fixed-carrier bioreactor at the end of a wastewater plant. Survey results are reported as percentages in prose rather than plotted.","datascience":"A 136-response consumer survey on sunscreen habits and environmental awareness (93% use sunscreen regularly; 68% say environmental friendliness influences purchase; 57% aware some sunscreen ingredients harm the environment; 52% read ingredient lists; 52% believe sunscreen slows tanning but only 9% skip it for that reason; 70% would protect their skin over the environment if forced to choose). Percentages are honestly computed per question because response counts varied. No statistical modelling.","software":"None. Sequence work was done with off-the-shelf tools: NCBI protein BLAST to find Rhodococcus homologues of every proposed pathway enzyme, Benchling for the Golden Gate overhang design and SnapGene for visualising the final construct.","stack":["NCBI protein BLAST","Benchling","SnapGene"],"techniques":["homologue search across Rhodococcus strains (USK10, USK13, R. jostii, R. oxybenzonivorans)","codon optimisation for E. coli","RFC10 / RFC1000 part compatibility","Golden Gate overhang design (BsaI, six positions A-F in pET28g)","NADH-coupled activity assay","triple-quadrupole LC-MS method adaptation"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A 136-person anonymous survey on sunscreen habits collected at public events and on social media, designed both to gather data and to raise awareness; it was later used to shape the team's social posts. Secondary-school visits with age-split formats (project pitch plus a Kahoot on synthetic biology fundamentals for upper secondary; a hands-on osmosis experiment for lower secondary), with a return invitation and a further school event booked for after the Jamboree. A red-cabbage pH indicator workshop for primary-school children at Turku main library during Turku Day, linked out to ocean acidification. A joint appearance with Aalto-Helsinki at Children's Medical Day at the Heureka Science Centre (22 August 2026) running three workshops, where the team also collected survey responses. An article about the project and about iGEM in the magazine of Suomen Solubiologit ry (the Finnish cell biologists' association), with a follow-up article agreed for after the Jamboree. A laboratory visit by science journalist Ritva Setala and photographer Marttiina Sairanen from the regional newspaper Turun Sanomat. Recruitment-oriented booths at the Study in Turku fair and the TYY Opening Carnival with Aboa Turku ry, where the team deliberately worked against first-year students' sense that an international synthetic biology competition is beyond them.","ihp":"ABOA's integrated human practices is genuinely integrated on the technical side and well-documented in method: previous ABOA teams advised contacting stakeholders before the project idea was fixed, and the team set a rule that every meeting had a written objective beforehand and a debrief afterwards whose notes fed project decisions. The strongest single causal chain runs through the Turku wastewater treatment plant. Process engineer Jouko Tuomi, with trainees Nea Lempiainen and Heli Karinkanta, told them that purified enzymes are too delicate and expensive to run in a plant, that enzyme activity decays, and that whole cells on fixed carriers in a flow-through bioreactor are what the activated sludge process already does well - and the team changed its implementation from purified enzymes to intact cells as a result, then built a Golden Gate system specifically to put all pathway enzymes into one cell. The same conversation produced three further changes: they dropped the idea of inoculating their strain into the activated sludge itself because the plant warned it would wreck the existing microbial balance for months and their strain would simply be out-competed; they moved the bioreactor to the end of the treatment train after filtration, with coagulation and UV kill as the existing backstop; and they took up the plant's suggestion of treating a concentrated side stream rather than the whole flow, since influent BP-3 is too dilute to treat economically. The plant also told them that in Finland plants operate underground so mining new space costs tens of millions of euros and changes are made essentially only when law requires them, and that efficiency ranks above cost in technology selection - which is why the team's own staging plan is wastewater-sample testing, then a small on-site test station, then integration. A second chain runs through the construct design: Dr. Rongbin Wang's explanation that BioBrick parts cannot cleanly build in-frame fusion proteins or swap purification tags made the team abandon the BioBrick route entirely for expression-ready plasmids modified with standard restriction enzymes; Dr. Jarmo Kapyla's point that neither His- nor GST-tag performance can be predicted made them commit to testing both experimentally with His as primary and GST as backup, and also told them colony PCR is insufficient verification (they could not afford sequencing primers and say so, recommending sequencing for the next stage); Dr. Tuomas Huovinen supplied concrete expression parameters they adopted (200 mL culture to OD600 0.8, 0.4 mM IPTG, 26 C post-induction, 16 h), the Western blot with HRP-conjugated anti-6xHis antibodies to see proteins SDS-PAGE could not, and electroporation to fix poor heat-shock transformation. A third chain is about not making the problem worse: Dr. Timo Vuorisalo (ecology) told them to check whether the pathway intermediates might themselves be endocrine disruptors, so they searched the ECHA ED Expert Group assessment list and found none of the intermediates listed; Professor Tuulia Hyotylainen (exposomes, Orebro) confirmed that degrading one aromatic ring is very likely to abolish the endocrine activity, which validated attacking only the early pathway steps, and warned that wastewater conditions will be far less favourable than the lab bench; Professor Emma Camp (Future Reefs, UTS) added that the bacteria must be tested under realistic wastewater conditions and contained, and that BP-3 is one stressor among many on reefs rather than the main one. Harri Helminen of the Finnish supervisory agency confirmed UV filters are among the top five endocrine disruptors of concern in water ecosystems, told them no comprehensive BP-3 measurement exists for Finnish waters, explained that Environmental Quality Standards are set 100-1000 times below the lowest concentration with observed biological effect, and placed BP-3 within the revised EU Urban Waste Water Treatment Directive (in force 2025, requirements generally expected by 2036, 80% micropollutant removal) - which is the regulatory anchor for the whole project. Health-side consultations changed emphasis rather than engineering: Merike Laine of the Helsinki Allergy and Asthma Association said UV filters are less prominent allergens than fragrances and preservatives, so the team deliberately de-emphasised skin reactions, and dermatologist Dr. Susanna Majasuo prompted them to research why BP-3 is already regulated and to add a comparison of alternative UV filters, which they did, and to run the consumer survey. Cosmetic manufacturer Dermosil explained that the industry has moved from single filters to multi-filter formulations (naming Diethylamino Hydroxybenzoyl Hexyl Benzoate, Ethylhexyl Triazone, Bis-Ethylhexyloxyphenol Methoxyphenyl Triazine and others) and that approved filters' risks are outweighed by unprotected UV exposure - useful context, though it mainly validated rather than redirected the project. Where this IHP is weaker than its documentation suggests is that the central technical claim was never demonstrated: no stakeholder input could rescue the activity assay, and the Golden Gate system the WWTP conversation motivated remains untested in the lab.","realWorld":"Implementation is specified concretely and in the plant's own terms: an enclosed bioreactor placed as a biological post-treatment step after the activated sludge process and a filtration step, with engineered E. coli immobilised on cellulose via an adhesive catecholamine moiety or on polystyrene beads to make coated filters, followed by coagulation and UV inactivation of escapees, plus a kill switch for environments outside the reactor and engineered auxotrophy as a further containment layer. The driver is regulatory and dated: the revised EU Urban Waste Water Treatment Directive entered force in 2025 and requires 80% removal of micropollutants including BP-3, with requirements generally expected to be met by 2036, and the team notes that ozonation leaves incompletely degraded residues, activated carbon only adsorbs and is expensive to replace, and reverse osmosis/nanofiltration achieved 95% BP removal in a South Korean pilot but at high capital and energy cost. SDG claims name sub-targets - 6.3, 14.1, 14.2, 14.7, 2.1, 12.4, 12.8, 11.4, 11.5, 11.6, 8.4, 8.9, 1.4, 13.3 - and are backed by cited literature on coral ecosystem services and BP concentrations (influent up to 3795 ug/L and effluent 223 ug/L in the UK; up to 241 ng/g dry weight in Hawaiian coral tissue; zooxanthellae harmed at chronic exposure as low as 60 ng/L). The outstanding feature is the Limitations and conflicts section, which is more honest than most: it states that implementation cost could not be estimated because it is highly regional and that even Finnish industry professionals could not help, that Finnish wastewater temperatures differ from the most BP-3-affected regions so strain survival and efficiency may not transfer, that high cost could worsen inequality between developed and developing countries, that the team cannot guarantee the degradation intermediates are safe to release, that the SDG 2030 horizon is unreachable for a technology needing years more development, that a plant-based solution may be less effective than one deployed at beaches, and that the project could be used for greenwashing of reef tourism - concluding that the best solution is to limit BP-3 use altogether and that Benzophe-none is explicitly the second-best option. After the Jamboree: 38 registry parts (10 characterised expression parts plus the 28-part untested Golden Gate set), a follow-up Suomen Solubiologit article, a school event already booked, and a continuing recruitment pipeline through Aboa Turku ry for the 2027 team.","partners":["Jouko Tuomi, process engineer, Turku wastewater treatment plant, with trainees Nea Lempiainen and Heli Karinkanta","Dr. Rongbin Wang, postdoctoral researcher, Biochemistry, University of Turku","Dr. Jarmo Kapyla, University Lecturer, Biochemistry, University of Turku","Dr. Tuomas Huovinen, University Lecturer, Biochemistry, University of Turku","Dr. Matilda Krakstrom, postdoctoral researcher, Turku Bioscience Centre","Professor Matej Oresic, University of Turku / Turku Bioscience Centre","Dr. Timo Vuorisalo, Docent in Ecology and Environmental Science, University of Turku","Harri Helminen, Water and Marine Management Unit, Finnish supervisory agency","Professor Tuulia Hyotylainen, Orebro University, Sweden","Professor Emma Camp, Future Reefs Team, University of Technology Sydney","Merike Laine, skin and cosmetics specialist, Helsingin Allergia- ja Astmayhdistys ry","Dr. Susanna Majasuo, dermatologist, CMO and CEO of Ihotalo, Turku","Dermosil (Finnish cosmetics company)","Dr. Sari Puustinen, senior researcher and coordinating teacher of sustainable development studies, University of Turku","Associate Professor Pauli Kallio (PI) and senior lab technician Merja Nylander, Department of Molecular Plant Biology, University of Turku","iGEM team Aalto-Helsinki","Aboa Turku ry","Suomen Solubiologit ry","Turun Sanomat (regional newspaper)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6245/wiki/images/wwtppersonnel-edited.avif","caption":"The team with process engineer Jouko Tuomi and trainees Nea Lempiainen and Heli Karinkanta at the Turku wastewater treatment plant, the meeting that switched the implementation from purified enzymes to whole cells on fixed carriers.","credit":"Team ABOA, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6245/wiki/images/description/figure6description.avif","caption":"Figure 4: the route from the Golden Gate construct to a fixed-carrier bioreactor at the end of a wastewater treatment plant, where immobilised E. coli degrade BP-3.","credit":"Team ABOA, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6245/wiki/images/description/figure5description.avif","caption":"Golden Gate assembly with homologous enzymes: pET28g backbone with six insert positions A-F and BsaI-designed overhangs, built to express the whole pathway in one cell (designed but not experimentally tested).","credit":"Team ABOA, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6245/wiki/images/description/figure3description.avif","caption":"Figure 1: the proposed catabolic pathway degrading benzophenone-3 to benzoic acid and 3-oxoadipic acid in Rhodococcus oxybenzonivorans, adapted from Baek et al.","credit":"Team ABOA, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Take ABOA's two transferable habits: write the objective of every stakeholder meeting before it happens and debrief it into notes immediately afterwards so the decision trail survives, and write an explicit Limitations and conflicts section that names the SDG trade-offs your own project creates - cost-driven inequity, unknown intermediate toxicity, and the risk of being used for greenwashing - rather than only the goals it serves.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/aboa/","https://2026.igem.wiki/aboa/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/aboa/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/aboa/sustainability","https://2026.igem.wiki/aboa/public-engagement","https://2026.igem.wiki/aboa/design","https://2026.igem.wiki/aboa/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/aboa/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/aboa/parts","https://2026.igem.wiki/aboa/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/aboa/safety-and-security","https://2026.igem.wiki/aboa/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/aboa/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/aboa/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/aboa/team"],"rank":7},"6249":{"team":"Heidelberg","id":"6249","section":"Undergrad","country":"Germany","village":"Foundational Advance","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/heidelberg/","projectTitle":"VOYAGE","tagline":"An acoustic platform for observation and organization of living systems: gas vesicles engineered into a programmable interface between ultrasound and biology.","summary":"Fluorescence microscopy sees molecular detail but light scattering stops it at tissue depth; X-ray reaches deep but uses ionising radiation; ultrasound penetrates deep without radiation and can even push cells around, but has no molecular specificity. VOYAGE closes that gap with gas vesicles — gas-filled protein nanostructures from aquatic microorganisms, built from GvpA with GvpC reinforcing the outer shell — which scatter ultrasound as genetically encodable contrast agents and buckle at a collapse pressure that can be tuned by engineering GvpC. From that one part the team built four capabilities: GvpC variants with distinct pressure responses as a basis for multiplexed acoustic imaging, a kinase-responsive GvpC that turns phosphorylation into an acoustic signal, latch-based biosensors that report soluble targets, and DARPin- or SpyCatcher-directed vesicles that act as acoustic handles, enriching labelled HEK293T cells roughly tenfold at the side outlet of an acoustophoretic chip and lining them up at pressure antinodes while unlabelled cells sit at the nodes. It won Best Wiki and Best Part Collection because the delivery matched the science: a modular part collection with expression systems for Dolichospermum flos-aquae gas vesicles in mammalian cells and Serratia gas vesicles in E. coli, an accessibility guide for working with gas vesicles on a budget, and ATLAS — a full computational companion spanning all-atom molecular dynamics, three protein design pipelines, a fine-tuned segmentation model and an ultrasound signal model.","awards":["Top 10 (Undergrad)","Best Part Collection — Winner (Undergrad)","Best Wiki — Winner (Undergrad)","Best Foundational Advance Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"ATLAS is the most physics-heavy dry lab of the five, in four parts. (1) All-atom molecular dynamics: two neighbouring ribs of 20-25 GvpA from PDB 8GBS in a periodic box, TIP3P water with 150 mM NaCl, CHARMM36 force field, GvpC 33-residue repeats docked on the outer face with full-length termini predicted by AlphaFold2, energy minimisation then restrained equilibration then 6-10 ns production at 310 K in GROMACS 2024, at least three independent runs per variant. Bending stiffness EI is extracted by decomposing each rib's height profile into waves and fitting the equipartition relation where mean squared amplitude falls as the fourth power of wave number, analysed in equal 1.5-2 ns blocks with Welch's t-test across runs, then converted to a critical buckling pressure by classical Timoshenko shell theory at R = 42.5 nm and rib spacing s = 4.9 nm. GvpC binding free energy comes from steered MD (1 nm/ns, force constant 1000 kJ/nm^2) seeding 25 umbrella sampling windows along the centre-of-mass reaction coordinate, recombined by WHAM into a potential of mean force. Wettability was tested by measuring water contact angle on the gas-facing wall face. (2) An in silico evolution pipeline for GvpC: AlphaFold2 predictions of a Serratia GvpA tetramer and a GvpC repeat aligned onto the experimental Dolichospermum GvpA-GvpC complex and repacked, then LigandMPNN redesigning interface residues across four tiers from fully native to all ten positions, with candidates screened by Boltz-2 co-folding, AlphaFold2 in initial-guess mode and PyRosetta relaxation. (3) A de novo binder pipeline: RFdiffusion3 generating backbones against four adjacent GvpA chains, ProteinMPNN designing eight sequences per backbone, AlphaFold2 re-prediction, then filtering on interface PAE, binder pLDDT and RMSD. (4) A biosensor pipeline where RFdiffusion3 designs a blocking latch fused to the binder at freely chosen hotspots, ProteinMPNN redesigns it, and AlphaFold2 scores three states — construct plus GvpA alone (should not bind), construct plus target alone (latch should displace by more than 3.0 A RMSD), and construct plus both (both bound, latch fully dissociated) — with PyRosetta interface delta-G estimates on each bound state.","dataviz":"This is the Best Wiki winner and the visualisation is doing real work rather than decoration. Every technical term carries an inline definition on hover (acoustic contrast, acoustic pressure, xAM, acoustophoresis, DARPin, pLDDT, i_pAE), and every computational tool gets an 'Explore this software' panel explaining what it is, how it works and what its published benchmarks are — so a reader can follow the pipeline without already knowing LigandMPNN or CellSAM. Structures are interactive: a 'View in 3D' control turns the progression from one GvpA, to a rib inside its cryo-EM density (EMD-14238), to the 13,450-copy vesicle, to the GvpC cage; MD trajectories play as interactive animations of the wall rippling; and biosensor constructs can be rotated with and without bound GFP. The GVSAM results are presented as a ten-image gallery where the reader switches each test image between raw, ground truth, GVSAM prediction with true positives, false positives and false negatives marked, and the base CellSAM prediction — which lets a sceptic check the model rather than take the F1 score on trust. Design pipelines appear as schematic flow diagrams, and the binder filtering is shown as KDE plots overlaying all 1,429 designs against the 13 accepted ones on each metric, making visible that many designs pass individual gates while almost none pass all three.","datascience":"The honesty is the distinguishing feature. The MD model predicts a 1.63-fold stiffness increase from truncated GvpC against 1.48-fold measured experimentally — close — but its absolute collapse pressure estimate of 124-137 kPa without GvpC sits well below the experimental 195 kPa, and the team states plainly that ATLAS is therefore suited to ranking variants rather than predicting absolute pressures, because a whole vesicle is not an idealised wall patch. The umbrella sampling gives 43.5 kJ/mol to remove one GvpC repeat (about 17 k_B T at 310 K) and notes that the free energy plateaus once the repeat has moved 0.55 nm, when only 24% of original atom contacts remain, so most of the cost is paid before the last contacts break. The wetting hypothesis was tested and rejected on its merits: 122.8 degrees without GvpC against 122.2 with, a 0.6-degree difference against the roughly 6 degrees a condensation mechanism would require. Screening thresholds were calibrated against controls rather than chosen by feel — the redesigned sequences were run alongside native Serratia GvpC repeat 3 and nine negative controls, and of all metrics tested only AlphaFold2 interface PAE separated them cleanly (135 of 200 designs passed the 12.0 gate, all nine negative controls failed, the native repeat passed at 11.42), with the team stating explicitly that only that one threshold is calibrated and the other three are a priori safeguards whose predictive value is unproven. PyRosetta interface energies are reported but excluded from selection because they did not discriminate the controls. GVSAM's evaluation was adapted to the problem: intersection over union is unsuitable for objects this small because a one-pixel shift wrecks it, so a hit requires the annotated box centre to lie inside the prediction within 2 px and the areas to differ by at most fourfold, each annotation matchable once, highest-scoring first — with recall, precision and F1 pooled across images and 95% confidence intervals bootstrapped over images. They report F1 rising from 0.2% (base CellSAM) to 42% (GVSAM) with false positives down 97%, and openly diagnose overfitting: validation loss bottomed at epoch 6 while training loss kept falling, so that checkpoint was taken. Two team members annotated independently to reduce single-annotator bias, images of deliberately varying quality and images with no vesicles at all were kept for robustness, and the 108 annotated images were split 70/20/10 at image level with vesicle and non-vesicle images split separately. Ultrasound analysis in GAS uses median intensity and median absolute deviation rather than mean and standard deviation because ultrasound speckle makes single-pixel brightness fluctuate with intensity, with background subtracted as the median recorded after all vesicles were destroyed, and collapse pressure taken as P50 from a four-parameter regression fit (R-squared above 0.99 on all curves).","software":"ATLAS ships as a documented end-to-end pipeline with its own comprehensive user guide, covering the MD characterisation route, the GvpC in silico evolution pipeline and the de novo binder and biosensor design pipelines. GVSAM is a fine-tuned derivative of CellSAM (itself built on Meta's Segment Anything Model with an Anchor DETR based CellFinder detector and a ViT-B encoder) retrained to detect gas vesicle clusters rather than whole cells, trained with Dice plus binary cross-entropy with logits, batch size 3, learning rate 1e-4 (backbone 1e-5), weight decay 1e-4, annotated in napari and converted to bounding boxes by a Python script, with 90 and 270 degree rotation augmentation to cope with only 108 images. GAS is the physics-informed fitting model that converts raw cross-amplitude-modulation ultrasound data into pressure-dependent signal curves. On the wet side the team released the VOYAGE part collection (expression systems for D. flos-aquae gas vesicles in mammalian cells and Serratia gas vesicles in E. coli, plus characterisation and purification parts), an extensive collection of optimised gas vesicle protocols including AFM and darkfield imaging, and an accessibility guide for working with gas vesicles on a budget — which includes using the open-source 3D-printed OpenFlexure microscope for darkfield imaging of purified vesicles and live-cell imaging of producers, explicitly so that teams with limited resources can replicate the work. The Fail Forward Guide is the fourth released artefact.","stack":["GROMACS 2024 with CHARMM36 and TIP3P","Umbrella sampling with WHAM","Steered molecular dynamics","Martini coarse-grained MD (tested and rejected)","AlphaFold2 (including initial-guess mode)","Boltz-2","LigandMPNN","ProteinMPNN","RFdiffusion3 (Rosetta Commons Foundry)","BindCraft (hallucination, with custom loss penalty)","PyRosetta","CellSAM / Segment Anything Model (fine-tuned as GVSAM)","napari","k-Wave acoustic wave simulation","Verasonics Vantage NXT (v2.3.3), 5.2 MHz linear probe, xAM sequence","OpenFlexure open-source 3D-printed microscope","Atomic force microscopy"],"techniques":["Thermal-fluctuation spectrum analysis to extract bending stiffness","Timoshenko shell theory conversion of stiffness to buckling pressure","Potential of mean force / binding free energy calculation","Contact-angle measurement to test a wetting collapse mechanism","Cross-species structural templating justified by sequence identity and repeat periodicity","Tiered interface redesign (native through full redesign)","Negative-control-calibrated metric gating","Multi-state conditional scoring of a conformational switch","Transfer learning / fine-tuning a segmentation foundation model on 108 images","Position-and-size matching criterion in place of IoU for small objects","Bootstrapped confidence intervals over images","Robust statistics (median, MAD) against ultrasound speckle","Cross-amplitude modulation nonlinear ultrasound imaging with hydrophone calibration","Four-parameter regression for P50 collapse pressure","Acoustophoretic cell sorting and standing-wave spatial patterning"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Heidelberg's education programme, Fail Forward, takes error culture in science as its subject rather than synthetic biology content, which makes it unusually distinctive. The centrepiece is the Error Bar, billed as 'a night of scientific f*ck ups': around 80 students and researchers in the university's student bar in July, with successful professionals telling their own stories of things going wrong and what they learned. It was deliberately not a lecture — a short presentation introduced structural problems including publication bias against negative results and mental health stressors in academia, then interactive activities invited participants to share their own experiences, and recreation therapist Brady Hughes ran a workshop on distinguishing a fiasco from a crisis, reappraising situations and using grounding exercises, ending with the group shredding their recent failures together. A panel discussion with around 120 participants extended the theme from personal to institutional failure in the healthcare system, bringing researchers, healthcare professionals, patient advocates and the public into one room, with one panellist making the publication-bias argument in concrete terms: unpublished negative studies mean the same approach gets tried repeatedly, wasting resources and re-exposing participants to risk. All of it was distilled into the Fail Forward Guide, which includes background on failure in academia, expert interviews, and a tutorial for hosting your own Error Bar anywhere in the world — and the team has already committed to making the Error Bar recurring, with an open-mic session planned and PIs who missed it asking to join the next one. Alongside this they ran a Science Cinema with the local student cinema Unikino Heidelberg (over 70 participants for GATTACA, followed by a presentation and open discussion on how realistic the scenario is and which elements of that society we can already find in our own), a documentary screening with gynaecologist Dr Kathrin Haßdenteufel providing medical context and a Q&A (40 participants, every seat taken), a Science Pub Quiz, a Science Slam, school workshops, a laboratory summer school, a lecture series, and a full-day alumni event at the Marsilius-Kolleg bringing around 45 current and former iGEM Heidelberg members from every year the university has competed.","ihp":"The clearest example of stakeholder input changing method rather than framing came from Prof Dr Frauke Gräter, interviewed on modelling strategy. The team first built exactly what she proposed — two Martini coarse-grained sheets with gas between them, tested at different pressures — and it taught them something by failing: the flat patch collapsed even without any applied pressure, because it lacks the closed curved geometry that holds a real vesicle open. That killed the approach and, building on her point that relative differences are what matter for ranking and that a small wall section is representative, they switched to measuring bending stiffness on an all-atom repeating patch and converting it through shell theory. Her warning about sampling is why they chose bending rather than stretching as the primary measurement, ran every simulation at least three times and compared several GvpC variants rather than only wild type; her advice on pulling speed went into the steered MD, where they pulled at several speeds and used only runs in which GvpC genuinely came off. They also tried her suggested coarse-grained model as a fast pre-screen, found it could not distinguish the variants, and state that every reported result therefore comes from all-atom simulation. Elsewhere: Prof Pfeifer warned that GvpA is highly conserved and vulnerable to mutation, redirecting the whole engineering effort onto GvpC as the modular target, and explained which accessory genes the expression constructs needed. Dr Huber's feedback on how long even one sub-idea takes changed how many aspects they attempted and forced explicit prioritisation. A stakeholder conversation led them to replace the D. flos-aquae / P. megaterium expression mix with a Serratia-based cassette in E. coli, which is what finally gave them expression and purification and set the host for everything downstream. Protein design expert Paul Kittner diagnosed a real failure mode: hallucination tools like BindCraft are biased toward hydrophobic interfaces because their structure predictors are trained on natural ones, and GvpA's outward-facing surface is hydrophilic — he advised adding a custom penalty term to the generation loss, which worked and let them target the hydrophilic face, and also pointed them to diffusion models as less biased, which is why RFdiffusion3 became the backbone generator. Dr Michael Jendrusch told them bluntly that no existing pipeline suited their biosensing goal and sketched the binder-plus-latch architecture they built, including the multi-state scoring step and the advice to screen with pooled assays and Twist Oligo Pools rather than testing candidates individually. Prof Dr Karl Rohr's advice is why GVSAM fine-tunes CellSAM rather than training from scratch. Mentor Molina Ramirez moved from interview subject to collaborator, supervising imaging, adapting the xAM script to their specific transducer, and advising them to use beamformed rather than pixel data and median rather than mean normalisation to suppress outliers. Prof Dr Georg Schmitz gave them a falsifiable clinical test — look first with the transducer you already have at frequencies close to clinical scanners, and only go higher if nothing appears — which they followed and passed at 5-7 MHz. Dr Lakshmanan's practical warnings (closing a low-quality tube cap can generate enough pressure to collapse vesicles) shaped handling, and her advice to modify GvpC termini shaped the latch design.","realWorld":"The target application is monitoring engineered cell therapies, chosen because the alternatives are genuinely inadequate: PET tracking needs suitable radioactive tracers and costly specialised equipment, with each scan requiring tracer administration so measurements are days apart rather than continuous; bioluminescence imaging needs no such infrastructure but cannot penetrate patient tissue; and biopsy is invasive, reports only the sampled site, and cannot show how therapeutic cells redistribute. Ultrasound is comparatively inexpensive, widely available and needs no ionising radiation or tracer, which is the whole argument for a genetically encoded acoustic reporter. Crucially they tested the frequency question rather than assuming it: all measurements were made at 5-7 MHz, a range clinical scanners use, so purified vesicles, GV-expressing bacteria and mammalian cells were all detected as clear scattering signals against a degassed negative control without resorting to high frequencies that would limit penetration depth — while stating openly that whether a therapeutic cell can accumulate enough vesicles for a detectable in vivo signal remains to be established. The team has patent work on a modular, reversible acoustic label: because interchangeable binding proteins attach vesicles to a chosen target, the target's acoustic properties change without genetically modifying it, which matters for cell-therapy manufacturing where the product must not be altered. Named next steps are specific — test one ATLAS binder against a marker with existing clinical use such as HER2 or PD-L1, and test two gas vesicle variants with distinct collapse pressures in a tissue-mimicking phantom to establish whether both signals can be read in one measurement, with a published liver phantom protocol cited as a starting point — plus quantifying sorting efficiency and validating cell viability after label removal. A collaboration with PHOENICS is sketched on shared mechanism: the PHOENICS cell computes through phosphorylation and the GvpC sensor turns phosphorylation into ultrasound, so together they would make an engineered cell's internal decision readable from outside the body.","partners":["Prof Dr Frauke Gräter (molecular dynamics and modelling strategy)","Prof Felicitas Pfeifer (gas vesicle biology)","Dr Huber (gas vesicle structure)","Dr Anupama Lakshmanan (gas vesicle engineering)","Paul Kittner (protein design, hallucination bias)","Dr Michael Jendrusch (protein design pipelines)","Prof Dr Karl Rohr (biomedical image analysis)","Prof Dr Georg Schmitz, Chair of Medical Engineering, Ruhr University Bochum","Molina Ramirez (ultrasound imaging mentor and collaborator)","Brady Hughes, recreation therapist (Error Bar workshop)","Dr med Kathrin Haßdenteufel (documentary screening)","iGEM PHOENICS (proposed integration)","Unikino Heidelberg and ZEP Heidelberg","iGEM Heidelberg alumni network (2008-2026)","The OpenFlexure Project (open-source microscopy)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6249/wiki/img/model/gvpc-evolution-pipeline.svg","caption":"The complete in silico GvpC redesign pipeline: the template is split into interface and structural residues, interface redesign is deep-learning-guided with LigandMPNN while structural residues are chosen rationally, candidates are predicted and filtered by structure predictors and physical constraints, and validated variants feed back to retune the gating strategy.","credit":"Team Heidelberg, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6249/wiki/img/gvpa-binders/metrics-1-01788a672d.svg","caption":"Interface PAE distribution across all 1,429 de novo GvpA binder designs (orange) against the 13 accepted ones (blue). Nearly half of all designs failed on this metric alone, which is why the pipeline reports each gate separately rather than a single composite score.","credit":"Team Heidelberg, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6249/wiki/img/model/gvsam-base-vs-finetuned-a.webp","caption":"Recall, precision and F1 with bootstrapped 95% confidence intervals for GVSAM against the base CellSAM model on 10 held-out microscopy images containing 114 annotated gas vesicle clusters — F1 rose from 0.2% to 42% after fine-tuning on just 108 annotated images, with false positives down 97%.","credit":"Team Heidelberg, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6249/wiki/img/education/error-bar-1.webp","caption":"The Error Bar, 'a night of scientific f*ck ups': around 80 students and researchers in the university student bar hearing established scientists talk about their own failures, with interactive activities and a workshop on distinguishing a fiasco from a crisis.","credit":"Team Heidelberg, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"The transferable dry-lab habit is calibrating your filters against negative controls before you trust them: Heidelberg ran nine deliberately bad sequences plus the real binder through the identical pipeline, found that only AlphaFold2 interface PAE separated them, said so, and refused to select on the metrics that failed the test — a discipline that costs nothing but compute and turns a pile of prediction scores into an actual decision rule. On the human side, copy Fail Forward: an evening where senior scientists tell students about their own failures, plus a written guide that includes instructions for running the event yourself. For a high-school-plus research centre whose students will mostly meet failure before success, an institutional format that makes failure discussable is worth more than another outreach workshop — and the guide means you can run it next term without inventing it.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/heidelberg/","https://2026.igem.wiki/heidelberg/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/heidelberg/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/heidelberg/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/heidelberg/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/heidelberg/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/heidelberg/application","https://2026.igem.wiki/heidelberg/part-collection","https://2026.igem.wiki/heidelberg/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/heidelberg/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/heidelberg/public-outreach"],"rank":129},"6254":{"team":"UAlberta","id":"6254","section":"Undergrad","country":"Canada","village":"Therapeutics","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/","projectTitle":"gleyeco","projectTitle_zh":"gleyeco","tagline":"A modular fusion protein that uses the eye's own sugar coating as an anchor, delivered in a hydrogel, so dry eye medicine stays put.","tagline_zh":"一個模組化融合蛋白，把眼睛本身的糖衣當成錨點，並以水膠遞送，讓乾眼症藥物留在原處。","summary":"Dry eye disease affects an estimated 34.6% of people globally and 21.3% of Canadian adults, and the central problem is not the drug but the delivery: blinking and tear drainage clear a topical therapeutic within minutes. gleyeco treats the ocular glycocalyx as a docking site rather than a barrier, fusing a Galectin-3 carbohydrate-recognition domain (binding Core 1 O-glycans on mucins), a tandem pair of the 12-residue hyaluronic-acid-binding peptide HABpep, and IL-1RA (anakinra) as the therapeutic payload, delivered from a crosslinked PEG/hyaluronic acid hydrogel as a drop or a contact lens. The team built a five-stage dry lab pipeline with its own acronyms - GLARE, InSiGHT, VOIR, I-SPY, HOPE - that chooses the target, engineers the binder, sets the valency, predicts the yield and tunes the gel, and released GLARE as an installable Python package. It won Best Entrepreneurship on an unusually rigorous commercial case (38-patient survey, two clinician letters of support, a letter of intent from a clinic, competitor matrix against Restasis/Cequa/Xiidra, PESTEL, 10-year plan) and was nominated for the Inclusivity Award for an open-access Inclusivity in Research course, an Adaptive Technology Kit and a rural teachers' programme.","summary_zh":"乾眼症估計影響全球 34.6% 的人口，以及 21.3% 的加拿大成人，而核心問題不在藥物、而在遞送：眨眼與淚液排出會在幾分鐘內把局部用藥沖掉。gleyeco 把眼表的糖萼視為停靠位點、而非屏障，將一個 Galectin-3 的碳水化合物辨識區（結合黏液素上的 Core 1 O-glycan）、一組串聯的 12 殘基玻尿酸結合胜肽 HABpep，以及作為治療酬載的 IL-1RA（anakinra）融合在一起，再由交聯的 PEG／玻尿酸水膠以點眼液或隱形眼鏡形式遞送。團隊建了一條五階段的乾實驗流程，各有自創的縮寫——GLARE、InSiGHT、VOIR、I-SPY、HOPE——分別負責選定標的、改造結合子、設定價數、預測產率與調校水膠，並把 GLARE 釋出為可安裝的 Python 套件。它以一份異常嚴謹的商業論證（38 位病患問卷、兩封臨床醫師支持函、一家診所的意向書、對照 Restasis/Cequa/Xiidra 的競品矩陣、PESTEL、10 年計畫）拿下最佳創業獎，並以一門開放取用的「研究中的包容性」課程、一套輔具技術套件與一項偏鄉教師計畫獲得包容性獎提名。","awards":["Top 10 (Undergrad)","Inclusivity Award — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Entrepreneurship — Winner (Undergrad)","Best Therapeutics Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Five named operations, each handing its result to the next. GLARE (Glycan-Lectin Analysis for Recognition and Evaluation) mines global glycan databases of 50,000+ catalogued sequences, filters to the 134 unique structures documented in ocular tissue (cornea, tear film, lacrimal gland), confirms O-glycans dominate, then screens Galectin-3's off-target risk across other organs and three cancers under identical statistics with multiple-hypothesis-testing correction, and finally re-runs the analysis under a dry-eye disease signature, finding the disease phenotype exposes over 2.5x more accessible binding sites. InSiGHT (In Silico Glycan Honed Targeting) engineers Galectin-3 to favour Core 1 over LacNAc: mutation sites were chosen from the literature (H46, N48, R50, N62, W69, E72 hydrogen-bonding residues plus nearby polar R32, E53, R74), a Clustal Omega multiple sequence alignment of all available mammalian galectins from PDB and NCBI (which excluded the perfectly conserved W69 and flagged the poorly conserved E53), and a PyMOL structural alignment of 12 galectin CRDs against Galectin-3 (PDB 3ZSJ, 0.86 Angstrom) that identified the E53-V58 loop and the I33/N31 positions as differentiators; a Python script generates mutant combinations, FoldX builds the structures, HADDOCK and Schrodinger dock Core 1 and LacNAc in parallel after AutoDock Vina proved unable to handle large flexible glycans, and GROMACS scores binding strength - batched across RunPod for parallel FoldX jobs. Ten mutants (Alpha through Kappa) went to the bench. VOIR (Valency Optimization and Integrated Retention) uses the valentBind model to compute bivalent avidity as a function of linker length and glycan target density, concluding that a second binding domain gives the largest gain, a third a moderate one, and a fourth nothing - and recommending (GGGGS)6-16 linkers. I-SPY (I Shall Produce Yield) curates the BL21(DE3)-based iBB1018 genome-scale reconstruction in COBRApy for the SHuffle T7 Express chassis, adds a demand reaction for the heterologous fusion protein, and runs flux balance analysis to locate metabolic bottlenecks. HOPE (Hydrogel Optimization for Pharmacokinetic Evaluation) models mesh size with the Peppas-Merrill and then the Canal-Peppas form of Flory-Rehner, using interpolated PEGDA swelling data and MeHA degree of methacrylation, and derives protein diffusivity from it.","frameworks_zh":"五項具名的作業，每一項把結果交給下一項。GLARE（Glycan-Lectin Analysis for Recognition and Evaluation）從收錄超過 50,000 條序列的全球糖鏈資料庫中挖掘資料，篩出在眼部組織（角膜、淚膜、淚腺）中有文獻記載的 134 種獨特結構，確認 O-glycan 為主，接著以完全相同的統計方法、並施以多重假說檢定校正，篩查 Galectin-3 在其他器官與三種癌症上的脫靶風險，最後再以乾眼症的疾病特徵重跑分析，發現疾病表現型會暴露出超過 2.5 倍的可及結合位點。InSiGHT（In Silico Glycan Honed Targeting）改造 Galectin-3，使其偏好 Core 1 而非 LacNAc：突變位點的選擇依據文獻（形成氫鍵的 H46、N48、R50、N62、W69、E72，再加上鄰近的極性殘基 R32、E53、R74）、一份以 Clustal Omega 對 PDB 與 NCBI 中所有可得哺乳類 galectin 所做的多序列比對（因此排除了完全保守的 W69，並標記出保守性很低的 E53），以及一份用 PyMOL 把 12 個 galectin 的碳水化合物辨識區對比 Galectin-3（PDB 3ZSJ，0.86 埃）的結構比對，由此指出 E53-V58 這段環與 I33/N31 位點是關鍵差異處；接著以 Python 腳本生成突變組合、以 FoldX 建構結構，並在 AutoDock Vina 被證明無法處理大型柔性糖鏈之後，改用 HADDOCK 與 Schrödinger 並行對接 Core 1 與 LacNAc，再以 GROMACS 評分結合強度——FoldX 的工作則透過 RunPod 分批並行執行。最終有十個突變體（Alpha 到 Kappa）進入實驗檯。VOIR（Valency Optimization and Integrated Retention）以 valentBind 模型計算雙價的親合力如何隨連接子長度與糖鏈標的密度變化，結論是加上第二個結合區收益最大、第三個中等、第四個則毫無助益——並建議採用 (GGGGS)6-16 的連接子。I-SPY（I Shall Produce Yield）在 COBRApy 中整理以 BL21(DE3) 為基礎的 iBB1018 基因組尺度代謝模型以符合 SHuffle T7 Express 底盤，加入該異源融合蛋白的需求反應，再以通量平衡分析找出代謝瓶頸。HOPE（Hydrogel Optimization for Pharmacokinetic Evaluation）以 Peppas-Merrill、再以 Flory-Rehner 的 Canal-Peppas 形式建模網目孔徑，使用內插的 PEGDA 膨潤資料與 MeHA 的甲基丙烯醯化程度，並由此推導蛋白質的擴散係數。","dataviz":"The modelling page is organised as a relay: five labelled operations (Choose, Improve, Multiply, Produce, Deliver) in a flow a reader clicks into, each with its own write-up and its own Impressiveness/Design/Validation/Exemplarity framing. The software page embeds a live in-browser CLI simulator for GLARE with clickable example commands (--cell eye, --binding-galectins eye, --target-compare eye core1 stn, --disease-compare dry_eye) so a judge can run the pipeline's logic without installing Python. For audiences without a biology background the team built the gleyecobuddies: Lecto (Galectin-3, with the binding site built into the character design), Ana (IL-1RA, a red plus sign) and Happy (HABpep, a blue rectangle standing for a wall that holds the drug in place), deliberately layered on top of the standard Symbol Nomenclature for Glycans rather than replacing it, and justified as serving visual learners, neurodivergent people and children. All InSiGHT results are reported with the predictors' disagreements visible rather than averaged.","dataviz_zh":"建模頁面組織成一條接力賽：五個具名作業（Choose、Improve、Multiply、Produce、Deliver）排成一條讀者可點入的流程，每一項都有自己的說明，並各自以 Impressiveness／Design／Validation／Exemplarity 的架構呈現。軟體頁面內嵌一個可在瀏覽器執行的 GLARE 命令列模擬器，附上可點擊的範例指令（--cell eye、--binding-galectins eye、--target-compare eye core1 stn、--disease-compare dry_eye），讓評審不必安裝 Python 就能跑過整條流程的邏輯。為沒有生物背景的對象，團隊設計了 gleyecobuddies：Lecto（Galectin-3，角色設計中直接畫出結合位）、Ana（IL-1RA，一個紅色加號）與 Happy（HABpep，一個藍色長方形，代表把藥物留在原處的一道牆），並刻意疊加在標準的糖鏈符號命名法（SNFG）之上、而非取代它，理由是要服務視覺型學習者、神經多樣性者與兒童。所有 InSiGHT 的結果都把各預測工具之間的不一致直接呈現出來，而不是平均掉。","datascience":"The team repeatedly uses modelling to avoid spending bench time, and reports the limits of each prediction. GLARE's stated limitations are unusually frank: the database records which structures have been documented in a tissue, not how much is displayed, so enrichment results describe structural patterns and must not be read as surface density; the diseased-versus-healthy split is built from literature signatures rather than a labelled patient dataset, and the pipeline is written so a real patient-derived list can be dropped in unchanged; binding strengths come from published microarray data, not from their own fusion protein; the tissue panel is small, and the cervix moved along the same mucin O-glycan axis as the eye so other mucosal surfaces would need direct testing. In InSiGHT they caught their own pipeline's instability - mutating key polar residues to alanine did not abolish predicted binding as it should, and one HADDOCK run gave mutant Gamma -6.495 kcal/mol against Core 1 while a separate run of the same mutant gave -3.84, which they report as evidence the pipeline needs repeated runs. For VOIR they state the point is the optimal linker length range, not the headline avidity ratio, because the values are literature-derived estimates not validated in vitro. For HOPE the model behaved as theory predicts (mesh falling from 16 nm at 5% w/v PEGDA to about 10 nm at 25%, predicted protein diffusivity from about 60 to 37 micrometres squared per second against 97 in free water) and they say plainly they could not build the equivalent alginate model, and that an OpenFOAM CFD attempt failed because the corneal absorption boundary condition had to be written in C++ and did not run reliably, so they fell back to a 1D Python model for sensitivity analysis.","datascience_zh":"團隊反覆以建模來省下實驗檯時間，並報告每項預測的限制。GLARE 所聲明的限制異常坦白：資料庫記錄的是某組織中有哪些結構被記載過、而不是展示了多少，因此富集結果描述的是結構模式，絕不可讀成表面密度；疾病與健康的分組是依文獻特徵建構、不是來自有標註的病患資料集，流程寫法則讓真正的病患來源清單可以原封不動地替換進來；結合強度來自已發表的微陣列資料、而非他們自己的融合蛋白；組織樣本面很小，而子宮頸在黏液素 O-glycan 這個軸上與眼睛走向相同，因此其他黏膜表面仍需直接測試。在 InSiGHT 中，他們抓出自己流程的不穩定：把關鍵極性殘基突變為丙胺酸後，預測的結合並未如理應發生那樣被消除；而同一個突變體 Gamma 對 Core 1 的一次 HADDOCK 執行給出 -6.495 kcal/mol，另一次獨立執行卻給出 -3.84，他們把這點報出來，作為流程需要多次重複執行的證據。在 VOIR 方面，他們聲明重點在於最佳連接子的長度區間、而不是那個醒目的親合力倍數，因為那些數值是文獻推導的估計、未經體外驗證。HOPE 的模型行為符合理論預期（網目孔徑從 5% w/v PEGDA 時的 16 nm 降到 25% 時約 10 nm，預測的蛋白質擴散係數從約每秒 60 平方微米降到 37，自由水中則為 97），他們也直白表示自己無法建出對應的 alginate 模型，而一次 OpenFOAM CFD 的嘗試失敗了，因為角膜吸收的邊界條件必須用 C++ 寫、執行起來不穩定，於是他們退回用一維 Python 模型做敏感度分析。","software":"GLARE, released as an importable Python package (v0.2.0, Python 3.10+) at https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/ualberta/software-glare, runnable from the command line with a clear module structure separating tissue validation, binding analysis, cross-tissue comparison, disease signatures and docking-structure generation behind a single pipeline interface, with generalised inputs so another team can point it at a different tissue, lectin or glycan. A browser-based CLI simulator on the wiki lets anyone try it without installing. The Adaptive Technology Kit is an open-source hardware release: 3D-printable PCR strip-tube and microfuge-tube openers (in multiple design variants, because user testing showed different researchers preferred different models), an agarose gel loader, an SDS gel loader, a braille stamper, a keyboard tool, a pencil holder, a non-slip tray, a microscope phone holder, and a tactile map of the iGEM lab with published blueprints. A Synthetic Biology Lab Manual and the full Rural Teachers Synbiosium materials are published as free PDFs, as is the DNA-as-Code Kit.","software_zh":"GLARE 以可匯入的 Python 套件釋出（v0.2.0，需 Python 3.10+），位於 https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/ualberta/software-glare ，可由命令列執行，模組結構清楚，把組織驗證、結合分析、跨組織比較、疾病特徵與對接結構生成分開，並統一在單一流程介面之後；輸入設計得夠通用，讓其他隊伍能把它指向不同的組織、凝集素或糖鏈。wiki 上的瀏覽器版命令列模擬器讓任何人不必安裝就能試用。輔具技術套件則是一項開源硬體發布：可 3D 列印的 PCR 連管與微量離心管開蓋器（有多種設計版本，因為使用者測試顯示不同研究者偏好不同款式）、瓊膠膠體上樣器、SDS 膠上樣器、點字壓印器、鍵盤輔具、鉛筆握持器、防滑托盤、顯微鏡手機架，以及一張 iGEM 實驗室的觸覺地圖，圖紙全部公開。一本《合成生物學實驗手冊》與偏鄉教師 Synbiosium 的完整教材都以免費 PDF 發布，DNA-as-Code 套件亦然。","stack":["Python 3.10+","COBRApy","iBB1018 genome-scale reconstruction","BiGG Models","Glycowork","GlyTouCan / GlyGen","Glycam-Web","FoldX","HADDOCK","Schrodinger","GROMACS","AutoDock Vina (rejected)","AlphaFold 2","PyMOL","Clustal Omega (EMBL-EBI)","RunPod (parallel compute)","valentBind","OpenFOAM (attempted)","Next.js / React wiki"],"techniques":["Database mining with multiple-hypothesis-testing correction","Disease-signature enrichment analysis","Cross-tissue off-target screening","Multiple sequence alignment for conservation-guided site selection","Structural alignment of homologue binding pockets","Combinatorial in silico saturation mutagenesis","Protein-glycan docking","MD-based binding strength estimation","Batched GPU/cloud job parallelisation","Flux balance analysis","Genome-scale model curation for a non-reference strain","Bivalent avidity / valency modelling","Flory-Rehner (Peppas-Merrill and Canal-Peppas) mesh-size calculation","Diffusivity estimation from mesh size","1D transport modelling for sensitivity analysis","Isothermal titration calorimetry (experimental Kd)"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Three distinct, durable programmes rather than one-off booths. (1) The Inclusivity in Research Course, an open-access training run through Google Classroom, built from a nationwide survey and expert consultations, with modules on a Native Land activity, the team's own 'Just Ask' framework and neurodivergent inclusion, creating open spaces, blind and visually impaired inclusion, Deaf and hard-of-hearing inclusion, racialized people, women and 2SLGBTQIA+ and gender minorities, navigating reporting processes, and an accessibility resource bank - each with downloadable slides, infographics and interactive summaries. It was piloted with their own team, neighbouring labs and Canadian iGEM teams, and the three pieces of pilot feedback (offer multiple learning formats, add scenario-based practice, cover more groups) were each implemented as narrated audio and slideshows, self-reflection prompts and real lab case studies, and two new modules. (2) The Rural Teachers Synbiosium, a half-day online professional development event for rural Alberta teachers, mapped explicitly onto the Alberta middle and high school curriculum, covering case studies and how to secure funding, with three guest speakers including Amino Labs CEO Julie Legault, 9 free hands-on kits distributed (teachers chose between a one-day yeast-fermentation race car and a multi-day pigment-engineering agar art project) and all materials shipped in advance to lower the burden. (3) Public outreach at K-Days, an Edmonton summer festival, where visitors attempted lab tasks while simulating different visual impairments, plus a DNA-as-code bracelet activity, and tabling at Alberta's Women in STEM week after being invited by the Alberta Women in Science Network. The team also presented at the Canadian Glycomics Symposium, CNAS Research Day, Darwin Day, Cell Biology Research Day, the RE Peter Conference and the Canadian iGEM GCI Conference, and ran a hands-on workshop at Canmore Collegiate High School - which is what revealed the rural access problem and started the Synbiosium.","publicEngagement_zh":"三項各自獨立、能持續下去的計畫，而不是一次性的攤位。(1)「研究中的包容性」課程，是一門透過 Google Classroom 開放取用的訓練課程，由一份全國性問卷與專家諮詢建構而成，模組涵蓋原住民土地認識活動、團隊自創的「Just Ask」框架與神經多樣性包容、營造開放空間、視障者包容、聽障與重聽者包容、被種族化的群體、女性與 2SLGBTQIA+ 及性別少數、如何走通申訴流程，以及一個無障礙資源庫——每個模組都有可下載的簡報、資訊圖與互動摘要。課程先在自己團隊、鄰近實驗室與加拿大其他 iGEM 隊伍試行，三項試行回饋（提供多種學習形式、加入情境演練、涵蓋更多群體）分別被落實為旁白音檔與投影片、自我反思提問與真實實驗室案例，以及兩個新模組。(2) 偏鄉教師 Synbiosium，是一場為亞伯達省偏鄉教師辦的半日線上專業發展活動，明確對齊亞伯達省國中與高中課綱，內容涵蓋案例研究與如何爭取經費，有三位客座講者（包括 Amino Labs 執行長 Julie Legault），發出 9 份免費的動手做套件（教師可在一日的酵母發酵賽車與多日的色素工程洋菜藝術專題之間選擇），所有材料都事先寄達以降低教師負擔。(3) 公眾科普：在愛德蒙頓的夏季節慶 K-Days 設攤，讓參觀者在模擬不同視覺障礙的狀態下嘗試實驗室工作，另有 DNA 編碼手環活動；並在受亞伯達女性科學網絡邀請後，於該省 Women in STEM 週設攤。團隊也在加拿大糖體學研討會、CNAS 研究日、達爾文日、細胞生物學研究日、RE Peter 會議與加拿大 iGEM GCI 會議發表，並在 Canmore Collegiate 高中辦了一場動手做工作坊——正是那場活動揭露了偏鄉的取用問題，並促成了 Synbiosium。","ihp":"Every stakeholder entry is logged as a Key Insight paired with an Action Taken, and the actions are real design reversals. Dr Warren Wakarchuk (Scientific Director of GlycoNet) warned that small-molecule binding pockets hold cargo too tightly to release on the eye and that yeast adds problematic sugar tags, and noted eukaryotic tissue autofluoresces green under UV - so the team abandoned the binding-pocket release concept, chose E. coli over yeast, switched the reporter from GFP to mScarlet, and retargeted abundant normal ocular glycans instead of rare disease-specific ones. Dr Lisa Willis (glyco-immunology) raised immune safety and challenged them to test whether the Galectin-3 and HA domains cooperate or compete for binding - so instead of assuming more binding is better, they redesigned the experimental plan to measure each domain separately by isothermal titration calorimetry. Dr Carr advised narrowing from retinal delivery to corneal inflammation in dry eye with IL-1RA cargo and offered Xenopus eye tissue for ex vivo testing. An advisor recommended the SHuffle T7 strain and told them their fusion protein was not complex enough to justify a chaperone plasmid, so they dropped it. Dr Amandeep helped unify the five separate models into one pipeline and suggested using eye images as GLARE input to make it diagnostic - the team pursued it, found it infeasible, said so, and redirected to modelling; he also pointed them to RunPod, which is why FoldX now runs in parallel. Jezlyn warned that chemical and UV crosslinking would denature mScarlet, so they moved to physical ionic crosslinking with calcium chloride, wrote autoclaving protocols for sterility, and were pointed at the Peppas-Merrill and Flory-Rehner equations that became HOPE. Dr Cortez told them not to add a second nickel column but to optimise their existing HisTrap/FPLC wash stringency, which they did and documented on Coomassie gels. Optometrist Dr Abdo Kattan explained that his multi-product dry eye package (omega 3s, drops, lid wipes, goggles) has very low compliance because it is time-consuming, expensive and impossible to attribute benefit to - which refocused the whole project on one affordable single-product treatment. Separately, CD44 was dropped entirely as the HA-retention domain in favour of tandem HABpep after it kept appearing in the insoluble fraction and the literature revealed isoforms linked to cancer therapy resistance. On the inclusivity side, Nicholas Piroddi (a medical researcher with autism) was consulted, then consulted a second time to review how the course represented neurodiversity, which added the institutional reporting-pathways module; ASVI's input became the blind and visually impaired module; and user testing of the 3D-printed tube openers at the WinSTEM expo is why the kit ships multiple variants of the same tool.","ihp_zh":"每一條利害關係人紀錄都登錄為一則關鍵洞見配一則採取的行動，而這些行動都是真正的設計翻盤。GlycoNet 科學總監 Dr Warren Wakarchuk 警告，小分子結合口袋抓得太緊、到了眼睛上無法釋放酬載，而酵母會加上有問題的糖基修飾，並指出真核組織在紫外光下會發出綠色自體螢光——於是團隊放棄了結合口袋釋放的構想、選擇 E. coli 而非酵母、把報告基因從 GFP 換成 mScarlet，並把標的從罕見的疾病專一糖鏈改為量多的正常眼部糖鏈。Dr Lisa Willis（糖免疫學）提出免疫安全性問題，並要他們檢驗 Galectin-3 區與玻尿酸結合區在結合上是協同還是競爭——於是他們不再假設結合越多越好，而是重新設計實驗計畫，以等溫滴定量熱法分別量測兩個區域。Dr Carr 建議從視網膜遞送收斂到以 IL-1RA 為酬載的乾眼症角膜發炎，並提供 Xenopus 眼組織供離體測試。一位顧問推薦 SHuffle T7 菌株，並指出他們的融合蛋白還不夠複雜、不足以正當化使用伴護蛋白質體，於是他們把它去掉。Dr Amandeep 協助把五個獨立模型統整成一條流程，並建議以眼睛影像作為 GLARE 的輸入，使其具診斷功能——團隊確實去嘗試、發現不可行、如實說明，並把方向轉回建模；他也指點他們使用 RunPod，這就是 FoldX 現在能並行執行的原因。Jezlyn 警告化學與紫外交聯都會使 mScarlet 變性，於是他們改用氯化鈣的物理離子交聯、撰寫高壓滅菌的無菌操作規程，並被指向後來成為 HOPE 的 Peppas-Merrill 與 Flory-Rehner 方程式。Dr Cortez 告訴他們不要再加第二根鎳管柱，而是把現有 HisTrap/FPLC 的沖洗嚴苛度最佳化，他們照做並以考馬斯染色膠記錄下來。驗光師 Dr Abdo Kattan 說明他那套多產品的乾眼療程（omega 3、點眼液、眼瞼清潔棉片、護目鏡）順從性極低，因為耗時、昂貴，而且根本無法歸因是哪一項帶來改善——這使整個專題重新聚焦到一項負擔得起的單一產品療法上。另外，CD44 作為玻尿酸滯留區被完全捨棄、改用串聯 HABpep，原因是它一再出現在不可溶部分，且文獻顯示其某些異構體與癌症治療抗性有關。在包容性這一端，他們諮詢了 Nicholas Piroddi（一位自閉症的醫學研究者），之後又第二度請他審閱課程如何呈現神經多樣性，由此增補了機構申訴途徑的模組；ASVI 的意見成為視障模組；而 3D 列印開蓋器在 WinSTEM 展會上的使用者測試，正是套件為同一項工具提供多種版本的原因。","realWorld":"The strongest undergraduate commercial case of the five. Evidence of demand is tabulated by customer role with the strength of evidence named: letters of support from Dr Abdo Kattan and Dr Matthew Benson (and a signed letter of intent from Kattan's clinic to work with them), 86% of 38 surveyed dry eye patients interested in a synthetic biology treatment, and an application in interview stage with the Nucleate Canada accelerator. The patient survey plus three clinician interviews produced five explicit unmet needs - fewer doses, longer retention, no burning or stinging, targeted anti-inflammatory action, contact lens compatibility - which the product is then measured against. A competitor matrix compares gleyeco line by line with Restasis (AbbVie), Cequa (Sun Pharma) and Xiidra (Bausch + Lomb) on mechanism, dosing, time to effect, clinical evidence, tolerability, lens compatibility, 30-day cost and Canadian availability, citing prescribing information and Drugs.com prices as of 15 October 2026, and crucially labels gleyeco's own entries as design goals that preclinical and clinical data must confirm. The gap identified is precise: every anti-inflammatory option is dosed at least twice daily and none occupies targeted once-daily treatment. TAM/SAM/SOM, regional opportunity, bottom-up dynamics, current distribution network, a Size-Potential-Access analysis, a beachhead market defined by role (users, decision makers, payers, pharmaceutical partners), a 10-year implementation plan and an exit strategy all follow. The PESTEL analysis is specific to Canadian biotech: Health Canada's Reliance Order syncing review with the FDA if filed within 120 days, Alberta Innovates and FAST cutting trial start-up from 90+ to 45 days, PMPRB price controls pushing them toward private payers first, over 75% of Canadian life-science investment coming from abroad so Phase 2 needs a partner, the USD/CAD rate at 1.4, and the fact that the RE Peter Conference and Jamboree disclosures start the novelty clock (12 months in Canada, absolute novelty required in Europe). Clinical milestones were set directly from a clinician's roadmap, and lab eye models have been offered by two separate researchers for the move from proof of concept to preclinical.","realWorld_zh":"五支隊伍中大學部最強的商業論證。需求證據依客戶角色列表，並標明證據強度：Dr Abdo Kattan 與 Dr Matthew Benson 的支持函（以及 Kattan 診所簽署的合作意向書）、38 位受訪乾眼症患者中有 86% 對合成生物學療法感興趣，以及一份已進入面試階段的 Nucleate Canada 加速器申請。病患問卷加上三場臨床醫師訪談，整理出五項明確的未滿足需求——更少的給藥次數、更長的滯留時間、不刺痛不灼熱、標的性的抗發炎作用、與隱形眼鏡相容——產品隨後就以這些標準來檢視。競品矩陣逐項把 gleyeco 與 Restasis（AbbVie）、Cequa（Sun Pharma）與 Xiidra（Bausch + Lomb）在機制、給藥、起效時間、臨床證據、耐受性、隱形眼鏡相容性、30 天費用與加拿大可取得性上比較，引用的是處方資訊與 2026 年 10 月 15 日的 Drugs.com 價格，而關鍵在於他們把 gleyeco 自己那一欄標示為設計目標，有待臨床前與臨床資料確認。他們指出的缺口很精確：所有抗發炎選項都至少每日給藥兩次，沒有任何一項占住「標的性、每日一次」這個位置。接著是 TAM/SAM/SOM、區域機會、自下而上的動態分析、現行通路網絡、一份 Size-Potential-Access 分析、依角色界定的灘頭市場（使用者、決策者、付費方、製藥夥伴）、一份 10 年執行計畫與一套退場策略。PESTEL 分析專就加拿大生技環境而寫：加拿大衛生部的 Reliance Order 在 120 天內送件即可與 FDA 審查同步、Alberta Innovates 與 FAST 把試驗啟動時間從 90 天以上縮短到 45 天、PMPRB 的價格管制推使他們先走自費市場、超過 75% 的加拿大生命科學投資來自海外因此第二期需要夥伴、美元兌加元匯率為 1.4，以及 RE Peter 會議與 Jamboree 的公開揭露會啟動新穎性時鐘（加拿大 12 個月，歐洲則要求絕對新穎性）。臨床里程碑直接依一位臨床醫師的路線圖設定，而兩位不同的研究者都提供了實驗室眼睛模型，供他們從概念驗證邁向臨床前。","partners":["GlycoNet (Canadian Glycomics Network)","Nucleate Canada","Amino Labs","Alberta Women in Science Network (AWSN)","Alberta Sports and Recreation Association for the Blind / ASVI","MolScreen","Genome Alberta","University of Alberta Student Innovation Centre","Canmore Collegiate High School","Dr Abdo Kattan's optometry clinic (letter of intent)","Alberta Innovates / FAST","Canadian iGEM GCI Conference","Canadian Glycomics Symposium","rural Alberta school teachers (Synbiosium cohort)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6254/wiki/model-page/glare-fig1.avif","caption":"GLARE, the glycan-lectin screening pipeline: 50,000+ catalogued glycan sequences filtered to the 134 documented in ocular tissue, then screened for Galectin-3 off-target risk across other organs and under a dry-eye disease signature.","caption_zh":"GLARE，糖鏈—凝集素篩選流程：從收錄超過 50,000 條糖鏈序列中篩出在眼部組織有文獻記載的 134 種，再篩查 Galectin-3 在其他器官上的脫靶風險，以及在乾眼症疾病特徵下的表現。","credit":"Team UAlberta, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6254/wiki/model-page/insight-folder/insight-figure2.avif","caption":"Predicted binding strength of Galectin-3 mutants against the Core 1 target, scored by HADDOCK, Schrodinger and GROMACS, with the predictors' disagreements left visible rather than averaged.","caption_zh":"Galectin-3 突變體對 Core 1 標的的預測結合強度，由 HADDOCK、Schrödinger 與 GROMACS 評分，並把各預測工具之間的不一致直接保留下來、而非平均掉。","credit":"Team UAlberta, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6254/wiki/model-page/hope-folder/hydrogel-modelling-figure-3.avif","caption":"HOPE hydrogel modelling: mesh size falls from 16 nm at 5% w/v PEGDA to about 10 nm at 25%, and predicted protein diffusivity falls from roughly 60 to 37 micrometres squared per second against 97 in free water.","caption_zh":"HOPE 水膠建模：網目孔徑從 5% w/v PEGDA 時的 16 nm 降到 25% 時約 10 nm，預測的蛋白質擴散係數則從每秒約 60 平方微米降到 37，而自由水中為 97。","credit":"Team UAlberta, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6254/wiki/inclusivity-page/map-in-use.avif","caption":"The tactile map of the iGEM lab in use - part of the open-source Adaptive Technology Kit, published with blueprints alongside 3D-printable tube openers, gel loaders and a braille stamper.","caption_zh":"iGEM 實驗室觸覺地圖的實際使用畫面——這是開源輔具技術套件的一部分，與可 3D 列印的開蓋器、膠體上樣器與點字壓印器一同連同圖紙公開。","credit":"Team UAlberta, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6254/wiki/model-page/voir-folder/fig1-voir.avif","caption":"VOIR valency modelling: bivalent avidity as a function of linker length from the valentBind model, which showed a second binding domain gives the largest gain, a third a moderate one, and a fourth none.","caption_zh":"VOIR 的價數建模：以 valentBind 模型算出雙價親合力隨連接子長度的變化，結果顯示加上第二個結合區收益最大、第三個中等、第四個則毫無助益。","credit":"Team UAlberta, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Copy UAlberta's two-column human practices habit - every conversation written as one Key Insight and one Action Taken, where the action is a concrete reversal (GFP to mScarlet, yeast to E. coli, CD44 dropped for HABpep, chemical crosslinking dropped for calcium) - because it forces a team to admit when advice changed nothing. The other directly adaptable asset is their rural pivot: they went in planning to help schools found competition teams, learned from the teachers that capacity was the real constraint, and instead built a curriculum-aligned half-day online session with pre-shipped kits and a free lab manual, which is exactly the model a Taiwanese research centre could run for under-resourced schools.","gemsTakeaway_zh":"值得借鏡的是 UAlberta 那套雙欄式人類實踐習慣——每一次對話都寫成一則關鍵洞見配一則採取的行動，而行動都是具體的翻盤（GFP 改成 mScarlet、酵母改成 E. coli、捨棄 CD44 改用 HABpep、捨棄化學交聯改用鈣離子）——因為這會迫使團隊承認哪些建議其實什麼都沒改變。另一項可直接移植的資產是他們在偏鄉的轉向：他們原本打算協助學校成立競賽隊伍，從教師那裡才明白真正的限制是能量不足，於是改為設計一場對齊課綱的半日線上課程，搭配事先寄達的實驗套件與一份免費實驗手冊——這正是台灣的研究中心可以為資源不足學校推行的模式。","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/overview","https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/proof-of-concept","https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/hydrogels","https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/inclusivity","https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/science-communication","https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/parts","https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/ualberta/safety-and-security","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/ualberta/software-glare"],"rank":110},"6263":{"team":"Bist-China","id":"6263","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/bist-china/","projectTitle":"PyrLac Glow","tagline":"A dual lactate-pyruvate fluorescent sensing system as a low-cost grassroots pre-screening tool for cancer risk","summary":"PyrLac Glow reads the Warburg effect directly: two allosteric fluorescent biosensors, built by inserting YFP into the transcription regulators PdhR (pyruvate) and LldR (L-lactate), report the concentrations and the ratio of the two metabolites through a dual-lock mechanism. The project targets a specific structural gap in Chinese cancer screening - CT, endoscopy and liquid biopsy are accurate but inaccessible at grassroots level, while conventional serum tumour markers are cheap but not specific enough - with fewer than 10% of patients diagnosed early. The team ran 16 in-depth interviews across clinical practice, research, industry, public health, insurance, education and engineering, plus two questionnaires (208 and 113 valid responses), organised into five sequential stages each answering one question and each closing with a 'What we changed' statement. The biomarker architecture, the product category, the deployment scenarios, the hardware scope, the software permission model and the outreach strategy all changed as a direct result.","awards":["Best New Composite Part — Nominee (High School)","Best Hardware — Nominee (High School)","Best Presentation — Nominee (High School)","Best Integrated Human Practices — Nominee (High School)","Best Village Project — Nominee (Infectious Diseases / Therapeutics / Diagnostics / Oncology)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A multi-evidence computational screening workflow to choose YFP insertion breakpoints in each sensor, combining conserved domain annotation, static structural rigidity assessment, physicochemical profiling, molecular docking and molecular dynamics. For PdhR they built a five-feature weighted scoring model that scores and ranks every residue along the full-length sequence, with C-terminal oligomerisation residues included but penalised by steric hindrance and conformational tolerance terms, and high-scoring candidates still requiring manual secondary verification. For LldR they started from experimentally validated insertion hotspots reported in patent CN113004420A rather than scoring blind.","dataviz":"An interactive five-stage IHP architecture diagram with collapsible numbered nodes, a four-group stakeholder classification map (end screening users, clinical practitioners, industry and technical developers, public health and policy regulators) with each group's concerns attached, and a closed-loop summary figure pairing core achievements, key limitations and future plans.","datascience":"Questionnaire analysis with explicit sampling-bias reporting: 78.37% female respondents, 91.83% urban, income above 20,000 RMB per year, and the team states outright that the sample under-covers rural, low-income and elderly male populations and makes those groups a target for later outreach. Hardware requirement data were gathered in a second, deliberately non-overlapping questionnaire. Apo-to-holo conformational modelling explains the sensing mechanism: hinge flexibility distorts the embedded YFP beta-barrel for low basal fluorescence, and ligand-induced contraction rigidifies the hinge so YFP refolds and fluorescence rises.","software":"A modular data processing backbone designed with a former Microsoft vice president: signal acquisition, data buffering, data quality verification, sample labelling, separate processing pipelines for CMOS sensors and photoresistors, data storage and visualisation, with anonymous sample IDs, full retention of both raw and processed data, spreadsheet export at prototype stage, and module decoupling so sensors or verification algorithms can be upgraded without rebuilding the system.","stack":["molecular docking","molecular dynamics simulation","conserved domain annotation","weighted multi-feature residue scoring","CMOS sensor and photoresistor pipelines","Kahoot (for outreach assessment)"],"techniques":["allosteric transcription-factor biosensor engineering (YFP insertion into PdhR and LldR)","insertion breakpoint screening","standard curve construction with biological and technical replicates","fluorescence characterisation","POCT prototype design with disposable preloaded cartridges"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Outreach is unusually self-critical for a high school team. They produced two differentiated brochures (a children's version with illustrations and simple language, and a systematic middle/high school version covering experimental principles), ran an activity at Suzhou Science and Technology Town Foreign Language High School for about 60 ninth-graders using a Kahoot quiz to build the prerequisite cell-biology concepts before introducing the project, and a themed lacquer-fan creation exercise so students re-expressed the science visually. A shopping-mall event reached a broad cross-section but returned only three completed questionnaires from high foot traffic, and the team published that failure with a diagnosis: a mall suits short accessible outreach rather than detailed survey collection, their material distribution lacked interactive elements and 'often raised suspicion', and next time they would lead with their school and iGEM identity to build trust and standardise the introduction between team members. For a professional audience they rewrote the talk, cutting health-management content and expanding the Warburg effect, dual-biomarker and protein-expression material, then coded the questions received into knowledge and attitude dimensions. A 30-student pre-study tested whether a single outreach event can shift awareness at all.","ihp":"Bist-China's five-stage structure forces each stakeholder round to produce a change, and the changes are substantial rather than cosmetic. The single biggest one is the biomarker architecture: the initial design used lactate alone, and a pathologist at a hospital in Zhuhai, Guangdong told them that many benign physiological fluctuations produce fluorescent signals resembling malignant signatures, so a single-marker assay 'would not be clinically accepted for large-scale pre-screening' - the team abandoned the single-lactate scheme and adopted combined lactate-pyruvate detection, making specificity and anti-interference the primary optimisation goals. Dr Feiran Han (Director of the Institute of Science and Technology, LC-Bio) then confirmed dual-marker feasibility but told them two markers were the right number for a high-school project because a third would dilute validation depth, so they locked the panel at two and built standardised SOPs with replicates and standard curves converting fluorescence into metabolite concentrations. Stage 1 produced a product-category change: cancer survivors described the 1-2 year early warning window missed through fear of positive results, and oncologist Dr Wu Qing explained that fewer than 10% of cases are caught early and that clinicians fear false positives triggering public panic - crucially, Dr Wu partially contradicted the patient interviews, saying patients often refuse screening not because of cost but because they do not know how to interpret an ambiguous result, which the team records as shifting their attention 'from reducing cost to designing unambiguous result communication'. PyrLac Glow was repositioned from a diagnostic device to a risk pre-screening tool that refers high-risk individuals onward, with an explicit trade-off rule carried forward into Stage 2: prioritise reducing missed diagnoses while tolerating interpretable false positives. Staff at Cuiyuan Community Health Service Center in Xihu District, Hangzhou killed the household self-test idea outright - community centres have no high-precision instruments or full-time pathologists, send samples out for 3-7 day report cycles, have overloaded general practitioners, and will only adopt after official medical device certification - so the team abandoned household positioning and fixed three deployment scenarios. Prof. Ying Xiao of Shanghai University of Traditional Chinese Medicine changed the report interface: avoid absolute 'cancer / no cancer' conclusions and use physical-examination-style wording (metabolic abnormality, potential risk, re-test recommended), and treat constitution information as auxiliary explanation only since using it to reduce false positives remains a hypothesis. The most consequential safety change came from Erika Ferreri (Bellevue College, Washington State Department of Health, 21 years in medical laboratory education), who found the prototype could output cancer risk conclusions directly to ordinary users: the team re-scoped it as a bench-side research prototype for trained professionals, stripped risk judgments from the device interface so it reports only raw concentrations and quality-control status, added unique sample IDs, full raw-data retention and error-triggered automatic re-testing, separated the operator backend from the doctor and patient report interface, and deferred patient-facing reports until clinical validation - 'this transformed the prototype from an open prototype to a controlled medical research device'. A mechanical manufacturing chairman stopped them wasting the season on shell appearance and tolerances, imposing a core-function-first rule and forward design from commercially available standard components. Commercially, an AIA insurance specialist's view that insurers will not lead on immature technology and barely accept results from private organisations directly removed insurance as a primary channel, redirecting the strategy to corporate physical examinations and public medical screening; a corporate HR director with a 500-RMB-per-employee annual budget set a 200-RMB consumable cost target and added the third deployment scenario the team had missed; an IVD company chairman located the real gap between student prototype and product in batch stability and clinical validation rather than principle verification, turning a 5% to 15% CV benchmark into a quality-control design target. Most tellingly, they record advice they declined with reasons: they rejected educational psychologist Margaret's suggestion to invest in short-video platforms because a high-school team lacks the resources for continuous content production and the compliance capacity for medical-adjacent content, substituting a school health-curriculum lecture series and printed booklet; and they only partially accepted Erika Ferreri's multi-language recommendation, supporting Chinese and English now and deferring the rest. They also resolved a genuine disagreement among the iGEM teams they consulted about whether to validate biology before building hardware by choosing a middle path with a stated rule - hardware parameters must be re-validated against final Stage 2 experimental parameters before freezing.","realWorld":"The need is quantified against the system that would have to absorb the product: roughly 50% of cancers worldwide diagnosed at advanced stage, fewer than 10% of Chinese patients diagnosed early, 3-7 day report turnaround at community centres with no on-site pathologist, and 58.65% of their own 208 respondents unfamiliar with or completely unaware of early screening - from which they draw the sharpest framing in the project, that the bottleneck is the public 'does not know screening is needed' rather than refuses screening. Cost targets come from stakeholders rather than guesswork and are triangulated across two independent sources: public expectation of under 1,000 RMB per test from the questionnaire, and a per-person threshold of 200 RMB from the corporate HR budget of about 500 RMB per employee per year. Hardware constraints are equally specific: results within 30 minutes, wireless transmission to a phone (62.83% called this very necessary), disposable preloaded disc cartridges, single-use safety (76.11% support), and professional-scenario priority. The regulatory path is laid out concretely - medical device registration and official certification as the precondition for community adoption, POCT specifications for the operating manual, and prospective clinical trials enrolling high-risk populations with 1-2 years of follow-up to establish consistency and positive and negative predictive value, with a staged roadmap of top-tier hospital pilot, data-driven validation, then guideline endorsement, and a stated commercialisation horizon of 3-5 years (5-10 for widespread adoption). No SDG is claimed anywhere on the wiki, which is a genuine gap for a project that frames itself in public-health terms. The limitations section is honest and specific: laboratory validation only with no large clinical sample set for threshold training, no medical device qualification, the science communication plan still at design stage, and the questionnaire sample biased toward urban populations. Future work is committed to a clinical-pilot-first route before any market expansion.","partners":["Cuiyuan Community Health Service Center, Xihu District, Hangzhou","LC-Bio (Dr Feiran Han)","Multicell Biotech (Dr Qingliang Yang)","Shanghai University of Traditional Chinese Medicine (Prof. Ying Xiao)","Bellevue College / Washington State Department of Health (Erika Ferreri)","AIA Insurance","an IVD companion diagnostic company","a mechanical processing enterprise","Suzhou Science and Technology Town Foreign Language High School","ZJU-China, ZJUT-China, HiZJU-China, Hangzhou-Fourteen-AP, OTIA-Hangzhou, WUXI-DSAS, iZJU-China and ZZU-China iGEM teams"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6263/wiki/hp/h-2.avif","caption":"Interview with oncology clinician Dr Wu Qing, who partially contradicted the patient interviews and moved the team's focus from cost reduction to unambiguous result communication","credit":"Team Bist-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6263/wiki/hp/h-3.avif","caption":"Interview at Cuiyuan Community Health Service Center, Hangzhou, which ended the household self-test positioning and fixed three professional deployment scenarios","credit":"Team Bist-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6263/wiki/hp/h-5.avif","caption":"Interview with Dr Feiran Han of LC-Bio, who confirmed the dual-biomarker design and advised locking the panel at two markers rather than adding a third","credit":"Team Bist-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6263/wiki/hp/h-9.avif","caption":"Cross-team communication session with nine Chinese iGEM teams, where a disagreement about validating biology before building hardware was resolved into an explicit re-validation rule","credit":"Team Bist-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Record the advice you declined and why, alongside the advice you took: Bist-China's refusals (short-video outreach beyond their compliance capacity, multi-language deferred to commercialisation) and its openly flagged stakeholder contradictions are what prove the engagement was deliberation rather than endorsement-collection.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/bist-china/","https://2026.igem.wiki/bist-china/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/bist-china/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/bist-china/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/bist-china/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/bist-china/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/bist-china/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/bist-china/results"],"rank":35},"6264":{"team":"NBJF","id":"6264","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"Space / Foundational Advance (Best Village Project nominee; the village is not named on the wiki, but the project is framed as DNA data storage for long-duration spaceflight)","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/nbjf/","projectTitle":"AI-assisted de novo design of a thermostable TdT for enzymatic DNA synthesis","tagline":"Redesigning nature's DNA typewriter so information can be written into DNA","summary":"NBJF tackled the write step of DNA data storage. Enzymatic DNA synthesis using terminal deoxynucleotidyl transferase (TdT) avoids the toxic chemistry of phosphoramidite synthesis, but wild-type TdT has a melting temperature of roughly 40 C and a catalytic pocket that does not accommodate bulky modified nucleotides. Over seven Design-Build-Test-Learn cycles the team built an AI-assisted de novo protein design pipeline (RFdiffusion backbone generation, ProteinMPNN/LigandMPNN inverse folding, ESMFold and AlphaFold refolding checks, TemStaPro and SaProt thermostability scoring), screened a large candidate library down to a shortlist, expressed 85 designs, and obtained a de novo TdT that retains DNA extension activity at elevated temperature and accepts oxyamino-modified nucleotides. A final cycle used 100 ns molecular dynamics at 300/350/400 K to explain why.","awards":["Best New Basic Part — Nominee (High School)","Best Village Project — Nominee (Space / Foundational Advance / Software & AI / Biomanufacturing)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Structure-based generative protein design plus all-atom molecular dynamics, not kinetic modelling. The design loop is: functionally constrained RFdiffusion backbone generation (motif scaffolding, keeping the DNA-binding region and active site as constraints) -> ProteinMPNN/LigandMPNN inverse folding (LigandMPNN used for sequence design in the DNA-containing structural environment) -> ESMFold for structural recovery -> AlphaFold refinement -> TemStaPro (sequence-based) and SaProt (structure-based) thermostability scoring. Cycle 7 is a full biophysics workflow: AlphaFold 3 protein-DNA-dATP-2Mg2+-Na+ complex model, ORCA quantum-chemical geometry optimisation of dATP, RESP charges via Multiwfn, AmberTools parameterisation, ff19SB protein / OL21 DNA / OPC water / GAFF ligand force fields, energy minimisation, NVT heating, NPT density equilibration with gradual restraint release, then 100 ns production runs per system at 300 K, 350 K and 400 K.","dataviz":"Quantitative screening plots rather than decoration: RMSD-versus-pLDDT scatter of the whole candidate library showing the trade-off and the small fraction satisfying both criteria, representative predicted-structure overlays showing the failure mode (compact Rossmann-like folds instead of the open catalytic conformation), and MD analysis panels for RMSD, RMSF, DSSP secondary-structure occupancy, hydrogen-bond counts, radius of gyration, SASA, free-energy landscapes and Markov state model populations. The engineering page also carries a reading-guide layout that routes a non-specialist through four entry points.","datascience":"Library-scale screening with explicit multi-metric criteria instead of a single score: two independent design batches of 100 backbones each, 1,000 inverse-folded sequences per backbone, scored on both RMSD to the design target and pLDDT, yielding 94 candidates meeting both thresholds. Later cycles add cross-model agreement (ESMFold recovery plus two orthogonal thermostability predictors) and a spatial-placeholder strategy to enlarge the catalytic pocket. Experimental side: 85 de novo sequences expressed under one unified B0034/expression framework, 25 giving detectable SDS-PAGE expression - reported as an application dataset rather than a success claim.","software":"No standalone released application, but the team wrote automated scripts chaining backbone generation, sequence design, structural validation, candidate screening and MD analysis, and publish this as a reproducible, scalable de novo protein design workflow explicitly intended to lower the barrier for future iGEM teams. The Software special-award page was not among the project's own pages.","stack":["RFdiffusion (motif scaffolding)","ProteinMPNN and LigandMPNN","ESMFold","AlphaFold and AlphaFold 3","TemStaPro","SaProt","ORCA (QM geometry optimisation)","Multiwfn (RESP charge fitting)","AmberTools (ff19SB, OL21, OPC, GAFF)","molecular dynamics production runs (100 ns per system)","DSSP, RMSD/RMSF/Rg/SASA analysis, free-energy landscapes, Markov state models","automation scripts for the screening pipeline"],"techniques":["functionally constrained generative backbone design","inverse folding in a ligand/DNA-aware structural context","multi-model cross-screening (fold recovery + two thermostability predictors)","RMSD/pLDDT joint thresholding to filter a large candidate library","spatial placeholder strategy to enlarge a catalytic pocket","temperature-series MD (300/350/400 K) to compare designed vs wild-type protein","Markov state modelling and free-energy landscape analysis of conformational states","closing the loop: computational mechanism analysis run only after wet-lab activity data existed"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A seven-stage education programme that is unusually serious about access rather than reach: synthetic biology classes in schools; accessibility work including sign-language science communication and multilingual courses; creative formats (picture books, board games, art activities); community-specific sessions; digital microlearning; an explicit 'Inclusion and Equal Opportunities in STEM' stage; and international/cross-school scientific exchange. The team also co-built an educational website referenced by ZQT-Nanjing.","ihp":"An ASK -> LISTEN -> REFLECT -> INTEGRATE -> EVALUATE framework applied across four milestones, with the team stating up front that they did not want Human Practices to be a photo album. The decisive conversation was with Li Yang, an information-storage professional at Huawei, who pointed out that storage density alone decides nothing and that write/read/reliability/maintenance costs govern adoption - after which the team explicitly abandoned 'build a DNA storage device' and narrowed to the enzymatic-writing bottleneck. Han Minghao (synthetic biology / DNA engineering) then identified TdT thermostability, substrate compatibility and reaction controllability as the specific handles. Later stages cover intellectual property (two lawyers, Zhang and Wu, on who owns an AI-designed protein and on open science versus commercialisation), sustainability (Mr Liao on agricultural production, leading to a stated sustainability position on whether enzymatic synthesis is genuinely greener), and a Responsible AI section. Eight stakeholder categories were mapped.","realWorld":"The project is positioned as a tool-enzyme improvement inside a named industrial bottleneck rather than a finished product, which is the right call and was itself a Human Practices outcome. Deliverables for reuse: six new coding parts (BBa_263ET0E5 De novo TdT as the primary characterised part, plus five sequence-diverse variants BBa_26DIWVPI, BBa_266N6QG1, BBa_26BMB5EM, BBa_26NOOCP1, BBa_26YHUEKK), new application data added to the existing RBS BBa_B0034 documenting its behaviour across a library of 85 artificially designed coding sequences, and the automated de novo design workflow itself. The IP strand is unusually mature for a high-school team: they asked practising lawyers who owns an AI-generated sequence before assuming they could license it.","partners":["Li Yang, Huawei (information storage)","Han Minghao (synthetic biology and DNA engineering)","Lawyer Zhang (research achievements and intellectual property)","Lawyer Wu (open science and technology commercialisation)","Mr Liao (agricultural production / sustainability)","iGEM team ZQT-Nanjing (shared educational website)","partner schools in the cross-school exchange programme"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6264/wiki/engineering/img1.avif","caption":"The seven Design-Build-Test-Learn cycles, from the first unconstrained de novo design through structural reanalysis of wild-type TdT, pocket enlargement, expression screening and the closing molecular-dynamics cycle.","credit":"Team NBJF, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6264/wiki/description/img4.avif","caption":"'Meet our DNA typewriter': terminal deoxynucleotidyl transferase, the template-independent polymerase the project redesigns for controlled, letter-by-letter DNA writing.","credit":"Team NBJF, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6264/wiki/contribution/img2.avif","caption":"The reproducible de novo protein design workflow the team released for future iGEM teams, chaining RFdiffusion, ProteinMPNN, LigandMPNN, ESMFold, TemStaPro and SaProt with automation scripts.","credit":"Team NBJF, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6264/wiki/education/img16.avif","caption":"Education Stage VI, inclusion and equal opportunities in STEM, part of a seven-stage programme that also included sign-language science communication and multilingual courses.","credit":"Team NBJF, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"This is the ceiling, not the benchmark: the generative-design half (RFdiffusion, ProteinMPNN, ESMFold, AlphaFold, TemStaPro) is genuinely reachable by a strong high-school team in one season because the tools are free, documented and runnable on Colab-class GPUs, but Cycle 7 - ORCA quantum chemistry, RESP charge fitting, four-force-field Amber parameterisation and 100 ns MD at three temperatures with Markov state analysis - is not something students assemble unaided. The limiting factors there are mentorship and compute in that order; a Taiwanese programme could reproduce NBJF's screening pipeline with a laptop and a cloud GPU, but would need a university collaborator to attempt the MD.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/nbjf/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nbjf/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/nbjf/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/nbjf/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/nbjf/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/nbjf/parts","https://2026.igem.wiki/nbjf/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/nbjf/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/nbjf/notebook"],"rank":14},"6269":{"team":"UZurich","id":"6269","section":"Overgrad","country":"Switzerland","village":"Conservation","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/","projectTitle":"SeisMIC","tagline":"Stabilising Alpine slopes from within: engineered bacteria precipitate calcite between soil grains, with four linked models deciding where it is worth doing.","summary":"SeisMIC adapts microbially induced calcite precipitation (MICP) to Alpine slope stabilisation, where heavy rainfall is now 26% more frequent and 12% more intense and concrete anchoring is often out of proportion to the risk. Sporosarcina pasteurii hydrolyses urea so calcium carbonate crystallises around soil particles, filling pores and binding loose grains, and the team worked on the four limits that stop MICP transferring to the Alps: uneven cementation, scaling across large slopes, cold sensitivity and ammonium production. The distinctive contribution is the dry lab, which is a geospatial and economic decision system rather than a protein pipeline: an infinite-slope Factor of Safety model run across all of Switzerland on daily historical rainfall, a PHREEQC reactive transport model of calcite formation down a soil column, a QGIS MICP feasibility map, and an economic model using Flow-Py runout simulation to put a Swiss franc figure on damage avoided. The models are linked to each other and were reshaped by named expert feedback, which is what earned the Best Model nomination.","awards":["Top 10 (Overgrad)","Best Model — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Presentation — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Wiki — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Conservation Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Four models, explicitly chained so each one's output is the next one's input. (1) Slope Stability: an infinite-slope model computing the Factor of Safety from effective cohesion, effective friction angle, slope angle, soil unit weight and the pore-pressure ratio, split into a temporal model that drives soil saturation and pore-water pressure from daily historical rainfall through a bucket hydrology scheme and is validated against recorded landslide events, and a spatial model that runs the same calculation Switzerland-wide to find unstable pixels and, crucially, to output the additional effective cohesion MICP would have to supply - a direct, quantitative target the wet lab can be measured against. Root cohesion is modelled as a parallel natural source, with scenarios for bare soil, roots, MICP and roots plus MICP; the modelled unstable share falls from 82.8% to 28.9% under combined roots and MICP, stabilising 65.04% of initially unstable pixels. (2) Reactive Transport: an adaptation of the Razbani et al. model in PHREEQC, simulating a 52 cm sand column as ten stacked cells with bacteria pre-attached to grains and a urea/CaCl2 cementation solution pumped from below over ~52 hours, using Michaelis-Menten ureolysis kinetics (Rmax, Km, initial reactive surface area, biomass decay time td) and calcite precipitation rate constants k1 = 1.55e-6 and k2 = 0.501 mol m-2 s-1, reproducing both continuous-flow and stop-flow experiments; run with the wet lab's own recipe (1.015 M urea, 2 M CaCl2) it showed more than 2 M CaCl2 brings no benefit, and it predicts 77-79% of lab calcite still forms at 4 C, identifying acidic pH rather than temperature as the bigger obstacle. (3) MICP Feasibility: a binary suitability classification in QGIS combining public Swiss soil and terrain layers on stone content, water storage capacity, permeability and slope, giving 67.06% of Switzerland as technically feasible, then overlaid on landslide hazard and on the stability output to produce a MICP Injection Map - 67.32% of modelled unstable pixels fall inside feasible areas. (4) Economic: unstable cells (FoS <= 1) become release areas fed into the open-source Flow-Py gravitational mass-flow model, producing a runout envelope of 425.2 km2 from 568,627 release cells in the mpp = 1.0 scenario (62.0% of canton Glarus, 348.7-425.2 km2 across tested hydrological conditions); historical landslide frequencies and damage costs then give expected annual damage per asset class (roads, buildings, railways, forests, agricultural land), and tracing the highest-damage locations back to their contributing release areas says where treatment would pay. Combined roots and MICP lower estimated annual damage from CHF 583,000 to CHF 351,000, a 39.8% reduction. A directed evolution strand runs alongside, aimed at a non-GMO second strain.","dataviz":"The modelling work is presented as a prototype decision tool, not a figure dump. An Integrated Dashboard connects slope stability, MICP feasibility, rainfall and potential damage into a single interactive surface for deployment planning, and the team is unusually honest about its state: it currently covers slope stability and selected treatment scenarios and does not yet integrate all four models, so it is labelled a prototype of the intended end-user tool. The model landing page leads with four headline numbers (-53.9% unstable area, 67.06% of Switzerland feasible, 67.32% overlap, -39.8% annual damage, 77-79% calcite at 4 C) each linked to the model that produced it, with arrow navigation between models. Supporting visuals are decision-oriented rather than decorative: unstable share and p95 pore-pressure by canton (which ties instability to the cantonal offices that actually do prevention planning), seasonal cohesion requirements, a required-cohesion histogram, sensitivity analysis, an agreement map against the SilvaProtect reference dataset, and per-asset risk maps for roads, railways, buildings, forest and agricultural land. Derivations are offered as downloadable PDFs (infinite-slope FoS, critical saturation, bucket model) so the maths can be checked independently. An Awards page states plainly which awards the team is claiming and summarises the evidence for each.","datascience":"Their strongest data-science moment is a debugging story they chose to publish. The adapted PHREEQC model initially would not run at all, failing with 'Model failed to converge for initial solution 0'; raising iteration counts, changing tolerances and step size and improving initial guesses did nothing, and removing the calcite-equilibrium constraint made it converge to a physically absurd pH of 1.5. They computed the charge balance at fixed pH from 1 to 12, found it never reached zero, inspected the species and discovered ammonium was almost entirely in its neutral form (5.67e-2 M Amm against 8e-11 M AmmH+) because the reaction AmmH+ = Amm + H+ in the phreeqc.dat database carried no equilibrium constant, so PHREEQC set it to 0 instead of about -9.25; they fixed it with the parameters of the database's own NH4+ = NH3 + H+ reaction. The stated lesson - always check the values a model produces, not just the absence of errors - is the reusable part. The rest of the pipeline is integration work: joining national rainfall records, landslide inventories, digital elevation models, land cover and soil property rasters into one framework, validating predicted instability against recorded events and against SilvaProtect, running sensitivity analyses, and carrying each model's limitations on its own page.","software":"Code is published: the rainfall-triggered slope instability and MICP modelling at https://github.com/Alizzie/RainfallTriggeredSlopeInstabilityMICP, with the team repository at https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/uzurich. They did not build a standalone released application; the deliverables are the four validated models, the nationwide MICP Feasibility Map and MICP Injection Map (which they note did not previously exist for Switzerland in any public form), and the Integrated Dashboard prototype on the wiki. They also published a measurement framework for MICP experiments - biological screening, calcium measurement, powder recovery and soil analysis as several independent readouts rather than one, with assay limitations and validation checks documented so future teams can interpret MICP experiments more reliably.","stack":["PHREEQC (+ patched phreeqc.dat)","QGIS","Flow-Py","Python","R","Swiss digital elevation and soil/terrain rasters","MeteoSwiss rainfall records and climate scenarios","Swiss landslide inventories","SilvaProtect (validation reference)","GitHub / iGEM GitLab","interactive web dashboard"],"techniques":["infinite-slope Mohr-Coulomb Factor of Safety","bucket hydrology model for antecedent soil moisture","pore-pressure ratio scenario sweeps","back-solving for required additional cohesion as a wet-lab target","root cohesion versus engineered cohesion scenario comparison","Michaelis-Menten ureolysis kinetics in a 1D reactive transport column","charge-balance diagnosis of a thermodynamic database error","sensitivity analysis to identify controlling parameters","binary multi-criteria raster suitability classification","map overlay to find instability-feasibility intersections","gravitational mass-flow runout simulation","expected annual damage (EAD) estimation per asset class","tracing damage back to contributing release areas","validation against an independent national hazard dataset"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education was run as a two-way exchange explicitly tied to the values the team set in its Human Practices work - transparency, honesty, communication and collaboration - and they state that those became practical criteria for how they communicated rather than abstract principles. Social media carried three recurring formats: 'What even is...?' deep dives into a single concept, 'Word of the Week' introducing one piece of terminology at a time without burying readers in project detail, and 'Myth vs. Fact' separating common assumptions about bacteria, biotechnology and climate change from what the evidence supports. In-person work included an Activity Fair stand and workshops, plus ZurichLernt, and across every activity they tried to distinguish three things for their audience: what is already known, what their own project demonstrated, and what they could not investigate within the time and resources available. They brought in a strategic communication professional to test their assumptions about how to build a campaign, since nobody on the team had communications training.","ihp":"The interview process itself is the method: prepare (write down why this person, what you hope to learn, which assumptions you want tested, and how their input could change SeisMIC), interview with enough flexibility to follow unexpected leads, then reflect back in an interview log on what actually changed, what challenged an assumption, what new concern it raised and who to speak to next. Stakeholders were mapped on a power-interest matrix used to decide how to approach each one rather than to rank importance, and ELSI was treated as a connected framework rather than three boxes. Concrete changes: a researcher told them to start from the environment rather than the organism rather than defaulting to E. coli because it is well characterised. A pore-scale fluid dynamics researcher listed the parameters no MICP model should omit (temperature, pH, oxygen, ion and calcite concentrations, urea hydrolysis, water saturation) and recommended sensitivity analysis to find which dominate - so they dropped a machine learning idea rather than spending the summer discovering it could not be trained, moved the reactive transport work onto established software instead of a custom implementation, and added the sensitivity analysis. Dr. Joaquin Jimenez-Martinez's feedback changed how they treat temperature, bacterial survival and pH. Stakeholders and their PIs repeatedly asking how much vegetation already contributes is why root cohesion was added to the stability model. A microbiologist corrected their premise directly - ammonia release makes soil more basic, not acidic - sending them back to locate the real problem, and suggested reading pH change around colonies with plate indicators; another suggested nitrification inhibitors to stop nitrate forming. An expert pointed out that innovative biological methods usually fail on political opposition rather than feasibility, technology or financing, and suggested they also consider protected natural areas. They dropped CLIMADA after Prof. David Bresch's guidance and reframed the economic benefit as fewer slope failures. Residents below the slopes said what they value most is the surrounding nature, which made the ecological cost of the treatment something to investigate rather than assume; their hesitation about engineered bacteria eased once biomineralisation was explained as a natural process, which told the team their job is explaining the mechanism rather than defending the idea.","realWorld":"The business case is built on a gap they verified rather than assumed: many at-risk Swiss slopes get no protection because concrete and anchors are disproportionate to the risk, and two cantons, Lucerne and Glarus, independently described exactly such slopes. Interviews with Marco Peyer (Risktec) and Prof. David Bresch (ETH Zurich) moved them off insurers and onto the real decision chain - the canton decides and pays, an engineering office proposes the method, the federal government co-finances - so the customer is cantonal natural-hazard offices and their consulting engineers. The offer is deliberately a bundle: a site-specific treatment delivered together with the modelling that shows how much damage it avoids, because as Ulrich Kaiser pointed out, prevention has a visibility problem - a stabilised slope produces no event, no headline and no credit, while the cost is immediate and concrete, so proving avoided damage has to be part of the product. Interest is reported honestly as interest, not sales: one canton offered to connect them with a suitable slope and another asked to follow the damage model, with the team stating plainly that neither is a customer yet. The roadmap is about five to eight years from lab to a first slope, with Swiss approval staged as lab, then field trial, then market. Risks are named with mitigations: urea run-off requires rinsing (one company converts the run-off to fertiliser) and they are investigating a lower-urea route while stating nothing is settled at field scale; containment is handled by a kill switch plus a second strain adapted by directed evolution without genetic engineering.","partners":["Prof. David Bresch, ETH Zurich (climate risk / economic framing)","Dr. Joaquin Jimenez-Martinez (pore-scale fluid dynamics in MICP)","Marco Peyer, Risktec (natural hazard consulting)","Ulrich Kaiser (economics of prevention)","Canton of Lucerne (natural hazard office)","Canton of Glarus (natural hazard office)","University of Zurich (UZH MNF, ULF, Science Alumni)","Galbiati Stiftung","Alpine residents and farming communities below at-risk slopes"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6269/wiki/stability-model/pipeline-overview.avif","caption":"The slope stability modelling pipeline, which joins rainfall records, landslide inventories, terrain and soil data into an infinite-slope Factor of Safety calculation and outputs the extra cohesion MICP would need to supply.","credit":"Team UZurich, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6269/wiki/stability-model/stability-interactive.avif","caption":"The interactive slope stability view behind the Integrated Dashboard prototype, which the team presents as a planning tool for deciding where MICP treatment is worth investigating rather than as a finished product.","credit":"Team UZurich, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6269/wiki/economic-model/risk-map-rounded.avif","caption":"Economic risk map for canton Glarus: Flow-Py runout from unstable release cells combined with historical landslide frequency and damage costs to give expected annual damage by location.","credit":"Team UZurich, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6269/wiki/human-practices/education/activity-fair/af1.avif","caption":"The team at their Activity Fair stand, part of an education programme run as two-way exchange and explicitly tied to the transparency and honesty values set in their Human Practices work.","credit":"Team UZurich, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Steal their interview discipline, which needs no equipment: before every expert conversation write down why this person, what you hope to learn, which assumption you want tested and how their answer could change the project, then log afterwards what actually changed and who to talk to next - that single loop is what let them kill an untrainable machine learning idea in one conversation instead of losing a summer to it. Their published PHREEQC debugging story is the second lesson worth printing on the wall: a model that runs without errors can still be wrong, so check the values, not just the exit code.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/stability-model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/reactive-transport-model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/injection-model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/economic-model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/methods/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/directed-evolution/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/measurement/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/results/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/human-practices-overview/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/education/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/entrepreneurship/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/sustainability/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/contribution/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uzurich/awards/"],"rank":98},"6276":{"team":"Michigan","id":"6276","section":"Undergrad","country":"United States","village":"Therapeutics","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/michigan/","projectTitle":"MagNav","tagline":"Magnetically steered Magnetospirillum magneticum carrying a heat-triggered therapeutic, with RiboTherm, an MCMC optimiser for RNA thermometers.","summary":"MagNav uses Magnetospirillum magneticum AMB-1, a magnetotactic bacterium that follows external magnetic fields and thrives in low-oxygen environments, as a vector for delivering ClyA into ovarian cancer and endometriotic tissue. Alternating magnetic fields generate heat inside the bacteria, which induces therapeutic expression through a sigma-32 heat shock promoter; because heat shock promoters leak and imprecise expression would damage healthy tissue, the team added an RNA thermometer in the 5' UTR that folds to sequester the Shine-Dalgarno sequence and physically block ribosome binding until the temperature rises. The dry lab built RiboTherm to redesign that thermometer: an open-source Python package that searches 32 designable positions with a Metropolis-Hastings MCMC sampler against a two-term objective combining a ddG-open switching score with a novel Jensen-Shannon ensemble regulariser that keeps the 37 degree C silent state close to the parent. Three designs went to the bench, one (M1) held basal expression below the Neupert U8 parent while still responding at 45 degree C, and the team reports the rest of the comparison with explicit caveats about a single unreplicated blot.","awards":["Best New Improved Part — Winner (Undergrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"RiboTherm is a standalone open-source Python package built on ViennaRNA (RNAfold/RNAheat and base-pair probability matrices) and distributed as a 30 KB ZIP from the wiki at https://2026.igem.wiki/michigan/downloads/rnatherm-design-main.zip, with installation, directory layout, CLI and a worked example in the repository README. A design campaign is specified entirely in one YAML file, and the package's architecture keeps four things declared independently so any one can be swapped without touching the others: the construct and which positions may mutate, the feature functions that score a candidate, the objective weights that combine them, and the sampler. The team is explicit that their own scientific contribution sits only in the middle two, and that a new feature is registered as a function taking the folded ensemble, the temperatures and a window and returning a number. Each run writes a copy of its own configuration alongside one trajectory file per chain, and stores both feature values rather than only the combined objective, so a campaign can be re-scored at a different lambda without re-folding anything. Null-distribution comparison and final design selection are deliberately left outside the package. No hosted web deployment; wiki repo at https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/michigan.","dataviz":"The model page is written as a methods paper and figures carry that weight: minimum-free-energy structures of the Neupert U1-U10 thermometers with SD, spacer and start codon colour-coded by role; heat-capacity curves computed with RNAheat plus a two-state test across the Sen et al. library; the correlation between ddG-open and measured fold change as a function of the scoring window half-width; a context-length convergence plot shown on a log scale with and without the base-pair span cap, alongside a full context-by-context pairwise divergence matrix; the Pareto front with 5,000 grey null sequences behind the four design campaigns shaded light to dark by lambda and the three selected designs marked; a figure explaining how a YAML campaign is specified and what it produces; MFE structures of the three designs against the parent with black rings on mutated positions; and the western blot. Every figure caption states what the figure does and does not support.","datascience":"The design space is roughly 4^32, about 2 x 10^19 sequences, which the team notes would take about a year to enumerate even parallelised, so they used a Metropolis-Hastings MCMC optimiser with single-nucleotide uniform proposals. Four campaigns of eight independent chains at 20,000 moves each gave 640,000 scored proposals, 391,835 of them unique. A 5,000-sequence null distribution was built first to calibrate hyperparameters, and it revealed that the two objective terms sit on completely different scales: random sequences score about 0.91 on JS-mean against the parent's 0.0095, nearly two orders of magnitude apart, while ddG-open spans only about +0.5 to -1.8 kcal/mol against the parent's -1.33, with only about 3% of random sequences beating the parent at all. The selection rule was fixed before any results were inspected: beat U8+2GC on ddG-open, then rank by lowest JS-mean. The headline number is published plainly: 335,408 sequences beat the parent on switching, but only 28 of those also beat it on ensemble similarity, which the team presents as the clearest statement of how sharp the Pareto front is. They connect that front to published theory, noting that recent work finds threshold temperature inversely proportional to peak sensitivity in two-state models and that the tradeoff survives in multi-state and branched models. Two methodological choices are documented with their justification. First, the base-pair span is capped at 150 nt throughout, because ViennaRNA's predictions become unreliable beyond roughly 100-200 nt, and applying the cap is what makes truncation defensible: with it, the windowed ensemble converges to 0.0095 at 100 nt of flanking context, while without it the metric never converges, staying between 0.024 and 0.048 at every length because unpredictable long-range pairs keep reshuffling the ensemble. Second, the reference pairing vectors are computed once from the full 1,189 nt construct folded at 37 degree C, not from the truncated layout the sampler scores on, and the team flags this as the detail easiest to get wrong on reimplementation. They also publish an accessibility check that was never used in selection, P(SD unpaired) at 42 over 37 degree C, where all three designs improve on the parent's 1.95x (M1 3.03x, M2 4.78x, M3 4.33x). Limits on the incoming data are stated too: the Sen et al. library used for fitting was measured in a cell-free E. coli extract with no membrane, no chromosomal transcription and a different ribosome and RNase load, so transferring it to living AMB-1 is named as the largest untested assumption carried by the model.","software":"The interesting engineering contribution is the Jensen-Shannon ensemble regulariser, which answers a different question from standard RNA inverse design. Rather than asking whether two sequences share a single most stable structure, it fixes a 30-nucleotide window centred on the Shine-Dalgarno sequence, reads each position's in-window pairing-partner distribution off the base-pair probability matrix, renormalises it to a probability distribution (assigning a uniform distribution where in-window pairing probability is negligible rather than leaving it undefined), and takes the mean Jensen-Shannon divergence against the reference. JS was chosen over KL because it is symmetric, always finite even where one distribution puts no weight, zero for identical distributions and bounded above by one bit. The consequence is visible in the results: all three designs fold to an identical MFE structure at both 37 and 42 degree C, so their predicted switching comes entirely from reweighting within the ensemble rather than from a change in the single most stable fold, and the team notes that inverse-design methods matching MFE structures at two temperatures cannot produce these sequences by construction. The structural finding is also reported: all three designs leave the anti-SD, loop and spacer at wild type and remodel only the anti-spacer, a pattern that held across the entire low-JS candidate set, suggesting the other elements of U8+2GC are already near-optimal for this scaffold. M2 is reported as the best-supported design in the sweep, independently rediscovered by two chains under both lambda = 5 and lambda = 10 and visited 45 times. The limits are listed without hedging: the package relies on ViennaRNA equilibrium thermodynamics so anything kinetically controlled is out of reach; it searches by single-nucleotide substitution only so insertions and deletions, including a changed stem length, are unreachable by construction, which the team notes is a real restriction given that the two most differently behaved thermometers in the Sen library differ by a single deletion; it needs a new reference ensemble per construct; runs are not resumable; and a design question involving several interacting switches or a target that cannot be written as a number is out of scope. Three things are named as what must change to apply it elsewhere (rewrite the construct block and rebuild the reference, set the temperatures and base-pair span for the new regime, re-tune the sampler temperature because lambda rescales the objective and the acceptance behaviour with it), with lambda = 0 offered as a pure ddG-open search for systems with no silent reference. The wet-lab validation is reported with unusual restraint: a single western blot without a loading control or replicates, induced at 45 degree C rather than the 42 degree C the designs were optimised for, so only a qualitative ordering is claimed and none of the predicted fold changes can be checked. M3 gave no detectable band in any lane including the 30 degree C control and is read as a construct that did not express, which the team notes cost them the one clean test of the regulariser, since M2 and M3 were matched on ddG-open (-1.851 vs -1.830) and differed mainly in JS-mean (0.0204 vs 0.0166) at only four positions. Of the two results they do claim, the second is qualified as 'an observation rather than evidence' because with n = 2 and a qualitative readout coincidence cannot be excluded. AI use is disclosed: Claude Code helped create the wiki figures and scaffolded much of the RiboTherm code, with all output reviewed before implementation.","stack":["Python","ViennaRNA (RNAfold, RNAheat, base-pair probability matrices)","NUPACK (reference literature method)","YAML campaign configuration","numpy/scipy-style numerics","ZIP source distribution","iGEM GitLab (wiki repo)"],"techniques":["Metropolis-Hastings MCMC discrete sequence optimisation","custom two-term objective with weighted regularisation","Jensen-Shannon divergence over per-position base-pair-probability distributions","ddG-open ensemble free-energy difference between temperatures","partition-function and heat-capacity (Cp) based melting-temperature estimation","two-state van't Hoff fitting","synthetic melt curves from base-pair probability matrices","null distribution construction for hyperparameter calibration","Pareto front analysis","base-pair span capping for folding-model reliability","sequence-context convergence testing","pre-registered selection rule","western blot qualitative validation"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"MSBTalks is a multimedia podcast series of recorded in-person and Zoom conversations with experts across synthetic biology, cancer biology, reproductive health, microbiology, chemical engineering and biophysics, published on the team's YouTube channel. The stated motive is unusual: the team modelled the episodes on office-hours conversations and published them specifically to show students what approaching an expert looks like, because they knew from their own experience how much nervousness precedes those meetings. Additional accessible outputs include a pre-printed manuscript, a videogame and a physical modeling kit.","ihp":"Human practices was framed around the fact that live-bacteria therapeutics attract scrutiny because bacteria are associated with contamination and infection rather than benefit, so the team worked through the bioethical considerations and then tested MagNav's framing with stakeholders. Expert conversations changed specific things. Dr. Costas Lyssiotis (Maisel Professor of Oncology, Michigan) agreed that localisation and specificity were the most important goal, told them the novelty of magnetically guided treatment meant AMB-1's magnetotaxis would need thorough characterisation, and told them to spell out why injecting AMB-1 near a tumour would not cause infection or sepsis; he also pushed them to hold the wiki to publication standards. Dr. Nicole Koropatkin (Microbiology and Immunology, Michigan) advised fusing synthetic surface proteins to small native proteins already known to localise where needed, and on working with a strain like AMB-1 that resists standard transformation. Dr. Geoffrey Greene (Ben May Department for Cancer Research, Chicago) endorsed the two-step targeting approach of hypoxia plus folate-receptor-alpha binding because combining two steps reduces off-target effects, and was sceptical of selective estrogen receptor degraders.","realWorld":"The problem is framed with cited figures: over 21,000 estimated new US ovarian cancer diagnoses in 2026, a 52% five-year relative survival rate for 2016-2022, 190 million reproductive-aged women affected by endometriosis worldwide, and an average 6.7-year endometriosis diagnostic delay for patients aged 18-45. MagNav is positioned as a modular and more precise alternative or addition to existing standards of care rather than a replacement, potentially usable alongside existing medication and surgery, and the team notes that novel therapies take years to become accessible. The customisable framework is presented as extensible to other cancers and reproductive diseases by changing the payload and targeting ligand.","partners":["University of Michigan Medical School (Rogel Center for Pancreatic Cancer; Microbiology and Immunology)","Ben May Department for Cancer Research, University of Chicago","Michigan Synthetic Biology Team / University of Michigan"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6276/wiki/wiki2-model-final-008.webp","caption":"The Pareto front between switching (ddG-open) and basal expression (JS-mean): 5,000 grey null sequences behind four design campaigns shaded by lambda, with the three selected designs marked on the low-JS end.","credit":"Team Michigan, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6276/wiki/wiki2-model-final-009.webp","caption":"How a RiboTherm design campaign is specified: one YAML file declaring construct, features, objective weights and sampler independently, running eight chains and writing both feature values so a campaign can be re-scored without re-folding.","credit":"Team Michigan, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6276/wiki/wiki2-model-final-007.webp","caption":"Choosing how much sequence context to fold: with the base-pair span capped at 150 nt the windowed ensemble converges by 100 nt of flanking context, while without the cap it never converges.","credit":"Team Michigan, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6276/wiki/wiki2-model-final-011.webp","caption":"Western blot against ClyA for the three RiboTherm designs and the two reference constructs, a single run without a loading control or replicates, with M3 giving no detectable band in any lane.","credit":"Team Michigan, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Fix the selection rule before looking at any results, then publish the number that shows how hard the problem is: 335,408 of 391,835 sequences beat the parent on switching but only 28 also beat it on ensemble similarity, which turns an optimisation run into a statement about the design space rather than a list of winners. Also copy their habit of justifying a computational shortcut by showing what happens without it, as with the 150 nt base-pair span cap that is the only reason truncated folding converges at all.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/michigan/","https://2026.igem.wiki/michigan/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/michigan/parts","https://2026.igem.wiki/michigan/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/michigan/downloads/rnatherm-design-main.zip","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/michigan"],"rank":26},"6278":{"team":"Stanford University","id":"6278","section":"Undergrad","country":"USA","village":"Therapeutics","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/stanford-university/","projectTitle":"KelePatch","tagline":"A logic-gated, cell-state-specific RNA therapy for keloid scars, delivered by a microneedle patch shaped to the wound.","summary":"KelePatch builds an ADAR-based RADAR RNA sensor that only switches on inside keloid myofibroblasts, so a therapeutic payload is produced in diseased cells and not in healthy skin. The team designed a 26-part modular sensor collection across five fibrosis transcripts (ADAM12, POSTN, ASPN, COL11A1, SPP1), validated them in HEK293 cells, combined the two best into a dual-input AND gate for extra selectivity, and tested in healthy dermal fibroblasts and keloid-derived fibroblasts; they also paired a sensor with Cas12a2 to show the output is not limited to fluorescent reporters. Alongside the wet lab they built RADAR-Scout, a published web platform that takes a cell type and a gene and returns a ranked, structure-aware list of RADAR sensor candidates plus a mechanistic simulation of how it will behave. It won the Grand Prize because every layer connects: 960,518 single cells of transcriptomics pick the trigger, ViennaRNA folding energy ranks the sensor, ODE models explain the delay they saw at the bench, and a U-Net++ computer vision pipeline turns a photo of a scar into a 3D-printable patch.","awards":["Grand Prize Winner (Undergrad)","Top 10 (Undergrad)","Best Model — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Wiki — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Therapeutics Project — Winner"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Four stacked layers. (1) Single-cell transcriptomics at scale: a processing pipeline integrating 26 scRNA-seq cohorts across cardiac, cutaneous, renal, hepatic and pulmonary fibrosis - 960,518 cells and 1,728 donor-population observations from CELLxGENE, CELLxGENE Census and GEO - with donor-level statistics averaged at equal donor weight so large-cell-count donors do not dominate. Rather than ordinary differential expression, they score each candidate across three populations (Pathological, Healthy, Bystander) to ask whether a transcript is abundant in the target cell and absent from neighbours, which is what an intracellular sensor actually requires. (2) RNA structure prediction: 19 predictors computed with ViennaRNA 2.7.2 (RNAfold for MFE and ensembles, RNApfold for per-nucleotide unpaired probability, RNAcofold for the sensor-trigger duplex) spanning sequence composition, secondary structure, accessibility and hybridization. (3) Mechanistic kinetics: five interconnected deterministic mass-action ODE models with a stochastic counterpart, covering plasmid nuclear entry, single-trigger plasmid, single-trigger RNA, AND-gate plasmid and AND-gate RNA delivery, built on Ligon et al.'s lipoplex delivery cascade with occupancy resolved into nine pit states and ten endosome states; 82 parameters are tabulated with provenance, and four are fitted by simulated annealing in Python against Cohen et al.'s qPCR nuclear copy-number data (p_entry = 0.107, K_sat = 232, k_TX = 0.273). A nine-state hybridization/editing scheme tracks the joint status of both AND-gate sites. (4) Device physics: finite element analysis using Fick's law, the Stokes-Einstein relation and Darcy's law for LNP diffusion through keloid extracellular matrix, plus a nociceptor-count model for pain.","dataviz":"RADAR-Scout is the visualization: a deployed web app (https://radar-scout.vercel.app/, with a companion dashboard at https://radar-scout-dashboard.vercel.app/) where the keloid view ranks 600 filtered genes across five cohorts on the left and plots every candidate sensor for the selected gene on the right, so a target and a sensor are chosen in the same screen, with filters for region type, codon variant, duplex length and isoform, and shortlist/CSV export. Changing the selected tissue reruns the isoform analysis live. The wiki itself is a hand-built site with per-page accent colours and mascot illustrations, and the modelling page is written so a reader can follow each decision: predictor correlations are shown three ways (full Spearman matrix at n = 24, per-replicate rho, then all predictors ranked) and the team states plainly that non-significant predictors are 'unresolved at n = 24 rather than confirmed null'. Parameter tables flag which values are fitted, which are placeholders, and which disagreements remain unresolved.","datascience":"The core result is a replacement for a field convention. The informal RADAR design guideline was to pick the candidate with the lowest GC content. Stanford built a 5x5 experimental library of 25 sensors, measured them by flow cytometry in HEK293 across two replicates (r = 0.94), gated the top 5% mCherry-positive cells and took geometric-mean GFP / geometric-mean mCherry as the output metric, then correlated 19 computational predictors against it. Sensor partition-function folding free energy reached Spearman rho = 0.62-0.63, against -0.29 for GC content and -0.31 for longest homopolymer - so folding energy, not composition, became the ranking filter inside RADAR-Scout. They were honest about what failed: linear, Ridge and Elastic Net regression on the same features reached only Q2 = 0.20, which is explicitly what pushed them from statistical fitting to mechanistic ODEs. Cross-organ analysis of the top 300 genes per organ found 857 of 1,136 distinct genes appeared in only one organ and pairwise Jaccard similarity of 0.050-0.145, so they rejected the idea of a universal fibrosis biomarker set. Isoform filtering uses GTEx Oxford Nanopore long-read data (~150,000 transcripts, 92 samples, 15 tissues) to check the trigger sequence is actually present in the isoforms that cell type expresses.","software":"RADAR-Scout, live at https://radar-scout.vercel.app/ with a dashboard at https://radar-scout-dashboard.vercel.app/. It solves a real engineering problem: the Gao lab's published RADAR candidate table has roughly 7 million rows and could not be held in memory, so build_database.py ingests human_RADAR_sensor_candidates.csv.gz into a SQLite database in 100,000-row chunks with an index on the gene column, and the app queries it read-only with 50 candidates per API page. The computer vision pipeline for personalized microneedle patches uses a U-Net++ with a ResNet34 encoder (from segmentation_models.pytorch) to segment keloid wound photographs, then drives the Autodesk Fusion 360 API to emit a CAD/STL file for 3D printing. Separately, SynBase (https://synbase.web.app/home.html) is a released, free, account-based online learning platform. Parts: 26 modular RADAR parts including 15 functional sensors across five transcripts, novel composite synthetic triggers that each test an entire sensor panel for one gene, a dual-input AND gate, and T7 in vitro transcribed capped polyadenylated mRNA versions.","stack":["ViennaRNA 2.7.2 (RNAfold, RNApfold, RNAcofold)","CELLxGENE / CELLxGENE Census","GEO (GSE163973, GSE181316)","Human Dermal Fibroblast Atlas","GTEx long-read (Oxford Nanopore) RNA-seq","Ensembl / GENCODE annotations","Python","SQLite","Vercel","U-Net++ with ResNet34 encoder (segmentation_models.pytorch)","Autodesk Fusion 360 API","Benchling","Firebase (SynBase)"],"techniques":["Deterministic mass-action ODE modelling","Stochastic (occupancy-resolved) simulation","Simulated annealing parameter fitting","Quasi-steady-state approximation for competitive ADAR binding","Nine-state hybridization/editing state machine","Differential expression with pathological/healthy/bystander contrast","Isoform-level expression filtering","RNA minimum free energy and partition-function analysis","Spearman and Pearson predictor screening","Linear/Ridge/Elastic Net regression (reported as insufficient)","Jaccard similarity for cross-organ overlap","Flow cytometry gating (95th percentile mCherry)","Finite element analysis (Fick, Stokes-Einstein, Darcy)","Semantic image segmentation","Parametric CAD generation"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Two deliberately linked programmes. SiBRP (Stanford iGEM Bioengineering Research Program) is a free, fully online three-week bioengineering bootcamp for high school students and incoming freshmen, with nine synchronous two-hour sessions plus three supplemental ones, progressing from molecular biology fundamentals through biodesign, genetic circuit design, plasmid design and experimental workflow to entrepreneurship and ethics. Students work in small groups to produce a full research proposal with literature review and experimental design, submitted as a draft, returned with TA feedback, then revised against a published rubric. It drew nearly 5,000 applications from all 50 US states and over 100 countries (up from 321 in its first year), with two-thirds of applicants female and over 60% from low-income and first-generation backgrounds; 230 participated. Nine guest speakers included iGEM co-founder Drew Endy. Because mentored capacity could not meet demand, the team converted the whole curriculum into SynBase (https://synbase.web.app/home.html) - 'Khan Academy, but for synthetic biology' - nine self-paced modules with accounts that save progress, knowledge checks, interactive activities and discussion boards, no application and no deadline, free worldwide. As of 17 October 2026 it had 750+ registered learners and 650+ free-response discussion contributions, with dry lab modules in development, and the team explicitly invites other iGEM teams to use or adapt it for onboarding their own members.","ihp":"The team was trained in Stanford's Biodesign process by Dr Ross Venook, who told them that biodesign means shadowing clinicians rather than searching online, and they built the whole project around that. Ideation ran as a weekly discipline: every member interviewed one person a week - over twenty conversations with professors, researchers and people in their lives - and a team member's experience with ReSurge, an NGO training reconstructive surgeons abroad, surfaced the statistic that 30% of global disease burden is surgical and reframed abnormal scarring as an access problem. Professor Fan Yang told them burns and keloids are separate research areas and doing both would muddle the work, so they picked one. At the Stanford BIOME Shark Tank they pitched to eight judges (faculty, investors, biotech entrepreneurs) who returned written scorecards; the published response table shows each criticism and what they did, including a judge's suggestion to build an AI-CAD platform for microneedles, which became the U-Net++ segmentation-to-Fusion-360 pipeline. When they looked for keloid patient advocacy groups there were almost none, and the one foundation that replied told them to talk to clinicians instead - the team says plainly that physicians cannot stand in for patients' lived experience and documents this as a second-best route. They then contacted 28 Stanford dermatologists and plastic surgeons and interviewed seven, with a standard instrument of Likert-scale ranking statements plus specialty-specific open questions. Three concerns recurred - recurrence within two years, pain and inconvenience of repeated injections, and difficulty getting drug into dense scar tissue - and each changed the design: Dr Teng's point that late-stage keloids are far harder to treat moved the target from prevention to established keloids; Dr Li's recommendation of collagen-scaffold fibroblast and hydrogel mechanotransduction assays changed the validation plan; physicians' complaint about repeated injections, plus Dr Li's endorsement of a patch, drove the wound-shaped microneedle array, held at 900 um because needles over 1000 um are documented to cause bleeding and pain. Dr Miranda consulted her own network on whether viral-derived parts are inflammatory, and the team decided against combining saRADAR with RNA export machinery as a result. With no animal model for keloids (they occur only in humans), they met Genoskin about their ex vivo human skin models and identified that as the next safety step.","realWorld":"The team was explicit at the Shark Tank that a target product profile was secondary to characterising a modular sensor platform other teams and scientists can reuse, and the contribution page is written as a handoff: swap the sensor region for a new transcript, add a second input as an AND gate, deliver as DNA or RNA, attach your own payload. The clinical path is staged and named - validate the Gao lab sensors and their own in HEK293, validate the AND gate, move to keloid and normal human fibroblast lines, add payload, then terminal assay in Genoskin's ex vivo human skin model for immunotoxicity, phenotypic and transcriptomic readouts - and Genoskin representatives engaged and advised on how to run it. The Cas12a2 payload work and the in vitro transcribed mRNA format are both framed as moving toward the form a real therapy would take rather than a reporter demo. SynBase is maintained beyond the competition as a continuing programme rather than a competition artefact.","partners":["ReSurge International","Genoskin","Stanford Biodesign","Stanford Hospital Department of Dermatology","Stanford Department of Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery","Stanford BIOME (Biological Interdisciplinary Open Maker Environment)","Bay Area Bioengineering Symposium","Stanford Arc Institute","Gao Lab (RADAR technology)","Covert Lab","CELLxGENE / Chan Zuckerberg Initiative","GTEx Consortium"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6278/wiki/m2-fig4-trigger-selection.webp","caption":"Trigger selection in RADAR-Scout: 600 filtered genes ranked across five keloid cohorts on the left (POSTN first at DSS 1.288), with every candidate sensor for the selected gene plotted on the right, so target and sensor are chosen in one view.","credit":"Team Stanford University, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6278/wiki/m2-fig10-rho-ranked.webp","caption":"All 19 computational predictors ranked by Spearman rho against sensor output: the two folding-energy terms lead at 0.62-0.63 while GC content, the field's informal selection rule, reaches only -0.29.","credit":"Team Stanford University, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6278/wiki/m3-cv1-patch.webp","caption":"A microneedle array patch generated from a photograph of a keloid scar: U-Net++ with a ResNet34 encoder segments the wound, and the Autodesk Fusion 360 API turns the mask into a 3D-printable CAD file.","credit":"Team Stanford University, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6278/wiki/m2-fig20-nine-state.webp","caption":"The nine-state hybridization and editing scheme for the AND-gate RADAR sensor; only the doubly-edited state is translated into GFP, and the enumerated transitions are how the system was verified to be complete.","credit":"Team Stanford University, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6278/wiki/sibrp-call.webp","caption":"The final session of SiBRP 2026, the team's free three-week online bioengineering bootcamp, with students joining from 24 US states and 40 countries.","credit":"Team Stanford University, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Stanford's SiBRP-to-SynBase pivot is the directly copyable move: they ran a small mentored cohort, discovered demand they could not staff (5,000 applications for 230 places), and then converted the exact same curriculum into a free self-paced online course with progress tracking and discussion boards - so the teaching asset outlives the cohort. A high-school-plus centre in Taiwan can do the same with its own course material, and should also adopt their dry-lab habit of testing the field's received wisdom (lowest GC content) against its own measured data and replacing it with a better predictor.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/stanford-university/","https://2026.igem.wiki/stanford-university/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/stanford-university/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/stanford-university/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/stanford-university/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/stanford-university/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/stanford-university/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/stanford-university/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/stanford-university/parts","https://2026.igem.wiki/stanford-university/safety","https://radar-scout.vercel.app/","https://radar-scout-dashboard.vercel.app/","https://synbase.web.app/home.html"],"rank":230},"6279":{"team":"UBC-Vancouver","id":"6279","section":"Undergrad","country":"Canada","village":"Diagnostics","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/ubc-vancouver/","projectTitle":"FAST: a point-of-care antibiotic susceptibility test","tagline":"Three devices, a 200-promoter screen and a measurement page that opens by admitting the readout is the whole diagnostic.","summary":"UBC-Vancouver built FAST, a point-of-care antibiotic susceptibility test in which a patient sample and a candidate antibiotic are combined on a microfluidic chip, and whatever antibiotic survives that step reaches stress-responsive E. coli biosensors downstream: a susceptible sample leaves the antibiotic active, the stress promoter fires and sfGFP is expressed, while a resistant sample degrades the antibiotic and the signal stays near baseline. Because the fluorescence is the diagnosis rather than a supporting observation, the team treated measurement as the project's foundation, establishing baselines, finding the usable concentration window, measuring the response and anchoring everything to controls. Three devices remove the infrastructure a point-of-care test cannot assume: a PDMS microfluidic chip at one to five dollars, a $204.48 fluorescence detector, and a $106.68 bioreactor to produce the biosensor cultures.","awards":["Best Hardware — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Diagnostics Project — Winner"],"dry":{"frameworks":"The measurement page is written in the order the work had to be done, establishing a baseline, determining the usable range, measuring the response, then controls and calibration, then scaling, with a limitations section at the end. Human Practices is counted as integrated only where the project would have been different without it, so every conversation is paired with what it changed. Each bioreactor iteration was assessed against a fixed question set covering ease of use, comparability to benchtop standards, modularity and monitoring, with outcomes recorded as what worked and what did not.","dataviz":"Growth curves with simultaneous OD600 and fluorescence for biosensor strains against wild-type EPI300; dose-response panels expressed as fold change against an untreated control on the same plate; a library-wide scatter in which most of the 200-plus promoter constructs cluster near a growth ratio and induction ratio of one and genuine hits appear as outliers from roughly 3-fold to 12-fold; LTSpice simulation node tables comparing expected against simulated voltages for two supply-rail configurations; sensor-reading-against-time traces under constant illumination for the optical density sensor; CAD models published as .glb files for every chip design iteration alongside engineering drawings.","datascience":"The baseline work is the part most teams skip. Before measuring any response the team generated growth curves for the CpxP and RecA biosensor strains alongside wild-type EPI300 with no antibiotic present, recording OD600 and fluorescence at 485/510 nm at every timepoint, and found two things that change how all later numbers must be read: the biosensor strains reach maximum cell densities about 35% lower than wild type, indicating metabolic burden from the reporter plasmids and meaning fluorescence cannot be compared across strains without normalising to cell density; and the CpxP strain shows roughly 18 to 20-fold higher basal sfGFP than wild type or RecA after 25 hours at 37 C, which ceases at 22 C. They state the consequence directly, that a team adopting CpxP without knowing this would mistake baseline for signal. OD600 calibration curves were produced from these runs so fluorescence can be normalised rather than reported raw. The first dose-response attempt, 13 two-fold concentrations sampled at 10-minute intervals over 40 to 60 minutes, produced no dose dependence, and the team read that as a failure of the measurement window rather than of the biosensors, publishing it because a team seeing a flat one-hour curve should not conclude their reporter does not work. Correcting it required knowing where the strains stay alive, so MIC titrations for gentamicin, tobramycin and amoxicillin with ranges seeded from published values gave provisional MIC ranges of 4 to 8 ug/mL, defining the subinhibitory window inside which every later measurement was placed. The repeated eight-hour dose response then found CpxP peaking between four and eight hours, reaching 2-fold at four hours and 3-fold at eight at 8 ug/mL amoxicillin, and RecA responding to amoxicillin but not to either aminoglycoside, a negative the team reports explicitly so that others do not reuse the SOS response as an aminoglycoside readout. Controls are anchored rather than assumed: wild-type EPI300 as the chassis negative control, untreated cultures on the same plate as the denominator for every fold change, and blank media wells subtracted from all fluorescence. The plasmid retention assay is itself a control on the measurement conditions, run because chloramphenicol confounds the stress response they are measuring; plasmids were lost within one hour without selection, so selection was retained and the confound documented rather than quietly accepted. Scaling to more than 200 promoter-GFP constructs with UBC's Biofactorial automation facility used apparent MICs cross-checked against EUCAST, subinhibitory concentrations at roughly 0.25 to 0.5 times apparent MIC, 30 384-well plates with OD600 and GFP sampled every 30 minutes over eight hours, plus a no-antibiotic control plate and a media-only blank, with each promoter's response calculated as GFP normalised to OD600 and then to its own control so that constructs with different growth characteristics remain comparable. The detector carries its own calibration routine: a baseline is taken by subtracting an LED-off reading from an LED-on reading, signal and reference voltage are read together and subtracted during collection so supply-rail drift is removed rather than recorded as signal, and gain is set from low upward until the brightest expected sample lands near the top of the 0.883 V usable range. The resolution is derived and published so others can repeat the calculation for their own configuration: the Arduino's 1.1 V internal reference gives an ADC step of 1.074 mV per count, and with a 10 MOhm transimpedance resistor at a gain of 101 the smallest detectable current is about 1 pA. Limitations are stated as limitations, that the MIC values are provisional because they came from endpoint OD600 in a two-fold series rather than standardised broth microdilution against a reference strain, so they locate a working range rather than establish a clinical breakpoint.","software":"PRISM (Promoter Response Index and Selection Map), a relational SQLite evidence database that integrates RNA-seq differential expression results, regulatory interactions, promoter and transcription-unit annotations and sequence information to rank antibiotic-responsive promoters for screening, published on GitLab with a separate figures repository. The team is explicit that their contribution is the integration, interpretation and review workflow rather than the expression model or the source measurements, and that PRISM makes those relationships inspectable and produces a reproducible selection proposal; identifier mappings retain the source row, reference release and mapping basis so that one symbol mapping to multiple loci is represented rather than silently collapsed. Supporting modelling covers a degradation model, a promoter library analysis and a patient-sample design of experiments. A protocol database covers LB medium preparation, growth curves, the plasmid retention assay, MIC titration, the biosensor dose-response assay, cloning, the antibiotic degradation assay, PDMS casting, bioreactor culture and assembly, flow testing, and calibration SOPs for the SEN0169 pH probe and TSL2591 optical density sensor, each written to be followed by someone who was not present.","stack":["Arduino with 1.1 V internal reference ADC","AD8606 op-amp transimpedance front end","488 nm LED, 500 nm long-pass filter, photodiode on a shared vertical axis","KiCad and Altium Designer, JLCPCB manufacture","LTSpice","SolidWorks flow simulation","PDMS cast from FDM-printed PLA molds","TSL2591 optical density sensor and SEN0169 pH probe","SQLite (PRISM)","RNA-seq differential expression","384-well automated screening (Biofactorial)"],"techniques":["Baseline characterisation before response measurement","OD600 calibration curves and per-construct normalisation","MIC titration to define a subinhibitory measurement window","Fold change against an untreated control on the same plate","Blank media subtraction","Plasmid retention assay as a control on assay conditions","Publishing negative and absent responses","LED-off baseline subtraction and reference-voltage subtraction","Published ADC step and minimum detectable current","Gain set from low upward to avoid saturation","Validation against a flask control in triplicate across three experiments","Hydraulic resistance modelling checked against flow simulation"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A wet-lab training video series of one to five minute clips covering pipetting, heat-shock transformation, LB media and plates, colony picking, autoclaving and waste disposal, and aseptic technique, made so a multidisciplinary team could learn asynchronously and review later. Beyond the team, the Human Practices group designed synthetic biology resources and workshops for primary and secondary students, for marginalised adults, and ran the Youreka Vancouver Symposium pairing high school students with research, plus a Geering Up microfluidics activity rebuilt after its first version leaked.","ihp":"Nine clinicians, researchers and patient partners were chosen for what each could say that the literature could not: researchers on what a test must detect, infectious disease physicians and a bedside nurse on what happens to patients once resistance is found, patient partners on living with it, and a patient engagement specialist on how a student team without ethics approval can involve patients at all. On the hardware side, Amin Abdolkhani talked the team out of abandoning PLA molds for resin printing, which would have been more expensive, more wasteful and dependent on another lab's printer, advising one more attempt against revised requirements; it worked. Bram Banik, a PCB designer at D-Wave, explained that adapting published circuits is standard practice rather than deriving from first principles, then ran a KiCad tutorial. Dr Celestine Hong hosted an industrial bioreactor tour that showed how sterility is maintained through screws and O-rings, positive internal pressure, sterile filtration and clamp-and-syringe sampling, recommended feedback control loops, suggested simplifying to a microcontroller, sensor and single control element on the available budget, and warned that the common optical-density-to-cell-count conversion is poorly supported below an OD of 1, recommending a dry cell weight calibration curve instead.","realWorld":"The need is costed: conventional susceptibility testing needs a microbiology laboratory and days of turnaround, fluorescence readers suitable for this output run from about $630 to over $42,000, and none of the commercial readers accept a custom chip format, so a rapid test that still needs a plate reader and a central lab is not a point-of-care test. The team scoped the hardware around removing those dependencies rather than around building the most capable instrument. Market work sizes FAST against the global clinical diagnostics industry using a TAM-PAM-SAM-SOM framework and sets out competitors and the regulatory rules that would govern the product, alongside needs-finding, business development, strategic planning and long-term growth pages. Reproduction materials are complete: each device page carries a bill of materials with current prices, the chip page provides CAD models for every iteration as .glb files plus engineering drawings for the final straight, gradient-generating and snaking designs, and the detector page provides both PCB designs, a 3D model and a user manual.","partners":["Biofactorial, UBC High-Throughput Biology and Automation Facility","Amin Abdolkhani (UBC SBME, CMED lab)","Bram Banik (UBC Engineering Physics / D-Wave)","Dr Celestine Hong (UBC Chemical and Biological Engineering)","Geering Up","Youreka Vancouver"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6279/wiki/assets/87edc504fab45511ac34a0233e32a223.avif","caption":"The overall setup of the fluorescence detection system. Aligning a 488 nm LED, the sample, a 500 nm long-pass filter and a photodiode on a single vertical axis removed one of the two optical filters conventional detectors need, cutting optical material cost by at least half.","credit":"Team UBC-Vancouver, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6279/wiki/assets/1049987edaae516c9d470c1dcf17c072.avif","caption":"The 30 mm by 90 mm main detection PCB, with the LED, the microfluidic chip well and the photodiode vertically aligned along the board. The complete device costs $204.48 to build.","credit":"Team UBC-Vancouver, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6279/wiki/assets/797aed1798be54a683e510a5b995770a.avif","caption":"The physical PDMS microfluidic chip beside its SolidWorks model. Cast from FDM-printed PLA molds over seven design cycles, it costs roughly one to five dollars per chip and needs neither a cleanroom nor a resin printer.","credit":"Team UBC-Vancouver, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6279/wiki/assets/cb607262e5ed54178078cdf0291acf72.avif","caption":"TSL2591 light sensor readings against time under constant illumination, part of the bioreactor's optical density calibration. The bioreactor costs $106.68, monitors temperature, pH and optical density, and was validated against flask culture in triplicate across three experiments.","credit":"Team UBC-Vancouver, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Characterise the uninduced baseline before you measure any response: discovering that one reporter strain carries 18 to 20-fold higher basal expression and 35% lower maximum density than wild type is the difference between a calibrated signal and mistaking a constitutive background for a result, and it is cheap to find and free to publish.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/ubc-vancouver/project/best-measurement","https://2026.igem.wiki/ubc-vancouver/project/best-hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/ubc-vancouver/hardware/fluorescence-detector","https://2026.igem.wiki/ubc-vancouver/hardware/bioreactor","https://2026.igem.wiki/ubc-vancouver/hardware/microfluidic-chip","https://2026.igem.wiki/ubc-vancouver/modelling/prism","https://2026.igem.wiki/ubc-vancouver/project/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/ubc-vancouver/administration/market-research-","https://2026.igem.wiki/ubc-vancouver/human-practices/education"],"rank":33},"6280":{"team":"LYON","id":"6280","section":"Undergrad","country":"France","village":"Bioremediation","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/lyon/","projectTitle":"BioThetis","tagline":"De novo protein binders anchored on cheap cellulose that capture trifluoroacetic acid from industrial water and release it with heat — no living organism in the filter.","summary":"BioThetis goes after trifluoroacetic acid, the smallest and most stubborn PFAS: an NGO found it in 34 of 36 tap water samples across eleven European countries in 2024, activated carbon barely retains short chains, ion-exchange resins are not approved for French drinking water, and reverse osmosis only concentrates TFA five to ten times at enormous energy cost — the elected official in charge of water at the Metropole de Lyon told the team a single installation would run to roughly one billion euros. Their alternative is a protein binder fused to the cellulose-binding module CBM3a, which sticks to ordinary microcrystalline cellulose with no chemical coupling, captures TFA, and gives it back when the column is heated to 65 C so the material is reusable. Because TFA weighs only 114 Da and no natural binder was on offer, they designed binders from scratch with BoltzGen — 10,000 candidates, 6,823 through the filters, top 5 kept, three taken to the bench in two anchor orientations each — and demonstrated dose-dependent TFA binding by nanoDSF that does not respond to difluoroacetic or acetic acid, so the recognition is TFA-specific. They also solved the fluoroacetate dehalogenase DAR3835 to 1.10 A, the highest resolution reported for that enzyme, and said plainly that no density on the processed datasets is attributable to TFA. It won Best Bioremediation and Best Presentation on an unusually honest project: 15 new Registry parts, 25 printable protocols, all code and all dead ends released CC BY 4.0, and a human practices record that names exactly which conversation changed which page.","awards":["Top 10 (Undergrad)","Best Education — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Presentation — Winner (Undergrad)","Best Bioremediation Project — Winner"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Two strands, both documented with their failures intact. Binder design used BoltzGen 0.3.2 (Stark et al. 2025) on the Neurosnap platform with protein length constrained to 80-120 residues: 10,000 candidates generated, 6,823 passing BoltzGen's geometric and energetic filters, then re-filtered with the documented parameters (alpha 0.2, RMSD threshold 3.0 A) to keep the top 5 — across that shortlist median RMSD 0.982 A, median pTM 0.859, median ipTM 0.859, which the team notes shows consistent confidence rather than one lucky outlier. Three binders (Galatea, Ianassa, Melite) went forward in two anchor orientations each. Separately, a rational-design pipeline for DAR3835 variants combined structure prediction (Boltz-2 and AlphaFold3 via Neurosnap), sequence redesign with LigandMPNN, and binding-energy scoring with AutoDock Vina, run first on the related dehalogenase RPA1163 and then on DAR3835. Its result was negative and reported as such: no automatically redesigned mutant beat its wild-type benchmark on either scaffold, backbone confidence stayed high so the losses were interface rather than folding effects, and with the ligand pose at pLDDT 46-48 on the fluorines a Vina difference of 0.4 kcal/mol sits below the method's noise and cannot rank designs. The nine variants were therefore picked on explicit structural reasoning and rotamer feasibility, with docking used only as a consistency check, and one design was dropped at review after a rotamer check. The second strand is a packed-bed breakthrough column model in MATLAB: advection, axial dispersion and binder capture along the bed, Danckwerts inlet condition at C0, zero outlet gradient, bed starting empty, solved by finite differences with the stiff solver ode15s, reporting the breakthrough curve, BV10 and BV50, empty-bed contact time, bed Peclet number, Damkohler number and total TFA captured. All AI-designed proteins were screened through ToxinPred2 and BLAST against known toxins before anything was ordered.","dataviz":"The dry lab page is built to be read and reused rather than admired. The column model is introduced by a single annotated schematic that shows water entering at concentration C0 and flow rate Q, the two state variables C(z,t) dissolved and q(z,t) captured, a front moving down the bed, the three things that happen to TFA (carried by flow, spread by mixing, captured by binder), and the breakthrough curve as the output — so the whole model is legible before any equation. BoltzGen's 10,000 designs are shown as three scatter plots against design length (predicted error, pTM, ipTM) with grey for all designs, red for top quality after filtering and blue for quality-and-diversity picks, which makes the funnel from 10,000 to 5 visible instead of asserted. Retained designs are presented as superpositions of four AlphaFold3 predictions each. Every figure's generating script is published alongside it. The wiki itself carries a light/dark theme the visitor chooses, and the human practices section is organised as a stakeholder ledger where each entry is tagged Opened, Changed or Confirmed, with the date, the topic, and the specific wiki pages that entry altered.","datascience":"The honest handling of uncertainty is the real data science contribution. The team established an analytical limit case, a mass balance check and an independent re-implementation of the column model before trusting it, and published the parameter file with units and sources — flagging openly that some support and column parameters remain placeholders because they did not finish the model as intended. The conclusion they draw from it is genuinely useful and counterintuitive: affinity and capacity, not column geometry, decide how long a filter lasts. On the protein side they converted thermal shift assays into quantitative affinities (Ianassa N-term apparent Kd 25.0 +/- 4.9 mM, C-term 24.9 +/- 4.0 mM against TFA, versus 105.01 for wild-type DAR3835) and quantified the cellulose anchor by depletion assay (Bmax 1.18 +/- 0.11 nmol/mg, Kd 0.66 +/- 0.33 uM on microcrystalline cellulose). Engineering was run through explicit decision gates with pass criteria written in advance — TFA binding required a Tm shift of at least 0.5 C at 50 mM, reproducible and dose-dependent (met); thermal reversibility required at least 80% of the unfolding transition recovered on a second ramp (not met, for either DAR3835 or the de novo binders, and recorded as a failure with a proposed fix). They also list four checks required before the next synthesis round: redo the ligand pose by docking (AutoDock Vina or GNINA) on PDB 8SDC followed by 100 ns of molecular dynamics with recomputed RESP charges for TFA to test whether the Protenix pose reproduces; a rotamer scan on every bulky substitution; nanoDSF Tm plus post-cycle refolding yield for every variant; and acetate and propionate negative controls so affinity is attributed to the CF3 group rather than a generic carboxylate interaction.","software":"Everything is released under CC BY 4.0 on the team GitLab. The column model (MATLAB column_model.m, the parameter sweep scripts, a parameter file with units and sources, and the script behind each figure) is at https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/lyon/-/tree/main/model/biothetis-column-model with an explicit invitation to plug in your own binder. BL21 is a browser video game that fits in a single 1.3 MB HTML file, runs entirely offline with no third-party assets, stores levels as data so the science is swappable (change the chassis and the target), takes about 15 minutes, works in French and English, and ships with 33 automated tests. The education kit adds three printable board games including an escape game with facilitator guides in English and French, colour-blind-safe design pairing every colour with a symbol, an experiments booklet, a handbook for school staff, and a before-and-after mind map to measure what pupils learned. They also published 15 new Registry parts (six binder constructs — Galatea, Ianassa and Melite each in two orientations — and nine DAR3835 variants, annotated region by region with one feature per mutated codon, numbered as PDB 8SDC plus 14 so mutations map straight onto the published structure), 25 bench protocols and three reference tables in one printable layout, and the survey questionnaire with anonymised aggregated results.","stack":["BoltzGen 0.3.2","Boltz-2","AlphaFold3","Neurosnap platform","LigandMPNN","AutoDock Vina (GNINA planned)","ToxinPred2 and BLAST toxin screening","MATLAB with ode15s stiff solver","X-ray crystallography (DAR3835 at 1.10 A, PDB 8SDC reference)","nanoDSF thermal shift","GitLab (iGEM instance)","Molecular dynamics with RESP charge recomputation (planned)"],"techniques":["De novo binder generation and multi-stage filtering (10,000 to 6,823 to 5)","Cofolding-based ligand pose prediction treated explicitly as a hypothesis","Rotamer feasibility screening of substitutions","Docking-based binding energy scoring with a stated noise floor","Packed-bed breakthrough modelling (advection-dispersion-capture PDE)","Danckwerts boundary conditions and finite-difference discretisation","Dimensionless analysis: Peclet, Damkohler, EBCT, BV10/BV50","Analytical-limit, mass-balance and independent-reimplementation validation","nanoDSF dose-response Kd determination with specificity comparators","Cellulose depletion binding assay (Bmax, Kd)","Pre-registered engineering decision gates with pass/fail criteria","Techno-economic cost-per-cubic-metre modelling"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"LYON built formats deliberately matched to audience rather than one activity repeated: children 6-14, high school students, adults, families, school staff, students, researchers and professionals, and anyone online from age 12. The flagship is four three-hour workshops run between 8 October and 19 November 2026 with a full ULIS class of 18 pupils in a primary school in Givors, south of Lyon, an area particularly affected by PFAS — ULIS being the unit that includes pupils with disabilities inside a mainstream school. Each session follows one line of reasoning: map environmental pollution with hands-on experiments, question filtration with a filter the pupils build themselves, define synthetic biology simply with a short video, and close with a board game. Pupils run the experiments themselves; the school aides who support them take part; the team adapts to children who need breaks and follows their rhythm rather than imposing a programme, and collects teacher and aide feedback after every session. They measured learning with a before-and-after mind map and published the experiments booklet, protocols and a school-staff handbook as a reusable kit, with partnerships continuing past the Jamboree and the guide left behind where the workshops happened. The materials are designed for reuse: three printable board games in French and English with facilitator guides, colour paired with symbols for colour blindness, and BL21, a single-file offline browser game with swappable science and 33 automated tests. A dialogue-free short film made with oKlama about the psychological impact of PFAS contamination carries no language barrier. They took shorter stand versions to Meet & Fabrik (winning two second prizes), visited three lycees, worked with biology, agriculture, dietetics, and history-and-geography teachers so PFAS gets studied from several angles, and organised an inter-school conference on 19 November where students present their own posters. A public survey drew 376 responses by 7 October, published anonymised with a frank list of what they would change. Community work included organising the French Mini Jamboree, a joint Jamboree talk with Berlin and Wageningen on PFAS, sending their game to iGEM Patras's community game library, joining Bochum's trading card project with 29 other teams, and a peer-reviewed article in Vector Volume 5 guided by Maastricht.","ihp":"The human practices record is structured as a ledger where every stakeholder entry is tagged Opened, Changed or Confirmed, dated, assigned a topic, and linked to the exact wiki pages it altered — which makes the influence auditable rather than claimed. The largest change: public concern about releasing engineered organisms moved them to a system containing no living cells at all, only purified protein on cellulose. Residents at an Institut Ecocitoyen PERFAO workshop set the target — their first request was depolluting drinking water because their catchment is over-contaminated and the installed activated carbon does not work on TFA — and testimony from PFAS Contre Terre, the plaintiffs of the 'proces des 250' against Arkema and Daikin, and team members' own relatives confirmed that TFA specifically, and the polluter-pays principle, is what local people want addressed. Veolia's technical director for France and two engineers across July and September calls reshaped the commercial design: they confirmed activated carbon barely works on short chains, that ion-exchange resins lack French health-authority approval for drinking water, that reverse osmosis concentrates TFA only five to ten times while being energy and water intensive and leaving an unmanageable concentrate, that resins and carbon are usually single-use so a regenerable system is commercially interesting, and that factory outflows typically carry 1-10 ug/L; they validated heat elution and CBM3a anchoring and suggested using it on reverse osmosis concentrate. Hector Osuna at Applexion pushed scale-up and multi-column systems, which became the carousel design. A nature protection association's plant visit taught them which treatment plants could realistically adopt it — large and relatively recent ones — and that economics, regulation and political decisions, not just feasibility, govern deployment. Florence Besoin of a residents' association in Saint-Genis-Laval, who approached them after seeing a flyer, set their public tone: residents are genuinely anxious and need to see people taking the problem seriously without being promised an unrealistic fix, so the team adopted 'honest and encouraging, never triumphant' and states on every page what the approach cannot do yet. A utopia-or-dystopia workshop at the French Mini Jamboree surfaced the failure mode of selling to households — clean water for those who can pay, risk left with the most exposed — confirmed by the survey where 96.3% of respondents wanted PFAS producers and users to pay, so customers are companies and operators only, never households. They also voted at the outset not to contact PFAS emitters, fearing reprisal and being used for greenwashing, and say so openly. After an intellectual property warning from Claude Mabillat they took IP training and then chose to release everything under an open licence anyway.","realWorld":"The product is specified as a treatment skid in a container: two cellulose columns carrying the binder, one capturing while the other is heated to 65 C to release TFA into a small volume that goes to destruction, capacity added by extending the carousel, sold, rented or charged per cubic metre treated with binder cartridges as consumables. First roadmap targets are pharmaceutical peptide synthesis, fluorinated chemistry and agrochemistry — industrial emitters and treatment operators, explicitly never households. The economics are worked and bounded: destroying the concentrate adds about 0.80 EUR per cubic metre at a placeholder 300 EUR per cubic metre of concentrate, cost barely moves between 1 and 10 ug/L, and since the support holds at most about 0.13 mg TFA per gram of cellulose the filter stays cheaper than destroying the whole stream up to roughly 40 mg/L at pilot pricing and a few hundred mg/L at industrial pricing, so the dilute regime is where it works — consistent with 2022 state measurements around the Pierre-Benite platform finding long-chain PFAS in industrial outlets from ug/L to low mg/L. Incumbents are costed side by side (activated carbon 29-33 kWh per kg to manufacture plus re-calcination above 850 C; ion-exchange resin 18-24 kWh per kg to make and 4.4 kWh per kg to regenerate at USD 18-33 per kg of medium), and one billion euros is used as the order of magnitude for the reference reverse-osmosis solution at drinking-water scale. The team's stated ethical position is that remediation complements regulation and never replaces it, repeated on every page and in every talk, with restriction supported first. They are open to founding a start-up as the 2025 Lyon team did, but on an open-licence basis, and a film screening with debate is planned for January.","partners":["Veolia (technical director for France plus two engineers)","Hector Osuna, R&D manager, Applexion","Metropole de Lyon (Anne Grosperrin, elected official for water)","Lyon-Feyssine water treatment plant staff","Institut Ecocitoyen pour la Connaissance des Pollutions","PFAS Contre Terre citizen collective (Lucas Miguel)","Florence Besoin, residents' ecological association, Saint-Genis-Laval","Plaintiffs of the 'proces des 250' against Arkema and Daikin","Marie-Charlotte Garin (member of parliament) and Stephane Horel (journalist)","Claude Mabillat (intellectual property)","ULIS class, primary school in Givors, with teachers and AESH school aides","oKlama (short film)","iGEM Berlin and iGEM Wageningen (joint PFAS talk)","iGEM Patras (community game library), iGEM Bochum (trading cards), iGEM Maastricht (Vector article)","iGEM Lyon 2025 (inherited plasmids)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6280/wiki/drylab/column-schematic.avif","caption":"The packed-bed filter model in one picture: water carrying TFA at concentration C0 and flow rate Q enters a cellulose column carrying the binder, with curves for C(z,t) dissolved and q(z,t) captured showing the front moving down the bed, and the breakthrough curve as the output.","credit":"Team LYON, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6280/wiki/drylab/image-1.avif","caption":"Design pTM against design length for every one of the 10,000 BoltzGen candidates — grey for all designs, red for top quality after filtering, blue for the quality-and-diversity picks — making the funnel down to five retained binders visible rather than asserted.","credit":"Team LYON, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6280/wiki/drylab/ian-overlay.avif","caption":"Superposition of the retained Ianassa designs, four AlphaFold3 predictions per design — the lead binder that went to the bench and showed TFA-specific, dose-dependent binding by nanoDSF.","credit":"Team LYON, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6280/wiki/education/image-2026-10-19-203152498.avif","caption":"Pupils running the experiments themselves during one of four three-hour workshops with a ULIS inclusion class of 18 in Givors, an area south of Lyon particularly affected by PFAS contamination.","credit":"Team LYON, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Steal LYON's human practices ledger: every stakeholder entry tagged Opened, Changed or Confirmed, with a date, a topic and a link to the specific project pages it altered — it turns 'we talked to people' into an auditable record and forces the team to admit when a conversation changed nothing. The second transferable habit is publishing failure as a deliverable: LYON state that their docking scores could not rank designs because the ligand pose confidence made a 0.4 kcal/mol difference meaningless, that thermal reversibility was never demonstrated, and that some column parameters are still placeholders — and release the code anyway so the next team starts further along. A high-school centre can adopt both tomorrow at zero cost, and both are exactly what judges and reviewers reward.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/lyon/","https://2026.igem.wiki/lyon/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/lyon/design","https://2026.igem.wiki/lyon/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/lyon/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/lyon/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/lyon/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/lyon/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/lyon/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/lyon/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/lyon/sustainability","https://2026.igem.wiki/lyon/safety-and-security","https://2026.igem.wiki/lyon/collaborations","https://2026.igem.wiki/lyon/communication","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/lyon/-/tree/main/model/biothetis-column-model"],"rank":129},"6283":{"team":"GYHS","id":"6283","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/gyhs/","projectTitle":"ReefBond: A Mussel-Inspired Bioadhesive for Coral Reef Restoration","tagline":"A mussel-inspired protein material, designed to help coral fragments hold on while they establish a new home.","summary":"GYHS (Guangdong Guangya High School, Guangzhou) built ReefBond, a recombinant fusion protein that joins a mussel foot protein adhesion module (Mfp3-v12 / Mfp3-v15) to an acidic mineralization module (a CARP3-derived peptide, (Asp)8, (DE)6 or (DDE)4) so that surface adhesion and interfacial mineral deposition act at the same coral-substrate interface. Eight fusion designs were expressed in E. coli BL21(DE3) from pET21a; the team reports qualitative surface-retention staining, in vitro CaCO3 deposition with SEM imaging, and a purpose-built two-version underwater test tank with a motor-guided force gauge, five-level wave generator and a six-channel monitoring interface. The project is unusually honest: nearly every claim is paired with what has not yet been measured, and no live-coral test has been done. Human Practices is the spine of the project rather than a decoration - expert and practitioner advice visibly reorders the experimental programme.","awards":["Best Sustainable Development Impact — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"No computational modelling framework. The Model and Software template pages are essentially unfilled iGEM boilerplate; the dry-lab contribution is the instrumentation and data-recording software for the hardware platform, plus a literature-based mechanistic review (Venn 2011, Mass 2013, Cornwall 2021, Lange 2024, Gavriel 2018, Laipnik 2020) used in place of simulation.","dataviz":"ReefBond monitor renders live time-series charts for six channels (electrical conductivity, water temperature, total dissolved solids, salinity, pH and a raw light-sensor ADC value), a recent-image gallery and time-lapse playback; records are written about once per second and plots refresh about every two seconds.","datascience":"Record discipline rather than analysis: readings and the manually selected wave level are written to CSV with timestamps, a channel is left blank after more than 6 s without a reading while a measured zero is kept as zero, and the team insists raw ADC and ppm values are not relabelled as lux/PAR or PSU without calibration. Planned work is to key sensor CSVs, photographs and mechanical test sheets to shared experiment and sample identifiers.","software":"ReefBond monitor - a browser-based acquisition and recording interface for the underwater test platform (device status, six environmental channels, scheduled photography at 5-86,400 s intervals, time-lapse, CSV export). Published at https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/gyhs/reefbondmonitor .","stack":["Arduino Uno","four-in-one digital probe over USB-RS485","analogue pH module (A1) and light sensor (A0)","stepper and DC motor drivers","USB camera","turbidity meter","CSV logging","web/touch monitoring interface","PETG 3D printing"],"techniques":["instrument calibration planning (two-point pH conversion, comparison against reference instruments)","SEM morphology of recovered deposits","Coomassie Brilliant Blue surface-retention staining and NBT reactivity staining","digital force-gauge pull testing with guide-rail loading","in vitro CaCO3 deposition (10 mM CaCl2, 25 mM MgCl2, 10 mM NaHCO3, 25 C, 7 d)"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A school club exhibition with a Chinese-language 'SAVE CORAL REEF' poster, a knowledge quiz with small prizes and whiteboard questions introduced coral biology, reef ecology, threats and existing restoration methods before explaining ReefBond; students and teachers read the displays and talked with the team. Social media extended this, with post-level viewing records of 1,489 views for the iGEM introduction and 679 for the coral-themed post. The strongest element is a published set of six quiz questions and answers written specifically to kill misconceptions the team had encountered - corals are animals, bleaching is not death, an acidic module is a design hypothesis and not proof of increased coral calcification, engineered bacteria stay in the lab. The team states plainly that it has evidence of participation (photos, view counts) but not of learning, and sets out the paired anonymous pre/post records it will collect next.","ihp":"The causal chain is explicit and runs through five strands. A field visit to the Guangdong Marine Science Education Base with Professor Xie (Shenzhen Research Institute, Guangdong Ocean University) and the coral husbandry and restoration staff produced the first redirection: Xie explained that the facility's existing modified mortar already wins on cost and underwater handling but needs surface cleaning, and recommended testing underwater setting time, substrate differences, resistance to water movement and temperature stability - so the team replaced 'bond strength' with a seven-part requirement set (working and setting time, substrate compatibility, disturbance resistance, stable positioning, durability, cost, effects on coral and water quality) and adopted a staged validation pathway starting in ornamental reef aquaria rather than the sea. Yusong Shi, a Westlake University doctoral student and stony-coral hobbyist, turned handling into structure: his insistence on minimising handling disturbance produced the V2 fixed base, screw-in detachable holders and recessed model interfaces, and his suggestion of an ointment-style tube became the roughly 0.5 g single-use small-dose packaging concept. The sharpest change came from four experts converging against the team's own favourite module - Xie doubted their equipment could measure coral calcification rates, Shi recommended simpler mineralization work, Professor Baowei Chen (School of Marine Sciences, Sun Yat-sen University) told them not to interpret external deposition as stimulation of coral metabolism, and Professor Wang (South China University of Technology) prioritised adhesion because mineralization tests are more demanding; instead of dropping or defending the module, the team rewrote its research question to 'does a candidate mineralization module change in vitro deposition, and can that change measurably affect attachment performance?', reinterpreted mineralization as material-interface deposition and kept only comparative screening of the four acidic peptide classes. Professor Wang's point that microbes will use the protein and raise local oxygen demand added aeration, dissolved-oxygen and coral-microbiome questions to the assessment plan, while Professor Xu (College of Environmental and Resource Sciences, Zhejiang University) converted 'did mineral form?' into a method - indirect turbidity and TDS monitoring followed by SEM of endpoint samples - which is why TDS recording and a turbidity meter were added to V2. A peer, Student Chen of Guangdong Guangya High School with internship experience at a South China Sea coral facility, asked how long ReefBond would hold and what failure would mean, which pushed the team from a single tensile number to attachment service life, reapplication after failure and pollution burden. Professor Chen's separation of composition, dose, release, bioavailability and the distinction between functional aging and biodegradation became a six-dimension safety endpoint framework (composition and residues; exposure; degradation; water quality and microbes; deposit contact; organism selection), and the team then read Chinese Biosecurity Law Articles 35-38 and environmental-code Articles 95 and 737-738 against their own plan. They state clearly that no regulatory consultation has yet happened and no live coral has been tested - the honesty is itself part of the method.","realWorld":"Need is framed with cited numbers rather than slogans: reefs are about 0.2% of the seafloor but support at least 25% of marine species, NOAA recorded bleaching-level heat stress over roughly 84.4% of global reef area in 2023-2025, and a review of historical restoration cases found 60-70% survival for common genera but a median restored area of only 100 m2 monitored for 12 months - which is why the team targets the early post-transplant attachment window rather than restoration as a whole. Four SDGs are claimed with named sub-targets and justification: 14.2 (attachment material for ecosystem restoration), 14.a (the open hardware, operating instructions and published software as marine research-capacity and knowledge transfer), 12.4 and 12.5 (composition, release, degradation and a proposed metric of material consumed per acceptable attachment over a defined period, including reapplication after failure), 9.5 and 9.4 (traceable development and testing capacity), and 11.4 (conservation practice and engagement); SDG 13 is explicitly held as indirect rather than counted. Deployment follows an evidence-gated pathway - laboratory production and functional testing, then functional and safety assessment in aquaria or nurseries, then carefully planned marine trials - with Xie's warning that cost could block large-scale restoration kept on the page. The regulatory path is named but unstarted: teachers and the partner institution will compile composition, residue, dose, release and site information for internal review before consulting local environmental, natural resources and fisheries authorities and the site manager about approvals, filings, organism sources, site use and monitoring. Cost is treated as full accounting - preparation and application losses, replacement, tool reuse, equipment cost, training and maintenance - and after the Jamboree the plan is calibration and repeatability testing of the platform, matched-control comparisons of fusion proteins against the adhesive component and commercial materials, staged safety assessment, aquarium user trials of dispensing and positioning, and returning the data to Professor Xie, Shi and Student Chen to ask whether their concerns were actually answered, recording the reasons for each decision including when results show no improvement.","partners":["Guangdong Marine Science Education Base (coral husbandry and restoration team)","Professor Xie, Shenzhen Research Institute of Guangdong Ocean University","Yusong Shi, School of Medicine, Westlake University (reef aquarium user)","Professor Baowei Chen, School of Marine Sciences, Sun Yat-sen University","Professor Wang, South China University of Technology (coral-associated microbiology)","Professor Xu, College of Environmental and Resource Sciences, Zhejiang University","Mr Xu, engineering and maker educator (hardware mentor)","Student Chen, Guangdong Guangya High School / South China Sea Institute of Oceanology intern (restoration workshop)","Worldshaper Academy (instructors)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6283/wiki/public/hp/figure-01-hp-overview.webp","caption":"Overview of Human Practices inputs, decisions and project responses: the five strands linking stakeholder advice to design, experiment, safety and follow-up.","credit":"Team GYHS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6283/wiki/public/hp/figure-03-facility-visit.webp","caption":"Field visit and discussion with Professor Xie at the Guangdong Marine Science Education Base, including coral husbandry aquaria and mounting bases.","credit":"Team GYHS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6283/wiki/public/hp/figure-04-attachment-workflow.webp","caption":"The current coral attachment workflow - nursery growth, attachment with bases, grids, screws or putty, then continued checks - compiled from discussions at the restoration facility.","credit":"Team GYHS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6283/wiki/public/hp/figure-05-validation-pathway.webp","caption":"The staged pathway for evaluating a coral attachment material, in which progression depends on evidence from the preceding stage.","credit":"Team GYHS, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Adopt GYHS's habit of letting stakeholders attack the module you are most attached to and then rewriting the research question instead of the conclusion: four experts doubted their mineralization story, so the team reinterpreted it as interfacial deposition and kept only a controlled comparative screen. Pair it with their discipline of printing, beside every result, the measurement that would be needed to make the claim and has not yet been made.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/gyhs/","https://2026.igem.wiki/gyhs/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/gyhs/sustainability","https://2026.igem.wiki/gyhs/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/gyhs/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/gyhs/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/gyhs/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/gyhs/safety-and-security","https://2026.igem.wiki/gyhs/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/gyhs/parts","https://2026.igem.wiki/gyhs/assets/index-5Lo3wIOn.js","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/gyhs/reefbondmonitor"],"rank":7},"6284":{"team":"HUST-China","id":"6284","section":"Undergrad","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/hust-china/","projectTitle":"IRIS","tagline":"Turning discarded cotton textiles into bacterial-cellulose nanocrystal films that reproduce the iridescence of kingfisher feathers, so the Dian Cui craft needs no birds","summary":"HUST-China built IRIS to resolve an ethical problem inside a Chinese intangible cultural heritage: Dian Cui, the court craft of inlaying kingfisher feathers into metal jewellery. Rather than finding another animal substitute, they went after the physics - keratin-and-air microstructures producing angle-dependent structural colour, with melanin absorbing stray light to raise saturation - and reproduced it by growing bacterial cellulose from discarded cotton textiles, converting it to cellulose nanocrystals and self-assembling those into an ordered photonic structure, layered with pigment-based functional layers. Their design philosophy, formed in dialogue with artisans and conservationists, is 'retain the aesthetic core while abandoning the outdated carrier'. They won the peer-voted iGEMers Prize, and the reasons are legible on the wiki: they hosted a regional forum for other teams modelled on the Jamboree itself, and co-produced open science-communication materials with multiple other teams rather than only publishing their own.","awards":["iGEMers Prize — Winner (Undergrad & Overgrad)","Best Fashion & Cosmetics Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A published 'Who / Why / What / How' stakeholder engagement matrix, offered explicitly as a reusable blueprint for ethical technology research, plus a value-system analysis with value-oriented task execution. Education is organised as a three-dimensional positioning matrix of audience age against outreach domain, so every activity occupies a named cell (for example 'community teenagers x synthetic biology x Dian Cui culture x ecological conservation') and gaps in coverage are visible. SDGs 4, 11 (target 11.4), 12, 15 and 17 (targets 17.16, 17.17) are mapped individually with the specific partner that delivers each.","dataviz":"A three-dimensional positioning map of educational practices (audience age x outreach domains); survey-result charts of public preferences for Dian Cui inheritance and conservation approaches; molecular dynamics trajectory analyses with reported standard deviations.","datascience":"Public surveys run as design instruments with reported n and percentages: 257+ then more than 400 valid responses (409 valid samples cited for the product-form survey), showing 63% had heard of Dian Cui but only 4% claimed in-depth understanding, 54.1% preferred recreating Dian Cui with substitute materials, 74.08% supported using synthetic biology to reproduce the structural colour, and 61.5% of science information reaching respondents came through short-video channels. The key analytic conclusion reshaped the whole programme: 'the inheritance dilemma stems from a lack of science communication, not public indifference', which produced tiered rather than uniform outreach.","software":"Molecular dynamics work on an engineered disulfide tether: the S38C/T101C pair was simulated across oxidised and reduced states sharing coordinates and differing only by the SSBOND entry, with pdb2gmx closing the specbond from a 4.0 A Cbeta-Cbeta start to S-S 2.027 A (100% of frames inside 0.18-0.22 nm); reduction released the C-terminal region (CTR-to-core centre-of-mass distance 1.39 +/- 0.05 to 2.41 +/- 0.70 nm, CTR RMSF up ~1.9x). In a six-chain 100 ns per state run the tether settled at 2.96 +/- 0.04 A, 45% beyond its unstrained length, with no frame inside the relaxed 1.95-2.15 A window, so the team explicitly reclassified it as an extended covalent tether rather than a textbook disulfide and modelled it as a deliberately softened harmonic SG-SG bond - a careful negative-result reinterpretation.","stack":["GROMACS / pdb2gmx molecular dynamics","ExPASy ProtParam","survey analysis","low-cost custom environmental-control hardware for film casting"],"techniques":["bacterial cellulose production from waste cotton textiles","BC-to-CNC conversion","cellulose nanocrystal self-assembly into ordered photonic films","structural-colour pitch and gradient tuning","protein tag modification for detection","engineered disulfide tether design","abandoned reflectin heterologous expression route"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"HUST-China's education programme is built as a matrix, not a list: a three-dimensional map of audience age against outreach domain, with each activity placed in a named cell so coverage and gaps are both visible. The analytical basis was their own survey work - more than 400 valid responses showing 63% had heard of Dian Cui but only 4% understood it in any depth - which produced the diagnosis that drove everything else: the heritage inheritance crisis is a science-communication failure, not public apathy, so outreach must be tiered rather than uniform. The youngest cell is remote-area online teaching: joining the HUST Graduate Teaching-Support Group in Long'an, Guangxi, they delivered online science classes to local primary-school students, using sharks as the narrative thread to explain a species' importance to marine ecosystem stability and how synthetic biology can produce substitute materials ('Microbial Superheroes: Protecting Sharks'). The most grassroots cell is the Huanyu Cup street outreach, 'Huanyu Together - Reviving the Ancient Craft - Guarding Kingfisher Vitality', run in three staged phases: a community street booth explaining Dian Cui heritage in age-appropriate language with physical replica samples and correcting misconceptions through quizzes and on-site Q&A; close-range handling of craft replicas followed by guided hands-on Dian Cui-style handcraft so children experienced 'listening, seeing and making'; and distribution of science handbooks and souvenirs to consolidate learning. This reached over a hundred community children free of charge and, in the team's own framing, broke the 'waiting for audiences' limitation of traditional lecturing and proved lightweight grassroots outreach is feasible. The 'Colorful Vacation' summer childcare class at the Zisong Yijing Huating neighbourhood in Wuhan deliberately opened three topics in one classroom - synthetic biology, Dian Cui culture and ecological conservation - using science-aesthetic integration and accessible metaphors, with feedback collected during the handcraft session feeding back into the design of activities for younger groups. For secondary students choosing their majors, team members ran an alma mater revisit programme over the winter vacation, delivering lectures at five schools: the First Affiliated High School of Central China Normal University, Zhengding High School in Hebei, Foshan No. 1 High School, Yali High School and Yongji County Experimental High School, covering synthetic biology basics, kingfisher conservation and competition-experience sharing as career guidance. On campus they ran outreach classes and science booths with IRIS culturally inspired creative products. Ecological education left the classroom entirely through joint birdwatching with the HUST Bird Association, explaining kingfisher habitat and wetland ecology in the field, alongside an agreement with the Wuhan Birdwatching Association (President Ming Liang) on data linkage and university-society outreach. Internationally, three rounds of overseas interviews plus cultural exchange in Singapore, the United Kingdom and France carried Chinese aesthetics and kingfisher conservation abroad, with an explicit stance against 'piling up fragmented Chinese symbols or catering to stereotyped Western imaginings of the East', and the narrative strategy drawn from those interviews was 'emotional connection first, transparent technology second'. The work most likely to explain the peer-voted iGEMers Prize is what they did for other teams. On 12 July 2026 HUST-China independently hosted the First Central-China iGEM Forum (CCiF) at the Qiming College Maker Space, deliberately replicating the structure of the international Jamboree - opening speeches, thematic keynotes, a LiveStage presentation block, judge comment sessions and poster-booth free communication - with 15 online and offline teams, invited iGEM senior consultants, former gold medallists and industry guests; 14 teams presented in sequence and received targeted commentary on experimental design, human practices arrangement and logical completeness, then moved to poster booths for peer feedback, and every attendee left with a certificate and themed souvenirs. They also attended Grand APiC, the first Asia-Pacific Synthetic Biology Youth Conference (16-19 August at Southern University of Science and Technology and the University of Hong Kong), joined NAU-CHINA's nationwide ICII (Into China, Into iGEM 2026) community initiative and explicitly borrowed ICII's community-construction logic when designing their own CCiF, and won a Gold Prize at SynBio Challenges 2026 - exchanging with more than ten teams including Jilin University, Wuhan University, Nanjing University and the University of Hong Kong. Three concrete co-productions followed. With Beijing University of Chemical Technology they co-created the science picture book 'Wukong Asks the Way: A Pilgrimage Through Biological Science', and separately contributed specialised content to BUCT's air-to-protein popular-science publication addressing public misconceptions about electro-biocatalytic protein production, jointly refining the argument that proteins made from CO2 and N2 are biologically derived rather than hazardous industrial chemicals and that purification and toxicological evaluation are mandatory before deployment; the text was reviewed by both teams and published on BUCT's wiki as a shared output. With JLU-FBH they joined 'Together with iGEM: Across Villages, From Myths to Facts', a community-driven myth-busting handbook where JLU-FBH acted as chief editor coordinating submissions from over 17 global iGEM teams; HUST-China independently wrote a complete entry debunking the pseudoscience claim that blackened silver ornaments can detect heavy-metal poisons, which after mutual review and format alignment was integrated into the collective handbook and released publicly as a shared anti-misinformation resource for student synthetic biology groups worldwide. Finally, and unusually, the team benchmarked itself against past Best Education winners and published six named next-iteration commitments, each crediting the team it learned from: establish pre/post classroom tests following GreatBay-SCIE's accuracy-based pre/post design; standardise and open-source the Huanyu Cup and childcare-class courses into reusable course packages following RWTH Aachen's open course model; build an online matrix of short videos, graphics and online classrooms to match the 61.5% short-video share found in their survey; turn picture books, handbooks and posters into continuously updated open resources; explore parent and family participation models following GreatBay-SCIE's parent workshops; and keep recording 'whom we asked, what we learned, and what we changed accordingly', writing education as a traceable decision log rather than a list of activities.","ihp":"Human Practices is described as the strategic engine and compass rather than a parallel track, and the evidence supports it. Early dialogue with Dian Cui artisans, cultural scholars and conservationists produced the zero-animal-harm ecological baseline and the design philosophy of retaining the aesthetic core while abandoning the outdated carrier. Expert consultation on the in vitro film-formation difficulty of reflectin triggered a decisive wet-lab pivot: the reflectin module was abandoned entirely for the fashion-waste-to-CNC route. Further expert feedback produced protein tag modifications for easier detection and optimisation of the BC-to-CNC conversion. Market research and public surveys redefined the product from a museum replica into mid-priced Bio-Fashion daily-wear jewellery, which in turn drove the team to design custom cost-conscious hardware for better environmental control during film casting. Stakeholder findings were specific: Teacher Liu Yang at Beijing 798's Slow Time Handicraft Workshop showed that peacock-feather imitations are too green and bright and crack and peel; the manager of the Guangzhou Yuequ Intangible Cultural Heritage Inheritance Institute explained that natural peacock feathers carry high loss and raw-material cost, that Dian Cui has high social-media popularity but far fewer offline experience visits than mother-of-pearl, that goose feathers and blue pattern paper cannot replicate the iridescence, and that a real Dian Cui sealing layer destroys the iridescence - a pain point that became the team's core engineering goal of reconciling film durability with structural-colour retention. Systematic museum benchmarking at the Palace Museum, Hong Kong Palace Museum, Zhenbao (Treasure) Museum and Hubei Provincial Museum set the optical performance target and informed film pitch and colour-gradient tuning; at the Hubei Provincial Museum the absence of genuine Dian Cui and the crudeness of the gift-shop imitations pushed them away from motif reproduction toward material reproduction. Government engagement produced a written reply from the Wuhan Bureau of Landscape Architecture and Forestry confirming Wuhan has no traditional Dian Cui manufacturers and no records of illegal hunting or trade, which deliberately shifted the team's narrative from 'solving current poaching' to 'preventing potential poaching risks' via positive biodiversity publicity; a dedicated symposium with the Wuhan Ecology and Environment Bureau on 10 September 2025 brought in solid-waste, ecological-protection and environmental-industry experts and standardised lab waste management and compliant waste-cellulose sourcing.","realWorld":"Four reusable outputs are named explicitly: the value-system analysis and value-oriented task execution framework; the documented Who/Why/What/How stakeholder engagement matrix as a blueprint for ethical technology research; open-source educational resources co-created with other teams; and low-cost hardware promoted so other teams and industry can fabricate structural-colour films more consistently on a limited budget. Market positioning was derived from field evidence: Wuhan SKP luxury retail (Louis Vuitton, Rolex) as the high end, the Tanhualin district in Wuhan and Chongqing cultural-creative markets as the affordable end, where the team found Dian Cui and imitation products essentially absent and most blue ornaments made from pigment, mother-of-pearl or spun thread - establishing the mid-tier sustainable jewellery gap IRIS targets.","partners":["Palace Museum (Beijing)","Hong Kong Palace Museum","Zhenbao (Treasure) Museum","Hubei Provincial Museum","Beijing 798 Slow Time Handicraft Workshop (Teacher Liu Yang)","Guangzhou Yuequ Intangible Cultural Heritage Inheritance Institute","Tashan Academy - Book Neighbor Haven","Wuhan Bureau of Landscape Architecture and Forestry","Wuhan Ecology and Environment Bureau","Wuhan Birdwatching Association (President Ming Liang)","HUST Bird Association","HUST Graduate Teaching-Support Group, Long'an, Guangxi","Zisong Yijing Huating community childcare class, Wuhan","First Affiliated High School of Central China Normal University; Zhengding High School, Hebei; Foshan No. 1 High School; Yali High School; Yongji County Experimental High School","Prof. Cai Xinyuan, School of Design, HUST","Wuhan SKP","iGEM teams: BUCT (picture book and air-to-protein publication), JLU-FBH (myth-busting handbook with 17+ teams), NAU-CHINA (ICII), Jilin University, Wuhan University, Nanjing University, University of Hong Kong","Grand APiC (SUSTech and HKU)","SynBio Challenges 2026"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6284/wiki/image/wiki/education-wiki/education1-1.avif","caption":"The three-dimensional positioning map of educational practices: audience age against outreach domain, so every activity occupies a named cell","credit":"Team HUST-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6284/wiki/image/wiki/education-wiki/education4.avif","caption":"The Huanyu Cup street outreach booth, 'Huanyu Together - Reviving the Ancient Craft - Guarding Kingfisher Vitality'","credit":"Team HUST-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6284/wiki/image/wiki/education-wiki/education5.avif","caption":"Community booth: immersive intangible cultural heritage experience for children, reaching over a hundred free of charge","credit":"Team HUST-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6284/wiki/image/wiki/education-wiki/education3.avif","caption":"Online class for primary-school students in Long'an, Guangxi: 'Microbial Superheroes: Protecting Sharks'","credit":"Team HUST-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6284/wiki/image/wiki/education-wiki/education10.avif","caption":"The myth-busting handbook co-developed with JLU-FBH and over 17 global iGEM teams, 'Together with iGEM: Across Villages, From Myths to Facts'","credit":"Team HUST-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6284/wiki/image/wiki/education-wiki/education11.avif","caption":"'Wukong Asks the Way: A Pilgrimage Through Biological Science', the science picture book co-created with the BUCT team","credit":"Team HUST-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6284/wiki/image/wiki/education-wiki/education9.avif","caption":"An on-site Dian Cui-style handcraft workshop, the 'making' stage of the three-stage booth design","credit":"Team HUST-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Earn peer goodwill by building infrastructure for other teams, not just audiences: HUST hosted a regional forum that replicated the Jamboree's own format (keynotes, LiveStage talks, judge commentary, poster walk) for 15 teams, then wrote entries into two other teams' open publications - and publicly benchmarked its own education against past Best Education winners with six named, credited improvements for next year.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/hust-china/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hust-china/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/hust-china/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/hust-china/collaboration","https://2026.igem.wiki/hust-china/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/hust-china/sustainable"],"rank":33},"6289":{"team":"ETH-Zurich","id":"6289","section":"Overgrad","country":"Switzerland","village":"Foundational Advance","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/eth-zurich/","projectTitle":"preCISe","tagline":"A modular tool for precise intracellular delivery using contractile injection systems","summary":"About 79% of the human proteome is intracellular and largely undruggable, and no approved protein therapeutic delivers an exchangeable protein cargo into the cytosol. preCISe engineers Photorhabdus virulence cassettes (PVCs), bacterial extracellular contractile injection systems that act as molecular syringes, into a retargetable delivery platform: a SpyTag/SpyCatcher-attached binder arm swaps the target without re-engineering the cage, demonstrated against CD20 on engineered mammalian cells with a piggyBac Cre-loxP reporter line (preCISion) that turns on GFP only when Cre reaches the cytosol. To raise specificity they added dual targeting, splitting the cargo across two PVCs against two receptors. It won Best Software and Best Foundational Advance because the platform ships as reusable infrastructure: 29 tested protocols, a part collection for evaluating intracellular delivery, and two open-source tools, deCISion and OpenSplitProtein.","awards":["Top 10 (Overgrad)","Best Part Collection — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Software — Winner (Overgrad)","Best Wiki — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Foundational Advance Project — Winner"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Both tools are deliberately model-free, which is the team's central dry-lab argument. OpenSplitProtein ranks every peptide bond in a .pdb or .cif structure on two separate questions rather than one blended score: split tolerance (packing density weighted by inverse squared distance, distance from the buried core, solvent exposure summed over the flanking pair) and fragment reassembly (cross-cut contacts within 8 A, size-normalised interface, interface-to-cohesion ratio). No network was trained and no coefficient was fitted into the ranking; the only constants are the direction of each measurement, two size exponents from the domain-parsing literature and the 8 A contact cutoff. Crucially they defined a structure-free baseline (the length of the shorter fragment, plus relative position i/n) and showed that cross-cut contacts flip sign once it is held fixed, from +0.174 to -0.108, meaning the naive positive correlation was an artefact of chain geometry. Validation used Tsuboyama et al. (2023) cDNA display proteolysis insertion-stability labels at 13,622 backbone positions across 293 domains in 129 sequence families for split tolerance, and 223 split-intein sites from the Int-In dataset (126 with graded efficiency) for reassembly, with feature selection frozen before the test sites were seen and no sequence family shared at 40% identity nor fold at TM-score 0.3. deCISion is a database-integration pipeline rather than a predictor, chaining the Cell Surface Protein Atlas, Human Protein Atlas, SAbDab, Cellosaurus, UniProt, RCSB PDB, NCBI, the iGEM Registry and the Kazusa codon table.","dataviz":"The benchmark is reported as a percentile table against three comparators of different kinds, and the team says so explicitly: SplitSeek-Pro (a true competitor), the 2019 iGEM Protein-split Model, and ThermoMPNN-I (not split software at all, but the only released model predicting the insertion label directly, included as the hardest baseline). On 21 published split sites across superfolder GFP, Cre recombinase, horseradish peroxidase, firefly luciferase, Cas9 and NanoLuc, OpenSplitProtein puts the working site at a median 21st percentile with 13 of 21 in the top quarter, against a random expectation of 50; a 22nd site (Cas9 713/714) is excluded and the reason given. Both tools run in the browser (OpenSplitProtein needs only the HTML file opened; structures never leave the user's machine) with a 3D viewer showing the cut and both halves, and the wiki itself is a searchable static site with term callouts, a 'cut anatomy' diagram and an interactive outreach map rendered with d3-geo and topojson over OpenStreetMap and Natural Earth data. Published figures carry explicit tables for how to read a correlation column.","datascience":"The project's data-science contribution is the separation of proxy label from real task. Insertion stability measures the cost of perturbing an intact chain, never the cost of releasing two fragments, and the wiki states that difference rather than eliding it; the split-intein set is then used as the only label that directly tests reassembly. Scores are converted to within-structure ranks (0-1, displayed 0-100) so results are comparable across proteins of different size, and selection and testing datasets are separated with structural alignment checks. deCISion turns a public mass-spectrometry atlas into an actionable ranking: it reports each surface receptor's measurement strength on the chosen cell type and how many of the 47 CSPA cell types it was detected on as a specificity proxy, counter-checks normal tissue, cell-type, blood and tumour expression from the Human Protein Atlas, and lists only nanobodies and scFvs from solved structures with measured Kd where one exists (and states that only 1,019 of 14,860 SAbDab binders, 6.9%, have one). Limitations are enumerated rather than hidden: 47 cell types only, selectivity across cultured lines is not tissue specificity, and 'not detected' is not absence because Cell Surface Capture only sees N-glycosylated protein.","software":"Two released tools. OpenSplitProtein (gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/eth-zurich/opensplitprotein) ranks split sites from a structure file, installation-free in the browser. deCISion (gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/eth-zurich/decision) turns a cell type into a PVC construct in five steps: pick one of 47 CSPA human cell types by name, disease or tissue; choose a receptor; choose a nanobody or scFv binder (whole antibodies are rejected as too large for a PVC); accept the published XTEN linker or paste your own (pointing users to iGEM Calgary 2023's LINKED database); assemble binder-linker-SpyCatcher and export protein and DNA sequences as FASTA plus GenBank and SBOL3, with the three plasmids to order (cage, cargo, binder arm) listed. It ships MIT-licensed with a web interface, a JSON API and a CLI, 28 automated tests on every push through GitLab CI, a Docker build, a 2.5-minute demo video, and documentation of the architecture, the data build, what did not work and what the software cannot tell you. The team also published 29 tested eCIS protocols and a piggyBac/SpyTag part collection.","stack":["GitLab CI","Python 3.11","bun","Docker","MIT licence","JSON API + CLI + web UI","FASTA / GenBank / SBOL3 export","Cell Surface Protein Atlas (CSPA)","Human Protein Atlas","SAbDab","Cellosaurus","UniProt / RCSB PDB / NCBI","Kazusa codon usage database","iGEM Registry (BBa_K1159201 SpyTag)","d3-geo / topojson","BioRender"],"techniques":["geometric structure scoring (packing density, SASA, cross-cut contacts)","within-structure rank normalisation","confounder adjustment against a structure-free baseline","benchmark against published split sites and a stability-prediction baseline","family- and fold-level data leakage control (40% identity, TM-score 0.3)","surfaceomics-driven target selection and counter-selection","SpyTag/SpyCatcher modular retargeting","split-protein and split-intein design","piggyBac transposon reporter line construction","SWOT stakeholder analysis"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education was structured on three pillars (outreach, media, events) with a defined target audience per group and a before-and-after survey used as the measurement instrument, not just feedback. They visited four Swiss high schools (Kantonsschule Uster, Seetal, the cantonal high school for adults, Hohe Promenade) reaching over 130 students in formats from 45 to 90 minutes, and ran a hands-on week at the Wyss Zurich mint & pepper BioSTARS summer camp with 20 students from across Switzerland who performed their own PCR and gel electrophoresis, co-hosted with iGEM Zurich; over 150 students in total. They published two scientific-journal articles including one in BIOspektrum, ran a YouTube channel, co-hosted the Swiss iGEM Meetup for five teams, and presented at the Student Biolab welcome event, with about 16,900 social views. All templates and teaching material are published for reuse.","ihp":"24 interviews across six stakeholder groups, each analysed with a SWOT grid, and the changes are concrete. The project began as an eCIS biopesticide against Drosophila suzukii in Swiss crops; conversations with Drosophila experts and BFH European Meet-Up judges (Dr. Nicole Gensch, Amelia Wei) established that this was not viable and the team pivoted to human intracellular delivery while keeping eCIS. Scientific experts in the Pilhofer and Food Microbiology labs drove the choice of CD20 as the proof-of-concept target and the design of the reporter systems. The dual-targeting split-cargo concept was invented in direct response to expert questions about off-target risk, and OpenSplitProtein exists only because that concept needed a cut site: the wiki states the idea came from those conversations, recorded under Human Practices. Dr. Max Brackmann (NBC arms control laboratory, Spiez) assessed the work case-by-case against CDC and Robert Koch Institute checklists and concluded neither the PVC work nor deCISion required additional biosafety layers; the idea of building deCISion on the CSPA came from Prof. Bernd Wollscheid, after the team found the existing SISYPHUS interface unusable for their actual question. Investors and companies (Athebio, Procavea, Nanosyrinx) pushed specificity, off-target data, IP and scalability, and advised focusing a platform on one lead application.","realWorld":"The team is explicit that this is a foundational advance handed to others rather than a product: the stated purpose is to let future iGEM teams and researchers engineer eCIS more easily, backed by 29 protocols with recommended controls for teams with no prior wet-lab experience, a part collection, and two MIT-licensed tools. Their own validation honesty is part of the case: they state that the best validation of deCISion would be wet-lab targeting of new cell types from its outputs, that they had neither the time nor the scale, and that confidence therefore rests on the validated public databases underneath. The outlook names the sequence required before any clinical path: uniform and consistent PVC expression, verification of predicted binders, validation of split cargo, an industrially scalable PVC production workflow, then in-vivo mouse work on immune response, degradation, accumulation and efficacy. Clinicians (University Hospital Zurich, Hirslanden) were approached partly to establish contacts should the project continue past the competition.","partners":["Pilhofer Lab, ETH Zurich (Adam Pinsler, David Schaumann, Dr. Charles Ericson)","Prof. Bernd Wollscheid, ETH Zurich (CSPA)","Dr. Enea Maffei, Food Microbiology, ETH Zurich","Prof. Martin Loessner, ETH Zurich","Prof. Nadia Mazouz, ETH Zurich (ethics)","Dr. Max Brackmann, NBC arms control laboratory Spiez","Dr. James Lapworth, Nanosyrinx","Dr. Tom Edwardson, Procavea Biotech","Dr. Richard Woods and Dr. Johannes Urban, Athebio","Lukas Frischknecht, University Hospital Zurich","Jan Duscha, Hirslanden medical group","Wyss Zurich mint & pepper BioSTARS summer camp","iGEM Zurich (UZH)","BFH European Meet-Up","Student Biolab Zurich","ScopeM, ETH Zurich"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6289/wiki/images/software/opensplitprotein/web1-03-ranked-v3.webp","caption":"OpenSplitProtein's browser interface showing every cut site in an uploaded structure ranked separately for split tolerance and fragment reassembly, instead of a single blended score.","credit":"Team ETH-Zurich, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6289/wiki/images/software/decision/howto4-2-receptor.webp","caption":"deCISion's receptor step: surface receptors measured on the chosen CSPA cell type, with measurement strength, how many of the 47 cell types each was detected on as a specificity proxy, and the number of PVC-compatible binders available.","credit":"Team ETH-Zurich, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6289/wiki/images/results/retargeting-v3.webp","caption":"Retargeting result: PVCs carrying an anti-CD20 binder arm attached through SpyTag/SpyCatcher act specifically on CD20-expressing preCISion cells.","credit":"Team ETH-Zurich, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6289/wiki/images/education/summer-camp-gel.webp","caption":"Students running their own gel electrophoresis at the Wyss Zurich mint & pepper BioSTARS summer camp, where 20 high-school students from across Switzerland worked through a realistic research scenario.","credit":"Team ETH-Zurich, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"The transferable move is cheap-but-honest computation: ETH beat heavier published tools by scoring six geometric quantities, refusing to fit a model, and then spending their effort on validation design instead (a structure-free confounder baseline, frozen feature selection, no shared sequence family or fold between selection and test sets). A school research centre can reproduce that whole method on a laptop, and should copy the companion habit of publishing a 'what the software cannot tell you' section alongside the results.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/eth-zurich/","https://2026.igem.wiki/eth-zurich/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/eth-zurich/software/","https://2026.igem.wiki/eth-zurich/software/decision/","https://2026.igem.wiki/eth-zurich/results/","https://2026.igem.wiki/eth-zurich/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/eth-zurich/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/eth-zurich/education/","https://2026.igem.wiki/eth-zurich/contribution/"],"rank":136},"6292":{"team":"Stockholm","id":"6292","section":"Overgrad","country":"Sweden","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/stockholm/","projectTitle":"TIDE","tagline":"A yeast that senses bisphenol A and degrades it from the same sensing event, rebuilt as a contained reactor after three experts said open release would never fly","summary":"Stockholm (KTH) built TIDE, a three-plasmid Saccharomyces cerevisiae system: a detection module encoding a synthetic LexA-mER-alpha transcription factor, a degradation module encoding laccase, and a GFP reporter, so that detecting BPA also triggers its breakdown. They assembled by Gibson, verified by sequencing, read GFP by microscopy and 96-well plate, measured laccase by a modified ABTS assay at 420 nm and BPA removal by LC-MS, and built a modular dry-lab pipeline (structure prediction with pLDDT/PAE early screening, then batch docking of a bisphenol analogue panel). They won the Safety and Security Award in the Overgrad section, and the reason is visible in the work: a three-expert advisory board, a formal STPA hazard analysis, a published wastewater-containment guidebook for future teams, and a documented decision to abandon their own central deployment assumption.","awards":["Safety and Security Award — Winner (Overgrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Systems-Theoretic Process Analysis (STPA), the aerospace hazard-analysis method from Nancy Leveson's MIT group, applied to a biological system: a control structure of regulators, development team, operator, engineered yeast and independent BPA measurement, yielding eight losses, system-level hazards with safety constraints, twenty-six unsafe control actions with controller constraints, and causal scenarios with candidate mitigations. They credit iGEM UCalgary 2024's ErythrO as the precedent for adapting STPA biologically. Alongside it: a structured expert advisory board, KTH's KLARA chemical risk-management documentation, and a self-built laboratory safety form.","dataviz":"An STPA control-structure diagram distinguishing control actions (solid) from feedback (dashed) with the BPA-clearing path highlighted, plasmid maps, a dry-lab pipeline schematic, sequencing alignment profiles, GFP microscopy panels, LC-MS figures, docking score and contact-map tables, and market-growth forecasts for BPA versus its alternatives with shaded inter-source variation and an explicit note that the data were compiled and visualised with AI assistance and the sources manually verified.","datascience":"A modular structure-prediction and docking pipeline with an early screening stage that filters candidates on configurable pLDDT and PAE cutoffs before the expensive full run, plus shared-memory and worker-RAM optimisation, and a batch mode that docks every ligand in the bisphenol analogue panel against each receptor candidate automatically. Validation: docking estradiol into 1ERE reproduces the crystal pose to within about 0.6 Angstrom. The code is deliberately split into modelling, docking and redesign modules rather than one end-to-end script, so other teams can reuse parts.","software":"A reusable sequence-to-binding-score pipeline (structure prediction, docking, redesign) released as separate modules with configurable confidence-score screening.","stack":["AlphaFold-style structure prediction with pLDDT/PAE confidence filtering","molecular docking","S. cerevisiae three-plasmid system","Gibson Assembly","LC-MS","ABTS laccase assay","fluorescence microscopy","KLARA risk-management system"],"techniques":["LexA-mER-alpha synthetic transcription factor sensing","laccase-mediated BPA degradation","multi-plasmid yeast transformation","LC-MS discrimination of degradation from uptake and adsorption","auxotrophic selection","STPA hazard modelling"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"They ran a Model United Nations conference simulating the UN Environment Assembly on 'Strengthening Global Monitoring and Regulatory Frameworks for Bisphenol A and Other Endocrine Disrupting Chemicals', and published the planning documents as a reusable toolkit so other iGEM teams can run one, explicitly designed to be approachable for beginners. A second online MUN for current and former iGEM members, on equitable access to biotechnological innovation, is being organised. They also built two SDG outreach games for different age groups, contributed a BPA literature review to the MSP Vector journal run by the Maastricht iGEM team and took part in its peer review, and appeared at the KTH Climate Action Centre, ForskarFredag, a school visit, a student magazine and conferences in Copenhagen, Munster and Oslo.","ihp":"Over twenty named stakeholders including Naturvardsverket (the Swedish EPA) and Stockholm Vatten och Avfall, with a regulatory comparison that is genuinely specific: Sweden's SFS 2012:991 restricting BPA-releasing coatings in food packaging ahead of the EU-wide ban, against the FDA's continuing position that BPA is safe at authorised levels. The decisive engagement, though, is the safety advisory board, where each of three KTH experts is documented with the questions asked, the answer given and the change made. Gunaratna Kuttuva Rajarao told them wastewater plants are not closed systems, that plants will not accept GMOs, that the safety of the organism cannot be guaranteed and that a kill switch alone would probably not be enough. Zeynep Cetecioglu Gurol explained the plant layout and identified the membrane-bioreactor stage as the only place a retained organism could sit, named Bromma as a plant planning to adopt membrane bioreactors, flagged that real operating temperatures of 20-25 degrees C differ from lab conditions, and recommended non-targeted metabolite analysis because transformation products may be more harmful than BPA itself. Gustav Sjoberg said physical containment in a closed reactor is sufficient (no open drains, double barriers, sealed reactors, fail-closed computer-controlled valves, autoclaved waste), that secreting laccase from yeast is hard and a high-secreting filamentous fungus would be the real production host, that holding yield over many generations is the real risk and should be addressed by genome integration near an essential gene, and bluntly that activated carbon followed by incineration is very cheap and hard to compete with.","realWorld":"This is the rare case where the safety work demolished the business case and the team published the demolition. Rajarao's feedback produced what they themselves call the project's largest change: they abandoned the assumption that TIDE would ever be released into municipal wastewater. The system is now proposed as a contained biological reactor with physical containment as the primary safeguard and genetic measures only as an additional layer; the application moved from large municipal volumes to a defined, more concentrated industrial stream (food packaging and manufacturing effluent, which Rajarao noted has more BPA and fewer competing contaminants); and they rebuilt the economic case around that smaller stream, stating enzyme demand at low concentration as a limitation rather than hiding it. They also stopped treating a drop in BPA as proof of safe effluent, because degradation products and enzyme demand are unanswered. Sjoberg's point that activated carbon plus incineration is cheap and hard to beat is accepted rather than argued away: their case now rests on degradation being more energy-efficient than boiling off water and burning, on picking the right stream, and on a credible operating model, with membrane cost and continuous dosing listed as limitations. The regulatory read is honest too: EU GMO regulation is not expected to open up, the EU wastewater directive currently requires only monitoring of micropollutants and pharmaceutical capture is expected to use activated carbon, and deployment is declared conditional on safety and regulatory assessment with the sequence set by Cetecioglu Gurol (prove laboratory function, then pilot, then full risk assessment, environmental and techno-economic work). Be clear about what this means: there is no business model here in the commercial sense, no company, no investor, no patent, no customer and no pricing, and the proposed implementation organism may not even be yeast, since they now describe S. cerevisiae as a proof-of-concept host and point at a high-secreting filamentous fungus for production. The results are equally unvarnished: sequence verification problems, an incorrect primer and an overly long PCR target muddied verification rounds, the positive control (tamoxifen) never arrived, and they state that sequence verification should precede functional testing and each assay needs a positive control. What they built instead of a venture is reusable safety infrastructure: a downloadable Guidebook to Wastewater Treatment Systems comparing nine systems (activated sludge, UASB, biofilm reactors, membrane bioreactors, nature-based lagoons and combinations) and setting out the containment, horizontal-gene-transfer and regulatory questions each one raises for a GMO project, closing with a checklist for future teams; the full STPA as a PDF; a modular dry-lab pipeline; and the MUN toolkit. Notably, the guidebook exists because they noticed, during an unmoderated caucus at their own MUN, that delegates had little understanding of how wastewater treatment plants work yet enthusiastically wrote remediation into the resolution anyway, and inferred the same gap would exist among iGEM teams. Continuation is framed as a research path rather than a company: transfer the circuit to a production organism, integrate essential genes into the plasmids under native promoters, build a CRISPR knockout strain for dependence, and characterise degradation products before any safety claim.","partners":["KTH Royal Institute of Technology, Dept. of Industrial Biotechnology (Johan Rockberg, PI)","Gunaratna Kuttuva Rajarao, KTH (wastewater treatment and bioremediation; safety advisory board and general safety training)","Zeynep Cetecioglu Gurol, KTH (wastewater bioremediation, SYMBIOREM Horizon Europe project; safety advisory board)","Gustav Sjoberg, KTH (metabolic engineering and GMOs in bioreactors; safety advisory board)","Naturvardsverket (Swedish Environmental Protection Agency)","Stockholm Vatten och Avfall (and Bromma wastewater treatment plant as a possible future test site)","KTH Climate Action Centre","MSP Vector journal, Maastricht University iGEM team (literature review and peer review)","iGEM UCalgary 2024 (STPA precedent)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6292/wiki/safety-and-security/figure1-stpa-control-structure.avif","caption":"STPA control structure for TIDE, mapping regulators, developers, operator, the engineered yeast and independent BPA measurement, with control actions as solid lines and feedback as dashed","credit":"Team Stockholm, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6292/wiki/safety-and-security/guna-meeting.avif","caption":"Safety and security advisory board interview with Gunaratna Kuttuva Rajarao, whose feedback ended the plan to release TIDE into municipal wastewater","credit":"Team Stockholm, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6292/wiki/safety-and-security/zeynep-meeting.avif","caption":"Advisory board interview with Zeynep Cetecioglu Gurol, who identified the membrane-bioreactor stage as the only containment point in a conventional treatment plant","credit":"Team Stockholm, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6292/wiki/community-impact/mun.avif","caption":"The team's Model United Nations simulation of the UN Environment Assembly on regulating bisphenol A and other endocrine disruptors, released with a reusable organiser toolkit","credit":"Team Stockholm, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Convene a small safety and security advisory board of domain practitioners (not just academics in your own field) early enough that their answers can still change the project, and publish each interview as questions asked, answer given and change made, including the change that kills your headline application. Then run a formal STPA on the deployed system, since modelling controllers, feedback loops and unsafe control actions surfaces failure modes that a biosafety checklist never reaches, and release the analysis as a document other teams can copy.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/stockholm/","https://2026.igem.wiki/stockholm/safety-and-security","https://2026.igem.wiki/stockholm/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/stockholm/assets/index-D8fvRSn0.js","https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6292/wiki/safety-and-security/stpa-tide.pdf","https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6292/wiki/safety-and-security/safety-security-guidebook-igem.pdf"],"rank":26},"6294":{"team":"SDU-Denmark","id":"6294","section":"Overgrad","country":"Denmark","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/sdu-denmark/","projectTitle":"Shewanode","tagline":"A microbial fuel cell built from scratch, and a measurement workflow for the outer membrane vesicles that carry its electrons.","summary":"SDU-Denmark engineered Shewanella oneidensis MR-1 to improve extracellular electron transfer and built the hardware to measure it: first a two-chamber microbial fuel cell as proof of concept, then a single-chamber design with an air-breathing cathode and carbon felt electrode that became the team's primary electrochemical measurement system. The measurement work centres on the outer membrane vesicles that carry the MtrCAB cytochrome complex, asking how to isolate them reproducibly and how to quantify their size, morphology, charge and concentration. Each question is answered with complementary methods, each with stated calibration, controls, replicates and limitations. Along the way the team documented a working anolyte recipe, which the literature generally leaves as 'Shewanella basal medium', and released it for other teams.","awards":["Best Alternative Platform — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Measurement — Nominee (Overgrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"The measurement page is structured by goal rather than by technique: each goal states the question, the method, the calibration, the controls and replicates, the results, a discussion and an explicit limitations section. Complementary quantitative and qualitative methods are paired deliberately (preparative size exclusion chromatography with quantitative BCA; qualitative helium ion and scanning electron microscopy with quantitative DLS and zeta potential), and the team states where a method cannot support a claim.","dataviz":"BCA calibration curve of blank-corrected absorbance against BSA concentration; per-fraction protein concentration plots with lysed and unlysed series and a zoomed inset; DLS size-distribution-by-intensity panels with correlation functions for each biological replicate; full Zetasizer statistics tables reporting mean, standard deviation, relative standard deviation, minimum and maximum, and including the instrument's own intercept and fit error; current-versus-time traces from the single-chamber MFC and the H-cell; heme concentration bar plots showing both means and individual replicate points.","datascience":"Vesicle isolation is verified rather than assumed. A BCA assay against a BSA dilution series at 562 nm gives the standard curve, and each size-exclusion fraction is then measured twice, once untreated and once lysed with Triton X-100 for 10 minutes on ice, with an isolation-buffer-plus-Triton control confirming the detergent itself does not shift absorbance. The lysed fractions read 100 to 200 ug/mL against lower unlysed values, which is the argument that intact vesicles are present and only open on lysis; fractions above 2 mg/mL are explicitly flagged as exceeding the assay's upper linear range and excluded from interpretation. Morphology is imaged by helium ion microscopy and SEM and quantified in Fiji (wildtype n = 29 particles, mean Feret diameter 288.3 +/- 97.9 nm, circularity 0.837; mutant n = 18, 300.6 +/- 69.6 nm, circularity 0.767), and the team then states that without a buffer-only blank slide taken through the same fixation and drying the structures cannot be definitively identified as vesicles, and that some sharp-edged objects may be crystallised solvent. Size, concentration and charge come from a Malvern Zetasizer Advance Ultra Red Label with every instrument setting published (material refractive index 1.45, absorption 0.001, 25 C, dispersant RI 1.33, viscosity 0.887, dielectric constant 78.5), three biological replicates from different colonies, and technical replicates where the instrument allowed. Main-peak diameters cluster at 130 to 171 nm with z-averages of 87 to 147 nm, polydispersity indices up to 0.39 are read as genuine heterogeneity, and the team reasons through the candidate causes (subpopulations, artefacts, residual protein) using the BCA separation as evidence against one of them. Zeta potential is reported as wildtype -5.532 +/- 0.5955 mV versus MtrCAB-overexpressing mutant -4.671 +/- 0.3632 mV, the direction predicted by the hypothesis but a smaller change than expected, which the team attributes to PBS ions partially neutralising surface charge and proposes repeating in lower-ionic-strength solvents. The reported limitations are unusually candid: BSA is acknowledged as an imperfect standard for a mixed vesicle proteome; DLS is noted as sensitive to dust and aggregates, blind to morphology, and dependent on analysis models the team could not inspect because only data reports were produced; and technical replicates missing from some samples are identified as a possible artificial source of the observed subpopulations. Electrochemistry is logged as a voltage drop across a 100 ohm resistor on a PicoLog 1216, with the first current rise after about two days reported as indicative only because the experiment ran without biological replicates. The heme assay uses a standard curve to convert absorbance to micromolar concentration, with two biological replicates whose individual points are plotted alongside the means and the explicit statement that no standardised protocol exists for this application so the method would need further validation.","software":"An Arduino-based voltage logger was built for the two-chamber MFC as a low-cost alternative to dedicated logging equipment; the single-chamber system was logged on a PicoLog 1216. A hardware parts list is published for download, together with the anolyte recipe and standard operating procedures for each measurement method.","stack":["Malvern Zetasizer Advance Ultra Red Label (DLS and zeta potential)","Helium ion microscopy","Scanning electron microscopy","Fiji / ImageJ particle analysis","Pierce-style BCA assay","IZON qEVoriginal 35 nm size exclusion columns","PicoLog 1216 data logger","Arduino voltage logger","Carbon felt / carbon weave electrodes","BioRender"],"techniques":["BSA standard curve with blank correction","Lysed versus unlysed paired fraction measurement","Detergent-only control","Explicit upper-linear-range exclusion","Three biological replicates from independent colonies","Published instrument settings for reproducibility","Polydispersity index as a heterogeneity readout","Zeta potential with conductivity reported alongside","Feret diameter and circularity from image analysis","Per-goal limitations sections","Voltage across a known resistor for current measurement"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"","ihp":"Human Practices is the largest single page on the wiki and is credited with changing the project's direction. Stakeholder discussion moved the target away from large-scale energy production toward reliability of low-power generation, which reframed the application space around environmental monitoring sensors, decentralised low-power supply, wastewater treatment with simultaneous energy recovery, and biosensor-style monitoring of marine, agricultural and remote infrastructure.","realWorld":"The application page sets out five pathways with explicit preconditions rather than claims: low-power generation for sensors triggered by a pollutant; decentralised continuous supply, conditional on storage; a battery alternative justified by the environmental cost of lithium, cobalt and nickel extraction; wastewater treatment, which would require redesigning the cell so water can flow through; and monitoring circuits where an interruption produces a signal. The team states that stability, output and maintenance all need assessment before any of these is feasible, and that the right application depends on matching the cell's capability to a specific device's energy requirement.","partners":["IZON Science (qEV columns)","University of Southern Denmark microscopy facilities","Novo Nordisk Fonden","BioRender","MathWorks"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6294/wiki/wetlab/calibration-curve-bca.avif","caption":"Calibration curve for the bicinchoninic acid assay: blank-corrected absorbance at 562 nm against a dilution series of bovine serum albumin, used to convert fraction absorbances into protein concentration.","credit":"Team SDU-Denmark, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6294/wiki/subpages/hardware/tc-mfc-prototype.avif","caption":"The two-chamber microbial fuel cell prototype assembled in the laboratory from two 50 mL falcon tubes, an inverted U-tube salt bridge and a hand-matted carbon weave electrode. It served as proof of concept before the team moved to a single-chamber air-breathing design.","credit":"Team SDU-Denmark, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6294/wiki/wetlab/him.avif","caption":"Helium ion microscopy of isolated vesicles from Shewanella oneidensis MR-1 wildtype and the MtrCAB-overexpressing mutant. Fiji analysis gave mean Feret diameters of 288 and 301 nm; the team notes that without a buffer-only blank slide taken through the same drying procedure these structures cannot be definitively called vesicles.","credit":"Team SDU-Denmark, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6294/wiki/wetlab/wetlab-results-figure7-current-scmfc.svg","caption":"Current from the single-chamber microbial fuel cell, recorded as the voltage drop across a 100 ohm resistor on a PicoLog 1216. The team reports the two-day rise as indicative only, because the experiment ran without biological replicates.","credit":"Team SDU-Denmark, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Publish the instrument settings, not just the result: the refractive index, absorption, viscosity and dielectric constant used for a DLS run, the resistor value behind a current measurement, and the statistics the instrument reports about its own fit quality. A number without its acquisition settings cannot be reproduced or contested.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/sdu-denmark/measurement","https://2026.igem.wiki/sdu-denmark/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/sdu-denmark/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/sdu-denmark/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/sdu-denmark/application","https://2026.igem.wiki/sdu-denmark/alternative-platform"],"rank":14},"6295":{"team":"Princeton","id":"6295","section":"Undergrad","country":"United States","village":"Foundational Advance","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/","projectTitle":"SymPleco: Making Precision Sequestration Sym-ple","tagline":"One M13 phage chassis, any cargo — bulk-capacity adsorption with antibody-grade specificity and light-triggered release.","summary":"SymPleco attacks a trade-off that runs through all remediation chemistry: activated carbon captures a lot but cannot tell similar molecules apart, while monoclonal antibodies bind precisely but need harsh pH or chaotropic salts to release and cannot be recovered or scaled. Princeton's answer is a filamentous M13 bacteriophage used as a programmable adsorbent: sortase A-mediated ligation staples engineered fusion proteins onto the N-terminus of every pVIII copy (making 'furry' phage that bypass classical display size limits), with pIII carrying a Cg-Defensin anchor for PLA filter attachment, a VHH7 nanobody for macrophage clearance, and an AsLOV2 optomonobody that holds cargo in the dark and lets go under 450 nm light. Because swapping the target means swapping only the displayed binder, the team paired it with SymPlify, a de novo binder design pipeline, so a new target does not wait on a new antibody. It won on foundational-advance logic: a genuinely modular chassis demonstrated across three deliberately unrelated applications (melanoma exosome sequestration, Parkinson's alpha-synuclein interception, microcystin/BPA water remediation), backed by an unusually self-critical ODE model and an IRB-approved patient engagement programme.","awards":["2nd Runner-up (Undergrad)","Top 10 (Undergrad)","Best Part Collection — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Measurement — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Foundational Advance Project — Winner"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Two distinct computational efforts. SymPlify is a de novo protein binder design pipeline that routes a target by type: a protein chain goes to BindCraft (AlphaFold2-multimer hallucination with gradient descent on logits through softmax, SolubleMPNN sequence design, AF2-monomer re-prediction as a deliberately harsh filter, then PyRosetta physical metrics for binding energy and surface hydrophobicity), while a small-molecule or macrocycle chain goes to RFdiffusion3 all-atom diffusion plus LigandMPNN (eight sequences per backbone) and an independent complex-prediction model. PeSTo supplies hotspot residue scoring, RDKit renders structures and finds pharmacophores, and freesasa computes hydrophobic patch fraction. Separately, the measurement work is backed by a mechanistic ODE model of the recursive Phage Jumpstart Assay (jumpstart.py, jumpstart_mechanistic.py, passage.py, phase2.py, recursion.py) tracking naive, infected and free-particle pools with superinfection exclusion (sigma = 0.05), saturating infection, carrying capacity, and a hybrid-coat infectivity a_h derived from real pIII gene dosage (a_h ~0.729 at m13ko7_copies=20); the 1:11 passage step samples each particle pool by Poisson rather than plain division so a lineage can genuinely go extinct.","dataviz":"SymPlify's web interface is the visualisation centrepiece: an RDKit 3D viewer colours the target by PeSTo binding probability, lists top hotspot residues with confidence scores, lets the user delete low-scoring ones with an x to tighten the patch, and recomputes the difficulty breakdown (spread, hydrophobic surface fraction, globularity) live as the selection changes — plus a warning when residues sit more than 30 A apart, because one binder cannot reach them all. A run-status page shows pipeline stage, target type, elapsed time, auto-resubmits, design count and job ID, and a final ranking screen lets the user click through designs and download .pdb files with or without GS linkers. The model page is unusually transparent as data presentation: it prints the full command reference, labels every parameter as measured, derived or assumed, and ranks assumptions by their sensitivity on the round-2 plate ratio.","datascience":"The Jumpstart assay turned a single colony-ratio readout into a trajectory: because each recursion is both a manipulation and a measurement, repeated rounds on a population being driven toward one genotype reveal behaviour a single ratio cannot. Statistics are handled carefully — intervals bootstrap over wells, leave-one-well-out checks are reported, panels yielding 0-2 Amp colonies out of 165-272 are reported as upper bounds rather than measurements, and a chi-square test (197 on 5 df) establishes that the six Run B constructs are not interchangeable while the team explicitly declines to lean on the ordering because the bottom four are indistinguishable from zero. They also report that three magnitude-based titer estimators disagreed by up to 20,000-fold on the same panel, which is why they built a ratio readout instead. Most notably the model documents its own error history: an initial m13ko7_copies=200 was simply the wrong figure (wild-type M13 rolling-circle copy number rather than M13KO7's actual p15A-driven one), corrected to 10 and then 20 as evidence improved, with the admission that the corrected model is more parameter-sensitive, not less.","software":"SymPlify, an integrated de novo binder design pipeline with a web interface, hotspot prediction, cluster job submission with auto-resubmission, and post-design filtering and ranking; released for the wider synthetic biology community and wet-lab tested on the team's own targets. Team repository: https://github.com/dianalluu/puigem2026, with an AlphaFold deployment for the Princeton Della cluster at https://github.com/09aaronl/alphafold_princeton-della. The ODE model ships as a Python package with 52 automated checks in test_model.py (~80 s full run, ~8 s in fast mode) covering mass-balance and neutrality invariants, the hybrid-coat gene-dosage derivation, the Poisson passage statistics and pinned regression values. Hardware: a 3D-printed PLA gyroid biofilter cartridge whose two winning PITCCH designs are published as downloadable source STEP assemblies.","stack":["BindCraft","AlphaFold2-multimer","AlphaFold2 monomer","RFdiffusion3 (RosettaCommons foundry)","LigandMPNN","SolubleMPNN / ProteinMPNN","PeSTo","PyRosetta","RDKit","freesasa","ChimeraX","Python (NumPy/SciPy ODE integration)","Benchling","SLURM GPU cluster (Princeton Della)"],"techniques":["De novo binder design by AF2 hallucination with gradient descent on logits","All-atom diffusion backbone generation around a fixed ligand","Inverse folding / sequence design","Hotspot (epitope) prediction and patch-tightness scoring","Target difficulty scoring (0-100, Easy to Very Hard) from flexibility, globularity, hotspot patch, size, epitope chemistry","Small-molecule scoring by logP 30%, size 20%, rigidity 20%, TPSA 20%, aromaticity 10%","ODE compartment modelling of phage-host population dynamics","Poisson resampling of passage dilutions to allow true extinction","One-at-a-time parameter sensitivity ranking","Bootstrap confidence intervals over wells and leave-one-well-out robustness","Chi-square test of construct interchangeability","Regression-pinned unit testing of a scientific model"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"PITCCH, the Princeton iGEM Team CAD Competition for Hardware, is the standout: entrants were given a real open engineering problem from the project — design a 3D-printable gyroid biofilter, 20 mm diameter by 25 mm height, maximising contact surface area — along with the team's actual print parameters. It ran free, fully asynchronous and online in a junior division (grades 5-12) and an open division (18+), explicitly permitted responsible AI use, and drew 42 registered submissions from the United States, United Kingdom and Mexico, of which 26 passed dimensional and printability screening before being sliced and computationally ranked by total surface area. Announcement emails went to thousands more via high school superintendents, undergraduate engineering directors and makerspaces, each carrying a project description and iGEM links. The team frames it as citizen science and backed that framing with credit: two winning designs appear on the wiki with the designers named on the attribution form, and the registration terms stated plainly that the team reserves the right to draw inspiration from submissions with attribution. They also postered at symposiums and presented at bioethics exchanges, and at the US-China iGEM Human Practices Summit showed their halted immunology work as a case study in how to pivot.","ihp":"This is the strongest documented chain of design changes of any team here, and several of them cut capability rather than adding it. Dr Bowen Jing's technical advice seeded SymPlify and his steric clash filter was adopted, but the team then cut AlphaFold3 from the pipeline entirely because Dr Martin Pacesa argued it often mispredicts binding sites; Pacesa also supplied PeSTo as the hotspot engine and, after the team ran competing designs to compare, AF2 monomer was implemented on his side of the argument. Dr Reynold Panettieri talked them out of sequestering IL-6 — their original software benchmark target — by pointing out IL-6's dual-sided effects on blood cell production and T-cell regulation, redirecting them toward a niche where cheaper-than-mAb production is the real advantage and toward naming one indication and working from there, which is exactly how the final applications are framed. Dr Douglas Galasko's distinction between biomarkers and toxins moved them off amyloid-beta for Alzheimer's and into the Parkinson's and rabies work. Two multiple myeloma patients, interviewed under Princeton IRB Protocol #20003, independently said the word 'virus' for a bacteriophage was a problem — one noting roughly 80% of myeloma patients are treated in community settings and take their doctor's word — which changed how the team describes the project in all outreach. A former FDA biologics deputy director, Dr Celia Witten, pointed them to CBER's phage therapy work; EPA Office of Pesticide Programs and OPPT staff sent them to the statutes; and marine microbiologist Dr Stephen Giovannoni plus phage ecologist Prof Forest Rohwer turned the Cg-Defensin antimicrobial worry into a specific planned avidity-comparison assay. Dr John Wnek, who conserves Diamondback terrapins, chose their environmental targets: microcystins and BPA, because nearby New Jersey plants discharge effluent half a mile offshore with no process for xenobiotics.","realWorld":"The regulatory path is mapped rather than asserted: phage therapy under FDA CBER for the clinical arms, and statute-level grounding for the environmental arm after meetings with EPA Office of Pesticide Programs and Office of Pollution Prevention and Toxics, with the team careful to state that nothing should be read as EPA guidance. Containment is designed for deployment — the phage stays inside a closed water treatment facility bound to a biodegradable PLA filter so it is retrievable and localised, with macrophage clearance via VHH7 as the biosafety route for therapeutic use. The commercial argument is reconfiguration cost: because capture specificity lives in one genetic part on pVIII, changing target means changing that part and not the media, housing, attachment chemistry or capital cycle, which is the case made against granular activated carbon for PFAS where GAC retains poorly over realistic service lifetimes. Work is mapped to SDG 3.4, 6.3 and 9. Continuation is concrete: further IRB submissions to interview melanoma patients and Parkinson's patients and caregivers, the Rohwer avidity assay, qPCR of M13KO7 copy number to settle the model's most sensitive parameter, and phage hydrogels as an alternative anchor that would remove the Cg-Defensin concern altogether.","partners":["Dr Martin Pacesa (BindCraft author)","Dr Bowen Jing (computational biology)","Dr Reynold Panettieri, Rutgers Translational Medicine and Science","Dr Jared Radbel, Robert Wood Johnson Medical School","Dr Douglas Galasko (neurology)","Dr Celia Witten, former deputy director, FDA biologics center","US EPA Office of Pesticide Programs and Office of Pollution Prevention and Toxics","Dr John Wnek (environmental conservation, Diamondback terrapin)","Dr Stephen Giovannoni (marine microbiology)","Prof Forest Rohwer (marine phage ecology)","Prof Ned Wingreen and Lawrence Abad (phage biology)","Prof Jared Toettcher (faculty PI, IRB Protocol #20003)","Princeton Institutional Biosafety Committee","Multiple myeloma patient advocacy organisations","US-China iGEM Human Practices Summit","IDT, GenScript, ODI (sponsors)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6295/wiki/figures/symplify-hotspots-protein.avif","caption":"SymPlify's hotspot selection screen: the protein target rendered in 3D and coloured by PeSTo binding probability, with top hotspot residues listed by confidence so low-scoring ones can be removed to leave the focused patch of three to five that BindCraft works best with.","credit":"Team Princeton, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6295/wiki/figures/symplify-filtered-designs.avif","caption":"SymPlify's ranking and filtering view, where accepted binder designs are sorted by AlphaFold confidence metrics and PyRosetta physical scores and can be downloaded as .pdb files with or without GS linkers.","credit":"Team Princeton, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6295/wiki/figures/hardware-pitcch-surface-area.avif","caption":"Ranked printable surface area for the 26 PITCCH entries that passed dimensional and printability screening, plotted against reference geometries — public CAD submissions evaluated computationally and used to pick the biofilter geometry.","credit":"Team Princeton, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6295/wiki/figures/saf-macrophage-uptake-gfp.avif","caption":"Overlaid phase-contrast and green-fluorescence micrograph of cultured macrophages after incubation with GFP-expressing phage, showing uptake by the VHH7 clearance arm. Scale bar 150 micrometres.","credit":"Team Princeton, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Copy PITCCH: hand the public a genuine, unsolved sub-problem from your own project with real constraints and real print parameters, judge entries computationally on a single objective metric, then credit the winners by name and actually build their design in. It converts outreach into contributed engineering at almost no cost, and it works for high-school students because spatial creativity, not synthetic biology training, is what the task rewards. Pair it with Princeton's habit of writing down which model parameters are measured, derived or merely assumed — and publishing the history of their own corrected mistakes — which is the cheapest credibility a student dry lab can buy.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/","https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/design-rationale","https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/measurement","https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/application","https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/sustainability","https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/parts","https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/safety-and-security","https://2026.igem.wiki/princeton/judging"],"rank":205},"6296":{"team":"KIT","id":"6296","section":"Overgrad","country":"Germany","village":"Foundational Advance","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/kit/","projectTitle":"ENCORE - Engineered Nanocompartments for Capture, Optimization and Reactor Engineering","tagline":"A standardized modular Golden Gate toolkit that expresses self-assembling encapsulin nanocompartments with custom cargo in yeast","summary":"KIT, the first iGEM team at Karlsruhe Institute of Technology, built ENCORE: a standardised modular cloning system (the toolKIT) that co-expresses a self-assembling encapsulin protein nanocompartment and its cargo in Saccharomyces cerevisiae, chosen because encapsulins assemble from a single repeating subunit and so need far fewer transcriptional units than bacterial microcompartments or virus-like particles. They won the 2026 Inclusivity Award for work that turned inward rather than outward: instead of role-model campaigns, they asked how tasks are actually distributed inside scientific teams and what role gender plays, surveyed 71 people, ran proper statistics, and published the negative result honestly. The resulting deliverables - a facilitated workshop with moderation guide and printable worksheet, and TeamKIT, a team-and-meeting-culture guide - are the reusable artefacts.","awards":["Inclusivity Award — Winner (Overgrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Survey research methodology applied with unusual rigour for an iGEM team: seven self-derived teamwork task categories (Coordination, Social, Operational, Scientific Conception, Creative Design, External Communication, Leadership/Mentoring) each with a written definition; separation of actual task distribution from perceived distribution; a 12-item five-point Likert instrument grouped into three constructs (Perception, Autonomy, Allocation) of four items each with one reverse-scored item; debriefing placed deliberately at the end of the instrument so as not to prime respondents, following social-science practice; expert instrument review; piloting; and an ethics-committee determination.","dataviz":"A heptagon dot-poster used as the physical pre-survey instrument at Campus Day, later rebuilt as an interactive clickable heptagon on the wiki; grouped mean-frequency bar charts of task distribution by gender for the full dataset and the iGEM subgroup; box plots of Likert sum scores for Perception, Autonomy and Allocation; diverging stacked bar charts of each Likert item by gender with sub-10% segments suppressed; an interactive TeamKIT map where a visitor picks their chapter and situation and is pointed to a model and an exercise; and a self-check tool so a reader can see which roles they take in their own team. Figures were generated with AI assistance (Claude) and labelled as such.","datascience":"Pre-survey n = 58 (30 female, 28 male) at KIT Campus Day; main survey n = 71 (45 female, 24 male, 2 non-binary, the latter excluded from gender comparison for sample size and stated as a limitation), of whom 59 were iGEM members, 8 from research groups and 4 from university groups, predominantly undergraduate (41) and graduate (18) students. Because the data were not normally distributed the team used two-sample Mann-Whitney U tests rather than Welch t-tests, at alpha = 0.05. Result: for every task area the null hypothesis held, except Scientific Conception in the full dataset (p = 0.039), where men reported taking it on more often; that difference vanished in the iGEM-only subgroup. All three Likert constructs showed no significant gender difference (p = 0.271, 0.750, 0.113) and scale reliability was good to excellent (Cronbach's alpha 0.822, 0.991, 0.930). The single most striking descriptive finding: for 'I receive adequate recognition for my contributions to the team', no male participant disagreed while 9 of 45 women did. Limitations are set out at length - voluntary-participation selection bias, no cultural-background data collected, comparability of iGEM teams with research groups uncertain, no participant reported being in a predominantly male team despite ~70% of KIT students being male, and the team states plainly it has no formal social-science training.","software":"Two integrated tools. The Open NC Database curates nanocompartment properties scattered across the primary literature - internal volume, pore diameter and charge, reported stability, associated targeting peptide - into a searchable, filterable form, with a data model that distinguishes the biological candidate from the experimentally reported assembly and its supporting evidence and explicitly marks unreported values as unreported; candidates are keyed by UniProt accession and structures by PDB identifier, a sequence enters the catalog only after a documented translation check, and the database accepts contributions by pull request. The ENCORE-Builder turns a database selection into a complete Golden Gate / MoClo design: it assigns fusion sites across three cloning levels, places start and stop codons, codon-optimises for S. cerevisiae, designs primers and oligonucleotide pairs, avoids sites forbidden by RFC 10 and RFC 1000, and emits annotated GenBank and SBOL 3 files plus order lists, with the toolKIT's combinatorial rules enforced so invalid designs cannot be produced. It was validated against a real cloning: the Builder's Level 2 design for the Quasibacillus thermotolerans shell with LGB4 matches the construct the team cloned in the lab.","stack":["Golden Gate / MoClo assembly","SBOL 3 and annotated GenBank output","UniProt and PDB identifiers as data keys","git / GitLab pull-request contribution model","Mann-Whitney U test","Cronbach's alpha","OpenDyslexic (SIL Open Font License 1.1)","Scientific Colour Maps v8.0.1 (Crameri)","Blender (encapsulin rendering)","Miro"],"techniques":["encapsulin shell self-assembly in S. cerevisiae","targeting-peptide cargo fusion","T=1/T=3/T=4 shell selection (24, 32, 42 nm)","VCPO reactor","oxygen-free space engineering","mRNA capture","building a lab from scratch"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"KIT won Inclusivity by doing what almost no previous iGEM gender-equity project had done: looking inward. The team read the iGEM Diversity & Inclusion Committee blog post 'Bursting demographic bubbles', surveyed prior iGEM work (Paris Bettencourt 2013, JIASHU-Shanghai 2024, Stony Brook 2022, Patras-Med 2024, Guelph 2024) and identified that almost all of it faces outward through role models, outreach to girls or awareness campaigns, with only Guelph coming close to an internal view by surveying its own composition. KIT's research question went further: not who is on the team, but how work is distributed - who ends up in the lab, who presents, who takes the organisational and invisible tasks, and, memorably, who empties the dishwasher in the institute kitchen. They derived seven task categories from reflecting on their own team, tested them as a physical heptagon dot-poster at KIT Campus Day (n = 58, colour-coded dots by gender), then designed a full instrument separating actual task distribution from perception, had it reviewed by Dr Melanie-Marita Leidecker-Sandmann of KIT's Department of Science Communication (who had them shorten items, add demographics, remove two questions that revealed the hypothesis, and add a proper debriefing), piloted it with Engineers Without Borders at KIT, obtained an ethics-committee determination, and distributed it through Instagram, the official iGEM Slack and a QR-code flyer at the Barcelona Meetup, plus KIT mailing lists. 71 responses came back. The honest headline is that their hypothesis was not supported - women did not take disproportionately more secretarial or communication work - but two findings held: most participants of either gender agreed organisational work receives less recognition than research work, and 9 of 45 women versus 0 of 24 men felt their contributions were not adequately recognised. They published the full statistics, the Cronbach's alphas, the raw data, both survey versions and the ethics statement, and wrote a long, specific limitations section. The transfer step is what makes this copyable. After discussing results with Ines Koehler, Head of KIT's Department for Equal Opportunities and Diversity Management, who invoked iGEM's 'give back to the community' principle, the team built two artefacts. The Gender Roles & Task Distribution Workshop is designed for newly formed teams at the start of collaboration, when patterns are easiest to shift: each person maps how their time splits across the seven task areas and rates satisfaction with each, then in paired conversations talks to someone who regularly carries a task area they themselves would feel least confident taking on, making invisible effort tangible; it ends with concrete next steps including a weekly challenge where members swap tasks and a check-in a few weeks later. The full moderation guide with a printable worksheet is downloadable, needs no prior gender-research knowledge, and adapts to 1.5-2.5 hour sessions. It was revised after written feedback from Ines Koehler and from Anietta Weckauff and Marina Jaehnert Giannitrapani, co-founders of the Women in STEM Initiative at the University of Stuttgart - changes included replacing 'blind spot' with 'perception gap' because unnoticed tasks are not wilfully ignored, changing 'a task I would never do' to 'a task area you feel least confident taking on' so the choice does not read as a judgment of the task's worth, adding a satisfaction rating, explicit ground rules, an opt-out in the warm-up, a note on intersectional factors and a recommendation for mixed-gender co-moderation. The team states plainly that neither version has been piloted yet and asks teams who run it to report back. TeamKIT is a downloadable guide to team and meeting culture built because, as the first KIT team with no predecessor, they had to work out task distribution, meetings and conflict from nothing - and found first-year teams at Aarhus and Berlin had the same problem; it moves from individual strengths and interests through interpersonal communication to the whole team, ending with meeting and conflict methods, with inclusion threaded through rather than placed in its own chapter, and it was reviewed by Freja from iGEM Aarhus. Public outreach for a Foundational Advance project was equally deliberate, since nanocompartments are invisible and hard to picture. Three members joined KIT's first science slam camp, eight workshop days on storytelling, stage presence, visualisation and PR, and performed to around 100 people at a Karlsruhe science communication event with a metaphor they arrived at only after scrapping draft after draft: the yeast cell is a ball pit and the nanocompartment a wonder machine that fetches a toy you are too big to reach, gives a child a protected space to make chewing gum without harming anything around it, and takes snapshots of children quarrelling among the balls (mRNA capture). CoLab was an art exhibition built on an open call that asked artists a question rather than commissioning illustrations: what becomes of a promoter, what could competent cells be, what does autoclaving mean, and what do you see in four unlabelled scientific figures from the team's own lab work; eleven works by nine artists (one dating from 1980) were shown over two weekends in October at the pavilions in the Fasanengarten in Karlsruhe with team members present throughout, and visitors asked questions that never come up in the lab - what exactly are you changing in those cells, what happens to them afterward, who decides what is allowed. 'The Yeast We Can Do' is a fully open board game for 3-6 players aged 12+, about 45 minutes, no prior knowledge needed, with 19 missions across six application areas from breaking down forever chemicals to capturing CO2 and growing nanocrystals, where all players compete for the same 20 amino acids on the same 37 fields of nutrient medium; rules, board image, mission cards, event cards, score pad and quick reference are downloadable PDFs and the yeast-cell and budding-yeast playing pieces are STL files for any FDM printer, all on GitLab. The team's stated design goal is that a complete newcomer leaves knowing a protein is a chain of twenty kinds of beads, some hard to come by, while an iGEMer might spot the catalytic triad in the plastic-degrading enzyme. They also ran two pub quizzes at the student-run venue Z10 (27 April and again on 15 October during first-year orientation week), staffed a Campus Day stand with a science quiz, a pipette-tip-box filling race and pipetting lessons, published ENCORE in BIOspektrum 04/26 (a leading German molecular life sciences journal, Springer Nature) and in the KIT student magazine clicKIT, built a social media identity from zero deliberately as team-building infrastructure for their successors, and hosted the first iGEM Baden-Wuerttemberg Meetup at KIT on 13 June with GU Frankfurt, Bonn, Saarland, Aachen, Berlin, Heidelberg and Stuttgart, opening with a poster-design session by Sylvia Erhardt of the Center for Synthetic Genomics and continuing with a peer-consultation workshop where teams brought their most pressing internal problems and bottlenecks for structured peer feedback, including team-dynamics questions that rarely surface in formal settings. The wiki itself is an accessibility deliverable, built following UniMuenster 2023's 'Inclusive Wiki Design' guide: large clear sans-serif type, a high-contrast palette of six colours in three shades each chosen for colour-vision deficiency, one-click OpenDyslexic font toggle, one-click dark mode, descriptive alt text on every figure for screen readers, a glossary of scientific terms and abbreviations, a site-wide search function, and shape-coded navigation (encapsulin-shaped octagons for research, circles for Human Practices) so section is distinguishable without relying on colour. Commitments extend past the competition: gender-specific task distribution may feature in next year's KIT Diversity Day, and an article about the project will appear in the KIT Diversity Magazine.","ihp":"Integrated Human Practices is tightly coupled to the inclusivity work - the interview with Ines Koehler of KIT's Equal Opportunities and Diversity Management department is documented on the iHP page and is what converted the survey from a finding into two deliverables. The survey's own development through expert feedback, piloting and revision is itself documented as an engineering cycle ('Survey on Task Distribution') on the Engineering page, applying DBTL to a social-science instrument. The team explicitly anchored the work to UN Sustainable Development Goal 5 (gender equality) and to the local fact that roughly 70% of KIT students in engineering and technical programmes are male, while in Europe only one in five ICT and engineering specialists is female.","realWorld":"Everything is downloadable and reusable: the workshop moderation guide and printable worksheet, the TeamKIT guide, the full board game (rules, board, cards, score pad, quick reference, STL print files) on GitLab, both survey versions, the raw data and the ethics statement, the Open NC Database (open to pull requests) and the ENCORE-Builder (new parts, adapters and backbones added as data files so other teams can extend it). The team's framing of why this matters for successors is worth copying: 'fair task distribution should not depend on whether a team happens to have someone who already cares about the topic', and the most useful thing a first team can leave behind is not a project but a starting point.","partners":["Ines Koehler, Head of Department for Equal Opportunities and Diversity Management, KIT","Dr Melanie-Marita Leidecker-Sandmann, Department of Science Communication, Institute for Technology Futures, KIT","Women in STEM Initiative, University of Stuttgart (Anietta Weckauff, Marina Jaehnert Giannitrapani)","Engineers Without Borders KIT (survey pilot)","KIT Ethics Committee","nine artists in the CoLab exhibition (Friederike Wallmen, Fabien Stark, Linus Hense, Silas Goettle, Marina Schreidl, Andreas Krueger, Lenara Bortscheller, Guenter Wallmen)","Z10 student-run venue, Karlsruhe","BIOspektrum (Springer Nature)","clicKIT magazine","Sylvia Erhardt, Center for Synthetic Genomics","iGEM Aarhus (TeamKIT review), iGEM Berlin","BaWue Meetup teams: GU Frankfurt, Bonn, Saarland, Aachen, Berlin, Heidelberg, Stuttgart","BFH European Meetup (Bielefeld, Frankfurt, Hamburg)","Mini Jamboree Eindhoven","KIT Diversity Magazine / Diversity Day"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6296/wiki/human-practices-resp/who-does-what-in-a-team/campus-day-presurvey-heptagon.avif","caption":"The heptagon pre-survey: visitors placed a gender-coded dot on the task category they most often take on in teamwork (n = 58)","credit":"Team KIT, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6296/wiki/human-practices-resp/who-does-what-in-a-team/task-frequency-all-20data.avif","caption":"Mean frequency of task distribution by gender across seven task areas, Mann-Whitney U tested (n = 69)","credit":"Team KIT, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6296/wiki/human-practices-resp/building-a-team-from-scrach/teamkit.avif","caption":"TeamKIT, the downloadable guide to team and meeting culture written for first-year iGEM teams","credit":"Team KIT, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6296/wiki/human-practices-resp/public-outreach/the-yeast-we-can-do/game-board.avif","caption":"'The Yeast We Can Do': the open-licensed board game board, 19 missions over 37 fields of nutrient medium, with 3D-printable yeast pieces","credit":"Team KIT, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6296/wiki/human-practices-resp/public-outreach/art-exhibition/pavillon-fasanengarten.avif","caption":"CoLab, the art exhibition at the Fasanengarten pavilions in Karlsruhe, built from an open call asking artists what lab words mean to them","credit":"Team KIT, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6296/wiki/human-practices-resp/public-outreach/science-20slam-2.avif","caption":"The Science Slam performance to around 100 people, explaining the yeast cell as a ball pit and the nanocompartment as a wonder machine","credit":"Team KIT, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6296/wiki/human-practices-resp/public-outreach/meetups/events/baw-meetup-everyone.avif","caption":"The first iGEM Baden-Wuerttemberg Meetup, hosted at KIT with eight German teams and a peer-consultation workshop","credit":"Team KIT, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Point inclusivity work at your own house before the public: survey how tasks are actually distributed inside your own teams with a properly reviewed instrument, publish the result even when it contradicts your hypothesis, and convert it into a ready-to-run workshop plus a team-culture guide that a brand-new cohort can use in week one, so fair task distribution does not depend on one person happening to care.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/kit/","https://2026.igem.wiki/kit/inclusivity","https://2026.igem.wiki/kit/public-outreach","https://2026.igem.wiki/kit/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/kit/integrated-human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/kit/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/kit/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/kit/building-a-lab"],"rank":26},"6297":{"team":"McMaster-Canada","id":"6297","section":"Undergrad","country":"Canada","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/mcmaster-canada/","projectTitle":"Chariot: A Platform Technology for OMV-based Therapeutics","tagline":"Inducible loading of bacterial outer membrane vesicles, plus the standardised generation, isolation and characterisation protocols the field does not have.","summary":"McMaster built Chariot, a platform that loads cargo into bacterial outer membrane vesicles (OMVs) using the VNp tagging system, so that accumulation of a VNp-fused protein forces membrane curvature and vesiculation under an inducible promoter. Having identified that OMV work is held back less by biology than by the absence of standard methods, the team made measurement the project: they characterised VNp-driven OMV generation, benchmarked four isolation methods against a shared filtrate reference, and wrote everything into an openly published Protocol Handbook. Alongside this sits Apollo and Artemis, an in-silico platform combining GFlowNet-based active learning for peptide design with molecular dynamics for VNp-cargo compatibility. The project was shaped by 40 stakeholder interviews run through a purpose-built OMVS framework.","awards":["Best Measurement — Nominee (Undergrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A declared 'dual measurement' policy: every conclusion must be supported by at least two independent measurement techniques, and every comparison must run against a control. Integrated Human Practices uses a bespoke OMVS framework (Observe, Modify, Vision, Synthesis) built on the UKRI AREA principles, with each letter mapped to a specific iGEM Human Practices judging question. Machine learning is framed as an explicit design-test-learn loop in which measurements become training data.","dataviz":"Interactive wiki charts with toggles for 'individual measurements', 'mean +/- SD', 'logarithmic scale' and 'show data', so a reader can switch between the summary and the underlying points; an interactive stakeholder network of 40 stakeholders across 37 nodes, colour-coded by category, where clicking a node jumps to its position on an engagement timeline; a conceptual platform-workflow animation for the Apollo/Artemis pipeline.","datascience":"The measurement work is built around the idea that a single endpoint cannot be trusted. OMV preparations are characterised by dynamic light scattering (Z-average diameter and polydispersity index on a Zetasizer Nano ZS) and by nanoparticle tracking analysis (particle concentration), with the team noting explicitly that DLS readings and NTA runs are independent and not paired by row, and flagging a date discrepancy between the workbook label and the raw file timestamps rather than quietly fixing it. Total protein is quantified with a Pierce BCA assay against a BSA standard curve (R2 = 0.97), with blank-subtracted technical triplicates and the individual absorbance readings published; the resulting 709.2 ug/mL is reported alongside the caveat that BCA measures total protein and cannot distinguish lumenal cargo from membrane-associated or co-isolated protein. Comparisons between isolation methods are tested statistically rather than by eye: one-way ANOVA on log10-transformed values with Tukey post-hoc at alpha 0.05 for size and polydispersity across ultracentrifugation, centrifugal concentration, the Norgen kit, a novel 'Push-Pull' adaptation and 0.22 um filtration, all referenced to a single shared 0.45 um PES filtrate so no method gets a head start; lysis conditions are tested by one-way ANOVA with Dunnett's test against untreated OMVs; and the 4-hour versus 18-hour vesiculation comparison uses Welch's t-test on log10 values (p = 0.0005). SDS-PAGE is quantified by ImageJ densitometry, giving 41% recovery of total extracellular mNeonGreen through OMV isolation. Crucially the team kept and measured every fraction each method produced, including supernatants, flow-throughs and intermediate washes they were meant to discard, so losses can be attributed to a step. Limitations are stated as findings: the proteinase K protection assay that would distinguish genuine vesicle lysis from detergent micelle formation was not completed, so DLS size shifts remain the only lysis evidence; the 0.45 um filtrate was never run on NTA; and BCA reports preparation-level protein, not cargo. On the modelling side, Apollo is a generative flow network trained with trajectory balance and coupled to Bayesian optimisation: an ensemble of five independently initialised MLP regressors on padded one-hot peptide sequences acts as a proxy for a fixed D2-AlBERT oracle, with a UCB acquisition score converted into the GFN reward, and the released CLAMP/DBAASP dataset deduplicated and split by target identifier. The team is careful about what this does not establish, writing that negative labels do not represent experimentally demonstrated inactivity, that grouping by target does not separate closely related sequences, and that a falling training loss does not verify exact reward-proportional sampling.","software":"Apollo (GFlowNet + Bayesian optimisation peptide design, built on the published GFlowNet biological-sequence-design framework and the CLAMP/DBAASP dataset) and Artemis (molecular dynamics comparison of VNp-cargo pairings). A Protocol Handbook covering molecular cloning through OMV generation, isolation, lysis and analysis is published for reuse. Wiki source at gitlab.igem.org/2026/mcmaster-canada; site content licensed CC BY 4.0.","stack":["Malvern Zetasizer Nano ZS (DLS, zeta)","Nanoparticle tracking analysis (NTA)","Pierce BCA protein assay","SDS-PAGE with ImageJ densitometry","Norgen Bacterial EV Isolation Kit","Ultracentrifugation","50 kDa centrifugal concentrators","GFlowNets (trajectory balance)","Bayesian optimisation / GP-UCB","MLP ensembles","Molecular dynamics"],"techniques":["Dual orthogonal measurement per conclusion","Shared reference control across methods","One-way ANOVA on log10 values with Tukey post-hoc","Dunnett's test against untreated control","Welch's t-test on log10 values","BSA standard curve with R2","Technical triplicates with blank subtraction","Measuring discarded fractions to locate losses","Explicit statement of unmeasured confounds","Active learning / design-test-learn loop"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education outputs include a SynBio Handbook and a zine series, classroom and community sessions with named educators, and outreach materials documented on the education page.","ihp":"Forty stakeholders were consulted across five groups (patients, healthcare providers, regulatory experts, industry experts and biosafety experts), with sub-expertise in clinical infection, biofilms and pathogen biology, OMV and EV engineering, and drug delivery and nanomedicine. Each conversation is written up through the OMVS framework and tied to a project change; the stakeholder map records three kinds of link (referrals, sequences where a question raised in one meeting was answered in a later one, and convergences where two stakeholders who had never met reached the same conclusion), so a reader can trace a design decision back to the conversation that caused it. The first major pivot came from Dr Coombes, who raised uncontrolled inflammation and septic-like responses as unavoidable risks of systemic bacterial-derived therapeutics and cautioned that peanut-allergy mechanisms are not well enough understood for rational design; the team dropped its oncology and allergy concepts and moved to localised gut-associated systems, judging every subsequent concept on biological feasibility and patient safety before therapeutic potential.","realWorld":"The entrepreneurship case positions Chariot as a modular OMV loading platform for biotechnology and pharmaceutical partners developing protein-based therapeutics, with antimicrobial resistance as the first application because OMVs fuse with bacterial and mammalian membranes and can deliver non-membrane-disrupting antimicrobial peptides past the permeability barrier. The stated value proposition is improved cargo loading plus more consistent and scalable production. The team also frames its protocol standardisation as the deliverable most likely to outlive the competition, benchmarking itself against earlier OMV teams (Freiburg 2024, NYU Abu Dhabi 2025).","partners":["Farncombe Family Digestive Health Research Institute","Didar Lab, McMaster University","Dr Brian Coombes (McMaster)","Dr Michael Surette (McMaster)","Dr Elena Verdu (Farncombe Institute)","Dr Robert Hancock","Dr Greg Hussack","iGEM Freiburg 2024","iGEM NYU Abu Dhabi 2025"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6297/wiki/measurement/measure-sds-page.avif","caption":"12% SDS-PAGE of E. coli BL21(DE3) pET26b(+) 6xHis-mNeonGreen-VNp6 induction and OMV isolation products. ImageJ densitometry on this gel gave 41% recovery of total extracellular mNeonGreen through the isolation.","credit":"Team McMaster-Canada, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6297/wiki/measurement/omv-filtrate-plate.avif","caption":"The 0.45 um PES-filtered vesicle preparation plated on LB agar. No growth confirms the absence of whole-cell contamination in the shared filtrate that every isolation method was benchmarked against.","credit":"Team McMaster-Canada, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6297/wiki/measurement/fluorescence-post-isolation.avif","caption":"mNeonGreen-VNp OMVs after Norgen kit isolation on a bench-safe blue light box: a 4-hour vesiculation period on the left, 18 hours on the right. The visible difference was then quantified by NTA, where the 18-hour preparation yielded significantly more vesicles (Welch's t-test on log10 values, p = 0.0005).","credit":"Team McMaster-Canada, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Keep and measure the fractions you were told to throw away. Benchmarking every isolation or purification method against one shared starting material, then analysing the supernatants, flow-throughs and washes as well as the eluates, turns a yield number into a map of where material is lost and at which step.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/mcmaster-canada/measurement","https://2026.igem.wiki/mcmaster-canada/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/mcmaster-canada/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/mcmaster-canada/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/mcmaster-canada/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/mcmaster-canada/hardware"],"rank":7},"6300":{"team":"NU Boston","id":"6300","section":"Undergrad","country":"United States","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/nu-boston/","projectTitle":"Soil Shield, with the FLARE soil simulation chamber","tagline":"A $300 fluorescence macroscope and controlled soil chamber that tests whether a strain still works under post-wildfire stress, instead of assuming it will.","summary":"NU Boston engineered Pseudomonas putida to survive post-wildfire soil conditions while degrading polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons, using the ectABC/D hydroxyectoine pathway for desiccation tolerance and a salicylate-dependent ccdA/ccdB toxin-antitoxin kill switch for biocontainment. Their hardware answer to the obvious objection, that a strain which works on a bench says little about a burnt hillside, is FLARE: a light-tight soil chamber that recreates oxidative stress and desiccation and images salicylate fluorescence in situ. It replaces lasers and arc lamps with 295 nm UVB COB LEDs and a 410 nm bandpass filter, bringing a fluorescence imaging rig that commercially costs thousands to tens of thousands of dollars down to roughly $300 to $500 in parts, with the full bill of materials published line by line.","awards":["Best Hardware — Nominee (Undergrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A separate Design-Build-Test-Learn cycle is run for each major subsystem (enclosure, kill switch, UV/camera module, hydrogen peroxide delivery), and the team adds a fifth stage of their own, 'How We Moved Forward', which records explicitly what each cycle's learning changed in the next design. Requirements are elicited from the wet lab as the primary stakeholder and then renegotiated: a formal requirements meeting established what stressors were needed and what could be dropped, and a follow-up meeting after first use produced a feedback-to-design-change table.","dataviz":"A calibration curve relating sodium salicylate concentration to mean blue fluorescence signal; a current-versus-voltage characterisation plot for both UV LEDs with the minimum rated voltage and maximum rated current marked as reference lines; flow-rate-against-duty-cycle curves for both pumps with trendlines and R2 values; before-and-after dose image panels for small and large salicylate doses; excitation and emission spectra for sodium salicylate with the chosen LED and filter wavelengths marked; CAD drawings with dimensions and tolerances for the quartz shield, bandpass filter and lens tube.","datascience":"The instrument is characterised component by component before it is trusted as a whole. Both UV LEDs were swept on a programmable DC supply from 1 V to the manufacturer's 6.2 V maximum, with current recorded and illumination checked at each step for 5 seconds, the same exposure used in the final capture cycle; both drew no current below 5 V, and the team stopped at 5.9 V rather than risk the 700 mA ceiling, with LED 1 reaching it at 5.9 V and LED 2 at 5.7 V, documenting that two nominally identical parts differ. Optics are chosen from the fluorophore's spectra rather than by convention: sodium salicylate excites with a peak at 299 nm and a 10% minimum normalised intensity range of 262 to 325 nm, and emits from 359 to 509 nm peaking at 412 nm, so the team specified 295 +/- 5 nm COB LEDs and a 410 nm bandpass filter, and explains why a bandpass rather than the longpass filter used in the DIY designs they built on. Camera height was set empirically, adjusted while live-viewing then measured with calipers at 79 mm to give full coverage of the dish. The first user test produced the most useful measurement finding: at 5 mM salicylate about a third of the dish image reached the maximum pixel value of 255, so differences in brightness above that limit could not be recorded, an explicit saturation limit on the dynamic range. The same test showed that the dish had to be held in a fixed position so control and experimental images could be compared and background properly subtracted, and that perlite in the soil interfered with imaging and had to be removed. Quantification is by pixel-wise comparison of each post-dose image against its own pre-dose control rather than by visual inspection, validated by showing that fluorescence intensity and coverage scale with dose. The final run produced the calibration curve the team will use for all future tests, Signal = 0.0495 x C + 31.44 with R2 = 0.9871. The fluidics were calibrated as carefully: cycle 1 could only switch a pump on and off, which the team identified as controlling duration but not volume, so cycle 2 added PWM duty cycle as a control variable and measured delivered volume into a graduated cylinder over 60 seconds per setting. Both curves came out nonlinear with a dead zone below 20% and little gain above 60%, the two pumps differed by a factor of about 1.5 at full duty despite pumping the same liquid, and the team concluded that each pump needs its own calibration table and, crucially, that doses should be interpolated from the measured values rather than read off the fitted trendline, which misses points at 30 to 40%. On the biology side, an intended OD600 plate-reader assay for the kill switch was invalidated once the team found that ccdB induces filamentation, which changes light scattering so that filamentous and normal populations cannot be compared by turbidity; flow cytometry live/dead staining then showed viability mirroring the uninduced control, and only a CFU assay with cells induced in mid-log phase at OD600 0.4 to 0.6 gave a statistically significant difference, with the forward-scatter increase across arabinose concentrations retrospectively confirming the filamentation. The team publishes that whole chain of invalidated assays rather than only the one that worked.","software":"A published FLARE manual (PDF, 2.4 MB) accompanies the hardware. Firmware runs on a Raspberry Pi 5 with a Raspberry Pi Camera Module 3 for imaging, and an Arduino driving MOSFET-switched 12 V peristaltic pumps via PWM; the LED program is written to turn the UV lights on for only 5 seconds per capture, 4 seconds for the camera to adjust plus 1 second for the shot, at intervals of 5 minutes or more, which is also the argument that UV exposure is too low to degrade the printed components. The kill-switch interlock was redesigned so that the Raspberry Pi reads the magnetic reed switch state on a GPIO pin and cuts power itself, rather than the switch physically breaking a circuit it was not rated for.","stack":["Raspberry Pi 5 and Camera Module 3 (1080p, 11.9 MP)","Arduino with MOSFET-switched 12 V peristaltic pumps (PWM)","295 nm UVB COB LEDs, 60 degree viewing angle","Edmund Optics 410 nm bandpass filter and 20 mm SM1 lens tube","Quartz glass shields rated to 1148 C","Magnetic reed switch lid interlock","Onshape CAD","FDM 3D printing and laser-cut acrylic","Flow cytometry and CFU assays"],"techniques":["Per-component characterisation before system validation","LED current-voltage sweep at the operational exposure time","Optics selected from measured excitation and emission spectra","Explicit pixel-saturation limit on dynamic range","Fixed sample positioning for background subtraction","Pixel-wise comparison against a matched pre-dose control","Calibration curve with R2 for concentration readout","Pump duty-cycle calibration by delivered volume","Interpolation from measured points rather than the fitted line","Published bill of materials with unit costs","Documented invalidated assays and why they failed"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A two-year partnership with CitySprouts, which runs schoolyard gardens with Boston public schools focused on sustainability, community and equitable access for students in underfunded areas. The team took on two new gardens at Nathan Hale and Higginson Lewis Elementary in Roxbury and tended them weekly through the summer, watering, weeding and harvesting. The work fed back into the project: handling many soil types showed how much texture and environment change with weather, and watching an extreme Boston heatwave desiccate the gardens reinforced the case for the soil chamber as a testing ground. The team also ran a microfluidic chip design activity at a Geering Up workshop and rebuilt it with paper towels and paint for the next session after the paper version leaked.","ihp":"Expert consultation shaped the optics and the fluidics. Dr Kai Zhang, a postdoctoral research associate in physics at Northeastern, resolved the team's confusion between excitation and emission wavelengths and established that they needed both an LED in the fluorophore's excitation range and a filter isolating its emission. Professor Timothy Lannin warned that condensation on the quartz LED shields and the camera filter could degrade measurements over time and suggested adding a cold spot to collect it. The wet lab acted as the device's primary user throughout, and their feedback produced six concrete design changes including plastic rather than glass petri dishes, a lid handle, longer ribbon cables so modules can be removed while still connected, a friendlier interface, a kill switch against UV exposure, and ethanol-resistant materials for the final chamber.","realWorld":"The team states the broader case directly: fluorescence imaging is one of biology's most important tools and its price keeps it out of reach of smaller colleges, K-12 classrooms and community science programmes, with commercial systems running from a few thousand dollars into six figures. FLARE is costed at as low as $300 against $10,000, and the low cost is argued to enable running several units side by side to collect imaging data from many samples at once, which is impractical with one shared microscope. Beyond the wildfire application the team lists protein expression analysis, live/dead assays and expression-level detection as reusable uses. Chemical safety drove a scoping decision as well: the team avoided bringing naphthalene into an undergraduate teaching lab because of its carcinogenicity and shifted to salicylate and the nahG gene, keeping a genuinely relevant part of the degradation pathway while removing the exposure risk.","partners":["CitySprouts (Boston)","Nathan Hale Elementary and Higginson Lewis Elementary, Roxbury","Geering Up","Dr Kai Zhang (Northeastern University, Physics)","Professor Timothy Lannin (Northeastern University)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6300/wiki/hardware/hardware.avif","caption":"FLARE, the team's controlled soil chamber and fluorescence macroscope. The laser-cut opaque black acrylic enclosure keeps ambient light out so the UV/camera module can image salicylate fluorescence directly in soil.","credit":"Team NU Boston, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6300/wiki/hardware/figures/flare-calibration-curve.avif","caption":"Calibration curve relating sodium salicylate concentration to mean blue fluorescence signal, Signal = 0.0495 x C + 31.44 with R2 = 0.9871, produced on the completed system and adopted for all future tests.","credit":"Team NU Boston, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6300/wiki/hardware/figures/flare-salicylate-5mm.avif","caption":"5 mM sodium salicylate imaged in the first wet-lab user test. About a third of the dish reached the camera's maximum pixel value of 255, so brightness differences above that limit could not be recorded, an explicit saturation ceiling on the instrument's dynamic range.","credit":"Team NU Boston, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6300/wiki/hardware/figures/flare-final-test.avif","caption":"The final test run on the completed FLARE system, after the wet lab's feedback produced plastic dishes, a lid handle, longer ribbon cables, a reworked interface, a UV kill switch and ethanol-resistant materials.","credit":"Team NU Boston, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Calibrate the actuator as carefully as the detector, and then do not use the fitted line: the team measured delivered volume against pump duty cycle, found both curves nonlinear with a dead zone and a plateau, and ruled that doses must be interpolated from the measured points because the trendline missed the data where it mattered.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/nu-boston/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/nu-boston/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/nu-boston/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/nu-boston/outreach","https://2026.igem.wiki/nu-boston/results"],"rank":7},"6301":{"team":"UCNZ","id":"6301","section":"Undergrad","country":"New Zealand","village":"Biomanufacturing","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/ucnz/","projectTitle":"NanoBrew","tagline":"Enzymatic production of nanocellulose from brewers' spent grain - turning 39 million tonnes a year of brewing waste into a high-value biomaterial.","summary":"NanoBrew takes brewers' spent grain (BSG), which makes up about 85% of beer brewing waste by weight and is mostly landfilled or sold as cheap animal feed, and extracts nanocellulose from it enzymatically instead of with hot acid and energy-intensive mechanical grinding. The team expressed a Bacillus subtilis xylanase (XynA) to strip hemicellulose and open up the cellulose, plus an ancestrally reconstructed Cel5A endoglucanase fused to a carbohydrate binding module to cut cellulose down to nanofibrils, and tested six construct variants with and without the YebF secretion tag in E. coli. It was Top 10 and nominated for Presentation, Entrepreneurship and Biomanufacturing because the project is framed end to end as a New Zealand circular-economy story - built on a real brewery partnership, grounded in the Maori value of kaitiakitanga, with a full pilot-plant cost analysis and letters of support - and because the team is candid that it never managed to characterise its product. No previous iGEM team had extracted nanocellulose from lignocellulosic plant material rather than growing it bacterially.","awards":["Top 10 (Undergrad)","Best Presentation — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Entrepreneurship — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Biomanufacturing Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Modest but purposeful, and honestly scoped. Before ordering genes, all six constructs were folded with AlphaFold 3 and the predicted structures aligned in PyMOL against the unfused enzymes to check the YebF tag, linkers and CBM had not disturbed the catalytic core - RMSD came out at 0.101 and 0.117 Angstrom for XynA and YebF-XynA, and 0.183, 0.155, 0.173 Angstrom for the endoglucanase variants, all well under 2 Angstrom, with pTM reported per model and the flexible linker correctly flagged as an unstructured region. Enzyme assays were run as time-series DNS and fitted to Michaelis-Menten-like behaviour on both the control substrate (birchwood xylan) and on BSG, with enzyme inactivation used to freeze each timepoint. For the system-level question they built a causal loop diagram with 12 nodes linking the environmental, economic and social effects of an upscaled process, signed each causal link positive or negative, and decomposed the graph into balancing and reinforcing loops - while explicitly refusing to quantify link strength. The microfluidic viscometer was designed entirely in simulation (Capillarix, an unreleased capillary-microfluidics simulator supplied by its creator) with a simulated error table, and the absorbance sensor uses a machine learning calibration running on the device itself.","dataviz":"The two devices are the visualization story: the project needed a way to read nanocellulose concentration from microlitre samples, and the engineering subteam built it. The differential microfluidic viscometer compares a sample against a reference fluid in a sealed channel to cancel out the variable hydrophilicity of PMMA, computing relative viscosity as the ratio of average length-times-velocity products over the first second of flow, then calibrating to the expected sample range so unknowns are read by linear interpolation. The optical sensor strobes red, green and blue LEDs sequentially and feeds the three absorbance values to a machine learning model on an onboard ESP32, which infers concentration - and is deliberately built so a biotechnologist can recalibrate it for whatever property they want to infer. The wiki itself keeps each page to a clear sectioned structure with a sidebar contents list, and the stakeholder work is presented as an influence-interest grid rather than a list.","datascience":"The dry lab's strongest quality is calibrated honesty rather than volume of computation. The team states plainly at the top of the entrepreneurship page that its market research targeted cellulose nanofibrils because that was the anticipated product from the literature, but that it was unable to characterise what it actually made; the FTIR comparison against a pure nanocellulose reference sample came back inconclusive, and they published that, named ATR-FTIR as the next attempt, and said they were waiting on expert advice as of the wiki freeze. For the absorbance sensor they ran out of nanocellulose and substituted guar gum, justifying it as shear-thinning with a similar concentration-opacity relationship, and tabulating the results as such. The viscometer error table notes that surface roughness is not modelled. They also report that only one student in their school talks had heard of iGEM, and that a 2019 survey of 9,000 New Zealanders found 30% opposed selling GM food at all - using measured baselines rather than assertions about public attitudes.","software":"No standalone software release. The hardware is the deliverable: two sensors for reading nanocellulose concentration in microlitre volumes, one a differential capillary-microfluidics viscometer validated in simulation, the other a built RGB-strobing absorbance/turbidity sensor with on-ESP32 machine learning calibration, both developed through two documented iterations of the engineering design cycle and integrated into University of Canterbury engineering students' coursework with some of those students joining as external collaborators. Parts are the other contribution: six constructs registered, with EG-CBM (BBa_26TOG7XZ) highlighted as expressing and purifying extremely well with good activity on complex substrates, plus Pichia/yeast-targeted versions using an OST1 signal sequence and T2A self-cleaving peptide bicistronic designs (BBa_266IKFQ3, BBa_26OB3D76), and a characterisation of the YebF secretion tag (BBa_K1610300, from TAS_Taipei 2015) intended to let future teams choose a secretion system on evidence.","stack":["AlphaFold 3","PyMOL","SnapGene 8.2.3","Capillarix (capillary microfluidics simulation)","ESP32","Google Patents / BLAST (freedom-to-operate searching)","FTIR spectroscopy","SEM","solid-state NMR (via Bioeconomy Science Institute)"],"techniques":["Structure prediction and RMSD alignment for fusion-construct validation","pTM / confidence-based interpretation of predicted models","Time-series DNS enzyme assay with Michaelis-Menten fitting","Causal loop diagramming with balancing and reinforcing loop decomposition","Differential capillary viscometry","Multi-wavelength absorbance with on-device ML calibration","Sedimentation assay for aspect ratio","FTIR purity assessment","Two-cycle engineering design iteration","PEST and SWOT analysis","Pilot-plant cost forecasting","Influence-interest stakeholder mapping"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Outreach was built around a deliberate hypothesis: in New Zealand, synthetic biology means genetic modification and genetic modification means risk, so the team tested whether a local story changes how people engage. They gave three secondary-school talks (one at Burnside High School, two at Christchurch Girls' High School, both schools some members had attended) covering synthetic biology, iGEM, what a science degree looks like and how NanoBrew works, and structured them for dialogue - long question time, small-group breakout discussion, a quiz where answers were argued through rather than marked, contact details left for follow-ups, and teacher feedback collected. Their findings are reported as findings: students already knew breweries and brewery waste so the local hook carried the science; small groups worked far better than whole-cohort presentation; most questions were about science careers and preparing for university, where undergraduates were better placed to answer than any teacher; and only one student had ever heard of iGEM. For the wider public they worked with the university communications team on a press release framed as a local problem with a local solution, which reached The Press, NZ Herald, Radio New Zealand, NewstalkZB, The Breeze, The Platform and deliberately rural and regional outlets including the Ashburton Courier and Selwyn Times, with a team member and the PI giving radio interviews that explained containment in plain language; the Instagram account passed 23,000 views. They also presented at the Biomolecular Interaction Centre Winter Symposium. The published lessons for future teams are practical: get your institution's comms team involved early, and contact schools months ahead because they plan a year out.","ihp":"Human practices is organised around kaitiakitanga, the Maori concept of guardianship, with Bree Bell (Kaiarahi for UC Science) consulted early on how the project interfaces with iwi and hapu, and further consultation explicitly deferred to the scale-up stage rather than claimed as done. Stakeholders are mapped on an influence-interest grid and the design changes are specific. The team was split between on-site plants at each brewery and one centralised facility; Professor Jack Heinemann and Dr Brigitta Kurenbach, both involved in international synthetic biology regulation, argued that a distributed model multiplies accidental-exposure risk and regulatory burden because each site needs separate approval, so the team went centralised. The same pair identified the circular-economy rebound effect - if BSG becomes valuable, beer gets cheaper to make, production rises and total waste could increase - and told them 'sustainable' depends on timeframe and is often marketing; the team consequently narrowed its claim to reducing environmental impact relative to alternative BSG disposal, up to a stated horizon, and no further. Materially Kiwi (a startup making leather from kiwifruit waste) independently warned that customers buy on performance, consistency and price, not sustainability, and that a free feedstock does not mean a cheap product once collection, processing, testing and equipment are counted - which moved yield confirmation and full process costing to the top of the priority list. Dr Stefan Hill and Dr Mathias Sorieul at the Bioeconomy Science Institute warned that BSG-derived nanocellulose may be indistinguishable from wood-derived, so the low-cost waste feedstock, not the material, is the selling point; they also reframed BSG's high hemicellulose as a possible advantage, citing an Australian spinifex grass result where hemicellulose remnants improved material properties, and prescribed the three characterisation methods (SEM for fibril width, sedimentation for aspect ratio, FTIR for purity) the team then attempted. Dr Andrew Prest at Foodstuffs Own Brands listed what a packaging buyer needs and confirmed food-contact use would need substantial safety assessment, which is why the team targets non-food packaging first. Lincoln Agritech's suggestion of rheology as a measurement route is what started the viscometer, and Professor Volker Nock was met at the BIC symposium after researchers there raised the energy cost of freeze-thaw cycles at scale.","realWorld":"The commercial case is unusually complete for an undergraduate team and backed by two letters of support (Cassels Brewing Co. and Lincoln University). Local grounding: in Christchurch alone BSG accounts for an estimated 680-1,000 tonnes to landfill a year, costing breweries up to NZ$220,000 in disposal fees, and nationally roughly 13,700 tonnes to landfill producing 14,000 tonnes CO2-equivalent, which the promotional video renders as 3,300 petrol cars running for a year. Market: nanocellulose at US$947 million in 2026 growing at 23.74% CAGR to a projected US$6.4 billion by 2035, with the team noting that estimates vary between reports and stating which figure it uses throughout. Price reality from stakeholders sets the strategy: at around $100/kg nanocellulose suits high-value medical uses while broad uptake needs roughly $10/kg, so packaging is the entry market. The page carries a development roadmap, a commercial-scale cost forecast, a downloadable preliminary CNF cost analysis for a pilot-scale plant, financial analysis and timeline, a business exit strategy, minimum viable product definition, PEST, SWOT, risk and competitor analyses (including Nano-Sea/AgriSea making kelp-derived nanocellulose locally, which does not target packaging), and a pitch deck. On IP, the UC Technology Transfer Office told them a first filing runs NZ$10-15K and is only worth it if results look promising, that only novel elements need protecting, that much of their approach is already published so finding the novel element may be hard, and that they should BLAST their enzyme sequences against patented sequences to check freedom to operate - and that they should document negative results because that is how an invention's origin is evidenced. The team notes everything submitted to iGEM enters the public domain, so any filing had to precede the wiki. Continuation is real: the media coverage plus the results won University of Canterbury funding for a summer research project carrying the work on under Dr Kelsi Hall, one of only 18 scholarships awarded across all faculties in 2026. The team also commits to licensing the process to other agricultural and food-processing waste streams once protected, with documentation, stakeholder map and methods open now.","partners":["Cassels Brewing Co.","Lincoln University","Lincoln Agritech","Bioeconomy Science Institute (BSI)","Foodstuffs Own Brands","Materially Kiwi","Kai Commitment","Biomolecular Interaction Centre (BIC), University of Canterbury","UC Technology Transfer Office","Momentum (UC entrepreneurship programme)","University of Canterbury Communications and Events","Burnside High School","Christchurch Girls' High School","University of Canterbury School of Biological Sciences","University of Canterbury engineering students (external collaborators)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6301/wiki/hp/fig-2.avif","caption":"The causal loop diagram: 12 nodes linking the environmental, economic and social effects of an upscaled NanoBrew process, with each link signed positive or negative and the graph decomposed into balancing and reinforcing loops - including the circular-economy rebound effect raised by regulatory stakeholders.","credit":"Team UCNZ, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6301/wiki/hp/fig-1.avif","caption":"The stakeholder influence-interest grid used to decide who to consult and in what order, spanning the brewery partner, regulators, characterisation experts, potential customers and Maori advisors.","credit":"Team UCNZ, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6301/wiki/hardware/figure-1-1.avif","caption":"The final design for the differential microfluidic viscometer, simulated in Capillarix, which infers nanocellulose concentration by comparing relative viscosity of a microlitre sample against a reference fluid.","credit":"Team UCNZ, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6301/wiki/results/results-fig02.avif","caption":"A time-series DNS assay showing XynA xylanase activity rising on both the control substrate (birchwood xylan) and on brewers' spent grain, in Michaelis-Menten-like fashion.","credit":"Team UCNZ, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6301/wiki/education/school.avif","caption":"A NanoBrew talk at a Christchurch secondary school, run with long question time and small-group breakouts after the team found whole-cohort presentation far less effective.","credit":"Team UCNZ, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"UCNZ shows how to publish an unfinished result well: they never characterised their nanocellulose, said so at the top of the page that depended on it, named the failed method (FTIR, inconclusive against a reference sample), the planned replacement (ATR-FTIR) and the substitute material they used when samples ran out - and still won Top 10. The second transferable move is the local hook: anchor the project in an industry students already recognise, then get the institution's communications office involved early enough that national and regional media carry the story, which is what converted their outreach into continuation funding.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/ucnz/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucnz/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucnz/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucnz/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucnz/experiments","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucnz/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucnz/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucnz/education-and-outreach","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucnz/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucnz/parts","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucnz/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucnz/safety-and-security","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucnz/notebook"],"rank":91},"6306":{"team":"NYCU-Taiwan","id":"6306","section":"Undergrad","country":"Taiwan","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/nycu-taiwan/","projectTitle":"BITE — Biosensing for Instant Target Pathogen Evaluation","tagline":"A two-chamber swab that turns Cas12a collateral cleavage into a blue colour you can read with your eyes","summary":"NYCU-Taiwan built BITE, a hand-operated two-chamber cartridge for foodborne Salmonella detection: chamber one releases magnetic beads carrying DNA capture probes plus lysis buffer, heat lysis frees bacterial DNA, a magnet concentrates the bead-bound target, then chamber two delivers Cas12a with crRNA and a hairpin reporter whose G-rich segment, once cleaved, folds into a potassium-stabilised G-quadruplex that binds hemin to form a DNAzyme and oxidises TMB from colourless to blue. The point of the design is that the final step needs no instrument. They won Best Project Promotion Video in the Undergrad/Overgrad section, and the same communication discipline runs through the wiki, which is built as a scroll-driven narrative rather than a document.","awards":["Best Project Promotion Video — Winner (Undergrad & Overgrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A narrative structure applied consistently: everyday stakes, then the quantified global burden with its source named, then what existing methods do well, then the specific real-world constraints that make them impractical, then a refusal of the implied trade-off, then the solution and only then the mechanism. Each mechanistic step is introduced by the question it answers (Cas12a can cut DNA, but how do we turn an invisible molecular reaction into something we can see?), so the chemistry arrives as an answer rather than as content.","dataviz":"Roughly 67 separately numbered illustration layers on the landing page alone, assembled into a scroll-driven walkthrough: an exploded device diagram with each component labelled (two chambers, Y-connector, sampling swab, collection tube), a magnetic-bead sequence split into meet-the-beads, capture and magnetic separation, an RNP assembly and trans-cleavage sequence, and a hairpin-to-G4-to-DNAzyme-to-blue-TMB chain. Numbers are set as display type (866 million ill, 1.52 million deaths) with the WHO foodborne-hazards estimate cited beneath them.","datascience":"Education impact is measured rather than asserted: paired pre- and post-surveys at the 16 May outreach session moved the share of 102 high-school candidates rating their understanding of synthetic biology at 4 to 5 from 13.3 percent to 80.0 percent. The April workshop, lacking reflection surveys, was instead scored against observational rubrics and task-completion rates (96 percent produced clean four-tier density gradients, 92 percent kept sterile boundaries in the laminar hood, 88 percent of culture tubes stayed contamination-free at 14 days, 85 percent distinguished nicked, supercoiled and linear plasmid bands, 95 percent built a correct genetic circuit first time). Instagram is reported with the diagnostic metric rather than the vanity one: 41,851 views across 6 July to 6 October, views up 209.6 percent on the previous period, and 57.9 percent of views from non-followers.","software":"BITE & SEEK, a bilingual public food-safety website launched 10 August 2026, with a card-based kitchen-decision quiz that reshuffles each round so replaying tests understanding rather than recall, a Facts page keyed to the 7-60 degrees C temperature danger zone per Taiwan FDA guidance and the WHO Five Keys, a History page tracing five outbreaks that changed food-safety law, and a live visitor map with per-country quiz averages.","stack":["LbCas12a","crRNA","G-quadruplex/hemin DNAzyme","TMB colorimetry","streptavidin-biotin magnetic beads","HRP/TMB control readout","fluorescence time-course assays"],"techniques":["magnetic-bead target enrichment with capture probes","heat lysis","Cas12a trans-cleavage of a hairpin reporter","potassium-dependent G4 folding","colorimetric readout development and background characterisation"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Three channels with distinct jobs rather than three copies of the same message. BITE & SEEK carries the knowledge in replayable interactive form (133 visits from 5 countries by 18 October, which they report honestly as modest). A four-station hands-on workshop on 18 April took 25 students through micropipetting, sundew tissue culture, gel electrophoresis and BioBrick LEGO modelling, with the full station protocols published so another team can run it. A 16 May session reached 102 high-school candidates during departmental interviews, deliberately timed when the audience was already thinking about studying biotechnology. Instagram splits formats by function: posts for team and event information, Reels for lab life and concepts, Stories for real-time interaction, and the best-performing content was the team introduction post (4,169 views) and a lab Reel (3,039 views), which also drove the most new followers. Their own conclusion from that is the useful one: real people in authentic settings outperform polished explanation, and content anchored to daily life travels furthest.","ihp":"Two company visits on 5 September, both of which changed something concrete. Dr. Lance Chang, founder and executive director of Trade Wind Biotech, proposed a microfluidic format to cut reagent consumption (the G4 readout being their main reagent cost), asked whether Cas12a cleavage could be coupled directly to the G4 reaction without a transfer step and whether reagents could be pre-dried in the device, and gave them the single most important communication instruction in the whole report: do not open with the molecular mechanism of Cas12a collateral cleavage, open with the visible signal and then explain how target recognition produces it. He also insisted that a clear explanation rests on actually understanding the science, which sent them to the literature on why G4 prefers potassium over sodium (ion coordination plus the greater energetic cost of dehydrating sodium). At AccuSens Biomed, Dr. Chen told them to pick one specific potential advantage and define the evidence needed to support it rather than trying to beat PCR on every axis. Acting on that, they read competitors' technical documentation properly and found that Hygiena's BAX System Real-Time Salmonella assay already uses lyophilised single-tube reagents, holds AOAC OMA and AFNOR certification and offers quantification through SalQuant, meaning several features they had believed distinctive were already on the market. They published that finding. Dr. Chen also gave bench-level troubleshooting (1-5 ng purified plasmid, medium-sized colonies, three- or four-zone streaking with a 20 microlitre tip instead of a metal loop, a descending IPTG series, pre-induction growth to OD600 around 0.5 and never above 0.6) and set field-deployment targets they explicitly label as targets, not features: room-temperature lyophilised reagent beads, a reader that runs off an ordinary power bank, and software that works on a local offline network and syncs to cloud when connectivity returns.","realWorld":"There is no commercialisation claim here, and the restraint is the point. Every page separates demonstrated results from development directions in so many words: the microfluidic format, reagent pre-mixing and storage stability 'remain future development directions' whose feasibility 'has not yet been established'; the current results 'do not establish shorter sample enrichment, room-temperature reagent stability, or field-ready operation'; background colour development is named as a remaining limitation of their own colorimetric readout. They also state the general lesson, which is the one most iGEM teams miss: successful component tests provide a foundation but do not establish the performance of the complete system. The competitive honesty is equally unusual, since discovering that a commercial assay already has your differentiators and then publishing that discovery is the opposite of what a pitch rewards. What is worth copying, though, is the communication craft. Four things make it work. First, the arc puts stakes before mechanism, so the audience knows why they should care before any molecular biology arrives. Second, it states the constraints that disqualify existing methods in plain operational terms (a test may need lab equipment, a result may take time, testing may need trained personnel) rather than claiming existing methods are bad, which keeps the claim defensible. Third, it refuses a false choice out loud ('but why should we have to choose?') and that refusal becomes the product definition, with the five requirements (fast, sensitive and specific, simple, accessible, portable) spelling out the acronym the device is named after. Fourth, each mechanistic step is framed as the answer to a question the previous step raised, and the chain terminates in something sensory, a blue colour, which is also the actual engineering contribution. The invitation to act is a single pun, 'take a BITE before every bite'. Supporting all of this is real production investment: dozens of bespoke illustration layers, three custom web fonts including a hand-lettered one, bilingual content, and a scroll-driven build rather than a page of text and figures. Continuation is framed as community infrastructure rather than a company: a team leaderboard opening the BITE & SEEK quiz to every iGEM team at the Grand Jamboree with prizes for the top ten, progressive challenges, shareable result cards, full English coverage, and in-person workshops linking the website to hands-on demonstrations.","partners":["Trade Wind Biotech Co., Ltd. (Dr. Lance Chang, Founder and Executive Director; device format, reagent integration and communication strategy)","AccuSens Biomed Co., Ltd. (Dr. Chen; competitive positioning, field-deployment requirements, offered materials for reagent pre-mixing tests)","National Yang Ming Chiao Tung University, Department of Biological Science and Technology","IDT and CEB (listed sponsors)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6306/wiki/01-home/279-home-walk-dev-base.webp","caption":"One layer of the exploded BITE device walkthrough, built from dozens of separately drawn illustration components so the cartridge can be assembled step by step as the reader scrolls","credit":"Team NYCU-Taiwan, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6306/wiki/01-home/138-home-hero-people-back.webp","caption":"Opening illustration of the landing-page narrative, which starts at a shared meal rather than at a molecule","credit":"Team NYCU-Taiwan, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6306/wiki/17-hp-integrated-hp/253-ihp-tradewind-1.webp","caption":"Visit to Trade Wind Biotech, where Dr. Lance Chang told the team to lead with the visible signal rather than with Cas12a collateral cleavage","credit":"Team NYCU-Taiwan, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6306/wiki/18-hp-education/30-hp-edu-expo-2.avif","caption":"Four-station hands-on workshop, with full station protocols published so other teams can reproduce it","credit":"Team NYCU-Taiwan, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Adopt their narrative order for every public-facing explanation: stakes with a sourced number, what current methods do well, the operational constraints that disqualify them, an explicit refusal of the trade-off, then the solution, then the mechanism told as a chain of answers ending in something a person can see. And take Trade Wind's instruction literally: open with the visible result, not the enzyme, and only explain the molecular step once the audience wants to know how the result happened.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/nycu-taiwan/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nycu-taiwan/education/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nycu-taiwan/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nycu-taiwan/project","https://www.youtube.com/@NYCU_Taiwan_2026"],"rank":26},"6308":{"team":"Tsinghua-T","id":"6308","section":"Undergrad","country":"China","village":"Fashion & Cosmetics","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/tsinghua-t/","projectTitle":"GALATEA","tagline":"Yeast-based glabridin production inside engineered liquid-liquid phase-separated condensates, with success criteria written by industry","summary":"Glabridin is 0.08-0.35% of licorice root dry weight and all three Glycyrrhiza species are on China's National Key Protected Wild Plants Catalogue, so one gram of the skincare active corresponds to roughly 286-1,250 g of dried root; GALATEA replaces that extraction route with Saccharomyces cerevisiae. The team built tunable protein condensates - an FTH1-24 ferritin iron core as nucleation seed, intrinsically disordered regions, and an SH3/PDZ scaffold at 3:1 recruiting the OC and DMT enzymes - instead of relying on random co-localisation. Their integrated human practices is organised as a four-act loop (Define, Optimize, Calibrate, Echo) in which each act must produce a change, and the loop closes by returning the engineering improvements to the same 96 street respondents for re-validation. Advice from Tsinghua chemical engineering professors reordered the biosynthetic pathway itself, and seven company visits rewrote the project's definition of success.","awards":["Best New Composite Part — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Sustainable Development Impact — Winner (Undergrad)","Best Fashion & Cosmetics Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A six-module dry-lab pipeline run over four engineering rounds: M0 evidence collection, M1 sequence-level screening, M2 structural and assembly screening, M3 enzyme recruitment and partitioning, M4 pathway kinetics, M5 experimental comparison. Every module states explicitly what a negative screen does NOT establish (for example, 'M1 flags sequence and topology risks for structural follow-up; a negative screen does not establish enzyme activity or scaffold assembly'). Outputs were deliberately changed from a single yield prediction to 'recommended conditions + sensitivity ranking + uncertainty interval + failure criteria'.","dataviz":"A before/after paired bar chart of the same 96 street respondents' judgments; a stakeholder-by-theme emphasis matrix (eight engagement records x five themes, graded not highlighted / mentioned / discussed in depth); an interview coding grid (seven participants x five themes); consumer-needs and technical-concerns word clouds; a three-stage deployment-path diagram; and a two-column 'Measured Results / Next-Step Validations' format applied to every presentation slide.","datascience":"A 1,397-DOI literature analysis, a 16-compound computational safety screen against a fixed skincare reference panel, and a three-tier evidence table (Production, Skin Health, Safety) in which each entry records the experimental system, concentration range, source and evidence grade. Sequence screening uses IUPred2A disorder, SignalP, DeepTMHMM, PSIPRED, net charge per residue and mean hydropathy; all external data on the wiki carry source and experimental-condition labels, with literature values visually separated from the team's own measurements.","software":"GALATEA-Caelum, an integrated platform combining a literature-retrieval algorithm with an Agent harness that turns a researcher's prompt plus registered tools into a reviewable dry-lab plan grounded in the project's own wet-lab data. The retrieval algorithm queries OpenAlex, Crossref and Europe PMC, then ranks with BM25 (k1=1.5, b=0.75) plus BAAI/bge-m3 semantic embeddings, fuses with Reciprocal Rank Fusion, deduplicates by Jaccard, diversifies with MMR, rereads the full text of top records to extract numerical parameters, and runs AI-assisted quality evaluation. Built to be reused by future iGEM teams.","stack":["GALATEA-Caelum","BM25 + BAAI/bge-m3 embeddings","Reciprocal Rank Fusion / MMR","OpenAlex, Crossref, Europe PMC APIs","IUPred2A","SignalP","DeepTMHMM","PSIPRED","confocal fluorescence microscopy"],"techniques":["FTH1-based Corelets condensate modelling","modular SH3/PDZ recruitment modelling","partition-coefficient and leakage modelling","pathway kinetic modelling","LLPS scaffold design with linker length and flexibility gradients","retrieval-augmented parameter extraction","sensitivity ranking and uncertainty interval reporting"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Public engagement is built as a measurement instrument rather than a broadcast. Two rounds of street interviews (118 then 96 participants) bracket the engineering work: round one asked 'what do you need', round two revisited the same sites, gave respondents a short questionnaire, showed them the improved plain-language cards and the engineering evidence, then asked the same questions again - acceptance of biosynthetic ingredients rose 54.2% to 78.1%, the belief that a titre number alone is enough to judge success fell 71.9% to 22.9%, and willingness to pay 10% more for traceable production rose 26% to 51%. A 286-response campus questionnaire (18 items, two open-ended) plus 7 young-consumer interviews and 137 Q&A exchanges run with NUS supplied the baseline. Also four on-campus seminars (210 attendees), an offline outreach session at Beijing 101 High School, 23 articles on the WeChat account 'Tanwei iGEMer', two contributed pages in a science-outreach artbook with Rice iGEM, and the organisation of Tsinghua University's first Synthetic Biology Innovation Contest (62 teams from 21 universities).","ihp":"GALATEA states its IHP function in one sentence - 'at each decision point it brings external stakeholders into the process and converts their judgment into concrete changes' - and then shows the conversions. The deepest chain runs through Professor Zheng Liu and Professor Chong Zhang of Tsinghua's Department of Chemical Engineering, who were shown the team's initial plan of directly fusing enzymes and relying on random co-localisation. They made three objections: random co-localisation cannot stop intermediates diffusing away before reaching the next enzyme; the DMT enzyme has high substrate promiscuity and poor selectivity, with a reported extracellular fraction of the intermediate demethylvestitol of 88.4 +/- 4.2%; and OC is hydrophobic, so it can be recruited into relatively hydrophobic droplets, and since OC is the rate-limiting step the OC:DMT ratio is the lever. The team changed four things: they replaced direct fusion with a tunable FTH1-24 ferritin-seeded scaffold plus IDR condensate and SH3/PDZ recruitment at 3:1 that keeps local OC concentration above DMT; they moved the DMT demethylation step to the very end of the biosynthetic pathway so promiscuity cannot contaminate intermediate steps; they expanded readouts from 'final yield only' to product identity, purity, intra- and extracellular intermediates, by-products, batch-to-batch stability and functional relevance; and they embedded red and green fluorescent markers in the scaffold so droplet formation and enzyme co-localisation are observed under the microscope rather than inferred. That is a stakeholder conversation changing the reaction order of a metabolic pathway. The seven company visits, sampled deliberately across supply-chain roles (Blue-Peptides and INNOBIO upstream in Dalian; WuXi Biologics and Zerun Biotech as CDMO in Shanghai; CHANDO Beauty Science City and Guyu Beauty as end brands in Guangzhou; IMEIK against medical-device standards in Beijing), were run with the same four questions each time, and each produced a specific change: Blue-Peptides' line that 'an unrepeatable yield figure equals zero in industry' added a batch-to-batch variation column to the experimental records; WuXi Biologics' thresholds of purity >= 95% and +/- 5% batch variation went into the wet-lab detection items; CHANDO's raw-material gate (efficacy, safety, cost and supply stability all must pass) and Guyu's four-document procurement logic split efficacy evidence into in vitro cellular and formulation tiers so in vitro results are never presented as efficacy claims; IMEIK's insistence that a complete data package matters more than any single impressive metric produced a data-package checklist consolidating all seven companies' requirements with a tick-box for whether the team currently holds each item. Together these rewrote the judgment chain from 'LLPS works -> leakage falls -> yield rises -> success' to that chain plus product identity and quality evidence plus functional relevance to specific skin problems. NUS professors' critique that partition coefficient, leakage rate, linker flexibility and effective enzyme concentration were implicit and invisible drove the model-output change and the three-tier evidence table. Peer iGEM teams each closed a specific gap: Nanjing Normal University on genomic integration versus plasmid expression to reduce batch variation; Nankai University on platform scope and the scale-up bottleneck, which the team admits they could not answer at the time and then added to the public project description; Beijing Institute of Technology on provenance, pointing out that an unlabelled 88.4% leakage figure would read as the team's own measurement - which is why every external number on the wiki now carries a source label. Conference feedback was treated the same way: NCIM made them split every slide into 'Measured Results' and 'Next-Step Validations'; CCiC's objection that a single leakage percentage without a stated loading ratio is meaningless added the three comparison groups (free enzyme, random co-localisation, LLPS scaffold) and the 1:1 / 1:2 / 2:1 recruitment gradient to the formal protocol; APiC moved the fluorescence co-localisation data out of the appendix and into results; and a question at the Peking-Rice Summit about skin-tone controversy produced the impact-boundary assessment. They also adopted Beijing Institute of Technology's HP process discipline - preparation, execution, review, with a named note-taker per phase - so every visit produced minutes in a fixed format.","realWorld":"The need is quantified at the resource level: 0.08-0.35% glabridin content in licorice root, all three Glycyrrhiza species protected under Chinese law, 286-1,250 g of dried Uzbek root and stolon per gram of product assuming complete recovery, and documented habitat degradation from overharvesting. Only three SDGs are claimed - 3 Good Health and Well-being, 9 Industry Innovation and Infrastructure, 12 Responsible Consumption and Production - and each is tied to a specific question (what makes the ingredient useful, how it should be produced, how materials are used responsibly). Crucially, the sustainability page contains a table mapping each HP concern to its source participant or specialist, to the assessment dimension it created, to what was actually included in the analysis, and to the SDG connection, so the SDG link is derived from stakeholder evidence rather than asserted. The regulatory path is checked item by item against Chinese cosmetic law: spot-fading and whitening claims require human efficacy evaluation trials, naming follows the Cosmetic Classification Rules and Catalogue, biotechnological raw materials fall under YY/T 10001-2026, and new ingredients require registration and filing - from which the team concludes that efficacy claims are their most constrained category because their evidence stops at the in vitro and yeast level, far below what the claim would require. A negative-impacts table lists who is affected, under what conditions, the residual uncertainty and the team's own boundary for three topics including colorism, committing to never rank skin tones by lightness and to use specific skin-problem wording instead. Deployment is staged with a cost target: 1-2 years to prove platform portability to other high-value molecules, 2-3 years to pilot-scale fermentation with dry-lab models recalibrated against the industrial parameters collected on the visits, aiming to bring cost from about RMB 100,000 per kilogram at lab scale to below RMB 30,000, then 3-5 years into cosmetics, traditional Chinese medicine and nutraceuticals via licensing and joint development. Most tellingly, the one thing public communication could not fix is reported unfixed: 56.3% still regarded price as a major barrier after seeing the cards, so the team wrote price back into the Part 3 cost targets 'unchanged' and added 'efficacy claims running ahead of evidence' to its red lines for future communication.","partners":["Department of Chemical Engineering, Tsinghua University (Prof. Zheng Liu, Prof. Chong Zhang)","National University of Singapore (professors and iGEM team)","Blue-Peptides (Dalian)","INNOBIO (Dalian)","WuXi Biologics (Shanghai)","Zerun Biotech (Shanghai)","CHANDO Beauty Science City (Shanghai)","Guyu Beauty (Guangzhou)","IMEIK (Beijing)","NNU-Nanjing-China iGEM","Nankai University iGEM","Beijing Institute of Technology iGEM","Rice University iGEM","Peking University iGEM","Beijing 101 High School"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6308/wiki/assests/human-practice/hp-figure-10-01.avif","caption":"Expert interviews with the Department of Chemical Engineering, Tsinghua University - the conversation that moved the promiscuous DMT demethylation step to the end of the pathway","credit":"Team Tsinghua-T, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6308/wiki/assests/human-practice/hp-figure-19-01.avif","caption":"Dalian company visits to Blue-Peptides and INNOBIO, where 'an unrepeatable yield figure equals zero in industry' added a batch-to-batch variation column to the lab records","credit":"Team Tsinghua-T, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6308/wiki/assests/human-practice/hp-figure-20-01.avif","caption":"Shanghai visits to Zerun Biotech, WuXi Biologics and CHANDO Beauty Science City, which supplied the purity >=95% and +/-5% batch-variation thresholds","credit":"Team Tsinghua-T, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6308/wiki/assests/human-practice/hp-figure-22-01.avif","caption":"IMEIK in Beijing, where medical-device-grade raw material review produced the team's data-package checklist","credit":"Team Tsinghua-T, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Close the loop by measuring it: take the engineering changes stakeholder feedback produced back to the same respondents, ask the same questions before and after, and publish the one metric that did not move - then convert industry's hard thresholds into the project's own definition of a successful design, so a higher titre alone can no longer count as success.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/tsinghua-t/","https://2026.igem.wiki/tsinghua-t/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/tsinghua-t/hp-part-1/","https://2026.igem.wiki/tsinghua-t/hp-part-2/","https://2026.igem.wiki/tsinghua-t/hp-part-3/","https://2026.igem.wiki/tsinghua-t/hp-part-4/","https://2026.igem.wiki/tsinghua-t/sustainability/","https://2026.igem.wiki/tsinghua-t/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/tsinghua-t/software/"],"rank":40},"6329":{"team":"Baltimore","id":"6329","section":"High School","country":"United States","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/baltimore/","projectTitle":"KeraTINT","tagline":"A chromoprotein-keratin-binding-peptide fusion that colours hair and repairs it in the same step","summary":"Baltimore Biocrew, based at the Baltimore Underground Science Space community lab, engineered fusion proteins joining chromoproteins (aeblue, UM) to keratin-binding peptides so that a semi-permanent dye deposits colour while reinforcing the hair shaft. The entrepreneurship work was run through iGEM's Venture Creation Labs curriculum, the same incubator route their 2023 project RhizeUp took, and it produced an OKR table with numeric key results, a scored risk register, a US-specific patent strategy and a competitor map. Market evidence rests on two IRB-approved consumer surveys (56 then 54 responses, translated into Chinese and Filipino) plus named interviews with a cosmetics founder, two L'Oreal North America hair-colour-lab staff, a cosmetology student and the Boeke Lab at NYU Langone. They were nominated for Best Entrepreneurship in the High School section.","awards":["Best Entrepreneurship — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"iGEM Venture Creation Labs curriculum as the scaffold, Golden Circle, Unique Value Proposition, Lean Business Model Canvas, SWOT, a seven-phase Objectives and Key Results table with business-day estimates and fixed-cost lines, a risk register with a published 1-5 impact x 1-5 likelihood scoring rubric and named owners, direct and indirect and future competitor tiers, and the iGEM judging ballot answered question by question.","dataviz":"Interactive click-through SWOT, a nine-slide pitch deck embedded as a carousel, a lean canvas, a long-term impact-assessment graphic, a 2027-2029 timeline, and a horizontally scrollable OKR and risk table. Survey results are reported as percentages and cross-tabulated by language group and age.","datascience":"Two-round survey analysis with a genuine iteration: a bimodal distribution on grey-coverage priority in Survey 1 (a quarter rating it 1, nearly half rating it 10) was hypothesised to be two age cohorts, and Survey 2 confirmed it by adding age, hair type and prior chemical-treatment questions. Reported figures include 64.3 percent rating less hair damage a 10/10 priority, 89 percent rating it 8 or above, 50 percent using at-home boxed kits and only 25.9 percent relying solely on salons.","software":"","stack":["Google Forms","chromoprotein-keratin-binding peptide fusion constructs"],"techniques":["fusion protein design","colour retention and wash-cycle testing (planned)","cytotoxicity assay development (started, not completed)","pH and thermal stability assessment (literature-based)"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Surveys were deliberately multilingual, translated into Chinese and Filipino to reach their own communities, and the results split cleanly by language and age in ways that changed the product thesis: younger English-speaking respondents wanted fashion blues, pinks and purples, which happens to be what their chromoproteins produce, while older Chinese and Filipino respondents wanted grey coverage and natural shades. They also found that the phrase 'genetically engineered' on a label worried more respondents than it attracted, with several linking it to harmful chemicals or illness, and responded by planning a consumer FAQ booklet distributed through partner salons instead of a call centre. They presented at the July 2026 Mid-Atlantic Meetup alongside eight other regional teams.","ihp":"A Closed-Loop Framework structured each stakeholder conversation into relevance, insight, integration and future question. IRB approval from the BUGSS Board of Directors was obtained before surveying, which is unusual rigour at high-school level. Specific conversations changed specific decisions: Savannah Shumaker (chemist, co-founder and CEO of Eight Count Cosmetics) pushed branding toward audience values and simplified their science communication, and suggested contacting cosmetology schools, which led to Rachel Lu; Lindsay Menzer and Yun Yong Jang (L'Oreal Hair North America, Head of Hair Color Lab) flagged patenting during early testing, which launched the US patent-strategy investigation; the Boeke Lab at NYU Langone recommended storage conditions for chromoproteins, prompting a preservation study; and a question from another team at the Mid-Atlantic Meetup about pH and temperature sensitivity, which they had deprioritised, is what sent them to the Boeke Lab in the first place.","realWorld":"This is a credible early-stage venture plan with the finance section still hollow. What is genuinely strong is the execution scaffolding. The OKR table is the best artefact: it sets falsifiable targets with costs and durations attached, including catalogue 15 salons statewide, a minimum of 10 qualitative interviews, at least 5 Letters of Intent, 10 investor pitches, 10,000 dollars from stakeholder investment plus research grants, cell viability above 70 percent in cytotoxicity assays, dye longevity of 40 wash cycles, protein stability at 50 degrees C, 1,000 sales per month and two new production labs in other mid-Atlantic states. Named funding targets are real and local (Wexford SciTech Venture Fund, TEDCO grants, Connect Labs at 4MLK as prospective lab space, youth competitions such as Blue Ocean, Paradigm and Slingshot). Crucially, every one of these is still an aspiration: the Letters of Intent are a key result, not a signed document; the grant is applied for, not won; there is no registered entity, though forming an LLC is floated inside the liability risk row. The regulatory path is the most concretely researched part of the whole analysis and is credible: they identify that the FDA Office of Cosmetics and Colors certifies coal-tar and synthetic colour additives but that a chromoprotein appears to fall into neither bucket, name 21 CFR parts 73 and 74 subpart C, name the Color Certifications Inquiry Branch as the body to ask, and note that certified and uncertified colours carry legally distinct names. The IP strategy is equally specific and actually actionable: a provisional patent on the aeblue-keratin fusion first, converted to a non-provisional within twelve months, with USPTO micro-entity status claimed for an 80 percent fee reduction, and they check their own eligibility against the 262,380 dollar gross-income threshold. Market sizing, by contrast, is the weakest link, resting on Grand View Research hair-colour market reports rather than any bottom-up estimate, with no price point, no cost of goods and no unit economics anywhere. Continuation is plausible rather than secured: they state plainly that as a high-school iGEM team they can never test on human hair, so KeraTINT must pursue third-party testing or operate independently of iGEM after the competition, and they sequence cytotoxicity, pH and thermal assays as the first post-Jamboree work. The precedent helps their case, since the same team's 2023 RhizeUp project went through the same incubator.","partners":["iGEM Venture Creation Labs / Venture Foundry (incubator curriculum)","Baltimore Underground Science Space (BUGSS) community lab and its Board of Directors (IRB approval)","Savannah Shumaker, chemist and co-founder/CEO, Eight Count Cosmetics","Lindsay Menzer and Yun Yong Jang, L'Oreal Hair North America, Head of Hair Color Lab","Rachel Lu, cosmetology student and freelance makeup artist","Dr. Jef Boeke and Aleksandra Wudzinska, Boeke Lab, NYU Langone Health","Mid-Atlantic Meetup regional iGEM teams"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6329/wiki/entrepreneurship/lbmc.avif","caption":"KeraTINT lean business model canvas identifying local salons and cosmetic companies as first customers","credit":"Team Baltimore, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6329/wiki/entrepreneurship/timeline.avif","caption":"Commercialisation timeline from 2027 stakeholder re-engagement to a 2029 salon product roll-out","credit":"Team Baltimore, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6329/wiki/entrepreneurship/pitch-deck/2.avif","caption":"Slide from the nine-slide KeraTINT pitch deck covering market sizing and distribution channels","credit":"Team Baltimore, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6329/wiki/entrepreneurship/impact-assessment.avif","caption":"Long-term positive and negative impact assessment for consumers and the wider hair-care market","credit":"Team Baltimore, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Steal the OKR table: every commercialisation objective gets a numeric key result, a business-day estimate and a fixed-cost line, including scientific gates such as cell viability above 70 percent and dye longevity of 40 wash cycles, so a business plan becomes a checklist a successor team can inherit. Also copy getting institutional IRB approval before running consumer surveys, which both protects participants and makes the resulting data citable.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/baltimore/","https://2026.igem.wiki/baltimore/entrepreneurship/","https://2026.igem.wiki/baltimore/human-practices/"],"rank":7},"6330":{"team":"HBUT-China","id":"6330","section":"Undergrad","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/hbut-china/","projectTitle":"IGNITE — oHSV2-Neo-IL-2","tagline":"An AI-redesigned IL-2 that activates CD8 T cells without expanding Tregs, delivered from an oncolytic HSV-2 into microsatellite-stable cold tumours","summary":"HBUT-China targeted microsatellite-stable colorectal cancer, the roughly 80-85 percent of advanced cases that behave as immunologically cold tumours, by arming an attenuated oncolytic herpes simplex virus type 2 with an engineered interleukin-2. Their Best New Basic Part, Neo-IL-2, is an AI-guided interface redesign that weakens binding to IL-2R-alpha (CD25) while keeping signalling through the IL-2R-beta/gamma-c complex, so it activates CD8 T cells and NK cells without driving the regulatory T-cell expansion and dose-limiting toxicity that have crippled wild-type IL-2. The cassette was recombined into an HG52 backbone already deleted for ICP34.5 (neurovirulence) and ICP47 (TAP inhibition, so MHC class I presentation is restored), replacing a CMV-GFP cassette at the gamma-34.5 locus. They won Best New Basic Part in the Undergrad section and Best Oncology Project.","awards":["Best New Basic Part — Winner (Undergrad)","Best Oncology Project — Winner"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Two named, reusable frameworks offered as contributions: SHIELD, a six-module full-chain safety paradigm covering safety-by-design, wet-lab operational governance, hardware infrastructure assurance, emergency response, training and education, and public outreach; and HOPES, a closed-loop human-centred methodology for integrated human practices. Plus a documented chassis-comparison exercise weighing HSV-1 against HSV-2 across oncolytic capacity, payload size and other dimensions before committing.","dataviz":"Construction schematics showing the HG52 (ICP34.5-/ICP47-) backbone with TRL/IRL/IRS/TRS repeats and the homologous-recombination replacement of CMV-GFP with CMV-Neo-IL-2-BGH-polyA, three-round plaque-purification panels in bright-field, green and merged channels, flow-cytometry Treg percentage comparisons, qPCR and RTCA traces, tumour growth curves and survival plots, and a watercolour shield diagram linking the six SHIELD dimensions.","datascience":"AI-assisted protein interface design followed by multi-tool computational triage: molecular docking, affinity prediction, stability and manufacturability analysis, with PRODIGY used to forecast receptor-binding profiles at 37 degrees C and confirm reduced CD25 affinity alongside retained CD122/CD132 association. The design hypothesis is then tested rather than assumed, with SPR used for direct receptor-binding verification.","software":"","stack":["AI-assisted protein design","PRODIGY affinity prediction","molecular docking","HSV-2 HG52 (ICP34.5-/ICP47-) backbone","pHG52d34.5-CMV-GFP shuttle vector","ICP4 complementing cells","calcium phosphate co-transfection","SPR","RTCA real-time cytotoxicity","flow cytometry","ELISA","qPCR"],"techniques":["rational receptor-bias engineering of a cytokine","homologous recombination into a viral genome at a defined locus","three-round plaque purification","Treg selective-activation assay","T-cell activation assay","high-passage stability testing of a transgene in a recombinant virus","in vivo tumour volume and survival monitoring in tumour-bearing mice"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Tiered outreach designed per audience rather than one talk repeated: young children (storybooks, five published as PDFs), special-needs children and groups with intellectual disabilities, university students, and elderly communities, including a graded calisthenics set with a basic and an advanced version so seniors of different fitness levels can use it. Formats span hands-on experiments, physical teaching aids and salons.","ihp":"Patient, clinician and expert interview transcripts were analysed alongside a public questionnaire on understanding of cold versus hot tumours and a review of previous iGEM human-practices cases, organised through their HOPES closed-loop framework. Safety input came from named virologists, including Qiu Yang, a researcher at the Wuhan Institute of Virology, Chinese Academy of Sciences, who works on viral vector safety evaluation and animal model assessment, with multiple rounds of interviews on virology and animal experimentation feeding the risk-assessment design.","realWorld":"There is no venture here and the team does not pretend otherwise, so the instructive material is the part and the safety practice. On reusability, Neo-IL-2 is one of the better-engineered iGEM parts because the characterisation is layered rather than single-assay: SDS-PAGE for expression, qPCR and ELISA for transcript and protein, SPR for direct receptor binding, a Treg selective-activation assay and a T-cell activation assay for the functional claim that actually matters, RTCA for real-time cytotoxicity, and crucially a stability test of Neo-IL-2 expression after high-passage propagation of the recombinant virus, which is the test that tells a downstream user whether the part survives in a working vector. They also state the reuse envelope explicitly and in vector-agnostic terms: the coding sequence is intended for any context needing selective CD8 T-cell and NK activation without Treg expansion, and they name oncolytic viruses, mRNA-LNP and chassis strains as delivery platforms it can move into. Eight new parts were built (six basic, two composite), two existing parts reused, and functional annotations and characterisation descriptions on the Registry entries were deliberately expanded, with a named Part Leader owning the documentation. That combination, a design rationale, a computational prediction, an orthogonal physical measurement of the predicted property, a functional assay of the intended benefit, and a passage-stability result, is what makes a part genuinely inheritable rather than merely registered. On safety, the standout is institutional rather than technical: HBUT initiated and led a five-school joint biosafety manual for anti-tumour synthetic-biology projects with four other university iGEM teams (ZJU-China, BNU-China, JLU-FBH and ZJUT-China), covering oncolytic-virus modification operating standards, GMO leakage hazards and waste-disposal guidance, published as a downloadable PDF and explicitly designed with internally unified but differentiable risk-assessment protocols, since the five teams use different carriers. Their reasoning for doing it is the honest one: an individual iGEM team is limited in research vision, experimental conditions and risk-assessment competence, so cross-team safety communication is how those limits get overcome. Safety is also built into the construct rather than bolted on, with ICP34.5 deleted to cut neurovirulence and improve tumour selectivity and ICP47 deleted to restore antigen presentation, and they state plainly that genetic attenuation cannot eliminate risk entirely because viruses are inherently infectious. Wet-lab practice is documented at BSL-2 with risk assessment, PPE, waste handling and training, photographed down to biosafety-cabinet operation, eyewash stations and fridge labelling. The blunt limitations are theirs: the project is explicitly still in progress, systematic toxicity assessment requires expansion to multiple animal models, and the AI protein-screening system needs further experimental iteration.","partners":["Qiu Yang, Wuhan Institute of Virology, Chinese Academy of Sciences (viral vector safety evaluation and animal models)","ZJU-China, BNU-China, JLU-FBH and ZJUT-China iGEM teams (five-school joint biosafety manual for anti-tumour synthetic biology)","Clinicians and patients interviewed on MSS colorectal cancer treatment options"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6330/wiki/safety/wiki/safety/review-20261019/d-shield-framework.webp","caption":"The SHIELD safety framework, consolidating safety-by-design, wet-lab governance, hardware infrastructure, emergency response, training and outreach into one reusable full-chain paradigm","credit":"Team HBUT-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6330/wiki/description/description-figure-6-hd.avif","caption":"Construction of oHSV2-Neo-IL-2: homologous recombination replaces the CMV-GFP cassette at the gamma-34.5 locus of the ICP34.5-/ICP47- HG52 backbone with CMV-Neo-IL-2 and a BGH poly(A) signal","credit":"Team HBUT-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6330/wiki/safety/icp47-antigen-presentation-20261021.avif","caption":"Rationale for the ICP47 deletion: relieving TAP inhibition restores MHC class I antigen presentation, a safety and efficacy choice made at the design stage","credit":"Team HBUT-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6330/wiki/safety/wiki/safety/review-20261019/i-bsc-front.webp","caption":"Documented BSL-2 practice for oncolytic HSV-2 work, photographed as part of the SHIELD infrastructure-assurance module","credit":"Team HBUT-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"For any part GEMS wants other groups to reuse, publish the five-layer evidence stack HBUT used for Neo-IL-2: design rationale, computational prediction of the specific property changed, an orthogonal physical measurement of that property (SPR, not just docking), a functional assay of the intended benefit and of the harm avoided, and a stability result after many passages in the working vector. Separately, copy the five-school joint biosafety manual: co-author a shared risk-assessment document with other groups working on the same hazard class, since one lab's risk-assessment competence is narrower than five labs'.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/hbut-china/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hbut-china/parts","https://2026.igem.wiki/hbut-china/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/hbut-china/safety","https://2026.igem.wiki/hbut-china/assets/index-B5AKokKr.js","https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6330/wiki/education/pdf/education-biosafety-manual-v1.pdf"],"rank":52},"6337":{"team":"NJU-China","id":"6337","section":"Undergrad","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/nju-china/","projectTitle":"Starase Atlas — Atlas-BRIDGE, Atlas-COMPASS and Atlas-EDGE for enzyme discovery","tagline":"Given a target reaction and limited experimental resources, which enzyme candidates should a researcher test first?","summary":"NJU-China built a three-part platform around one decision: which enzyme to test next. Atlas-BRIDGE (Broad Retrieval with Inference-Driven Gated Experts) is a dual-tower contrastive retrieval model that will rank any protein it can encode, then lets specialist 'expert' models and two kinds of memory nudge that ranking only where their evidence genuinely applies; Atlas-COMPASS is a natural-language agent front end that resolves entities before it computes anything; Atlas-EDGE is a MySQL/graph knowledge base of compound nodes and enzyme edges built from UniProt, Rhea and ChEBI. The model's recommendation was then taken to the bench: M5AW86 was predicted and confirmed to convert FPP to beta-farnesene by GC-MS, TLC and 1H NMR against empty-vector controls. It won Best Software & AI Project and was nominated for Best Model.","awards":["Best Model — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Software & AI Project — Winner"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Atlas-BRIDGE is a machine-learning information-retrieval model, not a kinetic one, and its central design idea is worth copying regardless of domain: separate *eligibility to be ranked* from *availability of evidence*. The base model ('Broad') is a two-tower encoder — one tower for protein sequence, one for reaction transformation — trained with a multi-positive contrastive objective that respects the many-to-many nature of enzyme data, L_MP = lambda*L_R2E + (1-lambda)*L_E2R, where each directional loss sums over the full set of known positives rather than treating a single pair as the truth. Because an unrecorded enzyme-reaction pair is not a true negative, they apply positive-unlabeled (PU) learning plus sequence-cluster masking to decide which pairs are even admitted for contrast, and because experimental screening only tests the top of a list they add an explicit head-ranking hinge, L_head = softplus(n_K - p* + m), pushing the best positive above the K-th admissible negative, with hard negatives mined from the candidates the current model confuses most. The final score is additive and auditable: S = S_Broad + alpha_LT*Delta_LT + alpha_epi*Delta_epi + sum_k g_k*Delta_k. The Gated Experts are plug-in models carrying functional, structural/mechanistic or family/domain evidence; each must publish candidate-wise scores *and an availability mask*, has its applicability gate, normalisation and maximum correction magnitude locked on separate validation data before any external test, and reverts exactly to the prior ranking wherever its evidence is missing — so absent data is never silently read as a low score. Long-term memory replays the training-cutoff catalytic graph at inference, projecting 16 annotated protein neighbours and 8 annotated reaction neighbours back into the Broad space with query-conditioned permission weights fitted on 5,216 annotated development associations, and it only re-sorts the top 1,000 Broad candidates. Episodic memory handles positives that appear *after* the training cutoff (new curation, new assays, a collaborator's private hit) without retraining anything: each support is encoded in the frozen Broad space and combined by parameter-free attention, a_i = softmax(zscore(q^T s_i)), m_epi = sum a_i s_i, with authority scaled by support count, internal coherence and conflict with the baseline; positives already in the training graph are stripped out first to prevent double-counting with long-term memory. Atlas-COMPASS wraps this in a DeepSeek-API-driven agent that first resolves every reaction, protein and compound in a plain-language question to a Rhea / UniProt / ChEBI record and shows a confirmation card the user must approve before anything is computed, then plans the retrieval, and can additionally run thermodynamic Max-min Driving Force analysis and E. coli iML1515 genome-scale flux checks on candidate pathways when asked.","dataviz":"The visual argument is carried by the evaluation figures rather than by decoration. Benchmark comparisons are plotted as grouped MRR / Hit@10 / Hit@20 bars against EnzymeCAGE on two external test sets, with the harder Orphan-335 set shown alongside Enzyme-405 so the reader sees where the gain is largest. The four-configuration study is drawn as a controlled 2x2 (reference, coverage-only, ranker-only, complete system) in both retrieval directions, so the figure itself separates 'we found more candidates' from 'we ranked them better'. Ablation panels remove one evidence block at a time in both directions. Seed-count sensitivity is shown both as performance-versus-number-of-positive-seeds line plots under two evaluation protocols (random-positive and the much stricter protein-cluster-cold) and as grouped Hit@3/10/20 bars for one, two and three seeds. The model page also renders the architecture itself — dual-tower geometry, anchored reranking that visibly protects the base order, and query-level gating of each expert — as labelled schematics, and the five development cycles are laid out as a descending staircase so the reader walks the DBTL history. Atlas-EDGE's own interface is the other half of the dataviz: a hand-built SVG graph in which compounds are nodes and enzymes are directional edges, with composite edges that collapse multiple enzymes between two compounds and expand on click, click-through compound and enzyme info cards, zoom, drag, filtering, path highlighting and URL-synced view state.","datascience":"Evaluation is the strongest part of this project and is unusually self-sceptical. External benchmarking used the EnzymeCAGE authors' own test sets under their protocol: 21,505 training-unseen positive relationships ranked over the full encodable universe of 185,918 protein candidates (11,081 reaction candidates in the reverse direction). Reported gains: Enzyme-405 MRR +16.0% and Hit@10 +4.55pp; Orphan-335 MRR +44.0%, Hit@10 +17.32pp, Hit@20 +18.51pp. Four ablation studies follow, including a difficulty-balanced re-aggregation that freezes every prediction, candidate set and rank and changes *only* the averaging — giving equal weight to seen, protein-cold, reaction-cold and double-cold exposure classes and then to the graph-degree strata within each — explicitly to stop frequent, highly connected, easy relations dominating a micro-average. Domain experts were tested only on queries where they are applicable, with deterministic family held-out splits for P450 and phosphatase and a frozen semantic applicability gate selecting 18 of 1,042 strict double-cold queries for terpene synthases; gains were P450 MRR 0.0394 to 0.0503, phosphatase 0.3012 to 0.3077, TPS 0.1225 to 0.3114 with Hit@10 11.11% to 33.33%, candidate sets and core scores held fixed. Wet-lab closure: M5AW86 was recommended for FPP to beta-farnesene and confirmed by a converging evidence chain (differential GC-MS peak at ~5.5 min with base peak m/z 69, fragments at 41/81/93/107/121/135 and a low-abundance molecular ion at m/z 204; TLC spots absent from empty-vector controls; 1H NMR olefinic signals at delta 6.3-6.4 and 5.0-5.3 ppm matched to a literature reference). They also publish a disconfirmation: for D9XD61 the model predicted (+)-T-muurolol but the isolated product was identified as 7-epi-alpha-eudesmol, and they say so. Preliminary GC-MS hit rate was 7 of 14 recommended candidates (50%). The interface discipline matches: the 0-100 displayed model score is explicitly documented as 'not a catalytic success rate', not activity or yield, not comparable across retrieval routes, and a high rank means 'deserves priority verification, not that it has been biologically proven'; 'unknown' in a compatibility cell means missing records, not incompatibility.","software":"Both instruments are Apache 2.0 open source in the official iGEM GitLab repository, deployable with git clone plus bash scripts/bootstrap.sh, setup_release.sh --download and --check, then manage.sh configure-key / start / status. Linux with Python 3.12 is the validated environment, ~5 GiB for model assets, WSL2 for Windows, macOS explicitly flagged as not validated — and crucially no GPU is required, since validation and inference run on CPU. The DeepSeek API key is stored in a git-ignored runtime directory and the docs tell deployers to put the service behind HTTPS with access control, rate limiting, log monitoring and API quotas, and to explain how external model services handle data. Atlas-EDGE is a full production stack: React + TypeScript + Vite front end (hand-drawn SVG graph, History API URL sync, localStorage session persistence, AbortController to cancel stale searches), FastAPI + Uvicorn + Pydantic + async SQLAlchemy/aiomysql backend on a /api/v1 prefix, MySQL 8.0.46, a four-round UniProt REST crawl plus Rhea SPARQL and ChEBI flat files, pandas/RDKit ETL into entity and association tables with a unified sha1-keyed search index, local NCBI BLAST+ (blastp/makeblastdb, run in a thread with a mutex guarding database construction and an sha1 cache key), Ketcher for draw-a-molecule structure search, and DeepSolNet run locally with original weights to generate per-protein solubility scores used as a search filter.","stack":["Python 3.11 / 3.12","PyTorch (dual-tower encoders)","FastAPI","Uvicorn","Pydantic","SQLAlchemy asyncio + aiomysql","MySQL 8.0.46","React + TypeScript + Vite","pandas","RDKit","NCBI BLAST+","Ketcher","DeepSolNet","DeepSeek API","UniProt REST","Rhea SPARQL","ChEBI flat files","Pfam","cobrapy / iML1515 genome-scale model","scikit-learn / random forest / gradient boosting (experts)"],"techniques":["dual-tower contrastive retrieval","multi-positive InfoNCE-style loss","positive-unlabeled learning","sequence-cluster negative masking","hard-negative mining","listwise head-ranking hinge loss","mixture-of-experts gating with availability masks","retrieval-augmented long-term graph memory","parameter-free attention episodic memory (few-shot, training-free update)","protein language model embeddings","differential reaction fingerprints (DRFP)","learning-to-rank (LambdaMART lineage)","ablation studies","cold-start / double-cold stratified evaluation","difficulty-balanced metric re-aggregation","MRR and Hit@K ranking metrics","graph database modelling","pathway search over a directed multigraph","Max-min Driving Force thermodynamic analysis","genome-scale flux balance analysis (iML1515)","natural-language agent with entity grounding"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Nine primary-school lessons from March to July 2026 (five plant lessons, four summer science lessons), each treated as its own Design-Build-Test-Learn unit: Design fixed audience and objectives, Build made slides and materials, Test watched what pupils actually explained and where they needed help, Learn turned the observed problems into changes to the next lesson. From that they distilled SPARK as a reusable design and review lens — See, Probe, Ask, Record and Respond, Keep improving — and then applied it back onto their secondary-school intro and lab teaching and their public science conversations at Starlight Market. The handover is concrete: slides, activity materials, a lesson design checklist, guidelines for experimental and simulation activities, a feedback and evaluation form, and 'SPARK-Edu Skill', an AI-assisted guide that encodes their principles, workflow and examples so a future education team can adapt rather than restart.","ihp":"Human Practices is presented as evidence that changed the build, with a counted audit trail: 24 evidence records, 6 stakeholder lenses, 4 design shifts, 3 intended influence pathways, across academic (8), iGEM and user (4), industry (5), technology transfer (3), safety (2) and education contacts. The four shifts are stated as before/after pairs: from a black-box compatibility score to explicit experimental prioritisation; from searching known pairs to open exploration with uncertainty; from ranked names only to explainable recommendations; from a post-hoc warning to responsibility by design. The origin is traceable: in November 2025 Jing Shi pointed out that a promising enzyme record may behave differently in a new host, Fei Zhou described the preparatory work caused by scattered information, and Long Wang warned that sequence similarity is not function — which is why the platform separates recorded associations (the factual layer) from model candidates (the prediction layer) in every view. The team also took on the dual-use question directly: if an AI tool makes finding functional enzymes easier, which questions should it decline to answer lightly, how should high-risk queries be handled, and what may private data be used for.","realWorld":"The entrepreneurship case is for a screening *service* rather than another database: computational screening carried through to wet-lab validation so the customer receives a confirmed candidate, with the pipeline and its documentation left behind as a reusable toolkit and the methods and data kept public. Numbers are stated with their baselines: enzyme-to-reaction accuracy 15.32% (up from 8.47% in the team's own historical runs), a 1.92x top-20 hit rate against CLIPZyme (15.97% vs 8.33%) over 166,202 benchmark candidates, a 50% preliminary GC-MS hit rate (7 of 14), an estimated core enterprise TAM of RMB 14.42M annually in the baseline forecast, and a proposed tiered price range of RMB 4.3k to 319.5k per year from Academic to Enterprise Advanced. They are candid that the current demo only accepts target reactions and candidate proteins and returns rankings, with traceability, version management and full decision support still to come. The stated audiences are research labs (inspectable enzyme discovery), the iGEM community (reflective HP practice) and the bio-manufacturing ecosystem (governed, compatible pilots).","partners":["Nanjing University School of Life Sciences","Nanjing University School of Intelligence Science and Technology","Nanjing University School of Chemistry and Chemical Engineering","Nanjing University School of Software","Vazyme","WuXi","BioSphere"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6337/wiki/model/model.avif","caption":"Atlas-BRIDGE architecture: a shared dual-tower retrieval geometry that will score any encodable protein or reaction, with query-level gated experts and dual (long-term graph plus episodic) memory applying additive corrections only inside their valid scope.","credit":"Team NJU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6337/wiki/model/7.avif","caption":"The Broad Retrieval dual-tower architecture for bidirectional enzyme-reaction ranking: one tower encodes protein sequence, the other the reaction transformation, trained with a multi-positive contrastive loss plus a head-ranking constraint so the top of the list — the part experiments actually test — is sharpened.","credit":"Team NJU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6337/wiki/model/seed-performance-lines-v2.avif","caption":"Performance as a function of the number of positive seeds, plotted under two evaluation protocols — random-positive and the much stricter protein-cluster-cold — so the reader can see how much of the apparent gain survives when close homologs of the known positives are withheld.","credit":"Team NJU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6337/wiki/model/9.avif","caption":"Query-level gating of the functional, structural/mechanistic, family/domain and memory experts. Each expert must emit an availability mask as well as scores, and reverts exactly to the prior ranking wherever its evidence is missing, so absent data is never read as a low score.","credit":"Team NJU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Make every model output carry an availability mask, so 'we have no evidence about this candidate' and 'this candidate scores badly' are never the same number — and separate the factual layer (what a database records) from the prediction layer (what your model guesses) in every table and figure you publish. Then re-aggregate your headline metric with equal weight across difficulty strata to check your result is not just the easy cases.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/nju-china/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nju-china/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nju-china/software/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nju-china/compass/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nju-china/edge/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nju-china/proof/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nju-china/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nju-china/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nju-china/education/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nju-china/entrepreneurship/"],"rank":33},"6338":{"team":"ASIJ-Tokyo","id":"6338","section":"High School","country":"Japan","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/asij-tokyo/","projectTitle":"Project 茶(Sa)kure-it-all","tagline":"Yeast cocultures that produce four plant specialized metabolites from sakura and tea - sakuranetin, quercetin, EGCG and L-theanine - without the plant","summary":"ASIJ-Tokyo engineered Saccharomyces cerevisiae to make four plant specialized metabolites tied to Japanese culture: sakuranetin, quercetin, EGCG and L-theanine. Rather than one overloaded strain, they split pathways across cocultured strains at optimised ratios (7:3 for sakuranetin and quercetin, 5:3:2 for the three-strain EGCG system), with every enzyme cassette behind a GAL promoter and a constitutive pTEF1 fluorescent reporter so strain ratios can be verified before induction. Their education portfolio is unusually broad for a high-school team and explicitly gap-driven: each activity was created to fill a named gap they had identified. They contributed 34 new parts, a no-HPLC semi-quantitative screening workflow and a low-cost DIY bioreactor with full build instructions, all aimed at other resource-limited high-school teams.","awards":["Best Part Collection — Nominee (High School)","Best Education — Nominee (High School)","Best Village Project — Nominee (Space / Foundational Advance / Software & AI / Biomanufacturing)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Stakeholder analysis structured into three domains (agricultural supply, health and consumer needs, production and commercial viability); Duke iGEM's Risk and Research Ethics Assessment tool used as an external bioethics compliance check.","dataviz":"Stakeholder map figure grouping identified issues and stakeholders into the three domains; coculture architecture diagrams.","datascience":"A semi-quantitative screening workflow designed specifically for teams without HPLC access, published as a contribution. In-silico modelling of a proposed active-transport system was explored with guidance from a Johns Hopkins biomedical engineering student, then explicitly abandoned because without HPLC the team could not measure intra- versus extracellular compound concentrations to validate it - a documented negative result.","software":"Village 茶(Sa)kura: a free Animal Crossing-style educational game built in Unity and coded in C# over two years with the Japanese technology entertainment company ABAL Inc. Players receive villager requests (for example 'bring me anti-inflammatory sakura cream'), scavenge ingredients in the Sakura Forest, read recipes at crafting stations, synthesise items in in-game labs and return them, with up to 10 encoded pathways; published free on itch.io with a game manual. Also a memory card game, a 'What is?' YouTube explainer series, and The Catalyst: Science & Curiosity, a student science news/publication website.","stack":["Unity Engine","C#","itch.io distribution","YouTube","web publishing platform (The Catalyst)","HPLC (via International Christian University)"],"techniques":["yeast coculture at optimised strain ratios","dual-plasmid selection (pRS316/URA3 + pRS315/LEU2 on SC -Ura -Leu dropout)","GAL-inducible enzyme cassettes","pTEF1 constitutive fluorescent reporter for ratio verification","modular pathway splitting across strains","DIY low-cost bioreactor build","CRISPR-Cas9 teaching lab","agarose gel electrophoresis","strawberry and banana DNA extraction"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"ASIJ-Tokyo opened its education work with a diagnostic question - who is not yet part of the synthetic biology conversation - and then built one artefact per identified gap, which makes the portfolio unusually legible. Gap: low public awareness of sakura's health properties, addressed by an Earth Day booth (22 April 2025 and 2026) where elementary, middle and high school students painted flower pots and took home sakura seeds while being briefed on anti-inflammatory and antioxidant properties, reaching 70+ participants each year, plus a Sakura & Matcha Goodies recipe book whose recipes each carry a 'the science behind' blurb. Gap: almost no synthetic biology video content pitched at high school level, addressed by a 'What is?' YouTube series running since 2023 covering bioethics, cellular transport, yeast in synthetic biology, metabolic engineering, genetic switches, cocultures, biosensors and cellular fluorescence, deliberately sequenced so concepts build on each other. Gap: little attention to memory degradation in Japan's ageing population, addressed by a memory card game run at a senior home on 13 October 2026, using six cards depicting cluttered domestic interiors with recall questions (colour of the couch, number of pencils) across repeated rounds individually and in groups of 2-3; the team was scrupulous about its limits, stating plainly that this was a small pilot and not a clinical study, and left the game with the facility and its nurses as a low-pressure cognitive exercise. Gap: no easy way for teachers outside iGEM or biology to run these activities, addressed by a free downloadable workbook of seven tested lesson plans covering DNA, natural pigment, cell modelling, chromatography, biomaterials and polymer creation, refined so that the labs connect into a holistic overview, plus The Catalyst: Science & Curiosity, a newspaper-style website that also acts as a publication platform where any secondary school student can publish science writing from 300-word pieces to 20-page experimental reports. The flagship format is Village 茶(Sa)kura, an Animal Crossing-style Unity/C# game co-developed over two years with ABAL Inc., a Japanese technology entertainment company, iterated against industry-expert feedback and published free on itch.io with a manual. Direct teaching reached a wide spread of ages: a four-year-running CRISPR-Cas9 and gel electrophoresis lab for 8th graders built into their sickle cell anaemia unit (13-14 May 2025 and 12-13 May 2026, including why researchers target the BCL11A enhancer rather than the mutation itself); DNA extraction workshops for over 30 students at Tokyo Bay International School and Montessori School Tokyo in Azabu (31 March and 22 July 2026); the same experiment with bananas for 80+ children aged 5-10 daily at the school's Summer Day Camp, deliberately reaching local and non-international-school children; a 60+ child booth with leaf-rubbing and plant-engineering discussion at Aoyama Gakuin's Global Day (21 October 2025), tied to the UN SDGs and to English-language learning; a Winterfest campus-wide CSI escape-room-style DNA mystery (4 December 2025) with three stations - DNA matching to eliminate suspects, leaf-morphology comparison to locate the crime scene, and gel electrophoresis to identify the culprit; a Community Health Fair obstacle-course race (11 April 2025) where participants acted as skin cells carrying sakuranetin past crawl-space 'constricted blood vessels' and hurdle 'blockages' on a two-minute timer; and Back to School Night in 2025 and 2026, the 2026 edition adding a hands-on flower pipetting activity and recipe-book matcha cookies for 100+ parents, students and teachers. Evidence of iteration is explicit and honest: PCR was cut from the 8th grade lab because crucial steps ran out of time, lesson plans were reworked so activities connect, pipetting was added to Back to School Night, and the team states openly that it did not systematically record feedback this year and therefore added a feedback page to the workbook so teachers who use it can report back. Collaboration was a deliberate education strategy in its own right: activities were created or joined with eight teams across eight countries (Duke, Maastricht, Manipal, Concordia, Ruhr University Bochum, St Stephen's College Hong Kong, Patras, KCIS Xiugang) plus the iGEM Community Blackboard - contributing a scent to Manipal's Scents of the World, an abstract to Maastricht's peer-reviewed MSP Vector journal, a Pokemon-style card to RUBochum's Trading Card Project, a Japanese translation of HKSSC's food-waste comic, and both of their games to Patras's downloadable game gallery.","ihp":"Four stakeholder engagements reshaped the project, each with a recorded design consequence. Tea producer Masahiro Okutomi of Sayama-cha Okutomien (10 April 2026) explained that overseas matcha orders have risen sharply while new tea plants take at least five years to mature and processing equipment three years to arrive, and that L-theanine is what gives matcha much of its quality - so extracting it from leaves for supplements would leave farmers with a degraded product. This directly strengthened the decision to produce L-theanine in yeast rather than extract it, and reframed the team's positioning from replacement to 'an extra source that works beside farms'. He also noted Japanese companies market catechins like EGCG while consumers do not know what L-theanine does, which changed the team's communication plan to explain each compound separately starting with L-theanine. Yukari Kawahito of Sakura Science Beauty (May 2026) introduced transdermal patches as a delivery format the team had not considered and opened a second business route of selling compounds to companies with existing formulation capability. Vikki Adams (Johns Hopkins) advised on an in-silico active-transport model that was ultimately dropped for lack of HPLC validation. A visit to the six-generation family-run Maruichi Mizuno Tea Farm in Shizuoka (16 June 2026) showed how the farm covers plants with sheets, harvests three times a year, processes its own hojicha and sencha and is now seeking matcha manufacturers to benefit from the boom - confirming producers already market L-theanine and EGCG benefits while demand for fermentation-derived ingredients remains untested. The visit was filmed as a vlog.","realWorld":"The project's framing is a supply constraint, not a novelty: sakura-flavoured products appear across Japanese supermarkets every spring and vanish by May because the raw material does, sakuranetin being bound to one of the shortest harvest windows in agriculture, while tea faces the opposite problem of a demand boom farms cannot meet. Contributions were deliberately designed for resource-limited high-school teams: a reusable coculture architecture where a future team can keep Strain N unchanged and only build its own downstream strain, 34 new Registry parts, a semi-quantitative screening workflow usable without HPLC, and a low-cost DIY bioreactor with full build instructions. The team hosted six students from St Mary's International School to build a biosensor, gained HPLC access through a bioanalytical chemistry professor at International Christian University, and will give an opening keynote alongside university professors at ASIJ's first semi-annual science fair on 14 November 2026 to roughly 100 students and teachers.","partners":["ABAL Inc. (Japanese technology entertainment company, two-year Unity game co-development)","Tokyo Bay International School","Montessori School Tokyo, Azabu","Aoyama Gakuin (Global Day)","International Christian University (bioanalytical chemistry professor, HPLC access)","St Mary's International School","Recolle Team Hayate (STEM Racing student team)","Sayama-cha Okutomien (tea producer Masahiro Okutomi)","Sakura Science Beauty (Yukari Kawahito)","Maruichi Mizuno Tea Farm, Shizuoka","Johns Hopkins University (Vikki Adams)","itch.io (game distribution)","Japan iGEM meet-up at Hiroo Gakuen (UTokyo, TUS, Waseda, Keio, Oakridge, HG)","iGEM teams: Duke, Maastricht, Manipal, Concordia, RUBochum, HKSSC, Patras, KCIS Xiugang"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6338/wiki/education/crafting-screenshot.avif","caption":"A crafting station in Village 茶(Sa)kura, the free Unity/C# synthetic biology game built with ABAL Inc. and published on itch.io","credit":"Team ASIJ-Tokyo, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6338/wiki/education/seniorhouse.avif","caption":"Running the six-card memory game with residents at a senior home, 13 October 2026","credit":"Team ASIJ-Tokyo, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6338/wiki/education/winterfest-igem.avif","caption":"The campus-wide CSI-themed DNA mystery stations at Winterfest, 4 December 2025","credit":"Team ASIJ-Tokyo, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6338/wiki/education/igem-backtoschool-2-1.avif","caption":"Back to School Night 2026: hands-on flower pipetting activity for 100+ parents, students and teachers","credit":"Team ASIJ-Tokyo, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6338/wiki/education/booth2.avif","caption":"The Earth Day booth, where 70+ students painted sakura flower pots and took home seeds","credit":"Team ASIJ-Tokyo, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6338/wiki/education/youtube-ss.avif","caption":"The 'What is?' YouTube explainer series, built to fill the gap in synthetic biology video pitched at high school level","credit":"Team ASIJ-Tokyo, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Start from a written list of named gaps (which audience, which missing resource) and build exactly one artefact per gap, then package the reusable ones - a seven-lesson tested workbook with a built-in feedback page, a free game, a sequenced video series - so teachers outside synthetic biology can run them without you.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/asij-tokyo/","https://2026.igem.wiki/asij-tokyo/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/asij-tokyo/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/asij-tokyo/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/asij-tokyo/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/asij-tokyo/entrepreneurship"],"rank":21},"6339":{"team":"Muenster-University","id":"6339","section":"Overgrad","country":"Germany","village":"Agriculture","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/muenster-university/","projectTitle":"P.A.C. Immunity","tagline":"A modular platform that retrofits native plant immune sensors so a crop detects a pathogen's own protease directly and triggers an instant immune response.","summary":"P.A.C. Immunity rewires plant immunity instead of breeding for it. A plant NLR immune receptor is held inactive by a synthetic blocker peptide containing a protease cleavage site; when a pathogen secretes its effector protease into the host cell - a step many viruses, bacteria, fungi and nematodes cannot skip - the protease cleaves the blocker, the NLR fires, and the plant mounts a hypersensitive response. Because only the cleavage site changes between pathogens, swapping one short sequence retargets the whole system, which is the modularity argument: classical resistance breeding takes years and pathogens overcome new resistances quickly. The bottleneck they hit is that almost no pathogen protease has a known cleavage motif, so the dry lab built ProTEUS (Protease Target Elucidation Using Structural Modeling), a de-novo-binder-style pipeline chaining AlphaFold3, RFdiffusion3 and LigandMPNN with a mechanistically grounded geometric scoring function to generate candidate cleavage peptides for proteases with no characterised substrates at all.","awards":["Top 10 (Overgrad)","Best New Composite Part — Winner (Overgrad)","Best Presentation — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Wiki — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Agriculture Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"ProTEUS repurposes the de novo mini-binder design stack for an unsolved problem - predicting cleavage sites for proteases whose substrates are unknown - which existing tools (PROSPER, PROSPERous, Procleave, iProt-Sub) cannot do, since they only predict where a given substrate is cut by a protease with 30 or more already-described sites. The pipeline, named as machines on the wiki: AlphaFold3 predicts the target protease structure (AF3 machine I), since no crystal structure existed for any of RipT, RipE1, RipBN or HopN1; the structure is inspected in ChimeraX and aligned by Matchmaker against papain (PDB 9PAP) and other characterised proteases to derive catalytic triads and specificity residues, whose solvent-exposed atoms become hotspot constraints (scanner); RFdiffusion3 generates 5,000 binder backbones per target (1,000 batches of 5) with atom-level rather than residue-level hotspot conditioning and 'is_non_loopy' set to false so no helical bias blocks accessible peptides, with gamma_0 raised from 0.2 to 0.6 to reduce duplicate sequences (RFD3 machine); a Python filter rejects backbones closer than 1.7 A to the protease or farther than 8.0 A from the catalytic centre, with target-specific pass rates of 94.2% for HopN1, 51.1% for RipE1, 48.1% for RipT and 12.3% for RipBN, which they attribute to differences in pocket depth and hotspot geometry (cannon I); LigandMPNN (checkpoint ligandmpnn_v_32_010_25, seed 111, sampling temperature raised to 0.3 from 0.1 for short-sequence diversity) designs 6-10 sequences per backbone with sidechain conformations (MPNN machine); AlphaFold3 re-folds each unique designed sequence in complex with the target protease (AF3 machine II); and a Python scoring script extracts binding geometry and ranks with selected weights (cannon 2), handing the top 100 per protease to wet-lab screening (portal). Everything ran on the PALMA II HPC cluster at Munster - RFdiffusion3 on an RTX 4090 (24 GB) node at about 14 h per protease, LigandMPNN on 8 CPU cores at about 10 h, AlphaFold3 on an A100 (40 GB). Confidence handling is deliberate: they analysed pLDDT and minimum binder-target PAE rather than pTM/ipTM, which have been reported as weaker predictors for protein-peptide interactions, found mean binder pLDDT of 39.73-49.00 across the four targets, and chose explicitly not to filter hard on confidence (a pLDDT > 80 cut would keep only a handful; a pLDDT > 50 intermediate filter changed nothing in the final 100 after structural assessment), reasoning that badly predicted designs would fail the geometric assessment anyway.","dataviz":"The wiki is a single-page React application built as an explorable argument rather than a document. It opens with Gary, a farmer whose story carries the problem (30% of global yield losses to plant pathogens, pesticide treadmill, resistances overcome quickly) before any molecular biology appears, and that narrative thread was a direct result of human practices advice. The dry lab page presents the ProTEUS pipeline as a machine metaphor - scanner, RFD3 machine, cannon, MPNN machine, portal - with an animated workflow, and each of the four candidate proteases gets a card showing its AlphaFold3 prediction with per-residue pLDDT for each catalytic triad member and for the whole and core enzyme, plus the hotspot atoms chosen for diffusion. Quantitative figures include a pLDDT-versus-PAE hexbin density plot with the official AlphaFold confidence bands marked, before-and-after pLDDT bars showing what trimming disordered N-terminal secretion signals does to each protease's confidence (raising RipBN above 70), and side-by-side renders of a rejected design versus a kept one. An interactive 3Dmol viewer serves structures (including an AlphaFold3 resistosome model), Rive animations drive the cloning and engineering-cycle explanations, and inline tooltips expand every acronym. Education results are themselves visualised as radial comparison charts of pre- versus post-event survey answers.","datascience":"Their most transferable piece of work is converting enzymology into a scorable geometry, because no training data existed. Since their four targets have no known cleavage motifs, they could not fit a model; instead they derived scoring parameters from the catalytic mechanism of protein-nucleophile proteases - the nucleophile sulfur or oxygen within attack distance of the base nitrogen, the nucleophile-to-carbonyl-carbon distance, the hydrogen-bond distance from the oxyanion hole amide NH to the scissile carbonyl oxygen, the nucleophile's reactive rotamer (gauche- versus trans, which determines whether the oxyanion hole is formed by the nucleophilic residue's own amide NH or the one C-terminal to it), the near-universal angle between the nucleophile atoms and the base, and the nucleophilic attack angle, with the explicit correction that cysteine proteases take a different ideal attack angle than serine proteases because sulfur hybridises more weakly than oxygen. These were combined into a weighted score over AlphaFold3 complex geometry. They also engineered the cost down: profiling showed the jackhmmer MSA search accounted for over 86% of AlphaFold3 runtime, and because every binder in an iteration is co-folded with the same protease they cached the protease MSA and skipped MSA generation for the artificial peptides entirely (homologs of a designed peptide being meaningless), cutting time per prediction from about 13 minutes to 30 seconds and making a 5,000-30,000 prediction campaign feasible where the naive estimate was 45 to 270 days. Validation was retrospective: run on NIa-Pro, a protease with a known motif, the pipeline recovered the correct residues (E/P6, V/P4, Q/P1) among its top 100 candidates, and for the four uncharacterised proteases it pinpointed potentially important residues, with preliminary wet-lab signal for HopN1, RipBN and RipT that the team states needs a refined screening assay to confirm.","software":"ProTEUS is the team's software contribution, documented step by step on the model page with every tool version, checkpoint, seed, non-default parameter and HPC node specification stated - enough for another group to rebuild it - but no public repository link is given on the wiki. Their released artefact is instead the part collection on the iGEM Registry, which is where the Best New Composite Part came from: a modular toolkit for plant-immunity engineering comprising pathogen effector protease expression constructs (NIa-Pro from Potato Potyvirus Y with an N-terminal myc tag, plus AvrPphB, HopN1, RipT, RipE1 and RipBN from Pseudomonas syringae and Ralstonia with C-terminal myc tags), a blocker peptide that prevents NLR activity when fused to the N-terminus (experimentally demonstrated on autoactive AtNRG1.1 [D485V], BBa_26V5N8GY), graded series of protease cleavage sites for NIa-Pro, AvrRpt2 and AvrPphB with short, medium and asymmetric GS-linkers plus non-cleavable mutant negative controls, a FRET pair (mTurquoise / cpVenus173) for Nicotiana benthamiana, and synthetic BsaI, BsaI-with-internal-NdeI and PaqCI dropout segments designed so an insert can be swapped into a composite part by Golden Gate assembly - built specifically for pooled library cloning, which is what makes the collection modular 'for anyone to advance with standard cloning practices'.","stack":["AlphaFold3","RFdiffusion3","LigandMPNN / ProteinMPNN","ChimeraX (Matchmaker)","Python (filtering + geometric scoring)","jackhmmer (MSA, cached)","PALMA II HPC (NVIDIA RTX 4090, A100)","3Dmol.js","React + Vite (wiki)","Rive (animations)","iGEM Registry","Golden Gate / MoClo","Gibson assembly","Western blot and GFP degradation-tag reporter screening","Nicotiana benthamiana transient expression"],"techniques":["de novo binder design repurposed for protease substrate discovery","atom-level hotspot conditioning in structure diffusion","structural alignment to characterised homologs to locate catalytic triads without crystal structures","steric and distance filtering of backbone-only diffusion output","mechanism-derived geometric scoring in place of a trained model","reactive rotamer analysis to identify the active oxyanion hole","pLDDT and minimum binder-target PAE instead of pTM/ipTM for peptide complexes","disordered-terminus trimming before confidence assessment","MSA caching and MSA-free folding of synthetic peptides for throughput","retrospective validation on a protease with a known motif","screen-many-good-predictions rather than pick-the-best","GFP-cleavage-site-degradation-tag high-throughput plate screening","FRET-based cleavage readout in planta","Design-Build-Test-Learn cycles documented per module"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"The broadest and most systematically evaluated education programme of the five teams, and almost every activity was measured with pre- and post-activity questionnaires decided on in advance. Formats: a stand on the MS Wissenschaft science exhibition ship (a German federal research ministry project visiting 33 cities across Germany, Poland and Austria) during its Munster stop, drawing on roughly 5,000 weekend visitors, where people isolated DNA from bananas with household chemicals, built DNA double strands from 60+ gummy-bear model kits (deoxyribose, phosphate and four coloured bases) and translated their own codon to an amino acid on a take-home worksheet with a QR code back to the project; a workshop series at the LWL Museum of Natural History over the summer holidays bridging microscopic to macroscopic DNA, with agar-plate cultures cleared in writing with museum management and lab management, ending with participants designing their own Petri dishes, and follow-up feedback collected from parents rather than only participants; a protease workshop series for 8th and 9th grade school classes using digestive enzymes - ginger-juice proteases curdling milk at different temperatures, fruit juices degrading gelatine - iterated after anonymous participant feedback that the first round's instructions were 'a little hard to understand'; a bio pub quiz with the question rounds embedded in a narrative frame; 'Design Your Crop', a 3-6 player card game in which players become plant breeders guarding a hidden genome, built as a scalable substitute for events that only reach as many people as the team's time allows; a children's book featuring a farmer and a planned primary-school reading-plus-worksheet collaboration; a bioethics lecture analysing P.A.C. Immunity as a case study under the new EU NGT Directive; 'A Mosaic of Opinions', a dialogue event designed against the finding that consumer fear of gene editing in the food chain comes from campaigns plus shallow understanding; and a Fishbowl discussion in Nottuln co-organised with the Westphalia-Lippe Agricultural Association (WLV), with roughly two rounds pairing critical and supportive voices - fruit grower and pomology expert Hans-Joachim Bannier and Bioland farmers against Prof. Jochen Schmid (IMMB Munster) and the team - attended by regional farmers, Bioland farmers, association representatives, science students and the general public. They also hosted their own three-day conference, Junior Jam Munster, at the Munster castle, with expert talks, interactive workshops, poster sessions, a panel discussion and a session on iGEM judging criteria, and reported the meta-lesson from participant feedback that interactive workshops retain more than frontal ones and that Zoom talks land far weaker than in-person. The most durable piece is curricular: they developed a lesson concept on proteases for 8th and 9th grade biology, refined with teachers at a partner school and compliant with North Rhine-Westphalia's rules on genetic engineering experiments in schools; recognising that thermocyclers, electrophoresis chambers and photometers are not available in every school, they designed a lending experiment-kit concept, and they are working to shape teacher training through a university module in which master's students build and trial a lesson plan with invited school classes - aimed partly at the fifth Abitur examination subject with experimental assessment arriving in 2027-28.","ihp":"They state their principle as treating criticism as an ally and letting unanswered questions dictate which experts to approach next, and the chain is traceable. Prof. Dr. Dirk Prufer (Institute of Plant Biology and Biotechnology, Munster) validated the concept but said a project is only as strong as its ability to be explained, which is why the work up to that point - almost entirely experimental - was rebuilt around a narrative thread, and why they distilled their science communication learning into a reusable form. Public-trust interviews produced the framing that their biggest challenge is outside the lab, since without public trust there is no foundation for engineered crops in Europe. The bottleneck conversation is the most consequential: with no reliable way to identify protease cleavage motifs, they interviewed Prof. Dr. Kummel's working group and Lasse Middendorf, Michel Westermann and Michel Stevens, who told them that AlphaFold predicting a peptide in a pocket is not evidence it will be cleaved, advised a screen-many-good-predictions approach over seeking a single best prediction, recommended validating the pipeline on a protease with a known motif, and warned that AlphaFold would struggle with short peptides - all four of which became design decisions in ProTEUS, including the separate geometric scoring layer and the NIa-Pro retrospective validation. They advised against an alternative N-terminal-binding-domain NLR engineering route on feasibility grounds, which the team dropped. Verification strategy changed too: they settled on Western blotting with the cleavage site placed between two differently sized tagged proteins, and on co-infiltrating the NLR construct with the protease construct to guarantee both are expressed, judging the live-pathogen route better suited to stably transformed plants later. Industry contacts advised focusing on crops with higher production margins and identifying which chemical pesticides are likely to be restricted so the technology can be positioned as a replacement. An early farmer-focused interview changed the education strategy outright: they contacted the WLV agricultural association to reach farmers directly, and used the resulting discussion to extract farmers' specific requirements for genetic engineering, quoting farmers' own statements back as design references.","realWorld":"There is no entrepreneurship page; the real-world case is made through regulation, agronomic positioning and safety. The project is timed against the EU's new genomic techniques regulation: they tracked the European Parliament debate through the season, committed in advance to analysing the outcome's effect on their project, and published a bioethics case study assessing P.A.C. Immunity under the new NGT Directive alongside a risk analysis, noting that it remains to be seen how the rules play out in practice. Their market framing is agronomic rather than financial - pathogens cause roughly 30% of global yield losses, pesticide dependence carries economic and ecological costs, classical resistance breeding is slow and resistances are overcome quickly, so the selling point is a platform that updates by swapping one short cleavage sequence - and industry advice pushed them toward higher-margin crops and toward positioning against pesticides facing restriction. Safety is addressed as a staged transition: current work is under laboratory containment, and they state explicitly that moving toward pathogen-resistant crops in the field introduces a fundamentally different risk picture. The honest limitation is published as its own section: not all crop pathogens secrete proteases into host cells, so the platform is not universal, and ProTEUS is positioned as what would let P.A.C. Immunity expand from a few pathogens toward broad-spectrum use. The modular part collection on the Registry, plus the documented ProTEUS methodology, are the handover to whoever continues it.","partners":["Prof. Dr. Dirk Prufer, Institute of Plant Biology and Biotechnology, University of Munster","Prof. Dr. Kummel and working group, University of Munster (structural modelling)","Lasse Middendorf, Michel Westermann and Michel Stevens (modelling advisors)","Prof. Dr.-Ing. Jochen Schmid, Institute for Molecular Microbiology and Biotechnology (IMMB), University of Munster","Westphalia-Lippe Agricultural Association (WLV) - Stefan Wolfert, Michael Uckelmann, Tim Richter","Hans-Joachim Bannier (pomology expert, critical perspective)","Jorg Schulze Buschhoff (farmer)","Dr. Holger Ophoff (official oversight perspective)","LWL Museum of Natural History, Munster","MS Wissenschaft / German Federal Ministry of Research, Technology and Space","PALMA II HPC, University of Munster","Partner school and Biology Education Department, University of Munster","Junior Jam Munster participant teams; iGEM Dusseldorf Meetup; BFH"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6339/wiki/dry-lab/figures/fig3.avif","caption":"AlphaFold3 confidence for the four candidate effector proteases before and after excluding disordered N-terminal regions, averaged over 10 samples, with the share of each protein trimmed shown above each bar.","credit":"Team Muenster-University, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6339/wiki/dry-lab/figures/fig4.avif","caption":"The HopN1 protease with the hotspot atoms used to steer RFdiffusion3, shown as ribbon and surface, next to a rejected design filtered out by the Python geometry check and one kept for sequence design.","credit":"Team Muenster-University, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6339/wiki/education/cardgame/dsc9496-gro.avif","caption":"'Design Your Crop', the 3-6 player card game in which players become plant breeders guarding a hidden genome, built so the team's engagement could scale past events limited by their own time.","credit":"Team Muenster-University, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6339/wiki/education/fish-bowl-discussion/dsc05178.avif","caption":"The Fishbowl discussion in Nottuln, co-organised with the Westphalia-Lippe Agricultural Association, bringing regional farmers, Bioland farmers, association representatives and researchers into the same conversation about green genetic engineering.","credit":"Team Muenster-University, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Two things are directly portable. First, when no training data exists, derive a scoring function from the mechanism instead of waiting for a dataset: Munster turned textbook protease enzymology - nucleophile-to-base distance, oxyanion hole hydrogen bonds, reactive rotamer, nucleophilic attack angle, with the serine-versus-cysteine correction - into a weighted score over predicted structures, and validated it by recovering a known motif. Second, copy their education evaluation habit: decide before each event how you will check whether the learning objective was met, run a short pre- and post-questionnaire, and publish the result including what failed - and copy the curricular endgame, where a workshop becomes a lesson plan for local schools plus a lending kit for schools without thermocyclers, which is how one season's outreach keeps running after the team disbands.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/muenster-university/","https://2026.igem.wiki/muenster-university/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/muenster-university/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/muenster-university/results/","https://2026.igem.wiki/muenster-university/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/muenster-university/experiments/","https://2026.igem.wiki/muenster-university/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/muenster-university/education/","https://2026.igem.wiki/muenster-university/contribution/","https://2026.igem.wiki/muenster-university/safety-and-security/"],"rank":117},"6341":{"team":"KAUST-KSA","id":"6341","section":"Overgrad","country":"Saudi Arabia","village":"Space","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/kaust-ksa/","projectTitle":"SHIHAB","tagline":"SHIHAB (shooting star): resilient microbial chassis and a suitcase bioreactor for on-demand therapeutic protein manufacturing in space","summary":"Stocking an inventory of medicines for long-duration missions costs payload mass, so SHIHAB makes the medicine instead: a small library of lyophilised engineered microbes ('pills'), each producing a different nanobody, plus a compact automated bioreactor and purification train that an untrained astronaut can run. The wet lab integrated Dsup, the tardigrade damage-suppressor protein, genomically into three chassis (Bacillus subtilis, Saccharomyces cerevisiae, Pichia pastoris) and quantified radiation resistance against UV-C and X-ray doses with four complementary readouts, then expressed and purified a payload protein by HisTrap. The dry lab answered which host, what feedstock and when to induce using genome-scale metabolic models plus an ODE layer, and COMSOL CFD decided the rotor geometry for mixing under Mars, Moon and transit gravity. It won Best Hardware and Best Space Project; the whole platform was taken out of the lab and run on desert dunes to prove the 'anywhere' claim.","awards":["Top 10 (Overgrad)","Best Measurement — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Hardware — Winner (Overgrad)","Best Wiki — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Integrated Human Practices — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Space Project — Winner"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Flux balance analysis on three published genome-scale reconstructions (Yeast9 for S. cerevisiae, iBsu1147 for B. subtilis, iMS837 for Synechococcus elongatus PCC 7942, itself built on iJB792), plus a dynamic ODE layer integrated with scipy.integrate.solve_ivp (RK45) because FBA assumes steady state and cannot answer a timing question. Shared constraints are stated: glucose exchange 5, glycerol 0, oxygen 10 (aerobic) or 0 (anaerobic) mmol/gDW/h, nitrate capped at 10 for anaerobic Bacillus, habitat-analogue light at 145 mmol photons/gDW/h for the cyanobacterium, maximum nanobody flux computed with no growth requirement. The team repaired iBsu1147 by adding two reactions (NadB L-aspartate oxidase for de novo NAD+ synthesis and PyrD/PyrK dihydroorotate dehydrogenase for orotate), each justified with in-vitro literature evidence, because the published model failed without oxygen. Results: under oxygen restriction B. subtilis out-produces yeast roughly 3.4-fold on nanobody flux provided nitrate is supplied, and loses 46% of growth capacity against yeast's 82%; an engineered cyanobacterial supplier raises anaerobic yeast growth 13-fold (0.014 to 0.18 /h) once its sucrose export (0.81 mmol/gDW/h, tripled by capping the supplier's own growth) and oxygen (up to 4.2 mmol/gDW/h) are passed in as uptake bounds; the supplier is nitrogen-limited rather than carbon- or light-limited, and candidate gene knockouts do nothing. The ODE layer returns a closed-form optimal induction window of 6.5 to 7 h. Hardware modelling is COMSOL Multiphysics CFD comparing three rotor geometries for bubble fate, air distribution and vortex depth at 50-400 rpm across Earth, Mars, Moon and transit gravity.","dataviz":"The dry-lab page is an interactive model map: a scheme of the three chassis plus the cyanobacterial supplier where every label is a clickable result, and a 'TRY ME' prompt tells the reader to select a label to open that finding and jump to the section that develops it. Each result is also stated as a one-line claim before any plot ('Induction window: 6.5 to 7 h', 'Knockouts do nothing', 'Capping growth triples sucrose export'), with headline deltas as large-type stat tiles (3.4x, -46% vs -82%, 13x, 2 reactions). Table 1 is the most unusual piece of visualisation discipline on any of these wikis: for every link between models it states what is actually passed between them and labels the link Modeled, Identified or Assumed, so the reader can see exactly where the chain is evidence and where it is an assumption. The hardware page carries an animated 3D walkthrough of the purification sequence in its carry case, labelled 'illustrative flow, not measured data', and a live simulation of the bioreactor's touchscreen dashboard where the reader can drag the motor-speed dial and change temperature and pH setpoints. CFD results are shown as four-gravity comparison panels. All stat tiles and dashboards are reader-operable rather than screenshots.","datascience":"Measurement was designed as a framework rather than a set of assays: wild-type and Dsup-expressing B. subtilis, S. cerevisiae and P. pastoris were exposed to UV-C (0-30 mJ/cm2, and 0-300 J/m2 series) or X-rays (mock to 2000 Gy in 200 Gy steps) and read out four complementary ways (serial-dilution spot assay, OD600 time course, resazurin dye-reduction and FUN-1 staining), so a resistance claim has to survive four independent readouts rather than one. Three Dsup integration strains per host were compared against wild type and a nanobody control. On the engineering side the team derived a calibration mapping the analog voltage of a DFRobot SEN0189 turbidity sensor to NTU and then a linear OD600 = a(NTU) + b fit against reference spectrophotometer readings, following Fan et al. (2016) on Bacillus coagulans, which is what makes automatic IPTG induction at OD600 0.5 possible with no human in the loop. The modelling output is explicitly handed to the bench: a 'For the Wet Lab' box tells the experimenters where to start the co-culture and what growth cap to impose on the cyanobacteria.","software":"No standalone released application, but the code is published: ODE models and GEM notebooks are linked from the model page, and the whole wiki plus hardware design lives at gitlab.igem.org/2026/kaust-ksa under CC BY 4.0. The hardware itself is the deliverable and is documented for reproduction: an Arduino Mega control stack with a touchscreen dashboard in a compact enclosure, closed-loop temperature (DS18B20 probe to heating elements), pH (DANOPLUS KIB-87 probe with signal-conditioning board to acid/base dispensing) and OD (turbidity sensor to IPTG induction), hollow structural supports routing all wiring, a filtration unit with user-selectable stages of decreasing pore size in gasketed modules (Kapton, paper, Acrodisc), syringe-pump buffer handling and affinity chromatography, all released with a Hardware User Manual, a Radiation Resistance Testing Handbook and a Protein Expression and AKTA Purification Handbook.","stack":["COBRA-style FBA on Yeast9, iBsu1147, iMS837 (iJB792 lineage)","scipy.integrate.solve_ivp (RK45)","Python / Jupyter notebooks","COMSOL Multiphysics (CFD)","Arduino Mega","DS18B20 temperature probe","DANOPLUS KIB-87 pH probe","DFRobot SEN0189 turbidity sensor","3D printing / CAD","Xstrahl X-ray irradiator","AKTA / HisTrap affinity chromatography","GitLab","React (wiki)"],"techniques":["genome-scale metabolic modelling and model curation (gap repair with literature-backed reactions)","anaerobic and oxygen-sweep constraint analysis","co-culture modelling by passing computed fluxes as uptake bounds","sequential nutrient co-limitation cascade","growth versus product-secretion trade-off (Pareto) analysis","in-silico knockout screening","ODE dynamic induction-timing optimisation with closed-form optimum","computational fluid dynamics across multiple gravity regimes","sensor calibration to OD600 for closed-loop autoinduction","four-readout radiation resistance characterisation","genomic integration of Dsup","Comet assay for DNA damage"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Engagement was built around a stated regional gap: synthetic biology is largely absent from secondary curricula in Saudi Arabia and the wider MENA region, and almost no learning resources exist in Arabic. The flagship is the Tawasol Initiative, a network uniting MENA iGEM teams through film, podcasts and social media specifically to reach Arabic speakers, run alongside a Tawasol Hackathon; it extended to a joint programme with NYU Abu Dhabi iGEM (28-30 August) and reached as far as Peru and Kazakhstan. Programmes are differentiated by audience: the Thuwal Science Pioneers Program brought middle and high school students onto the KAUST campus for a lecture with a before-and-after knowledge check, a 'design your own microbe to help astronauts' activity, tours of the Nanofabrication and Robotics core labs, and lunch with the team; a trip to Zahrat Al Sahra International School 80 km south reached 58 middle schoolers; a KAUST Summer Mentorship Program is paired with Oboor (Arabic for 'transition'), a university-adaptation programme for Saudi students built with a counselling-psychology researcher at Umm Al-Qura University; a farmer-facing course trains youth volunteers who then teach rural farmers; and family-facing 'Copy-Paste Plants' booths and science movie nights ran for the wider community, with just over two thirds of the film audience staying for the discussion. One standout artefact is a bilingual illustrated dialogue between two young Peruvian students working through whether a CRISPR edit of a plant's own gene is a Living Modified Organism under Peru's Law 31.111 moratorium or exempt under Ministerial Resolution D000068-2026-MINAM-DM of April 2026, a genuinely difficult regulatory distinction turned into a readable comic.","ihp":"Over 30 activities and 15 named conversations, and the wiki is explicit that seven parts of SHIHAB changed, with an interactive map letting the reader pick either a person or a component. The team built their own ORBIT framework (Observe, Reach, Build, Iterate, Translate) and four values (autonomy, adaptability, responsibility, accessibility). Documented changes: Dr. Christopher E. Mason's feedback made Dsup one of the protective genes in the chassis-engineering strategy and added the Comet assay to the experimental workflow; Konstantinos Vergos and Dr. Akshay Chandrashekhar converged on microgravity as a mandatory part of validation, which is why the COMSOL simulations exist (as a precursor to parabolic flight); Sarah Al Harbi's point about crew supervision load produced the dry-lab monitoring dashboard and shaped the hardware; KAUST Health, Safety and Environment directly wrote the structure of the Safety Handbook (hazard identification, risk assessment, containment failure, accidental exposure, environmental release, emergency response) and shaped the Hardware manual; a regulatory expert pushed them to prioritise therapeutics by the conditions astronauts actually face on specific missions rather than by ease of production, which is how Spaceflight-Associated Neuro-ocular Syndrome and carcinogenesis entered the payload list; and conversations with humanitarian responders Rachel Kessler and Jonathan Grant replaced a generic 'disaster zone' use case with a stated principle, design for a specific context, not an abstract disaster zone. The project also started on oxygen production and moved to therapeutics after team and PI discussion, with the earlier adviser's emphasis on automation, monitoring, product quality and space-relevant validation carried over. Astronaut Rayyanah Barnawi and Starr Corbin informed the astronaut-facing requirements; the Tawasol Hackathon surfaced three governance priorities (remote quality assurance, operational accountability, healthcare integration).","realWorld":"Two application contexts are carried in parallel and the second was added because of stakeholder input: space missions, and remote or disaster-affected settings with disrupted medicine supply chains, each treated as a specific deployment context rather than one generic 'remote healthcare' market. The continuation plan is staged as a roadmap, beginning with demonstrating small-scale biomanufacturing in Low Earth Orbit and evaluating production under microgravity and space radiation, with a long-term pathway developed out of conversations with Savi Glowe and industry contacts (Deep Space Biology, BIOASTRA). Practical adoptability is the strongest part of the case: the only manual step is loading the pill, the platform is designed for low power and low payload mass, and it is documented well enough for a non-specialist to run from the Hardware User Manual, which the team tested by setting the bioreactor and fluid-dispensing system up on a folding table in the desert dunes, far from any bench.","partners":["Rayyanah Barnawi (Saudi astronaut)","Starr Corbin","Dr. Christopher E. Mason, Weill Cornell Medicine","Prof. Alexandre Rosado, KAUST","Dr. Luis Zea","Konstantinos Vergos and Dr. Akshay Chandrashekhar","Kimberly Washington, Deep Space Biology","BIOASTRA","Savi Glowe","KAUST Health, Safety and Environment","Rachel Kessler and Jonathan Grant (humanitarian response)","NYU Abu Dhabi iGEM","Tawasol Initiative (MENA iGEM network)","Zahrat Al Sahra International School, Jeddah","Thuwal community schools","Renad Almalki, Umm Al-Qura University (Oboor programme)","StruBE Lab, KAUST"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6341/wiki/content/hardware/cfd-prototype-3.webp","caption":"COMSOL Multiphysics CFD of the third rotor concept (three rows of small tilted blades) at 200 rpm, comparing bubble fate under Earth, Mars, Moon and transit gravity: the simulation that selected the final rotor geometry.","credit":"Team KAUST-KSA, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6341/wiki/content/hardware/final-bioreactor.avif","caption":"The built SHIHAB bioreactor: glass vessel with 3D-printed lid and rotor between two hollow supports carrying all wiring, heating band around the vessel, and the Arduino-driven touchscreen dashboard in the base.","credit":"Team KAUST-KSA, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6341/wiki/content/hardware/desert-pic-1.avif","caption":"SHIHAB tested on desert dunes with a folding table and a laptop, putting the 'operable anywhere' claim to a field test rather than asserting it.","credit":"Team KAUST-KSA, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6341/wiki/content/public-engagement/copy-paste-plants-activity.avif","caption":"The Copy-Paste Plants activity at a family-facing community booth, part of an engagement programme built around the near-absence of synthetic biology from MENA school curricula and of Arabic-language resources.","credit":"Team KAUST-KSA, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Steal Table 1: for every link between two models, write down what is actually passed and label it Modeled, Identified or Assumed. It costs one table and it immunises a student modelling chain against the usual criticism that the pieces were never really connected. Pair that with KAUST's four-readout rule (no resistance or phenotype claim unless it survives several independent assays) and the habit of ending each model section with a 'For the Wet Lab' instruction, so the dry lab visibly changes what gets done at the bench.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/kaust-ksa/","https://2026.igem.wiki/kaust-ksa/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/kaust-ksa/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/kaust-ksa/measurement","https://2026.igem.wiki/kaust-ksa/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/kaust-ksa/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/kaust-ksa/science-communication","https://2026.igem.wiki/kaust-ksa/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/kaust-ksa/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/kaust-ksa/safety-and-security"],"rank":143},"6345":{"team":"BGI-College","id":"6345","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/bgi-college/","projectTitle":"BioH2","tagline":"A wild Clostridium isolated from a Guangdong wetland, made genetically tractable, then redesigned into a closed-loop biorefinery once the arithmetic killed hydrogen-only","summary":"BGI-College took Clostridium beijerinckii S63, a strain newly isolated from sediment at Yundonghai Wetland Park in Foshan, Guangdong (a site of interest because of unusually high natural soil hydrogen in the Sanshui Basin), and turned a non-model anaerobe into a working chassis. They sequenced it to a single circular 5,870,246 bp chromosome, measured 40.20 plus or minus 3.45 percent hydrogen in its gas output, built a metabolic flux model that identified PFOR and HydA overexpression plus thl deletion as targets, and established an electroporation transformation system through three documented DBTL cycles, two of which failed outright. Their economic check then did something unusual: it proved their own original premise impossible, since breaking even on glucose alone would need 6.70 mol H2 per mol glucose against a hard biochemical ceiling of 4.0, which forced a redesign around byproduct valorisation. They won Best Alternative Platform in the High School section and were nominated for Best New Basic Part and Best Presentation.","awards":["Best New Basic Part — Nominee (High School)","Best Alternative Platform — Winner (High School)","Best Presentation — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Explicit DBTL cycles used as the organising structure for platform development, each written as Design, Build and Test, then Learn, with the failed cycles kept in place. A metabolic flux framework integrating pathway stoichiometry, carbon allocation and electron transfer, released with a visual interface so non-modellers can use it. Hydrogen pathways benchmarked in a four-way comparison table (grey, blue, green, bio-green) on carbon footprint, levelised cost, supply-chain risk and commercial status.","dataviz":"Baseline versus engineered model runs shown side by side so the predicted yield change is legible, the full electroporation workflow drawn as a process diagram with voltages and buffers labelled, a parameter-sweep figure for the optimisation attempts, and, notably, photographs of the empty selective plates from the failed transformations alongside the successful ones. Field photographs of the wetland sampling site locate the strain in a real place.","datascience":"The modelling is used as a decision tool, not decoration: it put theoretical yield at 2.46 mol H2/mol glucose for wild type rising to 3.60 under an idealised engineered scenario, and the HPLC product profile (acetate and butyrate dominant, little lactate) is what selected thl as the deletion target rather than a generic guess. The economic model is the standout piece of quantitative reasoning: industrial glucose at about 3,000 RMB per tonne against hydrogen at 40 RMB per kg requires 6.70 mol H2 per mol glucose to cover feedstock alone, which exceeds the 4.0 mol theoretical maximum of dark fermentation, so a hydrogen-only business is arithmetically impossible. Genome work includes ANI above 98 percent against C. beijerinckii DSM 791 (GCF_018223745.1), phylogenetic placement, whole-genome alignment and VFDB virulence screening, published as a separate PDF.","software":"A visual interface over the metabolic flux model, built explicitly to lower the barrier for researchers who do not routinely do computational modelling.","stack":["Clostridium beijerinckii S63 (non-model anaerobe)","Bacillus subtilis 941","E. coli DH5-alpha","pNICKclos2.0 CRISPR editing vector","electroporation in an anaerobic chamber","whole-genome sequencing and annotation","ANI and phylogenetic analysis","VFDB","HPLC","gas chromatography"],"techniques":["electrocompetent cell preparation under strict anaerobiosis","electroporation at 1.8 kV in a 2 mm cuvette with erythromycin selection","CRISPR knockout design in Clostridium","native promoter plus CDS plus terminator part cloning from a wild isolate","dark fermentation with HPLC organic-acid tracking","secondary cultivation of B. subtilis on spent fermentation broth"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"","ihp":"Human practices was run as a test of the project's core assumption rather than as outreach. They consulted academic researchers and industrial practitioners including engineers at China General Nuclear Power (CGN), and report the difference in how the two groups framed the problem: academics asked whether the pathway was technically feasible and rigorous, industry asked what it would cost and whether it would scale. Industry input on hydrogen's transport and storage barriers, combined with their own break-even arithmetic, is what turned a hydrogen-only project into a closed-loop biorefinery. A second consultation was decisive technically: after two failed DBTL cycles, Dr. Youduo Wu of Dalian University of Technology told them to reconsider anaerobic handling across the whole workflow rather than keep tuning electroporation parameters, which led them to move the electroporator inside the anaerobic chamber and finally obtain transformants.","realWorld":"Three things here are worth copying, and the honesty running through all of them is the reason the platform is credible. First, the economics. Their break-even calculation is the single most useful piece of commercialisation reasoning in this cohort precisely because it falsifies their own premise: at roughly 3,000 RMB per tonne of industrial glucose and 40 RMB per kg of hydrogen, covering only the sugar feed needs 6.70 mol H2 per mol glucose, while dark fermentation cannot exceed 4.0 mol, so no amount of strain improvement makes a hydrogen-only product profitable. They state that plainly and redesign rather than hedge. The replacement model is coherent: HPLC confirmed the broth still holds organic acids after hydrogen evolution stops, so instead of paying for chemical waste disposal they use the spent broth as a free substrate to grow commercial Bacillus subtilis and sell it as a liquid biofertiliser, a secondary revenue stream that offsets the feedstock cost and sidesteps hydrogen storage and transport entirely. Note what is and is not claimed: they say the biofertiliser revenue 'substantially offsets' feedstock cost when scaled against raw material inputs, but publish no kit price, no biofertiliser price, no yield per litre of broth and no full P&L, so the loop is a validated concept with the unit economics still missing. There is no company, no patent and no investor. Second, the platform. What makes S63 genuinely reusable by other groups is that they published the route in, not just the destination: the full electroporation workflow with buffers, voltage and cuvette gap specified, the parameter sweep they tried (OD600 0.2 to 1.0, 600 to 1800 V, 100 to 400 microlitres, 1 and 2 mm cuvettes at fixed 200 ohms and 25 microfarads), photographs of the blank plates from both failed cycles, and the one change that actually worked. They also record a failure that did not resolve, stating that the Thl-targeting editing plasmid could not be assembled even though all four fragments amplified and sequenced correctly. Fifteen basic parts were cloned from S63 as native promoter plus CDS plus terminator triples across three HydA and two PFOR genes, which is the right format for a non-model host where heterologous regulatory elements may not work. The genome is published as a separate annotated report. And they label the limits precisely: the transformation system is 'an early-stage platform, rather than a fully optimised or universally reliable protocol', the model 'is not a validated predictor of experimentally achieved hydrogen production', and the oxygen hypothesis 'needs further controlled experiments' to confirm its specific contribution. Third, the safety reasoning, which is more sophisticated than most undergraduate work. The chassis was changed from C. butyricum to C. beijerinckii during an early safety review to avoid strain-dependent pathogenicity risk; they explicitly refuse to let a species-level BSL-1 classification (ATCC 35702) transfer to their own isolate, and instead confirm identity by ANI and phylogeny and screen against VFDB, while recording the correct caveat that a database match does not by itself show a functional virulence factor and that several hits were partial or low-coverage. They are candid that as high-school students they depend on instructors for safety decisions and authorised tasks, do not adjust gas-supply settings or gas-line connections themselves, and they report that three students failed the safety assessment on first attempt and had to re-sit before the team reached a 100 percent pass rate. Continuation is framed as community reuse: the model, the parts, the transformation protocol and the troubleshooting record are offered so that future dark-fermentation teams 'reuse our rationales, protocols, and lessons rather than repeat them'.","partners":["BGI Research (Dr. Yingshan Li, secondary PI; isolated and sequenced S63, ran the genome and virulence analyses and taught the team to interpret them)","Dr. Youduo Wu, Dalian University of Technology (diagnosed oxygen exposure as the transformation bottleneck)","China General Nuclear Power (CGN) engineers (cost and scale-up framing that drove the redesign)","Yundonghai Wetland Park, Foshan, Guangdong (environmental source of strain S63)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6345/wiki/assets/alternative-platform/fig3.avif","caption":"The electroporation transformation workflow established for Clostridium beijerinckii S63, published with buffers, voltage and cuvette gap specified so another group can reproduce it","credit":"Team BGI-College, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6345/wiki/assets/alternative-platform/fig4.avif","caption":"Published evidence of failure: blank erythromycin selective plates from the first transformation attempt, kept on the wiki alongside the eventual success","credit":"Team BGI-College, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6345/wiki/assets/alternative-platform/fig5.avif","caption":"The electroporation parameter sweep across cell density, voltage, competent-cell volume and cuvette gap that still did not yield transformants, before the anaerobic-chamber redesign","credit":"Team BGI-College, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6345/wiki/assets/contribution/fig2.avif","caption":"Model-guided engineering run showing the theoretical hydrogen yield change from PFOR and HydA overexpression with thl deletion, shown against the wild-type baseline","credit":"Team BGI-College, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Run the break-even arithmetic against the biochemical ceiling before committing a year of lab work: BGI-College showed a hydrogen-only product needs 6.70 mol H2 per mol glucose while dark fermentation caps at 4.0, which killed their premise early and forced a byproduct-valorisation design that actually closes. And when publishing a platform for a non-model chassis, publish the failed cycles too — the parameter sweep that did nothing, the photographs of blank plates, the plasmid that would never assemble — because the route in is what another lab needs, not the destination.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/bgi-college/","https://2026.igem.wiki/bgi-college/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/bgi-college/alternative-platform/","https://2026.igem.wiki/bgi-college/contribution/","https://2026.igem.wiki/bgi-college/safety-and-security/","https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6345/wiki/assets/alternative-platform/genome-analysis-of-s63.pdf"],"rank":40},"6350":{"team":"Marburg","id":"6350","section":"Overgrad","country":"Germany","village":"Alternative Platform","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/marburg/","projectTitle":"CLiPPR - Chloroplast Library for inducible PPRs","tagline":"Making the chloroplast switchable: inducible designer PPR proteins paired with synthetic 5'UTRs","summary":"Chloroplasts are arguably the cheapest protein factories available (around 90% of global primary production, up to 70% of a plant cell's protein as transgenic product, linear rather than capital-intensive scaling), but they lack the one tool microbial hosts have: inducibility, so growth and production compete permanently and a toxic product means no plant at all. CLiPPR outsources that inducibility to the nucleus: nuclear-encoded, inducibly expressed synthetic pentatricopeptide repeat proteins are imported into the plastid, where they bind matched synthetic 5'UTRs placed upstream of a chloroplast gene and switch translation up or down by three mechanisms (blocking the start codon, protecting an unstable 5'UTR from exonucleases, or resolving a hairpin over the ribosome binding site). The team designed 30 fully synthetic 5'UTRs de novo, produced, purified and tested 19 new-to-nature PPR proteins, reported the highest transgene expression yet recorded in a chloroplast in vitro, and validated across three systems of rising complexity: chloroplast cell-free extract, Chlamydomonas reinhardtii, and Nicotiana benthamiana. It won Best Alternative Platform and was nominated for Part Collection, Education, Presentation, Wiki and Foundational Advance.","awards":["Top 10 (Overgrad)","Best Part Collection — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Alternative Platform — Winner (Overgrad)","Best Education — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Presentation — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Wiki — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Foundational Advance Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"The computational work is sequence and assembly engineering rather than structure prediction, and it is tightly coupled to a hard constraint: PPRs are long tandem repeats, and the high GC content of the C. reinhardtii nuclear genome makes conventional gene synthesis of those repetitive stretches expensive or impossible, which is what forced an organism-specific toolbox instead of ordering full coding sequences. Adapting the published GRASP Golden Gate toolbox (Dennis et al. 2025, consensus S-type repeats with a programmable PPR code, 42 level-1 modules assembling 9-, 14- and 19-nt binders) from E. coli to Chlamydomonas meant codon-optimising every module, which shifts the Golden Gate fusion sites and therefore changes assembly fidelity and module boundaries, a set of interdependent decisions the team first worked through by hand. They placed the new fusion sites inside the ARELF motif (the most variable codons in the repeat, giving the largest overhang pool), pulled C. reinhardtii codon usage from the Kazusa table, excluded every codon below 50% relative abundance among the most abundantly expressed proteins, searched the remaining ARELF translations for overhang sets, and scored candidates with the NEB ligase fidelity calculator against a target above 75%, first running the original GRASP level 0 and level 1 overhangs through the same calculator to get a baseline on the same scale rather than comparing a prediction against a published measurement. B- and D-modules were intronized per Baier et al., offered with and without the LHCBM1i2 intron. Binding was validated biophysically by fluorescence polarisation to extract dissociation constants, with one optimised PPR reaching a Kd among the best in the literature.","dataviz":"The wiki is unusually honest and unusually readable. Every page carries a per-page inventory in the subtitle ('7 sections / 17 pictures / 10 references'), a key-achievements list before any narrative, and a scroll progress indicator themed as a PPR walking along its binding sites ('PPR Bound Site 1 / 8'), with a Reinhardt mascot reacting to the content. Negative results are given the same prominence as positive ones: the XRN-1 titration and pair screening are reported as showing the nuclease is barely active under the chosen conditions, with the reason stated (room temperature and a buffer chosen to keep the chloroplast extract working rather than to keep the nuclease happy), followed by the redesigned assay that removed the extract and the translation step entirely; the semi-automated purification is reported as robust and reproducible but too low-yielding, with a recommendation about which other teams it would still suit. The Chlamydomonas screen reports that only a handful of mNeonGreen-positive transformants were usable because of their transplastomic background. The software is published as form-driven Colab notebooks with a 'click to explore our tools' interface, and the codon-usage comparison is given as a full 64-codon table with per-codon percentage-point differences between C. reinhardtii and E. coli rather than a summary statistic.","datascience":"The characterisation campaign is a throughput argument. Building and testing a library of this size by hand was not feasible, so three automation technologies were made integral to the experimental design rather than bolted on. An Echo 525 acoustic liquid handler, programmed with the PyEcho script, assembled all large assays (the largest replacing 868 final pipetting steps per replicate) and, by dispensing 25 nl droplets, allowed reaction volumes to be cut to a quarter of the 10 ul manual minimum, which both saved purified PPR protein and removed the pipetting inaccuracy inherent in sub-0.5 ul manual additions; planning the plate layout in software also made reagent demand calculable in advance (including when to buy expensive XRN-1), made pipetting-scheme errors catchable before they happened, and cut run-to-run variance because a 384-well plate is assembled in under five minutes rather than over an hour of reagents sitting out of the freezer. The BMG Clariostar autoinjector dispensed furimazine for the NanoLuc reporter at an identical incubation time every run, measurably lowering standard deviation against manual addition. A 96-well semi-automated protein purification workflow adapted from the Baker Lab protocol combined IMAC and automated size-exclusion chromatography so purification and characterisation happened in one run.","software":"PPR-opt, released as two form-driven Google Colab notebooks that run entirely remotely with no local install: PPR-opt Designer builds a PPR for a single target RNA sequence in a chosen host organism, and PPR-opt Inventory generates a whole GRASP-style toolbox able to clone every possible PPR for that organism. It automates the process the team first did manually: codon-optimising each PPR module for the target organism and redistributing the Golden Gate module boundaries accordingly. The team states plainly that all outputs are software predictions not yet experimentally validated, and that so far one PPR from the resulting Chlamy-GRASP toolbox has been successfully transformed into the C. reinhardtii nucleus. Alongside it they published the first PPR parts collection in the iGEM Registry: matched sets of synthetic 5'UTRs and their corresponding PPR proteins with sequence information, functional descriptions and characterisation data, plus the Chlamy-GRASP level 0 and level 1 modules; the wiki repository is gitlab.igem.org/2026/marburg.","stack":["Google Colab (form-driven notebooks)","GRASP Golden Gate PPR toolbox (Dennis et al. 2025)","Kazusa codon usage database","NEB ligase fidelity calculator","PyEcho (HN-lab)","Beckman Coulter Labcyte Echo 525 acoustic liquid handler","BMG Clariostar plate reader with autoinjector","automated size-exclusion chromatography / IMAC in 96-well format","NanoLuc / firefly luciferase / mNeonGreen reporters","fluorescence polarisation assay","iGEM Registry"],"techniques":["codon optimisation with fusion-site redistribution","Golden Gate overhang selection and fidelity prediction against a same-scale baseline","intronization for expression in C. reinhardtii","de novo synthetic 5'UTR design (30 UTRs)","three orthogonal PPR regulation mechanisms (blocking, exonuclease protection, hairpin resolution)","chloroplast cell-free extract screening","dissociation-constant determination by fluorescence polarisation","acoustic nanolitre liquid handling for 384-well assay assembly","automated substrate injection for reproducible luminescence","semi-automated parallel protein expression and purification","nuclear inducible/repressible promoter construction (estradiol, IPTG, rapamycin, MetE, THI4)"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Marburg's education work is explicitly meta: they did not just build activities, they studied how to build them, after their first Girls' Day event prompted the question of what happens once an event is over. They reviewed the literature, consulted 15 experts across education, science communication and evaluation research, and found that existing iGEM documentation covers how outreach was organised but almost never how to ground it in theory or evaluate it beyond whether participants enjoyed it. Four outputs followed. A curriculum-aligned Teaching Toolbox ('Die CLiPPR Toolbox'), co-designed with education experts and aligned to the four German KMK national competency domains, tested with seven teachers at three schools and revised on their feedback. Plasmid Panic, an escape game playable by anyone over 12 with no scientific background, distributed through schools and with iGEM Patras in English and German. A SciComm and Evaluation Guide written specifically for future iGEM teams, covering how to set goals, pick evaluation methods and feed findings back. And a documented Evidence and Feedback process, published so others can see not only what was made but why, what changed and what was learned. Three expert quotations frame the whole approach: 'Reach is not impact, and satisfaction is not learning' (Dorothee Menhart), and 'Why are we communicating, and why should people care?' (Dr. Sascha Vogel).","ihp":"45 stakeholders, organised by the six application domains the technology touches (scientific impact, agriculture, space, molecular farming, environment and sustainability, law and regulations) rather than by job title, and the design changes are specific and attributed. Dr. Silvia Ramundo rejected the team's original plan to base the 'resolving' 5'UTR on Prikyl et al., where the hairpin the PPR resolves also contains the ribosome binding site, and recommended a design in which the PPR site and the RBS are locally disconnected so the PPR cannot interfere with ribosome binding; the team adapted to the Rojas et al. 2019 binding mechanism as a result. Prof. Ralph Bock (Max Planck Institute of Molecular Plant Physiology, a pioneer of chloroplast transformation) strongly advised dropping variable RBS testing and sticking to his validated Shine-Dalgarno sequence for predictable chloroplast translation, which they did. Prof. Alison Smith's input led them to combine two well-established repressible parts, the MetE and THI4 promoters, in one construct specifically to minimise leakiness, after Dr. Reimo Zoschke identified leakiness as the real unsolved problem ('what remains problematic are tight systems'). Tania Ryzhkova and another adviser steered characterisation away from an EMSA toward a fluorescence polarisation assay and then advised on RNase-free practice, labelled-RNA design, protein concentration ranges and controls, and on the analysis. An interview with an explosives-degradation expert made them realise phytoremediation bottlenecks come from pollutant kinetics and bioavailability rather than chloroplast gene timing, so they dropped that application. Prof. Yuri Gleba supplied the economic case (recombinant protein from plants at around 100 USD per kilogram; plants scale linearly while fermentation requires buying the next-size bioreactor), and Elena Lesch and Farley Kwok advised on testing in the 2021 Marburg chloroplast cell-free extracts rather than only E. coli, warning that such extracts are far less common than standard E. coli systems. On the education side, Prof. Malte Schwinger (educational psychology, Marburg) told them to use validated Likert-scale instruments instead of writing their own, and one evaluation expert advised against factual recall as the primary measure for the Teaching Toolbox.","realWorld":"The team frames CLiPPR as enabling infrastructure for molecular farming rather than a product, and is candid that it is one of several missing pieces: chloroplast transformation is still not established in many plant species, selecting successful transformants is often as hard as making them, and the absence of post-translational processing limits which proteins can be made there. Fourteen molecular-farming stakeholders were interviewed on what integration would actually look like, covering compound classes, the advantages of stable transformants, inducer choice, production setup and regulation; Jess Bunchek and Dr. Don Stewart established that higher-plant molecular farming would realistically run in contained greenhouses rather than open fields. Containment is also a design argument, since in most higher plants the chloroplast is maternally inherited, so transgenes are not spread by pollen. Light-based induction via optogenetics was investigated with Lars Broker (PULSE system) because it costs nothing, leaves no residue, and is already applied by drone in modern agriculture, and is held as the most attractive long-term inducer from a safety standpoint. The five remaining application domains (agriculture, space, sustainability, law and regulation, scientific impact) each have their own analysis page, and the parts collection is the handover mechanism: documented, Registry-deposited, and intended for other teams doing organelle engineering and RNA-level regulation in plants.","partners":["Prof. Dr. Yuri Gleba (plant molecular farming)","Dr. Reimo Zoschke (chloroplast gene expression)","Prof. Dr. Ralph Bock, Max Planck Institute of Molecular Plant Physiology","Dr. Silvia Ramundo","Prof. Alison Smith","Prof. Dr. Ian Small / GRASP toolbox authors","Tania Ryzhkova, Philipps-Universitat Marburg","Elena Lesch and Farley Kwok","Lars Broker (PULSE optogenetics)","Jess Bunchek and Dr. Don Stewart (molecular farming in higher plants)","Prof. Dr. Malte Schwinger, Educational Psychology, Philipps-Universitat Marburg","Nina Miller (science communicator)","Monica Dechene, Munich Science Communication Lab","Dr. Sascha Vogel","Dorothee Menhart","Seven teachers across three schools (Teaching Toolbox co-design)","iGEM Patras (escape game distribution)","iGEM Marburg 2021 (chloroplast cell-free extract)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6350/wiki/src/contents/project/alternative-platform/ccfs-utr-screening-1280.avif","caption":"Screening the library of synthetic 5'UTR and designer PPR pairs in chloroplast cell-free extract, the lowest-complexity of the three test systems; one of these 30 de novo UTRs gave the highest transgene expression yet reported in a chloroplast in vitro.","credit":"Team Marburg, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6350/wiki/src/contents/project/alternative-platform/chlamy-ppr107-microscopy-1280.avif","caption":"Microscopy of PPR107 in Chlamydomonas reinhardtii, confirming that a nuclear-encoded designer PPR is imported into the chloroplast, the step the whole 'outsource inducibility to the nucleus' design depends on.","credit":"Team Marburg, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6350/wiki/src/contents/lab/ppropt/automation/sapp-plates-1024-1280.avif","caption":"Stacked plates for semi-automated protein purification in 96-well format: a fritted Ni-NTA plate, a filter plate and a flat-bottom plate assembled for centrifugation, adapted from the Baker Lab protocol for scaled characterisation of designed proteins.","credit":"Team Marburg, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6350/wiki/src/contents/education/escape-game/escape-game-cover-1280.avif","caption":"Plasmid Panic, the team's escape game, redesigned after school visits showed students were far more curious about what daily lab life looks like than about the science content; released in English and German with multiple difficulty levels.","credit":"Team Marburg, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Marburg's most transferable asset is the SciComm and Evaluation Guide mindset: decide the intended outcome first, use validated Likert instruments rather than home-made ones, and never accept attendance or enjoyment as evidence of learning ('reach is not impact, and satisfaction is not learning'). On the dry-lab side, copy their automation-as-design-decision argument: an acoustic liquid handler plus a planned plate layout does not just save pipetting, it shrinks reaction volumes fourfold, makes reagent budgets predictable in advance, and cuts variance, which is exactly what lets a small team characterise a real library instead of three constructs.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/marburg/","https://2026.igem.wiki/marburg/project/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/marburg/alternative-platform","https://2026.igem.wiki/marburg/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/marburg/lab/automation","https://2026.igem.wiki/marburg/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/marburg/human-practices/molecular-farming","https://2026.igem.wiki/marburg/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/marburg/education/escape-game","https://2026.igem.wiki/marburg/project/parts-collection","https://2026.igem.wiki/marburg/contribution"],"rank":131},"6356":{"team":"TU Darmstadt","id":"6356","section":"Overgrad","country":"Germany","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-darmstadt/","projectTitle":"UNRAVEL: Unlocking New Resources And Value from End-of-Life textiles","tagline":"Enzymes and thermophilic hosts for mixed textile waste, plus a 134 euro anaerobic chamber, a 115 euro oxygen monitor and a 68 euro shaker, all documented including the failures.","summary":"TU Darmstadt attacked mixed textile waste, of which roughly 92 million tonnes are generated globally each year and less than 1% is recycled back into fibres, by working with two thermophilic organisms: Acetivibrio thermocellus, a strict anaerobe with a cellulosome that degrades cotton at 60 C, and Geobacillus thermocatenulatus, whose carboxylesterase the team characterised and registered as GeoEsterase. Because those organisms need equipment the team did not have, they built it: a movable DIY anaerobic chamber for under 150 euros, a portable ESP32 oxygen monitor when resazurin proved too slow and cumbersome to verify the atmosphere, and two generations of orbital shaker to fit inside an existing 60 C incubator. What makes the work a measurement case study is the discipline of separating what was demonstrated from what was not, in both the enzymology and the hardware.","awards":["Best New Basic Part — Winner (Overgrad)","Best Hardware — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Presentation — Nominee (Overgrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Every hardware page is structured as motivation and design requirements, design decisions, bill of materials and costs, construction instructions, materials-processing lessons, testing, evaluation, limitations and conclusion, with a recurring distinction between what was built, what was tested and what has not yet been demonstrated quantitatively. The same discipline runs through the results page, where computational predictions are labelled as predictions and never presented as measured enzyme performance. The team frames its contribution to iGEM as the designs, methods and troubleshooting lessons for working with non-model organisms, so that later teams do not start from scratch.","dataviz":"Interactive parameter plots for kinetic constants with buttons to switch between kcat, KM and kcat/KM across temperature, and between temperatures on the initial-rate plots, with axes held constant so panels can be compared directly; dashed lines for fitted Michaelis-Menten curves and dotted lines explicitly marking measurements for which no fit could be established, so an unfittable dataset is visible rather than absent; absorbance-against-time traces with the blank subtracted and each trace shown relative to its first read; ATR-IR spectra overlaid against simulated reference spectra; collapsible result sections with open-all and close-all controls; an interactive 3D protein model on the landing page.","datascience":"Enzyme activity is measured against p-nitrophenyl hexanoate as a soluble stand-in for one of the two ester bonds in PET, with the released 4-nitrophenol quantified by absorbance at 396 nm using a stated extinction coefficient of 18,100 M-1 cm-1 under their conditions, so the readout is anchored to a physical constant rather than left in absorbance units. Conditions are fully specified: 0.5 uM enzyme (0.25 uM for the deep-eutectic-solvent comparison) against 0.5, 1, 2 and 4 mM substrate in 5 C steps around 37 C, every value the mean of a triplicate. The initial rate is defined operationally as the highest rate of product formation between two consecutive reads, identified automatically by their evaluation sheet rather than chosen by eye, and Vmax and KM are then fitted by minimising the sum of squared differences in Excel Solver, with kcat following from Vmax and enzyme concentration. Measurements for which no fit could be established are excluded from the table and the figure and said to be excluded, and one suspect value is flagged twice, at 47 C the Thermo MHETase trace shows a single jump in absorbance shortly after the start, so the team warns that the derived initial rate and the fit containing it should be treated with caution. Every plate's evaluation sheet is published as a PDF with the date, the enzymes, the temperature and the notes, including one where well D12 was excluded for air bubbles, so the chain from raw plate to reported constant is auditable. Thermal stability is measured by thermal shift assay with both enzymes on the same plate under identical conditions (2 uM protein, 5x SYPRO Orange, 1x LEW buffer with 10% glycerol, n = 3), and the negative result is reported with its statistics rather than buried: GeoEsterase 74.54 +/- 0.03 C and Thermo GeoEsterase 74.63 +/- 0.13 C by Boltzmann fit with R2 at least 0.998, a difference of +0.09 C with a 95% confidence interval of -0.21 to +0.40 C and a Welch t-test p of 0.34, from which the team concludes not merely that no improvement was seen but that the interval excludes any stabilisation larger than about 0.4 C. Material identity is verified before use rather than assumed, with ATR-IR on a PerkinElmer FT-IR with MIR TGS detector confirming the nylon is Nylon 6 and the polyester is PET against simulated references, and solvent extraction with methanol and acetone followed by repeat spectra used to test for additives and dyes. Particle sizing produced an honest dead end: cryomilling was optimised by ball diameter (25 mm adopted after 5, 7 and 12 mm failed), recovery across 24 runs ran from 79 to 100% with two same-day replicates at 100 and 79%, which the team reads as powder retained in the jar and funnel rather than as a result, saying explicitly it is not a degradation readout; DLS on a Malvern Zetasizer Nano with the serial number and software version recorded showed none of the samples monodisperse with much of the material above the 10 um measuring range, sonication changed nothing, and the team concluded cryomilling cannot produce the monodisperse dispersions repeatable kinetics need and abandoned the approach in favour of weighed fabric pieces. Microscopy covered the coarse end that DLS cannot reach, 3.1 to 40 um for polyester and 3 to 50 um for nylon, with the caveat that only two samples with few particles were imaged so no distribution can be fitted, plus an incidental warning that polyester autofluoresces without any dye because of optical brighteners, UV stabilisers and degradation products. Computational work is held to the same standard: 51 substitutions across five proteins are reported with the explicit statement that a DeepSTABp-predicted +9.27 C melting-temperature change and a +167% TemStaPro score gain answer different questions and must not be treated as equivalent, that 73% versus 97% binding-pocket residue overlap indicates similar identified residues but does not prove correct substrate positioning or catalytic activity, that a substitution 6.55 angstroms from the catalytic serine is active-site-adjacent and not a mutation of a catalytic residue, and that a 28.2 percentage-point increase in near-serine contact fraction across 100 ns trajectories is geometry, not a measured reaction rate, with the roughly 3.3-fold ester-to-amide contact ratio labelled a simulation-derived geometric comparison and not a change in catalytic specificity.","software":"Hardware is released as build documentation rather than code: a full assembly procedure for the anaerobic chamber with bills of materials and per-item recorded costs, a step-by-step oxygen-monitor build with the complete I2C scanner sketch and both the simple and advanced Arduino display programs printed in full on the wiki, a wiring table mapping every OLED and sensor pin to its ESP32 pin, and an orbital shaker build with its own BOM, tool list and assembly steps. Nine 3D models and a seventeen-image gallery accompany the shaker, with bearing specifications listed. Plate-reader evaluation sheets are published per plate as PDFs, including the current version of the sheet with a worked example of the layout and calculation steps.","stack":["ESP32 NodeMCU with DFRobot SEN0465 factory-calibrated electrochemical oxygen sensor","0.91 inch 128x32 I2C OLED, Arduino IDE 2.3.10, DFRobot_MultiGasSensor and Adafruit GFX/SSD1306 libraries","12 V DC gear motor with PWM control and MOSFET switching","PerkinElmer FT-IR with ATR accessory and MIR TGS detector","Malvern Zetasizer Nano (DLS)","Light and confocal microscopy","Thermal shift assay with SYPRO Orange","AKTA and gravity His-tag affinity chromatography","Excel Solver (GRG Nonlinear) for Michaelis-Menten fitting","DeepSTABp, TemStaPro, ProteinMPNN","100 ns explicit-solvent molecular dynamics with MM-GBSA and MM-PBSA","3D printing and cryomilling"],"techniques":["Absorbance converted with a stated extinction coefficient","Operationally defined initial rate, selected automatically","Michaelis-Menten fitting by least squares with published evaluation sheets","Unfittable datasets shown as dotted lines rather than omitted","Suspect traces flagged and carried through to the limitations","Paired same-plate comparison for thermal shift","Negative result reported with a confidence interval that bounds the effect","Material identity confirmed by ATR-IR against reference spectra","Solvent extraction to test for additives before interpreting spectra","Recovery reported as process loss rather than as a result","Abandoning a method when its dispersions cannot support repeatable kinetics","In-tube thermometry and leak testing for DIY equipment","Separating prediction from measurement throughout"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A sustainability page sets out the environmental case alongside the science, and the project's framing is that recycling is only part of the answer, with buying less and wearing clothes for longer mattering just as much.","ihp":"Human Practices treats textile waste as a humanitarian problem first: rich countries export their waste and the communities that handle it are never the ones who benefited from producing it. The team quantifies the flow, with EU exports of used textiles more than doubling since 2005 to over 1.4 million tonnes in 2025, Germany exporting approximately 462,500 tonnes in 2022 and second only to the USA, an estimated 30 to 40% of German exports ending in landfills in receiving countries, and Chile receiving about 131,000 tonnes in 2022. They also note that only about 15% of the EU's 6.94 million tonnes of textile waste was collected separately, with 85% going into mixed household waste where it can no longer be recycled, and they sought out textile companies and the local collectors, sorters and thrift stores who keep materials in circulation. Their stated position is that responsible science means asking who the work should be for, not only whether it can work.","realWorld":"An entrepreneurship page addresses whether biological textile recycling makes economic sense, from cultivation and enzyme production costs to the practical obstacles of bringing the approach out of the laboratory, on the argument that scientific ideas often fail to leave the lab for economic rather than technical reasons. The hardware is the most directly reusable output: the anaerobic chamber is costed at 134.30 euros in materials against roughly 3,000 euros for a cheap professional chamber, a 95% reduction and the cheapest DIY solution the team could find, with the oxygen monitor at 114.60 euros per unit (the sensor being about 83% of that) and the orbital shaker at 68.08 euros. The build guides are written for reproduction, including which parts must be matched to each other, and the team says what it would record differently next time, specifically hole centres, hole diameters, edge distances and fastener lengths, to reduce another team's trial and error.","partners":["Prof. Warzecha (TU Darmstadt)","Futury Startup Summer School","Textile companies and local collectors, sorters and thrift stores (Human Practices)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6356/wiki/hardware/ac5.avif","caption":"The DIY anaerobic chamber: a transparent 55 L plastic storage container fitted with 125 mm glove ports, brass ball valves for gas inlet and outlet, an EPDM-sealed lid clamped with C-clamps along aluminium U-profile, and a two-container transfer lock, for 134.30 euros in materials against roughly 3,000 euros for a cheap commercial chamber.","credit":"Team TU Darmstadt, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6356/wiki/hardware/oxygen-sensor.avif","caption":"The portable oxygen monitor inside the chamber, reading 0.5% on its OLED. Built from an ESP32, a factory-calibrated DFRobot SEN0465 electrochemical sensor and a 0.91 inch display in a repurposed plastic box for about 115 euros, it was made because resazurin proved too slow to tell the team whether the chamber had actually reached an anaerobic atmosphere.","credit":"Team TU Darmstadt, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6356/wiki/hardware/shaker/further-pictures/shaker-in-chamber-2.avif","caption":"The orbital shaker, built from perforated plate and angle, a 12 V gear motor with PWM control and furniture casters as eccentrics, for 68.08 euros in materials so it fits inside an existing 60 C incubator for thermophilic cultures.","credit":"Team TU Darmstadt, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6356/wiki/chem-results/petandreference.avif","caption":"ATR-IR spectrum of the team's polyester sample overlaid on a simulated PET reference, recorded on a PerkinElmer FT-IR with MIR TGS detector. Material identity was confirmed before any degradation experiment, rather than assumed from the label.","credit":"Team TU Darmstadt, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Report a null result with the interval that bounds it: measuring both enzyme variants on the same plate under identical conditions let the team say not just that the engineered variant was no more stable, but that the data exclude any stabilisation larger than about 0.4 C, which is a usable constraint rather than an absence of evidence.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-darmstadt/","https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-darmstadt/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-darmstadt/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/tu-darmstadt/human-practices"],"rank":40},"6366":{"team":"Peking","id":"6366","section":"Undergrad","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/peking/","projectTitle":"TermiTox — engineered yeast baits for species-specific termite colony control","tagline":"Two engineered yeast strains, modelled from molecular dynamics to whole-colony collapse, to protect wooden heritage buildings without broad-spectrum pesticide.","summary":"Peking built a genuinely three-scale model of a termite bait. Strain A delivers a pH-gated listeriolysin O mutant that lyses the hindgut protozoa a termite depends on for cellulose digestion; Strain B releases hairpin RNA under hindgut hypoxia to silence RsEG (a termite cellulase) and Hexamerin-1 (a caste-development regulator). The Molecular Model used all-atom MD to verify the H311A-LLO safety premise, the Individual Model is a cohort-ODE system calibrated by MAP fitting against quantitative data extracted from 43 papers, and the Colony Model is a spatially explicit agent-based stochastic simulation of trophallaxis through a two-layer nest network with caste structure. The colony model produced a non-obvious and testable deployment schedule that the team then designed hardware for, plus a dose and collapse-time estimate anchored to published hexaflumuron field trials.","awards":["Best Model — Nominee (Undergrad)","Safety and Security Award — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Conservation Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Three models at three scales, each answering a different design question, and the output of each feeds the next. (1) MOLECULAR — all-atom molecular dynamics in GROMACS-style protocol on LLO (PDB 4CDB, residues 39-526) to test whether the H311A mutant is really pH-gated. PROPKA3 predicted pKa for all 141 titratable residues, identifying E247 and H311 as the residues whose protonation flips between pH 5.5 and 7.4; ten systems were built (four solution, two membrane, four crystal-contact dimers from ChimeraX packing) in CHARMM36-jul2022 with TIP3P water, 310 K V-rescale thermostat, 1 atm C-rescale barostat with semi-isotropic coupling for the membranes, 2 fs timestep, 1.2 nm non-bonded cutoff, LINCS on H-bonds, through minimisation, NVT, NPT and production. The result is quantitative: under acidic conditions the H311A acidic triad (D208/E247/D320) tightens to a D208-D320 distance of 3.94 Angstrom, while at neutral pH the distances open to 6.05-6.20 Angstrom and the salt bridges collapse, and in the membrane systems the protein sits 29 Angstrom from the phosphorus plane at pH 5.5 but drifts to 58 Angstrom at pH 7.4 by t = 20.5 ns. H311A is 17-18 Angstrom from the triad and never touches it, so the mechanism claimed is allosteric. (2) INDIVIDUAL — a cohort-structured ODE model. Because repeated bait feeding and in-gut yeast division create cells of different ages, yeast is divided into cohorts, each with its own hindgut-age clock; founder cells arrive with preloaded payload Q_0 while hindgut-born cells start empty and must build payload. All A and B cohorts share one logistic hindgut carrying capacity, b_s = r_s - [r_s]_+ Y_total/K_Y. A DAN1-calibrated hypoxia clock a_D(a) = l_D + (phi_H - l_D) G_2(a; tau_D) gates payload expression and Strain B's release module. Strain A uptake uses a delayed waiting function and saturates as protozoa are depleted, with a per-yeast kill probability p = 1 - exp(-Psi_A q), and because protozoan enzymes outlive the protozoa, digestive capacity follows through a first-order lag dE_P/dt = (ln2/T_EP)(F_P - E_P). Strain B's hairpin RNA feeds a hindgut pool with first-order decay, and the gut-pool-to-knockdown step is a convolution with an empirical time kernel fitted from oral RNAi studies, X_j(t) = A_j * integral u_j(s) K_j(t-s) ds with M_j = exp(-X_j); mRNA then drives protein pools through further lags, and total digestive function is a weighted sum D_E = w_R + w_P E_P + w_C C_H. (3) COLONY — a spatially explicit, stochastic agent-based model. The nest is a two-layer network: a macro graph linking the royal chamber, six wood modules and one or two bait modules by tunnels, with each module containing a micro branching tunnel network generated by a stochastic excavation process adapted from Lee and Lee's agent-based termite tunnelling model and converted to a continuous centreline graph. Colony members are coarse-grained weighted agents (2,000 worker agents at 250 workers each, 300 larval agents at 125 each, one explicit king and 50 explicit queens) with resolution convergence checked at 1,000/150, 2,000/300 and 4,000/600. Workers run a three-state FORAGE/RETURN/DISTRIBUTE behavioural loop; when two meet, trophallaxis fires with probability P_ij = p_max * normalised_local_density * |F_i - F_j| and half the food-load difference transfers, with a one-relay-only rule for food en route to the royal chamber. Each termite tracks food load, transferable A and B payload and accumulated damage, with worker damage Delta_D = alpha_A Q_A + alpha_B Q_B + gamma_AB * 2 Q_A Q_B/(Q_A + Q_B + eps) — a harmonic-mean synergy term that only fires when both payloads are active in the same insect, with coefficients ordered alpha_A > alpha_B > gamma_AB from the individual model. Strain A damage is assigned only to workers on the biological ground that queens and larvae lack the worker hindgut protist system. The model deliberately rejects a conventional SIR epidemic formulation because nest space and caste direction are what make trophallactic spread non-uniform.","dataviz":"The headline is interactivity that is genuinely explanatory rather than ornamental: an embedded individual-model explorer where the reader sets total dose and treatment duration, presses Update model, and then drags a timeline through 42 days watching a labelled flow diagram (INPUT, YEAST, PAYLOAD, ACTION, TARGETS, HOST) light up — clicking any element in the diagram highlights that quantity's trajectory. The colony model ships six embedded simulation videos selectable by schedule (nest construction, worker movement, A-only, B-only, A+B mixed, best schedule) with a draggable progress bar and playback speed, and one video follows a single tracked worker's food load, A payload, B payload and damage in an inset as it feeds, transfers and dies. Both explorers degrade gracefully, with the page explicitly stating that the static figures below show the same modelled outcomes when JavaScript is off. The spatial figures are the best static work: Figures 8 and 9 are matrices with treatment days 10-120 as columns and worker cohorts grouped by home module as rows, showing ever-exposed fraction, payload burden in a no-damage tracer run, and functional-worker fraction — making the distance-to-bait gradient and the spatial refuges immediately visible, then showing them disappear when a second bait station is added. Stochastic outputs are reported as three-seed medians with Q25-Q75 shading, and every caption lists the parameter values used (s = 1.40, home/adjacent/global target probabilities 0.65/0.20/0.15, global bait weights 4/2/1).","datascience":"This is a parameter-provenance project. The team collected quantitative experiments from 43 papers covering yeast persistence, trophallaxis, hindgut oxygen, LLO, protozoa, oral RNAi, cellulase activity and yeast release systems, recording species, delivery route, exposure schedule, observation times, units and readout for each — and then published an EVIDENCE MAP table that states, row by row, what each dataset can estimate, what remains unresolved, and an identifiability status of Composite, Partly identifiable, Structural constraints only, Scenario only, Structure identifiable but rates unresolved, or Not identifiable. For example, LLO entering protozoan food vacuoles is marked 'Not identifiable', and A+B synergy is marked 'Not identifiable' with the honest note that no LLO-plus-RNAi study exists, so independent, additive, limiting-factor and multiplicative scenarios are all carried instead of one being asserted. The model structure was then deliberately built as the SMALLEST structure the data can constrain: when several microscopic steps were only ever observed through one final readout, they were kept together as one effective process rather than split into unidentifiable rates. Parameters were calibrated by maximum a posteriori fitting, theta_hat = argmin[-sum_e log p(y_e | H_e(x_e(theta))) - log p(theta)], jointly across studies rather than one parameter set per paper, following the biological chain (yeast dynamics, then protozoa-to-digestion, then hex RNAi, then cellu RNAi, then terminal dose-response), with directly reported quantities fixed first, multiple starting points per block, and each study keeping its own dose schedule and control. Validation is reproduction before prediction: seven published experiments were reproduced by the model before it was used to predict TermiTox. Real time was anchored by simulating a reference compound through the same two models — hexaflumuron, chosen because both individual and colony data exist — giving a model-time ratio of 137/120 = 1.14 that converts Im and Han's 56-day arena collapse into ~65 days for TermiTox at ~10^4 termites and Tsunoda's 9-month field result into ~10.3 months, with the dose converted to a bait loading of 2.03e9 cells per g dry bait, or ~5.1% w/w at 4e10 cells per g lyophilised preparation.","software":"RNAiWeave, a local web application that turns one target gene sequence into ranked, traceable hairpin RNAi candidates. It does sliding-window fragment filtering (default arm 300-400 nt, GC 30-60%, 21-nt siRNA window, all adjustable) screening out homopolymers, low complexity and tandem repeats with siRNA features computed once and reused via prefix sums; an activity estimate from four features reported in the published dsRIP study (terminal thermodynamic asymmetry, antisense self-folding, antisense GC and others); off-target screening against a local FASTA or RefSeq RNA scope that retains matching positions and records; and full-precursor folding in ViennaRNA. The structure score H is an explicit weighted formula over seven quantities (inter-arm stem coverage R at weight 0.50, linker-pairing burden J, MFE-per-nucleotide suitability E benchmarked to a project reference of 0.80 kcal/mol/nt, equilibrium probability of the MFE structure P, 21-nt unpaired-window accessibility U, overall paired fraction F, and a penalty for unexpected pairs X), so a reader can see exactly why one candidate outranked another. Environmental persistence is modelled separately as first-order decay with DT50 and DT90, with a Q10 temperature correction and literature reference scenarios (15-28 h for DvSnf7 RNA in agricultural soils, 56-72 h for non-bioactive dsRNA in water-sediment microcosms). Exports are FASTA, CSV, versioned JSON, dot-bracket and SVG. The team is scrupulous about limits: without off-target screening the output is labelled a preview ranking with sequence safety 'not assessed', and they state plainly that they have not compared knockdown efficacy or runtime against dsRIP. Model code is public at gitlab.igem.org/2026/peking/-/tree/main/Model_code.","stack":["Python","GROMACS (CHARMM36-jul2022, TIP3P)","PROPKA3","ChimeraX","ViennaRNA / RNAplot","NumPy / SciPy ODE solvers","custom agent-based simulator","local web app (RNAiWeave)","NCBI RefSeq / local BLAST-style off-target search"],"techniques":["all-atom molecular dynamics","pKa prediction and constant-protonation-state MD","membrane-bilayer simulation with semi-isotropic pressure coupling","protein-protein dimer MD for oligomerisation tendency","salt-bridge and distance trajectory analysis","cohort-structured ODE modelling","logistic growth with shared carrying capacity","delay / convolution kernel modelling of oral RNAi","first-order lag chains (mRNA to protein to function)","maximum a posteriori parameter estimation with literature priors","structural identifiability assessment","minimal-model construction from evidence","literature benchmark reproduction (7 experiments)","spatially explicit agent-based simulation","stochastic tunnel-network generation","coarse-grained weighted agents with resolution convergence check","contact-process trophallaxis modelling","multi-seed stochastic replication with quantile bands","cross-scale parameter handoff (individual to colony)","reference-compound anchoring of model time to real time","RNA secondary-structure thermodynamics","multi-criteria weighted scoring","first-order environmental fate modelling with Q10 correction"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education was pitched per audience: a 'Code of Life' session at Huangchenggen Primary School on 13 April 2026 explaining DNA, genes and proteins with locally resonant analogies (the double helix as a twisted Chinese fried dough twist) followed by hands-on strawberry DNA extraction with Grade 6 pupils using dish soap, salt and ethanol; lab visits connecting textbook content to a working research environment; interactive games on termites, evolution and biodiversity; a May Day fun fair co-hosted with PKUHSC; and a Biodiversity Fair booth, reaching primary and middle school students, university students, families and the general public.","ihp":"The origin story is unusually concrete and honest: a team member looked up at a century-old campus building and saw termite tunnels inside a wooden beam no maintenance record had noted, and the team then realised every member came from a termite-affected region (Beijing, Sichuan, Fujian, Shanghai, Chongqing, Suzhou). Before any protocol was drafted they ran a questionnaire across ages, backgrounds and regions in China and overseas, collecting 539 valid responses; respondents rated heritage-building termite risk at 7.99 out of 8 and named three priorities — early-warning monitoring, low environmental impact, and target specificity — which the team acknowledge essentially outline the final project. Fifteen students ran a closed-loop review every Saturday evening from April to October 2026, feeding ~17 deep consultations with entomologists, heritage conservators, frontline control officers, RNAi industry people, PIs and past iGEMers and judges. They record what they killed as well as what they built: broad-spectrum pesticides were ruled out as leaving residues unacceptable for sites like the Forbidden City, and crude biocontrol strains were ruled out as too blunt for ancient wooden halls, each discarded idea costing weeks. Community work included six gatherings (NCIM meetup, Synbiopunk-CCiC Dalian, the 1st Grand APiC where TermiTox won Best Project, Synbio Challenge Shenzhen, the Peking-Rice International HP Summit they co-organised with 50+ universities, and the SZU green-bio roundtable).","realWorld":"The application is cultural-heritage conservation — the Forbidden City, old temples and traditional courtyard houses — where residue-free, species-specific control matters more than speed. The modelling fed directly into deliverables: the colony model's counter-intuitive finding that Strain B must be *kept* in the bait when Strain A is added (because withdrawing B lets surviving larvae become replacement queens and the colony recovers) is implementable only with a refillable bait station, which the team designed as hardware; and the finding that multiple bait stations break the distance gradient and remove spatial refuges became a stated deployment principle for placing several recoverable stations around a protected structure. The quantitative deliverable is a usable specification: ~5% w/w dry yeast loading, ~65 days to collapse for a constrained colony of order 10^4 termites, ~10-10.5 months for a field colony of several hundred thousand.","partners":["Peking University","PKUHSC (Peking University Health Science Center)","Huangchenggen Primary School","Rice University (co-organised International HP Summit)","Shenzhen University (SZU green-bio roundtable)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6366/wiki/model/quick-view/termitox-model-whole-picture-v5.webp","caption":"The whole picture of the TermiTox multiscale model: molecular dynamics of the pH-gated LLO mutant, a cohort-ODE individual model of yeast persistence through payload release to functional decline, and a spatially explicit agent-based colony model of trophallactic spread, with each scale's output feeding the next.","credit":"Team Peking, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6366/wiki/model/colony-scale/figure-08-spatial-progression-one-bait.avif","caption":"Figure 8: spatial progression with one bait station. Columns are treatment days 10-120, rows are worker cohorts grouped by home module, and the three stacked panels show ever-exposed fraction, payload burden in a no-damage tracer run, and functional-worker fraction. Distant modules are exposed later and stay functional longer, acting as spatial refuges — a result that only appears because the nest geometry is modelled explicitly instead of as an SIR epidemic.","credit":"Team Peking, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6366/wiki/project/dry-design/model-validation-seven-literature-benchmarks-v2.avif","caption":"Seven published experiments reproduced by the individual-level model before it was used to predict anything about the team's own system — on yeast persistence, protozoa-dependent digestion and oral RNAi.","credit":"Team Peking, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6366/wiki/model/molecular-scale/figure-03-acidic-triad-closeup.avif","caption":"The acidic triad (D208/E247/D320) of H311A-LLO under acidic (left) and neutral (right) conditions. The salt-bridge network holds at pH 5.5 and separates at pH 7.4, supporting the safety premise that the pore-forming toxin is active only inside acidic protozoan food vacuoles — an allosteric effect, since the mutation site sits 17-18 Angstrom away and never contacts the triad.","credit":"Team Peking, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Before writing a single equation, build an evidence map: a table listing every process you want to model, the published experiment that constrains it, what that experiment can and cannot separate, and a verdict of identifiable / composite / not identifiable — then build only the smallest model those data support, and carry multiple scenarios where the verdict is 'not identifiable' instead of asserting one. Then anchor model time to reality by simulating a well-documented reference compound through the same pipeline.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/peking/","https://2026.igem.wiki/peking/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/peking/software/","https://2026.igem.wiki/peking/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/peking/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/peking/results/","https://2026.igem.wiki/peking/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/peking/education/"],"rank":21},"6379":{"team":"NCKU-Tainan","id":"6379","section":"Undergrad","country":"Taiwan","village":"Infectious Diseases","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/ncku-tainan/","projectTitle":"Capture: detecting and inhibiting Pseudomonas aeruginosa quorum-sensing signals","tagline":"A US$54 to US$161 single-cuvette fluorescence reader, and a browser app that turns its counts into an AHL concentration with a 95% confidence interval.","summary":"NCKU-Tainan targeted the acyl-homoserine lactone signals that Pseudomonas aeruginosa uses to coordinate toxin release and biofilm formation in healthcare-associated infections, with two systems reading the same molecule: one that detects the signal and reports the infection, and one that inhibits it with published single-stranded DNA aptamers acting as molecular sponges. To read their GFP reporter without booking a shared plate reader in another building they built CAPTURE-Screen, a single-cuvette fluorescence reader in two versions, 3D-printed and laser-cut, costing 21 to 65 times less than an open-source plate reader. LasReader, a browser application, completes the chain by fitting a weighted four-parameter logistic calibration, deriving limits of detection from the blanks and returning each sample's concentration with an approximate confidence interval.","awards":["Best Hardware — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Infectious Diseases Project — Winner"],"dry":{"frameworks":"The hardware page opens by deriving its requirements from the assay rather than from an instrument wish list: 200 uL of sfGFP culture per reaction, read every hour for six hours at 37 C, benchmarked against the plate-reader standard of 485/510 nm, and cheap enough to rebuild. The modelling is split into three parts that each serve a different part of the team (an inhibition model for the wet lab, an imaging model for the software, a fluorescence model for the hardware). Software, hardware and model are written as one workflow, with LasReader checking the reader, showing which tube to read next, and keeping every saved curve with its limit of detection and usable range.","dataviz":"Plan-view and cut-away optical diagrams drawn to scale with a stated pixel-to-millimetre ratio; an interactive exploded view of the instrument; counts-versus-condition plots that always show the emission channel beside the scatter channel; a calibration page in the app that renders the fitted curve as a PNG alongside the CSV export; a step bar at the top of every CAPTURE-Screen page showing the reader status, the number of calibration runs, how many produced a usable curve, and whether Measure is ready.","datascience":"The instrument is honest about what its numbers are. Readings are raw sensor counts from an AS7341 ten-channel spectral sensor, with F4 (515 nm) as the emission channel and F3 (480 nm) reported beside it as the scatter channel, because the team found that dense suspensions give a few counts of F4 with no reporter present once F3 passes about 46 and none below about 33, so a few counts alone are not evidence of GFP. Excitation and emission are separated by angle (detection at 90 degrees) and by colour (the sensor's own bands), with no emission filter, and a light trap whose end wall slopes at about 41 degrees turns transmitted blue up into the roof rather than back at the sample. Every measurement cycle begins and ends with a dark read, and under the shield every channel must read exactly zero or the cycle is void. Repeatability is quantified at the level that actually varies: five re-insertions of one tube gave 0.76% standard deviation at about 50 counts. Validation is comparative rather than self-referential, with one batch of sfGFP culture at five dilutions plus medium and a non-fluorescent culture read on the team's reader and on a SpectraMax M3 on the same day, ranking the tubes the same way, with the green reading rising from 2.44 to 86.44 counts and about 104 counts per unit OD600 across the three denser tubes. The team states plainly that counts from the two readers are not interchangeable, and reports the failures: the laser-cut build could not distinguish the AHL sensor strain from cells without sfGFP, and the 3D-printed build read zero on its emission channel for that strain. LasReader carries the statistics. It requires at least four concentrations and two blanks as the minimum for a four-parameter curve and a limit of detection, and fits a weighted four-parameter logistic in which EC50 is fitted as its logarithm to keep it positive and the Hill slope is bounded between 0.05 and 20, with blanks entering at zero concentration so they fix the baseline directly. Weighting is used because replicates scatter more at high signal than at low, and the uncertainty of the fitted curve is propagated through the Jacobian of the model derivatives with a diagonal weight matrix, which is what produces the approximate 95% confidence interval on every reported concentration. Detection limits follow the blank-based convention, LOD as the inverse curve evaluated at the blank mean plus three blank standard deviations and LOQ at ten, with documented fallbacks when every blank reads identically, and the usable range starting at whichever is higher, the LOD or the lowest standard, so that a sample can clear the LOD and still be reported as below the usable range. Exports are auditable: one CSV with every reading, every exclusion and its reason, and every result, plus the curve as a PNG, with a curve's own exclusions kept with the curve in its JSON backup. The mechanistic modelling matches this care, with two parameters fitted to swarming data and uncertainty assessed by 400 joint draws combining plate-level bootstrap resampling with uncertain model inputs and refitting each time (296 successful), reporting 5th to 95th percentile ranges, PRCC sensitivity indices, and the explicit statement that these are effective values and not confidence intervals for measured biochemical constants.","software":"LasReader, a browser application with nothing to install, released under the MIT License with source on iGEM GitLab, carrying a research-use-only disclaimer that it reports concentrations inferred from a calibration curve and is not intended for diagnostic use. It works either with CAPTURE-Screen, where the instrument becomes part of the workflow, or with data from any plate reader through the same steps, and the analysis never uses the target's name so it transfers to other biosensors whose rising response suits a 4PL fit. The hardware is released as 53 STL files covering 66 pieces across both versions, with firmware that controls LED timing and integration, plus the laser-cut design, wiring and schematic.","stack":["AS7341 ten-channel spectral sensor (SEN0365 board)","Cree 470 nm excitation LED","UVette 200 uL cuvettes","3D printing (FDM) and laser cutting","SpectraMax M3 as reference instrument","Four-parameter logistic regression (weighted)","Bootstrap resampling and PRCC sensitivity analysis","Browser-based analysis app (MIT licence)"],"techniques":["Dark read at the start and end of every cycle, voided if non-zero","Scatter channel reported alongside the emission channel","Re-insertion repeatability as a stated percentage","Side-by-side benchmarking against a commercial plate reader","Weighted 4PL calibration with bounded Hill slope","Confidence intervals propagated through the fit Jacobian","Blank-derived LOD and LOQ with documented fallbacks","Usable range set by the higher of LOD and lowest standard","Auditable CSV export of every exclusion and its reason","Bootstrap plus input-uncertainty joint refitting","PRCC parameter sensitivity"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education work includes a board game and an online game alongside a documented education programme, a promotion page and a survey.","ihp":"A meet-with-experts programme fed the project's scope and its claims. Prof. Nan-Si Li's framing, that at this stage the project detects signals and does not diagnose infections, is quoted directly in the software's own disclaimer, so the limit on the claim is visible inside the tool rather than only on the wiki.","realWorld":"The problem is framed around healthcare-associated infections, where P. aeruginosa resists many antibiotics, releases tissue-damaging toxins and forms biofilms that antibiotics struggle to cross, all behaviours that depend on cells coordinating through chemical signals. The instrument's justification is operational: a shared plate reader is booked, scheduled and in one building, while either build can sit next to the incubator. Cost is given against a named alternative, at most US$161 for the 3D-printed build and US$54 for the laser-cut one versus under US$3,500 for a published open-source plate reader, with the point that anyone with the source files can rebuild it. The reader is positioned for the commonest reading in synthetic biology, green fluorescence from a GFP reporter in a liquid sample, and for cell-free portable sensors that hold no cells at all.","partners":["Prof. Nan-Si Li","National Cheng Kung University"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6379/wiki/hardware/hardware.avif","caption":"CAPTURE-Screen, the team's single-cuvette fluorescence reader for GFP reporter cultures, built so it can sit next to the incubator instead of competing for a shared plate reader in another building.","credit":"Team NCKU-Tainan, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6379/wiki/hardware/printed-run-1-cuvette-in.avif","caption":"A 200 uL UVette loaded into the 3D-printed build. Excitation enters from the side and the AS7341 detector reads at 90 degrees, with no emission filter; the colour separation is the sensor's own.","credit":"Team NCKU-Tainan, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6379/wiki/haddwarelacerreader/haddwarelacerreader/front.avif","caption":"The laser-cut version of the reader in its own enclosure, costed at US$54 against under US$3,500 for the open-source plate reader the team benchmarked against.","credit":"Team NCKU-Tainan, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6379/wiki/software/curve.avif","caption":"LasReader's calibration view. A weighted four-parameter logistic curve is fitted with the blanks fixing the baseline, limits of detection and quantification are derived from the blanks, and each sample inside the usable range is returned with an approximate 95% confidence interval.","credit":"Team NCKU-Tainan, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Ship the analysis with the instrument: a calibration that fits a weighted 4PL, derives its detection limit from the blanks, propagates a confidence interval onto every reported concentration, and exports every excluded reading with its reason turns a cheap reader's raw counts into a number someone else can audit.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/ncku-tainan/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/ncku-tainan/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/ncku-tainan/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/ncku-tainan/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/ncku-tainan/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/ncku-tainan/human-practices"],"rank":33},"6381":{"team":"UCL","id":"6381","section":"Undergrad","country":"United Kingdom","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/ucl/","projectTitle":"SHELLter — capturing cisplatin from patient urine with a chelator made from shellfish waste","tagline":"A point-of-care cartridge that chelates platinum chemotherapy drugs out of patient urine, with the chelator made enzymatically from crab shell.","summary":"About half of each cisplatin dose leaves the patient in urine within days, and UK hospital effluent is not treated for cytotoxics at all. SHELLter intercepts it at the point of care with a monoacetylchitosan chelating ligand produced from shellfish-processing waste by an engineered SmChiA-VcCDA fusion enzyme. The dry lab is presented as four Python files on an interactive laptop — kinetic_model.py, docking_simulation.py, life_cycle_assessment.py and techno_economic_analysis.py — and all four feed each other: the kinetic model sets reaction conditions and predicts how downstream purification affects product yield, that yield drives the techno-economic cost per gram, and the same mass balance underpins the openLCA life cycle assessment. The docking study is a rigorously controlled computational experiment with negative controls, a pre-specified acceptance rule, multiple-comparison correction and a stated power analysis.","awards":["Best Model — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Integrated Human Practices — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Sustainable Development Impact — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Bioremediation Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Four models, deliberately coupled. (1) KINETIC MODEL — a mechanistic ODE system rather than an empirical fit, chosen precisely because the fusion enzyme is novel and PpChi is barely characterised, so no dataset exists to fit against. It is built from inhibited Michaelis-Menten forms: competitive inhibition for product rebinding, and noncompetitive inhibition for process impurities where, lacking any single inhibition constant for a mixture, they substitute chitin's measured protein-holding capacity (Cm = 0.032573 g/g) times substrate concentration as the rate-limiting term, giving dP/dt = kcat*ET*S / [Km(1 + I/Ki + D/(Cm*S)) + S(1 + D/(Cm*S))]. SmChiA's non-Michaelian processive mechanism on insoluble chitin is handled by converting polymer mass to N-acetylglucosamine residues (R0 = S0/203 g/mol), and PpChi's substrate is converted to GlcN-GlcN-GlcNAc motifs with the motif yield derived from degree of acetylation, Y = DA(1-DA)^2, and an average residue weight W = DA*203 + (1-DA)*161. Environmental dependence is interpolated with double-sigmoid rate modifiers for pH (F) and temperature (G) multiplying kcat, with all nine fitted sigmoid constants tabulated per enzyme, and thermal enzyme decay modelled with Bigelow's law. Twelve assumptions are tabulated with their impact AND their limitation, and the most influential are tested in a dedicated Choice Sensitivity section. (2) DOCKING SIMULATION — a ten-stage pipeline built as a controlled experiment, which is what makes it exceptional. Four fusion constructs (varying only the two things literature could not settle: domain order and His-tag terminus; all 1015 residues, GGGGSGGGGS inter-domain linker, GGGGS tag linker, native signal peptides retained) were each predicted five times by AlphaFold 3 with different seeds, giving twenty structures. Two design rules govern everything: every measurement is a difference taken WITHIN a single predicted structure, never between structures, because across seeds the CDA domain moved 25.6 +/- 11.0 Angstrom relative to ChiA so a between-structure comparison would measure AlphaFold rather than the protein; and every effect is measured against an apo' control in which the stochastic relaxation is re-run with nothing changed but the random seed, giving a genuine noise floor. Active-site residues were MEASURED rather than quoted: heavy atoms within 4.5 Angstrom of a bound chito-oligosaccharide across multiple crystal structures (1EHN, 1NH6 for SmChiA; 4NZ1, 4NZ3, 4OUI for VcCDA, 98.7-99.8% identity), with a residue required to appear in at least two independent structures, a 6.0 Angstrom criterion defining the mobile cleft, ligands under ten heavy atoms ignored to exclude buffer and cryoprotectant, and SIX NEGATIVE-CONTROL structures expected to return nothing, which returned zero contacts. Relaxation is Rosetta FastRelax under ref2015 via PyRosetta, five rounds, with a movemap freeing only the ~400 residues within 10 Angstrom of either cleft, computed once per replicate from the apo structure and reused unchanged across all four conditions so that apo and holo are compared over an identical mobile set. Substrates (tetraacetylchitotetraose, 57 heavy atoms, for the chitinase groove; diacetylchitobiose, 29 heavy atoms, for the deacetylase pocket) were built from PubChem with RDKit, parameterised with Meeko, and verified atom by atom. Docking is AutoDock Vina at exhaustiveness 32 with three independent seeds per receptor-substrate pair, 148 searches total, into a box centred on the contacting residues padded 6 Angstrom and clamped 18-32 Angstrom with a guard flagging any box centre more than 5 Angstrom from the cleft centroid. (3) LIFE CYCLE ASSESSMENT — a cradle-to-use LCA of four process steps (chitin extraction from shellfish waste, fusion production in E. coli, ligand production, device use), built in two independent halves that must agree: a component mass balance tracking every stream in every unit operation, and an openLCA model reproducing that arithmetic separately. Functional unit is one treatment course: one patient, five cycles, five cartridges per cycle, 60 kg of urine carrying 0.336 g of drug, with the baseline being the status quo of untreated discharge. (4) TECHNO-ECONOMIC MODEL — built on the same central mass balance, with a localised impurity-prediction part that feeds back into project design and a full cost-of-goods and discounted-cash-flow analysis.","dataviz":"The model landing page is an interactive laptop whose screen lists the four models as Python filenames, which the reader clicks to open — a small piece of framing that tells the reader immediately that the dry lab is four programs, not one vague 'model'. The kinetic results are presented as parameter sweeps with the optimum marked by a dot on each curve: time to 50% and 90% substrate conversion against temperature for each enzyme separately (PpChi 45 C, SmChiA 43 C, VcCDA 39 C) and a two-dimensional temperature-by-pH heatmap for the fusion (optimum 43 C, pH 6.1) drawn in the Okabe-Ito colour-blind-safe palette with darker colours for faster conversion — the team say so in the caption. Figure 20 is the decisive one: an enzyme molar-ratio sweep from 0.1 to 40 at constant total enzyme mass, showing a 15:1 SmChiA:VcCDA optimum roughly twice as fast as the 1:1 ratio a fusion is structurally locked into. The docking pipeline is drawn as a ten-stage flow diagram where each box names the stage, what it does and the software used, with stage 0 (measuring active sites from crystal structures) and stage 3 (building substrates from PubChem) shown as completing before the work they feed. Structures are shown in an embedded 3Dmol.js v2.5.5 viewer with a toggle between colour-by-part and colour-by-pLDDT confidence, and every AlphaFold figure caption carries the warning 'NOT experimentally determined or validated'. The LCA opens with a calibrated comparison instead of an abstract number: one SHELLter course emits 19.76 kg CO2eq, about 36 caffe lattes, 2.1 CT scans or one chemotherapy cycle — immediately followed by a note that these equivalence figures come from papers using different impact methods and databases and are 'given only for contextual perspective'.","datascience":"The statistical design of the docking study is the standout. The initial pose-convergence test (maximum pairwise RMSD across seeds) was found to conflate two different failure modes — seeds genuinely scattering versus a majority agreeing with one outlier — and was replaced mid-run with a rule written down BEFORE the run finished and then applied uniformly: a pose is accepted only if a strict majority of seeds agree within 2.0 Angstrom, the best-scoring pose falls inside that majority, at least 60% of its heavy atoms lie within 5 Angstrom of the cleft, and it clears every face of the search box by at least 1 Angstrom; every non-unanimous replicate got two further seeds. Results are reported with explicit counts and the honest verdict for each of five pre-set questions: both sites still bind (35 of 40 dockings accepted); each site responds structurally to its OWN substrate and not the other (25 of 32 paired comparisons, p = 0.0021, with Holm-Bonferroni correction cited); both sites can be occupied simultaneously (16 of 20 replicates); occupying one site produces no detectable effect at the other by three independent measurements, with the effect size BOUNDED below the apo' noise floor and the Rosetta additivity residual below ~4 REU; and domain order is reported as 'Not resolved at this sample size' with the explicit gloss that this means insufficient power, not absence of an effect. They then do the power analysis properly: at 9-12 replicates per group the null can only be rejected on unanimity, at 16 one may disagree, at 20 three may, so twenty per group is where the design starts to be able to detect what it currently cannot — with the per-step compute cost given (7.4 min per ligand docking, 16-24 min per relaxation on four cores) so the extension is actionable. Ten numbered assumptions are tabulated with impact and limitation, including that the VcCDA catalytic Zn2+ is simply absent from predicted structures (which they offer as the likely cause of DACB poses sitting partly off the pocket), that Vina affinities 'should be read as a ranking aid, not as delta-G', and that the docking score's 8 Angstrom interatomic cutoff could not register a direct 34-47 Angstrom cross-site interaction even if one existed — which is precisely why they also ran the cutoff-free Rosetta additivity test. The models genuinely changed decisions: the kinetic model's 15:1 ratio finding and the fusion-vs-dual-enzyme-vs-PpChi comparison table (time to 90% conversion: fusion 2.05 h, dual single-pot 1.17 h, dual multi-pot 1.84 h, PpChi 12.68 h) reframed the construct choice; the impurity model showed that going from 6 to 8 downstream unit operations nearly doubled product at 10 hours (11.44 to 22.40 mM), and feeding that into the TEA gave a cost per gram of chitobiose for each of five flowsheets (78.66, 84.57, 59.98, 172.62, 180.01 GBP/g), selecting PEG precipitation over chromatography on the reasoning that the fusion is not a biopharmaceutical so its purity target exists only to improve function. The DCF analysis, solved with GoalSeek to NPV = 0 at a 12% discount rate, gives a 17-year payback and a unit price of GBP 146.45, contextualised as ~1.9% of the GBP 7,670 NHS cost of treating one patient with systemic anti-cancer therapy.","software":"The kinetic model is released on the team's software GitLab at gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/ucl/model. The docking pipeline is parameterised and scripted end to end, which is what makes the stated extension (add seeds, re-run the same scripts) credible. Structures are presented in-browser with 3Dmol.js v2.5.5 (BSD-3-Clause) with a pLDDT colouring toggle. The LCA is built in openLCA alongside an independent spreadsheet mass balance as a cross-check.","stack":["Python","SciPy ODE integration","AlphaFold 3 (AlphaFold Server)","PyRosetta / Rosetta FastRelax (ref2015)","AutoDock Vina","Meeko","RDKit","3Dmol.js v2.5.5","openLCA","Excel / GoalSeek (discounted cash flow)","PubChem","Protein Data Bank","Benchling"],"techniques":["mechanistic ODE enzyme kinetics","competitive and noncompetitive inhibited Michaelis-Menten kinetics","processive-enzyme substrate conversion (polymer to residue/motif)","double-sigmoid environmental rate modifiers for pH and temperature","Bigelow thermal inactivation","multi-dimensional parameter sweeps for process optimisation","enzyme ratio optimisation / rate-limiting step identification","mass-balance error checking as a solver test","structure prediction with multi-seed replication","within-structure paired comparison design","stochastic-relaxation noise-floor control (apo')","active-site definition measured from crystal structures with negative controls","localised movemap relaxation","molecular docking (AutoDock Vina) with multi-seed convergence acceptance rules","induced-fit measurement","dual-occupancy / additivity testing","Holm-Bonferroni multiple-comparison correction","statistical power analysis and sample-size planning","effect-size bounding when a null is not rejected","life cycle assessment (cradle-to-use, openLCA)","component mass balance with independent reproduction","techno-economic analysis","cost-of-goods and flowsheet comparison","discounted cash flow, NPV and IRR analysis"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"An education programme with its own substantial page, built around two recurring illustrated characters (Cisplatin and Shelly) who appear throughout the wiki, including in the loading animation — a consistent visual voice that makes a technical oncology-waste project approachable. The team's public-facing identity extends to Instagram and a LinkedIn company page for SHELLter.","ihp":"The strongest part of the project's non-technical work, and genuinely regulatory rather than decorative. Conversations with NHS England's healthcare and sustainability teams uncovered a specific, exploitable regulatory gap: Water UK forbids direct discharge of cytotoxic and cytostatic medications to foul sewers under any circumstances, including rinsing their containers, but patient bodily discharges containing 'metabolised medications' are permitted — while the actual degree of metabolism varies from 10-97%, giving patient discharge rates of roughly 3-90%, so metabolic-rate statistics can be selected to bypass waste-management rules. Dr Anne Woolridge explained that England's focus is on protecting personnel from cytotoxic exposure rather than downstream treatment, visible in the Pan London Cytotoxic Policy; the team then cite evidence that even tertiary membrane-bioreactor treatment removes only up to 51% of hydrophilic cisplatin, and that 22% of platinum compounds were detected in the outflows of a major UK hospital (Derriford, Plymouth) after conventional treatment. Anne O'Connor and Dr Kumud Kantilal established why point-of-care capture is the right intervention: outpatient chemotherapy is becoming the norm, but patient bodily fluids remain hazardous for up to seven days after discharge, so a large fraction of excreted cytotoxic residue can never reach any hospital treatment system. Joe Burton and Dr Sharon Pfleger surfaced a gap in NHS clinical-waste sustainability priorities. Stakeholders including Dr Jay Burt, Professor Louis Grandjean, Dr Anne Woolridge, Professor Laurence Lovat, Dr Sophie Fridman and Alex Senechal independently asked for the economic case, which is explicitly why the techno-economic model exists and why it is structured to produce a cost per unit of environmental benefit.","realWorld":"The commercial and environmental case is quantified rather than asserted. The LCA's functional unit is a real clinical course (one patient, five cycles, fifteen cartridges, 60 kg of urine carrying 0.336 g of drug) measured against the actual status quo of untreated discharge, and the headline is framed as a trade: 19.76 kg CO2eq to prevent an emission that currently happens unchecked, roughly a fifth added to the ~100 kg CO2eq of the five-cycle treatment it cleans up. The objective is stated as ecotoxicity avoided per unit of climate and energy burden, with unit operations ranked by their contribution to each impact category. The techno-economic model selects the full nine-step downstream train (centrifugation, resuspension, homogenisation, flocculation, centrifugation, depth filtration, PEG precipitation, tangential flow filtration, resolubilisation) on cost-per-gram grounds, and gives a sellable unit price of GBP 146.45 at NPV = 0 with a 17-year payback, deliberately benchmarked against NHS treatment cost. The feedstock is shellfish-processing waste, which makes the chelator itself a valorised waste stream.","partners":["University College London","UCL Department of Biochemical Engineering","UCL Faculty of Engineering Sciences","VaxHub","Resilience","Ribbon","NHS England healthcare and sustainability teams"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6381/wiki/dockingpipeline.avif","caption":"The ten-stage docking pipeline, with each box naming the stage, what it does and the software used. Stage 0 defines the active sites by measuring them from substrate-bound crystal structures independently of any model built later, and stage 3 builds and verifies the substrates from PubChem — both complete before the work they feed into begins.","credit":"Team UCL, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6381/wiki/figure-20-km.avif","caption":"Figure 20: the enzyme-ratio parameter sweep that settled a construct decision. Holding total enzyme mass constant at 0.111 g/L, the SmChiA:VcCDA ratio was swept from 0.1 to 40; the 90%-conversion optimum sits at 15:1, roughly twice as fast as the 1:1 ratio a fusion protein is structurally locked into, identifying SmChiA as the rate-limiting step.","credit":"Team UCL, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6381/wiki/figure-18-km.avif","caption":"Figure 18: time to 50% and 90% substrate conversion for the fusion enzyme across temperature and pH, drawn in the Okabe-Ito colour-blind-safe palette with darker colours for faster conversion and a dot marking the optimum (43 C, pH 6.1). The surface shows the fusion optimum is weighted far more toward SmChiA than VcCDA.","credit":"Team UCL, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6381/wiki/fusion.avif","caption":"AlphaFold 3 model of the ChiA-CDA-His fusion, coloured by prediction confidence: two compact well-predicted domains with an extended low-confidence loop arcing above them. The team use this honestly — because the CDA domain moved 25.6 +/- 11.0 Angstrom relative to ChiA across five seeds, every measurement in the study is a difference taken within a single structure rather than between them.","credit":"Team UCL, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Run a computational study as a real experiment: define your measurement target by measuring it (active-site residues from crystal structures, with negative controls that must return nothing) rather than quoting a number, include a do-nothing control that captures the method's own noise (re-run the stochastic relaxation with only the seed changed), write the acceptance rule down before you finish the run, and when a comparison fails to reach significance say 'not resolved at this sample size' and state how many replicates would be needed.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/ucl/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucl/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucl/kinetic-model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucl/kinetic-model-structure/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucl/kinetic-model-results/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucl/docking-simulation/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucl/life-cycle-assessment/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucl/techno-economic-analysis/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucl/techno-economic-analysis-results/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucl/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucl/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucl/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ucl/education/"],"rank":28},"6389":{"team":"UFABC-Brazil","id":"6389","section":"Overgrad","country":"Brazil","village":"Diagnostics","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/","projectTitle":"Patchlepsy","tagline":"A paper-read toehold biosensor that gives people with epilepsy the one thing they do not have: warning time.","summary":"Patchlepsy is a toehold-switch biosensor designed to detect three tRNA-derived fragments (5'GlyGCC, 5'AlaTGC, 5'GluCTC) whose plasma levels rise before seizures in temporal lobe epilepsy, as reported by Hogg et al. (2019). Each switch releases a different chromoprotein reporter (mRFP1, AmilCP, fwYellow), read by a low-cost ESP32 plus AS7341 multispectral device and logged in a mobile app. To the team's knowledge these are the first toehold switches targeting tRFs rather than microRNAs. The cell-free assays never activated in either a CFPS extract kit or PURExpress, and the team publishes that failure with its two mechanistic hypotheses; the whole-cell system did work, with the GlyGCC/mRFP1 switch reaching a fold change of up to 23 in the presence of its trigger. The whole wiki is bilingual English and Portuguese.","awards":["Best Integrated Human Practices — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Diagnostics Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Design followed the Green et al. (2014) toehold architecture with the recognition domains rewritten as the complement of each target tRF, and domains c and d constrained by explicit sequence patterns (c defined first as N4VVVVVVVGAGGAGAWWWWN2AUG, then revised to N4VVVVVVVAGAGGAGAWWWWN2AUG with an added adenine to widen the RBS, with A4/C4/G4/U4/K6/M6/R6/S6/W6/Y6 runs and stop codons forbidden in domain d). Candidates were generated by an in-house script, 30 in the first round and 80 per target in the second, and ranked in NUPACK on equilibrium probability, predicted folding, free energy of toehold alone versus toehold-target complex, and probability of strand displacement. Structures were built in RNAComposer, docked in HADDOCK3, and the complexes simulated in GROMACS 2024 (steepest-descent minimisation, 100 ps NVT, 1 ns NPT, AMBER99SB-ILDN force field, explicit TIP3P water in a periodic dodecahedral box, 0.15 M Na+/Cl-, Particle Mesh Ewald, 1.0 nm cutoffs), reporting RMSD, radius of gyration, hydrogen-bond counts and per-nucleotide RMSF. Three switches are deposited in the Registry.","dataviz":"DataSUS and IBGE epidemiology is visualised as time series of hospitalisations and costs (2020-2026), choropleth maps of Brazil by state and of the seven ABC Paulista municipalities normalised per 10,000 inhabitants using IBGE SIDRA Tabela 6579, stacked contributions of epilepsy to all nervous-system disease hospitalisations and costs, Likert distributions for the 44-respondent survey, a before-and-after SWOT matrix pair, and a two-axis stakeholder interest-versus-influence matrix built from scores each interviewee gave on a 0-10 scale.","datascience":"Two reproducible pipelines, both published on GitLab. The tRF quantification pipeline reanalyses the Hogg et al. (2019) small RNA-seq dataset across two collection sites: fastp preprocessing (minimum Phred 20, 15-50 nt), Bowtie2 alignment to a tRNA reference in --very-sensitive-local mode reporting up to 10 alignments per read because of tRNA similarity, and Samtools handling, quantifying at both isoacceptor and individual-fragment level as a built-in consistency check. The cross-reactivity pipeline runs BLASTn of query sequences against a genome panel and classifies alignments by similarity tier; run with three complete tRNA sequences against 150 E. coli genome assemblies it produced 12,480 unique alignments, predominantly moderate similarity, before anything was tested in the chassis.","software":"A Python acquisition and processing application drives the ESP32 and AS7341 across ten spectral channels, with background correction added after the first run saturated channels F2, F4, F5, F6, F7 and Clear at 65,535, and with raw readings preserved separately from background-corrected values for traceability plus an export function. A mobile prototype built in MIT App Inventor records readings, keeps a diary and raises an alert when a previously registered value recurs; the team states clearly that automatic sensor integration and spectral-marker interpretation were not completed.","stack":["NUPACK","RNAComposer","HADDOCK3","GROMACS 2024","AMBER99SB-ILDN / TIP3P","fastp","Bowtie2","Samtools","BLASTn","Python","Arduino / ESP32","AS7341 multispectral sensor","MIT App Inventor","React","GSAP","GitLab"],"techniques":["toehold switch thermodynamic design","RNA-RNA molecular docking","all-atom molecular dynamics (RMSD, Rg, H-bonds, RMSF)","small RNA-seq tRF quantification at isoacceptor and fragment level","BLASTn cross-reactivity screening against a 150-genome panel","3D-printed low-cost spectrophotometry","cell-free (CFPS and PURExpress) and whole-cell reporter assays","DataSUS/IBGE epidemiological analysis","survey-validated SWOT"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Engagement was built around stigma rather than around the technology. The team joined the Marco Roxo awareness walk organised by the Brazilian Epilepsy Association (ABE) in Sao Paulo in March 2026, produced an original documentary, 'Epilepsy: What You Don't See', featuring people living with epilepsy and their relatives, and on 29 September 2026 screened it with ABE followed by a roundtable with a pediatric neurologist (Dr. Daniela Bezerra), a person living with epilepsy (Gustavo Theodoro) and the mother of a child with a rare neurological condition associated with epilepsy (Angelica Akemi). Educational work was gamified: escape rooms in public state schools across the ABC region during Brain Awareness Week (10-14 March 2025, with Pense Brain and faculty, for 9th grade to 3rd year of high school, using puzzles, quizzes and 3D skull and brain models), and a synthetic-biology escape room at UFABC for Biotechnologist Day with LiNA Biotecnologia UFABC in which teams assembled complementary DNA sequences and constructed plasmids. Explanatory flyers were written separately for young people and for older adults, on the reasoning that informational needs differ by group, and they teach bystanders how to assist during a seizure safely. An Introduction to Synthetic Biology mini-course, a poster and talks at the II Brazilian Synthetic Biology Congress, Bio's Start and Semana de Biotecnologia round it out. The team also published a funding guide, 'Overcoming Financial Barriers in Brazil: A Guide to Public and Private Funding', documenting how a parliamentary amendment actually works and how to approach companies in a structured way, because Brazilian teams cannot cover iGEM registration or Jamboree travel from conventional research grants.","ihp":"The IHP is organised as a four-step causal chain and is genuinely integrated rather than consultative. Step one asked whether the problem is real, using DataSUS (SIH/SUS) with IBGE population denominators: epilepsy hospitalisations in Brazil rose from 49,204 in 2020 to 73,222 in 2025 (+48.8%) while their cost to SUS rose from R$ 43,692,171 to R$ 92,460,210 (+111.6%), so cost per admission grew faster than admissions; epilepsy accounts for 28-30% of all nervous-system disease hospitalisations nationally and 40-50% in the team's own ABC Paulista region. Critically, the team reads its own maps against itself, noting that Sao Caetano do Sul, long the highest-HDI municipality in Brazil, also records the most hospitalisations, which more plausibly reflects access to the health system than disease frequency, so 'the real burden is likely greater than what DataSUS is able to capture', and citing IEPS data that average travel time to an ICU bed is 3.3 hours in the Legal Amazon against 0.3 hours elsewhere. Step two put the team's own internal SWOT to the people who would use the device: a survey of 44 people with epilepsy, reached through ABE and approved by a Brazilian Research Ethics Committee, with each SWOT point converted into a Likert question and a rule for confirmation or refutation declared before the results were seen. Two assumptions were refuted and the matrix was redrawn: the expected concern about personal health data moved from weaknesses to strengths, and distrust of a seizure-predicting technology moved from threats to opportunities. Step three was eleven ethics-approved stakeholder interviews across research, clinical practice, industry and public policy, each closing with 0-10 scores for interest and influence that built a stakeholder matrix; the team's own conclusion from it is that the people with most influence over whether Patchlepsy reaches patients are not the technology developers but clinicians, industry and public policy. Step four is where the design actually moved, and the strongest chain is convergent rather than single-source: five stakeholders independently pushed away from a pipetted cell-free reaction, for five different reasons, with Prof. Cintia Marques Coelho (UnB Synthetic Biology Lab) saying the cell-free system is expensive, needs refrigeration, pipetting and controls and would make the device inaccessible, Fabricio Pamplona proposing a strip format and portability from the start, Karen Uchiyama recommending filter paper specifically because it makes the device safer and easier to document for ANVISA, Amanda Mendes do Carmo (clinical research pharmacist, market access) asking for something easy to maintain and carry, and Prof. Danielle Biscaro Pedrolli insisting the test must not depend on the qualification of whoever uses it. The hardware was rebuilt around a filter-paper strip inserted through a slot between the LED and the sensor, with the cell-free reaction embedded in the paper as the declared next step, citing Karlikow et al. (2022), who validated paper-based cell-free toehold assays on patient samples in Recife at US$ 5.48 per test against US$ 11 for RT-qPCR in a freeze-dried, refrigeration-free format. A second chain changed the DNA itself: Danielle flagged that the antibiotic resistance gene in the plasmids rules out home use and complicates disposal, Karen reinforced that ANVISA would require a documented use-and-disposal workflow, and because the team had kept BioBrick prefix and suffix on its toehold plasmids from the start it could produce the constructs as linear DNA with no resistance marker (untested at the deadline, and the team says so). A third chain made leakage the central technical question after Prof. Elibio Rech, Danielle and Luiz Caires independently warned about leakage and physiological tRF concentrations, which is why the team characterised leakage experimentally in its own constructs instead of relying on predictions. Two stakeholder inputs were integrated as honest downgrades rather than features: Prof. Alexandre Kihara made the team distinguish predicting an imminent seizure from monitoring seizure susceptibility, after which they describe their result as a proof of concept of tRF-responsive sensing and not prediction, and Elibio pointed out their tRF evidence comes from one population with gender differences, so they state plainly that they do not yet know for whom these biomarkers work. Dr. Cezzar Santos de Souza, a psychiatrist at CAPS Nucleo de Atencao Casa Aberta in the public system, showed them that for patients with intellectual disabilities who cannot recognise or communicate an aura, an alert is only useful if it reaches somebody else, which, with 93.2% of survey respondents saying early detection would help caregivers, became a committed design change: the alert goes to a registered support network. And because 40.9% said such a technology could itself cause anxiety, they decided the alert must communicate increased risk within a time window plus what to do about it, never a seizure as a certainty, with the user choosing how and whether they are warned.","realWorld":"The real-world framing is unusually concrete on health-system economics and unusually thin on sustainability. Need is grounded in SUS data rather than global prevalence quotes, down to local news reporting that someone is hospitalised for epilepsy every eight hours in the Greater ABC region, and the mechanism of benefit is stated modestly: knowing in advance would not prevent a seizure but could let someone reach a safe place and avoid the admission that drives the cost. The regulatory path was identified only because a stakeholder raised it, and the team says so: after Karen Uchiyama's point about documentation, they established that Patchlepsy would be regulated in Brazil as an in vitro diagnostic under ANVISA RDC 830/2023 and that ANVISA, FDA and EMA harmonise requirements through IMDRF, concluding that the usage and disposal workflow has to be designed together with the device rather than documented afterwards. Any future work with human participants or clinical samples would need CEP/CONEP ethical review; the project itself used synthetic tRF mimics and no patient material. The deployment plan is SUS-oriented: Amanda do Carmo's route is market entry followed by incorporation into public provision, with price justified against the cost of high-cost antiseizure medication, and the team's own cost strategy is to develop an in-house cell-free system because commercial kits are a large part of what makes such a test expensive. There is no business model, no unit economics and no market sizing. There is also no SDG claim anywhere on the wiki, not even a logo wall, which for a diagnostics project with this much public-health data behind it is a missed open goal rather than hand-waving. What is published instead, and what will outlast the Jamboree, is reusable: three Registry parts, two pipelines, the low-cost spectral reader and its software, a fully documented cell-free negative result with its two hypotheses and the troubleshooting route they would take next (linear PCR expression templates instead of circular plasmids), the survey-validated SWOT method, and the Brazilian funding guide. Next technical steps are the cell-free reaction embedded in paper, an intermediate integrase-controlled amplification module proposed after Luiz Caires raised sensitivity, and replacing resistance markers with a plasmid-dependency or auxotrophic selection system following Danielle's suggestion.","partners":["Brazilian Epilepsy Association (ABE) - survey reach and documentary support","Dr. Daniela Fontes Bezerra (pediatric neurologist) - documentary, survey design, clinical perspective","Dr. Cezzar Santos de Souza, CAPS Nucleo de Atencao Casa Aberta (SUS community mental health centre)","Dr. Ana Maria Amorim (pediatric neurology)","Dr. Guilherme Marques (municipal cannabis-derived treatment project)","Prof. Danielle Biscaro Pedrolli, Unesp Araraquara and PI of iGEM Unesp Brazil","Prof. Cintia Marques Coelho, UnB Synthetic Biology Lab","Prof. Elibio Rech (toehold switches and biosensors)","Prof. Alexandre Hiroaki Kihara, ARI-UFABC (neuroscience)","Amanda Mendes do Carmo (clinical research pharmacy, market access, ICESP/ICON)","Karen Uchiyama (pharmaceutical market intelligence)","Luiz Caires, Vyro Biotechnologies; Fabricio Pamplona, Mind the Graph","Pense Brain and LiNA Biotecnologia UFABC","FAPESP, CNPEM, INCT-EngBio, Inova UFABC, FUNDEP (UFMG), MathWorks, Twist Bioscience, IDT, GenScript, Ansa Biotechnologies"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6389/wiki/human-practices/integrated/fluxograma-hp-english.avif","caption":"The four-step integrated human practices workflow: DataSUS epidemiology, SWOT validation with people with epilepsy, stakeholder interviews, and project refinement.","credit":"Team UFABC-Brazil, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6389/wiki/human-practices/integrated/new-fig-18-ing.avif","caption":"The four changes already made to Patchlepsy, each traced back to the survey, the SWOT validation or a named stakeholder interview.","credit":"Team UFABC-Brazil, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6389/wiki/human-practices/integrated/the-stakeholder-influence-mattrix-fig17.avif","caption":"Stakeholder interest-versus-influence matrix, scored 0-10 by the interviewees themselves, which showed the team that clinicians, industry and policy hold more implementation power than technology developers.","credit":"Team UFABC-Brazil, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6389/wiki/human-practices/public-outreach/documentario-toodos.avif","caption":"Premiere of the team's documentary 'Epilepsy: What You Don't See' with the Brazilian Epilepsy Association, followed by a roundtable with a neurologist, a person living with epilepsy and a parent.","credit":"Team UFABC-Brazil, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Copy the survey-validated SWOT: write your internal SWOT first, convert every point into a question your actual users can answer, declare the confirmation or refutation rule before you see the data, then redraw the matrix. UFABC had two assumptions refuted this way, which is exactly the kind of error a team never finds by assessing itself.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/","https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/assets/index-CX6oK0XP.js","https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/wet-lab-results","https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/dry-lab-results","https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/public-outreach","https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/safety-and-security","https://2026.igem.wiki/ufabc-brazil/attributions"],"rank":14},"6391":{"team":"Oxford","id":"6391","section":"Undergrad","country":"United Kingdom","village":"Agriculture","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/oxford/","projectTitle":"NECTAR","tagline":"An end-to-end platform for designing, validating, producing and deploying RNAi interventions, stress-tested on Varroa destructor","summary":"NECTAR is a programmable RNAi pipeline: FORAGER (computational dsRNA design with off-target screening against the Apis mellifera transcriptome), microbial production in yeast, and delivery to hives in a pollen patty. Varroa destructor, the single biggest threat to honeybees, is the first real-world case study. The team built HIVE, an explicit four-step human-practices decision procedure (Hear, Investigate, Verdict, Evaluate) run over six open project questions with 28+ named stakeholders including US EPA/FDA/USDA staff, the Chair of the UK Advisory Committee on Releases to the Environment, and the Secretariat of the Convention on Biological Diversity. Stakeholder evidence changed the chassis (living engineered Snodgrassella alvi to heat-inactivated yeast), the delivery format, the off-target screening stage, the survey instrument and the definition of success.","awards":["Best Wiki — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Integrated Human Practices — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Sustainable Development Impact — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Agriculture Project — Winner"],"dry":{"frameworks":"FORAGER, a three-stage standardised dsRNA design pipeline: target gene identification (most abundant transcripts of well-connected genes, weighted by known Varroa RNAi data), within-gene region selection (endogenous Varroa siRNA sequence features, guide competence, RNAplfold target accessibility, combined as three equally weighted complementary evidence layers rather than one fused score), and off-target analysis. Also a BEEHAVE-based colony population model and a bespoke partial-equilibrium economic model.","dataviz":"Hand-drawn mechanism illustrations throughout (FORAGER stages, the five-step path of a dose through the hive, the SDG goal map), a geocoded stakeholder map with latitude/longitude per interviewee, and per-cycle engineering tables; the wiki is a custom React/Astro-style build with light and dark themes.","datascience":"Construction of a clean Varroa destructor small-RNA dataset from public sequencing, basic population feature analysis of that sRNA pool, sequence feature analysis, whole-region homology and local exact-match screening against the honeybee transcriptome (16-nt strict mapping plus relaxed whole-region similarity), BLAST-based non-target screening, and a documented limitations table stating that the three evidence layers are equally weighted only because no Varroa RNAi efficacy data existed to fit weights.","software":"FORAGER is released with one file per stage and a documented frontmatter/body contract so other teams can re-run it; the HIVE method and its full interview question bank are released under CC BY 4.0. Hive insert and PCR-tube feeding adaptor are downloadable 3D-printable hardware.","stack":["ViennaRNA / RNAplfold","BLAST","Bowtie","BEEHAVE (NetLogo)","Boltz structure prediction","molecular docking","R","Python","React / Astro wiki build"],"techniques":["functional network connectivity analysis (STRING-type)","mRNA abundance weighting","small-RNA population profiling","RNA secondary structure and accessibility prediction","MS2 hairpin array folding optimisation (6% to 67% complete-array folding)","partial-equilibrium economic modelling with supply/demand elasticities","sensitivity analysis"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Buzz In, a three-episode stakeholder podcast built deliberately to put stakeholders who disagreed with each other into contact rather than collecting views in isolation: episode 1 paired Varroa-resistance academic Prof. Stephen Martin with commercial beekeeper Paul Horton on whether to treat at all; episode 2 brought together the CEO of the Australian Honey Bee Industry Council, Amateur Beekeepers Australia and Hive & Wellness; episode 3 set the project against social, environmental and economic lenses with a social scientist, a bee researcher and an agricultural economist. GMO 101, a joint Zoom workshop with NYU Abu Dhabi iGEM on 8 October 2026, measured participation through Nearpod (24 participants, 83% took part). A beekeeper survey received a favourable opinion from a subcommittee of the Oxford Central University Research Ethics Committee (ref MS IDREC 3973787), with public task as the lawful basis and informed consent before questions; 100+ respondents, 63% reported struggling with Varroa at mean severity 5.74/10 and 70% said they would be open to a GMO-based treatment. School sessions at St Clare's summer course were run as a two-way choice exercise (present two delivery routes with honest trade-offs, ask which students would accept, measure the acceptance shift before and after) rather than a lecture. Plus street interviews, a bee campaign, Instagram and TikTok.","ihp":"Oxford's IHP is the strongest kind: a documented decision procedure with a mandatory 'How we implemented the advice to change NECTAR' field on every one of 28+ interview write-ups, and a rule that 'We considered their feedback is not an implementation'. The largest single change is the chassis. Danny Le Feuvre (CEO, Australian Honey Bee Industry Council) and Mike Allerton (VP and Biosecurity Officer, Amateur Beekeepers Australia) both preferred a persistent living engineered Snodgrassella alvi gut symbiont because it minimises beekeeper labour; the team did not simply follow them but took the question to regulators, and Laura Bowden (GM manager, Science and Advice for Scottish Agriculture), Elizabeth Frost (NSW Department of Primary Industries), Tom Hartley (Senior Certification Officer, Soil Association Certification) and the Scottish Government Honey Bee Health Team pushed the opposite way, so the team switched to heat-inactivated, dried engineered yeast and stated plainly what that cost: the persistence that made S. alvi attractive, meaning repeat dosing and more beekeeper labour, against the preference of beekeepers they had interviewed. Austein McLoughlin of the Convention on Biological Diversity Secretariat then confirmed the inactivated product is not a living modified organism under the Cartagena Protocol, but also refused to let the team stop at SDG alignment, pushing them to ask whether NECTAR produces 'measurable improvement' - which is why the sustainability analysis widened to the whole NECTAR lifecycle and built baseline comparisons into the modelling. A joint meeting with Mike Mendelsohn and Alan Reynolds (US EPA), Adam Moyer and Laura Epstein (FDA) and Alan Pearson (USDA) then 'prevented us from treating our shift to heat-inactivated yeast as a universal regulatory shortcut', forcing jurisdiction-by-jurisdiction regulatory mapping instead of one global classification. The deepest economic chain runs through Prof. Wally Thurman (Agricultural and Resource Economics, NC State, interviewed 29 July 2026) and Prof. Brittney Goodrich (Agricultural and Consumer Economics, Illinois, 7 August 2026): Thurman set five methodological commitments (start from an average commercial operation not an industry aggregate; use existing treatments as the counterfactual; assess costs and revenues not survival rates; use simple partial equilibrium; restrict to paid pollination markets), and Goodrich's operation-level cost structure redefined the cost of Varroa to include labour, colony replacement and lost honey and pollination revenue rather than just the price of acaricide. The team then ran the chain backwards - what a beekeeper can afford, to allowable cost per dose, to allowable manufacturing cost, to required mass of intact dsRNA per gram of dry yeast - converting 'high expression' into a pass/fail wet-lab specification of 0.005 mg dsRNA per g yeast for US viability and 0.05 mg/g for both markets, against a fermentation cost of about 2.33 USD per gram. They also deliberately recruited dissent: the Oxfordshire Natural Beekeeping Group (about 20 chemical-free hobbyists) and treatment-free beekeeper Mark Sandham argued that treating removes the selection pressure that would produce tolerant bees, an argument against the entire premise; rather than abandoning the project the team narrowed its target user to commercial operations and wrote that OxNatBees changed 'not the molecular mechanism of NECTAR, but the problem we believed NECTAR should - and should not - try to solve'. Smaller but equally traceable: Lord John Krebs (first FSA Chairman) and Prof. Jim Dunwell (Chair, ACRE) made environmental fate and off-target effects explicit engineering requirements, moving non-target organisms into the FORAGER off-target screening stage and adding in vivo dsRNA-persistence experiments; Prof. Paul Lam (environmental chemistry, Hong Kong Metropolitan University) drove the adoption of BLAST off-target screening and reframed public engagement as risk management rather than promotion; Dr Michael Morrison (HeLEX, Oxford Law) rewrote the survey instrument so it asked separately about pollen patties, constitutively active engineered bacteria and inducible engineered bacteria rather than about 'GMOs' in general; Dr Théotime Colin's point about secondary pests prompted dsRNA constructs for wax moth and small hive beetle; Prof. Giles Budge's reassurance kept the adult-bee oral delivery route alive and produced the 300/500/700 bp length comparison; and Melanie Teece (Head of Technical, Hilltop Honey) and Wade Ford (Hive & Wellness) turned honey purity into a reason for additional in vivo work. The published HIVE guide names its own failure modes (interviewing agreeable people, treating 'the public' as one stakeholder, letting the Verdict drift into a summary, consulting regulators too late to change anything) and requires every Verdict to state what was decided, what was rejected and what that cost.","realWorld":"The need is framed with numbers rather than adjectives: Varroa is an invasive alien species across most of its range and the most serious pest of the western honeybee; Australia's failed eradication attempt cost A$101 million and destroyed about 30,000 hives, and surveyed US commercial operations lost around 62% of colonies in 2024-25, estimated at over $600 million. SDGs are chosen, not collected: 15 (Life on Land) and 2 (Zero Hunger) are the primary goals with 17 and 4 as enabling goals, each mapped to named sub-targets (15.8 on invasive alien species is the headline, plus 15.1, 15.5, 15.9), and the analysis extends into the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework targets 7, 10, 11 and 17 at the CBD Secretariat's suggestion. The team then writes a dedicated negative-impacts section on goal conflicts - accessibility across economic status, pollution, ecological threat, and whether healthier managed colonies put pressure on wild pollinators (goal 15 against goal 2) - and admits an unresolved contradiction: stakeholders insisted cost was decisive while 48% of their own survey respondents ranked cost least important, with the honest line 'We have not resolved this'. Deployment rides on existing practice (dsRNA-bearing heat-killed yeast in a conventional pollen patty laid over the frames, plus a 3D-printable hive insert), the regulatory path is mapped per jurisdiction after the EPA/FDA/USDA conversation, and the cost model gives both a per-colony net private benefit and the titre threshold manufacturing must hit. They are unusually candid about what is not demonstrated: no dsRNA titre was measured against the model thresholds, the yeast could not be cloned and the E. coli route gave no detectable dsRNA, so 'this is a case for the approach, not a demonstration of the product'. Handover material - FORAGER, the HIVE cycle and question bank, the bee research guide, protocols and hardware files - is released CC BY 4.0 for future teams.","partners":["Amateur Beekeepers Australia","Australian Honey Bee Industry Council","Hive & Wellness Australia","NSW Department of Primary Industries","Science and Advice for Scottish Agriculture (SASA)","Scottish Government Honey Bee Health Team","Advisory Committee on Releases to the Environment (ACRE)","Soil Association Certification","Secretariat of the Convention on Biological Diversity","US EPA, FDA and USDA","Hilltop Honey","Sustainable Conservation / Almond Board of California","Oxfordshire Natural Beekeeping Group","NYU Abu Dhabi iGEM","University of Oxford Department of Biology (Prof. Geraldine Wright)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6391/wiki/assets/drawings/sdg-description.avif","caption":"NECTAR at the centre of four chosen SDGs - 15 Life on Land and 2 Zero Hunger as primary goals, 17 Partnerships and 4 Quality Education as enabling goals - each with its own justification rather than a logo wall","credit":"Team Oxford, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6391/wiki/assets/education/gmo-webinar-zoom.avif","caption":"GMO 101, the joint Zoom workshop with NYU Abu Dhabi iGEM on 8 October 2026, with participation measured through Nearpod","credit":"Team Oxford, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6391/wiki/assets/bee-research-guide/walking-to-the-hives.avif","caption":"The team walking to the hives - fifteen members with zero beekeeping experience at the start of the project","credit":"Team Oxford, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6391/wiki/assets/education/street-interview.avif","caption":"Street interviews on public attitudes to GMOs in bee treatment, run as risk management rather than promotion after advice from Prof. Paul Lam","credit":"Team Oxford, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Make the write-up template itself enforce integration: every stakeholder record must carry a 'what this changed' field, and every verdict must name what was decided, what was rejected and what that cost - then run the affordability chain backwards from what the user can pay to a numerical pass/fail specification for the bench.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/oxford/","https://2026.igem.wiki/oxford/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/oxford/sustainability","https://2026.igem.wiki/oxford/economic-modelling","https://2026.igem.wiki/oxford/case-studies","https://2026.igem.wiki/oxford/beekeeper-survey","https://2026.igem.wiki/oxford/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/oxford/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/oxford/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/oxford/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/oxford/project-description"],"rank":47},"6395":{"team":"NUS-Singapore","id":"6395","section":"Undergrad","country":"Singapore","village":"Biomanufacturing","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/nus-singapore/","projectTitle":"ORCHID","tagline":"Multiplexed fluorescent stress biosensors in yeast plus a machine-learning layer that turns intracellular stress into the next experiment to run.","summary":"Industrial bioreactors hold hundreds of thousands of litres and a single bad batch is expensive, yet conventional monitoring tracks only physical and chemical parameters such as pH and dissolved oxygen — nothing about what is happening inside the cell. Omics and LC-MS can see inside, but they are offline, destructive and slow enough that results arrive after the batch has finished, so they cannot act on anything. ORCHID puts biosensors for endoplasmic reticulum, oxidative and ATP stress into Saccharomyces cerevisiae as fluorescent reporters readable straight from a plate reader, solves the resulting spectral overlap with a linear unmixing model, and feeds the separated stress signals into SABLe, a neural-network framework that predicts growth, product and stress from process conditions and then proposes which culture to run next. It won nominations across parts, presentation, wiki and integrated human practices because the loop actually closed: SABLe's exploration rule proposed 27 C, the team grew that plate, and the measured product signal reached 491 mApple RFU/OD600 against 204 and 179 at the 24 and 30 C conditions it was trained on.","awards":["Top 10 (Undergrad)","Best Part Collection — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Presentation — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Wiki — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Integrated Human Practices — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Biomanufacturing Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Three layers, built in sequence. First, a linear unmixing model adapted from multispectral fluorescence imaging to plate-reader wells: each sample's readings are modelled as a mixture matrix with one column per reporter and one row per channel, with diagonal entries carrying a reporter's own signal and off-diagonal entries the crosstalk, inverted to recover each reporter's share. It was validated on mixtures of single-reporter strains including untransformed BY4741 for autofluorescence and water-only wells for background, six replicates per condition. Second, a mechanistic baseline: Hill dose-response curves fitted at each temperature for DTT against the stress reporter and galactose against the product reporter, plus simple ODE time-course equations. The ODEs tracked growth well (R-squared about 0.91-0.93) but fitted stress (0.33-0.47) and product (0.41-0.42) poorly, and the team uses that failure as the explicit justification for moving to machine learning rather than assuming ML was needed. Third, SABLe: a multilayer perceptron trained on 700 culture-time records from 40 unique condition combinations (two temperatures at 24 and 30 C, five DTT concentrations 0-1 mM, four galactose concentrations 0-0.2%, three independent plate cultures each, measured at 0, 3, 5, 7, 9 and 24-26 hours), predicting OD600, mApple/OD600 and mCitrine/OD600 without ever receiving their measured values as inputs. On top of the trained network they run gradient ascent (network frozen, 64 starting conditions, 500 steps each, 32,000 evaluations without growing a culture), a ten-member bootstrap ensemble for disagreement-based uncertainty, and UMAP projection of the 64-dimensional latent response to 20,000 queried conditions to inspect what the network learned.","dataviz":"The wiki is a Three.js scrollytelling experience that walks a reader from the $2-4 trillion bioeconomy projection down to a single yeast cell, with hoverable bioreactors explaining Titer, Rate and Yield before the project is even introduced — the argument is built visually before any data appears. The dry lab page is laid out as a numbered slide sequence (raw extremes, normalisation, normalised trajectories, stress dose fit, product dose fit, time model fit, fivefold split, held-out scores, held-out trajectories, gradient search, ensemble uncertainty, exploration score, optimisation versus exploration, latent UMAP, measured DTT response, UMAP robustness), so the reasoning chain is the navigation. Two choices stand out. The exploit-versus-explore panel shows side by side that maximising predicted signal just returns to a corner already measured, while the exploration rule spreads eight proposed tests across under-sampled combinations — making the value of the method visible rather than argued. And the UMAP is drawn sixteen different ways with the caption telling the reader to compare colour gradients rather than outlines, with an explicit note that the map axes have no biological units, which is an honest treatment of a technique usually presented as if its shape meant something.","datascience":"The statistical discipline here is well above the usual standard. Cross-validation groups all biological replicates and time points from a single cultivation condition into one split, because splitting correlated measurements across train and test would inflate performance — so the reported scores (R-squared 0.955 for OD600, 0.891 for mApple/OD600, 0.842 for mCitrine/OD600) measure generalisation to genuinely unseen condition combinations. Channel selection asked how few reads are needed and found one well-chosen channel per reporter matches a full spectral scan (three channels as good as six for three reporters, four as good as eight for four), turning an hour-long scan into minutes so a bioreactor can be sampled routinely. A simulation study set the design rule for adding reporters: for each separation angle from 2 to 90 degrees they generated 3,000 random two-reporter mixtures with 5% noise and found median error stays within 5 percentage points once reporters are at least 28 degrees apart — which is why mCitrine and eGFP at 20 degrees are ruled out. Errors are diagnosed rather than reported: the consistent 3-point overestimate of mTurquoise2 and underestimate of mApple in three-reporter mixtures is attributed to sample preparation rather than the algorithm because noise alone would scatter in both directions, and the larger four-reporter errors are traced to the whole plate being 6-17 times dimmer, leaving mApple and mTurquoise2 only about 160 and 690 RFU above water. Then the model generated a biological hypothesis: UMAP showed conditions with more DTT clustering where both stress and product are predicted high (79% of high-predicted-product conditions were also high DTT, 81% high predicted stress, against 25% expected by chance), the team went back to the measured cultures and confirmed it (Spearman rho, p < 0.001), checked that mCitrine bleed into the mApple channel could explain at most 8% of the rise, and named the next mechanistic question. They also caught their own education-survey analogue of this problem in the model: the 27 C validation plate was read at 24 hours while earlier plates were read at about 25, and they say so.","software":"SABLe and the linear unmixing algorithm are released on the iGEM GitLab at https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/nus-singapore/model, framed explicitly as a reusable framework rather than a one-project script — future teams can use the unmixing to quantify several fluorescent proteins at once and track multiple cellular processes from a single strain design. The part collection is the other deliverable: 17 modular basic parts (stress-sensing elements including altered and native Yap1 response elements, UPRE1 and UPRE2 Hac1 binding sites, biosensor tuning elements, promoters of differing strengths, terminators, and fluorescent reporters including a genetically encoded green ATP sensor) plus 12 composite parts for the ER, oxidative and ATP stress biosensors, designed for plug-and-play assembly. They also characterised leakiness-reduction design principles as a reusable pattern: Sko1 repression upstream of the TATA box, a cP_CYC1 core promoter to lower basal expression, an ODC degradation tag for continuous turnover of background protein, and an RPP2Bt terminator. Two education artefacts are software: a browser game in which players build genetic circuits in virtual yeast populations, with every number and equation documented by source category (published, game-balance tuned by scripted playtesting, or stated rule) and an honest statement that no value was fitted to a real culture so the game shows the shape of the biology rather than predictions; and SynVision, an app whose camera scanner links everyday objects to synthetic biology concepts and then runs DBTL-guided questioning.","stack":["Python with a multilayer perceptron (ReLU)","Deep ensembles for predictive uncertainty","UMAP dimensionality reduction","Gradient ascent over a frozen network","Linear unmixing / matrix inversion on plate-reader channels","Hill dose-response curve fitting","ODE time-course models","Spearman correlation with Holm correction","Saliency-map style latent inspection","Three.js scrollytelling wiki","Microsoft Forms with anonymous participant linking codes","GitLab (iGEM instance)"],"techniques":["Multiplexed fluorescent biosensing with spectral deconvolution","Reference-spectra calibration including autofluorescence and background wells","Condition-grouped cross-validation to prevent leakage from correlated replicates","Channel-subset selection to minimise readout time","Simulation-based design thresholds (28-degree separation rule)","Bootstrap ensemble disagreement as an uncertainty proxy","Exploit-versus-explore acquisition scoring (normalised disagreement plus distance to nearest tested condition)","Latent-space projection to generate testable biological hypotheses","Robustness checks across 16 hyperparameter settings","Model-proposed condition validated at the bench","Systematic error diagnosis distinguishing preparation artefacts from algorithm error"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"NUS treated their educational game as a research object, which is rare at any level. It was designed against Self-Determination Theory with autonomy, competence and relatedness mapped to specific mechanics (free choice of parts, a shared leaderboard, facilitated peer discussion), and every simulation value published with its provenance. Evaluation used paired pre- and post-surveys via Microsoft Forms where participants generated the same anonymous linking code on both forms from details only they would know, so before-and-after answers could be matched without collecting names or emails. They deployed across six settings — Project STEMpact Workshop 3 with secondary school students, NCEB Engineering Biology Week FUTURES Day with polytechnic students, two undergraduate modules (SP2718C and BN4501), NUS Telegram channels and a Raffles Girls' School email blast — getting 58 pre-surveys and 27 post-surveys between 5 September and 18 October 2026, of which 24 paired. The analysis is where it becomes exemplary: four Intrinsic Motivation Inventory subscales were shortened and reworded, then checked for internal consistency with Cronbach's alpha in their own data, which exposed that Perceived Choice at alpha 0.23 was not a single construct (its two items measured having choices and feeling obliged to play) so they reported them separately instead of averaging. Three items were negatively worded and reverse-scored to catch acquiescent responders. Attrition bias was tested — only 41% of pre-survey takers paired — and no item differed (all p > .18). Self-ratings on all three understanding statements rose 1.3-1.8 points (d = 0.76-0.95) and intent to pursue synthetic biology from 4.0 to 4.9 (d = 0.64), all surviving Holm correction. But they also scored free-text definitions as an independent check: promoters rose from 64% to 91% correct, sensors from 23% to 45%, genes stayed at 55%, and the overall written score moved only 1.4 to 1.9 out of 3 (p = .06). Crucially, self-ratings matched written answers before playing (rho = .65) and did not afterwards (rho = -.04) — participants felt they understood more than they could explain — so the team explicitly treats the self-reported gains as an upper bound. Their own headline finding is that participants valued the game more than they enjoyed it: the highest-rated statement in the survey was that the game is useful for understanding synthetic biology (5.5) and the lowest was about enjoying it while playing (4.3).","ihp":"The project's scope was set and then substantially narrowed by stakeholders. An application scientist at TJX Bioengineering established that a single failed batch causes substantial financial loss and shifted the team's attention from the product to the production process and the changing conditions cells experience; Anomaly Bio, a precision fermentation startup, established that conventional monitoring tracks physical and chemical parameters while the cell's inner workings are overlooked because they are hard to measure and hard to interpret. The largest single change came from Dr Bruce Li, Alan Yang and Prof Yong-Su Jin raising scale-up challenges, deployment barriers and startup resource constraints: in response the team moved ORCHID's primary intended application from continuous industrial monitoring to early-stage R&D, naming strain-engineering and process-development teams at startups as the primary users and dropping production-scale deployment as an immediate objective. Several design elements are individually attributable — Dr Jee Loon Foo's guidance set the initial oxidative and ER stress targets, Sheena Chan's feedback added the ATP depletion sensor, and Dr Bruce Li's concerns about whether the biosensors themselves perturb the cell led them to build parental-versus-biosensor-strain comparisons into the experimental design. Sook Wei explained how genome-scale metabolic models represent competition between growth and product formation but warned that conventional metabolic models may not match real cellular behaviour because of unaccounted byproducts, competing pathways and biological constraints, stressing that experimental data is what closes that gap and pointing toward combining genome-scale modelling with machine learning — advice visible in the final architecture, where a mechanistic ODE baseline is fitted first, shown to fail on stress and product, and only then replaced by a learned model. Later feedback also asked them to extend the model to weigh productivity, yield and cost together rather than optimising a single predicted output, which is recorded as future work rather than claimed as done.","realWorld":"The deployment story is deliberately modest after the industry reality check. ORCHID is positioned as an early-stage R&D platform for strain engineering and process development teams at startups, not as production-scale instrumentation, because the team accepted that industrial implementation carries technical and financial constraints they cannot yet meet. The workflow they specify is concrete: build or adopt modular biosensors for the analytes of interest in whatever chassis is being engineered, culture under varied process conditions, train the model on how conditions map to stress responses, use it to interpolate and recommend conditions, then run the organism under those conditions — with the intracellular data also making unintended effects on the host easier to spot. The framing they use for the value proposition is a grey box rather than a black box: in-line pH and dissolved oxygen sensors show how organism and environment affect each other, but when production is inefficient researchers still cannot tell which pathway is the constraint, and high-dimensional intracellular stress data gives a window into that. Because the biosensors are modular, they argue the collection builds toward a shared library: metabolic engineering teams can track the burden a heterologous pathway places on the cell, and environmental synthetic biology teams can assess strain robustness in harsh conditions. Troubleshooting is published as a first-class deliverable, with issues and fixes in segmented boxes down the results page specifically so later teams hit them less hard.","partners":["TJX Bioengineering (application scientist, cell culture bioprocess)","Anomaly Bio (precision fermentation startup)","Dr Bruce Li","Alan Yang","Prof Yong-Su Jin","Dr Jee Loon Foo","Sheena Chan","Prof Matthew Chang","Prof Dong-Yup Lee","Prof Tom Ellis","Sook Wei (genome-scale metabolic modelling)","Lucas Gelain","Goh Lay Koon","Chionh Yok Hian","Project STEMpact","NCEB Engineering Biology Week (FUTURES Day)","Raffles Girls' School"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6395/wiki/pages/model/ml-stuff/sable-slide-12-exploration-score.avif","caption":"SABLe's acquisition rule made visible: model disagreement across the ten bootstrap networks and distance from already-tested conditions highlight different gaps, and their combined exploration score first selected 27 C, 1 mM DTT and 0.15% galactose as the next culture to grow.","credit":"Team NUS-Singapore, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6395/wiki/pages/model/ml-stuff/figure-18-27c-product-comparison.avif","caption":"The closed loop: measured mApple per OD600 at 0.2% galactose across DTT doses for 24, 27 and 30 C. The model-proposed 27 C plate reached 491 RFU/OD600 at 0.5 mM DTT, against 204 and 179 for the matched 24 and 30 C cultures the model was trained on.","credit":"Team NUS-Singapore, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6395/wiki/pages/model/ml-stuff/sable-slide-14-latent-umap.avif","caption":"UMAP projection of the network's 64-dimensional internal response to 20,000 untested process conditions, the same points coloured by DTT dose, predicted stress and predicted product — the view that generated the testable hypothesis that higher DTT accompanies both more stress and more product.","credit":"Team NUS-Singapore, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6395/wiki/pages/outreach-and-education/game/game-fig2-written-definitions.avif","caption":"Share of 22 paired participants giving a correct written definition before and after playing the circuit-building game — the independent check that showed smaller gains than self-ratings and led the team to treat the self-reported improvement as an upper bound.","credit":"Team NUS-Singapore, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Two things are directly copyable and neither needs a bioreactor. First, NUS's active-learning loop: fit a simple mechanistic model, show where it fails, train a small neural net on your own plate data, then use ensemble disagreement plus distance from tested conditions to pick the next experiment — and actually run it, so the write-up ends with a measured confirmation rather than a prediction. Second, and more unusual, evaluate your outreach the way you evaluate an assay: paired pre/post surveys with anonymous linking codes, reverse-scored items to catch acquiescence, Cronbach's alpha on any scale you shorten, attrition checks, and a free-text knowledge score as an independent check on self-reports. NUS found their participants felt they had learned more than they could explain, and said so — that kind of honesty about one's own teaching is both rare and cheap to adopt.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/nus-singapore/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nus-singapore/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/nus-singapore/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/nus-singapore/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/nus-singapore/experiments","https://2026.igem.wiki/nus-singapore/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/nus-singapore/parts","https://2026.igem.wiki/nus-singapore/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/nus-singapore/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/nus-singapore/implementation","https://2026.igem.wiki/nus-singapore/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/nus-singapore/safety-and-security","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/nus-singapore/model"],"rank":105},"6399":{"team":"Kyoto","id":"6399","section":"Undergrad","country":"Japan","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/kyoto/","projectTitle":"OiLipase — a protein timer that stops rice-bran lipase without destroying rice-bran protein","tagline":"Degrade the enzyme that spoils rice bran oil, then build a molecular timer that degrades the protease once the job is done.","summary":"Rice bran goes rancid because endogenous lipase attacks the oil after milling. Kyoto tethered trypsin to an interface-seeking carrier so it preferentially cleaves lipase at the oil-water interface, then faced the real problem: once the lipase is gone, unselective trypsin starts eating the valuable albumin and globulin. Their answer is a protein timer — a split HRV 3C protease whose N-terminal half is sequestered by an excess decoy that is also a 3C substrate, producing an autocatalytic, tunable lag before 3C fires and destroys the trypsin. Three models carry the project: an ODE timer model with full sensitivity analysis, an induction-diffusion model that derives an interior optimum for leucine-zipper dissociation rate, and a protease-resistance design model that failed its own experiment and was then rebuilt into CleaveRank, released under GPL-3.0.","awards":["Best Part Collection — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Model — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Food & Nutrition Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Three distinct models, and the first thing to notice is that each one is a piece of mechanistic reasoning rather than a simulation run for its own sake. (1) TIMER MODEL — a competing-substrate ODE system for a split-protease delay circuit. Species: A (N-terminal split HRV 3C + zipper AN3.5), B (C-terminal + BN3, Kd 279 nM), B' (decoy: zipper BN3.5 with Kd 5.15 nM plus a 3C cleavage site), AB (active 3C), AB' (inactive), and Tr (engineered trypsin). Because 3C sees Tr, B' and AB' as competing substrates, all three rates share a Michaelis denominator den = KM + [Tr] + rel*([B'] + [AB']), with rel being the designable relative cleavability of decoy versus trypsin. Zipper association is treated as at equilibrium, justified because heterodimeric leucine zippers associate in seconds while the lag spans minutes to hours — a reduction that drops k_on from the equations and takes the integration from four variables to two, with A recovered by solving a conservation law; the team notes no measured k_on exists for their zippers and that the equilibrium approximation was checked only against a kinetic version of their own model. Integration is SciPy solve_ivp with LSODA. The conceptual heart of the model is the derivation of WHY the lag scales with decoy amount: a first-order decoy-consumption reaction has a time constant independent of initial concentration, so adding more decoy buys no time; two independent routes to zeroth-order kinetics are identified — Route 1 enzyme saturation (rel*[B']_0 >> KM) and Route 2 sequestration ([B']_0/Kd_Bp >> [B]_0/Kd_B AND [B']_0 >> [A]_0, making [AB] proportional to 1/[B'] so [B'] cancels out of k[AB][B']) — and the team computes their own degree of saturation as 0.38, concluding Route 1 contributes only modestly and the lag is bought almost entirely by sequestration, with the two routes together pushing the order toward -1 and the delay toward quadratic in decoy. They then derive the general result that an n-th order consumption gives depletion time proportional to amount^(1-n), and show the measured local exponent runs 1.75 to 2.82, with the operative 'amount' being u = [B']_0 - [A]_0, the decoy not spent sequestering A. (2) INDUCTION-DIFFUSION MODEL — a transport-and-kinetics model of a two-component induced system (a trypsinogen-zipper-carrier 'Z form' at 0.99 uM and an enterokinase-zipper-carrier 'E form' at 0.01 uM, plus a 1.0 uM free zipper-trypsinogen pool), where the carrier is an inactivated trypsin-resistant lipase that self-targets the oil-water interface. The mean reaction time is assembled from an induction rate k_ind = p_B/tau_search (bulk diffusion to the interface times adsorption probability), a reloading rate k_re = k_on * C_free_TG, the zipper off-rate and the interfacial reaction rate, giving tau_total = 1/k_ind + k_off/(k_ind k_re) + 1/k_off + 1/k_r. The insight that generalises: when the tethered enzyme cannot reach its target (K_act near 0), dissociation becomes an OBLIGATORY step on the reaction path, but dissociation that is too fast wastes transport — so there is an interior optimum in k_off, which means a catalogued leucine-zipper collection spanning a range of dissociation rates has real design value, and a covalent SpyTag/SpyCatcher linkage cannot work at all. They then tested the generalisation against six literature and past-iGEM systems (liposomal release, inhaled formulations, antibody-drug conjugates, Linkoping 2019, Imperial 2010, an intra-articular PLGA depot) and found only one case met both conditions — publishing the degenerate cases as figures. Reported gains: ~18.5x selectivity and 1.6x time-to-completion versus free trypsin, with 91% of water-soluble protein preserved against 0%. (3) PROTEASE RESISTANCE / CleaveRank — see datascience and software.","dataviz":"The timer model's figures are a model of how to present a sensitivity analysis. Figure 3 shows the lag directly (no decoy: Tr below 90% in under a minute; with 3.0 uM decoy: a 27-minute lag) alongside the active-3C trace held near zero through the lag then rising sharply, so the reader sees the autocatalysis rather than being told about it. Figure 4 plots the decoy sweep on log-log axes and reports the LOCAL EXPONENT of the tangent (1.75 to 2.82) rather than claiming a single power law. Figure 5 sweeps the four waveform-shaping parameters in a top row of lag and rise time and a bottom row of sharpness (defined as lag divided by rise time), and the caption explains why kcat gets no panel — it only rescales the time axis and leaves sharpness exactly unchanged. A parameter table gives every sweep range with its resulting lag, rise and sharpness span, so a reader can see that Kd_Bp moves the lag from 8.3 min to 4.5 days and sharpness from 0.59 to 310. The induction-diffusion generalisation is visualised as six SVG figures of the objective function for six different reference systems, with captions that state the failure mode ('there is nothing to optimise', 'without the stage of induction the objective function degenerates', 'Pi_rel is not a design variable') — negative results drawn as carefully as positive ones. CleaveRank's output is organised into four quadrants on three axes (cleavability, impact, risk to activity) so design targets are chosen by rank within a quadrant.","datascience":"The protease-resistance work is the single most honest piece of dry-lab self-criticism in this cohort. The team wrote a 317-line script to design trypsin-resistant 3C protease variants: compute secondary structure and SASA, enumerate loops flanked by stable elements, evaluate with a 'slack' geometry term (slack = 3.3*(loop residues - 7) + 11.3 - anchor distance, from the 7-residue P4-P3' extension spanning 11.3 Angstrom that a protease requires), exclude everything within 14 Angstrom of the catalytic triad, and tier exposed Lys/Arg. Five variants were built. THE EXPERIMENT DENIED BOTH PREMISES: wild-type 3C was already trypsin-resistant across the whole tested range (5 uM substrate, 5-500 nM trypsin, 5-120 min, no cleavage detected), and four of five variants failed to fold. The team then re-ran the original script and diagnosed six specific defects in public. (i) Secondary structure was assigned in-house via a local Kabsch-Sander implementation instead of DSSP; against mkdssp 4.2.2 agreement was 0.761 with entirely one-sided error — 43 beta-strand residues called loop, 44 of 94 'loop' residues actually beta strand, 15 of 20 enumerated loops containing strand, and the largest-slack 'loop' 61-72 actually two beta strands joined by a turn. (ii) The replacement residue was never really chosen: after the exclusion rules the pool was six residues, within which Lys-to-Gln and Arg-to-Gln are uniquely maximal under BLOSUM62, so 'Gln everywhere' was a deterministic artefact — and the exclusions were hard-coded for chymotrypsin and elastase, proteases absent from the experiment. (iii) A crystal structure's B-factor column was read as pLDDT; given the X-ray structure 6KYZ of the same protein the script silently returns zero tier-A positions. (iv) Ranking used descending exposure alone, and later validation showed a structure-only predictor reaches AUC 0.4466 — indistinguishable from chance — so the original code ranked on the one axis that does not work while computing and discarding the axis (specificity) that does. (v) Thirteen thresholds were hand-set, and K175 entered the design by clearing a 14.0 Angstrom cut-off with 0.12 Angstrom to spare. (vi) Substitution sites were scored independently although they are not. Every defect was fixed: DSSP output only; a continuous specificity score built from 22,992 MEROPS records; risk = cleavability x impact; input structure provenance and MD5 recorded with a warning on replacement; an interaction layer for combined substitutions; and 1180 regression-test checks freezing every numeric value, with measurements that would move a threshold PRE-REGISTERED before they are run. Re-ranking the same ten positions under the fixed implementation spreads them 22-fold and puts mut1's K82 and R84 first and third — mut1 being the only variant that folded. Validation went from 4 systems to 48 systems and 9 proteases, giving a mean AUC of 0.7186 over the 47 systems with positive sites, 95% CI [0.642, 0.791] — with the explicit caveat that per-system performance spans [0.38, 1.00] so the interval must not be applied to a single target. Benchmarks: against ExPASy PeptideCutter rules (which by construction cannot rank within their own set, AUC 0.5) CleaveRank reaches 0.7225; against the trained sequence model ProsperousPlus over 45 systems, 0.9305 vs 0.8957 over all residues and 0.7787 vs 0.6873 within the candidate set, with sensitivity 45/45 vs 36/45, paired difference +0.0914 [+0.0043, +0.1855], winning in 25 of 45 — and they then decompose that advantage and report that it CANNOT be attributed: sequence-only features tie the comparator (+0.0036), and neither the structural factors nor the impact weight reaches significance alone, so 'part of the advantage rests on an uncalibrated weight'. They also rule out contamination by stratifying into systems that may and may not have been in ProsperousPlus's training data, showing the gap widens in the unseen stratum. Finally, they tested whether a structure predictor could do the job instead: AlphaFold3 given human trypsin plus LIP2 plus Ca2+, five samples from one seed, with the trypsin-BPTI inhibitor complex as positive control. BPTI gave ipTM 0.95, minimum inter-chain PAE 0.78 Angstrom, P1 Lys15 carbonyl at 2.6 Angstrom from the catalytic Ser, 14/14 shared interface residues; LIP2 gave ipTM 0.14-0.15, PAE 15.3-15.8 Angstrom, nearest carbonyl 5.4-7.0 Angstrom and not at any cleavage site, 0 of 85 shared interface residues, and 23.8-29.3 Angstrom chain displacement — while both monomers were reproduced at 0.16-0.52 Angstrom RMSD. Their conclusion is a genuinely sharp piece of reasoning about method limits: structure prediction returns stable complexes, the PDB is full of protease-inhibitor complexes and almost empty of Michaelis complexes with folded globular substrates because those dissociate on cleavage, and susceptibility to cleavage is not a property of a stable complex — 'this asymmetry is the mechanism of the result, and it will not be removed by scale'.","software":"CleaveRank, a command-line tool released under GPL-3.0-or-later. It takes a target's sequence and structure, the residues whose cleavage abolishes function, and the cleavage rules and complex structure of the protease you want resistance against; it ranks the sites that will actually be cleaved, proposes concrete mutations (substitution, loop shortening, proline introduction, disulfide or salt-bridge insertion), evaluates each one's effect on activity and the interactions between them, then builds and relaxes the chosen structure in PyRosetta and verifies it on three axes. The development discipline is the lesson: 1180 frozen regression checks where the current output is the expected value so any code change that moves a number fails at the point it moved, expected values updated only for an intended change with the change recorded first, documented 'conditions under which the tool may and may not be used' fixed as explicit statements, and threshold-moving measurements pre-registered. The timer model's rate-equation derivation and lag derivation are published as separate companion PDF notes.","stack":["Python","SciPy solve_ivp (LSODA)","PyRosetta","mkdssp 4.2.2 (DSSP)","MEROPS database (22,992 records)","AlphaFold3 (tested as a comparator and rejected)","ExPASy PeptideCutter (benchmark)","ProsperousPlus (benchmark)","BLOSUM62","regression-test harness (1180 checks)"],"techniques":["competing-substrate Michaelis-Menten ODE system","quasi-equilibrium reduction of binding steps","conservation-law solving for free species","reaction-order analysis (zeroth-order routes to a tunable delay)","autocatalytic positive-feedback circuit design","analytical approximation and derivation of a lag expression","one-at-a-time parameter sweeps with lag / rise / sharpness metrics","local-exponent (log-log tangent) analysis instead of assumed power laws","diffusion-limited transport modelling (Damkohler number)","mean-first-passage-time reasoning","interior-optimum optimisation of a kinetic design variable","cross-system generalisation testing against literature and past iGEM projects","structural bioinformatics (DSSP, SASA, loop geometry)","continuous specificity scoring from a curated proteomics database","ranking-metric validation (AUC) with paired bootstrap confidence intervals","training-contamination stratification","ablation decomposition of a benchmark advantage","negative control design (BPTI) for a structure-prediction test","regression-test value freezing and pre-registration"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A dialogue-first mission — 'to communicate the fun of synthetic biology to a wide range of age groups through dialogue and hands-on experiences' — delivered at Kyoto University's November Festival, TEDxKyotoUniversity 2026 and CHILDREN'S PARK UNIVERSITY. Activities were hands-on with real research equipment: a broccoli DNA extraction booth with the buffer recipe published (38 g salt and 50 mL neutral detergent in 1 L tap water) so anyone can reproduce it, plus colour-change demonstrations. The stated method was to adjust the content and depth of explanation to each visitor's interest and level rather than deliver a fixed script.","ihp":"Kyoto draw a line most teams blur: 'not all HP constitute Integrated Human Practices'. They ran 19 interactions (interviews, site visits, email exchanges), state that 16 of them led to a design decision, and keep two separate pages — an HP page documenting everything and an IHP page tracing only the interactions that changed the design, decision by decision. They are also candid that they abandoned their chosen food-related project theme more than once after researcher conversations exposed real-world implementation problems, before arriving at rice bran. Stakeholder interviews with industrial processors and smaller milling businesses established that rice bran is not simply waste — it already flows to oil extraction, feed, fertiliser and household uses — which reframed the project question as whether better preservation and quality assessment can make higher-value uses feasible inside existing collection routines, and surfaced the key commercial constraint that bran-specific capital investment is hard to justify when the material has low sale value.","realWorld":"Rice bran is roughly 10% of brown rice by weight in Japan and contains about 20% oil plus dietary fibre, functional lipids and proteins, vitamins and minerals, but endogenous lipase starts hydrolysing triacylglycerides to free fatty acids as soon as milling disrupts the grain. Existing stabilisation is thermal (extrusion and heating), which costs energy and capital and affects bran components. The venture, OiLipase, has two parts: KANNAME, the enzymatic stabilisation system that localises protease activity at the oil-water interface to knock down lipase at ambient temperature, and NIINAME, a quality-assessment component. The team state plainly what remains undemonstrated in their own system: selective degradation of Lipase-II, preservation of other valuable proteins, and controlled termination of proteolysis. The computed dose is 115 mg/L, and the timer gives 91% preservation of water-soluble protein against 0% for free trypsin.","partners":["Kyoto University","COSMO BIO","MIYAKO CAPITAL","Twist Bioscience","IDT","IDEA BANK"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6399/wiki/dry/fig3-timer-core.avif","caption":"Figure 3: the timer working. Without decoy, trypsin falls below 90% in under a minute; with 3.0 uM decoy a 27-minute lag appears. The lower panel shows active 3C held near zero through the whole lag then rising sharply as the decoy runs out — the autocatalysis made visible rather than asserted.","credit":"Team Kyoto, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6399/wiki/dry/fig4-sens-decoy-1.avif","caption":"Figure 4: the decoy sweep on log-log axes. Rather than claiming a single power law, the team report the local exponent of the tangent moving from 1.75 to 2.82, consistent with their derivation that an n-th order decoy consumption gives depletion time proportional to amount^(1-n) and that two independent routes to zeroth-order kinetics push the system toward quadratic.","credit":"Team Kyoto, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6399/wiki/dry/fig5-sens-shape-2.avif","caption":"Figure 5: sweeps of the parameters that shape the waveform, with lag and rise time on the top row and sharpness (lag divided by rise time) below. kcat gets no panel because it only rescales the time axis and leaves sharpness exactly unchanged — the caption says so, which is how a sensitivity analysis should read.","credit":"Team Kyoto, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6399/wiki/dry/fig05-linkoping.svg","caption":"One of six figures testing whether the induction-diffusion generalisation applies to other systems. This one, for Linkoping 2019's reservoir-type design, is captioned 'there is nothing to optimise' — a negative result drawn with the same care as a positive one, which is how the team established that only one of six reference systems met both conditions for an interior optimum in dissociation rate.","credit":"Team Kyoto, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"When an experiment contradicts your model, treat the model's source code as the next object of study: Kyoto re-ran their own script, enumerated six specific defects (DSSP done in-house, B-factor read as pLDDT, ranking on the one axis that measured at chance AUC, thresholds cleared by 0.12 Angstrom), published every one, and then froze 1180 regression checks so no number can move unnoticed. Pre-registering any measurement that would move a threshold is a practice a school lab can adopt immediately and it is worth more than a bigger model.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/kyoto/","https://2026.igem.wiki/kyoto/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/kyoto/software/","https://2026.igem.wiki/kyoto/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/kyoto/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/kyoto/results/","https://2026.igem.wiki/kyoto/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/kyoto/education/","https://2026.igem.wiki/kyoto/entrepreneurship/"],"rank":21},"6401":{"team":"HKU-HongKong","id":"6401","section":"","country":"Hong Kong","village":"Therapeutics","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/hku-hongkong/","projectTitle":"Omni-Patch","tagline":"A cell-free single-layer sodium alginate dressing carrying a de novo TLR4/MD-2 antagonist peptide and FGF2 for hard-to-heal wounds","summary":"Omni-Patch is a cell-free sodium alginate wound dressing loaded with aTi-14, a de novo designed peptide intended to block LPS binding to the MD-2/TLR4 complex, plus FGF2 as a repair-supporting growth factor. The team's first concept used a living chassis secreting a literature peptide (TAP2) under nitric-oxide control via NorR; recombinant TAP2 could not be recovered and the macrophage assay showed no reduction in inflammatory markers, so they pivoted to de novo design and a cell-free carrier. A nitric-oxide diffusion model then showed NO penetration depth was far shorter than the hydrogel thickness needed for exudate handling, which killed the NO-sensing component and reframed the device as open-loop. The wiki is unusually candid: aTi-14 left-shifted FITC-LPS binding at 25 uM in a one-concentration THP-1 M0 screen while five sibling variants did not, but matched qPCR showed no transcript drop, the Griess nitrite run was discarded for bacterial contamination, and no IC50 is claimed.","awards":["Best New Composite Part — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Presentation — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Therapeutics Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Four chained mechanistic modules plus a design-space inversion. Module 1 models payload release from the alginate matrix and transport from gel surface into wound tissue, recalibrated against the measured FGF2-G3 BCA release fraction after the wet lab released less than predicted. Module 2 models competition between aTi-14 and LPS for the MD-2 pocket, using the measured relative reduction in LPS binding at 25 uM as a dissociation-constant proxy to output receptor-occupancy fraction. Module 3 propagates occupancy to downstream NF-kB signalling output (nuclear p65, NO, accumulated nitrite). Module 4 is a Fisher-KPP reaction-diffusion wound-closure model in which the FGF2-G3 arm drives fibroblast proliferation and inflammation suppresses growth through the aTi-14 arm, with a front-speed criterion drawing the heal/no-heal boundary and predicted closure time as the patient-facing output. A separate NO-sensing model (NorR regulator circuit, penetration-depth heatmap, NO-vs-NorR threshold) was built before the planned experiment and its negative result removed the sensing component from the wet-lab design.","dataviz":"Figure set is systematically numbered per module (m1-m4, ds-, sa-, no-, ps- prefixes) and served through a custom DryLabFigure/FigureLightbox React component with figure number, caption and note. Includes solver-convergence plots, release curves overlaid on BCA data, kymographs of aTi-14 and FGF2 concentration through gel depth and time, MD-2 occupancy curves, endotoxin-load shift plots, p65-vs-occupancy curves, closure-time curves, a front-speed verification plot, a Sobol dose-vs-closure sensitivity figure, an NO penetration-depth heatmap, and a design map from the inverse run.","datascience":"Global sensitivity analysis (Sobol) across the chained modules, confirming the dominant uncertainties (endotoxin load, receptor affinity, mobile fraction) propagate into the design criteria without amplification, so conclusions are robust to constants that could not be directly validated. Solver-convergence verification for each module before use. After verification the whole chain was run in reverse as a design-space inversion, deriving the loading and thickness criteria the patch must satisfy to reach a target closure time, with a time-above-target/dosing-interval figure and a design map. A bespoke 'mathematical filter' scores candidates on three sub-modules (binding suitability, structural burden, proteolytic stability); applied retrospectively it flagged structural liabilities in the failed TAP2 peptide that the earlier affinity-only score had missed, and cleared aTi-14.","software":"RFD3-binder-studio: a locally deployable, open-source ten-stage de novo binder design and triage pipeline behind one command line, published at github.com/igemhku/rfd3-binder-studio and gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/hku-hongkong/rfd3-binder-studio. Stage 1 generates binder backbones against the MD-2 target structure and its hotspot residues with RFdiffusion3; stage 2 writes sequences with LigandMPNN/ProteinMPNN across a temperature/noise grid; stage 3 re-folds and validates with RoseTTAFold3 against pLDDT, PAE and backbone RMSD gates; stage 4 co-folds target and binder de novo with Boltz-2 for ipTM, interface pLDDT, PAE and affinity; stage 5 reads interface biophysics with PRODIGY (binding free energy, hydrogen bonds, salt bridges, buried surface area); stage 6 screens immunogenicity with MHCflurry, MHCnuggets and IEDB; stage 7 scans off-targets by MMseqs2 homology search of the target then co-folds candidates against anti-target receptor PDBs with the same Boltz-2 engine for like-for-like comparison; stage 8 applies hard pass/fail gates then a block-weighted composite rank; stage 9 runs in silico directed evolution whose children re-enter at stage 4 so every generation is re-folded, re-scored and re-gated on identical terms, with full lineage in a database; stage 10 writes ranked_candidates.csv and report.md. All parameters live in editable YAML. Ships a --dry-run mode with fabricated metrics that validates the full pipeline on any laptop, a doctor command that reports what the current machine can run, --resume, and an init-example campaign. Stages 1-4 and 7 need CUDA GPU; 5, 6, 8, 9 run on CPU. The team explicitly states the scoring weights are reasoned priors, not measured calibration, so output is a triage order and not an affinity.","stack":["RFdiffusion3 (RFD3)","ProteinMPNN / LigandMPNN","RoseTTAFold3 (RF3)","Boltz-2","PRODIGY","MHCflurry 2.0","MHCnuggets","IEDB","MMseqs2","YAML-driven config","Python CLI","GitLab / GitHub"],"techniques":["De novo binder backbone generation against hotspot residues","Independent refold validation (pLDDT / PAE / RMSD gating)","De novo co-folding for ipTM and interface confidence","Binding free energy estimation","MHC class I/II immunogenicity screening","Homology-based off-target panel construction and like-for-like co-folding","Hard gating then block-weighted composite ranking","In silico directed evolution with revalidation re-entry","Reaction-diffusion (Fisher-KPP) front-speed modelling","Receptor competitive-binding / occupancy modelling","Release and tissue-transport kinetics with wet-lab recalibration","Sobol global sensitivity analysis","Inverse design / design-space inversion","Solver convergence verification"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A structured SynBio Workshop Series rather than one-off events, each with matched pre/post Likert surveys and reported means. 'Running with DNA' at South Tuen Mun Government Secondary School (28 September 2026) gave 13 Form 4-5 students a full agarose gel electrophoresis and DNA fingerprinting run in their own school lab, co-led by STMGSS alumni on the iGEM team; the pre-survey established the access gap (13/13 reported few opportunities to run gels, 10/13 for micropipettes) and the post-survey returned an aggregated mean of 4.46/5.00 across 16 items with 92.3% reporting better understanding of synthetic biology. A separate lower-secondary workshop (18 S1-S2 respondents) scored 4.67/5.00 on micropipetting and 4.39/5.00 on hands-on learning being more effective than lectures. A case-based DBTL Healthcare Challenge for secondary biology students built around a fictional 62-year-old diabetic patient moved understanding of engineered bacteria from 3.06 to 4.13/5.00 and of the DBTL cycle from 3.44 to 4.19 across 16 matched responses. The HKU-iBRIDGE SynBio Bootcamp (3-4 October 2026, HKU Medical Campus) brought 40+ S3-S5 students from across Hong Kong through two dry-lab sessions. The team leader also appeared as an expert guest on Episode 121 of the Disconnected podcast, distributed on web, Spotify, Apple Podcasts, Amazon Music and YouTube, discussing AlphaFold, generative diffusion models, human-in-the-loop governance and the stigma researchers face. An Omni-Patch Arcade of four browser games with a built-in feedback portal and dual difficulty tiers extends engagement past the physical workshops.","ihp":"Five stakeholder tiers defined up front with a stated reason for approaching each: lived experience (patients, home caregivers, bedside nurses), clinical and technical specialists, health-system and regulatory actors, public and educational actors, then a final synthesis tier that is explicitly not new conversations but a thematic analysis across all of them, mapping agreement, disagreement and tension. Each interview is written to a fixed four-part template (background and why approached, problems and gaps identified, takeaways and advice, closed-loop action plan). The closed loops are concrete and often restrictive rather than flattering. Prof. Chen (Institute of Antibiotics, Huashan Hospital, Fudan University) established that bacterial colonisation is not infection and that LPS or inflammatory signal alone cannot justify antibiotics, which rewrote both the scientific hypothesis (partial modulation of excessive bacteria-associated inflammation, with host-defence and bacterial-clearance evidence required alongside cytokine readouts) and the education materials (emphasise regular foot observation and prompt professional assessment, never self-diagnosis). A burn-surgery director at Beijing Jishuitan Hospital established that diabetic foot ulcer healing is multifactorial and forced the team to test one peptide and one defined mechanism before proposing combinations, and to drop the M1/M2 framing and NO trigger pending evidence. A plastic surgery consultant pointed out hydrogels absorb exudate poorly relative to foam and negative-pressure wound therapy and that high exudate flow could wash out a topically released peptide, suggesting integration with NPWT or application to sterile surgical dressings instead.","realWorld":"The project is consistently positioned as a preclinical adjunct to standard care, not a replacement for debridement, offloading, infection treatment, vascular assessment or clinical judgement, and the wiki repeats that boundary on description, measurement and IHP pages. Health-system and regulatory stakeholders (clinicians managing wound-care workflows, MedTech entrepreneurs, trade and regulatory specialists familiar with Hong Kong and Greater Bay Area pathways) shaped the value proposition, target indication and translation route. The epidemiological framing is specific to Hong Kong, built on Census and Statistics Department population projections to 2046 for residents aged 65+, and cites pooled chronic-wound prevalence and diabetic foot ulcer lifetime risk from systematic reviews rather than asserted numbers. Both educational games are open-source single-file HTML that run offline in any browser, work on mobile, are fully bilingual English/Chinese, need no account or install, and carry a public live visit counter so uptake is externally verifiable.","partners":["South Tuen Mun Government Secondary School (STMGSS)","Pui Ching Middle School","HKU-iBRIDGE","Asia-Pacific iGEM Conference (APIC)","Institute of Antibiotics, Huashan Hospital, Fudan University","Beijing Jishuitan Hospital / Capital Medical University Burn and Wound Repair","Disconnected podcast"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6401/wiki/modeling/updated/m4-fig2-closure-curves-and-time.avif","caption":"Module 4 Fisher-KPP wound-closure model: predicted closure curves and closure time, the patient-facing output of the chained model stack.","credit":"Team HKU-HongKong, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6401/wiki/modeling/updated/no-fig4-penetration-depth-heatmap.avif","caption":"Nitric-oxide penetration-depth heatmap. Simulated NO depth fell short of the hydrogel thickness needed for exudate handling, so the NO-sensing module was cut from the wet-lab design before the experiment was run.","credit":"Team HKU-HongKong, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6401/wiki/modeling/updated/ds-fig3-design-map.avif","caption":"Design map from the inverse run: with all modules verified, the chain was reversed to derive the loading and thickness criteria the patch must satisfy to reach a target closure time.","credit":"Team HKU-HongKong, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6401/wiki/education/edu-bootcamp-graph-knowledge-pre-post.avif","caption":"Pre/post knowledge gain across ten technical topics at the HKU-iBRIDGE SynBio Bootcamp, where baseline scores were weakest exactly in computational tools and mathematical modelling (both 1.52/5).","credit":"Team HKU-HongKong, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Build the dry lab's own workflow into a teachable artefact: HKU turned their real de novo campaign into two free single-file browser games that make students apply the team's actual gates (pLDDT >= 70, ipTM >= 0.80, MMseqs2 off-target screens, MHCflurry immunogenicity) to the team's actual ten candidates, and deliberately let students run the wrong decay model first so the correct rule is discovered as a fix rather than announced as a formula. Pair this with their discipline of publishing the modelling result that killed a design feature (the NO penetration-depth run) as a headline finding, which is the cheapest way for students with no GPU budget to show real engineering judgement.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/hku-hongkong/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hku-hongkong/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hku-hongkong/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hku-hongkong/software/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hku-hongkong/measurement/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hku-hongkong/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hku-hongkong/results/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hku-hongkong/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hku-hongkong/education/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hku-hongkong/contribution/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hku-hongkong/parts/","https://2026.igem.wiki/hku-hongkong/safety-and-security/","https://github.com/igemhku/rfd3-binder-studio"],"rank":21},"6405":{"team":"CalPolySLO","id":"6405","section":"Undergrad","country":"United States","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/calpolyslo/","projectTitle":"Accessible Science: Expanding the Synthetic Cell Toolkit for All","tagline":"A cheap polyphosphate-powered energy module, a reproducible synthetic-cell fabrication device, and the calibrated ATP assay that makes both measurable.","summary":"Cal Poly SLO built a cell-free and synthetic-cell platform aimed at putting synthetic cells into undergraduate hands. The science problem is that PURE-type cell-free reactions run out of energy and that commercial creatine-phosphate regeneration is one of the most expensive parts of the kit, so the team screened a library of polyphosphate kinase 2 (PPK2) enzymes, filtered from roughly 18,000 sequences down to 16 phylogenetically diverse candidates, that regenerate ATP from cheap inorganic polyphosphate. To compare those enzymes they had to build the measurement first: a scalable, interference-corrected luciferase ATP assay with matched standard curves, published protocols, OpenTrons scripts and Excel templates. They also designed a 3D-printed emulsification 'washboard' and a tip-wipe recovery step to make hand-made vesicles reproducible, and wrote the whole thing into CHEM 471, a new undergraduate synthetic-cell lab course.","awards":["Best Alternative Platform — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Measurement — Winner (Undergrad)","Best Education — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Foundational Advance Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Design-Build-Test-Learn applied separately to the assay, to the 3D-printed emulsification device (v0 to v8) and to the course materials; an explicit 'problem -> approach -> solution -> outcome' framing on every major page; measurement treated as a prerequisite for enzyme screening rather than a reporting step; Human Practices feedback logged as 'feedback -> action' pairs that changed protocols.","dataviz":"Interactive charts embedded in the wiki (per-condition time courses, Michaelis-Menten fits, reproducibility datasets) with selectable conditions; side-by-side uncorrected vs corrected Michaelis-Menten fits; log-scaled ATP standard curves; per-cell log10 GFP scatter plots across 24 timepoints with per-timepoint median lines and a dashed per-plate subpopulation threshold; a two-clock explainer diagram teaching readers how to read the quench-validation figures; SolidWorks drawings of every finalized 3D-printed part.","datascience":"The core contribution is an ATP assay that was validated before it was trusted. Three quench methods were compared head to head (cold dilution, 95 C heat stop, EDTA chelation) by sampling a DrPPK2 reaction at fixed reaction times and then varying the hold time before adding CellTiter-Glo; a flat line means the reaction stopped, a rising line means it did not. EDTA was chosen because it scales to 16 enzymes in pre-poured plates, and the concentration was then tuned from 10 mM to 5 mM when enzyme load dropped from 50 to 7.5 ng/uL. The team then defined the assay's reliable ATP range by testing whether they could extend Promega's 10 nM to 1 uM window in either direction, found they could not (0.061 nM ATP still read above 10,000 RLU; the 100 uM standard deviated from linearity), and committed to reading only inside that range and never extrapolating, discarding data that fell outside. Because EDTA, AMP and ADP all suppress luciferase, every sample is compared against ATP standards prepared at the same pre-reagent EDTA concentration and the same substrate concentration, and the ratio of slopes gives per-condition correction factors (tabulated for all eight AMP and ADP levels at both 1:25 and 1:50 dilutions, e.g. AMP CF 0.0822 at 2 mM and 0.6113 at 0.0156 mM) that are hard-coded into the published Excel templates. Correcting recovers the kinetic trend that inhibition had destroyed: the same DrPPK2 AMP dataset moves from Km 0.020 mM / Vmax 5.66 uM/min uncorrected to Km 0.139 mM / Vmax 23.2 uM/min corrected, and the 2 mM AMP point is openly excluded from the fit because the correction does not fully recover it. Benchmark kinetics are reported with R2 (DrPPK2 ADP Km 0.985 mM, Vmax 11.7 uM/min, R2 0.9894; ManPPK2 ADP Km 2.67 mM, Vmax 42.6 uM/min, R2 0.9993; FtPPK2 ADP Km 3.16 mM, Vmax 80.05 uM/min, R2 0.9963). Reproducibility was tested as an experiment in its own right: three team members ran the same full-range assay on the same enzyme aliquot on the same day, giving Km 0.0775 +/- 0.0145 mM and Vmax 8.62 +/- 1.39 uM/min, and the team states plainly that these do not match the earlier full-range values and lists the candidate causes (different purification batch, new polyP lot, new AMP lot) as unresolved. Microscopy is handled by a named pipeline, CellScope, which runs Cellpose segmentation at 1.332 um/pixel after 4x downsampling, exports one row per object per timepoint to parquet (over a million objects on one plate), applies a QC gate on diameter 5 to 60 um, circularity 0.80 to 1.25 and no saturated pixels, reports each well as fold over its own background, and runs a two-mode (delta-BIC) test for subpopulations; a dedicated figure documents a case where the segmentation silently failed on a visibly good well, which the team published rather than hid. Every bulk plate carries a 0.125 uM fluorescein well as a dye reference, and the wiki maintains an explicit glossary distinguishing RFU (plate reader) from AU (microscope) as non-comparable units.","software":"OpenTrons OT-2 Python protocols for dilution-plate creation and dilution execution (full-range and confirmatory, four enzymes), published as .py downloads; Excel analysis templates for the full-range AMP, full-range ADP and confirmatory assays with correction factors built in; a master-mix calculator, titration design workbooks, plate-map template and osmolarity worksheet; the CellScope image-analysis pipeline (Cellpose segmentation, OzaLabCP/Imageanalysis) with a published vesicle_pipeline.txt; STL files for the washboard insert and rubber-band sled; raw time-course data and raw image data/masks released. All downloads are collected on https://2026.igem.wiki/calpolyslo/downloads and the lab manuals are released under CC BY 4.0.","stack":["Promega CellTiter-Glo 2.0 luciferase ATP assay","Promega GloMax luminometer","BioTek Cytation5 plate reader","Cephla Squid automated fluorescence microscope","OpenTrons OT-2 liquid handler","Cellpose / CellScope segmentation pipeline","Python","Parquet","Excel analysis templates","SolidWorks","FDM 3D printing"],"techniques":["Matched-condition standard curves","Interference correction factors","Quench-method validation","Defined linear measurement range (no extrapolation)","Michaelis-Menten fitting with R2","Inter-operator reproducibility testing","Fluorescein dye reference wells","Image segmentation with explicit QC gates","Bimodality testing (delta BIC)","Osmolarity control","DBTL hardware iteration"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"The team designed CHEM 471: Engineering Synthetic Cells, described as the first known undergraduate synthetic-cell course in the US, wrote and tested ten open-licence (CC BY 4.0) lab manuals plus an instructor packet with prep lists, reagent costs, timing and common failure points, taught it to ten students in spring 2026, and surveyed them before and after. Confidence rose in 9 of 12 skills; the three that did not became design inputs. Students rated fluorescence microscopy lower at the end than at the start, so the microscope protocols were rewritten and re-tested by the team's least experienced members; manual cytosol-recipe maths was replaced by auto-scaling Excel calculators; NanoOrange/A280 protein quantification was replaced with a Bradford assay plus BSA standard curve; and the Promega AMP/ADP protocol was replaced with the team's own real-time assay. A student's suggestion became the tip-wipe oil-removal method that was then tested against the standard method.","ihp":"Consultations with ethicists, legal and biosecurity scholars and industry scientists were run as feedback-to-action pairs. Dr Hank Greely advised publishing safety and containment thinking before starting work, so the team published aims, protocols, lab manuals and safety forms. Dr Ryan Jenkins recommended survivability testing as risk-assessment evidence, so the team tested whether synthetic cells survive outside the tube across pH, salinity and real environmental water samples (Los Osos Creek wetland, Avila Beach ocean water, campus pond, tap and deionised water) and found the cells lyse outside pH 7 +/- 1, at seawater salinity and in every environmental sample; he also prompted a lab-notebook safety checklist. Dr Keith Robison raised dual-use scenarios, which produced a benefits-vs-misuse framework. Dr Tae Seok Moon raised public perception, which produced IRB-approved surveys (Cal Poly IRB #2026-194 and #2026-195) of 10 CSHL Summer Synthetic Biology participants and 30 Cal Poly FSURP students on comfort, trust and regulation. Dr Zachary Sun's view that education may be the realistic near-term application reshaped the project's scope toward enzyme characterisation and teaching.","realWorld":"The framing throughout is cost of access rather than novelty: PPK2 plus polyphosphate is pursued because it lowers the price floor of cell-free protein synthesis, and the 3D-printed washboard replaces a hand-raking step that varies between operators. The course is explicitly packaged as a template other undergraduate institutions can adopt, with reagent costs and set-up in an instructor packet, and the full protocol set released so other programmes can either reproduce the six enzyme-characterisation experiments or swap in their own enzymes. Six characterised PPK2 enzymes and sixteen candidate-panel enzymes are deposited as registry parts with their datasets linked.","partners":["Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory Summer Synthetic Biology Program","Cal Poly Frost Summer Undergraduate Research Program (FSURP)","b.next (Nucleus cytosol kit)","Promega","Dr Hank Greely (Stanford)","Dr Ryan Jenkins","Dr Keith Robison","Dr Tae Seok Moon","Dr Zachary Sun"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6405/wiki/measurement/meas-opentrons-deck.avif","caption":"The Opentrons OT-2 deck loaded with tip racks and plates; the robot was revived after five years to prepare the EDTA stop plates and the fixed 1:25 and 1:50 dilution plates for the ATP assay.","credit":"Team CalPolySLO, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6405/wiki/measurement/meas-glomax-reader.avif","caption":"The Promega GloMax plate reader used to convert quenched, diluted PPK2 reactions into luminescence, which is then converted to ATP concentration against EDTA- and substrate-matched standard curves.","credit":"Team CalPolySLO, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6405/wiki/measurement/meas-celltiter-glo.avif","caption":"CellTiter-Glo 2.0, the luciferase chemistry the assay is built on. Because the reagent carries an undisclosed amount of magnesium, the safe upper EDTA limit could not be calculated and had to be measured.","credit":"Team CalPolySLO, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6405/wiki/emulsion-device/emu-final.avif","caption":"The finalized 3D-printed emulsification device: a semicircle chassis with a ridged washboard insert and a 30-degree rubber-band sled, which shears cytosol into lipid-in-oil for four tubes at once in place of hand-raking a single tube along an empty rack.","credit":"Team CalPolySLO, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Before comparing anything, prove the measurement: validate the quench, establish the instrument's honest linear range and refuse to extrapolate outside it, then build a separate standard curve for every interfering condition and hard-code the resulting correction factors into the analysis template you ship. Then test reproducibility by handing the written protocol to people who have never run it, and publish the disagreement when their numbers differ from yours.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/calpolyslo/","https://2026.igem.wiki/calpolyslo/measurement","https://2026.igem.wiki/calpolyslo/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/calpolyslo/alternative-platform","https://2026.igem.wiki/calpolyslo/emulsion-device","https://2026.igem.wiki/calpolyslo/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/calpolyslo/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/calpolyslo/downloads"],"rank":47},"6409":{"team":"RDFZ-China","id":"6409","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/rdfz-china/","projectTitle":"GlacierGuard","tagline":"Protect the ice. Leave less behind.","summary":"RDFZ-China engineered E. coli to produce bacterial cellulose (BC) and built GlacierGuard, a biodegradable BC composite membrane intended to slow localized glacier surface ablation. Three genetic systems support it: heterologous bcsABCD plus a pgm/galU UDP-glucose precursor boost for BC yield, a urease (ureABC) biomineralization module that precipitates white CaCO3 inside the BC fibre network to raise albedo, and a CspA cold-shock-protein module to lower the fermentation temperature needed on the Qinghai-Tibet Plateau. BC production reached 230.6 +/- 15.3 mg/L in C41(DE3), roughly 65.9x the empty-vector control, and covered ice retained 3.2 percentage points more mass than geotextile-covered ice in a refrigerator day-night simulation. The team deliberately deployed only commercially sourced (non-engineered) BC membranes during its Tibet field trial and removed all material before leaving.","awards":["Best Sustainable Development Impact — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"ESM-C protein language model scoring combined with a MuZero reinforcement-learning agent and Monte Carlo Tree Search over AlphaFold-predicted structure; Rosetta used for structural-energy scoring. Candidates ranked by AI Score = 0.5 x ESM-C percentile + 0.5 x Rosetta percentile.","dataviz":"Figure-based reporting of screening hit rates and benchmark score distributions, BC yield comparisons, ice-mass-retention curves, infrared transmission by membrane layer count, and a power/interest stakeholder map. The wiki also carries an interactive 3D 'Glacier Atlas' globe with five Chinese glacier records (Dagu, Azha, Urumqi No. 1, Baishui River No. 1, Mingyong).","datascience":"Benchmarked MuZero/MCTS against genetic algorithms, Beam Search and Random Search, and against SaProt, ESM-C and ESM-1v foundation models, using 50 candidate sequences per method and a hit rate defined as the fraction falling in the top 10% of the benchmark score distribution. MuZero/MCTS reached 24% hit rate vs GA 10%, Beam Search 8%, Random Search 0%; 40% vs 0% for all three foundation models. 1,855 unique BcsD variants were generated after 10,000 model updates; top candidate W19R + G113E (AI score 0.8445).","software":"No standalone released software tool; the dry lab is an in-house screening pipeline. The wiki itself is a hand-built server-rendered site with an interactive glacier atlas. Note: the /model path on this wiki serves leftover template content from an unrelated project and is not the team's dry lab.","stack":["ESM-C","ESM-1v","SaProt","AlphaFold","Rosetta","MuZero","Monte Carlo Tree Search"],"techniques":["protein language model variant scoring","reinforcement-learning sequence search","structural energy calculation","method benchmarking against GA/Beam/Random search","life-cycle and cost reasoning drawn from published BC LCA and techno-economic studies"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A 440-response public survey (online forms, social media, QR codes on posters) found 93.6% thought glacier protection 'very necessary' but 92.0% knew little or nothing about glacier blankets, and 70.5% named 'biodegradable and free from harmful substances or microplastic release' as a top material requirement. The team turned respondents' nicknames and messages into a physical team flag and carried it to the glacier. Other engagement: a visit to the China Quaternary Glacial Vestige Exhibition Hall in Beijing (interview with a staff member surnamed Ma); Xiaohongshu/RedNote science communication that deliberately shifted the message from 'how do we protect a glacier' to 'why protect glaciers and what can individuals do'; a campus exhibition of BC samples and expedition photographs; glacier-themed penguin badges; project slogans printed on racing apparel and a racing helmet sticker; and an online fundraiser for Tibet disaster relief after the August 2026 Gyirong Port debris-flow disaster. In Tibet the team ran outreach for about 150 students across three classes at Bomi County Middle School, built around local glaciers and ecosystems, with a Tibetan-language title and a strawberry DNA extraction experiment; feedback cards came back in both Chinese and Tibetan.","ihp":"This is one of the strongest high-school IHP chains of the year: 27 interviews, site visits and engagement activities organised under an explicit Why-How-What-Adaptation (WHWA) loop in which each entry states the change made. Dr. Donghui Shangguan (cryosphere scientist, glacier change) said in substance 'rather than trying to protect every glacier, we should first determine which glaciers should be prioritised,' and pointed out that glacier surfaces host microorganisms and pioneer plants; the team therefore abandoned 'cover as much glacier area as possible' and repositioned GlacierGuard as targeted protection of high-value, human-accessible sites (parks, research stations, culturally or scientifically significant glaciers), and rewrote its customer definition from bulk consumers to institutions with monitoring and impact-assessment capacity. Jiaojiao Hu of Polar Future warned that glacier winds lift and tear thin membranes and that the team's planned metal anchoring nails would add thermal conductivity and foreign material; she suggested using stones already present on site, and the team both adopted stone/biodegradable anchoring and converted her concern into measurable tests - 11.7 N peak force to failure under freezing conditions and a twisted BC rope carrying 9.5 kg. Professor Haibo Zhang told them a working genetic module does not guarantee an efficient host, so instead of keeping their assumed chassis they built bcsABCD in both BL21(DE3) and C41(DE3), measured yields, and switched to C41(DE3). Polar scientist Limin Xia said unmodified BC alone would probably not reach the needed optical performance and recommended biomineralisation whitening plus attention to infrared wavelengths - this is the direct origin of the ureABC/CaCO3 System 2, and of the added water-absorption (842.0% mass gain) and layered infrared transmission tests (1200 W/m2 bare, falling to 605/370/340 W/m2 for one/two/three layers). Associate Professor Xuan Yu of Xihua University was consulted about using highland barley (qingke) liquor residues as a cheap local carbon source (an idea seeded by iGEM team BUCT-China); she judged the residue route technically difficult and instead recommended the cold-shock protein CspA to cut fermentation heating, which became System 3, while the barley residue was honestly demoted to 'future investigation, yield unmeasured.' Arctic researcher Dr. Ma Liheng pushed them on a hypothetical polar bear ingesting the membrane, which triggered a comparative soil-burial test (BC fully degraded in 7 days, geotextile unchanged) and an explicit admission that wildlife-ingestion safety is unresolved. Professor Jian Zhang (Tsinghua) attacked the evidence base - summer-only observations cannot represent annual glacier trends, biodegradation in soil does not predict biodegradation at glacier temperatures, retention and refreezing on sloping ice is unproven, and someone must pay for production, transport, installation and maintenance - and the team responded by date-stamping its late-August observation window, flagging those uncertainties as open, and adding campus exhibition and Glacier Casualty List-style storytelling to its plan. Negative results are reported with equal weight: essential-oil hydrophobic coating failed the contact-angle test and was dropped, mechanical reinforcement was dropped because the unmodified membrane already passed the tests and extra layers would hurt biodegradability and cost, and a judge's suggestion (Ho Chun Loong, Shenzhen SynBio Challenge) to add ice-nucleating proteins was researched and then explicitly rejected because INPs address nucleation rather than meltwater runoff or radiation absorption. The stakeholder map is two-dimensional (power x interest) and, unusually, names non-human stakeholders - glacier ecosystems, glacier microbial communities, alpine ecosystems and downstream aquatic ecosystems - as parties whose needs must enter design decisions.","realWorld":"Implementation is specified down to a four-step field procedure (site preparation to remove sharp gravel, membrane placement with overlapping sheets and minimal trapped air, biodegradable edge anchoring, final inspection), with membranes dried, cut, folded or rolled for compact transport and hand-carried in batches to glaciers vehicles cannot reach, installed in a cold window before the melt season. Named customers are glacier conservation organisations, national park and nature reserve authorities, high-altitude local governments and restoration/adaptation programmes, with glacier tourism sites and high-altitude ski resorts as early pilot hosts. The regulatory path is real rather than gestural: the team read the Ecological and Environmental Code of the People's Republic of China and the Regulations of the Tibet Autonomous Region on Glacier Protection, emailed iGEM Headquarters and submitted an Environmental Risk Assessment before fieldwork, used only commercial non-engineered BC on the ice, and removed every membrane before leaving. SDG claims are tied to named sub-targets with the team's own evidence: 13.1/13.2/13.3 (melt-reduction test, policy reference materials, climate education), 12.2/12.4/12.5/12.8 (BC life-cycle, cited cradle-to-gate LCA by Forte et al. 2021, residue reuse), 9.5 (industrial fermentation feasibility, citing Dourado et al. 2016), 6.1/6.4/6.6 and 15.1/15.4, plus a candid spillover analysis flagging SDG 7 energy demand from scale-up, SDG 8 high-altitude worker safety, and an SDG 10 equity risk that high deployment cost would concentrate protection in well-funded locations. On cost the team refuses to overclaim: it states that agricultural by-products do not automatically make BC cheaper, that the alternative-carbon-source process is unvalidated and its yield unmeasured, and that a full-life-cycle cost model covering production, maintenance, replacement, waste treatment and recovery - expressed as cost per unit area and per unit of ice melt avoided - must precede any scale-up. Next steps are paired control/treatment plots on real glaciers with continuous monitoring through research stations such as the Aza Glacier Citizen Science Monitoring Site (now part of Polar Future's long-term observation network), plus a standing offer from Professor Xian-En Zhang (Shenzhen University of Advanced Technology) to host further experiments.","partners":["Polar Research Institute of China (virtual tour led by Dr. Wang Luo)","China's Zhongshan Station, Antarctica (station leader Cui Xiangbin)","Dr. Ma Liheng, Arctic field researcher","Dr. Donghui Shangguan, glacier/cryosphere scientist","Jiaojiao Hu, Polar Future","Limin Xia, polar expedition scientist","Professor Haibo Zhang","Professor Weilin Xu","Professor Jian Zhang, Tsinghua University","Associate Professor Xuan Yu, Xihua University","Professor Xian-En Zhang, Shenzhen University of Advanced Technology","Lanzhou University Chayu Monsoon Corridor Multisphere Research Station, Tibet","Southeast Tibet Observation and Research Station for the Alpine Environment, Chinese Academy of Sciences","Aza Glacier Citizen Science Monitoring Site","Daosheng Bio fermentation facility","China Quaternary Glacial Vestige Exhibition Hall, Beijing","Bomi County Middle School, Tibet","iGEM team BUCT-China","Ho Chun Loong, Shenzhen SynBio Challenge judge"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6409/wiki/human-practices/img16.avif","caption":"GlacierGuard stakeholder map plotted on power and interest axes, including non-human stakeholders such as glacier microbial communities and downstream aquatic ecosystems.","credit":"Team RDFZ-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6409/wiki/human-practices/img18.avif","caption":"The team interviewing glacier scientist Dr. Donghui Shangguan, whose advice to prioritise specific glaciers rather than cover area redefined the project's target users.","credit":"Team RDFZ-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6409/wiki/human-practices/img55.avif","caption":"Temporary on-site placement of a commercially sourced (non-engineered) bacterial cellulose membrane on the Aza Glacier surface during the Tibet field investigation; all material was removed before leaving.","credit":"Team RDFZ-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6409/wiki/human-practices/img26.avif","caption":"Nature education session at Bomi County Middle School in Tibet, linking glaciers to forests, wetlands and grasslands for roughly 150 local students.","credit":"Team RDFZ-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Adopt RDFZ-China's Why-How-What-Adaptation template, where every stakeholder entry must end in a named design change or an explicitly rejected option, and copy their habit of converting a stakeholder's worry into a measurable bench test (wind-tearing concern becomes an 11.7 N tensile figure; reflectivity advice becomes an infrared transmission curve).","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/rdfz-china/","https://2026.igem.wiki/rdfz-china/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/rdfz-china/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/rdfz-china/sustainability","https://2026.igem.wiki/rdfz-china/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/rdfz-china/parts","https://2026.igem.wiki/rdfz-china/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/rdfz-china/safety-and-security","https://2026.igem.wiki/rdfz-china/team","https://2026.igem.wiki/rdfz-china/education"],"rank":7},"6422":{"team":"UiOslo-Norway","id":"6422","section":"Overgrad","country":"Norway","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/uioslo-norway/","projectTitle":"HePatch","tagline":"A thermostable hepatitis B surface antigen for a dissolvable microneedle patch - and a hard look at whether that is actually the right problem","summary":"HePatch engineers the hepatitis B surface antigen (HBsAg) for thermostability so it could be delivered in a dissolvable microneedle patch without a cold chain, benchmarked against the WHO controlled temperature chain condition of 28 days at 37 C. The dry lab scored 2,260 ESM2/Rosetta substitutions on a 238-residue E. coli construct, retained 989 after a ddG filter, and ranked candidates for the bench. What distinguishes the team is that it put the project in front of ethicists, legal scholars, Norway's national research ethics committees, a medical officer in Kenya's highest-prevalence county and a youth-led organisation in Nairobi's informal settlements - and then published the places where those people broke the project's own premise. Each stakeholder round is closed with a 'What changed?' box naming the previous assumption, the new approach and the updated framing.","awards":["Best Presentation — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Wiki — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Integrated Human Practices — Nominee (Overgrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A two-phase candidate-prioritisation pipeline for HBsAg substitutions. Phase 1 scores substitutions on sequence, structure and developability features; Phase 2 prepares checked ProteinMPNN and molecular-dynamics packages. Ethical reflection is structured on Kenneth Pimple's three questions for responsible conduct of research - is it true, is it fair, is it wise - with most of the human-practices work deliberately placed under 'is it wise'.","dataviz":"Original GIS cartography made by the team rather than borrowed from publications: population density, mean annual temperature, road network and hospital locations for Turkana and Nairobi counties, rendered in QGIS at WGS 84 (EPSG:4326), with every data source, resolution and limitation stated in the caption. Plus per-variant structural figures (WT, S54T, T56A, T113S) and the recurring 'What changed?' three-column comparison boxes.","datascience":"2,260 ESM2/Rosetta-scored substitutions filtered to 989 by ddG; an earlier construct-v2 exploration ran AlphaFold2 and ProteinMPNN on six candidates, kept as a separately labelled history rather than merged. Provenance discipline is unusually strict: the pipeline records every input, output and source checksum, and the team states that the selected run reuses preserved ESM2 and Rosetta outputs whose original software versions and seeds were not recorded. Geospatial analysis used WorldPop 2020 constrained counts at 100 m, WorldClim 2.1 BIO1 at 30 arc-seconds, GADM 4.1 boundaries and OpenStreetMap amenity and road tags.","software":"A reproducible released pipeline containing the reusable code, tests and a synthetic example, with a separate archive preserving the selected run and its full provenance history. The model page carries a blanket disclaimer that none of the in silico output establishes expression yield, solubility, antigenicity, disulfide bonding, particle assembly or biological function.","stack":["ESM2","Rosetta (ddG)","ProteinMPNN","AlphaFold2","molecular dynamics","QGIS","WorldPop","WorldClim","GADM","OpenStreetMap"],"techniques":["in silico saturation substitution scoring","ddG stability filtering","developability feature scoring","inverse folding","geospatial triangulation of stakeholder testimony","checksum-based provenance recording"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education ran from kindergarten upward - children building model viruses and extracting DNA, sessions at Forskningstorget (the Norwegian public research fair), and presentations to biology students - with photo documentation of each. A separate Dialogues page records the conversations held with ethics and legal experts. The notable choice is a principle adopted from a stakeholder and applied to their own outreach: June Alfreds of Youth and Urbanism told them that raising awareness of a vaccine a family then cannot obtain does not build trust, it destroys it, and the team now treats that as a firm constraint on their own public communication.","ihp":"UiOslo's IHP is the clearest example in this set of engagement that attacks the project rather than endorsing it, and every round ends in a published 'What changed?' box. Professor Kristin Bergtora Sandvik (Criminology and Sociology of Law, University of Oslo, fifteen years on the legal and ethical side of global health including vaccines and cold chains) pointed out that in Norway a vaccination appointment is also when a nurse weighs the child, checks for malnutrition, asks after the mother and notices when a family stops coming - so the team had been thinking about removing the syringe and the fridge without noticing they were also removing the healthcare visit. Professor Kristine Baeroe (Institute of Health and Society) refused to let reduced healthcare involvement count as an automatic benefit, and said of the recipients that children are 'the vulnerable among the vulnerable'. The design consequence is explicit: they moved away from designing for full self-administration towards a trained person being present, began investigating community health workers as administrators, and now describe HePatch as replacing a healthcare visit rather than an injection. Baeroe also told them that studying one country in depth beats a general claim about low-resource settings, which is why the project now writes about Kenya and specifically Turkana County; and she made the communication risk concrete by asking them to imagine a patch arriving in a community with no prior context for it, described as a cure, noting that mistrust in that situation is not irrational and that an intervention can be read as something done to a child rather than for them. Then the team did the thing most teams skip: they designed the Kenyan conversations as a falsification test, stating in advance that the alternative they were genuinely prepared to find - that cold-chain dependence was not a leading barrier in either setting - 'would have undercut the premise of the project as a whole'. Dr Vincent Ebenyo, medical officer at Lodwar County Referral Hospital in Turkana (16.8% hepatitis B prevalence in KENPHIA 2018, the highest county figure in Kenya), partly did undercut it: asked for the single biggest driver of low birth-dose coverage he named unsterilised shared cutting instruments used in ceremonies such as scarification and late health-seeking behaviour first, not the cold chain, which taught the team that transmission prevention and vaccine access are two different problems and a delivery-technology fix only addresses the second. He did confirm the core rationale with a precedent - his hospital had already switched from oxytocin to heat-stable carbetocin because local power instability made cold storage unreliable - but located the cold-chain failure specifically at sub-county and outreach facilities rather than the referral hospital, and noted mothers travelling up to 100 km who arrive a week or a month after birth, far outside the WHO 24-hour window. On self-administration he drew a comparison the team had not considered, that insulin-dependent patients are trusted to self-inject after training, while insisting that training must cover recognising side effects and knowing when to seek care, not just application; and he named the Pharmacy and Poisons Board as the body that would need to run sample trials, which is why the team now treats engagement with Kenyan regulators as part of the project path rather than an afterthought. Edwin Odhiambo, June Alfreds and nurse Steve Donell of Youth and Urbanism in Nairobi's informal settlements went further: Odhiambo said flatly that if HePatch can still only be administered inside a hospital, a mother gains nothing from the fact that it no longer needs a fridge, because she makes the same trip to the same limited set of facilities - a distribution and licensing problem, not a temperature one. Alfreds added barriers the team had not identified at all: teenage mothers unaware of the 24-hour window and stigmatised by providers, Social Health Authority registration requirements that undocumented mothers cannot meet, financial dependency and intimate partner violence determining whether a mother can attend at all, and a day queueing at a hospital being a day of lost income. Donell showed that stigma is locally specific rather than generic - in Nairobi hepatitis B is wrongly linked to sexual behaviour and drug use and mentally associated with HIV, whereas in Turkana the same disease is more often mistranslated as an alcohol-related liver condition - and recommended routing messaging through trusted community health volunteers and faith leaders rather than through specialists or the project itself. The result is a conditional value proposition rather than one universal pitch: transport and storage resilience in remote off-grid Turkana, and expanded distribution to non-hospital providers in Nairobi only if paired with a licensing pathway. The team also publishes two arguments against itself - that solving the cold chain for one vaccine could remove a reason to fund and maintain the shared cold-chain infrastructure every other vaccine depends on, and that since the WHO already permits some vaccines outside 2-8 C under controlled temperature chain rules, protein stability may not be the real bottleneck at all - and names its remaining gap honestly, that the Network for Adolescent and Youth of Africa could not attend, so the adolescent perspective 'remains a genuine gap in what we can currently report'.","realWorld":"The need is framed at the level of a specific failure point rather than a continent: hepatitis B birth dose must be given within 24 hours, the conventional vaccine is an aqueous aluminium-adjuvant suspension that loses potency irreversibly if frozen as well as if overheated, and the cold chain in Turkana holds at the county referral hospital but not at the generator-dependent sub-county and outreach facilities below it, across a county of about 68,700 square kilometres served by eight hospital-level facilities spaced one to two hundred kilometres apart, with mean annual temperatures above 30 C across most of the inhabited lowlands. SDGs are used as tests, not labels: SDG 3 as primary with named targets 3.3, 3.8 and 3.b and a quantitative benchmark (28 days at 37 C, the WHO controlled temperature chain condition), SDG 9 and SDG 10 as supporting, and an explicit statement that these are intended contributions and not measured outcomes. They decline to claim a fourth, environmental SDG at all, writing that removing refrigeration and sharps could cut some material and energy demand but the polymer patch, sterile packaging and manufacturing have impacts, so a life-cycle assessment would be needed before any environmental claim - a refusal that is rarer and more credible than a claim. A trade-offs table pairs each possible benefit with its risk and with what would have to be measured to settle it (for example, delivery closer to home against work shifting to already stretched community health workers, measured by training time, workload, follow-up and user preference). The regulatory path runs through Kenya's own Pharmacy and Poisons Board rather than an external or parallel route. On equity they commit that a patch must not become a cheaper, less supported option offered only where health systems have fewer resources, and that any future use needs the same safety, dose and protection evidence as other vaccine formats - operationalised as comparing HePatch against the vaccination a child would otherwise receive rather than against no vaccination, because 'measuring our option against nothing makes it look better than it is'. What they claim now is bounded: antigen candidates designed and tested, no complete thermostable vaccine patch, no demonstrated lower emissions, lower cost or improved coverage.","partners":["Department of Criminology and Sociology of Law, University of Oslo (Prof. Kristin Bergtora Sandvik)","Institute of Health and Society, University of Oslo (Prof. Kristine Baeroe)","NEM - Norwegian National Research Ethics Committee for Medicine and Health","NENT - Norwegian National Research Ethics Committee for Science and Technology","Lodwar County Referral Hospital, Turkana County, Kenya (Dr Vincent Ebenyo)","Youth and Urbanism, Nairobi","Network for Adolescent and Youth of Africa (NAYA, invited, unable to attend)","Forskningstorget public research fair"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6422/wiki/human-practices/kenya-1.avif","caption":"Conversations with practitioners in Kenya, designed as a falsification test of the project's own premise that cold-chain dependence is the main barrier to hepatitis B vaccination","credit":"Team UiOslo-Norway, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6422/wiki/human-practices/kenya-2.avif","caption":"The Turkana and Nairobi conversations were held separately because the team expected - and found - that the two settings would answer the cold-chain question differently","credit":"Team UiOslo-Norway, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6422/wiki/human-practices/kenya-3.avif","caption":"Engagement with Youth and Urbanism, the Nairobi youth-led organisation whose licensing and stigma critique turned HePatch's benefit into a conditional, setting-specific claim","credit":"Team UiOslo-Norway, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6422/wiki/education/gruppebildemheplatket.avif","caption":"The team with the HePatch model during public education work, which ran from kindergarten sessions to the Forskningstorget research fair","credit":"Team UiOslo-Norway, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Design the stakeholder conversation as a falsification test, stating in advance which answer would undercut the project, then publish it when it partly does - and close every round with a three-column box naming the previous assumption, the new approach and the updated framing, so integration is auditable rather than asserted.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/uioslo-norway/","https://2026.igem.wiki/uioslo-norway/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/uioslo-norway/dialogues","https://2026.igem.wiki/uioslo-norway/sustainability","https://2026.igem.wiki/uioslo-norway/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/uioslo-norway/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/uioslo-norway/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/uioslo-norway/education"],"rank":21},"6426":{"team":"CAU-China","id":"6426","section":"Undergrad","country":"China","village":"Food & Nutrition","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/cau-china/","projectTitle":"Fungal Sentinel, with the OptiX phone spectrometer","tagline":"A $12 to $30 phone-based spectrometer and the two-client software stack that turns one RAW photograph into a concentration with an uncertainty attached.","summary":"CAU-China built Fungal Sentinel, engineered yeast that senses mould volatiles such as 1-octen-3-ol through a GPCR and reports them as fluorescence, and then built the instrument to read it where the mould actually is. OptiX is a pocket spectrometer that uses the phone's own camera as the detector: a threaded interchangeable excitation source, a sample chamber with light-trap fins, a collection module, a frosted-glass slit, a transmission grating, and two USB-C reference lamps that calibrate wavelength and spectral response per device. The software is two programs implementing one written specification, a Python reference implementation and an Android deployment client, held together by a parity test suite that enforces numerical agreement between them. The result is quantitative fluorescence with a limit of detection of 0.81 nM purified EGFP on an early build with no emission filter.","awards":["Best Hardware — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Sustainable Development Impact — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Food & Nutrition Project — Winner"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Five explicit hardware DBTL cycles, each stated as a bottleneck that the previous cycle exposed: separate wavelengths, reject excitation, calibrate wavelengths, block ambient light, collect fluorescence. The software is organised as one shared specification implemented twice, with a parity suite that holds the Python and Android implementations to identical expectations on the algorithms they share, so that a field result and a desk result are the same number rather than two approximations of it. Every validation result is accompanied by its limitations.","dataviz":"An interactive light-path simulation in which the reader drags a spectrum to trace a chosen wavelength through the instrument; an exploded CAD view with numbered, selectable components; row-wise intensity profiles of the three Bayer channels inside the automatically detected spectral band with dynamic peak windows shaded and fitted centroids marked, plotted against a converted wavelength axis; held-out-point calibration residual plots; per-channel absolute response curves inside a dual mask with the response-proportional fusion weights shown as a partition of unity and the channel crossover wavelengths labelled; standard curves with insets marking the limit of detection as a dashed line and the limit of quantification as dotted.","datascience":"This is an unusually complete instrument-to-number pipeline. Raw pixel values are first made physical: exposure time is read from TIFF/EXIF tag 33434 and the sensor black level from DNG tag 50714, and the frame is normalised to (raw minus black level) over exposure time, so what leaves the first stage is proportional to a photon flux rate rather than to brightness. Wavelength calibration is two-point by design and validated on a held-out channel: blue and red LED peaks fit a linear pixel-to-wavelength model, the green peak at a nominal 522.5 nm is deliberately excluded from the fit and used only to turn a pixel residual into a wavelength error (reported as +15.3 px, i.e. +5.57 nm), with quality grades of PASS at 2.5 nm or better, WARNING to 10 nm and FAILED beyond, and a FAILED calibration blocking downstream steps unless explicitly overridden. Peaks are located inside valley-bounded windows and refined by a log-parabola vertex fit accepted only if the curvature is negative and the vertex falls inside the window, with a half-height edge midpoint as fallback, windows containing multiple local maxima tagged suspect, and the legacy intensity-weighted centroid still reported as a diagnostic so a reviewer can see how much the estimator choice mattered. Spectral response is measured per channel against a NICHIA white LED whose spectral power distribution the manufacturer publishes, inside a dual mask restricting the estimate to wavelengths both inside the usable 430 to 660 nm band and lit strongly enough, and the team deliberately does not smooth the response curves (smoothing fabricates detail the sensor never measured, exactly where the response is least trustworthy) and does not normalise them to each other (that would destroy the relative magnitudes that say which channel to trust where). Order of operations is enforced rather than suggested: blank subtraction is additive and clipped at zero before averaging so a noisy blank cannot produce a negative spectrum, then response division is applied only where the response exceeds 20% of its maximum and reported as zero elsewhere, because dividing before subtracting would multiply the background up as well. Spikes are removed by a local median-absolute-deviation test with a 2% amplitude floor so the filter does not fire on flat regions. Quantification uses spectral unmixing rather than band integration: the sample spectrum is fitted pointwise over an emission window as a linear combination of the measured reference emission shape (taken as the highest standard minus its own blank, on this instrument, not an idealised literature spectrum), the measured blank carrying scatter and Raman structure, and a constant offset, solved by ordinary least squares, with the metric being the fitted coefficient times the area under the reference emission. Because scatter and offset are fitted out before integration, the background no longer sets the detection floor, and with scattered excitation about 100 times stronger than EGFP emission at the lowest levels the unmixing gives a limit of detection ten times lower than blank subtraction alone (0.81 nM versus 7.8 nM). Three safeguards are built around it: automatic and auditable reference selection with a diagnostic naming every candidate's in-window area, a window that starts just beyond the measured scatter peak rather than a fixed symmetric band, and a t-test on the calibration slope (t below 3 is reported as not significant with the LoD and LoQ flagged unreliable rather than printed). Detection limits follow the IUPAC convention from the residual standard deviation of the fitted curve, LoD = 3.3 s_yx / slope and LoQ = 10 s_yx / slope, with weighted regression supported for the heteroscedastic, approximately Poisson character of fluorescence data, and the reported LoD taken from the lowest exposure block whose slope is significant with that provenance printed beside it. Saved calibration curves are re-fitted on import and rejected if the stored slope or intercept do not reproduce, so a hand-edited preset cannot silently change a result. Validation covers accuracy and dynamic range (0.81 nM LoD, linear 6.6 to 1684 nM, recovery 80 to 120%), EGFP in living yeast, mCherry in E. coli, OD600 against a bench spectrophotometer (R2 0.994, slope 1.02), absorbance spectra matched against a Nanodrop, and stability over 27 minutes at 0.30% coefficient of variation with all 14 stability criteria passed. Limitations are published alongside: the lowest standard was still detected so the LoD is extrapolated, and long 16-second exposures read lower than short ones for reasons not yet resolved.","software":"FSSA (Fungal Sentinel Spectral Analyzer), a Python desktop reference implementation requiring Python 3.10 or later with numpy, scipy, matplotlib and tifffile, with pytest for the test suite and no network access at any stage; MycoSpec, the Kotlin Android client built on Camera2 RAW that reimplements the validated pipeline natively so a RAW-capable phone performs the whole analysis on device; and a CSV Data Cleaner that prepares lamp spectral power distributions from plot-digitised datasheet points, clipping negatives, dropping duplicate wavelengths and resampling onto a 1 nm grid using shape-preserving PCHIP interpolation specifically because a natural cubic spline would overshoot and invent emission structure that is not in the datasheet. Both programs are released under the Apache License 2.0, on GitHub (github.com/LittleSky-CN/Fungal-Sentinel-Spectral-Analyzer and github.com/LittleSky-CN/Mycospec) and mirrored on iGEM GitLab (gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/cau-china/). The instrument itself is modelled and rendered from a Fusion 360 assembly, and the team cites the open-source smartphone spectrophotometer literature it builds on.","stack":["Phone CMOS sensor with RAW (DNG) capture","600 to 1200 line/mm transmission grating","NICHIA NFSW757DT reference white LED with published SPD","USB-C powered positioning and calibration lamp PCBs","Fusion 360","3D printing","Python (numpy, scipy, matplotlib, tifffile, pytest)","Kotlin / Android Camera2 RAW","PCHIP (Fritsch-Carlson) interpolation","Apache License 2.0"],"techniques":["Exposure and black-level normalisation to photon flux rate","Two-point wavelength calibration validated on a held-out channel","Log-parabola vertex peak fitting with fallback and suspect flagging","Per-device, per-channel absolute spectral response calibration","Dual masking to avoid estimating response from noise","Enforced subtract-then-divide order with a guarded division","MAD-based local spike removal with an amplitude floor","Spectral unmixing against a measured reference emission shape","IUPAC LoD and LoQ from residual standard deviation","Weighted regression for heteroscedastic fluorescence data","Slope significance testing before reporting a detection limit","Exposure-block LoD selection with printed provenance","Calibration preset re-validation on load","Cross-implementation parity testing"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"An age-inclusive education programme spanning a science summer camp, one-day lectures, science-themed orienteering and community talks, reaching preschool and primary children through to university students and older adults, with biosensor concepts tied to everyday mould-prevention practice and courseware tailored per age group. Every activity and its stakeholder feedback was documented and used to revise the next session.","ihp":"Integrated Human Practices is organised through an F-Ring model with four stakeholder groups (Fungal, Feasibility, Field, Future) and a Focus-Finding-Feedback conversation structure, with each conversation routed back into the DBTL cycle. The project's origin is a reported need rather than an assumed one: students in Science and Technology Backyards in Malawi and Zambia described smallholder farmers in remote and resource-limited communities relying on visual inspection because laboratory testing is too costly, large, maintenance-heavy and technically demanding, and missing early-stage or hidden fungal contamination.","realWorld":"The entrepreneurship work treats the device as a product and tests that hypothesis against real users, opening with questions the lab cannot answer: who would own the device, a farmer, a cooperative, a warehouse or an extension station; who keeps it working after the pilot ends and who replaces a broken light source three hundred kilometres from the nearest city; how much a household living on stored grain would pay; and what happens if a farmer receives a warning they cannot act on. The technical case is framed around coverage as much as cost, since fungal contamination in stored maize is unevenly distributed by location, depth and batch, so a method that can only analyse a few transported samples cannot represent the warehouse. The hardware is explicitly dual-purpose, usable as a general pocket spectrophotometer, fluorometer or spectrometer by other teams simply by changing the light source.","partners":["Science and Technology Backyards (Malawi and Zambia)","China Agricultural University"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6426/wiki/optix-wiki-package/images/design/hero-cad-render.avif","caption":"OptiX, the phone-based spectrometer, rendered from the team's Fusion 360 assembly. Materials cost $12 to $30 per unit excluding the optional filter, because the most expensive component, the detector, is the camera the user already owns.","credit":"Team CAU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6426/wiki/optix-wiki-package/images/design/exploded-view-cad.avif","caption":"Exploded view of the instrument: interchangeable excitation source, light shields, sample chamber with light-trap fins, collection module, frosted-glass slit, diffraction grating and phone-holder assembly. Excitation enters the cuvette from the side and fluorescence is collected at 90 degrees.","credit":"Team CAU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6426/wiki/optix-wiki-package/images/design/software-wavelength-calibration.avif","caption":"Two-point wavelength calibration validated on a held-out channel. Only the blue and red LED peaks enter the linear pixel-to-wavelength fit; the green peak is predicted from its nominal 522.5 nm and its residual becomes the accuracy the per-device calibration preset must hold.","credit":"Team CAU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6426/wiki/optix-wiki-package/images/validation/accuracy-standard-curve.avif","caption":"EGFP standard curve with the lowest exposure block inset, marking the limit of detection as a dashed line and the limit of quantification as dotted. Both follow the IUPAC convention from the residual standard deviation of the fit, giving 0.81 nM on an early build with no emission filter.","credit":"Team CAU-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Write the analysis as a specification first, then implement it twice and hold the two implementations to a parity test suite; and inside that specification, validate the calibration on a point you deliberately held out of the fit, fit the background out of the signal rather than subtracting a band, and refuse to print a detection limit when the calibration slope is not statistically significant.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/cau-china/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/cau-china/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/cau-china/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/cau-china/integrated-human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/cau-china/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/cau-china/education"],"rank":40},"6439":{"team":"NFLSHS-CHINA","id":"6439","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/nflshs-china/","projectTitle":"CroTeen","tagline":"Microbial crocetin: a controllable cell-factory supplement to saffron farming, taken all the way to B2B ingredient specs","summary":"NFLSHS-China built a fully heterologous crocetin pathway in E. coli (idi, CrtE, CrtB, CrtI, CrtY, CrtZ upstream to zeaxanthin; CsCCD2 plus Neurospora crassa NcALD downstream to free crocetin), then re-engineered it after wet-lab failure from a two-plasmid system into a single-plasmid, two-T7-cassette construct (pET-Ds-Cro) for strain stability under scale-up. They used AlphaFold3, PrankWeb and CB-Dock2 to guide semi-rational mutagenesis of the rate-limiting CsCCD2 enzyme, with the N366G mutant giving a 1.13-fold yield increase confirmed by HPLC. The commercial side is unusually disciplined for a high-school team: a named B2B beachhead, a filed and accepted patent application on the CsCCD2 mutant, two physical MVPs with full formula tables, and an explicit separation of what is designed from what is still unvalidated. They won Best Entrepreneurship and Best Presentation in the High School section.","awards":["Best Presentation — Winner (High School)","Best Entrepreneurship — Winner (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Lean Canvas (problem, solution, UVP, key metrics, customer segments, channels, unfair advantage, cost structure, revenue streams), TAM-SAM-SOM with an explicit refusal to take a percentage of the macro market, SWOT, a risk-assessment matrix, a stage-gated Gantt chart from 2026 to 2032, three named exit options, and Techno-Economic Analysis plus Life Cycle Assessment named as future obligations.","dataviz":"Nineteen numbered entrepreneurship figures: pathway maps for the two-plasmid and single-plasmid constructs, the biomanufacturing-to-application three-stage chain, a capability-gap table, a partnership-network map with a disclaimer about which relationships are confirmed, a risk matrix, a SWOT quadrant and an SDG panel. HPLC chromatograms carry the quantitative claims.","datascience":"HPLC quantification of crocetin as the core analytical readout; mutant screening comparing predicted variants against measured titre (N366G at 1.13x). No fermentation kinetics model or cost model with numbers.","software":"","stack":["AlphaFold3","PrankWeb","CB-Dock2","HPLC","pET-Duet-1 backbone","E. coli BL21(DE3)","E. coli DH5-alpha"],"techniques":["heterologous carotenoid pathway assembly","single-plasmid multi-cassette expression with RBS re-tuning","semi-rational enzyme engineering from binding-pocket prediction","site-directed mutagenesis","vacuum freeze-drying and bead-beating extraction","soft-capsule and essence-oil formulation"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"An online survey plus street interviews run 12-17 March 2026 across mixed demographics found over 60 percent of respondents had never heard of crocetin and routinely confused it with crocin, and that over 40 percent would pay only 5-10 RMB per day for a mood-soothing product. That cognitive gap triggered a dedicated education page and a Xiaohongshu (Rednote) account translating biosynthesis into public infographics. They also presented at the 10th iSCRM and the 1st Grand APiC conference, and built peer resources after hearing that team members elsewhere felt unsure their assigned role mattered.","ihp":"Five explicitly staged iHP phases, each written as motivation, action and integration, with dates and named interlocutors. Phase I traced the supply chain to source: an online interview with Iranian saffron grower Ali Norouzi (17 March) produced concrete constraints (15-20 day harvest window, 1-2 g dried saffron per person per day, water shortage, currency volatility), and visits to Daofengtang Rende TCM Clinic and chain pharmacies produced a real price point of 60-90 RMB per gram and the observation that pharmacies barely stock it. Phase II is the strongest: after near-zero crocetin yield on 12 May, Dr Huang Danqiong diagnosed metabolic burden and plasmid instability and told them to collapse to a single plasmid, which they did; Prof Huang Guanqin then reviewed the single-plasmid circuit against scale-up cost on 20 June; Fapon's technical director on 22 July pushed them off blind screening onto AI-guided rational design. Phase III used Associate Professor Li Chenyang twice to kill an unstable aqueous formulation on physicochemical grounds and pick the oil and capsule routes, and a perfumer, Ms Weng, taught the actual blending process. Phase IV took the business plan to Attorney Zhang on 17 September for NMPA/FDA classification, licensing and labelling risk, which changed their claims language across the wiki and social media. This is iHP that visibly rewrote both the construct and the marketing copy.","realWorld":"This is a real venture attempt, not a canvas exercise. The business model is specifically B2B-first: the beachhead is small-to-medium functional skincare brands and boutique cosmetic R&D labs, chosen because they have shorter decision cycles than multinationals, and the first deliverable is explicitly not a consumer product but standardised samples plus HPLC chromatograms to support a customer's own formulation prototyping. Market evidence is real but qualitative: interviews across the full chain (Iranian grower, TCM clinic and pharmacies, boutique formulators, Fapon, an iGEM-mentor founder, a lawyer), a public survey with reported percentages and a willingness-to-pay band, and a visit to Shenzhen University's fermentation facility. They refuse to multiply the roughly USD 2.0 billion TAM by a made-up share and instead say SOM must be computed from reachable R&D nodes times sample volume per test, which is the correct instinct even though they then do not finish the arithmetic. Hard assets exist: a patent application, Carotenoid Cleavage Dioxygenase 2 Mutant, Preparation Method and Application, filed and accepted, and two physical MVPs with published formula tables down to percentages (essence oil at 0.03 percent crocetin, 0.5 percent vitamin E in cold-pressed olive oil; capsule at 70 percent crocetin-olive oil, 15 percent L-theanine, 13 percent soy lecithin, 2 percent vitamin E). The regulatory path is credible and specific, naming NMPA and FDA classification, production and distribution licensing, and the prohibition on medical claims, with a consequence they actually implemented, standardising functional claims site-wide. The continuation plan is a stage-gated Gantt from 2026 lab validation through 2027 customer testing, 2028 CDMO pilot and 2029 B2B commercialisation to 2030-2032 international registration, where each gate has named prerequisite resources and a numeric-in-principle pass condition, plus three exit routes (trade sale to BASF, Givaudan or DSM-Firmenich; technology licensing with royalties; VC/PE buyout). What is genuinely missing is the money: there are no unit economics, no cost of goods, no price per gram, no funding raised, no registered entity and no incubator place, and the partnership map carries its own honest disclaimer that everything except university support and paid service relationships is a prospective contact rather than a formal agreement. They also list, in their own words, the data still absent before industrialisation, including yield, purity, recovery, batch consistency and pilot-scale mutant validation. Even the downside is faced squarely, including the possibility that fermentation's carbon footprint exceeds agriculture's and that cheap biomanufacturing could destroy saffron growers' livelihoods, for which they propose market segmentation that leaves the high-end plant premium alone.","partners":["Fapon (biotech company; technical director and business development; AI platform exposure and commercialisation advice)","Shenzhen University (Prof. Wang Chaogang, Prof. Huang Guanqin, Prof. Chen Weizhao; fermentation facility access)","Dr. Huang Danqiong (fermentation expert; diagnosed the two-plasmid failure)","Associate Professor Li Chenyang (formulation and safety screening)","Ali Norouzi (Iranian saffron grower and supplier)","Daofengtang Rende TCM Clinic and local chain pharmacies","Li Shiyuan (founder, Shanghai Transformant Information Technology Co.; iGEM mentor; technical evaluation)","Attorney Zhang (regulatory and IP legal review)","Ms. Weng (perfumer; essential-oil production process)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6439/wiki/entrepreneurship8.avif","caption":"Patent application for the CsCCD2 mutant, filed and accepted, shown on the entrepreneurship page as the project's first hard IP asset","credit":"Team NFLSHS-CHINA, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6439/wiki/entrepreneurship10.avif","caption":"Stage-gated development plan from 2026 laboratory validation through 2029 B2B commercialisation to 2030-2032 international expansion","credit":"Team NFLSHS-CHINA, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6439/wiki/entrepreneurship9.avif","caption":"Business exit strategy: trade sale to an ingredient major, technology licensing with royalties, or VC/PE buyout","credit":"Team NFLSHS-CHINA, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6439/wiki/entrepreneurship17v2.avif","caption":"SWOT analysis supporting the B2B-first ingredient strategy","credit":"Team NFLSHS-CHINA, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Copy their honesty architecture: a 'Current Validation Status' block that splits completed designs from data still required, and a partnership map annotated to say which relationships are confirmed and which are merely prospective contacts. Pair it with their stage-gate habit, where each phase of the roadmap names its prerequisite resources and the single pass condition that unlocks the next phase, so a project cannot drift forward on enthusiasm.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/nflshs-china/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nflshs-china/entrepreneurship/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nflshs-china/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nflshs-china/product/"],"rank":52},"6450":{"team":"IISER-Kolkata","id":"6450","section":"","country":"India","village":"Conservation","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/iiser-kolkata/","projectTitle":"FINS","tagline":"An estrogen-responsive E. coli biosensor coupled to secreted bacterial laccase, immobilised in PVA-alginate beads as a contained tank inside an existing wastewater treatment train","summary":"FINS detects and degrades estrogenic endocrine disruptors (estrone E1, 17beta-estradiol E2, 17alpha-ethinylestradiol EE2) in wastewater. Module 1 uses EdcR, a TetR-family estrogen-dependent repressor from Caenibius tardaugens, expressed constitutively from BBa_J23105 to hold the Pb promoter shut; estrogen de-represses Pb, a T7 RNA polymerase stage amplifies the partial de-repression, and the output is either mScarlet3 (detection build) or secreted 6xHis-tagged BPul laccase from Bacillus pumilus, which oligomerises estrogens by oxidative coupling in the bulk phase. Module 2 is a holin-endolysin kill switch whose trigger was rebuilt from UV/LexA-SOS to RclR with the rclA promoter after wastewater practitioners pointed out Indian plants disinfect with sodium hypochlorite, not UV, on cost grounds. The project is sited as a discrete tank after secondary treatment and before chlorination, so the plant's own disinfection stage doubles as containment. The dry lab is the standout: 13 coupled ODEs, exact Gillespie and Linear Noise Approximation cross-checks, Fisher information and a Cramer-Rao limit of detection, a lattice-Boltzmann packed-bed solve, and a bespoke C++ elastic network solver released as open software.","awards":["Best Presentation — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Wiki — Nominee (Undergrad)","Best Conservation Project — Nominee"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A ten-page modelling stack, each page ending in numbers and an explicit uncertainty page that re-derives the uncertainty of the other nine using school-level arithmetic. Deterministic core: 27 mass-action reactions reduced to 13 ODEs under three stated assumptions (well-mixed 1 fL cell so Omega = 0.602192 molecules per nM; mRNA at quasi-steady state since delta_m = 0.231 >> delta_p = 0.0261; one dilution rate for all proteins). Hill repression at the operator fitted directly by least squares in SciPy against digitised fluorescence from Ibero et al. Figure 12, giving K_eff and n = 1.49; the team flags that the repression coefficient was tuned to reproduce the measured leak and is therefore 'an input wearing a prediction's clothes', while every other number is a prediction. A pure elongation calculation from actual construct lengths, with transcription and translation overlapping in E. coli, gives 1.158 min to synthesise and 38.158 min to first photon. Transport: a diffusion-based molecular communication model (built on Adam Noel's framework but for a sustained source rather than a pulse) carrying estrogen from the well through medium, across membrane, to the repressor, justified by measured octanol-water partition coefficients satisfying Overton's rule, with a three-layer cell and conservative-solver mass-balance closure to machine precision. Reactor: a lattice-Boltzmann solve (D3Q19, TRT) of the packed bead bed reproducing porosity to 0.04% and Kozeny-Carman permeability to 0.998x, validated against Zick and Homsy within 2.4%, feeding a geometric depth-removal argument. Structural: AlphaFold 2 (32 models across three runs) on wild-type EdcR, docking of E1 and EE2 to BPul laccase and to the EdcR dimer, plus two independent 100 ns GROMACS MD runs (amber99sb-ildn, TIP3P, GAFF2/AM1-BCC ligand, ~80,300 atoms, 4 fs with hydrogen mass repartitioning).","dataviz":"Figures carry their own epistemic status. Dose-response panels overlay the digitised source bars, the Hill fit as a dashed line and the integrated ODE steady state as a solid line, with the unrepressed control marked. Gillespie histograms are drawn under LNA curves for each of the three core species across the estrone sweep. The stochastic dose-response plots single Gillespie cells as dots, their mean with 1 SD bars as circles, and the ODE steady state as a line, on both linear and log axes. Fisher information is plotted per cell against estrone for four constitutive promoter strengths. A dedicated dry-vs-wet figure and a knob-ranges figure put model predictions against what the bench actually produced. An interactive browser Normal Mode Explorer renders modes as per-residue displacement arrows coloured blue to red on the structure, overlays CCP4/MRC density as contour mesh or solid isosurface, and reports cross-correlation before and after flexible fitting.","datascience":"The information-theoretic treatment is the strongest in this cohort. One LNA solve per estrone level gives mean and variance of each species; derivatives are taken by central differences with h = 0.01*theta (closed form 6.2560 vs finite difference 6.2559 for the reporter at 322.5 ng/mL). ODE, LNA and exact Gillespie (1,500 cells per level) agree to within 0.17% and 0.49% on means, with the largest gap (T7 at 409 ng/mL, +1.8%) attributed to gate curvature the LNA omits. From Fisher information they derive a Cramer-Rao bound and a limit of detection of 54.5 ng/mL at N = 10^3 cells, and show analytically that only K_E1, the noise CV/gain of the molecule read, and N enter the LOD formula (matching the full LNA to 0.5%). A systematic knob sweep raising each parameter up to x1000 with the full 9-species LNA shows amplification scales signal and noise together so SNR is unchanged: three orders of amplification move the LOD by 1.9 ng/mL while three orders of k3 move it by 53. They explicitly retire the Fano factor as a figure of merit here ('a low value means a brighter circuit, not a quieter one'), identify a tighter estrone-binding protein as the only real lever, note LOD scales as N^(-1/4), and then conclude against themselves: surface water and effluent hold under 0.01 ng/mL, over three orders of magnitude below their LOD. Elasticity analysis identifies the Hill coefficient as the largest elasticity (-0.613 on the width of the working window, an order of magnitude above the next constant) and the quantity the wet lab most clearly contradicts. The working window where fluorescence actually encodes concentration is bounded at 147 to 988 ng/mL, a 6.70x span, taken as 10% and 90% of the climb from G_off to G_on. Reactor sizing is translated into plant terms: 95 m2 cross-section for one 57 MLD sewage plant, 889 m2 for all of Kolkata's 534 MLD, and a 3400x bead penalty for treating a 17 m3/day factory stream downstream at the city plant instead of at source.","software":"Quiver, at gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/iiser-kolkata/quiver: a compiled elastic network model solver (enm-solve, ANM and GNM) with a dependency-free browser viewer, the Normal Mode Explorer, and a 27-page PDF handbook. It takes PDB/mmCIF, optionally an AlphaFold predicted aligned error matrix, or a multi-model conformational ensemble or MD trajectory; it outputs mode files and per-residue fluctuation profiles in native formats for VMD, ProDy, PyMOL, ChimeraX, NumPy and MATLAB. The viewer does normal-mode display, cryo-EM density display, normal-mode flexible fitting of a structure into a map, and an AlphaFold-informed dynamics and essential-dynamics workspace. Validation is the remarkable part. (1) A 206-structure crystallographic B-factor benchmark, median Pearson r = 0.633, reported on a single-chain protocol with the 75 multi-chain files flagged as making that a lower bound, and the selection queries, rejected entries with reasons and download commands committed to the repo. (2) Independent cross-check: five structures re-run end to end through ProDy's own parser, Kirchhoff matrix and fluctuations, agreeing to within 0.01 (1UBQ 0.806 vs 0.804, 2LZM 0.578 vs 0.576, 7RSA 0.628 vs 0.628, 1GPB 0.400 vs 0.399, 1HRC 0.192 vs 0.19). (3) MD validation against the two 100 ns trajectories, with the XTC decoder itself verified frame-0 atom-by-atom against the deposited start.pdb before any analysis, because a subtly wrong decoder produces plausible numbers. Amplitude correlation 0.824-0.840 against simulated RMSF over 388 residues, apo and holo agreeing to within 0.016. Cutoff robustness: ANM varies by at most 0.05 between 10 and 18 A and peaks at the 15 A default taken from literature and not fitted, while GNM's 10 A default is shown to be suboptimal here by about 0.06. Directional validation by RMSIP against essential dynamics: 0.715 at k = 10 against a random expectation of 0.092 confirmed over 200 random orthonormal subspace pairs, specific to the input structure (each network matches its own trajectory at 0.715 and the other at 0.51-0.55) and, strikingly, the two MD trajectories agree with each other at only 0.598, so the elastic model predicts each trajectory better than the other trajectory does. Three of 1,164 coordinates carry half the motion. Rigid-body sanity: exactly six zero modes at 20,000 residues with overlap 1.000000 against the analytic basis. 33 tests, a pinned Docker image, Linux/macOS Intel and Apple Silicon/Windows via WSL2, an explicitly stated domain of applicability (compact globular protein-only structures), and a stated requirement that release builds disable fused multiply-add contraction or the sparse-vs-dense Hessian consistency check fails on arm64.","stack":["C++ (enm-solve) with LAPACK/BLAS","SciPy / NumPy","GROMACS","mdtraj","ProDy","AlphaFold 2","Docker","React / three.js wiki","VMD / PyMOL / ChimeraX output formats","GitLab"],"techniques":["Deterministic ODE circuit modelling with stated reduction assumptions","Hill-function parameter fitting by least squares on digitised literature data","Exact Gillespie stochastic simulation","Linear Noise Approximation","Fisher information and Cramer-Rao bound","Analytic limit-of-detection derivation and knob sweeps","Elasticity / local sensitivity analysis","Diffusion-based molecular communication modelling","Lattice-Boltzmann (D3Q19 TRT) porous-media flow","Kozeny-Carman permeability validation","Anisotropic and Gaussian network models","Essential dynamics / PCA of MD trajectories","RMSIP subspace overlap with randomised null","Normal-mode flexible fitting into cryo-EM density","Molecular docking","Reactor sizing and process-train siting calculations"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Between June and September 2026 the team ran a structured science-education programme reaching about 1,000 students aged 8 to 18 across four schools and their own institute, pitched separately for each age band from class 3 to class 12 and deliberately extended to students who are rarely asked. Teaching was mostly in Bengali, keeping the English terms and building explanations around them, because synthetic biology's vocabulary (plasmid, promoter, transcription, chassis) has no settled Bengali equivalents. Rani Rashmoni School (24 June, class 3-4): living versus non-living through a card game, then cells, DNA and a live DNA extraction. Satish Chandra Memorial School (8 July, class 11-12): genetic engineering, CRISPR and synthetic biology as a discipline; the team found this audience knew more of the content than expected and less of the practice than assumed, so the useful addition was not information but the fact that a person sits down and designs recombinant DNA. Bharat Sevashram Sangha (8 July, class 10), a residential school for Scheduled Tribe students: the prepared class 10 session had to be rebuilt from the base vocabulary mid-session, and the team names the lesson plainly, that prior exposure and not age sets the starting point, and that they had not noticed the age assumption because it had held everywhere else. Institute Open Day (10 July) ran FINS itself as the exhibit, including the parts that did not work, delivered forty to fifty times in short bursts to mixed class 9-12 groups; it was covered by DD Bangla, the state public broadcaster, carrying the project to a general Bengali-speaking audience. A week-long institute summer camp for about 70 students from North-Eastern India, organised with Kendriya Vidyalaya, included lab tours, the modelling side of the project and an original synthetic-biology crime-scene investigation. A long-term partnership with Ek Pehal runs Saturday on-campus sessions and Sunday neighbourhood visits for children from settlements around IISER Kolkata, for which the team wrote 41 free teaching files in English, Hindi and Bengali for classes 8-12 plus 36 literacy/numeracy/science files for younger children. A free webinar on Master's and PhD study abroad drew 151 registrants with Dr Deepak Kumar Malik (President, DAAD IndiAlumni) and the Emerging Scholars Council. Education props were built from cardboard, paper and reused items, which the team notes as an unplanned consequence worth keeping: materials that cost nothing to make are materials a school with no science budget can remake exactly.","ihp":"Around thirty engagements written to an explicit template that starts with 'Need: the assumption we were carrying and the gap we hoped to fill'. The project originates outside the lab, on the deck of the Fishery Survey of India vessel M.F.V. Matsya Darshini off Visakhapatnam, where the team lead logged a haul of twenty-six fish before the team existed; months later they returned to the same coast to test the observation. The page's integrity is its best feature: three engagements are documented as having declined to give the finding the team went in for. Mr Mohadep Dutta, who has fished the Ganga since he was seven, could not comment on a shift in sex ratio because it is not visible to him, and the team records that as evidence the effect is invisible without instrumentation rather than resolving the disagreement in their favour. The closed loops are structural. Wastewater practitioner S.K. Ghosh (Director, Effluents and Water Treatments Engineer) established that Indian plants disinfect with sodium hypochlorite rather than UV on cost grounds, which forced the kill-switch trigger to be rebuilt around RclR, an AraC-family activator responding specifically to hypochlorous acid and one of only three HOCl-sensing regulators known in E. coli K-12, chosen partly because it activates rather than de-represses so the lysis cassette is off by default; the original UV/LexA-SOS switch was retained and published as a part for the global market rather than discarded. A SAV Water WWTP engagement supplied the operating envelope (aerobic, 8-16 hours aeration). An oceanographer corrected their dispersal modelling, which had assumed static water and annual averages, and established that any dispersal work must rest on seasonal INCOIS current and sea surface temperature data for the Bay of Bengal. A fish ecologist supplied three zebrafish endpoints (egg-laying, mating patterns, growth) and a two-layer safety framework that now structures the toxicity plan, plus the caution that wild-caught fish do not reproduce reliably in confinement, which is why the team nowhere extrapolates from model organisms to wild populations. An account of broken enforcement changed who the Human Practices work addresses, so community and regulatory engagement now run as two parallel levers of equal weight rather than outreach built around regulation. A hospital-effluent intervention branch was closed rather than kept as an alternative. Literature was treated as the first stakeholder, and stakeholders handed over documents (Central Pollution Control Board sector-specific effluent discharge standards, the Department of Fisheries Handbook on Fisheries Statistics) that are cited as such. Prior iGEM teams were studied as precedent: JU Krakow 2024 for an environmental biosensor in a regulatory context where the compound was not monitored, and Sao Carlos 2019 for documenting a regulatory framework that did not fit the work rather than forcing the work into it.","realWorld":"Deployment is specified down to plant siting and footprint: a sealed tank with cells in a PVA-alginate matrix placed after secondary treatment and before chlorination, so the influent is already low in solids and organics and the plant's own chlorination stage serves as containment. The matrix composition window is argued from transport, not convenience, with alginate alone rejected because ionic Ca2+ crosslinks are reversible and destabilised by phosphate and citrate, and the blend bounded below roughly 1.5% alginate (skin forms too slowly to prevent agglomeration during extrusion) and above roughly 12% PVA (network tightens enough to impede transport). Chassis choice is reasoned against Pseudomonas putida KT2440, the standard bioremediation chassis. Sensitivity is framed as the principal engineering constraint from the outset, citing published EdcR EC50 of 3.32 uM for E1 and 1.38 uM for E2 against typical environmental loads, and the team builds the circuit on a low-copy p15A origin in pTU2-A to trade absolute expression for reduced metabolic burden. The target was set by Indian conditions, where estrone dominates the pollutant profile and is reported at ug/L in Indian WWTP influent, and the economic case is made against granular activated carbon, ozonation and advanced oxidation, which work but are largely absent from Indian plants on capital cost, energy demand and retrofit grounds. They cite EU Directive 2024/3019 on quaternary treatment for micropollutants at plants above 150,000 p.e., phased to 2045, as the regulatory precedent, and are explicit that FINS targets a compound no Indian monitoring framework measures. The claim at the end is deliberately narrow, and the modelling's own verdict, that the LOD sits over three orders of magnitude above environmental concentrations, is published rather than buried. Deliverables left behind include a Biosafety and Bioethics Handbook as a standalone educational product covering pre-synthesis part screening, contained-versus-released design decisions and stakeholder integration, and the genetic engineering and CRISPR slide deck released for other teams.","partners":["Fishery Survey of India (FSI), Visakhapatnam","CIFRI Barrackpore (Dr S.K. Nag, Dr Kavita Kumari)","CIFNET","SAV Water / municipal WWTP engineers","Central Pollution Control Board contacts","Ek Pehal (student-led education initiative)","Kendriya Vidyalaya","Rani Rashmoni School","Satish Chandra Memorial School","Bharat Sevashram Sangha Residential School for ST students","DD Bangla (state public broadcaster)","DAAD IndiAlumni / Emerging Scholars Council","iGEM VIT Vellore","iGEM IISER Thiruvananthapuram","iGEM IISER Berhampur","iGEM IIT Kharagpur","IISER Kolkata Institutional Biosafety Committee"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6450/wiki/software/software/quiver-mode-arrows.webp","caption":"The Normal Mode Explorer, Quiver's browser interface: a structure drawn as a ribbon coloured blue to red by displacement with per-residue mode arrows overlaid.","credit":"Team IISER-Kolkata, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6450/wiki/software/software/quiver-fit-result.webp","caption":"Normal-mode flexible fitting of a structure into a cryo-EM density map, reporting cross-correlation before and after fitting, model displacement and largest bond strain.","credit":"Team IISER-Kolkata, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6450/wiki/model/noise-fisher-information.webp","caption":"Fisher information of mScarlet3 per cell against estrone for four constitutive promoter strengths; the design curve peaks at 322.5 ng/mL, below the EC50 of 409 ng/mL.","credit":"Team IISER-Kolkata, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6450/wiki/model/dry-vs-wet.webp","caption":"Model prediction set against the bench result, one of several figures where the team publishes where the dry lab and wet lab disagree.","credit":"Team IISER-Kolkata, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Teach students to compute the detection limit their design can actually reach, then publish it even when it damns the project: IISER-Kolkata derived an LOD of 54.5 ng/mL from Fisher information and a Cramer-Rao bound, showed by sweeping every gain parameter x1000 that amplification moves signal and noise together, and then stated plainly that environmental levels sit three orders of magnitude lower. For a centre with school-age students, their second transferable practice costs nothing: build every teaching prop from cardboard, paper and reused items, because a resource that costs nothing to make is one a school with no budget can rebuild exactly as you ran it.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/iiser-kolkata/","https://2026.igem.wiki/iiser-kolkata/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/iiser-kolkata/design/","https://2026.igem.wiki/iiser-kolkata/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/iiser-kolkata/software/","https://2026.igem.wiki/iiser-kolkata/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/iiser-kolkata/results/","https://2026.igem.wiki/iiser-kolkata/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/iiser-kolkata/public-outreach-and-collaboration/","https://2026.igem.wiki/iiser-kolkata/education/","https://2026.igem.wiki/iiser-kolkata/inclusivity/","https://2026.igem.wiki/iiser-kolkata/safety-and-security/","https://2026.igem.wiki/iiser-kolkata/parts/","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/iiser-kolkata/quiver"],"rank":21},"6456":{"team":"Jilin-China","id":"6456","section":"Undergrad","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/jilin-china/","projectTitle":"A DNA-based recorder of transient fermentation stress in Pichia pastoris","tagline":"Turn fleeting glucose and oxygen limitation during a fermentation run into permanent, readable marks in DNA.","summary":"Jilin-China built a two-channel genetic event recorder: pGTH1 drives Cre (recording glucose limitation) acting on a lox71/lox66 pair, and PsADH2 drives FLP (recording oxygen limitation) acting on an FRT-LE/FRT-RE pair, each inversion flipping a fluorescent reporter read after the run. Five separate models answer five design questions that experiments could not settle: which synonymous FLP sequence to synthesise, how bulk glucose maps to a promoter input, whether an alginate capsule isolates its cells from the broth, what DNA states the construct can occupy, and which published promoter evidence actually applies. The most striking feature is epistemic discipline: nearly every claim is accompanied by a statement of what the calculation does NOT establish, and when the glucose model's predicted low-glucose crossing time (7.56 h) disagreed with the measured 0.11 g/L at 8 h, the team reported the disagreement and downgraded the 0.05 g/L figure to a scenario threshold rather than a promoter activation threshold.","awards":["Best Model — Nominee (Undergrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Five models, each tied to a design action. (1) RecombiOpt — synonymous CDS design. It works in the real construct context (the 6,628 nt pET28a-FLP plasmid with a BL21(DE3) host profile), correctly identifies that translation starts at position 107 while FLP starts at 221 because of a 114 nt / 38 aa fusion tag, and computes accessibility as an opening free energy Delta_G_open = -RT ln P_unpaired for the contiguous 48 nt window [-24, +24) around the ACTUAL translation start using local RNA folding in ViennaRNA at 30 C with W = L = 210 nt. A greedy coordinate-descent local search over the first 10/15/30 FLP codons (max three rounds, methionine preserved) produced 'target5prime-30', which changed only 15 nt across 14 codons and cut opening energy from 10.6473 to 7.9007 kcal/mol while leaving CAI essentially flat (0.5184 to 0.5246), versus a constrained-maxCAI design that changed 352 nt to reach CAI 0.9948 but only reached 8.3520 kcal/mol. A complementary RNAstructure 6.6 analysis at 30 C compared MFE and mean single-base unpaired probability across the first 30, 90, 150 nt and full 1,272 nt CDS windows. (2) Glucose model — a coupled ODE of enzymatic glucose release, cellular uptake and OD growth. Sterile release was calibrated FIRST and separately in water and in YP medium (no parameter transfer between them) as a sum of first-order releasable pools dD_i/dt = -k_i D_i with r_h(t) = sum k_i D_i, giving the closed form G(t) = G_0 + sum A_i(1 - exp(-k_i t)); a one-pool model was retained unless adding a second pool cut fitting RMSE by more than 40%. Uptake and growth were then fitted jointly with shared parameters across conditions, with time and condition holdouts. (3) Capsule2Memory — a spherically symmetric reaction-diffusion PDE for an immobilisation bead, dG/dt = (D_eff/r^2) d/dr(r^2 dG/dr) - X q_max G/(K_m + G) with Monod uptake, solved under three distinct boundary regimes (prescribed surface concentration; a Robin condition D_eff dG/dr|_R = k_L[G_b - G(R,t)] for finite interfacial transfer; and a finite-bath case with instantaneous partitioning c_g(R,t) = K C_b(t) that solves bath and interior together including the sampling withdrawals). Four model variants are compared — M0 (follows input directly), M1 (diffusion only), M2 (diffusion plus uptake), M2-lumped (one uniform internal state with k_eff = 15 D_eff/R^2, where the factor 15 is derived from the steady-state mean deficit of a sphere with constant volumetric uptake) — and the page explicitly derives the exact volume-averaged balance and states why the lumped closure is an approximation, since Monod uptake is nonlinear so <G/(K_m+G)>_V is not G_bar/(K_m+G_bar). Numerics are a spherical-shell finite-volume discretisation with implicit BDF integration, solved separately across input discontinuities. (4) Recombistate — a discrete state machine over DNA sequences. The 16,098 bp final plasmid is annotated down to coordinates (lox71 at 4,767-4,800, lox66 at 6,050-6,083, FRT-LE at 6,272-6,305, FRT-RE at 7,784-7,817, with the reverse-strand FRT-RE reported in both genomic-forward and feature-oriented conventions), and the state graph is enumerated on an earlier 3,367 bp reporter fragment under specified Cre/lox and FLP/FRT rules, max two recombination steps, yielding four distinct DNA sequences, four transitions and five event histories. The key result is a negative one about observability: the two orderings of events A and B converge on the SAME final sequence, so the final DNA does not retain event order. (5) FermentPromoterBank — a promoter evidence registry (9 core constructs, 8 watchlist candidates, 252 discovery entries, 12 design entries) that keeps sequence boundaries, host and culture conditions in one record, explicitly described as not an activity predictor.","dataviz":"Twenty-two numbered figures, and the captions are the most instructive part of them. Each caption states the axis meaning, the exact computational settings used, and what the figure may not be read as: 'connecting lines guide the eye and do not represent a time course'; 'the panels use different metrics and horizontal scales'; 'Error bars and asterisks are reproduced from the original figure. Replicate counts, the error measure and the statistical comparisons are unspecified, so we do not infer P values or statistical significance from these marks'; 'the graph is a structural calculation under the registered FRT rule; it is not a measurement of four fluorescence channels'. Figure 3 plots mean paired gains with 95% intervals from 5,000 group-bootstrap resamples, and the caption notes the intervals come from saved out-of-fold predictions and do not include full-retraining uncertainty. Figure 1 is a model-dependency diagram that distinguishes solid arrows (within-module workflows and documented design selections) from dashed arrows (conceptual interfaces that are NOT a validated coupled prediction) — a distinction almost no iGEM team draws. Figure 4 shows the three-way trade-off (CAI, opening energy, nucleotide edits) as separate aligned panels rather than a composite score. Figure 20 is a conditional DNA-state graph that visually separates sequence states from event histories, making the two converging paths to S_CF legible.","datascience":"The machine-learning work is a model of restraint. They tested whether RNA structure features add information to expression proxy models by holding the ExtraTrees algorithm, base features and data splits fixed and only adding opening energy and local MFE, across three tasks (Boel expression levels, TIsigner detectable-expression labels, Nieuwkoop mRFP synonymous variants) with grouped five-fold validation and five random seeds — grouping by protein family for the first two and by experimental plate for the third, specifically to stop related samples appearing in both train and test. Gains were small but consistent: Boel QWK 0.1391 to 0.1677 (+0.0286 [0.0229, 0.0344]), TIsigner AP 0.8851 to 0.8997 (+0.0146), Nieuwkoop Spearman 0.7622 to 0.7906 (+0.0283), all five seeds positive — and they then note that even with RNA features the Boel QWK of ~0.168 means expression-level agreement 'remained limited', and that Boel and TIsigner share 2,363 protein-family components so positive results in both are not two independent replications. Crucially, they then DECLINED to use those models to rank their FLP candidates: an out-of-distribution protocol (MMseqs2 10-6d92c family search with predefined thresholds fident >= 0.30 and bidirectional coverage qcov, tcov >= 0.80, plus explicit feature distance, prediction disagreement and construct context) classified all 12 candidate-task combinations as OOD, so candidate selection was made on hard constraints (protein and vector invariance) plus a qualitative trade-off, with the team stating 'we did not add numerical weights after the fact' and that target5prime-30 'is not the unique optimum across every metric and window' since a five-window sensitivity analysis changed the ranking. Model selection followed predefined performance-and-complexity rules that retained simple linear models for two tasks and rejected frozen CodonBERT representations for lack of consistent gain. Wet-lab closure: FLP-Var (target5prime-30) gave a stronger anti-His Western signal than FLP-WT after 0.5 mM IPTG for 6 h and a higher OD600-normalised RFP recombination-reporter curve — reported as qualitative support only, with the team noting the two assays use different regulatory constructs, that OD600 normalisation does not equalise FLP amounts, and that no RNA-decay assay was run so the proposed hydrolysis-resistance mechanism remains a hypothesis. The glucose dataset is 138 concentration and OD600 records; six '<0.02 g/L' readings were retained as upper bounds rather than coerced to 0.02.","software":"RecombiOpt is a released tool (v0.3.0 noted) with host profiles for E. coli BL21(DE3) and P. pastoris GS115, a conditional synonymous generator, a separate 'engineering repair' step that searches for synonymous fixes to declared rule violations and then re-runs all checks, protein and vector invariant verification, and retained tool versions and complete parameters alongside every analysis. The team is explicit that a current optimize run cannot reproduce the entire historical study, and that repair 'addresses whether a sequence meets engineering requirements; it does not predict expression'. The validation table lists, per module, exactly which checks were completed and what evidence supports them — analytical and numerical checks plus replay of a public transport subcase for Capsule2Memory, comparison against an independent solver for the bacterial parameter example, mass-balance and numerical-refinement checks for the tracer experiment, grouped internal validation and OOD checks for RecombiOpt, sterile-source calibration plus joint fitting plus time and condition holdouts for the glucose model, and DNA/junction/convergence checks for Recombistate.","stack":["Python","SciPy (implicit BDF integration)","ViennaRNA (local folding)","RNAstructure 6.6","MMseqs2 10-6d92c","scikit-learn (ExtraTrees, linear models)","CodonBERT (evaluated and rejected)","custom finite-volume PDE solver","custom DNA state-machine enumerator (RecombiOpt / Recombistate)"],"techniques":["synonymous codon design with greedy coordinate descent","RNA local folding accessibility / opening free energy","RNA secondary-structure MFE and base-pair probability analysis","codon adaptation index with project-specific host reference","supervised regression and classification with grouped cross-validation","group bootstrap confidence intervals (5,000 resamples)","out-of-distribution applicability protocol with prespecified thresholds","predefined model-selection rules favouring simplicity","coupled ODE fitting with shared parameters across conditions","parsimony criterion for adding model components (40% RMSE rule)","time and condition holdout validation","spherically symmetric reaction-diffusion PDE with Monod kinetics","Dirichlet, Robin and finite-bath boundary conditions compared","volume averaging and lumped-parameter model reduction with derived closure","finite-volume spatial discretisation","mass-balance and independent-solver numerical verification","discrete DNA state-machine enumeration","event-history vs state-observability analysis","structured evidence registry"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A sustained programme rather than one-off events, organised under the 'Continue' step of their 5C Guidelines: the 5th Annual Community Day, the Apricot Blossom Festival, high-school and middle-school outreach, a Popular Science Series Course, a Summer Science Exploration Camp, senior-community outreach and a Sci-Tech Festival, reaching audiences across generations and educational backgrounds through lectures, hands-on activity and conversation. A promotion brochure is published as a downloadable PDF.","ihp":"The team built a named framework from the sociology-of-technology literature: a Social Shaping Loop of Encounter, Reflect, Respond, Rewrite, grounded in Argyris's distinction between single-loop learning (improving the existing method) and double-loop learning (questioning the assumptions behind it), layered on their own 5C Guidelines (Collect, Comprehend, Compromise, Continue) carried over from 2025, and framed by MacKenzie and Wajcman's The Social Shaping of Technology. They then applied the distinction honestly: single-loop work was adjusting recombinant expression conditions, codon optimisation, leakage-test conditions and hydrogel diffusion; the double loop was realising that a strong fluorescence signal does not establish industrial usefulness, and that the real questions are whether a recorded state accurately represents a relevant environmental event, whether the information stays interpretable after the event has passed, and whether the system works under representative fermentation conditions. Industrial engagement at BYHEALTH and vaccine and pharmaceutical production facilities surfaced stability, process compatibility, data interpretation and operational safety as criteria. Scientific exchange at the iGEM Northeast China Exchange and university visits fed directly into a modelling result: the Recombistate finding that different event sequences converge on the same final DNA state changed the design goal, pushing them toward a modular sensing-memory-readout toolkit while stating plainly that the toolkit is a direction rather than a validated set.","realWorld":"The application target is industrial fermentation monitoring: a recorder that preserves information about transient stress events (glucose limitation, oxygen limitation) that a bulk probe reading cannot capture, read out after the run. Alginate-style encapsulation is part of the deployment concept, which is exactly why Capsule2Memory exists — the model shows that splitting one large bead into several of equal total biomass shortens the diffusion distance, but that insufficient interfacial exchange can still produce substantial error during a long low-glucose event, so size, cell loading and exchange capacity must be screened together rather than separately. The team repeatedly marks the boundary of the claim, noting that glucose trajectory, promoter response and DNA writing have not yet been measured in the same experiment.","partners":["Jilin University","BYHEALTH","iGEM Northeast China Exchange (NECE)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6456/wiki/day-lab/model/model-1.avif","caption":"Figure 1: connections among the five models, with solid arrows for within-module workflows and documented design selections and dashed arrows for conceptual interfaces that are explicitly NOT a validated coupled prediction — a distinction that lets a reader see exactly where the chain of evidence is real and where it is aspiration.","credit":"Team Jilin-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6456/wiki/day-lab/model/model-4.avif","caption":"Figure 4: the three-way trade-off between codon adaptation index, predicted RNA opening energy of the 48 nt translation-initiation region, and number of nucleotide edits, shown as three aligned panels. The locally optimised candidate changed 15 nt and reached the lowest opening energy (7.90 kcal/mol); the full-length maxCAI design changed 352 nt to reach CAI 0.9948 but only 8.35 kcal/mol.","credit":"Team Jilin-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6456/wiki/day-lab/model/model-12.avif","caption":"Figure 12: dynamic responses to low-glucose events under equal-resource encapsulation designs, from the spherically symmetric reaction-diffusion model with Monod uptake. Splitting one bead into several of the same total biomass shortens the diffusion path, but finite interfacial exchange can still mistime a long low-glucose event.","credit":"Team Jilin-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6456/wiki/day-lab/model/model-20.avif","caption":"Figure 20: the conditional DNA-state graph for the reporter fragment, which separates sequence states (S0, SC, SF, SCF) from event histories. The two paths into SCF are different orders of the same two events reaching an identical final sequence, so the recorder cannot report event order — a negative result that changed the design goal.","credit":"Team Jilin-China, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Write every figure caption and every model claim with an explicit scope limit attached — what this calculation does not establish, which constructs and conditions it covers, which arrows in your diagram are validated and which are aspirational — and when a prediction disagrees with a measurement, publish the disagreement and demote the prediction rather than quietly dropping it. Jilin also shows the right way to use an off-the-shelf ML model: run a prespecified out-of-distribution check first, and if your target fails it, do not use the score.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/jilin-china/","https://2026.igem.wiki/jilin-china/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/jilin-china/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/jilin-china/human-practices/"],"rank":7},"6462":{"team":"Eton-College-UK","id":"6462","section":"High School","country":"United Kingdom","village":"Infectious Diseases, Therapeutics, Diagnostics & Oncology","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/eton-college-uk/","projectTitle":"ProteaSign","tagline":"A point-of-care electrochemical sensor that quantifies individual protease activities in chronic wound exudate in about ten minutes.","summary":"ProteaSign is a disposable-cartridge electrochemical diagnostic that separately measures MMP-9 (which degrades the extracellular matrix) and human neutrophil elastase (which degrades the growth factors needed for repair) in chronic wound fluid, turning wound assessment from a visual judgement into a measurement. The sensing interface is a gold electrode carrying methylene-blue-labelled, protease-cleavable peptides whose cleavage is read by square-wave voltammetry, with an independently anchored ferrocene reporter providing internal ratiometric normalisation and a matched non-cleavable peptide control on a second working electrode. The peptide sequences were not guessed: the team built a seven-protease machine-learning substrate predictor trained on 10,472 curated cleavage windows, and validated the predictions with two reprogrammable recombinant sfGFP protease biosensors. It won on the rare combination of genuinely publication-grade dry lab (cluster-aware cross-validation, Laplace-transform kinetics derivations, a physics-based SWV forward model), working hardware, and a human practices programme with over twenty named clinical and industrial stakeholders that visibly moved the design.","awards":["Top 10 (High School)","Best Education — Nominee (High School)","Best Integrated Human Practices — Nominee (High School)","Best Village Project — Nominee (Infectious Diseases / Therapeutics / Diagnostics / Oncology)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Three distinct modelling efforts, all unusually deep for high school. (1) A protease substrate predictor: for each of seven proteases (MMP-2, MMP-8, MMP-9, MMP-14, neutrophil elastase, LasB, and a pooled digestive serine protease group) they trained two additive scorers on 8-residue cleavage windows — an L2-regularised logistic regression on VHSE physicochemical descriptors (8 descriptors per residue, so 64 standardised features) and a BLOSUM62-smoothed position-specific scoring matrix — using 10,472 confirmed windows from MEROPS, Eckhard et al. 2016 proteomic MMP profiling, and a re-extracted LasB elastin-digestion table from Yang et al. 2015. Negatives were constructed 3:1 (half other proteases' real windows, half random Swiss-Prot 8-mers at natural amino-acid frequencies). (2) A surface-bound enzyme kinetics model: they derived both the steady-state solution and the exact biexponential solution for Michaelis-Menten kinetics on a surface-attached substrate using Laplace transforms and partial-fraction decomposition, then proved analytically and numerically that the steady-state approximation is only valid as their single parameter lambda approaches 1. (3) A square-wave voltammetry forward model (swv_forward_model.py) that computes net SWV current from probe-level physics — about 3.1e10 probes at 7.4 nm spacing, with a 1.4 nm methylene-blue lateral excursion used to justify treating probes as non-interacting.","dataviz":"The substrate predictor page ends in a live in-browser scorer ('Try It — Score a Peptide'): you type a peptide, mark the scissile bond, and every protease in the panel scores it as you type, with warm/cool per-position attribution bars that sum exactly to the logit and the PSSM score, and grey bars for unknown (gapped) positions. The sensor probe itself is shown scored at every bond by the MMP-9 and elastase models, with the P4-to-P4' window shaded and the actual cut marked. The SWV page carries an interactive forward-model plot where moving across reads every predicted current curve at one potential. Results are presented as out-of-fold ROC curves, precision-recall curves against a 0.25 prior, and held-out percentile distributions against a uniform null, plus paired difference plots with 95% cluster-bootstrap intervals where a filled marker means the interval excludes zero. Equations are rendered in KaTeX and the human practices page uses globe.gl.","datascience":"The evaluation methodology is the real achievement and is more careful than most undergraduate iGEM dry lab. They recognised that near-duplicate cleavage windows cause data leakage under ordinary K-fold CV, so they defined Hamming-distance clusters (any pair with d_H <= 2, taken as connected components, found in near-linear time via a 3+3+2-block pigeonhole trick with union-find) and used stratified group 5-fold splitting whole clusters, with a nested 3-fold inner CV to pick the regularisation strength C per protease, and the null percentile distribution and PSSM rebuilt per outer fold to avoid leaking into the background. They separated two questions — Detection (held-out positives vs random background) and Discrimination (held-out positives vs another protease's confirmed sites), noting the latter is what actually matters for a multiplexed sensor. They derived and Monte-Carlo-verified an analytic ceiling on measured AUROC under false negatives (measured AUROC <= 1 - pi/2 for a fraction pi of mislabelled negatives), ran three controls (label shuffle collapsing AUROC to 0.49-0.53; composition-only ablation showing e.g. 0.664 vs 0.874 for MMP-2 but 0.886 vs 0.877 for LasB because 76% of its positives come from elastin; and random vs cluster-aware folds, where LasB drops 0.886 to 0.879 once leakage is removed). Scores from the two models are converted to percentiles against 100,000 random Swiss-Prot background windows so they are comparable across proteases, combined by harmonic mean (high only when both are high), and reported as a 'specificity margin' = target consensus percentile minus the strongest competitor's. They also published an explicit list of eight assumptions and limitations, including that additivity costs at most 0.007 AUROC against gradient-boosted trees, that VHSE PCA captures only 64-79% of the full positional signal, and that the harmonic-mean consensus was reasoned rather than validated.","software":"The substrate predictor is released as a protease-agnostic Python package (modules spred.data, spred.model, spred.pssm, spred.train, spred.validation, spred.evaluation, spred.panel) that another team retrains on its own protease panel's known substrates on a basic laptop in a few hours; the team explicitly frames it as a reusable contribution. Hardware: a handheld reader built around the Analog Devices AD5940 electrochemical analogue front end with an nRF52840 microcontroller and a TI TMUX1104 4:1 precision multiplexer, sequentially interrogating four working electrodes against a shared reference and counter electrode, with full KiCad schematics (5 sheets) and an exported bill of materials released as PDF. The hardware builds on the open-source Biocoin wearable multiplexed biosensing platform (github.com/ProfDrewHall/Biocoin; Hack & Hall, npj Biosensing 2026). They also contribute two reprogrammable recombinant protease biosensors with swappable substrate 'cassettes': pES-01 (FLAG-sfGFP / peptide / C-terminal His6, read by Ni-NTA depletion, ELISA, Western blot or SDS-PAGE) and pDUAL (split-sfGFP with GFP11 embedded in an eglin c surface loop, giving a fluorescence readout). Code and wiki at https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/eton-college-uk.","stack":["Python","scikit-learn","NumPy","SciPy","logistic regression (L2)","position-specific scoring matrix (PSSM)","BLOSUM62","VHSE amino-acid descriptors","gradient-boosted trees (ablation)","MEROPS database","NCBI/UniProt","Swiss-Prot background frequencies","React + Vite wiki SPA","KaTeX","globe.gl","KiCad","AD5940 AFE","nRF52840","TMUX1104 multiplexer","GitLab (iGEM)"],"techniques":["cluster-aware stratified group K-fold cross-validation","Hamming-distance clustering with union-find + pigeonhole blocking","nested inner cross-validation for hyperparameter selection","cluster bootstrap confidence intervals (500 resamples)","AUROC and precision-recall evaluation","label-shuffle, composition-only and fold-construction controls","analytic false-negative bound on AUROC with Monte Carlo verification","percentile normalisation against a 100,000-window null","harmonic-mean consensus scoring and specificity margin","gapped-window masking (neutral logistic features, background-weighted PSSM expectation)","Laplace transform solution of surface enzyme kinetics","partial fraction decomposition","square-wave voltammetry forward modelling","ratiometric (MB/Fc) internal normalisation","self-assembled monolayer electrode functionalisation"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A genuinely reusable education portfolio rather than a set of one-off visits. 'What If?' is a team-written and illustrated comic modelled on Marvel's What If...? series, built directly from the four ideas children drew at the Eton Porny workshop (colour-changing plants, bacteria making medicines, programmable cells, healing wounds); over 350 printed copies were distributed in two months and it was translated into two further languages. A 58-page Activities Handbook of printable exercises at graded difficulty, with instructions and answer keys written in conversation with a secondary school teacher, was inspired by Leiden iGEM 2025's approach to reusable materials. 'Bio-Detectives' is a museum-sabotage mystery workshop for Year 8 in which teams work five stations — reconstructing DNA sequences, exploring protein production, critiquing flawed experiments, comparing lab labels, and modelling genetic control through AND/OR/NOR gates — and must explain their reasoning to unlock each piece of evidence, ending in a fixed-budget redesign task; student and facilitator packs plus the presentation are released so it can be rerun. Year 11 volunteers facilitated and reported their own gains ('I'm not a science student but still really enjoyed it because of the mystery format'). They report honestly that the content was too hard for pupils who had not yet met DNA and recommend targeting Year 10/11 instead. Other sessions: a hands-on goat-DNA genetic modification build for 34 Year 5 pupils at St George's Windsor (physically assembling glowing / curly-hair / spider-silk gene templates from spare nucleotides), an edible animal-cell modelling workshop with a published allergen risk assessment, protease kits for a carers' workshop, street interviews (8 of N respondents had no personal experience of chronic wounds), and biosafety videos.","ihp":"Over twenty named stakeholders across wound care, electrochemistry, health economics, regulation and patient advocacy, with a 'pinpoint / event / action' structure that states what changed. Concrete examples: Dr Anatoliy Markiv (King's College London) moved them off pET-24a(+) to pSB1C3 as a reusable starting plasmid, reviewed their primers and proposed a better substrate-swapping method, and pointed them to the split-GFP protease-sensing paper that became their second design cycle; he also required construct sequences for biosafety assessment before permitting experiments. Dr Ben Bullen (podiatry) cemented the reusable-reader / disposable-cartridge split and the ~20 microlitre sample volume, and set a 15-minute workflow target against the team's estimated 30 minutes — which the team records as an unmet goal requiring shorter incubation. Ms Kathleen Leak (tissue viability) and Trish Idensohn drove the requirement for fast readouts and simple operating procedures, which produced the cartridge's standardised metering, dilution and incubation steps before SWV acquisition. Dr Honda Hsu (plastic surgeon, Taiwan) confirmed the device fits a real clinical workflow and his account of delegated wound care created an explicit usability requirement that routine dressing-change staff, not just specialists, must be able to run it. Dr Kevin Lye (Accorto Regulatory Solutions) and Dr Douglas Queen (health economics of wound care) covered the regulatory and reimbursement path; Dr Martin Peacock (Zimmer and Peacock) and Professor Kevin Lam (synthetic electrochemistry, Greenwich) and Dr Ana Maria Totea advised on electrodes and liquid handling; Professor Keith Harding (Cardiff), Professor Steven Jeffery (Pioneer Wound Clinics), Professor Dato Harikrishna Nair, Professor Paul Davis (co-founder of Mologic) and Professor Eleanor Stride (Oxford biomedical engineering) reviewed the clinical and device case. Patient and charity voices included 'Bob', a person living with a chronic wound, Breakthrough T1D and Diabetes Scotland. Feedback also reinforced measuring cleavage rate with calibration across known enzyme concentrations. The anonymised 'David' narrative on the description page is explicitly constructed from real accounts heard through these conversations.","realWorld":"The implementation page is a structured device risk assessment rather than a business pitch: it enumerates infection transfer through reusable components, pain or damage to fragile healing tissue, allergic reaction to wound-contacting materials, unnecessary anxiety or treatment escalation from false positives, and exposure of identifiable patient data, each with a named mitigation (prefer single-use patient-contacting components, biocompatibility assessment of all wound-contacting materials, clinically justified interpretation criteria with evaluated specificity and false-positive rates, calibration and quality-control procedures with error alerts and clear invalid-test instructions, minimised personal data collection with access restriction and retention policies). The intended route to market is a reusable reader plus disposable cartridge for community wound care — GPs, wound-care nurses, podiatrists and carers — positioned to guide selection of the existing protease-modulating dressings (e.g. UrgoStart) and to track proteolytic activity over time alongside wound size. Costing came from the KiCad bill of materials plus estimated enclosure and reagent costs. The team is candid that clinical validation, bacterial confounding of the chosen peptides, and testing on real clinical samples all remain outstanding. A Smith + Nephew work experience business insight day and an Imperial iGEM mini-jamboree (24 August, UK and European teams) fed the commercial framing.","partners":["Dr Anatoliy Markiv (King's College London)","Dr Ciaran Devoy (author of the synthetic protein protease sensor platform)","Dr Brian Callahan (split-GFP protease sensing)","Dr Ben Bullen (podiatry and wound care)","Ms Kathleen Leak (tissue viability specialist)","Trish Idensohn","Dr Honda Hsu (plastic surgeon, Taiwan)","Professor Keith Harding (Wound Healing Research Unit, Cardiff University)","Professor Steven Jeffery (Pioneer Wound Clinics)","Professor Dato Harikrishna Nair","Professor Eleanor Stride (University of Oxford)","Professor Robert Marks (biosensors and biotechnology)","Professor Kevin Lam (University of Greenwich)","Professor Paul Davis (co-founder of Mologic)","Dr Martin Peacock (Zimmer and Peacock)","Dr Ana Maria Totea","Dr Kevin Lye (Accorto Regulatory Solutions)","Dr Douglas Queen (health economics of wound care)","Breakthrough T1D","Diabetes Scotland","Smith + Nephew (business insight day)","Imperial College London iGEM (mini-jamboree)","Professor Drew Hall / Biocoin open-source platform"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6462/wiki/f09.avif","caption":"Out-of-fold performance of the consensus score for all seven proteases: ROC curves with per-protease detection AUROC, precision-recall curves against a 0.25 prior, and the distribution of held-out positives' consensus percentiles against the uniform null.","credit":"Team Eton-College-UK, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6462/wiki/probe-cleavage-mmp9.webp","caption":"The sensing probe before and after MMP-9 cleavage: methylene blue on peptide SGKIPRTLTA joined by a PEG6 spacer to the gold electrode among ferrocene-hexanethiol, cut between T7 and L8, releasing the MB-ATL fragment.","credit":"Team Eton-College-UK, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6462/wiki/wiring-diagram.webp","caption":"Wiring diagram of the ProteaSign reader, built around the AD5940 electrochemical analogue front end and an nRF52840 microcontroller multiplexing four working electrodes.","credit":"Team Eton-College-UK, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6462/wiki/bio-detectives.webp","caption":"Year 8 pupils at Holyport working through the Bio-Detectives museum-sabotage clues with a team member; student and facilitator packs were released so the workshop can be rerun.","credit":"Team Eton-College-UK, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Copy their evaluation discipline, not just their model: before reporting any ML metric, cluster near-duplicate sequences by Hamming distance and split whole clusters across folds, then run a label-shuffle control and an ablation that strips the information you claim to be using — three cheap steps that turn a high-school classifier from a number into evidence. Their second transferable move is shipping the model as a live in-browser scorer with per-position attribution bars, so a judge or clinician can interrogate the prediction instead of taking the AUROC on trust.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/eton-college-uk/","https://2026.igem.wiki/eton-college-uk/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/eton-college-uk/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/eton-college-uk/assets/DescriptionPage-CRFAzJI5.js","https://2026.igem.wiki/eton-college-uk/assets/SubstratePredictorPage-CyEQQMJS.js","https://2026.igem.wiki/eton-college-uk/assets/SurfaceEnzymeKineticsPage-B3hFHqb0.js","https://2026.igem.wiki/eton-college-uk/assets/SWVPage-Dx0cJgd7.js","https://2026.igem.wiki/eton-college-uk/assets/HardwarePage-DvJAf84t.js","https://2026.igem.wiki/eton-college-uk/assets/HumanPracticesPage-Dqe8y5eH.js","https://2026.igem.wiki/eton-college-uk/assets/EducationPage-DjCpVrhR.js","https://2026.igem.wiki/eton-college-uk/assets/ImplementationPage-kdhRbM8d.js","https://2026.igem.wiki/eton-college-uk/assets/ContributionPage-brszWapD.js","https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/eton-college-uk"],"rank":91},"6463":{"team":"Yucai-SZ","id":"6463","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/yucai-sz/","projectTitle":"SpotAway: a dry-activatable emergency stain patch","tagline":"De novo designed pigment binders and a lipase fusion, measured with explicit methodological boundaries on every assay.","summary":"Yucai-SZ designed SpotAway, a concept for a portable dry patch that treats fresh oil stains where they happen. The functional layer pairs a cellulose-binding-module fusion carrying a de novo designed capsanthin binder, for capturing the hydrophobic pigment in chili oil, with a triolein-binding-domain lipase fusion that anchors near oil droplets and hydrolyses triglycerides, all held in a trehalose-mannitol-protected xerogel that is rehydrated with one or two drops of water. The dry lab extended the standard Foundry de novo design pipeline by layering a docking-based binding-ability pre-test onto structural screening, after wet-lab results showed that structural metrics alone could not rank candidates. What distinguishes the measurement work is that every assay is published with a section defining what it cannot show.","awards":["Best Measurement — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Four measurement modules (M1 to M4), each written as introduction, experimental setup and validation, results and discussion, methodological boundaries, and applications. The boundaries section is not an afterthought: it states the wavelength, concentration range, temperature and pH over which each conclusion holds and names the techniques that would be required to go further. Four wet-lab Design-Build-Test-Learn cycles are layered onto a two-round computational screening loop in which wet-lab disagreement with the dry-lab ranking is the trigger for changing the pipeline.","dataviz":"UV background scans from 240 to 320 nm in 5 nm steps for seven separate control groups, with the absorbance maximum arrowed on each; delta-OD bar charts with mean +/- SD, individual significance annotations and n stated; two paired standard curves for the lead binder, one for protein quantification and one for the binding response; time-course photographs of pigment adsorption alongside the quantitative data; lycopene stability curves comparing light-exposed and light-protected groups over 270 minutes with the sample photographs beside them; an oleic acid calibration curve.","datascience":"The measurement wavelength is derived rather than assumed. Seven control groups covering buffer, pure solvent, the biphasic solvent background, pigment absorption and intrinsic protein absorption were scanned from 240 to 320 nm in 5 nm increments, which showed the binder's 280 nm peak shifting about 5 nm shorter in the petroleum-ether biphasic system, fixing 275 nm as the quantification wavelength, with the explicit rule that 275 nm must not be adopted without rescanning if the pigment, solvent ratio or biphasic conditions change. Protein specificity of the response is then tested with a negative protein control, egg white, which also absorbs near 280 nm but does not reproduce a comparable delta-OD on adding capsanthin, and independent-samples t-tests distinguish genuine responses (Binder-1 and Binder-3 increased, p < 0.01; Binder-2 decreased, p < 0.001) from non-responses (Binder-4 and egg white, not significant). Two standard curves are built for the lead candidate rather than one, a binder concentration curve at 275 nm over 0 to 1.5 mg/mL (y = 0.388x + 0.03, R2 = 0.990) to account for protein background and a delta-OD against concentration curve (y = 0.108x - 0.006, R2 = 0.993) measured against a blank at matched binder concentration after a 30-minute light-protected reaction, with the stated limit that the fits are valid only over 0 to 1.5 mg/mL and must not be extrapolated, and that the method cannot yield a dissociation constant, which would require ligand titration across orders of magnitude and separation of free from bound states by SPR, ITC, MST or fluorescence quenching. The most instructive module is M3, where transferring the UV strategy to lycopene produced unstable results and the team stopped to measure the measurement system itself: a lycopene standard curve in petroleum ether (y = 0.1109x - 0.00223, R2 = 0.994) plus light-exposed and light-protected time series read at 0, 30, 60, 120, 180, 240 and 270 minutes showed the OD474.5 signal drifting with an apparent half-life of about 2.5 hours under illumination, which meant an observed OD change could not be attributed to binder activity. The team terminated the lycopene route on that basis and states the conclusion precisely, that the current lycopene assay system lacks sufficient stability for binder assessment, not that lycopene cannot be used at all, and notes that they did not identify the degradation products or separate photodegradation from thermal degradation. Lipase activity is quantified by copper-soap colorimetry at 710 nm against an oleic acid standard curve (y = 0.0123x + 0.0452, R2 = 0.999), with free lipase at 4.19 U/mL and the Lipase-Binder fusion at 3.68 U/mL at matched 1 mg/mL protein (87.8% retention), and the team is careful that the 143% apparent retention per catalytic centre is a theoretical molar correction based on an unverified 1.63x molecular-weight ratio calculated from amino acid composition, not an independent measurement of enhancement. The unit is defined (1 U equals 1 umol fatty acid released per minute at 37 C and pH 7.0) and the assay conditions are justified against the intended use, olive oil as a stand-in for the long-chain triglycerides in cooking-oil stains, 37 C as warm-water washing and pH 7.0 as neutral washing, while stating that performance at 20 C or pH 9 to 10 is not established.","software":"The computational pipeline is built on RFdiffusion3 for backbone generation, LigandMPNN for sequence design, RoseTTAFold3 for pTM and ipTM structure evaluation with RMSD as a designability filter, and AutoDock Vina docking added in round two as a binding-ability pre-screen after the wet lab showed that four candidates with near-identical structural metrics behaved very differently in adsorption. Redesigning 200 sequences on the Binder-1 backbone and docking-screening them produced Binder-5 with the strongest predicted binding energy (-10.9 kcal/mol), which improved about 40% over its parent in the wet lab without overtaking the round-one best candidate, a result the team reports as showing docking can rescue weak candidates rather than as a validation of docking.","stack":["UV-Vis spectrophotometry (240 to 320 nm scans, 275 nm and 474.5 nm quantification)","Copper-soap colorimetry at 710 nm","RFdiffusion3","LigandMPNN","RoseTTAFold3","AutoDock Vina","PubChem ligand preparation","Independent-samples t-tests"],"techniques":["Wavelength selection by multi-control background scanning","Negative protein control to establish specificity","Paired standard curves (protein background and response)","Declared linear range with no extrapolation","Analyte stability testing before attributing signal change","Light-exposed versus light-protected controls with a time series","Apparent half-life as a measurement-window criterion","Enzyme activity in defined units against a calibration curve","Assay conditions matched to intended use conditions","Explicit methodological boundaries section per assay","Dry-lab ranking tested against wet-lab outcome"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"The team runs an education programme and publishes a cookbook alongside the project, with collaborations and a sustainable-development-goals page documenting wider activity.","ihp":"The project began from a questionnaire with 719 valid responses plus interviews with hotpot enthusiasts, used to test whether the team's own experience of oil stains reflected a broader need before committing to the problem.","realWorld":"An entrepreneurship page accompanies the project. The team is careful to describe the patch as a concept whose integration remains to be experimentally validated, and frames the measurement conditions, 37 C and pH 7.0 with olive oil as substrate, as deliberately matching the product's intended use so that the reported activity reflects performance in context rather than serving only as a proof of principle.","partners":[]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6463/wiki/wetlab-oct15/figure-17a5a3588f362703.avif","caption":"Standard curves for the lead binder at 275 nm: a protein quantification curve in petroleum ether (R2 = 0.990) used to account for protein background, and the delta-OD against concentration curve for Binder-2 in the capsanthin system (R2 = 0.993), both declared valid only over 0 to 1.5 mg/mL.","credit":"Team Yucai-SZ, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6463/wiki/wetlab-oct15/original-image22.avif","caption":"Oleic acid calibration curve (y = 0.0123x + 0.0452, R2 = 0.999) used to convert the 710 nm copper-soap absorbance change into lipase activity in U/mL, with one unit defined as 1 umol fatty acid released per minute at 37 C and pH 7.0.","credit":"Team Yucai-SZ, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6463/wiki/wetlab-oct15/figure-15556142df20e307.avif","caption":"Assay stability testing with lycopene: the standard curve in petroleum ether (R2 = 0.994), photographs of light-exposed and light-protected samples, and the time-dependent OD curves showing an apparent half-life of about 2.5 hours under illumination, which led the team to terminate the lycopene route.","credit":"Team Yucai-SZ, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6463/wiki/wetlab-oct15/engineering-oct18-image6.avif","caption":"Change in absorbance at 275 nm for each candidate binder and for the egg white negative protein control after incubation with capsanthin, shown as mean +/- SD (n = 3) with independent-samples t-tests, which separates a protein-specific spectral response from a response any protein would give.","credit":"Team Yucai-SZ, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Before attributing a signal change to your molecule, measure whether the analyte itself is stable under the measurement conditions: light-exposed versus light-protected time series and an apparent half-life define the window in which a reading means anything, and are cheap enough to run before every new target.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/yucai-sz/measurement","https://2026.igem.wiki/yucai-sz/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/yucai-sz/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/yucai-sz/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/yucai-sz/engineering"],"rank":7},"6475":{"team":"BGCFullerton","id":"6475","section":"High School","country":"United States","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/bgcfullerton/","projectTitle":"MycoVela — helping mycorrhizal fungi establish with plants in lunar regolith simulant","tagline":"Protect arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi from the oxidative chemistry of lunar regolith so they can form symbiosis with crops off Earth.","summary":"Lunar regolith generates hydroxyl radicals and stunts plant growth, and arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi (AMF) are the obvious partner to help plants reach nutrients in it — if the spores survive long enough to germinate. MycoVela tests whether pyomelanin, catalase, trehalose and calcium alginate can protect AMF during establishment in regolith simulant. The dry lab is a five-part collection built by a Boys and Girls Club team drawing students from ten schools, and its statistical standard is genuinely graduate-level: a 34-parameter Monte Carlo oxidative-stress simulation, a Fisher-information identifiability and Sobol sensitivity analysis that found exact degeneracies and an unobservable parameter and so changed the model's own equations, a hierarchical Bayesian dose-response model with partial pooling across three laboratories and 400 simulation-based calibration runs, a reproducible image-analysis tool (MycoLens) whose failure cases are published alongside its successes, and a structural screen of KatE catalase surface variants.","awards":["Best Model — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Five distinct computational pieces, each answering a different question, and the chain between them is the real achievement. MODEL-03, the Oxidative Stress and AMF Protection Model, is a Monte Carlo simulation over 34 biological parameters covering side-reaction kinetics, reactive-oxygen-species regeneration and antioxidant effects, predicting AMF germination (24 h) and hyphal development (240 h) under a declared lunar stress scenario phi. Treatments are compared under the SAME sampled conditions, which is what makes the probabilistic comparison meaningful, and the model is built around real mechanism: vitamin C is a strong scavenger of hydroxyl radical and superoxide but reacts slowly with peroxide and reduces Fe(III) to Fe(II), feeding the Fenton reaction, so the model weighs protection against that side reaction; pyomelanin by contrast coats the regolith and reduces stress at source but binds iron. The headline output is a trade-off rather than a winner: pyomelanin protects germination more strongly than vitamin C in 61-76% of parameter draws under every variation of the ranges, but reduces hyphal growth at high doses in 17-50% of draws. MODEL-04, the Measurement Design Model, is the standout. It takes MODEL-03's own equations and asks which parameters the planned measurements can actually distinguish: it computes the sensitivity matrix S, forms the Fisher information matrix F = S^T S, and counts how many parameter combinations a measurement panel determines to within +/-10% (eigenvalues of F above 1/0.1^2) and +/-30%; it separately finds the largest identifiable subset by greedy search under a collinearity index threshold gamma <= 15, and reports both because the greedy subset need not grow when measurements are added while the Fisher count must. Candidate exact degeneracies are not merely asserted but VERIFIED numerically by moving the model 10% along each direction and measuring the change in every observation — exact if under 0.001 standard deviations, against a benchmark that a genuine 10% change in one parameter moves observations by about one SD. Three exact degeneracies were confirmed with their mechanism named (k_fen and f_pH appear only as a product in the Fenton term; p_max and pi_pH only as a product in the germination map; growth sees only Fe_tot/K_N while Fenton chemistry sees only Fe_tot*k_fen). Run on MODEL-03's ORIGINAL parameterisation it also flagged R_0 and phi_sim as exactly confounded, which, with the analytical result that k_dmg, D_50 and D_g50 act only through their ratios, is why the team fixed the damage scale and demoted phi_sim to a declared scenario — a model changed by its own identifiability analysis. Total-order Sobol indices from 512 base samples complement the local analysis, with damage analysed on a log scale because on the original scale 1% of samples carried 89% of the variance. Final verdict: of 34 parameters, 13 identifiable alone, 8 only with a correlated partner, 6 structurally confounded, 6 weakly sensitive, and one (rho_root) unobservable. MODEL-05, the Bayesian Dose-Response Model, fits protection and toxicity curves with a hierarchical model that lets the three collaborating laboratories (UCI, Chapman, Sino American Cancer Foundation) have different protection EC50 values via partial pooling, ec50_s = ec50_pop * exp(ec50_site_sd * z_s) with z_s ~ N(0,1), estimating the between-site standard deviation from the data rather than fixing it. An ordered transform constrains the protection curve to be non-decreasing, and the team state plainly that this is a LIMITATION they cannot fix within the model: if colonization rose and then fell at high dose the model could not represent it, and the separate plant-toxicity likelihood would not repair the missing decline — and they note MODEL-03 predicts exactly that shape on mechanistic grounds, so the two models are in productive tension. MycoLens measures fungal geometry from microscopy images by building a pixel graph and skeletonising it to extract hyphal length and junction nodes. The KatE screen is a structural-bioinformatics design: starting from E. coli KatE/HPII (UniProt P21179, 753 residues; PDB 28WU four-subunit structure, chosen over KatG/HPI and B. subtilis KatA), it excludes positions 1-509 as a conservative rule, then requires every candidate site to pass, in all four subunits, relative solvent accessibility >= 0.35 (Biopython Shrake-Rupley, 1.4 Angstrom probe, 300 sphere points per atom, Tien maximum-accessibility values), <= 5 Angstrom^2 accessibility lost on tetramer assembly, >= 25 Angstrom from heme, >= 10 Angstrom from another chain, >= 20 Angstrom from protected sites and >= 4 Angstrom between basic side-chain nitrogens and acidic oxygens; six variants were modelled in PyMOL 3.2.0a with low-strain rotamers and cross-checked against a five-homolog panel (P30266, P42234, P50979, P95539, Q9X576), selecting K624E primary and K621E backup, with the double substitution deliberately deferred 'to keep the first comparison interpretable'. MycoFerre, the radiation-transport side of the hardware, uses NIST attenuation and stopping-power tables with referenced material properties.","dataviz":"Figures are built to answer design questions, not to look impressive. Figure 4.2 is a measurement-by-parameter sensitivity heatmap where darker means the measurement responds more strongly and is therefore more useful for estimating that parameter — and the caption reads the pattern for you (germination responds to stress and damage parameters, hyphal length to growth parameters, peroxide and superoxide to pigment chemistry, surface coverage weakly to everything). Figure 4.3 shows the identifiability of all 34 parameters grouped by class with a sensitivity floor drawn as a dashed line. Figure 4.4 is the one that changed the experiment: cumulative measurement panels ordered by assumed effort, showing germination alone determines only two parameter combinations to +/-30%, adding the hyphal time course raises it to five, adding peroxide to ten (the largest single gain), superoxide and residual pigment add one each, and surface coverage adds nothing. Figure 4.5 ranks measurements by information added AND by information lost if dropped, which is a different and more useful question. Figure 5.1 plots protection and toxicity curves on one dose axis with 94% credible bands and shades the safe window where both criteria hold (at least 0.10 gain in colonization over control and under 0.10 additional plant damage). Figure 5.6 draws the shape the model CANNOT fit next to the shape it can. Figure 5.9 compares each laboratory fitted independently against the pooled fit and reports that all three shifts are under 0.5 mg/plant and well inside their credible intervals, so with this much data the pooling choice barely matters. Table 5.3 is a prior-by-prior evidence table. The MycoLens image pilot is a published failure report: original, mask and skeleton-plus-junction overlays side by side, with draft reference traces in magenta against MycoLens skeletons in cyan, and the numbers that disagree stated outright (skeleton 3,195 um versus draft trace 500 um on one frame; 1,139 versus 437 on another; 12 um of skeleton produced from background debris in a region with no visible hyphae).","datascience":"The epistemic discipline here exceeds most undergraduate entries. MODEL-03 was deliberately NOT calibrated to the team's own laboratory data, and they say why and what that costs: absolute predictions depend on literature-estimated ranges, so 'the rankings describe the chosen equations and ranges' and 'their stability across the tested variations does not establish the ranking in AMF experiments'. Pyomelanin doses are labelled explicitly as model-equivalent scenario coordinates with no molecular-mass or repeat-unit basis, so the apparent sixtyfold potency gap against vitamin C 'cannot be converted into experimental doses or compared as a measured potency difference' — a unit-honesty most teams skip. The calibration procedure itself was checked against synthetic germination counts with known truth. MODEL-05's validation is textbook Bayesian workflow: parameter recovery on simulated colonization and plant-damage counts, 400 simulation-based calibration runs, 14 prior-sensitivity fits and nine pooling comparisons, with a DELIBERATELY BROKEN equation used to demonstrate why parameter recovery is needed in addition to convergence checks — because a wrong model can still converge. MCMC is four chains, 1500 tuning steps and 1500 draws each at target acceptance 0.9, with a hard gate of R-hat below 1.01, bulk and tail effective sample size above 400, and zero divergences, judged on the worst diagnostic across all eight parameters, followed by the line that matters: 'Passing is a prerequisite for interpretation; it does not show that the biological model is correct.' Table 5.3 grades every prior by its evidence: two rest on a genuine quantitative literature base (Hill slopes from Prinz and Schonichen 2008 and Prinz 2010, chosen over a HalfNormal because that peaks at zero and would make 'no dose-response at all' the most likely shape), two on one-sided bounds from studies that never measured the needed quantity, one qualitative only, and four on reasoning and bounds alone — and they point out that the two parameters which most strongly determine the final recommendation, EC50 and tox_EC50, are among the least well evidenced. They further identify a unit-conversion blocker: every published figure is in mg/L while their dose axis is mg/plant, the conversion needs an applied volume that is not recorded, so both priors currently fall back to scaling from the configured maximum dose — and 'the model reports which basis is in force on every run rather than concealing the fallback'. The ec50_site_sd prior is deliberately wide because with only three sites the between-site SD is weakly identified and 'a tighter prior would manufacture false confidence in site similarity'. MycoLens was verified against eleven hand-defined skeletons at three calibrations and on degraded synthetic images, then run on three public fungal-colony crops WITHOUT retuning — and the results are reported as failures where they failed: default dark Otsu masks followed background texture, particle edges and phase halos; the frozen S1 preset (bright adaptive threshold, 51 px window, offset 15, minimum component 30 px) left disconnected fragments and missed faint strands; settings were tuned on one movie (S1) with S2 and S3 held out and all frames from a movie kept together to avoid leakage; input JPEGs were checked against Zenodo MD5 checksums; and the honest conclusion is that 'these comparisons do not establish biological measurement accuracy' because the missing reference is human agreement, for which they built a blank two-reviewer tracing workspace that presents the same nine regions with no model overlays or AI traces so independent polylines can be compared spatially as well as by total length. They also note that a similar total length can hide completely different traced structures. An independent check against published growth data (Serghi et al. 2021, 219 spores across nine strains, CC BY 4.0) is flagged as extending beyond MODEL-03's configured 240-hour horizon.","software":"Everything is built for reuse by other teams. Each model keeps treatment inputs, shared parameter ranges and run settings in separate files with source notes for every value, and the exact run configuration is published: 0.05 h default step, 3,000 germination draws, 800 hyphal-length draws, seed 20260809. MycoLens saves the input hash, settings and calibration with every measurement, pins its source version and exact dependencies, gives the commands to reproduce each validation figure, and carries a recorded test suite of 99 tests; the pilot analysis names its exact build (MycoLens 2.0, commit 1e030449). The team state the reuse limitation that matters most: the Bayesian model's protection curve cannot describe a decline at high dose, and MycoLens's default segmentation performs poorly on images with different characteristics, so a team using it on new specimens would need to check the masks and validate against reference annotations. Model documentation is also published as a PDF. Two games, Lunar Traitor and MycoVela: Lunar Lab, plus a transport simulator and 3D designs, carry the science into lessons. A U-Net segmentation pipeline exists but is explicitly untrained pending annotated AMF images.","stack":["Python","NumPy / SciPy","Monte Carlo sampling (Latin hypercube)","Sobol sensitivity analysis","Fisher information / sensitivity matrix analysis","Bayesian MCMC with R-hat and ESS diagnostics","simulation-based calibration","Biopython (Shrake-Rupley SASA)","PyMOL 3.2.0a","scikit-image style pixel-graph skeletonisation (MycoLens)","U-Net (pipeline present, untrained)","NIST attenuation and stopping-power tables","pytest (99-test suite)"],"techniques":["multi-parameter mechanistic ODE/kinetic simulation","Monte Carlo uncertainty propagation with shared sampled conditions across treatments","probability-of-superiority treatment comparison","structural identifiability analysis","Fisher information matrix eigenvalue counting","collinearity-index greedy subset search","numerical verification of exact parameter degeneracies","total-order Sobol global sensitivity analysis","optimal experimental design / measurement panel ranking by information gain","power analysis for replicate and dish number","hierarchical Bayesian inference with partial pooling and shrinkage","ordered-constraint transforms for monotonic curves","prior elicitation with explicit evidence grading","prior-sensitivity analysis","simulation-based calibration","parameter recovery on synthetic data","deliberately broken-model control","MCMC convergence diagnostics (R-hat, bulk and tail ESS, divergences)","image segmentation and skeletonisation for morphometry","held-out tuning with group-aware splits","checksum verification of input data","published failure-case reporting","inter-rater reliability study design","structural bioinformatics surface-site screening (SASA, distance constraints)","homolog panel comparison for residue tolerance","rotamer modelling and steric contact screening","radiation transport calculation"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"An outstanding programme for a club-based team. Genesis brought students from ten schools together through the Boys and Girls Club of Fullerton, and over 80% of the schools in their ten-lesson programme were Title I schools, with free after-school and home participation. Across seven school and club locations children used micropipettes, tested protective structures and designed organisms with safety switches; the seven planned lessons became nine. Outcomes are measured and reported with numbers: 83% of Speaker Series respondents reported learning about synthetic biology and 95% wanted to return; across two high-school lessons 82.5% reported greater interest in synthetic biology and 77.3% said they would seek further research opportunities; at Discovery Cube the proportion rating their space-agriculture knowledge highly rose from 26.7% to 86.7%; at Rocket Fever 95.5% reported learning more about space agriculture. Activities include a Moon Farm Challenge, a Save the Moon Plant model and hands-on roots-and-AMF models, plus two original games. Individual learners are spotlighted by name and story rather than counted (Ryan sharing his designs at Speaker Series, Cora teaching her parents at Discovery Cube, Anya explaining fungal networks over Zoom).","ihp":"Structured as four repeating steps — Aspiration, Action, Analysis, Adaptation — with each cycle starting from a question, recording the feedback received, and explaining what was done with it, then linking that decision to the specific experimental plan, model, design or activity it changed. The team are explicit that some conversations made them let an idea go, and they name which: Robertas Ursache's feedback led them away from CIF peptides, Julie Brisset changed how they planned their regolith mixtures, and Ian Sanders pushed them to look more closely at moisture and spore germination. A stakeholder assessment table matches each question to relevant expertise across six perspectives — plant and space biology (Marzan, Ursache, Blancaflor, Sanders, Levy, Berliner), regolith and lunar systems (Horanyi, Amoros Trepat, Brisset, Yong), safety and future use (Kutz, Demick, Fulmer, Exponent), educators and families, design and reuse, and prospective users — and, unusually, it also tracks which perspectives their records do NOT yet cover. Dr Florian Schunck advised on using leave-one-out validation and WAIC to compare alternative model structures, and Dr Marco Bisoffi of Chapman served as scientific advisor; the honesty extends to the business side, where they write that 'confirmed adoption and purchasing decisions remain to be demonstrated'.","realWorld":"The scientific case is built on cited evidence rather than enthusiasm: Hendrix et al. (2024) found experimentally reduced lunar simulants generated roughly 5 to 100 times more hydroxyl radicals in deionized water than non-reduced simulants, linked to metallic iron from reduction; Paul et al. (2022) grew Arabidopsis in Apollo 11, 12 and 17 regolith and found about 71% of differentially expressed genes associated with salt, metal or ROS stress, with the most mature sample (Apollo 11) producing the slowest growth; Atkin et al. (2026) showed an AMF inoculum let chickpeas set seed in up to 75% LHS-1 simulant but not in 100%, where plants were colonised and survived two weeks longer yet died without flowering. The commercial plan is deliberately terrestrial first and candid about what it needs: it targets nursery and transplant growers, and the team state they 'will need to find a crop and stress condition where adding the carrier improves on existing inoculants', that potential use in degraded soil would require separate work, and that they would simplify the formulation if fewer components work just as well. Cost per treatment is published.","partners":["Boys & Girls Club of Fullerton","University of California, Irvine","Chapman University","Sino American Cancer Foundation","Fleet Science Center","Discovery Cube","Inside the Outdoors","America on Tech","Apple Pi","CDE Foundation","LA STEM Collective","Max Apogee","Exponent","Azusa Pacific University"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6475/wiki/models/models/source-p35-1.avif","caption":"Figure 4.2: sensitivity of each planned measurement to each of the 34 model parameters. Darker cells mean the measurement responds more strongly and is therefore more useful for estimating that parameter — germination tracks the stress and damage parameters, hyphal length the growth parameters, peroxide and superoxide the pigment chemistry, and surface coverage almost nothing.","credit":"Team BGCFullerton, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6475/wiki/models/models/source-p40-1.avif","caption":"Figure 5.1: protection and toxicity curves on the same dose axis with 94% credible bands from the hierarchical Bayesian model. A dose enters the safe window only where both criteria hold — at least a 0.10 gain in colonization over control and under 0.10 additional plant damage — so the recommendation is a window, not a number.","credit":"Team BGCFullerton, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6475/wiki/models/models/table-5-3-model-priors.avif","caption":"Table 5.3: every prior in the Bayesian model with the evidence behind it, graded. Only two rest on a quantitative literature base; two rest on one-sided bounds from studies that never measured the quantity needed, one is qualitative, and four rest on reasoning alone — including the two parameters that most strongly determine the final dose recommendation.","credit":"Team BGCFullerton, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6475/wiki/models/mycolens-figure-11-1.avif","caption":"Figure 11.1: MycoLens output on a public fungal-colony image — original, mask, and overlay with the extracted skeleton in red and junction nodes in yellow. The team ran the tool on public images without retuning and published where it failed, noting the colony is not AMF and that these comparisons do not establish biological measurement accuracy.","credit":"Team BGCFullerton, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Before you fit anything, run an identifiability analysis on your own model: build the sensitivity matrix, form the Fisher information matrix, count how many parameter combinations each candidate measurement panel can actually pin down, and verify suspected degeneracies numerically by perturbing along them. BGCFullerton used exactly this to discover that germination alone constrained two parameter combinations while adding peroxide raised it to ten — changing both their equations and the wet lab's data request — and they pair it with a prior-by-prior evidence table that grades how much each number is really known. Both are achievable by high-school students and are worth more than a larger simulation.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/bgcfullerton/","https://2026.igem.wiki/bgcfullerton/model/","https://2026.igem.wiki/bgcfullerton/software/","https://2026.igem.wiki/bgcfullerton/description/","https://2026.igem.wiki/bgcfullerton/engineering/","https://2026.igem.wiki/bgcfullerton/results/","https://2026.igem.wiki/bgcfullerton/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/bgcfullerton/education/","https://2026.igem.wiki/bgcfullerton/entrepreneurship/","https://2026.igem.wiki/bgcfullerton/hardware/"],"rank":7},"6478":{"team":"Athens","id":"6478","section":"Overgrad","country":"Greece","village":"Conservation","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/athens/","projectTitle":"ApiconIASIS","tagline":"Healing honeybees, sustaining pollinators: a precision phage-derived enzyme therapy for European Foulbrood","summary":"ApiconIASIS targets European Foulbrood (EFB), a statutory honeybee brood disease caused by Melissococcus plutonius for which the only legal response in most of Europe is burning the colony. The team mined 165 M. plutonius genomes for dormant prophages, ranked hundreds of candidate lysins and selected two enzymes (an endolysin and a GH25 muramidase), each built with and without a fused antimicrobial peptide, expressed and purified in E. coli. They showed roughly 40% loss of OD600 against M. plutonius (LMG 20360) with 50 ug/mL purified endolysin while producing no effect distinguishable from the untreated control against the bee-gut commensals Lactobacillus apis and Bombilactobacillus mellis, both Lactobacillales like the pathogen. It won because the whole chain is closed: a protein (not a replicating phage) delivered in brood food, three linked dry-lab models (protein optimisation, larval-gut pharmacokinetics, bioprocess scale-up), and an entrepreneurship case built on the cost of hive burning.","awards":["Top 10 (Overgrad)","Best Model — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Education — Nominee (Overgrad)","Best Entrepreneurship — Winner (Overgrad)","Best Conservation Project — Winner"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Three distinct model layers. (1) A semi-rational protein engineering cascade for the poorly soluble GH25 muramidase (Protein-Sol 0.411, below the 0.45 aggregation threshold, with inclusion bodies confirmed in the wet lab): a 40-residue 'freeze list' built from three independent evidence sources (structural role, ESM-2 650M evolutionary constraint, literature), validated by all-atom molecular dynamics (RMSF < 2 A), then ThermoMPNN point-mutation ddG scanning, an ESM-2 log-likelihood filter at -2.0 to drop family-implausible substitutions, NSGA-II multi-objective search via pymoo over the 17 surviving mutations, and ColabFold refolding as a final structural gate catching epistasis; AlphaFold pLDDT > 70 was a stated input requirement. (2) A deterministic single-compartment ODE pharmacokinetic model of the honeybee larval midgut treating the lumen as a sealed, expanding compartment and the pathogen as absolute cell number N, with an Emax saturating kill law fitted to in-vitro lysis data (phi_max ~ 0.006125 /min, KE ~ 0.633 ug/mL, R2 = 0.935). (3) A bioprocess flowsheet model of a medium-scale E. coli plant with a three-stage seed train (baffled shake flask, seed bioreactor, production fermenter under high-cell-density culture), solving for biomass and product mass per batch.","dataviz":"The wiki stages results as a narrative rather than a figure dump: the landing page counts down the disease (90% brood mortality, 36% of surveyed colonies carrying the bacterium with 72% of those looking healthy) before showing the funnel 165 genomes to hundreds of candidates to two enzymes to one lead, then flask to bioreactor to hive to landscape. The model section front-loads a one-sentence summary of each pipeline and marks P1-P4 as falsifiable predictions, with P4 flagged as the main untested exposure because binding selectivity was never an optimisation objective. The optimisation page carries a Venn diagram of the three freeze-list evidence sources, RMSF and DCCM plots from the MD run, an ESM-2 log-likelihood filter plot and the NSGA-II Pareto front.","datascience":"Biological measurements were converted into decision rules rather than descriptive statistics. A pH-plate experiment was decomposed into two separable effects: kill rate is essentially flat across the lumen band (pH 5.5-7.5) while stability is strongly pH-dependent (t_half ~140-280 h at pH 5.5-6.7, ~7 h at pH 4, ~12 h at pH 7.5), which showed the enzyme is about 30x more stable in the lumen than assumed and dropped the required food concentration about 31-fold, making dilution rather than degradation the dominant loss term. Because nurse bees feed roughly 4,300 times a day, delivery was modelled as a continuous infusion at quasi-steady state. Full sterilisation within 48 h holds only up to about 455 cells (a saturation, not a dose, limit; a 300-cell inoculum already needs 26.2 ug/mL against a larva-safe cap of 23 ug/mL), so the team switched to a 'recovery' criterion that raised the handleable inoculum by four to five orders of magnitude to about 10^7 cells. The model's stated output is a starting dose plus an exposure profile (peak concentration, AUC, dosing duration, clearance time) handed to the wet lab and to a companion toxicity model.","software":"ApiconIASIS: Bee Wanderer, a browser-based educational game built for the EU-CONEXUS Hackathon in plain JavaScript, HTML5 Canvas, CSS3 and Three.js with no game engine: a custom 2D platformer engine (requestAnimationFrame loop, AABB collision, sinusoidal moving platforms, parallax) in level-engine.js with per-level config files, plus an interactive WebGL globe using Three.js OrbitControls and raycasting for level selection across Athens, the Himalayas, Tanzania, Uganda and New Zealand. Collectibles map to biotech stages (DNA Pollen, Enzyme Drops, Purification Beads); progression persists in localStorage with no backend, and a Weather Station pulls live data from Open-Meteo and wttr.in. All dry-lab scripts are released at https://github.com/igemathens2026/iGEM-Athens-2026---Software-; the wiki repository is gitlab.igem.org/2026/athens.","stack":["ESM-2 650M","ThermoMPNN","pymoo (NSGA-II)","ColabFold","AlphaFold","Protein-Sol","all-atom molecular dynamics (RMSF, DCCM)","Python","JavaScript / HTML5 Canvas","Three.js / WebGL","Open-Meteo API","wttr.in API","GitHub","GitLab"],"techniques":["multi-objective Pareto optimisation (NSGA-II)","protein language model constraint profiling","hard-constraint freeze lists from multi-source evidence","ddG stability scanning","structural validation gate (refolding)","single-compartment ODE pharmacokinetics","Emax saturating kill-law fitting","prophage mining across 165 genomes","bioprocess flowsheet simulation","seed-train scale-up modelling"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education was run as a programme rather than a set of visits, across age groups and education levels, and deliberately bilingual (every pamphlet and deck in English and Greek). At NTUA Open Days (17 March 2026) they reached over 100 STEM-track candidates at an engineering school where students have largely dropped biology, pairing an interactive presentation on industrial biotechnology and its ethical framework with a tour of the Laboratory of Biotechnology and Industrial Biocatalysis; the team recorded that the students were most engaged by ethics, and built that framing into every later event. The portfolio also includes a multi-day summer programme at Villa Aimilia (design-a-microbe, strawberry DNA extraction, bees-leaves-cells), Second Chance Schools in Peristeri and Piraeus for adult learners, the 4th Panhellenic Synthetic Biology Riddle Competition, ChemExpo, the Pasteur institute and iGEM Fest. The Bee Wanderer game extends the same material into a free browser format.","ihp":"The human practices page is written as a ledger of what the project gave up. Two requirements came from beekeeping, not from the team, and now define success: the protein must reach the brood, and it must survive the larval gut. Delivery was moved from spray to feed because adjuvant surfactants are documented to harm bees and because the person holding the sprayer inhales it; protective equipment therefore appears in the protocols, not in the product. They chose a purified non-replicating enzyme over a live phage knowing it is weaker and more expensive, because a protein cannot spread, establish or transfer genes. They counter-screened against Lactobacillus apis and Bombilactobacillus mellis, the closest relatives of the pathogen in the hive, instead of easier distant organisms, and they used a reduced-virulence M. plutonius lineage although a virulent strain was available, accepting a weaker efficacy claim. Advisor Anastasis Galanis and beekeeper Peter Kasztelewicz (whose own hive footage is on the wiki) shaped these choices while they were being made; Peter's gentler methods, requeening and partial clean-out, are what motivated the feed route.","realWorld":"ApiconIASIS is positioned as the first target-specific sustainable EFB treatment, with the value proposition pinned to a quantified loss: quarantine and hive burning halt honey production for about eight weeks on top of the destroyed colony. Unlike antibiotics (not authorised in the EU, and resistance-breeding where used) or fungal extracts, the enzyme is argued to leave the bee microbiome intact and to leave no residue in honey, preserving market value. The business plan carries a pitch deck and an investor one-pager; the entrepreneurial analysis includes a customer map built from interviews with commercial beekeeping companies and individual beekeepers, and the scale-up model gives the costing basis (105 L final working volume, 51.62 g/L maximum biomass, 2.55 g product per batch) with the explicit target of pricing below the financial loss of hive burning so that no beekeeper is excluded.","partners":["Peter Kasztelewicz ('Beeman'), beekeeper, UK","Anastasis Galanis (team advisor)","National Technical University of Athens, School of Chemical Engineering (Prof. E. Topakas)","Laboratory of Biotechnology and Industrial Biocatalysis, NTUA","EU-CONEXUS Hackathon","TechnosetBee","Greek beekeeping associations","Villa Aimilia summer programme","Second Chance Schools, Peristeri and Piraeus","Hellenic Pasteur Institute","Twist Bioscience","SnapGene"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6478/wiki/optimization/fig7-pareto.avif","caption":"Pareto front from the NSGA-II search over the 17 mutable positions, trading predicted solubility against thermostability (ddG) for the GH25 muramidase; variants A, B and C were selected along this front.","credit":"Team Athens, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6478/wiki/optimization/venn-freeze.avif","caption":"Venn diagram of the three independent evidence sources (structural role, ESM-2 evolutionary constraint, literature) used to build the 40-residue freeze list; a position was frozen only if at least two sources agreed.","credit":"Team Athens, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6478/wiki/optimization/fig6a-rmsf.avif","caption":"Root-mean-square fluctuation from the all-atom MD run, confirming that the frozen residues are genuinely rigid (RMSF below 2 A) and turning the freeze list from a heuristic into a tested claim.","credit":"Team Athens, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6478/wiki/education/day2-strawberry-dna-villa-aimilia.avif","caption":"Strawberry DNA extraction with children at the Villa Aimilia summer programme, day two of a hands-on sequence that began with design-a-microbe and ended with bees, leaves and cells.","credit":"Team Athens, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Copy the freeze-list discipline: before optimising anything, lock the residues (or variables) that at least two independent lines of evidence call functional, then prove the lock with a simulation, and only then search aggressively over what is left; it converts a student ML pipeline into a defensible claim. Equally transferable is Athens' habit of writing down what each stakeholder conversation cost them (spray to feed, phage to enzyme, virulent to weak strain), which is far more persuasive to judges than a list of meetings.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/athens/","https://2026.igem.wiki/athens/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/athens/model/in-silico-optimization","https://2026.igem.wiki/athens/model/pharmacokinetics-model","https://2026.igem.wiki/athens/model/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/athens/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/athens/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/athens/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/athens/entrepreneurship/business-plan"],"rank":136},"6479":{"team":"PSI Korea","id":"6479","section":"High School","country":"South Korea","village":"Biomanufacturing / materials and measurement (Best Village Project nominee; the village is not named on the wiki)","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/psi-korea/","projectTitle":"Bio Color ID - design and validation of a product authentication system using synthetic biology","tagline":"An authentication tag whose identity is the material itself, read as 60 optical features","summary":"Bio Color ID is a counterfeit-detection tag made by casting biologically produced indigoid pigments into bacterial PHB, so that the authentication feature is the material's own optical response rather than a printed code that can be copied or transferred. Two pathways were engineered into E. coli - phaCAB for PHB from acetyl-CoA, and a tryptophan-derived halogenated-indigoid route - with the team solving substrate competition between the halogenase and TnaA by deleting chromosomal tnaA by lambda-Red, moving the host to BL21-AI to stop T7 leakage, screening seven TnaA variants for intermediate rather than maximal activity, and screening six halogenases before settling on SttH. Tags are then read by a team-built reader: a camera plus five LEDs over four coloured backgrounds, giving 60 RGB features per tag. The team shows that three independently fabricated tags agree to Pearson r >= 0.9977 (MAE 3.58 DN) while visually indistinguishable tags and watercolour paper imitations separate clearly.","awards":["Best Presentation — Nominee (High School)","Best Wiki — Nominee (High School)","Best Village Project — Nominee (Space / Foundational Advance / Software & AI / Biomanufacturing)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Measurement science and statistical modelling rather than mechanistic simulation, and done to a standard most undergraduate teams do not reach. The matching model (BioColor Verify) explicitly decomposes variance into capture variance (repeated photographs of one tag) and specimen variance (independently manufactured tags of the same recipe), standardises each of the 60 features by its own standard deviation, pools variance across colour IDs with the assumption stated and flagged, and weights specimen means equally so a heavily photographed tag cannot dominate the reference centre. Matching combines three metrics (standardised distance, maximum single-feature deviation, outlier count) rather than one distance, because a single large deviation gets diluted in a 60-dimensional norm. Thresholds are set by whole-specimen holdout - all captures of one tag are removed, the model is rebuilt, and the excluded tag is scored - with the team noting that holding out single captures would leak. Rejection of unregistered tags is framed as open-set recognition. Design review is anchored to the Eurachem method-validation guide.","dataviz":"60-feature profile plots with a fixed, documented ordering (background -> LED -> channel) so any mismatching feature is traceable back to one illumination, one background region and one channel; overlaid profiles for independently fabricated tags with min-max shading; side-by-side profiles of tags versus paper imitations in three colours; sensitivity-score charts per lighting/background configuration; cumulative pixel-selection curves across tolerance; absorption spectra for pigment identification. Every figure caption states what the result does not establish.","datascience":"MAE, RMSE and Pearson r reported together with the explicit warning that high correlation does not imply agreement in absolute value; 51 of 60 features within 10 DN across three tags; variance-ratio feature screening that subtracts repeat-capture variance from between-specimen variance and floors negatives at zero (49 of 60 features positive, 11 zeroed); a specimen-variability sensitivity score of 34.6 across all features, with the team pointing out that a higher score is not automatically good because the signal being measured is manufacturing noise. Algorithm performance is evaluated on synthetic data generated from measured variation (480 records = 4 IDs x 4 specimens x 5 captures x 6 random datasets), and the report states repeatedly that these are synthetic results and do not establish authentication performance on physical tags. Instrument-level caveats are unusually sharp: JPEG gamma and colour correction mean RGB is not proportional to light intensity, RGB565 bit-shift maxima are 248/252/248 so a value of 248 does not prove saturation, and records before 28 September 2026 have illumination labels offset by one acquisition step.","software":"Three programs sharing one database: an exploratory pixel/region analyser written in Python with Streamlit (region statistics including mean, SD, quartiles, coefficient of variation and saturation fraction, with a warning below 20 selected pixels, and pixel selection by maximum channel difference, RGB Euclidean distance or channel ratio), a data-acquisition tool, and the BioColor Verify matching application. Database connection handling was tested against four mock servers, row-level security policies block direct client access to classification tables, and the admin key is kept in server environment variables. The team states candidly that integration testing against the live server was blocked by network restrictions, that the analyser still needs a local Python process and ships as an archive, and that at the record cutoff the public repository and release commit were not finalised although lockfiles, schema scripts and an example environment config were prepared.","stack":["Python","Streamlit (exploratory pixel/region analyser)","scikit-learn","ESP32-S3 with ESP-IDF LEDC for LED control","GC0308 camera module (RGB565 -> JPEG quality 80)","CAD and 3D printing for the reader shell and tag jig","server database with row-level security","UV-Vis absorption spectroscopy, FTIR, Nile red staining"],"techniques":["60-feature optical fingerprinting (5 LEDs x 4 backgrounds x RGB)","two-level variance decomposition (capture vs specimen)","whole-specimen holdout validation and threshold setting","multi-metric matching (standardised distance + max deviation + outlier count)","open-set recognition framing with explicit Mismatch reasons","MAE / RMSE / Pearson r reported jointly with interpretation caveats","variance-ratio feature selection with noise floor","synthetic-data algorithm testing with perturbation types and fixed random seeds","gray-card normalisation with its approximation limits stated","fixed-ROI coordinates stored as image fractions for resolution independence","independent third-party hardware rebuild as a reproducibility test"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Maker Faire Seoul 2026, where roughly 100 visitors over two days engaged with the exhibit, and the team recorded the questions rather than the headcount: imitation resistance, whether a dedicated reader is really needed, identification performance, LED selection, how it compares with QR codes and holograms, and variation between smartphones. Each question was converted into a named development priority (evaluation with independent samples, light-source characterisation, calibration with reference samples, simplified reading procedure, total cost assessment). The team also learned anti-counterfeiting design from the Bank of Korea Money Museum and discussed consumer verification behaviour with industry at Seoul Beauty Week (DDP) and the KINTEX K-Beauty Expo.","ihp":"Expert consultation that visibly changed the measurement protocol. Professor Youngkyung Park first assessed whether LED-plus-RGB-camera measurement was feasible at all; the team then measured samples and returned for a second consultation, which produced the requirement to separate material contributions from instrument contributions. Professor Sungsoo Kang covered measurement consistency and operating procedures. Professor Brian T. Cunningham advised by email to use LEDs with known output spectra and pointed them toward work combining reference samples with computational analysis - the team responded by disabling auto-exposure and auto-white-balance, fixing per-illumination exposure and recording imaging conditions. Dr Jina Son challenged the environmental rationale directly, noting that using PHB in a small marker does not by itself justify the material, which pushed the team into scoping application range, production consistency and extraction time. Industry feedback on adoption cost and verification procedure is what defined the B2B model.","realWorld":"An agreement with cosmetics company IEUM&Co. to supply real products so the team can test attachment position, packaging curvature, damage, removal and transfer, and readout ease, with the team stating that they will judge the collaboration by recording product provision, attachment trials, field readout and actual adoption. Collaboration with K-beauty brand Atelier Glow on product application. Arts collaborator CRETION made the watercolour paper imitations that serve as the negative controls. The most striking real-world validation is on hardware: four mechanical engineering students from Hanyang University rebuilt the reader from the released documentation alone, buying parts from the same vendors and printing the released files with the same slicer settings. The team is careful about what it has not shown: a profile match does not establish tag uniqueness or distribution history, and acceptance of genuine physical tags and rejection of unregistered ones has not yet been measured.","partners":["IEUM&Co. (cosmetics company, product supply agreement)","Atelier Glow (K-beauty brand)","CRETION (arts collaborator, imitation samples)","Professor Youngkyung Park (optical measurement)","Professor Sungsoo Kang (measurement consistency)","Professor Brian T. Cunningham (advised by email on LED spectra and reference samples)","Dr Jina Son (PHB and environmental rationale)","Hanyang University Department of Mechanical Engineering students (independent reader rebuild)","Bank of Korea Money Museum","Maker Faire Seoul 2026, Seoul Beauty Week (DDP), KINTEX K-Beauty Expo"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6479/wiki/description/figure-11-reader-assembly.webp","caption":"Assembly of the Bio Color ID Reader: a fixed camera, a hemispherical shell carrying five LEDs (405, 525, 625, 660 nm plus broadband white) and a tag holder over four coloured background panels.","credit":"Team PSI Korea, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6479/wiki/description/figure-12-optical-conditions.webp","caption":"Tags on four coloured backgrounds imaged under five LED illumination conditions - the acquisition scheme that produces 60 RGB features per tag.","credit":"Team PSI Korea, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6479/wiki/description/figure-16-independent-tags.webp","caption":"Profiles of the 60 optical features for three tags independently fabricated under identical conditions, which agreed at Pearson r >= 0.9977 with a summary MAE of 3.58 DN.","credit":"Team PSI Korea, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6479/wiki/description/figure-20-paper-imitation-light-purple.webp","caption":"Bio Color ID tags compared with watercolour-painted paper imitations across the 60 features: visually similar samples separate clearly under specific illumination-channel combinations.","credit":"Team PSI Korea, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"This is the single best model in this cohort for what a high-school dry lab should look like, and almost all of it is reachable in one season: the maths is variance decomposition, holdout validation and three summary statistics, the tooling is Python plus Streamlit plus a 20-dollar ESP32 and a camera module, and the compute requirement is zero. The limiting factor is not tooling or compute but intellectual discipline and the mentorship that instils it - the habit of writing what a result does not establish next to every result, of holding out whole specimens rather than single images, and of reporting that integration tests were blocked instead of quietly omitting them.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/psi-korea/","https://2026.igem.wiki/psi-korea/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/psi-korea/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/psi-korea/measurement","https://2026.igem.wiki/psi-korea/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/psi-korea/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/psi-korea/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/psi-korea/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/psi-korea/sustainability","https://2026.igem.wiki/psi-korea/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/psi-korea/project/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/psi-korea/project/parts","https://2026.igem.wiki/psi-korea/wet-lab/experiments","https://2026.igem.wiki/psi-korea/safety-and-security"],"rank":21},"6485":{"team":"WUXI-DSAS","id":"6485","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/wuxi-dsas/","projectTitle":"ReNovo","tagline":"A hidden signal in a drop.","summary":"ReNovo is a whole-cell E. coli biosensor for urinary gentisic acid (2,5-dihydroxybenzoic acid), built as a non-invasive early-screening route for renal cell carcinoma (RCC), which is 80-85% of primary kidney malignancies and asymptomatic exactly when it is curable. The team adapted the maleylpyruvate-responsive GtdR/PgtdA system of Cupriavidus necator, deliberately omitting the gtdT transporter from the published circuit to obtain a monotonic, quantifiable dose-response, and used mCherry to dodge urine's green autofluorescence. Because urinary analyte concentration tracks hydration, a parallel colorimetric creatinine assay is run on the same chip and the result is reported as a gentisic acid-to-creatinine ratio in a three-tier risk band. The second-generation sensor PG2 gave a linear response over 0-12 uM (y = 1.094x + 16.8, R2 = 0.9764) with no significant artificial-urine matrix effect and no cross-reactivity to 2-, 3-, 4-HBA or salicyluric acid.","awards":["Best Sustainable Development Impact — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"Business and policy analysis frameworks applied explicitly: PEST analysis of China and global markets, Porter's five forces, SWOT, a marketing-mix positioning exercise, a five-phase evidence-gated development roadmap to 2035 with documented decision gates, and a dated risk register. A concentric three-layer SDG impact model (Inner Core / Proximal Field / Outer Ripple) organises the sustainability analysis by causal distance rather than importance.","dataviz":"Unusually strong, data-first wiki: an interactive GLOBOCAN 2024 choropleth of age-standardised kidney-cancer incidence across 186 countries and territories with the underlying CSV published for download, keyboard-navigable; per-question survey charts that print exact n, option counts and percentages as accessible text; a concentric SDG framework figure and a cross-goal synergy/trade-off figure; an experiment-report calendar.","datascience":"Survey instrument run in two waves (n = 131 general awareness; n = 70 product-preference, including a ranked-preference question scored out of 5) with results reported per option and used to justify named design choices. Wet-lab statistics are reported properly: linear regressions with R2 (PG2 0.9764; creatinine Jaffe calibration R2 = 0.98; enzymatic cascade calibration R2 = 0.9614; undiluted induction R2 = 0.9294), two-way ANOVA for matrix effect (concentration p < 0.0001, matrix p = 0.6), one-way ANOVA for reciprocal interference (p = 0.9837), exponential and log-linear fits of positive-cell fraction (R2 = 0.9954 and 0.9723).","software":"No standalone software deliverable. The /software page states plainly that it covers only wiki tools (interactive kidney-cancer map, scientific illustrations, experiment-report calendar) with the implementation in the wiki repository. The /model page is equally candid: it is marked RECORDS PENDING and states that a team model with documented assumptions, parameters, code and validation has not been published, pointing readers to Results instead. A phone mini-program that computes the gentisic-acid-to-creatinine ratio, asks a pre-test aspirin question and prints a tiered report is described as a proposal, not a built artefact.","stack":["interactive web map (GLOBOCAN 2024 / IARC data)","CAD hardware drawings","proposed WeChat-style mini-program","wiki repository on GitLab"],"techniques":["microfluidic chip and optical-reader design with spatial and temporal baseline subtraction against a sealed fluorescent standard","four-enzyme creatinine cascade design with documented interferents (endogenous creatine, hemoglobin)","survey design and reporting","regression and ANOVA analysis","PEST / Porter / SWOT market analysis","risk register with gated review points"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Two public surveys underpin the engagement work rather than decorating it: n = 131 on awareness (71.76% had only heard the name of kidney cancer, 35.11% had never considered that early RCC is asymptomatic, 57.25% each named hospital queues and fear of invasive procedures as screening barriers) and n = 70 on product expectations (safe handling ranked top at 4.39/5; 61.43% wanted digital confirmation of a colour readout rather than reading it themselves; 61.43% felt only 'somewhat reassured' about engineered bacteria and wanted more safety information; 44.29% wanted a built-in inactivation step before disposal; 58.57% would share anonymised data only with identity confidentiality; 68.57% preferred short science videos and 67.14% detailed articles with charts). Outreach was then built to that evidence: dual-track materials (comics, posters, brochures in English and Chinese, videos for younger audiences; rigorous seminars for senior students and faculty), age-tiered workshops from kindergarten to Grade 11 (LEGO cell models for Grades 1-3, strawberry DNA extraction for Grades 6-8, gel electrophoresis loading and interpretation for IB Grade 11), a presentation for parents and faculty, and WeChat / RedNote / Instagram channels. On Ms. Fiona You's challenge to 'go beyond iGEM', the team committed to a permanent campus Synthetic Biology Club and structured knowledge transfer so the next cohort builds on rather than restarts the work.","ihp":"Nineteen named stakeholders across clinical medicine, diagnostics, regulation, bioethics and education, each mapped to the specific project section their input changed - and the changes are real, not cosmetic. The single strongest chain is the circuit redesign: the first-generation gtdR-gtdA-gtdT-mCherry sensor gave a non-monotonic response that peaked around 2 uM and then fell, making quantification impossible. Professor Hangxiang Wang suggested testing lower concentration gradients to check for promoter saturation; the team did, and the non-linearity persisted. Dr. Jing Shi then diagnosed the mechanism from the sequence architecture - the large expressed proteins and heavy transporter expression imposed metabolic strain - and Dr. Tengfei Hu proposed replacing active symport with passive diffusion by excising gtdT to stop intracellular 3-maleylpyruvate over-accumulation. Dr. Christina Feng reinforced it from a different angle: heavy metabolic load creates selection pressure for spontaneous loss-of-function mutations and plasmid clearance, which would make a deployed biosensor unreliable. The team deleted gtdT, and the second-generation PG2 construct restored linearity to R2 = 0.9764. Second chain, normalisation: Dr. Zhou (diagnostics researcher) warned that a single urinary metabolite moves with hydration, diet, medication and age so an elevated reading cannot be distinguished from a concentrated sample, and Dr. Gu (urology director) specifically recommended creatinine correction and first-morning-urine collection, while Dr. Xuan supplied the physiology - before a tumour invades the collecting system, biomarker secretion is very low. The team added a parallel creatinine assay as an internal reference and changed its reported output from raw fluorescence to a gentisic acid-to-creatinine ratio; it then changed chemistry between contexts for a stated reason, keeping the Jaffe picric-acid method for 96-well lab characterisation but switching the device to a four-enzyme cascade because Jaffe responds to non-creatinine urinary compounds and needs strongly alkaline conditions unsuited to dried reagents. Third chain, specificity: Dr. Wu (clinical laboratory physician, Wuxi No. 2 People's Hospital) said routine urine tests cannot separate nephritis or UTI from RCC, and Dr. Zhong warned that herbal medicines and diet confound urinary organic acids; the team ran an artificial-urine matrix panel (Na2HPO4, NaCl, KCl, creatinine, albumin, urea) and a look-alike panel (2-, 3-, 4-hydroxybenzoic acid, salicyluric acid, salicylic acid as the main aspirin metabolite), finding no matrix effect and no cross-reactivity, and added a pre-test aspirin question to the proposed app. Fourth chain, hardware and logistics: Dr. Wu demanded elimination of manual pipetting in favour of a single-use enclosed cassette plus automated reader; Dr. Vargas pointed them to Cologuard's non-contact sample handling as a benchmark; Dr. Christina Feng said in Chinese that she would 'recommend that you consider freeze-drying', naming -40 to -60 C cold chain as a commercial killer, and Dr. Zhong noted community clinics lack refrigeration - so lyophilised cells dried into the chip became the design target. Fifth chain, ethics and framing: Mr. Matthew Peatman argued a false positive is ethically acceptable because it only triggers non-invasive imaging whereas a false negative is disastrous, which set sensitivity as the priority over specificity; he also warned of 'psychosomatic health dysmorphia' from unregulated self-testing, and Dr. Martin Goffriller argued results must stay in the user's own hands, which produced local-only processing, opt-in anonymised data sharing and a three-tier Low/Borderline/Elevated report with an explicit disclaimer instead of a raw number. Dr. Wang Keming's insistence that the device be positioned strictly as a preliminary screening aid rather than a diagnosis is carried through the whole wiki. The notable discipline here is how consistently the team labels unvalidated claims: the 80 C / 20-minute thermal inactivation hold, hydrophobic vent containment, post-lyophilisation viability, and the three-tier cutoffs are each written as 'requires validation' or 'has not yet been demonstrated'.","realWorld":"The real-world framing is quantified and sourced: 442,570 new kidney-cancer cases and 144,871 deaths worldwide in 2024 (GLOBOCAN), China carrying roughly 18% of cases (80,211) and the highest national mortality (25,029) while sitting below the world age-standardised rate, so the burden is population scale rather than per-capita risk; 93.6% five-year relative survival for localised disease against 20.3% once metastatic; around 60% of cases found incidentally. The SDG case is built on named sub-targets with the team's own evidence rather than a logo wall: SDG 3 (3.4, 3.8, 3.d), 4 (4.4, 4.7, 4.a), 9 (9.1, 9.5, 9.b), 12 (12.4, 12.5, 12.8), 8 (8.2, 8.3, 8.5), 10 (10.2, 10.3, 10.4) and 17 (17.6, 17.16, 17.17), arranged in a concentric model and accompanied by a cross-goal synergy and trade-off analysis. The team also does something most teams skip: it checks its claim against an external commitment, noting that the UICC World Cancer Declaration 2025-2035 target of diagnosing 60% of cancers early is framed around cancers with existing evidence-based screening (breast, cervical, colorectal) and that RCC's absence from that list is precisely the gap. Regulation is specific: the National Medical Products Administration catalogues instruments and in-vitro diagnostic reagents separately and assesses them independently, so the reader and the biologically active chip follow two tracks of different length and the chip governs the launch date; the EU IVDR is cited as a separate conformity regime; China's Cancer Prevention and Control Action Plan 2023-2030 is noted as favouring early detection but not listing kidney cancer. On cost the team refuses a headline number, stating instead that cost per result is dominated by how often the reusable reader is amortised and that it avoids setting a selling price at this stage, while positioning unit cost low enough to be absorbed into a subsidised programme or public insurance, and identifying that payer, decider and beneficiary are three different parties. After the Jamboree: a five-phase evidence-gated roadmap to 2035 with a documented decision gate between phases and a dated risk register (clinical validity 2028, specificity confounded by salicylate or diet 2028, unresolved creatinine-versus-specific-gravity normalisation 2028, production QC variability 2031, regulatory classification or evidence gap 2033), plus the campus Synthetic Biology Club and the Jiangnan University School of Life Sciences link as the institutional carriers.","partners":["Dr. Haiwen Zheng, community hospital physician","Dr. Wang Keming, Head of Oncology, Second Affiliated Hospital of Nanjing Medical University","Dr. Xuan, Urology Department Director, Wuxi People's Hospital","Dr. Gu, Urology Department Director, Clinical Urological Center","Dr. Zhou, diagnostics researcher, Jiangnan University","Dr. Wu, clinical laboratory physician, Wuxi No. 2 People's Hospital","Dr. Zhong, integrative oncology and early diagnosis expert","Dr. Hangxiang Wang, First Affiliated Hospital of Zhejiang University","Dr. Jing Shi, synthetic biology specialist","Dr. Tengfei Hu, synthetic biology specialist","Dr. Christina Feng, academic principal and biochemist","Dr. Vargas, diagnostic testing and regulatory expert","Mr. Matthew Peatman, Head of Upper Secondary Humanities","Dr. Martin Goffriller, humanities specialist","Ms. Fiona You, Executive Principal","Ms. Lulu Zhu, Director of School Pastoral","Ms. Shuyi Xu, biology educator","Fan Jia, public representative","Ms. Gu, public representative","Jiangnan University School of Life Sciences"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6485/wiki/sustainability-figure-01-concentric-impact-framework.avif","caption":"ReNovo's concentric SDG framework: SDG 3 at the clinical core, SDGs 4/9/12 at the user interface, and SDGs 8/10/17 in the outer ripple, with layer position set by causal distance rather than importance.","credit":"Team WUXI-DSAS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6485/wiki/sustainability-figure-02-cross-goal-synergies-and-trade-offs.avif","caption":"Cross-goal synergy and trade-off analysis across the seven claimed Sustainable Development Goals.","credit":"Team WUXI-DSAS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6485/wiki/human-practices-specificity-panel.avif","caption":"The specificity panel built in response to clinicians Dr. Wu and Dr. Zhong: urine matrix components (Na2HPO4, NaCl, KCl, creatinine, albumin, urea) and structurally related phenolics (2-, 3-, 4-HBA, salicyluric acid) tested against gentisic acid.","credit":"Team WUXI-DSAS, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6485/wiki/human-practices-reader-concept.avif","caption":"Proposed reusable optical reader, shown closed and open, 90 x 110 x 100 mm, designed after survey respondents asked for digital confirmation rather than reading a colour change themselves.","credit":"Team WUXI-DSAS, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Copy WUXI-DSAS's stakeholder map that indexes each of nineteen interviewees to the numbered project section their advice changed, so a reader can audit the causal claim; and copy their discipline of writing 'requires validation' next to every unproven design feature (thermal inactivation hold, lyophilisation viability, risk cutoffs) instead of letting a proposal read as a result.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/wuxi-dsas/","https://2026.igem.wiki/wuxi-dsas/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/wuxi-dsas/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/wuxi-dsas/sustainability","https://2026.igem.wiki/wuxi-dsas/entrepreneurship","https://2026.igem.wiki/wuxi-dsas/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/wuxi-dsas/results","https://2026.igem.wiki/wuxi-dsas/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/wuxi-dsas/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/wuxi-dsas/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/wuxi-dsas/engineering","https://2026.igem.wiki/wuxi-dsas/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/wuxi-dsas/safety-and-security","https://2026.igem.wiki/wuxi-dsas/team"],"rank":7},"6497":{"team":"Worldshaper-Shanghai","id":"6497","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/worldshaper-shanghai/","projectTitle":"SweetCycle","tagline":"Don't sell the molecule, sell the step that makes it cheap to separate: engineered glycosyltransferases licensed into existing Reb A refineries","summary":"Worldshaper-Shanghai engineered the two glycosyltransferases that perform the final steps to Rebaudioside M (SrUGT76G1 and SrUGT91D2), screened eight designed variants in a contained Stevia hairy-root chassis with qPCR and HPLC read-out, and found that T284I raised Reb M to 21.96 micrograms per gram fresh weight against 15.44 for wild type while the SrUGT91D2 variants did nothing. The commercial insight is genuinely original: Reb M is expensive not because the pathway is hard but because it sits at about 2 percent of a pool of near-identical glycosides, so the only lever that matters is raising that fraction (eta), and the party who benefits is whoever owns the separation column. They therefore sell a licensed process asset to Reb A refiners rather than a product, backed by a published, recomputable techno-economic model that ranks three production routes and finds their own current enzyme performance gives a negative NPV in every scenario. They were nominated for Best Entrepreneurship in the High School section.","awards":["Best Entrepreneurship — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A purpose-built Reb M Commercialisation Decision Model (25-year NPV at a 12 percent discount rate across mild, neutral and fast price-convergence scenarios) plus PESTEL, Porter's Five Forces scored force by force, SWOT with deliberately unbalanced counts because the null results are listed as weaknesses, 4P, Business Model Canvas rewritten for licensing, bottom-up TAM/SAM/SOM, a four-phase milestone table with quantitative gates and pre-committed fallback decisions, and a risk register where every row has a triggering measurement and the decision that follows.","dataviz":"Eighteen figures carrying analysis rather than decoration: an evidence chain where node area is influence on the plan and colour is source type, a log-scale cost-per-sweetness positioning map, an S3 cost build-up split into bought-in versus engineerable lines, a Sherwood-type separation-cost curve, a compliance-status matrix with ok / work-in-progress / not-assessed, a 25-year NPV chart, an economic-window heatmap, a product-architecture diagram and a stakeholder map that deliberately includes the parties their success would harm.","datascience":"The standout dry-lab contribution. They normalise every price to RMB per kilogram of sucrose sweetness equivalent (RMB/SSE) because a 300x and a 250x sweetener cannot be compared per kilogram, which immediately shows that their real competitor is sucralose at 0.33 RMB/SSE, not sucrose at 5.40. The separation-cost model is calibrated as C_sep = 40/eta on top of a shared RMB 198.9/kg, giving a twenty-fold fall from about RMB 2,000/kg at eta = 2 percent to about RMB 100/kg at 40 percent. Decision thresholds are stated as checkable numbers: alpha greater than or equal to 0.9 or TON greater than or equal to 108 for the enzyme route to beat the fermentation proxy, eta greater than or equal to 9, 16.8 and 26.5 percent for three different comparisons. The model is published as runnable code with a parameter spreadsheet.","software":"model_core.py producing model_results.json and then the figures, published so a counterparty can re-run the analysis, with a supplementary Excel of parameters and scenarios.","stack":["Python (model_core.py)","JSON results pipeline","Excel parameter and scenario workbook","HPLC","qPCR","Stevia hairy-root culture via Rhizobium rhizogenes","Questionnaire Star"],"techniques":["glycosyltransferase variant design (T284I, T284S)","RFC-compliant part registration","contained hairy-root functional screening in 8-10 weeks","steviol glycoside quantification by HPLC","techno-economic route modelling with NPV and sensitivity","Sherwood separation-cost calibration"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"A 503-respondent consumer survey (Questionnaire Star, 2026) reported with the uncomfortable parts intact: natural/healthy/safe drives 61.95 percent of motivation but taste only 12.06 percent and price 4.16 percent, while 57.38 percent would preferentially buy if taste approached sucrose at a reasonable price, and 35.34 percent had never heard of stevia or monk-fruit sweeteners at all. They pair this with a brand-marketing observation that 80-90 percent of consumers cannot distinguish sweetener types, and draw the warning rather than the flattering conclusion: a natural label does not sell itself. Consumer content on Xiaohongshu and Douyin is scoped explicitly to label literacy and evidence-based sugar reduction, with a stated compliance boundary of no health claims and no in-house taste panels.","ihp":"Thirteen stakeholder interviews plus the survey, tabulated with who said what and, in a separate column, exactly what it changed. Three decisions are traceable to specific conversations rather than to any market report. AGV (Ai-Chi-Wei) brand R&D gave the priority order cost before supply stability before natural origin, which moved the success metric to cost per unit sweetness and narrowed the first market to premium beverage; AGV marketing added where not to compete, naming mass-market fruit tea as unwinnable and partial replacement as the realistic ask. Tiancao Technology, a functional food ingredient supplier, killed the plant-is-cheaper claim outright and pushed them from building capacity toward licensing. A fermentation engineer reordered the roadmap by stating that fermentation or in vitro catalysis is the pragmatic route for 5-10 years, that a new plant variety takes 7-12 years to commercialise, and that LCAs typically favour fermentation over leaf extraction by roughly 92 percent less cropland and 90 percent less water, which caused them to delete every claim that sunlight makes plants greener. Mr Lu, a grower and extension author, supplied the three clauses growers actually respond to (yield not reduced, purchase premium, guaranteed contract) and the line that without a demonstration field there is no trust, which became a hard Phase 3 gate. The China Food and Beverage Association established that different production processes are legally different raw materials even for an identical molecule, turning process disclosure into a named workstream. Most tellingly, three separate interviews told them whole-plant residue valorisation is a brand story rather than a purchase criterion, and they removed it from the base business case rather than argue with the data.","realWorld":"The most intellectually honest commercialisation analysis in this cohort, high school or otherwise, and the honesty is structural rather than decorative. The business model is a licence, not a product: a characterised SrUGT76G1 variant plus immobilisation and UDP-glucose-recycling parameters delivered as a technology transfer file, priced at a running royalty of 15 percent of the licensee's incremental gross margin (range 10-25 percent) with signing and milestone fees sized only to recover transfer cost, plus a per-hectare trait royalty of 10-15 percent later and a hairy-root pre-screening service throughout. Every price is anchored to a number the counterparty can verify in their own plant, which they state as the point: nobody is asked to believe a claim, only to run a calculation. Unit economics are fully built: target process cost RMB 438/kg at alpha 0.90 and TON 30, licensee incremental margin RMB 362/kg at a Reb M price of RMB 800/kg, royalty about RMB 54/kg, a five-year indicative P&L with every input as a substitutable row, cumulative break-even in commercial year 2 to 3, and a next-twelve-months funding ask of RMB 150,000-200,000 (USD 21,000-29,000) itemised down to calibration standards and two counterparty visits, with the explicit comment that they would rather present a small itemised ask than a round number. Market evidence is primary: 13 interviews and a 503-person survey, with secondary market data (Mordor, Grand View) used only where it is the right layer and with the two series explicitly declared non-comparable. The TAM is left unquantified and flagged as data gap G1 rather than fabricated. The regulatory path is specific and already open for the lead route: China's National Health Commission announcements 2024 No. 2 and 2025 No. 1 approved steviol glycosides by enzymatic conversion and by fermentation as food additives, which is precisely why the enzyme route leads and the engineered trait follows, with the non-GM conventional-crossing route (published at 56.8-61.6 percent Reb M) kept as a pre-planned fallback that avoids the GM layer. Now the blunt assessment. There is no company, no signed licence, no letter of intent, and one engaged counterparty rather than a customer; they say so in their own weaknesses. Their SrUGT91D2 variants produced a null result across five samples and they publish it, arguing correctly that doing so is what makes the SrUGT76G1 result credible. Their own Reb M quantification is labelled directional only: single batch, no biological replicate, all peak areas below the lowest calibration standard, so absolute values are extrapolated, and the fix (0.5, 1 and 2 microgram standards) is listed as outstanding work. Every performance number in the business case is still a literature value, which they say outright. And the model's most important finding is one that undermines their own pitch: at today's enzyme performance the NPV is negative in every scenario, and the economic window for the in vitro route is 0.7-4.6 years, shorter than the payback period, so the advantage is a window rather than a moat. The continuation plan is correspondingly disciplined: a four-artefact customer-validation gate for the next twelve months (a named refinery completing non-food performance testing, a brand defining partial-replacement acceptance criteria, a toll manufacturer quoting the kilogram-scale process, a regulatory and freedom-to-operate screen), with the statement that until those exist the NPV and P&L remain scenario analyses rather than sales forecasts. They even list the parties their success would disadvantage, including Reb A-only refiners holding the wrong asset and smallholders likely to be reached last, and the public-health trade-off that cheaper sucrose-like sweetness is only a gain if it displaces sugar rather than water.","partners":["Tiancao Technology (functional food ingredient supplier; first named economic buyer, engaged)","AGV / Ai-Chi-Wei, China Taiwan (brand R&D and marketing; specification pull)","China Food & Beverage Association (regulatory and standard-setting convening)","Mr Lu, stevia grower and extension author (trait adoption and demonstration plots)","Shanghai Chenshan Botanical Garden (plant and scientific infrastructure)","A fermentation engineer and a plant synthetic biologist (route and containment advice)","Toll manufacturer or enzyme house (to be contracted in Phase 2)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6497/wiki/worldshaper-shanghai/entrepreneurship/image3.webp","caption":"Positioning map of cost per sucrose-sweetness equivalent on a log scale, showing sucralose at 0.33 RMB/SSE as the ceiling over the whole natural-sweetener category","credit":"Team Worldshaper-Shanghai, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6497/wiki/worldshaper-shanghai/entrepreneurship/image15.webp","caption":"Twenty-five-year NPV by route and scenario at a 12 percent discount rate; only the combined enzyme-then-trait strategy stays positive across all three price-convergence paths","credit":"Team Worldshaper-Shanghai, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6497/wiki/worldshaper-shanghai/entrepreneurship/image16.webp","caption":"Economic-window heatmap: the year the enzyme licence stops making money under each price path, giving the 0.7 to 4.6 year window on today's enzyme performance","credit":"Team Worldshaper-Shanghai, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6497/wiki/worldshaper-shanghai/entrepreneurship/image1.webp","caption":"Evidence chain in which node area is the influence a source had on the plan and colour is the source type, built from 13 interviews and a 503-person survey","credit":"Team Worldshaper-Shanghai, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Build one recomputable decision model per project, published as code plus parameters, whose job is to tell you which route your asset belongs in and what performance threshold makes it worth pursuing, then write every milestone as a quantitative gate with a pre-committed continue, modify or stop decision. The practice that makes it work is publishing the result that hurts: their model says today's enzyme gives a negative NPV, and saying so is what makes every other number believable.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/worldshaper-shanghai/","https://2026.igem.wiki/worldshaper-shanghai/entrepreneurship/","https://2026.igem.wiki/worldshaper-shanghai/assets/entrepreneurship-DyASDvRD.js"],"rank":7},"6511":{"team":"Labi-Taiwan","id":"6511","section":"High School","country":"Taiwan","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/labi-taiwan/","projectTitle":"BlueCatcher: a cell-free electrochemical biosensor for MDD-associated circulating microRNAs","tagline":"A multistep biosensor validated stage by stage, from three-way-junction target recognition to a calibrated square-wave voltammetry readout.","summary":"Labi-Taiwan built BlueCatcher, a portable cell-free electrochemical biosensor for circulating microRNAs associated with major depressive disorder, intended as objective biological evidence alongside clinical assessment rather than as a diagnosis. The signal chain is deliberately long: a three-way junction recognises the target miRNA and releases a trigger strand, the trigger activates a toehold switch that expresses a nuclease, the nuclease cleaves a methylene-blue-labelled DNA reporter, and the released reporter is captured on a gold-modified screen-printed carbon electrode and quantified by square-wave voltammetry. Because a final signal alone cannot show that every step behaved, the team built a stepwise measurement framework in which each stage is independently validated before integration, with the degree of calibration deliberately matched to each measurement's role. The project also carries a machine-learning design suite and a strong education programme grounded in its own 432-respondent survey; it won the iGEMers Prize in the High School section.","awards":["Best Measurement — Nominee (High School)","iGEMers Prize — Winner (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A stepwise measurement framework that follows the sensor from target recognition to electrochemical readout, with a published table listing for each method its purpose and its reusable output. Each measurement is classified by the question it can answer: structural validation, relative comparison under matched conditions, or absolute quantification. Three modular measurement workflows are released separately from the project so that another team can adopt one without adopting BlueCatcher. The software follows a Design-Predict-Test loop in which predictions are returned to the wet lab and the results are used to judge where the model performed well.","dataviz":"A heatmap of background-adjusted fluorescence response across all 25 three-way-junction probe combinations, measured every five minutes for 30 minutes; time-course FRET curves with mean +/- SD (n = 3); dose-response and specificity bar panels with individual data points overlaid and significance annotated; overlaid baseline-corrected SWV voltammograms across the reporter concentration series with an inset log-linear calibration; batch-to-batch SWV bar charts with individual measurements shown; an interactive experimental-design flow diagram mapping every assay onto the stage of the sensor it validates.","datascience":"The calibration philosophy is stated explicitly and is the most transferable thing here: different measurements are calibrated to different degrees according to what they are for. FRET measurements, used only for comparison under matched conditions, are reported as a background-adjusted response (delta F equals fluorescence with target minus fluorescence without target) and are explicitly said to be in arbitrary units, intended for within-experiment comparison and not for absolute cross-instrument quantification. Toehold-switch fluorescence is interpreted against a three-way control framework of sensor-only, trigger-only and sensor-plus-trigger, with fold change calculated as (sensor+trigger minus trigger-only) over (sensor-only minus trigger-only) so that background and OFF-state leakage are separated from activation; this is what revealed a 43.4-fold response in BL21(DE3) against 3.6-fold in pLysS and justified the strain choice. Native PAGE is used only as qualitative structural validation, and the team states that the paired plus- and minus-target lanes are different experimental conditions and not independent replicates, with quantitative reproducibility deferred to the replicated FRET measurements. Only the final electrochemical step is developed as an absolute quantitative endpoint: SWV on functionalised Au@SPCEs across 0 to 500 nM methylene-blue reporter gives a nonlinear full-range response but an approximately linear relationship against log concentration, Ip = 2.313 log10(C) - 2.028 with R2 = 0.9457, and the limit of detection is derived properly from the blanks as I_LOD = I_blank + 3 sigma_blank then inverted through the calibration to give 7.53 nM, with the 0 nM condition serving both as the blank for the threshold and as the negative control. Reproducibility is measured at the level that actually varies, the electrode: three independently fabricated batches of Au@SPCE were measured against the same 200 nM reporter, showed no statistically significant difference, and gave a combined coefficient of variation of 10.66%. Upstream quality control is explicit and non-binary: UV absorbance (A230, A260, A280) is used as a checkpoint rather than a pass/fail gate, with the full table of ratios published including a sample flagged for an anomalous A230 of 1.097 and a 260/230 of 0.048, and samples carried forward to Sanger sequencing as the higher-resolution arbiter in a declared chain of plasmid extraction, purity check, restriction digest, sequence confirmation, then functional measurement. Electrode fabrication itself is characterised stepwise by cyclic voltammetry, chronoamperometry and electrochemical impedance spectroscopy across bare SPCE, Au@SPCE, probe-modified, MCH-blocked and reporter-hybridised states, with EIS used as interface characterisation rather than as the quantitative readout. Statistics are named: two-way ANOVA with Tukey multiple-comparisons for the cell-free screening, with significance levels reported alongside n = 3 and individual points. The team also states what has not been done, that the toehold-switch-to-AciI construct is not yet built so the system is not integrated, and refuses to claim that BlueCatcher is faster, more sensitive or more accessible than qRT-PCR until it is, marking every projected time in its comparison table with an asterisk.","software":"The BlueCatcher Software Suite, with independent design modules for three-way-junction probes (trained Random Forest) and toehold switches (trained XGBoost), available through a browser interface and as a local install. A user supplies a target or trigger sequence, the suite generates candidate designs, computes sequence, structural, thermodynamic and interaction features using NUPACK and custom scripts, applies the trained model, and returns ranked candidates with prediction confidence plus the complete sequence components needed to order and test them, exportable as CSV. Documented limits of applicability are published: 18 to 25 nucleotide targets for the TWJ module and up to 30 nucleotide triggers for the toehold module, stated as the sequence spaces represented in training rather than as biological limits, together with a discussion of dataset coverage, how prediction confidence should be interpreted, and the NUPACK dependency that constrains distribution. Supporting material includes complete Sanger sequencing datasets as PDFs and three standalone protocol documents (nucleic-acid characterisation, toehold-switch cloning and expression, electrochemical signal generation).","stack":["Square-wave voltammetry on gold-modified screen-printed carbon electrodes","Cyclic voltammetry, chronoamperometry, open circuit potential, EIS","FRET fluorescence (FAM/BHQ1)","Native and SDS-PAGE with in-gel fluorescence","Cell-free expression systems","Sanger sequencing","NUPACK","Random Forest and XGBoost","ESP32-WROOM-32 portable reader with WiFi/Bluetooth","Polyimide flexible heater"],"techniques":["Calibration depth matched to measurement purpose","Background-adjusted response (delta F) for relative screening","Sensor-only / trigger-only / sensor+trigger control framework","Log-linear SWV calibration with R2","Blank-derived LOD (mean + 3 sigma, inverted through the curve)","Batch-to-batch reproducibility with coefficient of variation","Standardised baseline correction","Two-way ANOVA with Tukey post-hoc","Orthogonal protein-level validation of a fluorescence readout","Quality-control chain with a higher-resolution arbiter","Machine-learning pre-screening with declared domain limits"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Education began with research rather than assumption. An anonymous online survey, preceded by an informed-consent statement and screened for careless or too-fast responses (12 excluded, 432 retained), used translated versions of three validated instruments: the six-item Depression Literacy and eight-item Misconceptions subscales of the DepSter scale and the nine-item perceived-stigma subscale of the Depression Stigma Scale, with internal consistency reported for this sample (alpha 0.66, 0.84 and 0.72). Literacy was high (mean 25.1 of 30) and misconceptions were broadly rejected (15.7 of 40), while perceived public stigma sat in the moderate-to-high range (29.3 of 45), with the highest-scoring items describing expected social exclusion. The team's conclusion, that the gap in Taiwan is stigma rather than knowledge, redirected the education programme; a saturated path model was estimated to test how education and personal contact relate to literacy, misconceptions and the perceived limits of counselling-only assessment. The programme that followed used different approaches for different audiences: a flipped classroom, a summer laboratory camp whose toehold-switch protocol is published as a reusable four-day workflow, family information sessions, a podcast, TGEM community-building among Taiwanese teams, and social media.","ihp":"Stakeholder work spans healthcare professionals, researchers, regulatory specialists, potential users and investment professionals, and fed an entrepreneurship roadmap covering regulatory planning and market analysis. The project's framing, that BlueCatcher complements rather than replaces clinical evaluation, comes from this engagement, as does the explicit statement that the device detects signals and does not diagnose.","realWorld":"The clinical gap is stated concretely: MDD assessment depends on interviews, symptom reporting and professional judgement, and patients face irregular follow-up because of stigma or access, no quantitative way to assess recovery or relapse, and trial-and-error treatment selection. The long-term aim is a portable format operating closer to the point of care in settings without centralised laboratory infrastructure, avoiding the reverse transcription and PCR amplification that qRT-PCR requires. The hardware is specified down to the reader's internals: an insertable electron reader module carrying the electrode pad and a cellulose overflow pad, a battery, a polyimide flexible heater, a lever that mechanically breaks a separation membrane in a two-chamber microtube to release the second reagent, and an ESP32 module that processes the signal and transmits results by WiFi and Bluetooth to a companion application that reports Low, Moderate or High biomarker variation with timestamped metadata rather than a binary diagnosis.","partners":["TGEM (Taiwanese iGEM community)","Previous Taipei-KCISLK teams (V1 2023, V2 2024, V3 2025)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6511/wiki/wet-lab/measurement/v2/figure-23.avif","caption":"Square-wave voltammetry quantification of the methylene-blue reporter on functionalised Au@SPCEs across 0 to 500 nM. The inset shows the approximately linear relationship between peak current and log concentration (R2 = 0.9457), from which a blank-derived limit of detection of 7.53 nM is calculated.","credit":"Team Labi-Taiwan, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6511/wiki/wet-lab/measurement/v2/figure-24.avif","caption":"Batch-to-batch reproducibility of the SWV readout: three independently fabricated batches of functionalised Au@SPCE measured against the same 200 nM reporter, showing no significant difference and an overall coefficient of variation of 10.66%.","credit":"Team Labi-Taiwan, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6511/wiki/measurement/flow/full.avif","caption":"The experimental design of the project, mapping every assay onto the stage of the sensing pathway it validates, from three-way-junction target recognition through toehold-switch signal generation to electrode fabrication and the electrochemical readout.","credit":"Team Labi-Taiwan, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6511/wiki/dry-lab/hardware/figure-3.avif","caption":"Exploded view of the portable electrochemical reader's internal components: the insertable electron reader module with the electrode pad and cellulose overflow pad, a battery, a polyimide flexible heater, a lever that breaks the microtube's separation membrane, and an ESP32-WROOM-32 module on the main PCB.","credit":"Team Labi-Taiwan, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Match the amount of calibration to the job each measurement does: screening comparisons can stay in background-subtracted arbitrary units if you say so, but the one measurement you report as a concentration needs a real calibration curve, a blank-derived limit of detection, standardised baseline correction and a between-batch coefficient of variation. Treating every signal as equally quantitative is where overclaiming starts.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/labi-taiwan/measurement","https://2026.igem.wiki/labi-taiwan/software","https://2026.igem.wiki/labi-taiwan/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/labi-taiwan/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/labi-taiwan/education"],"rank":33},"6520":{"team":"Al-Nahrain-IRAQ","id":"6520","section":"Undergrad","country":"Iraq","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/al-nahrain-iraq/","projectTitle":"SYNOVA","tagline":"The first Iraqi iGEM team: a software platform and home-built bioreactor for turning date-palm waste into bioethanol, built under hard local constraints","summary":"Al-Nahrain-IRAQ is the first Iraqi team ever to compete in iGEM, from Al-Nahrain University, with a team drawn from Biotechnology, AI & Robotics Engineering, Civil Engineering and Business Economics. SYNOVA tackles yeast fermentation of date-palm waste into bioethanol, with a software platform of four apps whose governing rule is that a prediction must never be presented as a measurement, so predicted, published-measured and your-own-lab-measured results are kept separate and never combined into one number. The project is defined as much by what Iraq lacks: no local S. cerevisiae collection to borrow, no liquid ethanol sensor purchasable anywhere in Iraq or neighbouring countries at a reasonable price or wait, no local gene bank because of national restrictions, and RT-qPCR primers that took months and arrived only on 19 October. They built the sensor themselves, isolated four candidate wild yeasts from local sourdough, pomegranate vinegar, date vinegar and an overripe date from Najaf, and set an explicit goal of leaving behind protocols, tools and trained people that the next Iraqi team can start from.","awards":["iGEM Spirit Award — Winner (Undergrad & Overgrad)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"A hard evidence-provenance rule enforced in code and in every claim: two engines kept separate, with Engine 2 handling measured evidence and Engine 1 handling predicted evidence, and every result labelled predicted, measured (published) or measured (your lab). Pre-registered checks: the team fixed pass criteria before testing and published the failures rather than tuning parameters to pass, writing that 'a model tuned to pass would say less about how it behaves on real batches'. Human Practices used a four-column what-we-heard / who-said-it / what-we-changed / where-it-landed table.","dataviz":"Hand-built accessible SVG figures with full text descriptions in <desc> elements, including a three-band dot figure showing the funnel from every testable strain, gene and condition down to the five experiments worth running first at the bench, a two-engine diagram with a dark band separating prediction from measurement, a 74-square grid of environmental samples with four marked as candidate isolates, a four-row prototype-evolution figure, and a load-cell density-sensor explainer.","datascience":"Engine 2 is a differential-expression pipeline: RNA-seq results analysed with DESeq2 (PyDESeq2), filtered at padj < 0.05 and at least two-fold change, gene IDs resolved through the R64 reference genome, narrowed across five layers to an 18-gene hand-checked catalogue each with a published effect, covering ethanol, heat, sugar transport and osmotic stress. Its validation check: 83 genes were significant in both of two experiments where about 42 were expected by chance, and MED15 came out at log2 fold change -6.58. Engine 1 is a batch kinetics model plus optimizer whose check failed and was published as failed: it predicted 2.4 g/L ethanol at 13.25 hours where 7.6 g/L was measured, and its grid sweep did not recover the published optimum from Ahmad et al. (2021). The team states that four of Engine 1's parameter values have no published source, that parameters were read from papers with AI assistance and have not yet been re-checked by a team member, that values from Ghose and Tyagi (1979) could not be re-checked at all for lack of full-text access, and that the statistical design of the differential-expression analysis has not been reviewed in depth so its tables should be treated as unreviewed.","software":"SYNOVA: four apps behind one landing page. Engine 1 (kinetic model of one batch fermentation plus condition optimizer, which refuses results breaking mass-balance rules), the micro-max method (re-implementation of a published growth-rate method, which matched the published method within a pre-set tolerance and passed a held-out strain), Lab Data (tools where any lab enters its own growth curves, RT-qPCR Ct values, primer and isolate sequences and fermentation runs), and Engine 2 (the differential-expression pipeline). Code on GitLab, data on Zenodo (10.5281/zenodo.23533297), with a docs/DATA.md listing file sizes and checksums and an honest note that two data files are not yet in the public record and must be requested from a team member. A guided demo was added after stakeholder feedback that the platform had to be usable even by experts. The dry lab also built interactive educational games based on SYNOVA for children. Bioinformatics workflows were built in Galaxy with Trimmomatic, HISAT2 and SAMtools.","stack":["Galaxy","Trimmomatic","HISAT2","SAMtools","DESeq2 / PyDESeq2","Google Colab","NCBI BioProject / BLAST","GitLab","Zenodo","Arduino","MQ3 vapour sensor","load-cell density sensor (own design)","SD-card data logging"],"techniques":["wild yeast isolation from local environmental samples (74 samples, 4 candidates)","ethanol tolerance screening on PDA with 7.6%, 8% and 10% ethanol","PCR with S. cerevisiae-specific MEX67 primers","ITS region amplification and sequencing (pending)","agarose gel electrophoresis","YPS30 anaerobic fermentation","crystal violet staining and 100x oil immersion morphology","four-generation home-built bioreactor with foam seal, SD logging, own liquid density sensor and coil condenser"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"The Spirit story is structural, not sentimental: the first Iraqi team in iGEM built a public-engagement programme that ran from primary-school children up to a deputy minister, and documented every rung. School workshops: Ajyal Al-Amal School on 15 July 2026 for 25 children and Sarh Baghdad School on 20 July 2026 for 30 children, 45 minutes each, explicitly designed so children could participate 'regardless of their previous knowledge'. Each session centred on hands-on banana DNA extraction so that a scientific concept became something children could observe directly rather than hear about, supported by interactive games the dry lab built from SYNOVA itself, themed colouring sheets, lab-coat-shaped candies and a question-and-answer competition. Both schools asked the team to return, and the principal of Sarh Baghdad School awarded the team certificates of appreciation. For older audiences they ran two 'AI in Biotechnology' workshops: an online session on 30 July 2026 with the KAUST iGEM team's Synthetic Biology Mentorship Program (13 students, 45 minutes, where Al-Nahrain was hosted as a special guest) and a two-hour session on 30 August 2026 at the American Space inside the American University in Baghdad for 90 participants drawn from students, educators and the wider community. They then convened a public event at Al-Farabi University with two moderated discussion panels, hosted by their supervisor Dr Zaid Nsaif Abbas: 'The AI Revolution: From Data to New Horizons of Innovation' with the AI Research Center at Al-Farabi University, the CEO of First Finance and the Dean of the College of Excellence at the University of Baghdad; and 'From Presence to Impact: Iraq's Voice on the Global Stage', moderated by Dr Muntadher Qasim with an assistant professor from Al-Farabi, a representative of the Office of the Deputy Minister for Scientific Research Affairs and the CEO of Al-Jisr Marketing Company - a panel built squarely around the question of Iraqi participation in global competitions like iGEM, which is the Spirit theme made into a programme. Institutional engagement climbed deliberately: the President of Al-Nahrain University on 28 April 2026, where the team pitched three project ideas to assembled professors and, on the feedback, abandoned all three and started again before arriving at SYNOVA; and Dr Hayder Abdul Zahid, Deputy Minister of Higher Education and Scientific Research, together with the syndicate presidents of human medicine and dentistry, on 6 September 2026, to spread the idea of iGEM in Iraq. They also exhibited at ITEX, the Iraqi International Telecommunication and Information Technology Exhibition, talking to technology companies and meeting the President of Al-Imam Al-Sadiq University. Internationally they were visibly a team being helped and then helping back - mentorship from other teams before they started, guest slot in KAUST's mentorship programme, project exchanges with KFUPM and McGill, the KAUST TAWASOL Showcase, and MIT-MAHE's Scents of the World activity where they chose a scent to represent Iraq. Their own stated lesson is unusually clear-eyed: there is no single way to teach science, a hands-on experiment suits a child while open discussion suits university students, 'our responsibility as educators is not just to explain information, but to make it understandable and leave room for curiosity and questions', and they documented their activities and methods specifically so other iGEM teams and educators can adapt them. Accessibility is built into the wiki as a reading-settings panel offering looser spacing (more space between letters, words, lines and paragraphs), narrower lines, a plain background with no grain or glyph field, motion reduction layered on top of the system setting, and high contrast, with settings kept on-device and ignored by printing; every SVG figure carries a written description.","ihp":"Human Practices was run as an input to design with the change recorded each time. Raghad Al-Shabandar, president of the National AI Center, pointed out that without clear or abundant labelled public data an AI model was the wrong tool and computational and statistical methods would pay off - so the team switched to equation-based models and statistics. Hussain Ali Mohammed, an AI instructor and data scientist, told them their ethanol-yield accuracy was unreliable and pointed them to ODE-based papers, which shaped Engine 1. Abdulrahman Faisal, CEO of Nabu Academy, warned the platform would not be adopted unless it informed labs or industry from their own data - which produced the Lab Data page where any lab enters its own growth curves, Ct values, sequences and fermentation runs. Ahmed Al-Katib, an economic expert and entrepreneurship trainer, said the platform must be as user-friendly as possible even for experts, so they added a guided demo. Muslim Sagban Altamimi, then Head of the Agricultural Engineers Syndicate in Diyala, discussed agricultural production, domestic consumption and spoilage and suggested extending beyond dates to figs and grapes, which went into future work. Dr Mohammed of Al-Khutwat Al-Sareea Company gave them access to his agricultural land to collect raw materials. Deans of Business Economics and Engineering at Al-Nahrain shaped the economic and feasibility thinking, and Manar Al-Obaidi (CEO of First Finance, known from Iraq's Shark Tank) became the team's sponsor after several meetings. The team also completed the two-day iGEM Entrepreneurship Boot Camp and a one-week British Council entrepreneurship programme. Their closing note on all this is refreshingly disciplined: 'We do not consider encouragement alone proof that our scientific design has changed.' They also name the dilemmas they faced - whether to train an AI model or build from published equations, and what to do when a model failed pre-fixed checks - and record choosing the equations and keeping the failures visible.","realWorld":"The explicit deliverable is infrastructure for the teams that follow: a page titled 'Building the ground for future Iraqi iGEM teams' lists what can be reused - the S. cerevisiae isolate data on Zenodo (10.5281/zenodo.23533297), SYNOVA's four apps on GitLab, the bioreactor design together with its failure notes, and 22 qPCR primers documented as iGEM Registry parts with their specificity warnings - plus hard-won practical advice (mind the season; start where fermentation is already happening; make your own reference; don't start with ethanol; use enough inoculum for tolerance screening; our media recipes; plan for delays). Because Iraq has no local gene bank, SYNOVA ships a small reference set of yeast genes labs can use to check primers and isolates. The environmental case is date-palm waste valorisation into bioethanol as a substitute for gasoline; the social case is public exposure to bioinformatics, a field the team notes most people locally do not know exists. Content is licensed CC BY 4.0, and AI assistance is disclosed on a Responsible AI section of the Attributions page, including that the PyDESeq2 and SNP-matching Colab code were AI-assisted and that which assistant was used was not recorded.","partners":["Al-Nahrain University (President Prof. Dr. Ali Abdulaziz Al-Shawi; Deans of Business Economics and Engineering)","Ministry of Higher Education and Scientific Research (Deputy Minister Dr. Hayder Abdul Zahid; Office of the Deputy Minister for Scientific Research Affairs)","Ajyal Al-Amal School","Sarh Baghdad School","American Space, American University in Baghdad","Al-Farabi University (AI Research Center; Dr. Zaid Nsaif Abbas; Dr. Ahmed Falah)","University of Baghdad, College of Excellence","ITEX - Iraqi International Telecommunication and Information Technology Exhibition","Al-Imam Al-Sadiq University","National AI Center of Iraq (Raghad Al-Shabandar)","Nabu Academy (Abdulrahman Faisal)","Agricultural Engineers Syndicate, Diyala (Muslim Sagban Altamimi)","Al-Khutwat Al-Sareea Company (Dr. Mohammed, land access)","First Finance (Manar Al-Obaidi, sponsor)","British Council","iGEM teams: KAUST (Synthetic Biology Mentorship Program, TAWASOL Showcase), KFUPM, McGill, MIT-MAHE (Scents of the World)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6520/wiki/hp-education/banana-dna-interactive-learning-01.avif","caption":"Banana DNA extraction with schoolchildren at Ajyal Al-Amal and Sarh Baghdad schools","credit":"Team Al-Nahrain-IRAQ, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6520/wiki/hp-education/banana-dna-interactive-learning-04.avif","caption":"Lab-coat-shaped candies made for the school workshops","credit":"Team Al-Nahrain-IRAQ, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6520/wiki/hp-education/banana-dna-interactive-learning-05.avif","caption":"Children working through the team's themed colouring sheets","credit":"Team Al-Nahrain-IRAQ, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6520/wiki/hp-education/inclusivity-creating-opportunities-01.avif","caption":"A school workshop session: children and team members working together","credit":"Team Al-Nahrain-IRAQ, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6520/wiki/hp-education/bringing-together-academic-institutional-international-01.avif","caption":"Bringing academic, institutional and international partners together around SYNOVA","credit":"Team Al-Nahrain-IRAQ, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6520/wiki/hp-education/connecting-synova-local-resources-01.avif","caption":"Connecting SYNOVA to local agricultural resources: date-palm waste as feedstock","credit":"Team Al-Nahrain-IRAQ, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Build the engagement ladder deliberately and publish your failures: Al-Nahrain went schoolchildren to university students to industry to a deputy minister in one season, each conversation logged as what-we-heard / what-we-changed, and left behind a reuse page (isolates on Zenodo, code on GitLab, Registry primers, bioreactor design with its failure notes, and seven blunt pieces of practical advice) so the next team in their country starts further along than they did.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/al-nahrain-iraq/","https://2026.igem.wiki/al-nahrain-iraq/education","https://2026.igem.wiki/al-nahrain-iraq/human-practices","https://2026.igem.wiki/al-nahrain-iraq/engagement","https://2026.igem.wiki/al-nahrain-iraq/contribution","https://2026.igem.wiki/al-nahrain-iraq/model","https://2026.igem.wiki/al-nahrain-iraq/hardware","https://2026.igem.wiki/al-nahrain-iraq/bioinformatics"],"rank":26},"6523":{"team":"NIS Almaty-Medeu","id":"6523","section":"High School","country":"Kazakhstan","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/nis-almaty-medeu/","projectTitle":"MiRVOX (Pulmora and OncoNose)","tagline":"Two approaches to accessible lung cancer screening: programmable RNA detection of blood microRNAs, and exploratory breath volatile organic compound patterns","summary":"NIS Almaty-Medeu built MiRVOX, two parallel platforms for accessible lung cancer research: Pulmora, a synthetic biology platform for programmable detection of circulating microRNAs in blood, and OncoNose, an exploratory engineering project on volatile organic compound patterns in exhaled breath. The team states plainly on its landing page that neither platform is a clinically validated diagnostic test. The project is framed by hard numbers - 2.5 million lung cancer diagnoses and 1.8 million deaths worldwide in 2022, 12.4% of new cancers and 18.7% of cancer deaths, and 4,429 estimated new cases in Kazakhstan where it is the second most diagnosed cancer and the most common cancer in men. Their education and inclusivity work is extraordinarily large for a high-school team and is written with unusual methodological honesty, including a published disagreement between two of their own documents' participant counts.","awards":["Inclusivity Award — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"An explicit four-step human practices loop (Ask, Understand, Change, Check back) with the questions for each stakeholder group published before the conversations happened, deliberately 'to keep us honest about what we learned afterwards'. Inclusivity was structured as three questions: what prevents participation, whose input should guide our response, and what can we change so people have a meaningful opportunity to contribute - with a barrier-to-response table published for each strand. A five-stage workshop framework (Introduction, Demonstration, short explanation, Practical work, Presenting the result) with three prepared difficulty levels per activity.","dataviz":"Barrier-and-response tables mapping each identified barrier to the specific adaptation it produced; a day-by-day accelerator schedule table with focus, activities and output per day; a feedback table mapping each piece of feedback to the implication it had for programme delivery; partnership tables distinguishing institutions from contributions. The wiki also uses explicitly labelled 'Limitation' callout boxes throughout.","datascience":"Reach figures are reported with deliberate methodological care: the team distinguishes the 70-school partnership network from the 23 schools visited in person, flags that summer attendance figures may include returning children, and separately records mentor-network size versus completed mentoring outcomes. Most strikingly, they publish a 'Limitation: two different participant counts' box stating that their Inclusivity document reports 120 participants in the biocomputing course while the Education document reports 64, that they have not established which is correct, and that neither figure should be quoted until confirmed. They also state that their evidence shows participation and application but that longer-term changes in understanding would require more consistent follow-up.","software":"Code Against Cancer, a three-module no-equipment computational biology course: 'Find the Bug in DNA' (compare sequences in Google Sheets, identify differences, then encounter sequence search via BLAST), '3D Molecular Tetris' (explore protein structures in Mol* Viewer and relate molecular shape to interaction) and 'Pipeline of Life' (order the stages of a simplified biological analysis workflow on a collaborative Miro board). Lab Ladder, a 54-page illustrated code-free handbook, walks beginners through six tool 'rungs' with screenshots and worked accessions: NCBI (NM_000207), UniProt (P42212), Benchling (BBa_J23100), BLAST, Geneious Prime and AlphaFold (Q9NZQ7). A Kazakh-language facilitator platform, Tagylym, hosts the methodology.","stack":["BLAST","NCBI","UniProt","Benchling","Geneious Prime","AlphaFold","Mol* Viewer","Google Sheets","Miro","LEGO robotics programming","Google Meet","Kahoot"],"techniques":["microRNA biomarker detection","cell-free reactions intended for use outside a laboratory","primer design","volatile organic compound pattern analysis from exhaled breath","simple optical reader concept for low-cost local manufacture"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"Three large programmes, each documented barrier-first. First Qadam, run jointly with Panheya Robotics (Panheya supplied LEGO sets and robotics mentors, the iGEM team supplied biological content and volunteers), brings practical STEAM, engineering and biotechnology education to children aged 6-17 facing barriers of location, money, institutional setting, health or unadapted teaching formats. Six school visits in January 2026 reached 226 children; the team then contacted over 100 school directors and built a 70-school collaborating network (the Keleshek network), visiting 23 schools in person near Almaty, Taldykorgan and Taraz between February and May with online sessions and lesson recordings for the rest. Their key finding is quotable: access to equipment did not automatically mean access to meaningful participation, because teachers and children often needed help to start using resources they already had. So they trained teachers alongside students and supplied reusable instructions - and by September teachers and older students in nine partner schools were delivering activities themselves, with five school teams entering a dedicated competition league in June after the team helped create an entry route for Keleshek schools. Daniyar, a research project mentor at Al-Farabi School No. 31, reported running his own activity using the materials from their joint workshop. With Integrity Unite, a volunteer organisation supporting students from unstable financial backgrounds, a first online robotics session for 40 children showed the format was too theory-heavy and depended on kit the children did not own; the team responded by building the no-equipment, mentor-supported Code Against Cancer biocomputing course, run over one week in March after two weeks of recruitment, which produced roughly 34 completed mini-projects with 21 in revision and 26 at the idea stage. With 'House of Mercy: Autism Can Be Overcome', a first April session for 15 children revealed that shared LEGO sets meant nothing stayed with the children; the team then partnered with Sheber Bala to add supervised woodworking so each child made an individual wooden honey spoon plus a drawing on ecological and biological themes to take home, used calm communication and named badges, and allowed flexibility in pace, repetition, breaks and individual assistance across roughly eight summer visits of 10-20 children each. Crucially they write that they adapted to the particular group 'rather than treating a diagnostic label as a complete description of a learner' and explicitly refuse to generalise from one group of autistic children to all. An April workshop for 20 children in residential care combined supported LEGO work with age-banded books on innovation and biotechnology. A paediatric oncology visit for 15 children in Bishkek exposed a continuity barrier - the volunteers and the LEGO left with them - so after consulting KAUST iGEM representatives and a Central Asian iGEM ambassador the team built 12 individual hospital kits containing warm socks, stickers, a book, science colouring activities and crosswords, a change prompted by medical oncologist Baurzhan Ospanovich and summarised as a shift in planning question from 'what can we deliver during a visit?' to 'what opportunities will remain afterwards?'. Delivery was in Russian and Kazakh with visual demonstration alongside verbal instruction, three difficulty levels, two-to-four-hour sessions with flexible pacing, groups capped at five where intensive support was needed and 15 otherwise, with three to five volunteers per group, and multiple contribution routes within a session (assembling, programming, drawing, choosing materials, explaining a result, presenting). Second programme: Girls Go First, which targets the gap between interest in STEM and access to mentorship, networks, resources and leadership roles. A January online workshop with Technovation Girls put six female speakers in front of more than 130 girls across CIS countries; a spring global forum with Yurt Space (a girls-led aerospace engineering community) and Technovation Girls drew participants from more than three countries; a National Forum and StartUp Contest in January-February required every project to be girl-led with girls at least a third of each team, drew about 700 applications from around 386 teams, brought roughly 300 participants from 70 teams to finals in Almaty and Astana, and distributed a KZT 1,000,000 prize pool (backed by Women in Tech, InvestlyHub and StemTrades) as seed funding to seven girl-led teams; an April-June Business Case Championship with Astana Hub and its 11 regional subhubs involved 137 teams and 441 girls across 11 regions of Kazakhstan, each girl-led, with the challenge being to examine existing STEM systems and propose ways to make them more inclusive - and the ideas from that championship fed back into First Qadam's own inclusion policy. An ongoing global mentorship programme with the National Student Research Institute links 65 mentors to more than 45 mentees across over 15 countries, 31 of the mentors being FIRST Robotics and iGEM alumni. The team documents one concrete continuation chain honestly and modestly: Aidana, a Grade 11 participant, met judge Alexander Tyutin (Google Developer Groups) at one of their events, he became mentor for her EcoHub project, and her team went on to win an award at Technovation Girls - with the team noting that the award was Aidana's team's achievement and their own contribution was the opportunity through which the mentoring began. They also publish a limitation box stating that mentor-network size and completed mentoring outcomes are counted separately and that further follow-up is needed. Third: two flagship events. 'Can We Outsmart Cancer?', a free online forum on 8-9 August 2026 on Google Meet with five invited speakers (from UC Berkeley, IIT Patna, Oxford and KAUST) plus two student organisers, three tracks (fundamental research; applications, startups and commercialisation; synthetic biology and student participation through iGEM), a 'Truth or Myth?' Kahoot quiz on cancer misconceptions, and Q&A after each talk; 54 participants on day one and 41 on day two (95 participations) from ten countries - Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, the United States, Romania, Tanzania, Indonesia, India, Pakistan, Saudi Arabia and the United Kingdom - with an EdTech partner, 1609+, giving three free subscriptions and a 10% discount to everyone else. The team published both their own organising lessons (cold LinkedIn outreach works when personal and specific; one Instagram post is not enough so registration plus a WhatsApp group plus reminders are needed; attendance dropped on day two so send inter-day reminders; split content into beginner and advanced next time) and the speakers' critical feedback (schedule delays, technical difficulties, a suggestion to prepare backup questions). Then the Bio-Innovator Accelerator, a ten-day hybrid programme from 10-21 August 2026 for 55 participants in teams of three or four - 23 in person at American Corner Almaty and 32 online from Almaty, Astana and regional centres - built because promising laboratory developments in Central Asia rarely reach commercialisation. Week one covered problem validation, customer discovery, TAM/SAM/SOM market sizing, no-code MVP prototyping and unit economics; week two covered biosafety by design, regulatory pathways, intellectual property and freedom-to-operate searching in Google Patents, scientific storytelling, pitch decks and a live Demo Day before an independent jury. Eleven named guest lecturers ran the modules, including founders of ArtSkin, Grader.ai, LUMO/AsarQ and SoundVision, NU iGEM members on Human Practices and dry-lab prototyping, and the KAUST iGEM lead on project design and storytelling with optional 30-minute per-team mentoring. Demo Day projects included FermentAI, a computational platform predicting fermentation outcomes and simulating strains and reactor conditions, and MycoBlock, insulation and building panels grown from Ganoderma lucidum mycelium on local oak sawdust waste as an alternative to imported petroleum insulation. Finally, four open-access magazines published digitally in Kazakh, Russian and English, each deliberately serving one reader intent: Synapse (two issues, 15 and 20 pages - what synthetic biology is, iGEM's history from a 2003 MIT course, Kazakhstan's iGEM history from the first Nazarbayev University team in 2013, a five-step roadmap for joining a lab, questions to ask a lab before joining, six career paths, and national grants such as Zhas Galym and Bolashak); Beyond the Diagnosis (24 pages - cancer causes and types, modern treatments, eight myths versus facts, a patient story and clinician insight, microRNA biomarkers); Lab Ladder (54 pages - the illustrated code-free tool handbook); and iGEM Atlas (20 pages - the Oncology Village, award-winning 2024 projects, commercial transitions such as PvP Biologics to Takeda, startup guides). All four are archived in a public folder and offered explicitly as an adaptable blueprint future Central Asian teams may freely adopt, translate and build on, with Lab Ladder positioned as a new-member onboarding manual.","ihp":"The human practices page is built around a published commitment: list the groups whose answers would change the project and publish the questions for each before the conversations, so the team cannot retrofit what it learned. Five stakeholder groups are specified with their questions - clinicians (where in the pathway a triage test could help, what accuracy would earn their trust, what a false alarm costs), patients and the public (whether breathing into a device is acceptable and where, how an elevated-risk result should be explained, what should happen next and how fast), public health and policy (how lung cancer screening is organised in Kazakhstan today, what evidence a pilot would require, which regions have least CT access), bioethics and biosafety (what is required before collecting human breath samples, how to handle results the project is not qualified to interpret, what biosafety rules apply to cell-free reactions used outside a lab) and engineers and manufacturers (what a simple optical reader would cost to build locally, how cell-free reagents could ship without a cold chain). The team's framing sentence is that a screening test is a health-system decision, not a device decision, and that affordability, portability and follow-up capacity shape the design as much as the biology.","realWorld":"Consent and privacy practice is unusually explicit for a high-school team: activities were pre-coordinated with receiving organisations through correspondence, calls and preliminary visits; parents or legal representatives gave permission, with photography consented separately so children whose parents declined were not photographed; participants could decline an activity, a photograph or a question; access to original photographs and video was restricted to designated representatives of the visiting team and the receiving organisation and publication followed agreement with the organisation; and the team states that their photographs therefore do not represent every participant or activity. Prize-pool money in Girls Go First went through official consent-related documentation. Open resources: four trilingual magazines in a public folder, lesson recordings, age-banded books, science colouring activities and crosswords, guides and workshop methodology, with the full methodology available through partnership at a published contact address. External recognition includes a letter dated 22 April 2026 from the Ministry of Health of the Kyrgyz Republic thanking the team for supporting people with oncological conditions. Partnership documentation covers hospital work across multiple countries and is presented with an explicit distinction between resources already delivered and offers of future collaboration.","partners":["Panheya Robotics (LEGO sets, robotics mentors)","Integrity Unite (students from unstable financial backgrounds)","House of Mercy: Autism Can Be Overcome","Sheber Bala (woodworking expertise)","Keleshek school network (70 collaborating schools; 23 visited)","Al-Farabi School No. 31","National Centre for Motherhood and Childhood, Bishkek","Asan ophthalmology department, Dushanbe","MIOT International, Chennai","BLK-Max","Marengo Asia Hospitals","Artemis Hospital (Gurugram)","Fortis Healthcare / National Research Center for Maternal and Child Health, Astana (UMC branch)","Ministry of Health of the Kyrgyz Republic (letter of thanks)","KAUST iGEM and a Central Asian iGEM ambassador (hospital kit design)","Technovation Girls","Yurt Space","Astana Hub and its 11 regional subhubs","Women in Tech Kazakhstan, InvestlyHub, StemTrades (prize pool)","National Student Research Institute (mentor network)","American Corner Almaty (accelerator venue)","1609+ EdTech platform","Nazarbayev University iGEM","Startup Lab 119, iHub, Accelerate Prosperity and High Technology Park (Kyrgyzstan)"]},"images":[],"gemsTakeaway":"Copy two habits: publish your stakeholder questions before the interviews so you cannot retrofit your conclusions, and shift the planning question from 'what can we deliver during a visit?' to 'what will remain afterwards?' - which is what turned a hospital workshop into 12 take-home kits and turned 23 school visits into nine schools now running the activities themselves.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/nis-almaty-medeu/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nis-almaty-medeu/education/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nis-almaty-medeu/inclusivity/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nis-almaty-medeu/human-practices/","https://2026.igem.wiki/nis-almaty-medeu/model/"],"rank":7},"6529":{"team":"CHINAGuangdongShimen","id":"6529","section":"High School","country":"China","village":"","wiki":"https://2026.igem.wiki/chinaguangdongshimen/","projectTitle":"Re-CDI Alert: an engineered EcN platform for monitoring and treating recurrent Clostridioides difficile infection","tagline":"A p-cresol-sensing probiotic biosensor, characterised with a measurement protocol written so that other teams can repeat it.","summary":"Shimen built an Escherichia coli Nissle 1917 (EcN) biosensor that detects p-cresol, the metabolite Clostridioides difficile produces to suppress competing gut microbes and secure its own niche, and couples detection to a therapeutic output targeting the TcdB toxin. Because recurrence after CDI treatment is diagnosed only once symptoms return, the aim is to shift from symptom-triggered diagnosis toward proactive risk sensing during the post-treatment window. The dry-lab contribution is the measurement protocol itself: a documented, reusable workflow for characterising a small-molecule biosensor, covering plate layout, normalisation, chassis comparison, tolerance limits, dose response and specificity against structural analogues.","awards":["Best Measurement — Nominee (High School)"],"dry":{"frameworks":"The measurement page is written as a contribution: seven numbered measurement strategies are stated up front, then each is given its own design, methods, results and discussion, with the standardisation framed explicitly as something future iGEM teams can reuse. Measurements are ordered so that each answers a prerequisite for the next, establishing the reporter, then the chassis, then the tolerance window, then the dose response, then specificity.","dataviz":"Nine numbered measurement figures covering the chassis comparison, the tolerance assay, the concentration-response series and the specificity panel, each expandable on the wiki alongside the protocol that produced it.","datascience":"Three parts of this stand out for a high-school team. First, plate layout is treated as a source of error: three empty wells are left between each set of three replicate wells, because repeated experiments showed that when adjacent wells differed substantially in p-cresol concentration, the high-concentration wells affected the readings from the low-concentration wells. That is an optical and chemical cross-talk control most teams never run. Second, normalisation is written out as a formula rather than implied, with normalised fluorescence calculated as (sample fluorescence minus fluorescence background) divided by (sample OD600 minus medium OD600 blank), and the team specifies what each blank must be: the fluorescence background from a GFP-negative culture matched to the experimental conditions, and the OD600 blank from cell-free medium. The stated reason is that total fluorescence depends on cell abundance, so raw fluorescence cannot be compared across conditions and only a per-biomass value answers the question. Third, the viable measurement window is established before the dose response is interpreted: a tolerance assay incubating EcN at 0 to 20 mM p-cresol with OD600 read every two hours over 24 hours found no appreciable inhibition at 0.1 to 1 mM, inhibition emerging at 2 mM, strong inhibition at 5 to 10 mM and near-total inhibition at 20 mM, which produced the rule that induction experiments must stay at or below 1 mM so that growth inhibition cannot be mistaken for a sensor response. Only then is the full dose response run, across fifteen concentrations from 0 to 5 mM, locating a discernible rise at roughly 500 nM to 1 uM and a working range of 1 uM to 1 mM. Chassis comparison is measured rather than argued: BL21 and modified EcN (cryptic plasmids pMUT1 and pMUT2 removed and the flagellar regulators flhDC deleted to free cellular resources) are run side by side, and the team reports that OD600 stayed between about 0.77 and 0.89 in both strains with no decrease as concentration rose, which is what licenses the claim that the fluorescence rise is not a cell-number artefact. Specificity is tested against the structural analogues that would actually confound a gut measurement, with o-cresol, m-cresol and phenol all at the same 10 uM concentration, and all reading close to the uninduced control while only p-cresol rose. All fluorescence is read on a BioTek plate reader at 485 nm excitation and 528 nm emission in triplicate, with a no-p-cresol negative control throughout. The team notes a p-cresol stock preparation protocol down to the weighed mass and 0.22 um filtration, with light-protected aliquots stored at -20 C.","software":"","stack":["BioTek microplate reader (485/528 nm)","OD600 growth monitoring in a plate reader","E. coli Nissle 1917 chassis (pMUT1/pMUT2-cured, flhDC-deleted)","GFP reporter","PcrSR-Pcmh two-component p-cresol sensing system"],"techniques":["Spaced replicate wells to prevent inter-well interference","OD600 normalisation with specified fluorescence and medium blanks","Tolerance assay to define the non-inhibitory working range","Fifteen-point concentration-response series","Specificity testing against structural analogues at matched concentration","Chassis comparison under identical conditions","Technical triplicates with a no-inducer negative control","Protocol documentation written for reuse"]},"good":{"publicEngagement":"An education page and an inclusivity page accompany the project.","ihp":"Human Practices is reported in four stages with four named changes of direction. Conversations with a Chinese clinician reframed the opening question from whether CDI exists in China to whether patients are being identified in time, because the physician attributed low reported incidence partly to insufficient testing and clinical awareness rather than low disease occurrence. Interviews with two physicians abroad narrowed the target population from the general public to people with a confirmed CDI history who remain at high risk of recurrence. Interviews at Guangdong Hospital of Integrated Chinese and Western Medicine highlighted that antibiotic treatment itself further disturbs the gut microbiota, which moved the project from a standalone detection concept to coupling monitoring with targeted intervention. Advice from a microbiology researcher, Dr Peng, replaced a planned multivalent antibody with a single E3 monovalent nanobody against TcdB to improve experimental feasibility and reduce cost, and also informed the EcN chassis optimisation that improved protein expression.","realWorld":"The intended use is a monitoring platform for the post-treatment recurrence window in patients with a confirmed CDI history, chosen because recurrence occurs in 20 to 30% of patients after an initial episode and up to 60% after a second, and because diagnosis of recurrence usually waits for overt symptoms such as diarrhoea. Chassis selection is justified against three stated criteria: adaptation to the human intestinal environment, availability of established genetic tools, and biosafety with a history of clinical use. The project also states a biosafety framework as one of its outputs.","partners":["Guangdong Hospital of Integrated Chinese and Western Medicine","Dr Peng (microbiology researcher)","Dr Miti (clinician, childhood diarrhoea research)"]},"images":[{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6529/wiki/public/measurement/measurement-figure-01.webp","caption":"Measurement figure from the Re-CDI Alert characterisation workflow, which reads GFP fluorescence at 485 nm excitation and 528 nm emission alongside OD600 so that every value can be normalised per unit biomass.","credit":"Team CHINAGuangdongShimen, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6529/wiki/public/measurement/measurement-figure-05.webp","caption":"Measurement figure from the chassis and dose-response work comparing BL21 with the modified EcN strain across a p-cresol gradient, with OD600 recorded alongside fluorescence to show that the rise is not driven by changes in cell number.","credit":"Team CHINAGuangdongShimen, iGEM 2026 wiki"},{"url":"https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6529/wiki/public/measurement/measurement-figure-07.webp","caption":"Measurement figure from the tolerance and specificity work. The tolerance assay fixed 1 mM as the upper usable p-cresol concentration, and the specificity panel compared p-cresol with o-cresol, m-cresol and phenol at a matched 10 uM.","credit":"Team CHINAGuangdongShimen, iGEM 2026 wiki"}],"gemsTakeaway":"Run a tolerance curve before the dose-response curve. Establishing the concentration at which the chassis itself starts to suffer defines the window in which a reporter signal can honestly be attributed to sensing rather than to dying cells, and it costs one 24-hour plate.","sources":["https://2026.igem.wiki/chinaguangdongshimen/measurement","https://2026.igem.wiki/chinaguangdongshimen/description","https://2026.igem.wiki/chinaguangdongshimen/human-practices"],"rank":7}};
